(225,13,0,0,'Outside the East Gate of Grimhaven','  You are just outside the gates of the city of Grimhaven that lies west of\nhere.  You are fairly near the edge of the plateau upon which the city of\nGrimhaven was built and it looks like a wide, dusty road stretching east may\nlead off into the wilds beyond.  A pathway follows the wall to the north\nand south.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(226,-13,0,0,'Outside the West Gate of Grimhaven','  You are just outside the gates of the city of Grimhaven that lies east of\nhere.  You are fairly near the edge of the plateau upon which the city of\nGrimhaven was built and it looks like a wide, dusty road stretching west may\nlead off into the wilds beyond.  A pathway follows the wall to the north\nand south.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(227,0,13,0,'Outside the North Gate of Grimhaven','  You are just outside the gates of the city of Grimhaven that lies south of\nhere.  Where you stand is the very edge of the plateau upon which the city\nwas founded, and the road away from town leads north and downward from\nhere.  A pathway runs along the wall to the east and west.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(228,-6,-1,0,'Commonwealth Lane','  This is a well maintained, north-south road running through a large city.\nTo the west, a large building sits.  To the east is a popular mage store.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(229,-6,-2,0,'Commonwealth Lane','  This is a well maintained, north-south road running through a large city.\nTo the west, a large building sits.  To the east you see the side of a\nsmall shop.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(230,-6,-3,0,'Commonwealth Lane','  This is a well maintained, north-south road running through a large city.\nTo the west, a large building sits.  To the east is Market Road.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(231,-6,-4,0,'Commonwealth Lane','  This is a well maintained, north-south road running through a large city.\nTo the west, a large building sits.  To the east, you see the side of a\nsmall shop.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(232,-6,-5,0,'Commonwealth Lane','  This is a well maintained, north-south road running through a large city.\nTo the west of here is a fortified door leading into the back of a large,\nstone building.  To the east lies a pawn shop.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(233,-6,-6,0,'Commonwealth Lane','  This is a well maintained, north-south road running through a large city.\nTo the west, you see a large building and from the east the smell of\ngarbage wafts over a tall wooden fence.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(234,-6,-7,0,'Commonwealth Lane','  This is a well maintained, north-south road running through a large city.\nTo the west, you see the wall of a large building while east is a\nbrilliantly lit up store.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(235,-6,-8,0,'Commonwealth Lane','  This is a well maintained, north-south road running through a large city.\nTo the west and south you see Perimeter Road.  Commonwealth Lane runs north\nfrom here.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(236,-5,-3,0,'Market Road','  You are at the west end of the shopping district in Grimhaven.  Immediately\nto your west is Commonwealth Avenue with Ye Olde Leather Shoppe to the north\nand a fine jewelry store to the south.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(237,-4,-3,0,'Market Road','  This part of Market Road seems to be well traveled.  Market Square is\nimmediately to your east with the road continuing westward.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(238,-3,-3,0,'Market Square','  This is the center of Grimhaven\'s Trading District.  There are shops of\nall sorts about the square, seemingly you could get anything you wanted\nhere.....for a price.  A large building sits to the northeast, a wonderful\naroma of various foods coming from the open doorway facing the square.  To\nthe south two small shops sit to each side of the square while a larger\nshop is to the northwest with a sign hanging over the entrance bearing a\nsword and shield upon it.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(239,-2,-3,0,'Market Road','  This part of Market Road seems to be well traveled.  Market Square is\nimmediately to your west with the road continuing eastward.  To the north\nlies a large building housing one of the best restaurants in all of\nGrimhaven!\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(240,-1,-3,0,'Market Road','  You are at the eastern edge of Grimhaven\'s shopping district.  Immediately\nto your north is the famous Roaring Lion Inn.  Just thinking of its\ncomfortable beds makes you kind of tired!  South of here lies a barn used\nby the Inn as a stable.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(241,-3,-1,0,'Branish Way','  You are on the north part of Branish Way.  King\'s Way is to the north of\nhere and a shop to the west.  The side of a large building sits to the\neast while south leads towards the center of the Market District.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(242,-3,-2,0,'Branish Way','  This is near the heart of the busy marketplace of Grimhaven.  Market\nsquare is directly south of you and the side of the armory is to your west.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(243,-3,-4,0,'Branish Way','  Immediately to your west is the side of Taloc\'s general store and from\nthe east the smell of fine food emanates from Froddor\'s through a tiny\nlouvered window which vents heat and fumes from the cookstoves.  Market\nSquare is to the north.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(244,-3,-5,0,'Branish Way','  You are at a gate in this very busy shopping street.  To the west is the\ndonation area and to the east you hear the sound of puppies barking.  South\nof here, beyond a gate, is the newer southern market district.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(245,-7,7,0,'Furfoot Path','  This short road connects Commonwealth Lane with Perimeter Road and\nis so named because the Hobbit embassy\'s entrance is to the east beyond a\nsmall ironwork gate.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(246,-6,7,0,'Hobbit Embassy Grounds','  A small plot of grassland growing in the midst of the urban sprawl of\nGrimhaven is maintained by the local hobbit ambassadorial squad.  To the\nwest lies a simple but stout ironwork gate out to Furfoot Path while north\nof here lies a door into the Embassy.  A window looks east into the embassy.\n',2,131073,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(247,-6,8,0,'Hobbit Embassy Reception','  This is a small (although not by hobbit standards) room at the front of the\nembassy designed for the greeting of visitors.  South lies a door out to the\nembassy grounds and east are some ornate double doors.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(248,-5,8,0,'Hobbit Embassy Conference Room','  A small but ornate room serves the embassy as a place to hold official\nfunctions and other meetings.  West there are ornate double doors leading\nto the reception area and south lies the ambassador\'s office.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(249,-5,7,0,'Hobbit Ambassador\'s Office','  A simple, small but elegant room serves as the ambassador\'s office.  A\nwindow looks west out onto the Embassy Grounds while a door leads north to\nthe Conference Room.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(250,1,10,0,'A Small, Disorganized Office','This is a fairly small room of modest decoration.  Its ceiling is vaulted,\nwith a single banner hanging down in the center.  The room has a stone floor\nand stone walls.  An archway leads out to the east.\n',-1,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(251,2,10,0,'An Entryway','  It would seem that this is some sort of entryway.  The stone walls and\nstone floor are quite drab.  To the south, a hallway stretches deeper into\nthe building.  There is an archway to the west, and large doors on the\nnorth wall.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(252,3,10,0,'A Small, Ornate Bedroom','  Nauseatingly gaudy, this bedroom is covered with doo-dads and gizmos.\nDoors to the north and east provide a means of escape from this clutter.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(253,4,10,0,'A Scummy Kitchen','  Foul odors insult your taste buds as you survey this grisly scene.\nAlthough it\'s quite apparent that this room is used as a kitchen, you find\nit disgusting to thing that someone actually eats the food that is created\nhere.  Basically, the place is filthy.  To the west is a small doorway.  To\nthe south, an archway leads out.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(254,1,9,0,'A Metal Stairwell','  The wooden floor below you is strongly fastened to the stone walls of\nthis room.  A twisting, metal stairwell lies in the center of the room,\nleading both upwards and downwards.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(255,2,9,0,'A Dull Hallway','  Running from the north to the south, this dull hallway hardly deserves\nmuch description.  A small archway leads out to the west and to the east.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(256,3,9,0,'A Mess Hall','  You are in the north-west corner of a huge mess hall.  Rows of wooden\ntables surround you, most with benches before them.  To the west, a small\narchway leads out of this room.  There is a small sign on the wall here.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(257,4,9,0,'A Mess Hall','  You are in the north-east corner of a large mess hall.  Rows of tables\nsurround you, and an archway leads out of the room to the north.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(258,1,8,0,'An Entryway','  This is a small entryway before a set of large doors, to the west.  This\nbuilding is made of cold stone, and doesn\'t ventilate very well.  You are\nquite uncomfortable.  A hallway stretches to the east, while an archway\nprovides escape to the south.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(259,2,8,0,'Hallway','  A dull hallway turns here from the north to the west.  In the southwest\ncorner of this room someone has made a pathetic attempt at decorating the\nwall with an ugly banner.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(260,3,8,0,'A Mess Hall','  You are in the south-west corner of a huge mess hall.  To the south, a\nhigh archway leads out of this room.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(261,4,8,0,'A Mess Hall','You are in the south-east corner of a huge mess hall.  Rows of wooden tables\nsurround you, most with benches before them.  There is a banner hanging from\nthe southern wall which catches your eye.\n',-1,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(262,1,7,0,'A Tidy Office','  This small room seems to function as someone\'s office.  They keep the\nplace quite well organized, as you can tell by the well swept stone floor\nand the plain, bare stone walls.  To the north, an archway provides an exit.\nTo the south is a door.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(263,2,7,0,'A Small Latrine','  This is a small, dirty latrine.  You are overwhelmed by the stench of this\nplace.  A wooden doorway to the east provides escape.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(264,3,7,0,'A Narrow Hallway','  This short, north-south hallway is quite narrow.  It runs from a high\narchway to the  north, to a caved in (under-construction) passageway to the\nsouth.  To the east, you can see a small office.  To the west is a wooden door.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(265,4,7,0,'A Small Office','  This is a small office with stone walls and floor.  You are not impressed.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(266,1,10,1,'A Small Storage Room','  This is a small room, apparently used to store things.  The walls are\nwooden, and the place looks quite clean and freshly painted.  A small door\nlies on the east wall.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(267,0,0,0,'Wombat Hunter Barracks','This is a particularly large and decorated room.  A door on the east wall\nmakes way to the rest of the barracks, which seem in comparison much plainer.\nThis room is decorated with various drawings and paintings of \'The Enemy\' --\nthe Wombat.  Graffiti is scrawled now and then, only to be washed up later,\nthings like, \"The wombat killed my parents!\" and \"He took my mom out for dinner\nand then he didn\'t call her!\" There are trophies on the wall, bits and pieces\nof the Wombat.  Maps are tacked up, showing the trail of the Wombat; where\nhe\'s been, where they\'ve encountered him and where they expect him next.\nEverything refers to \"the\" wombat, but it seems there are many, thus ensuring\nthe need for a Wombat Protection Squadron.  And those, those are the brave men\nand women who take up residence here.\n',0,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(268,3,10,1,'In the Barracks','  This is a huge room, stretching in almost every direction.   You figure it\ncould house quite an army!\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(269,4,10,1,'In the Barracks','  This is a huge room, stretching to the west and south.  You figure it\ncould house quite an army!\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(270,1,9,1,'The Middle of a Stairwell','  This is a wooden platform providing access to a circular stairwell.  The\nwalls are quite narrow here, and the ceiling is quite low.  To your east is\na hallway and the staircase goes down out of sight and up to a watchtower.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(271,2,9,1,'A Wooden Hallway','  The wooden floor and wooden walls look quite freshly painted.  Everything\nis institution white.  Even the ceiling looks so clean you could eat off of\nit!  The hall continues southward, while archways lead out in the other\ncompass directions.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(272,3,9,1,'In the Barracks','  This is a huge room, stretching to the north and east.  You figure it could\nhouse quite an army!  To the west, an archway leads out.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(273,4,9,1,'In the Barracks','  This is a huge room, stretching in to the north and west.   You figure it\ncould house quite an army!\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(274,1,8,1,'A Small Office','  This is a small, official-looking office.  It is kept nice and neat, with\nbeautiful pictures on the wooden walls.  Doorways lie on the east and south\nwalls.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(275,2,8,1,'End of a Hallway','  This white-walled hallway comes to an end before three doors, to the east,\nwest and south.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(276,3,8,1,'A Large Office','  This is a large and extremely official looking office.  Charts and graphs\nhang from the walls, along with maps of various locations.  Doorways lead\neast and west, while an archway leads south.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(277,4,8,1,'A Large Bedroom','  This wooden-walled bedroom looks quite expensively decorated.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(278,1,7,1,'Simple Living Quarters','  Someone lives here quite simply.  The walls are bare, and the floor is\nclean swept.  There is a door on the north wall.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(279,2,7,1,'A Clean Latrine','  This latrine is well kept.  Someone must have polished it for hours,\nbecause it shines beautifully.  You really feel like if you had to go, this\nis where you\'d want to be.  A doorway leads out to the north.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(280,3,7,1,'A Peaceful Study','  This is a luxurious, plush study which is painted in quiet, pleasing tones.\nAn archway leads out to the north.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(281,4,7,1,'A Walk-in Safe','  This is a large, walk-in safe.  The room is quite dusty.  A small door\nleads out through the north wall.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(282,1,9,2,'High Up in a Watch-tower','  You are atop a wooden platform, high in a tower.  From this vantage point,\nyou can survey a large city.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(283,1,9,-1,'Bottom of a Stairwell','  You are at the bottom of a metal stairwell, which stretches into the\ndarkness above.  The stone floor here is cracked, and degrades into dirt as\na tunnel stretches to the east.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(284,2,9,-1,'A Dirt-walled Tunnel','  You are inside a dirt-walled tunnel, which runs from east to west.  The\nwalls and ceiling are held up by wooden support beams which seem quite old.\nTo the south, a small side tunnel juts off into darkness.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(285,3,9,-1,'A Dirt-walled Tunnel','  You are inside a narrow, dirt-walled tunnel.  The walls and ceiling are\nsupported by ancient wooden beams.  There is a small door where the tunnel\nends to the east and a cell to the south.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(286,4,9,-1,'An Armory','  It\'s quite clear this room is used as an armory from the sign on the wall.\nOther than that, it\'s rather nondescript, being small and dull.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(287,1,8,-1,'Untidy Living Quarters','  Some slob lives here, thats for sure.  This is a small bedroom which\nlooks like it hasn\'t been cleaned in ages.  The dirt floor is just covered\nwith junk, while the walls and support beams are rotting away and caving\nin.  A wooden archway leads out to the east.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(288,2,8,-1,'A Damp, Musty Tunnel','  You are inside a damp, musty tunnel which runs from the north to the\nsouth.  The tunnel floor is rather muddy here, and you can smell human\nwaste nearby.  A wooden archway leads to the west, while the tunnel ends in\na door to the south.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(289,1,7,-1,'A Dirty Cell','  You stand in a stinking, rat-infested (if you are so lucky!), damp cell.\nYour only means of escape is the cell door to the east.\n',2,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(290,2,7,-1,'Before the Cells','  You are before two cells, which lie to your east and west.  There is a\nsmall door on the north wall.  To the south, this long room continues.\n',2,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(291,3,7,-1,'A Stinking Cell','  You stand in a stinking, rat-infested (if you are so lucky!), damp cell.\nYour only means of escape is the cell door to the west.\n',2,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(292,1,6,-1,'A Dull Cell','  This is a cold, boring cell.  The walls are dull grey stone, and a metal\ngate provides escape to the east.\n',2,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(293,2,6,-1,'Before Some Cells','  You are before three cells, which lie to your east, west, and south.  To\nthe north, this long room continues.\n',2,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(294,3,6,-1,'A Dull Cell','  This is a cold, boring cell.  The walls are dull grey stone, and a metal\ngate provides escape to the west.\n',2,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(295,2,5,-1,'A Dull Cell','  This is a cold, boring cell.  The walls are dull grey stone, and a metal\ngate provides escape to the north.\n',2,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(296,1,6,0,'Training Yard','  This is the Warrior training yard, which is surrounded by a high fence.\nThere is a door to the north leading into the Garrison.\n',2,133285,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(299,3,8,-1,'A Dull Cell','  This is a cold, boring cell.  The walls are dull grey stone, and a metal\ngate provides escape to the north.\n',2,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(300,1,-6,0,'Staircase Landing','  You are at the bottom of a wide staircase.  The stairs lead up towards the\nwest here.  The railing on the staircase is made of thick, white marble and is\npolished to a smooth shine.  You can see groove marks in the marble due to the\nmany years of use.  A smaller set of similiar stairs lies almost hidden in the\nshadows and leads downwards.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(301,1,-7,0,'Theater Lobby','  You are standing in the lobby of a plush theater.  A large door is mounted on\nthe east wall, leading to the theater itself.  To the north, a large staircase\nlanding sits.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(302,1,-8,0,'Theater Entrance','  You are standing in the lobby of plush theater.  The <r>deep red carpet<1> cushions\nyour step.  You see a large door to your west and the lobby continues north and\nsouth.  There is a <y>large sign<1> on the wall to the east.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(303,1,-9,0,'Theater Lobby','  You are standing in the lobby of a plush theater.  A large door is mounted on\nthe east wall, leading to the theater itself.  To the south, a large staircase\nlanding sits.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(304,1,-10,0,'Staircase Landing','  You are at the bottom of a wide staircase.  The stairs lead up towards the\nwest here.  The railing on the staircase is made of thick, white marble and is\npolished to a smooth shine.  You can see groove marks in the marble due to the\nmany years of use.  A smaller set of similiar stairs is almost hidden in the\nshadows and leads downwards.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(305,2,-6,0,'Theater Seats','  You see a section of 12 seats here.  The seats are padded and covered with a\nplush, red velvet.  The view from here is pretty good.  You figure there isn\'t\na bad seat in the house in this theater!\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(306,2,-7,0,'Theater Aisle','  This aisle slopes downward from west to east at a slight angle.  The aisle\nextends from the lobby all the way down to the stage.  You see seats to the\nleft and right as you face the stage.  To the west, you see a large door.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(307,2,-8,0,'Theater Seats','  You see a section of 12 seats here.  The seats are padded and covered with a\nplush, red velvet.  The view from here is pretty good.  You figure there isn\'t\na bad seat in the house in this theater!\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(308,2,-9,0,'Theater Aisle','  This aisle slopes downward from west to east at a slight angle.  The aisle\nextends from the lobby all the way down to the stage.  You see seats to the\nleft and right as you face the stage.  To the west, you see a large door.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(309,2,-10,0,'Theater Seats','  You see a section of 12 seats here.  The seats are padded and covered with a\nplush, red velvet.  The view from here is pretty good.  You figure there isn\'t\na bad seat in the house in this theater!\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(310,3,-6,0,'Theater Seats','  You see a section of 12 seats here.  The seats are padded and covered with a\nplush, red velvet.  The view from here is pretty good.  You figure there isn\'t\na bad seat in the house in this theater!\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(311,3,-7,0,'Theater Aisle','  This aisle slopes downward from west to east at a slight angle.  The aisle\nextends from the lobby all the way down to the stage.  You see seats to the\nleft and right as you face the stage.  Immediately to the east is the stage.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(312,3,-8,0,'Theater Seats','  You see a section of 12 seats here.  The seats are padded and covered with a\nplush, red velvet.  The view from here is pretty good.  You figure there isn\'t\na bad seat in the house in this theater!\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(313,3,-9,0,'Theater Aisle','  This aisle slopes downward from west to east at a slight angle.  The aisle\nextends from the lobby all the way down to the stage.  You see seats to the\nleft and right as you face the stage.  Immediately to the east is the stage.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(314,3,-10,0,'Theater Seats','  You see a section of 12 seats here.  The seats are padded and covered with a\nplush, red velvet.  The view from here is pretty good.  You figure there isn\'t\na bad seat in the house in this theater!\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(315,4,-6,0,'Off Stage','  You are just off-stage.  There is a door on the south wall that leads to\nstage right.  To the east, you see a small waiting area.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(316,4,-7,0,'Stage Right','  You feel like a star!  You are standing on the stage.  The floor here is made\nof thick wooden boards.  You see drops of dried paint on the floor.  As you\nlook to the west, you see where your adoring fans would sit.  To the north, you\nsee a small stage door for the players to make their dramatic entrances.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(317,4,-8,1,'Center Stage','  You feel like a star!  You are standing on the stage.  The floor here is made\nof thick wooden boards.  You see drops of dried paint on the floor.  As you\nlook to the west, you see where your adoring fans would sit.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(318,4,-9,1,'Stage Left','  You feel like a star!  You are standing on the stage.  The floor here is made\nof thick wooden boards.  You see drops of dried paint on the floor.  As you\nlook to the west, you see where your adoring fans would sit.  To the south, you\nsee a small stage door for the players to make their dramatic entrances.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(319,4,-10,0,'Off Stage','  You are just off-stage.  There is a door on the north wall that leads to\nstage left.  To the east you see a small dressing room.  To the northeast, you\nsee backstage.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(320,5,-6,0,'The Green Room','  This room is colored green, and has several chairs strewn about.  This is\nwhere the players sit, while awaiting their entrance.  To the south you see a\nbunch of props.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(321,5,-7,0,'Storage Room','  This room is a storage room for many sets and props that will not fit in the\nprop room.  To the south you see the prop room.  To the north is a green room.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(322,5,-8,0,'Prop Room','  This is where the props are stored between the different performances.  Most\nof the props are in large, wooden boxes with some canvas back-drops leaning up\nagainst the walls.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(323,5,-9,0,'Backstage','  This cluttered passage is where the hustle and bustle of the performance arts\nis most strained.  There are various props and sets leaning up against the wall\nhere.  To the south, you see a small dressing room.  To the north is the prop\nroom.  A small spiral staircase leads downwards to the theater\'s basement.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(324,5,-10,0,'Dressing Room','  This is where the players prepare their appearance for performances.  The\nroom is small and smells of cosmetics.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(325,1,-6,1,'Staircase Landing','  You are at the top of a wide staircase.  The stairs lead down towards the\neast here.  The railing on the staircase is made of thick, white marble and is\npolished to a smooth shine.  To the south, you see the entrance to the balcony\nsection.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(326,1,-7,1,'Entrance to the Balcony','  You are upstairs, just west of the balcony section.  The seats are cheaper,\nbut the view can sometimes be better!  To the south, you see a door.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(327,1,-8,1,'Lamp Room','  This room is cluttered and small.  You see a door on both the north and south\nwalls.  On the east wall, you see a large hole that looks down onto the stage.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(328,1,-9,1,'Entrance to the Balcony','  You are upstairs, just west of the balcony section.  The seats are cheaper,\nbut the view can sometimes be better!  To the north, you see a door.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(329,1,-10,1,'Staircase Landing','  You are at the top of a wide staircase.  The stairs lead down towards the\neast here.  The railing on the staircase is made of thick, white marble and is\npolished to a smooth shine.  To the north, you see the entrance to the balcony\nsection.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(330,2,-6,1,'Theater Seats','  You see a section of 12 seats here.  The seats are padded and covered with a\nplush, red velvet.  The view from here is pretty good.  You figure there isn\'t\na bad seat in the house in this theater!\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(331,2,-7,1,'Theater Aisle','  This aisle slopes downward from west to east at a slight angle.  The aisle\nextends from the lobby all the way down to the edge of the balcony.  You see\nseats to the left and right as you face the stage.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(332,2,-8,1,'Theater Seats','  You see a section of 12 seats here.  The seats are padded and covered with a\nplush, red velvet.  The view from here is pretty good.  You figure there isn\'t\na bad seat in the house in this theater!\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(333,2,-9,1,'Theater Aisle','  This aisle slopes downward from west to east at a slight angle.  The aisle\nextends from the lobby all the way down to the edge of the balcony.  You see\nseats to the left and right as you face the stage.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(334,2,-10,1,'Theater Seats','  You see a section of 12 seats here.  The seats are padded and covered with a\nplush, red velvet.  The view from here is pretty good.  You figure there isn\'t\na bad seat in the house in this theater!\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(335,4,-8,0,'Stage Pit','  This pit is directly below the stage.  It is often used for quick exits and\nentrances to and from the stage.  It is constructed between floors of the \ntheater stage and basement and is incredibly small, barely big enough for\ntwo persons.  A trap door overhead gives access to stage while a panel\nbelow you would most likely allow one to exit the pit downstairs.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(336,-5,9,0,'Inside a Lived-In House','  This house is just off the Perimeter Road in the good part of Grimhaven.\nIt is definitely lived in.  In fact it borders on the rather messy.\nPerhaps the owner just doesn\'t care about cleanliness or perhaps he or she\nis making a statement.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(337,-4,7,0,'Inside a Tidy House','  This house is just off of Oak Lane in the good part of Grimhaven.  It is\nvery neat and tidy.  The house is rather small for the neighborhood but\nhas expensive furniture.  The owner obviously cares about appearances.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(338,-3,7,0,'Inside a Messy House','  This house is just off of Oak Lane in the good part of Grimhaven.  It is\nvery messy with papers strewn all over the place.  On the walls are\nvarious drawings most of them obscene.  On one wall is a dart-board but\njudging by the holes surrounding the board the owner isn\'t very good.\nThe owner is obviously an artist or a person of sloth.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(339,-2,7,0,'Inside a Tidy House','  This house is just off of Oak Lane in the good part of Grimhaven.  It is\nvery neat and tidy.  The house is rather small for the neighborhood but\nhas expensive furniture.  The owner obviously cares about appearances.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,110,0,'',NULL),
(340,-1,7,0,'Inside a Very Clean House','  This house is just off of Oak Lane in the good part of Grimhaven.  It is\nextremely clean.  The owner has religious icons on all the walls and\ncoverings on all the furniture.  The owner obviously has made some sort of\nconnection between cleanliness and godliness.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,110,0,'',NULL),
(350,3,1,0,'Front Lawn','  You are in front of a very large and ornate palace.  Obviously, a very\nimportant person lives here.  There is a large archway to the north.\n',2,131073,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(351,3,2,0,'Entryway To Palace','  You are standing under a large archway.  There is a grand door to the north\nand a plush lawn to the south.\n',2,131073,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(352,2,3,0,'Alcove','  This tiny alcove is completely white, and quite small.  There is a small port\nhole in the west wall and a passage to the east leading to the foyer.  There is\na door on the north wall.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,110,0,'',NULL),
(353,3,3,0,'Palace Foyer','  This is a large foyer with paintings on the ceiling, and an alcove to the\nwest.  There is a small door on the east wall and a passage to the north.  A\ngrand door is on the south.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,110,0,'',NULL),
(354,4,3,0,'Back Passage','  This room is small and cramped.  You see a stairway going down to the north.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(355,2,4,0,'Staircase','  You are at the base of a large staircase.  There are several cloak-hooks on\nthe west and east walls.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(356,3,4,0,'Entrance Hall','  This is an elegant long hallway.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(357,4,4,0,'Top of Staircase','  You are standing at the top of a staircase.  It seems to be dark down\nthere...\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(358,2,5,0,'Servant\'s Quarters','  This humble room looks like it is used for housing a few servants.  There is\na small door to the east and a large door to the west.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(359,3,5,0,'Dining Room','  This room is a large dining area.  The highlight of the room is a large oaken\ndining table in the center of the room.  A swinging door is on the east\nwall, a large oak door on the north and a small door is on the west.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(360,4,5,0,'Kitchen','  This kitchen looks well used.  You can imagine all the good food that was\nprepared here.  There seems to linger a smell of curry.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(361,2,5,-1,'Hidden Corridor','  This corridor is full of dust and dirt.  There are footprints on the floor.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(362,3,5,-1,'Dark Passage','  This room is much like the others down here.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(363,4,5,-1,'Wine Cellar','  This is where the wine and ale are kept.  You can tell from the odor that\novercomes you.  There is a wine rack on the east wall.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(364,2,4,-1,'Hidden Storage Hold','  This area could hold lots of equipment, crates, and bottles, and probably did\nat one time.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(365,3,4,-1,'Main Passage','  This is the main passage in the basement.  All sorts of smells fill the air.\nDampness, mold, and spirits fill your nostrils.....\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(366,4,4,-1,'Bottom of Staircase','  You are at the bottom of a staircase.  It is damp and smells of mold down\nhere.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(367,2,3,-1,'Cheese Room','  This is the room in which the royal cheese is stored.  It smells of mold and\nmouse droppings.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(368,3,3,-1,'Dark Passage','  This passage is damp.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(369,4,3,-1,'Dark Passage','  This passage leads west and north.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(370,2,5,2,'Base of Watchtower','  This is the base of one of the Palace watch-towers.  Spiral stairs lead up and\nthe passage continues eastward.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(371,3,5,2,'Crawlway','  This crawlway connects the watchtowers.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(372,4,5,2,'Base of Watchtower','  This is the base of one of the Palace watchtowers.  There is a\ndoor up to some spiral stairs leading to the tower.  The lead passage\ncontinues westward down the hallway to the rest of the Palace.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(373,2,4,2,'Palace Landing','  This small room is atop stairs leading down to the palace main floor.  There\nis a door on the north wall.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(374,3,4,2,'Middle Junction','  This room is in the center of the palace.  Steep stairs lead you up higher.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(375,4,4,2,'End Room','  This room is at the far east-end of the palace.  There is a door to the\nsouth.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(376,2,3,2,'Base of Watchtower','  This is the base of one of the Palace watchtowers.  Spiral stairs lead up and\nthe passage continues eastward.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(377,3,3,2,'Crawlway','  This crawlway connects two of the palace watchtowers.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(378,4,3,2,'Base of Watchtower','  This is the base of one of the Palace watchtowers.  Spiral stairs lead up and\nthe passage continues westward.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(379,2,5,3,'Northwest Watchtower','  You are standing in the northwest watchtower.  You are overlooking a barracks\nand a large church.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(380,4,5,3,'The Northeast Watchtower','  You are standing in the northeast watchtower.  You are overlooking a barracks\nand a fine shopping district.  You see the city walls in the distance.\nThere is a door back down from the tower to the rest of the Palace.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(381,2,3,3,'Southwest Watchtower','  You are standing in the southwest watchtower.  You are overlooking a large\nchurch, Market Square, and a beautiful park.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(382,4,3,3,'Southeast Watchtower','  You are standing in the southeast watchtower.  You are overlooking a a\nbeautiful park, and the Mage\'s Academy.  You can see the city walls in the\ndistance.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(383,3,4,3,'Base of Lookout Tower','  This is the base of the main lookout tower.  Steep stairs lead you up the\ntower and down to the palace.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(384,3,4,4,'Crawlway','  This tight passage runs up and down on steep stairs.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(385,3,4,5,'Palace Tower Top','  You are standing atop the Palace main tower.  You can see over the entire\ncity.  Wow, what a view! To the north you see a barracks.  To the east you\nsee many fine shops.  To the west you see a church and houses.  To the south you\nsee a beautiful park.  Center square is to the southwest.\n',2,131073,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(386,1,5,0,'Walkway',' This walkway connects the main road to the west to the back entrance to\nthe Palace to the east.  A large door stands in the wall of the palace.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(387,0,0,0,'Staircase','Near the base of a large staircase, there are several cloak-hooks on the west\nwall.  The stairs continue up and there is a passage to the east.\n',0,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(388,3,4,1,'Hallway','  This ornate east-west hall is decorated with rich tapestries and elegant\ncarpets from far away lands.  There are family portraits on the walls.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(389,3,5,1,'Prince\'s Room','  This is the bedroom of the heir to the throne, the prince of Grimhaven.  The\nroom is rather plain and colorless; reflecting the personality of the prince.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(390,3,3,1,'Princess\' Room','  This is the room of the King\'s daughter, the Princess of Grimhaven.  The room\nis simple, with pink paper on all four walls.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(391,4,4,1,'Hallway','  This ornate east-west hall is decorated with rich tapestries and elegant\ncarpets from far away lands.  There are family portraits on the walls.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(392,4,5,1,'King\'s Bedroom','  This is the bedroom of the King.  The carpet is thick and red.  The walls are\ncovered with pictures depicting great battles that the king won.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(393,4,3,1,'Queen\'s Bedroom','  This is the bedroom of the Queen.  The carpet is thick and red.  There are\nseveral beautiful tapestries hanging on the walls.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(394,3,6,0,'The Business Office','This is the main business office for the palace.  It looks like a busy\nplace.  There is not much decorations to the room except for a picture\nof the King\'s father hanging prominently on the wall.\n',-1,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(395,0,0,0,'A Large Meeting Hall','You are in the Grimhaven City Council meeting room, a most unusual room thats\nactual size seems more determined by the number of people in the room than by\nits physical dimensions.  The center of the room is dominated by a large\nconference table, covered with empty coffee cups and ashtrays.  A number of\nchairs line the walls, somehow there always seems to an extra when you need\none.\n',-1,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(400,8,6,0,'Sauna','  This room is hot and humid.  The steam rising from the floor obscures your\nview and fills your nostrils with the aroma of incense, mint, and lemon.  Even\nthough the heat is overwhelming, it is quite refreshing!\n',2,131081,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(401,8,5,0,'Dressing Room','  This room has benches lined up on either side of the room.  This is where you\ncan leave you clothes to enter the sauna, which lies north of this room.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(402,8,4,0,'Entrance To Health Spa','  The walls in this plush entryway are covered with draperies.  You smell a\nfaint sense of incense, lemon, and mint.  There is a small door on the north\nwall.  West lies the streets of Grimhaven and south of here is the hospital.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(403,6,5,0,'The History of Grimhaven','  This room is dedicated to the grand history of Grimhaven.  There are murals\npainted on all four walls and the ceiling.  One painting shows a great eruption\nfrom a volcano to create the land Grimhaven now sits on.  Another picture shows\na great battle of Good and Evil forces until all parties died, thus leaving\nGrimhaven neutral to all.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(404,6,4,0,'Museum Entrance','This is the entrance to the Grimhaven Museum.  To the north lies the\ndisplay to show the history of Grimhaven.  To the south is the room dedicated\nto the history of Imperia.\n',0,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(405,6,3,0,'Hall of Imperia','  This grand room is the history of Imperia.  It shows the older gods\ncreating a place in the sky called Imperia for the gods to live and play.\nThere are pictures of all the gods who followed these founders who have\nexpanded The World and Imperia to its present form.  Some of these gods\nstill grace The World some have ventured on.  It is the goal of all mortals\nto be with the gods.\n',2,131113,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(406,-7,2,0,'Grimhaven Main Post Office','  You are in Grimhaven\'s post office.  This is where you can send and receive\nmail with your friends or even the gods!  A value at twice the price!  There is\na large sign on the wall here.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(407,-7,3,0,'Fortune Teller','  This small shop is filled with beads, strange music, and symbols on the wall.\nHere, Madame Alexis will tell you your fortune.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(408,-7,6,0,'The Sharper Image','  This fine shop is where your dull, nicked, mistreated swords and knives are\nsharpened.  Just let the fine young man behind the counter help you out!\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(409,-7,5,0,'Grimhaven Repair Shop','You are in the shop of Piggot, the repairman of Grimhaven.  You see a wide\nassortment of old, broken-down equipment, patched together by the magical hands\nof Piggot, who is sitting behind the large counter.  A small sign is tacked to\nthe wall.\n',-1,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(410,-7,1,0,'Grimhaven First Kingdom Bank','This bank is a full-service bank, and the most modern in all the land!  The\ninterest rates may not be real great, but your money is safe with us!  There is\na stairway leading down to the bank lobby.\n',-1,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(411,9,5,0,'Chamber of the Grand Crusader','  This is where the Grand Crusader works with aspiring knights to prepare\nthem for the crusades to come.  This is a holy place, and a place for\nbattle.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(412,9,4,0,'Crusader\'s Round','  This room is where the Paladins gather to plan and discuss their various\ncrusades in the name of their deity.  There is a large table in the center of\nthe room and exits east to the entryway and north to an office.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(413,10,4,0,'Entrance of Crusader\'s Guild','  You stand in an ornate entrance hall.  You see large murals on the walls.\nYou see and exit to the north out to Perimeter Road, and an exit to the west\nwhich leads further into the Guild House.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(414,8,2,0,'Hospital Waiting Room','  You are in the Hospital waiting room.  Here is where you can wait for your\nfriends while they are patched up by the fine doctors at this Hospital.  You\ncan visit them to the east or get yourself fixed up while you are here.\nThere is a small stairway here, leading up to the second floor, and also\na door leading into a hallway to the north.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(415,9,2,0,'Hospital','  This is the intersection where you choose which type of health care you\nneed.  You can go east into the Examination Room, southeast into the\nOperating Room, or south into the Intensive Care Unit.  To the north lies\na small door.  A rickety staircase leads down into the City Morgue.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(416,10,2,0,'Examination Room','  You should feel lucky!  All this care at such a low price.  Have a seat,\nthe nurse should make her rounds shortly.  There is a wooden door on the\nnorth wall, you may also exit to the west.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,19,'',NULL),
(417,8,1,0,'Hospital Reception','  You are standing in the entrance to the Grimhaven Hospital.  The facilities\nhere are inadequate, but they will have to do.  To the north is what looks\nlike the waiting room, and to the south you see King\'s Way.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(418,9,1,0,'Intensive Care Unit','  Wow!  You really must have taken a beating!  This is the highest price,\nbut well worth it.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,17,'',NULL),
(419,10,1,0,'Grimhaven Hospital','You must be having a rough day!  This room will let you heal for a good\nprice.  Sit on down, the doctor should be with you shortly.  There is a\nlarge sign on the wall that says READ ME.\n',-1,207021,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(420,8,3,0,'Short Hallway','  You stand in a short hallway in the Grimhaven Hospital.  There is a sign\non the wall with an arrow pointing to the north.  There is a slight draft\nof warm air coming from that direction.  To the north is a large archway\nleading into the Grimhaven Health Spa.  Through the door to the south is\nthe waiting room.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(421,9,3,0,'Supply Room','  You find yourself standing in a small supply room, which is more like a\nlarge closet.  There is very little in the way of supplies here, except\nfor some linens stacked up on shelves.  You wonder if the patients here\nare any better off coming here, due to the lack of supplies.  The only exit\nis back through the door on the south wall.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(422,10,3,0,'Staff Lounge','  This small room is the lounge where hospital employees take their breaks\nand come to relax.  The room is quite featureless, and with the number of\npatients that they service here, you doubt they get much time to themselves.\nThe small door to the south provides the only exit.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(423,8,3,1,'Recovery Room','  This room is small, and smells as if someone has died in it recently.  The\nroom is well-lit, and somewhat clean.  The few supplies that are here, appear\nto be very crude, but still helpful.  This is definitely not the type of\nplace that you would want to find yourself in any time soon.  The only exit\nfrom here is through the door to the south, which leads back into the hallway.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(424,9,3,1,'Recovery Room','  This room is small, and smells as if someone has died in it recently.  The\nroom is well-lit, and somewhat clean.  The few supplies that are here, appear\nto be very crude, but still helpful.  This is definitely not the type of\nplace that you would want to find yourself in any time soon.  The only exit\nfrom here is through the door to the south, which leads back into the hallway.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(425,10,3,1,'Recovery Room','  This room is small, and smells as if someone has died in it recently.  The\nroom is well-lit, and somewhat clean.  The few supplies that are here, appear\nto be very crude, but still helpful.  This is definitely not the type of\nplace that you would want to find yourself in any time soon.  The only exit\nfrom here is through the door to the south, which leads back into the hallway.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(426,10,2,1,'Nurse\'s Station','  You stand at the end of a long hallway.  This would appear to be a nurse\'s\nstation.  There is a long counter here with medical supplies stacked upon it.\nJudging by the clutter on the counter, it appears that this hospital is quite\nbusy.  The hallway leads west, and there doors on both the north and south\nwalls which have signs hanging on them.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(427,9,2,1,'Long Hallway','  You stand in the middle of a long, well-lit hallway through the Recovery\nWard.  There are doors on the north and south walls, with small signs hanging\non them.  There is a putrid smell in the air here.  To the east, there\nappears to be some sort of Nurse\'s Station, and the hallways also continues\nwest.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(428,8,2,1,'Recovery Ward','  You stand at the top of a stairwell.  This is the Recovery Ward of the\nGrimhaven Hospital.  This hallway is lined with doors on both the north\nand south walls which have small signs hanging on them.  The doors lead\ninto recovery rooms for those unfortunate enough to require extended\ntreatment.  The hallway is remarkably clean, although it has a horrible\nsmell.  A stairwell here will take you down to the ground floor, and the\nhallway leads east.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(429,8,1,1,'Recovery Room','  This room is small, and smells as if someone has died in it recently.  The\nroom is well-lit, and somewhat clean.  The few supplies that are here, appear\nto be very crude, but still helpful.  This is definitely not the type of\nplace that you would want to find yourself in any time soon.  There is a small\nwindow on the south wall, and the only exit from here is through the door to\nthe north, which leads back into the hallway.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(430,9,1,1,'Recovery Room','  This room is small, and smells as if someone has died in it recently.  The\nroom is well-lit, and somewhat clean.  The few supplies that are here, appear\nto be very crude, but still helpful.  This is definitely not the type of\nplace that you would want to find yourself in any time soon.  There is a small\nwindow on the south wall, and the only exit from here is through the door to\nthe north, which leads back into the hallway.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(431,10,1,1,'Recovery Room','  This room is small, and smells as if someone has died in it recently.  The\nroom is well-lit, and somewhat clean.  The few supplies that are here, appear\nto be very crude, but still helpful.  This is definitely not the type of\nplace that you would want to find yourself in any time soon.  There is a small\nwindow on the south wall, and the only exit from here is through the door to\nthe north, which leads back into the hallway.\n',2,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(432,6,1,0,'Grimhaven Shipping Office','  This building houses the Grimhaven office of Cobra Shipping Ltd.,\nthe largest organized shipping firm in all the realms.  The shipping\noffice is in a state of constant turmoil, with people coming and\ngoing at all hours of the day or night, both to drop off things for\nshipment to another city or to pick up merchandise which arrived on\nthe latest caravan.  The room itself is tastefully done in light\nwood paneling, with a hard stone floor.  A large counter in the\ncenter of the room serves as a drop off and pick up point for\nmerchandise.\n',6,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(433,9,2,-1,'Grimhaven Morgue','  The walls of the morgue serve as the resting place of those killed\nin battle in the fair City of Grimhaven.  A number of body sized \ntables serve as workspace for the kingdom\'s mortitian to do the work\nneeded to keep the cities streets and alleyways clean of rotting\nflesh.  A rickety staircase leads up into the City Hospital\'s upper\nlevels.\n',6,139561,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(449,0,0,0,'The Reception Desk at the Blackridge Travellers\' Lodge','  The Blackridge Travellers\' Lodge is a large building built in the log-cabin\nstyle. The ceilings are high and arched, and lost in the shadows of the poorly\nlit room.  The reception desk here is where to go if you\'d like to rent a room\nfor the night.  The entrance to the lodge is located west of here, and the\ntavern can be found to the south.  A stairway leads up to the second floor,\nwhere the private rooms are located.  \n',259,164024,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(450,5,9,0,'Stairwell','  This small room attached to the outside of Adder\'s Coffee House is used\nfor general storage and contains a stairwell leading to the basement of\nthe building.  A <c>door in the north wall<1> leads out into the street, and\nthe stairs hug the western wall as they descend into the darkness.\nNumerous boxes and broken pieces of furniture are piled against the\neastern wall.  A cleared aisle leads through the room to the south, where\na large poster leans against the wall.  A <y>colorful sign<1> hangs above the\nstairs.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,4,'',NULL),
(451,5,8,0,'Private Room','  This elegantly furnished room is set aside for private meetings that\nare inappropriate for the main floor.  The walls are paneled in dark\nstained walnut and the floor is covered in thick carpet.  A large\nfireplace is set in the western wall, and a life-size painting hangs on\nthe northern wall.  The <c>door into the main room<1> of the coffee house\nis set in the southern wall.\n',7,131084,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,4,'',NULL),
(452,6,8,0,'Entryway','  You are in the entryway to Adder\'s Coffee House, an important meeting\nplace in Grimhaven.  Numerous merchants come here to conduct business\nover a cup of Adder\'s famous coffee and a pastry.  The popularity of the\nplace is such that some businessmen permanently reserve tables and\nconduct all their business from Adder\'s, rarely seeing their own\noffices.  <c>Doors lead out onto the Perimeter Road and Park Avenue to the\nnorth and east respectively<1>, and an archway leads to the main room of the\ncoffee house to the south.  A <o>brass plaque<1> is mounted on the western\nwall.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(453,5,7,0,'Back of the Main Floor','  You find yourself near the back wall of Adder\'s Coffee House, under the\nbalcony.  This area has a warm homey feel to it and is the area of the\ncoffee house that the \"common man\" of Grimhaven uses when he comes to have\na quick cup of coffee.  The main floor continues to the east, and a\nserving station stands to the south.  The staircase to the balcony is to\nthe southeast.  A <c>wooden door to the north<1> leads to a private room.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(454,6,7,0,'Front of the Main Floor','  You find yourself in the front of the main floor of Adder\'s Coffee House,\nnear both the <D>large windows<1> looking out onto Park Avenue and the\nfront door.  This is the area of the Coffee House where those people\nwishing to \"be seen\" come to make an appearance.  Politicians, actors from\nthe theater, even an occasional member of the royal family come here to\nhave a cup of coffee, press the flesh and be admired by their fans.  The\nentry to the coffee house is through an archway to the north, and the main\nfloor continues under the balcony to the west.  To the south is the\nstaircase up to the balcony, and to the southwest is the main serving\nstation.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,200,0,'',NULL),
(455,4,6,0,'Kitchen','  This is the kitchen of Adder\'s, where some of Grimhaven\'s finest chefs\nbrew the famous coffee and make some of the best pastries in the realm.\nThis is a complete kitchen, capable of making just about any dish any of\nthe patrons could possibly want.  A large cutting table stands in the\ncenter of the room.  A large sink stands next to a <c>swinging door to the\neast<1>, leading into the coffee house.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(456,5,6,0,'Serving Station','  This is the main serving station, where waiters come to get their\norders from the kitchen and take them to their tables.  A large counter\nstands to the south, holding urns of various coffees and teas, serving\nutensils, napkins and numerous other things needed to make the dining\nexperience enjoyable.  The main floor lies to the north and northeast.  A\nstaircase to the balcony is to the east and the <c>swinging door to the\nkitchen lies to the west<1>.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(457,6,6,0,'Under the Staircase','  This dark and gloomy area under the staircase is probably the worst\narea in the tavern, and is used by some of the more shady characters to\nmake somewhat questionable deals.  The main floor lies to the north and\nnorthwest.  The main serving station lies to the west, and the staircase\nitself leads up to the balcony.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(458,5,8,1,'Northwest Corner of the Balcony','  You\'re in the northwest corner of the balcony of Adder\'s Coffee House.\nThis area is reserved for some of the better patrons of the coffee house,\nthose that are willing to pay to keep a table available 24 hours a day.\nThe balcony continues to the east and south, and you can look over a\nwooden rail to the southeast and see the main floor of the coffee house\nbelow.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(459,6,8,1,'North Side of the Balcony','  You\'re on the north side of the balcony of Adder\'s Coffee House.  This\nis considered the best spot in the coffee house, as you can see everyone\nwho enters and leaves through the door below you with ease, but are well\nout of the main traffic path, so you can carry on conversations with some\nprivacy.  Tables here are rented on a lifetime basis and are very\nexpensive, only the most successful of merchants conduct business here.\nThe balcony continues to the west, and you can look over a wooden rail to\nthe south and see the main floor of the coffee house below.  Across on the\nopposite side of the balcony, you can see a stairway leading to the main\nfloor.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(460,5,7,1,'West Side of the Balcony','  You\'re on the west side of the balcony of Adder\'s Coffee House.  Having\na table in this section is very prestigious, as the merchants who conduct\nbusiness in this section can see and be seen not only from the main floor\nbelow, but also through the large windows on the eastern side of the\ncoffee-shop.  Tables here are rented on a yearly basis and are moderately\nexpensive, this is where most of the successful merchants of Grimhaven\nmaintain tables.  The balcony continues to the north and south, and you\ncan look over a wooden rail to the east and see the main floor of the\ncoffee house below.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(461,6,7,1,'Above the Main Floor','  How does it feel to be hanging in mid-air with nothing below you?\nUnless you\'re flying, you won\'t be here long, so take a look around\nquick.  Wooden rails separate you from the balcony of Adder\'s\ncoffee house, and below you is the main floor.  Large windows in the\neastern wall look out on Park Avenue.\n',7,131080,34,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(462,5,6,1,'Southwest Corner of the Balcony','  You\'re in the southwest corner of the balcony of Adder\'s Coffee House.\nThis area is reserved for some of the better patrons of the coffee house,\nthose that are willing to pay to keep a table available 24 hours a day.\nThe balcony continues to the north and east, and you can look over a\nwooden rail to the northeast and see the main floor of the coffee house\nbelow.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(463,6,6,1,'South Side of the Balcony','  You\'re on the south side of the balcony of Adder\'s Coffee House.  This\nsection is reserved for some of Adder\'s newest customers, including\nthose who are financially unable to rent a table full time.  Tables here\nare rented either on a daily or weekly basis and are reasonably priced,\nthis is where many of those new merchants currently trying to make a name\nfor themselves in Grimhaven congregate.  The balcony continues to the west,\nand you can look over a wooden rail to the north and see the main floor of\nthe coffee house below.  The staircase serving the balcony leads downward\nfrom here to the main floor below.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(464,5,9,-1,'Base of the Stairwell','  This small room houses the stairwell leading to the basement of the\nbuilding containing Adder\'s Coffee House and the Snake Pit.  A hallway\nlies to the south and the stairs lead up to street level.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(465,4,8,-1,'Hallway','  This hallway is dark and fairly gloomy, but at least it\'s dry and\nfairly clean.  The hall continues to the east and a door marked \"Storage\"\nlies to the south.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(466,5,8,-1,'Hallway','  This hallway is dark and fairly gloomy, but at least it\'s dry and\nfairly clean.  The hall continues to the west and a staircase lies to the\nnorth.  A <c>solid door<1> with a peep-hole in it sits in the south wall.\nThere is a <y>sign<1> beside the door.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(467,6,8,-1,'Private Room','  This small room has been set aside for the mercenaries who frequent the\nSnake Pit to conduct \"private business\" away from prying eyes.  It is\nalso used to hold parties for smaller, select groups.  The lighting in\nthe room is kept low, and the furniture consists mostly of low tables and\nlarge pillows.  Life-size paintings of famous adventurers cover the\nwalls.  The <c>door<1> into the main room of the Snake Pit lies to the south.\n',7,131084,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(468,4,7,-1,'Front of the Storage Room','  This storage room is used by both Adder\'s Coffee House and the Snake Pit\nBar.  This part of the room appears to be used to store tables, chairs\nand numerous large boxes.  The storage room continues to the south, and a\n<c>door<1> leads out of the room to the north.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(469,5,7,-1,'Entry to the Snake Pit','  You find yourself just inside the door of the Snake Pit, an exclusive\nbar and hangout for mercenaries.  This is where some of the hard-core\nadventurers come to unwind and spend some of their hard earned gold when\nthey happen to be in Grimhaven.  The place is dark and smoky, dimly lit\nexcept for the occasional flash of light from the dance floor to the\nsoutheast.  The bar lies to the south, and the <c>door<1> out to the north.\nThe Snake Pit continues to the east.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(470,6,7,-1,'In the Snake Pit','  You\'re in the Snake Pit, an exclusive bar and hangout for mercenaries.\nThis is where some of the hard-core adventurers come to unwind and spend\nsome of their hard earned gold when they happen to be in Grimhaven.  The\nplace is dark and smoky, dimly lit except for the occasional flash of\nlight from the dance floor to the south.  The bar lies to the southeast,\nand a <c>door in the north wall<1> leads to a private room.  The Snake Pit\ncontinues to the west.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(471,4,6,-1,'Back of the Storage Room','  This storage room is used by both Adder\'s Coffee House and the Snake Pit\nBar.  This part of the room appears to be used to store food and\nbeverages.  Several large kegs of ale stand against the eastern wall and\nwine-racks line the western wall.  Boxes and bags of various foodstuffs\nare stacked in the middle of the room.  The room continues to the north.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,16,100,0,'',NULL),
(472,5,6,-1,'The Snake Pit Bar','  You\'re in the Snake Pit, an exclusive bar and hangout for mercenaries.\nThis is where some of the hard-core adventurers come to unwind and spend\nsome of their hard earned gold when they happen to be in Grimhaven.  The\nplace is dark and smoky, dimly lit except for the occasional flash of\nlight from the dance floor to the east.  A large wooden bar stands in the\nsouthwest corner, with taps for beer and ale set in the western wall.\nVarious glasses and mugs are stacked atop the bar against the southern\nwall.  The Snake Pit continues to the north and northwest.\n',7,166073,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(473,6,6,-1,'On the Dance Floor','  It\'s time to Tango....!  The dance floor of the Snake Pit is made of\nblack marble, with tiny flecks of silver that reflect the flashing lights\noverhead.  It is usually packed with dancers, but you\'re able to squeeze\nyour way in.  As you take in your surrounding, you notice the walls in\nthis section of the club are painted a flat black, as is the ceiling.\nLooking downward at the floor, you suddenly experience a severe case of\nvertigo, it almost looks like there is nothing beneath your feet except\nopen sky.  You quickly recover, but the effect is disconcerting.\n',7,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(499,0,0,0,'Sky Above Adders Coffee House','  There is nothing of interest here.\n',7,139584,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(500,6,-1,0,'Lab of Pyros','  This is where the fire dean <r>Pyros<z> does most of his studies.  The\nroom is built out of solid, cold granite.  A good choice of material\nconsidering the type of experimentation that goes on here.  It is apparent\nthat <r>Pyros<z> isn\'t very lucky with a lot of his experiments.  <k>Soot<z>\nmarks cover the walls making them appear black.  Parts of the wall look\nblown away, probably due to a fireball gone awry.  A fireproof door lies to\nthe south.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(501,7,-1,0,'Scribe\'s Private Study','  The smell of musty scrolls, tallow candles, and freshly made ink assails\nyour nostrils.  This quiet back-room is where the academy\'s scribe pens his\nmagic scrolls.  Fresh <y>scrolls<z> are scattered across the room, and a <W>fancy\nfeather quill<z> and <B>ornate ink pot<z> draw your attention.  A large <g>musty\ntome<z> is also prominently displayed.  People are seldom let back here\nwhile the scribe is at work, for he guards his trade secrets rather\njealously.  A door lies to the south.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(502,8,-1,0,'Entrance of the Grimhaven Mage Academy','  The numerous sounds of people and activity seem to fall silent as\nyou pass under the <c>mithril archway<z> that marks the entrance to\nGrimhaven\'s prestigious Mage Academy.  An unnatural silence seems to\nfollow, and it seems that in the silence a soft hum can be heard from\nthis magic archway.  Apparently the magic archway was specially\ndesigned to prevent any invading monsters from gaining access to the\nacademy.  A <Y>gold plaque<z> can be seen on the side of the archway,\nwelcoming all those who care to visit.\n',8,131085,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(503,9,-1,0,'Private Lab of the Alchemist','  Light filtering in from the outside barely pierces the murky darkness\nof this lab.  A hellish light springs from the alchemist\'s cauldron\nand gives the surrounding gloom an eerie lighting.  Images of flaming\nskulls spring into sight and vanish into black smoke.  From somewhere\ncomes the sound of insane laughter.  The alchemist apparently keeps\na unique workplace within the academy.  Perhaps his unusual nature adds\nto the skillful brewing of his potions.  A door lies to the south.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(504,10,-1,0,'Lab of Terros','  The lab of <g>Terros the Earth Dean<z> looks more like an excavation\nsite than a room.  Huge piles of fresh <o>earth<z> are stacked all along\nthe room, and the room itself appears to have been constructed from hard\nbaked clay.  Parts of the muddy floor shift constantly as if something was\nliving under the dirt and mud.  Apparently <g>Terros<z> has no problems\ngetting his hands a little dirty.  A hard clay door lies to the south.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(505,6,-2,0,'Office of Pyros','  This is the office of <r>Pyros, the Fire Dean<z>.  He instructs students\nin the art of fire magic.  The office is simple in nature.  You notice a\nblast mark on the ceiling and on the floor.  It looks like something must\nhave gone wrong.  A <Y>gold plaque<Z> is on the east wall.  A fireproof\ndoor lies to the north and a <R>fiery red door<z> lies to the south.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(506,7,-2,0,'Scribe Shop','  The smell of old scrolls and fresh ink fill this room.  Though the room\nseems bare of decorations and simple in design, it is more than adequate\nto serve the needs of the village scribe specially hired by the Mage\nAcademy to deal with the buying and selling of magic scrolls.  A small\nsign hangs on the western wall and a door lies to the north.\n',8,166141,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(507,8,-2,0,'Lobby','You are in the middle of the Mage Academy\'s lobby.  The sound of hurrying\nstudents, talkative visitors, and chanting mages fills the room.  The smell of\nold scrolls and ink wafts in from the west, and a rather noxious odor seems to\nbe coming from the east.  To the south, a faint blue glow can be seen.  Passing\npeople eye you in frustration.  Your decision to loiter here is apparently\nmaking it harder for people to enter and leave the academy.\n',-1,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(508,9,-2,0,'Alchemy Store','  A foul odor fills this room making you feel a little sick.  Strange\nsymbols deck the walls and floors.  Strange <b>bottles<z> and <r>philters<z>\nline the shelves in this room.  Though the Dean of Alchemy seldom has time to\nmake an appearance, this has not stopped the academy from selling his\nwonderful creations.  They have even gone so far as hiring another alchemist\nto sell the dean\'s wares.  A door lies to the north.\n',8,166141,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(509,10,-2,0,'Office of Terros','  This is the office of <g>Terros the Earth Dean<z>.  He has been given the\ntask of instructing young mages on the secrets of earth magic.  The office\nseems spartan in decoration, and looks more like a  sculptor\'s studio than\na mage\'s office.  Wet clay and mud seem to cling to everything.  Despite\nthe office\'s rather messy appearance, it still has a certain warm cozy\nfeeling to it.  A <Y>gold plaque<z> hangs on the east wall.  An <o>earthy\nbrown door<z> lies to the south and a hard clay door lies to the north.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(510,6,-3,0,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made of beautiful <D>white marble<z>.  The\nmarble is flawless and so highly polished that you can see your own\nreflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <b>blue aura<z> of intense\nbrightness that seems to emanate from the walls and ceiling.  The musty\nsmell of spell components and old paper seems to fill this entire hall.  An\ninvisible force tugs at you, urging you onward through the Mage Academy.  A\n<R>fiery red door<z> lies to the north and a <B>watery blue door<z> lies to\nthe east.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(511,7,-3,0,'Office of Hydros','  This is the office of <B>Hydros, Dean of Water<Z>.  He is in charge of\ninstructing students in the art of water magic.  The office is quaint and\ncozy.  You can\'t help but notice how wet the floor is.  In fact, the entire\nroom looks like it has been flooded recently.  A <Y>gold plaque<z> is on the\neast wall.  A <B>watery blue door<z> lies to the west and a waterproof\ndoor lies to the south.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(512,8,-3,0,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made of beautiful <D>white marble<z>.  The\nmarble is flawless and so highly polished that you can see your own\nreflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <b>blue aura<z> of intense\nbrightness that seems to emanate from the walls and ceiling.  The musty\nsmell of spell components and old paper seems to fill this entire hall.  An\ninvisible force tugs at you, urging you onward through the Mage Academy.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(513,9,-3,0,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made of beautiful <D>white marble<z>.  The\nmarble is flawless and so highly polished that you can see your own\nreflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <b>blue aura<z> of intense\nbrightness that seems to emanate from the walls and ceiling.  The musty\nsmell of spell components and old paper seems to fill this entire hall.  An\ninvisible force tugs at you, urging you onward through the Mage Academy.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(514,10,-3,0,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made of beautiful <D>white marble<z>.  The\nmarble is flawless and so highly polished that you can see your own\nreflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <b>blue aura<z> of intense\nbrightness that seems to emanate from the walls and ceiling.  The musty\nsmell of spell components and old paper seems to fill this entire hall.  An\ninvisible force tugs at you, urging you onward through the Mage Academy.\nAn <o>earthy brown door<z> lies to the north and an <C>airy blue door<z>\nlies to the south.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(515,6,-4,0,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made of beautiful <D>white marble<z>.  The\nmarble is flawless and so highly polished that you can see your own\nreflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <b>blue aura<z> of intense\nbrightness that seems to emanate from the walls and ceiling.  The musty\nsmell of spell components and old paper seems to fill this entire hall.  An\ninvisible force tugs at you, urging you onward through the Mage Academy.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(516,7,-4,0,'Lab of Hydros','  This is the lab of <B>Hydros, the Water Dean<Z>.  This lab is not the\ntypical lab.  In fact, all around you is vast amounts of water, as if you\nwere standing in the middle of an ocean.  This must be where <B>Hydros<z>\ncomes up with his fascinating water spells.  It probably also provides the\ndean with a nice swimming area for when he gets bored.  In the waters\nbeneath you, you notice a <k>dark shape<Z> moving about.  A waterproof door\nlies to the north.\n',8,131081,52,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(517,8,-4,0,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made of beautiful <D>white marble<z>.  The\nmarble is flawless and so highly polished that you can see your own\nreflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <b>blue aura<z> of intense\nbrightness that seems to emanate from the walls and ceiling.  The musty\nsmell of spell components and old paper seems to fill this entire hall.  An\ninvisible force tugs at you, urging you onward through the Mage Academy.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(518,9,-4,0,'<C>Lab of Aeris<z>','  This is the lab where <C>Aeris the Air Dean<z> conducts most of her\nstudies.  A magical wind sweeps across the lab ensuring that her test\nsubjects stay airborne.  The entire chamber looks more like a wind tunnel\nthan your average lab.  This is probably where the dean comes up with her\nbest work, and probably where she goes for a little stress relieving aerial\nacrobatics.  A wind battered door lies to the east.\n',8,131081,65,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(519,10,-4,0,'<C>Office of Aeris<z>','  This is the office of <C>Aeris the Air Dean<z>.  She has been entrusted\nwith the task of imparting her knowledge of air magic to the young mages\nwho come to this academy to learn.  Her office could be described as\nelegant if it were not for the fact that it looks like a hurricane has come\nsweeping through it.  Hanging on its last nail is a gold plaque on the\neastern wall.  A wind battered door lies to the west and an <C>airy blue\ndoor<z> lies to the north.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(520,6,-5,0,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made of beautiful <D>white marble<z>.  The\nmarble is flawless and so highly polished that you can see your own\nreflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <b>blue aura<z> of intense\nbrightness that seems to emanate from the walls and ceiling.  The musty\nsmell of spell components and old paper seems to fill this entire hall.  An\ninvisible force tugs at you, urging you onward through the Mage Academy.  A\ndoor with a <y>sign<z> on it lies to the south.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(521,7,-5,0,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made of beautiful <D>white marble<z>.  The\nmarble is flawless and so highly polished that you can see your own\nreflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <b>blue aura<z> of intense\nbrightness that seems to emanate from the walls and ceiling.  The musty\nsmell of spell components and old paper seems to fill this entire hall.  An\ninvisible force tugs at you, urging you onward through the Mage Academy.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(522,8,-5,0,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made of beautiful <D>white marble<z>.  The\nmarble is flawless and so highly polished that you can see your own\nreflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <b>blue aura<z> of intense\nbrightness that seems to emanate from the walls and ceiling.  The musty\nsmell of spell components and old paper seems to fill this entire hall.  An\ninvisible force tugs at you, urging you onward through the Mage Academy.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(523,9,-5,0,'A Great Marble Staircase','  A great marble staircase dominates this area.  Carved from fine white marble\nand magically set here, it seems to spiral so high up that you can not make\nout where it ends.  A gentle pulse seems to be coming from the magic stairway,\nbeckoning you upwards.  A bright white hallway can be seen to the west while\na slightly smaller but no less grand stairway leads downwards.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(524,6,-6,0,'Receptionist\'s Office','  This is the office of the receptionist.  The office is quite large and\neasily accommodates whoever may be waiting for the Head Mage or the\nGuildmaster.  Papers are scattered everywhere, making the office look like\na strong wind blew through here earlier.  Plush carpeting covers the floor\nand fancy wallpaper covers the walls.  Doors can be found to the east and\nsouth.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(525,7,-6,0,'Office of the Head Mage','  A sense of order and propriety is exuded by the office of the Head Mage.\nEverything appears to be immaculately cleaned and in perfect order.  An\naura of magic seems to well up from everything in this office.  Simple\ncolors adorn this room and the furniture in here is very sparse.  The only\nthing out of the ordinary is an elaborate oaken shelf on the northern wall.\nVarious <g>exotic items<z> are arranged along it.  A <Y>gold plaque<z>\ndominates the wall to the south.  Doors lie to the west and east.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(526,8,-6,0,'Records Office','  This is the Mage Academy\'s Office of Records.  Current files of each\nstudent in the academy are kept here, as well as the Head Mage\'s personal\nfiles on certain mages who have captured his attention over the years.  All\nof them are kept in painstaking order within a series of <k>filing\ncabinets<z> that line the eastern wall.  A <o>large sign<z> hangs above\nthem.  A door back to the Head Mage\'s office lies to the west.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(527,6,-7,0,'Office of the Guildmaster','  The office of the Guildmaster is very simply fashioned.  Soft oriental\ncarpeting of plain design covers the floors.  The Guildmaster\'s many\nplaques and certificates line the oak paneled walls.  The room is lit by\na <Y>bright light<z> that does not seem to have a source.  Judging by\nthis room, it would appear that the Guildmaster is a very simple and\nhumble man.  One of the panels seem to be slightly out of place.\nDoors lie to the east and north.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(528,7,-7,0,'Meditation Chamber','  This entire chamber is empty of decorations and frivolous material items.\nThere is nothing here to distract a mage from his focused meditations.\nThis must be where the Guildmaster does his deep reflections and serious\nthinking.  Judging by this room, the Guildmaster is a truly serious and\ncontemplative individual.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(529,6,-8,0,'Private Chambers of the Guildmaster','  This is the hidden chambers of the Guildmaster.  Unlike his office and\nmeditation chamber, this room does not seem to lack any possible comfort.\nPlush carpeting covers most of the room, with a fancy tile floor\nsurrounding the Guildmaster\'s jet-water jacuzzi.  Pictures of some of the\nGuildmaster\'s trips away from the academy line the walls.  A soft hum\nfrom the Guildmaster\'s vibrating bed is the only sound  that breaks up\nthe peaceful silence of the Guildmaster\'s resting chambers.  One of the\npanels in the north wall seems loose.  This room appears to be the bottom\nof a tower, and gold stairs spiral upwards.\n',8,131117,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(530,6,-8,1,'Private Study','  A comfortable warmth fills this room though no heat source is evident.\nShelves line the walls encircling this room, and the back of the room\nhas apparently been designed for quiet study.  A sense of relaxation and\npeace is exuded by this room and it feels like the ideal place to get\nsome quiet reading in.  Apparently the Guildmaster uses this room for\nquiet meditation and thought and leaves the meditation room for the\ngullible mage apprentices who believe in candles and incense.  A gold stair\nleads back down the tower and a mysterious portal glows from the other end\nof the room.\n',8,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(531,0,0,0,'<C>Observatory<z>','  This magic room has been secretly placed in the clouds above Grimhaven.\nYou panic as you notice that you are in the middle of the sky, but you soon\nrealize that the <D>walls<z> and the <D>floor<z> are just transparent.  In\nfact, looking through them presents a terrific view.  It must take a great\ndeal of power to keep this room in the sky from falling.  The only things\nto be found in this remarkable chamber is a portal back to the\nGuildmaster\'s private study, and a large magic mirror set here for viewing.\nThis must be where the Guildmaster and Head Mage keep watch over The World\noutside the Mage Academy.\n',8,131081,65,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(532,8,-1,1,'Lab of Magos','  This is where <D>Magos<z> conducts most of his research.  The room has\nbeen lined with blast-proof armor, and extra layers of shielding has been\nplaced over top.  Judging by the poor melted condition of the top layer of\nshielding, it would appear that this room suffers damage on a regular\nbasis.  This room appears perfect for practicing high damage spells or\nrelieving paranoid anxiety in a burst of disintegrating energy.  A\nblast-proof door lies to the south.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(533,6,-2,1,'Back of Auditorium','  This entire auditorium has been modeled as a miniature amphitheater.\nAttention is focused towards the center of the auditorium.  Even from the\nback of the auditorium, it appears that the acoustics remain excellent.\nThis section of the auditorium must be used for when the crowds attending\nthe academy\'s lectures grow too large.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(534,0,0,0,'Archives','  This dusty back-room has been set aside to hold the files that are no longer\nheld in the Records Office.  Some of the older more antiquated pieces of\nliterature have also made their way back here.  Given that some of the books\nback here are older than the academy, a great deal of respect is given to this\nroom by the mages who come to study here.  Pulsing golden sigils outline a\ndoor to the north. \n',0,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(535,8,-2,1,'Office of Magos','  This is the office of <d>Magos the Sorcery Dean<z>.  He has been put in\ncharge of instructing the young mages in the powerful art of sorcery.  His\noffice seems more like that of a military commander than an academy dean.\nCamouflage lines the walls and combat armor lies scattered around.  This\noffice looks ready for an invasion.  A <Y>gold plaque<z> adorns the west\nwall.  A blast-proof door can be seen to the north and an <b>ionic blue\ndoor<z> can be seen to the east.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(536,9,-2,1,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made from stunning <k>black marble<z>.  The\nmarble appears to be flawless and is so highly polished that you can see\nyour own reflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <g>greenish glow<z> of\ngentle luminescence that emanates from the walls and ceiling.  The sick\nsweet smell of decaying spell components and the acrid stench of burning\nsulfur fills this hall.  An invisible force seems to tug at you, urging you\nonward through the Mage Academy.  An <b>ionic blue door<z> shines in the\nwest, and a <p>shifting patterned door<z> pulses in the east.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(537,10,-2,1,'Office of Puck','  This is the office of <p>Puck the Spirit Dean<z>.  He happily brings\nstudents here to impart his knowledge of spirit magic.  This office\nseems like it came straight out of a story-book.  A <g>bean-stalk<z> grows\nquietly in a corner.  Wreaths of ivy hang from the ceiling, and tiny\ncreatures seem to be playing on the floor somewhere.  This office clearly\nhas been made to suit its eccentric owner.  A <Y>gold plaque<z> hangs\non an ivy branch along the eastern wall.  A <o>wooded door<z> lies to the\nnorth and <p>shifting patterned door<z> can be seen to the west.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(538,6,-3,1,'Front of Auditorium','  This entire auditorium looks like a miniature amphitheater and stretches\nback to the north.  Attention is focused to the center of the auditorium.\nThe acoustics in this auditorium are amazing and even the sound of your\nbreathing carries nicely across the room.  This room must be where the\nacademy gathers for mass announcements and general lectures.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(539,7,-3,1,'Library Shelves','  You are among the shelves of the academy\'s library.  Dust flies\neverywhere as you pass among these ancient tomes.  Many of these books have\nbeen entrusted to the academy by people who have long since passed away.\nThe books in this room account for most of the historical knowledge of the\nacademy\'s masters.  Several tomes of magic can be seen along some of these\nshelves as well.  This room is a truly a treasure house of knowledge.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(540,8,-3,1,'Library Front Desk','  A sense of forced silence fills this library and it would appear that\nthe quiet policy is strictly enforced.  Large motes of dust fill the air,\nand it appears most of the books kept in this library are very old.  The\nroom itself appears warm and inviting.  Given the studies required by most\nmages, this is probably one of the most used areas in the academy.  A <o>small\nsign<z> hangs above the front desk.  The library door can be seen to the\nsouth.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(541,9,-3,1,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made from stunning <k>black marble<z>.  The\nmarble appears to be flawless and is so highly polished that you can see\nyour own reflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <g>greenish glow<z> of\ngentle luminescence that emanates from the walls and ceiling.  The sick\nsweet smell of decaying spell components and the acrid stench of burning\nsulfur fills this hall.  An invisible force seems to tug at you, urging you\nonward through the Mage Academy.  A lab door can be seen to the east.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(542,10,-3,1,'Student Lab','  Unlike the other labs in the academy, this room appears to be very\nnormal in appearance.  Sterile walls and floors shine immaculately and the\nwhole room is lighted by a gentle <y>yellow light<z> streaming from the\nceiling.  The entire room has been safely padded in blast-proof shielding\nand soft overlapping cushions.  This room looks like it could withstand a\ndirect explosion and not lose its sparkle.  This room has apparently been\nset aside for those mages who still need to refine their magic skills and\nthose who tend to backfire their spells a lot.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(543,6,-4,1,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made from stunning <k>black marble<z>.  The\nmarble appears to be flawless and is so highly polished that you can see\nyour own reflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <g>greenish glow<z> of\ngentle luminescence that emanates from the walls and ceiling.  The sick\nsweet smell of decaying spell components and the acrid stench of burning\nsulfur fills this hall.  An invisible force seems to tug at you, urging you\nonward through the Mage Academy.  A door lies to the north.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(544,7,-4,1,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made from stunning <k>black marble<z>.  The\nmarble appears to be flawless and is so highly polished that you can see\nyour own reflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <g>greenish glow<z> of\ngentle luminescence that emanates from the walls and ceiling.  The sick\nsweet smell of decaying spell components and the acrid stench of burning\nsulfur fills this hall.  An invisible force seems to tug at you, urging you\nonward through the Mage Academy.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(545,8,-4,1,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made from stunning <k>black marble<z>.  The\nmarble appears to be flawless and is so highly polished that you can see\nyour own reflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <g>greenish glow<z> of\ngentle luminescence that emanates from the walls and ceiling.  The sick\nsweet smell of decaying spell components and the acrid stench of burning\nsulfur fills this hall.  An invisible force seems to tug at you, urging you\nonward through the Mage Academy.  The library door can be seen to the\nnorth.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(546,9,-4,1,'Hall of Magic','  You are in a mystical hallway made from stunning <k>black marble<z>.  The\nmarble appears to be flawless and is so highly polished that you can see\nyour own reflection.  The halls are lit by an eerie <g>greenish glow<z> of\ngentle luminescence that emanates from the walls and ceiling.  The sick\nsweet smell of decaying spell components and the acrid stench of burning\nsulfur fills this hall.  An invisible force seems to tug at you, urging you\nonward through the Mage Academy.  A classroom door lies to the east.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(547,10,-4,1,'Classroom','  Simple in design and decorations, this small classroom has been set\naside for study groups and free study periods away from the eyes of\nthe demanding deans of the academy.  It has all the marks of a typical\nclassroom.  The <k>blackboard<z> appears to be in working order, and\nnothing seems out of the ordinary except for the slightly irregular\n<b>ceiling<z> and an <o>odd desk<z> in the corner.  A door out can\nbe seen to the west.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(548,9,-5,1,'Top of Great Marble Staircase','  After a climb that seems like forever, the staircase appears to shimmer and\nthe marble is now black as night.  The ceiling and surrounding halls appear\nto be made from black marble as well.  The dark swirling atmosphere seems\nto serve as a balance to the bright halls below.  A gentle force tugs you\ndownward gently, but the strange lights ahead appear to beckon to you.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(549,10,-1,1,'Lab of Puck','  This is where <p>Puck<z> conducts most of his experiments.  This entire\nroom appears to be a small forest magically growing within this chamber.\nSounds of wildlife echo in the chamber, and glowing eyes stare at you from\ninside the shrubbery.  A misty fog covers most of the chamber, and it\nbecomes very hard for you to see what is making that growling noise in the\ncorner.  This room has been constructed to imitate the dean\'s old home.\nFeeling at home in this chamber allows <p>Puck<z> to develop innovative\nspirit magic spells and teach his students better.  A <o>wooded door<z> can\nbe found to the south.\n',8,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(550,-5,-7,0,'Lumor\'s Illuminations','This walls of this shop are covered in bright golden glows.  Evenly spaced wooden shelves appear to support a \nvariety of lighting supplies.\n',0,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(551,-4,-1,0,'Pious Products','Everything a practicing cleric needs to pay respect to his or her deity!\n',-1,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(552,-4,-4,0,'Taloc\'s General Supply','  This shop looks neat and organized, apparently a place one can buy many\nof their general supplies at.  There is a counter along one wall with\nvarious wares stacked neatly on shelfs behind it.  An open doorway to the\nnortheast leads to the main square of the Market District.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(553,-1,-1,0,'Green Dragon Tavern','  Many come here for a friendly smile and a good pint of ale, relaxing from\na hard day or an evening out with comrades.  There are many tables and\nchairs about, with a good sized bar built in the southwest corner of the\nroom, a kitchen apparently beyond.  An open archway to the south appears to\nlead to an Inn of some kind and a doorway to the northeast to the Center\nSquare of Grimhaven.  A smaller open archway to the west appears to lead\ninto a wing occasionally rented out for larger groups.  High overhead the\nsturdy dwarven and gnomish craftsmanship makes itself known with the display\nof huge cut timbers braced and connected with various metal brackets,\ndesigned by gnomes, forged and built by dwarves.\n',2,164025,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,24,'',NULL),
(554,-5,-1,0,'Camron\'s Components','  This shop is filled with scents and odors from all the unique items that are\nbought and sold here.  If you don\'t have components, you can\'t cast spells!\nA set of stairs apparently built after the original structure lead upwards\nalong the south wall of the room.  A small sign hangs on the wall at the\nbase of the stairs.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(555,-4,-2,0,'The King\'s Shield','  This armorer\'s shop can provide the best protection in all of Grimhaven.\nNothing is too exotic in here, but it\'s enough to keep you safe.  An open\ndoorway leads west to the Tanner\'s Clothery while a sturdy looking set of\nstairs lead upwards to a weapons shop overhead.\nAn open doorway to the southeast leads back to the main square of the\nMarket District.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(556,-2,-2,0,'Kindred Pub','  Brightly lit whether noon of day or the latest hour of the evening this\nfine establishment serves only the best food and the finest drink in all of\nGrimhaven.  A small serving counter is built into the northeast corner, a\nkitchen apparently beyond.  An open archway to the east appears to lead to\nan Inn of some kind and a doorway to the southwest to the Market Square of\nGrimhaven.  A smaller open archway to the north appears to lead into a wing\noccasionally rented out for larger groups.  High overhead the sturdy\ndwarven and gnomish craftsmanship makes itself known with the display of\nhuge cut timbers braced and connected with various metal brackets, designed\nby gnomes, forged and built by dwarves.\n',2,141801,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,24,'',NULL),
(557,0,0,0,'The Roaring Lion Inn','This inn appears busy with its staff and patrons moving about at all\nhours of the day.  The worn-in path of mud near the door lends further\ncredit to the Inns number of patrons.  This room is a little humid, but\nwarm enough to sleep, with a small counter set in the northwest corner of\nthe room.  A small opening is just beyond the counter leading to a tiny\nalcove, a staircase winding upwards just visible.  Apparently you must speak\nwith the Inn\'s receptionist before being allowed to your room.  \n  High overhead the sturdy dwarven and\ngnomish craftsmanship makes itself known with the display of huge cut\ntimbers braced and connected with various metal brackets, designed by\ngnomes, forged and built by dwarves.\n',0,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,144,0,'',NULL),
(558,-5,-4,0,'Prigon\'s Precious Gems and Metals','  This store sends shivers up your spine!  All the shiny and beautiful\ngems and metals that are bought and sold here could buy Grimhaven!  A\nspiral stair leads up to another store above.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(559,-4,-2,1,'The Glinting Dagger','This weapon shop is one of the best in all the land.  You can buy and\nsell the best weapons known to all of Grimhaven.  A long counter has\nbeen constructed along three sides of the small room with weapons of\nevery conceivable kind either encased within the counters or hanging\nupon the walls behind the counters.  Most appear to be for sale, but a few\nappear to be for show only, personally owned by the shops proprietor.\n',-1,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(560,-2,-4,0,'Froddor\'s Foodstuffs','  The smells of the fresh baked bread and rare cheeses fill your nose as\nsoon as you enter this popular shop.  Here apparently only the best\ningredients are used to produce wholesome, quality foods for your day to\nday needs!  An open doorway to the northwest leads to the main Market\nSquare of Grimhaven.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(561,-5,-1,1,'Quazar\'s Realm of Magic','  Quazar the great Wizard welcomes you to his shop.  Quazar deals only in the\nmost high quality magic items known to Grimhaven.  If you don\'t want to pay for\nquality, you might as well use a stick.  A small set of stairs lead down\nfrom this room to Camron\'s Component Shop below.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(562,-5,-5,0,'The Curio Shop','  You may buy and sell those unique items that other places don\'t seem to deal\nwith.  The owner of this shop will be glad to give you a quote on those\nold\nitems that are useless to you, but may be a little valuable to others.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(563,-4,-5,0,'Surplus','  This room is for the surplus items you would like to give to charity.\nIf something can help, please take it and use it.  If you take from here,\nreturn the favor when you can leave something for those less fortunate.\nFor those truly destitute, the Grimhaven Welfare Office is in the tower\nabove you.\n',2,166073,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(564,-2,-5,0,'Carnivorous Companions','This shop is usually loud with the barking of dogs and screeching of hawks.\nYou can buy a trained familiar to help you in your quest for fortune.  There is\na window on the wall that you can look through to see today\'s selection.  There\nis a small sign on the wall.\n',0,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(565,-5,-4,1,'Tanni\'s Jewelry Store','This is one of the finest shops you\'ve ever seen.  The walls are covered\nin gold leaf and drapes of thick velvet.  Expensive carpets cover the\nfloor, muffling the sound of your footsteps.  Numerous glass display cases\nare placed throughout the room, holding the many rings, signets and other\njewelry items.  Your spine tingles with the magic used to help protect\nthese items from theft.\n',0,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(566,0,0,0,'Pet Room','  This room is where the pets are kept.  The pet room looks nicer than the room\nyou are in.  There are several bowls of water and food lying about.  In the far\nwest of the room you see some pet toys.\n',2,166075,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(567,-2,-1,0,'The Board Room','Normally a small room rented to various groups, currently it seems to be\nused as a board room for adventurers of the World to post their thoughts\nand ideas.  A large sign on the west wall proclaims the sanctity of this\nestablishment, and the lamps gently burning on the walls destroy any\nsemblance of shadows.  A small staircase ascends to another rented room\nabove while small archways to the south and east lead to the Tavern and Pub\noperated by the Roaring Lion Inn.  Overhead the sturdy dwarven and gnomish\ncraftsmanship makes itself known with the display of huge cut timbers braced\nand connected with various metal brackets, designed by gnomes, forged and\nbuilt by dwarves.\n',-1,167101,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(568,-5,-2,0,'Tanner\'s Clothery','The smell of finely tanned and meticulously cured leather permeates\nthe air.  Leather of all shapes and sizes surround you as well as an odd\nassortment of second-hand clothing.  An open doorway leads east into the\nKing\'s Shield.\n',-1,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(569,-7,4,0,'Hornsby\'s Monogramming Shoppe','  This tiny room is dark and smells strongly of ozone that the engraver\'s tool\nmakes as it etches items brought here.  There is a disclaimer on the wall.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(570,-4,-5,1,'The Grimhaven Welfare Department','This square and slightly dilapidated old room seems oft used, judging by\nthe wear on the wooden planks that constitute the floor.  In the southwest\ncorner of the room is a small desk, behind which a chair provides comfort\nfor whoever works there.  A small placard rests on the front of the desk.\nA ladder-shaft continues both upwards and downwards from this room.\n',32,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,180,0,'',NULL),
(571,-4,-5,2,'Observation Platform','  As you enter the room, the first thing that strikes you is the view of the\nrest of Grimhaven- it is somewhat breathtaking.  The whole city sprawls out\nbefore you, from the bustle of commerce in the Market District to the\nfanfare of the Royal Palace.  This room, windowless and sheltered only by\na four-poster wooden ceiling platform, serves as a tourist attraction of\nsorts.  While not actually listed on any maps or official brochures describing\nGrimhaven\'s features, this little tower is quite the interesting stopping\npoint.  A hole cut in the north part of the floor allows for a ladder that\ncan take you back down.\n',32,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(572,-5,-2,1,'Delayn\'s Hide and Herbal Shop','   Walls covered in hides, skins, and pouches containing different organic\nand herbal commodities, Dwayne\'s wife Delayn has opened her own shop here\nabove his tannery.  Delayn deals in such things as skins and hides, bone,\nspecial organic and herbal ingredients and sometimes fabrics.  Delayn uses\nmany of the hides to repair and create her husband\'s wares and trades the\nother merchandise at a marginal profit to herself.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(573,-1,-4,0,'Roaring Lion Stables','  Understanding the need of its clients to have suitable storage areas for\ntheir pets and mounts the owners of the Inn invested in this barn.  Used\nonly for its short term guests, the animals of their longer staying guests\nare taken outside the city walls to pastures and stables with more\navailable space to make sure of proper exercise for the animals.  Stalls\nline the east and west walls each with a sturdy dwarven lock to make sure\nof the security of the clients animals as well as making sure the client\npays before retrieving their animal.  Centered in the south wall is a large\nopening with a huge grate blocking passage through it, solid wood used for\nthe lower half and a metal gratework for the upper half.  A set of large\ndouble doors in the north wall lead out to the street while a ladder near\nthe center of barn apparently leads upwards to a hayloft through a small\nopening in the ceiling.\n',9,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(574,-1,-4,1,'Hayloft','  Although every conceivable amount of wall space has some piece of tack or\nother device attached to it, everything is neat and orderly.  Large stacks\nand piles of hay cover the entire floor area to the south while large\nstorage bins for grain have been built along the north wall.  A few small\nfurnishings are tucked away behind a low wall along the west side of the\nloft and the east side is completely covered with tack.  A small hole near\nthe center of the loft has short half walls built around three sides of it,\none with a ladder attached to one of the walls.  This appears to be the\nonly exit from the loft.\n',9,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(575,-1,-5,0,'Exercise Lot','  Fenced in with a sturdy looking tall fence apparently this is a lot used\nby the stables for the exercising of the animals.  A huge contraption of\nwood, metal, and leather sits at its center and apparently works through\nsome magical means to both walk the animals attached to it as well as pump\nand store water for the animals later use.  Off to the west side of the lot\nyou can just make out the back of the petshop where various animals are\npenned.  Barely outside the door of the stables and to the east sits a huge\npile of manure, probably waiting some farmer\'s purchase as fertilizer.\n',9,139712,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(576,-4,-4,1,'The Grimhaven Employment Office','  File cabinets line the north wall, behind a large and well organized desk.\nCrates and boxes take up a fair amount of the floor space, neatly stacked\nand labeled.  A number of contracts are available here, for citizens who\nare unable to find regular work elsewhere.  There\'s no promise that these\njobs will be pleasant or easy, but when you\'re down on your luck, there is\nlittle choice.\n',32,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,180,0,'',NULL),
(578,0,0,0,'Alchemic Visions','  This out of sorts store has cluttered floors and is dusty and grimey from\nyears of neglect. The shopkeeper here has made a good business of identifying\nobjects for the citizens of Lionheart. He has relocated to Grimhaven only \nrecently taking over this dusty old shop.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(579,-2,-4,1,'Yun\'s Grocery and Cooking Supply','  Wooden crates with their tops open display fresh produce from around the\nWorld.  Crates packed with ice present top grade meats for your inspection.\nCooking implements of all kinds are sitting on wooden shelves along with\nnumerous recipe books.\n',2,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,144,0,'',NULL),
(580,-4,-2,1,'A Peaceful Garden','High up on the third floor in downtown Grimhaven, the noise of Market Square\nis just a distant hum pierced by the occasional shout.  A short protective\nwall encircles the garden, high enough to prevent kicking rocks onto the\npopulace below, but not so high as to block the expansive views of the\ncity.  To the south, the Twilight Square district spreads out, while to the \neast you can make out the Royal Palace and the Grimhaven Park.  Enough soil\nhas been transplanted here to support a wide range of plant life.  A small\nbut sturdy grate is mounted into the ground in one corner, leading down\ntowards street level and a door leads into an apartment to the west.\n',-1,139264,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(581,0,0,0,'<r>A Grand Study<1>','<o>Rich mahogany and oak compose the walls, floor and furniture of this study,\ngiving it a very stately feel.  Masterfully crafted inlaid wood form graceful\npatterns on the oak floors, while a giant oak door leads out to the garden\nto the east.  A rich mahogany arch forms a passageway to the bedroom to the\nnorth.  Windows have been mounted in the south, southwest and west walls,\nproviding views of the street life below.\n',-1,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(582,0,0,0,'<o>A Quiet Bedroom<1>','<k>Well insulated from the surrounding city and lacking windows, this bedroom \nis dark and cozy.  Stained wood floors and solidly\nconstructed furniture enhance the feeling.  A study lies to the south,\nthrough an ornate mahogany arch.\n',-1,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(583,-4,-1,0,'<Y>The Frobozz Magic Company<1>','<p>The large shelves and display cases full of wierd and wonderful items\nused to create magic are a dead giveaway that this store sells\ncomponents.  Powerful magics have been used to prevent anyone except\nthe shopkeeper from accessing the shelves and cases.  Through a doorway\nto the south lies a weapon shop, while down a small staircase below\nyou is a shop selling religious items.<1>\n',-1,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(584,0,0,0,'A Pleasantly Decorated Alcove','This small alcove off the stairs has been decorated warmly, with thick tapestries covering the walls and plush cushions lined up on the floor and propped against the wall. Many small, delicate glass stars have been hung from hooks randomly distributed around the walls and ceiling so the light will catch and cast glimmering brightness onto the walls. Here and there, small oil paintings have been hung.  A large, luxurious looking baanta fur covers the floor here. \n',0,164029,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,144,0,'',NULL),
(585,-2,-5,0,'Dorian\'s Pet Clinic','This clinic was setup to treat pets that have been injured horribly for\nsome reason or another.  They often crawl their way back to the pet shop,\nso Petir leads them up to Dorian for treatment.  Stacks of cages against\nthe back wall hold the animals until their owners show up to claim them.\n',0,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(600,0,0,0,'The Grimhaven City Dump','It is surprisingly clean here!  You wonder to yourself where all of the\nwaste products generated by the citizens of Grimhaven could have gone, but\nthen you remember hearing something about the Mage Academy setting up a\nmagical dump for the benefit of the city.  Beware, if something is dropped\nhere, it will be surely lost and gone forever.  A break in the refuse\nindicates a spot where something has dug its way up out of the sewers; you\ncould probably climb down if you wanted.\n',0,166065,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(601,0,0,0,'Garbage Strewn Alley','Various bits of trash and refuse litter the floor of this side alley, which\nleads directly to the Grimhaven City Dump.  Although the dump itself remains\nspotless due to the Mage Academy\'s magic, garbage doesn\'t always make it all\nthe way there.\n',-1,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(602,0,0,0,'Branish Way','  A well used path leads to the west, towards the city dump and another path\nleads down a narrow alley to the east.  This section of town appears to be\nmuch more recently constructed than other sections.  The path is well cobbled,\nthe walls are relatively free of cracks and decay and the street lights are\nshining brightly.\n',10,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(603,0,0,0,'An Alley','  This side alley runs between Branish Way and a couple of shops.\n',10,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(604,0,0,0,'The Lock and Key','A faint metallic taste pervades the air of this cluttered locksmith\'s shop.\nOn the walls are hung all manner of devices for home and business security:\nlocks and keys of all shapes and sizes are displayed prominently, as are many\nchains and grates, both simple and ornate.  Iron-wrought puzzles sit atop a \ntable in the back corner to amuse the young and the old.  An open doorway\nleads to the street to the west, and, behind the counter, a grated window in \nthe east wall affords a view of South Main Street.\n',-1,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(606,0,0,0,'Branish Way','  There are shops both east and west, while the main path leads north\nand south.  This section of town appears to be much more recently\nconstructed than other sections.  The path is well cobbled, the walls\nare relatively free of cracks and decay and the street lights are\nshining brightly.\n',10,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(607,0,0,0,'The Traders Exchange','<k> Dimly lit countertops stretch along the unfinished walls of this\nseedy shop.  Patches of <1><g>peeling paint<1><k> slump down from a\nsoggy ceiling.  A <1><o>rusty metal sign<1><k> is nailed to the\nbackside of the door.  A stairway behind the counter looks like it\nmight have led somewhere, but is out of order currently.\n',-1,428221,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(608,-4,-2,0,'Sanford\'s Empire','Inside this quiet, dusty shop, there is a slight moldy odor. Many \npeople who have visited the shop have kicked the dirt and dust off \nthe ground, layering the many junk piles with dust. On the counter \nitself are several posters advertising the Grimhaven Loan Sharks.\n',-1,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(609,0,0,0,'<k>Twilight Avenue<1>','<k>  The avenue reaches a dead end here.  Twilight Square is directly\neast.  Dark grey cobblestones cover the ground.<1>\n',10,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(610,0,0,0,'Nynaeve\'s Components','This shop is filled with a great deal of items with a mystical nature, and\nthe store radiates a strong sensation of magical presence.   The walls are\nlined with shelves, each shelf packed with neatly labelled jars of\nvarious magical components.   A large counter in the center of the room\ncommands attention.  A striking statue of a golden cat sits serenely on the\ncounter.\n',-1,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(611,0,0,0,'<k>Twilight Square<1>','<k>  The cobblestones that cover the ground here are dark grey, nearly black.\nTwilight Avenue, cobbled in a similar manner, leads off to the east and west,\nwhile Branish way begins to the north.  Twilight Square is the hub of the\nsouthern market district of Grimhaven, where the slums once stood.<1>\n',10,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(612,0,0,0,'<k>Twilight Avenue<1>','<k>  Shops exist in nearly every direction, while Twilight Square is directly\nwest.  The avenue continues on to the southeast.  Dark grey cobblestones cover\nthe ground.<1>\n',10,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(613,0,0,0,'A Dirty Attic Laboratory','Inside a dark, dusty room, there is a pungent and awful odor. Within\nthe smokey gloom, there are stacks and rows of potions, which line the\nwalls while still fizzling and boiling, long after they have been\nremoved from the cauldrons.  Hidden in the dank pallor are several\ncases with stacks of parchment, that give off an aura which makes your\nsenses tingle.  A small, rickety counter sits over in the corner of\nthe room, and behind, several cauldrons, smoking and steaming with\nbrews of power.  In the floor, a small trapdoor to the magic shop\nbelow is propped open by a half rotten stick.\n',0,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(614,0,0,0,'<k>Twilight Avenue<1>','<k>  The dark grey cobblestone of the avenue merges with South Main Street to the\neast.  The southern market district of Grimhaven lies to the west, along\nTwilight Avenue.<1>\n',10,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(616,0,0,0,'The Mace and Machete','  The front portion of this shop is quite small, and consists entirely\nof brand new and quite exotic-looking weapons with no prices attached.\nToward the rear of the shop are more common weapons of all sorts,\nhanging on hooks, collected in barrels, and lying on a few large\ntables. The shopkeeper\'s counter is directly beside the door, where an\neagle eye can be kept on all customers.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(617,0,0,0,'An Unfinished Room','The basic building frame and floor of a shop has been built here.  Various\nremenants of construction lie about, a pile of boards here, a few blocks of\nconcrete there, a pile of tools in the corner.  When this building has been\npurchased, construction will continue to fulfill the desires of the owner.\nA narrow set of stairs lead up to a trapdoor in the back of the room.\n',-1,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(618,0,0,0,'<r>A Sitting Room<1>','A large bay window dominates the western wall of this elegant sitting room.\nDuring the day, sunlight streams in, cheerfully lighting the room and\nilluminating every corner.  Fancy cream colored wallpaper increases the feeling\nof openness and light.  A remarkable view of the streets and shops of\nTwilight Square can be seen to the southwest, west and northwest.\nA trapdoor has been cleverly fitted into the maple flooring in the back\nof the room.\n',-1,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(619,0,0,0,'<p>An Elegant Bedroom<1>','Beautiful damask wallpaper gives this bedroom a very elegant image, while\nmaple flooring and a window in the western wall keep it bright and cheery.\nAn archway leads to a sitting room to the north.\n',0,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(624,0,0,0,'GK Highrollers Casino Entrance','  A massive sweeping <W>marble staircase<1> leads upwards to the lobby of\nthe casino.  The <o>inlaid wooden banister<1> of the staircase serves as\nfirst introduction to the opulence and wealth of this establishment.  Huge\n<w>iron supports<1> are built into the structure in the corners of this room,\nthe one piece of evidence of the massive architectural achievement that\nstands above you.  Gusts of wind intermittently whip through the area\nfrom the street, while the raucous clatter of the casino invades from above.\n',23,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(625,0,0,0,'A Grungy Hideout','A simple room with few furnishings is here.  It is often used by those on\nthe run from the authorities as law officials seldom frequent this part of\nthe city.  A rickety stairway leads downward.\n',-1,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(626,0,0,0,'A Small Loft','This small room contains nothing of any great importance other than the\noccasional burlap bag seen laying around on the floor.  A stairway leads\ndownward.\n',-1,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(627,0,0,0,'<c>Torkyn<1>\'s Clothing','  A large table in the center of the room holds various swathes of fabric,\nseveral pairs of scissors and measuring tapes.  A short platform sits in\nfront of a set of mirrors on the south wall, where the tailor will take\nmeasurements.  The entire west wall is composed of cubby holes, containing\nstacks of various types of cloth.  Several finished suits of clothing hang\non racks near the north wall.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(628,0,0,0,'<r>Felicia\'s Fantasies<1>','<r>  Light velvet curtains swathe the walls in sepulchral elegance. The\nsmell of incense hovers in motionless air.  In the center of the room,\na ring of jewelry cases circles an embroidered throw rug.  Around the\ncases are mannequins in daring poses, wearing suits of armor.<1>\n',-1,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(629,0,0,0,'Branish Way','  This section of town appears to be much more recently constructed\nthan other sections.  The path is well cobbled, the walls are\nrelatively free of cracks and decay and the street lights are shining\nbrightly.\n',10,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(630,0,0,0,'PAACS Fifth Avenue','A floor of inlaid and interspersed <r>redwood<1> and <o>cedar<1> sprawls beneath\nyour feet, hidden in some places by <r>exq<Y>u<1><r>isite or<b>i<r>ent<b>a<r>l r<Y>u<1><r>gs<1>, in others\nshaded by racks of clothing.  The floor is so impeccably clean, that\nupon closer inspection, you notice that the rugs are the only things\non the floor.  The racks appear to float above the ground, although\nthey are suspended from the ceiling on transparent fishwire.  The\nclothes are kept in strict order, and nothing seems out of place.  The\nwalls are draped in <k>ornately decorated silk tapestries<1>.  A <C>tinted\nskylight<1> allows a <p>purple aura<1> to permeate the store.  The scent of\nmothballs is in the air.  To the north lies The Traders Exchange.  A\nsign hangs over the door.\n',-1,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(631,0,0,0,'Tenement Building','This building seems to house some manner of being occasionally, but for the\ntime being it seems mostly deserted.  Various torn up mattresses and old\nragged clothing have been strewn about, and the stench is nearly unbearable.\nThe smell of urine and decay is very strong here.  Stairs lead up and a peculiar\nexit is to the north.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(632,0,0,0,'Tenement Building - Penthouse','This building seems to house some manner of being occasionally, but for the\ntime being it seems mostly deserted.  Various torn up mattresses and old\nragged clothing have been strewn about, and the stench is nearly unbearable.\nThe smell of urine and decay is very strong here.  Stairs in the corner\nlead downward.\n',10,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(633,0,0,0,'<P>Crossroads of the Arcane<1>','<p>  The interior of this shop both warms your heart and shivers your\nspine.  One side is dedicated to the medicinal uses of theological and\nherbal remedies while the other gloomier side spreads the eerie chill\nof the dabblers of magical arts.  The surrounding shelves inside this\ncircular room are filled to their edges with the finest merchandise\nof either variety.  The smell of burning incense secretes comfort into\nthe air from the counter in the rooms center.<1>\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(634,0,0,0,'Jennica\'s <b>Exotic<1> Imports','  With a high ceiling, concrete floors and unfinished walls, this large shop\nlooks more like a warehouse than a typical shop.  Many <o>crates<1> are stacked up\nnext to the walls, some of which have been open, spilling forth with packing\nmaterial.  A particularly large crate next to the east wall appears to have \nnot been moved in some time.  Near the entrance, a small desk covered in papers\nand ledgers sits next to a loading pallet.\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(635,0,0,0,'The Den','This is the center of the den, a place where thieves seem to just loiter and\ntalk about recent activities or happenings.  The room has very dim lighting and\nthere is a constant gloom in the corner of this place.\n',10,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(636,-1,-3,0,'<o>A Deck<1>','<o>Thick oak planks form a railing around the edges of this deck, preventing\naccidental departure from the third floor.  Far below, <k>Twilight Avenue<1><o>\ncan be seen stretching off to the east, through <k>Twilight Square<1><o>.  A\nsmall apartment lies to the north and a trapdoor leads down into the building\nbelow.<1>\n',-1,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(637,-1,-3,0,'A Small Bedroom','<b>This is a typical small downtown Grimhaven apartment, one room with no\nwindows.  The din of the Casino Lobby below echoes up through the floor and\nthe occasional whine of the elevator running up and down the Casino Tower\nrattles the northern wall.  A door leads out to a deck to the south.<1>\n',0,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(639,0,0,0,'Short Hallway','A short hallway in part of the thieves den leads between the main room and the\ndeeper parts of the guild hall.  It is very dim here and the gloom could hide\nanything or anyone.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(640,0,0,0,'Back Room','A nondescript room with few furnishings (and fewer furnishings that aren\'t\nnailed down).\n',10,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(641,0,0,0,'Short Hallway','A short hallway in part of the thieves den leads between the main room and the\ndeeper parts of the guild hall.  It is very dim here and the gloom could hide\nanything or anyone.\n',10,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(642,0,0,0,'Short Hallway','A short hallway in the nether parts of the thieves guild is here.  It is very\ndark and the gloom could hide anything or anyone.\n',10,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(643,0,0,0,'Short Hallway','A short hallway in the nether parts of the thieves guild is here.  It is very\ndark and the gloom could hide anything or anyone.\n',10,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(644,0,0,0,'An Evil Abode','This is the home of one of the more evil men in Grimhaven.  Wicked\nimplements of torture and destruction hang from wooden pegs on the walls.\n',10,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(645,0,0,0,'A Training Room','This is the chief production center for all thieves in the city, a room\nwhere they can come to improve their abilities as well as make new\nacquaintances.\n',10,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(646,0,0,0,'The Thief\'s Corner','This mini-warehouse of supplies for thieves of all sorts seems to offer\ndecent prices.  The clientele here is the most elite in all the district.\nYou approach the counter and examine the wares for sale carefully.  How\nmuch can you trust the salesman?\n',10,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(647,0,0,0,'Dearly Divine','The flickering light of tinted lamps on the warm-toned wood gives a\nsense of harmony relaxing your travel-weary muscles.  All about are\nmarvelous objects, no two alike.  They overflow the multitude of\nshelves, display cases, and racks that line the interior of the\nshop. Books and bookmarks, bookstands, pen and paper lie on a glass\ndisplay case.  Within are jewelry of all shapes and descriptions.\nAlong one wall, symbols of holy might are strung like fruit from a\ntree above row upon row of vials of sacred water.  Everything you\ncould possibly need can be found here.\n',-1,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(648,0,0,0,'<b>The Fellowship of Mezan<1>','<B>  Walking in from below you immediately feel uplifted.  The room is well\nlit from the <Y>sunrays<B> cascading through the <g>st<C>a<R>in<O>ed<1><p>-gl<W>ass<B> windows that\nadorn every wall.  Following the trail of rose petals and scent of\njasmine you almost lose yourself in the vast clerical goods that\nsuspend from the shops ceiling.<1>\n',2,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(650,0,-14,0,'Sloping Road','  This road slopes sharply southward.  To the north lies a large path leading\ninto a very large city.  There are exits to the southeast and southwest that\nlead down a large hill.  There are cliff faces to the east and west.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(651,-1,-15,0,'Steep, Sloping Road','  This road slopes down dramatically here!  The path is well worn and is strewn\nwith loose gravel.  There is a walled city north of here.  To your west, a rock\ncliff goes down.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(652,-2,-16,0,'Steep, Sloping Road','  This road slopes down dramatically here!  The path is well worn and is strewn\nwith loose gravel.  There is a walled city north of here.  To your west, a rock\ncliff goes down.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(653,-3,-17,0,'Steep, Sloping Road','  This road slopes down dramatically here!  The path is well worn and is strewn\nwith loose gravel.  There is a walled city north of here.  To your west, a rock\ncliff goes down.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(654,-4,-18,0,'Steep, Sloping Road','  This road slopes down dramatically here!  The path is well worn and is strewn\nwith loose gravel.  There is a walled city north of here.  To your west, a rock\ncliff goes down.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(655,-5,-19,0,'Steep, Sloping Road','  This road slopes down dramatically here!  The path is well worn and is strewn\nwith loose gravel.  There is a walled city north of here.  The road levels out\nto the west.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(656,-6,-19,0,'Well Worn Road','  You are on a road that is heavily traveled.  To the east, the road turns to\ngo up a steep hill.  To the west is a bridge.  In the distance to the north,\nyou see a large city.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(657,-7,-19,0,'Bridge over the River Kranor','  This bridge is sturdy and large.  Four carts could pass here side by side!\nYou see well trod roads to the east and west.  In the distance to the north you\nsee a large city.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(658,-8,-19,0,'Well Traveled Road','  You are on a road that is heavily traveled.  To the west, the road goes into\nthe forest.  To the east is a bridge.  In the distance to the north, you see a\nlarge city.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(659,-9,-19,0,'Well Traveled Road','  This road travels through a wooded area.  The forest grows dense to the west\nand opens up into a clearing to the east.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(660,-10,-19,0,'Intersection in the Woods','  This intersection connects a road deeper into the woods to the south and west\nand into a lighter part of the forest to the east.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(661,-10,-20,0,'Decaying Path','  This path is decaying as it goes deeper into the forest to the south.  To the\nnorth is a large intersection.  The trees create a cathedral-like appearance.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(662,-10,-21,0,'Decaying Road','  This path is decaying as it runs north to south in the forest.  The trees\ncreate a cathedral-like appearance.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(663,-10,-22,0,'Decaying Road','  This path is decaying as it runs north to south in the forest.  The trees\ncreate a cathedral-like appearance.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(664,-10,-23,0,'Decaying Road','  This path is very decayed as it bends north to west.  The trees create a\ncathedral-like appearance.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(665,-11,-23,0,'Decaying Road','  This path is very decayed as it runs east to west.  The trees create a\ncathedral-like appearance.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(666,-12,-23,0,'Decaying Road','  This path is very decayed as it runs east to north.  The trees create a\ncathedral-like appearance.  To the north you see the edge of a vast forest.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(667,-11,-19,0,'Forest Road','  This road is damp and dark as it runs through a deep forest.  It is hard to\ntell if it is night or day!  It appears to get lighter to the east.\n',11,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(668,-12,-19,0,'Forest Road','  You are at a bend in this damp and dark road.  It is hard to tell if it is\nnight or day!\n',11,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(669,-13,-18,0,'Forest Road','  This road is damp and dark as it runs northwest to southeast through a deep\nforest.  It is hard to tell if it is night or day!\n',11,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(670,-14,-17,0,'Forest Road','This road is damp and dark as it runs through a deep forest.  It is hard to\ntell if it is night or day!\n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(671,-15,-16,0,'Edge of Forest Road','  You are at the edge of a large forest.  The road runs deep into the woods to\nthe southeast and into the open plains to the west.\n',11,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(672,-16,-16,0,'Dirt Road','  You are traveling on a dirt road.  To the east you see a large forest.  To\nthe west, you see a range of mountains.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(673,-17,-16,0,'Dirt Road','  You are traveling on a dirt road.  To the east you see a large forest.  To\nthe west, you see a range of mountains.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(674,-18,-16,0,'Dirt Road','  The dirt road bends here.  To the west you see a large horse stable.  The\ndirt road continues to the east and there is a stone road to the southwest.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(675,-19,-16,0,'Horse Stable','This stable is clean and comfortable.  Obviously, the owner takes a great\namount of effort to make this stable comfortable for the horses and the\ncustomers.  There is an open extension of the stable to the north.\n',-1,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,180,0,'',NULL),
(676,1,-15,0,'Steep, Sloping Road','  This road slopes down dramatically here!  The path is well worn and is strewn\nwith loose gravel.  There is a walled city north of here.  To your east, a rock\ncliff goes down.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(677,2,-16,0,'Steep, Sloping Road','  This road slopes down dramatically here!  The path is well worn and is strewn\nwith loose gravel.  There is a walled city north of here.  To your east, a rock\ncliff goes down.\n',11,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
