(1125,31,58,-1,'Outside the West Gates of Amber','  To the east lie the thick granite walls of the city of Amber.  The road\nleads through an archway in the walls, at the far end of which stands the\nsturdy iron gate that protects the town.  To the west, a trail heads across\nthe featureless plains of the frozen north.\n',16,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1130,24,40,-2,'A Trail Through Some Rocky Hills','  Rough terrain lies all about you as you make your way along what is\nlittle more than a gamepath.  The rock strewn hillsides on either side\nforce to you to stay to the trail if you wish to avoid spraining an\nankle.  Scraggly brush grows in the gaps between the rocks, providing\na hiding place for who knows what type of wildlife.  An occasional\npine or spruce tree grows atop the windswept hills.  A rough road\nleads away to the southeast.\n',130,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
