(1169,22,-30,0,'A Narrow Rutted Path','The ruts in the path are fairly numerous cutting it in several places \nas the drivers of the wagons tried to avoid previous ruts and the risk of \nbecoming bogged down in the mud that was once present.  Most of the ruts \nare at least twelve inches deep and a couple are almost as deep as two feet.  \nThe path is now dry and hard packed making the ruts quite an obstacle for \none to avoid.  Wagons are most likely bounced about tossing their cargo in \nall directions with the ever present threat to crush a wooden wheel lingering\nover the drivers head.  At the same time any traveler on foot must be wary of \neach foot step or risk turning an ankle.  Vegetation boundaries on both sides\nof the path forcing anyone to remain on it or risk being cut to pieces by the \nvarious thorned underbrush which is all about.  The path heads northeast\nand west from here.\n',-1,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1170,21,-30,0,'A Narrow Rutted Path','  The ruts in the path are fairly numerous cutting it in several places \nas the drivers of the wagons tried to avoid previous ruts and the risk of \nbecoming bogged down in the mud that was once present.  Most of the ruts \nare at least twelve inches deep and a couple are almost as deep as two feet.  \nThe path is now dry and hard packed making the ruts quite an obstacle for \none to avoid.  Wagons are most likely bounced about tossing their cargo in \nall directions with the ever present threat to crush a wooden wheel lingering\nover the drivers head.  At the same time any traveler on foot must be wary of \neach foot step or risk turning an ankle.  Vegetation boundaries on both sides\nof the path forcing anyone to remain on it or risk being cut to pieces by the \nvarious thorned underbrush which is all about.  The path heads in a basic\neast to west direction at this point.\n',16,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1171,20,-30,0,'A Narrow Rutted Path','  The ruts in the path are fairly numerous cutting it in several places \nas the drivers of the wagons tried to avoid previous ruts and the risk of \nbecoming bogged down in the mud that was once present.  Most of the ruts \nare at least twelve inches deep and a couple are almost as deep as two feet.  \nThe path is now dry and hard packed making the ruts quite an obstacle for \none to avoid.  Wagons are most likely bounced about tossing their cargo in \nall directions with the ever present threat to crush a wooden wheel lingering\nover the drivers head.  At the same time any traveler on foot must be wary of \neach foot step or risk turning an ankle.  Vegetation boundaries on both sides\nof the path forcing anyone to remain on it or risk being cut to pieces by the \nvarious thorned underbrush which is all about.  The path heads east and\nwest at this point apparently bending to the north farther to the west and \ncontinueing on for some ways to the east.\n',16,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1172,19,-30,0,'A Narrow Rutted Path','  The ruts in the path are fairly numerous cutting it in several places \nas the drivers of the wagons tried to avoid previous ruts and the risk of \nbecoming bogged down in the mud that was once present.  Most of the ruts \nare at least twelve inches deep and a couple are almost as deep as two feet.  \nThe path is now dry and hard packed making the ruts quite an obstacle for \none to avoid.  Wagons are most likely bounced about tossing their cargo in \nall directions with the ever present threat to crush a wooden wheel lingering\nover the drivers head.  At the same time any traveler on foot must be wary of \neach foot step or risk turning an ankle.  Vegetation boundaries on both sides\nof the path forcing anyone to remain on it or risk being cut to pieces by the \nvarious thorned underbrush which is all about.  The path rounds a bend here\nas it heads to the northwest and east.  The sound of rushing water can be\nheard to the west but it is impossible to see its source through the thick\nunderbrush.\n',16,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1173,18,-29,0,'A Narrow Rutted Path','  The ruts in the path are fairly numerous cutting it in several places \nas the drivers of the wagons tried to avoid previous ruts and the risk of \nbecoming bogged down in the mud that was once present.  Most of the ruts \nare at least twelve inches deep and a couple are almost as deep as two feet.  \nThe path is now dry and hard packed making the ruts quite an obstacle for \none to avoid.  Wagons are most likely bounced about tossing their cargo in \nall directions with the ever present threat to crush a wooden wheel lingering\nover the drivers head.  At the same time any traveler on foot must be wary of \neach foot step or risk turning an ankle.  Vegetation boundaries on both sides\nof the path forcing anyone to remain on it or risk being cut to pieces by the \nvarious thorned underbrush which is all about.  The path rounds a bend here\nas it heads to the north and southeast.  The sound of rushing water can be\nheard to the west but it is impossible to see its source through the thick\nunderbrush.\n',16,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1174,18,-28,0,'A Narrow Rutted Path','  The ruts in the path are fairly numerous cutting it in several places \nas the drivers of the wagons tried to avoid previous ruts and the risk of \nbecoming bogged down in the mud that was once present.  Most of the ruts \nare at least twelve inches deep and a couple are almost as deep as two feet.  \nThe path is now dry and hard packed making the ruts quite an obstacle for \none to avoid.  Wagons are most likely bounced about tossing their cargo in \nall directions with the ever present threat to crush a wooden wheel lingering\nover the drivers head.  At the same time any traveler on foot must be wary of \neach foot step or risk turning an ankle.  Vegetation boundaries on both sides\nof the path forcing anyone to remain on it or risk being cut to pieces by the \nvarious thorned underbrush which is all about.  The path heads north and\nsouth at this point apparently bending to the east farther to the south and \napproaching a large structure to the north.\n',16,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1175,29,-35,0,'A Faded Path','  This narrow, overgrown path leads basically north-south, from some low hills\nto the north downhill toward the shores of the Myrian Ocean to the south.  The\npath doesn\'t look like it has been used a lot recently, the plant life has\nencroached on the trail and you can barely find your way.\n',16,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1176,29,42,-2,'A Trail Through Some Rocky Hills','  Rough terrain lies all about you as you make your way along what is\nlittle more than a gamepath.  The rock strewn hillsides on either side\nforce to you to stay to the trail if you wish to avoid spraining an ankle.\nScraggly brush grows in the gaps between the rocks, providing a hiding\nplace for who knows what type of wildlife.  An occasional pine or spruce\ntree grows atop the windswept hills.\n',130,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1177,0,0,0,'A Treehouse','The floor of this treehouse has been formed by extending large wooden\nplanks over some of the stouter branches of the tree. The walls and\nceiling of the room are a thick mass of interwoven braches that,\nluckily enough, seems to have prevented birds from nesting inside the\nroom. It has not, however, kept it free from leaves and twigs. As the\nwind blows through the leaves, it creates a mantra-like tone. An oddly\nfamiliar and soothing fragrance lingers about the room.\n',-1,139272,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(1178,0,0,0,'<o>Inside a Foxhole<Z>','As you walk, hunched over, through a short tunnel behind the stack of logs\nand concealing brush, you quickly realize someone occupies this hole in the\nearth regularly!  Pictures of soldiers in desert garb pepper the ceiling.\nThe walls are made of stacked sandbags, and the smell of fresh soil fills\nyour nostrils.  A few empty wine skins and several discarded iron rations\nfill a bright orange bag.  The ones labelled Jambalaya and Hamburger are\nuntouched. Some beads cover a door to another room.  A space between two\nof the logs in the ceiling allow you access to the road above.\n',16,139528,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(1179,0,0,0,'<o>Entrenched in a Foxhole<Z>','The first thing you notice is that this room is much cleaner and organized.\nDoor beads cover an exit to the east.  Bits of trap making materials and\na large scorch on the wall, appear to be the result of a failed attempt at\nexplosives production in the past.  Someone has written someething in the\nsoot. As you walk around carelessly you hear a *click* beneath your feet.\nYour eyes widen and your heart drops.  You slowly look down to see if you\'ve\ntriggered something unpleasant, but it turns out to be a large cockoroach.\n',16,139528,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(1200,-49,-28,0,'The Great Western Crossroads','You stand in the central square of the largest intersection of roads in the\nwestern part of The World.  Four great roads lead off in all of the major\ndirections, the most notable being the western road.  Down that road, you see a\nlarge white town rising from the horizon, encircled in her walls and set\ndefensively against the Agorian Sea.  A large signpost stands here, just off to\nthe side of the road.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1201,-50,-28,0,'Seacrest Way','  You stand on a large road which runs east and west through a variety of farm\nfields.  In the distance to the east can be seen a large crossroad, and far to\nthe west the white walls of a large town rise up to greet you.\n',17,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1202,-50,-27,0,'A Farm Field','  You are somewhere in the middle of a large field of grain, probably intended\nto feed a large populace.  A slight breeze begins to pick up, and the grain\nwaves as if being gently combed out.  To the south, a large road can be seen.\n',17,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1203,-50,-29,0,'A Farm Field','  You are somewhere in the middle of a large field of grain, probably intended\nto feed a large populace.  A slight breeze begins to pick up, and the grain\nwaves as if being gently combed out.  To the north, a large road can be seen.\n',17,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1204,-51,-28,0,'Seacrest Way','  You stand on a large road which runs east and west through a variety of farm\nfields.  Here the road begins to enter the outskirts of a large walled town to\nthe west, and continues far into the distance towards the east.\n',17,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1205,-51,-27,0,'A Farm Field','  You are somewhere in the middle of a large field of grain, probably intended\nto feed a large populace.  A slight breeze begins to pick up, and the grain\nwaves as if being gently combed out.  At the northern end of the field, a large\nwhite fence keeps out intruders.  In the middle of the fence can be seen a\ngate.  To the south, a large road can be seen.\n',17,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1206,-51,-29,0,'A Farm Field','  You are somewhere in the middle of a large field of grain, probably intended\nto feed a large populace.  A slight breeze begins to pick up, and the grain\nwaves as if being gently combed out.  To the north, a large road can be seen.\n',17,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1207,-52,-28,0,'Seacrest Way','You stand in the middle of a large road which runs from east to west.  On\nboth sides of the road can be seen houses and buildings lining the streets\nwhich run north and south from here.  Directly to the west rise the huge white\nwalls of the town of Brightmoon.  Strong walls amid proud towers jealously guard\nthe town\'s contents, as a large formidable gatekeep rises to meet you.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1208,-51,-26,0,'A Large Farm','  You stand in the middle of a large farm.  Various animals can be heard\nthroughout the area.  This is somewhat of an enclosed field, with a fence to\nthe west and south, a farmhouse to the north, and a large barn to the east.  A\nlarge window is set in the farmhouse, shaded with drapes from the inside.  A\ngate is set in the southern fence.\n',17,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1209,-51,-25,0,'A Large Farmhouse','  You are standing inside of a homely farmhouse.  It has a very country air to\nthe place, and seems quite restful.  Various china is set upon shelves on the\nwalls, and homemade crafts decorate the room.  A large boar\'s head hangs from\nthe wall over a fireplace.  Two windows are set here in both the southern and\neastern walls.\n',17,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(1210,-50,-26,0,'A Large Barn','  You are standing inside of a large barn.  Several animals are kept here, as\nwell as all the tools necessary to maintain the fields in the local area.  You\nhear the sounds of chickens clucking from up in the rafters.  The barn doors\nare west from here, and a side door is set in the north wall.\n',17,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(1211,-49,-26,0,'Bottom of The Barn Silo','  You stand at the bottom of a large empty barn silo.  Nothing of note seems to\nbe present, save a few bits of grain and straw lying about.  A ladder does\nhowever, lead upwards to a trapdoor in the ceiling.\n',17,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(1212,-49,-26,1,'Top of the Barn Silo','  You are standing at the top of a large barn silo.  Nothing of note about the\nroom seems to catch your attention.  The only exit is a trapdoor set in the\nfloor.\n',17,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(1213,-50,-25,0,'Backyard','  This is the backyard of a large farmhouse which lies directly to the west.\nSet in the wall of the house is a large window.  The grass grows abundantly\nhere, and the yard seems to be well maintained.  A large barn lies south, and a\nwhite fence blocks off the eastern and northern ends of the yard.  A set of\nstorm cellar doors leads downwards under the farmhouse.\n',17,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1214,-50,-25,-1,'A Storm Cellar under the Farmhouse','  This cellar seems to be the common type used on farms to weather out rough\nstorms.  Various crates, barrels, tools, and dried foodstuffs line the dirt\nwalls here.\n',17,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(1215,-53,-28,0,'Outside the Main Gatekeep','  You are standing directly in front of the town walls of Brightmoon directly\nto the west.  The main gatekeep stands before you, welcoming all guests and\nrepelling all intruders.  The land is open for defensive purposes next to the\ntown walls, forming paths which run north and south from here around the town\nwalls.\n',17,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1216,-53,-27,0,'Outside the Town Walls','  You are standing outside the walls of the great Town of Brightmoon.  There is\nnothing here of note save a few arrow slits in the walls, and the great defense\nthey provide.  A huge guard tower segments the walls here.\n',17,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1217,-53,-29,0,'Outside The Town Walls','  You are standing outside the walls of the great Town of Brightmoon.  There is\nnothing here of note save a few arrow slits in the walls, and the great defense\nthey provide.  A huge guard tower segments the walls here.\n',17,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1218,-54,-28,0,'Inside the Main Gatekeep','  You stand underneath and inside the large hallway which is the main gatekeep\nof Brightmoon.  To the west you see a large portcullis.  To the east are the\nmain town gates.  To the north and south are tower doors leading into the\nguard towers of this gatekeep.\n',17,139272,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(1219,-54,-27,0,'Bottom of a Guard Tower','  You are standing at the bottom of a large guard tower.  Various guardsman\ntools, tables, benches, and cots make this a comfortable post for the\ntown guards.  A large set of stairs climb the far wall to the top of the tower.\n',17,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(1220,-54,-29,0,'Bottom of a Guard Tower','  You are standing at the bottom of a large guard tower.  Various guardsman\ntools, tables, benches, and cots make this a comfortable post for the\ntown guards.  A large set of stairs climb the far wall to the top of the tower.\n',17,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(1221,-55,-28,0,'Intersection: Seacrest Way & Trader\'s Lane','  You stand here in the middle of an intersection of two streets.  Directly to\nthe east looms a huge gatekeep, main entrance to the town.  To the southwest\nlies a general store in which you see an assortment of the more common items.\nTo the northwest you see a grinder\'s shop.  Far to the west can be seen\nBrightmoon Harbor.\n',17,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1222,-53,-26,0,'Outside The Town Walls','  You are standing outside the walls of the great Town of Brightmoon.  There is\nnothing here of note save a few arrow slits in the walls, and the great defense\nthey provide.\n',17,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
