(1487,43,35,-3,'Versilard\'s Highway Through the Foothills','Constructed during the reign of Emperor Versilard in the Third Age, this\nancient highway was once the main route over the Sympathians, but as shorter\nroutes were opened up, fell into disuse.  Now, it is little more than a\nrocky path displaying the effects of time and the weather.  Somewhere\nsouth of here, through a pass in the mountains that rise majestically to\nthe southeast, lie the Badlands with the city of Logrus beyond.  To the\nwest, the land slopes downward toward a vast forest and further north, the\ncity of Amber.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
