(1492,43,40,-3,'Versilard\'s Highway Through the Foothills','Constructed during the reign of Emperor Versilard in the Third Age, this\nancient highway was once the main route over the Sympathians, but as shorter\nroutes were opened up, fell into disuse.  Now, it is little more than a\nrocky path displaying the effects of time and the weather.  Somewhere\nsouth of here, through a pass in the mountains that rise majestically to\nthe southeast, lie the Badlands with the city of Logrus beyond.  To the\nwest, the land slopes downward toward a vast forest and further north, the\ncity of Amber.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1493,43,41,-3,'Versilard\'s Highway Through the Foothills','Constructed during the reign of Emperor Versilard in the Third Age, this\nancient highway was once the main route over the Sympathians, but as shorter\nroutes were opened up, fell into disuse.  Now, it is little more than a\nrocky path displaying the effects of time and the weather.  Somewhere\nsouth of here, through a pass in the mountains that rise majestically to\nthe southeast, lie the Badlands with the city of Logrus beyond.  To the\nwest, the land slopes downward toward a vast forest and further north, the\ncity of Amber.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1494,43,42,-3,'Versilard\'s Highway','  You are at the northern terminus of Versilard\'s Highway.  Constructed\nduring the reign of Emperor Versilard in the Third Age, this ancient\nhighway was once the main route over the Sympathians, but as Grimhaven\nbecame more the center of trade and traffic between Amber and Logrus\ndwindled, fell into disuse.  Now, it is little more than a rocky path\ndisplaying the effects of time and the weather.  Somewhere south of here,\nthrough a pass in the mountains that rise majestically to the southeast,\nlie the Badlands with the city of Logrus beyond.  To the west can be seen\nthe trees of a large forest, and to the northeast, the highway exits onto\na road along the shore of a large bay.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1495,44,43,-3,'Road Along the Cliffs','  This road runs between the base of a cliff and a gravel strewn beach on\nthe shores of a large bay.  A chill wind whips across the cold water,\nforcing you to hug the cliff for warmth.  The cliff itself is very high\nat this point, and is steep and would be difficult to climb.  The trees\nof a large forest can be seen atop the cliff to the west.  The road\ncontinues along the shore of the bay to the north and southeast, while\nto the southwest, another larger road heads into the foothills of a range\nof high mountains that form the southern boundary of the bay.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1496,44,44,-3,'Road Along the Cliffs','  This road runs between the base of a cliff and a gravel strewn beach on\nthe shores of a large bay.  A chill wind whips across the cold water,\nforcing you to hug the cliff for warmth.  The cliff itself is very high\nat this point, and is steep and would be difficult to climb.  The trees\nof a large forest can be seen atop the cliff to the west, while to the\nnorthwest, you can just make out the tops of buildings over the trees.\nImmediately to the west, water has eroded a narrow gully down the side\nof the cliff, which your trained eye tells you would be climeable in dry\nweather.  The gully continues eastward toward the beach.  To the south,\na range of high mountains looms, forming the southern boundary of the\nbay.  The road runs north and south a short distance inland from the shore.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1497,44,45,-3,'Road Along the Cliffs','  This road runs between the base of a cliff and a gravel strewn beach on\nthe shores of a large bay.  A chill wind whips across the cold water,\nforcing you to hug the cliff for warmth.  The cliff itself is very high\nat this point, and is steep and would be difficult to climb.  The trees\nof a large forest can be seen atop the cliff to the west, while to the\nnorthwest, you can just make out the tops of buildings over the trees.\nTo the south, a range of high mountains loom in the distance, forming the\nsouthern boundary to the bay.  The road runs north and south a short\ndistance inland from the shore.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1498,44,46,-3,'Road Along the Cliffs','  This road runs between the base of a cliff and a gravel strewn beach on\nthe shores of a large bay.  A chill wind whips across the cold water,\nforcing you to hug the cliff for warmth.  The cliff itself is very high\nat this point, and is steep and would be difficult to climb.  The trees\nof a large forest can be seen atop the cliff to the west, to be replaced\nby the walls of a large town further to the northwest.  The road follows\nthe shores of the bay around to the north and south.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1499,44,47,-3,'Road Along the Cliffs','  This road runs between the base of a cliff and a gravel strewn beach on\nthe shores of a large bay.  A chill wind whips across the cold water,\nforcing you to hug the cliff for warmth.  The cliff itself is very high\nat this point, and is steep and would be difficult to climb.  The trees\nof a large forest can be seen atop the cliff to the west, to be replaced\nby the walls of a large town further to the northwest.  The road follows\nthe shores of the bay around to the northwest and south.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1500,43,48,-3,'Road Along the Cliffs','  This road runs between the base of a cliff and a gravel strewn beach on\nthe shores of a large bay.  A chill wind whips across the cold water,\nforcing you to hug the cliff for warmth.  The cliff itself is very high\nat this point, and is steep and would be difficult to climb.  The walls\nof a large town can be seen atop the cliff, which appears to dip down\ntoward the water to the north, and rise higher to the south.  The road\nitself follows the shores of the bay around to the northwest and southeast.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1501,42,49,-3,'Road Along the Cliffs','  This road runs between the base of a cliff and a gravel strewn beach on\nthe shores of a large bay.  A chill wind whips across the cold water,\nforcing you to hug the cliff for warmth.  The cliff itself is very high\nat this point, and is steep and would be difficult to climb.  The walls\nof a large town can be seen atop the cliff, which appears to dip down\ntoward the water to the north, and rise higher to the south.  The road\nitself follows the shores of the bay around to the southeast, and\ncontinues toward a tower in the town wall in the distance to the north.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1502,42,50,-3,'Road Along the Cliffs','  This road runs between the base of a cliff and a gravel strewn beach on\nthe shores of a large bay.  A chill wind whips across the cold water,\nforcing you to hug the cliff for warmth.  The cliff itself is fairly\nhigh at this point, but is steep and would be difficult to climb.  The\nwalls of a large town can be seen atop the cliff, which appears to dip\ndown toward the water to the north, and rise higher to the south.  The\nroad itself continues to the south, and heads toward a tower in the town\nwall a ways to the north.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1503,42,51,-3,'Road Along the Cliffs','  This road runs between the base of a cliff and a gravel strewn beach on\nthe shores of a large bay.  A chill wind whips across the cold water,\nforcing you to hug the cliff for warmth.  The cliff itself is moderately\nhigh at this point, but is steep and would be difficult to climb.  The\nwalls of a large town can be seen atop the cliff, which appears to dip\ndown toward the water to the north, and rise higher to the south.  The\nroad itself continues to the south, and heads toward a tower in the town\nwall a ways to the north.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1504,42,52,-3,'Road Along the Cliffs','  This road runs between the base of a cliff and a gravel strewn beach on\nthe shores of a large bay.  A chill wind whips across the cold water,\nforcing you to hug the cliff for warmth.  The cliff itself is not very\nhigh at this point, but is steep and would be difficult to climb.  The\nwalls of a large town can be seen atop the cliff, which appears to dip\ndown toward the water to the north, and rise higher to the south.  The\nroad itself continues to the south, and ends before a tower in the town\nwall to the north.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1506,50,19,0,'An Overgrown Rocky Trail','  This narrow, rocky trail is seldom used and has mostly been reclaimed by\nthe local vegetation.  The mighty Sympathian Mountains loom to the the\nwest, and this trail follows a gully through the foothills.\n',18,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1507,49,18,0,'An Overgrown Rocky Trail','  This narrow, rocky trail is seldom used and has mostly been reclaimed by\nthe local vegetation.  The mighty Sympathian Mountains loom to the the\nwest, and this trail follows a gully through the foothills.\n',18,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1510,45,42,-3,'Road Along the Bay','  This road runs along the southern shores of a large bay.  A chill wind\nout of the north whips across the cold water, driving spray in your face,\nand generally making life miserable.  To your south lie a range of tall\nmountains.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1600,-26,39,-1,'A Rocky, Dusty Trail','   This trail heads generally east-west and is fairly nondescript.  To the\neast you can make out a tree-line.  An unbroken chain of mountains dominates\nthe western horizon while faintly to the south can be made out a large plateau\nwith a great city atop it.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
