(1623,-49,40,0,'Near the Forest','  This is part of a well traveled path that branches off.  To the east, the\ntrail heads across rocky terrain toward the mountain range dominating the\nhorizon.  The southern fork seems to bear a good deal of traffic and the\nwagon ruts are many.  The western fork leads a short distance before entering\ninto a sparse forest beyond which a small village can be seen.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1624,-49,39,0,'Norman\'s Road','  A long, unbroken chain of mountains runs parallel to this well traveled\nroad.  The road itself is made of carefully hewn granite cobblestones\nmeticulously maintained although some weeds and moss grows up between a\nfew of the rocks here and there.  The road runs due north-south and a low\nmisty fog rolls down off the mountain obscuring the horizon.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
