(1641,-48,28,0,'Small Path','  The small path runs haphazardly in an east-west direction winding around\nhills, rocks and boulders.  It looks like it may run into a larger road to\nthe west, but what lies east of here remains obscured - it seems to run into\nthe mountains but you\'d have to get closer to be sure what\'s up ahead.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1642,-40,39,-1,'Gravelly Path','  This trail is hardly wide enough to stand on.  You brace yourself between\nthe two smooth granite walls that rise vertically overhead not 5 inches on\neither side of you and pick your way forward slowly.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1643,-48,36,0,'Just off Norman\'s Road','  This path runs between Norman\'s Road to the west and a small clearing to\nthe east.  Unlike Norman\'s Road, this area is not so well kept.  The\ncobbled road has been badly marked by time and even the grass has given no\nmercy.  Large cracks between the stones give places for weeds and other\nsuch plants to show their cruelty.  Obviously this path is not used much.\n',18,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1650,-49,22,0,'Norman\'s Road','  A long, unbroken chain of mountains parallels this road to the east,\nwhile the trees of a large forest loom to the south.  The road itself is\nmade of carefully hewn granite cobblestones meticulously maintained\nalthough some weeds and moss grows up between a few of the rocks here and\nthere.  The road runs due north-south and a low misty fog rolls down off\nthe mountain obscuring the horizon.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1651,-49,21,0,'Northern Entrance to Mordant\'s Deep','  A long, unbroken chain of mountains parallels this road to the east,\nwhile the trees of a large forest block any further progress south except\nalong the road.  The road itself is made of carefully hewn granite\ncobblestones meticulously maintained although some weeds and moss grows up\nbetween a few of the rocks here and there.  The road runs to the north and\ncurves southwest into the forest.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1652,-50,20,0,'Norman\'s Road Through Mordant\'s Deep','  The thick trunks of the trees in this old-growth forest line both sides\nof the road.  The thick undergrowth hinders any movement other than along\nthe road and limits visibility to only a few feet in most directions.  The\nroad itself is made of carefully hewn granite cobblestones fairly well\nmaintained although tree roots are beginning to buckle the paving rocks\nhere and there.  The road curves out of the forest to the northeast and\ncontinues south into the forest.\n',19,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1653,-50,19,0,'Norman\'s Road Through Mordant\'s Deep','  The thick trunks of the trees in this old-growth forest line both sides\nof the road.  The thick undergrowth hinders any movement other than along\nthe road and limits visibility to only a few feet in most directions.  The\nroad itself is made of carefully hewn granite cobblestones fairly well\nmaintained although tree roots are beginning to buckle the paving rocks\nhere and there.  The road continues to the north and south into the forest.\n',19,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1654,-50,18,0,'Norman\'s Road Through Mordant\'s Deep','  The thick trunks of the trees in this old-growth forest line both sides\nof the road.  The thick undergrowth hinders any movement other than along\nthe road and limits visibility to only a few feet in most directions.  The\nroad itself is made of carefully hewn granite cobblestones fairly well\nmaintained although tree roots are beginning to buckle the paving rocks\nhere and there.  The road curves deeper into the forest to the southwest\nand continues to the north.\n',19,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
