(1697,-48,-24,0,'Norman\'s Road','  Norman\'s Road continues basically north-south here, through the flat\ngrasslands to the west of the Parnithian Mountains.  A vast prairie\nborders the road to the east, with the mountains rising in the distance\nbeyond.  To the west, a vast field of wheat stretches as far as the eye can\nsee.  The road itself is packed gravel, and continues north and south.  A\nlittle path leads east across the prairie to a small house.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1698,-48,-25,0,'Norman\'s Road','  Norman\'s Road continues basically north-south here, through the flat\ngrasslands to the west of the Parnithian Mountains.  A vast prairie\nborders the road to the east, with the mountains rising in the distance\nbeyond.  To the west, some farms border the road.  The road itself is\npacked gravel, and continues north and south.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1699,-48,-26,0,'Norman\'s Road','  Norman\'s Road continues basically north-south here, through the flat\ngrasslands to the west of the Parnithian Mountains.  A vast prairie\nborders the road to the east, with the mountains rising in the distance\nbeyond.  To the west, some farms border the road.  The road itself is\npacked gravel, and continues north and southwest.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1700,-37,1,0,'Trail Along the Kranor River','  This trail runs north-south along the western bank of the Kranor river.\nIt climbs gradually into the foothills of the Parnithian Mountains to the\nnorth, and descends into the flatlands to the south.  The trail itself is\njust hard packed dirt mixed with rocks, leaves and sticks.  To the south,\nyou can see an intersection, and to the southeast a bridge crossing the\nKranor itself.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1701,-37,2,0,'Trail Along the Kranor River','  This trail runs north-south along the western bank of the Kranor river.\nIt climbs gradually into the foothills of the Parnithian Mountains to the\nnorth, and descends into the flatlands to the south.  The trail itself is\njust hard packed dirt mixed with rocks, leaves and sticks.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1702,-37,3,0,'Trail Along the Kranor River','  This trail runs north-south along the western bank of the Kranor river.\nIt climbs gradually into the foothills of the Parnithian Mountains to the\nnorth, and descends into the flatlands to the south.  The trail itself is\njust hard packed dirt mixed with rocks, leaves and sticks.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1703,-37,4,0,'Trail Along the Kranor River','  This trail runs north-south along the western bank of the Kranor river.\nIt climbs gradually into the foothills of the Parnithian Mountains to the\nnorth, and descends into the flatlands to the south.  The trail itself is\njust hard packed dirt mixed with rocks, leaves and sticks.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1704,-37,5,0,'Trail Along the Kranor River','  This trail runs north-south along the western bank of the Kranor river.\nIt climbs gradually into the foothills of the Parnithian Mountains to the\nnorth, and descends into the flatlands to the south.  The trail itself is\njust hard packed dirt mixed with rocks, leaves and sticks.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1705,-37,6,0,'Trail Along the Kranor River','  This trail runs north-south along the western bank of the Kranor river.\nIt climbs gradually into the foothills of the Parnithian Mountains to the\nnorth, and descends into the flatlands to the south.  The trail itself is\njust hard packed dirt mixed with rocks, leaves and sticks.  The trail bends\nto the northwest here, following the river and heading deeper into the\nmountains.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1706,-38,7,0,'Trail Through the Mountains','  This trail runs east-west in the Parnithian Mountains.  Far below you\nto the north, you can see the Kranor River as it winds its way through a\nvalley, and across the river you see some vast and dark forests.  The\nmountains themselves loom to your west, and you think you can make out a\npass the trail might be headed for.  The trail itself is a combination of\nhard packed dirt and solid rock.  The trail bends to the southeast here,\nfollowing the river valley.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1707,-39,7,0,'Trail Through the Mountains','  This trail runs east-west in the Parnithian Mountains.  Far below you\nto the north, you can see the Kranor River as it winds its way through a\nvalley, and across the river you see some vast and dark forests.  The\nmountains themselves loom to your west, and you think you can make out a\npass the trail might be headed for.  The trail itself is a combination of\nhard packed dirt and solid rock.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1708,-40,7,0,'Trail Through the Mountains','  This trail runs east-west in the Parnithian Mountains.  Far below you\nto the north, you can see the Kranor River as it winds its way through a\nvalley, and across the river you see some vast and dark forests.  The\nmountains themselves loom to your west, and you think you can make out a\npass the trail might be headed for.  The trail itself is a combination of\nhard packed dirt and solid rock.  The trail bends to the northwest here.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1709,-41,8,0,'Trail Through the Mountains','  This trail runs east-west in the Parnithian Mountains.  Far below you\nto the northeast, you can see the Kranor River as it winds its way through\na valley, and across the river you see some vast and dark forests.  The\nmountains themselves loom to your west, and just to the west you can see\nthe trail heads through a pass.  The trail itself is a combination of hard\npacked dirt and solid rock.  The trail bends to the southeast here.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1710,-42,8,0,'Pass in the Parnithian Mountains','  The trail leads east-west through this seldom used pass high in the\nMountains.  Tall, snow-covered peaks prevent travel to the north and south.\nThe trail itself is solid rock and the footing can be precarious.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1711,-43,8,0,'Pass in the Parnithian Mountains','  The trail leads east-west through this seldom used pass high in the\nMountains.  Tall, snow-covered peaks prevent travel to the north and south.\nThe trail itself is solid rock and the footing can be precarious.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1712,-44,8,0,'Pass in the Parnithian Mountains','  The trail leads east-west through this seldom used pass high in the\nMountains.  Tall, snow-covered peaks prevent travel to the north and south.\nThe trail itself is solid rock and the footing can be precarious.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1713,-45,8,0,'Trail Through the Mountains','  This trail runs east-west in the Parnithian Mountains.  Far below you\nto the west, you see a vast and dark forest.  The mountains themselves loom\nto your east, and just to the east you can see the trail heads through a\npass.  The trail itself is a combination of hard packed dirt and solid\nrock.  The trail bends to the northwest here.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1714,-46,9,0,'Trail Through the Mountains','  This trail runs southeast-northwest in the Parnithian Mountains.\nDownhill to the west, you see a vast, dark and ancient forest.  The\nmountains themselves loom to your east, and you think you can make out a\npass the trail might be headed for.  The trail itself is a combination of\nhard packed dirt and solid rock.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1715,-47,10,0,'Trail Through the Mountains','  This trail runs southeast-northwest in the Parnithian Mountains.\nDownhill to the west, you see a vast, dark and ancient forest.  The\nmountains themselves loom to your east, and you think you can make out a\npass the trail might be headed for.  The trail itself is a combination of\nhard packed dirt and solid rock.\n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1716,-48,11,0,'Eastern Entrance to Mordant\'s Deep','  The thick trunks of the trees in this old-growth forest line both sides\nof the trail.  The thick undergrowth hinders any movement other than along\nthe road and limits visibility to only a few feet in most directions.  The\ntrail is made of hard packed dirt mixed with leaves and twigs.  Eastward,\nthe forest ends and the trail heads upwards into a range of high mountains.\nTo the west, the trail continues into the forest.\n',19,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1717,-49,11,0,'A Lesser Trail Through Mordant\'s Deep','  The thick trunks of the trees in this old-growth forest line both sides\nof the trail.  The thick undergrowth hinders any movement other than along\nthe road and limits visibility to only a few feet in most directions.  The\ntrail is made of hard packed dirt mixed with leaves and twigs.  The trail\ncontinues to the east and west.\n',19,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1718,-50,11,0,'A Lesser Trail Through Mordant\'s Deep','  The thick trunks of the trees in this old-growth forest line both sides\nof the trail.  The thick undergrowth hinders any movement other than along\nthe road and limits visibility to only a few feet in most directions.  The\ntrail is made of hard packed dirt mixed with leaves and twigs.  The trail\ncontinues to the east and west.\n',19,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1720,-34,42,-1,'A Small Rocky Path','  Winding its way up through the foothills this small path seems moderately\ntraveled.  The vegetation closes in tightly on each side threatening to \novertake the small hard packed path.  Various broken branches and cut vines\ngive evidence that while no large group has passed this way, at least a few\nindividuals have done so recently.  The small path seems to continue to the \nnorthwest or to the south where it meets a larger trail.  \n<o>A small sign sits here made of simple wood and a stout post.<1>\n',19,131076,24,0,0,0,0,-1,3,-1,0,'',NULL),
