(1728,-37,44,-1,'A Small Rocky Path','  Winding its way up through the mountains this small path seems moderately\ntraveled.  The vegetation closes in tightly on each side threatening to \novertake the small hard packed path.  Various broken branches and cut vines\ngive evidence that while no large group has passed this way, at least a few\nindividuals have done so recently.  \n',19,131072,5,0,0,0,0,-1,3,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1729,-37,45,-1,'A Small Rocky Path','  Winding its way up through the mountains this small path seems moderately\ntraveled.  The vegetation closes in tightly on each side threatening to \novertake the small hard packed path.  Various broken branches and cut vines\ngive evidence that while no large group has passed this way, at least a few\nindividuals have done so recently.  The path continues to the south but seems \nto come to an end a little farther to the north.  The undergrowth appears to \ngive way to a field of short grass to the north and the sound of running \nwater can be heard as it echos through the forest.\n',19,131072,5,0,0,0,0,-1,3,-1,0,'',NULL),
(1730,0,0,0,'An Overgrown Path','  Shrubs press in on both sides of this narrow path.  The remains of broken\ncobblestones are barely visible between the long grasses and patches of weeds\nthat cover the ground.  Some <r>red<z> and <p>purple<z> flowers grow wildly, but may once\nhave been planted as decoration.  Clearly this way has not been tended for\nquite some time.  \n',19,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
