(2103,15,50,-2,'Upon a Narrow Ledge','   The ledge seems fairly stable, but it is obvious that one must\nconcentrate on the task at hand to avoid what could be a fatal mistake.  A\nsmall opening can be seen in the mountain to the north.  To the south a\nsteep trail leads to the base of the mountain.\n',21,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2104,15,51,-2,'Entrance to the Mountain','   The walls of the hall are rough, but obviously done by hand.  The dirt\non the ground seems to have been undisturbed for quite some time.  Light\nfilters in from an exit to the south casting strange shadows along the\nwalls of the hall.  The wind is brisk, leaving clothing flapping in its\nwake.  To the north, the shaft continues in a roughly straight ahead manner.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,23,'',NULL),
(2105,15,52,-2,'Inside the Mountain','   A very steep decline leads further down into the mountain.  Light seems to\ncompletely diminish in that direction.  To the south lies the entrance to the\nmountain.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2106,15,52,-3,'Inside the Mountain','   The walls are cold and a distant howling echoes through the tunnels.  It\nis evident that the passages were at one time inhabited, however it doesn\'t\nseem that it was any time recently.  The tunnel continues upward on a steep\nincline.  Not much can be seen farther down.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2107,15,52,-4,'Inside the Mountain','   The shaft continues leading sharply upwards or downwards.  Looking up you\ncan see that it continues for many meters, however looking down it is\napparent that level ground is near.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2108,15,52,-5,'The Mining Tunnels','   This cavern is fairly large and empty.  The first thing you notice upon\nentering is that your steps seem to be echoing oddly, as if the ground was\nhollow.  Exits lead in three directions: To the south, a very steep incline\ndisappears upwards into the darkness, to the northeast a narrow passage can\nbe seen, and to the northwest a slightly wider passage that seems a bit\nmore illuminated.  The dank smell of the  tunnel is strong, the air thick\nand cool like a heavy vapor.  Faintly, but  almost certainly, sounds can be\nheard echoing through the tunnel walls.  They seem to be coming from the\nnorthwest, but with the heavy echo of the tunnels, one can\'t be too sure.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2109,14,53,-5,'A Narrow Tunnel','   The tunnel is very narrow and shows signs of recent construction.\nWhether it is the result of a mining operation or something tunneling\nthrough the mountain is uncertain.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2110,13,54,-5,'A Narrow Tunnel','   The tunnel is very narrow and shows signs of recent construction.\nWhether it is the result of a mining operation or something tunneling\nthrough the mountain is uncertain.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2111,12,55,-5,'A Narrow Tunnel','   The tunnel is very narrow and shows signs of recent construction.  Whether it\nis the result of a mining operation or something tunneling through the mountain\nis uncertain.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2112,11,56,-5,'A Narrow Tunnel','   The tunnel is very narrow and shows signs of recent construction.  Whether it\nis the result of a mining operation or something tunneling through the mountain\nis uncertain.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2113,10,57,-5,'A Narrow Tunnel','   The tunnel is very narrow and shows signs of recent construction.  Whether it\nis the result of a mining operation or something tunneling through the mountain\nis uncertain.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2114,9,58,-5,'A Narrow Tunnel','   The tunnel is very narrow and shows signs of recent construction.  Whether it\nis the result of a mining operation or something tunneling through the mountain\nis uncertain.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2115,8,59,-5,'A Narrow Tunnel','   The tunnel is very narrow and shows signs of recent construction.  Whether\nit is the result of a mining operation or something tunneling through the\nmountain is uncertain.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2116,7,60,-5,'A Narrow Tunnel','   The tunnel is very narrow and shows signs of recent construction.  Whether\nit is the result of a mining operation or something tunneling through the\nmountain is uncertain.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2117,5,58,-5,'Abandoned Tunnel','   The passage is narrow and shows no signs of recent use.  Blood stains the\nwalls and a message is painted on the walls in this crimson ink.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2118,6,61,-5,'A Narrow Tunnel','   The passage continues far to the southeast, and seems to end abruptly to\nthe northwest.  From the south a warm wind blows, accompanied by an acrid\nsmell.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2119,7,56,-5,'Bend in the Passage','   The passage bends sharply, north in one direction and southeast in the\nother.  To the north a faint light can be seen.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2120,7,57,-5,'Lighted Tunnel','   The brightly glowing torches lining the walls of this tunnel cast\nstrange shadows about the passage.  Murmuring can be heard echoing through\nthe passageway.  The lighting of the tunnel seems to get brighter farther\nto the north where the passage declines steeply.  The ground is noticeably\ntrash free, as if the miners felt it was necessary to have a clear ground\nto work on.  Light dances off the walls, which for some reason reflects\nwith almost a mirrorlike intensity.\n',21,131081,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2121,7,57,-6,'Lighted Tunnel','   You can\'t help but notice the enormous size of this mining operation.\nThe miners either work extremely efficiently or are outrageous in number.\nHammering and stone cutting can be heard coming from a northern direction,\nbut the immense echoes make it hard to discern a precise location.  Light\nintensity increases somewhat to the north, while to the south it seems to\nfade out.  To the south, the passage rises on a steep incline.\n',21,131081,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2122,7,58,-6,'Lighted Intersection','The walls of the tunnel shine brilliantly, reflecting the precious metals\nburied within.  Sounds can be heard clearly through the passage.  To the\nnorth, hammering and stone cutting can be heard.  To the east is a\nlarge wooden door with the words, \"Authorized Personnel Only.\" inscribed\nabove a small window.\nThere is a sign on the wall.\n',0,131081,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2123,7,59,-6,'Finely Carved Corridor','   This section of the corridor is well lit, most likely so everyone can get\na clear view of the large murals and carvings on the walls.  It\'s quite a\nstartling transition from the bare walls to the south to these paint covered\nwalls.  The tunnel continues northward in a snake-like manner, and to the\nsouth where the mining operations continue.  But before departing, you can\nprobably tell these walls draw second glances from whoever passes between\nthem.\n',21,131081,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2124,7,60,-6,'Finely Decorated Corridor','   The painted corridor continues northward, where boisterous sounds can be\nheard in the distance, and to the south where tunnel darkens a bit.  It\'s\nhard to resist the temptation of studying the walls carefully.\n',21,131081,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2125,7,61,-6,'The Warning of the Messengers','   The painted walls and relief carvings are fashioned in a clearly welcoming,\nbut serious manner.  Depictions of elven servants on their knees carrying\nwater basins to wash your feet with.  Small ponies to carry your supplies\nline the wall with their heads lowered in a reverent manner.  But on each\nside of the northern end of the tunnel, a messenger of death raises his\ngleaming scythe in one hand and a silver scale of balance in the other.  To\nthe north the hall ends in a small arched ceiling, however the light prevents\nyou from seeing much from this distance.\n',21,131081,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2126,12,53,-5,'Abandoned Tunnel','  Cobwebs drape heavily from the walls and ceiling of the tunnel.  The air\nis stale, foul smelling, and humid which brings upon a light sweat.  To the\nwest the passage continues into the darkness, and to the northeast it\nascends a bit into a dim light.  You smell a musty odor coming from the\nnorth.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2127,11,53,-5,'Abandoned Tunnel','   The walls are covered in dust and cobwebs, and the air carries a acrid\nstench.  The immense humidity in the tunnels makes it easier to breathe in\nthan the other wind-chilled tunnels.  To the east and west the tunnel\ncontinues in darkness.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2128,10,53,-5,'Abandoned Tunnel','   The walls are covered in dust and cobwebs, and the air carries a acrid\nstench.  The immense humidity in the tunnels makes it easier to breathe in\nthan the other wind-chilled tunnels.  To the east and west the tunnel\ncontinues in darkness.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2129,9,53,-5,'Abandoned Tunnel','   The walls are covered in dust and cobwebs, and the air carries a acrid\nstench.  The immense humidity in the tunnels makes it easier to breathe in\nthan the other wind-chilled tunnels.  To the east and west the tunnel\ncontinues in darkness.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2130,8,53,-5,'Abandoned Tunnel','   The walls are covered in dust and cobwebs, and the air carries a acrid\nstench.  The immense humidity in the tunnels makes it easier to breathe in\nthan the other wind-chilled tunnels.  To the east and west the tunnel\ncontinues in darkness.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2131,7,53,-5,'Abandoned Tunnel','   The walls are covered in dust and cobwebs, and the air carries a acrid\nstench.  The immense humidity in the tunnels makes it easier to breathe in\nthan the other wind-chilled tunnels.  To the east and west the tunnel\ncontinues in darkness.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2132,6,53,-5,'Abandoned Tunnel','   The walls are covered in dust and cobwebs, and the air carries an acrid\nstench.  The immense humidity in the tunnels makes it easier to breathe in\nthan the other wind-chilled tunnels.  To the east the tunnel continues in\ndarkness, and the tunnel bends slightly to the northwest.  A strange kind\nof scraping sound echoes in from the northwest.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2133,5,54,-5,'Abandoned Tunnel','   The walls are covered in dust and cobwebs, and the air carries an acrid\nstench.  The immense humidity in the tunnels makes it easier to breathe than\nthe other wind-chilled tunnels.  To the northwest the tunnel continues into\ndarkness, and to the southeast you can see that the tunnel bends to the\neast.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2134,4,55,-5,'Abandoned Tunnel','   The walls are covered in dust and cobwebs, and the air carries an acrid\nstench.  The immense humidity in the tunnels makes it easier to breathe than\nthe other wind-chilled tunnels.  To the northwest the tunnel continues into\ndarkness, and to the southeast you can see that the tunnel bends to the\neast.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2135,3,56,-5,'Abandoned Intersection','   The air is very damp here, with a small draft of humid air drifting in\nfrom the east.  To the northeast and southeast the tunnel continues into\ndarkness.  You notice the east wall is made completely of ice.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2136,4,56,-5,'Tunnel of Dancing Lights','   A soft clear light bounces off the walls of this tunnel.  The sound of\ndripping water can be heard echoing in from the east.  Losing your footing\nfor a moment, you realize the entire tunnels is covered in ice.  Stalactites\nlook down upon their complementary stalagmites, which cause you work a path\naround them.  To the west the passage ends in a solid wall of ice, but to the\neast the tunnel seems to continue.  Something is very odd about this place.\n',21,131081,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2137,5,56,-5,'Ledge of the Ice Cavern','   A soft clear light bounces off the walls of this tunnel.  The sound of\ndripping water can be heard echoing in from the east.  The ice covered\ntunnel demands caution as one could easily slip and be impaled\nunceremoniously upon a sharp stalagmite.  To the west the ice tunnel\ncontinues, and the vision to the east takes your breath away.  You stand\nupon a ledge that overlooks an enormous ice crystal cavern.  You can only\nguess how high you stand on this ledge, for below all that can be seen is\ndarkness.  The sound of dripping water comes from below.\n',21,131081,15,0,0,0,0,0,0,400,0,'',NULL),
(2138,6,50,-6,'Ice Cavern','   Halfway between the ledge above you and the ground below, you deduce that\nthe ledge is about a hundred yards high.  Below a small lake can be seen as\nthe center of the cavern, and beautiful ice formations surround it.  Giant\nstalagmites jut out of the ground posing a dangerous threat to the\nunfortunate climber.  You notice something strange about the ice however, it\nseems that a portion of it seems to be moving.\n',21,131081,15,0,0,0,0,0,0,400,0,'',NULL),
(2139,6,50,-7,'Lair of Kylish\'Ra','  This ice cavern is so large that while you stand at one end of it, the\nrest just disappears into darkness.  Breathtaking ice sculptures surround a\nlake of crystal blue water.  The lake flows freely through small rivers in\nthe ice.  Unfortunately, as much as you\'d like to stand here and indulge\nyourself in the beauty of it all, you seem to have disturbed the cavern\'s\noccupant.  You can do nothing but stand in fear as the mighty Kylish\'Ra, the\ngreat dragon of ice, raises from her snowy bed.  It looks as if she\'s\nhungry, and you\'re the main course.  There is a sign posted on a stalagmite.\n',21,133129,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,400,0,'',NULL),
(2140,2,55,-5,'Abandoned Tunnel','   The air is thick and heavy in this dark and still tunnel.  Cobwebs hang\nfrom the ceiling in a haphazardly fashion.  The dripping of water can be\nheard from the southwest, and a slight draft comes in from the northeast.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2141,3,56,-5,'Abandoned Tunnel','   The air is thick and heavy in this dark and still tunnel.  Cobwebs hang\nfrom the ceiling in a haphazardly fashion.  The dripping of water can be\nheard from the southwest, and a slight draft comes in from the northeast.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2142,4,57,-5,'Abandoned Tunnel','   The air is thick and heavy in this dark and still tunnel.  Cobwebs hang\nfrom the ceiling in a haphazardly fashion.  The dripping of water can be\nheard from the southwest, and a slight draft comes in from the northeast.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2143,16,53,-5,'Windy Passage','   A steady breeze blows through the tunnel bringing fresh air to your\nnostrils.  A scuffing sound echoes as you make your way along the sandy\nfloor.  To the northeast the tunnel continues widening a bit, and to the\nsouthwest the tunnel opens into a small cavern.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2144,17,54,-5,'Windy Passage','   A steady breeze blows through the tunnel bringing fresh air to your\nnostrils.  A scuffing sound echoes as you make your way along the sandy\nfloor.  To the northeast the tunnel continues widening a bit, and nearby to\nthe southwest you can see the tunnel open to a small cavern.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2145,18,55,-5,'Windy Passage','   A steady breeze blows through the tunnel bringing fresh air to your\nnostrils.  A scuffing sound echoes as you make your way along the sandy\nfloor.  To the northeast the tunnel continues widening a bit, and a ways to\nthe southwest you can see the tunnel open to a small cavern.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2146,19,56,-5,'Windy Passage','   A steady breeze blows through the tunnel bringing fresh air to your\nnostrils.  A scuffing sound echoes as you make your way along the sandy\nfloor.  To the northeast the tunnel continues widening a bit, and far to the\nsouthwest you can see the tunnel open to a small cavern.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2147,18,55,-5,'Windy Passage','   A steady breeze blows through the tunnel bringing fresh air to your\nnostrils.  A scuffing sound echoes as you make your way along the sandy\nfloor.  To the northeast the tunnel continues widening a bit, and to the\nsouthwest the tunnel continues with a faint light at the end.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2148,19,56,-5,'Windy Intersection','   There are marks upon the ground that indicate recent activity in this\narea.  Judging from the hammering sounds echoing in from the north, this\npassage is probably currently being mined.  To the northeast the tunnel\ncontinues with a northward bend far ahead.  The passage to the north is well\nlit.\n',21,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2149,21,59,-5,'Active Tunnel','   There is much activity in this section of the mountain.  Loads of cut\nrock are carried north through the tunnel on wheelbarrows, mining\ncaptains shouting orders to the elven slaves, and many dwarven men cutting\naway at the stone walls.  The elven slaves are much more pale than the usual\nelf, and all of them have snowy white hair.  The dwarves themselves are\nstocky, but most of them look very powerful despite their height.  The\ndwarven mining captains are just as dirty as their workers, it seems they\nput in just as much effort as the rest do.  To the north the mining\noperation continues, and to the south an empty intersection leads to other\ntunnels.\n',21,131081,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2150,21,60,-5,'Active Tunnel','   There is much activity in this section of the mountain.  Loads of cut\nrock are carried north through the tunnel on wheelbarrows, mining\ncaptains shouting orders to the elven slaves, and many dwarven men cutting\naway at the stone walls.  The elven slaves are much more pale than the usual\nelf, and all of them have snowy white hair.  The dwarves themselves are\nstocky, but most of them look very powerful despite their height.  The\ndwarven mining captains are just as dirty as their workers, it seems they\nput in just as much effort as the rest do.  To the north the mining\noperation continues, and to the south an empty intersection leads to other\ntunnels.\n',21,131081,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
