(2176,20,57,-5,'Pickup Tunnel','   This tunnel is filled packed with every type of cart imaginable.  Along\nthe west wall lie carts that are broken and in line for repair, and along\nthe east wall lie carts that are currently not in use.  The middle of the\ntunnel has a clear path for a long line of carts constantly moving southwest.\nSeveral dwarves lounge about the tunnel, apparently on break.\n',21,131081,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2177,26,69,-5,'Disposal Ramp','    The steep carved ramp is flooded with traffic.  Dwarves coming from\nbelow to bring empty carts back for another load, and others arriving from\nthe west to empty their full carts.  From below you feel a draft of fresh\ncool air softly surround you.\n',21,131081,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2178,26,69,-6,'Disposal Ramp','   The steep carved ramp is flooded with traffic.   Dwarves coming from\nbelow to bring empty carts back for another load, and others arriving from\nthe above  to empty their full carts.  From below you feel a fresh cold breeze\nblowing.  Above you, the top of the ramp can be seen.\n',21,131081,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2179,26,69,-7,'Entrance to the Mountain','   You have come upon the entrance to the mountain where it seems much\nactivity is taking place.  Dwarves move busily carrying large carts of\nmaterial from above and dump them to the side of the mountain.  Looking\naround at the debris around you, you realize just how big this mining\noperation is.\n',21,131081,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2180,8,58,-6,'Small Hallway','   This hall doesn\'t look much different from most of the mountainous\ntunnels, except for the wooden doors set in the walls.  The doors are set in\nthe north, south, and east walls.\n',21,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2181,8,59,-6,'Lavatory','   This small cubicle reeks of feces.  A large hole dug in the ground\nserves as the only means of relieving oneself.  You think it best that you\nleave before you loose your lunch.\n',21,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2182,8,57,-6,'Supply Room','   The supply closet is filled with many extra tools and equipment.  Most\nof it, however, looks old and decrepit.  There are some tools that don\'t\nseem to be broken, but it\'s probably been quite a while since anyone has\nused this closet.\n',21,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2183,9,58,-6,'Supervisor\'s Office','   The office of the supervisor is minimally furnished.  It seems the\nsupervisor is more interested in working than interior decorating.  There is\na small wooden door to the south.\n',21,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2184,9,57,-6,'Supervisor\'s Quarters','   In contrast to the bare office, this room is finely furnished.  The\nfloor is all oak, the walls and roof smoothly shaped from the natural stone\nof the mountain.  A large bed with an obviously expensive embroidered quilt\nlie in the center of the room.  A small oaken nightstand rests to the right\nof the bed, with a tall candle upon it.  Carved within the east wall is a\nstone bookshelf, completely full of books.  A fine throw-rug lies before the\nbed waiting to service your feet.\n',21,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2185,10,57,-6,'Narrow Path','   This passage has been cut very carefully to produce the smooth walls,\nceiling, and floor.  There are odd symbols inscribed upon the walls, some\nyou recognize as having religious significance, and others you can\'t make\nout at all.  The air in the tunnel is still, but smells fresh.  To the east\nyou see the tunnel disappear into darkness.\n',21,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2186,11,57,-6,'Narrow Path','   This passage has been cut very carefully to produce the smooth walls,\nceiling, and floor.  There are odd symbols inscribed upon the walls, some\nyou recognize as having religious significance, and others you can\'t make\nout at all.  The air in the tunnel is still, but smells fresh.  A\ngopher-like hole has been dug in the ground and seems to lead far below into\nthe mountain.  A long ladder rests against the side of the hole.  Below and\nto the west, the tunnel disappears into darkness.\n',21,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2187,11,57,-7,'Temple Path','   To the east the tunnel exits to a giant valley.  A large structure can be\nseen blocking some of your view of the mountain on the other side.  The\nbuilding looks much like a temple of some kind, but it\'s hard to tell at this\ndistance.  A ladder rests against the west wall that leads upwards into\ndarkness.\n',21,139584,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2188,12,57,-7,'Temple Path','    To the east you can make out the side of a giant temple that lies\nsomewhere in a large valley.  To the west lies the path leads back into\ndarkness.\n',21,139584,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2189,13,57,-7,'Path Around the Temple','You stand in the northwest side of a giant valley surrounded by mountains\non all sides.  A magnificent three story temple sticks out of the northern\nmountain.  From what you can see of the temple, being on the western side of\nit, it seems to be made completely from marble.  Beautiful carvings\ndepicting deities and heroes line the temple wall.  The artist was\nobviously a master.  The path continues to the south around the corner of\nthe temple and to the west which disappears into the mountain.\n',0,139584,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2190,13,56,-7,'Path Around the Temple','You stand in the northwest side of a giant valley surrounded by mountains\non all sides.  A magnificent three story temple sticks out of the northern\nmountain.  From what you can see of the temple, being on the western side of\nit, it seems to be made completely from marble.  Beautiful carvings\ndepicting deities and heroes line the temple wall.  The artist was\nobviously a master.  The path leads southeast around the corner of the\ntemple and to the north where it ends abruptly at the mountain face.  You\ncan spot a small passage just west of the end of the path.\n',0,139584,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2191,14,55,-7,'Path Around the Temple','You stand at the base of a set of giant marble stairs that lead to the\neast.  Upon the banister of the staircase there are small statues of dwarven\ndeities at intervals all the way up.  There are stairs to the\nsouth and east as well as this one, but they all seem to lead to the same\nplace.\n',0,139584,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2192,14,55,-6,'Temple Entrance','The entrance to the temple is two ten foot golden doors with symbols and\npictures engraved upon every inch.  At each side of the door stands a giant\nstatue set in heavy platinum, depicting the two great deities of the dwarven\nrace.  Ivryn stands dressed in an elegant gown of flowers with her arms\noutstretched and a tender smile graces her lips.  To the south and west are\ngiant staircases leading down.\n',0,139584,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2193,16,55,-5,'Before the Cathedral','The entrance to the temple is two ten foot golden doors with symbols and\npictures engraved upon every inch.  At each side of the door stands a giant\nstatue set in heavy platinum, depicting the two great deities of the dwarven\nrace.  Thrombul stands in full battle uniform with his thick arms crossed\nand a powerful expression of might upon his face.\n',0,139584,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2194,16,55,-6,'Path Around the Temple','To the north, the path continues into the valley.  To the west, the entrance to the Dwarven Temple can be seen.\n',0,139584,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2195,18,56,-6,'Path Around the Temple','You stand in the northeast side of a giant valley surrounded by mountains\non all sides.  A magnificent three story temple sticks out of the northern\nmountain.  From what you can see of the temple, being on the eastern side of\nit, it seems to be made completely from marble.  Beautiful carvings\ndepicting deities and heroes line the temple wall.  The artist was\nobviously a master.  The path leads southwest around the corner of the\ntemple and to the north where it ends abruptly at the mountain face.  You\ncan spot a small passage just east of the end of the path.\n',0,139584,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2196,19,69,-7,'Path Around the Temple','You stand in the northeast side of a giant valley surrounded by mountains\non all sides.  A magnificent three story temple sticks out of the northern\nmountain.  From what you can see of the temple, being on the eastern side of\nit, it seems to be made completely from marble.  Beautiful carvings\ndepicting deities and heroes line the temple wall.  The artist was\nobviously a master.  The path continues to the south around the corner of\nthe temple and to the east which disappears into the mountain.\n',0,139584,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2197,15,54,-6,'Southern Temple Entrance','You stand in the south side of a giant valley surrounded by mountains on\nall sides.  You can see two other staircases coming from the east and west\nleading to the same place this one does.  A magnificent three story temple\nsticks out of the northern mountain.  It is completely constructed from marble and\nthe gold trims add to the brilliance of the structure.  Upon the roof is a\ngiant bell.\n',0,139584,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2198,15,53,-6,'Temple Path','   You stand in a large valley surrounded by mountains on all sides.  To the\nnorth you can see a grand temple sticking out of the northern mountain.  A\ngiant bell graces the top of the three story structure.  To the south a\ntunnel leads into the darkness of the mountain.\n',21,139584,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2199,15,52,-6,'Below the Mining Tunnel','Used by the dwarves as an easy go between from the mines above and the cleric temple to the north, the scents of\nthe mines and pious holy water mingle while thunderous digging and deep chants echo.\n',0,139592,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2200,13,56,-6,'Prayer Alcove','   You count twenty candles lit in a semi-circle on a small ivory table.\nStrong incense and other herbs create a thick scent in the air.  Upon each\ncorner of the table a small statuette stands facing the candles at the\ncenter.  The statuettes seem to be a continuation of the ivory itself, not\njust an attachment.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2201,14,57,-6,'Meditation Chamber','    This small room is dedicated for meditation and prayer.  It is furnished\nwith nothing but a small cushion on the floor and a candle placed in front\nof it.  A small window looks out on the valley below.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2202,14,58,-6,'Meditation Chamber','    This small room is dedicated for meditation and prayer.  It is furnished\nwith nothing but a small cushion on the floor and a candle placed in front\nof it.  A small window looks out on the valley below.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2203,14,59,-6,'Meditation Chamber','    This small room is dedicated for meditation and prayer.  It is furnished\nwith nothing but a small cushion on the floor and a candle placed in front\nof it.  A small window looks out on the valley below.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2204,14,60,-6,'Meditation Chamber','This small room is dedicated for meditation and prayer.  It is furnished\nwith nothing but a small cushion on the floor and a candle placed in front of\nit.  A small window looks out on the valley below.\n',-1,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2205,14,61,-6,'Stair Landing','   You stand at the base of a tight spiral staircase leading up to the\nsecond floor of the temple.  The staircase itself is exquisitely carved in a\ndark, thick oak.  Above you can see that the stairs seemingly lead all the\nway to the top of the temple.  To the east is the temple altar.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2206,14,56,-6,'Cathedral Entrance','   You stand within the giant temple of Thrombul and Ivryn.  To your east\nand west are small prayer alcoves, and to your north two sets of columns\nline the way to the altar.  Several doors run along the sides of the room.\nSoft chanting can be heard flooding throughout the building as acolytes and\npriests go about their business in prayer.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2207,15,57,-6,'Temple Floor','   The temple is carefully decorated with marble sculptures, grand oil\npaintings, tapestries, and intricately designed carpets.  Engraved columns\napproximately ten feet high line the temple floor.  Along the east and west\nwalls are four small oaken doors.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2208,15,58,-6,'Temple Floor','   The temple is carefully decorated with marble sculptures, grand oil\npaintings, tapestries, and intricately designed carpets.  Engraved columns\napproximately ten feet high line the temple floor.  Along the east and west\nwalls are four small oaken doors.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2209,15,59,-6,'Temple Floor','The temple is carefully decorated with marble sculptures, grand oil\npaintings, tapestries, and intricately designed carpets.  Engraved columns\napproximately ten feet high line the temple floor.  Along the east and west\nwalls are four small oaken doors.\n',-1,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2210,15,60,-6,'Temple Floor','The temple is carefully decorated with marble sculptures, grand oil\npaintings, tapestries, and intricately designed carpets.  Engraved columns\napproximately ten feet high line the temple floor.  Along the east and west\nwalls are four small oaken doors.\n',-1,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2211,15,61,-6,'Before the Altar','You stand before the altar of Thrombul.  To your east and west you can\nwooden spiral stairs leading up to other areas of the temple, and to your\nsouth lies the temple floor, where large ceremonies must take place.  Along\nthe east and west walls are four oaken doors.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2212,15,56,-6,'Cathedral Entrance','   You stand within the giant temple of Thrombul and Ivryn.  To your east\nand west are small prayer alcoves, and to your north two sets of columns\nline the way to the altar.  Several doors run along the sides of the room.\nSoft chanting can be heard flooding throughout the building as acolytes and\npriests go about their business in prayer.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
