(2223,17,61,-6,'Stair Landing','   You stand at the base of a tight spiral staircase leading up to the\nsecond floor of the temple.  The staircase itself is exquisitely carved in a\ndark, thick oak.  Above you can see that the stairs seemingly lead all the\nway to the top of the temple.  To the west is the temple altar.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2224,16,62,-6,'Altar of Thrombul','   You stand at the onyx altar of Thrombul.  The altar itself stands about\nthree feet high and five feet long.  Two ceremonial bowls are carved into the\nsurface of the altar.  Various other instruments used during ceremonies lie in\nan organized fashion on the altar.  You can see a slight residue upon the\nsurface of the altar, the color of dried blood.  You assume sacrifice is\nsomething Thrombul condones.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2225,14,56,-5,'A Monk\'s Office','   The monk\'s office is furnished with a large desk and chair, two visitor\nseats, and a large stacked bookshelf.  Other than the parchment scattered on\nthe desk, the office is very tidy.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2226,14,57,-5,'A Monk\'s Office','   The monk\'s office is furnished with a large desk and chair, two visitor\nseats, and a large stacked bookshelf.  Other than the parchment scattered on\nthe desk, the office is very tidy.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2227,14,58,-5,'A Priest\'s Office','    This office is modestly furnished, leaving little walking room other\nthan from the entrance to the desk.  Whoever resides in this office is\nobviously a heavy reader, for books lie everywhere.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2228,14,59,-5,'A Priest\'s Office','    This office is modestly furnished, leaving little walking room other\nthan from the entrance to the desk.  Whoever resides in this office is\nobviously a heavy reader, for books lie everywhere.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2229,14,60,-5,'A Priest\'s Office','    This office is modestly furnished, leaving little walking room other\nthan from the entrance to the desk.  Whoever resides in this office is\nobviously a heavy reader, for books lie everywhere.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2230,14,61,-5,'Spiral Staircase','    You stand at a landing of a tight spiral staircase.  Made of dark oak,\nthe staircase blends well with the rest of the surroundings.  The stairs\nlead up to the third floor of the temple, and down to the temple floor.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2231,15,56,-5,'Bend in the Hallway','   This hallway has a dim glow to it, though you are unsure of the source.\nThe smooth marble walls are cold to the touch, and your footsteps seem to\necho very loudly in the corridor.  The hall continues to the north and bends\naround to the east.  There is an small oaken door to the west.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
