(2243,17,56,-5,'Temple Dining Room','   This is an elegant room with several long marble tables under golden\ntablecloths.  Crystal chandeliers hang low from the high ceiling just over\nthe tables.  Long wooden benches line the sides of the tables.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2244,17,57,-5,'Temple Dining Room','   This is an elegant room with several long marble tables under golden\ntablecloths.  Crystal chandeliers hang low from the high ceiling just over\nthe tables.  Long wooden benches line the sides of the tables.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2245,17,58,-5,'Temple Dining Room','   This is an elegant room with several long marble tables under golden\ntablecloths.  Crystal chandeliers hang low from the high ceiling just over\nthe tables.  Long wooden benches line the sides of the tables.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2246,17,59,-5,'Kitchen','   This room is filled with wooden cabinets, gas stoves, and various cooking\nutensils.  To the south is a swing door that leads to the dining room.  As\nmuch as the dwarves take their religion and art seriously, it is obvious\nthat food is just as important.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2247,17,60,-5,'Kitchen','   This room is filled with wooden cabinets, gas stoves, and various cooking\nutensils.  To the south is a swing door that leads to the dining room.  As\nmuch as the dwarves take their religion and art seriously, it is obvious\nthat food is just as important.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2248,17,61,-5,'Spiral Staircase','    You stand at a landing of a tight spiral staircase.  Made of dark oak,\nthe staircase blends well with the rest of the surroundings.  The stairs\nlead up to the third floor of the temple, and down to the temple floor.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2249,15,62,-5,'High Priest\'s Office','   You stand in the large, well furnished office of the high priest.  A\nlarge bookshelf contains neatly stacked books and scrolls.  The desk is\norderly and spotless as is pretty much the rest of the room.  The high\npriest seems to be very anal when it comes to cleanliness.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2250,16,62,-5,'Bishop\'s Office','   The office of the Bishop is large and elegant.  Every piece of furniture\nmust be priceless, for it is all ancient and beautiful.  A high chair sits\nbehind a long wooden desk and you get the impression that his is a man of\ngreat authority.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2251,14,56,-4,'Small Stairwell','    This small stairwell is made completely of marble.  You know the\ncraftsmen of this structure were brilliant to be able to create such a\ncomplex structure out of such tough material.  The stairs are short and end\nat a hatch in the roof.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2252,14,57,-4,'Bedroom','   You are in what seems to be the bedroom of a monk.  The furniture is, of\ncourse, bare.  Through the small window in the room, a gorgeous panoramic\nview of the valley far below.  The monk\'s bed is nothing but a small cot\nwith a heavy blanket.  The chest at the foot of his bed is probably to hold\npersonal belongings, and a small closet for his clothes.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2253,14,58,-4,'Bedroom','   You are in what seems to be the bedroom of a monk.  The furniture is, of\ncourse, bare.  Through the small window in the room, a gorgeous panoramic\nview of the valley far below.  The monk\'s bed is nothing but a small cot\nwith a heavy blanket.  The chest at the foot of his bed is probably to hold\npersonal belongings, and a small closet for his clothes.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
