(2275,15,62,-4,'Chambers of the High Priest','   The high priest\'s bedroom is very well furnished.  A nice sized bed\nresting in one corner of the room invites pleasant sleep.  And two\ncomfortable looking chairs are available for visitors.  A few paintings on\nthe walls and sculptures here and there tell that the man is an art lover.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2276,16,62,-4,'Chambers of the Bishop','   This room is large and luxurious, with a gigantic red curtained bed resting\nin the center.  Two plush chairs and a comfortable looking couch line one\nwall, and a long desk and high chair line the other.  Two nightstands sit\nbeside the bed.  On the floor is an outrageously expensive elven carpet.  The\nbishop obviously lives in comfort.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2277,14,56,-3,'Bell Tower','   Standing on the temple roof you are struck with awe as you look out\nacross the valley; the beauty is exhilarating.  You are completely\nsurrounded by mountains and an icy wind blows in your face.  Above you a\nsmall tower holds a large bell.  Below you, a wooden hatch leads back into\nthe temple.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2278,14,56,-2,'Bell Tower','   You stand inside the bell tower of the temple.  In front of you, a\ngigantic black bell hangs unmoving in the heavy winds.  An freezing wind\nblows in from above the mountains, numbing you.  It might be a good idea to\nget down before you loose your footing.\n',21,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2300,0,0,0,'Norman\'s Road','  This road runs parallel to a long, unbroken chain of mountains in the east. \nIt is made of carefully hewn and well-maintained granite cobblestones, though\nsome weeds and mosses grow here and there in the cracks.  The road continues\nto the north and south.  \n',22,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
