(2308,0,0,0,'Norman\'s Road','  This road runs parallel to a long, unbroken chain of mountains in the east. \nIt is made of carefully hewn and well-maintained granite cobblestones, though\nsome weeds and mosses grow here and there in the cracks.  The road continues\nto the north and south.  A narrow path of beaten dirt leads to the northwest.\n',22,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2309,0,0,0,'Norman\'s Road','  This road runs parallel to a long, unbroken chain of mountains in the east. \nThe granite cobblestones of which it is made are cracked in places, and many\nweeds and mosses grow on and between the stones.  The road continues to the\nnorth and south.  \n',22,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2310,0,0,0,'Detour from Norman\'s Road','  This path of beaten dirt follows a narrow hillside ledge.  It appears to\nhave been hastily constructed;  no attempt was made to level the ground, or to\nwiden the path beyond what is required for a horse and rider.  The path does,\nhowever, appear to be well-traveled.  It continues to the northwest and\nsoutheast. \n',22,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2311,0,0,0,'Norman\'s Road','  This road runs parallel to a long, unbroken chain of mountains in the east. \nThe granite cobblestones of which it is made are cracked in places, and many\nweeds and mosses grow on and between the stones.  The road continues to the\nnorth and south.  \n',22,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
