(2350,0,0,0,'The Lobby','  This is the lobby of the trendy and elite GK Highrollers Casino.\nAdmission prices are steep and talens flow like water in this fairy\ntale land of fast living, bright lights and big risks.  Luxurious\nthick <r>red carpet<1> woven with <Y>gold patterns<1> covers the floor and\n<W>glittering chandeliers<1> hang from the high vaulted ceiling.  The walls\nare covered in a cream colored wall paper bearing the same patterns as\nthe carpet.  Several expensive looking paintings hang on the walls.\n',23,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2351,0,0,0,'Grimhaven Bank Branch','  Luxurious thick <r>red carpet<1> woven with <Y>gold patterns<1>\ncovers the floor and <W>glittering chandeliers<1> hang from the high\nvaulted ceiling.  The walls are covered in a cream colored wall paper\nbearing the same patterns as the carpet.  A friendly bank teller\nbehind a steel bars is here to assist with any banking needs that\nCasino clients may need.  Although not a full fledged branch of the\nGrimhaven Bank, it does have the financial backing of the Casino and\nall deposits are guaranteed safe until transfered to the main branch.\n',23,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,7,'',NULL),
(2352,0,0,0,'Elevator Platform','  Luxurious thick <r>red carpet<1> woven with <Y>gold patterns<1>\ncovers the floor and <W>glittering chandeliers<1> hang from the high\nvaulted ceiling.  The walls are covered in a cream colored wall paper\nbearing the same patterns as the carpet.  Several expensive looking\npaintings hang on the walls.  An open elevator shaft lined with large\nwindows extends far above, up to the Casino floor.  A <r>red velvet\nrope<1> forms a barrier around the elevator landing.\n',23,131081,65,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2353,0,0,0,'Cashier\'s Cage','  Luxurious thick <r>red carpet<1> woven with <Y>gold patterns<1>\ncovers the floor and <W>glittering chandeliers<1> hang from the high\nvaulted ceiling.  The walls are covered in a cream colored wall paper\nbearing the same patterns as the carpet.  Several expensive looking\npaintings hang on the walls.  Inside of the cashier\'s cage, several\nstout safes are lined up and neatly arranged stacks of casino chips\noverburden several tables.\n',23,172537,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2354,0,0,0,'Elevator Shaft','  Extremely thick steel columns support each of the four corners of\nthis elevator shaft.  Large glass windows span between the columns,\nsupported by stout steel crossbars.  Through the windows, the southern\nmarket district of Grimhaven can be seen.  A particularly <k>dark<1>\nspot to the southeast can be recognized as <k>Twilight Square<1>.\n',23,131081,35,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2355,0,0,0,'Elevator Shaft','  Extremely thick steel columns support each of the four corners of\nthis elevator shaft.  Large glass windows span between the columns,\nsupported by stout steel crossbars.  Through the windows, the majority\nof the southwest section of Grimhaven can be seen, including Market\nSquare, the Roaring Lion Inn, the theatre and most of the park.\n',23,131081,35,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2356,0,0,0,'Elevator Shaft','  Extremely thick steel columns support each of the four corners of\nthis elevator shaft.  Large glass windows span between the columns,\nsupported by stout steel crossbars.  Through the windows, all of\nGrimhaven can easily be seen.  The Royal Palace stands tall and\nbright, as does the Grimhaven Church.  The park provides a\nparticularly picturesque scene.\n',23,131081,35,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2357,0,0,0,'Elevator Shaft','  Extremely thick steel columns support each of the four corners of\nthis elevator shaft.  Large glass windows span between the columns,\nsupported by stout steel crossbars.  Through the windows, all of\nGrimhaven can be made out as well as much of the surrounding area.\nThe <g>Haon-Dor Forest<1> occupies most of the area to the north,\nwhile the <b>Kranor River<1> can be seen snaking its way to the\nocean, to the west and south.\n',23,131081,35,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2358,0,0,0,'Poker Table','  Luxurious thick <r>red carpet<1> woven with <Y>gold patterns<1>\ncovers the floor and <W>glittering chandeliers<1> hang from the high\nvaulted ceiling.  To the west, the gleaming city of <W>Brightmoon<1>\ncan be seen.\n',23,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2359,0,0,0,'Hi-Lo Table','  Luxurious thick <r>red carpet<1> woven with <Y>gold patterns<1>\ncovers the floor and <W>glittering chandeliers<1> hang from the high\nvaulted ceiling.  To the south, a large window looks out far above the city\nof Grimhaven.  Off in the distance the great <b>Myrian Ocean<1> can be\nmade out amid the haze.\n',23,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2360,0,0,0,'Blackjack Table','  Luxurious thick <r>red carpet<1> woven with <Y>gold patterns<1>\ncovers the floor and <W>glittering chandeliers<1> hang from the high\nvaulted ceiling.  To the south and east, large windows look out far above\nthe city of Grimhaven.  Off in the distance the great <b>Myrian\nOcean<1> can be made out amid the haze.  To the east, a good view of\nthe city park and the eastern marketplace can be seen.\n',23,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2361,0,0,0,'Baccarat Table','  Luxurious thick <r>red carpet<1> woven with <Y>gold patterns<1>\ncovers the floor and <W>glittering chandeliers<1> hang from the high\nvaulted ceiling.\n',23,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2362,0,0,0,'Casino Floor','  Luxurious thick <r>red carpet<1> woven with <Y>gold patterns<1>\ncovers the floor and <W>glittering chandeliers<1> hang from the high\nvaulted ceiling.  A <r>red velvet<1> rope surrounds an elevator shaft\nin the center of the room to protect customers from accidentily\nfalling in.  An ornate set of spiral stairs lead upwards.\n',23,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2363,0,0,0,'Craps Table','  Luxurious thick <r>red carpet<1> woven with <Y>gold patterns<1>\ncovers the floor and <W>glittering chandeliers<1> hang from the high\nvaulted ceiling.  A large window to the east looks out far above the\ncity of Grimhaven.  The city park can clearly be made out, as well as\nthe eastern marketplace and the wilderness beyond.\n',23,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2364,0,0,0,'Casino Hotel','  Luxurious thick <r>red carpet<1> woven with <Y>gold patterns<1>\ncovers the floor and <W>glittering chandeliers<1> hang from the high\nvaulted ceiling.  GH Highrollers offers a number of deluxe suites for\novernight guests, or for those that wish to relax in privacy without\nleaving the casino.\n',23,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2365,0,0,0,'Slots','  Luxurious thick <r>red carpet<1> woven with <Y>gold patterns<1>\ncovers the floor and <W>glittering chandeliers<1> hang from the high\nvaulted ceiling.  A small number of high stake slot machines form a\nsmall island in the middle of the room.  Slots are not popular among\nhigh rollers, but the casino caters to those who enjoy a pull now and\nthen.\n',23,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2366,0,0,0,'<g>Kav<c>o<g>d\'s<p> I<g>sla<o>n<g>d Ba<c>r<g> & Gr<p>i<g>ll<1>','  The atmosphere in this small establishment takes you right to the\ntropics.  The walls and ceiling are lined with long rows of kale and\nthe smell of delicious food permeates the air.  Large, full wall\nwindows look out onto the street to the north and the east, and there\nis a large skylight which lets light in from above.  There is some\nfunky caribbean music playing softly from a record player behind the\nbar.\n',10,174585,55,0,0,0,0,-1,100,100,0,'',NULL),
(2367,0,0,0,'Casino Lounge','Luxurious thick <r>red carpet<1> woven with <Y>gold patterns<1>\ncovers the floor.  This room sits at the very top of the GK Highrollers\nCasino and all of the walls and the ceiling are made of glass panels.\nThe panoramic view of Grimhaven is truly amazing.  The <g>Haon-Dor Forest<1>\noccupies most of the area to the north, while the <b>Kranor River<1> can be\nseen snaking its way to the ocean, to the west and south.  This lounge\nprovides a relatively quiet and relaxing atmosphere for casino patrons\nwho want a short break from the hectic casino floor.  A set of ornate\nspiral stairs lead down into the havoc.\n',0,131085,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2368,0,0,0,'Elevator Shaft','  Extremely thick steel columns support each of the four corners of\nthis elevator shaft.  Large glass windows span between the columns,\nsupported by stout steel crossbars.  Through the windows, all of\nGrimhaven can be made out as well as much of the surrounding area.\nThe <g>Haon-Dor Forest<1> occupies most of the area to the north,\nwhile the <b>Kranor River<1> can be seen snaking its way to the\nocean, to the west and south.\n',23,131081,35,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2369,0,0,0,'Elevator Shaft','  Extremely thick steel columns support each of the four corners of\nthis elevator shaft.  Large glass windows span between the columns,\nsupported by stout steel crossbars.  Through the windows, all of\nGrimhaven can be made out as well as much of the surrounding area.\nThe <g>Haon-Dor Forest<1> occupies most of the area to the north,\nwhile the <b>Kranor River<1> can be seen snaking its way to the\nocean, to the west and south.\n',23,131081,35,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2370,0,0,0,'The Casino Elevator','  The walls, ceiling and floor of this elevator are made of large, thick\n<W>glass panes<1>.  An unobstructed view out of the elevator provides astonishing\nviews of the surrounding city of Grimhaven.  Intricate <Y>gold filigree<1> makes\nup the supporting structure and hand rails.\n',23,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2371,0,0,0,'<k>An Enormous Spinning Fan<1>','<k>  This entire room is dominated by an enormous fan, producing a great deal\nof upward lift.\n',23,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2372,0,0,0,'Casino','<1>  This is the infamous GK Highrollers Casino.\n',23,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,178,0,'',NULL),
(2373,0,0,0,'<k>A Dimly Lit Foyer<1>','<k>  Light comes into this room from a dingy window in the door to the\nnorth and the crack under the door.  The wooden floor is dusty and dirty\nand the walls are barren.  A pile of guano in the corner indicates that\nthere may be bats nesting in the rafters overhead, mostly obscured by\ndarkness.<1>\n',2,166076,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2374,0,0,0,'<b>A Darkened Workshop<1>','<w>  Swathes of cloth<o> hang from rafters overhead and <p>spools of thread<o> sit\non shelves and work tables all about this workshop.  A few strategically\nplaced <W>candles<o> provide just enough <y>light<o> to navigate by, but much of the\nroom is left in <k>darkness<o>.  Various implements of tailoring lie about in\npiles, from scissors to needles to measuring tapes and other tools that\nare so obscure as to possibly be arcane in nature.  A single large table\nin the center of the room displays a large pile of bags of various styles,\ncolors, shapes and styles, in no particular organization.<1>\n',2,166076,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2375,0,0,0,'<k>The Knot<1>','<k>  Off in the distance, tiny pinpoints of light can be seen, rifts in\nreality leading to far off lands.  Here in the knot, reality seems confused,\nmoving a small distance feels like a journey of many miles and time shifts\nfrom slow motion to fast motion in an instant.  There even seems to be a\nlack of gravity, as up and down become confused and orientation becomes\narbitrary.<1>\n',217,172364,60,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,31,'',NULL),
