(2700,0,0,0,'Path Near the Outer Pathway','The path widens as it meets the outer pathway and narrows as it disappears\naround a small stand of trees and brush.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2701,0,0,0,'A Small Clearing','There is a small clearing in the scrub brush and trees. Much of the grass is\ntrampled, as if animals or someone slept on the ground.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2702,0,0,0,'A Copse of Small Trees and Scrub Brush','The trees and bushes are thick enough here to hide a person or animal. There is\nan opening to a game trail to the west and you and hear the hustle and bustle of\nthe East Gate Settlement to through some suspicious looking scrub brush to the\nsoutheast.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,2,36,0,'',NULL),
(2703,0,0,0,'Path Through Some Low, Rocky Hills','A path winds around a copse of trees and brush as it traveses the low rocky\nhills. The path continues to the southwest and east, there is a small clearing\nto the southeast and a game path into the brush to the north.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2704,0,0,0,'Path Through Some Low, Rocky Hills','A path winds around a copse of trees and brush as it traveses the low rocky\nhills. The path continues to the north and west.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2705,0,0,0,'A Sleeping Yurt','The yurt is a four foot, domed hut.  Made with sticks, vines and debris from\nthe forest, it provides more than adequate protection from the elements.  As\nlong as someone continuously repairs the roof.  The pygmies are not particular\nwhere they sleep nor do they need anything much more than a blanket in this\ntemperate weather. There is an exit to the northeast.\n',0,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,48,0,'',NULL),
(2706,0,0,0,'A Rocky Tor','The pygmies have haphazardly heaped rocks into a pile that allows them to watch\nover the camp and the surrounding areas from this small hill. You can even see\nthe pastures and outer pathway from this vantage point.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2707,0,0,0,'On the Side of a Rocky Hill','A faint path picks its way up a small rocky hill. To the west is a large pile of\nrocks while the trail continues to the east. The backs of the buildings in the\nEast Gate Settlement can be seen to the south.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2708,0,0,0,'On the Side of a Rocky Hill','A faint path picks its way up a small rocky hill. The path continues to the west\nand ends to the east in a small clearing. The backs of the buildings in the East\nGate Settlement can be seen to the south.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2709,0,0,0,'A Small Clearing','There is a small clearing in the scrub brush and trees. Much of the grass is\ntrampled, as if animals or someone slept on the ground. There is a path up the\nside of a small hill to the west and faint game paths to the northwest and east.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,5,0,0,'',NULL),
(2710,0,0,0,'A Small Game Path','A faint path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. The path ends in a\nclearing to the west and continues to the east.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2711,0,0,0,'A Small Game Path','A faint path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. The path continues the\nthe west and ends in a copse of trees and brush to the south.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2712,0,0,0,'Small Game Path Near a Fence','A faint path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. To the north there is\na fence protecting a cornfield. The path continues to the southwest and\nsoutheast.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,3,0,0,'',NULL),
(2713,0,0,0,'Path Near the Haon-Dor Forest.','The path widens as it merge with a more traveled path on the edge of the\nHaon-Dor forest. It joins the second path to the northwest and continues through\nthe hills to the southeast.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,7,0,0,'',NULL),
(2714,0,0,0,'A Copse of Trees and Brush','The trees and bushes are thick enough here to hide a person or animal. A\nsmall gamepath leaves to the south.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,2,36,0,'',NULL),
(2715,0,0,0,'Camp Entrance','The path is wider and well worn here as it merges with the surrounding camp.\nTo the north and east is a circle around the fire, the fire pit is to the\nnortheast and a path leaves to the south.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2716,0,0,0,'Fire Circle','  Around the firepit is a well worn circle where the pygmies gather for warmth \nand comradery. The circle continues around the fire to the northeast and \nnorthwest with the fire to the north and the camp entrance is to the west.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2717,0,0,0,'Work Area','Between the yurts and the firepit is a small work area where the pymies\nperpare their meals and products.  Larger flat rocks were brought back to the\ncamp\nto use as tables.  There are smaller huts to the northeast and southwest, the\nfire is to the northwest and a small gamepath heads to the east.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2718,0,0,0,'Game Path','A faint game path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. It runs\neast and west.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,3,0,0,'',NULL),
(2719,0,0,0,'Game Path','A faint path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. There is an\nintersection here with pathes running off to the west, northeast and \nsoutheast.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,'',NULL),
(2720,0,0,0,'Sleeping Yurt','The yurt is a four foot, domed hut.  Made with sticks, vines and debris from\nthe forest, it provides more than adequate protection from the elements.  As\nlong as someone continuously repairs the roof.  The pygmies are not particular\nwhere they sleep nor do they need anything much more than a blanket in this\ntemperate weather. There is an exit to the northeast.\n',0,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,48,0,'',NULL),
(2721,0,0,0,'Fire Circle','  Around the firepit is a well worn circle where the pygmies gather for warmth\nand comradery.  The circle continues around the fire to the northeast and\nsouthest with the fire to the east and the camp entrance is to the south.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2722,0,0,0,'Fire Pit','A small stone circle surrounds a fire that smells of burnt grease and herbs.\nThere is a path to the southwest, a large hut to the northeast, work areas to\nthe northwest and southeast and a circular area around the fire.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2723,0,0,0,'Fire Circle','  Around the firepit is a well worn circle where the pygmies gather for warmth\nand comradery.  The circle continues around the fire to the southeast and\nsouthwest with the fire to the west.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2724,0,0,0,'Sleeping Yurt','The yurt is a four foot, domed hut.  Made with sticks, vines and debris from\nthe forest, it provides more than adequate protection from the elements.  As\nlong as someone continuously repairs the roof.  The pygmies are not particular\nwhere they sleep nor do they need anything much more than a blanket in this\ntemperate weather. There is an exit to the southwest.\n',0,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,48,0,'',NULL),
(2725,0,0,0,'A Copse of Small Trees and Scrub Brush','The trees and bushes are thick enough here to hide a person or animal. The\nonlyexit is by a small game path to the north.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,5,36,0,'',NULL),
(2726,0,0,0,'Game Path','A faint path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. The path continues to\nthe north and southwest.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,3,0,0,'',NULL),
(2727,0,0,0,'Work Area','Between the yurts and the fire pit is a small work area where the pygmies\nprepare their meals and wares.  Larger flat rocks were brought back to the camp\nto use as tables.  There are smaller huts to the northeast and southwest, the\nfire is to the southeast and a small game path heads to the northwest.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2728,0,0,0,'Fire Circle','  Around the firepit is a well worn circle where the pygmies gather for warmth\nand comradery.  The circle continues around the fire to the southeast and\nsouthwest with the fire to the south.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2729,0,0,0,'Work Area','Between the yurts and the fire pit is a small work area where the pygmies\nprepare their meals and wares.  Larger flat rocks were brought back to the camp\nto use as tables.  There is a large hut to the northeast that looks like it has\nbeen expanded several times and the fire is to the southwest.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,6,0,0,'',NULL),
(2730,0,0,0,'Storage Yurt Addition','This small pen was sloppily added to the main storage yurt. It looks and smells\nlike its main purpose in life is storing animals for slaughter. The is an exit\nto the north through a gate.\n',0,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,3,36,0,'',NULL),
(2731,0,0,0,'Game Path','A faint path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. The path continues to\neast and end in a copse of trees and scrub brush to the south.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,3,0,0,'',NULL),
(2732,0,0,0,'Game Path','A faint path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. Pathes continue to the\nnorth, south and west.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,'',NULL),
(2733,0,0,0,'Path through Some Low, Rocky Hills','A path traverses the low rocky hills. The path continues to the southeast and\nnorth and a small path winds up the side of a hill to the east.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,5,0,0,'',NULL),
(2734,0,0,0,'On the Side of a Rocky Hill','A faint path picks its way up a small rocky hill. The path exits to the w and\ncontinues to the north.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'',NULL),
(2735,0,0,0,'Sleeping Yurt','The yurt is a four foot, domed hut.  Made with sticks, vines and debris from\nthe forest, it provides more than adequate protection from the elements.  As\nlong as someone continuously repairs the roof.  The pygmies are not particular\nwhere they sleep nor do they need anything much more than a blanket in this\ntemperate weather. There is an exit to the southeast.\n',0,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,48,0,'',NULL),
(2736,0,0,0,'Storage Yurt Addition','This small pen was sloppily added to the main storage yurt. It looks and smells\nlike its main purpose in life is storing animals for slaughter. The is an exit\nto the east through a gate.\n',0,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,48,0,'',NULL),
(2737,0,0,0,'Storage Yurt','This yurt is a lot larger then the others, but it is not much taller. It is also\nthe driest and most secure of any of the yurts. The pygmies use this for storage\nof all of their trading supplies. From the look of things, the pygmies\' fortunes\nhave been pretty thin as of late. There are additions to the build to teh north,\nsouth east and west and the exit is to the southwest.\n',0,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,48,0,'',NULL),
(2738,0,0,0,'Storage Yurt Addition','This small pen was sloppily added to the main storage yurt. It looks and smells\nlike its main purpose in life is storing animals for slaughter. The is an exit\nto the west through a gate.\n',0,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,3,36,0,'',NULL),
(2739,0,0,0,'Game Path','A faint path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. The path continues to\nthe south and northwest.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,'',NULL),
(2740,0,0,0,'Path through Some Low, Rocky Hills','A path traverses the low rocky hills. The path continues to the north and south\nand a small game path breaks off to the northeast.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'',NULL),
(2741,0,0,0,'On the Side of a Rocky Hill','A faint path picks its way up a small rocky hill. The path ends at a large pile\nof rocks to the east and continues down the hill to the south.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'',NULL),
(2742,0,0,0,'Rocky Tor','The pygmies have haphazardly heaped rocks into a pile that allows them to watch\nover the camp and the surrounding areas from this small hill. You can even see\nthe pastures and the Haon-Dor Forest from this vantage point. There is a path\ndown to the west.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'',NULL),
(2743,0,0,0,'Game Path','A faint path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. There is a hole\nentering a copse f trees to the north and the trail continues to the northwest\nand northeast.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,-1,4,0,0,'',NULL),
(2744,0,0,0,'Storage Yurt Addition','This small pen was sloppily added to the main storage yurt. It looks and smells\nlike its main purpose in life is storing animals for slaughter. The is an exit\nto the south through a gate.\n',0,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,5,36,0,'',NULL),
(2745,0,0,0,'Game Path','A faint path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. The path continues to\nthe northwest and southeast.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,3,0,0,'',NULL),
(2746,0,0,0,'Path through Some Low, Rocky Hills','A path traverses the low rocky hills. The path continues to the northwest and\nsouth. A small game path exits to the east.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,5,0,0,'',NULL),
(2747,0,0,0,'Game Path Near a Field of Corn.','A faint path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. To the northeast a\nfield of corn who\'s fence has seen better days. There is a dug out area at the\nbase that makes it look like someone is sneaking through on a fairly regular\nbasis. Pathes exit to the east, west and soutwest.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,'',NULL),
(2748,0,0,0,'Game Path Near a Field of Corn.','A faint path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. A fence to the north\nprotects a field of corn. The path contiues to the west and southeast.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,-1,3,0,0,'',NULL),
(2749,0,0,0,'A Copse of Small Trees and Scrub Brush','The trees and bushes are thick enough here to hide a person or animal. There is\na corn field barely visible through the brush and fence to the north. The single\nexit is though a small game path to the south.\n',0,0,24,0,0,0,0,-1,3,36,0,'',NULL),
(2750,0,0,0,'Beneath The Watchtower','  You\'re in an open area beneath a town watchtower.  There are some stairs up\nhere.  There\'s a small dirt path to the north and Pearl Alley is to the east.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2751,0,0,0,'Pearl Alley','  This is a dark alley that runs between the southern town wall and the\nwall of the Grand Hotel.  There\'s a small door to the north.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2752,0,0,0,'Pearl Alley','  Pearl Alley is a narrow, dark road that runs east and west between the\nsouthern town wall and the side of the Grand Hotel.  To the east is the\nbrightly lit Pearl Street.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2753,0,0,0,'Pearl Avenue','  The intersection of Pearl Avenue and Hill Street.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2754,0,0,0,'Pearl Avenue','  This is a very nice street.  The town wall is to the south.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2755,0,0,0,'Pearl Avenue','  This is a very nice-looking street.  The town wall is to the south.\n',24,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2756,0,0,0,'Seaward Street','  This is the intersection of Seaward Street and Pearl Avenue.  A guard\nhouse stands on the east side of the road.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2757,0,0,0,'Town of Amber Guardhouse','  This looks like a typical guardhouse.  Tables and chairs are here and there.\nLooks like some pinups might be hanging on the back wall.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2758,0,0,0,'Dirt Trail','  This is a small dirt trail running north and south by the town wall.\n',24,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2759,0,0,0,'Kitchen','  A large and well-stocked kitchen.  Doors lead north, east and south.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2760,0,0,0,'Grand Dining Room','  This is a richly decorated dining room.  The finest brocade tablecloths,\ngleaming silverware, and the finest china.  There is a swinging door\nleading west from here.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2761,0,0,0,'Hill Street','  This street is bordered by the colorful lights of the Grand Hotel to\nthe west.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2762,0,0,0,'Bank Vault','  You are in a very secure bank vault.  The door is east.\n',24,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2763,0,0,0,'First Bank of Amber','  A bank with a long counter of teller windows is here.  Doors lead out\nto the east and south.  The vault is west of here.\n',24,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2764,0,0,0,'Seaward Street','  A broad street in the town of Amber.  The bank is west and the jail\nis east of here.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2765,0,0,0,'Town of Amber Jail','  It\'s a small jail.  There\'s a desk up front; the cages are in the back.\n',24,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2766,0,0,0,'Dirt Trail','  This is a small dirt trail running north and south by the town wall.\n',24,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2767,0,0,0,'The Stage','  This is a small stage in the Grand Nightclub.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2768,0,0,0,'The Grand Nightclub','  The lighting is dim but you can see that this is a fine nightclub that\nprobably offers up some good entertainment.  In fact, there are some foxy\nbabesdancing on stage now.  There is a placard here, on an easel by the\ndoor.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2769,0,0,0,'The Grand Lobby','  You\'re in the lobby of the Grand Hotel and you\'ve never seen such a\nlavishly decorated room.  Gold curtains hang upon marble columns, large oil\npaintings adorn the walls, the carpet is deep burgundy in color and very\nplush.  There is a stair here going up.  The Grand Nightclub is west; the\nGrand Dining Room is south.\n',24,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2770,0,0,0,'Hill Street','  This street is bordered by the colorful lights of the Grand Hotel to\nthe west.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2771,0,0,0,'The Altar of the Unicorn','  You\'re at the front of the Church.  There\'s an altar here.  Tapestries hang\nhigh on the walls.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2772,0,0,0,'Church of the Unicorn','  You\'re in a small chapel, very lavishly decorated with tapestries\ndepicting various members of the royal family.  There are some pews here.\nThe altar is west.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2773,0,0,0,'Seaward Street','  This is a street in Amber.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2774,0,0,0,'Park Playground','  OOOHH!  This is a really neat children\'s playground.  There\'s a\nslide, some swings, and some monkey bars here.  The park fence is to the west\nand the town wall is east.\n',24,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2775,0,0,0,'Outside the West Gate of Amber','  You are standing in a small clearing.  To the west you see a trail leading\nout into a vast tundra.  To the east you see the entrance to a large town.\n',24,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2776,0,0,0,'Inside West Gate of Amber','  A round, cobblestoned area just inside the western gate of Amber.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2777,0,0,0,'Shell Avenue','  This is a town street running east and west.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2778,0,0,0,'Shell Avenue','  This is a town street running east and west.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2779,0,0,0,'Oberon Center','  This is a somewhat somber square in the town honoring Oberon.   There is a\nstatue here.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2780,0,0,0,'Shell Avenue','  This is a town street running east and west.  There is a small hut\nnorth of here.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2781,0,0,0,'Shell Avenue','  A town street running east and west.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2782,0,0,0,'Deirdre Square','  You are in a festive square in the town of Amber.  Music fills the air\nfrom the nearby Cafe.  To the east is the town park.  There is a statue\nhere of Deirdre, Princess of Amber.  A door leads east into a park.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2783,0,0,0,'A Path through the Park','  This is a pretty little walking path through the park.  A door leads\nwest out of the park and a gate leads east down a path.\n',24,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2784,0,0,0,'Small, Paved Path','  A small, paved path that runs east and west.\n',24,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2785,0,0,0,'Dirt Track By The Wall','  This is a rough trail that crewmen use for making repairs to the town\nwall.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2786,0,0,0,'Main Room','  You are in the main entertainment room of Fiddler\'s Green.  There are a\nvariety of diversions available here.  A door leads eastward.\n',24,131085,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2787,0,0,0,'Fiddler\'s Green','  You are in the front hall of a private club called Fiddler\'s Green.\nA door leads south out of the club, or west further in.\n',24,131085,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2788,0,0,0,'Hill Street','  A town street in decent repair running north and south.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2789,0,0,0,'Tourist Information','  This looks like a good place to learn about Amber.  There are signs on\nall the walls.  A door leads back south.\n',24,131085,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2790,0,0,0,'Hard Rock Cafe Amber','  Wow! This is a way cool restaurant!\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2791,0,0,0,'Seaward Street','  The smell of the ocean is detectable here.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2792,0,0,0,'Park','  There are lots of trees here.  It looks like a nice place for a picnic.\nThe park fence is to the west and the town wall is east.\n',24,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2793,0,0,0,'Dirt Track By The Wall','  This is a rough trail that crewmen use in making repairs to the wall.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2794,0,0,0,'Main Room','  You are in the main entertainment area of Fiddler\'s Green.  There are a\nvariety of diversions available here.  There is a spiral staircase here.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2795,0,0,0,'Sleazy Tattoo Parlor','  You\'re in a sleazy tattoo parlor.  There\'s sleazy artwork on all the walls.\nThere\'s a sleazy counter here.\n',24,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2796,0,0,0,'Hill Street','  A town street running north and south.  You see the wall of some building\nto the east.  To the west is a tattoo parlor.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2797,0,0,0,'Bloody Eddie\'s','  This place is reputed to serve the best seafood in the universe but from\nthe looks of this dump, that\'s hard to believe.  There\'s sawdust on the\nfloor, holes in the tablecloths, and rips in the wallpaper.  There\'s a\nblackboard hanging on the wall over the cash drawer.\n',24,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2798,0,0,0,'Bloody Eddie\'s Bar','  There\'s a long bar here with stools.  A few more tables and chairs are\nscattered about.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2799,0,0,0,'Seaward Street','  The smell of the ocean is very strong here.  There\'s a window in the wall\nto the west and a warehouse of some sort to the east from which you hear the\nsounds of various metals being thrown into bins.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2800,0,0,0,'Bayle\'s Warehouse','  This is a big warehouse.  There\'s sawdust on the floor.  Bottles of wine\nare securely locked into rows and rows of wine racks.  You hear commercial\ntype noises coming from the east.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2801,0,0,0,'Bayle\'s Commodity Exchange','  A pretty fancy name for a back room business.  The exchange is run by\nthe father-in-law of Bayle\'s bastard son\'s second cousin\'s third mistress\nbut like all businesses in Amber belongs to the family.  This particular\nexchange is dedicated only to the buying and selling of metals and other\nprecious treasures.  You can ask the clerk for an estimate but make sure to\ncheck for his finger on the scale.\n',24,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2802,0,0,0,'Dworkin Circle','  This is a quiet square in the town of Amber honoring Dworkin.  There is a\nstatue here.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2803,0,0,0,'Fishmonger\'s Road','  This is a rather rundown road running east and west.  The smell of fish,\nbooze, and blood is almost overpowering.  A wood framed office building\nstands to the north.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2804,0,0,0,'Fishmonger\'s Road','  This is a rather rundown road running east and west along the seawall.\nThe smell of fish, booze, and blood is almost overpowering.  A sleazy shop\nlies south of here.\n',24,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2805,0,0,0,'Minion Mall','  This is a boisterous little square honoring Minion (a.k.a.  Death\'s Head II).\nThere is a statue here.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2806,0,0,0,'Fishmonger\'s Road','  This is a really seedy part of town but the restaurant to the south is\nsupposedly worth the trip.  The seawall is to the north.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2807,0,0,0,'Fishmonger\'s Road','  This is a really bad part of town.  The docks are north a window looking\ninto Bloody Eddie\'s is south, but there is no door here.\n',24,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2808,0,0,0,'Eric Court','  This is a grimey little square honoring Eric.  The docks are north.\nFishmonger\'s Road is west.  Seaward Street is south.  There is a statue here.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2809,0,0,0,'Bayle\'s Warehouse','  Actually, it\'s a huge warehouse.  Are the Bayles selling any wine?  There\nare more locked racks of wine bottles here.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2810,0,0,0,'Amber Shipping Office','  This building houses the main office of Cobra Shipping Ltd.,\nthe largest organized shipping firm in all the realms.  The shipping\noffice is in a state of constant turmoil, with people coming and\ngoing at all hours of the day or night, both to drop off things for\nshipment to another city or to pick up merchandise which arrived on\nthe latest caravan.  The room itself is tastefully done in light\nwood paneling, with a hard stone floor.  A large counter in the\ncenter of the room serves as a drop off and pick up point for\nmerchandise.\n',24,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2811,0,0,0,'Armorer','A nondescript armor shop.  The items for sale are displayed all about you.\n',24,164025,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2812,0,0,0,'Flood Street','  This muddy path runs north along the harbor.  Occasional ocean waves\nbreak over the seawall east of here keeping the ground moist.  A shop\nis to the west.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2813,0,0,0,'Docks','  Part of the docks of Amber.  There is a gangplank north of here.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2814,0,0,0,'Docks','  Part of the docks of Amber.  A ship is in.\n',24,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2815,0,0,0,'Weaponer','  A nondescript weapon shop.  The items for sale are displayed all about\nyou.\n',24,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2816,0,0,0,'Flood Street','  This muddy path runs north along the harbor.  Occasional ocean waves\nbreak over the seawall east of here keeping the ground moist.  A shop\nis to the west.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2817,0,0,0,'Gangplank','  You find yourself moving gently up and down on a perfectly ordinary\ngangplank.  Suddenly you notice the ship is flying pirate colors.  This\nmight not be such a good idea after all.\n',24,131076,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2818,0,0,0,'Repair Shop','  A forge and blacksmithery surrounds you.\n',24,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2819,0,0,0,'Flood Street','  This muddy path runs north along the harbor.  Occasional ocean waves\nbreak over the seawall east of here keeping the ground moist.  A shop\nis to the west.\n',24,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2820,0,0,0,'Bow','  You are on deck of a sea-going warship.\n',24,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2821,0,0,0,'Amidships','  You\'re on deck of a sea-going warship.  There is a hatch leading down.\n',24,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2822,0,0,0,'Stern','  You on on deck of a sea-going warship.\n',24,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(2823,0,0,0,'Brig','  This is the Brig.  It\'s not a good place to be.\n',24,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2824,0,0,0,'Below Deck','  You are below deck on a sea-going warship.  The captain\'s quarters\nlie east from here, and the brig is west.  Fresh sea air can be smelt\nfrom the hatch leading up out of the hold.\n',24,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2825,0,0,0,'Captain\'s Quarters','  This looks like a bedroom for a seafaring man.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2826,0,0,0,'Cult of the Logrus','  Brrr!  This is a creepy place.  It seems to be some sort of secret\ntemple.  There\'s an elaborate mosaic of a dragon on the wall.  There\'s a\nstone altar with reddish-brown stains on it.\n',24,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2827,0,0,0,'Town Vault','  It looks like a big hole in the ground.  You wonder if there might be\nburied treasure here...\n',24,131208,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2828,0,0,0,'Inside The Watchtower','  Unexpectedly, this room looks more like an office than a watch station.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2829,0,0,0,'The Prince\'s Suite','  You are in a lavish guest room in the Grand Hotel.  A door lies north.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2830,0,0,0,'The Princess Suite','  You are in a lavish guest room in the Grand Hotel.  A door lies east.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2831,0,0,0,'Second Floor','  You\'re on the second floor of the Grand Hotel.  Doors lead north, east,\nsouth and west into suites.  A sturdy door leads northeast marked \"Manager\".\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2832,0,0,0,'The Queen\'s Suite','  You are in a lavish guest room in the Grand Hotel.  A door lies west.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2833,0,0,0,'The King\'s Suite','  You are in a lavish guest room in the Grand Hotel.  A door lies south.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2834,0,0,0,'The Manager\'s Office','  You are in the office of the hotel manager.  A door leads southwest.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2835,0,0,0,'Lounge','  You are upstairs in Fiddler\'s Green.  The furnishings are plush.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2836,0,0,0,'Lounge','  You are upstairs in Fiddler\'s Green.  The furnishings are plush.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2837,0,0,0,'Lounge','  You are upstairs in Fiddler\'s Green.  The furnishings are plush.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2838,0,0,0,'Lounge','  You are upstairs in Fiddler\'s Green.  The furnishings are plush.\n',24,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2850,35,75,-3,'Nook','  This small, cheerful area is probably where the servants eat and where\nmembers of the royal family sneak midnight snacks.  A door leads west into\na garden.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2851,36,75,-3,'Kitchen','  This appears to be where the dishes and stuff are cleaned.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2852,37,75,-3,'Kitchen','  This appears to be the main area where food is prepared.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2853,38,75,-3,'The Grand Stair','  You are standing on a broad, ornate staircase that goes up to the second\nfloor.\n',24,139277,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2854,39,75,-3,'Guest Bedroom','  You are in a comfortable bedroom for guests of the castle.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2855,40,75,-3,'Armory','  You are in the castle armory.  New and antique weapons are probably\nstored here.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2856,41,75,-3,'Armory','  You are in the castle armory.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2857,35,74,-3,'Spiral Staircase','  You are in a small room containing a spiral staircase.  It must be the\nstair that the servants use.  Doors lie south and east.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2858,36,74,-3,'Servants\' Quarters','  There is room here for many bunks, with screens to partition the area a\nbit and provide some privacy.  There is a door west.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2859,37,74,-3,'Kitchen','  This appears to be the part of the kitchen where the finishing touches are\nmake to the food and it is placed on trays for serving.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2860,38,74,-3,'Main Hall','  The floor here is dark flagstone and the walls are white marble streaked\nwith bluish gray.  There are vibrant tapestries firmly affixed to the walls\nhere.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2861,39,74,-3,'Guest Room','  You are in a comfortable sitting room for guests of the castle.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2862,40,74,-3,'Guard Room','  You are in a large guard room in front of the Armory.  A door leads\nsouth from here.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2863,41,74,-3,'Atrium','  You are in the odd court.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2864,35,73,-3,'Corridor','  You are in a corridor near the servants\' quarters.  Doors lead\nnorth and south.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2865,36,73,-3,'Corridor','  You are in a corridor near the kitchen and the servants\' quarters.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2866,37,73,-3,'Corridor','  You are in a short corridor near the kitchen.  A door leads south.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2867,38,73,-3,'Main Hall','  The floor here is dark flagstone and the walls are white marble streaked\nwith bluish gray.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2868,39,73,-3,'Hallway','  You are in a small hallway.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2869,40,73,-3,'Hallway','  You are in a hallway.  A door lies in the north wall.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2870,41,73,-3,'Atrium','  You are in a courtyard that is open to the outside but somehow protected\nfrom the weather.  The view out the east wall is stunning, looking straight\noff the slope of Kolvir.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2871,35,72,-3,'Bar','  You are near a small, well-stocked wet bar.  Doors go north and south.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2872,36,72,-3,'The Northwest Corner of the Great Hall','  The Great Hall measures approximately 50 feet wide by 90 feet long.  Its\nbeamed and plastered ceiling is almost 40 feet above the floor.  Royal\nweddings, coronations, and funerals occur here.  On the south wall,\ndoorways lead to sitting rooms, while on the north wall two doors lead to a\ncorridor near the kitchen.  A bar stands in the corner west of here.  There\nis a statue of the Unicorn here.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2873,37,72,-3,'The Northeast Corner of the Great Hall','  The Great Hall measures approximately 50 feet wide by 90 feet long.  Its\nbeamed and plastered ceiling is almost 40 feet above the floor.  Royal\nweddings, coronations, and funerals occur here.  On the south wall,\ndoorways lead to sitting rooms, while on the north wall two doors lead to a\ncorridor near the kitchen.  A bar stands in the northwest corner.  Light\ncomes through beveled windows from 25 feet up the west wall.  The effect is\nalmost prismatic and the Hall takes on a beautiful, hypnotic shimmer.  The\n<g>deep green vein<z> in the <W>white marble walls<z> seems to slither its way from the\nceiling to the floor.  Under a bright moon, the vein is predominant.  The\nGreat Hall at night is eerie.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2874,38,72,-3,'Main Hall','  The floor here is dark flagstone and the walls are white marble streaked\nwith bluish gray.  There are weapons and shields hanging high on the walls.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2875,39,72,-3,'Reading Room','  This is a small, comfortable room that looks like a good place to read a\nbook.  There is a fireplace against the west wall.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2876,40,72,-3,'Lounge','  If you didn\'t know better, you wouldn\'t know you were in a huge castle.\nThis cozy room has warm wood paneling and a low, textured ceiling.  There\'s\na friendly circular fireplace set into the floor at the room\'s center.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2877,41,72,-3,'Atrium','  You are in the strange court.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2878,35,71,-3,'Hallway','  This is a short hallway going north and south.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2879,36,71,-3,'The West Side of the Great Hall','  Immediately above you is the musicians\' loft.  Above that are the beveled\nwindows.  There are shields of the Golden Circle Kingdoms securely affixed to\nthe wall here.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2880,37,71,-3,'The East Side of the Great Hall','  The Great Hall measures approximately 50 feet wide by 90 feet long.  Its\nbeamed and plastered ceiling is almost 40 feet above the floor.  Royal\nweddings, coronations, and funerals occur here.  On the south wall,\ndoorways lead to sitting rooms, while on the north wall two doors lead to\na corridor near the kitchen.  A bar stands in the northwest corner.  Light\ncomes through beveled windows from 25 feet up the west wall.  The effect is\nalmost prismatic and the Hall takes on a beautiful, hypnotic shimmer.  The\n<g>deep green vein<z> in the <W>white marble walls<z> seems to slither its way from the\nceiling to the floor.  Under a bright moon, the vein is predominant.  The\nGreat Hall at night is eerie.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2881,38,71,-3,'Main Hall','  The floor here is of dark flagstone and the walls are white marble\nstreaked with bluish gray.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2882,39,71,-3,'Small Library','  This is a small library, presumably for the use of family and friends.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2883,40,71,-3,'Billiards Room','  How can you play pool on this table?  It has no pockets!\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2884,41,71,-3,'Small Bar','  You are near a small, well-stocked wet bar.  There is a sign here.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2885,35,70,-3,'Throne Storage Room','  This is a small, plain storage room where the Throne of Amber is stored\nwhen it is not needed in the Great Hall for official occasions.  A door\nstands on the south wall.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2886,36,70,-3,'Southwest Corner of the Great Hall','  Immediately above you is the musicians\' loft.  Above that are the windows.\nThere are shields from the Golden Circle Kingdoms securely affixed to the\nwall here.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2887,37,70,-3,'The Southeast Corner of the Great Hall','  The Great Hall measures approximately 50 feet wide by 90 feet long.  Its\nbeamed and plastered ceiling is almost 40 feet above the floor.  Royal\nweddings, coronations, and funerals occur here.  On the south wall,\ndoorways lead to sitting rooms, while on the north wall two doors lead to a\ncorridor near the kitchen.  A bar stands in the northwest corner.  Light\ncomes through beveled windows from 25 feet up the west wall.  The effect is\nalmost prismatic and the Hall takes on a beautiful, hypnotic shimmer.  The\n<g>deep green vein<z> in the <W>white marble walls<z> seems to slither its way from the\nceiling to the floor.  Under a bright moon, the vein is predominant.  The\nGreat Hall at night is eerie.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2888,38,70,-3,'Main Hall','  The floor here is dark flagstone and the walls are white marble streaked\nwith bluish gray.  False arches and columns nearly hide the high, beamed\nceiling.  There are large, colorful tapestries firmly affixed to the walls\nhere.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2889,39,70,-3,'Hallway','  You are in a hallway.  There is a door on the south wall.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2890,40,70,-3,'Hallway','  You are in a hallway.  A door is in the north wall.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2891,41,70,-3,'Treasury','  This looks like the kind of place where money, records, and valuables\nmight be stored.  An iron door lies on the south wall.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2892,35,69,-3,'The Great Stair','  You are on a huge stone spiral stair.  It appears to have been carved\nfrom the solid rock of Mount Kolvir.  A door leads north.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2893,36,69,-3,'Sitting Room','  This is a small, comfortable room where small groups can visit.\nA door leads north.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2894,37,69,-3,'Sitting Room','  This is a small, comfortable room where small groups can visit.\nA door leads north.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2895,38,69,-3,'Main Hall','  The floor here is dark flagstone and the walls are white marble streaked\nwith bluish gray.  A door leads south into a courtyard.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2896,39,69,-3,'<Y>The Yellow Room<z>','  This is a small sitting room where the King of Amber conducts official\nbusiness.  The floors and walls are constructed of a <Y>yellowish stone.<z>\nDoors lead north and east.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2897,40,69,-3,'Guard Room','  This looks like a room used by guards.  Doors lead east and west.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2898,41,69,-3,'Counting Room','  This appears to be a room where money could be counted.  Doors lead\nnorth and west.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2900,35,75,-2,'Bleys\' Bedroom','  Bleys\' bedroom is sparse and untidy.  There are various unidentified\nmagical items about.  His books are mostly arcane and linguistically\nimpenetrable.  There is a door on the east wall.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2901,36,75,-2,'Bleys\' Sitting Room','  Bleys\' rooms are very untidy.  His bookshelves are lined with books on\nall sorts of magics, chess, military history, heraldry, weapons design, and\nship construction.  Doors lead east and west.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2902,37,75,-2,'Hall','  The floor here is of light-gray marble with bluish-gray streaks.\nA door goes west.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2903,38,75,-2,'The Grand Stair - 2nd Floor','  You are on a broad and ornate stair leading up and down.\n',24,139277,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2904,39,75,-2,'Hall','  The floor here is of light-gray marble with bluish-gray streaks.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2905,40,75,-2,'Hall','  The floor here is of light-gray marble with bluish-gray streaks.  There\nare doors in the south and east wall.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2906,41,75,-2,'Bathroom','  This bathroom has an <g>emerald-green floor<z> and <g>jade-green walls.<z>  The\ntoilet and tub appear to be carved from <W>solid white marble<z>.  There is\na\ndoor in the west wall.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2907,35,74,-2,'Caine\'s Bedroom','  The bedroom maintains the nautical motif.  A door goes east.\n',24,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2908,36,74,-2,'Caine\'s Living Room','  Although not as motif-oriented as some, Caine\'s apartments clearly reflect\nhis interests in naval and military matters.  Doors go east and west.\n',24,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2909,37,74,-2,'Hall','  The floor here is of light-gray marble with bluish gray streaks.  A\ndoor goes west.\n',24,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2910,38,74,-2,'Hall','  The floor is a light-gray marble with bluish gray streaks.  There is\na door south from here.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2911,39,74,-2,'Hall','  The floor here is of light-gray marble with bluish-gray streaks.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2912,40,74,-2,'Merlin\'s Sitting Room','  Merlin\'s room reflects his esoteric tastes.  A large, colorful Oriental\nrug depicting a hunting scene covers the floor.  Its line of trees\noverwhelms the entire room.  The furniture is simple, perhaps to counter\nthe rug\'s dominance.  Doors lead north and south.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2913,41,74,-2,'Hall','  The floor here is of light-gray marble with bluish-gray streaks.  There\nis a door heading south and the way back through the secret toilet lies\nnorth from here.\n',24,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2914,35,73,-1,'Eric\'s Bath','  This is a neat and functional room.\n',24,139277,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2915,36,73,-1,'Julian\'s Bath','  The hunter\'s motif is extended to the bath.  There\'s a huge sunken tub\nhere with a small waterfall.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2916,37,73,-2,'Benedict\'s Back Room','  Benedict has converted this room into a combination bedroom and Japanese\ngarden bath.  A door leads east.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2917,38,73,-2,'Benedict\'s Front Room','  Benedict has imported all his furnishings from one specific shadow,\npre-nineteenth century Japan of Shadow Earth.  On entering this room,\nvisitors are expected to remove their shoes.  Doors go north and west.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2918,39,73,-2,'Hall','  The floor here is of light-gray marble with bluish-gray streaks.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2919,40,73,-2,'Merlin\'s Bedroom','  This bedroom is neat and simple.  There is a Macintosh computer on the\narmoire but computers tend to malfunction in Amber.  A door goes north.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2920,41,73,-2,'Brand\'s Sitting Room','  Eclectic and tasteless, Brand\'s room reflects the man\'s volatile\ntemperament.  A door is in the north wall.\n',24,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2921,35,72,-1,'Eric\'s Room','  Eric\'s room is decorated in no particular style but it is, for the most\npart, neat and accessible.  A door goes south.\n',24,139277,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2922,36,72,-1,'Julian\'s Room','  This room has rugs and furniture made from various animal skins.  A door\nexits south.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2923,37,72,-2,'Gerard\'s Room','  Unlike all his siblings, Gerard preferred to eliminate the interior walls\nin his apartment in favor of one large, uninterrupted living space.  His\nbed is in this portion of the room.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2924,38,72,-2,'Gerard\'s Room','  Gerard\'s room reflects his physical orientation.  A huge dragon\'s head\nhangs stuffed and mounted on the far wall.  Gerard is less than tidy and\nthere are many items scattered about.  A door leaves east.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2925,39,72,-2,'Hall','  The floor here is of light-gray marble with bluish-gray streaks.  There\nis a door heading west.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2926,40,72,-2,'Hall','  The floor here is of light-gray marble with bluish-gray streaks.  A door\nheads south.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2927,41,72,-2,'Brand\'s Bedroom','  The bed is unmade and the remains of the last meal he ate here before his\ndeath still rest in dishes on the floor.  Chains have been embedded in the\nwall in one corner and there is a small pile of ashes near them.  Several\npapers - essays on magic and the Pattern - lie scattered on the desk.  Old\nand brittle, they are as useless as the vials and jars of unidentified\nsubstances that are pushed to the back.\n',24,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2928,40,72,-2,'Hall','  There is a spiral staircase here.  A door is on the north wall.\n',24,139277,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2929,41,72,-2,'Dining Hall','  You are in a small dining hall, probably used by the family when they\ndon\'t take their meals in their rooms.  A door is on the north wall.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2930,37,71,-1,'Hall','  The floor here is of light-gray marble with bluish-gray streaks.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2931,38,71,-1,'Hall','  The floor here is of light-gray marble with bluish-gray streaks.  A door\nexits south.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2932,39,71,-1,'Hall','  The floor here is of light-gray marble with bluish-gray streaks.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2933,40,71,-2,'Corwin\'s Room','  Corwin\'s decorating tastes appear to run to the functional and austere.\nDoors go north and east.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2934,41,71,-2,'Corwin\'s Bath','  Corwin apparently likes a good soak.  There\'s a huge sunken tub here with\nJacuzzi jets.  There is a panel to the south and a door goes west.\n',24,139273,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2935,40,71,-2,'Library','  You are in the library.  This one is much larger than the one downstairs.\nThere are books all over the place!\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2936,41,71,-2,'Library','  You are in the library.  This one is much larger than the one downstairs.\nThere are books all over the place!\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2937,37,70,-1,'Fiona\'s Bedroom','  The Scandinavian designs emphasize simplicity and sparseness, which Fiona\nturned to very good advantage here.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2938,38,70,-1,'Fiona\'s Sitting Room','  This room is tastefully decorated in the style called contemporary\nScandinavian on Shadow Earth.  A door goes north.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2939,39,70,-1,'Hall','  The floor here is of light-gray marble with bluish-gray streaks.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2940,40,70,-2,'Small Staircase','  You are on a small spiral staircase that goes up.\n',24,139404,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2941,41,70,-2,'Hall','  The floor is black marble here.  A door is on the south wall and\na panel bars the way north.\n',24,139273,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2942,40,70,-2,'Library','  You are in the library.  This one is much larger than the one downstairs.\nThere are books all over the place!\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2943,41,70,-2,'Library','  You are in the library.  This one is much larger than the one downstairs.\nThere are books all over the place!\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2944,37,69,-1,'Fiona\'s Bath','  The room features sleek, flowing fixtures which blend functionality and\nsimple elegance.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2945,38,69,-1,'Bathroom','  You are in a bathroom decorated in black and silver.  It\'s very striking.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2946,39,69,-1,'Hall','  The floor here is of light-gray marble with bluish-gray streaks.  There\nare doors on the east and west walls.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2947,40,69,-1,'Deirdre\'s Sitting Room','  The sitting room is decorated in an elegant, modern Manhattan-style.\nThe chairs are genuine Frank Lloyd Wright designs.  A door goes west.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2948,41,69,-1,'Deirdre\'s Bedroom','  The bedroom is tasteful, modern, and expensive.  The bed is made and the\nroom is immaculate.  A door exits north.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2950,35,75,-1,'Racquetball Court','  This area looks just like a racquetball court.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2951,36,75,-1,'Weight Room','  If anyone lifts these weights, they must be superhuman.  A doorway\nleads west and the fireplace on the east wall looks large enough to\ncrawl into.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2952,37,75,-1,'Behind the Fireplace','  A dark, unfurnished room.\n',24,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2953,38,75,-1,'The Grand Stair - 3rd Floor','  You are on a broad and ornate staircase that goes down.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2954,39,75,-1,'Vialle\'s Studio','  You are in an artist\'s studio.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2955,40,75,-1,'Vialle\'s Studio','  You are in an artist\'s studio.  A door goes south.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2956,41,75,-1,'Vialle\'s Studio','  You are in an artist\'s studio.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2957,35,74,-1,'Steam Room','  There\'s steam all over! And it\'s hot in here.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2958,36,74,-1,'Fencing Room','  This room is used as a training room.  Apparently, some sword fighting\ngoes on here.  The room continues to the north.  A door goes west.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2959,37,74,-1,'Hall','  The floor here is bluish-gray marble with black streaks.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2960,38,74,-1,'Hall','  The floor here is bluish-gray marble with black streaks.  A door goes\nsouth.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2961,39,74,-1,'Hall','  The floor here is bluish-gray marble with black streaks.  The entrance to\nthe King\'s Quarters are to the east.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2962,40,74,-1,'The King\'s Entry','  The entryway to the King\'s office.  Do you have an appointment?  A door\nleads north.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2963,41,74,-1,'King\'s Waiting Room','  You are waiting in the King\'s waiting room.  It\'s very comfortable here.\nA door goes south.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2964,35,73,0,'Flora\'s Bath','  One of the most outlandish baths you\'ve ever seen, it carries the\nFrench-style decor into its historically weakest area.  Little, cute\nstatues spout water into a large, shell-shaped tub.  The fixtures are gold\non the sink, toilet, and...  what\'s that thing?  Oh, a bidet.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2965,36,73,0,'Flora\'s Bedroom','  The bedroom also features furnishings from the Napoleonic period.  A\n<R>bright red canopied bed<z> occupies most of the room.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2966,37,73,-1,'Martin\'s Bedroom','  Martin\'s bedroom is as devoid of personal artifacts as the front room.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2967,38,73,-1,'Martin\'s Room','  Martin\'s room looks like any guest room.  He must not be in Amber much.\nA door goes north from here.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2968,39,73,-1,'Hall','  The floor here is bluish-gray marble with black streaks.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2969,40,73,-1,'Conservatory','  This was once a part of the office but Random has had it walled off to\nprovide him a place to practice his drums.  South and east lie doors.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2970,41,73,-1,'The King\'s Office','  This is the official offices of the King of Amber and it contains all the\nlavish trappings of a powerful liege.  The room also has powerful spells\nplaced on it to prevent the King from being influenced by magic.  Doors go\nnorth and west.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2971,35,72,0,'Lab','  This looks like the family laboratory.  However, there are also a number\nof medical supplies about.  It appears that this room served as a hospital\nas well.  A door is in the south wall.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2972,36,72,0,'Flora\'s Sitting Room','  Flora\'s furnishings are French, from the Napoleonic era.  There is a\nlarge oil painting on the wall.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2973,37,72,-1,'Llewella\'s Bedroom','  The bedroom continues and extends the seashell motif.  A door heads\neast out of here.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2974,38,72,-1,'Llewella\'s Sitting Room','  Llewella\'s apartments reflect her fascination with Amana, the\ndeity of love, whom she claims to have met during her first Shadow-shift.\nHer rooms bear a beautiful seashell motif.  Doors head east and west.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2975,39,72,-1,'Hall','  The floor here is bluish-gray marble with black streaks.  A doorway\nleads west.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2976,40,72,-1,'Royal Sitting Room','  You are in the personal sitting room of the royal couple.   It\'s very\ncomfortable, a great place for a casual visit.  Doors head north, south and\neast.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2977,41,72,-1,'Royal Bath','  This is the royal couple\'s bath.  It\'s quite large.  A door heads west.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2978,35,71,0,'Hall','  The floor here is bluish-gray marble with black streaks.  You can see the\nlibrary downstairs to the south.  There is a spiral staircase here.  A\nsingle door leads north.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2979,36,71,0,'Hall','  The floor here is bluish-gray marble with black streaks.  You can look\nover the railing and see down into the library to the south.  A door heads\nnorth.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2980,37,71,0,'Hall','  The floor here is bluish-gray marble with black streaks.  A door lies\non the south wall.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2981,38,71,0,'Hall','  The floor here is bluish-gray marble with black streaks.  A door goes\nsouth.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2982,39,71,0,'Hall','  The floor here is bluish-gray marble with black streaks.  A door leads\nsouth.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2983,40,71,-1,'Royal Bedroom','  You are in the royal couple\'s bedroom.  The bed is quite large.  A\nfireplace is on the east wall and a door leads north.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2984,41,71,-1,'Behind the Fireplace','  A dark, unfurnished room.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2987,37,70,0,'Guest Room','  This guest room is elegantly and comfortably furnished.  A door heads\nnorth out of the room.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2988,38,70,0,'Guest Room','  The guest room is sparsely but comfortably furnished.  A door leaves\nnorth from here.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2989,39,70,0,'Fazoul\'s Retreat','  A rather spartan looking room is here.  The bed is a simple pile of soft\nfungi covered with linen.  The only real furniture is a stonewash stand\nthat holds a wash basin, a pitcher of water and a low vase of carefully\narranged fungi in colors of pale green and dark brown.\n',24,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2990,40,70,-1,'Small Staircase','  You are on a small staircase that goes down.  A door leads east.\n',24,139404,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2991,41,70,-1,'Dworkin\'s Bedroom','  Dworkin\'s bedroom is sparsely furnished.  It looks like it hasn\'t been\nused in years.  Doors go west and south.\n',24,139404,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2994,37,69,0,'Guest Room','  This part of the guest room is the sleeping quarters.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2995,38,69,0,'Guest Room','  This part of the guest room is for sleeping.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2996,39,69,-1,'Behind the Fireplace','  A dark, unfurnished room.\n',24,139404,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2997,40,69,-1,'Dworkin\'s Study','  This would be a very comfortable place to sit if there were any chairs\nand if it wasn\'t so dusty in here.  There is a fireplace here.  That\'s\nprobably where the dust has blown in.\n',24,139404,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2998,41,69,-1,'Dworkin\'s Library','  Everything is covered with dust here.  You hesitate to touch anything.\nA door leads north into the bedroom.\n',24,139404,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(2999,35,69,-2,'The Great Stair','  You are on a huge stone spiral stair that seems to have been carved from\nthe solid rock of Kolvir.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3000,35,70,-2,'Musicians\' Loft','  This is a small balcony over the Great Hall where the musicians sit and play.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3001,35,71,-2,'Corridor Between Floors','  You are in a passage for servants.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3002,35,72,-2,'Corridor Between Floors','  You are in a passage for servants.\n',24,139276,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3003,35,73,-2,'Corridor Between Floors','  You are in a passage used by servants to move between the first and second\nfloors.\n',24,139276,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3004,35,74,-2,'Corridor Between Floors','  You are in a passage used by servants to move between the first and second\nfloors.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3005,35,69,-4,'The Great Stair','  You are on a huge, stone spiral stair.  It appears to have been carved from\nthe solid rock of Kolvir.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3006,35,69,-5,'The Great Stair','  You are on a huge stone spiral stair.\n',24,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
