(3300,2,20,-1,'Outside a Cave Opening','Tall, forbidding-looking trees surround you on all sides.  Ominous\nshadows are cast all about the area by the sinister tree-line as\nyou stand just outside a dark cave opening.  A strange, unidentifiable\nemotion seems to be radiating from the cave mouth to the southeast.\n',25,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3301,3,19,-1,'The Cave Mouth','You stand inside a small dank cave, illuminated only by light\nfiltering in from the cave entrance to the northwest.  Smooth\nwalls of pale rock surround you and a spiraling ivory staircase\nleads downwards into darkness and mist.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3302,4,21,-2,'The Echo Cave','A thick white mist enshrouds the area, obscuring vision in all\ndirections.  Moisture beads on your brow as you survey the\nsurroundings, only to realize that all sense of direction is\nlost to you.  Through the mist you can make out a crumbling\nfortress somewhere in the distance, sprawled out on the cave\nfloor.  The only point of reference is a spiraling ivory staircase\nthat disappears into the mist above.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3303,4,21,-2,'By the Cave Wall','A thick mist surrounds you, hanging in the air heavily and obscuring\nyour vision.  Effectively disoriented, you realize with a creeping\nfeeling of dread that you have lost all sense of direction.  The only\npoint of reference available to you is the cold, glassy surface of\nobsidian that is the cave wall.  Perfectly smooth, the wall rises\nup to a cave ceiling that is hidden by the unnatural fog that\nencompasses you.  Spotting a crumbling fortress through the mist,\nlogic is defied as the bastion seems both closer yet further away.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3304,3,21,-2,'Lost in a Mist-Shrouded Cave','A thick mist surrounds you, hanging in the air heavily and obscuring\nyour vision.  Effectively disoriented, you realize with a creeping\nfeeling of dread that you have lost all sense of direction.  As the\nmist parts for a second, you can barely make out what appears to be\nthe cave wall in the distance.  The din of a fierce battle floats\non the air and reaches your ears as you see a crumbling fortress\nthrough another break in the milky white haze.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3305,4,20,-2,'Lost in a Mist-Shrouded Cave','A thick mist surrounds you, hanging in the air heavily and obscuring\nyour vision.  Effectively disoriented, you realize with a creeping\nfeeling of dread that you have lost all sense of direction.  As the\nmist parts for a second, you can barely make out what appears to be\nthe cave wall in the distance.  The din of a fierce battle floats on\nthe air and reaches your ears as you see a crumbling fortress through\nanother break in the milky white haze.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3306,5,20,-2,'Standing Before a Titanic War Machine','Before you stands an ancient monstrosity of war.  Rusted from centuries\nof moisture and aging, this instrument of destruction is hardly\nrecognizable anymore.  Whether it was a catapult, ballista, battering\nram or whatever, it does not seem to matter anymore.  A fine white mist\nblankets the area, allowing you furtive glimpses of other hulking\nand distant masses of metal through breaks in the milky haze.  Looking\naround, you realize that you can not seem to remember from which\ndirection you arrived.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3307,2,17,-2,'Lost in a Mist-Shrouded Cave','A thick mist surrounds you, hanging in the air heavily and obscuring\nyour vision.  Effectively disoriented, you realize with a creeping\nfeeling of dread that you have lost all sense of direction.  As the\nmist parts for a second, you can barely make out what appears to be\nthe cave wall in the distance.  The din of a fierce battle floats on\nthe air and reaches your ears as you see a crumbling fortress through\nanother break in the milky white haze.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3308,3,23,-2,'Standing Before a Titanic War Machine','Before you stands an ancient monstrosity of war.  Rusted from centuries\nof moisture and aging, this instrument of destruction is hardly\nrecognizable anymore.  Whether it was a catapult, ballista, battering\nram or whatever, it does not seem to matter anymore.  A fine white mist\nblankets the area, allowing you furtive glimpses of other hulking\nand distant masses of metal through breaks in the milky haze.  Looking\naround, you realize that you can not seem to remember from which\ndirection you arrived.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
