(3313,3,21,-2,'Lost in a Mist-Shrouded Cave','A thick mist surrounds you, hanging in the air heavily and obscuring\nyour vision.  Effectively disoriented, you realize with a creeping\nfeeling of dread that you have lost all sense of direction.  As the\nmist parts for a second, you can barely make out what appears to be\nthe cave wall in the distance.  The din of a fierce battle floats on\nthe air and reaches your ears as you see a crumbling fortress through\nanother break in the milky white haze.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3314,3,19,-2,'Standing Before Crumbled Ruins','The thick white mist lessens here, allowing for some semblance of\nvision.  Surveying your surroundings, crumbling ruins lie sprawled\nout to the southwest.  A shimmering veil of light, barely noticeable\neven from this distance, hangs above the ruins.  Directly to the\nnorth is what appears to be a pool of inky darkness, steaming and\nadding to the mist that is concentrated to the northeast.  A large\nfissure splits the cave wall nearby to the east, and the very rock\nof the cave floor has been unearthed downwards and to your west.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3315,1,21,-2,'The Fields of War','A break in the mist affords you with a unobstructed view of carnage\nand destruction.  You stand upon an ancient battlefield, surveying\nthe scene of a struggle played out ages ago.  Rusted metal and bones\nlitter the area, covered by a sooty crimson dust.  The stench of death\nyet lingers here, a cloying scent of rot and decay that penetrates\nyour nostrils and brings about a feeling of nausea.  All about you,\nthe white mist thickens, concealing the dimensions of this field of\nwar.  Glimpses of hulking masses in the mist can be seen off in the\ndistance.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3316,4,21,-2,'Lost in a Mist-Shrouded Cave','A thick mist surrounds you, hanging in the air heavily and obscuring\nyour vision.  Effectively disoriented, you realize with a creeping\nfeeling of dread that you have lost all sense of direction.  As the\nmist parts for a second, you can barely make out what appears to be\nthe cave wall in the distance.  The din of a fierce battle floats on\nthe air and reaches your ears as you see a crumbling fortress through\nanother break in the milky white haze.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3317,6,21,-2,'Lost in a Mist-Shrouded Cave','A thick mist surrounds you, hanging in the air heavily and obscuring\nyour vision.  Effectively disoriented, you realize with a creeping\nfeeling of dread that you have lost all sense of direction.  As the\nmist parts for a second, you can barely make out what appears to be\nthe cave wall in the distance.  The din of a fierce battle floats on\nthe air and reaches your ears as you see a crumbling fortress through\nanother break in the milky white haze.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3318,5,23,-2,'Lost in a Mist-Shrouded Cave','A thick mist surrounds you, hanging in the air heavily and obscuring\nyour vision.  Effectively disoriented, you realize with a creeping\nfeeling of dread that you have lost all sense of direction.  As the\nmist parts for a second, you can barely make out what appears to be\nthe cave wall in the distance.  The din of a fierce battle floats on\nthe air and reaches your ears as you see a crumbling fortress through\nanother break in the milky white haze.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3319,3,21,-2,'Lost in a Mist-Shrouded Cave','A thick mist surrounds you, hanging in the air heavily and obscuring\nyour vision.  Effectively disoriented, you realize with a creeping\nfeeling of dread that you have lost all sense of direction.  As the\nmist parts for a second, you can barely make out what appears to be\nthe cave wall in the distance.  The din of a fierce battle floats on\nthe air and reaches your ears as you see a crumbling fortress through\nanother break in the milky white haze.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3320,6,23,-2,'Lost in a Mist-Shrouded Cave','A thick mist surrounds you, hanging in the air heavily and obscuring\nyour vision.  Effectively disoriented, you realize with a creeping\nfeeling of dread that you have lost all sense of direction.  As the\nmist parts for a second, you can barely make out what appears to be\nthe cave wall in the distance.  The din of a fierce battle floats on\nthe air and reaches your ears as you see a crumbling fortress through\nanother break in the milky white haze.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3321,2,20,-3,'A Trench on the Battlefield','You stand in a crater in the cave floor.  It appears that large\ntracts were ripped from the cave floor ages ago, creating a\ntrench of sorts.  The footing here is tricky, even eons having\ngone buy have done nothing to smooth the rough edges of rock\nthat still protrude.  The trench continues on to the northwest\nwhile it seems possible to climb out towards the east by carefully\npicking a path over some of the larger shards of rock.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3322,1,21,-3,'A Trench on the Battlefield','You stand in a crater on the cave floor.  It appears that large\ntracts of rock were ripped from the cave floor ages ago, creating\na trench of sorts.  The footing here is tricky, even eons of having\ngone by have done little to smooth out the rough edges of rock\nthat still protrude.  A thick white mists floats just above your\nhead and eddies around the lip of the excavation.  The trench\ncontinues on to the southeast.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3323,6,19,-2,'Entrance to an Underground Bunker','You stand in a slightly cramped cave, the ceiling barely a few\nfeet above your head.  Bereft of any distinguishing marks, the\nonly thing worthy of notice in this chamber is a single, nondescript\nsteel door set in the eastern wall.  Passage can be found to the\nwest through a tunnel of inky darkness.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3324,7,20,-2,'Sentry Post','This room is Spartan in appearance.  Rough hewn walls encompass a small\narea, giving the chamber an almost claustrophobic sense.  A plain-looking\nsteel door rests in the wall to the southwest while a set of stone\nstairs in the northeast corner of the room allows for passage down into\nanother chamber below.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(3325,7,20,-3,'Staging Area','Rough hewn walls of granite pen in the vast chamber that you now are\nin.  Rusting metal that once might have resembled weapons and armor\nis strewn across the floor and give this room a cluttered appearance.\nA set of stone steps leads upwards through a hole in the ceiling and\ncontinues downwards into a chamber below.  Iron doors in each of the\nfour corners of this chamber provide other avenues of exploration.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3326,8,21,-3,'The War Room','You now stand in what appears to be the central planning center for\nthis underground bunker.  The chamber extends a ways to the northeast,\ngranite columns lining the entire length of the room.  A single,\nmassive oaken table rests in the middle of the floor amidst piles\nof rotting scripts.  A solid iron door rests in the southwestern\ncorner of the room.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3327,6,21,-3,'Storage Room','You are in what appears to be a room reserved for holding such\nthings as food stores and the like.  The granite walls are slick\nwith a viscous black liquid that slowly drips down from the\nceiling.  A rotting odor fills the air, bringing about a slight\nsense of nausea.  A single iron door set in the southeast wall\nprovides passage out of this chamber.\n',25,131085,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3328,8,19,-3,'Warriors\' Barracks','Rows upon rows of alcoves carved into rock line the walls of this\nroom.  Within each niche lies some straw to serve as makeshift\nbeds.  Other than the alcoves in the walls, this chamber is rather\nbereft of furnishings.  A sturdy-looking iron door rests in the\nnorthwestern wall.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3329,6,19,-3,'Equipment Room','You are in a room that seems to be reserved for the storage of\nweapons of war and other pieces of equipment.  A dark black ichor\nruns in trails down the walls of this chamber, rendering them\nslick to the touch.  Rusted scraps of metal lie all about you,\nmaking for slightly dangerous and difficult movement.  An iron\ndoor set in the northeast corner provides passage out of this\nroom.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3330,7,20,-4,'Main Chamber of the Lower Level','This room is bereft of anything out of the ordinary, that is if you\ndisregard the horrendous odor wafting in from a darkened corridor\nto the north.  A set of stone steps leads up through a hole in the\ngranite ceiling while sturdy iron doors are set in the southern\nand western walls.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3331,7,19,-4,'Prison Master\'s Office','This room is dominated by nothing other than bondage paraphernalia\nstrewn about on the floor.  Rusty manacles hang from the walls and\na single oaken desk rests near the back wall.  A solid-looking\niron door rests in the northern wall.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3332,6,20,-4,'Interrogation Room','Spartan is an apt term to describe this small, cramped chamber.  Grisly\nis easily another adjective to depict the horrid scene before you.\nThe room\'s only furnishing is a single, massive slab of malachite\nthat rests firmly in the center of the room.  Dark stains run down\nthe side of the table, leading to grooves cunningly carved into the\nfloor.  The reek of death hangs heavily in the air as you survey the\nsurroundings.  Random, unidentifiable tools of pain lie scattered about\namidst pools of blood.  A sturdy iron door rests firmly in the eastern\nwall.\n',25,163977,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3333,7,21,-4,'Prison Hallway','This damp and dark corridor reeks of rot and decay.  The acrid odor\nof rancid sweat and waste assaults your nostrils, apparently coming\nfrom the pitch black corridors leading off to the northeast and\nnorthwest.  The granite walls that encase you in this narrow hall\nas well as the ground that you tread is covered with a sort of\nstrange condensation, making passage here a bit treacherous.  An empty\nlooking chamber opens up to the south.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3334,8,22,-4,'Prison Hallway','The stench of fecal waste and rancid sweat grows stronger as you\ntraverse deeper down this corridor.  This darkened hall appears to\ncome to an end, and the odor is almost unbearable.  Imposing steel\ndoors rest in the northern and eastern walls of the corridor while\npassage to the southwest is possible as no obstruction stands in\nthe hall\'s way.\n',25,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3335,6,22,-4,'Prison Hallway','The stench of fecal waste and rancid sweat grows stronger as you\ntraverse deeper down this corridor.  This darkened hall appears to\ncome to an end, and the odor is almost unbearable.  Imposing steel\ndoors rest in the northern and western walls of the corridor while\npassage to the southeast is possible as no obstructions stand in\nthe hall\'s way.\n',25,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3336,8,23,-4,'A Rancid Prison Cell','This cramped cell is barely large enough for you to stand in, much\nthe less move around in.  Straw litters the floor, which is stained\ndark in places with some unknown substances that you would rather\nnot guess at.  The stench in here is virtually unbearable, as you are\non the brink of nausea.  The remainder of the cell is very typical\nfor its sort - impenetrable walls, a solid steel door and the like.\nYou notice some faint etchings on the far wall.\n',25,163976,32,0,0,0,0,0,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(3337,9,22,-4,'A Rancid Prison Cell','This cramped cell is barely large enough for you to stand in, much\nthe less move around in.  Straw litters the floor which is stained\ndark in places with some unknown substances that you would rather\nnot guess at.  The stench in here is virtually unbearable, as you are\non the brink of nausea.  The remainder of this cell is very typical\nfor its sort - impenetrable walls, a solid steel door and the like.\nYou notice some faint etchings on the far wall.\n',25,163976,32,0,0,0,0,0,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(3338,6,23,-4,'A Rancid Prison Cell','This cramped cell is barely large enough for you to stand in, much\nthe less move around in.  Straw litters the floor, which is stained\ndark in some places with some unknown substances that you would rather\nnot guess at.  The stench in here is virtually unbearable, as you are\non the brink of nausea.  The remainder of this cell is very typical\nfor its sort - impenetrable walls, squalor, a solid steel door and\nthe like.  You notice some faint etchings on the far wall.\n',25,163976,32,0,0,0,0,0,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(3339,5,22,-4,'A Rancid Prison Cell','This cramped cell is barely large enough for you to stand in, much\nthe less move around in.  Straw litters the floor, which is stained\ndark in places with some unknown substances that you would rather\nnot guess at.  The stench in here is virtually unbearable, as you are\non the brink of nausea.  The remainder of this cell is very typical\nfor its sort - impenetrable walls, squalor, a solid steel door and\nthe like.  You notice some faint etchings on the far wall.\n',25,163976,32,0,0,0,0,0,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(3340,3,20,-2,'A Pool of Darkness','You stand before a pool of ebony water.  Strangely, as you peer into\nits inky depths you realize that your reflection is absent.  The\npool appears to be completely still, but as you watch, the surface\'s\ntranquility is disturbed by something underwater.  A thick white mist\nrises off of the pure jet surface and drifts off, serving to thicken\nthe soupy haze that surrounds the pool.  Through a few wisps of mist,\nyou can make out an open area to the south and also a crumbling\nfortress sprawled out even further to the south.\n',25,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3341,2,21,-3,'Under the Surface of Night','Inky water surrounds you, chilling you to the bone with its coldness.\nFaint flickerings of light can be seen coming from above, or rather,\nthe direction in this dark environ that appears to be \'up.\' Off in\nanother direction, an unnatural emerald light pulsates steadily.\n',25,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3342,2,20,-3,'Kraegin\'s Lair','The walls of this underwater grotto are deeply pitted and give off\nan unnatural green glow.  The water, a deep emerald hue, broils about\nas if alive and agitated by some monstrous presence.  The bones of\ncountless beasts litter the floor of this subterranean chamber, some\nlooking vaguely humanoid.  Patches of darkness to the north and\nsoutheast look to be possible exits from this lair of aquatic horror.\n',25,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3343,3,19,-3,'Kraegin\'s Treasure Alcove','This subterranean chamber is littered with bones and a few pale,\nbloated corpses vaguely humanoid in shape.  The walls of this\nunderwater alcove are smooth and dark, a pitch backdrop for the\nslightly green-tinged water.  A steady, pulsating green light filters\nthrough the water at the northwest corner of the alcove.\n',25,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3344,2,18,-2,'Main Gate of Tanelorn','You are standing under the crumbling ruins of what appears to have\nbeen a colossal gateway made entirely of malachite.  Not much remains\nexcept for a few cracked dark green granite boulders lying about\non either side of a paved walkway leading to the southwest.  An\neerie white mist creeps in from the northeast, allowing glimpses\nof darkness beyond.\n',25,131081,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3345,1,17,-2,'Inside the Main Gate of Tanelorn','You are standing on a section of an ancient paved road, remarkably\nwell-kept considering its apparent age.  On either side of the road\nstand the ruins of what once must have been beautiful buildings\nconstructed entirely of different hued blocks of granite.  The\nrubble strewn about alongside the road proves to be an effective\nobstacle against any exploration of the roadside.  In the near\ndistance to the northeast stands what appears to be a crumbling\narch of malachite, while the pavement continues on to the southwest.\n',25,131081,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3346,0,16,-2,'Walnut Street','You are standing on a section of an ancient paved road, remarkably\nwell-kept considering its apparent age.  On either side of the road\nstands the ruins of what once must have been beautiful buildings\nconstructed entirely of different hued blocks of granite.  The rubble\nstrewn about alongside the road proves to be an effective obstacle\nagainst any exploration of the roadside.  Amidst the granite blocks,\nyou can barely make out what appears to be a plaque set in the\nground.  The road continues on to the northeast and southwest.\n',25,131081,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3347,-2,16,-2,'Walnut Street','You are standing on a section of an ancient paved road, remarkably\nwell-kept considering its apparent age.  On either side of the road\nstand the ruins of what once must have been beautiful buildings\nconstructed entirely of different hued blocks of granite.  The rubble\nstrewn about alongside the road proves to be an effective obstacle\nagainst any exploration of the roadside.  Amidst the crumbled stones\non the pavements edge, you catch a glimpse of what appears to be\nrotted sign.  This paved walkway continues on to the northeast as\nwell as to the southwest, where there appears to be some sort of\nan intersection.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3348,-3,15,-2,'Intersection of Walnut and Memory','  You stand at the intersection of two ancient thoroughfares.\nRuined buildings surround you on all sides, rendering a rather\nbleak panorama.  The stones beneath your feet seem almost alive,\nhumming gently and giving off a subtle heat.  Something about\nthis walk brings back memories of a distant world lost to you\nforever.  The feeling is fleeting, as you survey the surroundings\nand note the paved roads extending to the northeast and south.\nA seemingly empty lot lies to the west.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3349,-3,14,-2,'Memory Lane','An eerie feeling of deja vu washes over you as you walk down this\nvaguely familiar street.  The stones beneath your feet seem to hum\nsoftly with an inner life of their own while giving off a subtle\nwarmth.  You are suddenly overcome by a sense of longing for a distant\nworld lost to you forever.  Snapping out of your daze, you stop and\nsurvey what lies about you.  What appears to be an intact building\nsprawls out to your east, stretching out further to the southeast.\nTo the west, a building lies in ruins - a single window giving it\nthe appearance of a single-eyed portrait of loneliness.  The road\ncontinues on to the north and south.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3350,-3,13,-2,'Memory Lane','An eerie feeling of deja vu washes over you as you walk down this\nvaguely familiar street.  The stones beneath your feet seem to hum\nsoftly with an inner life of their own while giving off a subtle\nwarmth.  You are suddenly overcome by a sense of longing for a distant\nworld lost to you forever.  Snapping out of your daze, you stop and\nsurvey what lies about you.  A crumbling wall blocks passage to the\nwest.  A huge set of gilded, metal doors is set in what appears to be\na massive hall that remains standing to the east.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3351,-3,12,-2,'Memory Lane','An eerie feeling of deja vu washes over you as you walk down this\nvaguely familiar street.  The stones beneath your feet seem to hum\nsoftly with an inner life of their own while giving off a subtle\nwarmth.  You are suddenly overcome by a sense of longing for a distant\nworld lost to you forever.  Snapping out of your daze, you stop and\nsurvey what lies about you.  A massive hall, for the most part intact,\nlies sprawled out to the east while a darkened alley leads off to\nthe west.  The paved walkway continues to the north and south.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3352,-3,11,-2,'Memory Lane','An eerie feeling of deja vu washes over you as you walk down this\nvaguely familiar street.  The stones beneath your feet seem to hum\nsoftly with an inner life of their own while giving off a subtle\nwarmth.  You are suddenly overcome by a sense of longing for a distant\nworld lost to you forever.  Snapping out of your daze, you stop and\nsurvey what lies about you.  The road continues to the north and\nsouth while a set of double doors to the west leads into an\nrather seedy looking establishment.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3353,-3,10,-2,'Memory Lane','An eerie feeling of deja vu washes over you as you walk down this\nvaguely familiar street.  The stones beneath your feet seem to hum\nsoftly with an inner life of their own while giving off a subtle\nwarmth.  You are suddenly overcome by a sense of longing for a distant\nworld lost to you forever.  Snapping out of your daze, you stop and\nsurvey what lies about you.  You seem to be standing at some sort\nof an intersection with roads leading off in three of the four\ncardinal directions.  To the south lies a gargantuan malachite structure\nthat seems to have weathered the tests of time exceedingly well.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3354,-4,10,-2,'Cherry Street','You stand upon an ancient stretch of pavement.  Unfortunately,\nrubble strewn all about alongside this road prevents you from\nmoving in any direction except to the east.  Amidst the scattered\nblocks of granite, you make out what appears to be a tattered\nstrip of cloth.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3355,-2,10,-2,'Cherry Street','You stand upon a cracked section of an ancient roadway.  High above you,\nthe cave ceiling provides a dark backdrop for the ruined buildings\nthat surround you.  A gigantic malachite structure is sprawled out\nto the southeast while a decrepit building signals this road\'s end\nto the east.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3356,-2,14,-2,'Hall of Forgotten Heroes','You stand in what appears to be a massive, high-ceilinged chamber\nconstructed of a cream-colored marble.  Torches rest in the walls,\ncasting bizarre shadows off the many statues that line the\nroom.  Despite the dancing shadows that flit about the room, you\nfeel a sense of heroism and valor as you walk about this room\ndedicated to heroes of a time long ago.  The tribute devoted to\nthe adventurers long dead continues beyond large jeweled archways\nto the north and south.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3357,-2,13,-2,'Entranceway to the Hall of Forgotten Heroes','You stand in what appears to be a massive, high-ceilinged chamber\nconstructed entirely of cream-colored marble.  Torches rest in the\nwalls, casting bizarre shadows off the many statues that line\nthe room.  Despite the dancing shadows that flit about the room, you\nfeel a sense of heroism and valor as you walk about this room\ndedicated to heroes of a time long lost.  A massive set of gilded\nmetal doors rests firmly in the western wall, and the tribute to\npast glory continues to the north, east and south.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3358,-2,12,-2,'Hall of Forgotten Heroes','You stand in what appears to be a massive, high-ceilinged chamber\nconstructed of a cream-colored marble.  Torches rest in the walls,\ncasting bizarre shadows off the many statues that line the\nroom.  Despite the dancing shadows that flit about the room, you\nfeel a sense of heroism and valor as you walk about this room\ndedicated to heroes of a time long ago.  The tribute devoted to\nthe adventurers long dead continues beyond large jeweled archways\nto the north and south.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3359,-2,11,-2,'Hall of Forgotten Heroes','You stand in what appears to be a massive, high-ceilinged chamber\nconstructed of a cream-colored marble.  Torches rest in the walls,\ncasting bizarre shadows off the many statues that line the\nroom.  Despite the dancing shadows that flit about the room, you\nfeel a sense of heroism and valor as you walk about this room\ndedicated to heroes of a time long ago.  The tribute devoted to\nthe adventurers long dead continues beyond a large jeweled archway\nto the north.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3360,-2,15,-2,'Hall of Forgotten Heroes','You stand in what appears to be a massive, high-ceilinged chamber\nconstructed of a cream-colored marble.  Torches rest in the walls,\ncasting bizarre shadows off the many statues that line the\nroom.  Despite the dancing shadows that flit about the room, you\nfeel a sense of heroism and valor as you walk about this room\ndedicated to heroes of a time long ago.  The tribute devoted to\nthe adventurers long dead continues beyond a large jeweled archway\nto the south.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3361,-3,9,-2,'Museum Courtyard','You stand in a wide area enclosed on three sides by towering\nmalachite walls.  This square of sorts is remarkably clean and\nwell-kept.  The cobblestones under your feet appear to have been\nsmoothed out over the centuries by countless feet.  A large set\nof granite doors rests in the wall to the south while a vaguely\nfamiliar road lies to the north.\n',25,172045,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3362,-3,8,-2,'Main Room of the Museum of Lost Glory','You stand in the middle of an architectural masterpiece of monumental\nproportions.  Thick malachite columns rise up on all sides, soaring to\ntouch the painted ceiling high above your head.  Intricately carved\ngargoyles made of marble stand guard in niches cut into the granite\nwalls, peeking out from around countless tapestries that grace this\nchamber.  The air about you is slightly musty and reminds you somewhat\nof a silent tomb, but the momentary discomfort passes as you take in\nthe beauty of your surroundings.  A solitary sign stands in the middle\nof the floor while large archways in each of the four corners of the\nroom lead off to different areas of the museum.  A glass door rests\nin the south wall.\n',25,172045,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3363,-3,7,-2,'Curator\'s Office','This room is like no other that you have seen in the museum.\nNot present are the granite walls that are so common throughout\nthe rest of the structure.  In its place are walls and a floor of\npurest onyx, so dark that all light seems to be absorbed in\nits stygian night.  Standing in start contrast of the almost\nunnatural surroundings is a solid oak desk and chair.  A few\nancient maps are tacked on the wall and a glass door rests in\nthe north wall.\n',25,172045,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3364,-4,9,-2,'Weaponry of War Exhibit','Violence and death seems to be the theme of this room, as weapons\nof war are displayed in glass cases for all to see.  Looking all\nabout you, it suddenly dawns on you that killing has become an\nart form.  Varied are the tools of the artisan.  Blades, whips, hammers,\nand others of their ilk surround you - reminders that violence is\nso easy to perpetrate.  Colorful tapestries hang from the walls, each\ndepicting a different scene of war and death.  Large archways to the\nsouth and southeast lead away from this chamber of death.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3365,-4,8,-2,'Artifacts of Power Exhibit','You look about you with a sense of awe at the power you feel\nemanating from the glass display cases standing about the room.\nRefined power of quite some antiquity surrounds you on all sides,\nsecurely stowed away in the uniform looking glass cases.  Somber\ntapestries hang from the wall, depicting scenes of battle and\ndeath from some long-forgotten era.  Large archways lead off\nto the north and south.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3366,-4,7,-2,'Armors of War Exhibit','You are surrounded on all sides by huge suits of armor dating\nfrom all ages of known history.  Nothing is forgotten here - there\nis plate mail, chain, scale, ring, all forms of leather, and\ndozens of other forms of protection.  A few glass cases are set about\nthe room, displaying a few special articles of armor.  Colorful\ntapestries cover the walls while a chariot made entirely of crystal\nhangs from the ceiling.  Large archways to the north and northeast\nlead out of this room.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3367,-2,9,-2,'Waxworks Exhibit','The walls of this chamber are made of huge blocks of lapis\nlazuli.  Rising high to the ceiling, the wall is covered in places\nby tapestries of every size and shape, each depicting a different\nscene of battle.  The floor has a lustrous look about it and you\nare surrounded on all sides by wax figures.  Large archways to\nthe south and southwest provide exits to this azure chamber.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3368,-2,8,-2,'Waxworks Exhibit','The walls of this chamber are made of huge blocks of lapis\nlazuli.  Rising high to the ceiling, the wall is covered in places\nby tapestries of every size and shape, each depicting a different\nscene of battle.  The floor has a lustrous look about it and you\nare surrounded on all sides by wax figures.  Large archways to\nnorth and south provide exits from this azure chamber.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3369,-2,7,-2,'Waxworks Exhibit','The walls of this chamber are made of huge blocks of lapis\nlazuli.  Rising high to the ceiling, the wall is covered in places\nby tapestries of every size and shape, each depicting a different\nscene of battle.  The floor has a lustrous look about it and you\nare surrounded on all sides by wax figures.  Large archways to\nnorth and northwest provide exits from this azure chamber.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3370,-4,11,-2,'Waiting Room of Greely\'s','You stand in a rather plain-looking room that obviously serves\nas a waiting area.  A few chairs rest up against the north wall\nand a podium rests in the southwest corner of the room.  A few\nferns hanging from the ceiling add to the rooms decor, but do\nnothing to liven the waiting area up.  The smell of grilled food\nwafts on the air from the southwest.  A set of double doors leads out\neast to the street.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3371,-5,10,-2,'The Drooping Gut Tavern','You are standing in what could easily be coined as a cesspool.  The\nworst elements of society are nothing compared to the collection of\ndregs that haunt this shadowed tavern.  Wooden planks creak underfoot\nas you slowly make your way around the main room of this establishment.\nTables are scattered all around the room while a bar stands in the\nsouthwest corner.  Dark unidentifiable stains cover the floor, probably\nevidence of violence perpetrated on the premises.  A set of wooden\nstairs leads up to a second floor as well as downwards into a sublevel.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3372,-5,10,-1,'The Pipe Room','Smoke of all colors and scents mingle and intertwine all about\nthis room, making for an intoxicating atmosphere.  Your eyes begin\nto tear somewhat from the sheer amount of smoke circulating about\nthe room.  A hearty fireplace set in the north wall warms the\nroom and a few plush looking chairs, complete with accompanying\nfootrests, are arranged around the room amidst a divan or two.\nA set of wooden stairs leads downwards away from this smoky\nhaven.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3373,-5,10,-3,'Sin\'s Pleasure Emporium','You stand in the foyer of what appears to be a sex-for-money\njoint.  This seems evident from the curious noises coming through\na doorway to the east and the heady aroma of bodies engaged in\namorous activities that wafts about the room.  This room is rather\nunremarkable in appearance save for the enormous set of golden\ndoors set in the southern wall.  To the east, you can make out\nsome motion through an empty doorway and a set of wooden stairs\nleads upwards.  A set of love beads hangs in the northwest\ncorner of the room.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3374,-5,9,-3,'The Palatial Suite','You stand amidst a scene of orgiastic decadence and uninhibited\npleasures of the flesh.  Not a single talen was wasted in this\nrooms design, evident in the grandiose appearance of this chamber\nof sin.  Lavish tapestries hang from the walls, each depicting\ndifferent acts of carnal pleasure between men and women of all\nraces.  Huge cushions are littered across the floor, making for\neasily accessible and comfortable bedding for visitors to this\nden of iniquity.  The scent of some mysteriously alluring perfume\nis carried on the air, ticking your nostrils and causing a stirring\nin your loins.  A gigantic set of golden doors rests in the northern\nwall of this chamber.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3375,-4,12,-2,'Darkened Alley','Darkness surrounds you as shadows seem to creep upon you and slowly\nwrap their tendrils about your being.  As you traverse this alleyway,\nyou spot a number of unidentifiable lumps huddles alongside a\nbuilding to the south.  In the shadows, an empty doorway to the\nnorth yawns open to you, much like the maw of some great beast.  The\nalley continues on in shadow to the west, while the lights of a\nfamiliar street beckon from the east.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3376,-5,12,-2,'Darkened Alley','Darkness surrounds you as you stand in this alleyway.  Shadows seem\nto creep up behind you and wrap their tendrils about your body.\nLooking all about, you notice trash and refuse littered across the\nalleyway.  A giant metal door lies to the north, set in a building\nconstructed of granite.  Passage appears to be possible to the east\nand south, where darkness greets your inquisitive scans.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3377,-5,11,-2,'Dead End','Darkness surrounds you on all sides as the shadows seem to slowly\ncreep up behind you.  A slight chill runs down your spine as you\nlook about you and notice that the only visible exits are to the\nnorth and a sturdy looking steel door set in a wall to the south.\nThis dark alcove seems like the perfect location for a midnight\nrendezvous with the unhealthier members of society.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3378,-5,13,-2,'An Abandoned Warehouse','As you enter this area, you are immediately assaulted by the sheer\nsize of this deceptively proportioned building.  From the outside, the\nexterior seemed to hint at a modest sized building.  However, from\ninside, the area within the granite walls\' confines is simply\nastounding.  The roof stretches high above your head, reaching heights\nalmost out of sight while large, empty crates line the floor all\nabout you.  A giant set of metal doors lies in the south wall of this\nwarehouse while the storage area continues on the north.\n',25,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3379,-5,14,-2,'An Abandoned Warehouse','The chamber you find yourself in is of gigantic proportions.  The\nceiling rises high above your head while the granite walls, for the\nmost part intact, are set far apart to the north, east and west.\nThe floor of this area is virtually barren save for a few wooden\ncasks lying about in various states of decay.  Looking southward,\nyou realize that this storage area extends even further in that\ndirection.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3380,-4,15,-2,'An Empty Lot','  This barren plot is devoid of anything besides a few stray\nstone blocks and the occasional scrap of rusted metal.  Crumbling\ngranite walls pen this empty area in, affording passage only to\nthe west where an eerily familiar street lies.  Upon closer\ninspection of the west wall, you can barely make out the outlines\nof a granite door that you had previously missed.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3381,-4,13,-2,'Ruined Building','You stand within the confines of a ruined building, ages old and\nshowing every year of its existence.  You catch glimpses of the\ndarkness that must be the cave ceiling through wide cracks in the\nceiling.  The walls about you are crumbling and the floor is littered\nwith fragmented granite and dust.  An empty door frame set in the\nsouthern wall leads out to a darkened alleyway.\n',25,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3382,-4,14,-2,'Crumbled Ruins of a House','You stand now within the confines of a crumbling building of\nsome antiquity.  The architecture is completely foreign to you,\nyet strikes a chord in the depths of your memory.  The premises are\nbarren of any furnishings, testament to the decay of time and the\navarice of self-serving looters.  A single, empty window gazes\nout at the eerily familiar street outside, the glass most probably\ntaken years ago.  An empty doorway in the east wall leads out to\nthe walkway outside.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3383,-1,10,-2,'Crumbled Ruins of a House','You stand within a cracked and ruined old building.  An atmosphere\nonce vibrant with signs of life, any life, now is nothing but\nlonely and bereft of anything.  Drab walls of granite pen in a\nsmall, dust-covered floor while you can barely glimpse the cave\nceiling through small holes in the ceiling.  A doorway set in\nthe west wall provides an exit from this ancient dwelling.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3384,-5,10,-2,'Non-Smoking Section of Greely\'s','Tables and chairs are spread out across this section of Greely\'s\ndining area.  Hardwood planks line the floor and serve as the walls\nto this room, lending a somewhat down-home feel to the atmosphere.\nThe stench of pipe smoke and the ilk wafts over on the air from\nthe west, no doubt the area designated for the smoking patrons.\nThe dining room also continues on to the southwest.  Looking about\nyou a second time, you notice a strikingly detailed mural on the wall.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3385,-6,10,-2,'Smoking Section of Greely\'s','Smoke of all colors and scents mingle and intertwine all about\nthis room, making for an intoxicating atmosphere.  You eyes begin\nto tear somewhat from the sheer amount of smoke circulating about\nthis section of Greely\'s.  In fact, the cloying smoke is beginning\nto cause a bit of nausea to creep through your body.  Through the\nhaze of the dense smoke, you can make out a smattering of tables\nand chairs.  The dining room continues on to the south as well\nas to the cleaner air to the east.\n',25,163849,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3386,-6,9,-2,'Backroom of Greely\'s','Hardwood planks make up the floor and walls of this room.\nA few tables and chairs lie scattered about but are rarely\nfilled, seeing as how they are the worst tables in the house.\nThe smell of slightly burning food assails your nostrils\nfrom the east while the stink of the smoke patrons to the\nnorth of you are inhaling serves only to nauseate you further.\nNothing about this room seems either healthy or conducive\nto dining, the only optimistic looking option being the\ntables to the northeast in the non-smoking section of Greely\'s.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3387,-5,9,-2,'Kitchen of Greely\'s','The wonderful aromas of a multitude of cooking foods fill your\nnostrils as you walk into this room.  Your short sting of euphoria\nquickly turns to a sense of disgust as you look about you.  A short\nsojourn into the realm of culinary delight is definitely not what\nvisiting the food preparation area of Greely\'s is all about.  Quite\nthe contrary.  Mildew and rotten meat lie everywhere, and unidentifiably\nand unhealthy looking liquids course down the sides of steaming\ncauldrons.  As you continue to survey your environs, you stop short\nof almost tripping and realize in horror that the offending object\non the floor appears to be nothing less than a severed humanoid\narm.  A large metal door that is cool to the touch rests firmly\nin the east wall.  The only other exit from this madhouse appears\nto be west to the dining area of Greely\'s.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3388,5,19,-2,'Dark Tunnel','Darkness surrounds you on all sides as the slick obsidian walls\nof this tunnel provide narrow passage deeper into the rock.  The\ntunnel seems to widen further to the east while it continues on\nto the southwest.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(3389,4,18,-2,'Dark Tunnel','Darkness surrounds you on all sides as the slick obsidian walls\nof this tunnel provide narrow passage deeper into the rock.  The\ntunnel of darkness continues on into pitch blackness to the\nnortheast and northwest.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(3390,3,19,-2,'Dark Tunnel','Darkness surrounds you on all sides, as the slick obsidian walls\nof this tunnel provide narrow passage deeper into the rock.  A\nlarge fissure in the cave wall allows for passage to the north\nwhile the tunnel of darkness continues on to the southeast.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(3391,4,19,-2,'Gaping Fissure','You stand between two huge walls of obsidian.  Some primordial force\nages ago split the cave wall in twain, creating passage to a darkened\ntunnel to the south.\n',25,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(3392,-4,10,-3,'The Economy Room','You stand in a plain-looking room, unremarkable in most aspects.\nThe floor you are on is made of a spongy substance, slightly\nsticky with half-dried fluids.  The heady aroma of sweat and human\nflesh fills the air, dizzying in its intensity.  The walls are\ncovered with tattered tapestries, each depicting different scenes\nof carnal pleasure.  A slight draft comes in from a doorway to the\nwest, bringing in a bit of fresh air in this den of iniquity.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3393,-6,11,-3,'A Short Hall','You stand in a short, darkened hallway.  At one end rests a sturdy\nlooking oaken door set in the wall, while strings of beads hanging\nfrom the ceiling blocks passage at the other end of the hall.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3394,-7,12,-3,'Sin\'s Office','You stand amidst a tableau of decadence and luxury.  Priceless silks\nhang from the walls, an obscene clash of garish colors.  The floor\nis carpeted by countless pillows lying all about.  The scent of\nflesh and sweat is strong in this room and an intoxicating smoke\nwafts about the room.  The office is dim, lit only by torchieres\nstanding in the corners.  A solid oak door rests in the southeast\ncorner of the room while another door sits in the west wall.\n',25,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(3395,-4,9,-2,'A Frigid Meat Locker','You stand within the freezing confines of what appears to be a\nmeat storage facility.  Gigantic blocks of ice lines the walls\nand the ground is slick with frozen blood and beast entrails.\nThe chill air cools your skin and a shiver runs down your spine\nas you look about at the beast carcasses lying about the locker.\nA few cadavers that look suspiciously humanoid hang from hooks\nin the ceiling.\n',25,163976,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3396,-8,12,-3,'Sin\'s Private Paradise','  This chamber is nothing but a huge cushion or bed.  The floor\nis covered entirely by one gigantic, silk-covered pillow while\nthe walls are adorned with tapestries of all colors.  The lighting\nin here is dim, a torchiere here and there providing the only\nillumination in this inner chamber of decadence.  A large mirror\nacross the ceiling rounds out this room\'s decor.\n',25,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(3397,-5,15,-2,'Hall of the Eternally Damned','A strong sense of sadness and loss washes over you as you look\nall about this ancient chamber.  The countless ages and ravishings\nof time have not been gentle to this hall as the granite floors and\nwalls are cracked and pitted.  You sense that great beauty once\nexisted here, but through some tragic mistake in the course of\ntime it was lost forever.  Silence reigns supreme in this accursed\nhall.  You see the faint outline of a granite door set in the\neastern wall.\n',25,132105,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3398,-1,13,-2,'Hall of Forgotten Heroes','You stand in what appears to be a massive, high-ceilinged chamber\nconstructed of a cream-colored marble.  Torches rest in the walls,\ncasting bizarre shadows off the many statues that line the\nroom.  Despite the dancing shadows that flit about the room, you\nfeel a sense of heroism and valor as you walk about this room\ndedicated to heroes of a time long ago.  The tribute devoted to\nthe adventurers long dead continues beyond a large jeweled archway\nto the west.\n',25,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3401,-37,8,-1,'Riverfront','  The trees pull back offering a small clearing of grassy land where boats\nmay be grounded.  The river to the south, flows east-westerly with the\noccasional piece of flotsam flowing along.  To the north a path leads into\na forested area of great intrigue.\n',26,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3402,-37,9,-1,'A Well Worn Path in the forest','  A well worn path wanders its way through a forest.  Occasionally a tree\nbranch hangs low enough to come near.  The path splits to the east and west\nhere because of a dense growth of trees.  There is a slight sound of water\nthat can be heard to the south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3403,-38,9,-1,'A Well Worn Path in the Forest','  A well trodden path winds its way through the forest.  There is a slight\nincline to the path in the westerly direction.  Birds chirp in the canopy\nabove.  The path continues to the north, east, and west.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3404,-39,9,-1,'A Fallen Tree','A huge ancient tree has succumbed to age and fallen across the path blocking\nany further movement in the westerly direction.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3405,-36,9,-1,'A Well Worn Path through the Forest','  This well trodden path takes a curve around an old tree and heads off to\nthe west or north.  A few branches drop down far enough to pick a large\nleaf from the tree.  A faint sound of water may be heard far off to the\nsouthwest.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3406,-38,10,-1,'A Well Worn Path in the Forest','  A well trodden path winds its way through the forest.  Birds chirp in the\nlush canopy overhead.  A slight breeze rustles the leaves on the trees.  The\npath continues to the north and south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3407,-36,10,-1,'A Well Trodden Path in the Forest','  A well trodden path winds its way through the forest.  A faint sound of\nrunning water can be heard far off to the south.  The path continues south\nand off to the north you can see an intersection.  To the west you see a\nlarge boulder.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3408,-38,11,-1,'A Well Worn Path in the Forest','  A well trodden path idles along between the trees, brushes, and brambles.\nHigh above, birds sing songs in their hidden branches.   The path leads off\nto the south, and to the east.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3409,-37,11,-1,'A Well Used Path in the Woods','  A well trodden path winds its way through the forest.  A rustling of some\ncreature foraging in the background can be heard.  The wind blows fallen\nleaves across the path.  The path continues to the north, east, and west.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3410,-36,11,-1,'A Well Worn Path in the Forest','  A well trodden path winds its way through the forest.  The path splits\noff to the east, west, and south.  To the north, the trees crowd together\nand impede movement.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3411,-35,11,-1,'A Well Worn Path in the Forest','  A well worn path through the woods curves around some large trees.\nBrambles crowd the edges of the path, creating small vegetable fences.\nThe path continues to the west, and north.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3412,-37,12,-1,'A Worn Path through the Forest','  A well worn path wanders its way through the plush forest.  Small critters\nscurry up in the branches.  The occasional bird flutters by in a bursting of\nwings.  The path continues south and turns to the west.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3413,-35,12,-1,'A Twisting Path in the Forest','  The path twists and turns to avoid the many trees which grow here.  Bushes\ngrow near the path creating a natural barrier in any direction other than east\nand south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3414,-38,12,-1,'A Well Worn Path in the Forest','  A well worn path turns its way through the forest, thick with trees and\nother flora.  Small creatures may be heard overhead in the branches,\nchastising intruders.  The path leads off to the north and east\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3415,-38,13,-1,'A Well Worn Path in the Forest','  A well trodden path winds its way through the forest.  Large bushes block\nthe northern path, but the path continues off to the east west and south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3416,-34,12,-1,'A Twisting Path in the Forest','  The path twists and turns to avoid the many trees that are growing  in the\nvicinity.  Brushes grow thick, creating a natural barrier.  The path continues\noff to the north and west, while a smaller path may be seen to the south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3417,-34,11,-1,'A Small Path','  A smaller path that looks rarely used, turns north to east.  To the north a\nmuch larger path may be seen.  Large branches from nearby trees grow over the\npath forcing tall folk to duck occasionally.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3418,-33,11,-1,'A Blocked Path','  A tree has fallen across the pathway, blockading the way.  It appears\nthat whatever was on the other side has become very overgrown, and hasn\'t\nbeen used in a long time.  The ground near the tree seems to have been dug\nby some animal, maybe to create a burrow.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3419,-34,13,-1,'A Twisting Path in the Forest','  The path twists and turns around many a large tree growing in the vicinity.\nSome colorful flora of an unknown type break up the green-brown of the wood.\nThe path continues to the east and south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3420,-33,13,-1,'A Twisting Path in the Forest','  The path twists and turns around some trees threatening to block off the\npath entirely.  Bushes grow thick to the south, with a thorny wall.  The path\ncontinues to the north while a smaller path leads off to the east.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3421,-32,13,-1,'A Small Path','  A small path cuts through the thick forest, dodging many trees, whose\nbranches threaten to choke off the path entirely.  The path continues to the\neast and north.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3422,-31,13,-1,'End of a Small Path','  The small path ends as abruptly as it began.  There is a small clearing\nwith mossy ground.  Various bushes grow all around, As well as the ever\npresent tree.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3423,-32,14,-1,'End of the Path','  The small path end here as abruptly as they began,  The small clearing,\ncovered in moss, offers a nice respite, and could be a nice place to  break\ncamp.  Small animals rush back into the forest at the sound of intruders.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3424,-33,14,-1,'A Path in the Forest','  The path skirts a few bushes that threaten to overrun the path.  To the\nwest a larger path leads off into the wood.  The smaller path continues in a\nnortherly direction.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3425,-34,14,-1,'A Worn Path in the Forest','  The path seems to be fairly well trodden, with the occasional tree root\npoking up from the soil, trying to trip any careless passerbys.  Small birds\nflutter in and out of the brushes to the sides eating insects.  The path leads\noff to the east and west.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3426,-35,14,-1,'A Worn Path in the Wood','  The path seems fairly well trodden, with the occasional root poking up\nfrom the soil.  A couple larger stones are in the pathway, large enough to\nturn an ankle if stepped on wrong.  To the west there is a fairly close\ntogether clumping of trees, so the path turns to the south or to the east\nhere.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3427,-35,13,-1,'A Worn Path in the Wood','  The path seems fairly well trodden, with the occasional root poking up from\nthe soil.  A couple larger stones are in the pathway, large enough to turn an\nankle if stepped on wrong.  To the north there is a clumping of trees impeding\nmovement, forcing the path to turn around it.  The path turns off to the north\nand west.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3428,-36,13,-1,'A Worn Path in the Wood','  The path seems fairly well trodden, with the occasional root poking up from\nthe soil.  A couple larger stones are in the pathway, large enough to turn an\nankle if stepped on wrong.   There is a clumping of trees to the north\nimpeding movement, the path turns north to east here.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3429,-36,14,-1,'A Worn Path in the Wood','  The path seems fairly well trodden, with the occasional root poking up\nfrom the soil.  A couple larger stones are in the pathway, large enough to\nturn an ankle if stepped on wrong.  To the east there is a clumping of\ntrees impeding movement, forcing the path to turn south here, The path also\nleads off into the forest to the west.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3430,-37,14,-1,'A Well Worn Path in the Forest','  A well trodden path winds its way through the forest.  Large bushes block\nthe way west.  Far off to the west a few mountain tops may be seen through\nthe tops of the trees.  The path continues north or south.  A slightly less\nused path leads off to the east.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3431,-37,13,-1,'A Well Worn Path in the Forest','  A well trodden path winds its way through the forest.  A large rock hides\nunder some flora to the east.  The path turns from north to west  here.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3432,-33,15,-1,'A Small Path','  A small path traverses the forest here, it seems more used by animals\nthan by any large creatures.  The fauna closes in around the path, making\nit appear even smaller.  The trees close in and cut out all the light from\nabove.  The path continues to the north, while a larger path may be seen to\nthe south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3433,-33,16,-1,'A Small Path','  A small path traverses the forest here, it seems more used by animals\nthan by any large creatures.  The fauna closes in around the path, making\nit appear even smaller.  The trees close in and cut out all the light from\nabove.  The path continues to the north while a faint trail leads off to\nthe east.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3434,-32,16,-1,'A Faint Trail','  A faint trail in the woods twists and turns as if it was created by a\ncreature.  There seems to have been recent movement along the trail but\nthere are no prints of any sort.  There is a path back to the west, and\nthis faint trail continues to the east.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3435,-31,16,-1,'A Faint Trail','  A faint trail in the woods twists and turns as if it was created by a\ncreature.  There seems to have been recent movement along the trail but\nthere are no prints of any sort.  The trail continues to the west, north,\nand south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3436,-31,15,-1,'A Faint Trail','  A faint trail in the woods twists and turns as if it was created by a\ncreature.  There seems to have been recent movement along the trail but\nthere are no prints of any sort.  The trail continues to the north and east.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3437,-30,15,-1,'A Burrow','  The faint trail that has been winding through the forest ends abruptly at a\nlarge dug out hole, most likely the home of some mid-sized animal.  Scrapes\nmark the trees nearby, as if something was marking its territory.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3438,-31,17,-1,'A Faint Trail','  A faint trail in the woods twists and turns as if it was created by a\ncreature.  There seems to have been recent movement along the trail but there\nare no prints of any sort.  The trail continues to the north and south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3439,-31,18,-1,'A Faint Trail','  A faint trail in the woods twists and turns as if it was created by a\ncreature.  There seems to have been recent movement along the trail but there\nare no prints of any sort.  The trail continues to the west and south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3440,-32,18,-1,'A Faint Path','  A faint trail in the woods twists and turns as if it was created by a\ncreature.  There seems to have been recent movement along the trail but there\nare no prints of any sort.  The trail continues to the east and west.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3441,-33,18,-1,'A Small Path','  A small path meanders in the forest.  It seems more used by various\nanimals than by any larger creatures.  Trees cover the eastern landscape in\na myriad of types.  There are paths leading off to the north south and east.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3442,-33,17,-1,'A Small Path','  A small path meanders in the forest.  It seems more used by various\nanimals than by any larger creatures.  Trees cover the eastern landscape in\na myriad of types.  The small path leads north or south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3443,-33,19,-1,'A Small Path','  A small path meanders in the forest.  Trees are growing closer and closer\nshrinking the path even further, There does not seem to be any activity using\nthis path other than the normal nature creatures.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3444,-33,20,-1,'A Small Path','  A small path twists in the forest.  Multiple critters scurry into the\nsafety of the wood.  Strange fauna gild some of the large trees.  The path\nsplits east to west and south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3445,-32,20,-1,'A Curvy Path in the Wood','  A small faint curving path traverses the wood.  Roots from the nearby\ntrees attempt to trip up feet.  Many branches cover the path, making\nwalking difficult.  The air is damp and clammy here, and large mushrooms\ngrow on the tree trunks.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3446,-32,21,-1,'A Curvy Path in the Wood','  A small faint curving path traverses the wood.  Branches hang low\nsnagging on just about everything, and roots grow high, tripping anything\nfoolish enough to walk the area.  The air is moist and clammy,  almost\nthick enough to be cut with a knife.  The path curves east and south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3447,-31,21,-1,'A Muddy Swamp','  The trail ends abruptly in a very wet, very muddy, and rather ominous\nlooking swamp.  Thick gas rises from the muck, choking the air.  A\nmultitude of bugs swarm the area feasting on anything and everything.  The\nground attempts to suck everything down to the bottom of its depths.  The\nonly feasible way to go is to the west.\n',26,131072,27,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3448,-34,20,-1,'A Small Path','  A small path twist and turns in the forest.  Hidden animals stop\nchattering when something draws near.  Once in a while a bird will panic\nand fly off into the distance.  The path continues to the south, and a\nlight path heads of to the north.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3449,-34,21,-1,'A Light Trail','  A faint path skitters around the trees, as if some animal used it many\ntimes to find food.  There are a few scrapes on the trees, probably deer\nmarkings, or some other animals.  The trees cut off most of the sunlight.\nThe path goes off to the east or north, while a larger path may be seen to\nthe south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3450,-33,21,-1,'A Small Pond','  The trail ends at a small pond, deep in the woods.  Another place for\nanimals to get water, instead of always traversing back to the river.  The\noccasional fish jumps out of the mostly calm water, grasping at some insect\nflying overhead.  The path leads back to the west.\n',26,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3451,-34,22,-1,'A Hollow Tree','  The faint path ends at a large tree with a very large hole in it.  The\naperture is large enough to lean inside and look, but not quite large\nenough to fully enter.  There are bones around the area as if something was\nusing this as a den or home of some type.  The path leads back to the south.\n',26,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3452,-34,19,-1,'A Small Path','  A small path idles its way in the forest.  Trees attempt to crowd her with\ntheir branches etc.  Strange sounds may be heard coming from nearby bushes.\nProbably animals of some sort or another hiding from intruders.  The light is\nall but cut off from the area due to the many high trees.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3453,-35,19,-1,'A Small Path','  A small path makes its way around some thick bushes, threatening to slice\nto the bone with their thorns.  The air here seems heavier, or just maybe a\nbit more humid, but overall more oppressive.  The path continues to the\neast and west.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3454,-36,19,-1,'A Small Path','  A small path winds around some rock clusters, of which more appear off to\nthe south.  The sun breaks through the leaves occasionally when the wind\nblows.  The path continues east and west, while a faint path leads south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3455,-36,18,-1,'An Outcropping of Rocks','  The path ends at a outcropping of rocks probably about 10 feet tall at\nthe highest point.  There are about 5 stones combined in this\nconglomeration in such a way that they have held themselves together over\nthe years.  The openings between the stones could be used by animals\navoiding larger creatures.  The path leads back to the north.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3456,-37,19,-1,'A Narrow Trail in the Forest','The trail is hedged in on the western side by a boulder and some brushes\ngrowing around it.  Small birds chatter about and then vanish.  The path\ncontinues to the north and south, while another path leads off to the east.\n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3457,-37,20,-1,'A Narrow Trail in the Forest','  A narrow trail winds its way through the forest.  The usual noises that\nseem to have accompanied the forest have gone quiet, it\'s very unnerving.\nThe trees themselves stand straight, but almost as if afraid to move.  The\npath continues to the north and south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3458,-37,21,-1,'A Narrow Trail in the Forest','  The narrow trail stops abruptly in a large clearing.  The moss seems to\nhave been trampled, and the air is dead still.  Not a sound may be heard,\nstrange considering how noisy it has been.  The clearing continues to the\neast, while there is an opening to a large cave to the west.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3459,-36,21,-1,'A Large Clearing','  The forest folds back to a large clearing, covered in moss.  The moss\nappears to have been recently trampled by some very heavy creature.  With\nthe trees not blocking the sky.  Some mountains may be seen off to the\nsouthwest.  It is very strange the deathly quiet that hangs in the area.\n',26,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3460,-38,21,-1,'A Large Cave in the Forest','  The inside of this cave is huge, at least 25-30 feet high.  The nature of\nthe cave warps sounds, and it sounds like a constant heavy breathing is\noccurring.  The walls are covered in what could be dried blood, and the\nfloor is caked with bones.  Something lives here, and it looks quite\nstrong.\n',26,133128,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(3461,-37,18,-1,'A Path in the Wood','  The medium sized path circles around a small pond in the woods.  The\npond, to the southwest, is crystal clear, and is deep enough that the\nbottom can not be seen.  A few water plants may be seen, of beautiful\ncolor.  Ducks swim on the surface occasionally coming close to the shore to\ndry off.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3462,-38,18,-1,'A Path Around the Pond','  The path circles the pond which is to the southeast.  There are many\nhoof/paw prints of various animals that have come to parch their thirst.\nBeautiful flora grows near the waters edge, enticing a second look.  The\npath continues around the pond to the east and south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3463,-38,17,-1,'A Path around the Pond','  The path circles the pond which is to the northeast.  There are many\nhoof/paw prints of various animals which come here to drink.  Beautiful\nflowers grow near the waters edge enticing a second look.  The path\ncontinues around the pond to the north and east.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3464,-37,17,-1,'A Path in the Wood','  The medium sized path circles around a small pond in the woods.  The\npond, to the northeast is crystal clear, and is deep enough that the bottom\ncan not be seen.  A few water plants may be seen, of beautiful color.\nDucks swim on the surface occasionally coming close to the shore to dry off.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3465,-37,16,-1,'A Medium Sized Path in the Wood','  A medium sized path makes its way through the dense forest.  Birds may be\nheard chattering above in the tree tops.  The path continues to the north and\nwest, while a larger path is seen to the south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3466,-38,16,-1,'A Medium Sized Path in the Wood','  This medium sized path has a slight incline towards the west.  Through the\ntree tops, off to the west mountains may be seen.  The ground is  more rocky\nthan the usual, threatening to turn an ankle.  The path  continues to the east\nand west.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3467,-39,16,-1,'A Medium Sized Path in the Wood','  The path winds its way around some rocks.  There is a slant downwards to\nthe east, and it seems to be the base of some hill.  Through the tree tops\nbeautiful mountains to the west can be seen.  The path continues to the east\nand south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3468,-39,15,-1,'A Medium Sized Path in the Wood','  The path winds its way through the forest avoiding various trees and rocks.\nThe incline heading up to the west, down to the east, makes walking difficult.\nBeautiful mountains may be seen to the west through the tree tops.  The\noccasional bird flutters by in a hurry to go somewhere.  The path continues to\nthe north and south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3469,-39,14,-1,'A Medium Sized Path in the Wood','  The path winds its way through the forest avoiding various trees and rocks.\nThe incline heading up to the west, down to the east, makes walking difficult.\nBeautiful mountains may be seen to the west through the tree tops.  The\noccasional bird flutters by in a hurry to go somewhere.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3470,-39,13,-1,'A Medium Sized Path in the Wood','  The path winds its way through the forest avoiding various trees and rocks.\nThe incline heading up to the west, down to the east, makes walking difficult.\nBeautiful mountains may be seen to the west through the tree tops.  A few\nanimals scurry to shelter at the sound of visitors.  The path continues to the\neast and north.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3471,-37,15,-1,'A Well Worn Path in the Forest','  A well trodden path winds its way through the forest.  Large bushes block\nthe way west.  Far off to the west a few mountain tops may be seen through\nthe tops of the trees.  The path continues north or south.\n',26,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3472,-34,18,-1,'A Clearing','  A hidden clearing in the forest, which has seen some use in the recent\npast, judging by the few recent broken shrubs and other plants near the\nedges of the clearing.  Something or someone was here recently but its\nimpossible to tell why.\n',26,131076,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3473,-35,18,-1,'A Hidden Clearing','  A clearing, hidden from the rest of the forest, lies surrounded by many\ntrees and shrubs.  To the east, another clearing may be seen.  There is a\ntree in the center of the clearing with its branches offering some peaceful\nshade, almost a respite from the rest of the wood.  It seems very quiet here.\n',26,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3474,-35,17,-1,'A Sacred Grove','  A beautiful sacred grove hidden deep within the woods.  Strong trees grow\nalong the outside of the large grove, as a barrier to the outside wood.\nThere appears to have been some recent use, as if some recent ritual to the\ndeities of nature has occurred.  The grove continues to the east, west, and\nsouth.\n',26,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3475,-36,17,-1,'A Sacred Grove','  A beautiful sacred grove hidden deep within the woods.  Strong trees grow\nalong the outside of the large grove, as a barrier to the outside wood.  There\nappears to have been some recent use, as if some recent ritual to the deities\nof nature has occurred.  The grove continues to the east and south.\n',26,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3476,-36,16,-1,'A Sacred Grove','  A beautiful sacred grove hidden deep within the woods.  Strong trees grow\nalong the outside of the large grove, as a barrier to the outside wood.  There\nappears to have been some recent use, as if some recent ritual to the deities\nof nature has occurred.  The grove continues to the north, east,  and south.\n',26,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3477,-36,15,-1,'A Sacred Grove','  A beautiful sacred grove hidden deep within the woods.  Strong trees grow\nalong the outside of the large grove, as a barrier to the outside wood.  There\nappears to have been some recent use, as if some recent ritual to the deities\nof nature has occurred.  The grove continues to the north and east.\n',26,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3478,-35,15,-1,'A Sacred Grove','  A beautiful sacred grove hidden deep within the woods.  Strong trees grow\nalong the outside of the large grove, as a barrier to the outside wood.  There\nappears to have been some recent use, as if some recent ritual to the deities\nof nature has occurred.  The grove continues to the north, west, and east.\n',26,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3479,-34,15,-1,'A Sacred Grove','  A beautiful sacred grove hidden deep within the woods.  Strong trees grow\nalong the outside of the large grove, as a barrier to the outside wood.  There\nappears to have been some recent use, as if some recent ritual to the deities\nof nature has occurred.  The grove continues to the north and west.\n',26,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3480,-34,16,-1,'A Sacred Grove','  A beautiful sacred grove hidden deep within the woods.  Strong trees grow\nalong the outside of the large grove, as a barrier to the outside wood.  There\nappears to have been some recent use, as if some recent ritual to the deities\nof nature has occurred.  The grove continues to the north west and south.\n',26,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3481,-34,17,-1,'A Sacred Grove','  A beautiful sacred grove hidden deep within the woods.  Strong trees grow\nalong the outside of the large grove, as a barrier to the outside wood.  There\nappears to have been some recent use, as if some recent ritual to the deities\nof nature has occurred.  The grove continues to the west and south.\n',26,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3482,-35,16,-1,'The Center of the Grove','  This is the center of a beautiful sacred grove.  Tall trees line the\nfringes of the grove in a natural wall.  There is an incredibly large\nancient  tree in the direct center, spanning at least 7 feet in diameter.\nThe area has seen recent use, probably some ceremony to the elder deities.\n',26,133280,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3700,69,-13,0,'The Logrus Town Dump','  You have entered the town dump.  There isn\'t much to say except that you\ncan see trash for miles and miles.  My those piles of garbage are big.\n',27,139264,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3701,73,-14,0,'Logrus Center','  You are standing in the town center of Logrus.  The commotion here is very\nloud as various people of all races walk about.  In one corner, you hear some\ngoblins gossiping, and from the side of the center, a dark elf flashes you a\nwary look.  Far to both the east and west can be seen the large iron-wrought\ngates of this dark town.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3702,73,-13,0,'North Logrus Plaza','  You stand in the area which circles around the town center.  Various\nmysterious people walk around looking busy.  Some of the darker ones with hoods\nput your nerves on end.  You quickly reach down and find that your money-purse\nis still there.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3703,73,-12,0,'North Deadman\'s Walk','  You stand upon a long, black and broken path.  The cobblestones which once\nfilled this grand street are now loose and strewn about in a state of serious\ndisrepair.  You can hear a great deal of noise rising from the south where you\nsee the plaza.  To the north you see various shops, and a dark field off to the\nfar northwest.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3704,73,-11,0,'North Deadman\'s Walk','  You stand upon a long, black and broken path.  The cobblestones which\nonce filled this grand street are now loose and strewn about in a state of\nserious disrepair.  A large tower suddenly rises to the north and a small\nhouse to the east.  You wonder why you didn\'t see them before...\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3705,73,-10,0,'Entrance to the Black Tower of Sorcery','You have entered the base of the black tower.  As you look about, this room\nseems to be very well maintained.  Rich tapestries adorn the walls, thick\ncarpets line the floor, and lavish furniture rests about the room.  The walls\nthemselves seem to be constructed of a pitch black rock to a mirror finish;\nthese walls weren\'t made with any tools.  A large flight of stairs rests\nagainst the far wall, ascending higher into the tower.\n',0,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3706,73,-10,1,'Mage\'s Guild Room','  You have entered what appears to be a very large room, used for a variety of\npurposes.  Various shelves adorn the walls, filled with bottles of things\narcane.  Bookcases line the walls presenting their wares of books in rows upon\nrows of black leather display.  Obviously, this room is intended only for those\nof the Art.  If you have come here for any purpose other than training, beware!\n',27,174268,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3707,72,-11,0,'A Broken Path','  You are standing upon a broken dirt path, with rocks and boulders strewn all\nabout.  A few barren trees line the road as it leads towards the northwest\nwhere you see what appears to be some sort of graveyard.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3708,71,-10,0,'Cemetery','  You have entered a large cemetery.  As you turn to look back towards town,\ngrey mists swirl all around you and obscure your vision.  Various tombstones\ndot the scene, providing for a rather jagged scenery.  A rickety black\niron fence surrounds the cemetery with rotting and decayed vegetation\nintertwined within it.  An opening through the fence is to the southeast and\nwhat looks like a break in the fence is to the west as well, but it\nseems several tombstones have collapsed in a heap blocking that path.\n',27,174260,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3709,77,-13,0,'Maleck\'s Materials','  The shop you now stand in is very messy, and cluttered.  Goods are\nstrewn about with no evident organization.  The floor is littered with\ndebris, and you begin to wonder if this is a place you would like to do\nbusiness in.  The walls are bare, and the stench of cigars fills the\nthe air, smelling slightly less putrid than Maleck himself.\n',28,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3710,72,-13,0,'Northwest Logrus Plaza','  You stand in the area which circles around the town center.  Various\nmysterious people walk around looking busy.  Some of the darker ones with hoods\nput your nerves on end.  You quickly reach down and find that your money-purse\nis still there.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3711,72,-14,0,'West Logrus Plaza','  You stand in the area which circles around the town center.  Various\nmysterious people walk around looking busy.  Some of the darker ones with hoods\nput your nerves on end.  You quickly reach down and find that your money-purse\nis still there.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3712,72,-15,0,'Southwest Logrus Plaza','  You stand in the area which circles around the town center.  Various\nmysterious people walk around looking busy.  Some of the darker ones with hoods\nput your nerves on end.  You quickly reach down to find that your money-purse\nis still there.  Set in the middle of the street is a large man-hole\ncover.  To the south lies the side of a large manor house.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3713,73,-15,0,'South Logrus Plaza','  You stand in the area which circles around the town center.  Various\nmysterious people walk around looking busy.  Some of the darker ones with hoods\nput your nerves on end.  You quickly reach down and find that your money-purse\nis still there.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3714,74,-15,0,'Southeast Logrus Plaza','  You stand in the area which circles around the town center.  Various\nmysterious people walk around looking busy.  Some of the darker ones with hoods\nput your nerves on end.  You quickly reach down and find that your money-purse\nis still there.  The side of a large manor house can be seen just to the\nsouth.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3715,74,-14,0,'East Logrus Plaza','  You stand in the area which circles around the town center.  Various\nmysterious people walk around looking busy.  Some of the darker ones with hoods\nput your nerves on end.  You quickly reach down and find that your money-purse\nis still there.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3716,74,-13,0,'Northeast Logrus Plaza','  You stand in the area which circles around the town center.  Various\nmysterious people walk around looking busy.  Some of the darker ones with hoods\nput your nerves on end.  You quickly reach down and find that your money-purse\nis still there.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3717,75,-14,0,'Road of Deviance','  You are standing on a large and poorly kept road in the town of Logrus.\nVarious rocks, some the size of boulders, line the street.  The town center lies\nwest, and a large iron gate safe keeps the walls of the town to the east.\nTo the south a sign hangs over an open doorway.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3718,76,-14,0,'Road of Deviance','  This is not the best road you have ever traveled.  Various potholes fill the\nstreet, and nobody seems to care.  The town center lies west, while the eastern\ngates rise up in the east.  To the north you can see a glowing shop.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3719,77,-14,0,'Road of Deviance','  This is not the best road you have ever traveled.  Various potholes fill\nthe street, and nobody seems to care.  The town center lies west, while\nthe eastern gates rise up in the east.  From the south you smell an aroma\nof freshly baked goods.  This great smell is almost drowned by the stench\ncoming from the shop to the north.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3720,78,-14,0,'Inside the East Gate of Logrus','  You are standing just inside the eastern town gates.  Something eerie begins\ntingling your neck, but you can\'t quite place your finger on it.  The guards\nlook over at you warily from on the battlements, and then go back to their\npost.  As you look towards the gates themselves, they are wrought of pure iron,\nwith a large oaken beam barring entrance.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3721,71,-14,0,'Road of Deviance','  You are standing on a large and poorly kept road in the town of Logrus.\nVarious rocks, some the size of boulders, line the street.  The town center lies\neast, and a large iron gate safe keeps the walls of the town to the west.\nA run down looking building sits to the south with the word \"Inn\" painted\nover the door.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3722,70,-14,0,'Road of Deviance','  You are standing on a large poorly kept road in the town of Logrus.  Standing\nis a poor term; you almost fell into a hole the size of a large crater!  To the\nnorth you see a shop, the town center lies east, and a large iron gate\nsafe keeps the walls of the town to the west.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3723,69,-14,0,'Road of Deviance','  This road is not in very good condition, with divets, holes, and rocks lying\nscattered about.  You think about asking the mayor to get it fixed up sometime,\nbut in a town like this, you begin to wonder if it would do any good.  You\nthink you can make out what appears to be a small side street heading south\ninto an older section of town.  There is an old street sign here.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3724,68,-14,0,'Inside the West Gate of Logrus','  You are standing just inside the western town gates.  Something eerie begins\ntingling your neck, but you can\'t quite place your finger on it.  The guards\nlook over at you warily from on the battlements, and then go back to their\npost.  As you look towards the gates themselves, they are wrought of pure iron,\nwith a large oaken beam barring entrance.  A building stands to the north.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3725,73,-16,0,'South Deadman\'s Walk','  This is a strange path indeed.  An eerie breeze blows from nowhere in\nparticular; strange since you are inside a town.  You are accosted by strange\nthoughts that leave you feeling used and confused.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3726,73,-17,0,'Dread Square','  You have entered a large square in the southern portion of town.  Several dead\ntrees line the street here, and not even a songbird seems willing to inhabit\nthem.  This section of the street actually seems to be in decent shape as the\ncobblestones are still in place.  A large signpost stands by the side of the\nstreet here.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3727,75,-15,0,'Mo\'mar\'s Armory','  You have entered a rather stuffy shop, the heat emanating from a forge\nlocated in the back room.  As you look about, your eyes gather in a large\ncollection of armors and protective gear of every sort.  In the back of the\nroom is a large wooden counter.  A doorway leads to the street north of\nhere or a small set of stairs ascends to a room overhead.  A small sign\nhangs at the base of the stairs.\n',27,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3728,75,-15,1,'Rogar\'s Hack \'n\' Slash','You enter a dimly lit shop which has a strong smell of iron.  Weapons of all\nshape and size glint upon the walls in a shimmering array of lethality.  Glass\ncabinets adorn the room, etched with illegible graffiti.  A small set of\nsteps lead downwards to the buildings ground floor.\n',-1,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3729,74,-17,0,'A Dark Alley','  You have entered a dark alley which winds its way between the back walls of\nseveral brick buildings.  Nothing seems to stir here, but an uneasy feeling\ncomes over you; you quickly glance behind you to find nothing there.  You begin\nto wonder if this is the safest place to be...\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3730,75,-17,0,'A Dark Alley','  You stand in the middle of a back alley.  Trash dots the scene, and a sudden\ngust of wind blows papers all about.  A few figures hunch behind broken crates\nand barrels.  You wonder how many of them are really nothing more than bums.\nYou reach down to find your money-purse still there.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3731,76,-17,0,'A Dead End','  You have reached the end of a back alley.  You don\'t like the looks of this\nplace very much.  There are no windows in the walls which surround you, and the\nonly escape is back west.  Several figures hunch together in one corner and eye\nyou warily.  Glancing about, you also notice a manhole cover which probably\nleads into the town sewer system.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3732,72,-17,0,'Warrior\'s Path','  You are walking upon a very drab street.  Dust blows by as you look about,\nand there isn\'t really much of anything to be seen.  To the north and south you\nsee the back walls of buildings and houses, and further to the west you can see\nthe walls of the town arena rising before you.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3733,71,-17,0,'Warrior\'s Path','  You are walking upon a very drab street.  Dust blows by as you look about,\nand there isn\'t really much of anything to be seen.  To the north a run\ndown looking structure has been constructed from various relocated\nshacks.  To the south you see the back walls of buildings and houses, and\nfurther to the west you can see the walls of the town arena rising before\nyou.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3734,70,-17,0,'Entrance to the Arena','  You are standing before the large walls of the town arena.  From inside you\ncan hear the clashing sounds of battle and contest.  The street ends here at\nthe main gate of the arena.  To the south a filthy little stone building\nsits, a loud chorus of various animal howls coming from within.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3735,69,-18,0,'The Arena','  You have entered an arena of decent size, although not very large in its\nentirety.  You can see various figures about the place sparring off and\nsometimes dueling.  Several blood stains dot the floor and you begin to\nreconsider your presence here.\n',27,174260,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3736,72,-12,0,'The Logrus Hospital','  You have entered a ward of the hospital designated to treat the sick and ill.\nVarious implements fill the room, obviously used for care of patients.  Feel\nfree to rest here to restore your strength, but don\'t be surprised when you\nreceive the doctor\'s bill.\n',27,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,19,'',NULL),
(3737,70,-18,0,'Half-Ear\'s Pet Place','  Amazing, almost everything in this tiny little shop is covered\ntop to bottom with furs of every kind.  Fox, wolf, deer, anything,\nit appears the owner is quite the trapper.  Near the center of the\nroom a large clear spot shows itself to be a huge heavy grate set\ninto the floor over some pit.\n',31,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3738,0,0,0,'Kludge\'s Pet Pit','  Looking incredibly filthy and unkempt this is the Pit where Kludge\nkeeps his trapped animals.  Cages and hooks line the walls while\nother animals roam about or are tied securely to anchors.  A thick\nlayer of animal feces and urinal mixed coats the floor and walls\nappearing quite disgusting to the casual observer.  The animals\nthemselves appear rather healthy despite their living conditions\nand large bones about the room suggest they are at least well fed.\n',31,166075,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3739,74,-16,0,'A Nobleman\'s Manor','  You have entered a large and lavishly decorated manor.  Various treasures and\nheirlooms fill the walls, sparkling at you approach.  As you look closer, you\nnotice a few of them are damaged and cracked.  Obviously, they aren\'t being well\ntaken care of.  Then you begin to ponder something strange; all of these items\nare mismatched and out of place.  They certainly didn\'t all come from the same\nplace, and judging by what you know of this town, they have got to be the\nspoils of war.\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3740,72,-16,0,'A Nobleman\'s Manor','  You have entered a large and lavishly decorated manor.  Various treasures and\nheirlooms fill the walls, sparkling at your approach.  As you look closer, you\nnotice a few of them are damaged and cracked.  Obviously, they aren\'t being well\ntaken care of.  Then you begin to ponder something strange; all of these items\nare mismatched and out of place.  They certainly didn\'t all come from the same\nplace, and judging by what you know of this town, they have got to be the\nspoils of war.\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3741,77,-15,0,'Rednow\'s Bread Shop','  As you enter this small shop, the smell of freshly baked bread assails your\nsenses.  From behind various glass counters, although dinged and marred, you\ncan see an assortment of baked goods.\n',27,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3742,76,-13,0,'Nekcihc\'s Magic Emporium','  You have entered a quaint little shop.  It seems to be well kept up compared\nto the rest of this town.  But the room is totally cluttered! Various crates,\ncages, boxes, and barrels fill the entire room.  Your nose detects a faint\nspicy smell, the smell of things magical and arcane.  Peering around all this\nclutter, you can see a desk in the back of the room.\n',27,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3743,70,-13,0,'Hsif\'s General Store','You have entered a large general store it would appear.  Various storage\nbarrels and crates fill the room, racks display their wares, and tools hang\nfrom the walls.  In the back is a large dark counter with a large sign affixed\nto its front-center.\n',-1,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3744,73,-18,0,'South Deadman\'s Walk','  This is a strange path indeed.  An eerie breeze blows from nowhere in\nparticular; strange since you are inside a town.  You are accosted by strange\nthoughts that leave you feeling used and confused.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3745,73,-19,0,'South Deadman\'s Walk','  This is a strange path indeed.  An eerie breeze blows from nowhere in\nparticular; strange since you are inside a town.  You are accosted by strange\nthoughts that leave you feeling used and confused.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3746,74,-19,0,'Darmak Road','  You are currently standing upon a road which seems to be in very good\ncondition.  Looking about everything seems new as if this road was just\nrecently added.  Nothing seems out of the ordinary as this cobbled road leads\neastwards towards a large black building at the end of the street.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3747,74,-18,0,'A Nobleman\'s Manor','  You have entered a large and lavishly decorated manor.  Various treasures and\nheirlooms fill the walls, sparkling at your approach.  As you look closer, you\nnotice a few of them are damaged and cracked.  Obviously, they aren\'t being well\ntaken care of.  Then you begin to ponder something strange; all of these items\nare mismatched and out of place.  They certainly didn\'t all come from the same\nplace, and judging by what you know of this town, they have got to be the\nspoils of war.\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3748,72,-18,0,'A Nobleman\'s Manor','  You have entered a large and lavishly decorated manor.  Various treasures and\nheirlooms fill the walls, sparkling at your approach.  As you look closer, you\nnotice a few of them are damaged and cracked.  Obviously, they aren\'t being well\ntaken care of.  Then you begin to ponder something strange; all of these items\nare mismatched and out of place.  They certainly didn\'t all come from the same\nplace, and judging by what you know of this town, they have got to be the\nspoils of war.\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3749,74,-21,0,'The Mayor\'s Office','  You have entered the office of the mayor of Logrus.  There isn\'t much to be\nsaid about this place.  The room is rather dull and the only items of note are\na few plaques which precariously hang from the walls.  Obviously, this place\nreflects the lax attitude with which the town officials approach Logrus.\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3750,76,-15,0,'A Dark Alley','  You have entered a dark back-alley.  Nothing seems to thrive here, save the\nunused and unwanted elements of this town.  You warily peer behind your back,\nand a sudden draft of cold air sends shivers up and down you spine.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3751,76,-16,0,'A Dark Alley','  You stand at a turning point in a dark alley.  Looking up, all you see is a\nclouded sky and blank brick walls staring back down at you.  No windows open\nupon this alley to witness whatever events may occur down here.  Refuse lines\nthe street, and the unfortunate join the refuse here in comfort.  The alley\nitself turns to the east where it disappears into the darkness.\n',27,139272,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3752,75,-16,0,'A Dead End','  You have reached a dead-end in a back alley.  Glancing around, the only\nescape route is back east between the brick walls.  Garbage and refuse fill the\nstreet, covering everything.  You begin to get the feeling that maybe you\nshould leave this place quickly.\n',27,139272,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3753,71,-13,0,'The Emergency Room','  Here you can purchase expert medical attention which can remedy almost any\nailment instantly.\n',27,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3754,75,-13,1,'Logrus Sharpener','  A giant whetstone fills one side of the room.  Sparks fly from it as\nthe sharpener repairs damaged blades.  A set of rickety stairs lead\ndownward from the room to the repair shop below.\n',27,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3755,74,-12,0,'The Logrus Bank','You have entered a room which is moderately furnished.  Various windows line\nthe back wall along a large counter.  Each of these windows appears to be\nbarred, and bank tellers stand behind them ready to assist you.\n',-1,174265,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,7,'',NULL),
(3756,71,-12,0,'The Logrus Hospital Waiting Room','  You are standing within a moderately decorated room filled with tables and\nchairs.  Upon seeing you enter, a husky looking nurse jabs a finger at a\nsign-in sheet which seems to be a mile long.  Looking around, the only thing of\ninterest seems to be the various books which lie scattered about the tables.\nTitles such as \"Logrus and You\" and \"Brightmoon Women\" catch your eye.\n',27,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3757,75,-19,0,'Darmak Road','  You have reached the end of this small street and stand before a large black\nbuilding.  Looking upon its glossy obsidian face, you feel nothing but dread\nemanating from within.  Several large demon-like statues stare down at you from\nthe roof, and the ground about your feet feel deathly cold.  Two double-doors\nlead inside.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3758,0,0,0,'Guild of Dark Power','  You have entered a guild who\'s purpose serves the vilest powers of evil.\nVarious implements of destruction and chaos hang from the walls, and in the\nback of the room you can see an altar the color of blood.  You\'re filled with a\nsense of dread and have a sudden desire to flee this accursed place.\n',27,131085,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3759,73,-20,0,'South Deadman\'s Walk','  This is a strange path indeed.  An eerie breeze blows from nowhere in\nparticular; strange since you are inside a town.  You are accosted by strange\nthoughts that leave you feeling used and confused.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3760,73,-21,0,'South Deadman\'s Walk','This is a strange path indeed.  An eerie breeze blows from nowhere in\nparticular - strange since you are inside a town.  You are accosted by strange\nthoughts that leave you feeling used and confused.  Towards the south a large\ntemple begins to rise out of the distance.  Directly to the east is an office.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3761,73,-22,0,'Before The Dark Temple','  You stand before a large dark building which is shaped like a pyramid.\nApparently, it serves as the town hall and as a gathering place for other\npurposes unmentionable.  Large double doors lead inside, while the street\ncontinues back off into the town to the north.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3762,73,-23,0,'Entrance To Logrus Hall','  You stand in the entryway to Logrus\'s town hall, where the town council\ndecides what to do and not to do(usually not).  It looks as if they might not\nbe meeting here much longer, because it doesn\'t seem as if they fix the hall\nmuch either.  The walls are crumbling and there are not many of the onyx tiles\nleft on the floor.\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3763,74,-24,0,'Passage to the Council Chamber','  This is the passage leading to where the Logrus council meets.  Here the\nwalls, floor and ceiling are in good repair.  They look as if they are kept\nsturdy by magical means.\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3764,72,-24,0,'Passage to the Council Chambers','  This is the passage leading to where the Logrus council meets.  Here the\nwalls, floor and ceiling are in good repair.  They look as if they are kept\nsturdy by magical means.\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3765,73,-25,0,'Council Chamber','  You have entered a large chamber whose walls rise upwards into oblivion.\nLooking upwards in the direction of the walls, you cannot detect any sign of a\nceiling; just a swirling mass of darkness.  Tapestries of scenes depicting\nevil\'s triumph over good adorn the various walls, and a large circular table\nfills the center of the room.\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3767,73,-24,0,'The Vault','  This is a small hidden antechamber off the main council room.  It is here\nthat the council keeps its large treasury.\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3768,0,0,0,'Logrus Shipping Office','  This building houses the Logrus office of Cobra Shipping Ltd.,\nthe largest organized shipping firm in all the realms.  The shipping\noffice is in a state of constant turmoil, with people coming and\ngoing at all hours of the day or night, both to drop off things for\nshipment to another city or to pick up merchandise which arrived on\nthe latest caravan.  The room itself is tastefully done in light\nwood paneling, with a hard stone floor.  A large counter in the\ncenter of the room serves as a drop off and pick up point for\nmerchandise.\n',0,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3770,71,-16,0,'The Tavern of the Beast','  You have stumbled into what appears to be the most run down, poorest excuse\nfor a tavern you have ever seen.  The tables are cluttered with filth, and the\nreek of stale ale fills your nostrils until you feel ill.  You hear an outburst\nof laughter coming from a group of orcs in the rear of the room.   To the\nnorth an archway appears to lead to an inn of some kind.  South of here is\na road or pathway of some sort.\n',27,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3771,71,-15,0,'Inn of the Beast','  You stand at the front desk of a worn down inn.  The walls are somewhat bare,\nand you can feel a slight draft wafting through the room.  You can see a long\nhallway of doors, apparently the rooms of the inn, where many a traveler have\nrested their tired bones.  Although, in a place like this, you don\'t think\nyou\'re gonna get much rest.  A door to the north apparently leads back out\nto the street while an archway at the end of the long hallway to the south\nappears to lead to a tavern of some sorts.\n',27,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3772,67,-14,0,'Outside the West Gate of Logrus','  You stand just outside a large, massive gate of a walled town.  The walls\nthemselves seem to be made of some dark volcanic rock, and nothing grows near\nthem.  From up on the battlements, you hear the voices of the town guard,\ndiscussing the latest plunder.  The gate itself is solid iron and very\nformidable.  The sudden crow of a passing raven puts your hair on end.\n',27,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3773,66,-14,0,'A Well Beaten Dirt Road','  You stand in the middle of a very dusty, and well traveled road.  It would\nappear a great deal of movement occurs on this road, mayhap the size of armies.\nJust to the east, the town walls of Logrus rise into the air, and the clouds\nbrood over them.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3774,75,-13,0,'Logrus Repair','  A big prominent sign hangs by the door.  The smell of ironworking\npermeates the air.  The wooden walls bear many nicks and cuts where\nsatisfied customers have tested out their newly repaired weapons.  A door\nto the south apparently leads out to the street while a small set of\nrickety steps ascend to a room overhead.\n',27,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3775,69,-15,0,'Abbadon Way','  You have arrived at a smaller side-street which cuts its way into a rather\nworn-down and beat-up section of town.  As you look about, various windows\nflicker dark images suspended in candlelight.  A few of the windows are broken,\nand the rest of the houses themselves don\'t look like they\'re in any condition\nto repel the elements.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3776,70,-15,0,'An Old Dilapidated House','  You have entered a home of meager worth.  Come to mention it, this place is a\nregular hovel!  Filth and grime adorn the walls in a gruesome display of\nneglect.  The stench that fills your nostrils is repulsive, and brings to\nthought one thing; orcs!\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3777,68,-15,0,'An Old Dilapidated House','  You have entered a home of meager worth.  Come to mention it, this place is a\nregular hovel!  Filth and grime adorn the walls in a gruesome display of\nneglect.  The stench that fills your nostrils is repulsive, and brings to\nthought one thing; orcs!\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3778,69,-16,0,'Abbadon Way','You have reached the end of a small alley where the pitiful excuses for\nhouses lean precariously towards you.  Shadows flicker in candlelight upon\nwindow panes, and thick smoke rises from half-tumbled chimneys.  The street\nitself is broken and covered in about an inch of murky water that flows\ninto a metal grate.\n',27,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3779,70,-16,0,'An Old Dilapidated House','You have entered a home of meager worth.  Come to mention it, this place is a\nregular hovel!  Filth and grime adorn the walls in a gruesome display of\nneglect.  The stench that fills your nostrils is repulsive, and brings to\nmind only one thing - ORCS!\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
