(3856,73,-6,-1,'An Ancient Shrine','  You stand before a large and majestic shrine dedicated to an unknown deity.\nA large idol rises before you surrounded by braziers of incense.  Several palm\nfronds have been placed in front of the idol, as well as a collection of\nflowers.\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3857,74,-7,-1,'A Ninja Training Room','  You have entered a room which apparently serves as a place of practice for\nthose of the art of ninjitsu.  Weapons are fastened to the walls, and combat is\npresent within the room as pupils train in front of their master.\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3858,72,-7,-1,'A Small Anteroom','  You have entered a small anteroom just off the side of the main hallway of\nthis shrine.  The room seems fairly common, save for a large potted plant which\nrests against the west wall, and a oriental calendar which hangs on the wall\nabove it.  Three doors exit the room to the north, south, and east.\n',27,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3859,72,-6,-1,'Wan Fu\'s Weapons','  You have entered a small room which apparently serves as a shop.  Various\nweapons of the art of ninjitsu adorn the walls and a glass counter which rests\nin the back of the room.\n',27,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3860,72,-8,-1,'Shei Lo\'s Armors','  You have entered a small room which apparently serves as a shop of sorts.\nAround the room and upon the walls you see various implements of the art of\nninjitsu.  Their black gleam catches your eye.\n',27,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3861,79,-14,0,'Outside the East Gate of Logrus','  You stand just outside a large, massive gate of a walled town.  The walls\nthemselves seem to be made of some dark volcanic rock, and nothing grows near\nthem.  From up on the battlements, you hear the voices of the town guard,\ndiscussing the latest plunder.  The gate itself is solid iron and very\nformidable.  The sudden crow of a passing raven puts your hair on end.\n',27,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3862,80,-14,0,'A Well Beaten Dirt Road','  You stand in the middle of a very dusty, and well traveled road.  It would\nappear a great deal of movement occurs on this road, mayhap the size of armies.\nJust to the west, the town walls of Logrus rise into the air, and the clouds\nbrood over them.  To the north, you see a trail through the bushes.\n',27,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3863,0,0,0,'Dimly Lit Chamber','  A wide array of bottles, carefully labeled fills the rooms tidy shelves.\nThere is also a silvery tray holding a clear decanter and a small round\nbottle of green liquid.  A workbench holds stacked boxes and lined bottles\nalso labeled with faded lettering.  In the southwest corner, a small black\naltar surrounded by dried skin, untanned bat fur, tiny bones and maggots\nstand before a grim fat statue of a demon. There is a little dinky stairwell\nleading downward.\n',20,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3864,74,-11,0,'Dimly Lit Shop','  A long counter with a bunch of dusty bins behind it fills the eastern \ncorner of this dimly lit shop.  A giant phoney replica of a holy symbol\nflashes neon in the window.\n',20,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3865,74,-12,0,'Logrus Tax Office','This somber room serves as the office of the Logrus tax collector, where all\ntaxes are received and tallied.\n',-1,174265,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3866,0,0,0,'Adrielz Chest','A neatly organized witchcraft store welcomes you from your ascent. As \nyou enter, you notice a small cloud of smoke emanating from burning rose petals \nand incense in a heated miniature cauldron. The smell is soothing as you take \nin the shelves and chests aligned orderly and labeled to present the fine \nwares this shop has to offer. Warding glyphs and runic symbols adorn the walls \nand ceiling surrounding you in a tapestry of magic while you shop.\n',34,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3867,0,0,0,'A Balcony Overlooking the City','Coming through the trapdoor, you are amazed at the scenery you now find \nyourself surrounded by. Not visible from the ground, there is a balcony atop \nthe shops below that overlooks the entire city. The spire of this twisted tower \nrises up behind you, peaking at the top of it\'s height. Off to the East, you \nsee more towering structures, and a bustling marketplace. There is another dark \ntower in the distance to the north, past the bank and the hospital. A few \npotted bamboo trees decorate the darkened stone handrail running the edge of \nthe balcony and back into the walls of the tower itself where a black door \nleads to the northwest. A large wooden rocking chair sits in the center of the \nstone floor here, creaking with the wind as it blows.\n',34,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3868,0,0,0,'The Top of the Twisted Tower','The howling of the wind up here is enough to drive a person insane. You \nstand atop the stairs in a small opening inside the tip of the twisting spire. \nA small stone rail protects you from falling over the edge, though in this \nwind, venturing too close to the handrail could be hazardous to one\'s health. \nThere is room to move around safely however, and pick which vantage to view the \ncity. The scene from this high is breathtaking, almost stretching to the ocean \nin the east, and to the west you can see to the foothills of the mighty \nSympathian Mountain range.\n',34,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3869,0,0,0,'Skull Duggory\'s ','As you enter through the door of this establishment, you are greeted by \nthe stench of decay. The putrid odor in the air makes you wonder what kind of \nskin they use for equipment here. Three walls are lined with racks full of \nwares, each piece stamped with the trademark skull and dagger of the \nproprietor. In the ceiling, there is a small black trapdoor emblazoned with The \nletter \' L \' encased in an upside down star with a crown perched on the top \nleft arm. All along the ceiling is a banner of skulls and daggers. \n',34,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3870,0,0,0,'A Balcony Overlooking the City ','Coming through the ceiling of the room below, you are amazed to find \nyourself standing in a recessed balcony, not visible from the street. Behind \nyou, the spire of a sleek, blood red tower rises into the sky. Looking past the \nred stone handrail in front of you, almost the whole city spreads out before \nyour eyes. The marketplace is bustling with life below, as is the town center. \nTo your west you see an evil looking structure, twisting into the sky, and to \nthe east, the dreaded temple of The Arch Vampire. The floor here is cold, \nfreezing cold, cold enough to make your soul shiver. A small black door leads \ninto the tower.\n',-1,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3871,0,0,0,'<R>Inside the Blood Red Tower<z>','  You enter a glowing chamber inside the red tower. Somehow it seems the \nwalls are providing the light here, not quite light, but energy that \nilluminates the room. There is a couch and end-table along the far wall, \nfurnishings provided by the master of the tower. A cot is neatly folded up and \nstanding in the adjacent corner to your left. Although slight on furnishings, \nthere is plenty of space to live for those who stay. A black spiral staircase \nto your right, twists up into the spire of the tower itself.\n',34,139272,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3872,0,0,0,'Inside the Spire','  A cool breeze wafts into this stone room from the outside. Rectangular \nlookout windows cut into the spire walls allow for air circulation and light in \nthis otherwise dark chamber. Against the far wall, there is a couch and end \ntable, furnished by the master of the tower for tenants, and a military cot \nfolded neatly, standing in the corner. Though slight on furnishings, this room \nhas plenty of room to accommodate those who stay. A stone spiral staircase \ntwists upwards towards the top of the tower, each step smaller then the last.\n\n',34,139272,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(3873,0,0,0,'<R>Atop the Red Tower<z>','At the top of the staircase, the wind pounds against your body, \nscreeching and howling as if you are surrounded by a pack of furious banshees. \nYou are standing on a platform inside a crevice at the top of the tower, the \nview is astounding, stretching to the ocean in the east, and all the way to the \nfoothills of the Mighty Sympathian Mountains to the west. There is room to move \naround, though somehow moving around at this height doesn\'t seem all that \nappealing. There is a red handrail carved from stone along the edge of the \nplatform, protecting you from being blown over the edge by the menacing wind.\n',-1,139264,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(3900,0,0,0,'Inside A Red Covered Wagon','This rough but well-maintained wagon has a faded red canopy overhead and bare\nwooden floors and frame.  The deep gouges in the wooden frame, canopy tears\nlovingly stitched closed and multiple water stains all attest to the hard times\nbefallen this vehicle.\n',0,139593,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(3901,0,0,0,'Inside A Green Covered Wagon','This rough but well-maintained wagon has a faded green canopy overhead and bare\nwooden floors and frame.  The deep gouges in the wooden frame, canopy tears\nlovingly stitched closed and multiple water stains all attest to the hard times\nbefallen this vehicle.\n',0,139593,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(3902,0,0,0,'Inside A Blue Covered Wagon','This rough but well-maintained wagon has a faded blue canopy overhead and bare\nwooden floors and frame.  The deep gouges in the wooden frame, canopy tears\nlovingly stitched closed and multiple water stains all attest to the hard times\nbefallen this vehicle.\n',0,139593,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(3903,0,0,0,'Inside An Orange Covered Wagon','This rough but well-maintained wagon has a faded orange canopy overhead and bare\nwooden floors and frame.  The deep gouges in the wooden frame, canopy tears\nlovingly stitched closed and multiple water stains all attest to the hard times\nbefallen this vehicle.\n',0,139593,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(3904,0,0,0,'Inside A Purple Covered Wagon','This rough but well-maintained wagon has a faded purple canopy overhead and bare\nwooden floors and frame.  The deep gouges in the wooden frame, canopy tears\nlovingly stitched closed and multiple water stains all attest to the hard times\nbefallen this vehicle.\n',0,139593,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(3905,0,0,0,'Inside A Yellow Covered Wagon','This rough but well-maintained wagon has a faded yellow canopy overhead and bare\nwooden floors and frame.  The deep gouges in the wooden frame, canopy tears\nlovingly stitched closed and multiple water stains all attest to the hard times\nbefallen this vehicle.\n',0,139593,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
