(4100,0,0,0,'Gravelly Path','  This is a narrow trail situated between two smooth granite walls that reach\ntowards the sky as they rise vertically overhead.  To the west, the path of\nloose gravel climbs higher up the mountainside.\n',34,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4101,0,0,0,'Gravelly Path','  This is a narrow trail situated between two smooth granite walls that reach\ntowards the sky as they rise vertically overhead.  To the west, the path of\nloose gravel climbs higher up the mountainside.\n',34,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4102,0,0,0,'Gravelly Path','  This is a narrow trail situated between two smooth granite walls that reach\ntowards the sky as they rise vertically overhead.  The loose gravel path\neastward winds down the mountain while to the west the trail widens.\n',34,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4103,0,0,0,'Mountain Path','  This is a narrow trail situated between two smooth granite walls that reach\ntowards the sky as they rise vertically overhead.  The loose gravel path\neastward winds down the mountain while the trail widens to the south of here\nas it climbs steadily higher into the mountains.  The air is quite thin from\nthe high altitude.\n',34,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4104,0,0,0,'North Street and West Street','  Two paths intersect here as they pass between various huts scattered about\nthis fishing village.  The mountain cliffs block progress to the west as they\nrise up quite sharply blocking what would surely be a spectacular view.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4105,0,0,0,'Entrance into the Fishing Village','   This is the extreme north end of a large valley tucked away high up in the\nmountains.  Dirt paths lead into the village to the southeast and southwest, \nwhile a gravelly path winds its way northward down the mountain from here.  A\nvery narrow rocky path to the west winds steeply up the mountain.  A number\nof huts and some lazy commotion can be heard from the village.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4106,0,0,0,'North Street','  The dirt path wanders through this fishing village as it passes between the\nvarious huts scattered about.  The mountain cliffs block progress to the\nnortheast, they rise up quite sharply obscuring what would surely be a\nspectacular view.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4107,0,0,0,'North Street','  A dirt path winds past a hut to the south.  The valley wall rises sharply\noverhead to the north blocking progress in that direction.  They rise up quite\nsharply obscuring what would surely be a spectacular view.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4108,0,0,0,'North Street','  A dirt path winds past a hut to the south.  The valley wall rises sharply\noverhead to the north blocking progress in that direction.  They rise up quite\nsharply obscuring what would surely be a spectacular view.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4109,0,0,0,'West Street','  A dirt path winds its way between huts near the western valley wall.  The\nmountain cliffs block progress to the west as they rise up quite sharply\nblocking what would surely be a spectacular view.  A small shack is accessible\nto the east through a door.  A pungent odor emanates from the shack.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4110,0,0,0,'West Street','  A dirt path winds its way between huts near the western valley wall. The\nmountain cliffs block progress to the west as they rise up quite sharply\nblocking what would surely be a spectacular view. There is a large hut to\nthe west before the mountain wall, with a door leading inside.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4111,0,0,0,'West Street','  A dirt path winds its way south between huts near the western valley wall.\nThe path branches to the east through a small plaza in this modest\nfishing village.  A hut can be entered through a low doorway leading west. \n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4112,0,0,0,'West Street','    A dirt path winds its way south between huts near the western valley wall.\nThe cliff walls lie west of here just beyond a hut while to the south a vast\nlake takes up the southern two-thirds of this mountain valley.  The sides of\nvillage huts can be seen to the east and west, but no entrance presents itself\nfrom here.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4113,0,0,0,'Central Street','  This broad path passes through the very center of town in a north-south\ndirection.  The entrance to a hut lies through a doorway leading east while\nfar to the south beyond the other huts of the village is a vast lake.\nDirectly south is the village center.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4114,0,0,0,'Village Center','  This fishing village is hardly a thriving metropolis, but what there is of it\ncongregates here to exchange gossip and look for news of the outside world.\nThe gravelly dirt road ends here as the center of town has been tiled with thick\nslabs of gray shale.  There are thatched huts throughout the village, but no\nentrances appear to be present from here. Central Street runs to the north and\nsouth from here, a small elongated plaza is to the west.  Far to the south can\nbe seen a vast lake though it is somewhat obscured by the other huts of the\nvillage.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4115,0,0,0,'Central Street','  This broad path passes through the very center of town in a north-south\ndirection.  A vast lake lies a ways to the south.  Just before the lake,\nis a broad beach upon which the village\'s fishing gear has been spread.\nTo the north lies the village center.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4116,0,0,0,'Central Street','  This broad path passes through the very center of town in a north-south\ndirection.  The entrance to a shack lies through a doorway leading east while\nfar to the south a vast lake can be seen.  Just before the lake, a short\ndistance south is a broad beach upon which the village\'s fishing gear has\nbeen spread.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4117,0,0,0,'South Street','  This street parallels the lake edge just south of here. The beach to the\nsouth is littered with fishing tackle of all sorts, small outriggers and\nsome nets that have been spread. The street runs east and west, while to the\nsouthwest an oversized hut juts out over the water.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4118,0,0,0,'East Street','  This small path circles the village on the east side winding between the\nvarious huts.  There is a sizable hut east of here beyond which are the cliff\nwalls.  Another smaller hut lies to the west.  Neither of the huts are\naccessible from here.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4119,0,0,0,'East Street','  This small path circles the village on the east side winding between the\nvarious huts.  To the west the is back of a small hut, while east of here is\nthe side of a massive hut.  East street continues to the north and south.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4120,0,0,0,'East Street','  This small path circles the village on the east side winding between the\nvarious huts.  East Street continues north and south while a massive hut is\neast of here with a door leading inside. The back of a more modest hut can be\nseen to the west.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4121,0,0,0,'East Street and South Street','  Two streets intersect here at the corner of a village.  South of here there\nis the side of a large shack while to the east is a small shed. The shack sits\non the east side of a beach that lies south of here and beyond that a large lake\noccupies the southern two-thirds of this valley.  A bit of smoke lightly scents\nthe air.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4122,0,0,0,'South Street','  This street parallels the lake edge just south of here and there is a beach\nto the southeast upon which small outriggers and some nets have been spread.\nThe street runs east and west, while to the south is an oversized hut.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4123,0,0,0,'South Street and Central Street','  This street parallels the lake edge just south of here and there is a beach\nto the south upon which small outriggers and some nets have been spread.  To\nthe north another streets runs towards the center of the village.  A bit of\nsmoke lightly scents the air.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4124,0,0,0,'Beach Near a Large Lake','  A narrow expanse of sand and gravel leads to the edge of a vast lake to the\nsouth.  North of here is the village proper with thatched huts scattered about\nhaphazardly.  The beach is littered with fishing tackle of all sorts, small\noutriggers and some nets that have been spread.\n',34,131072,10,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4125,0,0,0,'Beach Near a Large Lake','  A narrow expanse of sand and gravel leads to the edge of a vast lake to the\nsouth.  North of here is the village proper with thatched huts scattered about\nhaphazardly.  To the east is a large shack with a door leading inside.  The\nmingled scents of smoking meat and fish come from a large shack to the south.\n',34,131072,10,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4126,0,0,0,'Inside a Hut','  This is one corner of a large, thatched hut - one of the many scattered about\nthe fishing village.  The walls are supported by beams of wood brought here at\ngreat expense from the plains below the tree-line and thick, dried lake grass\nhas been woven together and fixed in place to create a remarkably durable wall.\nThere is a small hole in the center of the roof to permit smoke to escape.  A\ndoor leads back outside in the southeast corner of the hut.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4127,0,0,0,'Inside a Hut','  This is one corner of a large, thatched hut - one of the many scattered about\nthe fishing village.  The walls are supported by beams of wood brought here at\ngreat expense from the plains below the tree-line and thick, dried lake grass\nhas been woven together and fixed in place to create a remarkably durable wall.\nThere is a small hole in the center of the roof to permit smoke to escape.  A\ndoor leads back outside in the southeast corner of the hut.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
