(4149,0,0,0,'Inside a Hut','  This is one corner of a large, thatched hut - one of the many scattered about\nthe fishing village.  The walls are supported by beams of wood brought here at\ngreat expense from the plains below the tree-line and thick, dried lake grass\nhas been woven together and fixed in place to create a remarkably durable wall.\nThere is a small hole in the center of the roof to permit smoke to escape.  A\ndoor leads back outside in the southwest corner of the hut.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4150,0,0,0,'Village Plaza','  Thick slabs of gray shale have been tiled throughout the plaza.  The slabs\nare clean and litter free.  A lone aspen to the northwest towers above the\nplaza, its small nearly circular leaves grasping at the lightest wind to\nrustle and flutter. The center of the village is to the east.  Huts of varying\nsizes are scattered throughout the village.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4151,0,0,0,'Storage Shed','  This low hut serves as a communal shed for the village.  Various items that\nthe entire village might need, but no individual would want to own are stored\nhere.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4152,0,0,0,'Provisions Shed','  Food for the entire village is stored in this hut.  Sawdust covers the floor\nand the smell of salted meats lingers in the air.  \n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4153,0,0,0,'Workshop','   This is a small shed attached to the larger hut to the south.  The south\nhut seems to be the villages boat repair facilities and can be entered\ndirectly through an arched opening in the south wall.  This shed is apparently\nstorage for various tools that the boatyard might need.  A door leads east\noutside.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4154,0,0,0,'Boat Repair','  This is a massive hut held up by a single post in the center of the room and\nhaving no other internal supports.  This must be where the village brings\nboats that need repair work done or builds new ones from scratch.  There is\na small doorway in the northwest corner leading into a small shed attached to\nthis room.  The southeast wall is a gigantic door that can be removed in order\nto push a boat from this hut outside into the lake.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4155,0,0,0,'Boat Repair','  This is a massive hut held up by a single post in the center of the room and\nhaving no other internal supports.  This must be where the village brings\nboats that need repair work done or builds new ones from scratch.  There is\na small doorway in the northwest corner leading into a small shed attached to\nthis room.  The southeast wall is a gigantic door that can be removed in order\nto push a boat from this hut outside into the lake.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4156,0,0,0,'Boat Repair','  This is a massive hut held up by a single post in the center of the room and\nhaving no other internal supports.  This must be where the village brings\nboats that need repair work done or builds new ones from scratch.  There is\na small doorway in the northwest corner leading into a small shed attached to\nthis room.  The southeast wall is a gigantic door that can be removed in order\nto push a boat from this hut outside into the lake.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4157,0,0,0,'Boat Repair','  This is a massive hut held up by a single post in the center of the room and\nhaving no other internal supports.  This must be where the village brings\nboats that need repair work done or builds new ones from scratch.  There is\na small doorway in the northwest corner leading into a small shed attached to\nthis room.  The southeast wall is a gigantic door that can be removed in order\nto push a boat from this hut outside into the lake.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4158,0,0,0,'A Large Hut','  This is the largest hut in the village and the internal supports are made\nfrom wood which is virtually priceless this far up the mountain.   There is\na small hole in the roof to allow smoke to escape and the remains of a camp-\nfire is directly under it.  A door in the southwest corner leads outside\nwhile on the northwest is a doorway leading into the back rooms of the hut. \n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4159,0,0,0,'A Large Hut','  This is the largest hut in the village and the internal supports are made\nfrom wood which is virtually priceless this far up the mountain.   There is\na small hole in the roof to allow smoke to escape and the remains of a camp-\nfire is directly under it.  A door in the southwest corner leads outside\nwhile on the northwest is a doorway leading into the back rooms of the hut. \n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4160,0,0,0,'A Large Hut','  This is the largest hut in the village and the internal supports are made\nfrom wood which is virtually priceless this far up the mountain.   There is\na small hole in the roof to allow smoke to escape and the remains of a camp-\nfire is directly under it.  A door in the southwest corner leads outside\nwhile on the northwest is a doorway leading into the back rooms of the hut.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4161,0,0,0,'A Large Hut','  This is the largest hut in the village and the internal supports are made\nfrom wood which is virtually priceless this far up the mountain.   There is\na small hole in the roof to allow smoke to escape and the remains of a camp-\nfire is directly under it.  A door in the southwest corner leads outside\nwhile on the northwest is a doorway leading into the back rooms of the hut.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4162,0,0,0,'Back Hall of a Large Hut','  This is the largest hut in the village and the internal supports are made\nfrom wood which is virtually priceless this far up the mountain.  Doorways\nlead north and east further into the private area of the hut or south back\ntoward the common area and the exit. \n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4163,0,0,0,'Small Room in a Large Hut','  This is the largest hut in the village and the internal supports are made\nfrom wood which is virtually priceless this far up the mountain.  There\nis a doorway leading out of the room to the west.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4164,0,0,0,'Small Room in a Large Hut','  This is the largest hut in the village and the internal supports are made\nfrom wood which is virtually priceless this far up the mountain.  This\nportion of the hut is the northernmost and abuts the mountain walls.  In\nthe southwest wall there is a door.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4165,0,0,0,'Small Room in a Large Hut','  This is the largest hut in the village and the internal supports are made\nfrom wood which is virtually priceless this far up the mountain.  This\nportion of the hut is the northernmost and abuts the mountain walls.  In\nthe southwest wall there is a door.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4166,0,0,0,'Smoke House','  This large shed is used by the village to clean, cook and preserve the food\nthat is caught and to store it for the winter months.  This western half of\nthe shed is the preparations portion where cleaning and cooking occurs.  A\nvent in the roof allows smoke to escape.  A door leads out directly onto the\nbeach west from here.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4167,0,0,0,'Smoke House','  This large shed is used by the village to clean, cook and preserve the food\nthat is caught and to store it for the winter months.  This eastern half of\nthis shed contains the preservatives (largely salt) and hanging racks to do\nthe initial preparations on freshly caught meat.  There is a small door leading\nnorth back into the village.\n',34,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4168,0,0,0,'West Street','    A dirt path winds its way south between huts near the western valley wall.\nThe cliff walls lie west of here just beyond a hut while to the south a vast\nlake takes up the southern two-thirds of this mountain valley.  A hut can be\nentered through a low doorway leading east. \n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4169,0,0,0,'West Street and South Street','   The main thoroughfare of Central Street meets with the southern pathway of\nSouth Street making this one of the busiest places in the village.  To the south\na large hut covers a portion of beach and juts out over the water.  To the\nsoutheast fishing tackle of all sorts is scattered upon a beach.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4170,0,0,0,'South Street','  This street parallels the lake edge just south of here.  The wall of a\nthatched hut fills the area directly north of the street.  A bit of smoke\nscents the air.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4171,0,0,0,'South Street','  This street parallels the lake edge just south of here.  The wall of a\nthatched hut fills the area directly north of the street.  The mingled scents\nof smoking meat and fish seem to come from a large shack to the south.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4172,0,0,0,'East Street','  This small path circles the village on the east side winding between the\nvarious huts.  East Street continues north and south while the southern end of\na massive hut is to the east of here. The back of a more modest hut can be\nseen to the west.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4173,0,0,0,'Village Plaza','  Thick slabs of gray shale have been tiled throughout the plaza.  The slabs\nare clean and litter free.  A lone aspen to the northeast towers above the\nplaza, its small nearly circular leaves grasping at the lightest wind to\nrustle and flutter. There is a dirt path to the west.  Huts of varying\nsizes are scattered throughout the village.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4174,0,0,0,'North Street and Central Street','  Two paths intersect here as they pass between various huts scattered about\nthis fishing village.  The mountain cliffs block progress to the northeast as \nthey rise up quite sharply blocking what would surely be a spectacular view.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4175,0,0,0,'North Street and East Street','  Two paths intersect here as they pass between various huts scattered about\nthis fishing village.  The mountain cliffs block progress to the northeast as\nthey rise up quite sharply blocking what would surely be a spectacular view.\nThe thatched wall of a large hut is to the east, but no entry presents itself.\n',34,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4176,0,0,0,'A Steep Mountain Path','  This narrow path wanders steeply up the mountain to the west. To the\nsoutheast is open air as the mountain drops off in bare cliffs.  A large\nintersection is seen down the path to the east.\n',34,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4177,0,0,0,'A Steep Mountain Path','  This narrow path wanders steeply up the mountain to a grassy plateau just to\nthe southwest.  To the southeast and north is open air as the mountain drops off\nin bare cliffs.  The rocky ground is sparsely covered in hardy mountain grasses.\n',34,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4178,0,0,0,'A Grassy Mountain Plateau','  Hardy mountain grasses grow in thick clumps between large boulders and the\njagged crown of the ridge.  An impressive view shows the land for miles in\nall directions.  Quite a bit of it is forested land.  A steep mountain path\nleads down the mountain to the northeast.  A small village is cradled between\nmountain peaks east of here and just south of this ridge, a spring fed lake\nhas pooled.\n',34,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4179,0,0,0,'A Grassy Mountain Plateau','  Hardy mountain grasses grow in thick clumps between large boulders and the\njagged crown of the ridge.  An impressive view shows the land for miles in\nall directions.  Quite a bit of it is forested land.  Down the cliff to the\neast, a small village is cradled between mountain peaks and just south of this\nridge, a spring fed lake has pooled.\n',34,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4180,0,0,0,'A Grassy Mountain Plateau','  Hardy mountain grasses grow in thick clumps between large boulders and the\njagged crown of the ridge.  An impressive view shows the land for miles in\nall directions.  Quite a bit of it is forested land.  Down the cliff to the\neast, a small village is cradled between mountain peaks and just south of this\nridge, a spring fed lake has pooled.\n',34,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
