(4459,8,-9,0,'Grimhaven Outer Pathway','  This pathway circles the outer perimeter of Grimhaven\'s city walls.  The\npath is used by maintenance crews who keep the wall in repair and by the\nKing\'s soldiers, who insure that no one is sneaking into the city, except\nvia the gates.  The pathway is made of hard packed dirt.\n',35,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4460,9,-8,0,'Grimhaven Outer Pathway','  This pathway circles the outer perimeter of Grimhaven\'s city walls.  The\npath is used by maintenance crews who keep the wall in repair and by the\nKing\'s soldiers, who insure that no one is sneaking into the city, except\nvia the gates.  The pathway is made of hard packed dirt.  To the east is\nthe side of a large warehouse.  The path continues northeast and southwest.\n',35,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4461,10,-7,0,'Grimhaven Outer Pathway','  This pathway circles the outer perimeter of Grimhaven\'s city walls.  The\npath is used by maintenance crews who keep the wall in repair and by the\nKing\'s soldiers, who insure that no one is sneaking into the city, except\nvia the gates.  The pathway is made of hard packed dirt.  Warehouse Road\nheads off to the east.  The path continues northeast and southwest.\n',35,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4462,11,-6,0,'Grimhaven Outer Pathway','  This pathway circles the outer perimeter of Grimhaven\'s city walls.  The\npath is used by maintenance crews who keep the wall in repair and by the\nKing\'s soldiers, who insure that no one is sneaking into the city, except\nvia the gates.  The pathway is made of hard packed dirt.  Warehouse Road\nleads off to the south, and there is a large warehouse to the east.  The\npath continues northeast and southwest.\n',35,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4463,12,-5,0,'Grimhaven Outer Pathway','  This pathway circles the outer perimeter of Grimhaven\'s city walls.  The\npath is used by maintenance crews who keep the wall in repair and by the\nKing\'s soldiers, who insure that no one is sneaking into the city, except\nvia the gates.  The pathway is made of hard packed dirt.  To the east is a\nloading dock, connected to the warehouse to the south.  The path continues\nnortheast and southwest.\n',35,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4464,13,-4,0,'Grimhaven Outer Pathway','  This pathway circles the outer perimeter of Grimhaven\'s city walls.  The\npath is used by maintenance crews who keep the wall in repair and by the\nKing\'s soldiers, who insure that no one is sneaking into the city, except\nvia the gates.  The pathway is made of hard packed dirt.  The back of a\nbuilding stands to the east, and there is a loading dock to the south,\nconnected to a warehouse beyond.  The path continues north and southwest.\n',35,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4465,13,-3,0,'Grimhaven Outer Pathway','  This pathway circles the outer perimeter of Grimhaven\'s city walls.  The\npath is used by maintenance crews who keep the wall in repair and by the\nKing\'s soldiers, who insure that no one is sneaking into the city, except\nvia the gates.  The pathway is made of hard packed dirt.  To the east, a\nfence separates you from a large animal paddock.  The path continues north\nand south.\n',35,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4466,13,-2,0,'Grimhaven Outer Pathway','  This pathway circles the outer perimeter of Grimhaven\'s city walls.  The\npath is used by maintenance crews who keep the wall in repair and by the\nKing\'s soldiers, who insure that no one is sneaking into the city, except\nvia the gates.  The pathway is made of hard packed dirt.  To the east, a\nfence separates you from a large animal paddock.  The path continues north\nand south.\n',35,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4467,13,-1,0,'Grimhaven Outer Pathway','  This pathway circles the outer perimeter of Grimhaven\'s city walls.  The\npath is used by maintenance crews who keep the wall in repair and by the\nKing\'s soldiers, who insure that no one is sneaking into the city, except\nvia the gates.  The pathway is made of hard packed dirt.  The market plaza\nstretches to the north and east.  The area outside the east gate of the\ncity is to your north, and the pathway continues south.\n',35,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4470,0,0,0,'An Abandoned Wine Cellar','This room was once the home of a bloodthirsty band of wretches. Thankfully,\nthe city has exploited their recent absence and has begun work on its\nreclaimation. The wine racks and velvet draperies have been removed and white\ncloth and worktables have replaced them. The floor has been torn up,\nand bare earth is exposed.\n',0,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4471,0,0,0,'A Gutted Lounge','Once a luxurious, swanky lounge for the rising socialites of Grimhaven,\nthis dwelling has been gutted in a new effort to corral inappropriate\nbehavior. This is in part at the request of several of establishments local\nto Red Light Lane. It is also rumored that King Leroy wants to take possession\nof the premises to build upward in hopes of attracting a more aviary clientele.\n',0,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4472,22,3,0,'Gutted Bathroom','<k>The walls have been stripped down leaving only the slats and a few\ntatters of covering. A couple of pipes poke through one of the walls\nabove a bracket. A large rectangular section of the floor against one\nwall looks clean and new while the rest of the floor is pitted and\nrough. Dust filled cobwebs hang among the rafters.  A small vent pipe\nruns up into the ceiling.<1>\n',-1,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4473,22,3,0,'<k>A Mouse Hole<1>','<k>A pack of mice have made a small nest here in between the walls.  A hole\nhas been gnawed into the wall, providing passage into a hovel, where food\nand nesting materials are scavenged.  Small piles of mouse poop dot the floor.<1>\n',-1,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,5,0,'',NULL),
(4496,19,3,1,'Bambi\'s Bedroom','  This small room appears to be a typical bedroom.  The walls are made of\nwhitewashed wooden planks and the floor is polished hardwood.  A window\nlooks out over the roof of a small building to the north, and a wooden\ndoor is set in the southeast corner of the room.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4497,20,3,1,'Bunny\'s Burrow','  This small room is somewhat dank and cool, your first impression is\nthat you\'re underground, say in a burrow....or a dungeon, instead of on\nthe second floor of a building.  The walls are made of large stone blocks,\nwith numerous shackles and brackets embedded in them.  There are no\nwindows in this room, only a thick steel door in the southern wall.     \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4498,19,2,1,'Barbie\'s Boudoir','  This small room appears to be a girl\'s bedroom.  Everything is done in\nwhite and pink, with lots of lacy and frilly decorations.  A window looks\nout over the roof of a building to the south, and a door is set in the\neastern wall.   \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4499,20,2,1,'Upstairs Landing','  This landing leads to the rooms on the second floor.  Doors to the\nnorth, west and northwest lead to other rooms.  Stairs lead downward to\nthe main floor.  \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4500,14,3,0,'Guard Substation','  This small building is the home of the \"New City\" detachment of the\nGrimhaven guardforce.  It is used both by the soldiers who patrol the ring\nroad and the watchmen who maintain order in the marketplace.  The room is\nsmall, only about 20 feet square and of simple wood construction with a\nminimum of furnishings.  The door in and out of the building is on the\nwestern wall.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(4501,15,3,0,'Bar of the Grinning Griffon','  This section of the Grinning Griffon is the bar, where food and drink\ncan be purchased.  This section of the tavern is fairly dim, as the light\nfrom the front windows doesn\'t reach this far.  The room is smoky and the\nconversation is loud.  The entry to the tavern lies to the southeast, the\nback room to the east, and the front room to the south.\n',37,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(4502,16,3,0,'Back Room','  This section of the Grinning Griffon is known as the \"Back Room\".  This\nsection of the tavern is dimly lit, at the conversation is low.  This part\nof the tavern is the home of the rougher crowd, mainly the teamsters and\nothers from the East End.  The entry to the tavern is to the south, the\nbar to the west, and the front room to the southwest,\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(4503,17,3,0,'Forest Road','  This road leads north from the Grimhaven Market plaza toward the\nresidential district, and eventually down off the plateau and into the\nsouthern part of the Haon-Dor Forest.  There is a shop to your east and\nto the west is the side of a building.  The road continues to the north\nand south.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4504,0,0,0,'Alchemical Treats','You have entered an orderly little shop.  Potions are racked along one wall,\nand scrolls in cubbies line another.  Behind the counter can be found all\nmanner of pots and jars of the types used to contain spell components.\n',-1,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4505,19,3,0,'Parlor','  This seems designed to make you as comfortable as possible.  Lighting is\nlow and indirect, the tempature is just right and the air is scented with\nrose petals and pine.  The furniture divides the room into small, cozy\nsections, each a discreet distance from the others for increased privacy.\nA set of curtains block off an archway to the east, and the room continues\nto the south.     \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(4506,20,3,0,'Foyer','  This room is elegantly done in hard woods, polished to a rich luster.\nThe floor is covered with thick rugs which muffle the sound of footsteps\non the thick plank floor.  A small reception desk sits against the north\nwall.  To the east is a door leading to the street, while to the west a\ncurtain covers an archway.  To the south you see a stairway leading\nupwards.     \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4507,0,0,0,'<o>Jem and Perry\'s Self Defense Studio<1>','<Y>  The stone walls and ceiling of this shop have been painted in bright\nyellows to highlight the many weapons that have been hung, slung, and\nlain about in ordered fashion. Toward the rear there is a collection\nof mannequins displaying well-maintained pieces of protective\nwear. Although the slightly sagging floors suggest that the building\nis quite elderly, everything about the shop speaks of a proprietor\nthat cleans and maintains with great vigor.<1>\n',0,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(4508,15,2,0,'Front Room','  This part of the Grinning Griffon is know as the \"Front Room\", as it is\nsituated to give a good view of the marketplace to the south.  This room\nis the favorite resting spot of many a shopper on market day.  The entry\nto the building lies to the east, and the bar lies to the north.  The back\nroom is the the northeast. \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(4509,16,2,0,'Grinning Griffon Tavern','  During the day, this small cozy pub serves the many farmers you come to\nthe Grimhaven Market to sell their produce, the merchants who run the\nlocal shops, and riders boarding their mounts at the stable across the\nplaza.  At night, the rougher crowd from the \"East End\" of town takes\nover, and the average citizen stays out.  A door to the east opens \nonto Forest Road, while one to the south opens out to the marketplace\nitself.  The front room of the tavern is to the west, and the back room is\nto the north.  The bar is to the northwest.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(4510,17,2,0,'Forest Road','  This road leads north from the Grimhaven Market plaza toward the \nresidential district, and eventually down off the plateau and into the \nsouthern part of the Haon-Dor Forest.  There is a tavern to the west and a  \nshop to your east, while to the south the the road opens into the market\nplaza.  The road continues to the north.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4511,18,2,0,'Gumdrop\'s Candy Store','  This store smells delicious.  Display cases hold every type of candy you\ncould imagine.  If you stay in here very long, you might become too fat to\nfit through the door.\n',37,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(4512,19,2,0,'Parlor','  This seems designed to make you as comfortable as possible.  Lighting is\nlow and indirect, the tempature is just right and the air is scented with\nrose petals and pine.  The furniture divides the room into small, cozy\nsections, each a discreet distance from the others for increased privacy.\nThe room continues to the north.    \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4513,20,2,0,'Stairs','  This broad wooden stair, easily wide enough for two people to walk\nabreast, leads upward to the second floor.  The stair tread is covered\nwith a plush. dark red carpet, which muffles your footsteps.  To the north\nyou can see the foyer.   \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4514,14,1,0,'Grimhaven Marketplace','This broad plaza is the center of commerce in Grimhaven.  During the day,\nit is always packed with scores of people; merchants selling their wares,\ntownspeople buying the basic necessities, farmers bringing their products\nto market and dozens of others.  Along the northern and eastern sides of\nthe plaza are rows of shops.  To the south are the livestock pens and the\nslaughterhouse.  A large stable occupies the southeast corner of the plaza.\nTo the west is the Grimhaven ring road and the city walls.  Roads leave the\nplaza from all four corners as well as the middle of the eastern side.  To\nyour immediate west is the pathway around Grimhaven.  To the north is a\nshop and the plaza continues to the south and east.\n',-1,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4515,15,1,0,'Grimhaven Marketplace','  This broad plaza is the center of commerce in Grimhaven.  During the day,\nit is always packed with scores of people; merchants selling their wares,\ntownspeople buying the basic necessities, farmers bringing their products\nto market and dozens of others.  Along the northern and eastern sides of\nthe plaza are rows of shops.  To the south are the livestock pens and the\nslaughterhouse.  A large stable occupies the southeast corner of the plaza.\nTo the west is the Grimhaven ring road and the city walls.  Roads leave the\nplaza from all four corners as well as the middle of the eastern side.  A\ntavern stands to the north, and the plaza continues in the other\ndirections.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4516,16,1,0,'Grimhaven Marketplace','  This broad plaza is the center of commerce in Grimhaven.  During the day,\nit is always packed with scores of people; merchants selling their wares,\ntownspeople buying the basic necessities, farmers bringing their products\nto market and dozens of others.  Along the northern and eastern sides of\nthe plaza are rows of shops.  To the south are the livestock pens and the\nslaughterhouse.  A large stable occupies the southeast corner of the plaza.\nTo the west is the Grimhaven ring road and the city walls.  Roads leave the\nplaza from all four corners as well as the middle of the eastern side.  A\ntavern stands to the north, and the plaza continues in the other\ndirections.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4517,17,1,0,'Grimhaven Marketplace','  This broad plaza is the center of commerce in Grimhaven.  During the day,\nit is always packed with scores of people; merchants selling their wares,\ntownspeople buying the basic necessities, farmers bringing their products\nto market and dozens of others.  Along the northern and eastern sides of\nthe plaza are rows of shops.  To the south are the livestock pens and the\nslaughterhouse.  A large stable occupies the southeast corner of the plaza.\nTo the west is the Grimhaven ring road and the city walls.  Roads leave the\nplaza from all four corners as well as the middle of the eastern side.\nForest Road leads out of the plaza to the north and a shop stands to the\neast.  The plaza continues to the south and west.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4518,18,1,0,'Hairy\'s Hardware','  This shop specializes in tools and other assorted building supplies.\nRacks filled with all sorts of implements fill the middle of the room,\nwhile the walls are covered in bins holding smaller items.  This is\nobviously a well stocked store, and you figure if you can\'t find it here,\nit doesn\'t exist.  Doors lead out of the building to the south and west.\n',37,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(4519,19,1,0,'Vacant Shop','  This shop is currently empty, awaiting a new tenant.\n',37,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(4520,20,1,0,'Redlight Lane','  This small street is the main route through the \"East End\", the eastern\nmost portion of the Grimhaven foulborough.  The \"East End\" is one of the\nseedier parts of the city, and includes many establishments which are not\nwelcome in other parts of town.  There is a small shop to the west, and the\nside of a building to the east here.  The road continues to the northeast\nand connects to Plateau Road to the south.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4521,14,0,0,'Grimhaven Marketplace','  This broad plaza is the center of commerce in Grimhaven.  During the day,\nit is always packed with scores of people; merchants selling their wares,\ntownspeople buying the basic necessities, farmers bringing their products\nto market and dozens of others.  Along the northern and eastern sides of\nthe plaza are rows of shops.  To the south are the livestock pens and the\nslaughterhouse.  A large stable occupies the southeast corner of the plaza.\nTo the west is the Grimhaven ring road and the city walls.  Roads leave the\nplaza from all four corners as well as the middle of the eastern side.  To\nthe west is the east gate of Grimhaven and the plaza continues to the\nnorth, south and east. \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4522,15,0,0,'Grimhaven Marketplace','  This broad plaza is the center of commerce in Grimhaven.  During the day,\nit is always packed with scores of people; merchants selling their wares,\ntownspeople buying the basic necessities, farmers bringing their products\nto market and dozens of others.  Along the northern and eastern sides of\nthe plaza are rows of shops.  To the south are the livestock pens and the\nslaughterhouse.  A large stable occupies the southeast corner of the plaza.\nTo the west is the Grimhaven ring road and the city walls.  Roads leave the\nplaza from all four corners as well as the middle of the eastern side. The\nplaza continues in all directions. \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4523,16,0,0,'Grimhaven Marketplace','  This broad plaza is the center of commerce in Grimhaven.  During the day,\nit is always packed with scores of people; merchants selling their wares,\ntownspeople buying the basic necessities, farmers bringing their products\nto market and dozens of others.  Along the northern and eastern sides of\nthe plaza are rows of shops.  To the south are the livestock pens and the\nslaughterhouse.  A large stable occupies the southeast corner of the plaza.\nTo the west is the Grimhaven ring road and the city walls.  Roads leave the\nplaza from all four corners as well as the middle of the eastern side.  The\nplaza continues in all directions. \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4524,17,0,0,'Grimhaven Marketplace','  This broad plaza is the center of commerce in Grimhaven.  During the day,\nit is always packed with scores of people; merchants selling their wares,\ntownspeople buying the basic necessities, farmers bringing their products\nto market and dozens of others.  Along the northern and eastern sides of\nthe plaza are rows of shops.  To the south are the livestock pens and the\nslaughterhouse.  A large stable occupies the southeast corner of the plaza.\nTo the west is the Grimhaven ring road and the city walls.  Roads leave the\nplaza from all four corners as well as the middle of the eastern side.  To\nthe east Plateau Road leads toward the edge of the plateau on which the\ncity is built.  The plaza continues to the north, south and west. \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4525,18,0,0,'Plateau Road','  This road leads from the east gate of Grimhaven through the foulborough\nand eventually down the eastern side of the plateau on which the city is\nbuilt, to the farmlands beyond.  To your west, the road opens out into the\nbroad plaza of the Grimhaven marketplace.  To your north stands a shop\nand to the south lies the entrance to Grimhaven\'s main stable.  The road\ncontinues to the east toward the edge of the plateau.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4526,19,0,0,'Plateau Road','  This road leads from the east gate of Grimhaven through the foulborough  \nand eventually down the eastern side of the plateau on which the city is   \nbuilt, to the farmlands beyond.  To the north stands a small shop and to\nthe south is the side of the Grimhaven\'s main stable.  The road continues\ntoward the edge of the plateau to the east and toward the marketplace and\nthe city gate beyond to the west.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4527,20,0,0,'Plateau Road','  This road leads from the east gate of Grimhaven through the foulborough\nand eventually down the eastern side of the plateau on which the city is\nbuilt, to the farmlands beyond.  To the north, Redlight Lane leads off into\nthe East End and to the south is the side of the Grimhaven\'s main stable.\nThe road continues toward the edge of the plateau to the east and toward\nthe marketplace and the city gate beyond to the west.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4528,14,-1,0,'Grimhaven Marketplace','  This broad plaza is the center of commerce in Grimhaven.  During the day,\nit is always packed with scores of people; merchants selling their wares,\ntownspeople buying the basic necessities, farmers bringing their products\nto market and dozens of others.  Along the northern and eastern sides of\nthe plaza are rows of shops.  To the south are the livestock pens and the\nslaughterhouse.  A large stable occupies the southeast corner of the plaza.\nTo the west is the Grimhaven ring road and the city walls.  Roads leave the\nplaza from all four corners as well as the middle of the eastern side.  To\nyour immediate west is the pathway around Grimhaven.  The fence of the\nlivestock pens blocks your way south.  The plaza continues to the north and\neast.  \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4529,15,-1,0,'Grimhaven Marketplace','  This broad plaza is the center of commerce in Grimhaven.  During the day,\nit is always packed with scores of people; merchants selling their wares,\ntownspeople buying the basic necessities, farmers bringing their products\nto market and dozens of others.  Along the northern and eastern sides of\nthe plaza are rows of shops.  To the south are the livestock pens and the\nslaughterhouse.  A large stable occupies the southeast corner of the plaza.\nTo the west is the Grimhaven ring road and the city walls.  Roads leave the\nplaza from all four corners as well as the middle of the eastern side.  The\nfence of the livestock pens blocks your way south, although there is a gate\nin the fence here.  The plaza continues to the north, east and west.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4530,16,-1,0,'Grimhaven Marketplace','  This broad plaza is the center of commerce in Grimhaven.  During the day,\nit is always packed with scores of people; merchants selling their wares,\ntownspeople buying the basic necessities, farmers bringing their products\nto market and dozens of others.  Along the northern and eastern sides of\nthe plaza are rows of shops.  To the south are the livestock pens and the\nslaughterhouse.  A large stable occupies the southeast corner of the plaza.\nTo the west is the Grimhaven ring road and the city walls.  Roads leave the\nplaza from all four corners as well as the middle of the eastern side.  A\nblacksmith\'s shop stands to the south and the plaza continues to the north,\neast and west.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4531,17,-1,0,'Grimhaven Marketplace','  This broad plaza is the center of commerce in Grimhaven.  During the day,\nit is always packed with scores of people; merchants selling their wares,\ntownspeople buying the basic necessities, farmers bringing their products\nto market and dozens of others.  Along the northern and eastern sides of\nthe plaza are rows of shops.  To the south are the livestock pens and the\nslaughterhouse.  A large stable occupies the southeast corner of the plaza.\nTo the west is the Grimhaven ring road and the city walls.  Roads leave the\nplaza from all four corners as well as the middle of the eastern side.  To\nyour immediate east is the entry to Grimhaven\'s main stable.  To the south,\nMuddy Lane leads toward the industrial district.  The plaza continues to\nthe north and west. \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4532,18,-1,0,'Stable Entry','  You are just inside the doors of <y>Omar\'s<z>, Grimhaven\'s largest commercial\nstable.  Omar specializes in boarding the mounts of Grimhaven\'s many\nvisitors, and also sells horses and riding supplies on the side.  The tack\nshop is to the east, and Omar\'s main office is to the south.  An aisle\nleads southeast into the main stable area.  Doors open onto Plateau Road to\nthe north and Grimhaven Market plaza to the west.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,8,100,100,0,'',NULL),
(4533,19,-1,0,'Tack Shop','  This small room smells deeply of old leather.  Shelves lining the back\nwall are filled with saddles and saddlebags.  Bits, bridles and other\nassorted hardware hang from pegs on the side walls.  The main door is to\nthe west.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4534,20,-1,0,'Stall','  The wooden walls of this small enclosure are strong enough to contain the\nwildest mount.  The floor is hard packed dirt, over which a clean layer of\nstraw has been spread.  The gate is in the southwest corner.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4535,14,-2,0,'Animal Paddock','  This large pen holds the animals brought to market in Grimhaven.  Beyond\nthe fence to the north is the market plaza.  The paddock continues to the\nsouth and east. \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4536,15,-2,0,'Animal Paddock','  This large pen holds the animals brought to market in Grimhaven.  Beyond\nthe fence to the north is the market plaza.  To the east is the back of a\nbuilding.  The paddock continues to the south and west.  There is a gate in\nthe fence.  \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4537,16,-2,0,'The Darkenelf Smithy','Boy it\'s hot in here!  Waves of heat coming out of the forge on the\nwestern wall totally overwhelm this small shop.  A large anvil stands in\nthe middle of the hard packed dirt floor, while a large trough of water,\nfor quenching the metal, stands against the southern wall.  This is\nobviously the place of business of the town blacksmith.\n',-1,166077,55,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(4538,17,-2,0,'Muddy Lane','  This small road leads from the Grimhaven market plaza to the north into\nthe city\'s main industrial district to the south.  The road got its name\nbecause when it rains, the road is churned into a thick gooey mud by the\npassage of wagons and animals.  To the west is a blacksmith\'s shop, and to\nthe east is the wall of the main stable.  The road empties north into the\nplaza, and continues to the south.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4539,18,-2,0,'Horse Trader','  This would appear to be the main office for the stable.  A counter\nseparates the front of the room from the working area in the back.  The\nwalls are covered with feeding schedules, stall assignments and a variety\nof other information about the beasts in the stable\'s care.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4540,19,-2,0,'Middle of the Stable','  This open area in the middle of the stable is where the animals are taken\ncare of before being put in or after being taken from the stalls.  There\nare stalls to the northeast, east, south and southwest.  A storage area\nlies to the southeast, and the main exit from the stables is to the\nnorthwest.  A ladder leads upward to a hayloft above.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4541,20,-2,0,'Stall','  The wooden walls of this small enclosure are strong enough to contain the\nwildest mount.  The floor is hard packed dirt, over which a clean layer of\nstraw has been spread.  The gate is in the western wall.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4542,14,-3,0,'Animal Paddock','  This large pen holds the animals brought to market in Grimhaven.  To the\nsouth a door leads into the slaughterhouse.  The paddock continues to the\nnorth and east.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4543,15,-3,0,'Animal Paddock','  This large pen holds the animals brought to market in Grimhaven.  To the \nsouth is the wall of the slaughterhouse.  The back of a building lies to\nthe east.  The paddock continues to the north and west.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4544,16,-3,0,'Butcher Shop','  This small shop is dark and somewhat cool.  A waist high wooden counter\ndivides the room in half.  Immediately behind the counter is a large\nwooden butcher block table, for cutting meat.  A rail runs along the\nceiling next to the rear wall of the shop, from it hang freshly\nslaughtered sides of meat, ready for cutting.  The floor of the shop is\ncovered in sawdust, to soak up the blood.\n',37,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(4545,17,-3,0,'Muddy Lane','  This small road leads from the Grimhaven market plaza to the north into  \nthe city\'s main industrial district to the south.  The road got its name  \nbecause when it rains, the road is churned into a thick gooey mud by the   \npassage of wagons and animals.  To the west is a shop, and to the east is\nthe wall of the main stable.  The road continues north and southwest, and a\nsmall alley leads around the side of the stable to the southeast. \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4546,18,-3,0,'Stall','  The wooden walls of this small enclosure are strong enough to contain the\nwildest mount.  The floor is hard packed dirt, over which a clean layer of\nstraw has been spread.  The gate is in the northeastern corner.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL);
INSERT INTO `room` VALUES (4547,19,-3,0,'Stall','  The wooden walls of this small enclosure are strong enough to contain the\nwildest mount.  The floor is hard packed dirt, over which a clean layer of\nstraw has been spread.  The gate is in the northern wall.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4548,20,-3,0,'Storage Area','  This area would appear to be a general storage area for the stable.  A\nwide variety of items are stored here, including food for the animals,\nequipment for their care, riding supplies, and occasionally a wagon or cart\nleft by a visiting guest. \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4549,19,-2,1,'Hayloft','  This large area under the eaves of the stable is used for storing straw\nand hay, bedding and fodder for the animals.  It is also the living space\nfor the stable boys who tend the mounts, each of whom has made a bed in the\nstraw.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4550,14,4,0,'Home','  This small domicile is a typical middle-class abode.  This house\nconsists of a single large room, which can serve a variety of uses,\ndepending on the families needs at the moment.  The home is sturdily\nbuilt, of wood construction, and is well maintained.  Maybe someday you\'ll\nbe able to get a home like this yourself.     \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4551,15,4,0,'Home','  This small domicile is a typical middle-class abode.  This house\nconsists of a single large room, which can serve a variety of uses,\ndepending on the families needs at the moment.  The home is sturdily\nbuilt, of wood construction, and is well maintained.  Maybe someday you\'ll\nbe able to get a home like this yourself.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4552,16,4,0,'Winding Way','  Winding Way is a narrow, serpentine street that meanders through one of\nGrimhaven\'s main residential districts.  The modest homes of city\'s\nworking class line both sides of the street, which is nothing more than\nhard packed dirt.  Forest Road lies to the east and Winding Way continues\nto the northeast.  A home lies to the west.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4553,17,4,0,'Forest Road','  This road leads north from the Grimhaven Market plaza toward the\nresidential district, and eventually down off the plateau and into the\nsouthern part of the Haon-Dor Forest.  To the west, Winding Way leads off\ninto the residential district.  There is a shop to the east.  The road\ncontinues to the northeast and south. \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4554,18,4,0,'Empty Building','  This building is currently unused and is completely empty.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4555,0,0,0,'Home','  This small domicile is a typical middle-class abode.  This house\nconsists of a single large room, which can serve a variety of uses,\ndepending on the families needs at the moment.  The home is sturdily\nbuilt, of wood construction, and is well maintained.  Maybe someday you\'ll\nbe able to get a home like this yourself.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4556,14,5,0,'Home','  This small domicile is a typical middle-class abode.  This house\nconsists of a single large room, which can serve a variety of uses,\ndepending on the families needs at the moment.  The home is sturdily\nbuilt, of wood construction, and is well maintained.  Maybe someday\nyou\'ll be able to get a home like this yourself.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4557,15,5,0,'Winding Way','  Winding Way is a narrow, serpentine street that meanders through one of\nGrimhaven\'s main residential districts.  The modest homes of city\'s\nworking class line both sides of the street, which is nothing more than\nhard packed dirt.  Homes lie to the east, west and southwest, and Winding\nWay continues north and southeast.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4558,16,5,0,'Home','  This small domocile is a typical middle-class abode.  This house\nconsists of a single large room, which can serve a variety of uses,\ndepending on the families needs at the moment.  The home is sturdily\nbuilt, of wood construction, and is well maintained.  Maybe someday\nyou\'ll be able to get a home like this yourself.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4559,17,5,0,'Home','  This small domocile is a typical middle-class abode.  This house\nconsists of a single large room, which can serve a variety of uses,\ndepending on the families needs at the moment.  The home is sturdily\nbuilt, of wood construction, and is well maintained.  Maybe someday\nyou\'ll be able to get a home like this yourself.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4560,18,5,0,'Forest Road','  This road runs through the northern part of the foulborough, from the\nGrimhaven Market plaza toward the edge of the plateau on which Grimhaven is\nbuilt and eventually into the southern Haon-Dor Forest.  A home sits on the\nwestern side of the road, and to the east Redlight Lane leads off into the\nEast End.  The road continues north and southwest.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
