(4579,13,8,0,'Winding Way','  Winding Way is a narrow, serpentine street that meanders through one of\nGrimhaven\'s main residential districts.  The modest homes of city\'s\nworking class line both sides of the street, which is nothing more than\nhard packed dirt.  Homes stand to the north and west, and Winding Way\ncontinues to the east and southwest.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4580,14,8,0,'Winding Way','  Winding Way is a narrow, serpentine street that meanders through one of\nGrimhaven\'s main residential districts.  The modest homes of city\'s\nworking class line both sides of the street, which is nothing more than\nhard packed dirt.  There is a home to the north and to the east stands the\nGrimhaven Public School.  Winding Way continues to the west and southeast.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4581,15,8,0,'School','  Just stepping into this building brings back all sorts of memories...\nGood old Grimhaven Public School #1.  Students from all over the realms\ncome here to learn the basics; reading, writing and a little arithmetic.\nThe building is of sturdy red brick construction, with real glass windows.\nTo the north is the junior classroom, for the younger students, and to the\neast is the senior classroom, for the more advanced students.  Wide doors\nopen onto Winding way to the west.      \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4582,16,8,0,'Senior Classroom','  This is the classroom for the school\'s advanced students, who range in\nage from 11 to 15.  Rows of desks fill this large whitewashed room.  A\nblackboard hangs on the east wall, behind the teacher\'s desk.  A door in\nthe north wall leads outside to the playground, and one in the west wall\nleads to the lobby.    \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4589,13,9,0,'Home','  This small domocile is a typical middle-class abode.  This house\nconsists of a single large room, which can serve a variety of uses,\ndepending on the families needs at the moment.  The home is sturdily\nbuilt, of wood construction, and is well maintained.  Maybe someday\nyou\'ll be able to get a home like this yourself.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4590,14,9,0,'Home','  This small domocile is a typical middle-class abode.  This house\nconsists of a single large room, which can serve a variety of uses,\ndepending on the families needs at the moment.  The home is sturdily\nbuilt, of wood construction, and is well maintained.  Maybe someday\nyou\'ll be able to get a home like this yourself.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4591,15,9,0,'Junior Classroom','  This is the classroom for the school\'s beginning students, who range in\nage from 5 to 10.  The room is painted in bright primary colors, with lots\nof pictures on the walls.  Thick rugs cover the floor, and there is little\nfurniture in the room, although there are lots of toys.  A door in the\neast wall leads outside to the playground, and one in the south wall leads\nto the lobby.     \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4592,16,9,0,'Playground','  This wide grassy area is where the students go for recess, to burn off\nall that excess energy kids are so full of.  A variety of things for kids\nto climb or play on are scattered throughout the area, including a swing\nset, some monkey bars, and a see-saw.  One area on the east side is marked\noff with white lines, obviously for some type of game.  The playground is\nenclosed by a white picket fence, to keep the kids from running off.  In\nthe distance to the north and east you can see the trees of the Haon-Dor\nforest.  Doors lead back into the school to the south and west.       \n',37,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4595,19,7,0,'Forest Road','  This road runs through the northern part of the foulborough, from the\nGrimhaven Market plaza toward the edge of the plateau on which Grimhaven is \nbuilt and eventually into the southern Haon-Dor Forest.  In the distance to\nthe north and east you can see the edge of the plateau, and to the south\nand west you can see the outskirts of the city of Grimhaven.  A small home\nsits to the west. The road continues north and southwest. \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4596,19,8,0,'Forest Road','  This road runs through the northern part of the foulborough, from the\nGrimhaven Market plaza toward the edge of the plateau on which Grimhaven is\nbuilt and eventually into the southern Haon-Dor Forest.  Nearby to the\nnorth and east you can see the edge of the plateau, and to the south and\nwest you can see the outskirts of the city of Grimhaven.  The road\ncontinues northeast and south.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4597,20,9,0,'Forest Road','This road runs through the northern part of the foulborough, from the\nGrimhaven Market plaza toward the edge of the plateau on which Grimhaven is\nbuilt and eventually into the southern Haon-Dor Forest.  You are at the\nedge of the plateau.  The road slopes downward here, toward the trees of\nthe Haon-Dor Forest to the north.  In the distance to the south and west\nyou can see the outskirts of Grimhaven.\n',-1,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4600,19,-7,0,'Glassblower','  This shop is the establishment of the Grimhaven glassblower.  If you\nneed something made of glass, this is obviously the place, as shelves\nfilled with all manner of bottles, glasses and vases line the walls.    \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4601,19,-6,0,'Craftman\'s Alley','  This narrow road runs along the eastern side of the foulborough, from    \nPlateau Road south into the industrial and warehouse district.  This road  \ngot its name because a number of craftmen have set up their shops along   \nthe roadside.  There is a shop to the east here, and another to the south.\nYou see sides of other buildings to the north and west.  The road continues\nnortheast and southwest. \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4602,20,-6,0,'Empty Building','  This building is currently empty, awaiting a tenant.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4603,19,-5,0,'Tailor Shop','This small shop is strewn with pieces of fabric of all sizes, shapes and\ncolors.  Stacks of incomplete garments cover the many tables in the shop.\nA number of tools used by the owner stand out, including two fitting\ndummies, a spinning wheel and a loom.  Your instincts tell you this must be\nthe Grimhaven Tailor shop.    \n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4604,20,-5,0,'Craftman\'s Alley','  This narrow road runs along the eastern side of the foulborough, from    \nPlateau Road south into the industrial and warehouse district.  This road  \ngot its name because a number of craftmen have set up their shops along   \nthe roadside.  There is a shop to the east here, and another to the west.\nThe side of a third building is to the south.  The road continues to the\nnorth and southwest. \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4605,21,-5,0,'Empty Building','  This building is currently empty, awaiting a tenant.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4606,19,-4,0,'Groom\'s Alley','  This narrow alley runs between the stable to the north and the tannery to\nthe south, connecting Muddy Lane and Craftman\'s Alley.  The alley got its\nname because it is the favorite hiding place of the stableboys, or grooms,\nwhen they\'re trying to avoid work.  The alley continues to the east and\nwest.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4607,20,-4,0,'Craftman\'s Alley','  This narrow road runs along the eastern side of the foulborough, from    \nPlateau Road south into the industrial and warehouse district.  This road  \ngot its name because a number of craftmen have set up their shops along   \nthe roadside.  There is a shop to the east here, and to the west a narrow\nalley runs between the stable to the north and another building.  The road\ncontinues to the northeast and the south. \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4608,21,-4,0,'Empty Building','  This building is currently empty, awaiting a tenant.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4609,21,-3,0,'Craftman\'s Alley','  This narrow road runs along the eastern side of the foulborough, from    \nPlateau Road south into the industrial and warehouse district.  This road  \ngot its name because a number of craftmen have set up their shops along   \nthe roadside.  There is a shop to the east here, and to the west is the    \nside of the main Grimhaven stable.  The road continues to the north and\nsouthwest.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4610,22,-3,0,'Empty Building','  This building is currently empty, awaiting a tenant.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4611,21,-2,0,'Craftman\'s Alley','  This narrow road runs along the eastern side of the foulborough, from    \nPlateau Road south into the industrial and warehouse district.  This road  \ngot its name because a number of craftmen have set up their shops along   \nthe roadside.  There is a shop to the east here, and to the west is the    \nside of the main Grimhaven stable.  The road continues to the north and\nsouth.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4612,0,0,0,'Gradys Fine Leather Goods','The smell of finely tanned and meticulously cured leather permeates the air.  Leather of all shapes and sizes surround you as well as an odd assortment of second-hand clothing.',39,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4613,21,-1,0,'Craftman\'s Alley','  This narrow road runs along the eastern side of the foulborough, from\nPlateau Road south into the industrial and warehouse district.  This road\ngot its name because a number of craftmen have set up their shops along\nthe roadside.  There is a shop to the east here, and to the west is the\nside of the main Grimhaven stable.  The road continues to the north, where\nis intersects Plateau Road, and to the south.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4614,0,0,0,'LaMonts Fine Weaponry','This weapon shop is tidy and well maintained. There \nare several barrels of fresh oil and a small anvil in the center of the room. Several ball-pien hammers are arranged \ncarefully on the long counter.',39,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4615,21,0,0,'Plateau Road','  This road leads from the east gate of Grimhaven through the foulborough\nand eventually down the eastern side of the plateau on which the city is\nbuilt to the farmlands beyond.  To the north stands a small shop and to the\nsouth Craftman\'s Alley heads off toward the industrial district.  The road\ncontinues toward the edge of the plateau to the east and toward the\nmarketplace and the city gate beyond to the west.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4616,22,0,0,'Plateau Road','  This road leads from the east gate of Grimhaven through the foulborough\nand eventually down the eastern side of the plateau on which the city is\nbuilt to the farmlands beyond.  To the north and south stand small shops.\nThe road continues toward the edge of the plateau to the east and toward\nthe marketplace and the city gate beyond to the west.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4617,23,0,0,'Plateau Road','  This road leads from the east gate of Grimhaven through the foulborough\nand eventually down the eastern side of the plateau on which the city is\nbuilt to the farmlands beyond.  To the north and south stand small shops.  \nThe road continues toward the edge of the plateau to the east and toward   \nthe marketplace and the city gate beyond to the west.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4618,24,0,0,'Plateau Road','  This road leads from the east gate of Grimhaven through the foulborough\nand eventually down the eastern side of the plateau on which the city is\nbuilt to the farmlands beyond.  The road leads down off the edge of the\nplateau and westward toward the marketplace and city gate beyond.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4619,23,-1,0,'Empty Building','  This building is currently empty, awaiting a tenant.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4620,21,1,0,'Empty Building','  This building is currently empty, awaiting a tenant.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4621,22,1,0,'Candlemaker\'s Shop','  This small shop smells of hot wax and spices.  The room is dark and\nsomewhat cool, lit by dozens of the proprietor\'s products.  Shelves around\nthe room hold the owner\'s many wares, while in the back of the shop sit\nseveral large tanks of hot wax, where he dips new candles.   \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4622,23,1,0,'Empty Building','  This building is currently empty, awaiting a tenant.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4623,0,0,0,'Redlight Lane','This small street is the main route through the \"East End\", the eastern\nmost portion of the Grimhaven foulborough.  The \"East End\" is one of the\nseedier parts of the city, and includes many establishments which are not\nwelcome in other parts of town.  A large building sits to the west,\nalthough there is no door in here.  A spooky mansion occupies the east\nside of the street. The back of a third building can be seen to the south.\nThe street continues north and southwest.\nA barricade bars the door to the building to the east. A multitude of signs\ncarpet its face. They read, \"THIS RESIDENCE HAS BEEN REZONED. ALL OCCUPANTS\nARE TO VACATE THE PREMISES.\"\n',0,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4624,0,0,0,'A Sawdust-Covered Foyer','This room once held a grand mahogany desk and its walls, celings,\nand floor were once tiled in marvelous blue and pearl marble tiles.\nRumor has it the mahogany was milled into trim to replace the trim in\nthe King\'s personal library and that the marble was junked for its\nstock value, in conjunction with a new project involving the town dump.\nDrafting plans and rezoning papers cover the bare walls currently, as\nmany of the resources intended to refinish this residence have been\nreallocated.\nA wooden barricade sits here, barring access to the door. A sign on it\nreads, \"THIS PREMISES HAS BEEN REZONED. ALL OCCUPANTS ARE TO VACATE.\"\n',0,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4625,21,3,0,'Redlight Lane','This small street is the main route through the \"East End\", the eastern  \nmost portion of the Grimhaven foulborough.  The \"East End\" is one of the   \nseedier parts of the city, and includes many establishments which are not  \nwelcome in other parts of town.  There is a doorway into a large building\nto the west, and another into a smaller building to the east.  The side of\nbuilding blocks the way north.  The road continues to the northwest and\nsouth.  There is a sign above the door to the west and a red light is\nmounted on either side of the door.\n',-1,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4626,22,3,0,'Slovenly Hovel','<k>Whole sections of the walls have fallen apart exposing the studs and\ndumping debris onto the floor.  Small patches of <o>discolored paper<k> cling\nto the walls, the pattern faint and worn.  The single window has been\nboarded up completely, blocking out all sight of the outside world. A\nfaded <r>reddish stain<k> dominates the uneven floor. Bits of <g>mold<k> dot the\nceiling where water has soaked through.\n',-1,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4627,19,4,0,'Parish House','  This small home is obviously the home of a very pious person, as\nnumerous religious symbols and works of art cover the walls.  The simple\nfurnishings and the lack of possessions lead you to guess that whoever\nlives here has taken a vow of poverty.   \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4628,20,4,0,'Redlight Lane','  This small street is the main route through the \"East End\", the eastern  \nmost portion of the Grimhaven foulborough.  The \"East End\" is one of the   \nseedier parts of the city, and includes many establishments which are not  \nwelcome in other parts of town.  Doorways lead into a large two-story\nbuilding to the north and a small chapel to the east.  The side of another\nsmall building lies to the west, and another two-story building sits to the\nsouth.  The road continues to the northwest and southeast. \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4629,21,4,0,'Mission Church','  This small church serves as place of hope and refuge for the poor and\nhomeless of Grimhaven.  The building is simply made of untreated wood.\nSimple wooden benches serve as pews during the services, and as seats\nduring meetings.  The door to the street is to the west, and the room\ncontinues to the east.    \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4630,22,4,0,'Mission Church','  This part of the church is raised slightly higher than the rest of the\nroom and serves as the altar during services.  The building is of simple\nwood construction, without decoration.  The room continues to the west.   \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4631,19,5,0,'Redlight Lane','  This small street is the main route through the \"East End\", the eastern  \nmost portion of the Grimhaven foulborough.  The \"East End\" is one of the   \nseedier parts of the city, and includes many establishments which are not  \nwelcome in other parts of town.  Doors lead into small buildings to the\nnorth and south, and the side of a large two-story building sits to the\neast.  The road continues to the southeast, and opens onto Forest Road to\nthe west.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4632,20,5,0,'Flop House Entry','  This dark and dingy room is the entry for the Grimhaven flop house.\nThis large building is home to many of those residents too poor to afford\nhousing of their own.  For just a few coins a night, they are allowed to\nstay in here, where at least they are off the streets and out of the\nelements.  The walls of the room are made of plain, unpainted wooden\nplanks that seem to show an inordinate number of knotholes.  The floor\nmight be wooden as well, it\'s kind of hard to tell what\'s under all that\ndirt.  To the north lies a wooden counter and to the east there lies\nanother, larger room.  A door leads out of the building to the south.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4633,21,5,0,'Flop House Common Room','  This large room is evidently the building\'s common room, where the\npeople that stay here hang out when they don\'t feel like sleeping.  The\nplace smells of smoke, spilled beer and vomit.  Looking at the accumulated\ndirt and assorted trash, you\'d guess this room probably hasn\'t been\ncleaned since the place was built.  To the north is a set of stairs, and\nadditional rooms can be seen to the east and west.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4634,22,5,0,'Flop House Dining Room','  This large room is the dining room of the establishment, although how\nany being other than a pig or an ogre could eat in a sty like this is\nbeyond understanding.  Long tables of cheap looking wood, the tops stained\nfrom spills, line the center of the room.  Rows of benches provide seating\nfor the brave souls who eat here.  To the north, a door leads into another\nroom, while to the west lies another large room.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4635,20,6,0,'Flop House Manager','  This small cubbyhole is the domain of the flop house manager.  A wooden\ncounter physically seperates this section of the building from the\nentryway to the south, but the manager still has a good view of the door\nso he can track his \"guests\".  Shelves and drawers cover the rear wall of\nthe room.  A variety of posters and notices are posted on the side walls.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4636,21,6,0,'Flop House Stairs','  This rickety wooden staircase leads upward to the landing on the second\nfloor.  You\'re not sure if theses stairs will hold your weight and they\nsure creak a lot. \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4637,22,6,0,'Flop House Kitchen','  This would appear to be the building\'s kitchen, although a quick look\naround would cause even the most hardy soul to have second thoughts about\neating anything prepared here.  The floor is made of badly stained wood.\nA large stone fireplace along the eastern wall is used for cooking, and a\nsmall oven is built into the side of it.  A door to the south is the only\nobvious exit.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4638,20,5,1,'Men\'s Dorm','  This large room is the men\'s dormitory, all males above the age of 13\nsleep in here.  The place is quite slovenly, as you might expect from a\nbunch of single guys.  Rows of bunks line the sides of the room, with an\naisle down the middle.  Pegs hammered into the wall hold the odd cloak or\ntunic.  The room continues to the north.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4639,21,5,1,'Flop House Bathroom','  This building has one modern feature, it is equipped with indoor\nplumbing, but one whiff of the smell in this room makes you wish for a\ngood, old-fashioned, outdoor outhouse.  The \"facilities\" consist of a hole\nin the floor, a bucket beside it with water for flushing, a pump to fill\nthe bucket, and a chipped basin to wash in.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4640,22,5,1,'Woman\'s Dorm','  This large room is the woman\'s dormitory.  All females and children\nunder the age of 13 sleep in here.  This is the only room in the whole\nbuilding that shows any sign of neatness or cleanliness.  Rows of bunks\nline each side of the room, each features a set of curtains that can be\nclosed for some privacy.  Pegs pounded into the wall hold cloaks and\ndresses.  The room continues to the north.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4641,20,6,1,'Men\'s Dorm','  This large room is the men\'s dormitory, all males above the age of 13\nsleep in here.  The place is quite slovenly, as you might expect from a\nbunch of single guys.  Rows of bunks line the sides of the room, with an\naisle down the middle.  Pegs hammered into the wall hold the odd cloak or\ntunic.  An archway lead out of the room to the east, and the room\ncontinues to the south.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4642,21,6,1,'Flop House Upper Landing','  This narrow wooden platform is the main passageway on the second floor\nof the building.  Archways lead into rooms to both the east and west, and\nthere is a door in the southern wall.  A set of rickety wooden stairs lead\ndownward.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4643,22,6,1,'Woman\'s Dorm','  This large room is the woman\'s dormitory.  All females and children\nunder the age of 13 sleep in here.  This is the only room in the whole\nbuilding that shows any sign of neatness or cleanliness.  Rows of bunks\nline each side of the room, each features a set of curtains that can be\nclosed for some privacy.  Pegs pounded into the wall hold cloaks and\ndresses.  The room continues to the south, and an archway leads out of the\nroom to the west. \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4644,19,6,0,'Empty Building','  This building is currently vacant, awaiting a new tenant.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4645,0,0,0,'Sky Over Grimhaven','Looking upwards, you see the vast expanse of the sky over your head.\n',37,140096,34,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4646,12,-6,1,'Warehouse Loft','  This second floor section of the warehouse is for \"special shipments\",\nmainly small or high value items that could be easily misplaced, damaged\nor stolen.  Access to this part of the building is strictly controlled.\nLooking over the railing to the east, you can see the warehouse floor\nbelow.  The loft continues to the south.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4647,12,-7,1,'Warehouse Loft','  This second floor section of the warehouse is for \"special shipments\",\nmainly small or high value items that could be easily misplaced, damaged\nor stolen.  Access to this part of the building is strictly controlled.\nLooking over the railing to the east, you can see the warehouse floor\nbelow.  The loft continues to the north.  A ladder leads downward through\na trapdoor to the main floor.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4648,0,0,0,'Private Office','  This well appointed office is home to the guildmaster of the local\nTeamster\'s guild.  The walls of this office are made of exotic woods,\nimported at great expense from the jungles far to the south.  Curtains and\ntapestries of silks and satins from distant continents cover the walls.  A\nthick carpet of the finest weave covers the floor to muffle your\nfootsteps.  Nothing is too good for the local Teamster\'s guildmaster.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4649,16,-7,1,'Fireman\'s Bunkroom','  This room appears to be the living quarters of the men of the Grimhaven\nFire Department.  It has that \"lived in\" look that can only come when a\nnumber of people spend a lot of time in a place with nothing to do other\nthan keep the place clean and make improvements.  Built-in bunks line the\nnorth and south sides of the room.  A small cast iron stove stands at the\neast end.  A stairway to the first floor and a fireman\'s pole are at the\nwest end of the room.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4650,14,-4,0,'Inspection Station','  This section of the building is where the incoming animals are\ninspected, to see if they are healthy and ready to slaughter.  The room is\ndivided in half by a chute made of wooden planks.  The chute leads from\nthe large door in the northern wall southward deeper into the building.\nThe room itself is fairly clean, with a layer of fresh sawdust on the hard\npacked dirt floor. \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4651,15,-4,0,'Cutting Room','  This section of the building is the cutting room, where the carcasses of\nthe recently slaughter animals are cut into sides of meat for shipment.  \nNumerous large hooks hang in rows along the ceiling of this large room,\nwhich seems unusually cold.  The floor of the rooms is covered in sawdust,\nbelow each of the hooks, the sawdust is covered with sticky red liquid.\nThere is another room to the south, and a small window opens through the\nwall to the northeast.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4652,16,-4,0,'Muddy Lane','  This small road leads from the Grimhaven market plaza to the north into\nthe city\'s main industrial district to the south.  The road got its name\nbecause when it rains, the road is churned into a thick gooey mud by the\npassage of wagons and animals.  To the west is the slaughterhouse, and to\nthe east is the wall of a shop.  The road continues northeast and south.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4653,17,-4,0,'Leather Shop','  This shop smells deeply of freshly tanned leather.  Racks along the\nwalls hold all manner of leather garments, while stacks of newly tanned\nhides sit in the center of the room, ready for the tailor.  If you need\nleather goods, this is obviously the place.\n',37,166076,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4654,18,-4,0,'Groom\'s Alley','  This narrow alley runs between the stable to the north and the tannery to \nthe south, connecting Muddy Lane and Craftman\'s Alley.  The alley got its \nname because it is the favorite hiding place of the stableboys, or grooms, \nwhen they\'re trying to avoid work.  The alley continues to the east and    \nnorthwest.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4655,13,-5,0,'Loading Dock','  This wooden platform sits about 3 feet above the ground, the same height\nas the average wagon bed, to facilitate the loading and unloading of\ncargo.  To the north and west is the Grimhaven Outer Pathway, to the east\nis the wall of a large building, and the the south a large door leads into\nanother large building.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4656,14,-5,0,'Killing Station','  This area is the killing station.  A small pen fills the center of this\nlarge room. The pen is composed of wooden slats and is just large enough\nto hold a cow or a horse.  The pen is connected to the wooden chute coming\nout of the room to the north and is closed off by a small gate.  The floor\nis covered in sawdust, and smells strongly of urine, offal and blood.  The\nbuidling continues to the north and east.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4657,15,-5,0,'Skinning Room','  This section of the building is where the carcasses are skinned, the\nfirst step in the butchering process.  Rails on the ceiling, from which a\nnumber of large metal hooks are suspended, connect this room with the ones\non either side.  Tables large enough to hold the carcass to be skinned\ntake up most of the floor space in the room.  The building continues to\nthe north and west, and there is a door to the east.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4658,16,-5,0,'Muddy Lane','  This small road leads from the Grimhaven market plaza to the north into\nthe city\'s main industrial district to the south.  The road got its name\nbecause when it rains, the road is churned into a thick gooey mud by the\npassage of wagons and animals.  To the west is the slaughterhouse, and to\nthe east is the tannery.  The road continues north and south.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4659,17,-5,0,'Inspection Station','  This part of the building is the inspection station, where incoming\nhides are sorted by type and inspected for flaws.  Large piles of raw\nhides occupy most of the floor space in this room.  The building continues\nto the east, south and southeast, and there is a door to the west.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4660,18,-5,0,'Storage Area','  This section of the building is the storage area for finished leather.\nNumerous lare stacks of leather, of all types and colors, occupies most of\nthe floor space in this part of the building.  The building continues to\nthe west, south and southwest.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4661,12,-6,0,'Warehouse','  You find yourself in the northwest corner of this large dusty building.\nStacks of crates occupy most of the space on the hard stone floor.  A row\nof dirty windows inset high along the top of the stout wooden walls allow\na bare minimum of light to filter in from the outside.  The building\ncontinues to the south and east.  A loft runs above your head, along the\nwestern wall of the building.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4662,13,-6,0,'Warehouse','  You find yourself in the northeast corner of this large dusty building.\nStacks of crates occupy most of the space on the hard stone floor.  A row\nof dirty windows inset high along the top of the stout wooden walls allow\na bare minimum of light to filter in from the outside.  The building\ncontinues to the south and west.  A second story loft runs along the\nwestern wall of the building.  A large door leads out of the building to\nthe north.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(4663,14,-6,0,'Dogleg Alley','  This alley got its name from its unusual shape, crooked like a dog\'s\nleg.  The alley is fairly narrow, surrounded on both sides by large\nbuildings.  A variety of trash litters the alley and makes footing\ntreacherous.  Numerous odors assail your senses as you traverse the alley,\nthere is little air movement in its close confines.  The alley makes a\nsharp turn here, continuing to the east and south.     \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4664,15,-6,0,'Dogleg Alley','  This alley got its name from its unusual shape, crooked like a dog\'s\nleg.  The alley is fairly narrow, surrounded on both sides by large\nbuildings.  A variety of trash litters the alley and makes footing\ntreacherous.  Numerous odors assail your senses as you traverse the alley,\nthere is little air movement in its close confines.  The alley opens onto\nMuddy Lane to the east and continues to the west.      \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4665,16,-6,0,'Muddy Lane','  This small road leads from the Grimhaven market plaza to the north into\nthe city\'s main industrial district to the south.  The road got its name\nbecause when it rains, the road is churned into a thick gooey mud by the\npassage of wagons and animals.  To the west is a narrow alley, and to\nthe east is the tannery.  The road continues north and southeast.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4666,17,-6,0,'Tanning Area','  This part of the building is where the tanning, the first step in\nturning hides into leather, takes place.  Numerous large vats, filled with\nfoul smelling concoctions in which the hides are soaked to remove the hair\nand skin or preserve and strengthen the leather, take up most of the floor\nspace in this part of the building.  The building continues to the north,\neast and northeast.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4667,18,-6,0,'Drying Area','  This part of the building is where the tanned skins are stretched, dried\nand trimmed.  Numerous large racks scattered throughout this part of the\nbuilding hold a wide variety of soon-to-be-leather skins.  This part of\nthe building is uncomfortably warm, as a multitude of lower burning fires\nare placed around the room, so that their heat can dry the leather.  The\nbuilding continues to the north, west, and northwest.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4668,11,-7,0,'Warehouse Road','  This hard-packed dirt road leads through the Grimhaven Warehouse\ndistrict.  Ruts from the many carts and wagons that traverse this street\ndaily are carved permanently in the road\'s surface.  The large warehouses\nthat give this road its name line both sides of the street.  You are at\nthe western end of the road, where it meets the Grimhaven Outer Pathway.\nThe road opens onto the pathway to the north and west, and leads southeast\ninto the warehouse district.  A large door opens into a warehouse to the\nsouth.       \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4669,12,-7,0,'Warehouse','  You find yourself in the southwest corner of this large dusty building.\nStacks of crates occupy most of the space on the hard stone floor.  A row\nof dirty windows inset high along the top of the stout wooden walls allow\na bare minimum of light to filter in from the outside.  The building\ncontinues to the north and east.  A loft runs above your head, along the\nwestern wall of the building.  A ladder leads upward to the loft.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4670,13,-7,0,'Warehouse','  You find yourself in the southeast corner of this large dusty building.\nStacks of crates occupy most of the space on the hard stone floor.  A row\nof dirty windows inset high along the top of the stout wooden walls allow\na bare minimum of light to filter in from the outside.  The building\ncontinues to the north and west.  A second story loft runs along the\nwestern wall of the building.  A large door leads out of the building to\nthe south.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(4671,14,-7,0,'Dogleg Alley','This alley got its name from its unusual shape, crooked like a dog\'s\nleg.  The alley is fairly narrow, surrounded on both sides by large\nbuildings.  A variety of trash litters the alley and makes footing\ntreacherous.  Numerous odors assail your senses as you traverse the alley,\nthere is little air movement in its close confines.  The alley continues\nto the north and opens onto Warehouse Road to the south.  A sign is\nattached beside a door leading into the two-story building to the east. \n',-1,393216,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4672,15,-7,0,'Teamsters Office','  This building houses the office of the Grimhaven Teamsters Guild.  Wagon\ndrivers can rest here while their cargos are being offloaded in the nearby\nwarehouses.  This is also where merchants come when they are looking to\nhire wagons to move their goods.  This room is small and fairly spartan.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4673,16,-7,0,'Grimhaven Firehouse #1','  This large building somewhat resembles a medium size barn.  The middle\nof the building is open space, enough room to hold two large wagons.\nThe area along the north wall is covered with straw, and the wall itself\nhas leads and feedboxes for 4 large horses.  The southern hall of the room\nis covered shelves, pegs and cabinets to hold equipment.  At the western\nend of the room, a stairway and a fireman\'s pole lead to the second floor\nof the building.  A pair of wide doors lead out of the building to the\neast.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4674,17,-7,0,'Three Corners','  This intersection is know as Three Corners, because three roads\nintersect here, creating three corners.  To the east, Craftman\'s Alley\nfollows the eastern edge of the plateau on which the city is built.  To\nthe southwest, Warehouse Road leads toward the city wall.  To the\nnorthwest, Muddy Lane heads toward the marketplace.  From the north comes\nthe stink of the Tannery, while from the south comes the fermenting grain \nsmell of the Brewery.  To the west stands a red-brick building with a\nsign over the door.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4675,18,-7,0,'Craftman\'s Alley','  This narrow road runs along the eastern side of the foulborough, from    \nPlateau Road south into the industrial and warehouse district.  This road  \ngot its name because a number of craftmen have set up their shops along   \nthe roadside.  To the north is the side of the Tannery, and to the south is\nthe side of the Brewery.  The side of a third building sits to the east.\nthe road continues to the northeast and west. \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4676,10,-8,0,'New Warehouse','  This building is so new that the air is still permeated with the smell\nof fresh sawdust.  The freshly whitewashed walls show none of the typical\nwarehouse stains and scuff marks.  The ceiling and rafters are remarkably\nfree of cobwebs and birdshit.  The hard slate floor is dust free and\ntotally empty.  The building continues to the east and south.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4677,11,-8,0,'New Warehouse','  This building is so new that the air is still permeated with the smell\nof fresh sawdust.  The freshly whitewashed walls show none of the typical\nwarehouse stains and scuff marks.  The ceiling and rafters are remarkably\nfree of cobwebs and birdshit.  The hard slate floor is dust free and\ntotally empty.  The building continues to the west and south.  A door\nleads out of the building to the north.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4678,12,-8,0,'Warehouse Road','  This hard-packed dirt road leads through the Grimhaven Warehouse\ndistrict.  Ruts from the many carts and wagons that traverse this street\ndaily are carved permanently in the road\'s surface.  The large warehouses\nthat give this road its name line both sides of the street.  A large door\nopens into a warehouse to the south.  The road continues to the northwest\nand east.     \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4679,13,-8,0,'Warehouse Road','  This hard-packed dirt road leads through the Grimhaven Warehouse\ndistrict.  Ruts from the many carts and wagons that traverse this street\ndaily are carved permanently in the road\'s surface.  The large warehouses\nthat give this road its name line both sides of the street.  A large door\nopens into a warehouse to the north.  The road continues to the east and\nwest.     \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4680,14,-8,0,'Warehouse Road','  This hard-packed dirt road leads through the Grimhaven Warehouse\ndistrict.  Ruts from the many carts and wagons that traverse this street\ndaily are carved permanently in the road\'s surface.  The large warehouses\nthat give this road its name line both sides of the street.  The road\nintersects an alley here.  Warehouse Road continues east and west, and the\nalley leads off to the north and south.     \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4681,15,-8,0,'Warehouse Road','  This hard-packed dirt road leads through the Grimhaven Warehouse\ndistrict.  Ruts from the many carts and wagons that traverse this street\ndaily are carved permanently in the road\'s surface.  The large warehouses\nthat give this road its name line both sides of the street.  A large door\nopens into a warehouse to the south.  The road continues to the east and\nwest.     \n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4682,16,-8,0,'Warehouse Road','  This hard-packed dirt road leads through the Grimhaven Warehouse\ndistrict.  Ruts from the many carts and wagons that traverse this street\ndaily are carved permanently in the road\'s surface.  The large warehouses\nthat give this road its name line both sides of the street.  To the\nnortheast lies and intersection, and the road continues to the west.  To\nthe east a door enters a large building from which eminates the odor of\nfermenting grain.  A large sign hangs above the doorway.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4683,17,-8,0,'Brewery','  This room is the entry to the Alt Haven Brewery, Grimhaven\'s finest (and\nonly) brewery.  This part of the building is a combination of waiting\nroom, sales office and taste testing lounge.  A bar made of polished wood\nstands along the northern wall, with racks of shelves above it.  The\nbuilding continues to the east, south and southeast, with a door to the\noutside to the west.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4684,18,-8,0,'Brewery','  This part of the brewery appears to be a storage area.  Pallets stacked\nfull of sacks of grain, large wooden beer barrels, and other tools of the\nbrewers trade can all be found here, if you look hard enough.  The room\nseems unusually cool and dry, enough to make you wonder if magic is\ninvolved to keep it that way, although maybe it\'s just the thick slate\nfloor and the thick stone walls of the building that make it so.  The room\ncontinues to the west, south and southwest.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4686,10,-9,0,'New Warehouse','  This building is so new that the air is still permeated with the smell\nof fresh sawdust.  The freshly whitewashed walls show none of the typical\nwarehouse stains and scuff marks.  The ceiling and rafters are remarkably\nfree of cobwebs and birdshit.  The hard slate floor is dust free and\ntotally empty.  The building continues to the east and north.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4687,11,-9,0,'New Warehouse','  This building is so new that the air is still permeated with the smell\nof fresh sawdust.  The freshly whitewashed walls show none of the typical\nwarehouse stains and scuff marks.  The ceiling and rafters are remarkably\nfree of cobwebs and birdshit.  The hard slate floor is dust free and\ntotally empty.  The building continues to the north and west.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4688,12,-9,0,'Warehouse','  This large warehouse appears to be used to store building materials.  \nThis part of the warehouse, the northwest corner, is filled with pallets\nof freshly fired bricks and bins filled with large stones.  The building\ncontinues to the east and south.  A door leads out of the building to the\nnorth.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4689,13,-9,0,'Warehouse','  This large warehouse appears to be used to store building materials.\nThis part of the warehouse, the northeast corner, is used to store freshly\ncut lumber.  Racks of stout framing timbers and stacks of smoothly planed\nboards fill the air with the scent of cedar, pine and redwood.  The\nbuilding continues to the west and south. \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4690,14,-9,0,'Narrow Alley','  This narrow alley appears to be somewhat of an afterthought, being\nlittle more than a hard packed dirt path between the large buildings to\neither side.  The alley runs north-south, and an intersection with a\nlarger road can be seen to the north.\n',37,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4691,15,-9,0,'Warehouse','  From the wide variety of smells permeating the air of this large\nbuilding, you would have to guess that this warehouse is used to store the\nCity of Grimhaven\'s incoming food supply.  Your nose leads you to believe\nthat if you look hard enough, you could find wheat, apples, onions, and\nprobably a dozen other types of fruit, vegetables and grains.  All the\nfood is stored in large bags, stacked in pallets by type.  From the\nrafters overhead you can hear the chirping of birds, drawn by the presence\nof spilled grain.  From the walls around you, you hear the scurrying feet\nof less desirable four legged scavengers.  The building continues to the\nsouth and east.  A door leads out of the building to the north.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4692,16,-9,0,'Warehouse','  From the wide variety of smells permeating the air of this large\nbuilding, you would have to guess that this warehouse is used to store the\nCity of Grimhaven\'s incoming food supply.  Your nose leads you to believe\nthat if you look hard enough, you could find wheat, apples, onions, and\nprobably a dozen other types of fruit, vegetables and grains.  All the\nfood is stored in large bags, stacked in pallets by type.  From the\nrafters overhead you can hear the chirping of birds, drawn by the presence\nof spilled grain.  From the walls around you, you hear the scurrying feet\nof less desirable four legged scavengers.  The building continues to the\nsouth and west.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4693,17,-9,0,'Brewery','  This part of the brewery is filled with several large ovens, under which\nsit low-burning fires.  The air is filled with the smell of roasting grain\nand hops.  The ingredients of the brewing process are prepared here before\nstarting the fermentation process.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4694,18,-9,0,'Brewery','  This part of building is permiated with the yeasty smell of fermenting\ngrain, so it must be where the actual brewing is done.  Several large\ncovered vats made of copper take up most of the floor space in this room.\nA tangle of copper piping runs along the ceiling, connecting all the vats.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4695,12,-10,0,'Warehouse','  This large warehouse appears to be used to store building materials.\nThis part of the warehouse, the southwest corner, is filled with bags of\nsand, gravel, coal and limestone.  The building continues to the north and\neast. \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4696,13,-10,0,'Warehouse','  This large warehouse appears to be used to store building materials.\nThis part of the warehouse, the southeast corner, is filled stacks of iron\nand steel ingots, and racks of cast iron pipes, in all lengths and\ndiameters.  The building continues to the north and west. \n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4697,0,0,0,'Dead End','  The alley comes to an abrupt dead end here, with a large concrete wall\nsealing off the route to the south, and large buildings blocking passage to the\neast and west.  A large vent on the southern wall emits a soft smoke.  The alley\ncontinues to the north.\n',0,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4698,15,-10,0,'Warehouse','  From the wide variety of smells permeating the air of this large\nbuilding, you would have to guess that this warehouse is used to store the\nCity of Grimhaven\'s incoming food supply.  Your nose leads you to believe\nthat if you look hard enough, you could find wheat, apples, onions, and\nprobably a dozen other types of fruit, vegetables and grains.  All the\nfood is stored in large bags, stacked in pallets by type.  From the\nrafters overhead you can hear the chirping of birds, drawn by the presence\nof spilled grain.  From the walls around you, you hear the scurrying feet\nof less desirable four legged scavengers.  The building continues to the\nnorth and east.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4699,16,-10,0,'Warehouse','  From the wide variety of smells permeating the air of this large\nbuilding, you would have to guess that this warehouse is used to store the\nCity of Grimhaven\'s incoming food supply.  Your nose leads you to believe\nthat if you look hard enough, you could find wheat, apples, onions, and\nprobably a dozen other types of fruit, vegetables and grains.  All the\nfood is stored in large bags, stacked in pallets by type.  From the\nrafters overhead you can hear the chirping of birds, drawn by the presence\nof spilled grain.  From the walls around you, you hear the scurrying feet\nof less desirable four legged scavengers.  The building continues to the\nnorth and west.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(4700,-24,-10,0,'Forest','You are in a forest of gigantic trees.  The branches seem to form a\ncanopy over your head, although they leave ample room for creatures\nof the forest to pass through.  You faintly smell moss and decaying\nleaves that cover both the ground and the trees of the forest.  You\nsee a cave to the north.\n',32,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4701,-26,-10,0,'Damp Forest','The ground seems a little wetter, taking on an almost marsh or swamp\nlike consistency.  The trees seem to close in over your head,\nalthough they leave ample room for the creatures of the forest to\npass through.  You see a dark entrance to your north.\n',32,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4702,-25,-10,0,'Forest','You are in a forest of gigantic trees.  The branches seem to form a\ncanopy over your head, although they leave ample room for creatures\nof the forest to pass through.  You faintly smell moss and decaying\nleaves that cover both the ground and the trees of the forest.\n',32,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
