(4725,-26,-15,0,'Steep Rocky Hills','The rocks on these hills are loose and start to slide as you move along.\nThe grade is much steeper than the rolling hills to your north, but not\nquite as sheer as the mountain to your south.  A thicket of brambles\nblock your way north.\n',32,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4726,-25,-15,0,'Steep Rocky Hills','The rocks on these hills are loose and start to slide as you move along.\nThe grade is much steeper than the rolling hills to your north, but not\nquite as sheer as the mountain to your south.  A thicket of brambles\nblock your way north.\n',32,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4727,-24,-15,0,'Steep Rocky Hills','The rocks on these hills are loose and start to slide as you move along.\nThe grade is much steeper than the rolling hills to your north, but not\nquite as sheer as the mountain to your south.  A gigantic tree stands to\nyour north and a mountain rises to the south.\n',32,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4728,-23,-15,0,'Steep Rocky Hills','The rocks on these hills are loose and start to slide as you move along.\nThe grade is much steeper than the rolling hills to your north, but not\nquite as sheer as the mountain to your south.  A mountain rises to the\nsouth.\n',32,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4729,-22,-15,0,'Steep Rocky Hills','The rocks on these hills are loose and start to slide as you move along.\nThe grade is much steeper than the rolling hills to your north, but not\nquite as sheer as the mountain to your south.  A mountain rises to the\nsouth.\n',32,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4730,-26,-16,0,'Steep Rocky Hills','The rocks on these hills are loose and start to slide as you move along.\nThe grade is much steeper than the rolling hills to your north, but not\nquite as sheer as the mountain to your south.  A mountain rises\nimmediately to the southeast.\n',32,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4731,-25,-16,0,'Steep Rocky Hills','The rocks on these hills are loose and start to slide as you move along.\nThe grade is much steeper than the rolling hills to your north, but not\nquite as sheer as the mountain to your south.  A mountain rises\nimmediately to the south and east.\n',32,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4732,-24,-16,0,'Base of a Mountain','You stand at the base of a mountain.  You can\'t see the mountain top due\nto the clouds.  The granite base rises at such a grade that climbing\nthe mountain seems to be impossible.  You figure you would have to fly\nif you wanted to see the rest of the mountain.  A few sprigs of grass and\nmoss grow out of the cracks in the rocks.\n',32,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(4733,-23,-16,0,'Steep Rocky Hills','The rocks on these hills are loose and start to slide as you move along.\nThe grade is much steeper than the rolling hills to your north, but not\nquite as sheer as the mountain to your south.  A mountain rises\nimmediately to the south and west.\n',32,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
