(5100,-5,5,-1,'The Corner of a Spider Web','  You are on a small pile of debris and small rocks.  This vast cavern is\ncovered with spider webs.  Even as you move through it, some of the lesser\nstrands break off and cling to you, while others are too strong and you bounce\noff of them.  You spit a piece of webbing out of your mouth.  In this corner\nit appears that eggs have been laid to mature.  Some have already hatched,\ntheir larva quickly growing into a deadly young spiders, while others still\npulse and move as the life within developes.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5101,-11,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  You are at the intersection of two tunnels.  The tunnel walls are damp and\nare sweating with a good deal of moisture.  There is about a foot of water\nflowing slowly eastward in the bottom of the pipe.  There is a small sign on\nthe wall, partially obscured by the slime and dirt.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5102,-11,1,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  You are in a north-south running pipe.  It is large enough to hold many\nthousands of gallons of water.  The sides of the pipe are covered with\na slick, slimy substance and a trickle of water flows southward.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5103,-11,2,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  You are in a large north-south running pipe.  Water tickles in a southerly\ndirection and the curved walls of the pipe are covered with a slick-slimy\nsubstance.  Your footing is unsure almost causing you to slip and fall into\nthe water!\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5104,-11,3,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  This large sewer pipe runs north and south.  The water that trickles through\nhere is getting your feet wet and you begin to feel uncomfortable.  You hope\nyour boots can withstand the rancid water.  The walls are covered in slime and\nthe water flows in a southerly direction.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5105,-11,4,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  The sewer pipe suddenly changes direction here.  A portion branches off\nto the northeast while the water heads down the pipe to the south.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5106,-10,5,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  The sewer pipe seems to be running in a northeast to southwest direction.\nThe water flows to the southwest as that is the direction that the ground\ngradually slopes.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5107,-9,6,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  The sewer pipe continues on its northeast to southwest trek.  The water\ncontinueing to flow to the southwest.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5108,-8,7,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  The slime seems to be more congealed in this region and the water seems to be\nmore stagnant.  The sewer pipe continues along its northeast to southwest\ntrack but the water that flows to the southwest seems to start from here.\nYou see some grates in the ceiling that allow almost no light.  Tiny drops\nof water fall from the grates to the floor and begin their journey southwest.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5109,-7,8,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  A very, very small amount of light enters this northeast-southwest pipe\nthrough the grates from the road above.  A thick slime covers the walls\nand small drops of water begin their journey to the northeast.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5110,-6,9,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  As you continue your journey through this northeast to southwest running\npipe, you notice the boots of what appears to be a cityguard standing on\nthe grate above you, but they quickly move on, most likely making rounds.\nThere is a slimy substance clinging to the walls all about this area.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5111,-5,10,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  This is a northeast to southwest running pipe.  The walls of the pipe\nare covered with a slimy coating while a trickle of water heads off to the\nnortheast.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5112,-4,11,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  The sewer pipe bends here.  Probably to follow the path of the road above.\nA portion heads to the southwest, while the other heads east.  There is\nsome very faint light entering from the grate above and a slick coating\non the walls of the pipe.  A trickle of water heads east.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5113,-3,11,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  The pipe slopes gently eastwards, causing the water to trickle in that\ndirection.  You hear boots scraping against the grate above you and the\nslime about the area oozes down the walls.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5114,-2,11,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  You journey through an east-west pipe.  It is large enough for wagons to\npass through and you can only begin to guess how much water it could hold.\nAs you look through the grate above you, you are splashed by someone who\nis conveniently disposing of their sewage.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5115,-1,11,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  This pipe journeys east and west and gently slopes upwards to the west,\nthe water flowing to the east.  As it begins to rain, you hope it\ndoesn\'t rain too hard until you have made it back to the surface.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5116,0,11,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  At this sewer intersection, the water from the east-west pipe joins and\nbegins its southerly journey.  This combination of water causes the flow\nto gain in depth and in speed.  As the cold water seeps to your foot, a\nchill races up your spine.  You see a sign on the wall.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5117,1,11,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  The water in this pipe mixes with the slime that covers the walls and\ngently flows to the west.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5118,2,11,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  This east-west sewer is large enough to hold several thousands of gallons of\nwater, though you probably wouldn\'t want to be here to prove it.  The walls\nglisten with a slimy substance and the water trickles to the west.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5119,3,11,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  This is an east and west running pipe.  The rounded stone walls are covered\nwith a slick slime.  You notice the garbage and human waste that is mixed\nin with the water as it slowly flows westward.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5120,4,11,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  The stone sewer pipe bends here.  A portion heads off to the southeast\nwhile another portion, and the water, head west.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5121,5,10,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  You journey through a northwest to southeast running piece of stone pipe.\nThe rounded walls are covered with a slimy substance.  There is little\nlight coming in from the grate above you.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5122,6,9,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  You continue to journey through a northwest to southeast running sewer pipe.\nThe little light that enters through the grate above, reflects off of the\nstone walls and that ever present slime.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5123,7,8,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  This sewer pipe intersection has a branch that goes south.  You see a\nsmall sign on the concrete wall, most of it is unobscured by the slime.\nSome of the water drifts south, but most goes to the northwest.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5124,8,7,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  As the water drips of the grate above you, down the slime covered walls\nand onto the floor, it starts its long, dreary path towards the southeast.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5125,9,6,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  A little light shines through the grate above.  Some of it reflects off the\nslime on the concrete walls.  The water gently flows towards the southeast.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5126,10,5,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  This northwest to southeast pipe is large enough to hold several thousands\nof gallons of sewage.  The small grate in the ceiling allows the water\nto seep in from the road above.  A slime coating covers the concrete walls\nof this engineering wonder and the water travels along a lazy course to the\nsoutheast.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5127,11,4,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  This large, rounded, concrete sewer pipe and local wonder of The World\nbends at this juncture.  A portion heads to the northwest while the water\ncontinues down the southern track.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5128,11,3,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  As a faint light shines through the grate above your face, if reflects off\na sign placed on the wall.  The sign is partially covered with this ever\npresent slime that is common in all sewers.  The water continues along its\nway to the south.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5129,11,2,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  This north-south running sewer is roughly round.  Its concrete walls are\ncovered with your typical sewer slime and the southward flowing water is\nyour normal mix of rain water, sewage, and human waste.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5130,11,1,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  This north and south running pipe could hold quite a bit of water.  There\nis little light entering in through the grate above.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5131,11,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  You stand at the juncture of two sewer pipes.  The water from the north-\nsouth pipe combine here to flow westward.  The joint flow gains speed and\nmomentum on its westward trek.  A chill draft seems to flow from the pipe\nto the south and it seems darker, if thats possible.  There is a small\nsign on the wall.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5132,11,-1,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','  What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  Water drips from the edges of the\ngrate, indicating a recent rain.  The water falls to the ground and joins\nthe stream of water flowing north.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5133,11,-2,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','  What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  Standing in a couple of centimeters\nof water the northward stream starts to get your feet wet.  It seems the\nstream has actually risen since you started wandering the sewers possibly\ndue to rain above.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5134,11,-3,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','    What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  Slime covers the rounded stone walls\nof the sewer.  This engineering marvel could channel several days worth of\nsewage and rain.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5135,11,-4,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','    What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  This is the juncture of two pipes.\nClose inspection reveals the small seam between the two is so tight, that you\ncan barely fit the tip of a dagger between the two.  One of the pipes heads\nnorth with the water flow, the other comes from the southwest.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5136,10,-5,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','    What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  You are in a diagonal running sewer\npipe.  Some slime drips off the walls onto your gear leaving a sticky film.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5137,9,-6,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','    What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  This pipe continues its diagonal run\nand the water flows to the northeast.  The slime drips down the walls and\nmixes with some congealed water.  A shadow passes over the grate above you\nbut quickly moves on.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5138,8,-7,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','    What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  The rounded concrete walls glow\ndimly  with the thin coating of gook and slime giving you you a fairly good\nindication of the waters content.  The water seems thinnest here as it begins\nits trek to the northeast.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5139,7,-8,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','    What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  You stand at the intersection of a\ncouple of sewer pipes.  It seems the main pipe runs northeast to southwest,\nbut a small branch heads north.  From the dark opening a strange chill seems\nto almost reach out and grip the back of your neck.  The water flows gently\nto the southwest.  The most obvious decoration is the graffiti chiseled on\nthe wall.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5140,6,-9,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','  What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  This diagonal running sewer channels\nthe water to the southwest.  The slime that covers the walls reflect water\nthat comes in from the grate above you.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5141,5,-10,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','  What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  The diagonal pipe continues, its\ncontent of water and slime oozing along to the southwest.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5142,4,-11,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','  This bend in the pipe directs the flow of the water from the northeast\npipe to head towards the west.  You have seen so much slime, you begin\nto wonder if it is edible.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5143,3,-11,-1,'City Sewer','  What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  The pipe is rounded and hard.  The\nflow of water causes something to bump into your foot.  You think about\nfinding out what it is, but the stench of the water quickly quells your\ncuriosity.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5144,2,-11,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','  What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  This east to west running pipe\nchannels water towards the west.  Its stone covered walls are covered with\nslime.  The sewage in the water stinks with the mix of water, garbage, and\nhuman waste.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5145,1,-11,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','  What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  The water in the pipe picks up speed\nas it flows westward.  Much of it eddies in stagnant pools, caught up in the\nflotsam and jetsam in the water.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5146,0,-11,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','  What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  The sign attached to the rounded,\nstone walls, reflects what little light shines through the grate.  The\nwaters from the east-west pipe, join and head north.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5147,-1,-11,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','  What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  The pipe seems to continue both\neast and west for some distance.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5148,-2,-11,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','  What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  If you listen very closely, you\ncan hear the sounds of footsteps nearby.  It sounds as if someone is walking\nalong a parallel path to you.  The sound reverberates through the tunnel-like\npipe.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5149,-3,-11,-1,'Eerie City Sewer','  What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  This east-west path channels the\nwater to the east.  As you move through the water, it stirs up the sediments\nand produces a wretched odor.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5150,-4,-11,-1,'Cave-in','  What little light shines in through the grate above your head seems to be\nabsorbed by the strange chill about you.  Water laps up against the pile of\nstones that blocks your path to the west.  It seems as if the roof has caved\nin and filled the gap to the west making the way impassable.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5151,-6,-9,-1,'Cave-in','  A massive pile of rubble blocks your passage to the southeast.  Almost\ncovered is a sign on the wall, after you rub off the dust, you can make\nout the words.  The water here is very stagnant and smells like somebody\nhasn\'t flushed their toilet in weeks.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5152,-7,-8,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  In this diagonal, northwest-southeast running pipe, the water seems to\nstagnate to the southeast, and lazily flow towards the northwest.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5153,-8,-7,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  The concave walls cause your footsteps on the water to echo throughout\nthe length of the pipe.  You hear chattering all around you and something\nbrushes by your foot in the water.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5154,-9,-6,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  This sewer must continue forever.  You notice the roadway above you as\nyou sneak a glance through the grate.  There is some graffiti chiseled on\nthe wall here.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5155,-10,-5,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  The diagonal continues.  You hope it doesn\'t rain too much or these sewers\ncould be filled, an unthinkable nightmare for anyone in them.  The slime\noozes down the side of the rounded concrete walls mixing with the water below.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5156,-11,-4,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  The pipe bends here, part of it heads north with the flow of the water, the\nother heads off to the southeast.  Light through the grate reflects off the\nslime that oozes down the walls.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5157,-11,-3,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  The pipe extends for as far as you can see to the north, and bends further\nto the south.  The water lazily floats to the north.  You slip on something\nin the water and catch yourself by placing your hand against the wall...  right\nsmack into some slime.  Yuck!\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5158,-11,-2,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  Rounded stone walls, complete with slime make this a picture perfect\nsewer.  Light enters in slivers from the grate overhead as the pipe continues\nto the north and south.  The water in the bottom of the pipe flows north on\nits slow lazy trek.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5159,-11,-1,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath Perimeter Road','  You stand near the middle of a north and south running sewer.  A faint\nlight beams through the grate above you, reflecting off the slimy walls and\nthe water.  The water gently flows north.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5160,-10,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath West King\'s Way','  The water flows at a decent pace to the east coming up to your knees.\nCold and unpleasant the water seems to move through the skin of your\nfeet chilling you to the bone.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5161,-9,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath West King\'s Way','  Water flows eastward here on its journey, gaining depth and speed as it\nproceeds.  The moving mix of water, garbage, and human waste kicks up a\ntremendous, almost toxic smell.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5162,-8,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath West King\'s Way','  The sewer continues its east-west trek at this point.  The water flowing\neastward, gaining depth and speed as it continues.  You hear the sound of\na waterfall in the distance.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5163,-7,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath West King\'s Way','  The water now reaches your thighs as it heads down the eastern path of this\nstraight pipe.  The slime on the walls has trouble clinging to the stone\nwalls due to the force of the water.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5164,-6,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath West King\'s Way','  You stand in the middle of a four-way intersection.  Waters from both the\nnorth and south pipe join the waters from the western pipe in a roar that\nrips through your ears!  The water quickly reaches your waist and heads\nfor your chest as it quickly heads east.  You see a sign on the wall.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5165,-5,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath West King\'s Way','  The virtual torrent of water gushes through as it is funneled to the east.\nIt is getting hard to keep your balance.  You fear that if you trip and fall\nyou might never regain your feet.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5166,-4,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath West King\'s Way','  White water cascades against the side of the stone walls, causing what\nis left of the slime to loose its grip and head east.  Twigs and other\ndebris crash downstream with the flow of the current.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5167,-3,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath West King\'s Way','  Water from a southern pipe adds to the already full pipe.  The sound of a\nwaterfall is so deafening that you think it is probably right next door.\nEast is definitely not the way you would choose to go.  A small sign has\nbeen attached high on the northern side of the pipe.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5168,-2,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath West King\'s Way','  Water from the east joins the torrential pour of water from the west and\ngoes ...  down? You timidly feel around the floor with your right foot and\nfind that the floor immediately in the center of the room is, well, missing.\nYou quickly put your foot back down as the flow of water from the west\nthreatens to knock you off of your feet.\n',40,131084,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5169,-1,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath West King\'s Way','  There is the very loud roar of a waterfall directly to the west.  There\nisn\'t much water around your feet, barely a trickle.  Might this be the\ncalm in the middle of the storm?\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5170,0,0,-1,'Under Center Square','  You stand in the middle of a four-way intersection.  You see the base of\nwhat looks like a round fountain in the ceiling above you and a large pipe\nleading from the fountain, straight into the floor.  Water seeps from\naround the edges of the pipe and the water trickles down each of the four\npassages around you.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5171,1,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath East King\'s Way','  You stand in a large east-west running pipe.  It extends for as far as\nyou can see.  There is a puddle of water here, slowly heading east.  A large\nroar can be heard immediately to the east.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5172,2,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath East King\'s Way','  Water from the east cascades down a pipe in the floor.  You barely have\nroom to stand around the edge of the pipe.  You fight to maintain your\nfooting as the force of the water and sewage rushes by.\n',40,131084,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5173,3,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath East King\'s Way','  A large volume of water flows westward almost reaching chest high.\nThe sewage begins to irritate your skin as you feel it soaking into your\nclothing and gear.  Ooooh, that itches.  You don\'t seem to be able to\nreach that annoying spot on your back!\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5174,4,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath East King\'s Way','  Water rushes to the west, filled with slime, garbage, and human waste.  The\nsmell irritates your olfactory senses.  You hear the sound of a waterfall to\nthe west.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5175,5,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath East King\'s Way','  The water continues its journey westward.  There is still some slime\nclinging to life on the walls.  The stone walls echo with the sound of a\nwaterfall in the distance to the west.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5176,6,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath East King\'s Way','  The rounded stone walls reverberate with the sound of water rushing westward.\nIt is hard to hear yourself think, over the deafening noise.  All about you\nwaste water, sewage, and slime speed by on their journey.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5177,7,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath East King\'s Way','  Water from the north joins with the water from the east as it heads to the\nwest.  The water comes up to your waist and chills you to the bone.  You see\na small sign on the wall.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5178,8,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath East King\'s Way','  There is a fair, but not a tremendous amount of water flowing through here.\nThe slime clings to the rounded stone walls and you see some light entering\nthrough the grate above.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5179,9,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath East King\'s Way','  Light enters through a grate above and gently shines off of the oozy slime\nthat adheres itself to the concave, stone edifice.  A branch, at least you\nhope it\'s a branch, brushes by your leg and continues to flow with the water\nto the west.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5180,10,0,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath East King\'s Way','  This room, with the slime covered walls and the light entering through\na grate above you, is filled with rushing water and the flotsam and jetsam\nthat is carried along with it.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5181,0,10,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath North Main Street','  This pipe continues to channel the water southward.  To the north you hear\nthe sounds of water crashing.  A very small amount of illumination enters\nthe sewer from the grate on the street above.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5182,0,9,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath North Main Street','  Something in the sewer water knocks you off of your feet, or did you slip?\nIt is hard to tell the difference.  There is a sign on the smooth stone wall\nthat is partially covered in slime.  It looks as if somebody actually tried\nto polish it recently.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5183,0,8,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath North Main Street','  The knee high water flows southward.  A shadow passes over the grate above\nyou, wait, did you know him?  As you jump up to take a closer look, you hit\nyour head on the ceiling!  Ouch!  That was pretty stupid.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5184,0,7,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath North Main Street','  As the water flows southward, and the tiny amount of illumination enters\nthrough the grate, onto the slime covered walls, you notice the indentations\nof some graffiti a teenage punk from Grimhaven chiseled in the wall.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5185,0,6,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath North Main Street','  Water from the west enters the pipe here joining with the southward flow.\nIt creates a small eddy and with some white foam at the surface of the water.\nThe water seems a bit murky from all the dirt that is mixed in with it.  A\nsign has been embedded high on the eastern side of the pipe.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5186,0,5,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath North Main Street','  As you continue your journey through this dark tunnel of dampness, you\ntrudge through a deep pile of what seems to be sand.  The wetness feels\ngrainy between your toes and you really wish you had watched your step.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5187,0,4,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath North Main Street','  The hairs on your leg begin to stand on end and your skin begins to form\ngoose bumps after prolonged exposure to the tepid water.  The unpotable water\nbegins to irritate the skin on your legs causing them to itch.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5188,0,3,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath North Main Street','  Thick with the filth the pipe about you is filled with sewer water, human\nwaste, and thick congealed bits of slime.  The water flows southward at\na hurried pace.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5189,0,2,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath North Main Street','  The water disappears from sight as gravity pulls it downward.  A whirlpool\nforms in the water as it spirals counter-clockwise in its descent.  You\nfight to remain back from the edge where you risk losing your footing.\n',40,131084,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5190,0,1,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath North Main Street','  There is a small trickle of water that backwashes from a drain to the north.\nThe water pauses, but still attempts to head in that direction as a stronger\nflow of water arrives from the south and pushes it north.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5191,0,-1,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath South Main Street','  Drops of water from the cascade to your south, splash in your face.  The\nlittle seepage from the north arrives and heads for the southern drain.\nYou hear a deafening roar from all the water pouring down the sewer, a\nrecent shower lending its aid.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5192,0,-2,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath South Main Street','  Water flushes in a downward spiral at an alarming rate.  A massive gush of\nwater feeds into the room and almost immediately disappears from view as it\ndrops straight down.\n',40,131084,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5193,0,-3,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath South Main Street','  This pipe heads north and south.  Water flows urgently from the southern\nsection and continues north through the pipe.  A loud waterfall type sounds\nechoes from the north.  You see a small sign on the wall.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5194,0,-4,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath South Main Street','  The north to south pipe continues its course.  A small amount of light\nenters from the grate above you.  The rounded stone walls of the pipe, give\nthis a tunnel like atmosphere.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5195,0,-5,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath South Main Street','  The pipe continues to the north and south.  The water, full of garbage,\nhuman waste, and various forms of debris continues its long journey, gaining\nspeed and momentum as it heads north.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5196,0,-6,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath South Main Street','  This long stretch of pipe continues.  There is a lot of slime covering the\nrounded stone walls.  You notice some strange slime formations clinging to\nsome odd indentations in the wall.  As you clear it away, you notice the\npattern that forms.  Something is written here.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5197,0,-7,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath South Main Street','  This is a large north to south running pipe.  It has smooth, rounded stone\nwalls and a layer of slime covers everything.  A small amount of light\nenters through a grate above you.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5198,0,-8,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath South Main Street','  You hear the sound of a large amount of water cascading towards you.  Hmmm...\nyou wonder if this is the right place to stand and take a good look of your\nsurroundings.  You are probably better off running for your life, but, that\never present slime has so aroused your scientific curiosity that you just\ncan\'t break away from it and you study it more closely.  It pulsates with a\nseemingly life of its own.  You wonder what it would look like in a petri-dish.\nYou begin to wonder what it would taste like.  You begin to wonder why you\nare still here wondering about slime and not running away.\n',40,131080,33,100,5198,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5199,0,-9,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath South Main Street','  You stand in a north to south running sewer.  The water has risen to your\nknees and you begin to hope that it hasn\'t rained too hard recently or this\npipe could fill up rather quickly.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5200,0,-10,-1,'A City Sewer Pipe Beneath South Main Street','  The water continues its trek to the north.  It is about knee deep and seems\nto be getting deeper quickly.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5201,-1,6,-1,'A Web Filled Sewer Pipe','  This sewer pipe is a little smaller then the main pipe and its upper regions\nare coated with thick masses of spider webs.  It seems that the sewer workers\navoid this section of pipe in their cleaning.  There is a grate up a really\nsmall shaft in the ceiling which is impossible to reach from here.  The water\nheads east towards the main pipe.\n',40,131084,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5202,-2,6,-1,'A Web Filled Sewer Pipe','  This sewer pipe is a little smaller then the main pipe and its upper regions\nare coated with thick masses of spider webs.  It seems that the sewer workers\navoid this section of pipe in their cleaning.  There is a grate up a really\nsmall shaft in the ceiling which is impossible to reach from here.   Water\ncontinues to trickle to the east.  There is so little water, compared to the\nmain shaft, that it is almost dusty in here.  As a matter of fact, you wonder\nif those are the remnants of footprints of a rat in the dust on the ground,\nseems an odd pattern.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5203,-3,6,-1,'A Web Filled Sewer Pipe','  This sewer pipe is a little smaller then the main pipe and its upper regions\nare coated with thick masses of spider webs.  It seems that the sewer workers\navoid this section of pipe in their cleaning.  There is a grate up a really\nsmall shaft in the ceiling which is impossible to reach from here.   This\nsection of pipe makes you feel real creepy.  The hair all over your body\nstands on edge and your blood begins to pump louder and faster.  You begin\nto think something\'s not quite right around here.  To the south you see\na crack in the wall of the sewer pipe.\n',40,131084,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5204,-4,6,-1,'A Web Filled Sewer Pipe','  This sewer pipe is a little smaller then the main pipe and its upper regions\nare coated with thick masses of spider webs.  It seems that the sewer workers\navoid this section of pipe in their cleaning.  There is a grate up a really\nsmall shaft in the ceiling which is impossible to reach from here.   Dried\nleaves at your feet soak up most of the water that enters from the west but\na faint trickle heads east.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5205,-5,6,-1,'A Web Filled Sewer Pipe','  This sewer pipe is a little smaller then the main pipe and its upper regions\nare coated with thick masses of spider webs.  It seems that the sewer workers\navoid this section of pipe in their cleaning.  There is a grate up a really\nsmall shaft in the ceiling which is impossible to reach from here.   The water\nin the bottom of the pipe heads east at a slow trickle.  The pipe seems to\ndisappear around a bend farther to the west.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5206,-6,6,-1,'A Web Filled Sewer Pipe','This sewer pipe is a little smaller then the main pipe and its upper regions\nare coated with thick masses of spider webs.  It seems that the sewer workers\navoid this section of pipe in their cleaning.  There is a grate up a really\nsmall shaft in the ceiling which is impossible to reach from here.   The pipe\nturns here water trickling away in both directions.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5207,-6,5,-1,'A Web Filled Sewer Pipe','  This sewer pipe is a little smaller then the main pipe and its upper regions\nare coated with thick masses of spider webs.  It seems that the sewer workers\navoid this section of pipe in their cleaning.  There is a grate up a really\nsmall shaft in the ceiling which is impossible to reach from here.   The water\nat the bottom of the pipe heads south at a slow trickle.  The pipe seems to\ndisappear around a bend to the north.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5208,-6,4,-1,'A Web Filled Sewer Pipe','  This sewer pipe is a little smaller then the main pipe and its upper regions\nare coated with thick masses of spider webs.  It seems that the sewer workers\navoid this section of pipe in their cleaning.  There is a grate up a really\nsmall shaft in the ceiling which is impossible to reach from here.   There is\na small trickle of water heading south in the bottom of the pipe.  Most of the\nwalls are caked with a dirt that represents the sediments contained within\nthe murky waters.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5209,-6,3,-1,'A Web Filled Sewer Pipe','  This sewer pipe is a little smaller then the main pipe and its upper regions\nare coated with thick masses of spider webs.  It seems that the sewer workers\navoid this section of pipe in their cleaning.  There is a grate up a really\nsmall shaft in the ceiling which is impossible to reach from here.   This pipe\nreveals its age by the slime and filth which is congealed on the cracked stone\npipe\'s surface.  A small trickle of water meanders its way south.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5210,-6,2,-1,'A Web Filled Sewer Pipe','  This sewer pipe is a little smaller then the main pipe and its upper regions\nare coated with thick masses of spider webs.  It seems that the sewer workers\navoid this section of pipe in their cleaning.  There is a grate up a really\nsmall shaft in the ceiling which is impossible to reach from here.   This side\npipe continues to head along its north-south guidelines.  Small rivets of water\ncontinue to head south.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5211,-6,1,-1,'A Web Filled Sewer Pipe','  This sewer pipe is a little smaller then the main pipe and its upper regions\nare coated with thick masses of spider webs.  It seems that the sewer workers\navoid this section of pipe in their cleaning.  There is a grate up a really\nsmall shaft in the ceiling which is impossible to reach from here.   The water\nin the bottom of the pipe heads south towards the main pipe.\n',40,131084,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5212,-5,1,-1,'The Corner of a Spider Web','  You are on a small pile of debris and small rocks.  This vast cavern is\ncovered with spider webs.  Even as you move through it, some of the lesser\nstrands break off and cling to you, while others are too strong and you bounce\noff of them.  You spit a piece of webbing out of your mouth.  In this corner\nit appears that eggs have been laid to mature.  Some have already hatched,\ntheir larva quickly growing into a deadly young spiders, while others still\npulse and move as the life within developes.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5213,-1,1,-1,'The Corner of a Spider Web','  You are on a small pile of debris and small rocks.  This vast cavern is\ncovered with spider webs.  Even as you move through it, some of the lesser\nstrands break off and cling to you, while others are too strong and you bounce\noff of them.  You spit a piece of webbing out of your mouth.  In this corner\nit appears that eggs have been laid to mature.  Some have already hatched,\ntheir larva quickly growing into a deadly young spiders, while others still\npulse and move as the life within developes.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5214,7,1,-1,'A Cluttered Sewer Pipe','  This pipe seems to be a higher quality then the others.  The stonework\ndoesn\'t seem as dirty, there is no slime, and the stone is smoother than the\nmain passageways.  What seems odd is that numerous bits of trash and other\nbroken debris have been neatly collected and stored  or displayed here, almost\nas if they were treasured artifacts  It almost seems as if someone is trying\nto live in this section of the sewer.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5215,7,2,-1,'A Cluttered Sewer Pipe','    This pipe seems to be a higher quality then the others.  The stonework\ndoesn\'t seem as dirty, there is no slime, and the stone is smoother than the\nmain passageways.  What seems odd is that numerous bits of trash and other\nbroken debris have been neatly collected and stored  or displayed here, almost\nas if they were treasured artifacts  It almost seems as if someone is trying\nto live in this section of the sewer.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5216,7,3,-1,'A Cluttered Sewer Pipe','  This pipe seems to be a higher quality then the others.  The stonework\ndoesn\'t seem as dirty, there is no slime, and the stone is smoother than the\nmain passageways.  What seems odd is that numerous bits of trash and other\nbroken debris have been neatly collected and stored  or displayed here, almost\nas if they were treasured artifacts  It almost seems as if someone is trying\nto live in this section of the sewer.  There is a highly polished sign placed\ninto the smooth, rounded walls of the sewer.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5217,7,4,-1,'A Cluttered Sewer Pipe','  This pipe seems to be a higher quality then the others.  The stonework\ndoesn\'t seem as dirty, there is no slime, and the stone is smoother than the\nmain passageways.  What seems odd is that numerous bits of trash and other\nbroken debris have been neatly collected and stored  or displayed here, almost\nas if they were treasured artifacts  It almost seems as if someone is trying\nto live in this section of the sewer.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5218,7,5,-1,'A Cluttered Sewer Pipe','  This pipe seems to be a higher quality then the others.  The stonework\ndoesn\'t seem as dirty, there is no slime, and the stone is smoother than the\nmain passageways.  What seems odd is that numerous bits of trash and other\nbroken debris have been neatly collected and stored  or displayed here, almost\nas if they were treasured artifacts  It almost seems as if someone is trying\nto live in this section of the sewer.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5219,7,6,-1,'A Cluttered Sewer Pipe','  This pipe seems to be a higher quality then the others.  The stonework\ndoesn\'t seem as dirty, there is no slime, and the stone is smoother than the\nmain passageways.  What seems odd is that numerous bits of trash and other\nbroken debris have been neatly collected and stored  or displayed here, almost\nas if they were treasured artifacts  It almost seems as if someone is trying\nto live in this section of the sewer.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5220,7,7,-1,'A Cluttered Sewer Pipe','  This pipe seems to be a higher quality then the others.  The stonework\ndoesn\'t seem as dirty, there is no slime, and the stone is smoother than the\nmain passageways.  What seems odd is that numerous bits of trash and other\nbroken debris have been neatly collected and stored  or displayed here, almost\nas if they were treasured artifacts  It almost seems as if someone is trying\nto live in this section of the sewer.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5221,8,3,-1,'A Cluttered Sewer Pipe','  This pipe seems to be a higher quality then the others.  The stonework\ndoesn\'t seem as dirty, there is no slime, and the stone is smoother than the\nmain passageways.  What seems odd is that numerous bits of trash and other\nbroken debris have been neatly collected and stored  or displayed here, almost\nas if they were treasured artifacts  It almost seems as if someone is trying\nto live in this section of the sewer.  There isn\'t a lot of water in this\neast to west running pipe, just enough to create puddles of water on the floor.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5222,9,3,-1,'A Cluttered Sewer Pipe','  This pipe seems to be a higher quality then the others.  The stonework\ndoesn\'t seem as dirty, there is no slime, and the stone is smoother than the\nmain passageways.  What seems odd is that numerous bits of trash and other\nbroken debris have been neatly collected and stored  or displayed here, almost\nas if they were treasured artifacts  It almost seems as if someone is trying\nto live in this section of the sewer.  There isn\'t a lot of water in this\neast to west running pipe, just enough to create puddles of water on the floor.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5223,10,3,-1,'A Cluttered Sewer Pipe','  This pipe seems to be a higher quality then the others.  The stonework\ndoesn\'t seem as dirty, there is no slime, and the stone is smoother than the\nmain passageways.  What seems odd is that numerous bits of trash and other\nbroken debris have been neatly collected and stored  or displayed here, almost\nas if they were treasured artifacts  It almost seems as if someone is trying\nto live in this section of the sewer.  There isn\'t a lot of water in this\neast to west running pipe, just enough to create puddles of water on the floor.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5224,-6,-1,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  This is a straight, north to south running pipe.  It is carrying water\ntowards the north to join the main stream.  It is made of a smooth, curved\nstone and the walls are slightly covered with slime.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5225,-6,-2,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  This prolonged cylinder channels water to the north.  High up a shaft in the\nceiling, you can see the silhouette of a grate that allows the water into the\nsewer system.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5226,-6,-3,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  You stand at a T intersection of the sewer system.  Most of the water still\nflows to the south and some water from the east joins it causing the flow to\nswirl and eddy before continueing on its journey.  A sign has been firmly\nattached to the upper portion of the pipe.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5227,-6,-4,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  This is a long north to south running pipe.  The sound of water flowing\nechoes and reverberates around you.  Your feet stir up the sediments along\nthe bottom of the pipe and mix with the already rancid looking water.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5228,-6,-5,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  Light from a small grate, far up a small shaft in the ceiling, reflects\noff the water flowing north and the slime clinging to the rounded stone\nwalls of the pipe about you.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5229,-6,-6,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  Water flows to the north, but it seems to be more and more stagnant to the\nsouth.  You think you see a tadpole in the water, but how something could\nlive in this filth is beyond you.  You start to imagine a mutated, three-\neyed tadpole.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5230,-6,-7,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  This pipe is channeling what little moving water there is to the north.  The\nwater already comes up to your knees and you can see reflections of oils and\nother chemicals mixing upon the surface.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5231,-6,-8,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  You are in a large stone pipe at the bottom of which is a small puddle of\nwater.  The water is fairly stagnant with a little water trickling out the\nnorthern end.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5232,-3,-1,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  This north-south sewer pipe channels water towards the north.  You can see\nmany shadows pass over the small grate, high up a shaft in the ceiling.  This\npipe seems to be under a fairly busy street of Grimhaven.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5233,-3,-2,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  Water passes through this pipe.  The rounded stone walls show little sign\nof erosion or abnormal wear.  Some slime hangs onto the smooth surface,\ngiving you an indication of the water\'s rancid contents.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5234,-3,-3,-1,'A Sewer Intersection','  You stand at a four-way pipe intersection.  Through the small grate at the\ntop of the shaft in the ceiling you can hear the sounds of a busy market\nplace.  Taking up a large space at the center of the intersection is a huge\ncontraption complete encased in stone and steel which goes from floor to\nceiling.  A sign has been attached to the side of the pipe.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5235,-3,-4,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  The pipe channels water to the north.  It is built of stone, chiseled and\nrounded to a concave finish.  The dirtiest dirt and the slimiest slime cling\nto these hallowed walls.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5236,-3,-5,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  The pipe channels water to the north.  It is built of stone, chiseled and\nrounded to a concave finish.  The dirtiest dirt and the slimiest slime cling\nto these hallowed walls.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5237,-5,-3,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  The water in this tunnel doesn\'t know which way to flow.  It seems to be\npulled in both directions at once.  As a result, it seems to swirl and eddy\nas it divides and slowly moves off each way.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5238,-4,-3,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  This water flows towards the intersection to the east.  Slime slowly drips\ndown the walls, adding to the polluted water.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5239,-2,-3,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  This room seems to be a little cleaner.  You can almost make out the thin,\nethereal form of somebody.  Could it be the ancient, lost immortal Niko?  You\nsee a little plaque on the wall.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5240,-1,-3,-1,'A Well Maintained Sewer Pipe','  The water from this pipe flows towards the main pipe to the east.  Some\nbubbles rise to the surface and you wonder if it is a chemical reaction in\nthe water or could something actually live in this filth?\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5241,-5,-6,-1,'Pipe\'s End','You stand at the end of a sewer pipe.  The end is capped so that no\nwater may leak.  What little water there is, eddies and tries to return\ntowards the east.  On the cover that caps the pipe, there seems to be\nsome graffiti in some purple dye.  In the ceiling, something has broken\nthrough the pipe and dug upwards to the surface.  A dirty, rancid odor\npermeates the air.\n',-1,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5242,-4,-6,-1,'A Narrow Sewer Pipe','  You sense a great evil nearby.  Even the slime on the walls curdle in the\naura of the evil that you feel.  It causes your skin to prickle and form\ngoosebumps.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5243,-3,-6,-1,'A Narrow Sewer Pipe','  A few beams of light enter through the small grate at the top of a small\nshaft in the ceiling.  Water from the east and west join here to flow to the\nnorth.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5244,-2,-6,-1,'A Narrow Sewer Pipe','  Whew! It smells in here.  You thought the other sewers were bad?  This\ndoesn\'t even come close.  The smell of garbage decomposing with the help of\nmany maggots mixed in with human waste and other items, fermenting for all\nthese days in the hot sun, makes you fight to keep your last meal down.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5245,-1,-6,-1,'A Narrow Sewer Pipe','  The pipe turns here, causing the water to change directions.  It seems to be\nmeandering like the alley you can just glimpse through a narrow grate high\noverhead.  There is a little trickle of water that heads west.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5246,-1,-7,-1,'A Narrow Sewer Pipe','  You stand in the middle of a pipe.  A small amount of water trickles down the\ncenter.  Around each bend, to the north and to the south, the pipe turns\nout of sight.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5247,-1,-8,-1,'A Narrow Sewer Pipe','  The pipe bends here and cause the water to change direction.  The water\nflows north through the pipe.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5248,-2,-8,-1,'A Narrow Sewer Pipe','  There is a small crack in the wall of the pipe here.  From the crack comes\na putrid odor.  Water seeps both to and from the crack and what lies beyond.\nYou hope somebody comes and patches up the northern section of the pipe soon.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5249,-3,-8,-1,'A Narrow Sewer Pipe','  The water stagnates in puddles on the floor.  Various pieces of stranded\ndebris lie scattered about the floor of the pipe.  What little water there\nis trickles slowly to the east around piles of substances no longer\ndescribable.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5250,-4,-8,-1,'A Narrow Sewer Pipe','  You see more puddles here.  The slime has dried up and withered away.  The\nfloor of the pipe is covered with dust and mud.  The pipe seems to disappear\nto the west.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5251,-5,-8,-1,'A Narrow Sewer Pipe','  The pipe bends here.  Small puddles of water form at your feet.  The suction\nof the mud below is such it could cause someone to pull a muscle in their\nankle or knee just trying to walk though it.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5252,-2,-7,-1,'A Land Fill','There seems to be a cavern created by the trash from the dump.  Some large\npieces of trash are intricately fitted together to form the ceiling and the\nwalls.  The floor contains trash from ages past.\n',-1,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5253,-1,5,-1,'The Corner of a Spider Web','  You are on a small pile of debris and small rocks.  This vast cavern is\ncovered with spider webs.  Even as you move through it, some of the lesser\nstrands break off and cling to you, while others are too strong and you bounce\noff of them.  You spit a piece of webbing out of your mouth.  In this corner\nit appears that eggs have been laid to mature.  Some have already hatched,\ntheir larva quickly growing into a deadly young spiders, while others still\npulse and move as the life within developes.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5254,-4,5,-1,'The Edge of a Spider Web','  You are on a strand of icky-sticky spider webbing.  This vast cavern is\ncovered with the strands.  Even as you move through it, some of the lesser\nstrands break off and cling to you, while others are too strong and you bounce\noff of them.  You spit a piece of webbing out of your mouth.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5255,-3,5,-1,'The Edge of a Spider Web','  You are in a cavern that is covered with strands of webbing going in every\ndirection.  Some of the major strands are very thick and you can actually\nwalk across them with ease.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5256,-2,5,-1,'The Edge of a Spider Web','  You are standing on a strand of spider webbing.  You can feel the connecting\nstrands vibrate with the movement of the arachnids.  You hope you can\nmaintain your balance.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5257,-5,4,-1,'The Edge of a Spider Web','  This is the edge of the spider\'s web.  You notice that it is anchored to the\nwall here with a firm piece of webbing.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5258,-4,4,-1,'A Spider Web','  You stand on a section of spider webbing.  The stickiness causes those who\nwalk on them to pull hard with their legs, fighting for each step.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5259,-3,4,-1,'A Spider Web','  You balance yourself on a thick strand of spider webbing.  It is thick enough\nfor you to walk along.  Occasionally, the strand will shimmer and shake as\none of the owners uses it as a jumping point, or merely walks across it.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5260,-2,4,-1,'A Spider Web','  This is a large spider\'s web.  In places, you can see cocoons of where the\nspiders have captured a meal.  Most of them are now dried out husks, others\nstill wiggle a bit.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5261,-1,4,-1,'The Edge of a Spider Web','  You continue to meander around the spider\'s web.  The thick strands seem to\nbe strong enough to hold all of your weight.  Thousands of tiny, ethereal\nlooking strands hang from the ceiling or float through the air.  They\ncontinually land on your face and your clothes.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5262,-5,3,-1,'The Edge of a Spider Web','  The spider web sways a little more here.  There must be a large amount of\nactivity nearby on the web.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5263,-4,3,-1,'A Spider Web','  You are standing on a thick strand of sticky spider webbing.  Scattered about\nare dried husks of lifeforms drained of their life\'s blood and left to decay.\nOccasionally, one of the husks is still fresh and twitches.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5264,-3,3,-1,'The Center of a Spider Web','  This is the middle of the spider\'s web.  From here, one can see and feel\nall of the movement and disturbances of every strand.  Even the sound of the\ncavern seems to focus on this spot.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5265,-2,3,-1,'A Spider Web','  This strand seems abnormally thicker than most.  It vibrates with the\nmovement of something nearby.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5266,-1,3,-1,'The Edge of a Spider Web','  This is the edge of some spider webbing.  It is anchored to the walls of\nthe cavern with a thicker and stickier piece of webbing.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5267,-5,2,-1,'The Edge of a Spider Web','  This corner of the web is anchored by a thick strand of spider webbing to\nthe edge of the cavern.  It makes the web look like a large trampoline.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5268,-4,2,-1,'A Spider Web','  You almost slip and fall off of the strand of webbing as it shakes and\nshivers with something else moving.  You cling for dear life.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5269,-3,2,-1,'A Spider Web','  You are standing on a thick strand of sticky spider webbing.  Scattered about\nare dried husks of lifeforms drained of their life\'s blood and left to decay.\nOccasionally, one of the husks is still fresh and twitches.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5270,-2,2,-1,'A Spider Web','  Many of the weightless strands of webbing float through the air.  Your entire\nbody is covered with the stuff.  You look like you\'re sprouting gray hair.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5271,-1,2,-1,'The Edge of a Spider Web','  This is a sticky piece of webbing.  You notice a boot or two still stuck\nsecurely to the web where their wearer had to leave them on the adhesive path.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5272,-4,1,-1,'The Edge of a Spider Web','  This webbing is so sticky that many loose their boots walking across it.\nA dried out husk of some poor, unfortunate creature is caught here.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5273,-3,1,-1,'The Edge of a Spider Web','  Strands of tiny pieces of webbing float through the air.  It makes it feel\na lot a lot like Christmas.  There is a small piece of paper stuck here.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5274,-2,1,-1,'The Edge of a Spider Web','  This is where the web is anchored to the wall of the cavern.  A thick piece\nof gooey, extra thick, amazingly sticky webbing is attached to the wall.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5275,7,-7,-1,'A Rancid Smelling Sewer Pipe','  An unnatural chill seems to fill this small pipe which absorbs all light.\nThe pipe seems to connect to the main sewer system to the south and ends\njust to the west in darkness.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5276,6,-7,-1,'A Small Rancid Smelling Lair','  This looks like a small trash dump.  There are bits and pieces of food and\ngarbage scattered everywhere.  An unnatural chill fills the air, almost\nseeming to devour the very light about you.  The pipe seems to move east.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5277,-1,9,-1,'A Tiny Sewer Pipe','  This is a small and insignificant side sewer pipe.  It\'s hard to imagine why\nit is even here.  There is a little water that is backwash from the main pipe\nto the east.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,1,100,0,'',NULL),
(5278,-2,9,-1,'A Tiny Sewer Pipe','  The sewer pipe abruptly terminates to the west, furthering your feeling\nthat some city architect had absolutely no clue what he was doing when he\ncreated this diversion.  There is a little graffiti on the wall.\n',40,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5279,-2,0,-2,'Drainage Pipe','  This large pipe is channeling thousands of gallons of water from the pipes\nabove through a drainage system that leads downward.  It is hard to keep\nyour balance with the flow of the water.\n',40,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(5280,-1,0,-2,'Drainage Pipe','  This pipe is channeling so much water that you feel like you\'re standing in\nthe middle of some white-water rapids.  It almost knocks you off of your feet.\n',40,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(5281,-1,0,-3,'Drainage Pipe','  The roar of the crashing water is deafening.  You hope that you don\'t\nloose any equipment is this gushing water.\n',40,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(5282,2,0,-2,'Drainage Pipe','  Water is cascading down the pipe, hitting you on your head and basically\ndrenching you and all of your equipment.  It will take weeks for you to dry\nout.\n',40,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(5283,1,0,-2,'Drainage Pipe','  Water enters this section from the east and plummets downward.  Your footing\nis very treacherous.\n',40,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(5284,1,0,-3,'Drainage Pipe','  Water slams into your body as you try to navigate the water flowing through\nthe pipe.  You momentarily loose your footing but quickly recover.\n',40,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(5285,0,2,-2,'Drainage Pipe','  This pipe is channeling so much water that you feel like you\'re standing in\nthe middle of some white-water rapids.  It almost knocks you off of your feet.\n',40,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(5286,0,1,-2,'Drainage Pipe','  This pipe is channeling so much water that you feel like you\'re standing in\nthe middle of some white-water rapids.\n',40,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(5287,0,1,-3,'Drainage Pipe','  This pipe is channeling so much water that you feel like you\'re standing in\nthe middle of some white-water rapids.\n',40,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(5288,0,-2,-2,'Drainage Pipe','  Your vision is virtually obscured by the torrent of water that descends\nupon you.  You wonder where does it all go?\n',40,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(5289,0,-1,-2,'Drainage Pipe','  The water\'s fall is broken as it crashes onto a level surface and then\ncontinues is journey down.  There must be some obscure purpose to this\ndrainage system.\n',40,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(5290,0,-1,-3,'Drainage Pipe','  This pipe is trying desperately to succeed in draining its share of the\nwater into the room to the north.  A faint light emanates from the room.\n',40,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(5291,0,0,-3,'Water Purification Plant','  Your ears are deafened by the sound of water filling the room and the massive\npumps that force the water into a large machine standing in the middle\nof the room.  It seems to be capable of holding the entire ocean.  A pipe\nextends from the machine into the ceiling.  You are being pulled into the\nmachine by the suction generated by the massive pumps...\n',40,131085,29,10,5292,1,1,5,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(5292,0,0,0,'Filter','  You are dragged underwater by the force of the pumps.  You loose all sense\nof direction and have no clue which way is up.  You pass through several\nlarge screens that seem to filter out the filth and debris.\n',40,131080,30,10,5293,1,1,5,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5293,0,0,0,'Filter','  The water tosses and turns you.  You hope you can hold your breath a little\nlonger.  You break through several small filters that were used to filter\nout the microscopic particles that polluted the water.\n',40,131080,30,10,100,1,1,5,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5300,-14,0,0,'A Short Way Outside the Gates','  You stand just on the outer edge of town where a long road winds its way\nwestward into a large forest.  Sounds of the city echo off the stone walls\nwhere merchants sell their wares.  The forest is rich in color and is yet\nuntouched by the hands of progress, or so it has yet to be..\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5301,-15,0,0,'A Path Near Grimhaven','  The path to the west slopes sharply downhill for a few hundred yards.  At\nthe base of the hill a thick forest begins and trees line the horizon as far\nas the eye can see.  Far beyond, jutting from the treetops, lies a tremendous\nmountain range that disappears in the clouds.  To the east, just beyond the\ngates, lies the wonderful city of Grimhaven.  Known for its incredible\ncultural diversity, Grimhaven sits as a melting pot for all races in what is\nthought to be the center of the known world.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5302,-16,0,0,'On a Sloping Path','  The path to the west continues on a sharp downhill slope ending at the\nentrance to a thick forest, which seems to be marked by two enormous trees.\nAnd to the east, a large iron gate serves as an entrance to a large city.\nA cobblestone path leads north.\n',41,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5303,-29,7,0,'Deep in the Dark Woods of Lan\'Quin Forest','  You are not sure if you are heading in the right direction or not.  The\nceiling overhead is a tangle of dead limbs and barely surviving leaves, with\nfog and gloom closing in everywhere.  Strange howling sounds resound in your\near, coming from every direction at once.  Your ears strain to make out that\nslight rustling which follows you wherever you go, but you can not determine\nwhat the source is.  You only hope you can find the light of day before you\nsuffocate in this death gulch.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5304,-28,7,0,'Deep in the Dark Woods of Lan\'Quin Forest','  You are not sure if you are heading in the right direction or not.  The\nceiling overhead is a tangle of dead limbs and barely surviving leaves, with\nfog and gloom closing in everywhere.  Strange howling sounds resound in your\near, coming from every direction at once.  Your ears strain to make out that\nslight rustling which follows you wherever you go, but you can not determine\nwhat the source is.  You only hope you can find the light of day before you\nsuffocate in this death gulch.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5305,-27,7,0,'Deep in the Dark Woods of Lan\'Quin Forest','You are not sure if you are heading in the right direction or not.  The\nceiling overhead is a tangle of dead limbs and barely surviving leaves, with\nfog and gloom closing in everywhere.  Strange howling sounds resound in your\near, coming from every direction at once.  Your ears strain to make out that\nslight rustling which follows you wherever you go, but you can not determine\nwhat the source is.  You only hope you can find the light of day before you\nsuffocate in this death gulch.  Almost completely overcome by large tangles\nof overgrowth lies a wrought iron gate.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5306,-29,6,0,'Deep in the Dark Woods of Lan\'Quin Forest','  You are not sure if you are heading in the right direction or not.  The\nceiling overhead is a tangle of dead limbs and barely surviving leaves, with\nfog and gloom closing in everywhere.  Strange howling sounds resound in your\near, coming from every direction at once.  Your ears strain to make out that\nslight rustling which follows you wherever you go, but you can not determine\nwhat the source is.  You only hope you can find the light of day before you\nsuffocate in this death gulch.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
