(5350,-24,1,-1,'Large Tunnel','  Carved out of limestone, the tunnel is large enough to accommodate several\ntravelers side by side.  The tunnel path leads off northeast into darkness.\nThe sound of dripping water echoes softly off the walls.\n',37,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5351,-23,2,-1,'Large Tunnel','  Carved out of limestone, the tunnel is large enough to accommodate several\ntravelers side by side.  A small makeshift ladder is nailed to the side of\na pit that descends into darkness.  To the southwest the tunnel continues\nbending slightly.  The sound of dripping water echoes in from below.\n',37,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5352,-23,2,-2,'Underground Pool','  Within the limestone tunnel runs a small stream of clear water from a\nlarge pool.  The stream runs north until it falls off the edge of a small\ncliff.  This water system seems to be hand-made.  A small ladder runs up the\nside of the small cave into darkness.\n',37,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5353,-23,3,-2,'Underground Stream','  A small stream rushes in from a ledge above to land in a pool that drains\nthrough a long pipe in the wall.  A sloped walkway ascends to the ledge above\nwhere the stream seems to originate.  The path ends suddenly to the north in\na large pile of rubble.\n',37,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5354,-28,-2,0,'Bridge Over the Serpent River','  A wooden drawbridge has recently been built here directly over the\nSerpent river.  Due north the great Lan\'Quin forest sits silently, only the\nbrief wheeze of the wind can be heard echoing along the treetops.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5355,-28,-3,0,'Shortcut Through the Forest','  A well beaten path leads east and north here.  This shortcut through the\nwoods provides easy access through the forest which is free of bothersome shrubs\ngrass and woodbine.  A drawbridge can be seen north of you where the Serpent\nruns freely.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5356,-27,-3,0,'Shortcut Through the Forest','  A shortcut through the great Lan\'Quin forest provides easy access for\ntravelers that venture here.  The ground is free of bothersome shrubberies,\nonly brown faded leaves lie crumpled at your feet.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5357,-26,-3,0,'Shortcut Through the Forest','  A Shortcut through the great Lan\'Quin Forest provides easy access through\nthe rough terrain.  Jumbled foot prints on this path leaves you to believe that\nit is well traveled.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5358,-26,-4,0,'Shortcut Through the Forest','  A shortcut through the forest seen here provides easy access over the\nrough terrain.  Jumbled footprints that mark the path leaves you to believe\nthat it is well traveled.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5360,-23,6,-1,'Dark Passage','  The small passageway is just barely wide enough for two.  However, the\nroof is high enough that crouching is not needed.  A small crack in the wall\nilluminates the room slightly.  The tunnel contiues westward, but it\'s far\ntoo dark to see much further.\n',37,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5361,-24,6,-1,'Dark Passage','  The air in the passageway smells fresh, giving some indication that the\ntunnel is used from time to time.  A ladder rests against the side of a large\nhole that descends into darkness.  The path continues to the east but it\'s\ntoo dark to tell how far.\n',37,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5362,-24,6,-2,'Temple of the Two-Headed Snake','   This giant antechamber holds what seems to be a religous cogregation.\nThe smooth granite walls carry deep guttural voices throughout the temple.\nA low, slow rhythmic chant that seems to just keep repeating itself.  The\ncircular chamber holds very little decoration and even less dust.  It is\nmeticulously clean which, for ogres, is particularly surprising.  Small\nmats cover the entire floor all the way to the obsidian altar.  Upon the\naltar is an emblem of a snake with another head for a tail wrapped about a\ngolden chalice.  A piece of bone sticking out of the altar gives you an idea\nof what they do with intruders who interrupt their ceremonies.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5363,-24,7,-2,'Altar of the Two Headed Snake','The obsidian altar is long, smooth, and cold to the touch.  Tools lay\nabout it in an orderly fashion, and a small washing basin lie at the foot of\nit.  Upon closer inspection, the washing basin seems to be filled with more\nblood that water.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5364,-23,6,-2,'Magi Barracks','   Rows of cots line the walls of this large rectangular room.  Beside each\ncot sits a table and chair.  At the foot of each cot is a small chest which\nmust hold their belongings.  It seems as if they were more of a military\nregiment than one of the dark arts.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5365,-24,5,-2,'Private Chambers','   This is obviously the room for the leaders of these fanatics.  It is\nobvious that all wealth that was available at the time of construction went\ninto this particular room.  A large oak table of a beautiful design rests in\nthe center of the room.  Surrounding it are twelve high-backed chairs,\nequally as elegant.  Tapestries and elven rugs give the perfect touch of\nnobility to the room.  It\'s hard to believe that ogres inhabit such a place\nas this.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5366,-25,6,-2,'Torture Chamber','   Various wicked looking devices are placed all about this room.  A rack\nfor stretching victims, shackles all along the walls, tongs for tongue\npulling, and a foul looking chair with spikes all over it.  Blood stains\ncover the walls and floor, pieces of flesh are still left on some of the\nmachines, and even some whole body parts are lying about.  This is truly a\ndisgusting place.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5367,-32,-3,-1,'Entrance Hall','  This circular room is adorned with all sorts of tapestries, carpets, and\nsculptures.  Most of them have themes of nature, the forest, or various\nfaerie folk.  At the center of the room a tight spiral staircase carved from the\nsame wood as the tree ascends as far as you can see.  There is very little else\nin the way of furniture.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5368,-32,-3,0,'Giant Staircase','  The enormous wooden staircase seems to be carved out from the giant tree it\nlies within.  This suggests that the rest of these rooms were hollowed out as\nwell.  Truley, this is a magnificent place.  The craftsmanship is meticulous\nand delicate leaving no traces of flaws in the work.  Two large wooden\ngargoyles sit at each side of the staircase warding off evil spirits.\n',37,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5369,-31,-3,0,'Entrance Hall','  All along the wall of this circular room are paintings and tapestries of\nvarious natures.  It seems the purpose of this floor is to impress visitors\nwith the expensive and luxurious items.  To the west is a wooden spiral\nstaircase that ascends high into the tree.\n',37,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5370,-33,-3,0,'Entrance Hall','  All along the wall of this circular room are paintings and tapestries of\nvarious natures.  It seems the purpose of this floor is to impress visitors\nwith the expensive and luxurious items.  To the east is a wooden spiral\nstaircase that ascends high into the tree.\n',37,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5371,-32,-2,0,'Entrance Hall','  All along the wall of this circular room are paintings and tapestries of\nvarious natures.  It seems the purpose of this floor is to impress visitors\nwith the expensive and luxurious items.  To the south is a wooden spiral\nstaircase that ascends high into the tree.\n',37,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5372,-32,-4,0,'Secret Meeting Room','  This room is dimly lit by candles that line around the chamber walls.\nTwo gargoyles sit against the north wall warding off evil spirits while a\nlarge table with dark varnish lies in the center of the room surrounded by\ntwelve tall plush chairs.  One of the chairs seems to be a bit larger then\nthe rest, which seems to signify that this chair belongs to someone\nimportant.  Various items lie strewn across the table.\n',37,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5373,-32,-3,1,'On a Spiral Stairway','  The spiral widens out until it lines the outer wall of the tree.  Small\nwindows are carved out in various places and through it you can see the vast\nLan\'Quin forest.  The stairs continue upward to the second floor and\ndescend back down the the entrance hall.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5374,-32,-3,2,'On a Spiral Stairway','  The spiral narrows again as it reaches the second floor of the tree.  Doors\nare set in the north, south, east, and west walls.  The stairs continue up\nas far as you can see and descend down quite a ways as well.\n',37,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5375,-32,-2,2,'Council Chamber','  Apparently this is the room where all council affairs are held.  From the\nnorth wall of the room extends a platform that houses three large chairs.\nAlong the other walls are other comfortable seats.  Two aisles lead to doors\nin the southwest and southeast corners.  A door to the south provides access\nto the stairs.\n',37,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5376,-31,-3,2,'Guest Room','  This room is using for housing official guests and diplomatic emissaries.\nIt is well furnished with plush elven works.  The beds are large and soft,\nand a desk is provided for each occupant.  A door to the west provides\naccess to the stairway, while doors in the southwest and northwest corners\nlead off to other places.\n',37,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5377,-32,-4,2,'Dining Hall','  Two large stone tables adorn this room, handcrafted and exquisite.  The\ntables are set for a large feast and many workers rush around in\npreparation.  A door in the north wall provides access to the stairway, and\ndoors in the northwest and northeast walls lead off somewhere else.\n',37,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5378,-33,-3,2,'Lounge','  This room is to give visitors a little rest and relaxation.  Small\ncircular tables surrounded by chairs are spread about the room.  People play\nvarious card and dice games, smoke their pipes, drink, and listen to the\nfine music that the lounge is famous for.  A door in the east wall provides\naccess to the stairway, and doors in the northeast and southeast walls lead\noff somewhere else.\n',37,164025,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5379,-32,-3,3,'On a Spiral Stairway','  The spiral widens out until it lines the outer wall of the tree.  Small\nwindows are carved out in various places and through it you can see the vast\nLan\'Quin forest.  The stairs continue upward as far as you can see and\ndescend back down to the second floor.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5380,-32,-3,4,'On a Spiral Stairway','  The stairs seem to lead on forever.  Above you can just barely make out\nthe top of the tree.  Small windows are carved out of the tree in various\nplaces allowing you to view the vast Lan\'Quin forest.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5381,-32,-3,5,'Top of the Stairway','  The stairs below narrow and come to abrupt stop here on a large platform.\nAll around are large holes cut out of the tree to allow ventilation of the\ntree.  This gives you an amazing view of your surroundings.  To the east you\ncan see the giant city of Grimhaven, and off to the west the majestic\nParnithian mountians run across the horizon.  To the north the forest extends\nas far as you can see, the Serpent River winding and twisting its way\nthrough.  To the south the Kranor runs from the parnition mountains, splits\noff to form the Serpent, then continues on its way southeast.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5382,-32,-3,6,'Top of the Tree','  The wind blows hard making you cautious about your footing.  It would\nbe quite a disaster to take a tumble from this high up.  Much of your vision\nis blurred by the thick clouds surrounding the tree.  High above you, you\ncan spot a rather odd looking cloud that floats in the shape of a perfect\ncircle.\n',37,139432,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5383,-32,-3,7,'In the Air','  The wind whips you around a bit, but you are able to stay on your path.\nAbove you can see a large circular cloud that seems quite out of place.\nBelow you is the top of an absolutely gigantic tree which looks like it\nwould be a good landing spot.\n',37,131072,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5384,-36,0,0,'Bridge Over the Kranor River','  The Kranor River is very narrow here allowing the bridge you see before\nyou exist.  The bridge is made of makeshift boards thrown hastily together.\nAlthough you wouldn\'t want to be marching an army over it, it seems sturdy\nenough.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5385,-19,4,0,'Deep in the Dark Woods of Lan\'Quin Forest','  You are not sure if you are heading in the right direction or not.  The\nceiling overhead is a tangle of dead limbs and barely surviving leaves, with\nfog and gloom closing in everywhere.  Strange howling sounds resound in your\near, coming from every direction at once.  Your ears strain to make out that\nslight rustling which follows you wherever you go, but you can not determine\nwhat the source is.  You only hope you can find the light of day before you\nsuffocate in this death gulch.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5386,-29,-1,0,'Deep in the Dark Woods of Lan\'Quin Forest','  You are not sure if you are heading in the right direction or not.  The\nceiling overhead is a tangle of dead limbs and barely surviving leaves, with\nfog and gloom closing in everywhere.  Strange howling sounds resound in your\near, coming from every direction at once.  Your ears strain to make out that\nslight rustling which follows you wherever you go, but you can not determine\nwhat the source is.  You only hope you can find the light of day before you\nsuffocate in this death gulch.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
