(5399,-25,6,0,'Deep in the Dark Woods of Lan\'Quin Forest','  You are not sure if you are heading in the right direction or not.  The\nceiling overhead is a tangle of dead limbs and barely surviving leaves, with\nfog and gloom closing in everywhere.  Strange howling sounds resound in your\near, coming from every direction at once.  Your ears strain to make out that\nslight rustling which follows you wherever you go, but you can not determine\nwhat the source is.  You only hope you can find the light of day before you\nsuffocate in this death gulch.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5400,-17,0,0,'Entrance to the Lan\'Quin Forest','  Right at the base of the mighty Grimhaven plateau tower two immense, slender\nwhite-barked trees which have grown together at their tops to form a natural\narchway of wood and leaves.  The trees are, in fact, so much larger than the\nothers that you suspect they might have served a purpose at one time.  The sounds\nand smells of the forest waft from the trail and assault your senses with a warm\npleasent feeling.  To the west, you see the forest extend as far as your eye can\nsee.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5401,-18,0,0,'Forest Path','     The mighty oaks and hickories of the Lan\'Quin tower above your head.\nThe forest has a unique music of its own, a steady rhythm of animal noises\ncoming from all directions.  To the east stand two giant trees in the manner\nof a portal.  The trail continues downhill to the west where a roof of some\nsort of shack can be seen just on the horizon.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5402,-19,0,0,'Guard Outpost','     A hut in the forest serves as the forest station for the rangers who keep\nwatch at this junction within the woods.  The hut is large and spacious with\nwalls made up of logs and dirt, and a shingled roof keeps out the rain.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5403,-19,1,0,'A Forest Trail','     The trail shows evidence of recent travel, being wide and well cleared of\nbothersome shrubbery.  The trees form a green ceiling over your head, and the\nrustling of a stream can just barely be heard over the crunching of leaves and\nthe singing of birds.  To the south stands a large log hut, with sounds of\nhuman activity coming from within.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5404,-19,-1,0,'Path Through the Forest','  The forest path here is well tended and boasts various flowers of great\nbeauty.  Much of the tangle-some brush has been cut back, and several tree\nstumps provide evidence of excavation.  The reassuring sounds of the outpost\nare dampened by the thick woods to either side of you.  A light scent of\nsmoke drifts by as a breeze catches your attention.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5405,-20,0,0,'An Overgrown Path','  You are very aware of how easy it would to be to become lost in the vast\nLan\'Quin forest as you attempt to make your way through its huge, twisted\ntrees and yard high brush.  The smell of sap reflects your slow advance, and\nthe gloom of a dark forest with dancing shadows puts your nerves on edge.  You\nare hopeful, though, for sounds and smells of civilization waft from the east.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5406,-20,1,0,'A Forest Trail','   The trees off to the side of the trail here are a little less dense,\nmaking this site improbable for ambush.  To the north you can see the wooden\nbridge that leads over Serpent River, a tributary of the Kranor.  To the\nwest another, longer bridge spans the same stretch of water.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5407,-20,2,0,'Small Bridge','  You have come across a small wooden rope bridge.  As you walk over its\nrotted planks, you can feel the bridge sway from your weight.  Steadily\nyou move forward, glancing left to right where the river rushes madly over\na few jagged rocks below.  Up ahead you see the overgrowth for the forest\nyet untamed.  Images of foul beasts and uncivilized savages play through your\nmind.  Yet the silence of the forest seems harmless enough.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5408,-21,1,0,'A Long Bridge','    This stone bridge looks to be centuries old, and of strange origin, for it\nhas several archaic runes carved into its sides.  Moss and algae cover the\noutside of the structure, making them impossible to make out.  Fortunately,\nthe walkway is clear of anything slippery.  The bridge spans the length of\nSerpent River, a tributary of the Kranor river, whose gently flowing\nwaters gurgle underneath.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5409,-20,3,0,'On a Northern Hillside','You are standing near a large grassy hillside just north of a wooden bridge.\nThe smell of pine trees wafts from the east along with faint sounds of\ncivilization.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5410,-24,0,-1,'Serpent River','  The beautiful Serpent River flows gently here gurgling contently.  The\nhuge trees of the Lan\'Quin forest grow peacefully on the banks of the river.\nAn occasional twig or leaf can be seen drifting with the current.  Silvery\nfish swim beneath the waters surface, heading up stream.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5411,-23,1,-1,'Serpent River','  The Beautiful Serpent River flows gently here gurgling contently.  Huge\ntrees of the Lan\'Quin forest grow peacefully on the banks where an\noccasional leaf or twig drifts on the waters current.  Silvery fish can be seen\nheading upstream towards a large bridge seen eastward.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5412,-22,1,-1,'Serpent River','   The beautiful Serpent River flows gently beneath you, gurgling contentedly.\nThe huge trees of the Lan\'Quin forest grow peacefully on the banks of the\ncreek.  The occasional twig or leaf can be seen drifting with the current.\nSilvery fish swim beneath the water\'s surface, heading upstream.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5413,-26,-2,-1,'Swirling Waters','  The current is particularly strong here, rushing you on southward.  To the\neast you can hear a splashing sound much different from the rushing sound of\nthe creek.  You can see some unusually thick weeds growing beneath the surface\nof the water.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,15,5,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5414,-25,-1,-1,'Serpent Fountain','    You see a beautiful little spring which ushers forth the waters of the\nSerpent River.  The reflected light from the pool creates an aura about the\nfountain that seems to cleanse you of all bad thoughts and feelings and to\nbring about a healing effect.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5415,-26,-2,-2,'Entrance to the Shrine of Zelpth','  You have entered what appears to be some sort of shrine.  This place looks\nlike it might have once been aboveground but it has been long underwater.\nThe water is very calm, yet surprisingly clear.  No fish or other animals\nswim about, but several plants do grow from cracks in the marble floor,\nwalls, and ceiling.  Empty torch sconces are covered with rust, but several\ncandelabra on insets in the walls remain free of tarnish.  Thick, lush and\nwater-logged carpet covers the floor, a deep red in color, with pieces of the\nmosaic ceiling scattered about in various places where the ceiling has begun\nto deteriorate.  What remains of the mosaic seems to depict some sort of\nlarge, fiery bird.  A dark stairway leads further down, and archways provide\nexits to the east, west, and south.\n',37,131081,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5416,-20,2,-1,'Under The Bridge','  Shadows from the wooden bridge overhead play across the surface of the\nSerpent River.  The current heads west, and you can see small silvery fish\nfighting their way upstream.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5417,-21,1,-1,'Beneath the Long Bridge','  Beneath the bridge, Serpent River continues on its never ending path.  But\nsomehow the water seems to be moving faster, as if it were somehow afraid and\nfleeing from some unknown terror.  The bottom of the bridge is completely\nsmothered with moss and algae, the stone-work completely hidden from view.\nYou notice that the normal sounds of wildlife are absent and beneath this\nbridge no birds can be heard chirping, insects seem to be non-existent, and\neven the silver fish who swim upstream refuse to splash, they simply continue\non their way at full speed.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5418,-28,-2,-1,'Serpent River','  The Serpent River seems to be rebuked by this muddy embankment directly\nunder the bridge.  The healthy grasses and vegetation of Lan\'Quin are missing\nhere; in fact the only form of life besides the ever-present silver fish is\nthe same moss and algae found all over the bridge.  Or at least, that is the\nonly visible form of life...\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5419,-27,-2,-1,'Serpent River','   The beautiful Serpent River flows gently beneath you, gurgling contentedly.\nThe huge trees of Lan\'Quin Forest grow peacefully on the banks of the creek.\nThe occasional twig or leaf can be seen drifting with the current.  Silvery\nfish swim beneath the water\'s surface, heading upstream.  A large stone bridge\ncrosses the stream to the east.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5420,-22,1,0,'A Long Bridge','   This stone bridge looks to be centuries old, and of strange origin, for it\nhas several archaic runes carved into its sides.  Moss and algae cover the\noutside of the structure, making the runes impossible to make out clearly.\nFortunately, the walkway is clear of anything slippery.  The bridge spans the\nlength of Serpent River, whose gently flowing waters gurgle underneath.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5421,-23,1,0,'Eastern Part of the Lan\'Quin Forest','  The trees here are extremely dense giving a sense of pressure from the\nforest.  Apart from an occasional bird chirping, all seems completely\nsilent.  Even the trees themselves seem to be still in the light winds.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5422,-32,3,0,'Near the Edge of the Forest','  The trees here are quite few in number compared to the thick forest that\ncan be seen to the east.  You note the lack of animal sounds in the area\nwhich gives your surroundings an eerie feeling.  A clearly defined\ncobblestone road can be seen at the edge of the forest to the west.  You can\ntell the road is clearly well tended which perhaps hints at the idea of\ncivilization.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5423,-32,2,0,'A Circle of Stones','  The stones that form the perfect circle glow with a pulsating light, or\nperhaps anti-light, for with each pulse the surrounding area seems to grow\ndarker and darker.  Faint runes inscribed upon each stone glow with a blood\nred light.  The grasses around the circle are sparse and stringy, but the\nground within the circle is singed and scorched as if some great cremation\nhad taken place here.  Bones of every size and description sanctify the\nground with their timeless vows of silence.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5424,-21,0,0,'Clearing in the Woods','  The mighty trees of the Lan\'Quin forest cloud you in gloom and despair.  The\nsmell of rotting leaves and other compost nearly makes you cover your face.\nOff to your left you see a large mound of dirt, lacking vegetation, almost a\nsmall clearing.  Then you realize that this spot had once been home to a large\ntree which has been ripped out of the ground, roots and all.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5425,-20,-1,0,'An Overgrown Path','  Large patches of crumbling stones covered with dirt and moss lie together\nin a broken mosaic of a trail here.  This path was once a thick stone road\nspaning ten feet in length, or so it seems.  But nature has won over this man\nmade artifact of the past, now weeds spawn through its eroded cracks and left\nonly a path slightly easier to travel then the underdeveloped Lan\'Quin\nforest.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5426,-22,0,0,'Clearing in the Woods','  The forest floor becomes littered here with rocks of varying sizes; some are\nas small as a coin, others the size of an ogre\'s head.  Large boulders are\ncovered with moss and lichens, silently keeping guard for the Lan\'Quin forest.\nSeveral spots on the ground are bare of both rocks and plant life, as if there\nwere once large objects sitting there.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5427,-23,0,0,'A Charred Path','  The path has been set on fire recently.  Blackend soot smolders off the small\nshrubs and grasses that forms a charcoal path.  Smells of refuse, sweat and\nother less tastful odors sweep through the stale air.  Worthless charred furs\nand leather skins have been sewn by an intense heat to what seems to be human\nremains.  Four skulls propped upon wooden stakes lie here as markings.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5428,-24,0,0,'Encampment on a Charred Path','  A large iron pot dominates the scenery, for within are bloated humanoid\ncorpses cooking in some sort of sludge.  A large hollowed leg bone serves as\nthe ladle for the massive pot, its flesh having been long ago stripped by the\nboiling waters.  The stench of the cooking flesh is carried by a brief gust of\nwind.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5429,-24,-1,0,'A Charred Path','  The constant stream of smoke fills the stale are here along this charred\npath where small entrails lie scattered on the ground.  Fragments of skeletal\nbones, possibly of an animals or many different animals can be seen portruding\nout of the soot layered ground like small spikes pointing upwards.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5430,-24,-2,0,'Scarecrow on a Charred Path','  A bloodstained cloth scarecrow is seen centered here in an secluded part\nof this path pegged to a wooded cross stake.  Toppled trees, burnt to the ground\nlay upon heaps of shrubs that block off any further navigation.  The smoke\nwafting around you creates a veil of mist that obscures your vision and\nleaves you choking violently.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5431,-24,-3,0,'Scarecrows Nest','  Branching off from the path, this section of the woods is filled with\nstraw and dirt, forming a soft barrier between your feet and the ground.\nPools of blood stain the charred shrubs and toppled trees around you as if\nsome poor soul exploded from a great force.  A sudden cold passes through you\nand for a split second you heard, or thought you heard screams echoing from\nthe south.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5432,-23,-1,0,'A Charred Path','Sections of brick and wooden shingles lie here in a mass heap.  This looks\nto have once been a small building of some sort that existed long ago.  Next to\nwhat use to be a chimney is a large broken steel circle interwoven with various\nspikes and orbs.  The device is truly beautiful, in its own hideous way, for it\ncould have surely at one time, or even now, rend flesh quite easily.\n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5433,-23,-3,0,'Lair of the Ghostkeeper','  This appears to be a crude nursery.  Piles of hay and other dead vegetable\nmatter make for beds, and several skulls and broken trinkets stolen from\nvictims serve as the toys.  This room is the source of the ear wrenching\nscreaming.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5434,-19,3,0,'A Bend in the Forest','  A small bend in the forest thickens here with wide spreading trees and\nrich soil.  Soft pine needles cushion the ground around you.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5435,-21,3,0,'Sleeping Area','  This clearing is covered with straw, fur and dung.  The absolute stench\nof the place is enough to send any ogre\'s bowels churning.  Scraps of clothing\nlay strewn about and stuff you would have to call food for lack of a better\nname.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5436,-20,-2,0,'An Overgrown Path','  Large pieces of crumbling stones covered in moss and dirt lie together in a\nbroken mosaic of a trail.  This path was once a lush stone road spanning ten feet\nin width, but nature has won over it leaving it decayed and eroded.  All thats\nleft of the road is a path slightly easier to travel on other than the\nunderdeveloped Lan\'Quin forest.  To the east you spot a large clearing off this\ngloomy trail.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5437,-19,-2,0,'A Forest Clearing','  The forest clears here for no apparent reason.  There are no stumps, and\nthe soil looks fertile.  But the clearing is noticeably lacking in sounds such\nas the chirping of birds and crickets or the croaking of frogs.  An overgrown\narchway stands to the south, resolutely guarding some ancient secret.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5438,-20,-3,0,'An Overgrown Path','  The path continues to the south, but signs of the once majestic road are\nbecoming more and more sparse.  However, it is evident that someone has been\ntraveling here recently, for the weeds are pushed down by footprints and\nseveral twigs lie broken on the ground.  Arrow shafts protrude from several\ntrees, but the arrows are of poor quality, with bent shafts and crude\nfeathering.  Many of the trees have a strange symbol carved into their side,\nsome even dark red in color as if blood were used as a stain on the hapless\ntrees.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5439,-20,-4,0,'Overgrown Path','  The ancient path is all but gone now, replaced by well trod dirt and sparse\nvegetation.  Some of the trees here have makeshift ladders nailed to them,\nconsisting of boards nailed directly onto the tree.  Unfortunately these\nboards have long since rotted away into perilous decay.  Small bones are\nscattered in various places, most seem to have once been fish or small birds.\nYou can just barely make out some noises to the south, sounding like movement\nthrough the brush and low, rough voices calling out.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5440,-21,-3,0,'An Overgrown Path','  This extremely narrow trail does not seem as if were made for normal size\ncreatures.  Indeed, one could hardly call this a trail, except for the way the\nshrubbery has been neatly trimmed by someone to allow easy passage, or, at\nleast, easy passage for someone only two feet tall.  Small rings of mushrooms\nare everywhere, many of them glistening with a green sparkle that is very\nunnatural, yet not malevolent in nature.  You swear you can see small pairs of\neye looking at you, but every time you turn to face them, they disappear like\nthe wind.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5441,-21,-2,0,'South of a Small Round Hill','  A small, almost perfectly round hill is the only feature of note.  The trees\nseem to have decided not to grow here, in fact, the only vegetation visible\nare many small mushrooms which grow in spurts across the mound in random\nformations.  It seems as thought the trail has brought you to a dead end,\nalthough you could walk around the perimeter of the mound, or simply up to the\ntop if the thought crossed your mind.  But for some strange reason, you seem\ncompelled to travel counter-clockwise ...\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5442,-19,-3,0,'Beyond The Archway','  You are assaulted by the need to run.  Demons seem to be leaping from behind\nthe malformed trees which are sneering at you in immortal disgust.  The wind\nscreams for mercy as it passes through the black and decaying leaves,\nparasites which refuse to loose their hold on their hosts.  A giant archway\ntowers over you in ancient arrogance.  However, it seems to be crippled on\none side, a long crack in the side slightly resembles a crutch.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5443,-19,-4,0,'A Circle of Stones','A large circle of stones, nearly twenty feet in diameter, stands here.  Each\nstone has some mystic inscription upon it which glows very faintly with a pale\nred aura.  The twelve stones hum softly, each stone giving off a different\npitch.  The resulting cacophony is dizzying, an anharmonic mix of bass\ntones.  The earth inside the stones is scorched, burned, consisting mostly of\nsoot covered rocks and various animal bones, mixed in with the flaky black\nsoil.  Small tendrils of steam arise from random locations within the stones,\nweaving a intoxicating dance for your eyes to follow.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5444,-20,5,0,'Deep in the Lan\'Quin Forest','  You are not sure if you are heading in the right direction or not.  The\nceiling overhead is a tangle of dead limbs and barely surviving leaves, with\nfog and gloom closing in everywhere.  Strange howling sounds resound in your\near, coming from every direction at once.  Your ears strain to make out that\nslight rustling which follows you wherever you go, but you can not determine\nwhat the source is.  You only hope you can find the light of day before you\nsuffocate in this death gulch.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5445,-20,6,0,'Deep in the Lan\'Quin Forest','  A small, almost perfectly round hill is the only feature of note.  The trees\nseem to have decided not to grow here, in fact, the only vegetation visible\nare many small mushrooms which grow in spurts across the mound in random\nformations.  It seems as though the trail has brought you to a dead end,\nalthough you could walk around the perimeter of the mound, or simply up to the\ntop if the thought crossed your mind.  But for some strange reason, you seem\ncompelled to travel clockwise ...\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5446,-19,6,0,'Deep in the Lan\'Quin Forest Northeast','  A small, almost perfectly <p>round hill<1> is the only feature of note.\nThe trees seem to have decided not to grow here, in fact, the only\nvegetation visible are many small mushrooms which grow in spurts across\nthe mound in random formations.  It seems as though the trail has brought\nyou to a dead end, although you could walk around the perimeter of the\nmound, or simply up to the top if the thought crossed your mind.  But for\nsome strange reason, you seem compelled to travel <y>clockwise<1> from\nthis spot...\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5447,-23,-2,0,'On a Small Hillside','  A small, almost perfectly round hill is the only feature of note.  The trees\nseem to have decided not to grow here, in fact, the only vegetation visible\nare many small mushrooms which grow in spurts across the mound in random\nformations.  It seems as thought the trail has brought you to a dead end,\nalthough you could walk around the perimeter of the mound, or simply up to the\ntop if the thought crossed your mind.  But for some strange reason, you seem\ncompelled to travel counter-clockwise ...\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5448,-22,-1,0,'West of a Small Hill','  A small, almost perfectly round hill is the only feature of note.  The trees\nseem to have decided not to grow here, in fact, the only vegetation visible\nare many small mushrooms which grow in spurts across the mound in random\nformations.  It seems as thought the trail has brought you to a dead end,\nalthough you could walk around the perimeter of the mound, or simply up to the\ntop if the thought crossed your mind.  But for some strange reason, you seem\ncompelled to travel counter-clockwise ...\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5449,-22,-2,0,'Southwest of a Small Hill','  A small, almost perfectly round hill is the only feature of note.  The trees\nseem to have decided not to grow here, in fact, the only vegetation visible\nare many small mushrooms which grow in spurts across the mound in random\nformations.  It seems as thought the trail has brought you to a dead end,\nalthough you could walk around the perimeter of the mound, or simply up to the\ntop if the thought crossed your mind.  But for some strange reason, you seem\ncompelled to travel counter-clockwise ...\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5450,-21,-1,0,'On Top of the Small Hill','  The top of the hill is about as interesting as the circumference.  The only\nthing of note is that the mushrooms at the very crest of the hill seem to have\ngrown in a strange pattern, but its probably just your imagination.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5451,-18,6,0,'Deep in the Lan\'Quin Forest','  A small, almost perfectly round hill is the only feature of note.  The trees\nseem to have decided not to grow here, in fact, the only vegetation visible\nare many small mushrooms which grow in spurts across the mound in random\nformations.  It seems as though the trail has brought you to a dead end,\nalthough you could walk around the perimeter of the mound, or simply up to the\ntop if the thought crossed your mind.  But for some strange reason, you seem\ncompelled to travel clockwise ...\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5452,-19,7,-1,'Inside the Faerie Mound','  The inside of the fairy mound literally sparkles with the light of small\ngreen stones implanted inside the earthen walls.  The floor is of a smooth\nmarble, white in color with wispy grey streaks.  The ceiling overhead is\ncovered with green vegetation, and mushroom rings here and there.  You can\nhear tiny laughter echoing throughout the caves, and the pitter patter of\nlittle feet.  A iron gate stands here as well.  Could you have truly\nstumbled upon the cave of the little people?\n',37,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,35,0,'',NULL),
(5453,0,0,0,'South of a Small Hill','  You seem to have come full circle, and for no apparent reason.  The hill sits\nresolutely to the north, and the trail leads back south.  You could continue\nwestward, but you have the feeling that it would only be another wasted trip\n...\n',37,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5454,-19,7,0,'On Top of a Small Hill','Upon reaching the top of the hill, you see that there is now a stairway\nleading down into the depths!  Strange how it was never here before, were your\neyes playing tricks on you or is there some strange force at work here?  In\nany event, you are hesitant to leave back south lest you lose what may be your\nlast chance to explore this strange place.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5455,-31,-1,-1,'A Tributary of Serpent River','  A small side branch of the Serpent River flows gently beneath you, gurgling\ncontentedly.  The huge trees of Lan\'Quin Forest grow peacefully on the banks\nof the creek.  The occasional twig or leaf can be seen drifting with the\ncurrent.  Silvery fish swim beneath the water\'s surface, heading upstream.\nTo the west a narrow path leads through the forest, but the trees there\nseem somehow more sinister, almost as if alive and malevolent.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5456,-18,7,-1,'A Sparkling Cave','  This cave is much like the entrance, but the laughter is much more distinct\nand clear, and is definitely feminine in nature.  The green stones in the\nwalls pulse slightly here, almost in time to a strange melody created by the\nechoing laughter ...  the effect is very dizzying.  The marble floor is purer,\nwith less streaks of grey, and more of a pure white.\n',37,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,35,0,'',NULL),
(5457,-19,6,-1,'Throne Room of the Sprite Queen','  Small little balls of light zip around the room at dizzying speeds, some\nstopping inches from your nose as if in observation, only to zoom off again in\nhasty flight.  Once your eyes adjust to the light you can see that the balls\nof light are actually miniature woman-like creatures with wings of some clear\nsubstance, each one different and remarkable to look at.  Each sprite also has\ntwo antennae springing from her head, much like a butterflies.  They buzz\naround, making small pipy noises at each other, and generally staying just out\nof reach to tease you.  Near the back of the room sits a throne of pure\nsilver, glistening in the lights, but it is unoccupied.\n',37,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,35,0,'',NULL),
(5458,-20,7,-1,'Throne Room of the Brownie King','  This cave is much larger then the others under this strange mound, nearly\ntwice the size as the entrance cave.  The marble in the entrance continues into\nthis room, but some streaks of red can be seen intermixed with the grey.  Small\nhats lie scattered about the floor, in all colors, but most of them are dark\nand brown.  Many eyes peer at you from the shadows of the cave walls, many of\nthem blinking rapidly.  A single throne seen in the center of the room is the\nonly decor.  It seems as if a very small halfling might be able to squeeze\ninto the chair, if he forced himself.\n',37,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,35,0,'',NULL),
(5459,-18,6,-1,'Throne Room of the Pixie Queen','  This cave has a floor of pure white marble, much like soft snow, yet the\nlight reflected by it is not blinding.  The green stones here have replaced by\nmilky white ones, which emanate a much softer light, its incandescence washing\nyou in peace.  In the center of the room a small throne sits, constructed of\nsome pale white wood, with plush seats of grey and silver, but the throne is\nunoccupied.\n',37,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,35,0,'',NULL),
(5460,-19,8,-1,'Secret Chamber','  Having passed through the large crack you enter into a room of dazing light.\nSmall gemstones in the wall sparkle with an inner light, sheding off a multi-\ncolored light show as you gaze in wonder.  A rug of purple color trimmed in\nresplendent gold covers the otherwise marble floor.  There is a small sign\nhere.\n',37,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,35,0,'',NULL),
(5461,-19,9,-1,'Treasure Room','  Only white gems adorn the walls of this room, reflecting off all of the\ngolden treasures below you: goblets, crowns, encrusted weapons, jewels of\nevery color, size and shape; a literal king\'s ransom at your feet.  The greed\nis overbearing ...  you know that you will need more bags to carry it all away!\nWhat can you do?  What if you can\'t find your way back again?  Could someone\nelse steal your treasure while you go to get more bags?  What if someone else\nknows?  You must guard it!  No!  You must do better!  You can never leave!\nYES!  You will stay forever, with your treasure, protecting it from all\nenemies!   The hysteria grows worse and worse ....  you need to get out of here\nwhile you can still think!\n',37,174217,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5462,-29,-3,-1,'Serpent River','   The beautiful Serpent River flows gently beneath you, gurgling contentedly.\nThe huge trees of the Lan\'Quin Forest grow peacefully on the banks of the\ncreek.  The occasional twig or leaf can be seen drifting with the current.\nSilvery fish swim beneath the water\'s surface, heading upstream.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5463,-29,-4,-1,'Serpent River','   The beautiful Serpent River flows gently beneath you, gurgling contentedly.\nThe huge trees of Lan\'Quin Forest grow peacefully on the banks of the creek.\nThe occasional twig or leaf can be seen drifting with the current.  Silvery\nfish swim beneath the water\'s surface, heading upstream.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5464,-29,-5,-1,'The Dark River','  This is a small side branch off the Serpent River.  To the north you can\nsee the function with the Serpent, and the river flows to the south.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5465,-21,6,0,'A Large, Knobbled Hill','  Off the bank of the slowly swirling Serpent River is a small gnarled\nhill which is free from the briars and tangles of the forest on all other\nsides.  The hill is covered only by the most sparse of vegetation, but small\nrocks are very common.  At they very top of the hill is a large hole, which is\nsoot black in appearance!  From this gaping maw ushers a black smoke the makes\nyour stomach turn inside out with disgust.  Although the thought does not\nappeal to you, you see that you could slide down it into the depths below.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5466,-31,-2,-1,'A Tributary of the Serpent River','  A small branch of the beautiful Serpent River flows gently beneath you,\ngurgling contentedly.  The huge trees of Lan\'Quin Forest grow peacefully on the\nbanks of the creek.  The occasional twig or leaf can be seen drifting with the\ncurrent.  Silvery fish swim beneath the water\'s surface, heading upstream.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5467,-32,-1,-1,'A Dark, Twisted Path','  Stepping from the calm, clear waters of Serpent River into the dread and\ngloom of this part of Lan\'Quin shocks your senses.  Where the babbling of the\ncreek brought on calm and comforting feelings, the trees bring on more of a\ntense and gloomy mood.  The trees in this part of the forest are twisted,\nstunted, malformed and completely malevolent in their effort to stop your\nprogress.  Their gnarled roots create a maze of a path making it all too\neasy to get lost or sidetracked in this open wound of a forest.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5468,-31,-3,-1,'A Tributary of the Serpent River','   The water of the Serpent River is warm and refreshing compare to the cold,\nbiting waters of the Kranor.  To the Northwest, the faint outline of a\nmountain range can barely be seen.  They are the Parnithian Mountains, the\nsource of the Kranor, and the source of the Serpent.  To the north are the\ntrees of the Lan\'Quin forest.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5469,-31,-4,-1,'A Tributary of the Serpent River','   The water of the Serpent River is warm and refreshing compare to the cold,\nbiting waters of the Kranor.  To the Northwest, the faint outline of a\nmountain range can barely be seen.  They are the Parnithian Mountains, the\nsource of the Kranor, and the source of the Serpent.  To the north are the\ntrees of the Lan\'Quin forest.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,8,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5470,-30,-5,-1,'The Serpent River','   The water of the Serpent River is warm and refreshing compare to the cold,\nbiting waters of the Kranor.  To the Northwest, the faint outline of a\nmountain range can barely be seen.  They are the Parnithian Mountains, the\nsource of the Kranor, and the source of the Serpent.  To the north are the\ntrees of the Lan\'Quin forest.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5471,-31,-6,-1,'The Serpent River','   The water of the Serpent River is warm and refreshing compare to the cold,\nbiting waters of the Kranor.  To the Northwest, the faint outline of a\nmountain range can barely be seen.  They are the Parnithian Mountains, the\nsource of the Kranor, and the source of the Serpent.  To the north are the\ntrees of the Lan\'Quin forest.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5472,-31,-7,-1,'The Serpent River','   The water of the Serpent River is warm and refreshing compare to the cold,\nbiting waters of the Kranor.  To the Northwest, the faint outline of a\nmountain range can barely be seen.  They are the Parnithian Mountains, the\nsource of the Kranor, and the source of the Serpent.  To the north are the\ntrees of the Lan\'Quin forest.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5473,0,0,0,'The Serpent River','   The water of the Serpent River is warm and refreshing compare to the cold,\nbiting waters of the Kranor.  To the Northwest, the faint outline of a\nmountain range can barely be seen.  They are the Parnithian Mountains, the\nsource of the Kranor, and the source of the Serpent.  To the north are the\ntrees of the Lan\'Quin forest.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,0,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5474,0,0,0,'The Serpent River','   The water of the Serpent River is warm and refreshing compare to the\ncold, biting waters of the Kranor.  To the Northwest, the faint outline of a\nmountain range can barely be seen.  They are the Parnithian Mountains, the\nsource of the Kranor, and the source of the Serpent.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,1,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5475,0,0,0,'The Serpent River','  The water of the Serpent River is warm and refreshing compared to the\ncold, biting waters of the Kranor.  The Serpent River is a tributary of the\nKranor and flows northeast through a thick woodland area.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,1,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5476,-29,-6,-1,'The Dark River','  The river bends here flowing west.\n',37,131073,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5477,-30,-6,-1,'The Dark River','  The river flows to the west.\n',37,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5478,-32,0,0,'A Dark, Twisted Path','  You are not sure if you are heading in the right direction or not.  The\nceiling overhead is a tangle of dead limbs and barely surviving leaves, with\nfog and gloom closing in everywhere.  Strange howling sounds resound in your\near, coming from every direction at once.  Your ears strain to make out that\nslight rustling which follows you wherever you go, but you can not determine\nwhat the source is.  You only hope you can find the light of day before you\nsuffocate in this death gulch.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5479,-33,-1,-1,'Deep in the Dark Woods of Lan\'Quin Forest','  You are not sure if you are heading in the right direction or not.  The\nceiling overhead is a tangle of dead limbs and barely surviving leaves, with\nfog and gloom closing in everywhere.  Strange howling sounds resound in your\near, coming from every direction at once.  Your ears strain to make out that\nslight rustling which follows you wherever you go, but you can not determine\nwhat the source is.  You only hope you can find the light of day before you\nsuffocate in this death gulch.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5480,-33,-2,-1,'Deep in the Dark Woods of Lan\'Quin Forest','  You are not sure if you are heading in the right direction or not.  The\nceiling overhead is a tangle of dead limbs and barely surviving leaves, with\nfog and gloom closing in everywhere.  Strange howling sounds resound in your\near, coming from every direction at once.  Your ears strain to make out that\nslight rustling which follows you wherever you go, but you can not determine\nwhat the source is.  You only hope you can find the light of day before you\nsuffocate in this death gulch.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5481,-32,-2,-1,'Tower of the Ranger Council','  This tower is actually an oversized oak tree that disappears in the\nclouds.  The tree is about a hundred feet wide and just as long.  It is\nobvious that the growth of this tree must have been magically aided.  Small\nwindows can be seen carved into the tree at different heights and flags of\ndifferent nations are hanging out some of them.  A large double door entry\nis carved at the base of the mighty tree.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5482,-32,1,0,'A Dark, Twisted Path','  You are not sure if you are heading in the right direction or not.  The\nceiling overhead is a tangle of dead limbs and barely surviving leaves, with\nfog and gloom closing in everywhere.  Strange howling sounds resound in your\near, coming from every direction at once.  Your ears strain to make out that\nslight rustling which follows you wherever you go, but you can not determine\nwhat the source is.  You only hope you can find the light of day before you\nsuffocate in this death gulch.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5483,-33,1,0,'A Circle of Stones','  You are at first overjoyed to have left the twisted paths of the forest\nbehind you, as you enter the clearing.  But upon gazing upon the circle of\nstones which dominates the clearing you are possessed by a want, a need, to\nflee back the way you came.  Unspeakable evil seems to radiate from the burnt\nground in the center of the stones.  The bones scattered about in a seemingly\nrandom fashion seem to move, ever so slowly, such that you are certain they\nare in different position each time you look at them, but you can never catch\nthem moving.  Each stone glows with a small inscribed rune which glows with a\nsickly green light, reminding you of some supernatural poison which seeks to\ninfest your brain.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5484,-34,1,0,'A Misty Trail','  A small trail twists and turns through the dense misty forest that can\nhardly be seen.  The mist seems to cause the trail to move slightly making your\neyes blink in utter confusion.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5485,-34,0,0,'A Misty Trail','  A small trail twists and turns about on itself in a feeble attempt to\nprovide passage through the dense forest.  Small tremors shake the ground\ncausing a few frail trees to plummet to the ground.  A strange mist floats about\neverywhere, blanketing the area completely.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5486,-35,0,0,'Western Entrance to Lan\'Quin Forest','  The path continues to twist and turn, although you have reached a toppled\ntree to the north which prevents further progress.  The thick fog slows\nprogress and makes it easy to become lost.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5487,-35,1,0,'A Misty Path near the Kranor River','  A small trail choked in a misty fog leads north and south here.  The strange\nmist floats about everywhere, blanketing the area completely.  You are almost\nthankful though, for the mist hides ever-moving shadows around you.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5488,-35,2,0,'A Misty Path Near the Kranor River','  The fog is at its thickest here, choking the area with a thick mist\nthat surrounds you.  To the northwest clouds billow forth over a large structure\nthat can\'t be made out.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5489,-34,2,0,'Ruins','  As the fog thins slightly, you make some ruins of what appears to have\nonce been a large keep.  The stone is heavily weathered and long since\ndecayed.  Some bones still remain however, but perhaps they are just from\nwandering animals.  To your north, a large thorn bush blocks your way.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5490,-34,3,0,'Wolf Den','The droppings, bones and smell are obviously marks as to the nature of this\nden.  A pack of dire wolves has taken up residence here in a small area of\nthe ruins, where they hunt the unsuspecting traveler.  Dirt is spread evenly\nabout the floor that ends before tall thickets and brush.\n',0,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5491,-35,3,0,'Dire Wolf Track','  A small and narrow trail leads east and west here where large prints of\nDire wolves mark the ground.  A dried up trail of blood seems to lead east,\nyou hear low tones of growls as you step closer.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5492,-34,4,0,'Sleeping Area','  This section of the den is slightly higher above the ground, and as such\nis the wolves preferred sleeping area.  Wolf hair is everywhere, leaving a musty\nsmell that permeates your senses.\n',37,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5493,-21,6,-1,'Lair of the Ogre Magi','     You drop down into what is obviously some sort of lair.  A sickly smell\nof burnt flesh enters your nostrils from the east, and your eyes water with\nthe smoke coming from the same place.  The cave has openings in all\ndirections, except the west, which is a large stone wall with a crack going up\nthe center.  Many bones litter the floor; some have burnt and are covered\nwith soot, while others have been crushed and broken in many places, and still\nothers have bits of frozen flesh and ice still clinging to them!\n',37,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5494,-20,6,-1,'Cooking Area','  Here is the source of the sickening smoke which has been assaulting your\nsenses.  A large, black, pitted iron cauldron sits atop a fire of wood and\nbones.  The black stew inside contains various limbs and other humanoid body\nparts you would much rather not know of.  The stench is of the flesh slowly\ncooking; it is all you can do not to empty your innards upon the filthy floor.\nA large spear serves as the stirrer, a few pieces of flesh have dried upon its\nmetal tip.\n',37,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5495,-21,7,-1,'Sleeping Quarters','  Surely this the bedroom of another creature, for it is nothing like the rest\nof the lair.  The chamber is actually civilized looking, with a wooden bed\nwith covers, a writing desk, bookshelves, several oil lamps, and a wooden\nchair that is old and well worn.  Had you not known the dweller, you might\nhave thought him merely a large human or ogre.  The thought that ogre magi\ncould be as civilized as their cousins is appalling and frightening ...  such a\ncivilization could very well threaten the rest of the known world.  You hope\nthat it is true that the ogre magi fight everyone, even their own kind ...\n',37,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5496,-21,5,-1,'Storage Room','  This room is lined with shelves and cabinets, each filled with jars and\nboxes with meaningless scribbles upon them.  You hate to think what might be\nin storage here, for it is well know that ogre magi often hibernate within\ntheir lairs, and must store up food to satisfy their cannibalistic appetite\nduring such reclusive periods.\n',37,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5497,-22,6,-1,'Treasure Room of the Ogre Magi','  This room is nothing like what you would have expected for a treasure horde.\nThe strangest items are placed with utmost care about the room on bookshelves\nand the wooden table at the back: a serpentine knife, a broken piece of\npottery, a large chunk of rock, several books in a language unreadable, a doll\nmade of cloth, a round piece of stone engraved with a strange symbol, many\ncolored spools of thread and a box of needles, a large bone from some gigantic\ncreature, and a stuffed fish hanging upon the wall are some the more notable\nitems.\n',37,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5498,-25,-2,-2,'The Tomb of Ferin','  This tomb is resplendent with tapestries which show bloody scenes of\ndwarves locked in mortal combat with various green and grey skinned goblins.  A\ncoffin sits atop a stone table engraved with various dwarvish runes, softly\nglowing.  The coffin is of a strange metal, and shows no signs of rust or\ntarnish.  It is also engraved with various markings, but most seem to be for\ndecoration, and they do not glow as the table does.  An archway leads west\nback into the shrine\'s entrance.\n',37,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5499,-26,-3,-2,'The Tomb of Kanji','  Several plants have sprung up all around in this room, growing from large\ncracks and gaping holes in the ceiling and walls, almost covering every inch\nof the marble.   The water here seems just a tad bit warmer than the water\nelsewhere in the shrine, and the heat seems to emanate from the plants\nthemselves.  Little bubbles of air cling to the leafy plants, giving this\nplace a very peaceful, mystical feeling.  A wooden coffin, carved with various\nanimal shapes, lies atop a large wooden table.  The coffin is very long and\nnarrow, and the animals carved upon it seem to watch you with curious eyes.\n',37,131081,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5500,-27,-2,-2,'The Tomb of Tyrog','  This tomb is very solemn and has a feeling of timelessness.  Marble walls\nstand unadorned; indeed, the room lacks any form of decoration.  A coffin lies\natop a tall table made of glass, or maybe crystal, gently sparkling.  The\ncoffin is of some black stone, engraved on top with one very large rune, just\nbarely glowing.  try as you might, you can not shake the eerie feeling you\nhave when in this room.  An archway leads east into the entrance to the\nshrine.\n',37,131073,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5501,-26,-2,-3,'Bottom of the Stairway','  You have arrived at the bottom of the long stairway.  Old waterlogged\nsconces line the walls and at some distant time would have provided some\nlight in the hall.  To the north is a hallway which bends to the east into\nwhat appears to be a sanctuary.  A large rope hangs from the ceiling, still\ngood from years of exposure to water.  It looks as if it might have been used\nto sound a bell, but all you can see is that it leads through a small hole in\nthe ceiling.\n',37,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5502,-26,-1,-3,'Entrance to the Sanctuary','  This hallway leads eastward into a small sanctuary.  To the south is the\nstairway leading upwards to the entrance to the shrine.  The marble walls here\nare a little less cracked, and are free of plants.  The carpet on the level\nabove is missing here; instead, you walk upon a cold bare stone floor.  A lone\ntorch sconce hangs upon the wall, but it is lacking the rust of the ones\nabove.\n',37,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5503,-26,0,-3,'The Tomb of Therin Altair','  At one time this room would have been dimly lit by the torches lined on\nthe walls, but now the room is dark, the only light coming in through the\ncracks in the walls is bent in the water for an eerie effect.  The room is of\nfine white marble, uncracked, and other than four thick pillars the only\ndecoration is the coffin floating in the center of the room.  The coffin is\nconstructed of some silvery crystal, which is just barely transparent.  A\nlarge iron-bound door is the only obvious entrance or exit to this holy\nplace.  This is the tomb of Therin Altair, savior of the Phoenix.\n',37,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5504,-25,0,-3,'Pews','  The pews are of the standard temple design, now, what remains of them are\nalgae covered wooden pieces.\n',37,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5505,-25,-1,-3,'Path Between Pews','  Slightly warped pews stand to either side of you, long ago having hosted\ntheir last occupants.  A purple rug leads down the middle to a magnificent\naltar.  The ceiling overhead is very high, nearly twenty feet, although the\nroom is small in terms of length and width.\n',37,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5506,-25,-2,-3,'Pews','   The pews are of the standard temple design, hard wood benches with plush\ncushions.  On the back of the pews are little racks which are meant to hold\nhymnals.\n',37,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5507,-24,0,-3,'Pews','   The pews are of the standard temple design, hard wood benches with plush\ncushions are now covered in algae.  On the back of the pews are little racks\nwhich are meant to hold hymnals.\n',37,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5508,-24,-1,-3,'Steps to the Altar','  The purple rug continues up along three marble steps which lead to the\nbase of the altar.  Shorter pews stand to both sides, with designs on them\nseeming to indicate the position of the person who sat there.\n',37,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5509,-24,-2,-3,'Pews','  The pews are of the standard design.  What was once hard wood benches\nfilled with plush cushions now remains a pile of broken algae sticks of a\nforgotten past.\n',37,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5510,-23,-1,-3,'The Altar of Zelpth','  The altar of Zelpth is a long, stone block, carved with many symbols which\nsing praise to a fat statue on the surface of the altar.  A small silver dish,\nonce used as a place where fruit served as offerings to this deity now lies\nempty and filled with dust.  Two large ceramic vases sit left and right of the\naltar, filled with long slender branches that almost reach the ceilings mount.\nIt was once believed that the branches of the forest held the essence of life\nand vitality.  Perhaps the former monks or priests that belonged to this\nsect\npreached of life? At least thats what the symbols on the altar seem to signify.\n',37,131081,29,0,0,0,0,3,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5511,-27,0,-3,'Within an Enchanted Air Fill Cavern','   This room is rather unusual, seeming out of place with the rest of the\nshrine.  It looks exactly like a study, and a recently used one at that.  A\nfireplace in the north wall has fresh ashes, and you can only guess where the\nchimney comes out.  Bookshelves cover every available space on the rest of\nthe walls, containing books that for the most part are in strange languages\nand are written with strange symbols.  A stone floor is covered in the middle\nby a large purple rug with gold trim.  Upon this rug sits a large wooden desk,\nwith several papers scattered across it.  A quill and ink jar occupy one\ncorner of the desk, and by the appearance of one of the papers the occupant of\nthis study had left in haste and without preparation.  One drawer stands open;\ninside this drawer sits a small rectangular box which was recently opened, and\nappears to have once held a wand.  The chair behind the desk is of fine cedar\nwood, polished to a sheen, and lacks any comforting cushions.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5512,-41,-3,0,'A Small Clearing','  Several trees have been chopped down here, allowing for a small clearing in\nthe mighty Lan\'Quin forest.  A few logs still lie where they were felled, and\none in particular is huge, commanding at least twenty feet of ground.  Piles\nof ashes surrounded by small stones mark old campfires ...  it seems as if this\nplace has served more than once as a lookout camp.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5513,-40,-3,0,'Outside the Goblin Outpost','  You have reached the Goblin outpost, a large village surrounded by a large\npole fence, sharpened at their ends, bound together with twine, dirt and dung.\nA foul stench mercilessly assaults your nose, and causes your eyes to water\n...  you then notice the black clouds bellowing forth from the outpost like\nsmoke from a forge containing cheap coals.  Grunts and shuffling footsteps can\nbe heard from within the walls, and you ponder the wisdom of entering such a\nplace.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5514,-40,-4,0,'At the Gate','  Tall wooden posts, consisting of logs which still have most of their bark,\nare sharpened at one end and hammered into the ground.  Then the protruding\ntop of the post is sharpened to provide a dangerous climbing surface.  Finally\nthe new post is connected to the others in the fence via twine rope and a\nhealthy supply of goblin dung.  Thus the goblins have established their main\ndefense against invasion and wandering hostiles.  This gate seems to be the\nonly opening in the primitive, albeit sturdy, barrier.  Footsteps have long\nsince trod out any vegetation, leaving only a dirt path to run beneath your\nfeet.  Through the gate you can see many huts and other wood and straw\nconstructions.\n',37,172212,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5515,-39,-4,0,'Along The Wooden Fence','  You stand outside the large wooden fence erected by the goblins.  Their\nsharp poles are stained in some places with blood and dried flesh.  This helps\nto explain the presence of large bones scattered about the outside of the\nfence.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5516,-41,-4,0,'Along The Wooden Fence','  You stand outside the large wooden fence erected by the goblins.  Their\nsharp poles are stained in some places with blood and dried flesh.  This helps\nto explain the presence of large bones scattered about the outside of the\nfence.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5517,-42,-4,0,'Along the Northern Fence','  You are on the outer edges of the goblin\'s campsite.  A large wooden fence\nshades you from any goblins that lie in wait for you on the other side....\nLoud sounds of combat can be heard coming from within.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5518,-38,-4,0,'Northeast Corner of the Fence','  The fence encompasses the entire camp, however it doesn\'t seem like its\nmuch of a military defense.  Perhaps it is mainly used to keep the wandering\nanimals within the camp.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5519,-43,-5,0,'Living Quarters','  This seems to be a recreational area for guards that are off duty.\nSeveral tables are scattered throughout with different card and dice games\nleft on them.  Bones and Fire & Water seem to be among the more popular\ngames, perhaps because they don\'t require much thinking.  Several dart\nboards hang from the walls, each of them have an ogre head nailed to the\ncenter and adjusted so the nose aligns as the bullseye.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5520,-42,-5,0,'Living Quarters','  This is apparently the goblin mess hall.  A large, slightly off level table\nsits in the middle of the room atop of a large bear rug.  Various chairs, some\nof which are clearly not of goblin make, surround the table, with the\noccasional bench along the walls.  A huge candle sits atop the table, its wax\nmaking a circle nearly six inches in diameter.  The floor is very clean, much\ndifferent from the outer outpost.  Several furs and hides hang from the walls,\neach one clean and shiny looking, and some of the hides have strange things\ncarved upon them.  All in all, you can barely tell that this is a goblin\nresidence and not a civilized home.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5521,-41,-5,0,'Living Quarters','  Trophies of all shapes and sizes, and races, grace the walls here with their\ngrisly beauty.  A black bear\'s head stares noble and proud, teeth bared in a\nmenacing growl.  A dwarf\'s bearded face appears dour and stern, except for the\nvarious arrows sticking out of his ears.  The human trophy is merely a\ncollection of four skulls, bleached totally white and facing away from each\nother in a macabre compass.  The ogre head has had its eyes burned out and\nhis ears cut off, making for a repulsive trophy.  A large rug covers the\nfloor, and seems to be a quilt of various hides ...  some of which may have\nprotected sentient creatures.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5522,-40,-5,0,'A Path through the Goblin Outpost','  A very wide path bends its way through the goblin outpost.  Litter is\nabundant, from old food to broken pottery to scattered bones.  Small rocks\noutline the edge of the path; you are surprised to see that the goblins even\nbothered defining such boundaries.\n',37,131080,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5523,-39,-5,0,'Slave Pen Guard Post','  A smaller replica of the outer fence serves as a barrier between the slave\npens and the outside world.  At the gate is a tarp; two poles jutting from the\nground about fifteen feet away from the fence, and canvas tied to the poles\nand connected to the fence itself.  Apple cores and other waste are abundant,\nbut the smell of the slave pens overrides any other consideration.  It is the\nsmell of rotting flesh and raw sewage, a very unpleasant combination.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5524,-36,-5,0,'A Slave Pen','  This pen does not contain any living slaves.  Rather, the corpse of a thin,\nwasted dwarven male sits here, rotting in the heat and covered with flies.\nYou struggle to contain your stomach as several maggots crawl out of his\nmouth.  His loin cloth was his only companion at the time of his death.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5525,-37,-4,0,'A Slave Pen','  Filthy straw covers the squeaky and warped floor of this pen.  Several bugs\ncrawl about, content with their new environment.  The smells outside reach a\nclimax here, nauseating your mind and threatening your stomach\'s contents.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5526,-38,-5,0,'Between the Cages','  You stand between two cages, constructed of wooden posts and twine, which\nallow just enough room for prisoners to breathe.  The cages sit atop wheeled\ncarts, supposedly for transport, for each cart has a hitch which currently\nsits on the ground, leaving the cages sitting at an angle.  Troughs are\nattached to the side of each cage, so that the slaves can eat their slop and\ndrink their slimy water by sticking their tongue through the posts and lapping\nup as much as they can.  Flies constantly fly around, buzzing their death song\nas their young grow and reproduce at astounding rates.  The smell is\natrocious, a mixture of dung and slop, urine and sweat ..  all the products of\nhumans in captivity.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5527,-37,-5,0,'Between the Cells','  Two more pens sit to the north and south of you, although the southern cage\nis slightly different from the others.  It seems as though some of the straw\nthat sits in the bottom of every cage has fallen out, concealing the ground\nunderneath the cart.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5528,-43,-12,-1,'Sealed Tomb','  The cave has a strange mist that lingers before your eyes.  You don\'t know\nwhat you have uncovered here in this dark tomb where small pools of water can\nbe seen along the splintery rocky floor.  A dark shape begins to materialize out\nof thin air, only to disappear again in the shadows where your light source\nrefuses to pierce.  By now you realize the pools of water now reach your\nankles and still the water rises.  An evil laughter echoes throughout the cave\nfilling your head with all the images of innocent beasts and townsfolk you have slain in\nthe past.\n',37,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5529,-42,-6,0,'Near The Living Quarters','  A large wood and straw building fit for the unfit stands here crudely built\nunder a thatched roof.  Actual wooden plank boards are put in a very human-like\nfashion for the goblin\'s sleep quarters.  The roof is slightly slanted, and\nglistens from a tree sap that binds it together waterproofing its housing.\n',37,131080,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5530,-41,-6,0,'A Smaller Path','  This path is much less traveled than the main road through the outpost.  It\nis also much cleaner though, with little in the way of trash or litter.  No\nstones mark its boundaries, but the ground is well trod and totally lacking of\nvegetation on the path.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5531,-40,-6,0,'A Path through the Goblin Outpost','  A very wide path bends its way through the goblin outpost.  Litter is\nabundant, from old food to broken pottery to scattered bones.  Small rocks\noutline the edge of the path - you are surprised to see that the goblins even\nbothered defining such boundaries.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5532,-38,-6,0,'A Slave Pen','  Filthy straw covers the squeaky and warped floor of this pen.  Several bugs\ncrawl about, content with their new environment.  The smells outside reach a\nclimax here, nauseating your mind and threatening your stomach\'s contents.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5533,-37,-6,0,'A Slave Pen','  You are in a small, squalid slave pen that sits upon some sort of wooden\ntrailer, complete with hitch.  Straw and dirt, but mostly dirt, covers the\nfloor beneath you.  Wooden posts tied in various location surround you, with a\nsturdy wooden tapestry above you.  The floor is warped everywhere, old with\nurine and sweat.  But the dirt on the floor seems to make a pattern, perhaps\nprevious slaves were trying to leave a message ...\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5534,-42,-7,0,'The Latrine','  This totally open area serves as the goblin latrine.  A large ditch is dug\ninto the ground, higher up toward the east and quickly slanting downwards\ntoward the westward fence.  The ditch empties into a pipe which presumably\nleads underground somewhere beyond the fence.  The smell is actually a little\nbetter than you thought, it seems that the horrible pervading smell that seems\nto seep through the outpost originates from somewhere else.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5535,-40,-7,0,'A Path through the Goblin Outpost','  A very wide path bends its way through the goblin outpost.  Litter is\nabundant, from old food to broken pottery to scattered bones.  Small rocks\noutline the edge of the path - you are surprised to see that the goblins even\nbothered defining such boundaries.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5536,-39,-7,0,'Entrance to the Barracks','  The entrance to the goblin barracks also serves as a goblin training ground.\nRecent victims of goblin raids serve as gruesome targets for the aspiring\ngoblin warrior; thick black blood oozes from the corpses, making it difficult\nto determine which wounds were the killing ones and which ones are the marks of\npractice.  Shockingly, you see that several goblin corpses also serve as\ntargets, it appears that the goblins have no respect even for their own dead.\nThe stench of death mixes well with the bloody ground, and the scent of dung\nthat permeates the entire camp.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5537,-38,-7,0,'The Goblin Barracks','  The goblin barracks appears to be the only stonework in the entire outpost.\nNot exactly dwarven masonwork, but stones of all types held together with some\nfoul smelling solvent; you are certain that dung is a main component.  Small\nwindows are covered with iron bars, but you do not remember seeing a blacksmith\nanywhere in the town.  On that thought, you wonder where all the iron weapons\nand arrowheads come from that the goblins use?  The floor is typical of goblin\nstructures, being plain dirt with lots of pine straw.  It seems that the\nbarracks is the most easily defended place in the outpost.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5538,-37,-7,0,'The Goblin Barracks','  This is a hallway running to the end of the barracks.  Assorted foot- prints\nspot the floor where straw does not hide their presence.  Not all of the\nfootprints are goblin in nature, some sort of dog prints and other, deeper and\nmore defined prints.  You wonder what sort of allies the goblins have?\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5539,-39,-8,0,'The Goblin Barracks','  This is the main quarters for the goblin warriors.  Crude straw mats are\nscattered everywhere, in a seemingly random fashion, but as you consider the\narrangement, there appears to be a method to the madness that would allow the\ngoblins to wake and fight in strategic positions in this very room.  But\nsurely the goblins are not that intelligent, it must be chance of the array you\nsee.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5540,-36,-7,0,'Officer\'s Quarters','  This chamber has the same straw mats found in the main quarters, but also\nseveral hides atop the mats; apparently officers in the goblin force have\nbetter accommodations.  Also different are several troughs, filled with some\nsort of meat, much like large dog bowls.  The strange footprints are much more\ncommon in this room than in the hallway outside.  Various knives hang from racks\non the walls, many with dried blood or some other dark liquid ...  it also\nappears that some of the knives are pitted, as if they had been dipped in acid.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5541,-38,-8,0,'War Chamber','  A large, fine quality table sits at the far wall, underneath a detailed map\nof Lan\'Quin forest with strange markings.  Weapons of war decorate the room,\nfrom crooked spears to cracked axe-heads.  The stonework in this room appears\nto be different from that of the rest of the barracks, the awful smell is much\nless and the stones appear to have been shaped before being placed.  In fact,\nit resembles a jail cell more than anything else, except for its size.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5542,-37,-8,0,'Kar\'ahsok\'s Quarters','  A small cot lies in the center of the room, underneath a curious array of\nspears arranged in a symbol of chaos on the ceiling.  Several teeth are\narrayed upon a piece of twine to hang along the far wall; teeth as small as\nyour own or as large as a dragon\'s fang, stretching from ceiling to floor.  A\nlarge iron bowl sits in one corner, with copper pieces spilling over.  Wolf\nhides serve as rugs, covering most of the dirt and straw that is present in\nevery goblin structure.  This is obviously the quarters of the commander of\nthe goblin army.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5543,-44,-8,0,'The Center of the Western Fence','  This ground near this side of the fence is slightly wet and smells of raw\nsewage.  The poles on the fence just above the squishy ground are slightly\nhigher than most of the neighboring poles.  You suspect that some sort of\ndrainage occurs somewhere underneath you.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5544,-35,-7,0,'The Center of the Eastern Fence','  You stand outside the large wooden fence erected by the goblins.  Their\nsharp poles are stained in some places with blood and dried flesh.  This helps\nto explain the presence of large bones scattered about the outside of the\nfence.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5545,-42,-12,0,'The Southwestern Corner of the Fence','  You stand outside the large wooden fence erected by the goblins.  Their\nsharp poles are stained in some places with blood and dried flesh.  This helps\nto explain the presence of large bones scattered about the outside of the\nfence.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5546,-41,-12,0,'The Center of the Southern Fence','  You stand outside the large wooden fence erected by the goblins.  Their\nsharp poles are stained in some places with blood and dried flesh.  This\nhelps to explain the presence of large bones scattered about the outside of\nthe fence.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5547,-40,-12,0,'Near The Southeastern Corner','  The fence here is slightly discolored, like it has been weathered much more\nthan the surrounding parts.  A faint smell of smoke reaches your nose, and it\nseems to originate from within the outpost.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5548,-39,-12,0,'The Southeastern Corner of the Fence','  The fence here is slightly discolored, like it has been weathered much more\nthan the surrounding parts.  A faint smell of smoke reaches your nose, and it\nseems to originate from within the outpost.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5549,-43,-8,0,'Storage Tents','  This tent\'s purpose is confusing.  It contains large quantities of logs,\nmany still with their bark, crushed crates and barrels, broken furniture, and\nstones of all shapes and sizes.  It looks more like a dump area than a storage\ntent.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5550,-42,-8,0,'Storage Tents','  Barrels of water with rusty iron bands are place everywhere, stacked on top\nof each other when size permits.  Water seems to be the only beverage, but you\nare sure you have heard tales of the goblin\'s love for alcohol; then again,\nmaybe it was their thirst for blood.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5551,-41,-8,0,'Storage Tents','  These \"tents\" are really open air tents; pieces of canvas tied to several\npoles, with no walls except hanging flaps of excess canvas.  This is where the\ngoblins seem to store things to protect them from the weather, such as grain\nand precious iron from raids.  This tent contains large numbers of sacks, which\nlook like Grimhaven import grain, apparently the goblins food is provided but\ntheir wagon raids and not on any form of agriculture.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5552,-40,-8,0,'A Path through the Goblin Outpost','  A very wide path bends its way through the goblin outpost.  Litter is\nabundant, from old food to broken pottery to scattered bones.  Small rocks\noutline the edge of the path - you are surprised to see that the goblins even\nbothered defining such boundaries.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5553,-43,-9,0,'Storage Tents','  This room contains wooden chests full of assorted clothing, of all sizes and\ncolors, most likely obtained from raid victims.  It would seem that goblins are\na parasite society, they can not exist without prosperous neighbors from which\nthey can steal their necessities.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5554,-42,-9,0,'Storage Tent','  Crates of several wood types are scattered about, each one contains some form\nof meat.  Sausage, jerky, salted pork, and others.  The crates are obviously\nnot of goblin fashion, and the words on the crates are in human for the most\npart.  More evidence of goblin raids.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5555,-40,-9,0,'A Path through the Goblin Outpost','  A very wide path bends its way through the goblin outpost.  Litter is\nabundant, from old food to broken pottery to scattered bones.  Small rocks\noutline the edge of the path - you are surprised to see that the goblins even\nbothered defining such boundaries.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5556,-39,-9,0,'Entrance To Goblin Temple','   From the outside the temple inspires emotions of fear and repulsion.  The\ntemple is a wooden construction, with hides sewn together serving as a roof.\nSymbols of chaos and destruction are everywhere, and several pikes with skulls\nimplanted atop them decorate the barren, earthen floor.  Two pools sit before\nthe door in placid oblivion to the rest of The World.  One pool is of a black\nstone material, and seems to be filled with water.  The other container is of\na grayish clay, and looks like it is filled with blood.  On both pools is an\ninscription in the goblin tongue.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5557,-38,-9,0,'Foyer of the Goblin Temple','  This hallway leads to the worship area, but you can barely see anything from\nall the intoxicating steam flowing around you.  Underneath your feet is a very\nhot grate, covering a pit of red hot embers.  Water pours forth from skulls\narrayed on the ceiling; the skulls are very small in size, perhaps halfling or\ngnome in origin.  Upon hitting the embers below, the water steams up, mixing\nwith whatever else the goblins have in the pit to give the smoke its dizzying\nodor.  You wonder how the goblins managed to get the water flowing; the goblins\nhave never been a building race like the dwarves and humans.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5558,-37,-9,0,'Worship Area','  The worship area consists of several mats, next to each is a bloody bowl with\na long knife within.  The knives are made from solid bone, or perhaps tooth,\nsharpened at the end so that they can pierce flesh easily.  It seems that\ngoblins include self-mutilation in their worship rituals.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5559,-36,-9,0,'Altar of Onrak the GnomeCrusher','  Perhaps the most grotesque place in the goblin camp, you can barely keep\nyour eyes open because they are watering from the foul stench in this chamber.\nThe walls are decorated with splotches of blood in various colors, a chaotic\nmosaic of death and suffering.  A stained altar, a cubicle of stone, is\nlittered with bones and flesh.  Corpses are hung from the ceiling on crude,\niron, chains; their flesh rotting and dropping to the floor.  A large iron\nicon stares at you from the far wall; its two red eyes piercing into your soul\nto judge you and your deeds.  It is a depiction of Onrak, the GnomeCrusher,\nLeafBlighter, and various other names.  It is said he eats the souls of those\nwho depart this world on this altar.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5560,-36,-8,0,'Alcove','  \"Tribute or suffer\" reads the inscription just above the bowl and just under\nthe iron icon of Onrak.  The bowl is, not surprisingly, empty.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5561,-42,-10,0,'Goblin Execution Chamber','  Several benches sit at the edges of this pitch black tent, illuminated only\nby the fire pit in the center of the room.  Above the pit there is a large iron\npike, at the top of which an icon of Onrak which has four faces points in each\nmain direction.  A platform stands to the side of the pike, maybe for the\naxeman to stand upon and behead the unworthy.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5562,-41,-10,0,'Hallway','  A large wooden door, complete with crude padlock, blocks passage to the\nsouth.  To the west a large tent serves as the goblin execution chamber.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5563,-40,-10,0,'The Goblin Palace','  The \"palace\" is really just a large collections of tents and wood buildings\nthrown together in a haphazard fashion.  But inside, furs cover every inch of\nthe floor, and stolen furniture make the palace resemble something of a\ncivilized place.  The awful smell of the camp is replaced by the odor of\nburning incense.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5564,-39,-10,0,'Hallway','  Precious dragon scales serve as the floor for the end of the hallway, just\nbefore the southern entrance into Gruum\'s bed chamber.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5565,-38,-10,0,'Smoke Pit','  The goblins indulge in only one form of self cleansing: the smoke pit.  This\nreligious ritual involves squatting around a pit of burning wood, naked except\nfor the exotic jewelry they wear.  It is a sign of endurance to be the longest\nto remain in the pit, some goblins have been known to stay in the pits until\nthey are rendered unconscious from inhaling the smoke.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5566,-37,-10,0,'Hallway Within the Goblin Temple','  A simple hallway, lacking in decoration or any form of unholy icons, but\nthere seems to be a supernatural presence guarding this passage.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5567,-36,-10,0,'Mishrak\'s Chamber','  A large iron pot sits in the corner of the room, gurgling and spurting forth\nbubbles of hot air.  Various bottles are strewn about the room, containing odd\nreagents.  This looks more like a mage\'s laboratory than a high priest\'s\nchamber, but then again goblin priests are much different from those of the\nmore common races.  Holy icons of Onrak are inscribed on various pieces of\nmetal, some in deteriorating condition.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5568,-41,-11,0,'Goblin Treasure Room','  This small room has thick oak walls and several goblin scribblings upon its\nwalls, cursing would-be thieves and traitorous goblin kin.  It is a wonder\nhow a room as bleak as this would be considered a treasure room.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5569,-40,-11,0,'Gruum\'s Throne Room','  It is from here where Gruum rules his people.  Perched upon an enormous\nthrone, he places himself above his subjects.  The throne looks to be made\nof bone due to its dull white color and the two skulls decorating the\narm-rests.  A half-broken chandelier hangs from the roof in an attempt to\nlight the room; it barely does its job.  Each wall is covered with a mural\ndepicting famous battle scenes, however any scholar would notice that the\nscenes did not historically turn out they way they are depicted.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5570,-39,-11,0,'Gruum\'s Bedroom','  A plush mattress serves as Gruum\'s bed, but he seems to be without pillows.\nA enormous wood carving of Onrak, the goblin patron, hangs on the wall above a\nshield over crossed spears.  Upon the shield is  carved a large symbol\nconsisting of three bones, pointing away from each other.  A pot full of\nsteaming water sits in the corner above a fire pit.  Several bottles of some\nfoul beverage sit upon a slightly off balance table.  Apparently only the\ngoblin king is allowed to suffer luxuries, and only in his bed chamber.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5571,-43,-7,0,'Along the Western Fence','  The fence seems to round the goblins fortress as you travel further.  All\naround you a dense forest prevents you from any passage west.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5572,-43,-6,0,'Along the Western Fence','  A large end spiked wooden fence has been built here that towers ten feet\nabout your head.  Just below the fence you can tell that someone has been trying\nto dig a hole here.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5573,-38,-12,0,'Along the Southern Fence','  You\'ve come to a dead end where a large wooden fence meets the forest\nthat spans out around you.  Toppled trees east and south prevent and movement\nin that direction.  Though the air is fresh, it collides with your face,\nrefreshing you a little.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5574,-42,-11,0,'Dusty Hall','  This hallway is lightly traveled, very few footprints dot the dirt floor.\nA small hole in the roof allows a light breeze to enter the room.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5575,-44,-5,0,'Along the Western Fence','   The construction of the fence is fairly well built, its mud packed seals\nmixed in with straw like materials for installation leaves you to truly wonder\nwho made this fence.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5576,-43,-4,0,'Northwest corner of the Goblin Outpost','  A large wooden spiked fence has been raised here to repel or keep anything\nfrom coming in or out.  Two skeletal figures drape over the top of the fence\nwith dozens of arrows puncturing their moss-cloth covered bodies.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5577,-37,-11,0,'A Small Library','  The last thing one would expect to find in a goblin outpost, but here it is,\na small library.  The books are thick, some even iron or silver bound, and a\nrare few with locks.  Shelves line every wall, and a small writing desk and\naccompanying chair sit in the middle.  An open book lies on the table, along\nwith a feathery quill and an inkwell.  A few bottles with strange contents also\nsit atop the desk.  The ceiling has been inscribed with many strange symbols,\nmost resembling a serpent in fashion.  You sense an otherworldly presence,\nsomething which your body tells you does not belong.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5578,-43,-10,0,'Dry Storage','  Crates and chests lie on the cold stone floor of this room, containing\nstrange green robes, with black trim, in human size.  In one crate are numerous\nfigures of a snake\'s head, reared back and ready to strike ...  the figures look\nlike they could be screwed atop a bedpost or staff.  Another chest contains\nvarious necklaces, strings with assorted bones attached, with miniature snake\nskulls being the most prominent.  Feathers also adorn the necklaces, and some\nnecklaces look like they could serve as bracelets instead.  Strangely, the\nadornments look and smell old, but show no signs of decay.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5579,-43,-11,0,'A Dusty Hallway','  This hallway is lined with nearly an inch of dust.  Not a trickle of water\npresent in the other hallway can be found here.  But you can make out unnatural\nsounds, of breaths that take too long to inhale, to groans that no animal could\nmake.  Your hairs stand on end, and it smells like the air does before a\nthunderstorm.   The sounds seem to be coming from the south.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5580,-36,-11,0,'Thaumaturgist\'s Laboratory','  A large pentagram is traced in the stone floor, with silver marking its\noutline.  At each point where the star meets the circle a single, lit candle\nrests, but you can not see where any wax has spilled.  Along the far wall a\ntable holds various large bottles, beakers, stirrers, and jars of various\npowders.  One beaker sits atop an iron burner, bubbling away its blue solution.\nNext to the potion is a piece of parchment.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5581,-35,-6,0,'Along the Eastern Fence','  Standing on the outer edges of the goblin outpost you can barely hear\nmuffled screams on the other side of the fence.  A dense and untamed forest\nto the east makes all other passage in that direction impossible.  Some great\nbeast has left its claw marks embedded deeply on the surface of the fence.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5582,-43,-12,0,'Locked Cell','  The hallway ends here, where a trapdoor can be seen leading downwards.\nThe trapdoor is of oak, very solid, and is outlined with iron.  The rune\ninscribed upon it resembles the head of a jackal, or it appears to you\nthat way.  Strange sounds invade your ears..heavy breathing at first\nfollowed by wailing and a distant sound of a subtle roar.  What ever is below\nthis trapdoor is something the goblins don\'t want to unleash.....\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5583,-35,-5,0,'Along the Eastern Fence','  A large wooden fence stands ten feet tall and continues back south.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5584,-36,-6,0,'Trolloc Lair','  This cell contains no straw, but plenty of black fur covers the ground.\nA few teeth also litter the floor, or fangs rather, each one looks as\nsharp as a elven blade.  A few bloodstains also appear on the ground are\nseen trailing off and suddenly disappear behind something.\n',37,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5585,-22,-3,0,'The Depths of the Forest','  The ageless trees of Lan\'Quin forest surround you.  The floor is composed of\ndecaying sticks and leaves intermixed with the rich, pungent soil.  The\ninsects and birds echo their music all around you.  The air has the scent it\nattains right before a thunderstorm, with the accentuating smell of pine straw\njust below it.  Truly the wonder of nature herself is best represented here in\nthis mighty wood.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5586,-19,0,1,'Balinor\'s Bows','  At the top of the hut, within the attic, is a shop displaying several well\ncrafted bows and arrows, and even the occasional crossbow or used melee\nweapon.  The bows are of the finest yew wood, carefully oiled, and come with\nauthentic dragon gut drawstring, guaranteed never to snap.  The arrows are of\nironwood, with deadly steel barbs and feathered with the feathers of the\nlegendary Parnithian Mountain Roc.  A glass display case shows off the goods,\nbut you have heard that Balinor deals in enchanted items as well.\n',37,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(5587,-23,-4,0,'The Depths of the Forest','  The ageless trees of Lan\'Quin forest surround you.  The floor is composed  of\ndecaying sticks and leaves intermixed with the rich, pungent soil.  The\ninsects and birds echo their music all around you.  The air has the scent  it\nattains right before a thunderstorm, with the accentuating smell of pine  straw\njust below it.  Truly the wonder of nature herself is best  represented here in\nthis mighty wood.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5588,-24,-4,0,'Deep in the Dark Woods of Lan\'Quin Forest','  You are not sure if you are heading in the right direction or not.  The\nceiling overhead is a tangle of dead limbs and barely surviving leaves, with\nfog and gloom closing in everywhere.  Strange howling sounds resound in your\near, coming from every direction at once.  Your ears strain to make out that\nslight rustling which follows you wherever you go, but you can not determine\nwhat the source is.  You only hope you can find the light of day before you\nsuffocate in this death gulch.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5589,-25,-4,0,'Deep in the Dark Woods of Lan\'Quin Forest','  You are not sure if you are heading in the right direction or not.  The\nceiling overhead is a tangle of dead limbs and barely surviving leaves, with\nfog and gloom closing in everywhere.  Strange howling sounds resound in your\near, coming from every direction at once.  Your ears strain to make out that\nslight rustling which follows you wherever you go, but you can not determine\nwhat the source is.  You only hope you can find the light of day before you\nsuffocate in this death gulch.\n',37,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
