(5613,0,0,0,'On Top of a Small Hill','  You are standing on top of a mound of dirt in the middle of the\nLan\'Quin forest.  Nothing very spectacular can be seen from this\nvantage point, but at least that annoying urge to travel clockwise\nis finally gone.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5614,-38,-1,0,'Small Path','  The small path runs haphazardly in an east-west direction winding around\nhills, rocks and boulders.  The Kranor Valley opens up and widens to the east\nwhile this path seems to narrow further to the west.  Dense vegetation\ncan be seen beyond the small trees that currently obstruct part of your\nview.\n',38,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5615,-39,-1,0,'Small Path','  Bushes and brambles begin to close in around you catching at your\ngear as you push your way passed.  The heavy smell of the rich plant life\nassail your senses with a mixture of refreshing aromas.  The beauty and\nfreedom of the great outdoors invigorate the playful creatures that run\nwild through this place.\n',38,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5616,-40,-1,0,'An Overgrown Path','  Old and broken cobblestones, probably tossed aside by workers as they\ntoiled long ago building Norman\'s Road, have been crushed by time and the\nbattering elements of nature.  Large weeds and tall grass jut wildly from\nthe ground, entangling themselves in the thick bushes and trees that\neffectively end the east-west trail at this point.  A freshly cut path\nhas been crudely hacked into the lighter bush to the south.\n',38,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5617,-40,-2,0,'An Overgrown Path','  Closed in on almost every side, the brambles have taken over all other\ntype of vegetation, suffocating it.  Birds call to one another from\nsomewhere unseen, the dense forest providing them a safe haven in which\nthey can play without worry.  Small dry patches of brown grass show signs\nof life struggling to survive.  There is a slight movement to the south\ncausing you to pause and listen.  Through the brush you can barely discern\nlow voices in the distance.\n',38,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5618,-37,-1,0,'Small Path','  The small path runs haphazardly around hills, rocks and boulders, turning\nfrom north to west here.  The Kranor Valley opens up and widens to the\neast while this path seems to narrow further to the west.  Dense vegetation\ncan be seen beyond the small trees that currently obstruct part of your\nview.\n',38,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5619,-37,0,0,'West Bank of the Kranor River','  This trail runs along the west bank of the Kranor River.  To the east, a\nbridge leads across the river into the Lan\'Quin Forest.  The trail also\ncontinues north along the river.  A small path leads off into the brush to\nthe south.\n',38,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5620,0,0,0,'A Trail Through Some Rocky Hills','  Rough terrain lies all about you as you make your way along what is little\nmore than a gamepath.  The rock strewn hillsides on either side force to you\nto stay to the trail if you wish to avoid spraining an ankle.  Scraggly brush\ngrows in the gaps between the rocks, providing a hiding place for who knows\nwhat type of wildlife.  An occasional pine or spruce tree grows atop the\nwindswept hills.  The path continues to the east and west.  \n',44,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
