(5658,0,0,0,'A Trail Through Some Rocky Hills','  Rough terrain lies all about you as you make your way along what is little\nmore than a gamepath.  The rock strewn hillsides on either side force to you\nto stay to the trail if you wish to avoid spraining an ankle.  Scraggly brush\ngrows in the gaps between the rocks, providing a hiding place for who knows\nwhat type of wildlife.  An occasional pine or spruce tree grows atop the\nwindswept hills.  The path continues to the east and northwest.  \n',44,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5659,0,0,0,'A Trail Through a Meadow','  The land lies lower and is more level here than in the surrounding hills. \nThe trees that grow on the hillsides are absent, leaving a stretch of wild\ngrasses and flowers.  The path continues to the east and west.  \n',44,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5660,0,0,0,'A Trail Through a Meadow','  The land lies lower and is more level here than in the surrounding hills. \nThe trees that grow on the hillsides are absent, leaving a stretch of wild\ngrasses and flowers.  The path continues to the east and west.  \n',44,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5661,0,0,0,'At the Edge of a Marsh','  The land lies lower and is more level here than in the surrounding hills. \nThe trees that grow on the hillsides are absent, leaving a stretch of wild\ngrasses and flowers.  The path continues west, but all traces of it fade into\na marsh to the east.  \n',44,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5662,0,0,0,'Marshland Near a Gamepath','  Rushes and grasses grow thickly amidst the many stagnant pools of water. \nThe air is heavy and smells of must.  Scraggly trees crouch where they can\nperch on occasional rocky promontories.  The land rises slightly to the north\nand west, and a faint path extends to the west.  The sodden marshland\ncontinues to the east and southeast.  \n',44,131072,27,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5663,0,0,0,'Marshland','  Rushes and grasses grow thickly amidst the many stagnant pools of water. \nThe air is heavy and smells of must.  Scraggly trees crouch where they can\nperch on occasional rocky promontories.  The sodden marshland continues in all\ndirections. \n',44,131072,27,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5664,0,0,0,'Marshland','  Rushes and grasses grow thickly amidst the many stagnant pools of water. \nThe air is heavy and smells of must.  Scraggly trees crouch where they can\nperch on occasional rocky promontories.  The sodden marshland continues in all\ndirections. \n',44,131072,27,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5665,0,0,0,'Marshland Near a Small Lake','  Rushes and grasses grow thickly amidst the many stagnant pools of water. \nThe air is heavy and smells of must.  Scraggly trees crouch where they can\nperch on occasional rocky promontories.  A small lake lies to the east and\nsoutheast. The sodden marshland continues in all other directions.  \n',44,131072,27,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5666,0,0,0,'Marshland Near a Small Lake','  Rushes and grasses grow thickly amidst the many stagnant pools of water. \nThe air is heavy and smells of must.  Scraggly trees crouch where they can\nperch on occasional rocky promontories.  A small lake lies to the east and\nnortheast. The sodden marshland continues in all other directions.  \n',44,131072,27,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5667,0,0,0,'Marshland Near a Small Lake','Rushes and grasses grow thickly amidst the many stagnant pools of water. \nThe air is heavy and smells of must.  Scraggly trees crouch where they can\nperch on occasional rocky promontories.  A small lake lies to the northeast. \nThe sodden marshland continues in all other directions.  \n',-1,131072,27,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5668,0,0,0,'A Small Lake','  Water has collected at this geographical low point to create a small lake. \nA few fish can be seen rising to the surface, partaking of some of the many\ninsects that make this area their home.  Lily pads adorn parts of its surface,\nwhile patches of duckweed cover much of the rest.  The lake continues to the\neast, south, and southeast.  The ground rises slightly in the other\ndirections, where the land becomes more marshy.  \n',44,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5669,0,0,0,'A Small Lake','  Water has collected at this geographical low point to create a small lake. \nA few fish can be seen rising to the surface, partaking of some of the many\ninsects that make this area their home.  Lily pads adorn parts of its surface,\nwhile patches of duckweed cover much of the rest.  The lake continues to the\nnorth, east, and northeast.  The ground rises slightly in the other\ndirections, where the land becomes more marshy.  \n',44,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
