(5676,0,0,0,'Marshland Near a Gamepath','  Rushes and grasses grow thickly amidst the many stagnant pools of water. \nThe air is heavy and smells of must.  Scraggly trees crouch where they can\nperch on occasional rocky promontories.  The land rises slightly to the south\nand east, and a faint path extends to the east.  The sodden marshland\ncontinues to the west and northwest.  \n',44,131072,27,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5677,0,0,0,'At the Edge of a Marsh','  Rough terrain lies all about you as you make your way along what is little\nmore than a gamepath.  The rock strewn hillsides on either side force to you\nto stay to the trail if you wish to avoid spraining an ankle.  Scraggly brush\ngrows in the gaps between the rocks, providing a hiding place for who knows\nwhat type of wildlife.  An occasional pine or spruce tree grows atop the\nwindswept hills.  The path continues to the east, but it all traces of it fade\ninto a marsh to the west.  \n',44,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5678,0,0,0,'A Dry and Well-Kept Cave','  This cave may have been natural in its formation, but since then its\nsurfaces were heavily sculpted by some masterful builder.  The walls, floor,\nand ceiling are completely smooth and polished to a shine, which brings out\nthe white and blue colors of the veins of various minerals that run through\nthe rocks.  There is a narrow chimney at the west end of the ceiling.  An\nopening in the northwest wall is blocked by a large boulder.  \n',44,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5679,0,0,0,'A Rocky Cliff Top','  This cliff top has a commanding view of the surrounding terrain.  A small\nlake and marsh lie to the northwest, and beyond those and in other directions\nis a large forest.  A rough road snakes through the foothills of a range of\nmountains that stands to the southeast.  The area at the top of the cliff is\nquite small, with steep dropoffs all around.  Any occupant of this perch would\nbe hidden from travelers below by thick bushes.  A small metal flap with a\nhole in it lies on the ground and may provide a means of egress.  \n',44,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5700,0,0,0,'A Small Grove Before the Auria Mountains','  This clearing seems unnatural, as if this sort of thing isn\'t happened\nupon frequently.  Tall trees surrounds the grove, casting eerie shadows\nupon the clearing.  Rustlings of forest animals can be heard from the\nsurroundings.  Birds overhead chirp cheerfully.  The clearing narrows\ninto a footpath to the north.\n',42,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,14,'',NULL),
(5701,0,0,0,'A Narrow Path Below the Auria Mountains','  This narrow path seems friendly in a way.  A well-worn path leads\nnorth up the mountain, and south into a small grove.  The path appears\nwell used with <o>footprints<1> going in both directions.\n',42,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5702,0,0,0,'Winding Path Below the Auria Mountains','  The path has a mild slope at this point.  The trees arch slightly in\na perpendicular fashion in relation to the path.  Somehow, by magical or\nmanual means, there are no upturned roots, rocks, or fallen leaves lying\non the path.\n',42,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5703,0,0,0,'Further Up the Mountain','  The trail continues along here, bordered on the northeast by an oddly\nshaped pumice formation.  A tall structure can been seen up ahead to the\nnorth.  Its beams are faintly visible through the thick foliage.\n',42,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5704,0,0,0,'A Path Before a Large Guard Tower','  The large tower to the north appears to be inhabited and well defended.\nShouts can be heard coming from higher up within the tower.  To the southeast\nthe path continues down the mountain.\n',42,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5705,0,0,0,'Inside a Large Guard Tower','  The cold wooden floors in this guard tower are a stark contrast to the\nwoodland surroundings in this portion of the forest.  The room is sparsely\ndecorated, with a couple of tables and wooden chairs meant for sitting.\nThere is a metal ladder in one corner of the room, leading up higher in\nthe tower.  Loud shouts and orders can be heard through the ceiling overhead.\nTo the north and south, sturdy wooden doors provide access to the rest of\nthe forest.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5706,0,0,0,'Midway up the Guard Tower','  This room has small slits in the walls around it, presumably for the\nguards to defend themselves with ranged weapons.  There is another metal\nladder leading upwards.  A <y>grate<1> made from bronze blocks the shaft leading\nup.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5707,0,0,0,'Top of the Guard Tower','  The surrounding forest can be seen from this great height, providing\na magnificent view.  Small streams dot the undergrowth off to the\nnortheast.  To the northwest is a building of some sort.  The room has\nonly foot-high walls circling around it.  It appears most useful as a\nway to scout out the forest for friend or foe.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5708,0,0,0,'A Wide Path Before the Auria Mountains','  The forest is not very dense here.  To the north, a structure can barely\nbe seen off in the distance.  A large guard tower sits to the south, blocking\nthe path.  The path starts to climb northeast up the mountains.\n',42,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5709,0,0,0,'A Wide Path Up the Auria Mountains','  The side of the path here has hardly any trees or other vegetation.\nTo the north the path continues up the mountain, and to the southwest\na large guard tower can be seen not too far away.  The path starts to\nnarrow to the north.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5710,0,0,0,'Halfway Up the Auria Mountains','  There is no vegetation on this medium slope, but squirrels and other\nsmall woodland creatures still scamper about.  To the north, the path\nsteepens drastically.  The south path leads back down into a dense\nforest.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5711,0,0,0,'A Steep Path in the Auria Mountains','  The slope is very steep here.  Several large boulders made of pumice rests\non the side of the path.  The path continues to wind up the mountain from\nhere.  Down the mountain to the south lies a dense forest with a guard tower\npeeking out above the tree line.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5712,0,0,0,'Nearing the Top of the Auria Mountains','  A tower peeks out from among the trees of a forest to the south.  To\nthe north, a steep cliff leads to the ridge on top of the mountain range.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5713,0,0,0,'Just Before the Ridge of the Auria Mountains','  Directly to the north lies a small plateau capping this end of the Auria\nMountains.  To the south the path continues down a steep slope.  In the\ndistance off to the east, an outcropping of rocks shrouded in fog can be seen.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5714,0,0,0,'A Plateau Overlooking a Forest','  This barren, wind-slept plateau seems mostly devoid of life.  However,\noff to the northwest there is a small forested area.  To the south the\npath begins its way down the mountain.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5715,0,0,0,'Center of a Plateau in the Auria Mountains','  This is the center of a small plateau which lies atop the Auria\nMountains.  This part of the plateau looks rather well-traveled, and paths\nlead in several directions from here.  To the west, a path leads towards a\nsmall forested area and to the east a path leads into thick fog.  The southern\npath leads to the southern edge of the plateau.  A path to the north slopes\ndown into a wide valley.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5716,0,0,0,'A Small Path in the Auria Mountains','  This path seems less traveled than others seen in this area.  There\nare a number of well-defined <o>footprints<1>.  On either side of the path,\nsharp cliffs of solid rock drop down to the valley to the north and and a\nlarge forest to the south.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5717,0,0,0,'A Quiet Path in the Auria Mountains','  The path is faint here.  Quaint sounds of small animals can be heard coming\nfrom the northwest.  The few trees along the path make the plateau to the\nsoutheast look empty and bare.  The smell of fresh bread drifts from deeper\ninto the forested area to the northwest.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5718,0,0,0,'Entrance to a Forested Area in the Auria Mountains','  The trees and vegetation are quite thick here, making the light filtering\nthrough the canopy appear like a sort of simple kaleidescope.  To the\nnorthwest seems to be some sort of residence.  The smell of food is strong\nhere.  The path to the southeast leads back to the plateau.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5719,0,0,0,'Inside the Grove','  This beautiful grove shines with pure goodness, the path changing from\ndirt to polished stone.  Birds flutter happily about, their calls adding\nto the ambiance of the grove.  Nearby to the northwest is a cabin.\n',42,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5720,0,0,0,'Inside the Grove','  This beautiful grove shines with pure goodness, the polished stone path\nglinting through magical means.  You hear numerous creatures nearby.  The\nporch of a cabin is immediately to the north.\n',42,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5721,0,0,0,'On the Porch','  This majestic porch glows brightly, its light cascading off of the front\nof the cabin.  To the north, a solid wooden door leads into the cabin.  The\nGrove lies to the south.\n',42,131073,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5722,0,0,0,'Inside Garthran\'s Cabin','  The room glows with a certain mysterious aura.  There is a handwoven rug\non the floor which is obviously the work of a master threader.  A door made\nof cedar, with a finely carved inscription gracing the top part of it, leads\nto the bedroom.  The doorway to the east leads into a warm study.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5723,0,0,0,'The Beginning of A Foggy Path','  Small puffs of fog drift along the crumbling path.  A solid wall of pumice\nto the north and the sheer drop into the forest below makes this place very\ndangerous.  The path leads west into a plateau while the view is obscured by\nthe fog to the east.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5724,0,0,0,'Along A Foggy Path','  Fog and mist completely enshrouds the path at this point.  The only thing\ndistinguishable through the fog is the pumice wall to the north and the sheer\ndrop to the south.  There is a sort of mysterious feeling emanating from the\neast.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5725,0,0,0,'Before A Foggy Outcropping','  The path is in bad shape here, loose rocks cover the path tripping the\nunwary.  The fog is lighter here, allowing a semi-clear view at the forest\nto the south.  To the southeast, the path heads out of the fog.  A heavy fog\nbank lies to the west.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5726,0,0,0,'Along A Foggy Outcropping','  The light fog swirls around in an odd pattern, as if controlled by some\nmeans.  To the south the cliff drops down to the forest.  To the north\na sheer pumice wall extends far overhead, disappearing into another layer\nof fog far above.  To the northwest the fog thickens, and to the southeast the\npath continues around the mountain.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5727,0,0,0,'Along A Foggy Outcropping','  The sheer face towers above you here, standing out like a red tombstone in\nthe wispy fog.  To the northwest the fog thickens into a soupy mixture, while\nto the south the outcropping continues.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5728,0,0,0,'Center of A Foggy Outcropping','  The fog is the least thick at this point on the outcropping.  The forest\nis below completely visible.  A sort of oasis from the fog, this spot has the\nmarks of many travelers stopping to enjoy the view.  To the north the path\nleads into thick fog.  To the southeast lies the entrance to a simple\ncave.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5729,0,0,0,'The Beginning of A Plain Cave','  The low stone walls make it difficult to walk here.  The cave is unadorned\nsave for the <k>large tablet<1> that stands firmly in the ground.  To the\nnorthwest lies a foggy outcropping.  To the east the cave continues through\nthe mountain.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5730,0,0,0,'Inside A Plain Cave','  The walls are moderately wide here.  The dim light from the northwest casts\nseveral dim shadows behind the pumice rocks on the floor of the cave.  To the\nwest the cave seems to narrow.  To the northeast the cave heads even deeper\ninto the mountain.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5731,0,0,0,'Bedroom','  This rather large room is mostly taken up by the large bed, but there is\nstill room for some simple furniture crafted from local woods.  The walls\nare for the most part bare, giving a clear view of the beautiful unstained\nwooden walls and floor.  The room looks like it is well kept and cleaned\nquite often.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5732,0,0,0,'Study','  This room is brightly lit, showing the various handicrafts and paintings\nwhich cover the walls.  Finely carved furniture distinguishes the room.\nTo the west lies the main room of the cabin.  To the north you is a small\nkitchen.  The smell of fresh bread drifts in from the kitchen.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5733,0,0,0,'A Small Kitchen in Cabin','  This cramped room is merely composed of a few tools used for preparing\nfood and several cabinets lining the walls.  To the south you see the\nstudy.  To the north a solid wooden wall blocks your way.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5734,0,0,0,'Nearing the End of A Plain Cave','  The cave is very tall here, the pumice ceiling towering many yards above.\nA few pebbles are all that cover the ground here, glistening softly from the\nlight.  The cave ends to the north.  The path leads southwest out of the cave.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5735,0,0,0,'End of A Plain Cave','  The cave abruptly terminates here, the solid wall to the north showing no\nmeans of passage.  There are several drawings on the walls here, however.\nOn the east wall you notice a small groove running vertically from the floor\nof the cave all the way to the ceiling.  The path back out is to the south.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5736,0,0,0,'Before A Beautiful Vista','  The air is rather cold here.  The path seems to glow faintly for a moment.\nTo the west lies a sheer pumice face.  To the southeast is a majestic\nviewpoint.  The wall to the west has a small crack-like line which extends\nabout 10 feet up from the ground.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5737,0,0,0,'A Beautiful Vista','  The view from this ledge is simply dazzling.  The light fog creates a sort\na of natural frame for the majestic expanse of forest below.  The strong\nwind adds to the unearthly experience.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5738,0,0,0,'Path Leading Towards The Valley','  The path is rather thin here, the towering pumice walls on both sides giving\nyou an eerie feeling.  Off to the north you hear many noises and loud shouts.\nTo the south lies a barren plateau.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5739,0,0,0,'Path Leading Towards The Valley','  The noises coming from the north are quite loud at this point, the pumice\nwalls acting as a sort of echo chamber.  To the south lies a barren plateau,\nand to the northeast the path continues down towards the valley.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5740,0,0,0,'Nearing A Small Village','  The path is quite wide here, the prints of many travelers cluttering the dirt\nfloor.  It seems as if the mountains have come alive here, the breeze blows\nthrough the air.  To the north, the gates of a small village can be seen.  To\nthe southwest, the path continues through the mountains.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5741,0,0,0,'Approaching The Southern Gates of Stratos','  The village to the north is clearly not a calm place, the villagers running\nabout, trying to barter for the goods their families need.  The villagers\nappear friendly, going about minding their own business.  To the south, the\npath continues through the mountains.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5742,0,0,0,'Outside The Southern Gates of Stratos','  The white wooden gates to the north glow with a faint yellow aura, the hinges\nkept rust-free by the village janitor.  Everything about the low stone walls\nrepresents light and goodness.  Overhead an eagle glides majestically by,\ncatching the eye.  To the south lies the path back through the mountains.\n',42,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5743,0,0,0,'Inside The Southern Gates of Stratos','  The village is quite busy, people bustling about trying to get their affairs\nin order.  The people of the town seem content yet paranoid, looking over\ntheir shoulders frequently for possible danger.  To the north lies Lycantor\nStreet, and to the south the southern gates lead out of the village.  To the\nnorthwest and northeast are official-looking huts with solid bamboo doors.\n',42,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5744,0,0,0,'A Small Guardhouse','  The walls are cluttered with various posters and documents, including some\nvery official-looking ones.  The hut is quite warm and cozy.  The door to the\nsoutheast leads back out to the town.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5745,0,0,0,'A Small Guardhouse','  The walls are cluttered with various posters and documents, including some\nvery official-looking ones.  The hut is quite warm and cozy.  The door to the\nsouthwest leads back out to the town.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5746,0,0,0,'Lycantor Street','  This busy street runs north and south through the village of Stratos.  The\n<y>cobblestone path<1> glows with a faint aura.  To the south are the southern\ngates.  A ways to the north is the center of the village.\n',42,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5747,0,0,0,'Lycantor Street','  This busy street runs north and south through the village of Stratos.  The\n<y>cobblestone path<1> glows with a faint aura.  Nearby to the south are the\nsouthern gates.  To the north is the center of the village.\n',42,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5748,0,0,0,'Lycantor Street','  This busy street runs north and south through the village of Stratos.  The\n<y>cobblestone path<1> glows with a faint aura.  A ways to the south are the\nsouthern gates.  To the north is the center of the village.\n',42,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5749,0,0,0,'Lycantor Street','  This busy street runs north and south through the village of Stratos.  The\n<y>cobblestone path<1> glows with a faint aura.  Directly to the north is the\ncenter of the village.  To the south the street continues through the village.\n',42,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5750,0,0,0,'Stratos Center','  This busy center lies below the level of the rest of the village, causing all\nof the rain water and trash to flow down into the gutters beneath the large\nfountain.  To the south, Lycantor Street runs through the residential section\nof the village.  To the east and west Dvalien Avenue goes through the commerce\nand trade sections of the village.  To the north lies a large official\nlooking building, protected by a solid steel door.\n',42,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5751,0,0,0,'Dvalien Avenue','  This busy avenue runs east and west through the commerce and trade sections\nof the village.  The <y>cobblestone path<1> glows with a faint aura.  To the east\nis the center of the village.  To the west the avenue continues through the\nmarketplace.\n',42,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5752,0,0,0,'Dvalien Avenue','  This busy avenue runs east and west through the commerce and trade sections\nof the village.  The <y>cobblestone path<1> glows with a faint aura.  To the north\nis a home of some sort.  To the east and west the avenue makes its way\nthrough the marketplace.\n',42,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5753,0,0,0,'A Small Residence','  This small one-room house is barer than bare, and seems to be devoid of any\nstable occupant.  Nothing else seems to be noticeable besides the bamboo\ndoor leading to the south.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5754,0,0,0,'Dvalien Avenue','  This busy avenue runs east and west through the commerce and trade sections\nof the village.  The <y>cobblestone path<1> glows with a faint aura.  To the west\nthe avenue abruptly stops in a dead end.  To the east it continues through\nthe marketplace.\n',42,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5755,0,0,0,'Dead End','  This surprisingly clean room shows no sign of occupancy.  To the east\nDvalien Avenue goes through the commerce and trade sections of the village.\n',42,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5756,0,0,0,'The Chamber of Abbot Stratos','  This is the chamber of the man who founded Stratos, Abbot Stratos.  The\nchamber seems to shine with the brightness of many moons.  The elegant\nfurnishings and fine paintings adds to the effect.  Well crafted <p>stained<1>\n<r>glass<1> <g>windows<1> glitter colorfully in the light.  The rooms is kept with the\nutmost cleanliness and seems almost fit for the heavens.  To the south a\nlarge steel door opens out onto the village center.\n',42,131080,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5757,0,0,0,'Dvalien Avenue','  This busy avenue runs east and west through the commerce and trade sections\nof the village.  The <y>cobblestone path<1> glows with a faint aura.  To the west\nyou see the center of the village, and to the east the avenue continues\nthrough the marketplace.\n',42,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5758,0,0,0,'Dvalien Avenue','  This busy avenue runs east and west through the commerce and trade sections\nof the village.  The <y>cobblestone path<1> glows with a faint aura.  To the north\nyou see a building marked \'General Supplies\', and to the east and west the\navenue continues through the marketplace.\n',42,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5759,0,0,0,'Alistayre\'s Adventuring Supply','  This store is cluttered about with various odds and ends, seemingly in a state\nof constant disorganization.  There is a large sign on the wall above you,\nscreaming out to be looked at.  To the south through a small doorway lies\nDvalien Avenue.\n',42,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5760,0,0,0,'Dvalien Avenue','  This busy avenue runs east and west through the commerce and trade sections\nof the village.  The <y>cobblestone path<1> glows with a faint aura.  To the south\nyou see a crowded Inn.  To the east and west the avenue continues through the\nmarketplace.  Nearby to the east you can make out the eastern gates of the\nvillage.\n',42,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5761,0,0,0,'Tirian\'s Tavern','  The tavern seems to be alive with joy, the many customers singing happy songs\nof glorious battles and of nature herself.  The bar seems well stocked with\nfood and drink.  A small staircase leads up into the inn itself.  A plain door\nleads north out onto Dvalien Avenue.\n',42,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5762,0,0,0,'Inside the Eastern Gates of Stratos','  The village is quite busy, people bustling about trying to get their affairs\nin order.  The people of the town seem content yet paranoid, looking over\ntheir shoulders frequently for possible danger.  To the west lies Dvalien\nAvenue.  To the east the eastern gates lead out of the village.  To the\nnorthwest and south you see official-looking huts with solid bamboo doors.\n',42,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5763,0,0,0,'A Small Guardhouse','  The walls are cluttered with various posters and documents, including some\nvery official-looking ones.  The hut is quite warm and cozy.  The door to the\nsoutheast leads back out to the town.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5764,0,0,0,'A Small Guardhouse','  The walls are cluttered with various posters and documents, including some\nvery official-looking ones.  The hut is quite warm and cozy.  The door to the\nnorth leads back out to the town.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5765,0,0,0,'Outside the Eastern Gates of Stratos','  To the west the sparkling gates of Stratos stand majestically.  To the\nnortheast, a small path weaves through the mountains leading to a tower of\nsome sort.  From the northeast, loud voices can be heard sounding like\ncommands given out to an army.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5766,0,0,0,'The Stratos Inn','  The inn appears well kept and has a familiar feel to it.  Doors down the\nhallway leads to the individual rooms.  The walls seem sturdy and the storage\nsafe looks impenetrable.\n',42,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5767,0,0,0,'Before A Large Garrison','  The noises coming from the northeast are quite loud at this point.  To the\nnortheast lies a large garrison bustling with some sort of preparation.  To\nthe southwest the path continues through the mountains.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5768,0,0,0,'Center of a Large Garrison','  The smell of leather polish and freshly sharpened swords permeates the air.\nThe local war complex appears to be very well organized.  Warriors are bustling\naround in a hurry, apparently preparing for a large battle of some sort.  To\nthe west is a large oak door with a small sign above it marked with a sword and\nshield.  To the east is yet another large oak door with an engraved picture of\na mage on the sign.  Up ahead to the north, a well-trodden path with dribbles\nof blood scattered bout leads to the battlefield.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5769,0,0,0,'Hall of Gladiators','  The walls are adorned with various old swords and shields with an\noccasional trophy or banner serving to remind the inhabitant of glorious\nbattles of the past.  To the northwest lies a large door fashioned from\nivory with a sword and a cross upon it.  To the southwest lies another\nivory door with gold-plated hinges and bearing an inscription of another\nlanguage.  To the west the hall continues.  To the east a large oak door\nleads back into the center of the garrison.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5770,0,0,0,'Dvalien\'s Sanctuary','  Everything about this room suggests the pursuit of goodness, from the evenly\npolished floors to the small shrine near the back of the room.  Small stained\nglass windows bearing pictures of Dvalien\'s deity allow rose-colored light to\nbathe the entire room beautifully.  A hand-woven rug covers the wooden floor.\nTo the southeast an ivory door leads back out into the hall.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5771,0,0,0,'Hall of Gladiators','  Wondrous sights fill this part of the hall.  The walls are adorned with\nvarious old swords and shields with an occasional trophy or banner to remind\nthe inhabitants of glorious battles of the past.  A grand staircase leads\nupwards into a beautiful tower of some sort.  To the east the hall continues.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5772,0,0,0,'The Hollow of Faeryth McLoebin','  The walls are no longer wood here, but polished stone; the mark of a master\nthief.  The furnishings are sparse, save for the various fine paintings hanging\non the walls.  It makes one wonder how they were acquired, and from who.\nIntuition suggests the paintings must have belonged to the unjust for the room\nglows with an aura of white light which belongs only to those with pure hearts.\nTo the northeast an ivory door leads back into the hall.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5773,0,0,0,'Hall of Sorcery','  Bright blazing light emanate from the floor tiles, which are decorated with\nrunes and arcane symbols.  A sort of empty feeling resides in this room\nconveying a feeling of hostility.  Various mystical engravings are seen on\nall the walls, even the ceiling.  A timeless melody can be faintly heard,\nrepeating over and over but never losing its pace.  To the northeast is a\nsolid wooden door with a white cross embossed into it.  To the southeast, a\nplain wooden door bars access to what lies beyond.  The hall continues to\nthe east.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5774,0,0,0,'Tower of Gladiator Yunghai','  This chamber is the epitome of a warrior\'s abode, the various instruments\nof the trade hangs on the walls along with various other terms of surrender\nand proclamations of victory.  The small windows bring in just enough light\nto reveal a small spyhole in the northern wall, presumably an outlook onto\nthe battlefield.  A grand staircase leads back down into the hall.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5775,0,0,0,'Nitellion\'s Chamber','  Various pious products adorn the simple white walls of this holy chamber.\nGigantic stained glass windows allows colorful light to shine in.  To the\nsouthwest, a solid wooden door with a white cross embossed into it leads back\ninto the hall.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5776,0,0,0,'The Garrison Spell Workshop','  The air crackles and fizzes with magical energy, various ether clouds floating\nhere and there.  Large supplies of magical components, staffs, and wands are\nstored here.  To the northwest, a solid wooden door leads back out into the\nhall.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5777,0,0,0,'Path To The Battlefield','  The stones and sticks along this path seem downtrodden and pushed aside as\nif hundreds of soldiers had come through this way.  Various broken weapons\nand drops of blood grace the plain dirt path.  To the north the path continues\ntowards the battle path.  To the south is the Stratos Garrison.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5778,0,0,0,'Hall of Sorcery','  Bright blazing light emanate from the floor tiles, which are decorated with\nrunes and arcane symbols.  A sort of empty feeling resides in this room\nconveying a feeling of hostility.  Various mystical engravings are seen on\nall the walls, even the ceiling.  A timeless melody can be faintly heard,\nrepeating over and over but never losing its pace.  Attached to the east wall\nis a giant staircase manufactured of a plasma-like substance.  The hall\ncontinues to the west.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5779,0,0,0,'Tower of Sorcerer Aradon','  This chamber is the epitome of a mage\'s abode, the various components and\ntools of the trade hangs on the walls along with various scrolls and daggers.\nThe huge windows bring enough light in for alchemy and scroll-writing as well\nas the various difficulties of spell memorization and meditation.  A staircase\nmade of a blue plasma-like substance leads back down into the hall.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5780,0,0,0,'Path To The Battlefield','  The stones and sticks along this path seem downtrodden and pushed aside as\nif hundreds of soldiers had come through this way.  Various broken weapons\nand drops of blood grace the plain dirt path.  To the north the path continues\ntowards the battle path.  To the south, the path leads back towards the\nStratos Garrison.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5781,0,0,0,'Path To The Battlefield','  The stones and sticks along this path seem downtrodden and pushed aside as\nif hundreds of soldiers had come through this way.  Various broken weapons\nand drops of blood grace the plain dirt path.  To the east sits a small shack.\nThe path continues to the north and south.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5782,0,0,0,'A Small Shack','  The plain walls are covered with paintings of great battles and various\ntools and weapons.  A small woven mat rests in front of the door.  An open\ndoorway to the west leads out of the shack.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5783,0,0,0,'Just Before The Battlefield','  The stones and sticks along this path seem downtrodden and pushed aside as\nif hundreds of soldiers had come through this way.  Various broken weapons\nand drops of blood grace the plain dirt path.  To the northwest loud screams\nand the sounds of warfare can be heard.  The path continues south towards\nthe Stratos Garrison.\n',42,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5784,0,0,0,'A Desolate Battlefield','  A warm wind blows across the sky, carrying with it the odor of blood and\ndeath.  Various broken weapons and drops of blood are randomly found strewn\nabout the ground.  It seems as though the battlefield stretches on infinitely\nin all directions.\n',42,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5785,0,0,0,'A Desolate Battlefield','  A warm wind blows across the sky, carrying with it the odor of blood and\ndeath.  Various broken weapons and drops of blood are randomly found strewn\nabout the ground.  It seems as though the battlefield stretches on infinitely\nin all directions.\n',42,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
