(5826,0,0,0,'A Desolate Battlefield','  A warm wind blows across the sky, carrying with it the odor of blood and\ndeath.  Various broken weapons and drops of blood are randomly found strewn\nabout the ground.  It seems as though the battlefield stretches on infinitely\nin all directions.\n',42,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5827,0,0,0,'A Desolate Battlefield','  A warm wind blows across the sky, carrying with it the odor of blood and\ndeath.  Various broken weapons and drops of blood are randomly found strewn\nabout the ground.  It seems as though the battlefield stretches on infinitely\nin all directions.  An enormous gate fashioned from titanium opens onto a\nforested path to the east.\n',42,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5828,0,0,0,'A Desolate Battlefield','  A warm wind blows across the sky, carrying with it the odor of blood and\ndeath.  Various broken weapons and drops of blood are randomly found strewn\nabout the ground.  It seems as though the battlefield stretches on infinitely\nin all directions.\n',42,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5829,0,0,0,'A Desolate Battlefield','  A warm wind blows across the sky, carrying with it the odor of blood and\ndeath.  Various broken weapons and drops of blood are randomly found strewn\nabout the ground.  It seems as though the battlefield stretches on infinitely\nin all directions.\n',42,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5830,0,0,0,'A Desolate Battlefield','  A warm wind blows across the sky, carrying with it the odor of blood and\ndeath.  Various broken weapons and drops of blood are randomly found strewn\nabout the ground.  It seems as though the battlefield stretches on infinitely\nin all directions.\n',42,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5831,0,0,0,'A Desolate Battlefield','  A warm wind blows across the sky, carrying with it the odor of blood and\ndeath.  Various broken weapons and drops of blood are randomly found strewn\nabout the ground.  It seems as though the battlefield stretches on infinitely\nin all directions.\n',42,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5832,0,0,0,'A Bloodstained Path','  The path is coated with dried blood and decaying remains, showing a obvious\nlack of regard for health or safety.  Various broken weapons and shredded bits\nof armor are strewn about.  To the south, loud shouts and screams can be heard.\nTo the north the path continues towards the mountain.\n',42,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5833,0,0,0,'A Bloodstained Path','  The path is coated with dried blood and decaying remains, showing a obvious\nlack of regard for health or safety.  Various broken weapons and shredded bits\nof armor are strewn about.  To the south, loud shouts and screams can be heard.\nTo the east and west are small caves barred by gates fashioned from a greenish\ncoral.  The path continues toward the mountains to the north.\n',42,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5834,0,0,0,'A Bloodstained Path','  The path is coated with dried blood and decaying remains, showing a obvious\nlack of regard for health or safety.  Various broken weapons and shredded bits\nof armor are strewn about.  The outcries of war can be heard far to the south.\nTo the northeast, the path leads into a large cave in the mountain.\n',42,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5835,0,0,0,'A Wooded Path','  The tall trees bordering the path casts eerie shadows upon the ground.  The\nsticks and leaves have been trampled down and pushed aside as if some large\ncreature had been through this way.  The path continues to the northeast.  To\nthe west is a large titanium gate which opens onto a vast battlefield.\n',42,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5836,0,0,0,'A Wooded Path','  The tall trees bordering the path casts eerie shadows upon the ground.  The\nsticks and leaves have been trampled down and pushed aside as if some large\ncreature had been through this way.  To the southwest, the path continues\nthrough the battlefield.  A large ladder fashioned of titanium leads up to\nanother level of the path.\n',42,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5837,0,0,0,'A Wooded Path','  The tall trees bordering the path casts eerie shadows upon the ground.  The\nsticks and leaves have been trampled down and pushed aside as if some large\ncreature had been through this way.  A large ladder fashioned from titanium\nleads down onto a lower level of the path.  The path continues to the east.\n',42,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5838,0,0,0,'A Wooded Path','  The tall trees bordering the path casts eerie shadows upon the ground.  Small\ntracks are scattered about, evidence of the animal activity nearby.  To the\nnortheast lies a giant grey tower.  The path continues west towards the\nbattlefield.\n',42,131080,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5839,0,0,0,'Bottom Floor of the Mystic Tower','  The plain grey stone walls glow with some sort of powerful and arcane\nenchantment.  Splendid tapestries depicting the glories of mystical study\ncovers the walls.  A huge broad staircase made of a blue plasma-like\nsubstance spirals upwards.  The tower opens up onto a wooded path to the\nsouthwest.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5840,0,0,0,'Second Floor of the Mystic Tower','  The plain grey stone walls glow with some sort of powerful and arcane\nenchantment.  On the walls, faded and outdated scrolls are hung with a\nsort of reckless abandon.  A staircase fabricated of a blue plasma-like\nsubstance leads upwards and downwards.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5841,0,0,0,'A Great Mystic\'s Abode','  This inner sanctum is bare in comparison to the floors below.  There are no\nwindows or portals save for the huge skylight in the center of the ceiling.  A\nstaircase made of blue plasma-like substance leads back downwards.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5842,0,0,0,'A Secret Bunker','  The walls of this small hideout are made from stainless steel.  Polished to\na glossy sheen, the walls can be used as mirrors if the need arises.  Assorted\ntactical maps and strategy guides are strewn about carelessly.  A gigantic\nvault door bars the way to the west.  The bunker continues to the north and\neast.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5843,0,0,0,'A Secret Bunker','  The walls of this small hideout are made from stainless steel.  Polished to\na glossy sheen, the walls can be used as mirrors if the need arises.  Assorted\ntactical maps and strategy guides are strewn about carelessly.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5844,0,0,0,'The Stratian Vault','  The thick steel walls and the vault door protects this place from intruders.\nThe walls seem infallible save for the vault door leading east.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5846,0,0,0,'A Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The moss-covered ceiling seems to extend a hundred feet up.  The hallway\nhas an eerie malefluous feeling to it.  Every sound made is amplified to a\nreverberating cacophony of noise.  The cave opens up onto a path to the\nsouthwest.  The hallway continues deeper into the cave to the north.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5847,0,0,0,'An Intersection in the Caves of Kiryl','  Many pools of stagnant water are found on the cave floor.  Eerie noises can\nbe heard reverberating through the caves, but its hard to tell where they\noriginate from.  Occasional screams intrudes on the normal humdrum of the caves.\nTo the northwest a huge hallway leads into a well-lit and loud section of the\ncaves.  To the northeast, the hallway shrinks slightly as it twists its way\ninto the heart of the mountain.  The hallway continues to the south.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5848,0,0,0,'A Huge Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  Hearty laughter and cheers can be heard coming from further north.  Small\ntrickles of water make their way down the limestone walls in a sort of odd\npattern.  The hallway enters an intersection to the southeast and continues\nto the north.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5849,0,0,0,'A Huge Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The sounds of laughter and merriment can be distinctly heard coming from a\ntavern to the west.  The sounds seems to contain a sinister element to it.\nThe hallway continues to the north and south.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5850,0,0,0,'Kiryl Tavern','  This place of high spirits itself seems to emanate an odd black aura of evil\nand death.  The large shelves, made from coral, hold an extensive amount of\nimported liquors and comestibles.  The lights are down low.  The crowded tables\nalmost seem to overlap each other.  A solid wooden door opens onto a hallway\nto the east.\n',42,164029,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5851,0,0,0,'A Huge Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The limestone walls seems to crowd in on the room giving off a feeling of\noppressiveness.  This part of the hallway has been cobbled for some reason,\nbut the cobblestones are fashioned of rough coral and are not adverse to\nwearing down footwear.  The hall continues to the north and south.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5852,0,0,0,'A Huge Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The limestone walls seems to crowd in on the room giving off a feeling of\noppressiveness.  This part of the hallway has been cobbled for some reason,\nbut the cobblestones are fashioned of rough coral and are not adverse to\nwearing down footwear.  To the west stands a large wooden door.  The gurgling\nsounds of water can be heard to the northeast.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5853,0,0,0,'Kiryl Supply','  Tools and other useful items rest on the aged oak shelves in this small\norderly room.  The lights are dimmer inside.  A large wooden door leads out\nonto a hallway to the east.\n',42,164029,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5854,0,0,0,'A Fountain Square in the Caves of Kiryl','  This appears to be the local gathering place for the occupants of these\ncaves.  For a gathering place, however, it seems awfully awkward here.  Small\nchunks of the cave ceiling fall into the fountain every so often.  A plain\nwooden door leads northwards.  To the southwest, a large hallway leads to\nparts unknown.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5855,0,0,0,'An Official-Looking Room','  The lack of moss or stagnant water in this room leads to the believe that it\nis occupied by a tidy person.  The cave walls are adorned with fine trophies\nand banners of war.  Somehow the echo has been eliminated in this room.  A\nplain wooden door leads out onto a fountain square to the south.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5856,0,0,0,'A Secret Bunker','  The walls of this small hideout are made from stainless steel.  Polished to\na glossy sheen, the walls can be used as mirrors if the need arises.  Assorted\ntactical maps and strategy guides are strewn about carelessly.  To the west,\nthe bunker continues.  A ladder leads back up onto the battlefield.\n',42,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(5857,0,0,0,'A Hall in the Caves of Kiryl','  The limestone walls are drenched in subterranean liquids, giving them a shiny\ntexture which adds to the mystery of these caves.  The cave ceiling somehow\nmanages to hold up under the pressure of the mountain.  Those unused to the\nsubterranean might still be wary of going deeper into the mountain.  The hall\ncontinues to the northeast and to the southeast.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5858,0,0,0,'A Hall in the Caves of Kiryl','  The limestone walls are drenched in subterranean liquids, giving them a shiny\ntexture which adds to the mystery of these caves.  The cave ceiling somehow\nmanages to hold up under the pressure of the mountain.  Those unused to the\nsubterranean might still be wary of going deeper into the mountain.  The hall\ncontinues to the east and to the southwest.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5859,0,0,0,'Before a Black Tower in the Caves of Kiryl','  A sinister tower rises out of the ground to the east.  It appears to be\nconstructed of a blackened metal.  Demonic symbols are inscribed upon its\nwalls.  The hall continues to the west.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5860,0,0,0,'The Black Tower','  The tower is very nondescript, only the two solid steel doors leading north\nand south being of any interest.  A distinct smell of fresh blood wafts through\nthe air.  Tower doors made of coral lead east and west.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5861,0,0,0,'Before a Black Tower in the Caves of Kiryl','  A sinister tower rises out of the ground to the west.  It appears to be\nconstructed of a blackened metal.  Demonic symbols are inscribed upon its\nwalls.  The hall continues to the northeast.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5862,0,0,0,'A Sacrificial Room','  The room is dominated by a humongous pentagram drawn in blood on the floor\nalong with several burning effigies of noble deities hung on the walls.  The\nwalls are covered with ghostly curtains further increasing the sinister\natmosphere.  A staircase made of coral leads up further in the tower.  A steel\ndoor leads southwards.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5863,0,0,0,'A Den of Thieves','  The walls are made of a blackened stone.  There are several fine paintings\non the wall, obviously stolen at the whim of the occupant.  A small coral\nstaircase leads further up in the tower.  A steel door leads to the north.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5864,0,0,0,'A Blackened Altar','  The bamboo floor is mostly taken up by the large altar, but the walls have\nroom for several weapons and medicinal salves.  There are no windows, but rather\ndark robes hung in a circle on the ceiling.  A small coral staircase leads\ndownwards.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5865,0,0,0,'A Dark Warrior\'s Abode','  The walls are covered with severed heads and scalps, all covered with a sickly\nred coat of dried blood.  There are also several pieces of discarded armor and\nbroken weapons lying about.  A small coral staircase leads downwards.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5866,0,0,0,'A Dark Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The moss on the walls here seems to absorb any light given off, resulting in\nan odd aura of darkness.  The hall continues to the north and to the southwest.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5867,0,0,0,'A Dark Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The moss on the walls here seems to absorb any light given off, resulting in\nan odd aura of darkness.  The hall continues to the north and to the south.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5868,0,0,0,'A Dark Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The moss on the walls here seems to absorb any light given off, resulting in\nan odd aura of darkness.  A small tunnel leads to the east while the hallway\ncontinues to the north and south.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5869,0,0,0,'A Small Tunnel in the Caves of Kiryl','  The low ceiling makes travel more difficult.  A warm wind blows through the\ntunnel from the southeast, bringing with it the distinct smell of death.  The\ntunnel opens up onto a dark hallway to the west and continues to the southeast.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5870,0,0,0,'A Small Tunnel in the Caves of Kiryl','  The low ceiling makes travel more difficult.  A warm wind blows through the\ntunnel from the east, bringing with it the distinct smell of death.  The\ntunnel continues to the northwest and east.  Shadowy contours of a building\nseems to be further east.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5871,0,0,0,'A Small Tunnel in the Caves of Kiryl','  The low ceiling makes travel more difficult.  The air is still here,\npresumably because of the huge dark tower to the east.  The tunnel continues\nback to the west.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5872,0,0,0,'The Unholy Tower','  Various effigies of holy deities stand burning on stakes fashioned of coral.\nA large pentagram on the floor serves to make unholy sacrificial offerings.\nA huge coral staircase leads upwards.  The tower opens onto a small tunnel to\nthe west.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5873,0,0,0,'Middle of the Unholy Tower','  This is the second floor of the tower.  The air seems to have become colder.\nThe chamber is marked with unholy symbols and demonic runes.  A huge coral\nstaircase leads both upwards and downwards.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5874,0,0,0,'Top of the Unholy Tower','  Fear, despair, and hopelessness rests like a heavy blanket upon this chamber.\nEvery facet and corner of the room is covered in dried blood and the decaying\nremains of past victims.  Several pentagrams are etched onto the floor.  A\nhuge coral staircase leads down to another section of the tower.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5875,0,0,0,'A Dark Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The moss on the walls here seems to absorb any light given off, resulting in\nan odd aura of darkness.  The hallway continues to the north and south.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5876,0,0,0,'A Dark Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The moss on the walls here seems to absorb any light given off, resulting in\nan odd aura of darkness.  The hallway continues to the northeast and south.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5877,0,0,0,'A Dark Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The moss on the walls here seems to absorb any light given off, resulting in\nan odd aura of darkness.  The hallway opens up onto a large intersection to\nthe north and continues southwest.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5878,0,0,0,'A Large Intersection in the Caves of Kiryl','  The hallway splits here, leading to two different and larger halls.  To the\nwest the hall seems lit, but to the northeast you can make out nothing due to\nthe absolute darkness.  A strange feeling of intense evil emanates from the\nnortheast.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5879,0,0,0,'A Shady Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  A cool subterranean wind blows through here, whistling through the porous\nsurface of the cave walls.  A sense of evil can be felt from the northeast.\nThe hallway opens up onto a large intersection to the southwest.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5880,0,0,0,'A Well-Lit Hall in the Caves of Kiryl','  The wet earth floor of this hall is covered in footprints, showing the large\nusage of this route.  The footprints seem to lead northwest.  The hallway\ncontinues to the northwest and east.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5881,0,0,0,'A Well-Lit Hall in the Caves of Kiryl','  The wet earth floor of this hall is covered in footprints, showing the large\nusage of this route.  The footprints end in front of a plain wooden door to\nthe north.  The hall continues back to the southeast.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5882,0,0,0,'A Tactical Chamber','  The room is filled with assorted maps and drawings, showing the unorganized\nstyle of the Kirylian army.  All the maps seem to indicate that the mountains\nto the south of the valley are the main targets.  A plain wooden door leads to\nthe south.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5883,0,0,0,'A Quiet Intersection in the Caves of Kiryl','  All is strangely still here, save for the occasional dripping of water into\nthe pools on the floor.  The hall to the north seems to emit a very strong\nfeeling of evil.  To the east, a small hallway leads to parts unknown.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5884,0,0,0,'An Arcane Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The cave walls are seething with a potent mixture of evil and magic.  The\nwalls are covered with ancient carvings and various aged scrolls.  To the south\nthe hallway opens onto an intersection.  The hall continues northwest towards\nthe source of magic.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5885,0,0,0,'An Arcane Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The cave walls are seething with a potent mixture of evil and magic.  The\nwalls are covered with ancient carvings and various aged scrolls.  The hallway\ncontinues to the west and to the southeast.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5886,0,0,0,'An Arcane Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The cave walls are seething with a potent mixture of evil and magic.  The\nwalls are covered with ancient carvings and various aged scrolls.  A gargantuan\ntower can be seen to the west.  The hallway continues to the west and east.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5887,0,0,0,'Before the Arcane Tower in the Caves of Kiryl','  The cave walls are seething with a potent mixture of evil and magic.  The\nwalls are covered with ancient carvings and various aged scrolls.  To the\nnorthwest stands a gargantuan tower which has a pulsating aura of evil\nsurrounding it.  The hallway continues to the east.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5888,0,0,0,'The Arcane Tower','  The room seems to hum due to the overwhelming magical forces affecting it,\nand the furnishings seem to shift from place to place in a strange manner.  A\ntransparent glass staircase leads up.  The tower opens onto a hallway to the\nsoutheast.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5889,0,0,0,'The Arcane Tower','  The room seems to hum due to the overwhelming magical forces affecting it,\nand the furnishings seem to shift from place to place in a strange manner.  A\ntransparent glass staircase leads up and down to different levels of the tower.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5890,0,0,0,'The Arcane Tower','  The room seems to hum due to the overwhelming magical forces affecting it,\nand the furnishings seem to shift from place to place in a strange manner.  A\ntransparent glass staircase leads up and down to different levels of the tower.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5891,0,0,0,'Top of the Arcane Tower','  This level of the tower emerges from the mountain and pushes up a good fifty\nfeet into the mountain, giving a good view of the battlefield through the\ncrystal-plate windows surrounding the room.  A small glass staircase leads\ndownwards into the mountain.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5892,0,0,0,'A Small Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  Small creatures move around quickly within the porous cave walls, sounding\nlike far off screams in this virtual echo chamber.  The hallway opens onto an\nintersection to the west and continues to the northeast.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5893,0,0,0,'A Small Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The cave walls are covered in a sickly-green moss, evident of the decadent\njanitorial system in these caverns.  The ground is covered with pools of\nvarious sizes, all containing separate ecosystems of mold and sludge.  The\nhallway continues to the east and to southwest.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5894,0,0,0,'A Small Hallway in the Caves of Kiryl','  The cave walls are covered in a sickly-green moss, evident of the decadent\njanitorial system in these caverns.  The ground is covered with pools of\nvarious sizes, all containing separate ecosystems of mold and sludge.  A\nblindingly bright light obscures the view to the east.  The hallway continues\nto the west.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5895,0,0,0,'A Glowing Cave','  This bleak cave is brightened by the blindingly bright light coming from a\nlarge circle of stones which dominates the center of the room.  The light\nhas made even the most brave creatures vacate, for there is an absence of\nlife anywhere on or within the walls.  A small hallway leads to the west.\n',42,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,22,'',NULL),
(5896,0,0,0,'Preparation Room','  This small room, carved out of solid rock, appears to have been made with\ngreat haste.  There are many lewd drawings on the walls, apparently chiseled\nby bored soldiers waiting for the blast of the bugle.  A gate made of greenish\ncoral leads back out onto a path to the east.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(5897,0,0,0,'Preparation Room','  This small room, carved out of solid rock, appears to have been made with\ngreat haste.  There are numerous lewd drawings on the wall, apparently done\nby bored soldiers waiting for the blast of the bugle.  A gate made of greenish\ncoral leads back out onto a path to the west.\n',42,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6100,0,0,0,'Sneezy Supreme Court','You are in what seems to be a large courtroom.  The walls, ceiling, and floor\nare constructed from a strange white stone-like material emitting warm white\nlight.  The light floods the room with a bright illumination leaving no\nshadows.  You find it strangely comforting on your eyes and also a bit\ndisconcerting as the glow reveals every imperfection on all that are herein..\ndetails that might otherwise prove difficult in conventional lighting.\n',41,139305,60,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6101,1,-31,0,'A Tangled Jungle Path','  As you hack your way through the twisted vegetation, you realize that you\nare now in the midst of a faint path that gradually winds north and south.\nTrees and bushes close in over your head ominously, as if the jungle itself\nwere trying to swallow you.\n',45,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6102,1,-32,0,'A Tangled Jungle Path','  The path you are following is barely discernible, and is often partially\nblocked by the dense vegetation.  As you struggle on through the brutal heat\nand humidity, you cannot help but wonder at the creatures that would inhabit\nsuch a remote and savage land.\n',45,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6103,1,-33,0,'A Tangled Jungle Path','  The path continues to wind amongst the massive trees and bushes that stand\neverywhere in sight.  The vegetation is incredibly dense to the north,\nwhile to the south it seems to slightly recede.\n',45,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6104,1,-34,0,'At the Edge of a Misty Valley','  You emerge from the various plants to suddenly confront a marvelous\nvista.  A huge valley stretches before you, its details shrouded in a haze\nof mist.  There is a faint path to the north, while to the south you see what\nseems to be a series of rope-like vines trailing down a steep slope into the\nvalley below.\n',45,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6105,1,-34,-1,'On a Steep Trail','  Although steep, it is barely possible to maneuver this trail.  Around\nyou are vines which quiver slightly with each of your movements.  The mist\nis now all around you, limiting your vision to nothing more than a few\nfeet.  You feel very exposed here, and can feel your your tension rise.\n',45,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6106,1,-34,-2,'At the Base of a Misty Valley','  You are now at the base of the valley walls.  A series of tangled vines\nleads upwards along a steep sloped path, quickly disappearing into the thick\nmist which lies above you.  A muddy footpath stretches away to the south,\nwhere you can hear the faint gurgling of water.  You can just make out a faint\ntrail leading into the jungle to the east.\n',45,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6107,1,-35,-2,'At the Edge of a Wide River','  You are on the northern bank of a wide river that flows strongly from\neast to west.  A muddy footpath winds to the north, while to the south you\nsee a decrepit stone bridge which spans the river.\n',45,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6108,1,-36,-2,'On The Stone Bridge','  As you cautiously cross the bridge, you realize that it is actually a very\nsturdy structure.  The flooring of the bridge has been scraped clean of dirt\nand slime, as if it were regularly used.\n',45,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6109,1,-37,-2,'At the Edge of a Wide River','You are on the southern bank of a wide river which flows in an east-west\ndirection.  An ancient stone bridge spans the river to the north, while to\nthe southeast, a muddy footpath disappears into the jungle.  Due to recent\nmonsoons, this footpath is extremely treacherous.\n',45,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6110,2,-38,-2,'A Massive Stone Arch','  You gaze in awe at the massive stone arch which stretches above you.  It\nseems to mark the entrance to some kind of ruins to the south.  A small\nmuddy footpath trails away to the northwest.\n',45,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6111,2,-39,-2,'Entrance to the Ruins','  You are standing at the entrance to the ruins.  A massive stone arch stands\nto the north, while a dark corridor runs to the south.  You can see where\nthe jungle suddenly ends to be replaced by withered and cracked stone.  A\nfaded carving of some sort has been placed into the eastern wall.  Strong\nyoung vines cling to the surface of the stone as the jungle slowly\nencroaches, reclaiming the ruins to mother nature.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6112,2,-40,-2,'An Intersection of Hallways','  You are at an intersection of stone hallways.  The passages are\napproximately twelve feet in height, with walls made from chiseled stone.\nThere are archways leading east and west.  An archway north leads out\ntoward the open air of the entrance to the ruins, while a passage southward\nleads deeper inside.  The air in here is thick and muggy and the\ntemperature is quite hot and tropical.  Sweat beads your forehead either\nfrom the heat or just from fear.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,144,0,'',NULL),
(6113,1,-40,-2,'A Large Stone Hallway','  You are standing in a large stone hallway that stretches east and west.\nThe ceiling is slightly crumbling here, and small pebbles drop onto your\nhead as you pass by.  From the corner of your eye you glimpse a flicker of\nlight coming from one of the cracks above.  The sound of strange chanting\ncan be heard coming from the west.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(6114,0,-40,-2,'A Large Stone Hallway','  The hallway you are in travels in an east-west direction.  In the distance,\nyou can faintly hear the scurrying sounds of some kind of small animal.\nThe stone that surrounds you sweats in the heat and humidity of the\ntropical air.  Strangely, the temperature here seems no cooler than the\ntropical atmosphere outside though surrounded by solid stone.  A sound of\nstrange chanting comes from the west and seems close by.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(6115,-1,-40,-2,'Altar of the Pantathians','  You have entered a holy chamber of some sort.  Ornate but but primitive\ncarvings adorn the walls.  The high ceiling of the chamber reaches up into\nblackness.  There is a large stone hallway to the east, while two small\nentryways stand to the north and south, respectively.  Against the west wall\nof the chamber stands a massive altar made from pure onyx.  The strange\nchanting heard earlier to the east is now strangely silent.  In fact nothing\nbut the occasional random drip of water can be heard reverberating from\nthroughout the sweating passages.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(6116,-1,-39,-2,'A Small Alcove','  You are in a small alcove that seems to serve as a meditation chamber of\nsome sort.  There is a small shrine against the northern wall where it would\nseem incense is burned during prayers to some unknown deity or deities.\nThe stone walls of the alcove are engraved with eerie glyphs and holy\nsymbols but show wear from the ages to the point where most are completely\nworn.  The smell of a sickeningly sweet incense fills your nose coming from\nlit braziers attached to the floor near the shrine.  A small exit to the\nsouth leads out to a larger chamber where part of a large black altar can\nbe seen.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6117,-1,-41,-2,'A Small Alcove','  You are in a small alcove that seems to serve as a meditation chamber of\nsome sort.  There is a small shrine against the southern wall where it\nwould seem incense is burned during prayers to some unknown deity or\ndeities.  The stone walls of the alcove are engraved with eerie glyphs and\nholy symbols but show wear from the ages to the point where most are\ncompletely worn.  The smell of a sickeningly sweet incense fills your nose\ncoming from lit braziers attached to the floor near the shrine.  A small\nexit to the north leads out to a larger chamber where part of a large black\naltar can be seen.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6118,-2,-40,-2,'An Abandoned Stairway','  You have discovered an abandoned stairway leading down into the darkness.\nThe stonework is much rougher here, as if the stairway were deliberately cut\ndown into a natural cave of some sort.  The only other visible exit is a large\ndoor which stands to the east.  You can faintly make out some kind of script\non its surface.  The air here seems slightly cooler and drier than that to the\neast.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(6119,-2,-40,-3,'An Ancient Tunnel','  You have entered an ancient tunnel of some sort, with rough-hewn walls and\na low ceiling.  There is a stairway which travels up from here, and a small\npassage which winds away to the southwest.  In the distance, you can hear the\nsounds of flowing water.  Large natural looking cracks can be seen throughout\nthe stone of tunnel, one to the west seeming larger and slightly more regular\nthen the rest.\n',45,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,70,0,'',NULL),
(6120,-3,-41,-3,'The Underground River','  You are standing at the banks of a small underground river, which flows in a\nsoutheast-northwest direction.  The sound of falling water roars LOUDLY to the\nnorthwest.  Although the water flows strongly, you see there are several\nstepping stones which span the narrow river.  The rocky walls of this chamber\nseem to press in all around you, and you notice a sharp drop in the\ntemperature, probably from the chill of the cold flowing water.\n',45,131080,56,1000,6177,1,0,0,0,70,0,'',NULL),
(6121,-3,-42,-3,'An Ancient Tunnel','  As you maneuver around the various piles of stone in this tunnel, you feel an\nunexplainable eerie tingling begin to travel down your spine.  Above your\nlabored breathing, you can hear the sound of rapidly flowing water to the\nnorth.  To the south, two natural tunnels branch off to the southwest and\nsoutheast.  Stalagmites rise from the floor here to meet their parents hanging\nominously above your head.\n',45,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,70,0,'',NULL),
(6122,-4,-43,-3,'An Ancient Tunnel','  The stone walls of this tunnel seem to press in upon you.  Large stalagmites\nformed from centuries of dripping mineral-rich water rise high into the\nblackness above.  A large outcrop of stone protrudes into the room from the\neast.  Sounds of rushing water echo faintly in from the north.  The tingling\nsensation here is intense.  You begin to think that lingering long here might\nnot be such a good idea.\n',45,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(6123,-3,-44,-3,'An Ancient Tunnel','  The stone walls of this tunnel seem to press in upon you.  Large stalagmites\nformed from centuries of dripping mineral-rich water rise high into the\nblackness above.  Tunnels to the northeast and northwest lead off into pitch\nblack darkness beyond.  The tingling sensation is very strong now.\n',45,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(6124,-2,-43,-3,'An Ancient Tunnel','  The stone walls of this tunnel seem to press in upon you.  Large stalagmites\nformed from centuries of dripping mineral-rich water rise high into the\nblackness above.  Tunnels to the southwest and northwest lead off into pitch\nblack darkness.  The tingling sensation is very strong now.\n',45,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(6125,-3,-43,-3,'An Ancient Grotto','  You are standing in a small stone grotto.  A trickle of frigid water flows\nthrough the chamber.  The air shimmers with mystical energy alerting you with\na sense of power and danger.  Magical wards of confinement throb rhythmically in\na dim pulsing blood-red hue and surround you along the walls of the room.  A\nmagic circle of confinement has been drawn on the floor matching the rhythm\nof the surrounding wards.  You get the distinct feeling that you were never\nmeant to be here.\n',45,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6126,2,-41,-2,'A Large Stone Hallway','  You are traveling in a large stone hallway which stretches north and south.\nThe floor here has been worn very smooth by years and years of foot-traffic.\nThe ruins here seem in good shape considering their overgrown condition\noutside.  A faint breeze of warm tropical air drifts in from the north as well\nas faint sounds of jungle life.  You discern the grade of the hall beginning to\ndip here as it travels further down to the south into silent darkness.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(6127,2,-42,-2,'A Large Stone Hallway','  You are traveling in a large stone hallway which stretches north and south.\nThe floor here has been worn very smooth by years and years of foot-traffic.\nThe ruins here seem in good shape considering their overgrown look from the\noutside.  You discern the downward grade of the hall steepening a bit to the\nthe south and figure this section must travel now below the jungle surface.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(6128,2,-43,-2,'A Large Stone Chamber','  You have entered some kind of large stone chamber.  The ceiling here is at\nleast twenty feet tall.  Large doorways have been cut into the north, east,\nand west walls.  It seems really dark here with only the northern passage\nseeming only dimly brighter.  The stone walls drip with sweat making faint\nsounds as their tears hit the floor.  You hear the faint sound to the west --\nalmost like that of a baby\'s crying suddenly stifled and then only silence.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6129,1,-43,-2,'Noble Family Commons Area','  This open room seems to serve as a commons area for the Pantathian people.\nVarious items of furniture are scattered around the room, all looking rather\nfrayed and torn.  The commons here seem to be a place where Pantathian citizens\nof relative importance congregate to interact and socialize.  There is a lot of\nroom for the serpent folk to take a casual stroll, discuss the good old\ndays, and for the better classed families to bring their children to play.\nA Large doorway has been cut into the east The area continues to the east, an entrance to some kind of dwelling to the\nsouth, and an archway to the north reveals another large stone chamber.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6130,0,-43,-2,'Noble Family Commons Area','  This open room seems to serve as a commons area for the Pantathian people.\nVarious items of furniture are scattered around the room, all looking rather\nfrayed and torn.  The commons here seem to be a place where Pantathian citizens\nof relative importance congregate to interact and socialize.  There is a lot of\nroom for the serpent folk to take a casual stroll, discuss the good old\ndays, and for the better classed families to bring their children to play.\nThe area continues to the east, an entrance to some kind of dwelling to the\nsouth, and an archway to the north reveals another large stone chamber.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6131,0,-44,-2,'A Noble Family Dwelling','  As far as modern Pantathian standards go, this family dwelling area is\ndecorated in style.  Various bits of old furniture scatter the place denoting\nthis family as one of means among the lizards.  This small room is one of the\nonly private family dwellings here.  Privacy seems to be a luxury afforded only\nto those of means where livable space is such a commodity.  The ceiling here\nis high at close to 20\', though the room itself is only about 10 by 10.  A small\nentrance in the north wall leads into the commons area which seems to be the\nonly way in or out.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6132,1,-44,-2,'A Noble Family Dwelling','  As far as modern Pantathian standards go, this family dwelling area is\ndecorated in style.  Various bits of old furniture scatter the place denoting\nthis family as one of means among the lizards.  This small room is one of the\nonly private family dwellings here.  Privacy seems to be a luxury afforded only\nto those of means where livable space is such a commodity.  The ceiling here\nis high at close to 20\', though the room itself is only about 10 by 10.  A small\nentrance in the north wall leads into the commons area which seems to be the\nonly way in or out.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6133,3,-43,-2,'Dining Hall','You are standing in what was once a majestic dining hall.  The remains of\ntapestries and other pieces of artwork hang on the walls, while a large stone\ntable runs the length of the room.  You can see a flickering glow through the\ndoorway to the south.  An archway to the west leads out into a large stone\nchamber.  You smell the unmistakable oder of charred meat coming from the\nsouthern doorway.  The longer you stay here, the more you begin to realize that\nyou are hungry.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(6134,3,-44,-2,'Kitchen','  This is obviously the room where the Pantathians prepare their meals.  A huge\ncooking fire roars along the eastern wall, while several large iron pots hang\nfrom rafters stretched along the ceiling.  High above the fire on the eastern\nwall, a hole in the ceiling draws the smoke from the fire up and out of the\nroom.  A doorway to the north leads into a large dining area.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6135,3,-40,-2,'A Large Stone Hallway','  You are in a large stone hallway which stretches to the east and west.  You\ncan see small vines and roots growing through the cracks in the walls.  A\nwarm tropical breeze wafts in from the west carrying with it the promise of\nrain.  There appears to be some crude writing scrawled about 3\' from the\nfloor on the stone wall north of here.  It seems to be written in a\ndwarvish dialect of the common tongue.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(6136,4,-40,-2,'A Large Stone Hallway','  You are standing in a large stone hallway which stretches east and west.  The\nhallway branches at the eastern end, to give you a choice of directions there.\nOne branches to the northeast where you can vaguely make out the outline of a\nlarge staircase, and the other to the southeast where you see only darkness.\nWhile inspecting the passage to the southeast, you believe you can faintly make\nout the scent of rotting food.  A tropical breeze wafts in from the west\ncarrying with it the smell of rain.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(6137,5,-41,-2,'Storage Room','  You have entered a huge cavern with an arched ceiling.  Piles of broken boxes\nlitter the chamber, spilling their moldy contents to the floor.  The cavern\ncontinues to the east where the smell of rotting food comes now much stronger,\nwhile a small passage leads from the room to the northwest.  Occasionally from\nthe darker corners of the cavern here, you make out small rustlings and the\nsqueak of small rodents.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(6138,6,-41,-2,'Storage Room','  You have continued further into the storage room.  From this vantage point\nyou can now detect the odor of rotten food.  Rat droppings are everywhere.\nThe ceiling here is high above you and arched.  Vines grow along the walls\nslowly tearing the stone apart.  Pieces of stone that have collapsed from the\nwalls and ceiling litter the floor in small piles of rubble.  Your first\nimpression here is that this place seems more like a dump than a place where\nuseful items might be kept.  At least it seems to be fairly dry here.  The only\nway out that you can see appears to be to the west, where the cavern continues\nin that direction.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6139,5,-39,-2,'A Curved Staircase','  The room you have entered is roughly circular, and is dominated by a large\ncurved staircase which rises upwards into the darkness.  The only other visible\nexit is a passageway to the southwest.  Two rather weathered looking grotesques\ncarved from stone adorn each side of the lower supports of the stair almost\nas if keeping eternal watch over the area.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(6140,5,-39,-1,'An Ornate Hallway','  You are standing in an ornate hallway.  Fine sculptures and carvings line the\nwalls, and the area has been swept clean of dirt and debris.  It is one of the\nfew areas you have seen that looks remotely cared for.  The stone walls here\nhave been polished smooth, almost to a high gloss.  The ceiling lies some\n20\' or so above the floor which is covered by a 5\' wide regal looking carpet.\nA stone staircase winds further down from here deeper into the ruins and the\nhallway continues to the east into darkness.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6141,6,-39,-1,'A Bend in the Ornate Hallway','  You have reached a bend in this ornate hallway.  Passages continues to the\nnorth and west, while a huge golden door stands to the east.  The walls here\nhave been engraved in a pictorial scene depicting Pantathians as a great\nwar-like race.  Some scenes show large armies of lizardmen dressed in fantastic\nand regal armors bearing down on armies of races you don\'t recognize which\nmust now be extinct.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6142,6,-38,-1,'End of the Ornate Hallway','  You have reached the end of the ornate hallway.  A rusty iron ladder has been\nbolted into the northern wall, and leads upwards to a small trapdoor.  The only\nother visible exit is a passage to the south.  The walls here have been\nengraved and painted in scenes depicting powerful mages in Pantathia\'s ancient\npast.  Some show battle scenes with groups of mages amongst massive Pantathian\narmies group-casting powerful magics against goblin hoards, evil looking\ndark-skinned elves, and other armies of ancient races you don\'t recognize.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6143,6,-38,0,'A Stone Tower','  You have entered a central stone chamber supporting the only remaining tower\nknown in the Pantathian ruins.  The walls of thick stone support the ceiling\nthat sits about twenty feet above your head.  A sturdy wooden door is set in\nthe west wall, and the outline of a wooden trapdoor can be seen in the center\nof the floor.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6144,5,-38,0,'Wizard\'s Workshop','  You are standing in some kind of wizard\'s workshop.  Tables line the walls,\neach covered with a variety of books, potions, and scrolls.  The walls and\nceiling are built here from smooth stone blocks tightly fit together without\nmortar.  The ceiling is about 20\' above and is cracked in places.  A sturdy\ndoor is set to the east and a simple brass door to the south.  This is where\nPantathian wizards develop their magic, write their scrolls, and mix their\npotions.  A strong tingling of magic fills the air.  An archway to the north\nseems to lead into some kind of library.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6145,7,-39,-1,'The Great Hall of the Onyx Throne','  You are standing in an enormous hall that extends to the east and south.  The\nceiling of this chamber is a graceful dome that sweeps up for at least fifty\nfeet.  The dome is constructed from a white stone you have never seen before.\nIt is cracked in places and discolored in others, though it seems quite stable.\nThere are no furnishings visible anywhere in the hall except for a huge throne\nfashioned from a dark black material located southeast of here, while a huge\ngolden door stands to the west.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,600,0,'',NULL),
(6146,8,-39,-1,'The Great Hall of the Onyx Throne','  You are standing in an enormous hall that extends to the west and south.  The\nceiling of this chamber is a graceful dome that sweeps up for at least fifty\nfeet.  The dome is constructed from a white stone you have never seen before.\nIt is cracked in places and discolored in others, though it seems quite stable.\nThere are no furnishings visible anywhere in the hall except for a huge throne\nfashioned from a dark black material located south of here.  A huge golden door\ncan be seen far to the west.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,600,0,'',NULL),
(6147,7,-40,-1,'The Great Hall of the Onyx Throne','  You are standing in an enormous hall that extends to the north and east.  The\nceiling of this chamber is a graceful dome that sweeps up for at least fifty\nfeet.  The dome is constructed from a white stone you have never seen before.\nIt is cracked in places and discolored in others, though it seems quite stable.\nThere are no furnishings visible anywhere in the hall except for a huge throne\nfashioned from a dark black material located eastward.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,600,0,'',NULL),
(6148,8,-40,-1,'The Onyx Throne of Pantathia','  You are standing in an enormous hall that extends to the north and east.  The\nceiling of this chamber is a graceful dome that sweeps up for at least fifty\nfeet.  The dome is constructed from a white stone you have never seen before\nand is cracked in places, discolored in others, though it seems quite stable.\nThe only furnishing in the entire hall, a large carven throne, dominates this\ncorner of the chamber.  A small golden door is set here in the eastern wall.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,600,0,'',NULL),
(6149,9,-40,-1,'The Prince\'s Private Chamber','  You have entered the personal chamber of the Pantathian Ruler: Prince\nS\'sthir.  The furnishings here are large and of good quality.  Several large\nancient rugs line the floor providing insulation from the cold stone below.\nLarge tapestries adorn the walls giving the room a regal look.  A small golden\ndoor in the western wall seems to be the only way in or out of this chamber.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(6150,5,-37,0,'A Musty Library','  You have entered a musty library, crammed to the ceiling with books of all\nkinds.  There are a few tables and several chairs scattered throughout the\nchamber.  The walls and ceiling are built from tightly fit together stone\nblocks.  The ceiling here is cracked in several places and water leaks in\nthrough them from outside.  The air is hot and humid and reeks of mildew.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6151,6,-37,0,'A Moldy Library','  You are in what must have once been a continuance of the Pantathian library\nto the west.  Once crammed to the ceiling with books of all kinds, the shelves\nnow seem to be filled with the wasted debris of once great knowledge.  Where\nonce must have been a ceiling of stone, now lies open to the sky.  Years of\ntropical rains have all but destroyed the knowledge that was stored here.  No\nattempt has been made to clear away the ruined mess that was once the east\nlibrary wing.  The stone debris that was once the ceiling and part of the\nnorthern wall now lie in heaped disarray on the floor.  An archway in the\nwall to the east seems to lead to some kind of storage room while to the\nwest, the better preserved west library wing stretches beyond your sight.\n',45,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6152,7,-37,0,'A Musty Storage Room','  A relatively dry storage room stands here mostly empty and sparsely\nfurnished.  Like most of the tower, the walls, ceiling, and floor here have\nbeen  constructed with tightly fitting stone blocks.  The ceiling rises some\n20\' above the floor.  An archway to the west leads into the Pantathian\nLibrary.  A single table against the eastern wall and a couple chairs break\nthe emptiness of the almost bare room.  The air smells strongly of mold and\nmildew.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6154,5,-39,0,'A Small Hallway','  You are in a small hallway traveling unimpeded to the east.  There is a new\nlooking heavy brass door set in the northern wall.  The hall is about wide\nfor two or three average sized lizardmen to walk closely side by side.  The roof\nabove stands at a height of about 20\'.  The roof and the walls along the sides\nare made up of stone that has been panelled rather recently with a rough wood\nveneer.  The floor is smoothly polished stone.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6155,6,-39,0,'A Small Hallway','  You are in a small hallway traveling unimpeded to the west.  There is a new\nlooking heavy brass door set in the eastern wall.  Strange wards have been\nengraved in its surface.  The hall is about wide enough for two to three\naverage sized lizardmen to walk closely side by side.  The roof above stands\nabove at a height of about 20\'.  The roof and the walls along the sides are\nmade up of stone panelled rather recently with a rough wood veneer.  The\nfloor is smoothly polished stone.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6156,7,-39,0,'The Wizard\'s Lair','  This room seems to be the lair of a rather powerful mage among the lizard\nfolk.  Bookshelves filled with cracked leather-bound tomes line the southern\nwall continuing across to the southeast corner.  The room is uncomfortably\nwarm heated by some unknown source and dimly lit by smoking oil lamps fastened\nto the walls.  You notice that this place is well organized unlike the majority\nof the ruins.  There is a new looking heavy brass door set in the western wall.\nStrange magical wards have been engraved in its surface.  The northern wall\nlooks strangely bare, in fact nothing has been placed within five feet of it.\n',45,131112,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,4,'',NULL),
(6157,8,-40,0,'A Spy Crawlspace','  This room seems to be some secret chamber used by the wizard to keep an eye on\nthings.  The space is small with about enough room for one average human to\ncrawl into.  The room is empty except for what looks like an eyepiece set in the\nfloor.  You can see the back of a bookshelf to the northwest that opens the\nconcealed exit into the wizard\'s lair in that direction.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,1,45,0,'',NULL),
(6158,7,-38,0,'Secret Hatch','  This is a small 4\'x 4\' room with walls of mortar-less stone block fitted\ntightly together.  Looking a bit weathered, different colored slime molds have\nbeen growing on the walls for quite some time being fed from moisture leaking\nthrough large cracks in the ceiling which stands about 20\' from the floor.\nOn the southern wall, you can see built some large interlocking gears.\nBesides about an inch thick layer of smooth mud that coats the floor, the room\nlooks quite plain except for a small spoked iron wheel coming out from a\n2\' diameter pedestal in the center of the floor.\n',45,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,4,'',NULL),
(6159,7,-38,-1,'On an Old Iron Ladder','  This vertical passage is extremely narrow with room for only one or two.\nFrom the looks of the slime on the ladder and walls, you\'d guess that\nthis place has been long forgotten.  Above your head is a heavy-looking\niron hatch.  Below you, the ladder stretches further down into blackness.\nYou find yourself losing your grip on the rung you now hug for dear life.\nIt is quite slippery due to the slime.\n',45,131080,58,60,6159,1,0,0,1,100,0,'',NULL),
(6160,7,-38,-2,'On an Old Iron Ladder','  This vertical passage is extremely narrow with room for only one or two.\nFrom the looks of the slime on the ladder and walls, you\'d guess that\nthis place has been long forgotten.  Above your head is a heavy-looking\niron hatch.  Below you, the ladder stretches further down into blackness.\nYou find yourself losing your grip on the rung you now hug for dear life.\nIt is quite slippery due to the slime.\n',45,131080,58,50,6160,1,0,0,1,100,0,'',NULL),
(6161,7,-38,-3,'A Dripping Natural Cavern','  This is a rather large natural cavern formed as a pocket in the natural\nbedrock.  Cold mineral rich water trickles down the walls forming interesting\nlooking calcium formations that span from floor to ceiling.  A light dusting of\ncoarse black sand covers the floor except for where shallow trickles of water\nfrom the dripping walls have eroded it clean in the low spots forming tiny\nveins of mineral deposits.  In the middle of the cavern, a slimy carbonate\ncoated thick iron ladder ascends upward through a 4\' diameter hole in the\nceiling.  A small beach extends to the east beyond which can be heard the sound\nof rapidly flowing water.\n',45,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6162,-3,-40,-3,'A Hidden Staircase Near the Falls','  This is a rather small natural cavern formed as a pocket in the natural\nbedrock.  Cold mineral rich water trickles down the walls forming interesting\nlooking calcium formations that span from floor to ceiling.  A light dusting of\ncoarse black sand covers the floor except for where shallow trickles of water\nfrom the dripping walls have eroded it clean in the low spots forming tiny\nveins of mineral deposits.  Carved expertly into the rock a narrow winding\nstaircase seems to lead downwards from here.  The stairs wrap around in a\nspiral, their western side exposed yet hidden from sight by a large waterfall\nfarther below.  To the east a panel is visible with several mechanisms\nattached to move it quietly aside.\n',45,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(6163,-3,-40,-4,'A Hidden Staircase Near the Falls','  This is a rather small natural cavern formed as a pocket in the natural\nbedrock.  Cold mineral rich water trickles down the walls forming interesting\nlooking calcium formations that span from floor to ceiling.  A light dusting of\ncoarse black sand covers the floor except for where shallow trickles of water\nfrom the dripping walls have eroded it clean in the low spots forming tiny\nveins of mineral deposits.  Carved expertly into the rock a narrow winding\nstaircase seems to lead upwards from here.  The stairs wrap around in a\nspiral, their western side exposed yet hidden from sight by a large waterfall\nfarther above.  To the north a panel is visible with several mechanisms\nattached to move it quietly aside.\n',45,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(6164,8,-38,-3,'Next to an Underground River','  You stand on the shore of a dark cold underground river.  A small beach of\nblack sand has been somehow formed here.  The air is warm but not tropical as\nyou are now far below the surface of the jungle above.  A large dark cavern\nleads to the west from the beach.  The sand here is dry and granular except\nfor where it edges up to the river to the southwest.  The water is dark and\ntravels at a rapid pace.  There is no natural light here.  The sound of the\nwater brings a sense of repose as you listen to its music.\n',45,131080,31,100,6164,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6165,10,-39,-3,'Underground River','  You are on an underground river that flows rapidly through a natural stone\ntunnel.  The tunnel is about 12\' wide and rises about 20\' above the surface of\nthe cold and dark water.  You cannot estimate the depth except that it is beyond\nthe reach of your feet.  A large iron grate is set just below the surface of the\nwater to the east.  Through it flows a high volume of dark cold water which\ncontinues down the tunnel to the west.  The river gets shallow and slower moving\nas it edges up on a beach of coarse black sand that stretches into a cavern in\nthat direction.\n',45,131080,29,100,6166,1,30,3,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6166,9,-39,-3,'Underground River','  You are on an underground river that flows rapidly through a natural stone\ntunnel.  The tunnel is about 12\' wide and rises about 20\' above the surface of\nthe cold and dark water.  You cannot estimate the depth except that it is beyond\nthe reach of your feet.  The water comes in from the east and continues down the\ntunnel to the southwest.\n',45,131080,29,100,6169,1,30,9,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6167,7,-40,-3,'Underground River','  You are on an underground river that flows rapidly through a natural stone\ntunnel.  The tunnel is about 12\' wide and rises about 20\' above the surface of\nthe cold and dark water.  You cannot estimate the depth except that it is beyond\nthe reach of your feet.  The water comes in from the northeast and continues\ndown the tunnel to the southwest.\n',45,131080,29,100,6170,1,30,9,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6168,6,-41,-3,'Underground River','  You are on an underground river that flows rapidly through a natural stone\ntunnel.  The tunnel is about 12\' wide and rises about 20\' above the surface of\nthe cold and dark water.  You cannot estimate the depth except that it is beyond\nthe reach of your feet.  The water comes in from the northeast and continues\ndown the tunnel to the southwest.\n',45,131080,29,100,6171,1,30,9,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6169,5,-42,-3,'Underground River','  You are on an underground river that flows rapidly through a natural stone\ntunnel.  The tunnel is about 12\' wide and rises about 20\' above the surface of\nthe cold and dark water.  You cannot estimate the depth except that it is beyond\nthe reach of your feet.  The water comes in from the northeast and continues\ndown the tunnel to the southwest.\n',45,131080,29,100,6172,1,30,9,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6170,4,-43,-3,'Underground River','  You are on an underground river that flows rapidly through a natural stone\ntunnel.  The tunnel is about 12\' wide and rises about 20\' above the surface of\nthe cold and dark water.  You cannot estimate the depth except that it is beyond\nthe reach of your feet.  The water comes in from the northeast and continues\ndown the tunnel to the southwest.\n',45,131080,29,100,6172,1,30,9,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6171,3,-44,-3,'Underground River','  You are on an underground river that flows rapidly through a natural stone\ntunnel.  The tunnel is about 12\' wide and rises about 20\' above the surface of\nthe cold and dark water.  You cannot estimate the depth except that it is beyond\nthe reach of your feet.  The water comes in from the northeast and continues\ndown the tunnel to the southwest.\n',45,131080,29,100,6173,1,30,9,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6172,2,-45,-3,'Underground River','  You are on an underground river that flows rapidly through a natural stone\ntunnel.  The tunnel is about 12\' wide and rises about 20\' above the surface of\nthe cold and dark water.  You cannot estimate the depth except that it is beyond\nthe reach of your feet.  The water comes in from the northeast and continues\ndown the tunnel as it bends to the west.\n',45,131080,29,100,6174,1,30,3,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6173,1,-45,-3,'Underground River','  You are on an underground river that flows rapidly through a natural stone\ntunnel.  The tunnel is about 12\' wide and rises about 20\' above the surface of\nthe cold and dark water.  You cannot estimate the depth except that it is beyond\nthe reach of your feet.  The water comes in from the east and continues further\ndown the tunnel to the northwest and the darkness beyond.\n',45,131080,29,100,6175,1,30,7,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6174,0,-44,-3,'Underground River','  You are on an underground river that flows rapidly through a natural stone\ntunnel.  The tunnel is about 12\' wide and rises about 20\' above the surface of\nthe cold and dark water.  You cannot estimate the depth except that it is beyond\nthe reach of your feet.  The water comes in from the southeast and continues\nfurther down the tunnel to the northwest and the darkness beyond.\n',45,131080,29,100,6176,1,30,7,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6175,-1,-43,-3,'Underground River','  You are on an underground river that flows rapidly through a natural stone\ntunnel.  The tunnel is about 12\' wide and rises about 20\' above the surface of\nthe cold and dark water.  You cannot estimate the depth except that it is beyond\nthe reach of your feet.  The water comes in from the southeast and continues\nfurther down the tunnel to the northwest where you can hear can hear the sound\nof falling water far in the distance.\n',45,131080,29,200,6176,1,30,7,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6176,-2,-42,-3,'Underground River','  You are on an underground river that flows rapidly through a natural stone\ntunnel.  The tunnel is about 12\' wide and rises about 20\' above the surface of\nthe cold and dark water.  You cannot estimate the depth except that it is beyond\nthe reach of your feet.  The water comes in from the southeast and continues\nfurther down the tunnel to the northwest where you can hear can hear the sound\nof falling water in the distance.\n',45,131080,29,200,6120,1,30,7,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6177,-4,-40,-3,'Near the Edge of the Falls','  You are on an underground river that flows rapidly through a natural stone\ntunnel.  The tunnel is about 12\' wide and rises about 20\' above the surface of\nthe cold and dark water.  You cannot estimate the depth except that it is beyond\nthe reach of your feet.  The water comes in from the southeast and drops down\nover a sudden dropoff to the west where the tunnel seems to just turn suddenly\nstraight down.  You estimate from the speed of the water that anything in the\nwater at this point has only a few seconds before being swept over the edge\nto certain doom below.  A heavy cold mist rolls up from below filling the tunnel\nwith chilled dampness.  The roar of the water is almost deafening.\n',45,131080,29,0,0,0,45,5,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6178,-4,-40,-3,'Over the Falls in Mid-air',' You are in mid-air below the lip of the falls above.  Heavy falling water\npummels your body flowing downward toward the darkness below.  The water chills\nyour skin.  The falling water and rising mist blinds and chokes you as you\ndescend wildly downward into the darkness.\n',45,131080,34,10,6179,1,0,0,0,480,0,'',NULL),
(6179,-4,-40,-5,'Underwater Vortex','  Water crashing down above you creates strong rolling currents that throw your\nbody around like a rag doll.  One second you feel yourself scrape the rocks\nat the bottom and the next you nearly break the surface.  You are absolutely\nout of control and at the mercy of the water.  Your lungs explode as\nconsciousness slips rapidly away.  Your see scenes from your life begin to flash\nthrough your mind.  You sense the end of your life is near.\n',45,131080,30,0,0,0,60,4,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6180,-4,-40,-5,'Rough Water Below the Falls','  Above you water crashes down through an opening in the stone ceiling.  The\nroom is filled with mist and spray like a cold fog.  The water surface around\nyou bubbles and boils from the rolling underwater currents caused by the falls\ncreating a heavy chop to the water.  High stone walls surround you blocking\ntravel in all directions save to the north where a dark underground lake\nstretches into the darkness beyond.  The roar from the falling water fills your\nears blocking out all other sound.\n',45,131080,29,0,0,0,30,0,0,500,0,'',NULL),
(6181,-5,-39,-4,'An Underground Lake','  You are on a large underground lake.  The murky water is dark and cold.  You\nhave no idea as to its depth but are unable to touch the bottom.  There is no\nnatural light to be seen here.  Above you, immense stalactites hang from the\nnatural stone of the ceiling high overhead.  The sounds of water dripping from\ntheir tips all around you gives an impression of a light rain.  The sound of a\nwaterfall can be heard loudly coming from the southeast feeding the lake.\nA wall of cold natural stone marks the western edge of the lake blocking travel\nin that direction.\n',45,131080,29,0,0,0,60,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(6182,-4,-39,-4,'North of the Falls','  You are on a large underground lake.  The murky water is dark and cold.  You\nhave no idea as to its depth but are unable to touch the bottom.  There is no\nnatural light to be seen here.  Above you, immense stalactites hang from the\nnatural stone of the ceiling high overhead.  The lake extends in all directions.\nDirectly to the south, a waterfall crashes down feeding the lake from a river\nabove.  The sound from the falling water fills your ears and cold mist rolls in\nclinging to your skin.\n',45,131080,29,0,0,0,30,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(6183,-3,-39,-4,'An Underground Lake','  You are on a large underground lake.  The murky water is dark and cold.  You\nhave no idea as to its depth but are unable to touch the bottom.  There is no\nnatural light to be seen here.  Above you, immense stalactites hang from the\nnatural stone of the ceiling high overhead.  The sounds of water dripping from\ntheir tips all around you gives an impression of a light rain.  The sound of a\nwaterfall can be heard loudly coming from the southwest feeding the lake.\nA wall of cold natural stone marks the eastern edge of the lake blocking travel\nin that direction.  Large natural looking cracks can be seen throughout the\nstone, one to the south seeming larger and slightly more regular then the rest.\n\n',45,131080,29,0,0,0,60,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(6184,-5,-38,-4,'An Underground Lake','  You are on a large underground lake.  The murky water is dark and cold.  You\nhave no idea as to its depth but are unable to touch the bottom.  There is no\nnatural light to be seen here.  Above you, immense stalactites hang from the\nnatural stone of the ceiling high overhead.  The sounds of water dripping from\ntheir tips all around you gives an impression of a light rain.  The sound of a\nwaterfall can be heard across the darkness from the south feeding the lake.\nA wall of cold natural stone marks the western edge of the lake blocking travel\nin that direction.\n',45,131080,29,0,0,0,60,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(6185,-4,-38,-4,'An Underground Lake','  You are on a large underground lake.  The murky water is dark and cold.  You\nhave no idea as to its depth but are unable to touch the bottom.  There is no\nnatural light to be seen here.  Above you, immense stalactites hang from the\nnatural stone of the ceiling high overhead.  The sounds of water dripping from\ntheir tips all around you gives an impression of a light rain.  The sound of a\nwaterfall can be heard across the darkness from the south feeding the lake.\nThe lake extends in all directions.\n',45,131080,29,0,0,0,30,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
