(6192,-4,-36,-4,'An Underground Lake','  You are on a large underground lake.  The murky water is dark and cold.  You\nhave no idea as to its depth but are unable to touch the bottom.  There is no\nnatural light to be seen here.  Above you, immense stalactites hang from the\nnatural stone of the ceiling high overhead.  The sounds of water dripping from\ntheir tips all around you gives an impression of a light rain.  The sound of a\nwaterfall can be faintly heard across the darkness from the south feeding the\nlake.  A wall of cold natural stone marks the northern and western edges of the\nlake blocking travel in those directions.\n',45,131080,29,0,0,0,30,1,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(6193,-3,-36,-4,'An Underground Lake','  You are on a large underground lake.  The murky water is dark and cold.  You\nhave no idea as to its depth but are unable to touch the bottom.  There is no\nnatural light to be seen here.  Above you, immense stalactites hang from the\nnatural stone of the ceiling high overhead.  The sounds of water dripping from\ntheir tips all around you gives an impression of a light rain.  The sound of a\nwaterfall can be faintly heard across the darkness from the south feeding the\nlake.  A wall of cold natural stone marks the northern edge of the lake blocking\ntravel in that direction.\n',45,131080,29,0,0,0,30,1,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(6194,-2,-36,-4,'An Underground Lake','You are on a large underground lake.  The murky water is dark and cold.  You\nhave no idea as to its depth but are unable to touch the bottom.  There is no\nnatural light to be seen here.  Above you, immense stalactites hang from the\nnatural stone of the ceiling high overhead.  The sounds of water dripping from\ntheir tips all around you gives an impression of a light rain.  The sound of a\nwaterfall can be faintly heard across the darkness from the south feeding the\nlake.  A wall of cold natural stone marks the northern edge of the lake blocking\ntravel in that direction.\n',45,131080,29,0,0,0,30,1,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(6195,-1,-36,-4,'An Underground Lake','  You are on a large underground lake.  The murky water is dark and cold.  You\nhave no idea as to its depth but are unable to touch the bottom.  There is no\nnatural light to be seen here.  Above you, immense stalactites hang from the\nnatural stone of the ceiling high overhead.  The lake here narrows and high\nstone walls surround you in all directions.  Just under the surface of the water\nto the east, a heavy iron grate blocks a tunnel where water from the lake flows\noff into underwater darkness.  Handholds have been chipped into the stone above\nthe grate to the east.\n',45,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(6196,-1,-36,-3,'An Ancient Tunnel','  This seems to be some kind of ancient tunnel traveling to the northeast.\nThere is a steep drop-off to the west with handholds chipped into the stone\nforming a natural ladder leading down to a large underground lake below.\nAbout 10\' wide and 20\' high, the walls and ceiling have been worked and\ntooled by unknown hands.  Tool marks show signs of long wear and erosion\nover thousands of years.  The quality of work on the tunnel, though quite old\nseem to resemble excavation techniques used by various subterranean races such\nas dwarves, drow, and kuo-toa.  The floor is polished smooth and seems to be\nfree of dust and debris usually found in passages long unused.\n',45,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6197,0,-35,-3,'An Ancient Tunnel','  This seems to be some kind of ancient tunnel traveling southwest and\nnortheast.  About 10\' wide and 20\' high, the walls and ceiling have been worked\nand tooled by unknown hands.  Tool marks show signs of long wear and erosion\nover thousands of years.  The quality of work on the tunnel, though quite old\nseem to resemble excavation techniques used by various subterranean races such\nas dwarves, drow, and kuo-toa.  The floor is polished smooth and seems to be\nfree of dust and debris usually found in passages long unused.\n',45,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(6198,1,-34,-3,'An Ancient Natural Cavern','  This place opens up into a large natural cavern.  Stalagmites on the floor\nseem to have been worn down and eroded to thick blunt stubs resembling\npetrified tree stumps.  Lichens and mosses of various colors grow along the\nwalls and floor.  Fungi of various shapes and size litter the cavern forming\nlarge groups and clusters in places.  The ceiling above lies somewhere shrouded\nin darkness.  The cavern is quite large with many places to conceal a hidden\nfoe.  The air smells musty and seems charged with danger as if you are not\nalone.  There is a tunnel leading to the southwest and an almost concealed\nalcove to the south.  The far eastern section of the cavern reveals a large\npassage that has been barricaded by tight fitting large blocks of stone\nresembling large bricks of about 100 pounds each making progress eastward\nimpossible.\n',45,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6199,1,-35,-3,'A Strange Lair','  This rather small cave or natural alcove seems to be the lair of a highly\nintelligent and organized creature.  Various strange devices of unknown origin\nor use are set here and there.  The whole southern wall is covered with an\nintricate scene depicting a community of strange humanoid beings dressed in\nmagical looking robes with even stranger looking faces.  Other artistic looking\nstatues have been built from pieces of bone which look quite intricate.\nShelves carved into the stone walls contain various useless looking tools and\nimplements.  Whomever lives here must have been here for some time.\n',45,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6200,0,-37,-2,'A Jungle Road Along a River','  You find yourself in the middle of an east-west road that runs along\nthe southern bank of a wide, slow moving river.  Actually, calling this\na road is being kind, in fact it is a packed dirt path through the jungle\nthat is only slightly better than your average game trail.  The thick\nfoliage of the numerous species of plants makes travel in any direction\nexcept along the road impossible.  To the east, you can see an intersection.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6201,-1,-37,-2,'A Jungle Road Along a River','  You find yourself in the middle of an east-west road that runs along\nthe southern bank of a wide, slow moving river.  Actually, calling this\na road is being kind, in fact it is a packed dirt path through the jungle\nthat is only slightly better than your average game trail.  The thick\nfoliage of the numerous species of plants makes travel in any direction\nexcept along the road impossible.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6202,-2,-37,-2,'A Bend in a Jungle Road Along a River','  You find yourself in the middle of a road that runs along the southern\nbank of a wide, slow moving river.  Actually, calling this a road is\nbeing kind, in fact it is a packed dirt path through the jungle that is\nonly slightly better than your average game trail.  The road makes a\nbend here, going east along the riverbank and southwest through the\njungle, away from the river.  The thick foliage of the numerous species\nof plants makes travel in any direction except along the road impossible.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6203,-3,-38,-2,'A Jungle Road','  This hard packed dirt trail through a thick tropical jungle could\nloosely be called a road, but it reminds you more of an slightly\nimproved game trail.  From the jungle around you comes the strange\ncalls of exotic birds and unseen animals, which you cannot locate in the\ndim light which filters down through the thick canopy of leaves above\nyou.  This deep in the jungle, the humidity is very high, and the heat\nis oppressive, your clothing is soaked with sweat almost instantly.\nThe road runs northeast to southwest here, and the thick foliage\nprevents movement in any direction except along the road.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6204,-4,-39,-2,'A Jungle Road','  This hard packed dirt trail through a thick tropical jungle could\nloosely be called a road, but it reminds you more of an slightly\nimproved game trail.  From the jungle around you comes the strange\ncalls of exotic birds and unseen animals, which you cannot locate in the\ndim light which filters down through the thick canopy of leaves above\nyou.  This deep in the jungle, the humidity is very high, and the heat\nis oppressive, your clothing is soaked with sweat almost instantly.\nThe road runs northeast to southwest here, and the thick foliage\nprevents movement in any direction except along the road.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6205,-5,-40,-2,'A Jungle Road','  This hard packed dirt trail through a thick tropical jungle could\nloosely be called a road, but it reminds you more of an slightly\nimproved game trail.  From the jungle around you comes the strange\ncalls of exotic birds and unseen animals, which you cannot locate in the\ndim light which filters down through the thick canopy of leaves above\nyou.  This deep in the jungle, the humidity is very high, and the heat\nis oppressive, your clothing is soaked with sweat almost instantly.\nThe road runs northeast to southwest here, and the thick foliage\nprevents movement in any direction except along the road.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6206,-6,-41,-2,'Bend in a Jungle Road','  This hard packed dirt trail through a thick tropical jungle could\nloosely be called a road, but it reminds you more of an slightly\nimproved game trail.  From the jungle around you comes the strange\ncalls of exotic birds and unseen animals, which you cannot locate in the\ndim light which filters down through the thick canopy of leaves above\nyou.  This deep in the jungle, the humidity is very high, and the heat\nis oppressive, your clothing is soaked with sweat almost instantly.\nThe road makes a curve here, heading from northeast to south, and the\nthick foliage prevents movement in any direction except along the road.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6207,-6,-42,-2,'A Road Through the Jungle','  This hard packed dirt trail through a thick tropical jungle could\nloosely be called a road, but it reminds you more of an slightly\nimproved game trail.  From the jungle around you comes the strange\ncalls of exotic birds and unseen animals, which you cannot locate in the\ndim light which filters down through the thick canopy of leaves above\nyou.  This deep in the jungle, the humidity is very high, and the heat\nis oppressive, your clothing is soaked with sweat almost instantly.\nThe road runs north to south here, and the thick foliage prevents\nmovement in any direction except along the road.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6208,-6,-43,-2,'A Road Through the Jungle','  This hard packed dirt trail through a thick tropical jungle could\nloosely be called a road, but it reminds you more of an slightly\nimproved game trail.  From the jungle around you comes the strange\ncalls of exotic birds and unseen animals, which you cannot locate in the\ndim light which filters down through the thick canopy of leaves above\nyou.  This deep in the jungle, the humidity is very high, and the heat\nis oppressive, your clothing is soaked with sweat almost instantly.\nThe road runs north to south here, and the thick foliage prevents\nmovement in any direction except along the road.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6209,-6,-44,-2,'A Winding Road Through the Jungle','  The hard packed dirt road winds through some hills here, rarely going\nstraight for any length of time.  Thick jungle vegetation presses closely\nalong both sides of the trail, preventing movement in any direction\nexcept along the trail, which runs north and southeast from here.  The\nstrange cries of exotic animal life come from all around you, and you\ncan hear things scrambling through the foliage, but you can\'t locate\nthe source of the noise.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6210,-5,-47,0,'A Winding Road Through the Jungle','  The hard packed dirt road winds through some hills here, rarely going\nstraight for any length of time.  Thick jungle vegetation presses closely\nalong both sides of the trail, preventing movement in any direction\nexcept along the trail, which runs northwest and south from here.  The\nstrange cries of exotic animal life come from all around you, and you\ncan hear things scrambling through the foliage, but you can\'t locate\nthe source of the noise.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6211,-5,-48,0,'A Winding Road Through the Jungle','  The hard packed dirt road winds through some hills here, rarely going\nstraight for any length of time.  Thick jungle vegetation presses closely\nalong both sides of the trail, preventing movement in any direction\nexcept along the trail, which runs north and southwest from here.  The\nstrange cries of exotic animal life come from all around you, and you\ncan hear things scrambling through the foliage, but you can\'t locate\nthe source of the noise.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6212,-6,-49,0,'A Winding Road Through the Jungle','  The hard packed dirt road winds through some hills here, rarely going\nstraight for any length of time.  Thick jungle vegetation presses closely\nalong both sides of the trail, preventing movement in any direction\nexcept along the trail, which runs west to northeast from here.  The\nstrange cries of exotic animal life come from all around you, and you\ncan hear things scrambling through the foliage, but you can\'t locate\nthe source of the noise.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6213,-7,-49,0,'A Winding Road Through the Jungle','  The hard packed dirt road winds through some hills here, rarely going\nstraight for any length of time.  Thick jungle vegetation presses closely\nalong both sides of the trail, preventing movement in any direction\nexcept along the trail, which runs southwest and east from here.  The\nstrange cries of exotic animal life come from all around you, and you\ncan hear things scrambling through the foliage, but you can\'t locate\nthe source of the noise.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6214,-8,-50,0,'A Winding Road Through the Jungle','  The hard packed dirt road winds through some hills here, rarely going\nstraight for any length of time.  Thick jungle vegetation presses closely\nalong both sides of the trail, preventing movement in any direction\nexcept along the trail, which runs northeast and southeast from here.\nThe strange cries of exotic animal life come from all around you, and you\ncan hear things scrambling through the foliage, but you can\'t locate\nthe source of the noise.  While looking about, you detect signs of what\nused to be a trail through the jungle to the west.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6215,-7,-51,0,'Road Along a Ridge','  This road runs northwest to southeast along the spine of a ridge\nof hills.  To either side of you the ground slopes away, revealing\nthe tops of the trees in the thick jungle surrounding you.  Far to\nthe northeast, the tops of some ruins can be seen poking above the\ntrees, to the southwest, the jungle is unbroken as far as you can\nsee.  Thick jungle growth prevents movement in any direction except\nalong the road.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6216,-6,-52,0,'Road Along a Ridge','  This road runs northwest to southeast along the spine of a ridge\nof hills.  To either side of you the ground slopes away, revealing\nthe tops of the trees in the thick jungle surrounding you.  Far to\nthe northeast, the tops of some ruins can be seen poking above the\ntrees, to the southwest, the jungle is unbroken as far as you can\nsee.  Thick jungle growth prevents movement in any direction except\nalong the road.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6217,-5,-53,0,'A Hilly Road Through the Jungle','  The road here traverses a hillside, sloping downhill to the east\nand uphill to the west.  Thick jungle vegetation crowds the road on\nboth sides, making travel in any direction except along the road\nimpossible.  The hair raises on the back of your neck as you get\nthe feeling you are being watched from the surrounding jungle, but\nin the dim light filtering down through the canopy of leaves, you\ncan\'t detect any sign of who or what it might be.  While glancing about,\nyou detect a little used trail through the jungle to the south.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6218,-4,-53,0,'A Hilly Road Through the Jungle','  The road here traverses a hillside, sloping downhill to the east\nand uphill to the west.  Thick jungle vegetation crowds the road on\nboth sides, making travel in any direction except along the road\nimpossible.  The hair raises on the back of your neck as you get\nthe feeling you are being watched from the surrounding jungle, but\nin the dim light filtering down through the canopy of leaves, you\ncan\'t detect any sign of who or what it might be.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6219,-3,-53,0,'A Hilly Road Through the Jungle','  The road here traverses a hillside, sloping downhill to the east\nand uphill to the west.  Thick jungle vegetation crowds the road on\nboth sides, making travel in any direction except along the road\nimpossible.  The hair raises on the back of your neck as you get\nthe feeling you are being watched from the surrounding jungle, but\nin the dim light filtering down through the canopy of leaves, you\ncan\'t detect any sign of who or what it might be.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6220,-2,-53,0,'Road Around a Jungle Lake','  The road runs along the shore of a small lake deep in the middle\nof the jungle at the this point.  You are standing on the western\nedge of the lake, the road continues around the lake to the northeast\nand disappears uphill into the jungle to the west.  Thick jungle\nfoliage prevent movement to the north or south.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6221,-1,-52,0,'A Road Around a Jungle Lake','  The road runs along the northern shore of a small lake deep in\nthe jungle here.  The road continues east and southwest along the\nshore of the lake.  The lake itself lies to the south, and thick\njungle blocks movement to the north and west.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6222,0,-52,0,'A Road Around a Jungle Lake','  The road runs along the northern shore of a small lake deep in the\njungle here.  The road curves along the shore, continuing to the\nwest and the southeast.  The lake itself lies to the south, and\nthick jungle prevents movement to the north and east.  An overgrown\npath leads off to the northeast.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6223,1,-53,0,'A Road Around a Jungle Lake','  You are standing on the eastern shore of a small lake deep in the\njungle.  The road you are standing on continues around the shore of\nthe lake to the northwest, and disappears into the jungle to the\nsoutheast.  Thick jungle vegetation prevents movement to the north\nand east, and the lake itself lies to the west.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6224,2,-54,0,'A Road Deep in the Jungle','  This hard packed dirt road runs northwest to southeast through the\nheart of a thick jungle.  Lush jungle growth crowds the edge of the\npath, forcing you to stay on the road.  Here far beneath the jungle\ncanopy, it is hot and humid, you can\'t help but sweat as you follow\nthe road, and the sweat draws numerous biting insects.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6225,3,-55,0,'A Road Deep in the Jungle','  This hard packed dirt road bends here, heading northwest and east\nthrough the heart of a thick jungle.  Lush jungle growth crowds the\nedge of the path, forcing you to stay on the road.  Here far beneath\nthe jungle canopy, it is hot and humid, you can\'t help but sweat as\nyou follow the road, and the sweat draws numerous biting insects.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6226,4,-55,0,'A Road Deep in the Jungle','  This hard packed dirt road bends here, heading  west and southeast\nthrough the heart of a thick jungle.  Lush jungle growth crowds the\nedge of the path, forcing you to stay on the road.  Here far beneath\nthe jungle canopy, it is hot and humid, you can\'t help but sweat as\nyou follow the road, and the sweat draws numerous biting insects.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6227,5,-56,0,'A Road Deep in the Jungle','  This hard packed dirt road runs northwest to southeast through the\nheart of a thick jungle.  Lush jungle growth crowds the edge of the\npath, forcing you to stay on the road.  Here far beneath the jungle\ncanopy, it is hot and humid, you can\'t help but sweat as you follow\nthe road, and the sweat draws numerous biting insects.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6228,6,-57,0,'A Road in the Jungle','  This hard packed dirt road bends here, heading northwest and east\nthrough the heart of a thick jungle.  Lush jungle growth crowds the\nedge of the path, forcing you to stay on the road.  Here far beneath\nthe jungle canopy, it is hot and humid, you can\'t help but sweat as\nyou follow the road, and the sweat draws numerous biting insects.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6229,7,-57,0,'A Road Along the Coast','  This hard packed dirt road runs through the thick tropical jungle\nalong the western edge of the Myrian Ocean.  To your east, through\nthe trees, the deep blue waters stretch as far as you can see toward\nthe horizon.  The road continues south along the coast, and heads\nwest, deeper into the jungle.  Thick vegetation prevents you from\ngoing any further north.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6230,7,-58,0,'A Road Along the Coast','  This hard packed dirt road runs through the thick tropical jungle\nalong the western edge of the Myrian Ocean.  To your east, through\nthe trees, the deep blue waters stretch as far as you can see toward\nthe horizon.  The road continues along the coast to the north and\nsoutheast.  Thick jungle blocks your passage south and west.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6231,8,-59,0,'A Road Along the Coast','  This hard packed dirt road runs through the thick jungle on the coast\nof the Myrian Ocean.  The deep blue waters stretch to the horizon to the\nnorth and northeast.  To the east of you, the jungle opens out onto a\nad sandy beach.  The road continues to the northeast along the shoreline\nand heads deeper into the jungle to the south.  Thick jungle lies to your\nwest, and prevents passage in that direction.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6232,8,-60,0,'A Muddy Jungle Road','  The road here is composed of a soft, gooey mud, making walking difficult.\nThe road runs to the north, where the increasing light indicates there is\na break in the thick vegetation, and into the increasing gloom to the\nsouth.  Thick jungle growth crowds the road to the east and west, forcing\nyou to remain on the road.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6233,8,-61,0,'An Intersection in the Jungle','  The road you have been following splits here.  The most frequently\nused path appears to run from the north to the southeast, but another\nslightly smaller road leads to the southwest.  Thick jungle growth\nlies all around you, and prevents travel off the road.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6234,9,-62,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Jungle','  From the state of the road, it must rain here a lot.  The normally\nhard packed dirt has turned to a gooey mud, making travel difficult.\nFrom the thick jungle around you, you can hear the cries of exotic\nbirds and strange unseen animals.  Clouds of insects buzz around your\nhead, drawn by the scent of your sweaty body.  The road continues to\nthe northwest and southeast, thick jungle blocks your path in all other\ndirections.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6235,10,-63,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Jungle','  From the state of the road, it must rain here a lot.  The normally\nhard packed dirt has turned to a gooey mud, making travel difficult.\nFrom the thick jungle around you, you can hear the cries of exotic\nbirds and strange unseen animals.  Clouds of insects buzz around your\nhead, drawn by the scent of your sweaty body.  The road continues to\nthe northwest and south, thick jungle blocks your path in all other\ndirections.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6236,10,-64,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Jungle','  From the state of the road, it must rain here a lot.  The normally\nhard packed dirt has turned to a gooey mud, making travel difficult.\nFrom the thick jungle around you, you can hear the cries of exotic\nbirds and strange unseen animals.  Clouds of insects buzz around your\nhead, drawn by the scent of your sweaty body.  The road continues into\nthe jungle to the north, and opens into a small clearing to the\nsoutheast.  Thick jungle blocks your path in all other directions.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6237,11,-65,0,'A Clearing in the Jungle','  You are in the western end of a small oval clearing deep in the jungle.\nFor one of the few times since entering the jungle, you can actually\nsee the sky above you, instead of an unbroken canopy of leaves.  Tall,\nthick grasses covers the floor of the clearing, just about anything\ncould be hiding in them.  The road heads into the jungle to the northwest\nand continues across the clearing to the east.  A small trail leads out\nof the clearing to the south.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6238,12,-65,0,'A Clearing in the Jungle','  You are in the eastern end of a small oval clearing deep in the jungle.\nFor one of the few times since entering the jungle, you can actually\nsee the sky above you, instead of an unbroken canopy of leaves.  Tall,\nthick grasses covers the floor of the clearing, just about anything\ncould be hiding in them.  The road heads into the jungle to the southeast\nand continues across the clearing to the west.  A trail leads out of the\nclearing to the northeast.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6239,13,-66,0,'On a Jungle Road','  This hard packed dirt road runs through some of the thickest tropical\njungle you have ever seen.  Lush green vegetation of all varieties\ncrowds both sides of the road, if someone didn\'t maintain this road\nregularly, it would probably be overgrown in less than a month.  Wildlife\nscurries through the underbrush, just out of your view, but you know\nit\'s there even if you can\'t see it.  The road heads into a clearing to\nthe northwest, and continues into the jungle to the east.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6240,14,-66,0,'On a Jungle Road','  This hard packed dirt road runs through some of the thickest tropical\njungle you have ever seen.  Lush green vegetation of all varieties\ncrowds both sides of the road, if someone didn\'t maintain this road\nregularly, it would probably be overgrown in less than a month.  Wildlife\nscurries through the underbrush, just out of your view, but you know\nit\'s there even if you can\'t see it.  The road continues into the jungle\nto the east and west.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6241,15,-66,0,'On a Jungle Road','  This hard packed dirt road runs through some of the thickest tropical\njungle you have ever seen.  Lush green vegetation of all varieties\ncrowds both sides of the road, if someone didn\'t maintain this road\nregularly, it would probably be overgrown in less than a month.  Wildlife\nscurries through the underbrush, just out of your view, but you know\nit\'s there even if you can\'t see it.  The road continues into the jungle\nto the west and southeast.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6242,16,-67,0,'On a Jungle Road','  This hard packed dirt road runs through some of the thickest tropical\njungle you have ever seen.  Lush green vegetation of all varieties\ncrowds both sides of the road, if someone didn\'t maintain this road\nregularly, it would probably be overgrown in less than a month.  Wildlife\nscurries through the underbrush, just out of your view, but you know\nit\'s there even if you can\'t see it.  The road continues into the jungle\nto the east and northwest.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6243,17,-67,0,'On a Jungle Road','  This hard packed dirt road runs through some of the thickest tropical\njungle you have ever seen.  Lush green vegetation of all varieties\ncrowds both sides of the road, if someone didn\'t maintain this road\nregularly, it would probably be overgrown in less than a month.  Wildlife\nscurries through the underbrush, just out of your view, but you know\nit\'s there even if you can\'t see it.  The road continues into the jungle\nto the east and west.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6244,18,-67,0,'On the Coast','  You are at the end of a hard packed dirt road leading through some\nthick jungle.  The road disappears into the jungle to the west, and to\nthe southeast lie the waters of the Myrian Ocean.  Thick jungle surrounds\nthis slight break in the foliage, your only real choices are to follow\nthe road, or brave the unknown waters before you.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6245,7,-62,0,'A Narrow Road Through the Jungle','  Barely 12 feet wide, this road runs northeast-southwest through the\nthickest part of the jungle.  Green jungle plants of all types, from\nthe tallest trees to waist high plants, thrive in this part of the jungle.\nBirds can be seen flying through the trees in search of insects to eat,\nand larger animals can be heard crashing through the brush, although\nyou can\'t see them due to the density of the foliage.  Passage in any\ndirection except along the road is impossible.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6246,6,-63,0,'A Narrow Road Through the Jungle','  Barely 12 feet wide, this road runs northeast-southwest through the\nthickest part of the jungle.  Green jungle plants of all types, from\nthe tallest trees to waist high plants, thrive in this part of the jungle.\nBirds can be seen flying through the trees in search of insects to eat,\nand larger animals can be heard crashing through the brush, although\nyou can\'t see them due to the density of the foliage.  Passage in any\ndirection except along the road is impossible.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6247,5,-64,0,'A Narrow Road Through the Jungle','  Barely 12 feet wide, this road runs northeast-southwest through the\nthickest part of the jungle.  Green jungle plants of all types, from\nthe tallest trees to waist high plants, thrive in this part of the jungle.\nBirds can be seen flying through the trees in search of insects to eat,\nand larger animals can be heard crashing through the brush, although\nyou can\'t see them due to the density of the foliage.  Passage in any\ndirection except along the road is impossible.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6248,4,-65,0,'Road Through a Jungle Valley','  The hard packed dirt road follows the bottom of a valley through a\nrange of low hills, which grow higher to the south and east, and flatten\nout and disappear to the northeast.  The sides of the hills are covered\nin thick jungle growth, climbing them would be a daunting task.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6249,3,-65,0,'Road Through a Jungle Valley','  The hard packed dirt road follows the bottom of a valley through a\nrange of low hills, which grow higher to the south and east, and flatten\nout gradually to the north and east.  The sides of the hills are covered\nwith thick jungle vegetation, making climbing them a daunting task.\nThe road winds along, following the lowest point in the valley, leading\neast and southwest from here.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6250,2,-66,0,'Road Through a Jungle Valley','  The hard packed dirt road follows the bottom of a valley through a\nrange of low hills, which grow higher to the south and east, and flatten\nout gradually to the north and east.  The sides of the hills are covered\nwith thick jungle vegetation, making climbing them a daunting task.\nThe road winds along, following the lowest point in the valley, leading\nsouth and northeast from here.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6251,2,-67,0,'Road Through a Jungle Valley','  The hard packed dirt road follows the bottom of a valley through a\nrange of high hills, which gradually flatten out to the north and east.\nThe sides of the hills are covered with thick jungle vegetation, making\nclimbing them a daunting task.  The road winds along, following the\nlowest point in the valley, leading north and south from here.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6252,2,-68,0,'Road Through a Jungle Valley','  The hard packed dirt road follows the bottom of a valley through a\nrange of high hills, which gradually flatten out to the north and east.\nThe sides of the hills are covered with thick jungle vegetation, making\nclimbing them a daunting task.  The road winds along, following the\nlowest point in the valley, leading north and southwest from here.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6253,1,-69,0,'Road Through a Jungle Valley','  The hard packed dirt road follows the bottom of a valley through a\nrange of high hills, which stretch as far as you can see in all directions.\nThe sides of the hills are covered with thick jungle vegetation, making\nclimbing them a daunting task.  The road winds along, following the\nlowest point in the valley, leading northeast and southwest from here.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6254,0,-70,0,'Road Through a Jungle Valley','  The hard packed dirt road follows the bottom of a valley through a\nrange of high hills, which stretch as far as you can see in all directions.\nThe sides of the hills are covered with thick jungle vegetation, making\nclimbing them a daunting task.  The road winds along, following the\nlowest point in the valley, leading west and northeast from here.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6255,-1,-70,0,'Road Through a Jungle Valley','  The hard packed dirt road follows the bottom of a valley through a\nrange of high hills, which stretch as far as you can see in all directions.\nThe sides of the hills are covered with thick jungle vegetation, making\nclimbing them a daunting task.  The road winds along, following the\nlowest point in the valley, leading east and southwest from here.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6256,-2,-71,0,'Road Through a Jungle Valley','  The hard packed dirt road follows the bottom of a valley through a\nrange of high hills, which stretch as far as you can see in all directions.\nThe sides of the hills are covered with thick jungle vegetation, making\nclimbing them a daunting task.  The road winds along, following the\nlowest point in the valley, leading northeast and southwest from here.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6257,-3,-72,0,'Road Through a Jungle Valley','  The hard packed dirt road follows the bottom of a valley through a\nrange of high hills, which stretch as far as you can see in all directions.\nThe sides of the hills are covered with thick jungle vegetation, making\nclimbing them a daunting task.  The road winds along, following the\nlowest point in the valley, leading west and northeast from here.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6258,-4,-72,0,'Road Through a Jungle Valley','  The hard packed dirt road follows the bottom of a valley through a\nrange of high hills, which stretch as far as you can see in all directions.\nThe sides of the hills are covered with thick jungle vegetation, making\nclimbing them a daunting task.  The road winds along, following the\nlowest point in the valley, leading east and southwest from here.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6259,-5,-73,0,'Road Through a Jungle Valley','  The hard packed dirt road follows the bottom of a valley through a\nrange of high hills, which stretch as far as you can see in all directions.\nThe sides of the hills are covered with thick jungle vegetation, making\nclimbing them a daunting task.  The road winds along, following the\nlowest point in the valley, leading northeast into the jungle, and\nsouthwest, where it opens into a clearing.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6260,-6,-74,0,'A Large Clearing in the Jungle','  You are on the northern edge of a large, roughly circular clearing deep\nwithin the jungle.  High hills ring this clearing, which sits at the bottom\nof a bowl formed by the hills.  Why this clearing is devoid of vegetation,\nwhen the surrounding jungle is so lush and thick is something of a mystery.\nA road leads off into the jungle to the northeast, and the clearing\ncontinues to the south.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6261,-7,-75,0,'A Large Clearing in the Jungle','  You are on the western edge of a large, roughly circular clearing deep\nwithin the jungle.  High hills ring this clearing, which sits at the bottom\nof a bowl formed by the hills.  Why this clearing is devoid of vegetation,\nwhen the surrounding jungle is so lush and thick is something of a mystery.\nThe clearing continues to the east.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6262,-6,-75,0,'Center of a Jungle Clearing','  You are at the center of a large, roughly circular clearing deep within\nthe jungle.  High hills ring this clearing, which sits at the bottom of a\nbowl formed by the hills.  Why this clearing is devoid of vegetation, when\nthe surrounding jungle is so lush and thick is something of a mystery.\nThe clearing continues to the north, south, east and west.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6263,-5,-75,0,'A Large Clearing in the Jungle','  You are on the eastern edge of a large, roughly circular clearing deep\nwithin the jungle.  High hills ring this clearing, which sits at the bottom\nof a bowl formed by the hills.  Why this clearing is devoid of vegetation,\nwhen the surrounding jungle is so lush and thick is something of a mystery.\nThe clearing continues to the west.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6264,-6,-76,0,'A Large Clearing in the Jungle','  You are on the southern edge of a large, roughly circular clearing deep\nwithin the jungle.  High hills ring this clearing, which sits at the bottom\nof a bowl formed by the hills.  Why this clearing is devoid of vegetation,\nwhen the surrounding jungle is so lush and thick is something of a mystery.\nThe clearing continues to the north.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6280,-9,-50,0,'A Faint Trail Through the Jungle','  This faint trail has been pretty much overgrown by the jungle.  The\nway west is completely overgrown, and you can\'t force your way through\nit any further.  To your east you see the main jungle road.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6281,-5,-54,0,'A Little Used Trail Through the Jungle','  This little used trail has seen better days.  Plant life encroaches\nfrom all sides, and roots and vines on the trail itself occasionally\ncause you to trip.  The trail seems to lead vaguely south, and to the\nnorth you see the main road through the jungle.  Passage east and west\nis blocked by the thick jungle around you.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6282,-5,-55,0,'A Little Used Trail Through the Jungle','  This little used trail has seen better days.  Plant life encroaches\nfrom all sides, and roots and vines on the trail itself occasionally\ncause you to trip.  The trail seems to lead vaguely north and southwest.\nPassage east and west is blocked by the thick jungle around you.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6283,-6,-56,0,'A Little Used Trail Through the Jungle','  You have come to what appears to be the end of the trail.  The thick\njungle is unbroken in every direction, except back along the trail to\nthe northeast, from whence you came.  Standing here, you get the feeling\nyou are being watched, but you can detect no signs of life around you.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6284,1,-51,0,'An Overgrown Jungle Path','  At one time this must have been a much used path from the lake which\nyou can see through the trees to the southwest to somewhere unknown\ndeeper in the jungle.  Now however it is so overgrown only this short\nstretch still remains.  The thick jungle blocks travel in all directions\nexcept back to the southwest.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6285,11,-66,0,'A Small Trail in the Jungle','  Whether this small trail was created by animals or by intelligent\nbeings, you can\'t determine.  It is fairly narrow, less than 6 feet wide,\nforcing you to proceed single file.  The trail leads from a clearing to\nthe north further into the jungle to the south.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6286,11,-67,0,'A Small Trail in the Jungle','  Whether this small trail was created by animals or by intelligent\nbeings, you can\'t determine.  It is fairly narrow, less than 6 feet wide,\nforcing you to proceed single file.  The trail comes to an end here, the\nway further south is blocked by a fallen tree.  The trail leads back to\nthe north.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6287,13,-64,0,'A Narrow Trail in the Jungle','  This narrow trail leads from a clearing to the southwest deeper into\njungle to the northeast.  The trail is very narrow, and you find that\nyou can\'t force your way any further northeast, the only way out is to\nretreat the way you came.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6288,0,0,0,'A Winding Road Through the Jungle','  The hard packed dirt road winds through some hills here, rarely going\nstraight for any length of time.  Thick jungle vegetation presses closely\nalong both sides of the trail, preventing movement in any direction\nexcept along the trail, which runs north and southeast from here.  The\nstrange cries of exotic animal life come from all around you, and you\ncan hear things scrambling through the foliage, but you can\'t locate\nthe source of the noise.\n',41,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6300,0,0,0,'Just Below The Surface','The <y>ocean floor<1> is littered with<g> garbage<1> and <k>waste,<1> all\ndiscarded from the nearby city. Several <W>humanoid bones litter the <y>sea\nfloor<1>, <b>drifting slowly with the current.<1>  <y>The coral reef is teeming\nwith sea life, as <r>thousands<1> of <p>colorful<1> and <c>tiny fish<1>\ndart about the <y>reef<1>.  The <g>thick kelp bed<1> is an excellent hiding\nplace for predators.\n',0,140608,53,0,0,0,0,0,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6301,0,0,0,'<B>Shallow Water Near the Harbor<1>','The unnatural presence of the city harbor and the shipping traffic have created\na swirling vortex of water that surges and ebbs with alarming regularity.  A\nlarge <y>wooden sign<1>, covered with <W>salt <c>crystals<1>, hangs magically in\nthe air.  A shiny object sparkles on the ocean floor momentarily before quickly\nvanishing.\n',0,139584,28,0,0,0,9,2,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6302,0,0,0,'Shallow Water Near the Harbor','The shipping traffic, currents, and unnatural shore break have rendered\nthe water murky and dirty.  Visibility under the water is limited to\napproximately ten feet.  There is a steady flow of shipping traffic\nhere, making this a very dangerous place to swim.\n',0,139584,51,0,0,0,100,1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6303,0,0,0,'<B>Shallow Water<1>','The shipping traffic, currents, and unnatural shore break have rendered the\nwater murky and dirty.  Visibility under the water is limited to approximately\nten feet.  There is a steady flow of shipping traffic here, making this a very\ndangerous place to swim.\n',0,139584,28,0,0,0,12,1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6304,0,0,0,'<B>Shallow Water<1>','The shipping traffic, currents, and unnatural shore break have rendered\nthe water murky and dirty.  Visibility under the water is limited to\napproximately ten feet.  There is a constant flow of shipping traffic\nhere, making this a very dangerous place to swim.\n',0,139584,28,0,0,0,9,8,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6305,0,0,0,'<B>Just Offshore<1>','The shipping traffic, currents, and unnatural shore break have rendered the\nwater murky and dirty.  Visibility under the water is limited to approximately\nten feet.  There is a steady flow of shipping traffic here, making this a very\ndangerous place to swim.\n',0,139584,28,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6306,0,0,0,'<B>Just Offshore<1>','The shipping traffic, currents, and unnatural shore break have rendered the\nwater murky and dirty.  Visibility under the water is limited to approximately\nten feet.  There is a steady flow of shipping traffic here, making this a very\ndangerous place to swim.\n',0,139584,28,0,0,0,11,1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6307,0,0,0,'Base of the Lighthouse','This cement lighthouse has been pounded by rough surf and inclement weather\nover the years.  A thin layer of salt, generated by years of sea spray and\nwhipping winds, leaves everything with a crusty and abrasive feel.  Many\nsailors have used this tiny beacon, while trapped in churning seas and storms,\nto safely return to port.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(6308,0,0,0,'Top of the Lighthouse','  The lighthouse is powered by a large <r>roaring fire<1> and dozens of angled\nmirrors that are used to reflect the light out to <b>sea<1>.  Surprisingly the\nfire does not give off any heat and glows with a <W>brilliant white light<1>. \nThe glass roof of the lighthouse allows the <o>sun<1> to power the lighthouse\nbeam during the <y>day<1>. \n',0,8512,22,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6309,0,0,0,'Just off the Pier','  Due to the recently constructed pier nearby, the water currents here are \nnearly nonexistent.  The ocean floor below is covered with sediment \nand garbage that collects near the pier.  \n',0,139584,28,0,0,0,4,7,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6310,0,0,0,'Captain\'s Quarters','  This lavishly decorated and poshly furnished room is out of place on this\ndecrepit schooner.  Large canvas paintings cover the walls, while a map of the\nocean is spread across a desk.  On both sides of the room, round portholes, \nwhich have been recently cleaned, offer a view of the sea.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,150,0,'',NULL),
(6311,0,0,0,'Southern Docking Berth','  Presently, this shipping berth is vacant.  During the busier seasons, when\nthe fishing boats are thriving, boats will line up two to three at a time to\nunload their cargo.  Due to the inactivity, the pier has been scrubbed and\npolished, and all of the grime, salt, and unused fish parts that often\nclutter the pier have been discarded.\n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,25,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6312,0,0,0,'<B>Turbulent Water<1>','  The shipping traffic, currents, and unnatural shore break have rendered \nthe water murky and dirty.  Visibility under the water is limited to \napproximately ten feet.  There is a constant flow of shipping traffic \nhere, making this a very dangerous place to swim.  \n',0,139584,28,0,0,0,1,2,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6313,0,0,0,'<B>Near the Harbor<1>','  Due to the recently constructed pier nearby, the water currents here are\nnearly nonexistent.  The ocean floor below is covered with sediment\nand garbage that collects near the pier.  The keel of a capsized boat is jutting\n\nout of the water.\n',0,139584,28,0,0,0,8,1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6314,0,0,0,'Before a Large Lighthouse','  The narrow road ends abruptly before a well kept lighthouse.  The \nlighthouse rises up above the rocky shoals, but is occasionally sprayed by \nwaves.  The windows and outer walls are constantly covered with salt and \nother mineral deposits, causing the lighthouse to sparkle and refract light.  \nThe lighthouse  acts as a beacon for ships out at sea.  \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,25,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6315,0,0,0,'Northern Docking Berth','Presently, this shipping berth is vacant.  During the busier seasons, when\nthe fishing trade is thriving, boats will line up two to three at a time to\nunload their cargo.  Due to the inactivity, the pier has been scrubbed and\npolished, and all of the grime, salt, and unused fish parts that normally\nclutter the pier have been discarded.\n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,25,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6316,0,0,0,'West End of the Pier','  This is western end of the harbor.  Shipping berths are to the north, south \nand west.  During the busier seasons ships will line up to unload their \ncargo.  Presently however, business has been slow and ships are venturing \ndeeper into the Myrian Ocean to catch their fish.  Usually the harbor \nmaster can be found here, pacing about nervously as he waits for ships \nto return to port. \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6317,0,0,0,'Aboard a Schooner','The rickety and weather beaten wooden planks creak and groan as the ship\nbobs up and down with the current.  A sticky black tar has been sloshed over\nthe planks to protect them from the elements.  Tall masts rise above\nthe deck of the ship, with tattered and torn sails that flap in the wind.\n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,25,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6318,0,0,0,'<B>Shallow Water South of the Pier<1>','  The shipping traffic, currents, and unnatural shore break have rendered \nthe water murky and dirty.  Visibility under the water is limited to \napproximately ten feet.  There is a constant flow of shipping traffic \nhere, making this a very dangerous place to swim.  \n',0,139584,28,0,0,0,11,1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6319,0,0,0,'Narrow Dirt Path','  A narrow and treacherous dirt path, cut into the side of a rocky cliff, \nleads to the harbor\'s solitary lighthouse.  The path has been cut into \na rocky and densely vegetated hillside.  Far below the waves are \npounding into the side of the cliff.  \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,25,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6320,0,0,0,'Shallow Tide Pool','  The receding tide has left a small pool of water behind that is teeming with \nsea life.  Small urchins, starfish and crabs line the rock crevices.  Tiny fish \ndart in and out of the crevices searching for food.  The rocks are slick with \nalgae, rendering it difficult to traverse the pool.  \n',0,139584,31,0,0,0,0,0,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6321,0,0,0,'Along the Pier','  The Xanesla pier is well kept and in fine condition, as the \nshipping industry is the heart of the city\'s economy.  Although\nbusiness has been slow of late, the pier is maintained\nin perfect condition.  The wooden planks are constantly \npolished and coated with a sticky substance that prevents\nthem from decaying in the sea air. \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6322,0,0,0,'Storage Room','Large white sheets have been placed over old and decaying furniture.  The\nsheets are covered with dust and billow up and swirl around from the breeze\ncoming in through an open window.  The room smells of mildew and\nsea air.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6323,0,0,0,'<B>Shallow Water Near the Coast<1>','  Due to the recently constructed pier nearby, the water currents here are \nnearly nonexistent.  The ocean floor below is covered with sediment \nand garbage that collects near the pier.  \n',0,139584,28,0,0,0,6,1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6324,0,0,0,'<B>Near the Shore<1>','  The shipping traffic, currents, and unnatural shore break have rendered \nthe water murky and dirty.  Visibility under the water is limited to \napproximately ten feet.  There is a constant flow of shipping traffic \nhere, making this a very dangerous place to swim.  \n',0,139584,28,0,0,0,4,1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6325,0,0,0,'Narrow Dirt Path','  A narrow and treacherous dirt path, cut into the side of a rocky cliff, \nleads to the harbor\'s solitary lighthouse.  The path has been cut into \na rocky and densely vegetated hillside.  Far below the waves are \npounding into the side of the cliff.  \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6326,0,0,0,'Shallow Tide Pool','  The receding tide has left a small pool of water behind that is teeming with\n<b>sea<1> life.  Small <k>urchins<1>, <o>starfish<1> and <R>crabs<1> populate\nthe rock crevices.  Tiny fish\ndart in and out of the crevices searching for food.  The rocks are slick with\n<g>algae<1>, making traversing the pool treacherous.\n',0,139584,31,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6327,0,0,0,'Along the Pier','  The Xanesla pier is well kept and in fine condition, as the \nshipping industry is the heart of the city\'s economy.  Although\nbusiness has been slow of late, the pier is maintained\nin perfect condition.  The wooden planks are constantly \npolished and coated with a sticky substance that prevents\nthem from decaying in the sea air. \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6328,0,0,0,'Cluttered Office','  This office is full of stray papers, charts, maps and graphs.  \nA cluttered desk is almost completely buried under an \navalanche of paper.  The clutter is so thick and complete, \nthat it is impossible to determine where the clutter ends and \nthe floor or furniture begins.  \n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6329,0,0,0,'<B>Just Offshore<1>','  The ocean water is surging toward the coast here, peaking \nin a set of large waves.  A rather strong undertow swirls \njust below the surface, mucking up the sediment.  Tiny fish \ncan be seen surging with the current, looking for a meal.  \n',0,139584,28,0,0,0,1,1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6330,0,0,0,'<B>Near the Shore<1>','  The ocean water is surging toward the coast here, peaking \nin a set of large waves.  A rather strong undertow swirls \njust below the surface, mucking up the sediment.  Tiny fish \ncan be seen surging with the current, looking for a meal.  \n',0,139584,28,0,0,0,2,0,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6331,0,0,0,'Narrow Dirt Path','  A narrow and treacherous dirt path, cut into the side of a rocky cliff, \nleads to the harbor\'s solitary lighthouse.  The path has been cut into \na rocky and densely vegetated hillside.  Far below the waves are \npounding into the side of the cliff.  \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6332,0,0,0,'Start of the Pier','  The pier is the hub of Xanesla\'s fishing industry. \nCrafted from sturdy oak planks and large \npillars secured into the ocean floor, the pier \nappears able to withstand the most violent of \nsea storms.  \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6333,0,0,0,'<B>Next to the Shore<1>','  The ocean water is surging toward the coast here, peaking \nin a set of large waves.  A rather strong undertow swirls \njust below the surface, mucking up the sediment.  Tiny fish \ncan be seen surging with the current, looking for a meal.  \n',0,139584,28,0,0,0,2,6,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6334,0,0,0,'Stench Filled Lagoon','  A small inlet from the ocean has created a stench filled bog \nthat collects garbage and has become a breeding ground for \nbacteria, algae and filth.  The water here is stagnant and \nacts as a breeding ground for massive mosquitoes.  \n',0,139584,27,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6335,0,0,0,'Stench Filled Lagoon','  A small inlet from the ocean has created a stench filled bog \nthat collects garbage and has become a breeding ground for\nbacteria, algae and filth.  The water here is stagnant and \nacts as a breeding ground for massive mosquitoes. \n',0,139584,27,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6336,0,0,0,'<g>Stench Filled Lagoon<1>','  A small inlet from the ocean has created a stench filled bog \nthat collects garbage and has become a breeding ground for\nbacteria, algae and filth.  The lagoon is perpetually \ngrowing, due to the conservationists\' adamant refusal to \ninterfere with nature.    \n',0,139584,27,0,0,0,1,6,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6337,0,0,0,'Camino del Sur','  This well traveled path is the main road running from Xanesla \nproper to the pier.  The constant use and heavy industrial \ntraffic have rendered the road decayed and riddled with pot \nmarks.  Because of the extensive use of the road, and the \nlack of alternative routes, the city is unable to \ncoordinate a repair schedule.  \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6338,0,0,0,'Stench Filled Lagoon','  A small inlet from the ocean has created a stench filled bog\nthat collects garbage and has become a breeding ground for\nbacteria, algae and filth.  On hot summer days the odor\nemanating from the lagoon carries downwind for miles.\n',0,139584,27,0,0,0,0,-1,15,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6339,0,0,0,'Center of the Lagoon','  The lagoon water here is pitch black and soupy.  Steam rises \nfrom the water and air bubbles are burping to the surface.  The \nfoul diseased filled water prevents anything from growing here, \nbeyond bacteria and a slimy black algae.  \n',0,172352,28,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6340,0,0,0,'Lagoon Floor','  The dark and murky water is obscured by churning \nsediment that swirls about the lagoon floor.  Thick tangles \nof weeds sway slowly with the current, as small serpents \ndart skittishly along the floor.  A large molted snake skin \nlies on the floor.  \n',0,132160,53,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6341,0,0,0,'Stench Filled Lagoon','  The murky and putrid water of the lagoon burps and froths with \nfoam, as rancid gas bursts to the surface from below.  Large \nreeds somehow manage to grow, spouting several yards above \nthe surface of the water.  \n',0,139584,27,0,0,0,0,-1,25,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6342,0,0,0,'Stench Filled Lagoon','  The lagoon here is drying up, leaving a shallow film of \nmurky water covering a rancid black mud.  Wilted weeds, \nwhich are slowly dying, are bent over and pointing toward \nthe ground.  \n',0,139584,27,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6343,0,0,0,'Stench Filled Lagoon','  The lagoon water here is pitch black and soupy.  Steam rises \nfrom the water and air bubbles are burping to the surface.  The \nfoul diseased filled water prevents anything from growing here, \nbeyond bacteria and a slimy black algae.  \n',0,139584,27,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6344,0,0,0,'Stench Filled Lagoon','  The murky and putrid water of the lagoon burps and froths \nwith foam, as rancid gas bursts to the surface from below.  \nLarge reeds somehow manage to grow, spouting several yards \nabove the surface of the water.  \n',0,139584,27,0,0,0,0,-1,9,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6345,0,0,0,'Swampy Path','  A narrow artificial path has been plowed through the weeds.\nHowever, the path appears to not have been used lately, as\nthe weeds are reclaiming the path.  The putrid smell of the\nlagoon wafts in with the ocean breeze.\n',0,139584,27,0,0,0,0,-1,26,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6346,0,0,0,'Outside a Small Cave','  The wide game trail leads directly into an ominously dark \ncave, from which a rancid smell is emanating.  A large \nassortment of bones have been strewn about the cave \nentrance, all of them having been picked clean.  Torn \nclothing and broken weapons lie scattered about.  A crude \nsign has been staked into the ground.    \n',0,139584,27,0,0,0,0,-1,25,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6347,0,0,0,'Cave Entrance','The entrance to this cave is cluttered with rotting carcasses and splintered\nbones.  The rancid smell of rotting flesh hangs in the air.  Large footprints\nriddle the cave floor, which is buzzing with flies and covered with writhing\nmaggots.\n',0,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6348,0,0,0,'Natural Cave','The wind howls around the corner of this cluttered cave, causing the gorged\nflies to tumble about unsteadily.  Large piles of trash and debris are scattered\nabout, cultivating molds and fungi.  A slick green film covers the floor, and\nthe air is thick with a powdery green haze.  A large pile of kindling has been\nstacked up against the southern wall.\n',0,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6349,0,0,0,'Natural Cave','The wind howls around the corners of this cluttered cave, steadily disturbing the\nnumerous piles of trash that have been carefully organized throughout the cave. \nA slick green powder coats everything it the cave, billowing and swirling in the\nbreeze.  Dozens of twitching flies thrash violently, struggling to get the\npowder off their delicate wings.\n',0,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6350,0,0,0,'Large Chamber','  The cave opens up into a massive circular chamber, with \nlarge stalactites, riddled with mineral deposits, which sparkle \nand shine.  Large amounts of weeds, leaves and shredded \nclothing have been pushed together to form a crude bed.  \nThe half eaten remains of various animals lie scattered \nabout the cave.  \n',0,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(6351,0,0,0,'Northern Lookout Post','  This lookout tower stands high above the front wall of \nXanesla.  From this vantage point, the guards are \nable to keep an eye on the harbor, the bay and the \nlagoon, vigilantly acting as an early warning sign \nfor any trouble.  The wall stands about twenty \nfeet high and is made of solid stone.  It would \ntake a tremendous force to even dent it.\n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,25,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6352,0,0,0,'Embarcadero Street','  <r>The red cobblestones<1> of this main thoroughfare have \nbeen recently repaired, adding an old town flavor to the \ntrendy street.  A large stone wall towers up twenty feet \nabove, providing the city with a formidable defense.  To the \neast a newly built jail has been constructed.  \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6353,0,0,0,'Embarcadero Street','  This main north south street has been paved with shiny new\n<r>red cobblestones<1>, making it difficult to run quickly across \nthe street.  A stone wall towers high above, protecting the city from\na sea invasion.  Something has been scratched into the street. \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6354,0,0,0,'Embarcadero Street','  This main north south street has been paved with shiny new \n<r>red cobblestones<1>, making it difficult to undulate  across the \nstreet.  A stone wall towers high above, protecting Xanesla from an \nunwelcome invasion.  Something has been scratched into the street.\n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6355,0,0,0,'Embarcadero Street','  <r>The red cobblestones<1> of this main thoroughfare have \nbeen recently repaired, adding an old town flavor to the \ntrendy street.  A large stone wall towers up twenty feet \nabove, providing the city with a formidable defense.  To the \neast is the Xanesla courthouse.  \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6356,0,0,0,'Embarcadero Street','  The is the main intersection for Xanesla\'s sea related traffic. \nTo the northwest Camino del Sur heads back toward the pier.\nTo the east is the foreign embassy where all foreigners are required to \nregister.  The <r>red cobblestone<1> street has been inset with <W>bright\nwhite stones.<1>\n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6357,0,0,0,'Embarcadero Street','  The southern end of Embarcadero Street is the posh and snotty \npart of Xanesla.  These wall front cottages cost ten times what \nthey are worth, and are inhabited by the richest of the Xanesla \ncitizens.  The <r>red cobblestones<1> that mark the northern end of\nthe street have been replaced with a smooth and polished white marble,\nthat doesn\'t get too hot under the summer sun.  \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6358,0,0,0,'Del Playa Road and Embarcadero','  The southern end of Embarcadero Streets Meets Del Playa here, \nresulting in a conflict between the those heading toward the \nbeach and the residents of Embarcadero who are appalled at the \nriffraff that passes through their neighborhood.  Towering \nabove, the sea wall acts as both a defense against invaders and \nnature.  \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6359,0,0,0,'South Embarcadero Street','  The southern end of Embarcadero Street is the posh and snotty \npart of Xanesla.  These wall front cottages cost ten times what they\nare worth, and are inhabited by the richest of the Xanesla citizens.  \nThe <r>red cobblestones<1> that mark the northern end of the \nstreet have been replaced with a smooth and polished white marble,\nthat doesn\'t get too hot under the summer sun.  \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6360,0,0,0,'South Embarcadero Street','  The southern end of Embarcadero Street is the posh and snotty \npart of Xanesla.  These wall front cottages cost ten times what they \nare worth, and are inhabited by the richest of the Xanesla citizens.\nThe sea wall towers high above, blocking the ocean view. \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6361,0,0,0,'South Embarcadero Street','  This is the expensive and snobby part of Xanesla.  This \nstreet once offered its residents a beautiful ocean view.  \nHowever, after the aquatic elf invasions and several devastating\ntsunamis, the towering wall was erected, ruining the view.\n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6362,0,0,0,'South Embarcadero Street','  The southern end of Embarcadero Street is the posh and snotty \npart of Xanesla.  The sea wall towers high above, blocking the \nocean view.  To the east is a museum on the history of Xanesla.    \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6363,0,0,0,'South Embarcadero Street','  This is the expensive and snobby part of Xanesla.  This \nstreet once offered its residents a beautiful ocean view.  \nHowever, after the aquatic elf invasions and several devastating\ntsunamis, the towering wall was erected.  \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6364,0,0,0,'South Embarcadero Street','  The southern end of Embarcadero street ends abruptly as the large\nwall turns to circle the city.  A manhole has been left open by which\nthe city sewers can be accessed.  To the east the University has set up a\nmarine laboratory, which is open to the public.\n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6365,0,0,0,'Southern Lookout Post','  This lookout tower stands high above the front wall of  Xanesla.  \nFrom this vantage point, the guards are able to keep an eye on the \nharbor and the bay, vigilantly acting as an early warning sign for \nany trouble.  The wall stands about twenty feet high and is made of \nsolid stone.  It would take a tremendous force to even dent it.\n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,25,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6366,0,0,0,'Newly Built Jail','  Recently constructed to hold troublemakers, aquatic elves, and \nother hooligans, this jail is the state of the art complex when it \ncomes to punishing criminals.  Unlike the Tsirin, this complex \nlacks any kind of trappings designed to make the prisoners\nmore comfortable.  \n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(6367,0,0,0,'Cramped Cell','  This small five by ten cell is barely large enough for one person to \nstay in, let alone the several that are often housed here at once.  The \ncell is completely devoid of any furniture, except for a flea infested \nstraw mattress that is lying in the far corner.  \n',0,172488,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(6368,0,0,0,'Juror Waiting Room','  Lavishly furnished with plush couches, this room was built to \nkeep jurors in comfort while they await being called for a trial.\nA small window allows a nice sea breeze to circulate the air in \nthe room.  \n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(6369,0,0,0,'Courthouse Entrance','  Impressively built out of solid marble, this Courthouse was \nintended to strike awe and fear into all litigants.  A massive \nmarble statue dominates the room.  During the day, the hustle \nand bustle of attorneys and clients scurrying about is inspiring.  \n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(6370,0,0,0,'Foreign Embassy','  A well furnished and lavish building, all foreign visitors are required \nto check into the foreign embassy within twenty-four hours of arriving \nin Xanesla.  A high vaulted ceiling above has banners of \nall the cities hanging down from above.   \n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6371,0,0,0,'Foreign Embassy','  This room is very bland and nondescript.  There is nothing \nthat stands out at all.  In fact, except for a single solitary torch \nthere is nothing else here.  \n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6372,0,0,0,'Del Playa Road','  A simple dirt  road runs east and west through Xanesla.  The \nroad is littered with trash, debris and a burnt couch.  \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6373,0,0,0,'Quaint Cottage','  Tastefully decorated and furnished, this cottage has a nice summery \nfeel to it.  A small flowered carpet sits on the floor, and quaint \nfurniture has been carefully placed.  Unfortunately the towering city \nwall blocks what was once a pristine ocean view.  \n',0,139592,22,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6374,0,0,0,'Small Beachfront Cottage','  <r>Gar<p>ish<b>ly <g>dec<y>ora<o>ted with <R>horrid <C>pastel<1> colors and\ntrendy\nfurniture, this place reeks of a single male owner.  It really\ncould use a make over.  A small glowing sign hangs on the north wall.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6375,0,0,0,'Private Dance Area','  <k>Black leather couches<1> adorn this poorly lit room.  The floor and\nfurniture are covered with a sheer plastic, which is quite sticky.  A hazy\nlayer of smoke hangs in the air.  Many a drunken and lecherous man has\nwasted away his time and talens in this room.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6376,0,0,0,'Museum Entrance','  This is an odd entrance for a museum.  There are posters of scantily clothed\nwoman on the walls and the lights are kept at a very dim level.  Also,\nunlike other museums, a haze of smoke hangs in the air, which reeks of stale\nbeer.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6377,0,0,0,'Aquatic Marine Lab','  The University has built magical vats to contain ocean water, to \nallow for animal testing in a controlled environment.  To the east \nand southeast is a large wall of water that can be entered. Various \nforms of sea life can be seen swimming about to the east and \nsoutheast.  \n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6378,0,0,0,'Aquatic Marine Lab','  The University has built magical vats to contain ocean water, to \nallow for animal testing in a controlled environment.  To the east \nand northeast is a large wall of water that can be entered. Various \nforms of sea life can be seen swimming about to the east and \nnortheast.  \n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6379,0,0,0,'Cramped Cell','This small five by ten cell is barely large enough for one person to\nstay in, let alone the several that are often housed here at once.  The\ncell is completely devoid of any furniture, except for a flea infested\nstraw mattress that is lying in the far corner.\n',0,172488,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6380,0,0,0,'Cramped Cell','  This small five by ten cell is barely large enough for one person to \nstay in, let alone the several that are often housed here at once.  The \ncell is completely devoid of any furniture, except for a flea infested \nstraw mattress that is lying in the far corner.  \n',0,173512,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6381,0,0,0,'Courtroom','  This room is dominated by the large desk from behind which the judge \ndelivers his sentences.  A small chair next to the judge serves as a \nwitness stand, while two small tables have been set up for counsel.  \nSeveral comfortable looking chairs adorn the sides of the room, \npresumably that is where the jury watches the show.  \n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6382,0,0,0,'Judge\'s Chambers','  Lavishly furnished with tacky paintings adorning the walls, this \noffice is decorated well beyond the financial means of a public servant.  \n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6383,0,0,0,'Foreign Embassy','  The foreign embassy is a well furnished and comfortable place.  \nOn most days there is a steady flow of traffic in and out of the \nembassy.  Many of the city immigrants spend much of their \nfree time in the embassy, reminiscing about their homeland. \n',0,140616,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6384,0,0,0,'Foreign Embassy','  The foreign embassy is a well furnished and comfortable place.  \nOn most days there is a steady flow of traffic in and out of the \nembassy.  Many of the city immigrants spend much of their \nfree time in the embassy, reminiscing about their homeland. \n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6385,0,0,0,'Del Playa Road','  A simple dirt  road runs east and west through Xanesla.  The\nroad is littered with trash and debris.\n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6386,0,0,0,'(null)','Empty\n',0,0,60,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6387,0,0,0,'(null)','Empty\n',0,0,60,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6388,0,0,0,'Center Stage','This stage is the focal point of the club.  From this vantage point the entire\nclub can be seen.  The stage is a nice polished maple floor, which is covered\nwith greasy smudge marks.  A steel pole extends down from the ceiling to the\ncenter of the stage.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6389,0,0,0,'Lounge Area','  The lounge area is designed to be a comfortable place in which the \ndancers can offer dances to the customers, thereby milking every last \ntalen from them.  From here the customers have an excellent view \nof the stage to the north.  \n',0,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6390,0,0,0,'Aquatic Marine Lab','  An artificial underwater environment has been somehow altered to \nprevent the water from spilling west into the next room.  The water \nis cold and murky, the perfect hiding place for a predator.  \n',0,173384,53,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6391,0,0,0,'Aquatic Marine Lab','  An artificial underwater environment has been somehow altered to \nprevent the water from spilling west into the next room.  The water \nis cold and murky, the perfect hiding place for a predator.  \n',0,173384,53,0,0,0,0,-1,25,1000,0,'',NULL),
(6392,0,0,0,'North Camino Pescadero','  The Northern end of Camino Pescadero ends here abruptly at the \nnorthern city wall.  To the east is a large shop.  To the south is the \nhustle and bustle of the heart of Xanesla.  This street has been paved \nwith a flaky shale that kicks up a fine white powder when disturbed.\n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6393,0,0,0,'North Camino Pescadero','  Camino Pescadero is a main north-south thoroughfare that runs \nthrough the heart of Xanesla\'s marketing district.  A large shop is \nto the east.  The street has been paved with a white and flaky shale \nthat kicks up a fine power when disturbed. \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6394,0,0,0,'North Camino Pescadero','  Camino Pescadero is a main north-south thoroughfare that runs \nthrough the heart of Xanesla\'s marketing district.  A large shop is \nto the east.  The street has been paved with a white and flaky shale \nthat kicks up a fine power when disturbed. \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
