(6447,0,0,0,'Mesa Road','  This short street is not well cared for and is covered with litter.  \nSmall puddles of water collect, creating a breeding ground for germs \nand stench.  \n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,50,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6448,0,0,0,'Nurse\'s Station','This well lit and sterile room is where the nurses keep their supplies\nand other useless sundries.  They spend most of their shift gathered\nhere gossiping about which of the doctors may be single.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(6449,0,0,0,'Hospital Entrance','  This well lit and sterile room is the entrance to the Xanesla hospital.  \nThe room is kept spotlessly clean and smells of ammonia. There is \ngenerally a lot of traffic through here, as the townsfolk as a whole \nseem to be very accident prone.  \n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(6450,0,0,0,'Del Playa Road','A simple dirt road runs north and south through Xanesla.  The road is littered\nwith trash and debris.  The Xanesla hospital is directly to the north.  City\nstreets run to the south, west and east from this point.  Through a metal grate\nthe city\'s sewers can be seen below, emitting a foul odor.\n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6451,0,0,0,'(null)','Empty\n',0,0,60,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
