(6497,0,0,0,'Mission Viewing Area','  This old stone building was built here long before the city was erected\naround it.  Originally it was used as a rallying point from which the Galekians\nbrought religion to the local natives.  Now it is kept solely as a tourist\nattraction. \n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6498,0,0,0,'Mission Visitor\'s Center','  This wing of the mission has recently been restored with an eye towards\nremaining true to its ancient origins.  The walls and floor have been given an\nartificial aged look, while the ceiling has been painted to give the\nimpression that it is cracked.  The famous Mission Garden lies to the east.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6499,0,0,0,'Classroom','  This classroom is a bland and generic modern classroom.  Over thirty tiny\ndesks have been crammed together in a semicircle, focused at the desk and\nchalkboard at the front of the room.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,30,100,0,'',NULL),
(6500,0,0,0,'Flyer Lined Hallway','  This modernized building was designed to instill thinking and creativity in\nits occupants.  Unfortunately the modern design, which focused more on\ncreative angles and fixtures, has left the building drafty and unstable.  Small\nbits of rubble cover the floor having fallen from the large cracked ceiling.\nThousands of flyers have been plastered to the walls creating quite a fire\nhazard.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(6501,0,0,0,'Classroom','  This classroom is a bland and generic modern classroom.  Over thirty tiny\ndesks have been crammed together in a semicircle, focused at the desk and\nchalkboard at the front of the room.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,30,100,0,'',NULL),
(6502,0,0,0,'Church Pews','  Although religion is not prominent in Xanesla, the church has become a social\nmeeting place for all sorts of people.  The church is very accepting of all\nreligious beliefs.  Many wooden pews have been lined up here allowing a large\ncrowd to gather here when needed.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(6503,0,0,0,'Belltower','  From high atop this church tower is a wonderful view of Xanesla.  A strong\nwind whips through the tower stirring up leaves and other debris.  Ten feet\nabove is a large bell with frayed rope that hangs down.  \n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,100,0,'',NULL),
