(6590,0,0,0,'Makeshift War Room','This intersection of the sewers has been transformed into a makeshift war room.\nCharts, diagrams, and maps have been adhered to the tunnel walls, and small\ntables have been placed throughout the area.  The raw sewage has been\nblocked off and irrigated along the sides of the tunnel, keeping the center\nof the area relatively clean and debris free.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,30,100,0,'',NULL),
(6591,0,0,0,'City Sewer','  The smell of fecal matter and rotting  food is immensely powerful and steeps\ninto everything.  The walls are coated with a shiny brown slime and glisten\nwith moisture.  A foul congealed brown substance coats the floor.  The stone\nwalls are beginning to crumble and dust trickles from the ceiling.  The tunnel\nbranches off in several directions.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(6592,0,0,0,'Camino del Sur','  This well traveled path is the main road running from the city proper to the\npier.  The constant use and heavy industrial traffic has rendered the road\ndecayed and riddled with pot marks.  Because of the extensive use of the road,\nand the lack of alternative routes, the city is unable to coordinate a repair\nschedule.\n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6593,0,0,0,'Camino del Sur','  This well traveled path is the main road running from the city proper to the\npier.  The constant use and heavy industrial traffic has rendered the road\ndecayed and riddled with pot marks.  Because of the extensive use of the road,\nand the lack of alternative routes, the city is unable to coordinate a repair\nschedule.\n',0,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6594,0,0,0,'Tower Hallway','  This newly designed tower was built shortly after a series of unsuccessful\nattempts on the life of the Queen of Xanesla.  It was not designed for style or\ncomfort, but was intended to use both man power and magical devises to protect\nthe Queen at all costs.  The corridors are very narrow, allowing only a few\npeople to pass at once.\n',0,175432,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(6595,0,0,0,'<B>Underwater Near the Pier<1>','  Garbage and sewage contaminate the water, surging about with the tide. \nAbove, through the murky water, is  the noisy city pier. \n',0,140608,53,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6596,0,0,0,'<B>Under the Pier<1>','  Garbage and sewage contaminate the water, surging about with the tide.  \nAbove, through the murky water, is  the noisy city pier.  The support beams \nof the pier disappear into the murky sea  floor. \n',0,140608,53,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6597,0,0,0,'<B>Under the Pier<1>','  Garbage and sewage contaminate the water, surging about with the tide.  \nAbove, through the murky water, is  the noisy city pier.  The support beams\nof the pier disappear into the murky sea floor.\n',0,9536,53,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6598,0,0,0,'<B>Underwater Near the Pier<1>','  Garbage and sewage contaminate the water, surging about with the tide.  \nAbove, through the murky water, is  the noisy city pier.  The support beams \nof the pier disappear into the murky sea  floor. \n',0,140608,53,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6599,0,0,0,'(null)','Empty\n',0,0,60,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6600,-5,-9,-1,'Cave-in','A pile of stones blocks your way south.  It seems as if the roof has caved\nin.  There are no visible seams or openings in the pile of rock.  You\nsee that the floor is rubbed smooth in the center of the room.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6601,-5,-9,-2,'On a Ladder','  You are in an empty shaft.  The only feature you see is the old wooden\nladder that you are climbing on.  The air here feels very thick.  The ladder\nleads upward toward the sewers and downward into complete darkness.\n',41,131084,33,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(6602,-5,-9,-3,'On a Ladder','  You are in an empty shaft.  The only feature you see is the old wooden\nladder that you are climbing on.  The air here feels very thick.  The ladder\nleads upward toward the sewers and downward into complete darkness.\n',41,131084,33,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(6603,-5,-9,-4,'Entrance to a Large Dungeon','  You are standing at the entrance to what you have determined to be a large\ndungeon.  The air is thick here, and the ground is damp.  You hear an eerie\nmoaning sound coming from somewhere nearby, although you are unable to\npinpoint exactly where.  There are doors on both the North and East walls.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6604,-5,-8,-4,'Narrow Passage','  You are standing in a long dark corridor.  The air feels thick and moist,\nleading you to believe that there must be water somewhere nearby.  The walls\nare covered with mildew and cobwebs.  This passage continues to the north and\nsouth.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6605,-4,-9,-4,'Small Room','  This room is very dark, and there are cobwebs everywhere.  There is a foul\nodor here, which you imagine is coming from the rotting pile of flesh in the\ncorner of the room.  There is a large iron door on the west wall, that leads\nout to the entrance.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6606,-5,-7,-4,'Passage Junction','  You stand at a junction between passages.  You hear an eerie howling coming\nfrom somewhere nearby, although you can not pinpoint exactly where.  There\nare what appear to be some type of footprints on the ground.  The narrow\npassage runs north and south from here, and another passage runs east.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6607,-5,-6,-4,'Narrow Passage','  The passage is very narrow here, and the lack of space makes it somewhat\ndifficult to move about freely.  The walls are covered with mildew and as you\nmove onward, you feel cobwebs sticking to your face.  The passage widens a\nlittle bit to the north and south.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6608,-4,-7,-4,'Sloping Corridor','  You are standing in a gradually sloping corridor.  The slope is downward\nas it continues east.  The way that it is sloped, you wonder if at some point\nin time, it may have been completely underwater.  You hear a noise coming\nfrom somewhere nearby, resembling insects although they would have to be quite\nlarge to produce a noise this loud.  The passage runs east and west from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6609,-5,-5,-4,'Narrow Passage','  This passage running north and south is a little narrow for your liking.  If\nyou were to encounter something here it would certainly make it difficult to\nfight.  There is mildew covering the walls, leading you to believe that there\nmust be water somewhere nearby.  You can hear an eerie howling coming from\nsomeone or something nearby.  Maybe this would be a good time to leave.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6610,-5,-4,-4,'Bend in the Passage','  The passage you are standing in make a sharp bend here.  The air is damp and\nmusty.  The walls here are covered with cracks, and they could come tumbling\ndown at any time.  To the south, there is a narrow tunnel and to the east is\ncomplete darkness.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6611,-4,-4,-4,'Long Dark Corridor','  This corridor is very dark, and cold.  There is an odd smell in the air,\nalthough you are unable to determine what exactly it is.  The walls are damp\nand cold to the touch.  The floor is smooth and packed down, as if there is\nmuch foot travel here.  From here, the tunnel travels east and west, and another\ntunnel leads north.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6612,-3,-4,-4,'Long Dark Corridor','  This corridor is very dark, and cold.  There is an odd smell in the air,\nalthough you are unable to determine what exactly it is.  The walls are damp\nand cold to the touch.  The floor is smooth and packed down, as if there is\nmuch foot travel here.  From here, you may travel east and west.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6613,-2,-4,-4,'Long Dark Corridor','  This corridor is very dark, and cold.  There is an odd smell in the air,\nalthough you are unable to determine what exactly it is.  The walls are damp\nand cold to the touch.  The floor is smooth and packed down, as if there is\nmuch foot travel here.  The tunnel continues east and west from here.  There is\nalso a breach in the southern wall.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6614,-2,-5,-4,'Hole in the Wall','  This breach in the wall is filled with garbage, and this must have been the\nsource of the foul odor.  The wall to the north looks as though it has been\neaten away, and you wonder what could have possibly done such a thing.  You\nshiver uncomfortably as a few thoughts come to mind.  Other than the garbage\nthere is little else to this hole.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6615,-1,-4,-4,'Long Dark Corridor','  This corridor is very dark, and cold.  There is an odd smell in the air,\nalthough you are unable to determine what exactly it is.  The walls are damp\nand cold to the touch.  The floor is smooth and packed down, as if there is\nmuch foot travel here.  This tunnel leads east and west from here.  You notice a\nsmall iron door to the north.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6616,0,-4,-4,'Long Dark Corridor','  This corridor is very dark, and cold.  There is an odd smell in the air,\nalthough you are unable to determine what exactly it is.  The walls are damp\nand cold to the touch.  The floor is smooth and packed down, as if there is\nmuch foot travel here.  The tunnel continues into darkness east and west.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6617,1,-4,-4,'Long Dark Corridor','  This corridor is very dark, and cold.  There is an odd smell in the air,\nalthough you are unable to determine what exactly it is.  The walls are damp\nand cold to the touch.  The floor is smooth and packed down, as if there is\nmuch foot travel here.  From here, the tunnel makes its way east and west.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6618,2,-4,-4,'Long Dark Corridor','  This corridor is very dark, and cold.  There is an odd smell in the air,\nalthough you are unable to determine what exactly it is.  The walls are damp\nand cold to the touch.  The floor is smooth and packed down, as if there is\nmuch foot travel here.  This dark passage continues east and west.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6619,3,-4,-4,'Dark Intersection','  You are standing in a very dark intersection.  There is an odd smell in the\nair here, although you are unable to determine what it is.  With some effort,\nyou are able to tell that passages lead in all directions from here.  You can\nhear a quiet mumbling to the north, but it is much too dark to see what it\ncould be.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,36,0,'',NULL),
(6620,3,-5,-4,'Partially Collapsed Tunnel','OUCH! You should really be more careful.\n  The tunnel is really cramped here.  The floor is covered with rock,\nlarge and small, making it very difficult to move.  The earth trembles\never so slightly, causing some small rocks to fall down upon you.  From\nhere, the tunnel opens up a little to the north and also continues south.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,44,0,'',NULL),
(6621,3,-6,-4,'Partially Collapsed Tunnel','OUCH! You just bumped your head.\n  The tunnel is really cramped here.  The floor is covered with rock,\nlarge and small making it very difficult to move.  Small pebbles fall from\nthe roof as you make your way through this dark passage, and you are\nhopefull that they do not get any larger.  Feeling your way along the walls\nyou can tell that this tunnel continues north and south from this point.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,44,0,'',NULL),
(6622,3,-7,-4,'Partially Collapsed Tunnel','OUCH! You should really be more careful.\n  The tunnel is really cramped here.  It is impossible to walk through.\nNot only is it very small, but there are rocks both large and small under\nyour feet making travel very slow.  The earth trembles ever so slightly,\nand some small rocks begin to fall down upon you.  The tunnel runs north\nand west from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,44,0,'',NULL),
(6623,2,-7,-4,'Partially Collapsed Tunnel','OUCH! You just bumped your head.\n  This tunnel is really cramped.  As you make your way through this tunnel\nthat looks as if it has recently collapsed, you can tell that you will\nneed to move very slowly.  There is an abundance of rocks, large and small\nlining the floor below your feet.  You feel the earth tremble ever so\nslightly, and it makes you fearful that another collapse could happen at\nany time.  The tunnel bends here making its way to the south and east.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,44,0,'',NULL),
(6624,2,-8,-4,'Sloping Corridor','  You are standing in a gradually sloping corridor.  The slope is uphill from\nhere as it makes its way west.  There is a noise in the air, that you\ndetermine to be coming from somewhere nearby to the west.  To the north you\ncan see another tunnel that seems to have collapsed recently, although you\nthink you could fit inside if you had to.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6625,1,-8,-4,'Sloping Corridor','  You are standing in a gradually sloping corridor.  The slope is downward\nas it continues east.  The way that it is sloped, you wonder if at some point\nin time, it may have been completely underwater.  You hear a noise coming\nfrom somewhere nearby, resembling insects although they would have to be quite\nlarge to produce a noise this loud.  The passage runs east and west from here,\nand the noise seems to be getting louder to the west.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6626,0,-8,-4,'Sloping Corridor','  You are standing in a gradually sloping corridor.  The slope is downward\nas it continues east.  The way that it is sloped, you wonder if at some point\nin time, it may have been completely underwater.  You hear a noise coming\nfrom somewhere nearby, resembling insects although they would have to be quite\nlarge to produce a noise this loud.  The passage runs east and west from here,\nand the noise seems to be getting louder to the west.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6627,-1,-8,-4,'Sloping Corridor','  You are standing in the middle of a long sloping corridor.  The corridor\nslopes more as it continues to the east.  The walls here, are covered with\ncobwebs, and there is a loud noise that seems to be coming from the south.\nFeeling along the walls in that direction you notice an extremely large web.\nFrom here, you may travel north and east.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6628,-1,-9,-4,'Spider Web','  This is a very large  spider web, and you are somewhat stuck in it.  As\nyou thrash around, you manage to free yourself from its sticky grip.  In the\ncorner of the room, there are dozens of large spider eggs, that have recently\nstarted to hatch.  The only exit from this web lies back to the north.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6629,-1,-7,-4,'Bend in the Corridor','  You are standing at a bend in this sloping corridor, which leads west and\nsouth.  The noise that you have been hearing seems to get louder to the south.\nThere are cobwebs along the walls here, and some small tracks on the ground.\nThere are many cracks in the walls, and the ceiling is quite low.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6630,-2,-7,-4,'Sloping Corridor','  You are standing in a gradually sloping corridor.  The slope is downward\nas it continues east.  The way that it is sloped, you wonder if at some point\nin time, it may have been completely underwater.  You hear a noise coming\nfrom somewhere nearby, resembling insects although they would have to be quite\nlarge to produce a noise this loud.  The passage runs east and west from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6631,-3,-7,-4,'Sloping Corridor','  You are standing in a gradually sloping corridor.  The slope is downward\nas it continues east.  The way that it is sloped, you wonder if at some point\nin time, it may have been completely underwater.  You hear a noise coming\nfrom somewhere nearby, resembling insects although they would have to be quite\nlarge to produce a noise this loud.  The passage runs east and west from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6632,4,-4,-4,'Long Dark Corridor','  This corridor is very dark, and cold.  There is an odd smell in the air,\nalthough you are unable to determine what exactly it is.  The walls are damp\nand cold to the touch.  The floor is smooth and packed down, as if there is\nmuch foot travel here.  The tunnel runs east and west from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6633,5,-4,-4,'Long Dark Corridor','  This corridor is very dark, and cold.  There is an odd smell in the air,\nalthough you are unable to determine what exactly it is.  The walls are damp\nand cold to the touch.  The floor is smooth and packed down, as if there is\nmuch foot travel here.  You see a bend in the tunnel to the east.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6634,6,-4,-4,'Bend in the Corridor','  You are standing in the middle of a bend between corridors.  Feeling the\nwalls around you, you determine that this corridor will continue to the\nnorth and west.  This corner is very dark, and someone or something could\nsneak up behind you and you probably wouldn\'t notice.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6635,6,-3,-4,'Well Traveled Tunnel','  This tunnel seems to be the most heavily traveled that you have seen to\nthis point.  There are many small footprints and pawprints in the dirt on\nthe floor.  The walls here are very rough and cold to the touch.  There is\na quiet squeaking noise coming from somewhere nearby.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6636,6,-2,-4,'Well Traveled Tunnel','  This tunnel seems to be the most heavily traveled that you have seen to\nthis point.  There are many small footprints and pawprints in the dirt on the\nfloor.  The walls here are very rough and cold.  There is a quiet squeaking\nnoise coming from somewhere nearby.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6637,6,-1,-4,'Well Traveled Tunnel','  This well traveled tunnel makes a turn here.  There are many small\npawprints and footprints in the dirt on the floor.  There is a quiet\nsqueaking and scuffling coming from the east.  You may continue in every\ndirection but north.\n',41,131084,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6638,7,-1,-4,'Rats\' Lair','  Now you know what that squeaking and scuffling that you heard was.  You\nare standing in the midst of what these large rats call home.  There is\ngarbage and body parts littering the floor, and the stench is unbearable.\nThese rats are no doubt angered by your presence.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6639,5,-1,-4,'Well Traveled Tunnel','  This tunnel you now stand in is the most heavily traveled that you have\nseen to this point.  There are many small footprints and pawprints in the\ndirt on the floor.  You can hear a quiet scuffling coming from somewhere\nnearby.  This tunnel continues to the east and west, and there is a tunnel\nleading north that appears to have some decent lighting.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6640,5,0,-4,'Dimly Lit Passage','  You are standing in a tunnel that is better lit than any you have seen down\nhere.  This tunnel is very clean compared to the others, and seems fairly well\ntraveled and maintained.  Further to the north you can make out what seems to\nbe a missing section of the tunnel.  The tunnel leads north and south from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6641,5,1,-4,'Dimly Lit Passage','  You are standing in a tunnel that is better lit than any you have seen down\nhere.  This tunnel is very clean compared to the others, and seems fairly well\ntraveled and maintained.  There seems to be a large section of the wall\nmissing to the north.  The tunnel also leads west and south from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6642,5,2,-4,'Breach in the Wall','  This is a large breach in the wall, that may or may not have led to some\nplace at one time.  There are boulders both large and small piled up high\non the floor, and it would take a very long time to try to move them.  It\nlooks like you will have to return the same way you came from.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6643,4,1,-4,'Dimly Lit Passage','  You are standing in a tunnel that is better lit than any you have seen down\nhere.  This tunnel is very clean compared to the others, and seems fairly well\ntraveled and maintained.  You feel your eyes start to adjust to this lighting,\nand you hope that you do not stumble back into darkness suddenly.  You can\ncontinue traveling to the east and west.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6644,3,1,-4,'Dimly Lit Passage','  You are standing in a tunnel that is better lit than any you have seen down\nhere.  This tunnel is very clean compared to the others, and seems fairly well\ntraveled and maintained.  You feel your eyes start to adjust to this lighting,\nand you hope that you do not stumble back into darkness suddenly.  You can\ncontinue traveling to the east and west.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6645,2,1,-4,'Dimly Lit Passage','  You are standing in a tunnel that is better lit than any you have seen down\nhere.  This tunnel is very clean compared to the others, and seems fairly well\ntraveled and maintained.  You feel your eyes start to adjust to this lighting,\nand you hope that you do not stumble back into darkness suddenly.  You can\ncontinue traveling to the east and west.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6646,1,1,-4,'Short Connecting Corridor','  This short corridor running north and south must be used primarily to\ngo between the various passages.  There is some graffiti on the walls here,\nand it appears to be well traveled.  There is another passageway leading\nto the east from here, and that passage looks to have better lighting.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6647,4,-1,-4,'Dead End','  You have come to the end of this well traveled tunnel.  This no doubt\nhad led to somewhere, but there has since been a cave-in and rocks now block\nyour path.  It looks as though you will have to turn around.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6648,3,-1,-4,'Gatekeeper\'s Quarters','  You are standing in the gatekeepers quarters.  There is a steady flow of\nwater coming from a large crack in the ceiling.  There is the stench of raw\nsewage, and it almost makes it unbearable to stay.  The water has formed a\nlarge puddle on the ground, which flows down through an iron grate in the\nfloor.  The water is also running underneath the door to the south.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6649,3,-3,-4,'Damp Hallway','  This is a very damp hallway, and there are small streams of water flowing\nin from the north.  There is a stench of raw sewage in the air and there are\nsmall gnats buzzing around your head.  This hallway continues to the north\nand into complete darkness to the south.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6650,3,-2,-4,'Damp Hallway','  This hallway is very damp, and you imagine it is due to the water\nflowing from underneath the door on the north wall.  There is a stench of\nraw sewage in the air, and there are small gnats buzzing around your head.\nBesides the door to the north, you can travel south and west from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6651,2,-2,-4,'Damp Hallway','  This hallway is very damp here, and you can see that is gets damper as it\nextends further to the east.  There is a strong stench in the air of raw\nsewage here, and it gets stronger to the east.  There are small gnats buzzing\naround your head, and they are quite irritating.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6652,1,-2,-4,'Short Connecting Corridor','  This short corridor, which serves to connect some of the other passages\nappears to be well traveled.  There is a stench in the air and it seems to\nbe getting stronger to the east.  This corridor also leads north.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6653,1,-1,-4,'Short Connecting Corridor','  This short corridor running north and south must be used primarily to go\nbetween the various passages.  There is a slight stench in the air here and\nit seems to get be getting stronger to the south.  This corridor appears to\nbe well traveled, and there is another tunnel to the west.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6654,1,0,-4,'Short Connecting Corridor','  This short corridor running north and south must be primarily used to\ngo between the various passages.  There is some graffiti on the walls here,\nand it appears to be well traveled.  There is a slight stench in the air\nhere and it seems to be coming from the south.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6655,0,-1,-4,'Well Traveled Tunnel','  This tunnel seems that it has been well traveled in recent times, as there\nare some small footprints in the dirt on the floor.  While this is somewhat\nreassuring, you wonder what it is that travels down here.  The walls feel very\ncold here, and there is a chilling stillness in the air.  The tunnel continues\nto the east and west.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6656,-1,-1,-4,'Well Traveled Tunnel','  This tunnel seems that it has been well traveled in recent times, as there\nare some small footprints in the dirt on the floor.  While this is somewhat\nreassuring, you wonder what it is that travels down here.  The walls feel very\ncold here, and there is a chilling stillness in the air.  The tunnel continues\nto the east and the west, and there is a small chute to the south.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6657,-1,-2,-4,'Dead End','  You are standing at what at one time was the beginning of a small tunnel that\nwould have run to the south from here.  It seems as though it has been blocked\ncompletely by huge boulders that have fallen from the ceiling.  There is no way\nthat you can make your way through them, and it looks like the only way out is\nback to the north.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6658,-1,-3,-4,'Storage Room','  This is a very small room, with rough dirt walls.  There is a musty\nsmell in the air here.  The floor is covered with small scraps of fabric\nand rotten food.  There are large bales of cloth stacked in one corner,\nthat have been virtually eaten away.  It is apparent that no one has been\nin this storage room for quite some time.  The small iron door on the\nsouth wall provides your only exit.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6659,-2,-1,-4,'Well Traveled Tunnel','  This tunnel seems that it has been well traveled in recent times, as there\nare some small footprints in the dirt on the floor.  While this is somewhat\nreassuring, you wonder what it is that travels down here.  The walls feel very\ncold here, and there is a chilling stillness in the air.  The tunnel continues\nto the east and west.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6660,-3,-1,-4,'Well Traveled Tunnel','  This tunnel seems that it has been well traveled in recent times, as there\nare some small footprints in the dirt on the floor.  While this is somewhat\nreassuring, you wonder what it is that travels down here.  The walls feel very\ncold here, and there is a chilling stillness in the air.  The tunnel continues\nto the east and west.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6661,-4,-1,-4,'Rubble-Filled Hallway','  The floor in this hallway is covered in rubble, that had no doubt fallen\nfrom the roof and walls.  The stones on the ground make it incredibly difficult\nto walk.  Occasionally you have to duck down to avoid hitting your head on\na low lying section of the roof.  There is a passage running to the east from\nhere, which looks fairly well lit.  The hallway you stand in continues to the\nnorth and the south.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6662,-4,-2,-4,'Rubble-Filled Hallway','  The floor in this hallway is covered in rubble, that had no doubt fallen\nfrom the roof and walls.  The stones on the ground make it incredibly difficult\nto walk.  Occasionally you have to duck down to avoid hitting your head on\na low lying section of the roof.  The hallway runs north and south from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6663,-4,-3,-4,'Rubble-Filled Hallway','  The floor in this hallway is covered in rubble, that had no doubt fallen\nfrom the roof and walls.  The stones on the ground make it incredibly difficult\nto walk.  Occasionally you have to duck down to avoid hitting your head on\na low lying section of the roof.  The hallway runs north and south from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6664,-4,0,-4,'Rubble-Filled Hallway','  The floor in this hallway is covered in rubble, that had no doubt fallen\nfrom the roof and walls.  The stones on the ground make it incredibly difficult\nto walk.  Occasionally you have to duck down to avoid hitting your head on\na low lying section of the roof.  The hallway runs north and south from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6665,-4,1,-4,'Rubble-Filled Hallway','  The floor in this hallway is covered in rubble, that had no doubt fallen\nfrom the roof and walls.  The stones on the ground make it incredibly difficult\nto walk.  Occasionally you have to duck down to avoid hitting your head on\na low lying section of the roof.  The hallway runs north and south from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6666,-4,2,-4,'Northwest Corner','  You stand in the northwest corner of this maze of tunnels.  You now see how\neasily one could get lost in here, and never return.  There is a small wooden\ndoor on the north wall, from which you can hear a quiet mumbling.  From here\nthe tunnels run east and south.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6667,-4,3,-4,'Hermits\' Home','  You now stand in a small room that is considered home by some poor soul\nthat wants to be left alone.  The room is very tidy, with a well kept decor.\nThere are many beautiful paintings of scenery on the walls.  The floor is dirt,\nbut looks as though it has been swept recently.  The only exit from this room\nis back out the door on the south wall.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6668,-3,2,-4,'Defaced Corridor','  You stand in a long corridor that has been defaced by some unruly group of\nhoodlums.  The walls have been marred with graffiti, most of which is not\nlegible to you.  You wonder what type of person would do such a thing, but\nsecretly hope that you don\'t find out.  This corridor leads both east and\nwest from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6669,-2,2,-4,'Defaced Corridor','  You stand in a long corridor that has been defaced by some unruly group of\nhoodlums.  The walls have been marred with graffiti, most of which is not\nlegible to you.  You wonder what type of person would do such a thing, but\nsecretly hope that you don\'t find out.  This corridor leads both east and\nwest from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6670,-1,2,-4,'Defaced Corridor','  You stand in a long corridor that has been defaced by some unruly group of\nhoodlums.  The walls have been marred with graffiti, most of which is not\nlegible to you.  You wonder what type of person would do such a thing, but\nsecretly hope that you don\'t find out.  This corridor leads both east and\nwest from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6671,0,2,-4,'Defaced Corridor','  You stand in a long corridor that has been defaced by some unruly group of\nhoodlums.  The walls have been marred with graffiti, most of which is not\nlegible to you.  You wonder what type of person would do such a thing, but\nsecretly hope that you don\'t find out.  This corridor leads both east and\nwest from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6672,1,2,-4,'Defaced Corridor','  You stand in a long corridor that has been defaced by some unruly group\nof hoodlums.  The walls have been marred with graffiti, most of which is\nnot legible to you.  You wonder what type of person would do such a thing,\nbut secretly hope that you don\'t find out.  This corridor runs south and\nwest from here, and there is a door on the northern wall through which you\ncan hear some loud noise.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6673,1,3,-4,'Seedy Hangout','  You are standing in the middle of what has got to be the most run-down living\nquarters that you have ever seen.  There is graffiti covering the walls, and\ntrash covering the floor.  These people are no doubt outcasts, most likely\nrun out of town due to their lack of cleanliness and moral standards.  The\nonly exit from here is back out the door that you came in through.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6674,3,-1,-5,'Soaked Tunnel','  You stand ankle deep in muddy water.  There is water running into the room\nfrom a grate that is in the ceiling.  The water is actually sewage, seeping\ndown through many layers of earth, from the sewers above.  The walls in this\ntunnel are covered with a moss-like fungus.  There is a putrid odor in the\nair here.  There is a small iron door on the east wall.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6675,3,-2,-5,'Soaked Tunnel','  You stand ankle deep in muddy water.  The water is flowing in from the\nnorth, and you determine it to be raw sewage.  There is a stench in the air,\nand it is a little sickening.  The walls are almost completely covered with\na moss-like fungus.  To the north, you see more mud, and there is a small step-\ndown leading to another tunnel to the south.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6676,3,-3,-5,'Sunken Tunnel','  You stand in a long tunnel, of which the floor seems to have dropped about\ntwo feet below the level of the other tunnels.  The floor is crumbling below\nyour feet, and it seems as though it could give way anytime soon.  The tunnel\nruns east and west from here, and there is a step-up to another tunnel north.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6677,2,-3,-5,'Sunken Tunnel','  You stand in a long tunnel, of which the floor seems to have dropped about\ntwo feet below the level of the other tunnels.  The floor is crumbling below\nyour feet, and it seems as though it could give way at anytime soon.  The tunnel\nruns east and west from here.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6678,1,-3,-5,'Sunken Tunnel','  You stand in a long tunnel, of which the floor seems to have dropped about\ntwo feet below the level of the other tunnels.  The floor is crumbling below\nyour feet, and it seems as though it could give way at anytime soon.  The tunnel\ncontinues to the east and west.\n',41,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
