(6794,6,5,-6,'Center of a Large Torture Chamber','  You stand in the center of a large torture chamber.  Looking around you see\nvarious implements for torturing prisoners large and small.  The air here is\nfilled with smoke, and it makes it a little hard to breath.  There are some\nsmall blood stains on the ground here.  From here, you may go any direction.\n',41,163848,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6795,5,5,-6,'Torture Chamber','  You stand along the western wall of this very large torture chamber.  There\nare scraps of metal, bone, flesh, and blood stains scattered about the floor.\nThere is a smoky haze filling the air, making it difficult to breath.  The\nwalls here are black, and covered with soot.  There are various implements of\ntorture filling the chamber.  There is a small holding cell to the west.\n',41,163848,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6798,0,0,0,'A Deserted Beach','  You are standing in the most beautiful place you have ever seen.  The sand\nfeels warm under your feet as the bright sunlight beats down upon it.  The\nwater is gently splashing upon the shore, and it feels very cool.  There are\nhuge cliffs extending up on all sides of you, making this beach very secluded.\nThere is a slight onshore breeze, that fills the air with a most pleasing\naroma.  You feel very peaceful here.\n',41,131072,60,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6800,0,0,0,'The Main Performance Circle','  This is the Main Performance Circle.  Many thousands upon thousands\nof Magical Rituals have gone on here, some rituals cost thousands upon\nthousands of man hours to complete, and yield one item.  The floor in\nthe building glows of an unknown plasma like substance, the walls are\nmulti-colored, and pleasing to the eye, the room is very clean.  As\nYou glance up, you fail to see a roof, although, by the weather,\nyou think surely there must be one.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6801,0,0,0,'The Entrance to the Main Performance Circle','  You stand in a small arch which continues to the north several\nhundred cubits.  To the south stands a very large room.  The Arch\nis wide, and very clean, it looks as though it is a combination of\na man-made materials, and some magical plasma like substance\nunknown to you.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6802,0,0,0,'A Hall leading to the Main Performance Circle','You stand in a long hallway which leads north to a very large\nroom.  The Hallway is very clean, and the floor, and walls glow slightly.\nThey appear to be made of a combination of man made materials, and\na magical plasma like substance unknown to you.\n',0,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6803,0,0,0,'Main Apprentice Lounge','   You stand in the Main Apprentice Lounge, the room looks comfortable\nand homey.  This room has become the hang-out of choice for all the great\nstudents of the greater Masters.  Other students come here as well to study.\nOr at least that is their pretense for coming to meet others of the\nopposite sex.  The Room is very clean, and very tidy, unexpectedly you would\nthink for a bunch of students, the walls and floor appear to be made\nof an combination of man made material, and a magical plasma like substance\nunknown to you.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6804,0,0,0,'Entrance to the Enclave','    You stand in a very large room, which leads into an even larger room.\n To the far north, you see a single fire burning.  You get a strange chill\ndown the back of your neck, a warning as it feels, that you should\nnot bring any more flames into this room.  The room is very clean, and\nthe walls and floor seem to glow slightly.\n',42,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6805,0,0,0,'The Main Enclave','  You stand in a very large room.  A wide open area encompasses you.\nIn the center of the room stands a pit of brewing fire.  The fire emits no\nsmoke, and appears to be burning some sort of very shiny metallic substance.\nThe room, is not covered, in soot, nor ash, in fact it is very clean.  The\nwalls and floor seem to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6806,0,0,0,'Passage-way to the Demon Containment Room','  You are in a very silent, eerie feeling room.  A voice calls\nin your head naggingly, \"Do NOT enter the Demon Containment room.  It is\nfor the strictest, and most disciplined, and wisest of the Masters.\nwe the souls of those who have not headed these warnings, give you\nthis message.  Turn around, and save yourself.\"\nThe walls, and floor in this room, appear to glow softly.\n',42,139264,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6807,0,0,0,'The Demon Containment Room','  You have stepped out of the realm of mankind and into the prison\nof demons, who were too powerful for even the masters to control.  This room\nwas created so long ago, not even the Masters know how to create one.\nIt has been told, that a Mighty Cleric created the containment room\nafter long hours of ceremonies in eight realms and thousands of mountain peaks,\nand offerings, to his mighty deity.  If you are not dead then you are immortal.\nIf you are not immortal, dying sucks doesn\'t it?\n',42,139264,62,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6808,0,0,0,'Sub-Master Gilthanthil\'s Office','  You are in a large clean office, the air is fresh like the mountains\nafter a long rain.   There is neither dust nor dirt, nor anything unclean\nabout this room at all.   The floor, and walls seem to glow slightly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6809,0,0,0,'The Office of Master Mastir','  The air in this room, is like pure oxygen, dizziness sets into you, then\nfades away.  You feel as though if you stay to long, you will begin to see\nbeautiful images that don\'t exist.  The walls, and floor in this room appear\nto glow slightly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6810,0,0,0,'Entrance to the Eye Room','  You are in a small corridor, leading to a larger room.  Strange emotions stir in your body, as you stand in this corridor, fear, love, peace, all whipping\nthrough your mind.  The floor and walls in this room appear to glow slightly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6811,0,0,0,'The Room of the Eye','  You are standing in a room, which seem to summon the most from your\nimagination.  You see pictures of faeries, and sprites darting about\nand playing, quickly the pictures in your head move to demons, slaying\ninnocent people in villages.  The floor, and walls in this room appear\nto glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6812,0,0,0,'The Main Stage of the Eye Room','  You are on a long, large stage.  You can feel every emotion,\nand thought through your mind surge through your body as if it had been\nin some way amplified.  The walls, and floor appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6813,0,0,0,'Behind the Main Stage of the Eye','  You are in a fairly large room, from a slight discoloration in the floor\nyou assume that many things have been dragged around in here, likely a storage\nroom of some sort.  The walls, and floor appear to glow slightly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6814,0,0,0,'The Office of Sub-Master Salzar','  You are in a large room, your body tingles slightly, and pictures\nof yourself at play as a small child scatter through your mind.  The walls\nand floor in this room appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6815,0,0,0,'The Office of Master Tsarnek','  You are in a large room, you feel fear rush throughout your body,\nyou feel as if you are being watched, a small voice runs over and over and\nover in your head, \"come now.  come to me.  look me in the eye.\".  The walls\nand floor appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6816,0,0,0,'The Bleachers','  You stand in the middle of a collection of bleachers.  This is clearly\nwhere students, and invited guests are seated during a lecture, or performance\nby Master, teacher, and student alike.  The walls, and seats appear to\nglow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6817,0,0,0,'Entrance To the Lab','  You are in a small corridor, leading towards a large room which\ncontains a lot of tools, machines, and tables.  The floor, and walls appear to\nglow slightly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6818,0,0,0,'Main Alchemy Lab','     You are standing in a large lab, tables, vials, and strange dusts,\nand stones, are scattered about the room.  The walls, and floor appear to glow\nsoftly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6819,0,0,0,'Office of Sub-Master Halendos','  You stand in a small office.  The room feels stuffy, and boring,\na feeling you attribute to its owner.  The walls and floor appear to glow\nsoftly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6820,0,0,0,'The Office of Master Slipendi','  You stand in a small office.  The office seems to make you feel\nstrong, and confident in yourself.  The feeling is quite relaxing, and falling\nasleep seems like it might be something you would consider soon.  The\nwalls, and floor appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6821,0,0,0,'Entrance to The Thaumaturgy Lab','  You are standing in a corridor, which extends into a large equipment\nroom.  The walls, and floor appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6822,0,0,0,'Thaumaturgy Lab','  You stand in a large equipment like room.  Balances, scales, ropes\nand strange looking machines are strewn about in an odd pattern.  The walls and\nfloor appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6823,0,0,0,'Office of Sub-Master Alicettin','     You stand in a small office.  You notice that the floor and walls in\nthis room appear wooden, and both appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6824,0,0,0,'Office of Master Texayor','  You stand in a large office, notes, and pages on the art of\nThaumaturgy are scattered about, as if the occupant were writing their\nmemoirs.  The floor, and walls appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6825,0,0,0,'A Long Hallway in the Main Study Building','  You stand in a long hallway.  To the south is a large lounge.  The\nwalls, and floor of the hallway appear to be your favorite color, and glow\nsoftly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6826,0,0,0,'A Large Hallway in the Study Building','     You stand in a long hallway.  The walls, and floor seem to come\nalive in your favorite color, glowing softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6827,0,0,0,'A Large Hallway in the Study Building','     You stand in a long hallway.  The room appears to come alive with\nyour favorite color.  The walls, and floor appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6828,0,0,0,'Before a Great Staircase','     You are on a great staircase, which appears to be made of a blue\nplasma like substance.  The walls appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6829,0,0,0,'A Great Staircase','     You stand on a great staircase, which appears to be made of a blue\nplasma like substance, your feet glide across it like walking on air.  The\nwalls appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6830,0,0,0,'Upon a Great Staircase','  You are standing on a great staircase, which appears to be made of a\nblue plasma like substance.  Your feet fly across the surface of each stair.\nThe walls appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6831,0,0,0,'Upon a Great Staircase','  You are upon a great staircase, which appears to be made of a blue\nplasma like substance unknown to you.  The walls appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6832,0,0,0,'Hallway leading to the Dean\'s Office','  You are in a long clean hallway, pictures decorate most of the walls.\nUnder each picture is a little plaque stating the date that the person\ndepicted in the picture was Dean of the Circle, and some of his or her\nmajor accomplishments.  The walls, and floor appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6833,0,0,0,'Entrance to the Library','  You are in a large room, with bookshelves, and scroll shelves,\nlining each wall of the building.  Tables, and chairs are scattered about\nso students, can study and read.  The floor, walls, tables, and chairs\nappear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6834,0,0,0,'In front of the Librarian\'s Desk','     You stand before the librarians desk, quills are scattered about it,\nand an image of her family can be seen hovering over the desk, a few books\nare scattered about.  The floor, walls, desk, quills, and books appear\nto glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6835,0,0,0,'Behind the Desk of The Librarian','     You are behind the desk of the librarian.  A small comfortable\nlooking seat sits under the desk, and small wastebasket off to the side\nof the desk.  The floor, walls, desk, seat, and wastebasket appear to\nglow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6836,0,0,0,'Near the Librarians Desk','     You are near the librarians desk, to the north begins the shelving,\nand to the west is a long hallway through the library.  The floor, and\nwalls appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6837,0,0,0,'Main Hallway through the Library','  You are at the north end of a long hallway leading through the\nlibrary.  To the north are rows of shelving.  The floor, and walls appear\nto glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6839,0,0,0,'Before a Bulletin Board','   You are in front of a large bulletin board, which appears new.\nFrom the placement of the bulletin board, you can assume that it is used\nto offer, used books, and other such knickknack for sale to students,\noff to one side is a list of current even information.\nThe floor, and walls appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6840,0,0,0,'A Small Pathway','     You are in a small pathway, leading between tables, and shelves in the\nlibrary.\nThe floor, walls, and tables appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6841,0,0,0,'A Small Pathway','     You are in a small pathway leading between shelving, and tables in\nthe library.\nThe floor, walls, tables, and shelving appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6842,0,0,0,'The Main Hallway through the Library','     You are in a long hallway leading through the library, book and\nscroll shelves line each side of you.\nThe floor, walls, and shelves appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6843,0,0,0,'The Main Hallway through the Library','  You are in a long hallway leading through the library, book, and\nscroll shelves, are placed in front, and behind you.  The floor, walls, and\nshelves appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6844,0,0,0,'The Main Hallway through the Library','  You are in the a long hallway leading through the library, book,\nand scroll shelves are placed in front, and behind you.  The floor, walls,\nand shelves appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6845,0,0,0,'The Main Hallway through the Library','  You are in a long hallway leading through the library, book, and\nscroll shelves are spread in front, and behind you.  The floor, walls, and\nshelves appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6846,0,0,0,'Near the End of the Main Hallway through the Library','  You are near the end of a long hallway leading through the library,\nbook, and scroll shelves are spread in front, and behind you.  The floor,\nwalls, and shelves appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6847,0,0,0,'The End of the Main Hallway through the Library','     You are at the end of a long hallway leading through the library.\nBook and scroll shelves are spread to the south.  The floor, walls, and shelves\nappear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6848,0,0,0,'The Last Row of The Library','     You are in the last row of the library, a shelf is to the south.\nThe floor, walls, and shelf appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6849,0,0,0,'The South-East Corner of the Library','     You are in the south-east corner of the library, a shelf stands\nto the north-west.  The floor, walls, and shelf appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6850,0,0,0,'A Small Pathway near the End of the Library','     You are in a small pathway near the south of the library, leading\nbetween shelving and tables.  The floor, walls, shelving, and tables appear\nto glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6851,0,0,0,'A Small Pathway','     You are in a small pathway leading between shelving, and tables in\nthe library.  The floor, walls, tables, and shelving appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6852,0,0,0,'A Small Pathway','     You are in a small pathway leading between shelving and tables in the\nlibrary.  The floor, walls, tables, and shelving appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6853,0,0,0,'A Small Pathway','     You are in a small pathway leading between shelving, and tables in the\nlibrary.  The floor, walls, tables, and shelving appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6854,0,0,0,'Between the Shelves of Books','  You stand between two large shelves of books, the shelves are very\nlarge, and clean.   Periodically along a shelf, a small label appears,\nshowing the type of book, and the name of the author corresponding to the\nbook above it.  The floor, walls, shelving, and labels appear to glow\nsoftly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6855,0,0,0,'Between a Set of Bookshelves','  You are between two large sets of shelves.  The shelves are very\nlarge, and clean.  Periodically along a shelf, a small label appears which\nis supposed to correspond to a book above it.  However, some of the books\nappear to be out.  The floor, walls, shelves, and labels appear to glow\nsoftly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6856,0,0,0,'The South-West Corner of the Library','  You are in the south-west corner of the library.  A large shelf is\nto your north-east.  The floor, walls, and shelf, appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6857,0,0,0,'A Small Pathway','     You are in a small pathway leading between tables, and shelving in\nthe library.  The floor, walls, tables, and shelving appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6858,0,0,0,'A Small Pathway','     You are in a small pathway leading between tables, and shelving\nin the library.  The floor, walls, tables, and shelving appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6859,0,0,0,'A Small Pathway','  You are in a small pathway leading between tables, and shelving in the\nlibrary.  The floor, walls, tables, and shelving appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6860,0,0,0,'A Small Pathway','     You are in a small pathway leading between tables, and shelving in\nthe library.  The floor, walls, tables, and shelving appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6861,0,0,0,'A Dead End','  You are in a small pathway leading between tables, and shelving in the\nlibrary.  The walls here seems to shimmer, in and out of existence, different\nviews showing each time.  The floor appears to glow slightly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6862,0,0,0,'Between Some Shelving','  You are between to large scroll shelves, little pockets are staggered\nthroughout the shelf, to hold the many scrolls.  The shelf itself glows\nsoftly in a pale purplish color.  The floor appears translucent and invisible\nthe walls are blindingly bright.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6863,0,0,0,'Between Some Shelving','     You are between to large scroll shelves, little pockets are staggered\nthroughout the shelf to hold the scrolls, the shelf itself appears invisible\nbut you know it is there.  The floors, and walls appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6864,0,0,0,'At the Study Tables','  You are in a open area where students sit down and study.  The walls\nhere seem to hum a silent relaxing hum.  Not the type of hum that would\nput you to sleep, but the type of hum that makes it much easier to study\nwith.  The floor appears to fade and lighten in color.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6865,0,0,0,'At the Study Tables','You are in the area where the students sit down to study.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6866,0,0,0,'Rare Book Storage Room','You are in a rather sterile looking room, where you would normally expect it to\nsmell musty, but this room is as clean as any other in the Study\nBuilding.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6867,0,0,0,'Rare Scroll Storage Room','You are in a rather sterile looking room, where you would normally expect it\nto smell musty, but this room is as clean as any other in the\nStudy Building.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6868,0,0,0,'Hallway leading to the Dean\'s Office','  You are in a long clean hallway, decorated with past Dean\'s portraits\nalong each of the walls.  Under each portrait is the date the Dean served\nand a small note of their major accomplishments.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6869,0,0,0,'Hallway Leading towards the Dean\'s Office','  You are in a long clean hallway, decorated with past Dean\'s portraits\nalong each of the walls.  Under each portrait is the date the Dean served,\nand a small note of their major accomplishments.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6870,0,0,0,'Hallway leading to the Dean\'s Office','  You are in a long clean hallway, decorated with past Dean\'s portraits\nalong each of the walls.  Under each portrait is the date the Dean served,\nand a small note listing their major accomplishments.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6871,0,0,0,'Hallway leading to the Dean\'s Office','  You are in a long clean hallway, decorated with past Dean\'s portraits\nalong each of the walls.  Under each portrait is the date the Dean served,\nand a small note listing their major accomplishments.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6872,0,0,0,'A Dead End Leading to the Dean\'s Office','  You have reached a dead end leading towards the Dean\'s Office.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6873,0,0,0,'Entrance to the Dean\'s Office','  You are in a very large office the walls look they are made of the finest\nwoods and the floor appears as if it is made of the shiniest marble,\nbut upon closer examination, the are both made of a strange unknown\nsubstance\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6874,0,0,0,'Deep Inside the Dean\'s Office','You are in a very large office the walls look like they are made of the finest\nwoods, and the floor appears to be made of the shiniest marble, but\nupon closer examination you find both to be made of a strange unknown\nsubstance.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6875,0,0,0,'Office of the Master of Admissions','You are in a fairly large room, the room is neat and organized.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6876,0,0,0,'Office of the Master of Admissions','You are in a fairly big room.  The room appears neat, and organized.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6877,0,0,0,'Office of the Master of Admissions','You are in a fairly large office.  The office appears to be neat and\norganized.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6878,0,0,0,'Office of the Master of Admissions','You are in a fairly large office.  The office appears to be neat and\norganized.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6879,0,0,0,'The Office of the Dean\'s Secretary','  You are in the humble office of the Dean\'s secretary, it is clean but\nbears a scent that smells a lot like your grandmother.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6880,0,0,0,'The Office of the Dean\'s Secretary','You are in a humble office.  It is clean but bears a faint scent a lot like\nyour grandmother.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6881,0,0,0,'The Office of The Dean\'s Secretary','You are in a humble office.  The Office is clean, but bears a faint scent\na lot like you grandmother.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6882,0,0,0,'The Office of the Dean\'s Secretary','You are in a humble office.  It is clean but smells a lot like your grandmother.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6883,0,0,0,'Office of the Circle\'s Accountant','  This office is very tidy, and neat.  No pictures adorn the walls, in fact\nit is terribly ordinary and plain.  Sea mist swirls about the room.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6884,0,0,0,'Office of the Circle\'s Accountant','  You are in a rather ordinary office.  It is clean, however no pictures adorn\nthe walls, and only an ordinary looking desk, and chair sit here.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6885,0,0,0,'Office of the Circle\'s Accountant','  You are in a rather ordinary looking office.  The office is simple, and\nrather plain.  An eerie feeling comes over you, perhaps it is the\nstale smell of the office?\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6886,0,0,0,'Office of the Circle\'s Accountant','  You are in a rather ordinary looking office.  The office is simple, and\nrather plain.  An eerie feeling comes over you, perhaps it is the\nstale smell of the office?\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6887,0,0,0,'Office of the Master of Religious Studies','     You are in a fairly large office.  The office appears white, gray, or\nblack depending on where you stand in the room.  Different pictures of deities\nadorn the walls.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6888,0,0,0,'Office of the Master of Religious Studies','  You are in a fairly large office.  The office appears white, gray, or\nblack depending on where you stand in the room, pictures of different deities,\nadorn the walls.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6889,0,0,0,'The Office of the Master of Religious Studies','  You are in a fairly large office.  The office appears white, gray, or\nblack depending on where you stand in the room.  Pictures of different deities,\nadorn the walls.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6890,0,0,0,'The Office of the Master of Religious Studies','  You are in a fairly large office.  The office appears white, gray, or\nblack depending on where you stand in the room.  Pictures of different deities,\nadorn the walls.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6891,0,0,0,'Office of the Master of Magical Studies','  You are in an enormous room, the colors of the walls continually change\nand feast your eyes on the most wonderful sensations.  You feel tired\nthen hyper, your emotions stir.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6892,0,0,0,'Office of the Master of Magical Studies','     You are in an enormous room, the colors of the walls continually change\nand feast your eyes on the most wonderful sensations.  You feel tired\nthen hyper, your emotions stir.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6893,0,0,0,'Office of the Master of Magical Studies','   You are in an enormous room.  The colors of the room feast your eyes\non one of the most sensual experiences the eyes can give.  You feel tired\nthen your emotions stir.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6894,0,0,0,'Office of the Master of Magical Studies','     You are in an enormous room.  The colors of the room feast your eyes\non one of the most sensual experiences the eyes can give.  You feel tired\nthen hyper, your emotions stir.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6895,0,0,0,'Staff Lounge','     You are in a large very comfortable looking room.  No doubt this is\nwhere the staff comes to take a break from classes.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6896,0,0,0,'Staff Lounge','     You are in a large very comfortable looking room.  No doubt this is\nwhere the staff comes to take a break from classes.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6897,0,0,0,'Staff Lounge','     You are in a large very comfortable looking room.  No doubt this\nis where the staff comes to take a break from classes.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6898,0,0,0,'Staff Lounge','     You are in a large very comfortable looking room.  No doubt this is\nwhere the staff comes to take a break from classes.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6899,0,0,0,'A Great Wall of Art in the Dean\'s Office','  You are standing before a great wall of art in the Dean\'s office, the wall\nis covered with a dozen magical, art works, each continually shifting and\nchanging to please every viewer.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6900,0,0,0,'Meeting Area in the Dean\'s Office','  You are in a meeting area in the Dean\'s Office, this is where the Dean\nhas little \"chats\" with staff, and students, the atmosphere in this portion\nof the Dean\'s office puts you in a seriously depressed mood.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6901,0,0,0,'Beside a Couch in the Dean\'s Office','  You are beside a couch in the Dean\'s Office, the couch is clearly used,\na lot during the Dean\'s famous social gatherings, and it is rumored that the\nDean has been caught more than once sleeping on the couch with some of the\nstaff, but don\'t tell his wife.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6902,0,0,0,'Beside a Potted Plant in the Dean\'s Office','  You are next to a potted plant in the Dean\'s office.  The plant doesn\'t look\nreal, however a note is hung just under it, and as you notice the note, you\nsee a flux in the color of the plant.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6903,0,0,0,'A Mingling Area in the Dean\'s Office','  You are in a small mingling area in the Dean\'s office.  To your west is a\nsmall window where patrons of the Dean\'s social gatherings can obtain the\ndelicious goodies stored on the other side of the bar.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6904,0,0,0,'Before the Entrance to the Dean\'s Private Bar','  You are in a small corner in the Dean\'s Office.  One really neat advantage\nto being Dean is you get lots of neat stuff like a private bar all his own.\nThe Dean certainly uses it a lot, in fact he has gotten quite a reputation\nfor his little \"social gatherings\".  The temperature in this room seems to\nchange rapidly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6905,0,0,0,'Behind the Dean\'s Private Bar','  You are in a small room, an open window to the west allows easy access\nto all the drinks, and goodies behind the bar, by the patrons in the\nDean\'s office.  The floor seems to slither.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6906,0,0,0,'Entrance to the Dean\'s Private Bar','  You are in a very small room, an arch to the south leads into the Dean\'s\noffice.  The bar is clean, and appears to be here, for the Dean\'s social\ngatherings, that he is famed for around the school.  The floor feels a lot\nlike feathers.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6907,0,0,0,'The Office of Sub-Master Bloodmarked','  You are in the small office of Sub-Master Bloodmarked, the room makes\nyou fee good about yourself.  You do not know why, but a true confidence\nsweeps over you.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6908,0,0,0,'Office of Master Stregus','  You are in the perfect room of Master Stregus.  The entire room is a large\nsphere, hollow, and not an object in room is out of place.  The walls flash\nred, then blue, then white then red again.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6910,0,0,0,'A Great Staircase','     You are at the base of a great staircase, the staircase seems to be made\nof a blue plasma like substance completely unknown to you.  The floor, and\nwalls appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6911,0,0,0,'A Hallway Leading through the Study Building','  You are in a large Hallway leading through the study building.  In front of\nyou stands a great staircase.  The floor and walls in this room spin in an\nelliptical fashion, careful you don\'t get dizzy.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6912,0,0,0,'A Hallway Leading through the Study Building','  You are in a large hallway leading through the study building.  The floor\nand walls spin in a cubic fashion, careful you don\'t get dizzy.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6913,0,0,0,'A Hallway Leading through the Study Building','  You are in a large hallway leading through the study building.  The floor\nand walls spin in a circular fashion, careful you don\'t get dizzy.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6914,0,0,0,'A Hallway Leading through the Study Building','  You are in a large hallway leading through the study building.  The floor\nand walls spin in a rectangular fashion, careful you don\'t get dizzy.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6915,0,0,0,'A Hallway Leading through the Study Building','  You are in a large hallway leading through the study building.  The floor\nand walls spin in a octagonal fashion, careful you don\'t get dizzy.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6916,0,0,0,'A Hallway Leading through the Study Building','  You are in a large hallway leading through the study building.  The floor\nand walls spin in a rectangular fashion, careful you don\'t get dizzy.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6917,0,0,0,'A Hallway leading through the Study Building','  You are in a large hallway leading through the study building.  The floor\nand walls spin in a hexagonal fashion, careful you don\'t get dizzy.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6918,0,0,0,'A Hallway leading through the Study Building','  You are in a large hallway leading through the study building.  The floor\nand walls spin in a linear fashion, careful you don\'t get dizzy.\n',42,141312,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6919,0,0,0,'A Line through the Cafeteria','You are in a corral like railing area, where students herd themselves\nthrough to order food.  To the east is a door to the Main Hallway, and to\nthe west is the entrance to the kitchen.\n',-1,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6920,0,0,0,'A Line through the Cafeteria','You are in a corral like rail system where students herd themselves\nthrough in order to eat the cafeteria food.  Everything in the room glimmers\nthen fades, then glimmers then fades.\n',-1,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6921,0,0,0,'By the Large Oven in the Cafeteria','You are by a very large sparkling clean oven in the kitchen.  The oven is\nwhite in color, matching the bright walls, the floor is covered in blood.\n',-1,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6922,0,0,0,'Exit From the Cafeteria','You are at the end of the a corral like rail system, which shuttles\nstudents waiting for food through.  To your east is the exit to the\ncafeteria.\n',-1,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6923,0,0,0,'Before a Great Grill in the Cafeteria','You stand before a great grill in the kitchen, the grill appears to be\nbrand new, and glows with a brilliant shine.  The floor is covered in blood.\n',-1,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6924,0,0,0,'Before a Large Walk in Freezer in the Cafeteria','You stand before a large walk-in freezer.  The freezer, as with everything\nelse in the cafeteria is a bright white.  The freezer is here to store meat,\nand vegetables to be served to the students.  The floor is covered with blood.\n',-1,141320,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6925,0,0,0,'Inside a Freezer','You are within a freezer, shelves line both sides of you, and strangely\nenough there is no blood on the floor.  However, faded images of frightened\nanimals keep appearing in the shiny reflections.\n',-1,141320,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6926,0,0,0,'Deep Inside a Freezer','You are deep within a freezer, shelves line both sides of you, and\nstrangely enough there is no blood on the floor.  However, faded images of\nfrightened animals keep appearing in the shiny reflections.\n',-1,141320,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6927,0,0,0,'A Booth to Sit Down, and Eat In','You are in a small booth where students frequently bring their food from\nthe cafeteria, to eat in.\n',-1,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6928,0,0,0,'A Small Booth to Eat in','You are in a small booth where students frequently bring their food from\nthe cafeteria, to eat in.  A strange noise emanates from everything in the\nroom, and some strange voice sings along with it.  \"ain\'t nothing but a\nhound dog.\"\n',-1,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6929,0,0,0,'A Small Booth to Eat In','You are in a small booth where students frequently bring their food from\nthe cafeteria, to eat in.  A strange noise emanates from everything in the\nroom, and some strange voice sings along with it: \"I love you, you love me.\"\n',-1,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6930,0,0,0,'A Booth to Sit Down, and Eat In','  You are in a small booth where students frequently bring their food from\nthe cafeteria, to eat in.  A strange noise emanates from everything in the\nroom, and some strange voice sings \"take this job, and shove it!\"\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6931,0,0,0,'Waiting Room of the Truant Officer','  You are in a cold, scary place.  The waiting room of the truant officer\nis barren except for a few gold metallic looking chairs.  The entire room\nlooks as if it is build of skeletons piled on top of each other.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6932,0,0,0,'Office of the Circle\'s Truant Officer','  You are in a rather cold feeling office.  The office of the Truant Officer\nof the circle.  This is a very powerful room in that it is a very powerful\nmans office.  The walls seem to whisper in your head to you, \"we are not yet dead, do not imprison us like this.\".\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6933,0,0,0,'Administration Room','  You are in the administration room, this is where students decide on which\ncourses, to take, and find out who teaches which classes, when and where.\nThe walls and floor tickle your body.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6934,0,0,0,'Registration Office','     You are in the warm inviting registration office.  It is here that hopeful\napplicants to the circle apply, and request classes.  The walls and floor\ntickle your body.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6935,0,0,0,'Observation Room','  You are in a small room separated by a semi-permeable shield from the room\nto the east.  The brighter of the students observe testing in the east room\nfrom here.  The not so bright ones enter the testing room to get a closer\nview.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6936,0,0,0,'Experimentation Room','  You are in a room where students, and master alike, come and try new\nincantations, spells, and magic rituals.  The room is protected by\na semi permeable shield to the west, which keeps the harmful results\nof the testing in this room.  The walls and floor appear to glow softly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6937,0,0,0,'Practice Room','     You are in a small room, the room itself has a calming effect on you.\nStudents about to be tested wait in this room for a master to call them\nin to the testing room.  It is understood that this room is only for practicing\nof skills, and spells already known to a good or great degree, it is not\nfor experimentation with new skills, and spells.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6938,0,0,0,'Testing Room','  You are in a room which is one of the most feared in the study building,\nnot because there are great demons in here which not even the masters can\ncontrol, but because it is where all the students are tested.  Truly\nif they are to become a master some day then this room is a bright cobblestone\nthey must travel on many times in their destiny.  The air smells as if you\nwere outside.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6939,0,0,0,'Office of the Secretary of Religious Studies','  You are in a small neat office.  The floor and walls of the office appear\nas if they have been covered in a fake animal fur.  There are doors in the\neast and west wall.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6940,0,0,0,'Master Cleric Salentod\'s Office','  You are in the office of the Master Cleric Salentod.  The office is very\nneat and organized, and smells of sacramental wine.  A sweet voice like that\nof an angel sings in the background.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6941,0,0,0,'Table Before the Student Bar','  You are standing between a collection of tables where students come to\nparty after classes.  The student bar is directly east.  You hear the voice\nof Azotelrar singing in the room.  Your eyes tingle slightly.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6942,0,0,0,'Behind the Student Bar','  You are standing behind the student bar, this is where the bartender\non duty for the students splashes together some of the finest tasting\ndrinks, and ales known to ever inhabit the great realism.  The walls, and\nfloor look as if they are made of a fluid of some sort.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6943,0,0,0,'In the Pews of the Church of the Circle','  You are in a very ordinary looking church pew.  Ordinary except for the\nfact that the floor seems to bounce you up and down for pleasure.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6944,0,0,0,'In the Pews of the Church of the Circle','     You are in a very ordinary looking church pew.  Ordinary except for the\nfact that the floor seems to bounce you up and down for pleasure.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6945,0,0,0,'In the Pews of the Church of the Circle','     You are in a very ordinary looking church pew.  Ordinary except for the\nfact that the floor seems to bounce you up and down for pleasure.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6946,0,0,0,'In the Pews of the Church of the Circle','     You are in a very ordinary looking church pew.  Ordinary except for the\nfact that the floor seems to bounce you up and down for pleasure.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6947,0,0,0,'At the Altar of the Church of the Circle','     You are at a large multi-shaded altar, the altar changes from white to\nblack as you look at it east to west.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6948,0,0,0,'At the Altar of the Church of the Circle','     You are at a large multi-shaded Altar, the Altar changes from white to\nblack as you look at it west to east.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6949,0,0,0,'Main Road','  You are on the main road of the circle village.  You are completely\nsurrounded by a blue plasma-likes substance except to the east, west,\nand south.  To the south is Pzanthar\'s Jewel Shop.  A door leads north.\n',42,141312,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6950,0,0,0,'Main Road','You are on the main road of Circle Village.  You are completely\nsurrounded by a blue plasma-like substance, except for exits to the east,\nand west.\n',-1,141312,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6951,0,0,0,'Pzanthar\'s Jewel Shop','  You are in the very distinguished shop of Pzanthar.  The shop is very\nneatly decorated and Pzanthar has put great effort into displaying his\nwhole line of jewels.\n',42,166077,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6952,0,0,0,'Main Road','  You are on the main road of the Circle Village.  Surrounding you except\nfor the south, east and west, is a large blue plasma like substance creating\na wall.  To the south is Caliyon\'s Component Emporium.\n',42,141312,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6953,0,0,0,'Dead End on a Main Road','You are at a dead end on the main road of Circle Village.  You are\ncompletely surrounded by a blue plasma-like field except for an exit to\nthe west.\n',-1,141312,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6954,0,0,0,'Terran\'s Tasty Treats','You are in the Shop of Terran.  Terran\'s Treats are known throughout 5\nRealms as the Best.  He\'s Also the Most Expensive.  His wares are displayed\nvery well, through the clear showcases before you.\n',42,141320,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6955,0,0,0,'Syntar\'s Specialty Shop','You are in Syntar\'s specialty shop, Syntar it appears specializes in Robes,\nand as that is the main dress of the circle, he has a lot and a great variety of\nthem, all displayed about his store.\n',42,141320,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6956,0,0,0,'Caliyon\'s Component Emporium','     You are in a very small hutlike shop, behind the counter is a small,\ngreen curtain to which Caliyon steps behind to get your purchase.\n',42,174269,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6957,0,0,0,'Main Road','     You are on the main road of Circle Village.  Surrounding you except\nfor the east, west, and north is a large blue plasma-like substance creating\na wall.  To the north is The Hall of Arch-Mages.\n',42,141312,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6958,0,0,0,'Wayne\'s Magical Weapons \'R\' Us','You are in a rather dirty, grungy looking shop, the floor seems to be made of\na rather flat looking, rock like substance, broken into perfect\nCubit like pieces of equal length, and width.\n',42,141320,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6959,0,0,0,'Main Road','  You are on the main road of Circle Village.  Surrounding you except for\nfor the east, west, north, and south is a large blue plasma like substance\ncreating a wall.  To the north is The Head Guard\'s Office, to the south is\nthe Lair of Tylon (The Arch-Mage\'s Dragon).\n',42,141320,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6960,0,0,0,'Office of the Head Guard','  You are in the office of the Head Guard of Circle Village.  His\noffice is cluttered with papers, and reports of different mishappenings that\noccur both within the town, and realism to which the village has been in\ncontact with.  It is clear justice for the circle does not stop at the\nvillage boundaries.\n',42,141320,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6961,0,0,0,'Lair of Tylon the Dragon','     You stand in a cave which by the weathering on the grey rock appears\nto be at the top of a great mountain within your realm, but the\nweather itself does not suit it, something is wrong about it.\n',42,141320,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,596,0,'',NULL),
(6962,0,0,0,'Main Road','You are on the main road of Circle Village.  Surrounding you except for\nthe east and west is a large blue plasma-like substance creating a wall.  The\nmain thoroughfare continues to the east and south.  A decrepit building stands\nto the south and appears to be accessible through a door set in its north\nwall.  Strange flashes of colored lights can be seen coming from the lone window\nof the building.\n',43,141320,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6963,0,0,0,'Inside Circle Village','     You are inside Circle Village, the road you stand on seems completely\nclean, and glows with a strange blue looking plasma, the same blue looking\nplasma which seems to surround you completely, except for the road\nwhich continues east, and the Main gate to your west.\n',42,141312,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6964,0,0,0,'At the Gate of Circle Village','  You appear to be walking amongst the stars, although you feel earth\nbeneath your feet, you can see nothing around you except to the east.\nTo the east stands a great wall made of a blue plasma-like substance,\nthe vibrant, and clearly powerful wall attempts to rip apart the very\nexistence of the realm in which you currently breathe, and the\nrealm itself appears to attempt to bash down the wall at its every chance.\n',42,141312,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6965,0,0,0,'Path Leading to Circle Village','You appear to be walking amongst the stars, although you feel earth beneath\nyour feet, you can see nothing around you except to the east where a large\nblue plasma-like wall stands erected.  A decrepit building to the south seems\nto be accessible through a door set in its north wall.  You notice an extremely\noffensive odor emanating from the direction of the building.\n',43,141312,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6966,0,0,0,'Keep of the Dragons','     You are in a large open plain in the wilderness of some realm you\ndo not know.  A large nest sits before you made of trashed straw, and\ncompacted with a blue plasma-like substance.\n',42,141312,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6967,0,0,0,'Path Leading to Circle Village','  You appear to be walking amongst the stars, although you feel earth\nbeneath your feet, you can see nothing around you except to the east,\nwhere a large blue-plasma like wall stands erected in the distance.\n',42,141312,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6968,0,0,0,'The Origin Circle','  You are standing in a large teleportation circle, the circles only\nfunction is to transport all who enter back to their home of origin.\nSeventy three glowing crystals each of a different color make up the circle,\nand each of those in turn holds a small flame in a small hollow within them.\n',42,172212,60,10,100,1,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6969,0,0,0,'The Arrivals Circle','  You stand in a large circle, which appears to be made of many\ndifferent styles of rocks and ivory like substances, seventy three\ntassels lie over each one of the rocks, each tassel lit on fire.\n',42,172212,60,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6970,0,0,0,'Hall of Arch-Mages','  You stand in a large hall, decorated with pictures of arch-mages of\nthe past and present.  The hall itself appears to be made of a white ivory\nlike substance, and the cleaning is absolute.\n',42,141312,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(6971,0,0,0,'Hall of Arch-Mages','  You stand in a large hall, decorated with pictures of arch-mages\nof the past, and present.  The hall itself appears to be made of a white ivory\nlike substance, and the cleaning is absolute.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6972,0,0,0,'Hall of Arch-Mages','  You stand in a large hall, decorated with pictures of arch-mages of the\npast, and present.  The hall itself appears to be made of a white ivory\nlike substance, and the cleaning is absolute.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6973,0,0,0,'Hall of Arch-Mages','  You stand in a large hall, decorated with pictures of arch-mages of the\npast, and present.  The hall itself appears to be made of a white ivory\nlike substance, and the cleaning is absolute.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6974,0,0,0,'Hall of Arch-Mages','  You stand in a large hall, decorated with pictures of arch-mages of the\npast, and present.  The hall itself appears to be made of a white ivory\nlike substance, and the cleaning is absolute.  There is a door the the west.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6975,0,0,0,'Office of the Arch-Mage','     You are in a small, neat tidy office, the type you might find anywhere.\nThere is a door to the east leading into the display hall.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6976,0,0,0,'Hall of Arch-Mages','  You stand in a large hall.  This portion of the hall is largely barren\nand empty.  The hall itself appears to be made of a white ivory like substance\nand the cleaning is absolute.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6977,0,0,0,'Hall of Arch-Mages','  You stand in a large hall.  This portion of the hall is largely barren\nand empty.  The hall itself appears to be made of a white ivory like substance\nand the cleaning is absolute.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6978,0,0,0,'Hall of Arch-Mages','  You stand in a large hall.  This portion of the hall is largely barren\nand empty.  The hall itself appears to be made of a white ivory like substance\nand the cleaning is absolute.  There is a doorway leading north.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6979,0,0,0,'A Storage Room','This storage room is dirty, and dusty, and seems to have been forgotten\nabout, for a very long time.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6980,0,0,0,'A Storage Room','This storage room is very neat, tidy, and clean, and seems to used quite a bit.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6981,0,0,0,'Office of the Head-Janitor','     You are in the office of the Head Janitor, it doesn\'t look as if anyone\nhas been here in quite a while though.  There is a door the the south.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6985,0,0,0,'Office of Sub-Master Galar','     The office is decorated with a wallpaper that is covered with\neyes, the whole atmosphere gives you the feeling that someone is watching\nyou.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(6987,0,0,0,'A Dark Laboratory','As you survey your immediate surroundings, a foul odor wafts across the room\nand assaults your nostrils.  Wanting to determine the source of your aggravation\nyou quickly realize that it is not just a single malodorous scent, but rather\nan entire medley of disgusting aromas combining above a multitude of bubbling\nflasks and vile-colored beakers that lie strewn all about this laboratory.\n',43,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,84,0,'',NULL),
(6988,0,0,0,'A Dusty Laboratory','A thin layer of dust covers everything in this building.  Massive oak shelves\nline the walls, stuffed with tomes covered with strange symbols along their\nspines.  Your head begins to ache and you quickly look away from the books and\nnotice a single large table resting in the middle of the room.\n',43,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,84,0,'',NULL),
(7000,46,-127,3,'Peasants House',' Sparsely furnished and considerably small this home is little\nmore than a shack made of four walls and a roof.  In the far corner\nbarely able to be seen is a wobbly set of stairs which lead to an upper\nlevel.  A small cook stove, 2 stools and small stack of dishes is about\nall you can see in here.  A small door is set into the east wall.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,120,0,'',NULL),
(7001,47,-127,3,'West Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your west\nyou can see the poor housing district with its several shacks\nthat the peasants call homes.  To you east is the side of the\nbailey walls and to the north you can see a large grid iron\ngate.  To the east of you are a series of vertical trellises\ncovered with greenery which cover the walls of the inner bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7002,49,-127,3,'Clergy Dining Hall',' This is the main dining hall for the general clergy of the\nCathedral.  A long table runs east west through the room, and\nyou can see a swinging door to the south that appears to lead\ninto the kitchen.  The only heat in the room comes from a small\nfireplace set into the south wall that is shared with the\nkitchen.  Small lamps hang on the wall granted the room its\nlight source and the odor of burning oil is strong in the air.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7003,50,-127,3,'Clergy Dining Hall',' This is the main dining hall for the general clergy of the\nCathedral.  A long table runs east west through the room, and you\ncan see a door set in the south wall.  Small lamps hang on the\nwall granted the room its light source and the odor of burning\noil is strong in the air.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7004,51,-127,3,'Storage Closet',' There is little in here that is surprising.  Simple cleaning\nsupplies, fresh linens, a small straw broom and damp mop\ncomplete with bucket.  Nothing appears to be worth taking as it\nis old and beat up.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,3,120,0,'',NULL),
(7005,58,-127,3,'Experimental Casting Chamber',' Covered in arcane runes, pentagrams, and chalk drawings the\nroom is covered from top to bottom in magical protections.  A\nlarge circle drawn with a glowing chalk stands out on the floor,\nwhile an opening can be seen in the south wall.  The smell of\nburnt flesh and sulfur is extremely strong in the air.  The only\nlight in the room comes from the same small globes placed\naround the tower.  To the west a bare patch of wall catches you\nattention.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,4,'',NULL),
(7006,59,-127,3,'Food Storage Room',' This room is used to store the food used in preparation of the\ntower\'s meals.  You see numerous sealed jars of food stores\nwaiting to be cooked for the tower.  A small door lies to the\neast.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,5,120,0,'',NULL),
(7007,60,-127,3,'Tower Kitchen',' Small but at least decently clean, this is where the towers\nmeals are prepared.  You can see a simple fireplace set into the\nsouth wall, a small door to the west and swinging door to the\nsouth beside the fireplace.  Small globes of light are attached\nto the wall keeping the kitchen well lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,120,0,'',NULL),
(7008,62,-127,3,'East Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your east\n you can see the poor housing district with its several shacks\nthat the peasants call homes.  To you west is the side of the\nbailey walls and to the north you can see a large grid iron\ngate.  To the west of you are a series of vertical trellises\ncovered with greenery which cover the walls of the inner bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7009,63,-127,3,'Peasants House',' Sparsely furnished and considerably small this home is little\nmore than a shack made of four walls and a roof.  In the far\ncorner barely able to be seen is a wobbly set of stairs which\nlead to an upper level.  A small cook stove, 2 stools and small\nstack of dishes is about all you can see in here.  A small door\nis set into the west wall.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,120,0,'',NULL),
(7010,46,-128,3,'Peasants House','Sparsely furnished and considerably small this home is little\nmore than a shack made of four walls and a roof.  In the far\ncorner barely able to be seen is a wobbly set of stairs which\nlead to an upper level.  A small cook stove, 2 stools and small\nstack of dishes is about all you can see in here.  A small door\nis set into the east wall.\n',-1,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7011,47,-128,3,'West Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your west\n you can see the poor housing district with its several shacks\nthat the peasants call homes.  To you east is the side of the\nbailey walls.  The road continues to the north and south.  To\nthe east of you are a series of vertical trellises covered with\ngreenery which cover the walls of the inner bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7012,49,-128,3,'Kitchen',' This is the Cathedral\'s kitchen to provide food for the\npermanent clergy which reside in the Cathedral.  It is simply\nfurnished with the basics needed to provide adequate meals.  A\nsmall fireplace shares space with a swinging door in the north\nwall and you can see a small door to the south as well.  Oil\nlamps hang on the wall lighting the room.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7013,50,-128,3,'Hallway',' Small and just barely lit by small oil burning\nlamps this hallway provides access to the Cathedral\'s dining\nhall and a couple of the clerics personal living cells.  The\nfloor is polished clean and smooth from years of use and the\nwalls are made of simple stone and mortar.  Doors can be seen\nboth to the north and south.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,120,0,'',NULL),
(7014,51,-128,3,'Hallway',' Small and just barely lit by small oil burning lamps this\nhallway provides access to the Cathedral\'s dining hall and a couple\nof the clerics personal living cells.  The floor is polished clean\nand smooth from years of use and the walls are made of simple stone\nand mortar.  Doors can be seen both to the north and south.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,120,0,'',NULL),
(7015,52,-128,3,'Basement of the Cathedral','Standing at the base of a set of stairs you are in the basement\nlevel of the Citadel\'s Cathedral.  On the northeast wall you can\nsee an oil painting hanging in between two oil lamps, one which is\nmysterious unlit.  A small hallway continues through this level to\nthe west.\n',-1,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,120,4,'',NULL),
(7016,58,-127,2,'In a Pit',' Surrounded by hundreds of ghastly creatures, both dead and\nalive, the stench almost overwhelms you.  You determine that\nthese creatures are the remnants of hideous experiments which\nare undertaken by the towers senior wizards.  A portal stands\nopen in the north wall of the pit but is about twelve feet above\nyour head.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,15,200,4,'',NULL),
(7017,59,-128,3,'Base of the Tower',' As you step into this room you begin to feel as light as\nair! You realize that you are able to fly up through the main\nlevels of the Tower from this shaft.  The space is well lit\nwith small magical globes of light securely fashioned to the\nwalls.  Otherwise there is little decorating the space.  You\ncan see a small door to the east and secure steel door to the\nnorthwest.\n',46,131081,65,0,0,0,0,0,20,500,0,'',NULL),
(7018,60,-128,3,'Dining Hall',' Furnished with little but a few chairs and a simple table the\nroom appears to be used strictly for eating.  Knowing mages\nand their generally attitudes towards others it is not surprising\nthat they do not seem to gather and discuss issues around the\ntable like most people.  The room is lit with the same globes\nfound around the tower.  A simple fireplace shares the north\nwall with a swinging door that most likely goes to the towers\nkitchen.  A simple door is set into the west all and the room\ncontinues to the south.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7019,62,-128,3,'East Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your east\nyou can see the poor housing district with its several shacks\nthat the peasants call homes.  To you west is the side of the\nbailey walls.  The road continues to the north and south.  To\nthe west of you are a series of vertical trellises covered with\ngreenery which cover the walls of the inner bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7020,63,-128,3,'Peasants House',' Sparsely furnished and considerably small this home is little\nmore than a shack made of four walls and a roof.  In the far\ncorner barely able to be seen is a wobbly set of stairs which\nlead to an upper level.  A small cook stove, 3 stools and small\nstack of dishes is about all you can see in here.  A small door\nis set into the west wall.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,108,0,'',NULL),
(7021,46,-129,3,'Workman\'s House',' Although not the greatest housing and not in the best part of\nthe town, this small home appears to be kept neat and in the\nbest repair that the owner can manage.  You see dishes neatly\nstacked against the far wall, a small table and chairs in the\ncorner ready to be pulled out when needed, a small cook stove\npolished neatly after its last use, and small mats used for\nresting on.  A small set of stairs in the back corner appear to\nlead to an upper level and a thick wood door is set in the east\nwall leading back out to Mordel Avenue.  The house is kept\nmoderately lit by small oil lamps attached to the walls.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,120,0,'',NULL),
(7022,47,-129,3,'West Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your west\nyou can see the poor housing district with its several shacks that\nthe peasants call homes.  To you east is the side of the bailey\nwalls.  The road continues to the north and southeast.  To the east\nof you are a series of vertical trellises covered with greenery\nwhich cover the walls of the inner bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7023,49,-129,3,'Storage',' This room is used to store the food used in preparation of\nthe clergy\'s meals.  You see numerous sealed jars of food stores\nwaiting to be cooked for the members of the clergy.  A small door\nlies to the north.  Oddly you notice that several tracks lead up\nto the southwest corner of the room yet there is no stores on the\nshelves near that wall.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,120,4,'',NULL),
(7024,50,-129,3,'Eerie Cell','This is the cell of the cleric in charge of sacrifices for the\nCathedral.  You see ghastly paintings and instruments of torture\nabout the room and fight to keep your breakfast down.  A small\ncot sits to one side the room made up of blood red sheets.  A\nfew small candles made of pure black wax burn on a shelf upon\none wall to pay homage to some deity of evil.  The room reeks of\nstale air and the scent of blood.  A door hidden slightly by a\ntapestry can be seen to the north.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,120,0,'',NULL),
(7025,51,-129,3,'Cleric\'s Cell',' This cell belongs to one of the higher clerics of the Cathedral.\nHis station grants him his own cell instead of the room shared by\nthe other clergy in the attic.  Although small, the room is filled\nwith pieces of furniture, tomes, and articles of clothing.  You see\na small doorway to the north.  A small lamp hangs from the wall\nkeeping the room constantly lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,120,0,'',NULL),
(7026,58,-128,2,'In a Pit',' Surrounded by hundreds of ghastly creatures, both dead and alive,\nthe stench almost overwhelms you.  You determine that these\ncreatures are the remnants of hideous experiments which are\nundertaken by the towers senior wizards.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,180,0,'',NULL),
(7027,59,-128,2,'In a Pit',' Surrounded by hundreds of ghastly creatures, both dead and\nalive, the stench almost overwhelms you.  You determine that\nthese creatures are the remnants of hideous experiments which\nare undertaken by the towers senior wizards.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,180,0,'',NULL),
(7028,60,-129,3,'Dining Hall',' Furnished with little but a few chairs and a simple table the\nroom appears to be used strictly for eating.  Knowing mages and\nthere generally attitudes towards others it is not surprising that\nthey do not seem to gather and discuss issues around the table like\nmost people.  The room is lit with the same globes found around the\ntower.  A large tapestry depicting the Citadel hangs from the\nsoutheast corner of the room.  The room continues to the north a\nbit farther.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,15,120,0,'',NULL),
(7029,62,-129,3,'East Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your east\nyou can see the poor housing district with its several shacks that\nthe peasants call homes.  The road continues to the north and\nsouthwest.  To the west of you are a series of vertical trellises\ncovered with greenery which cover the walls of the inner bailey.\nDirectly to the south of you lie the massive walls of the Citadel.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7030,63,-129,3,'Workman\'s House',' Although not the greatest housing and not in the best part of\nthe town, this small home appears to be kept neat and in the best\nrepair that the owner can manage.  You see dishes neatly stacked\nagainst the far wall, a small table and chairs in the corner ready\nto be pulled out when needed, a small cook stove polished neatly\nafter its last use, and small mats used for resting on.  A small set\nof stairs in the back corner appear to lead to an upper level\nand a thick wood door is set in the east wall leading back out\nto Mordel Avenue.  The house is kept moderately lit by small oil\nlamps attached to the walls.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,120,0,'',NULL),
(7031,48,-130,3,'West Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your southwest\nyou can see the massive walls of the Citadel itself.  To you northeast\nis the side of the bailey walls covered with vertical trellises and\ngreenery.  The road continues to the northwest and southeast.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7032,61,-130,3,'East Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your\nsoutheast you can see the massive walls of the Citadel\nitself.  To you northwest is the side of the bailey walls\ncovered with vertical trellises and greenery.  The road\ncontinues to the northeast and southwest.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7033,49,-131,3,'West Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your\nsouthwest you can see the massive walls of the Citadel itself.\nTo you north is the side of the bailey walls which are covered\nwith vertical trellises and greenery.  The road continues to the\nnorthwest and east.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7034,50,-131,3,'West Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your south\nyou can see a small shop entrance.  To you northeast is the side of\nthe bailey walls which are covered with vertical trellises and\ngreenery.  The road continues to the west and southeast.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7035,59,-131,3,'East Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your south\nlies the entrance to a small tavern, while to your northwest is\nthe side of the bailey walls which are covered with vertical\ntrellises and greenery.   The road continues to the southwest and\neast.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7036,60,-131,3,'East Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your\nsoutheast lie the massive walls of the Citadel, while to your north\nis the side of the bailey walls covered with vertical trellises and\ngreenery.  The road continues to the west and northeast.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7037,50,-132,3,'Braddock\'s Mercantile',' Although small in size, this little shop is packed tight with\nevery conceivable household and travel item you can imagine.  You\nsee wicker furniture, solid oak furniture, food stuffs, water skins,\nlanterns, torches, medical supplies, pots and pans, and the\nlist just goes on.  Although packed tight, the shop is in perfect\norder, with every item in its proper place where Braddock wants\nit.  A clear path leads to a small set of stairs at the back of\nthe shop.\n',46,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7038,51,-132,3,'West Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your south\nand west you can see a small shop entrance, while to you\nnortheast is the side of the bailey walls which are covered with\nvertical trellises and greenery.  The road continues to the\nnorthwest and southeast.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7039,53,-132,3,'Base of the Bailey Gate Tower',' Slightly cramped for space this is about the size of an average\ngate tower for a small keep.  You can see wood barricades and other\nstandard items you would expect to see the guard have on hand lying\naround the edges of the tower for quick access should a riot begin\nin the Citadel.  You can see a doorway set in the south wall of the\ntower and a small set of stairs that wind their way around the\ninside of the tower up to the next level.  Oil lamps are attached to\nthe walls of the tower for light.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7040,56,-132,3,'Base of the Bailey Gate Tower','  Slightly cramped for space this is about the size of an average\ngate tower for a small keep.  You can see wood barricades and\nother standard items you would expect to see the guard have on\nhand lying around the edges of the tower for quick access should\na riot begin in the Citadel.  You can see a doorway set in the\nsouth wall of the tower and a small set of stairs that wind\ntheir way around the inside of the tower up to the next level.\nOil lamps are attached to the walls of the tower for light.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7041,58,-132,3,'East Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your south\nand east you can see a small shop entrance, while to you northwest\nis the side of the bailey walls which are covered with vertical\ntrellises and greenery.  The road continues to the northeast and\nsouthwest.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7042,59,-132,3,'Drunken Boar Tavern',' Small and filthy, the tavern hardly portrays the feeling of\nwelcome.  Filthy mine guards and free mine workers are scattered\nabout the room waiting for the next shift change.  Broken pottery\nand empty mugs lie strewn about the floor as though it has not been\nswept in some time.  A simple bar has been set up to the south and\nyou can see two large kegs of what you guess to be some kind of mead\nor ale behind it.  Off in corner you see a small area where it\nappears someone prepares a cheap meal if that is a customers\ndesire.  In the other corner you spot a small ladder mounted to\nthe wall that appears to go up into an overhead loft.\n',46,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,30,120,0,'',NULL),
(7043,51,-133,3,'Gena\'s Breads and Pastry Shop',' This small shop has an amazing aroma of fresh baked pastries and\nbreads which immediately sets your stomach growling.  Two small\nshelves separate the small baking area from the customer area.\nTwo signs on the shelves say \"Day Old\" and \"Fresh\".  Hanging\nnear the door is a small wind chime that rings when brushed up\nagainst by those entering the shop to alert Gena.  Behind the\nshelves you see barrels of flour and fresh fruits waiting to be\nbaked into fresh pastries and delicious breads.  A set of stairs\nalso run up the south wall to a room overhead.  Two small doors\nlead to the north and east out onto Mordel Avenue.\n',46,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7044,52,-133,3,'West Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your west\nyou can see a small shop entrance, while to you north is the side\nof the bailey walls which are covered with vertical trellises and\ngreenery.  The road continues to the northwest and east.  To the\nsouth of you lies one of the better housing districts of town.\nYou can see a small traders house to the southwest and a well built\nhouse of a nobleman directly to the south of you.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7045,53,-133,3,'West Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your south\nyou can see the house of a rich merchant, while to your north is one\nof the gate towers to the bailey walls, a small door is set into its\nbase.  The road continues to the west and the outer bailey can be\nseen to the east.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7046,54,-133,4,'Outer Bailey',' Paved with cheap extracted stone from the mines, the outer bailey\nis the general gathering place of local peasants and such.  A few\nbeggars and diseased peasants lie along the edges of the bailey\nbegging for a few coins.  Directly to the north of you lie the gates\nto the inner bailey.  The outer bailey continues to the east and\nsouth while West Mordel Avenue begins to the west of you.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7047,55,-133,4,'Outer Bailey',' Paved with cheap extracted stone from the mines, the outer bailey\nis the general gathering place of local peasants and such.  A few\nbeggars and diseased peasants lie along the edges of the bailey\nbegging for a few coins.  Directly to the north of you lie the gates\nto the inner bailey.  The outer bailey continues to the west and\nsouth while East Mordel Avenue begins to the east of you.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7048,56,-133,3,'East Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  To your south\nyou can see the entrance to the stables, while to your north is one\nof the gate towers to the bailey walls, a small door is set into\nits base.  The road continues to the east and the outer bailey\ncan be seen to the west.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7049,57,-133,3,'East Mordel Avenue',' This is the main avenue which runs through town.  The road\ncontinues to the west and northeast.  North of you lie the bailey\nwalls which are covered with trellises and greenery.  To the east\nyou can see an entrance into the Black Dragon Inn.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7050,58,-133,3,'Black Dragon Inn',' While poorly lit and only moderately clean, the inn looks\nacceptable for a nights stay.  A small counter can be seen\nto the south behind which is a door most likely leading to the\nservants quarters.  Off to the east you can see a small set of\nstairs which lead up to the upper floor.  Both the north and\nwest walls have doors leading out to East Mordel Avenue.\n',46,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,30,120,0,'',NULL),
(7051,51,-134,3,'Traders House',' This is the home of one of wealthier traders of the Citadel.\nWhile not what people would call large for a home, it is decorated\nand furnished with above average items and is well kept and neat,\nhinting at servants.  Oil lamps burn brightly from overhead and\nyou discover your dirt covered boots are making a complete mess\nof the carpet.  The main door to the house is to the north and\na set of stairs lead up to the upper floor of the house.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,15,120,0,'',NULL),
(7052,52,-134,3,'Nobleman\'s House','  Either a distant cousin to the King or else a great grandson to\nsome war hero the owner of this home is considered a nobleman of\nthe town and draws his income from the royal treasury.  His home\nhas been decorated with lavish paintings, plush carpets, and\nfurniture of the best kind.  Hanging from the ceiling is a\nmagical lamp similar to those used in the Citadel Tower.  The\nentrance to the house is to the north and a set of stairs runs\nup the south wall into the upper level of the home.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7053,53,-134,3,'Merchant\'s House',' This home belongs to one of the richest merchants of the Citadel.\nThe home is furnished with exotic furnishings from distant lands.\nAn incense burning gives the room a strong odor of lilac, while\na weird flickering lantern of some type hangs from the ceiling\ndimly lighting the room and producing weird moving shadows on\nthe walls.  The homes entrance lies behind a large screen to the\nnorth and a set of solid crafted stairs spiral up out of the\nroom in the northeast corner.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7054,54,-134,4,'Outer Bailey',' Paved with cheap extracted stone from the mines, the outer bailey\nis the general gathering place of local peasants and such.  A few\nbeggars and diseased peasants lie along the edges of the bailey\nbegging for a few coins.  The outer bailey continues to the north,\neast and south of you, while the richer housing of the Citadel lies\nto your west.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7055,55,-134,3,'Outer Bailey',' Paved with cheap extracted stone from the mines, the outer bailey\nis the general gathering place of local peasants and such.  A few\nbeggars and diseased peasants lie along the edges of the bailey\nbegging for a few coins.  Directly to the east of you lies an\nentrance into the stables.  The outer bailey continues to the north,\neast and south of you.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7056,56,-134,3,'Citadel Stables',' Littered with straw and sawdust the stable is kept fairly clean.\nYou can see stacks of feed bags and hay for the horses and different\ninstruments for grooming and cleaning up after the animals.  The\nstalls are to the east of you and a small ladder goes up into a\nloft overhead.  Oil lamps are hung by the door away from any\nstraw to keep the stables lit at all times of the day.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,140,0,'',NULL),
(7057,57,-134,3,'In the Stalls',' Although appearing as though just cleaned, the stalls reek of\nanimal manure and horse hair.  A small manger is here for the\nanimal to eat out of and a tie has been left hanging here if\nanother horse needs to be put into the stalls.  The stables\ncontinue to the west.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7058,58,-134,3,'Servants Quarters',' A couple of small beds, a wash basin, and two small chests are\nabout the only things that are visible in this small cramped room.\nA door leads to the north into the lobby of the Black Dragon Inn.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7059,53,-135,3,'Base of the Citadel Gate Tower',' Slightly larger than the gate towers to the Inner Bailey the tower\nis still fairly cramped for space.  Locking bars and such can be seen\nstacked against one wall in case of a siege on the Citadel.  A set of\nstairs spirals around the outer wall of the tower leading up to the\nnext level and a door to the east leads out to the outer bailey.\nAttached to the walls are small oil lamps to keep the tower lit for\nthe guards.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,120,0,'',NULL),
(7060,54,-135,3,'Outer Bailey',' Paved with cheap extracted stone from the mines, the outer bailey\nis the general gathering place of local peasants and such.  A few\nbeggars and diseased peasants lie along the edges of the bailey\nbegging for a few coins.  Directly to the south of you lies the\nmassive Citadel gates.  The outer bailey continues to the north and east\nof you while a door to the west of you appears to lead inside the west\ngate tower of the Citadel.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7061,55,-135,3,'Outer Bailey',' Paved with cheap extracted stone from the mines, the outer bailey\nis the general gathering place of local peasants and such.  A few\nbeggars and diseased peasants lie along the edges of the bailey\nbegging for a few coins.  Directly to the south of you lies the\nmassive Citadel gates.  The outer bailey continues to the north and\nwest of you, while a door to the east of you appears to lead into\nthe east gate tower of the Citadel.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7062,56,-135,3,'Base of the Citadel Gate Tower',' Slightly larger than the gate towers to the Inner Bailey the\ntower is still fairly cramped for space.  Locking bars and such can\nbe seen stacked against one wall in case of a siege on the Citadel.\nA set of stairs spirals around the outer wall of the tower\nleading up to the next level and a door to the west leads out to\nthe outer bailey.  Attached to the walls of the tower are small\noil lamps to keep the tower lit for the guards.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,120,0,'',NULL),
(7063,46,-127,4,'Attic',' Cold and drafty, this is where the peasants that live in this\nshack of a house are forced to sleep.  Covered in straw you can see\na spot towards the south wall where the straw is packed down.  A\nsmall wobbly set of stairs lead down to the main room of the house.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,96,0,'',NULL),
(7064,49,-127,4,'Bishop Mercees\' Office',' This is the personal office of Bishop Mercees.  A small desk,\nseveral wall hangings, and a small wardrobe are the only furnishings\nof the room.  The floor is bare stone and extremely cold.  A small\nfirepot sits in the far northeastern part of the room but it\nprovides little heat for the room.  A small spiral staircase\nleads up to another chamber above this one.  A door stands to\nthe south.  The room is kept lit by small oil lamps fastened\nsecurely to the walls.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,120,0,'',NULL),
(7065,50,-127,4,'Pews',' Made of solid cherry the pews are quite sturdy.  As you look\ncloser you notice that many of the pews are actually soaked in blood.  Under each\npew you find a few small clay bowls.  The church aisle is south\nof you from this point while more pews can be seen to the east.\nHanging along the wall you see small oil lamps.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(7066,51,-127,4,'Pews',' Made of solid cherry the pews are quite sturdy.  As you look\ncloser you notice that many of the pews are actually soaked in blood.  Under each pew you find a few small\nclay bowls.  The church aisle is south of you from this point\nwhile more pews can be seen to the west.  Hanging along the wall\nyou see small oil lamps.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(7067,0,0,0,'Small Royal Garden',' This garden is generally tended by the clergy of the Cathedral\nfor the King and his family to use.  Several rose bushes and small\nferns are planted around the garden.  In the center there is a\nsmall fountain and bird bath.  From the fountain small channels of\nwater run throughout the garden keeping the garden constantly watered.\nA small gate to the southeast is provided for privacy.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7068,54,-127,4,'Before the Keep Doors','You are standing before the doors to the keep of the Citadel.\nThe doors themselves are made of carved obsidian taken from the\nmines below the Citadel.  Etched in their surface is the crest of\nthe royal family.  Hanging from the doors is a large sign.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7069,55,-127,4,'Before the Keep Doors',' You are standing before the doors to the keep of the Citadel.\nThe doors themselves are made of carved obsidian taken from the\nmines below the Citadel.  Etched in their surface is the crest of\nthe royal family.  Hanging from the doors is a large sign.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7070,57,-127,4,'Small Garden for Mages',' This garden is generally tended by the mages of the Tower for\nthe mages of the tower to use.  Several rose bushes and small\nferns are planted around the garden.  In the center there is a\nsmall fountain and bird bath.  From the fountain small channels\nof water run throughout the garden keeping the garden\nconstantly watered.  A small gate to the southwest is provided\nfor privacy.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7071,58,-127,4,'Dormitory',' This is the dormitory for the apprentice mages who come to study\nin the Tower.  It is quite bare of any objects besides a single bed\nand foot locker for each student.  Obviously the apprentices are not\nexpected to spend long hours in this part of the Tower.  A door lies\nto the south and the dormitory continues to the east.  Attached to\nthe walls, small globes of light keep the dormitory well lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7072,59,-127,4,'Dormitory',' This is the dormitory for the apprentice mages who come to study\nin the Tower.  It is quite bare of any objects besides a single bed\nand foot locker for each student.  Obviously the apprentices are not\nexpected to spend long hours in this part of the Tower.  The dormitory\ncontinues to the west.  Attached to the walls, small globes of light\nkeep the dormitory well lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7073,60,-127,4,'In the Stacks',' The library of the mages is quite extensive.  Unfortunately nothing\nof any real value to you seems to be here.  Probably any tomes of\nmagical nature are held by the master mages of the Tower.  All\nyou seem to find are simple tomes of histories that are boring and\nlong.  Small globes of light attached to the walls provide you light\nto read by.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,15,130,0,'',NULL),
(7074,63,-127,4,'Attic',' Cold and drafty, this is where the peasants that live in this shack\nof a house are forced to sleep.  Covered in straw you can see a spot\ntowards the south wall where the straw is packed down.  A small\nwobbly set of stairs lead down to the main room of the house.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,96,0,'',NULL),
(7075,46,-128,4,'Sleeping Room',' This room is used as a common sleeping room by the peasants that\nlive in this house.  There is one small bed, a pile of straw and a\nsmall chest in the room, but otherwise it is completely barren.\nAlthough a bit drafty the room is at least moderately decent for\nliving.  A set of stairs descends down out of the room to the lower\nlevel.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,108,0,'',NULL),
(7076,49,-128,4,'Sacrificial Altar',' A smooth slab of obsidian rest here on two short columns.  Around\nits edges are channels to collect the blood of victims as they are\nsacrificed.  At each corner the channels have holes in them and\nhangers so that the blood can be collected and distributed among the\nchurch fanatics.  Behind the altar is a large stain glass window\ndepicting a bloody sacrifice of an innocent maiden.  You find a\ndoor to the north and a door to the south both blocked from view\nby simple silk screens.  Small oil lamps attached to the walls\nkeep the altar area dimly lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,140,0,'',NULL),
(7077,50,-128,4,'Church Aisle',' This aisle runs through the center of the church from the altar\nto the west to the grand entry to the east.  A runner of crimson\ncarpet covers the floor and the pews are located both to the\nnorth and south.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,30,200,0,'',NULL),
(7078,51,-128,4,'Church Aisle',' This aisle runs through the center of the church from the altar\nto the west to the grand entry to the east.  A runner of crimson\ncarpet covers the floor and the pews are located both to the north\nand south.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,30,100,0,'',NULL),
(7079,52,-128,4,'Grand Entry Under the Cathedral Spire',' This is the main entrance to the Cathedral.  Directly overhead\nthe spire of the cathedral stretches upward.  Off to the south of\nthe entry you spot a small set of stairs that head down and a fancy\nstaircase which ascends to the balcony of the Cathedral.  High on the\neast wall hangs a gruesome statue depicting the merciless killing of\na young child.  The doors to the Cathedral are directly to the east.\nOil lamps hang to each side of the doorway.\n',46,131085,12,0,0,0,0,0,30,140,0,'',NULL),
(7080,53,-128,4,'Inner Bailey',' Paved with blocks of fine cut polished stone, with grass evenly\ngrowing in-between each block, the inner bailey is a place for nobles\nand their families to come and socialize, or the King to pronounce\ndecrees from.  Capturing the highlight of the space is a large\nfountain that rest in the center of the inner bailey.  Directly to\nthe west are the doors which lead into the Cathedral and a small gate\ncan be seen to the northwest blocking entrance into a small garden.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7081,54,-128,4,'Inner Bailey',' Paved with blocks of fine cut polished stone, with grass evenly\ngrowing in-between each block, the inner bailey is a place for nobles\nand their families to come and socialize, or the King to pronounce\ndecrees from.  Capturing the highlight of the space is a large\nfountain that rest in the center of the inner bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7082,55,-128,4,'Inner Bailey',' Paved with blocks of fine cut polished stone, with grass evenly\ngrowing in-between each block, the inner bailey is a place for\nnobles and their families to come and socialize, or the King to\npronounce decrees from.  Capturing the highlight of the space is\na large fountain that rest in the center of the inner bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7083,56,-128,4,'Inner Bailey',' Paved with blocks of fine cut polished stone, with grass evenly\ngrowing in-between each block, the inner bailey is a place for nobles\nand their families to come and socialize, or the King to pronounce\ndecrees from.  Capturing the highlight of the space is a large\nfountain that rest in the center of the inner bailey.  Directly to\nthe east are the doors which lead into the Tower and a small gate\ncan be seen to the northeast blocking entrance into a small garden.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7084,57,-128,4,'Tower Entrance',' This small vestibule is the main entrance to the Citadel\'s Tower\nof Magic, otherwise known simply as the Tower.  A pair of doors can\nbe seen to the west and the Grand Hall for Mages is to the east.\nHanging on the wall around the room are arcane phrases from long\nforgotten magical languages that only a master historian would be\ncapable of deciphering.  The room is lit by strange globes of light\nsecurely fastened to the walls.\n',46,131085,12,0,0,0,0,0,30,140,0,'',NULL),
(7085,58,-128,4,'Grand Hall for Mages',' This is the Grand Hall used by the Tower\'s master magicians to\nmake announcements to the Tower populace and hold meetings that\nregard issues concerning the entire Tower.  To the west is a small\nvestibule entrance and to the east is the Central Shaft to the Tower\nwhich has no floor.   As with all rooms in the Tower the room is lit\nby small globes of light securely fastened to the walls.  There are\ntwo doors discreetly placed to the north and south of the room.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(7086,59,-128,4,'Central Shaft',' Whoa! As you enter the shaft and expect to fall you actually\nbegin to float up a bit and have to work to keep yourself at this\nlevel.  Somehow the shaft grants you the ability to fly in order to\nascend or descend throughout the Towers main levels.  The Grand\nHall for Mages can be seen to the west and an arched doorway can\nbe seen to the east.  Small globes of light securely fastened to\nthe walls light the room.\n',46,131081,65,0,0,0,0,0,20,400,0,'',NULL),
(7087,60,-128,4,'Tower Library',' As you enter the Tower\'s Main library you are shocked to see\nnumerous mages flying about the room removing tomes from shelves\nthat are at least twenty feet high.  A large round desk catches your\nattention at the center of the room.  There are several comfortable\nchairs and small reading desks placed throughout this room for\nyou to use while reading.  To the north and the south are the main\nstacks of the library.  An arched doorway to the west will take you\nback out into the central shaft of the Tower.  Small globes of light\nare attached to the walls of the library giving you perfect light to\nread.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,30,120,0,'',NULL),
(7088,63,-128,4,'Sleeping Room',' This room is used as a common sleeping room by the peasants that\nlive in this house.  There is one small bed, a pile of straw and a\nsmall chest in the room, but otherwise it is completely barren.\nAlthough a bit drafty the room is at least moderately decent for\nliving.  A set of stairs descends down out of the room to the\nlower level.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,96,0,'',NULL),
(7089,46,-129,4,'Living Quarters',' Separated into three rooms this is where the workman and his\nfamily sleep and socialize.  There are two bedrooms off of a central\nroom for the workman and his wife and the other for their children.\nThe main living room is furnished with a simple cheap chair and sofa\nwhile the bedrooms each contain a small cot and chest.  A small\nsturdy set of stairs lead back down to the first floor of the\nhouse.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,15,108,0,'',NULL),
(7090,49,-129,4,'Maldar\'s Office',' Cluttered with robes and vestments for different formal functions\nthe office is considerably cramped.  Under a pile of paper and\nvestments you manage to spot a small wooden desk and chair at the\ncenter of the room.  The room itself is extremely hot and stuffy\nand you can smell the rich hickory that must be burning in the small\nfire pot placed in one corner of the room.  A door leading out to the\naltar can be seen to the east and a small set of chairs lead up to\nanother chamber above this one.  Oil lamps hanging around the rooms\nhelp to keep the room lighted.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7091,50,-129,4,'Pews',' Made of solid cherry the pews are quite sturdy.  As you look\ncloser you notice that many of the pews are actually soaked in blood.\nUnder each pew you find a few small clay bowls.  The church aisle is\nnorth of you from this point while more pews can be seen to the east.\nSecurely fastened to the walls you see some small oil lamps used to\nlight the pew area.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(7092,51,-129,4,'Pews',' Made of solid cherry the pews are quite sturdy.  As you look closer\nyou notice that many of the pews are actually soaked in blood.\nUnder each pew you find a few small clay bowls.  The church\naisle is north of you from this point while more pews can be\nseen to the west.  Securely fastened to the walls you see some\nsmall oil lamps used to light the pew area.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(7093,52,-129,4,'Small Public Garden',' This garden is generally tended by the clergy of the Cathedral for\nthe general public to use.  Several small fern plants and young trees\nare planted around the garden.  In the center there is a small\nfountain and bird bath.  From the fountain small channels of water\nrun throughout the garden keeping the garden constantly watered.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,30,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7094,53,-129,4,'Inner Bailey',' Paved with blocks of fine cut polished stone, with grass evenly\ngrowing in-between each block, the inner bailey is a place for nobles\nand their families to come and socialize, or the King to pronounce\ndecrees from.  Capturing the highlight of the space is a large\nfountain that rest in the center of the inner bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7095,54,-129,4,'Edge of a Large Fountain',' Standing at the edge of this magnificent fountain you can\'t\ncomprehend how something of such beauty could exist in this Citadel\nconsidering that the general populace seems so wickedly evil.  Paving\nblocks of fine cut stone polished to a perfect smoothness join up\nneatly with the base of the fountain.  In-between the paving blocks\ngrows an even strip of green grass accenting the grid pattern.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7096,55,-129,4,'Edge of a Large Fountain',' Standing at the edge of this magnificent fountain you can\'t\ncomprehend how something of such beauty could exist in this Citadel\nconsidering that the general populace seems so wickedly evil.  Paving\nblocks of fine cut stone polished to a perfect smoothness join up\nneatly with the base of the fountain.  In-between the paving blocks\ngrows an even strip of green grass accenting the grid pattern.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7097,56,-129,4,'Inner Bailey',' Paved with blocks of fine cut polished stone, with grass evenly\ngrowing in-between each block, the inner bailey is a place for\nnobles and their families to come and socialize, or the King to\npronounce decrees from.  Capturing the highlight of the space is a\nlarge fountain that rest in the center of the inner bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7098,57,-129,4,'Small Public Garden',' This garden is generally tended by the mages of the Tower for the\ngeneral public to use.  Several fern plants and small hardy trees\nare planted around the garden.  In the center there is a small\nfountain and bird bath.  From the fountain small channels of\nwater run throughout the garden keeping the garden constantly\nwatered.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,30,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7099,58,-129,4,'Dormitory',' This is the dormitory for the apprentice mages who come to study\nin the Tower.  It is quite bare of any objects besides a single bed\nand foot locker for each student.  Obviously the apprentices are not\nexpected to spend long hours in this part of the Tower.  The dormitory\ncontinues to the west and a door sits in the north wall.  Attached\nsecurely to the walls, small globes of light keep the dormitory well\nlit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7100,59,-129,4,'Dormitory',' This is the dormitory for the apprentice mages who come to study\nin the Tower.  It is quite bare of any objects besides a single bed\nand foot locker for each student.  Obviously the apprentices are not\nexpected to spend long hours in this part of the Tower.  The dormitory\ncontinues to the west.  Attached securely to the walls, small globes\nof light keep the dormitory well lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7101,60,-129,4,'In the Stacks',' The library of the mages is quite extensive.  Unfortunately\nnothing of any real value to you seems to be here.  Probably any\ntomes of magical nature are held by the master mages of the\nTower.  All you seem to find are simple tomes of histories that are\nboring and long.  Small globes of light have been attached to the\nwalls to provide you with adequate reading light.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,15,120,0,'',NULL),
(7102,63,-129,4,'Living Quarters',' Separated into three rooms this is where the workman and his\nfamily sleep and socialize.  There are two bedrooms off of a\ncentral room for the workman and his wife and the other for their\nchildren.  The main living room is furnished with a simple cheap\nchair and sofa while the bedrooms each contain a small cot and\nchest.  A small sturdy set of stairs lead back down to the first\nfloor of the house.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,108,0,'',NULL),
(7103,51,-130,4,'Barracks Kitchen',' This is the barracks kitchen, from the looks of things its\nbasically each guard for himself when it comes to meals.  A stocked\nlarder can be seen to one side of the room and there are utensils,\npots and pans covering about every square inch of horizontal space.\nIt appears that if you need a pan or utensil you\'ll going to have to\nwash it first.  A swinging door to the east goes to the barracks\nmess hall.  Two oil burning lamps are attached to the walls here to\nprovide light for the kitchen.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,15,120,0,'',NULL),
(7104,52,-130,4,'Barracks Mess',' This is where the guards sit to eat whatever meal they have\nprepared.  Dirty dishes and utensils can be seen covering many of\nthe tabletops.  Other than the chairs and tables used for eating\nthere is little to see in this room besides the swinging door going\nto the kitchen in the west wall, a door to the south and a set of\nstairs ascending up to the second level of the barracks.  The\nentrance door to the barracks can be seen to the east.  Oil burning\nlamps are attached to the walls around the room keeping the mess\nhall constantly lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(7105,53,-130,4,'Inner Bailey',' Paved with blocks of fine cut polished stone, with grass evenly\ngrowing in-between each block, the inner bailey is a place for nobles\nand their families to come and socialize, or the King to pronounce\ndecrees from.  Capturing the highlight of the space is a large\nfountain that rest in the center of the inner bailey.  The entrance\ndoor to the Citadel Barracks can be seen to the west.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7106,54,-130,4,'Edge of a Large Fountain',' Standing at the edge of this magnificent fountain you can\'t\ncomprehend how something of such beauty could exist in this Citadel\nconsidering that the general populace seems so wickedly evil.  Paving\nblocks of fine cut stone polished to a perfect smoothness join up\nneatly with the base of the fountain.  In-between the paving blocks\ngrows an even strip of green grass accenting the grid pattern.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7107,55,-130,4,'Edge of Large Fountain',' Standing at the edge of this magnificent fountain you can\'t\ncomprehend how something of such beauty could exist in this Citadel\nconsidering that the general populace seems so wickedly evil.  Paving\nblocks of fine cut stone polished to a perfect smoothness join up\nneatly with the base of the fountain.  In-between the paving blocks\ngrows an even strip of green grass accenting the grid pattern.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7108,56,-130,4,'Inner Bailey',' Paved with blocks of fine cut polished stone, with grass evenly\ngrowing in-between each block, the inner bailey is a place for\nnobles and their families to come and socialize, or the King to\npronounce decrees from.  Capturing the highlight of the space is\na large fountain that rest in the center of the inner bailey.\nA door to the Citadel Blacksmith\'s shop can be seen to the east.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7109,57,-130,4,'Blacksmith\'s Shop',' The walls of the room are covered with the silt produced by the\nforge in the room to the east.  A small desk is placed against one\nwall for the blacksmith to keep track of his orders.  A set of stairs\nascends to another room above this one.  A door is set into the\nsouth wall and a curtain covers the entrance to the forge.  A single\noil burning lamp hangs above the desk to provide light for the\nshop.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,16,130,0,'',NULL),
(7110,58,-130,4,'Blacksmith\'s Forge',' This is where the blacksmith spends the majority of his time.  To\nthe blacksmith this is basically his temple with the forge being his\nshrine, and the anvil his altar.  The room is extremely hot from the\nfires blazing in the forge.  A small set of stairs lead up to a\nserious of catwalks above the forge while a curtain of thick leather\ncovers the exit to the shop itself.\n',46,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,15,130,0,'',NULL),
(7111,52,-131,4,'Guards Office',' This small office is for the person in charge of the Citadel Guards.\nA neat organized desk and a sturdy chair are the only furnishings of\nthe room.  A set of stairs go up to a room on the second floor\nof the barracks and a door in the north wall leads to the\nbarracks mess hall.  One oil lamp hangs from the wall keeping\nthe office lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,15,120,0,'',NULL),
(7112,53,-131,4,'Inner Bailey',' Paved with blocks of fine cut polished stone, with grass evenly\ngrowing in-between each block, the inner bailey is a place for\nnobles and their families to come and socialize, or the King to\npronounce decrees from.  Capturing the highlight of the space is\na large fountain that rest in the center of the inner bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7113,54,-131,4,'Inner Bailey',' Paved with blocks of fine cut polished stone, with grass evenly\ngrowing in-between each block, the inner bailey is a place for nobles\nand their families to come and socialize, or the King to pronounce\ndecrees from.  Capturing the highlight of the space is a large\nfountain that rest in the center of the inner bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7114,55,-131,4,'Inner Bailey',' Paved with blocks of fine cut polished stone, with grass evenly\ngrowing in-between each block, the inner bailey is a place for\nnobles and their families to come and socialize, or the King to\npronounce decrees from.  Capturing the highlight of the space is\na large fountain that rest in the center of the inner bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7115,56,-131,4,'Inner Bailey',' Paved with blocks of fine cut polished stone, with grass evenly\ngrowing in-between each block, the inner bailey is a place for nobles\nand their families to come and socialize, or the King to pronounce\ndecrees from.  Capturing the highlight of the space is a large\nfountain that rest in the center of the inner bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7116,57,-131,4,'Blacksmith\'s Room',' Not very large in size the room is tightly packed with a small bed,\nsome chests and a night stand.  The room reeks of oil, sweat, and\nsmoke coming from old clothes the blacksmith has thrown in the corner\nafter a day working at the forge.  A door to the north leads to the\nblacksmith\'s shop.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7117,50,-132,4,'Vacant Apartment',' This apartment seems to be vacant at the moment.  There is nothing\nhere but a large open room filled with balls of dust.  Even the walls\nhave been stripped bare of any decorations.  A set of stairs towards\nthe southern part of the room lead down to Braddock\'s Mercantile.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,15,120,0,'',NULL),
(7118,53,-132,4,'In the Bailey Gate Tower',' Slightly cramped for space this is about the size of an average\ngate tower for a small keep.  You can see wood barricades and other\nstandard items you would expect to see the guard have on hand lying\naround the edges of the tower for quick access should a riot\nbegin in the Citadel.  You can see a doorway set in the east wall\nof the tower and a small set of stairs that wind their way\naround the inside of the tower going both up and down to\ndifferent levels of the tower.  Attached to walls of the tower\nare oil lamps to keep the tower lit for the guards.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7119,54,-132,4,'Inside the Bailey Gates',' Paved with blocks of fine cut polished stone, with grass evenly\ngrowing in-between each block, the inner bailey is a place for nobles\nand their families to come and socialize, or the King to pronounce\ndecrees from.  You stand in-between the gate towers to the walls\nsurrounding the inner bailey.  The bailey gates are to the south of\nyou and door used to enter the tower itself can be seen to the west.\nThe bailey slopes downward to the south quite a bit here as\nMordel Avenue is at a lower elevation.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7120,55,-132,4,'Inside the Bailey Gates',' Paved with blocks of fine cut polished stone, with grass evenly\ngrowing in-between each block, the inner bailey is a place for nobles\nand their families to come and socialize, or the King to pronounce\ndecrees from.  You stand in-between the gate towers to the walls\nsurrounding the inner bailey.  The bailey gates are to the south of\nyou and door used to enter the tower itself can be seen to the east.\nThe bailey slopes downward to the south quite a bit here as Mordel\nAvenue is at a lower elevation.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7121,56,-132,4,'In the Bailey Gate Tower',' Slightly cramped for space this is about the size of an average\ngate tower for a small keep.  You can see wood barricades and other\nstandard items you would expect to see the guard have on hand lying\naround the edges of the tower for quick access should a riot begin\nin the Citadel.  You can see a doorway set in the west wall of the\ntower and a small set of stairs that wind their way around the inside\nof the tower going both up and down to different levels of the tower.\nAttached to the walls of the tower are oil lamps to keep the tower\nlit for the guards.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7122,59,-132,4,'Sleeping Loft',' This loft is used by the tavern maids and occasionally the tavern\nowner if it suits him.  A couple of small beds are placed around the\nloft for the maids to share and small wash basin lies in one corner.\nPiles of clothes can be seen lying near each bed and a ladder leads\ndown to the tavern below.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,108,0,'',NULL),
(7123,51,-133,4,'Gena\'s Living Quarters',' These are Gena\'s living quarters.  Oddly you see many items that\nshould belong to a dwarf and wonder where exactly the mercantile\nowner Braddock spends his nights.  Other than a few personal items\nand simple furnishings there is little to see in the room.  A set of\nstairs run down out of the room.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7124,58,-133,4,'Upper Floor',' This is the upper floor to the Black Dragon Inn.  Several doors\nline the hallway and as you look into some of them you find little\nof interest.   Small lamps are attached to the walls to provide for\nthe patrons of the inn that find it necessary to move around at night.\nThe hall continues to the south while to the north you can see a set\nof stairs leading to the common room of the inn.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7125,51,-134,4,'Living Quarters',' These are the living quarters for the merchant and his family.\nSeveral rooms branch off of this main room.  As you explore them\nyou find a master bedroom and two smaller bedrooms for his\nchildren.  This room is furnished with some elegant furnishings\nmade from a solid maple wood.  A set of stairs lead back down\nto the main room of the home.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7126,52,-134,4,'Living Quarters',' Quite extravagant, this is the personal living quarters for the\nnobleman and his family.  You stand in the main living room and\nfind a master bedroom, 3 smaller bedrooms, and a den branching\noff this room.   Your search finds you nothing but standard\npersonal items and gaudy furnishings.  A set of stairs lead\nback down to the main room of the house.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,18,120,0,'',NULL),
(7127,53,-134,4,'Living Quarters',' Decorated with the same exotic furnishings as below this room also\nhas the same hypnotic odor of lilac coming from several incense\nburners placed around the room.  As explore this level you find what\nappears to be a master bedroom, a secondary bedroom and a small\ncluttered den.  All are dimly lit with the same weird lanterns found\nbelow and are decorated with numerous trinkets and such hanging from\nthe ceilings.  From this room you can see a set of stairs hidden\nslightly behind a silk screen that lead back downstairs to the main\nroom of the home.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,16,120,0,'',NULL),
(7128,56,-134,4,'Loft',' Covered with a thick layer of loose hay and straw the loft floor\nseems slightly unstable and forces your to tread very lightly.\nYou have to navigate around several holes in the floor as you\nlook around the room.  The only thing you find is a small area\nwhere it appears the stableboy sleeps at night.  You discover a\npiece of old wood that almost could be associated with a comb\nand a small cracked wooden bowl used as a wash basin for the\nboy.  A ladder hanging on the wall of barn provides access back\nto the stables below.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,15,108,0,'',NULL),
(7129,57,-134,4,'Upper Floor',' This is the upper floor to the Black Dragon Inn.  Several doors\nline the hallway and as you look into some of them you find little\nof interest.   Small lamps are attached to the walls to provide for\nthe patrons of the inn that find it necessary to move around at night.\nThe hall continues to the east.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7130,58,-134,4,'Upper Floor',' This is the upper floor to the Black Dragon Inn.  Several doors\nline the hallway and as you look into some of them you find little\nof interest.   Small lamps are attached to the walls to provide for\nthe patrons of the inn that find it necessary to move around at night.\nThe hall continues to the north and west.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7131,53,-135,4,'In a Citadel Gate Tower',' Slightly larger than the gate towers to the Inner Bailey the tower\nis still fairly cramped for space.  A set of stairs spirals around\nthe outer wall of the tower leading up to the next level and\ndown to the base of the tower below.  Oil burning lamps are\nattached to the tower walls to keep the tower lit for the\nguards.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,120,0,'',NULL),
(7132,56,-135,4,'In a Citadel Gate Tower',' Slightly larger than the gate towers to the Inner Bailey the tower\nis still fairly cramped for space.  A set of stairs spirals around the\nouter wall of the tower leading up to the next level and down to the\nbase of the tower below.  Oil burning lamps are attached to the\ntower walls to keep the tower lit for the guards.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,120,0,'',NULL),
(7133,45,-127,5,'On the Citadel Walls',' You stand on the massive walls of the Citadel.  To the west the\nwalls descend to merge with the canyon wall and you become dizzy as\nyou realize just how high up the cliff face the Citadel rests.  To\nthe north lies the face of the mountain that the Citadel rests\nagainst.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7134,49,-127,5,'Bishop Mercee\'s Room',' Decorated with simple but graphic tapestries depicting death the\nroom is fairly neat and organized.  A plush crimson carpet covers\nthe floor and what little heat that is in the room is drawn through\na pipe coming from the fire pot below.  A set of stairs lead down\nto the Bishops office and a small door to the south can just be\nseen peeking out from behind a large tapestry depicting the\nsacrifice of a holy cleric.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7135,50,-127,5,'Cathedral Balcony',' Besides the steep sloping floor of the balcony this area appears\nthe same as main hall below, the pews are made the same rich cherry\nwood.  Under each pew you find several small bowls.  The balcony\ncontinues to the east.  Securely fastened to the walls oil\nlamps are used to keep the balcony area dimly lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7136,51,-127,5,'Cathedral Balcony',' Besides the steep sloping floor of the balcony this area appears\nthe same as main hall below, the pews are made the same rich cherry\nwood.  Under each pew you find several small bowls.  The balcony\ncontinues to the west and south.  Securely fastened to the walls oil\nlamps are used to keep the balcony area dimly lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7137,58,-127,5,'Front of a Classroom',' A large desk with a solid stone top sits at the center of this part\nof the classroom.  Lying on the desk are the remains of numerous\nanimals that have been mutated and dissected.  Sections of\nclassroom desks can be seen both to the east and south of here\nand a set of double doors provide and exit to the room to the\nsoutheast.  Small globes of light attached to the walls keep the\nspace well lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,30,120,0,'',NULL),
(7138,59,-127,5,'Among the Classroom Desks',' Several desk capable of seating two or three students cover this\nsection of the room.  Chalk boards cover the walls of the area\nproviding space for students and masters both to express ideas and\nconcepts dealing with the amazing realm of magic.  The front of the\nclassroom can be seen to the west of here.  Small globes of light\nattached firmly to the walls keep the classroom well lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7139,60,-127,5,'Falcur\'s Chambers',' Second only to Valteez in the Tower these are the personal chambers\nof the Master Wizard Falcur.  Numerous books and tomes line the walls\nof the room.  In one corner hardly visible over the stacks of books\nyou discover a small bed that appears recently slept in.  Burners\nof incense flood the room with an odor of sulfur.  The air feels\nfairly warm and comfortable yet you can find no heat source or\nduct work anywhere.  A door to the south leads back to the\nprivate study shared by Valteez and Falcur.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7140,64,-127,5,'On the Citadel Walls',' You stand on the massive walls of the Citadel.  To the east the\nwalls descend to merge with the canyon wall and you become dizzy as\nyou realize just how high up the cliff face the Citadel rests.\nTo the north lies the face of the mountain that the Citadel\nrests against.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7141,45,-128,5,'On the Citadel Walls',' You stand on the massive walls of the Citadel.  To the west the\nwalls descend to merge with the canyon wall and you become dizzy as\nyou realize just how high up the cliff face the Citadel rests.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7142,49,-128,5,'A Narrow Walkway',' Stretching across the space above the altar of the Cathedral this\nsmall walkway is extremely narrow.  It appears to be a passage to\nmove between the Bishops and High Priests chambers.  Directly to the\nwest of you is the large stain glass window which adorns the west\nwall of the altar space.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,130,0,'',NULL),
(7143,52,-128,6,'Inside the Cathedral Spire',' Almost to the top of the spire you stop at this landing to take a\nbreath.  Both to the northwest and southwest you see openings which\nlead into the attic of the Cathedral.  The stairs continue both up\nto the top of the Cathedral Spire or downwards to the next lower\nlevel.  Small oil lamps fastened securely to the walls keep the spire\nstairway well lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,120,0,'',NULL),
(7144,51,-128,5,'Cathedral Balcony',' Besides the steep sloping floor of the balcony this area appears\nthe same as main hall below, the pews are made the same rich cherry\nwood.  Under each pew you find several small bowls.  The balcony\ncontinues to the north and south while the Cathedral Spire can be\nseen to the east.  Securely fastened to the walls small oil lamps are\nused to keep the balcony area dimly lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7145,52,-128,5,'Inside the Cathedral Spire',' The stairs inside the Spire come to a stop at this landing allowing\nyou access to the Cathedral balconies to the west.  The stairs\ncontinue up into the Spire higher of down to the Grand Entrance to\nthe Cathedral.  Attached securely to the walls small oil lamps are\nused to light the spire stairway.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,16,120,0,'',NULL),
(7146,58,-128,5,'Among the Classroom Desks',' Several desk capable of seating two or three students cover this\nsection of the room.  Chalk boards cover the walls of the area\nproviding space for students and masters both to express ideas and\nconcepts dealing with the amazing realm of magic.  The front of\nthe classroom can be seen to the north of here.  Small globes\nof light firmly attached to the walls keep the classroom well\nlit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7147,59,-128,5,'Central Shaft',' Whoa! As you enter the shaft and expect to fall you actually begin\nto float up a bit and have to work to keep yourself at this level.\nSomehow the shaft grants you the ability to fly in order to ascend\nor descend throughout the Towers main levels.  An arched doorway can\nbe seen to the east, while a set of double doors appear to lead to\nthe classrooms to the northwest, and a steel door is set in the south\nwall.  Small globes of light securely fastened to the walls light\nthe room.\n',46,131081,65,0,0,0,0,0,20,300,0,'',NULL),
(7148,60,-128,5,'Private Study',' This is the private study of the Sorcerer Valteez and the Master\nWizard Falcur.  Books adorn most of the walls of the room and two\nlarge plush chairs are here for the master magicians.  An arched\ndoorway to the west provides access to the Tower\'s central shaft,\nand two doors to the north and south appear to lead to the private\nchambers of the mages.  As with most rooms in the tower odd globes\nof light are securely fastened to the walls.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,15,120,0,'',NULL),
(7149,64,-128,5,'On the Citadel Walls',' You stand on the massive walls of the Citadel.  To the east the\nwalls descend to merge with the canyon wall and you become dizzy\nas you realize just how high up the cliff face the Citadel rests.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7150,45,-129,5,'On the Citadel Walls',' You stand on the massive walls of the Citadel.  To the west the\nwalls descend to merge with the canyon wall and you become dizzy as\nyou realize just how high up the cliff face the Citadel rests.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7151,49,-129,5,'Maldar\'s Room',' Appearing extremely disorganized the room is a shambles.  Clothing\nand religious items lie scattered about every surface of the room.\nLooking around you find little but personal affects and worthless\nitems for formal ceremonies.  A good sized bed rest against one wall\nand heat flows incredibly from a pipe ascending from the firepot\nbelow.  A set of stairs lead back down too the Priest\'s office and a\nsmall door is set in the north wall.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7152,50,-129,5,'Cathedral Balcony',' Besides the steep sloping floor of the balcony this area appears\nthe same as main hall below, the pews are made the same rich cherry\nwood.  Under each pew you find several small bowls.  The balcony\ncontinues to the east.  Small oil lamps fastened securely to\nthe walls keep the balcony area dimly lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7153,51,-129,5,'Cathedral Balcony',' Besides the steep sloping floor of the balcony this area appears\nthe same as main hall below, the pews are made the same rich cherry\nwood.  Under each pew you find several small bowls.  The balcony\ncontinues to the west and north.  Small oil lamps securely\nfastened to the walls keep the balcony area well lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7154,58,-129,5,'Target Area',' Scorch marks covers most of the walls of this area of the room.\nIt appears that apprentice mages stand to the east of here and\npractice casting there spells into this area of the room.  Besides\nthe scorch marks you can see small pitted areas on the floor along\nwith small hair line cracks covering areas of the walls, floor, and\nceiling.  Small globes of light attached to the walls keep the\ntarget area well lit.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,18,120,0,'',NULL),
(7155,59,-129,5,'Casting Area',' A small table rest here with for mages to keep there components\nhandy as they practice new spells and techniques.  The area to the\nwest of here appears to be the target area for the mages spells.\nA sturdy steel door is set into the north wall.  Small globes of\nlight keep the area well lit for mages to read their spell books\nand scrolls.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(7156,60,-129,5,'Valteez\'s Chambers',' These are the chambers of the Master Sorcerer Valteez.  He is the\nruling mage of the Tower and at this time joint ruler of the Citadel\nuntil word is heard from King Urik.  The room is inhumanely cold and\ncovered with magical items, tomes, and books.  A large comfortable\nlooking bed is placed against the south wall and a door to the\nnorth leads to the private study shared by Valteez and Falcur.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7157,64,-129,5,'On the Citadel Walls',' You stand on the massive walls of the Citadel.  To the east the\nwalls descend to merge with the canyon wall and you become dizzy as\nyou realize just how high up the cliff face the Citadel rests.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7158,46,-130,5,'On the Citadel Walls',' You stand on the massive walls of the Citadel.  To the southwest\nthe walls descend to merge with the canyon wall and you become dizzy\nas you realize just how high up the cliff face the Citadel rests.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7159,47,-130,5,'On the Citadel Walls',' You stand on the massive walls of the Citadel.  To the south the\nwalls descend to merge with the canyon wall and you become dizzy as\nyou realize just how high up the cliff face the Citadel rests.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7160,51,-130,5,'Barracks Sleeping Quarters',' There is little in this room besides hard cots and small\nfootlockers at the base of each bed.  Oil lamps hang on the walls\nand a door to the east leads to the barracks lounge area.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,30,120,0,'',NULL),
(7161,52,-130,5,'Barracks Lounge Area',' Tables and chairs are scattered throughout the room.  Dirty dishes,\nstale pieces of bread and other moldy food items can be found on\nmost of the tabletops.  On a couple of the tables you find a set\nof cards but do not recognize the game they belong to.  A door\nto the west leads to the barracks sleeping area and a set of\nstairs leads down to the barracks mess hall.  Oil lamps\nsecurely fastened to the walls keep the room well lit at all\ntimes.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,30,120,0,'',NULL),
(7162,57,-130,5,'Obsidian Cutter\'s Shop',' This is the small shop of the Citadel Obsidian Cutter.  You can\nsee several barrels with massive locks on them that you guess hold\nrough obsidian and under a glass class can see numerous items made\nof polished obsidian.  A set of stairs lead down to the blacksmith\'s\nshop and a small door to the south leads to the private chambers of\nthe shop owner.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,120,0,'',NULL),
(7163,58,-130,5,'Narrow Catwalk Above the Forge',' You are standing among several catwalks that move around the\nlarge forge of the blacksmiths shop.  Made from old boards and\nfrayed ropes you are not sure exactly how safe you should feel\nup here.  The smoke is extremely thick here as it leaks out of\nthe joints in the smoke stack.  Below is the main floor of the\nforge area.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,120,0,'',NULL),
(7164,62,-130,5,'On the Citadel Walls',' You stand on the massive walls of the Citadel.  To the south the\nwalls descend to merge with the canyon wall and you become dizzy as\nyou realize just how high up the cliff face the Citadel rests.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7165,63,-130,5,'On the Citadel Walls',' You stand on the massive walls of the Citadel.  To the southeast\nthe walls descend to merge with the canyon wall and you become dizzy\nas you realize just how high up the cliff face the Citadel rests.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7166,48,-131,5,'On the Citadel Walls',' You stand on the massive walls of the Citadel.  To the southwest\nthe walls descend to merge with the canyon wall and you become\ndizzy as you realize just how high up the cliff face the\nCitadel rests.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7167,52,-131,5,'Guards Room',' Allowed a private chamber for his position, this room belongs to\nthe head of the Citadel Guards.  Fairly cramped for space the room\ncontains a small cot slightly softer than those used by the regular\nguards in the barracks and a small foot locker for the head guard\'s\npersonal possessions.  A small stairway leads back down to the guards\noffice.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7168,57,-131,5,'Living Quarters',' A moderate sized room, the Gem Cutter keeps things neat and\norganized.  A small bed and desk adorn one side of the room and a\ndecent sized wardrobe is placed against the other wall.  A carpet\nmade in a distant lands lies on the floor of the chamber tells of\nthe cutters wealth in working for the Citadel.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7169,61,-131,5,'On the Citadel Walls',' You stand on the massive walls of the Citadel.  To the southeast\nthe walls descend to merge with the canyon wall and you become dizzy\nas you realize just how high up the cliff face the Citadel rests.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7170,49,-132,5,'On the Citadel Walls',' You stand on the massive walls of the Citadel.  To the southwest\nthe walls descend to merge with the canyon wall and you become dizzy\nas you realize just how high up the cliff face the Citadel rests.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7171,53,-132,5,'In the Bailey Gate Tower',' Slightly cramped for space this is about the size of an average\ngate tower for a small keep.  There is nothing at this level of the\ntower except this landing to catch your breath.  The stairs spiral\naround the outer wall of the tower going both up and down from here.\nOil burning lamps are attached to the walls to keep the tower lit at\nall times for the guards.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7172,56,-132,5,'In the Bailey Gate Tower',' Slightly cramped for space this is about the size of an average\ngate tower for a small keep.  There is nothing at this level of the\ntower except this landing to catch your breath.  The stairs spiral\naround the outer wall of the tower going both up and down from here.\nOil burning lamps are attached to the walls to keep the tower lit at\nall times for the guards.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
