(7196,52,-132,6,'On the Bailey Walls',' Standing on the walls of the inner bailey you can look down to the\nsouth onto Mordel Avenue or to the north and see the Inner Bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7197,53,-132,6,'Top of the Bailey Gate Tower',' Standing atop the Gate Tower of the Inner Bailey you can see a\ndoor to the west leading out onto the Bailey walls or a narrow\nstaircase which spirals downwards farther into the Gate Tower.\nAttached to the walls to provide light at all times are small oil\nburning lamps.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7198,56,-132,6,'Top of the Bailey Gate Tower',' Standing atop the Gate Tower of the Inner Bailey you can see an open\nexit to the east leading out onto the Bailey walls or a narrow\nstaircase which spirals downwards farther into the Gate Tower.\nAttached to the walls to provide light at all times are small oil\nburning lamps.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7199,57,-132,6,'On the Bailey Walls',' Standing on the walls of the inner bailey you can look down to the\nsouth onto Mordel Avenue or to the north and see the Inner Bailey.\n',46,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7200,49,-128,6,'Cathedral Attic',' Quite drafty and chilly this is the Cathedral Attic.  All around you\ncan be found straw sleeping mats where the lower clergy of the\nCathedral are forced to sleep.  As you scavenge through their belongs\nfind nothing of any interest.  The attic continues to the east,\nsoutheast, and south.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,96,0,'',NULL),
(7201,50,-128,6,'Cathedral Attic',' Quite drafty and chilly this is the Cathedral Attic.  All around you\ncan be found straw sleeping mats where the lower clergy of the\nCathedral are forced to sleep.  As you scavenge through their belongs\nfind nothing of any interest.  The attic continues to the west, east,\nand southerly directions.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,96,0,'',NULL),
(7202,51,-127,6,'Cathedral Attic',' Quite drafty and chilly this is the Cathedral Attic.  All around you\ncan be found straw sleeping mats where the lower clergy of the\nCathedral are forced to sleep.  As you scavenge through their belongs\nfind nothing of any interest.  The attic continues to the east,\nsouth and southeast, while the Cathedral Spire can be seen to the\nsouthwest.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,96,0,'',NULL),
(7203,49,-129,6,'Cathedral Attic',' Quite drafty and chilly this is the Cathedral Attic.  All around you\ncan be found straw sleeping mats where the lower clergy of the\nCathedral are forced to sleep.  As you scavenge through their belongs\nfind nothing of any interest.  The attic continues to the north, east,\nand northeast.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,96,0,'',NULL),
(7204,50,-129,6,'Cathedral Attic',' Quite drafty and chilly this is the Cathedral Attic.  All around you\ncan be found straw sleeping mats where the lower clergy of the\nCathedral are forced to sleep.  As you scavenge through their belongs\nfind nothing of any interest.  The attic continues to the east,\nwest, and northerly directions.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,96,0,'',NULL),
(7205,51,-128,6,'Cathedral Attic',' Quite drafty and chilly this is the Cathedral Attic.  All around you\ncan be found straw sleeping mats where the lower clergy of the\nCathedral are forced to sleep.  As you scavenge through their belongs\nfind nothing of any interest.  The attic continues to the west, north,\nand northwest, while the Cathedral Spire can be seen to the northeast.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,96,0,'',NULL),
(7206,59,-127,6,'Top of the Tower',' This level of the Tower is mainly used to store mages notes,\nexperiments never finished, or just plain junk.  Piles and piles\nof stuff can be found everywhere scattered around the room.  As you\nbegin to search through a few you quickly become disgusted realizing\nthat anything of value would probably not be stored up here.  This\nlevel continues both to the southwest and southeast while to the\nsouth lies the central shaft of the Tower.  The area is lit by the\nusual small globes of light found throughout the Tower.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7207,58,-128,6,'Top of the Tower',' This level of the Tower is mainly used to store mages notes,\nexperiments never finished, or just plain junk.  Piles and piles\nof stuff can be found everywhere scattered around the room.  As you\nbegin to search through a few you quickly become disgusted realizing\nthat anything of value would probably not be stored up here.  This\nlevel continues both to the southeast and northeast while to the\neast lies the central shaft of the Tower.  The area is lit by the\nusual small globes of light found throughout the Tower.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7208,59,-128,6,'Central Shaft',' Whoa! As you enter the shaft and expect to fall you actually begin\nto float up a bit and have to work to keep yourself at this level.\nSomehow the shaft grants you the ability to fly in order to ascend\nor descend throughout the Towers main levels.  On this level you find\nwhat appears to be the general storage area, or more commonly called\nan \"Attic\".  Piles and piles of papers, old experiments, and just\nplain junk surround you on all sides.  Attached to the walls you\nfind small globes of light which illuminate the area.\n',46,131081,65,0,0,0,0,0,20,200,0,'',NULL),
(7209,60,-128,6,'Top of the Tower',' This level of the Tower is mainly used to store mages notes,\nexperiments never finished, or just plain junk.  Piles and piles\nof stuff can be found everywhere scattered around the room.  As you\nbegin to search through a few you quickly become disgusted realizing\nthat anything of value would probably not be stored up here.  This\nlevel continues both to the northwest and southwest while to the\nwest lies the central shaft of the Tower.  The area is lit by the\nusual small globes of light found throughout the Tower.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7210,59,-129,6,'Top of the Tower',' This level of the Tower is mainly used to store mages notes,\nexperiments never finished, or just plain junk.  Piles and piles\nof stuff can be found everywhere scattered around the room.  As you\nbegin to search through a few you quickly become disgusted realizing\nthat anything of value would probably not be stored up here.  This\nlevel continues both to the northeast and northwest while to the\nnorth lies the central shaft of the Tower.  The area is lit by the\nusual small globes of light found throughout the Tower.\n',46,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7211,52,-128,7,'Top of the Cathedral Spire',' Squeezing your way through the last few steps you have arrived at\nthe top of the Spire.  You find yourself almost completely surrounded\nwith mechanical pulleys and large gears which make up the bell tower\nto the spire.  There are only a few very narrow slits in the walls\nto allow sound through so the view is very poor.  The only exit out\nof the room is back down the narrow staircase.\n',46,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7212,59,-128,7,'Tower Lookout',' Well you have finally reached the highest point to the Tower.  A\nwide walkway runs around the edge of the room and you step out of\nthe magical shaft to explore.  Around you magic has been used to make\nlarge stone sections of the Tower walls transparent for mages to look\nout onto the realms.  In between each large section of glass you see a\ndetailed tapestry which appears to map out The World in that direction.\nThe small globes of light used to light the Tower are attached in\nnumerous places around you making the room almost cheery.\n',46,131081,65,0,0,0,0,0,15,120,0,'',NULL),
(7213,57,-127,3,'Small Room',' The room is really nothing more then a connecting room between the\nKeep and the Citadel Tower.  You can see a door to the west and to\nthe east made of cut out portions of the walls.  Otherwise the room\nis completely bare.\n',46,139592,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,120,0,'',NULL),
(7214,59,-122,3,'Small Room',' This is tiny room between the back tunnels to the Keep and one of the\nmain paths into the Citadel Mines.  The room has been carved out of the\nmountain itself and its walls are still considerably rough.  You can see\nplain doors to the northwest and south of you.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7215,59,-123,3,'Eastern Mine Path',' Carved from the mountain itself this passage is one of the two\nmain routes one can take into, or out of, the Citadel Mines.  Two\ndeep parallel ruts run down the middle of the tunnel while overhead\noccasional wooden beam structures can be seen supporting the the\nmassive rock above.  A sturdy looking door sits in the north wall\nalmost completely concealed in the shadows.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7216,60,-123,3,'Eastern Mine Path',' Carved from the mountain itself this passage is one of the two\nmain routes one can take into, or out of, the Citadel Mines.  Two\ndeep parallel ruts run down the middle of the tunnel while overhead\noccasional wooden beam structures can be seen supporting the the\nmassive rock above.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7217,61,-124,3,'Eastern Mine Path',' Carved from the mountain itself this passage is one of the two\nmain routes one can take into, or out of, the Citadel Mines.  Two\ndeep parallel ruts run down the middle of the tunnel while overhead\noccasional wooden beam structures can be seen supporting the the\nmassive rock above.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7218,62,-125,3,'Eastern Mine Path',' Carved from the mountain itself this passage is one of the two\nmain routes one can take into, or out of, the Citadel Mines.  Two\ndeep parallel ruts run down the middle of the tunnel while overhead\noccasional wooden beam structures can be seen supporting the the\nmassive rock above.\n',46,139596,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7219,62,-126,3,'Eastern Mine Path',' Carved from the mountain itself this passage is one of the two\nmain routes one can take into, or out of, the Citadel Mines.  Two\ndeep parallel ruts run down the middle of the tunnel while overhead\noccasional wooden beam structures can be seen supporting the the\nmassive rock above.  To the south of you is the eastern portion of\nMordel Avenue, a gate has been placed across the passage to control\naccess to the mines and to keep slaves from escaping.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7220,47,-126,3,'Western Mine Path',' Carved from the mountain itself this passage is one of the two\nmain routes one can take into, or out of, the Citadel Mines.  Two\ndeep parallel ruts run down the middle of the tunnel while overhead\noccasional wooden beam structures can be seen supporting the the\nmassive rock above.  To the south of you is the western portion of\nMordel Avenue, a gate has been placed across the passage to control\naccess to the mines and to keep slaves from escaping.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
