(7228,55,-125,3,'Top of the Mine Lift',' Standing amidst numerous pulleys and a large wooden framework you\nhave found the top of the Mine Lift.  This lift is used to move goods\nfrom the Mine floor up to this level for transportation out of the Mines\nand vice versa.  The lift is considerably large taking up a good eight\nfoot square area.  Off to the side a large wooden pole hooked on a\nhinged mechanism seems to control the movement of the lift.  A ledge\nrunning around the main area of the lift can be seen to the northwest\nand southeast while a passage way through the mountain is to the\nnortheast.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,5,'',NULL),
(7229,56,-126,3,'Wide Ledge Above the Mines',' This ledge appears to run around the main portion of the Mine and is\nused by the guards for both the transportation of goods into and out of\nthe Mine and to observe and watch the Mine activities.  Deep ruts mar\nthe surface you walk on while you spot occasional wooden structures\noverhead.  The ledge itself is about six feet wide and has no railing\nof any type.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7230,56,-127,3,'Wide Ledge Above the Mines',' This ledge appears to run around the main portion of the Mine and is\nused by the guards for both the transportation of goods into and out of\nthe Mine and to observe and watch the Mine activities.  Deep ruts mar\nthe surface you walk on while you spot occasional wooden structures\noverhead.  The ledge itself is about six feet wide and has no railing\nof any type.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7231,55,-128,3,'Narrow Bridge',' This bridge arches over an opening below you between the main area of\nthe mining operation and the storage area.  To the west of you a little\nmining activity goes on as some of the older or injured slaves pick at\nspots in the walls removing obsidian from missed spots or spots that\nwere at the time overlooked for better areas.  Basically this area has\nbecome the hub of the mining activity as people move through it between\nthe active mine and the storage area to the east.  The storage area\nhouses all finished ore and mining supplies along with the meager food\nsupplies.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(7232,54,-129,3,'Wide Ledge Above the Mines',' This ledge appears to run around the main portion of the Mine and is\nused by the guards for both the transportation of goods into and out of\nthe Mine and to observe and watch the Mine activities.  Deep ruts mar\nthe surface you walk on while you spot occasional wooden structures\noverhead.  The ledge itself is about six feet wide and has no railing\nof any type.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
