(7245,55,-122,0,'Vertical Shaft',' It appears this shaft was carved through the mountain by water,\nprobably over decades.  Its sides while polished smooth do offer\nnumerous handholds for climbing.  Most of these handholds are formed\nwhere pockets of softer material was cut through by the water and it\nwashed away before its neighboring rock.  The shaft appears to continue\nboth up and down from here.  From below you can hear the movement of\nwater.\n',46,139592,15,0,0,0,0,0,6,120,0,'',NULL),
(7246,0,0,0,'Active Mine Area',' Surrounded by wood bracing and mine workers you are standing in\nthe active area of the Mine.  The Mine began in the main room to the\nsouthwest of here and after exhausting that region moved in this\ndirection.  There is a buzz of activity surrounding you as the slaves\nare forced to extract the ore from the mines.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,12,96,0,'',NULL),
