(7255,50,-127,-1,'River Canyon',' You seem to be at the end of this section of the river as the water\nis sucked into a large opening to the west.  Unfortunately the opening\nis just slightly larger then the water flow so only the tiniest sliver\nis of air is occasionally visible, you\'ll have to swim underwater if\nyou want to go that way.  Extremely fast and cold the water churns\nand crashes against the rock around you.  The walls of the canyon are\nincredibly slick and smooth and you can find no decent handholds up as\nyou fight to stay afloat.  Below you the undercurrents of the river are\nso strong they threaten to suck you under at any time.\n',46,139592,8,0,0,0,25,3,20,300,0,'',NULL),
(7256,51,-127,-1,'River Canyon',' Extremely fast and cold the water churns and crashes against the rock\naround you.  The walls of the canyon are incredibly slick and smooth\nand you can find no decent handholds up as you fight to stay afloat.\nBelow you the undercurrents of the river are so strong they threaten to\nsuck you under at any time.\n',46,139592,8,0,0,0,25,3,20,300,0,'',NULL),
(7257,52,-127,-1,'River Canyon',' Extremely fast and cold the water churns and crashes against the rock\naround you.  The walls of the canyon are incredibly slick and smooth\nand you can find no decent handholds up as you fight to stay afloat.\nBelow you the undercurrents of the river are so strong they threaten to\nsuck you under at any time.\n',46,139592,8,0,0,0,25,3,20,300,0,'',NULL),
(7258,53,-126,-1,'River Canyon Next to a Large Machine',' Blocking over half the river a large machine has been attached to the\ncanyon walls here to extract and polish obsidian ore.  A rusted metal\nladder has been hammered into the side of the canyon wall for workers\nand slaves to examine and repair the machine.  Extremely fast and cold\nthe water churns and crashes against the rock around you.  The walls of\nthe canyon are incredibly slick and smooth and you can find no decent\nhandholds in them as you fight to stay afloat.  Below you the under-\ncurrents of the river are so strong they threaten to suck you under at\nany time.\n',46,139592,8,0,0,0,25,9,20,300,0,'',NULL),
(7259,54,-125,-1,'River Canyon',' You seem to be at the source of this section of the river as the water\ngushes from a large opening to the north.  Unfortunately the opening is\njust slightly larger then the water flow so only the tiniest sliver is\nof air is occasionally visible, you\'ll have to swim underwater if you want\nto go that way.  Extremely fast and cold the water churns and crashes\nagainst the rock around you.  The walls of the canyon are incredibly\nslick and smooth and you can find no decent handholds up as you fight\nto stay afloat.  Below you the undercurrents of the river are so strong\nthey threaten to suck you under at any time.\n',46,139592,8,0,0,0,25,9,20,300,0,'',NULL),
(7260,0,0,0,'Slaves Sleeping Area',' Littered with refuse and brittle bones you are standing in the\nsleeping area for the slaves.  The entire area reeks from the stench\nof death and decay and occasionally you notice a corpse lieing on the\nground in a ball.  There are very few wooden braces in this area of the\nmine as it was almost a nature cavern when the mining began.  There is\nlittle else to be found as the slaves are locked in here in groups\nat different times of the day to allow the mines to be in production\ntwenty four hours a day.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(7261,0,0,0,'Slaves Sleeping Area',' Littered with refuse and brittle bones you are standing in the\nsleeping area for the slaves.  The entire area reeks from the stench\nof death and decay and occasionally you notice a corpse lieing on the\nground in a ball.  There are very few wooden braces in this area of the\nmine as it was almost a nature cavern when the mining began.  There is\nlittle else to be found as the slaves are locked in here in groups\nat different times of the day to allow the mines to be in production\ntwenty four hours a day.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(7262,0,0,0,'Slaves Sleeping Area',' Littered with refuse and brittle bones you are standing in the\nsleeping area for the slaves.  The entire area reeks from the stench\nof death and decay and occasionally you notice a corpse lieing on the\nground in a ball.  There are very few wooden braces in this area of the\nmine as it was almost a nature cavern when the mining began.  There is\nlittle else to be found as the slaves are locked in here in groups\nat different times of the day to allow the mines to be in production\ntwenty four hours a day.  A wide river canyon blocks you way to the\nsoutheast and effectively keeps the slaves in this area when so desired.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(7263,0,0,0,'Slaves Sleeping Area',' Littered with refuse and brittle bones you are standing in the\nsleeping area for the slaves.  The entire area reeks from the stench\nof death and decay and occasionally you notice a corpse lieing on the\nground in a ball.  There are very few wooden braces in this area of the\nmine as it was almost a nature cavern when the mining began.  There is\nlittle else to be found as the slaves are locked in here in groups\nat different times of the day to allow the mines to be in production\ntwenty four hours a day.  A wide river canyon blocks you way to the\nsouth and effectively keeps the slaves in this area when so desired.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(7264,0,0,0,'Slaves Sleeping Area',' Littered with refuse and brittle bones you are standing in the\nsleeping area for the slaves.  The entire area reeks from the stench\nof death and decay and occasionally you notice a corpse lieing on the\nground in a ball.  There are very few wooden braces in this area of the\nmine as it was almost a nature cavern when the mining began.  There is\nlittle else to be found as the slaves are locked in here in groups\nat different times of the day to allow the mines to be in production\ntwenty four hours a day.  A wide river canyon blocks you way to the\nsouth and effectively keeps the slaves in this area when so desired.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(7265,0,0,0,'Slaves Sleeping Area',' Littered with refuse and brittle bones you are standing in the\nsleeping area for the slaves.  The entire area reeks from the stench\nof death and decay and occasionally you notice a corpse lieing on the\nground in a ball.  There is little else to be found as the slaves are\nlocked in here in groups at different times of the day to allow the\nmines to be in production twenty four hours a day.  A wide river canyon\nblocks you way to the southeast but a shaky drawbridge has been\nconstructed here to allow passage over the river.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(7266,0,0,0,'Bottom of the Mine Lift',' Standing amidst numerous pulleys and a large wooden framework you\nhave found the bottom of the Mine Lift.  This lift is used to move goods\nfrom the Mine floor to the paths above for transportation out of the\nMines and vice versa.  The lift is considerably large taking up a good\neight foot square area.  Off to the side a large wooden pole hooked on\na hinged mechanism seems to control the movement of the lift.  To the\nwest of you a deep river canyon blocks your passage while the main mine\narea spreads out to the south of you.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,5,'',NULL),
(7267,0,0,0,'Main Mine Area',' Littered with rocks, obsidian ore, and scrapped mining tools this is\nthe main area of the mines.  Once a natural cavern the walls of the mine\nwere hacked away stripping them of almost all their ore.  A few slaves\nwork around the area removing small bits of obsidian overlooked for\nlarger areas earlier in the mining.  Otherwise most work occurs in the\nactive area of the mine to the northeast.  Occasionally a structural\nbracing element can be seen bracing a wall whose stability is in\nquestion.  A lot of noise can be heard through a passage to the\nnortheast where the active mining area is located.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(7268,0,0,0,'Main Mine Area',' Littered with rocks, obsidian ore, and scrapped mining tools this is\nthe main area of the mines.  Once a natural cavern the walls of the mine\nwere hacked away stripping them of almost all their ore.  A few slaves\nwork around the area removing small bits of obsidian overlooked for\nlarger areas earlier in the mining.  Otherwise most work occurs in the\nactive area of the mine to the northeast.  To the northwest a deep\nriver canyon can be seen but a shaky drawbridge has been constructed\nfor passage over it.  As you step closer to the edge you discover below\nyou, attached to the canyon walls, a massive machine using the power\nand water of the river to extract and wash the obsidian ore.  You can\njust make out a metal ladder attached to the canyon walls for repair\nand observation of the machine.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,5,'',NULL),
(7269,0,0,0,'Main Mine Area',' Littered with rocks, obsidian ore, and scrapped mining tools this is\nthe main area of the mines.  Once a natural cavern the walls of the mine\nwere hacked away stripping them of almost all their ore.  A few slaves\nwork around the area removing small bits of obsidian overlooked for\nlarger areas earlier in the mining.  Otherwise most work occurs in the\nactive area of the mine to the northeast.  Occasionally a structural\nbracing element can be seen bracing a wall whose stability is in\nquestion.  A deep river canyon blocks your way to the northwest.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(7270,0,0,0,'Main Mine Area',' Littered with rocks, obsidian ore, and scrapped mining tools this is\nthe main area of the mines.  Once a natural cavern the walls of the mine\nwere hacked away stripping them of almost all their ore.  A few slaves\nwork around the area removing small bits of obsidian overlooked for\nlarger areas earlier in the mining.  Otherwise most work occurs in the\nactive area of the mine to the northeast.  Occasionally a structural\nbracing element can be seen bracing a wall whose stability is in\nquestion.  To the southeast a passage leads to the storage area of the\nmines.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(7271,0,0,0,'Main Mine Area',' Littered with rocks, obsidian ore, and scrapped mining tools this is\nthe main area of the mines.  Once a natural cavern the walls of the mine\nwere hacked away stripping them of almost all their ore.  A few slaves\nwork around the area removing small bits of obsidian overlooked for\nlarger areas earlier in the mining.  Otherwise most work occurs in the\nactive area of the mine to the northeast.  Occasionally a structural\nbracing element can be seen bracing a wall whose stability is in\nquestion.  A deep river canyon blocks your way to the north.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(7272,0,0,0,'Main Mine Area',' Littered with rocks, obsidian ore, and scrapped mining tools this is\nthe main area of the mines.  Once a natural cavern the walls of the mine\nwere hacked away stripping them of almost all their ore.  A few slaves\nwork around the area removing small bits of obsidian overlooked for\nlarger areas earlier in the mining.  Otherwise most work occurs in the\nactive area of the mine to the northeast.  A deep river canyon blocks\nyour way to the north.\n',46,139592,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
