(7290,55,-122,-1,'Underground River',' Extremely fast and cold the water churns and thrashes you against the\nrocks around you.  The walls of the tunnel are incredibly slick and\nsmooth and you can find no decent handholds up as you fight to stay in\ncontrol.  The source of the waters flow is to the north as the water\ngushes through a lattice work of stone which is too small for any\nhumanoid creature to pass through.  Above you a vertical shaft rises\nupwards into the darkness and you finally find one foot hold which\nwould allow you to push yourself upwards and hopefully find handholds\nabove the waterline.  To the southwest of you the water pours through\nan opening just slightly larger then the water flow.  Only a thin\nsliver of air is visible between the waters surface and the top of the\npassage, you\'ll need to swim underwater to go that way.\n',46,139592,30,0,0,0,25,9,8,300,0,'',NULL),
(7291,54,-123,-1,'Underground River',' Extremely fast and cold the water churns and thrashes you against the\nrocks around you.  The walls of the tunnel are incredibly slick and\nsmooth and you can find no decent handholds up as you fight to stay in\ncontrol.  Rocks and other debris pound your body endlessly as the\ncurrents attempt to pull you along.\n',46,139592,30,0,0,0,20,2,8,96,0,'',NULL),
(7292,54,-124,-1,'Underground River',' Extremely fast and cold the water churns and thrashes you against the\nrocks around you.  The walls of the tunnel are incredibly slick and\nsmooth and you can find no decent handholds up as you fight to stay in\ncontrol.  Rocks and other debris pound your body endlessly as the\ncurrents attempt to pull you along.\n',46,139592,30,0,0,0,20,2,8,96,0,'',NULL),
(7293,55,-122,1,'Vertical Shaft',' It appears this shaft was carved through the mountain by water,\nprobably over decades.  Its sides while polished smooth do offer\nnumerous handholds for climbing.  Most of these handholds are formed\nwhere pockets of softer material was cut through by the water and it\nwashed away before its neighboring rock.  The shaft appears to continue\nboth up and down from here.  From below you can hear the movement of\nwater.\n',46,139592,15,0,0,0,0,0,6,120,0,'',NULL),
(7294,55,-122,2,'Vertical Shaft',' It appears this shaft was carved through the mountain by water,\nprobably over decades.  Its sides while polished smooth do offer\nnumerous handholds for climbing.  Most of these handholds are formed\nwhere pockets of softer material was cut through by the water and it\nwashed away before its neighboring rock.  The shaft appears to continue\nboth up and down from here.  From below you can hear the movement of\nwater.\n',46,139592,15,0,0,0,0,0,6,120,0,'',NULL),
