(7298,46,-128,-1,'Underground River',' Extremely fast and cold the water churns and thrashes you against the\nrocks around you.  The walls of the tunnel are incredibly slick and\nsmooth and you can find no decent handholds up as you fight to stay in\ncontrol.  Rocks and other debris pound your body endlessly as the\ncurrents attempt to pull you along.\n',46,139592,30,0,0,0,15,9,8,72,0,'',NULL),
(7299,45,-129,-1,'Underground River','Considerably small and cramped this section of the underground river\nappears to have cut its way through the rock.  A large gridwork of\nsolid stone still struggles in an endless battle with the current\nto survive, but has lost on many fronts.  Several holes in the\ngridwork can be seen and felt where a person might squeeze through\nto the south where you can just make out what appears to be\nlight of some type, possibly outside air.  To the northeast if\nyou can fight the strong current the tunnel continues.\n',46,139592,30,0,0,0,10,2,8,72,0,'',NULL),
(7300,18,-27,0,'Before a Towering Black Gate','  <B>A huge gate towers above you to the north.  It stands at least\ntwenty feet high and is about ten feet wide.  The gate is made of a strange\nglistening black metal.  Voices calling out in anguish can be heard from\nbeyond the gate.  A high wall made from stone spans to the east and west.\nA brick road runs to the south.<1>\n',51,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7301,19,-27,0,'Beneath a Towering Stone Wall','  You are at the base of a huge stone wall that runs along the southern\nedge of the prison.  The wall is riddled with holes and crevices here,\ntelling of an ancient assault upon the prison.  Originally, the peasants\nof Grimhaven rallied against the prison as a symbol of their oppression.\nEventually they decided that the countless adventurers roaming through\ntown, slaughtering them on sight, was a more pressing problem.\n',51,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7302,20,-27,0,'Beneath a Towering Stone Wall','  A low guttural growl is echoing from inside the prison.  The prison\nwall, though massive, serves to echo the noise, creating the illusion\nthat the sound is coming from all directions.  A small road runs east\nand west.\n',51,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7303,21,-27,1,'Halfway up a Prison Tower','  This is a small wooden platform halfway up the prison gate tower.  On\nextremely cold days the guards huddle down here, rather than standing\nabove and exposing themselves to the bitter elements.\n',51,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7304,21,-27,2,'Atop a Prison Tower','  From this vantage point you can see for miles.  Most of the prison yard is\nvisible.  However, there are numerous blind spots that the prisoners take\nadvantage of to sell contraband, start fights and occasionally kill each\nother in.  The prisoners also get to know which guards are diligent in\ntheir duties, and which ones are up here playing cards.\n',51,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7305,21,-27,0,'Beneath a Large Granite Rockface','  The prison wall molds into a large granite wall here.  It\nappears that the prison has been carved into a natural rock\nformation.  Because of this, the only way into, or out of\n the prison is through the front.  The natural granite walls\nmake tunneling out of the prison an impossibility.  It is\neasy to understand why it is said that anyone\nsentenced to life in prison here, is sentenced to death.\n',51,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7306,17,-21,0,'Weight Room','  The most common thing to do in prison, besides illegal drugs, is lifting\nweights.  Long rows of weight benches crowd this area.  Fights constantly\nerupt here, as the testosterone is usually in overdrive.  A wide assortment\nof prisoners are working out.  Some of them do it out of boredom, to take\ntheir mind off their troubles, others do it simply to sharpen their physical\nattributes in a futile attempt to prepare themselves for the inevitable\nbeating.  If you stand around here too long without working out,\nsomebody is bound to insult your mother and make derogatory slurs about\nyour choice of lifestyles.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7307,18,-21,0,'Gaming Area','  <b>The southern end of the recreation room is where the older prisoners\nplay cards, chess and various other games to eat away the time.  These\nolder prisoners take their games very seriously.  They have even established\ntheir own court system to deal with members caught cheating.  It is\nrumored that the prison chef is in charge of hiding the corpses of those\nexecuted for cheating.  One can only imagine how he could dispose of the\nbodies.  There is a strong breeze here that blows down the side of the\nsouthern wall, making it unbearably cold.  They choose this location for\ntheir games to reduce the likelihood of cheating.  It is rather difficult\nto cheat at cards with numb hands.<z>\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7308,19,-21,0,'Recreational Area','  This yard is where all prison grievances are taken out.  Any prisoner\nwho has a problem with another prisoner brings it to the yard.  The\nfights are usually short and fatal.  Most prisoners develop problems with\nthe old and infirm prisoners.  Other grievances arise because the guards\ntell a prisoner who they have a problem with.  Basically, the yard is a\nrecreation yard only in the sense that the guards use the prisoners in\nvarious hideous ways as recreation.  The rock hard ground has numerous\ngouges and pot holes that tell the tale of many battles.  A particularly\nlarge hole dominates the yard.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7309,20,-21,0,'Recreation Yard','  This is the southeast corner of the prison recreation yard.  The progressive\nbuilders of the prison envisioned this being the area where those wayward\nsouls could practice the social skills that would prepare them for their\neventual parole back into society.  However, what these benevolent people\nfailed to account for was the fact that the warden does not believe in\nparole.  The area is now the recreation area for the guards.  Their favorite\npast time is to take a small force of prisoners, arm half of them, and watch\nthe bloody chaos that ensues.  It is rumored that the head prison guard was\nonce a prisoner, who was successful in over twenty consecutive\nrecreational exercises.  Seeing the aptitude that this prisoner had for\nmutilating other prisoners, the warden figured he was a natural born guard.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7310,17,-20,0,'Recreation Yard','  Large clumps of grass are growing out of control here.  The ground is soft\nand mushy, and stinks of stagnant water.  With each step brown muddy\nwater seeps up from the saturated earth.  Guards take great pleasure in\nmaking prisoners exercise here, watching them shiver in the cold smelly\nmud.  A small hole in the wall, that was previously covered with mud,\nsoftly whistles as the wind whips through it.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7311,18,-20,0,'Recreation Yard','<p>It seems that one rather large prisoner has  claimed this area for himself,\nand nobody is in a big hurry to argue with him about it.  He likes to spend\nmost of his time camped under the tree reading and napping.  This seems to\nbe the one area in the prison where the ground is dry.  The warden ordered\nthe guards to amend the situation by soaking the ground with water, but\nthey were not very anxious to interfere with the prison hierarchy.<z>\n',-1,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7312,17,-27,0,'Beneath a Towering Stone Wall','  A huge wall towers above a dirt road running east and west.  The huge\nstone wall makes the prison impenetrable, breaking the spirit of the\nprisoners.  Since the time the prison was built, nobody has ever\nsuccessfully escaped the prison, and those who try are punished\nseverely.  It is rumored that the warden is able to keep people alive\nmuch beyond their normal life span for the sole purpose of torturing\nthem.\n',51,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7313,16,-27,0,'Beneath a Towering Stone Wall','  A huge stone wall towers above you to the north.  A small road\nruns east and west from here.  The wall is very solid and smooth,\nit almost impossible to climb.  An occasional scream can be heard from\nbeyond the wall.  There is a large <r>blood stain<z> on the wall, about\nfive feet off the ground.\n',51,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7314,15,-27,1,'Halfway up a Prison Watchtower','  This is a small wooden platform halfway up the prison gate tower.  On\nextremely cold days the guards huddle down here, rather than standing\nabove and exposing themselves to the bitter elements.\n',51,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7315,15,-27,2,'Prison Watchtower','  The guards are able to see for miles from this vantage point.  From\nhere the guards should be able to see and prevent any trouble in the\nprison yard.  However, the guards are poorly paid civil servants, and as\nsuch could not care whether the prisoners beat each other to death or not.\n',51,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7316,15,-27,0,'Beneath a Large Granite Rockface','  <g>The path beneath the large granite rockface abruptly ends at a  rickety\nlooking wooden staircase that leads up to the watchtower.  The guards have\ncarved various etchings into the rockface out of sheer boredom.<z>\n',51,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7317,17,-19,0,'Escape Tunnel','  <b>  A small escape tunnel has been started here.  Apparently whomever\nstarted it decided that tunneling through granite with makeshift\ntools was too much effort.<z>\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7318,16,-21,0,'Short Hallway','  <G>Plush carpets adorn this short hallway.  The walls are lined with archaic\ntapestries and a large gothic mirror sits along the northern wall.  There is a \nghostly howling sound as the wind wisps through the crevices in the walls.  \nThe air is slightly humid, despite its coolness.  The relative tranquility of \nthis room belies the harsh realities of the tumultuous prison yard that is a \nscant few feet away.<z>\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7319,16,-21,1,'Prison Library','  This is part of the huge prison library.  Endless books adorn the\nbookcases.  Several book stand out from the other nondescript titles.\nAt first glance it appears that the prison has a great interest in\neducating the inmates.  However, closer inspection reveals that\n the books are covered in dust and have probably not been read\nin years.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7320,16,-20,1,'Prison Library','  The prison library is a large and well-stocked facility that offers\na wide variety of titles for the educated prisoner to read.  However,\na thick layer of dust reveals that the books have not been read in\nyears.  The bright side to this is that the books are perfectly\norganized and easy to find.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7321,17,-20,1,'Prison Library','  This huge library houses an impressive collection of books and\ntombs to be read.  The thick layer of dust covering the books\nreveals how little they are used.  A lopsided table has been\npropped on a small book in an effort to stabilize it.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7322,17,-21,1,'Prison Library','<y>  Countless rows and stacks of books fill this room.  By the amount\nof dust coating the books it is quite apparent that the prisoners have\nno desire to read.  A small chart is pasted to the wall.\n<z>',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7323,18,-26,0,'Short Corridor','<c>  This short corridor runs north and south.  To the south is the\nproverbial path to freedom.  The corridor appears to be a\nmanmade cave that has been carved into the rock.  The walls\nand ceiling are made from solid stone, destroying any hope of a\nprisoner tunneling his way to freedom.  The walls are a shiny black\nmaterial that reflects images.  Parts of the wall are jagged and\nsharp.  These jagged areas could cause some nasty wounds.<z>\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7324,18,-25,0,'Register\'s Desk','<r>  This is the prison filter.  Everybody that enters the prison must\npass through here.  For many of the entering prisoners, this desk\nrepresents the last time they will be close to freedom.  Although\nmany criminals enter the prison here, few, if any ever leave the\nsame way alive.  The prison does not focus on rehabilitation, but\nrather on retribution and punishment.  The current warden\'s\nphilanthropic work consists of feeding dead prisoners to the prison\nrats and roaches.<z>\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7325,19,-25,0,'Guard Locker Room','  This is the guards locker room.  It is here that the guards swap\ntheir street clothes for their prison uniforms.  In here the guards\nmentally prepare themselves to risk life and limb guarding the scum\nof the earth.  Some people say it is here that they leave behind all of\ntheir humanity and become raging monsters willing to beat a prisoner\nsenseless with little or no provocation.  The guards rebut these\nallegations by claiming they never beat senseless an innocent man.\nSeveral footlockers containing the guards belongings are scattered\nabout.  You wonder why anyone who makes so little money, has\nnothing of value, and who is trained in the fine art of brutality needs\nto lock up their belongings.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7326,20,-25,0,'Bathroom','  This is the guards bathroom.  The stone walls are covered with\nmold and filth.  This room looks and smells as if it has not been\ncleaned in a very long time.  Apparently, nobody has pointed out to\nthe guards that they could assign prisoners the dubious job of\nkeeping this room spotless.  As you look around, you become\nconvinced that it is the solid prison walls that prevent the prisoners\nfrom escaping, rather than the sophistication of the prison guards.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7327,21,-25,0,'Laundry Room','  This is the laundry room that allows any guard who takes pride in\nhis uniform the ability to keep it clean and stain free.  Most of the\nequipment looks as if it has been unused for years.  Some of it is\nactually rotted and falling apart.  Most of the guards profess to\nkeep the blood stains on their uniforms as a warning to those\nprisoners contemplating stepping out of line.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7328,17,-25,0,'Visitor\'s Lounge','  This is the waiting room for friends and family of the prisoners.\nVisitors can wait here in comfort before they get to see the\nprisoners.  This room was built on the direct orders of the warden,\nwho was trying to curry favor with those who believe that prison\nshould be a chance for those wayward souls who run afoul of the\nlaw to redeem themselves.  The warden also realized that visitors\nwould wait longer if they were comfortable, thereby giving the\nguards some time to make the prisoners look as if they were being\ntreated humanely.  However, since it was built, the warden has\nnever allowed a single visitor.  It is rumored that early on there\nwere a few visitors who were adamant about visiting, but these\nwould be guests quickly became permanent residents.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7329,16,-25,0,'Visitor\'s Cafeteria','  This is a small relaxing room, designed to allow people to relax\nwhile they grab a bite to eat.  The walls are painted a melodic\nyellow, designed to keep even the most aggressive personalities\ncalm.  Several small tables clutter the room, and a small picture is\nhung on the wall.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7330,15,-25,0,'Bathroom','  This is a small seldom used bathroom.  The floor has been covered\nwith a nice red shag carpet.  Originally designed for the comfort of\nprison visitors, it is generally used now as a smoke room by the\nprison guards.  Some writing has been etched into one of the walls.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7331,17,-24,0,'Break Room','  This room is where the guards take a break and relax.  This room\nallows them some momentary solace from the hectic chaos that\nruns their lives in the prison.  The stone walls have been painted a\ndull blue to make the guards feel more at ease.  The walls in the\nroom make you feel more relaxed.  The peaceful decorum of this\nroom is a stark ironic contrast to the harsh realities of the prison.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7332,18,-24,0,'Search Room','  This room is where all people entering and leaving the prison are\nsearched for illegal contraband.  People entering the prison\nfrequently attempt to smuggle money, weapons, clothing and food\nto the prisoners.  People caught smuggling such items into the\nprison are quickly transformed from visitor, to inmate.  A large\ndesk dominates the room.  A small line drawn on the floor dictates\nwhere people are to wait while their belongings are searched.  If\nthe head guard is in a bad mood, he has been known destroy\nproperty, all in the name of safety.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7333,19,-24,0,'Observation Room','  This room allows the guards to luxury of watching all the\nincoming traffic into the prison.  Originally designed with security\nprecautions in mind, it serves more of a voyeuristic purpose for the\nsadistic guards.  This perch allows them the ability to stare at\npeople all day long, without ever having to get off their feet.  The\nwalls are made of the same solid stone that the rest of the prison is,\nexcept for a small panel that has been painted black along the\neastern wall.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7334,20,-24,0,'Weapons Cache','  This small room is the prison storage facility.  The room\nis easily accessible to the guards, and contains most of\nthe items that the guards would need to suppress a\nprison riot.  The room also contains numerous torture\ndevices designed to make even the hardiest of souls\nconfess to whatever crime the warden has decided they\nhave committed.  The room itself is carved into the\nsurrounding rock formation, which keeps the room cold\nand damp.  The sleek black walls act as a mirror, making\nthe room appear larger than it is.  The numerous\ninsidious devices scattered about give the room a cold\nand vile feel.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7335,17,-23,0,'Common Area','  This is the southwest corner of the common area.  It is here that\nthe crafty jailhouse veterans hang out.  Staying in the corner\nallows them to keep an eye on all evildoers, enemies and would be\nSodomites, without exposing their vulnerable backsides to any\npossible assailants.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7336,18,-23,0,'Common Area','  This is the southern entrance to the prison common\narea.  It is here, if the warden is in a good mood, that\nthe prison population is allowed to congregate to play\ncards, chat, or just sit by and idly kill the time.  Long\nrows of tables have been set out for the comfort of the\nprisoners.  The floor is made of a solid black stone.  The\narea is kept impeccably clean.  A small sign is hung up\nabove.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7337,19,-23,0,'Common Area','  This is part of the prison common area.  Here prisoners can kill\ntime while serving their sentence.  It is common practice in the\nprison to keep yourself occupied as often as possible to prevent\nprisoners from staring at their calendars.  Of course considering\nthe rancid nature that the prison is kept in, the violent nature of the\nprisoners and the guards, combined with the cold, damp\natmosphere, most prisoners die well before their sentence has\nexpired.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7338,20,-23,0,'Common Area','  This is part of the prison common area.  Here prisoners can kill\ntime while serving their sentence.  It is common practice in the\nprison to keep yourself occupied as often as possible to prevent\nprisoners from staring at their calendars.  Of course considering\nthe rancid nature that the prison is kept in, the violent nature of the\nprisoners and the guards, combined with the cold, damp\natmosphere, most prisoners die well before their sentence has\nexpired.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7339,17,-22,0,'Common Area','  This is the northwest of the common area.  You have heard\nscattered rumors about the people that hang out here being a little\noff kilter, and until now you dismissed them as being rumors.\nHowever, looking around at the attire of the prisoners here, their\nspeech patterns, the way they dress and their mannerisms you are\nbeginning to wonder.  The table here has been adorned with a\nflowered tablecloth, and is spotless.  Somebody has even taken\nthe time to carve some flowers into the walls.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7340,18,-22,0,'Common Area','  This is the common area of the prison.  Here is where the prisoners\noften gather to play cards, gossip, plan escapes and off each other.\nThis room has been home to some of the bloodiest revolts in\nhistory.  In this very room prisoners devised and orchestrated the\nChristmas Day Massacre, the New Years Eve Executions, and the\ninfamous Valentines Day beheadings.  Although the floor is made\nfrom solid black stone, it has been stained red by the blood that has\nsplattered on it.  Despite the wardens frequent assurances that the\nprison is relatively peaceful and smoothly operated, there are\nnumerous signs scattered about to the contrary.  You are\nbeginning to wonder if the warden is not only the consummate\npolitician, but also a compulsive liar.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7341,19,-22,0,'Common Area','<r>  Prisoners spend most of their time milling about here waiting for\nsomething to happen.  The life of a prisoner is full of contrast- hours\nand hours of boredom followed by instant flashes of horrific violence.<z>\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7342,20,-22,0,'Common Area','  <b>The damp prison air has soaked the ground here into a soupy\nconcoction of mud and human waste.  The disgusting mixture clings to\neverything it touches as the smell seeps into your skin.<z>\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7343,17,-22,1,'Librarian\'s Desk','  <b> A large desk fashioned from oak dominates this room.  This corner\nof the library has no book shelves or books.  The librarian is\ngenerally here shaking her fist at anything that makes a sound.\nDespite the fact that this is a prison library, she takes great pride in\nrunning an efficient, well stocked and happy library.<1>\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7344,16,-22,1,'Quiet Study Area','  <c>This is a small corner of the library where the prisoners can read\nbooks in relative peace.  The best way to forget their surroundings\nis to immerse themselves in a great piece of literature.  Ironically\nthis study area was placed in the \"How To\" section of the library.<1>\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7345,16,-19,0,'Watchtower Base','  This is the foundation of a large stone watchtower.  Immense support\nbeams make walking through here treacherous.  A large scorch mark in the\ncenter of the area suggests that on particularly cold days the guards build a\nfire and huddle shivering around it, rather than climb the tower and expose\nthemselves to the elements.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7346,16,-19,1,'Watchtower','  The wind howls through here stinging your flesh.  Your eyes water from its\nintensity, and you quickly have the urge to get down from here.  A stable\nwooden floor creaks below you, and while wooden support beams cross\nabove you.  This vantage point offers a great view of the prison yard.\nGuards sit up here armed with crossbows hoping that somebody gives them\na reason to practice using it.  Guards have been known to try to shoot\nweights, food and cards from unwary prisoners.  Unfortunately, the guards\nhave very little training with these weapons and they often end up drilling\nan inadvertent target.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7347,19,-20,0,'Recreation Yard','  Dead barren weeds dot the landscape.  The earth is soft and squishy, and\nspits out water with every step.  The mud latches onto your feet and does\nnot want to let go.  The foul sulfur like smell seeps into everything you\nown.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7348,20,-20,0,'Recreation Yard','  Dead barren weeds dot the landscape.  The earth is soft and squishy, and\nspits out water with every step.  The mud latches onto your feet and does\nnot want to let go.  The foul sulfur like smell seeps into everything you\nown.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7349,21,-21,0,'Prison Bathroom','  The prison bathroom might be the most revolting place that you have ever\nbeen.  Giant vats that are brimming with waste line the walls.  A pungent\nodor fills the room and seeps into your gear.  Of all the reasons to stay out\nof prison, this room takes the cake.  The stone floor has been stained\nbeyond recognition.  Prisoners that get out of line are sent to this room and\nare not allowed to leave until the room is spotless.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7350,22,-21,0,'Prison Shower','This is the dreaded prison shower.  There is a creepy feeling that haunts\nthis room.  You continually feel as if there is somebody right behind you,\nbreathing stale warm air on the back of your neck.  Large vats of water stand\nin the corner, awaiting a bather.  Prison showers consist of guards grabbing\nthe prisoner by the feet and dunking him head first into the large vat.  The\nguard then holds the prisoner under the water until he is clean, or dead. \nBecause of this it is a common occurrence for prisoners to bribe guards rather\nthan shower.  Mildew is slowly creeping up the damp walls, and covers the\nfloor.  The mildew makes the floors extremely treacherous and slippery.  This\nis a dangerous place to be moving about.\n',-1,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7351,19,-19,0,'Stairwell','  A large spiral staircase leads down into the belly of the prison.  A cold\nblast of air shoots up from below, bringing with it the smell of rot and\ndecay.  Horrible sobs interspersed with screams of agony echo up from far\nbelow.  It is rumored that once a prisoner is sent to the belly of the prison,\nthey never return.  Other myths suggest that a mad scientist inhabits the\nprison, torturing prisoners with gleeful insanity, swapping brains, limbs\nand vital organs between monsters and prisoners, creating horrific mutants\nthat walk the earth in eternal damnation  searching for human flesh to feast\non, cramming it into a deformed head with huge protruding fangs dripping\nwith deadly poison.  Others suggest that except for the rodents its not that\nbad of a place.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7352,19,-19,-1,'Stairwell','  The temperature in this room is uncomfortably cold.  The\nwalls seem to come to life as the torch light sends flickering images\ndancing across them.  The shadows seem to cavort  and frolic together in\nan strange bacchanalian ritual.  With every twist and turn in the ritual the\nshadow seems to crouch to leap out at you with piercing claws.  The walls\nare damp and covered with green slime.  A melodic dripping at first\nsoothes you but quickly begins to irritate you beyond belief.  Hideous\nhowls can be heard from deep within the prison.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7353,19,-20,-1,'Cell Block Entrance','  The air in this area is deathly still.  Water cascading down from the\nceiling quickly drenches your clothing.  A strange <g>green mold<z>\ncovers the walls and ceilings.  The wavering torchlight makes focusing on\nanything difficult.  Despite the relative calm appearance to the prison, the\ncell blocks sink into the mountain, forming a dark and somber chasm.\nThere is a constant buzzing of groans, shrieks and cries for help that\nblend together, creating a dismal ambiance.  You can feel the prison itself\nclutching onto your spirit as you yearn to feel the warmth of the sun and\nthe crisp air from above.  Your will is almost overborne as you wonder if\nyou will ever see the surface again.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7354,20,-20,-1,'Entrance to \'B\' Block','  This is the northern entrance to the secondary cellblock.  This block\nhouses those prisoners that are deemed problems.  There really is no\nmethod to determining who is a problem prisoner.  Basically, whenever\nthe warden is in a bad mood he wanders the prison yard and randomly\nselects the problem prisoners that are in need of discipline.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7355,18,-20,-1,'Short Hallway','  This is the entrance to one of the most dangerous places known to man.\nThis prison houses the most vile, perverted, cruelest scum that has\nwalked the realm.  Most of the people housed here are victims of\ncircumstance.  Essentially, they failed to grease the pockets of the powers\nthat be and were sent here to reform.  This prison then takes these gentle\nsouls and transforms them into the hardest of criminals.  The guards\njokingly refer to it as a Boot Camp for the deranged.  The walls and\nceiling are slick with perspiration and seem to pulse with life.  Something\nhas been etched into the wall.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7356,17,-20,-1,'Entrance To \'A\' Block','  To the south is the primary cellblock of the prison.  Here prisoners from\nthe outside are taken and gradually beaten into a <r>fleshy pulp<z> by\nthe guards.  Once they are sufficiently trained to be docile and quivering\nblobs of jelly, they are then allowed to roam the prison.  Then they\nencounter the savage and crafty prisoners who take advantage of these\nbeaten souls.  It is the wardens personal policy to curtail the ever\nexpanding prison population.  In fact, it is rumored that he gives out\nconjugal visits to the prisoner who shanks the most prisoners, thereby\nreducing the prisons overhead.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7357,17,-21,-1,'Cellblock','  This is the main hallway of the prison block.  The air is permeated by a\nfoul smell of human waste.  From behind the locked doors you can hear\npeople whimpering and crying.  Occasionally a guard will beat on a cell\ndoor and yell \"Shut up fresh fish, or I will give you something to cry\nabout!\"  The air is damp and muggy and has a stale quality that comes\nfrom poor circulation and over crowding.  Periodically bugs and spiders\nscurry across your path.  You wonder how anyone can survive being\ncaged in this place.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7358,17,-22,-1,'Cellblock','  This is the main hallway of the prison block.  The air is permeated by a\nfoul smell of human waste.  From behind the locked doors you can hear\npeople whimpering and crying.  Occasionally a guard will beat on a cell\ndoor and yell \"Shut up fresh fish, or I will give you something to cry\nabout!\"  The air is damp and muggy and has a stale quality that comes\nfrom poor circulation and over crowding.  Periodically bugs and spiders\nscurry across your path.  You wonder how anyone can survive being\ncaged in this place.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7359,17,-23,-1,'Cellblock','  <p>The main hallway of the prison block continues here.  The air reeks\nof the foul odor of human waste.  Cries and pleas for help can be heard\ninside the locked cells.  The air is thick and damp and makes breathing\ndifficult.<z>\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7360,17,-24,-1,'Cellblock','  This is the southern end of the cellblock.  An extremely offensive odor is\nwafting in from the east.  The floor has a slight red tinge to it.  Muffled\nscreams can be heard to the north.  The air is slightly damp and has\na musty odor.  The granite walls and ceiling are carved into the\nmountain.  A slight covering of soggy sawdust covers the floor.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7361,20,-21,-1,'Cellblock','  This is the main hallway of the prison block.  The air is permeated by a\nfoul smell of human waste.  From behind the locked doors you can hear\npeople whimpering and crying.  Occasionally a guard will beat on a cell\ndoor and yell \"Shut up fresh fish, or I will give you something to cry\nabout!\"  The air is damp and muggy and has a stale quality that comes\nfrom poor circulation and over crowding.  Periodically bugs and spiders\nscurry across your path.  You wonder how anyone can survive being\ncaged in this place.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7362,20,-22,-1,'Cellblock','  This is the main hallway of the prison block.  The air is permeated by a\nfoul smell of human waste.  From behind the locked doors you can hear\npeople whimpering and crying.  Occasionally a guard will beat on a cell\ndoor and yell \"Shut up fresh fish, or I will give you something to cry\nabout!\"  The air is damp and muggy and has a stale quality that comes\nfrom poor circulation and over crowding.  Periodically bugs and spiders\nscurry across your path.  You wonder how anyone can survive being\ncaged in this place.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7363,20,-23,-1,'Cellblock','This is the main hallway of the prison block.  The air is permeated by a\nfoul smell of human waste.  From behind the locked doors you can hear\npeople whimpering and crying.  Occasionally a guard will beat on a cell\ndoor and yell \"Shut up fresh fish, or I will give you something to cry\nabout!\"  The air is damp and muggy and has a stale quality that comes\nfrom poor circulation and over crowding.  Periodically bugs and spiders\nscurry across your path.  You wonder how anyone can survive being\ncaged in this place.\n',0,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7364,20,-24,-1,'End of the Cellblock','  The cellblock comes to an abrupt end to the south.  The mountain wall to\nthe south appears to be solid marble, prohibiting any further mining in\nthat direction.  Small pockets of pyrite trickle through the granite walls.\nThe floor is a limestone base covered with a sprinkling of soggy sawdust\nthat the mice burrow into.  Since the guards generally loiter about here,\nthey keep this area warmer than the rest of the prison.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7365,16,-21,-1,'Two Man Cell','  This cell is completely barren of any conveniences.  Surprisingly there are\nnot even any cots to lie on.  The cell is depressingly small and cramped,\nforcing the two men to almost lie on top of each other.  The air reeks\nbeyond belief.  In the far corner is a small tin bucket that serves as a\nchamber pot.  It is over flowing and appears that it has not been changed\nin weeks.  Various oddities have been carved into the walls.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7366,16,-22,-1,'Prison Cell','  This cell is completely barren of any conveniences.  Surprisingly there are\nnot even any cots to lie on.  The cell is depressingly small and cramped,\nforcing the two men to almost lie on top of each other.  The air reeks\nbeyond belief.  In the far corner is a small tin bucket that serves as a\nchamber pot.  It is over flowing and appears that it has not been changed\nin weeks.  Various oddities have been carved into the walls.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7367,16,-23,-1,'Grungy Cell','  This cell is completely barren of any conveniences.  Surprisingly there are\nnot even any cots to lie on.  The cell is depressingly small and cramped,\nforcing the two men to almost lie on top of each other.  The air reeks\nbeyond belief.  In the far corner is a small tin bucket that serves as a\nchamber pot.  It is over flowing and appears that it has not been changed\nin weeks.  Various oddities have been carved into the walls.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7368,16,-24,-1,'Torture Room','  <r>This is where the prisoners are taken for their daily beatings.  The guards\nbring them here, rather than beat them in their cells as a form of terror\ntraining.  The theory is that the prisoners will never want to leave their\ncells.  Regardless of how effective the practice is, it breaks the monotony\nfor the guards and causes the prisoners to shriek in agony whenever their\ncell doors are opened.<z>\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7369,18,-21,-1,'Two Man Cell','  This cell is completely barren of any conveniences.  Surprisingly there are\nnot even any cots to lie on.  The cell is depressingly small and cramped,\nforcing the two men to almost lie on top of each other.  The air reeks\nbeyond belief.  In the far corner is a small tin bucket that serves as a\nchamber pot.  It is over flowing and appears that it has not been changed\nin weeks.  Various oddities have been carved into the walls.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7370,18,-22,-1,'Prison Cell','  This cell is completely barren of any conveniences.  Surprisingly there are\nnot even any cots to lie on.  The cell is depressingly small and cramped,\nforcing the two men to almost lie on top of each other.  The air reeks\nbeyond belief.  In the far corner is a small tin bucket that serves as a\nchamber pot.  It is over flowing and appears that it has not been changed\nin weeks.  Various oddities have been carved into the walls.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7371,18,-23,-1,'Small Cell','  This cell is completely barren of any conveniences.  Surprisingly, there are\nnot even any cots to lie on.  The cell is depressingly small and cramped,\nforcing the two men to almost lie on top of each other.  The air reeks\nbeyond belief.  In the far corner is a small tin bucket that serves as a\nchamber pot.  It is over flowing and appears that it has not been changed\nin weeks.  Various oddities have been carved into the walls.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7372,18,-24,-1,'Morgue','  A large pile of rotting corpses is festering in the middle of this room.\nPieces of rotting flesh are scattered about the room.  Bimonthly the\nguards come here, scoop up the aging meat and take it to the ration\nfactory for processing.  They swear that it is the fermentation process\nthat gives rations their unique flavor.  Various herbs have been piled\naround the room.  It is unclear if this is to add flavor to the meat or to\ncurtail the foul odor of rotting flesh.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7373,19,-21,-1,'Four Man Cell','  This damp dark room houses some of the lowest scum on the earth.  This\nroom has held murderers, terrorists and assassins.  The rooms are kept\ncompletely empty to prevent the prisoners from making a makeshift\nweapon.  Early in the history of the prison the guards learned a lesson;\ndesperate prisoners can make a weapon from just about anything.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7374,19,-22,-1,'Small Prison Cell','  This damp dark room houses some of the lowest scum on the earth.  This\nroom has held murderers, terrorists and assassins.  The rooms are kept\ncompletely empty to prevent the prisoners from making a makeshift\nweapon.  Early in the history of the prison the guards learned a lesson;\ndesperate prisoners can make a weapon from just about anything.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7375,19,-23,-1,'<c>Prison Cell<z>','  This damp dark room houses some of the lowest scum on the earth.  This\nroom has held murderers, terrorists and assassins.  The rooms are kept\ncompletely empty to prevent the prisoners from making a makeshift\nweapon.  Early in the history of the prison the guards learned a lesson;\ndesperate prisoners can make a weapon from just about anything.\n',51,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7376,19,-24,-1,'Cellblock Showers','  This area was originally designed as a place where the prisoners could\nclean up.  The original founders designed the prison as a place to\nrehabilitate the street urchins of society.  However, the current warden\ntook over and now reigns with an iron fist.  The purpose of the prison is\nnow to punish and demean the prisoners.  There is no longer a goal of\nreintroducing rehabilitated prisoners back into the stream of society.  In\nfact, there are no longer any prisoners being released.  The only way a\nprisoner leaves is through the ration factory, to support the prisons\nbudding economic endeavors.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7377,21,-21,-1,'Four Man Cell','  This damp dark room houses some of the lowest scum on the earth.  This\nroom has held murderers, terrorists and assassins.  The rooms are kept\ncompletely empty to prevent the prisoners from making a makeshift\nweapon.  Early in the history of the prison the guards learned a lesson;\ndesperate prisoners can make a weapon from just about anything.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7378,21,-22,-1,'Small Prison Cell','  This damp dark room houses some of the lowest scum on the earth.  This\nroom has held murderers, terrorists and assassins.  The rooms are kept\ncompletely empty to prevent the prisoners from making a makeshift\nweapon.  Early in the history of the prison the guards learned a lesson;\ndesperate prisoners can make a weapon from just about anything.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7379,21,-23,-1,'Prison Cell','  This damp dark room houses some of the lowest scum on the earth.  This\nroom has held murderers, terrorists and assassins.  The rooms are kept\ncompletely empty to prevent the prisoners from making a makeshift\nweapon.  Early in the history of the prison the guards learned a lesson;\ndesperate prisoners can make a weapon from just about anything.\nOddly, unlike the other cells this room has a small toilet.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7380,21,-24,-1,'Guard Post','  What was once the largest prison cell in the prison has been turned into a\nbreak room for the guards.  The guards, who are supposed to be\npatrolling the cellblock, are often found relaxing here.  They coax a prisoner\nto walk the halls making a lot of noise to keep the prisoners in line.  Since\nthe prisoners cannot see out from their cells they do not know the\ndifference.  The temperature in this room is pleasantly warm, unlike the\nrest of the prison.  The guards have placed various herbs around the\nroom to suppress the prison odors.  They have placed a plush carpet on\nthe floor.  Various chairs and other conveniences are scattered about.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7381,18,-21,1,'Un-Furnished Room','  <r>This empty room is the warden\'s waiting room.  Apparently he\ncares very little for the comfort of his guests.  There room is\ncompletely devoid of furniture.  The floor and walls have been\nleft bumpy.  Large hills and holes cover the room, making\ntraversing the room difficult.  The air in the room is hot and\nmuggy.  You begin to wonder why the warden hates people so\nmuch.<1>\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7382,18,-20,1,'Well Furnished Office','  This is a huge office.  A solid oak desk sits along the far wall.\n>From his comfortable roost, the warden runs the entire prison.\nIn his office, detached from the heartbeat of the prison, the\nwarden decides which prisoners live, are paroled, or executed.\nThe room has a cold and vile feel about it.  There are no chairs\nin the room besides the one behind the wardens desk.  He likes\nto make people as uncomfortable as possible.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7383,22,-23,-1,'Start of an Escape Tunnel','  This room was once a budding desperate attempt to gain freedom.  It has\nsince been turned into a prison supply shop of contraband.  Because the\nshopkeeper is smart enough to grease the pockets of the guards they look\nthe other way.  The back of a small toilet is set into the east wall.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7384,17,-25,-1,'Spiral Staircase','  A small spiral staircase leads down into a dark somber hole,\nfrom which a small blast of cool air sporadically pulses up.  The\nsmall draft of wind keeps this room one of the few places in the\nprison that does not reek of stale air and mildew.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7385,17,-25,-2,'Bottom of a Spiral Staircase','  The air on this level is icy and stings the flesh.  This level of the prison\nwas recently built, and is approximately forty feet below the surface.\nMany who come down here wonder if they will ever see the surface\nagain.  The walls are carved into a dark and slick stone.  Unlike the\nmarble and granite walls of the above levels, nothing is able to grow\ndown here, despite the steady stream of water that cascades down the\nwalls.  The water forms a pool that is about an inch deep and ominously\ndark.  Small ice crystals float through the water.  Occasionally, a small\npocket of air burps to the surface.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7386,17,-24,-2,'Damp Hallway','  Black water cascades down the walls and is coagulating on the floor.\nThe water is slowly flowing to the south.  A small outgrowth that\nresembles a tiny volcano sits in the middle of the hallway.  The air is cold\nand crisp and your breath can be seen spewing out before you.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7387,17,-23,-2,'Damp Hallway','  The water flow from above has slowed to a trickle here.  Loud splashing\ncan be heard to the south.  The floor is slick and icy as the floor has\nleveled off and trapped the water, allowing it to freeze.  Small crystal\ngrowths hang from the roof of the cave.  The air stinks of wet fur,\nsuggesting that it was not always man that occupied it.  Deep claw marks\nfrom the caves former occupant are grooved into the wall.  You\nremember an old story that you had quickly dismissed when you heard it\nabout a fearsome man eating monster that the warden kept as a pet.\nDespite your best efforts you feel your stomach knot up at the thought of\nencountering the dreaded beast.  You cannot be sure, but you think you\nhear a low guttural growl coming from all directions.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7388,17,-22,-2,'Damp Hallway','  The smell of wet fur has become overwhelming.  It smells like a mangy\ndog that has been swimming in swamp water.  The black rock walls are\nglistening with water.  A low growling noise can be heard coming from\nthe north.  The growling is getting louder by the second.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7389,17,-21,-2,'Damp Hallway','  There is a small nest here made from straw and sawdust.  Small chicken\nbones lie scattered about.  In the northeast corner there is some paper on\nthe floor that a puppy has been using as a bathroom.  The guards keep\nthis area warm and well lit for their mascot.  A small water bowl has been\noverturned next to the nest.  Various puppy toys lie scattered about.\nOnce, a prisoner made the mistake of slapping the puppy, after it had\nstolen the prisoner’s bread.  The guards proceeded to torture the poor\nman, who was eventually put out of his misery when his fellow prisoners\nmercifully ended his suffering.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7390,18,-24,-2,'Guard\'s Recreational Room','  The guards often gather to gossip, play cards and reminisce about\nparticularly savage beatings that they have handed out over the years.\nThis room is starkly out of place here in the prison.  Blankets cover the\nwalls and floors, keeping some of the warmth in the room.  The guards\nchange the blankets every day, otherwise the blankets become saturated\nwith water from the dripping walls and begin to reek of mildew.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7391,19,-24,-2,'Coffee Room','  This is one of the many areas that functions as a break room for the\nguards.  Although the prisoners are denied every modern convenience,\nthe guards are living in luxury.  They channel most of the food and water\nmeant for the prisoners here for their own use.  They then sell the food to\nthe prisoners that is rightly theirs anyway.  This room is pleasantly warm\nand is well lit.  The dark rock walls have been covered with blankets that\nwere undoubtedly intended to keep the prisoners warm.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7392,20,-24,-2,'Weapons Cache','  The original purpose of this room was to store weapons in the advent of a \nprison riot.  The guards convinced the warden not to bother, insisting that \nif a riot were to happen a cache would just give the prisoners access to \nweapons.  While this seems logical, the reality is the prisoners are probably \nbetter armed than the guards are anyway.  There is some straw matting in the \ncorner of the room.  It seems that somebody has turned this room into a secret\nbedroom.  How he is able to get supplies remains a mystery though.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7393,18,-21,-2,'Entrance to the Prison Hospital','  The prison hospital reeks of formaldehyde.  The smell of medication\nseeps into everything.  This is the most feared place in the prison.\nPrisoners have been known to amputate limbs only needing stitches to\navoid having to see these butchers.  Ironically, most of the so called\ndoctors were previously butchers, who lost their jobs when most of\nBrightmoon decided to become vegetarian.  A small <p>plaque<z>\nhangs on the wall.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7394,19,-21,-2,'Prison Hospital','  Apparently, surgeries are performed right on the floor.  The surgeons,\nwho are realists, realize anyone strong enough to live through the surgery\nitself, is strong enough to live though some minor infections.  A small vat\nof anesthetic sits in the corner next to a table holding the surgical tools.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7395,20,-21,-2,'Recovery Room','  Inexplicably, this room appears to have never been used.  The beds are\nperfectly made, the bed pans are spotless and there is a fine film of dust\ncovering the floor, revealing that nobody has been in this room for ages.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7396,18,-22,-2,'Patient\'s Quarters','  Prisoners with minor ailments are kept here.  If they are financially able to\nbribe the doctors to leave them alone, then it is a nice place to stay.  The\nbeds are dry and soft, the food is often lukewarm, and the nurse is rather\ncute.  Buckets have been strategically placed to catch the dripping water,\nkeeping the floor relatively dry.  One of the doctors has a theory that the\nminerals in the water have amazing regenerative powers.  The jury is still\nout on this, but it does explain his hair loss.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7397,19,-22,-2,'Patient\'s Quarters','  Prisoners with minor ailments are kept here.  If they are financially able to\nbribe the doctors to leave them alone, then it is a nice place to stay.  The\nbeds are dry and soft, the food is often lukewarm, and the nurse is rather\ncute.  Buckets have been strategically placed to catch the dripping water,\nkeeping the floor relatively dry.  One of the doctors has a theory that the\nminerals in the water have amazing regenerative powers.  The jury is still\nout on this, but it does explain his hair loss.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7398,20,-22,-2,'Gift Shop','  Like any good hospital, even the prison hospital has an over priced gift\nshop.  Available for purchase are numerous useless trinkets that they are\ncharging an arm and a leg for, literally.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7399,18,-23,-2,'Patient\'s Quarters','  Prisoners with minor ailments are kept here.  If they are financially able to\nbribe the doctors to leave them alone, then it is a nice place to stay.  The\nbeds are dry and soft, the food is often lukewarm, and the nurse is rather\ncute.  Buckets have been strategically placed to catch the dripping water,\nkeeping the floor relatively dry.  One of the doctors has a theory that the\nminerals in the water have amazing regenerative powers.  The jury is still\nout on this, but it does explain his hair loss.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7400,19,-23,-2,'Experimentation Room','  This is where the dreaded prison doctor performs his infamous\nexperiments.  He seems to get a strange kick from attaching different\nlimbs to different creatures, creating exotic hybrid mutants.  There is a\nlarge table with retraining straps on it that serves to keep the patients\ndocile for him.  The dim torchlight flickering off the walls serves to make\nthis place even spookier than it would otherwise be.  He has etched\nsketches into the wall of some of his more horrific creations.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7401,20,-23,-2,'Biohazard Room','  Random body parts and chemicals have been thrown into this room to rot\nand gather dust.  This small dead end room serves as a storage space for\nthe messes that nobody wants to deal with.  The walls are scorched from\nthe monthly burns that are used to clear the room out.  Once a month, the\ndoctors throw some oil into the room and ignite the entire room, sealing\nit off to prevent the spread of the fire.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7402,16,-21,-2,'Sanitarium','  The prison sanitarium is where those members of society that\nare no longer right in the head are sent.  In an ideal society they\nwould obtain the treatment and counseling necessary to grant\nthem sanity.  Here, they appease the staff’s idol curiosity.  Most\nof the patients here were completely sane before they got here.\nNow they are clearly insane.  Strange noises permeate the air, as\nthe deranged attempt to convey messages with social skills that\nhave been warped beyond repair.  A small <b>wooden sign<z> hangs\n from the ceiling.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7403,15,-21,-2,'Sanitarium','  This area of the sanitarium appears to be Dr.  Laura’s work area.  The\nspace is cluttered and messy.  She has potted <g>flowers<z> scattered\nabout in an attempt to add some cheery hospitality to the room.  The\nplace reeks of coffee and ammonia.  There is a very fake and plastic feel\nto this area.  A <p>small poster<z> has been pasted to the wall.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7404,14,-21,-2,'Sanitarium','  This station is where Dr.  Prasler does most of his work.  His area is very\nwell organized and everything is clean.  The dark walls have been\ncovered with some <c>pastel paintings<1> that are designed to make\npeople happier.  His entire philosophy is better living through colors.\nThe floor is frequently mopped in a futile effort to keep it dry and clean.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7405,14,-22,-2,'Sanitarium','  Numerous devices are scattered about here, designed to administer\nvarious tests on the unfortunate patients.  Although all of the prison\npsychiatrists have the title of doctor, they have no real training.  It is a\ncushy job to get and allows them the freedom to practice every screwball\nidea that pops into their heads.  One of them even tried to cure a patient\nthat suffered from multiple personalities by surrounding him with mirrors.\nAnother crackpot tried to cure patients with barium enemas.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7406,15,-22,-2,'Sanitarium','  This room is home to a radical experiment.  It is designed to treat insane\npeople by reverting them to their childhood, and then retaking them step\nby step back to adulthood.  Currently numerous patients are scurrying\naround the place in pajamas playing with toys.  The patients are forced to\nact like children until such a time that they are deemed regressed, and then\nthey are raised back to adulthood.  The doctors have no idea if it works,\nbut they sure think it is funny to watch.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7407,16,-22,-2,'Sanitarium','  The <B>jet black rock walls<z> have been painted white in an effort to\ngive the room a more peaceful feel to it.  The constant <b>dripping\nwater<z>  has caused the paint to blur into the black rocks, resulting in a\nghoulish pattern resembling faces contorted in agony.  Small crystals\nglisten in the ceiling overhead when the flickering torchlight hits them.\nDespite the best efforts to the contrary, this room is a dark and somber\nroom.  There is a cold and sterile feel to the room that sucks the life from\nthose in it.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7408,14,-23,-2,'Entrance to the Morgue','  This is the morgues sorting room.  The corpses that  are brought in are\nsorted by various different categories here before being shipped to\ndifferent areas in the morgue.  There are currently no backlogged bodies,\nas this seems to be the only area of the prison that is run efficiently.  A\nlarge wooden sign is fixed to the wall.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7409,15,-23,-2,'Prison Morgue','  Judging by the various mutilated corpses and body parts strewn about\nthis must be area one.  A large pile of body parts is in the corner,\nawaiting to be dealt with.  The floor is slick with <r>blood<z>.  The\nfoul smell of rotting flesh permeates the air.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7410,16,-23,-2,'Prison Morgue','  The air here smells of spoiled meat.  This must be the dreaded area two.\nDisease and vermin are everywhere.  The body parts that lie about are\nbarely recognizable.  Most have been attacked by some unknown disease\nthat eats the flesh from the bones.  As you wonder about how safe it is to\nbe in here, you hope that the disease is not airborne.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7411,14,-24,-2,'Prison Morgue','  When this room is not overflowing with corpses, the morgue workers\n use it as a break room.  They try to keep this area relatively clean, but\nunder the circumstances it is just not possible.  <b>Water<z>  seeps\ndown the walls mixing in with the body parts to form a <r>bloody\nstew.<z>  This makes traversing this area exceptionally perilous.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7412,15,-24,-2,'Prison Morgue','A large number of corpses are strewn about.  These are the prisoners that the\nguards have beaten to death.  The number of corpses seem endless.  Amazingly,\nthis room is cleaned out on a weekly basis.  The corpses are barely\nrecognizable.  Most have been pummeled into a faceless jelly.\n',-1,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7413,16,-24,-2,'Prison Morgue','  This is area 3.  Judging by the large number of corpses scattered about,\nmedical malpractice must be a booming field.  The corpses were all supplied\ncompliments of the prison hospital.  Poorly sutured wounds were allowed to\nbleed out, became infected or were just neglected.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7414,17,-20,-2,'Top of a Stairwell','  A rickety stairway has been set into the wall.  It is continuously creaking\nand swaying in the wind.  A blast of cold air gushes in from below.\nChisel marks can be seen in the walls where the miners carved this tunnel.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7415,17,-20,-3,'Stairwell','  The temperature here is cold and brisk.  The water that drips down\n the walls has frozen, forming creepy frozen fingers that seem to be\nclutching the floor from above.  These icy fingers are frozen and\nblack and seam ready to clutch you at any second.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7416,17,-21,-3,'Damp Hallway','  The walls of this hallway are sheeted with <b>dark slick ice<z>.  The\nfloor appears to be regularly scraped and salted to prevent it from\nbecoming a treacherous runway.  Large icicles dangle from above,\nthreatening to launch down at you in a deadly attack.  Some of them are\nover four feet long and would impale you with a deadly force.  The salt\nand the ground threatens to rust anything metal that it comes into contact\nwith.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7417,17,-22,-3,'Damp Hallway','  The walls of this hallway are sheeted with <b>dark slick ice<z>.  The\nfloor appears to be regularly scraped and salted to prevent it from\nbecoming a treacherous runway.  Large icicles dangle from above,\nthreatening to launch down at you in a deadly attack.  Some of them are\nover four feet long and would impale you with a deadly force.  The salt\nand the ground threatens to rust anything metal that it comes into contact\nwith.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7418,17,-23,-3,'Damp Hallway','The walls of this hallway are sheeted with <b>dark slick ice<z>.  The\nfloor appears to be regularly scraped and salted to prevent it from\nbecoming a treacherous runway.  Large icicles dangle from above,\nthreatening to launch down at you in a deadly attack.  Some of them are\nover four feet long and would impale you with a deadly force.  The salt\non the ground threatens to rust anything metal that it comes into contact\nwith.\n',-1,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7419,18,-23,-3,'Short Hallway','  A short cold hallway runs east and west.  The stone walls are sheeted\nwith black ice.  The floor has been recently salted.  The cold air stings\nyour flesh.  The torchlight flickering off the black ice reflects your image\nback at you off the walls.  Due to the dim light and the uneven black\nsurface your reflection appears to be contorted in pain.  Your breath\nreflects back in at you, appearing to be a noxious vapor.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7420,19,-23,-3,'Entrance to the Prison Workshop','  You are entering the economic backbone of the prison.  The corpses of\nthe dead are brought here to be transformed into rations that are then\nshipped off to Grimhaven, Logrus, Amber and the Shire.  The ration\nfactory mashes, pounds, tenderizes, drains and then packages the human\nflesh into compact units that are easily carried and generate a lot of\nenergy.  There is a secret ingredient that the Chemist keeps that he will\nnot reveal to anyone.  He claims that it gives them that little extra spark\nto keep the weary traveler going.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7421,20,-23,-3,'Rotting Food Pile','  Rotting <r>piles of flesh<1> have been cut from the bone and are being\naged for the proper texture, elasticity and sponginess.  Strands of\n<g>herbs<1> have been hung from the ceiling to give the meat its proper\nflavor.  A large <p>vat<1> rests in the corner of the room.  The\n<r>flesh<1> has a shiny quality to it, obviously from some sort of\n<g>chemical<1> that it is being treated with.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7422,20,-22,-3,'Corpse Pile','  The corpses are piled here before the flesh is peeled from the bones.\nLarge mixers take the flesh and grind up the meat into a messy jelly, that\nis later combined with grass, twigs and the secret ingredient to create the\nwonder known as the ration.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7423,19,-22,-3,'Ration Factory','  After the flesh is removed from the bones it is taken here to be mashed\ntogether to form the ration shape.  Anything that falls into the meat pile\nhere is mashed into the ration.  Over the years rats, clothing, bandages\nand countless other oddities have found there way into the final product\nas well.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7424,19,-21,-3,'Ration Factory','  This is the quality control center of the ration factory.  Here the rations\nare inspected for any noticeable signs of the source of the rations.  One\ncan only imagine what would happen to the ration sales if the general\npublic discovered they were all cannibals.  Rations that show any signs of\ntheir ingredients, such as a protruding finger, are pulled aside here for a\nmakeover.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7425,20,-21,-3,'Ration Factory','  It is here that the chemist adds his secret ingredient to the rations.  He\nguards the secret with his life, refusing to share it with anyone.  He keeps\nthe chemical here in large vats until it is sprayed over the rotting flesh\nbefore it is mashed into the ration shape.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7426,19,-20,-3,'Sorting Room','  The rations are sorted here by quality.  Those that have been given a bit\nextra of the secret potion are labeled as iron provisions, and are sold at a\nhigher price.  Those with less are sold as ordinary rations.  The food\nstuffs are piled high above.  The mystery about the rations is that\nalthough they have a shelf-life of over fifty years, once purchased\nthey rapidly spoil.  This is the true magic of the secret sauce at work.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7427,20,-20,-3,'Shipping Room','This is where the final stages of the ration process are completed.  It is\nhere that the rations are sprayed with a rat poison to prevent the vermin\nfrom consuming them on the journey throughout the realm.  Large piles\nof rations are stacked beneath four signs, one each for Amber, the Shire,\nLogrus and Brightmoon.  A small sign is hanging from the ceiling.\n',0,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7428,16,-23,-3,'Short Hallway','  A short and cold hallway runs east and west.  The stone walls are\nsheeted with black ice and the floor has been salted recently.  As the\ncold air stings your flesh, the torchlight flickering off the black ice\nreflects your image back at you.  Due to the dim light and the uneven\nsurface of the ice your reflection appears to be contorted in pain.\nYour breath reflects back at you, appearing to be a noxious vapor.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7429,15,-23,-3,'Entrance to the Cafeteria','  <r>The prison cafeteria is the home of more prison hits than any other\narea in the prison.  In fact, so many people are killed here that the\nprisoners now refer to any meal to be eaten here as \'the last supper.\'\nThe prisoners prefer to eat their meals with their backs to the walls, to\nthwart any potential sneak attack.  This has led to a hierarchy centered\naround the seating, and many new prisoners are often shanked for unknowingly\nsitting in the wrong seat.<z>\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7430,14,-23,-3,'Long Row of Tables','  The prisoners gather three times a day to eat meals here.  The walls are\ncovered with ice as is the ceiling.  The tables are unsteady and often\ncollapse during the meals.  This is the most common place for a prisoner\nto be shanked.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7431,14,-22,-3,'Long Row of Tables','  The prisoners gather three times a day to eat meals here.  The walls are\ncovered with ice as is the ceiling.  The tables are unsteady and often\ncollapse during the meals.  This is the most common place for a prisoner\nto be shanked.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7432,15,-22,-3,'Long Row of Tables','  The prisoners gather three times a day to eat meals here.  The walls are\ncovered with ice as is the ceiling.  The tables are unsteady and often\ncollapse during the meals.  This is the most common place for prisoner\nto be shanked.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7433,14,-21,-3,'Private Dining Room','  As in any social system there is a hierarchy among the prisoners.  Those\nat the top of the food chain have their own private eating area, away from\nthe other prisoners.  The ice has been sloughed off the walls and floor\nhere.  A large warming pot is slowly burning in the center of the room\ngiving off heat.  The drawback to this is the ice is constantly melting and\ndripping down from above.  A canopy has been placed above the table to\nprevent the diners from getting wet.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7434,15,-21,-3,'Dishwashing Room','  Monstrous stacks of <y>dirty dishes<1> are towering above.  The\ncleaning process consists of sloughing the <g>dirty food<z> off the\ndishes into the corner and then stacking the now clean dishes in the\nopposite corner.  The pile of <y>uneaten food<1> is then recollected in a\nlarge pot to be served at the following meal.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7435,14,-20,-3,'Walk-In Freezer','  This room is naturally cold enough to freeze meat.  The walls and floor\nare frozen over, and the food is placed on top of the ice.  A small path\nhas been cut down the center of the room, allowing the chef to traverse\nthe treacherous ice.  Large piles of unappealing food lie piled about.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7436,15,-20,-3,'Food Preparation Area','  Large piles off food lie scattered about.  This is the most disgusting food\npreparation area you have ever seen.  The only thing that prevents the\nfood from rotting and spoiling is the fact that the temperature is far too\nlow for anything to live down here.  The walls are coated with a veneer\nof black ice that prevents the room from ever becoming warm.  The ice\nhas melted repeatedly around the stove, forming odd shapes in the ice.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7437,17,-24,-3,'Top of a Flight of Stairs','  A spiral staircase leads even deeper down into the depths of the prison.\nHideous laughter can be heard down below, intermingled with shrieks of\nhorror and agony.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7438,17,-24,-4,'Bottom of a Flight of Stairs','  The air in this level of the prison is stuffy and hard to breath, making\nphysical exertion  difficult.  The walls appears to be carved into <b>solid\nice<z>.  Some sort of <o>mesh<z> has been spread across the ground to\nprevent slipping, but it easily entangles the unwary and clumsy.  The air\nstinks of <y>sulfur<z> and burnt flesh.  The <b>icy cave walls<z> are\nstained back from some unknown crystal that has mixed with the water to\nform an exceptionally dense substance.  The thick walls muffle all sounds\nwhile acting as an arctic wind tunnel that stings the flesh and blurs the\nvision.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7439,18,-24,-4,'Poorly Lit Hallway','The poor lighting in this hallway, combined with the treacherous ice.\nThe air seams to have an oppressive and somber quality to it.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7440,19,-24,-4,'Dark Hallway','The poor lighting in this hallway, combined with the treacherous ice.\nThe air seams to have an oppressive and somber quality to it.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7441,20,-24,-4,'Very Dark Hallway','This hallway seams to be very well traveled.  Deep grooves in the icy\nfloor reveal how often prisoners are led down this path.  To the west the\nguards have built a small area to kill the time, to the south is the prisons\ndeath row.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7442,20,-25,-4,'Somber Hallway','  This somber hallway leads to the execution chamber.  For many prisoners\nit is the last walk they ever take.  Capitol punishment is used for any\ncrime the warden decides.  He generally starts with a random letter of the\nalphabet and begins to execute any prisoner who has the misfortune of\nhaving that letter begin his name.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7443,20,-26,-4,'Somber Hallway','This is the short hallway that leads to the execution chamber.  The air is\nkept cool and crisp to make sure the prisoners are fully conscious before\nthey are executed.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7444,20,-27,-4,'Somber Hallway','This is the short hallway that leads to the execution chamber.  The air is\nkept cool and crisp to make sure the prisoners are fully conscious before\nthey are executed.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7445,20,-28,-4,'Dead End Hallway','  This dead end hallway is the end of the line for many prisoners.  In\ntheory the warden can send a last minute reprieve, which he occasionally\ndoes.  However, he always sends a second letter that says, \"Just Kidding!\".\nThe warden, being a sadistic jerk, never tires of this joke.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7446,19,-25,-4,'Death Row Cell','  This small cell is completely empty.  Prisoners are forced to either sit on\nthe cold icy floor or to stand while they await their final hour.\nFortunately, they never have to wait very long.  The slick icy walls\ninsulate the cell in a extremely cold state.  Most of the prisoners are\nsuffering from severe hypothermia by the time they are executed.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7447,19,-26,-4,'Death Row Cell','  This small cell is completely empty.  Prisoners are forced to either sit on\nthe cold icy floor or to stand while they await their final hour.\nFortunately, they never have to wait very long.  The slick icy walls\ninsulate the cell in a extremely cold state.  Most of the prisoners are\nsuffering from severe hypothermia by the time they are executed.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7448,19,-27,-4,'Death Row Cell','  The death row cell is completely barren of any items.  The state wants to\nmake sure that the prisoner is not afforded anything that he might be able\nto end his life with.  If the body is not instantly treated with the secret\npreservative chemical the rations that are produced will be too chewy.\nThe cell is a cold and barren place that is pitch black when sealed.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7449,19,-28,-4,'Execution Room','  It is in this small and unremarkable room that thousands of prisoners\nhave been executed.  The prisoners are placed on their backs, strapped\nto the floor and then are killed.  They are compelled to watch this\nhappen by the executioner\'s assistant, who holds their eyes open.\nA large portrait has been painted on the ceiling.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7450,21,-24,-4,'Prison Guard Station','  This is where the guards kill time until they get the final go ahead to\nexecute the prisoners.  The prison generally executes between thirty and\nforty prisoners daily.  Generally, by the time a guard gets comfortable and\nwaits for them to clean up the mess from the previous execution he is\nneeded to bring in the next prisoner.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7451,21,-25,-4,'Death Row Cell','  This small cell is completely empty.  Prisoners are forced to either sit\non the cold icy floor or stand while they await their final hour.\nFortunately, they never have to wait very long.  The slick icy walls\ninsulate the cell in a extremely cold state.  Most of the prisoners are\nsuffering from severe hypothermia by the time they are executed.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7452,21,-26,-4,'Death Row Cell','This small cell is completely empty.  Prisoners are forced to either sit on\nthe cold icy floor or stand while they await their final hour.  Fortunately,\nthey never have to wait very long.  The slick icy walls insulate the cell in a\nextremely cold state.  Most of the prisoners are suffering from severe\nhypothermia by the time they are executed.\n',-1,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7453,21,-27,-4,'Death Row Cell','This small cell is completely empty.  Prisoners are forced to either sit on\nthe cold icy floor or stand while they await their final hour.  Fortunately,\nthey never have to wait very long.  The slick icy walls insulate the cell in a\nextremely cold state.  Most of the prisoners are suffering from severe\nhypothermia by the time they are executed.\n',-1,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7454,21,-28,-4,'Holding Cell','  Numerous headless corpses have been thrown into this room, waiting to\nbe gathered and taken up to the ration factory.  On days that the ration\norders are heavy, this room will be filled and emptied over a dozen\ntimes.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7455,16,-24,-4,'Dark Hallway','  This short hallway leads from the stairwell to the asylum.  The dense air\nis low in oxygen content and makes every movement exceptionally\ndifficult.  The frozen remains of a <r>huge monster<z> are perfectly\npreserved in the northern wall.  Razor sharp teeth are sneering through\nthe<c> ice<z>, and it seems the monster will spring forth, shattering the\ncave wall at any moment.  The <r>fiery red eyes<z> of the monster seem\nto track your every movement.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7456,16,-25,-4,'Entrance to the Asylum','  This is the main entrance to the <p>Michelob Memorial Insane\nAsylum<z>.  The freaks and oddballs of society that are beyond salvation\nare sent here.  This is the last stop for the lunatics that nobody else wants\nor knows how to help.  The icy walls have been padded with leather to\nprevent the inmates from slamming into the walls and doing harm to\nthemselves.  They are kept heavily sedated and are watched carefully.\nDespite the best efforts, the inmates run the asylum.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7457,16,-26,-4,'Asylum','  It seems that the prison has decided to take all of the uncontrollable\npatients and just throw them down here in a chaotic free for all.  This\narea is a complete mess.  Garbage and food are strewn about.  The patients\nare running around in complete chaos making all kinds of strange and\ndemented noises.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7458,16,-27,-4,'Asylum','  It seems that the prison has decided to take all of the uncontrollable\npatients and just throw them down here in a chaotic free for all.  This\narea is a complete mess.  Garbage and food are strewn about.  The patients\nare running around in complete chaos making all kinds of strange and\ndemented noises.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7459,16,-28,-4,'Asylum','  The further the patients get from the nurses station the more\nuncontrollable their behavior becomes.  The asylum is becoming\n more messy by the sort of made bacchanalian ceremony that\nonly the inmates seam capable of understanding.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7460,16,-29,-4,'Looney Bin','  Apparently the builders of the prison counted on there being no shortage\nof freaks and lunatics.  This cavernous asylum just seems to keep going\nendlessly.  The floor has been covered here with a leather cover.  The\ncave floor is very jagged and pointed, and otherwise it would begin to cut\ninto any exposed flesh.  The air is extremely cold and damp here.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7461,15,-26,-4,'Asylum','  It seems that the prison has decided to take all of the uncontrollable\npatients and just throw them down here in a chaotic free for all.  This\narea is a complete mess.  Garbage and food are strewn about.  The patients\nare running around in complete chaos making all kinds of strange and\ndemented noises.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7462,15,-27,-4,'Asylum','  It seems that the prison has decided to take all of the uncontrollable\npatients and just throw them down here in a chaotic free for all.  This\narea is a complete mess.  Garbage and food are strewn about.  The patients\nare running around in complete chaos making all kinds of strange and\ndemented noises.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7463,15,-28,-4,'Asylum','  The further the patients get from the nurses station the more\nuncontrollable their behavior becomes.  The asylum is becoming\nmore messy be the second.  Clothes and bedding materials are\nbeing slung about in some sort of made bacchanalian ceremony\nthat only the inmates seam capable of understanding.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7464,15,-29,-4,'Asylum','  Apparently the builders of the prison counted on there being no shortage\nof freaks and lunatics.  This cavernous asylum just seems to keep going\nendlessly.  The floor has been covered here with a leather cover.  The\ncave floor is very jagged and pointed, and otherwise it would begin to cut\ninto any exposed flesh.  The air is extremely cold and damp here.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7465,17,-26,-4,'Nurse\'s Station','  From here the nurse runs the asylum with an iron fist.  She manipulates\nthe patients illnesses to control them and have them do her bidding.  If\nshe chose to, she could probably have her own army of screwballs ready\nto execute her every command.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7466,17,-27,-4,'Asylum','  It seems that the prison has decided to take all of the uncontrollable\npatients and just throw them down here in a chaotic free for all.  This\narea is a complete mess.  Garbage and food is strewn about.  The patients\nare running around in complete chaos making all kinds of strange and\ndemented noises.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7467,17,-28,-4,'Asylum','  The further the patients get from the nurses station the more\nuncontrollable they behave.  The asylum is becoming more messy be the\nsecond.  Clothes and bedding materials are being slung about in some\nsort of made bacchanalian ceremony that only the inmates seam capable\nof understanding.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
