(7470,15,-30,-4,'Psycho House','  Apparently the builders of the prison counted on there being no shortage\nof freaks and lunatics.  This cavernous asylum just seems to keep going\nendlessly.  The floor has been covered here with a leather cover.  The\ncave floor is very jagged and pointed, and otherwise it would begin to cut\ninto any exposed flesh.  The air is extremely cold and damp here.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7471,16,-30,-4,'Asylum','  Apparently the builders of the prison counted on there being no shortage\nof freaks and lunatics.  This cavernous asylum just seems to keep going\nendlessly.  The floor has been covered here with a leather cover.  The\ncave floor is very jagged and pointed, and otherwise it would begin to cut\ninto any exposed flesh.  The air is extremely cold and damp here.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7472,16,-31,-4,'Wacko Ward','  This is perhaps the craziest place in the realm.  People are running about\nscreaming and yelling gibberish that only they seem capable of\nunderstanding.  Most of them are scantily clothed and have numerous\ncuts and abrasions.  It is  a lot like Brightmoon on New Years.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7473,15,-31,-4,'Crazy Corner','  This is the southwest corner of the asylum.  The air is cold and damp and\neverything in sight is soggy and moldy.  Sometimes it gets so cold that\nthe wet blankets become frozen solid.  On many occasions  a prisoner has\nbecome entombed in such a frozen cocoon and required the assistance of\nothers to free him.  The problem of course is trying to inspire a lunatic\nto assist in freeing somebody.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7474,17,-31,-4,'Asylum','  The asylum staff has abandoned the asylum for the most part.  Rather\nthan battle for control with the lunatics, the staff has decided to avoid the\nentire controversy.  The asylum is a complete shambles.  Litter and\ndebris have been scattered everywhere.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7475,16,-32,-4,'Stairway Down','  A small staircase leads down into a dark abyss.  A strange feral glow\nemanates up from below.  The staircase appears to be sturdy and is set\ninto the wall with solid granite rivets.  The stairs themselves look slick\nand are sheeted with a thin layer of black ice.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7476,16,-32,-5,'Bottom of a Dark Stairwell','  Surprisingly this part of the prison is warm.  A soft red glow seems to\nemanate from the walls and ceiling.  A strange purple haze floats above\nthe glow, seemingly sealing the heat on this level.  The walls are carved\nout of solid granite.  A sturdy looking stairway leads up to the next level.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7477,16,-31,-5,'Dungeon','  The dungeon is where the uncontrollable inmates are kept.  The prison\ndefines uncontrollable as any person who effectively intimidates the\nguards.  The granite walls sparkle in the soft light.  Oddly, this area is\nkept warmer than any other area in the prison.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7478,16,-30,-5,'Dungeon','  The walls and floor are carved from solid granite.  The\nworkmanship, though a little shoddy, left the floors and walls rather\nsmooth here.  The smooth floor, which is covered with a film of muddy\nwater, is slick and dangerous.  A faint red glows hangs in the air.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7479,16,-29,-5,'Dungeon','  A large stalactite has crashed into the floor with tremendous force,\nripping a deep groove into the granite floor.  Pieces of the splintered\nstalactite have been dispersed across the cave floor.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7480,16,-28,-5,'Dungeon','  The walls and floor are carved from into a solid piece of granite.  The\nworkmanship is rather shoddy and left the floor riddled with potholes and\ncrevices.  Small puddles of stagnant water have gathered in these holes,\nleaving the cave air musty and reeking of mildew and fungus.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7481,17,-28,-5,'Dungeon','  The walls and floor of the prison have been carved into the solid granite\nrock face.  Due to the dense and solid granite, the workers had a difficult\ntime smoothing out the walls and floors.  Brown water has stagnated in\nthe small potholes that riddle the cave floor.  Crystal stalactites hang from\nthe ceiling, threatening to break off and crash into the floor.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7482,17,-29,-5,'Dungeon','  The walls and floor are carved from solid granite.  The\nworkmanship, though a little shoddy, left the floors and walls rather\nsmooth here.  The smooth floor, which is covered with a film of muddy\nwater, is slick and dangerous.  A faint red glows hangs in the air.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
