(7489,18,-29,-5,'Dungeon','  The walls and floor of the prison have been carved into the solid granite\nrock face.  Due to the dense and solid granite, the workers had a difficult\ntime smoothing out the walls and floors.  Brown water has stagnated in\nthe small potholes that riddle the cave floor.  Crystal stalactites hang from\nthe ceiling, threatening to break off and crash into the floor.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7490,18,-28,-5,'Dungeon','  The walls and floor of the prison have been carved from solid granite.\nA faint red glow is hanging in the air.  A small picture of a door has\nbeen drawn on the wall.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7491,19,-28,-5,'Plush Hallway','  A well lit and warm hallway runs east and west.  Plush red carpeting\ncovers the cavern floor.  A large chandelier hands from the ceiling.  A\nfresh smelling herb has scented the air.  The smell of fresh baked pastries\nwafts in from the east.  An over-sized picture hangs against one wall.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7492,20,-28,-5,'Plush Hallway','  A well lit and warm hallway runs east and west.  Plush red carpeting\ncovers the cavern floor.  A large chandelier hands from the ceiling.  A\nfresh smelling herb has scented the air.  The smell of fresh baked pastries\nwafts in from the east.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7493,21,-28,-5,'Plush Hallway','  A well lit and warm hallway runs east and west.  Plush red carpeting\ncovers the cavern floor.  A large chandelier hands from the ceiling.  A\nfresh smelling herb has scented the air.  The smell of fresh baked pastries\nwafts in from the east.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7494,22,-27,-5,'A Luxurious Bedroom','The Capo\'s main duty is collecting on the debts and breaking bones on\nthose who cannot pay their debts.  This duty keeps him in the lap of\nluxury.  He has a warm bed and a room full of the necessary\nconveniences.\n',-1,131081,60,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7495,22,-28,-5,'Pleasant Room','  A large <r>red shag carpet<z> covers the cavern floor.  The walls are\ncovered by <p>silken tapestries<z>.  A <y>large chandelier<z> hangs\nfrom the roof.  Like every prison, this one has its hierarchy among the\nprisoners.  The prisoners living here control the alcohol, gambling and\ntobacco trade within the prison.  With the capital they earn they are able\nto bribe the guards and the warden, and probably live in more comfort\nhere in prison than they would on the outside.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7496,22,-29,-5,'Don\'s Room','  Arguably, this is the nerve center of the penitentiary.  From behind this\ndesk the Don controls the flow of everything in and out of the prison.\nRumors are beginning to circulate that it is the Don, not the warden, that\nis really in control of the prison.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7497,22,-30,-5,'Don\'s Bedroom','  This bedroom looks like it is for royalty.  Satin sheets cover the bed.  A\nlarge crystal chandelier hangs above the bed.  A large full length mirror\nrests on the southern wall.  The walls have been covered with pleasant\nlooking tapestries,  and the temperature is kept at a comfortable level.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7498,23,-27,-5,'Kitchen','  This area is furnished with its own kitchen.  Here, fresh breads, pastas,\nsausage and salads are prepared daily.  The guards are bribed to smuggle\nin the proper ingredients.  A large stove is kept spotless in the corner\nnext to a large cooking counter.  A nice set of cooking utensils hangs\nfrom the wall.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7499,23,-28,-5,'Bookie\'s Room','  From here, the prison bookie keeps track of the debts of every prisoner.\nIt is rumored that over one hundred thousand talens travel through here\nweekly.  Due to the high amount of money and the lack of trustworthy\nsouls in prison, the figures are checked repeatedly to prevent theft.\n',51,139528,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7501,-29,-31,0,'A Faint Trail Emerges','  As you look around, it would appear that you are lost in the middle of some\nwilderness save for the faint signs of a trail which widens here.  Surveying the\nscene, you discover several heavy boot prints heading to the east.  The\novergrowth to the north and south seems too thick to traverse, but the way to\nthe west seems passable.  Off to the southeast is what appears to be a volcano.\n',45,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7502,-28,-31,0,'The Trail Begins To Widen','  At this section of the trail, the overgrowth seems to pull back a bit, as if\nreluctant to hide the trail.  There is a great number of boot prints here\nheading both east and west.  You hear the warble of a songbird to the south,\nbut as you look for it, your view is completely obscured by the vegetation.\n',45,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7503,-27,-31,0,'A Faint Trail Emerges','  Standing here, you notice that the overgrowth is closing in on you from three\nsides; the north, east, and south.  The only obvious route of travel would seem\nto be a strange trail heading to the west.  But as you look around and see a\ngreat many boot prints, you notice that some of them head into the overgrowth\nto the east.  Maybe its not as impassable as it seemed before.\n',45,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7504,-26,-31,0,'A Dense Overgrowth','  You hack and slash as you try to gain some ground traversing through the\nheavy undergrowth.  Boot prints dot the ground all around going in every\ndirection not just along the path.  It seems as though many groups may\nhave stopped at this spot as though they were looking for something.  It\nseems pretty dim here, save for some light which filters through from the\neast and west.  To the north and south, the vegetation almost forms a wall\nof vines and trees.\n',45,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7505,-25,-31,0,'A Faint Trail Emerges','  At this point in the wilderness, you can see the open sky only to the east,\nsince thick vegetation blocks all sight to the north, west, and south.  You are\napparently standing upon a trail as evidenced by heavy boot prints which lead\nboth east and west.  As you gaze further to the east, you notice what appears\nto be a clearing.\n',45,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7506,-24,-31,0,'The Trail Widens','  Here a trail becomes very prominent as the vegetation at this point is rather\nsparse.  Heavy boot prints lead both to the west where the vegetation becomes\nthicker, and to the east towards an open clearing.  Off in the distance you can\nhear the sweet melody of a flock of song birds.\n',45,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7507,-23,-31,0,'A Clearing','  From out of the wilderness emerges a rather large clearing.  Song birds\nflutter everywhere, and grass covers the entire area.\n',45,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7508,-26,-32,0,'A Hidden Path','  Here is what appears to be a path hidden behind the natural vegetation and\nrock formations.  Boot prints mark the direction of the trail from north to\nsouth.  Looking north your vision is obscured by a thick overgrowth.  As you\ngaze southward, you are taken by awe as you spy a rather large, solitary\nvolcano which rises out of the wilderness.\n',45,139264,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7509,-26,-33,0,'The Base of a Dormant Volcano','  As you stand here, you notice several crevices which appear to be dried up\nhot-springs.  You can only guess, or hope, that the volcano is dormant.  Looking\nup the face of the volcano, you notice a very narrow trail which comes down the\nvolcano, and continues to the north where it widens out.\n',45,139296,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7510,-26,-33,1,'A Steep Path Up The Volcano','You stand here sweating profusely part-way up the side of the volcano.\nNavigation along the trail is almost impossible by night, and by day the sun\nbeats down upon you relentlessly as there is nothing except for some thick \nbushes to provide shade.  Looking around, you accept the fact that it will\nbe hard work going either up or down.  You also notice a much more tempting\npath, since it appears level, heading off around the side of the volcano to the\nwest.\n',0,139264,48,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7511,-27,-33,1,'A Bend Around the Side of the Volcano','  You stand upon a narrow ledge which goes around the sides of the volcano.  It\nseems to travel both south and east, disappearing from view as it wraps around\nthe volcano.  Gazing downwards, you spy a vast wilderness, and you begin to\ndaydream of the countless adventures to be had within its depths.\n',45,139264,48,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7512,-27,-34,1,'A Ledge on the Side of the Volcano','  You have come to a dead end of a ledge, which travels around the side of a\nvolcano.  The only route of passage seems to be to the north.\n',45,139264,48,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7513,-26,-33,2,'The Mouth of a Cave','  A very steep and narrow path up the side of the volcano ends here at the\nmouth of a rather large and dark cave.  Peering inside you suddenly get a\nstrange whiff of something which smells very metallic, and the ground below your\nfeet is covered with a reddish dust.  All your magic items begins to agitate\nwith excitement.\n',45,139304,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(7514,-26,-34,2,'Inside A Cave','  As you enter a large cave you notice piles of reddish dust scattered around\nthe room.  You also notice several deep, dark holes at the base of several of\nthe cave walls.  To the south you notice a rather large hole which descends\ninto darkness, but as you approach it, your skin begins to tingle.\n',45,140424,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7515,-26,-35,2,'Over A Deep Hole','  You hover over a very deep and dark hole at this point.\n',45,140424,55,10,7516,1,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7516,-26,-35,1,'An Underground River','  You find yourself submerged underwater in what seems to be an underground\nriver.  The current seems to be pulling you in what you estimate to be a\nsouthward direction.  You cannot be really sure since you have nothing to grasp\nyour bearings upon in these depths.  A faint glint of light in the darkness\ncatches your attention in the bottom of the river.\n',45,140424,30,30,7516,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7517,-26,-36,1,'An Underground River','  You find yourself submerged underwater in what seems to be an underground\nriver.  The current seems to be pulling you in what you estimate to be a\nsouthward direction.  You cannot really be sure since you have nothing to grasp\nyour bearings upon in these depths.\n',45,140424,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7518,-26,-37,1,'An Underground River','  You find yourself submerged underwater in what seems to be an underground\nriver.  The current seems to be pulling you in what you estimate to be a\nsouthward direction.  You cannot really be sure since you have nothing to grasp\nyour bearings upon in these depths.  To the west you see a faint greenish glow\nabove the surface of the water.  You think that you can make it to the surface\nif only you could beat the current.\n',45,140424,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7519,-27,-37,1,'A Moss Covered Bank Above The River','  You stand upon a cold, dark bank above the western edge of an underground\nriver.  The room is softly illuminated with an eerie greenish glow emitted by a\nstrange moss which grows on the walls here.  The moss grows thicker on the west\nwall, away from the river.\n',45,140424,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7520,-28,-37,1,'A Hidden Cache','  You have found what appears to be a hidden storage area, and it appears to be\nstill in use.  There are several fresh heavy boot marks scattered about the\nroom.  There are also various crates and barrels placed about the room.\n',45,139400,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7521,-26,-38,1,'An Underground River','  You find yourself submerged underwater in what seems to be an underground\nriver.  The current seems to be pulling you in what you estimate to be a\nsouthward direction.  You cannot really be sure since you have nothing to grasp\nyou bearings upon in these depths.\n',45,140424,30,0,0,0,5,2,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7522,-26,-39,1,'Rapids','  You find yourself submerged underwater in what seems to be an underground\nriver.  The current begins to grow fiercer at this point and pulls on you with\nincredible force towards what seems to be south.\n',45,140424,30,0,0,0,3,2,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7523,-26,-40,1,'A Whirlpool!','You head actually comes above water at this point in the river.  Unfortunately\nto your dismay, you find that the rapids have turned into a deep and dark\nwhirlpool, which funnels downwards into the icy depths of the water.\n',-1,140424,30,10,7524,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7524,0,0,0,'A Sandy Beach in an Underground Cavern','  You stand upon a sandy beach of what appears to be a small island in the\nmiddle of an underground lake.  Towards the south, in the middle of the lake,\nis a large funnel of water pouring out of a hole in the ceiling of the cavern\nin which you stand.  The roar of the water is loud, but not loud enough to\nobscure noise.  To the south is the underground lake.  To the east is what\nappears to be what remains of an ancient temple.  Stairs rise up out of sand\nand grass to approach a set of gates further up and east.\n',45,139276,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7525,0,0,0,'Steps of an Ancient Temple','  You stand upon various broken marble steps which lead up from a sandy beach\nfrom the west, to the gates of what appears to be an ancient temple up and to\nthe east.  Pebbles and rocks dot the scene, and strange fungi emerge from the\ncracks between some of the steps.\n',45,139272,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7526,0,0,0,'Outside the Main Gates of an Ancient Temple','  You stand before the main gates of what appears to be an ancient temple.  The\nhuge iron doors are set between marble walls.  The ground seems a bit solid\nhere, yet the marble floor is not as glossy as it would have been in its former\nglory.  Various statues line the walls outside of the gate, and they stare\noutward blankly, as if in vigilant watch over the gates to their temple.\nYour skin shivers as you detect what sounds like a faint wailing coming\nfrom inside of the temple, probably some horror long ago forgotten.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7527,0,0,0,'Inside the Main Gates of an Ancient Temple','  You stand inside the main gates of a long ago forgotten temple.  Glossy marble\nfloors glisten here as if never touched by age.  Empty torch sconces line the\nwalls, and faint whispers and moans can be heard upon strangely unnatural\nbreezes.  Various tapestries hang from the ceiling, depicting scenes of long\nago, their meaning lost in time.  The main gates to the temple lie to the west,\nand a hallway continues to the east.  A heavy iron tower door bars passage into\na marble tower to the south.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7528,0,0,0,'Base of a Marble Tower','  You are standing inside a pure white marble tower which seems to be of some\nimportance.  Glossy floors and fine furniture decorate the room, as well as\nfine tapestries which hang from the walls.  A flight of stairs ascend the back\nwall of the tower up to the next floor.  There is an iron door which leads\nnorth.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7529,0,0,0,'Anteroom at the Top of a Tower','  You have entered into a large anteroom, located at the top of a tower.  There\nare several minor windows in all directions, looking outside.  The one\nexception is a large window which faces west.  Drapes hang adjacent to each of\nthe windows, and large tapestries hang on the walls between the windows.\nFinely crafted furniture fill the room, and the marble floor is covered with a\nfine rug.  Against the back wall is a flight of stairs leading down.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7530,0,0,0,'A Marble Hallway','  You are standing in a large glossy-floored marble hallway.  Various\ntapestries hang from the ceilings, and empty torch sconces line the walls.  Off\nin the distance, you swear you could hear a faint moaning sound, or was it just\nthe wind?\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7531,0,0,0,'An Ancient Meeting Room','  You have entered what appears to be a meeting room of sorts.  Various chairs\nand tables fill the room, and cabinets full of books and scrolls line the\nwalls.  A huge chandelier hangs from the ceiling, its age old candles unlit.\nThere is not a speck of dust, or visible sign of age throughout the room.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7532,0,0,0,'An Ancient Bath House','  You are standing in a very large room, which seems rather humid.  Huge pools\nof water of various shapes and sizes fill up much of the room.  Waterfalls\nstreak the walls as water gently flows down into the various pools.  Green\nplants abound, and the pottery and planters are an architectural wonder.  Your\nmind begins to wander on how these plants can grow in such darkness.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7533,0,0,0,'An Intersection in the Marble Hallway','  You are standing at the intersection of two large glossy-floored marble\nhallways.  Various tapestries hang from the ceilings, and empty torch sconces\nline the walls.  Off in the distance, you swear you could hear a faint moaning\nsound, or was it just the wind?\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7534,0,0,0,'A Marble Hallway','  You are standing in a large glossy-floored marble hallway.  Various\ntapestries hang from the ceilings, and empty torch sconces line the walls.  Off\nin the distance, you swear you could hear a faint moaning sound, or was it just\nthe wind?\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7535,0,0,0,'Main Temple Entrance','  You have entered the main hallway of the central temple.  Statues line all of\nthe walls, depicting many figures of various races.  Tapestries abound, and\nluxurious carpeting covers all of the floors.  Near the entrance, to the south,\nare two decanters of holy water mounted upon the temple walls.  Chandeliers\nhang from the ceiling, all of their candles unlit.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7536,0,0,0,'Main Temple','  This is the main temple of the entire complex.  The room smells strongly of\nincense, yet nothing is lit, not even a single candle.  The chandeliers hang\nsilently from the ceilings, veiled in darkness.  The carpeting upon the floor\nis luxurious, and fine tapestries decorate the walls.  There are also a large\nnumber of marble pews here, arranged in a geometric pattern around the main\naltar, which rests at the top of a flight of stairs which begin here.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7537,0,0,0,'Temple Altar','  This is the main dais, stationed at the top of a flight of stairs, which lead\ndown to the rest of the main temple.  The smell of incense is very strong here,\nand you begin to feel a powerful presence.  You get the feeling that something,\nor someone is watching you.  A tomb is inset in the north wall.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7538,0,0,0,'The Tomb of Calishane Rhilyn\'tar','  You have entered a large marble room which is completely cold and bare.  You\ndefinitely begin to feel a presence here, watching you intently.  The tomb\nmay be exited through a door to the south.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7539,0,0,0,'A Marble Hallway','  You are standing in a large glossy-floored marble hallway.  Various\ntapestries hang from the ceilings, and empty torch sconces line the walls.  Off\nin the distance, you swear you could hear a faint moaning sound, or was it just\nthe wind?\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7540,0,0,0,'A Silent Garden Outside of the Temple','  You have entered a large garden just outside the ancient temple.  Huge\ntopiary are growing here at random intervals throughout the garden, and take on\na variety of shapes and images.  They are neatly trimmed, and look well\nmaintained.  To the east, behind some bushes, you see a gardening shed.  A large\nwalkway also leads to the west where you catch a glimpse of water.  You are\nsuddenly startled by a feeling of movement behind you, yet when you turn\naround, nothing is there save the bushes.  Could it have been the bushes?\n',45,140296,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7541,0,0,0,'A Garden Shed','  You have entered a gardening shed, located within a garden which lies to the\nwest.  Various implements and tools hang upon the walls.  They seem clean and\nwell oiled, as if they have been recently used.  The smell of fresh cut\ngreenery is present throughout the shed.  There is a trapdoor in the floor.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7542,0,0,0,'Cellar under the Shed','  You are standing within a cellar, which secretly lies under a gardening shed.\nThe walls are made of bare earth, yet somebody has managed to mount some\nshelves on them.  Various tools lean against the walls at some spots, and\nbarrels fill the corners of the room.  A swinging hammock hangs between two of\nthe walls, against the far back of the room.  A trapdoor is in the ceiling.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7543,0,0,0,'A Stony Pathway','  You are standing upon a stone pathway which is flanked on both sides by a\nthick hedge.  The pathway leads east to a garden, and downward to the edge of a\nbody of water.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7544,0,0,0,'A Dock On The Underground Lake','  This seems to be a dock used for trade and shipping upon the underground\nwaters.  Various ropes and barrels are stacked upon the dock.  To the west can\nbe seen an underground lake.  To the south is a warehouse, probably for storing\ntraded goods, and a stony pathway leads upward from here towards the ancient\ntemple.\n',45,139272,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7545,0,0,0,'A Warehouse','  You have entered a large, open warehouse, used in the storage of goods traded\nupon the underground waters.  Various barrels and crates line the walls, full\nof who knows what kind of goods.  Ropes hang from the ceiling, a few of them\nattached to suspended crates.  The warehouse seems surprisingly clean, but well\nused.  The docks on the lake lie to the north.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7546,0,0,0,'The Temple Fountain','  This seems to be the central plaza of a large, ancient temple.  Potted plants\nfill the room, and line the walls.  Several marble benches also sit around a\nlarge fountain in a circle.  It seems unusual that the plants here can grow\nwithout light, as all of the torch sconces on the walls are empty.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7547,0,0,0,'An Ancient Meeting Room','  You have entered what appears to be a meeting room of sorts.  Various chairs\nand tables fill the room, and cabinets full of books and scrolls line the\nwalls.  A huge chandelier hangs from the ceiling, its age old candles unlit.\nThere is not a speck of dust, or visible sign of age throughout the room.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7548,0,0,0,'An Ancient Armory','  You have entered a very dimly lit room.  The white walls seems reddish in the\nlow candle-light, and the glossy floors have the appearance of blood.\nTapestries do not hang from the ceilings here, or even on the walls as in the\nrest of the ancient temple.  Various shelves line the walls, filled with all\nsorts or weapons, tools, armor, and other miscellaneous items.  Standing a few\nfeet from the far back wall is a large counter.\n',45,174269,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7549,0,0,0,'An Intersection in the Marble Hallway','  You are standing at the intersection of two large glossy-floored marble\nhallways.  Various tapestries hang from the ceilings, and empty torch sconces\nline the walls.  Off in the distance, you swear you could hear a faint moaning\nsound, or was it just the wind?\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7550,0,0,0,'A Marble Hallway','  You are standing in a large glossy-floored marble hallway.  Various\ntapestries hang from the ceilings, and empty torch sconces line the walls.  Off\nin the distance, you swear you could hear a faint moaning sound, or was it just\nthe wind?\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7551,0,0,0,'A Marble Hallway','  You are standing in a large glossy-floored marble hallway.  Various\ntapestries hang from the ceilings, and empty torch sconces line the walls.  Off\nin the distance, you swear you could hear a faint moaning sound, or was it just\nthe wind?  To the south stands a large iron door, set into the side of a huge\nmarble tower.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7552,0,0,0,'An Ancient Kitchen','  You have entered a large kitchen used in the preparation of meals for the\ntemple.  Various tables and sinks fill the room, covered with animal,\nvegetable, and other unknown foodstuffs to be prepared for consumption.  The\nwalls and floors are bare and made of pure, polished marble.  Various shelves\nline the walls filled with unrecognizable spices.  A large chandelier of\ncandles hangs unlit from the ceiling.  There is a large cutting table standing\nin the center of the room.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7553,0,0,0,'An Ancient Wine Cellar','  This marble room is covered in tons of dust, quite ironic compared to the\ncleanliness of the rest of the temple.  There are quite a number of wine-racks\nlining the wall of this room, filled with liquors of various tastes and ages.\nA large, unlit chandelier hangs from the ceiling here.  There is a trapdoor in\nthe floor.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7554,0,0,0,'An Ancient Pantry','  This pantry is used for the storage of all the temple\'s spices and\nfoodstuffs.  The walls and floors are bare and made of pure, polished marble.\nVarious shelves line the walls filled with unrecognizable spices.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7555,0,0,0,'A Hidden Cellar','  This appears to be a hidden cellar within the temple\'s kitchen, used for\nstoring rare items to be used only in great festivities.  The walls and floors\nare bare and made of pure, polished marble.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7556,0,0,0,'A Hidden Room','  You seemed to have discovered a hidden room, located underneath the wine\ncellar of the temple.  This room is covered in dust, and filled with\nwine-racks.  A stone hallway leads off to the north and a trapdoor is in\nthe ceiling.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7557,0,0,0,'Base of a Huge Marble Tower','  You have entered a rather large marble tower.  The room is lavishly\ndecorated, with fine furniture filling the room.  Several empty torch sconces\ncircle the room, and a large chandelier hangs unlit from the ceiling.  A large\nset of stairs rests against the back wall, curving along the wall both up and\ndown.  A fireplace rests against the eastern wall.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7558,0,0,0,'Apprentice\'s Chambers','  This seems to be a room located underground, at the base of a large marble\ntower.  Lavishly furnished as the rest of the tower, this room also seems to be\nused as a living quarters.  Various books and furniture fill the room, making\nit quite cozy.  A large unlit chandelier hangs from the ceiling here, and a set\nof stairs climb the far wall up to the rest of the tower.  A wooden door is set\nin the west wall.  There is a large bunk-bed in the corner of the room.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7559,0,0,0,'An Ancient Laboratory','  This room seems to serve as the main laboratory for the dangerous experiments\nof young mages in their apprenticeship.  While its lacks the more spectacular\nitems that would be present in a learned mages study, it does contain enough\ntools and implements to be effective.  A large table stands in the middle of the\nroom.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7560,0,0,0,'Tower Library','  As you enter this room, it doesn\'t seem quite as decorated as the rest of the\ntower.  There aren\'t any extravagant fixtures on the walls or ceilings.  There\ndoesn\'t even seem to be anything usable as a light source.  Yet, lavish\ncarpeting lines the floors, and winds its way between various bookcases made of\nboth recognizable and unrecognizable materials.  A large flight of stairs\ndescends down the far wall and a trapdoor leads upwards.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7561,0,0,0,'The Chamber of the Magus','  This is the main chamber of the Magus of this tower.  The room is madly alive\nwith magic.  Strange and bizarre furniture and items fill the room, your mind\nwandering as to their mysterious use.  The floors are made of pure, polished\nwhite marble, and the walls as well.  There is a large grey table in the center\nof the room.  A large canopied bed occupies the far corner of the room.  And\na trapdoor is in an out of the way part of the floor.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7562,0,0,0,'A Stony Hallway','  You are standing in a narrow stone hallway.  Everything is dark, cold, and\nbare.  A musty scent wafts through the air, followed by a faint moaning in the\ndistance.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7563,0,0,0,'A Stony Hallway','  You are standing in a narrow stone hallway.  Everything is dark, cold, and\nbare.  A musty scent wafts through the air, followed by a faint moaning in the\ndistance.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7564,0,0,0,'A Stony Hallway','  You are standing in a narrow stone hallway.  Everything is dark, cold, and\nbare.  A musty scent wafts through the air, followed by a faint moaning in the\ndistance.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7565,0,0,0,'A Stony Hallway','  You are standing in a narrow stone hallway.  Everything is dark, cold, and\nbare.  A musty scent wafts through the air, followed by a faint moaning in the\ndistance.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7566,0,0,0,'A Stony Hallway','  You are standing in a narrow stone hallway.  Everything is dark, cold, and\nbare.  A musty scent wafts through the air, followed by a faint moaning in the\ndistance.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7567,0,0,0,'A Stony Hallway','  You are standing in a narrow stone hallway.  Everything is dark, cold, and\nbare.  A musty scent wafts through the air, followed by a faint moaning in the\ndistance.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7568,0,0,0,'A Bend in the Stony Hallway','  You are standing at the bend of a narrow stone hallway, which continues west\nand south from here.  Everything is dark, cold, and bare.  A musty scent wafts\nthrough the air, followed by a faint moaning in the distance.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7569,0,0,0,'A Stony Hallway','  You are standing in a narrow stone hallway.  Everything is dark, cold, and\nbare.  A musty scent wafts through the air, followed by a faint moaning in the\ndistance.  Two wooden doors are set in the walls here, one to the north and the\nother to the south.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7570,0,0,0,'A Wine Cellar','  This is an ancient wine cellar made from stone walls.  Various wine-racks\nfill the room, covered with dust and filled with liquors of various ages and\ntaste.  There is a wooden door to the north.\n',45,139272,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7571,0,0,0,'A Wine Cellar','  This is an ancient wine cellar made from stone walls.  Various wine-racks\nfill the room, covered with dust and filled with liquors of various ages and\ntaste.  There is a wooden door to the south.\n',45,139272,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7572,0,0,0,'A Stony Hallway','  You are standing in a narrow stone hallway.  Everything is dark, cold, and\nbare.  A musty scent wafts through the air, followed by a faint moaning in the\ndistance.  Two wooden doors are set in the walls here, one to the north and the\nother to the south.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7573,0,0,0,'A Wine Cellar','  This is an ancient wine cellar made from stone walls.  Various wine-racks\nfill the room, covered with dust and filled with liquors of various ages and\ntaste.  There is a wooden door to the north.\n',45,139272,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7574,0,0,0,'A Wine Cellar','  This is an ancient wine cellar made from stone walls.  Various wine-racks\nfill the room, covered with dust and filled with liquors of various ages and\ntaste.  There is a wooden door to the south.\n',45,139272,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7575,0,0,0,'A Stony Hallway','  You are standing in a narrow stone hallway.  Everything is dark, cold, and\nbare.  A musty scent wafts through the air, followed by a faint moaning in the\ndistance.  Two wooden doors are set in the walls here, one to the north and the\nother to the south.\n',45,139272,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7576,0,0,0,'A Wine Cellar','  This is an ancient wine cellar made from stone walls.  Various wine-racks\nfill the room, covered with dust and filled with liquors of various ages and\ntaste.  There is a wooden door to the north.\n',45,139272,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7577,0,0,0,'A Wine Cellar','  This is an ancient wine cellar made from stone walls.  Various wine-racks\nfill the room, covered with dust and filled with liquors of various ages and\ntaste.  There is a wooden door to the south and a stone door going north.\n',45,139272,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7578,0,0,0,'A Back Passage','  You have discovered what seems to be a back passage.  Everything is dark,\ncold, and bare.  A musty scent wafts through the air, followed by a faint\nmoaning in the distance.  The passage opens into a room to the east.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7579,0,0,0,'A Mysterious Portal Room','  You have entered a small stone chamber.  The floor and walls are completely\nbare and smooth.  Nothing seems out of the ordinary save a large portal-like\narchway which is set into the east wall.  It is surrounded by runes of magical\norigin.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7580,0,0,0,'The Portal','You have entered a strange white mist and are enveloped by it.\n',-1,139272,55,10,1200,1,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7581,0,0,0,'The End of the Stony Hallway','  You have reached the end of a narrow stone hallway.  Everything is dark,\ncold, and bare.  A musty scent wafts through the air, followed by a faint\nmoaning in the distance.  Two wooden doors are set in the walls here, one to\nthe north and the other to the south.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7582,0,0,0,'A Wine Cellar','  This is an ancient wine cellar made from stone walls.  Various wine-racks\nfill the room, covered with dust and filled with liquors of various ages and\ntaste.  There is a wooden door to the north.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7583,0,0,0,'A Wine Cellar','  This is an ancient wine cellar made from stone walls.  Various wine-racks\nfill the room, covered with dust and filled with liquors of various ages and\ntaste.  There is a wooden door to the south.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7584,0,0,0,'A Marble Hallway','  You are standing in a large glossy-floored marble hallway.  Various\ntapestries hang from the ceilings, and empty torch sconces line the walls.  Off\nin the distance, you swear you could hear a faint moaning sound, or was it just\nthe wind?\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7585,0,0,0,'An Ancient Meeting Room','  You have entered what appears to be a meeting room of sorts.  Various chairs\nand tables fill the room, and cabinets full of books and scrolls line the\nwalls.  A huge chandelier hangs from the ceiling, its age old candles unlit.\nThere is not a speck of dust, or visible sign of age throughout the room.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7586,0,0,0,'A Bend in the Marble Hallway','  This is a bend in a large glossy-floored marble hallway.  Various tapestries\nhang from the ceilings, and empty torch sconces line the walls.  Off in the\ndistance, you swear you could hear a faint moaning sound, or was it just the\nwind?\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7587,0,0,0,'A Turn in the Marble Hallway','  This is a turn in a large glossy-floored marble hallway.  Various tapestries\nhang from the ceilings, and empty torch sconces line the walls.  Off in the\ndistance, you swear you could hear a faint moaning sound, or was it just the\nwind?\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7588,0,0,0,'A Bend in the Marble Hallway','  This is a bend in a large glossy-floored marble hallway.  Various tapestries\nhang from the ceilings, and empty torch sconces line the walls.  Off in the\ndistance, you swear you could hear a faint moaning sound, or was it just the\nwind?\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7589,0,0,0,'A Marble Hallway','  You are standing in a large glossy-floored marble hallway.  Various\ntapestries hand from the ceilings, and empty torch sconces line the walls.  Off\nin the distance, you swear you could hear a faint moaning sound, or was it just\nthe wind?  There is a large wooden door set in the west wall.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7590,0,0,0,'An Ancient Training Room','  This room seems much different from the rest of the temple.  The floors are\nmade of pure wood, polished to a high shine.  Various weapons all makes and\norigins line the walls, and fill racks about the room.  Upon the far wall, is a\nlarge emblem of a magnificent Unicorn.  As continue to scan the room, you get\nthe feeling that you can barely hear the sounds of battle riding upon the\nwinds.\n',45,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7591,0,0,0,'On an Underground Lake','  You are floating upon the surface of what appears to be an underground lake.\nTo the southwest is a large funnel of water rushing out of a hole in the\nceiling of the cavern.  To the north can be seen a sandy beach.  To the east is\nthe wall of what appears to be an ancient temple.\n',45,139272,52,0,0,0,7,7,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(7592,0,0,0,'On an Underground Lake','  You are floating upon the surface of what appears to be an underground lake.\nDirectly to the west is a large funnel of water rushing out of a hole in the\nceiling of the cavern.  To the far north can be seen a sandy beach.  To the\neast is the wall of what appears to be an ancient temple.  As your gaze falls\nback upon the funnel of water, you notice a cave to the southwest leading from\nthe lake into further depths unknown.\n',45,139272,52,0,0,0,7,7,7,100,0,'',NULL);
INSERT INTO `room` VALUES (7593,0,0,0,'On an Underground Lake','  You are floating upon the surface of what appears to be an underground lake.\nTo the northwest is a large funnel of water rushing out of a hole in the\nceiling of the cavern.  To the east is the wall of what appears to be an\nancient temple.  To the south is the cavern wall, and to the southwest is a\nlarge cave leading from the lake into further depths unknown.\n',45,139276,52,0,0,0,7,7,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(7594,0,0,0,'On an Underground Lake','  You are floating upon the surface of what appears to be an underground lake.\nDirectly to the south is a large funnel of water rushing out of a hole in the\nceiling of the cavern.  To the northeast can be seen a sandy beach, and to the\nfar east is what looks like the wall of an ancient temple.\n',45,139272,52,0,0,0,7,7,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(7595,0,0,0,'On an Underground Lake','  You are floating upon the surface of what appears to be an underground lake.\nTo the southeast is a large funnel of water rushing out of a hole in the\nceiling of the cavern.  To the north and west are the walls of the cavern.  Far\nto the east is what looks like the wall of an ancient temple.\n',45,139272,52,0,0,0,7,7,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(7596,0,0,0,'On an Underground Lake','  You are floating upon the surface of what appears to be an underground lake.\nDirectly to the east is a large funnel of water rushing out of a hole in the\nceiling of the cavern.  To the west is the cavern wall, and to the southeast is\na large cave leading from the lake into further depths unknown.\n',45,139272,52,0,0,0,7,7,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(7597,0,0,0,'On an Underground Lake','  You are floating upon the surface of what appears to be an underground lake.\nTo the northeast is a large funnel of water rushing out of a hole in the\nceiling of the cavern.  To the west and south are the cavern walls, and to the\nsoutheast is a large cave leading from the lake into further depths unknown.\n',45,139272,52,0,0,0,7,7,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(7598,0,0,0,'On an Underground Lake','  You are floating upon the surface of what appears to be an underground lake.\nDirectly to the north is a large funnel of water rushing out of a hole in the\nceiling of the cavern.  To the far east can be seen the wall of an ancient\ntemple, and to the south is a large cave leading from the lake into further\ndepths unknown.\n',45,139276,52,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7599,0,0,0,'Entrance to Deeper Catacombs','  You are floating upon the surface of what appears to be an underground river\nleading from a lake.  The lake is to the north, while the river continues\nonward towards the south into the darkness of deeper depths.  Glistening rock\nformations hang from the ceiling, and the sound of rushing water grows louder\nas the waters become more violent.\n',45,139272,52,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7600,0,0,0,'A Room in the Roaring Lion Inn','This room is decorated very simply but kept as clean as possible for the use it gets. The walls are made of perfectly smooth yew wood and appear to be scrubbed daily, as there\'s no trace of mud or dirt of any kind on the walls. The floor is swept clean and covered in a simple woven rug.',0,131245,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,144,0,'',NULL),
(7601,0,0,0,'7601','Empty',0,131245,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,144,0,'',NULL),
(7700,-10,-50,0,'A Faint Trail Through the Jungle','This faint trail has been pretty much overgrown by the jungle.  The\nsurrounding area is way too dense to penetrate much further, so it\nappears that you are confined to traveling along the trail.  It\ncontinues on to the southwest and a short way in the distance to the\neast you notice the main jungle road.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7701,-11,-51,0,'A Faint Trail Through the Jungle','This faint trail has been pretty much overgrown by the jungle.  The\nsurrounding environs is way too densely filled with jungle fauna to\npenetrate much further, so it appears that you are confined to\ntraveling along the trail.  It continues on to the northeast and a\nsmall clearing can be spotted nearby to the west.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7702,-12,-51,0,'A Small Clearing in the Overgrowth','The jungle seems considerably less dense here and the sky is actually\nvisible overhead through the canopy of jungle fauna.  A faint trail\nthrough the jungle snakes off to the east and northwest while\nany further explorations in other directions seems to be blocked by\nimpenetrable brush all around.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7703,-13,-50,0,'A Faint Trail Through the Jungle','This faint trail has been pretty much overgrown by the jungle.  The\nsurrounding environs is way too densely filled with jungle fauna to\npenetrate much further, so it appears that you are confined to\ntraveling along the trail.  It continues on to the north and a\nsmall clearing can be spotted nearby to the southeast.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7704,-13,-49,0,'A Faint Trail Through the Jungle','This faint trail has been pretty much overgrown by the jungle.  The\nway north is completely overgrown and you cannot force your way\nthrough any of the brush surrounding you.  To the south is a faint\ntrail through the jungle.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7705,-13,-52,0,'A Small Clearing in the Jungle','The jungle seems considerably less dense here and the sky is actually\nvisibly high overhead through the canopy of jungle fauna.  A faint\ntrail through the jungle snakes off to the northwest and southwest\nwhile any further explorations in all other directions seem to be\nblocked by the impenetrable brush all around.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7706,-14,-51,0,'A Jungle Trail','This faint jungle trail has pretty much been overgrown by the\nfauna all around.  Everything about you appears damp, the air is\nmoist and strange scents hang heavily in the air.  Off in the\ndistance you can hear the occasional odd birdcall and a smattering\nof indecipherable noises.  The surrounding environs is way too\ndensely packed with jungle growth to penetrate much further, so\nit appears that you are confined to traveling along the trail.\nIt continues on to the northwest and a small clearing can be\nspotted nearby to the southeast.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7707,-15,-50,0,'A Faint Jungle Path','This faint jungle trail has pretty much been overgrown by the\nfauna all around.  Everything about you appears damp, the air is\nmoist and strange scents hang heavily in the air.  Off in the\ndistance you can hear the occasional odd birdcall and a smattering\nof indecipherable noises.  The surrounding environs is way too\ndensely packed with jungle growth to penetrate much beyond the\nobvious exits available to you.  A small thatch hut lies ensconced\nwithin some jungle growth south of you while the trail continues\non to the southeast and west.  Looming above you to the southwest\nis what appears to be a crude pyramid constructed of stone.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7708,-16,-51,0,'At the Base of the Pyramid','Towering above you to the southwest is a large pyramid crudely\nfashioned of stone.  Each block apparently was hewn roughly out of\nsome dark rock and appears to be stained dark with what looks to be\ndried blood.  A jungle path can be seen to the northeast and a clearing\naround the pyramid stretches off to the south and west.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7709,-17,-51,0,'A Clearing Around the Pyramid','Towering way above you to the south is a large pyramid crudely\nfashioned out of stone.  Each block apparently was hewn roughly out\nof some dark, porous rock and appears to be stained with what\nlooks to be blood...in fact, the rock appears to be bleeding in\nsome spots.  The base of a stairway up the pyramid can be seen to\nthe east while this clearing around the pyramid continues to the\nsouthwest.  A large grass hut covered with symbols of the sun is\nto the west.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7710,-18,-52,0,'A Clearing Around the Pyramid','Towering way above you to the east is a large pyramid crudely\nfashioned out of stone.  Each block apparently was hewn roughly out\nof some dark, porous rock and appears to be stained with what\nlooks to be blood...in fact, the rock appears to be bleeding\nin some spots.  A foul smell seems to be emanating from a fenced\nin area to the northwest and there is a large grass hut covered\nwith sun symbols to the north.  The clearing around the pyramid\ncontinues on to the northeast and southeast while a faint jungle\npath snakes off into the darkness to the south.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7711,-17,-53,0,'A Clearing Around the Pyramid','Towering way above you to the north is a large pyramid crudely\nfashioned out of stone.  Each block apparently was hewn roughly out\nof some dark, porous rock and appears to be stained with what\nlooks to be blood...in fact the rock appears to be bleeding in some\nspots.  A faint jungle path can be spotted snaking away into the\nfoliage to the south while a large grass hut is to the southwest.\nThe clearing around the pyramid continues on to the northwest\nand northeast.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7712,-16,-52,0,'A Clearing Around the Pyramid','Towering way above you to the west is a large pyramid crudely\nfashioned out of stone.  Each block apparently was hewn roughly out\nof some dark, porous rock and appears to be stained with what\nlooks to be blood...hell, in some spots the rock appears to be\nbleeding crimson.  A stone stairway leading up the northeast face\nof the pyramid lies nearby to the north while this clearing around\nthe pyramid continues on to the southwest.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7713,-17,-54,0,'A Faint Jungle Path','This faint jungle trail has pretty much been overgrown by the\nfauna all around.  Apparently, only the constant use of this\nnarrow trail has served to fend off the encroaching jungle growth.\nEverything about you appears damp, the air is moist and strange\nscents hang heavily in the air.  Off in the distance you can hear the\noccasional howl of a monkey and a smattering of other indecipherable\nnoises.  The surrounding environs is way too densely packed with\njungle growth to penetrate much further, so it appears that you are\nconfined to traveling along the trail.  It continues on to the\nnorth and east.  A crude stone pyramid looms over the jungle growth\nnearby to the north.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7714,-16,-54,0,'A Faint Jungle Path','This faint jungle trail has pretty much been overgrown by the\nfauna all around.  Apparently, only the constant use of this\nnarrow trail has served to fend off the encroaching jungle growth.\nEverything about you appears damp, the air is moist and strange\nscents hang heavily in the air.  Off in the distance you can hear the\noccasional howl of a monkey and a smattering of other indecipherable\nnoises.  The surrounding environs is way too densely packed with\njungle growth to penetrate much further, so it appears that you are\nconfined to traveling along the trail.  It continues on to the\nwest and northeast.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7715,-15,-53,0,'A Faint Jungle Path','This faint jungle trail has pretty much been overgrown by the\nfauna all around.  Everything about you appears damp, the air is\nmoist and strange scents hang heavily in the air.  Off in the\ndistance you can hear the occasional odd birdcall and a smattering\nof indecipherable noises.  The surrounding environs is way too\ndensely packed with jungle growth to penetrate much beyond the\nobvious exits available to you.  Small thatch huts lie ensconced\nwithin the jungle growth to the north and west of you while the\ntrail continues to the east and southwest.  A crude stone pyramid\ncan be spotted through the jungle overgrowth to the northwest.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7716,-14,-53,0,'A Jungle Trail','This faint jungle trail has pretty much been overgrown by the\nfauna all around.  Everything about you appears damn, the air is\nmoist and strange scents hang heavily in the air.  Off in the\ndistance you can hear the occasional odd birdcall and a smattering\nof indecipherable noises.  The surrounding environs is way too\ndensely packed with jungle growth to penetrate much further, so\nit appears that you are confined to traveling along the trail.\nIt continues on to the west and a small clearing can be\nspotted nearby to the northeast.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7717,-16,-50,0,'A Faint Jungle Path','This faint jungle trail has pretty much been overgrown by the\nfauna all around.  Everything about you appears damp, the air is\nmoist and strange scents hang heavily in the air.  Off in the\ndistance you can hear the occasional odd birdcall and a smattering\nof indecipherable noises.  The surrounding environs is way too\ndensely packed with jungle growth to penetrate much beyond the\nobvious exits available to you.  A small thatch hut lies ensconced\nwithin some jungle growth north of you while the trail continues\non to the east.  Another building constructed of grass and mud is nearby\nto the northwest.  A crude stone pyramid can be spotted through the\njungle overgrowth to the southwest.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7718,-18,-53,0,'A Faint Jungle Trail','This faint jungle trail has pretty much been overgrown by the\nfauna all around.  Apparently, only the constant use of this\nnarrow trail has served to fend off the encroaching jungle growth.\nEverything about you appears damp, the air is moist and strange\nscents hang heavily in the air.  Off in the distance you can hear\nthe occasional cries of some poor mofo getting ripped asunder, limb\nby limb.  A smattering of other cries, probably the same poor sod\nhaving his entrails nibbled on, can be heard...carried on the thick,\ndamp air.  The surrounding environs is way too densely packed with\njungle growth to penetrate much further, so it appears that you\nare confined to traveling along the trail...which, incidentally\nappears to end here.  The only egress from this particular section\nof rainforest lies to the north.  The path apparently once went west as\nwell, but has been disturbed and fresh vegetation planted in its wake.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7719,-15,-51,0,'A Small Thatch Hut','This small, pitiful hovel of a hut appears to be constructed mainly of\nsticks and grass held together by a generous slathering of dried mud.\nThe floor of this domicile is littered with small, inconsequential\nliving accouterments and the occasional piece of fecal matter.  What\nappears to  be a small collection of skulls sits in one corner, no doubt\nthe remains of yesterday\'s brunch.  A flimsy \'door\' rests in the north\n\'wall\' of the hut.\n',49,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,5,80,0,'',NULL),
(7720,-16,-49,0,'A Small Thatch Hut','This small, pitiful hovel of a hut appears to be constructed mainly of\nsticks and grass held together by a generous slathering of dried mud.\nThe floor of this domicile is littered with small, inconsequential\nliving accouterments and the occasional piece of fecal matter.  What\nappears to  be a small collection of pelvic bones sits in one corner,\nno doubt the remains of yesterday\'s breakfast.  A flimsy \'door\' rests\nin the south \'wall\' of the hut.\n',49,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,5,80,0,'',NULL),
(7721,-17,-49,0,'A Storage Shed','This small, pathetic excuse for a building appears to be constructed\nmainly of sticks, bones and grass held together by a generous\nslathering of dried mud and blood.  The floor of this hovel is\nlittered with various articles of who-knows-what.  Quite frankly,\nalmost nothing in this shed is recognizable to you besides the\noccasional knife or two-tined fork.  Bones are scattered all about\nand what passes as a \'door\' rests in the southeast \'wall\' of the\nshed.\n',49,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,5,80,0,'',NULL),
(7722,-18,-51,0,'Hut of the Savage Priest','Constructed primarily from sticks and grass, you can see a few human\nbones here and there stuck in the slatherings of dried mud that keep\nthe four walls around you upright.  Littered all about here and there\nare various small trinkets, mostly all useless, that no doubt were\nstripped from the persons served up to either the savage\'s deity or\nperhaps even to the savages themselves.  Regardless, the trinkets are\nstrewn all about, mixed in with various skulls and bone fragments.\nThe occasional hunk of semi-rotten meat can be spotted amongst the\nmix and the odor in here is absolutely atrocious.  Foul.  This grisly\nscene of the results of cannibalistic excess continues onwards to the\nnorth while a door made of leg bones provides egress to the east.\n',49,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,5,80,0,'',NULL),
(7723,-18,-50,0,'Hut of the Savage Priest','Constructed primarily from sticks and grass, the walls all around\nappear to be the final resting place of a select few of the savages\'\nvictims.  Held in place by a generous slathering of dried mud and\ncaked blood are the skeletal remains of a variety of humanoid\nvictims that were, no doubt, served up to either the cannibal deity\nor perhaps even the cannibals themselves.  The occasional hunk of\nsemi-rotten meat can be spotted lying here or there on the floor,\nmixed in with a variety of skulls and bone fragments.  The odor\nwafting about in here is absolutely atrocious...quite foul to say\nthe least.  This grisly scene of the end result of cannibalistic\nexcess continues onwards to the south.\n',49,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(7724,-19,-51,0,'A Slave Pen','This clearing in the jungle appears to be some sort of holding area\nmeant for those poor unfortunate souls destined to be sacrificed\nby the local contingent of savages or served up as entrees at the\nbarbecue normally held after each ceremony.  Whichever, it matters\nnot since this slave pen serves its purpose most adequately, keeping\nthe human cattle in.  The only egress from this clearing appears to\nbe a stout wooden fence to the southeast.\n',49,172032,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7725,-20,-51,0,'A Slave Pen','This clearing in the jungle appears to be some sort of holding area meant\nfor those poor unfortunate souls destined to be sacrificed by the local\nsavages, or served up as entrees at the feast normally held after each\nceremony.  Whichever, it matters not since this slave pen serves its\npurpose of keeping the human cattle in.  Amongst the litter on the ground\nis an old rusty grate set in the floor once used for the slave refuse to\ndrain out of the pen into a pit but it is unclear whether its used for\nanything now.  The clearing extends to the east somewhat.\n',49,172032,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7726,-18,-54,0,'Hut of the Savage Chief','This large, yet still pitiful hovel of a hut seems to be constructed\nmainly out of sticks and grass held together by generous slatherings\nof dried mud and caked blood.  Upon closer inspection you notice quite\nan interesting collection of bones amongst the sticks and grass making\nup the walls all around.  A small hole in the ceiling allows a gentle\nbreeze from outside to rustle about in here...a pleasant respite, no\ndoubt, from the foul stink of rotting flesh and sinew that hangs heavily\nin the air here.  The hut continues towards the south and a door made\nof leg bones provides egress from this charnel house.\n',49,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,5,80,0,'',NULL),
(7727,-18,-55,0,'Hut of the Savage Chief','This large, yet still mostly pitiful hovel of a hut seems to be\nconstructed mainly out of grass and sticks held together by a\ngenerous slathering of dried mud and caked bone marrow.  Upon closer\ninspection you notice quite an interesting collection of bones\namongst the sticks and grass that make up the walls all around.  A\nsmall hole in the ceiling allows a gentle breeze from outside to\nrustle about in here...a pleasant respite, no doubt, from the foul\nstink of rotting flesh and sinew that hangs heavily on the air in\nhere.  This grisly charnel house continues on to the north.\n',49,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(7728,-16,-53,0,'A Small Thatch Hut','This small, pitiful hovel of a hut appears to  be constructed mainly of\nsticks and grass held together by a generous slathering of dried mud.\nThe floor of this domicile is littered with small, inconsequential\nliving accouterments and the occasional piece of feces.  What appears\nto be a large pile of bones sits in one corner, no doubt the remains\nof yesterday\'s lunch.  A flimsy \'door\' rests in the east \'wall\' of\nthe hut.\n',49,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,5,80,0,'',NULL),
(7729,-15,-52,0,'A Small Thatch Hut','This small, pitiful hovel of a hut appears to be constructed mainly of\nsticks and grass held together by a generous slathering of dried mud.\nThe floor of this domicile is littered with small, inconsequential\nliving accouterments and the occasional piece of feces.  What appears\nto be a small pile of bones sits in one corner, no doubt the remains\nof last night\'s dinner.  A flimsy \'door\' rests in the south \'wall\' of\nthe hut.\n',49,131080,46,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(7730,-20,-51,-1,'An Underground Holding Cell','This dark hole in the ground you currently find yourself in is both dark\nand putrescent.  Obviously, this shallow excavation appears to be meant to\nbe a fresh, new grave but is being used as a holding cell for whatever new\nfresh meat is available.  A slight breeze comes in from what appears to be\nsome sort of rusty grate overhead.\n',49,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7731,-17,-52,0,'On the Pyramid\'s Stairs','This spot on the pyramid is roughly halfway up its crude stairways.\nThe view from here is breathtaking to say the least...you are afforded\na view of the surrounding jungle and the numerous clearings on all sides\nwhere pitiful grass hovels serve as housing for the savages of the\narea.  Curiously enough, a number of stone grates form a ring around\nthis layer of the pyramid, possibly to drain off all the blood and\nentrails that spill over from the sacrificial altar further up.  The base\nof the pyramid\'s stairs continues downwards to the northeast.\n',49,131072,59,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7732,-17,-52,1,'A Scene of Utmost Depravity','From atop this crude stone pyramid, you are afforded a magnificent\nview of the surrounding jungle and the light mist slowly coming\nup over the treetops.  You possibly might enjoy the view if it\nwas not for your present surroundings spoiling it.  All about you\natop this stone structure is blood, entrails, broken bodies, and\nsevered limbs.  The stench here is unnerving to say the least, and\nno doubt stinks to high heaven...perhaps that is part of the\npurpose of this setting.  Well, whatever cannibal deity exists in The\nWorld\'s pantheon, he or she is most assuredly pleased by this\ndisplay of grisly devotion.  What savage possibly could not be\nflattered by the collection of oozing brain, severed members, and\nleaking intestines at your feet? Refuge from this sickening scene\nof savage cannibalistic excess can be had by taking the pyramid\'s\nstairway down.\n',49,131072,59,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7733,-17,-52,-1,'Beneath the Pyramid','This chamber deep in the bowels of a crude stone pyramid is more\nakin to a subterranean pool rather than anything else.  A foul stench\nwafts about the room, the culprit being the half-congealed pool of\nblood that appears to be at least a foot deep.  Floating about in the\ncrimson is an odd assortment of entrails, brain matter, severed\nmembers and the occasional eyeball staring back at you.  A stone grate\nin the ceiling provides egress from this grisly scene and a heavy\nstone door rests in the southeast wall of this chamber.\n',49,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,5,80,0,'',NULL),
(7734,-16,-53,-1,'An Underground Burial Chamber','A crimson pool of blood surrounds you on all sides as you survey\nthe environs.  Roughly hewn walls of a dark porous stone serve as\nthe walls and ceiling of this chamber while the floor remains\nunseen beneath the sea of blood.  A heavy stone door blocks off\npassage to the northwest while this decrepit chamber continues on\nto the east.\n',49,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(7735,-15,-53,-1,'An Underground Burial Chamber','A crimson pool of blood surrounds you on all sides as you survey\nthe immediate environs.  Roughly hewn walls of some sort of dark\nporous stone serve as the walls and ceiling of this chamber while\nthe floor remains hidden beneath the sea of crimson.  This decrepit\nburial chamber continues on to the north and west.\n',49,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(7736,-15,-52,-1,'An Underground Burial Chamber','A crimson pool of blood surrounds you on all sides as you survey\nthe immediate environs.  Roughly hewn walls of some sort of dark\nporous stone serve as the walls and ceiling of this chamber while\nthe floor remains hidden beneath the sea of crimson.  This decrepit\nburial chamber continues on to the south.\n',49,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(7737,-13,-49,-1,'A Deep Hole in the Ground','This particular excavation into the earth for some reason does not\nappear to be natural.  This observation is probably due to the realization\nthat the earthen walls surrounding you exhibit signs of having been dug\nout of the ground and there are signs of recent upkeep.  A bit of brush\noverhead looks somewhat accessible and a sturdy-looking door fashioned\nout of crystal lies to the northwest.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7738,-14,-48,-1,'A Crystalline Tunnel','The tunnel you now gaze upon is a marvel to behold in that the walls\nof purest crystal seem to reflect any and every bit of light, even\nthe tiniest ray.  The effect is nothing short of breathtaking when\nviewed in the proper illumination.  A large crystalline door is set\nin the southeast end while the tunnel continues downwards.\n',49,141321,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7739,-14,-48,-2,'A Crystalline Tunnel','The tunnel you now gaze upon is a marvel to behold in that the walls\nof purest crystal seem to reflect any and every bit of light, even\nthe tiniest ray.  The effect is nothing short of breathtaking when\nviewed in the proper illumination.  This luminescent corridor continues\non to the north and upwards.\n',49,141321,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7740,-14,-47,-2,'A Crystalline Tunnel','The tunnel you now gaze upon is a marvel to behold in that the walls\nof purest crystal seem to reflect any and every bit of light, even\nthe tiniest ray.  The effect is nothing short of breathtaking when\nviewed in the proper illumination.  This luminescent corridor continues\non to the northeast and south.\n',49,141321,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7741,-13,-46,-2,'A Crystalline Tunnel','The tunnel you now gaze upon is a marvel to behold in that the walls\nof purest crystal seem to reflect any and every bit of light, even\nthe tiniest ray.  The effect is nothing short of breathtaking when\nviewed in the proper illumination.  This luminescent corridor continues\non to the southwest and to the north, where you can barely make out\nwhat appears to be two sets of crystalline gates.\n',49,141321,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7742,-13,-45,-2,'Before a Pair of Gates','This appears to be one end of the crystalline tunnel that causes many\nto take a moment to simply stare in wonder at the ambient light show.\nEven the merest hint of light is reflected and refracted wondrously\nby the walls and ceiling of this tunnel...a truly splendid crossfire of\nlight beams.  The crystalline corridor continues on to the south while\ntwo gargantuan gates block passage to the northeast and northwest.\n',49,141321,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7743,-14,-44,-2,'The Proving Ground','This particular chamber is large and stretches out to the north and\neast, providing ample space for combat training and other pursuits\nof that ilk that are no doubt practiced on this very ground.  The\nwalls, ceiling and floor of this area are constructed out of what\nappears to be onyx panels that seem to sap all the light out of\nthe surroundings.  A large crystalline gate rests in the southeast\nwall.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7744,-13,-44,-2,'The Proving Ground','This particular chamber is large and stretches out in multiple\ndirections, providing ample space for combat training and other\npursuits of that ilk that are no doubt practiced on this very\nground.  The walls, ceiling and floor of this area are constructed\nout of what appears to be onyx panels that seem to sap all light\nout of the surroundings.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7745,-12,-44,-2,'The Proving Ground','This particular chamber is large and stretches out to the north and\nwest, providing ample space for combat training and other pursuits\nof that ilk that are no doubt practiced on this very ground.  The\nwalls, ceiling and floor of this are are constructed out of what\nappears to be onyx panels that seem to sap all the light out of\nthe surroundings.  A Large crystalline gate rests in the southwest\nwall while a sturdy emerald door rests in the east wall.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7746,-14,-43,-2,'The Proving Ground','This particular chamber is large and spans further to the south,\nnortheast and southeast...providing more than ample space for\ncombat training and any other martial pursuits that no doubt\nare practiced on this very ground.  The walls, ceiling and floor\nof this area are constructed out of what appears to be onyx\npanels that seem to sap all the light out of the surroundings.\nUnlike in the rest of this proving ground, the panels do not\nseem to fit as tightly together for some reason.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7747,-12,-43,-2,'The Proving Ground','This particular chamber is large and stretches out to the south,\nnorthwest and southwest...providing ample space for combat\ntraining and other martial pursuits of that ilk that are no doubt\npracticed on this very ground.  The walls, ceiling and floor of\nthis area are constructed out of what appears to be onyx panels that\nseem to sap all the light from the surroundings.  A large sapphire\ndoor rests in the east wall.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7748,-13,-42,-2,'The Proving Ground','This particular chamber is large and spans further to the southeast\nand southwest, providing ample space for combat training and\nvarious other martial pursuits that are no doubt practiced on\nthis very ground.  The walls, ceiling and floor of this area are\nconstructed out of what appears to be onyx panels that seem to\nsap the light from the surroundings.  A large ruby door rests in\nthe north wall.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7749,-13,-41,-2,'A Crystalline Stairwell','This appear to be the top of a marvelously crafted stairwell made\nentirely of crystal.  Light all around seems to get caught by the\nsurfaces and reflected about in a dizzying array of light beams.\nA large ruby door is set in the south wall and the stairwell leads\nfurther downwards.\n',49,141321,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7750,-11,-43,-2,'Commando Barracks','This somewhat compact chamber apparently serves as a barracks room for\nthis outpost\'s commando squad.  The floor is spotlessly clean and there\ndoes not seem to be a single mote of dust on either the ground or on any\nof the bunks that line each wall.  Folded neatly on each bed is a silk\nblanket accompanied by a silk-covered pillow.  A delicate looking onyx\nspiral staircase leads downwards through a hole in the floor while a\nlarge sapphire door rests in the western wall.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7751,-11,-44,-2,'Assassin Barracks','This somewhat compact chamber apparently serves as a barracks room for\nthis outpost\'s assassin enclave.  The floor is spotlessly clean and there\ndoes not seem to be a single mote of dust on either the ground or on any\nof the bunks that line each wall.  Folded neatly on each bed is a silk\nblanket accompanied by a silk-covered pillow.  A delicate looking spiral\nstaircase hewn out of obsidian leads downwards through a hole in the\nfloor while a large emerald door rests in the western wall.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7752,-13,-41,-3,'A Crystalline Hallway','The crystalline hallway you now gaze upon is quite the marvel to behold in\nthat the walls seem to reflect and refract any and all rays of ambient\nlight.  The dazzling effect is nothing short of breathtaking when viewed\nin the proper illumination.  A delicate crystal staircase leads upwards while\nthis luminescent corridor continues to the south.  A onyx door is set in the\nnorthwest wall.\n',49,141321,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7753,-14,-40,-3,'The Praetor\'s Office','This office appears spartan in furnishings but makes up for it with the\nmess covering the floor.  Littered all about are broken and shattered\nbits of miniature mannequins and other assorted off items.  A large\nplatinum desk sits in one corner of the room with a wooden chair while\na large painting covers the west wall.  What appears to be some living\nquarters is to the north and a obsidian door is set in the southeast\nwall.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7754,-14,-39,-3,'The Praetor\'s Living Quarters','This room is spacious but the floor is dominated by an enormous bed lying\nin the middle of the floor.  You notice that the sheets of the bed seem to\nbe undulating gently.  Elegant tapestries hang from the onyx walls, a\npleasant contrast to the various and assorted weapons and shields arranged\nalongside them.  Heaped in one corner of the bedchamber is a pile of\nclothing.  What appears to be a tidy office can be spotted to the south.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7755,-15,-40,-3,'Chamber of a Solitary Oriel','This room is like no other you can think of having ever had the pleasure,\nor displeasure, of experiencing.  The closest approximation of this scene\nwould probably be the fabled observatory in Cimea...but this differs from\nit in that instead of flashing a blinding array of various images of The\nWorld all about you, it simply shows you a dizzying amount of different\nangles of the same scene over and over - the aforementioned observatory.\nThis relentless slide show from hell is having a disorienting effect on\nyou, and even the ground has been  usurped by more maddening images of\nthe observatory.  The only anchor of sanity remaining in this mad jumble\nof colors and forms is a stable rectangular outline to the east.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7756,-13,-42,-3,'A Crystalline Hallway','The crystalline hallway you now gaze upon is quite the marvel to behold in\nthat the walls seem to reflect and refract any and all rays of ambient\nlight.  The dazzling effect is nothing short of breathtaking when viewed in\nthe proper illumination.  A delicate crystal staircase can be seen to the north\nwhile the hallway continues on to the east.  A large onyx door rests in the\nnortheast wall of the corridor.\n',49,141321,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7757,-12,-41,-3,'A Storage Room','You are in what appears to be a room reserved for holding such things as\nfood stores and the like for the outpost\'s inhabitants.  The onyx walls\nare slick with a rime-like moisture and the temperature in here is a bit\nfrigid.  A single onyx door set in the southwest wall provides passage out\nof this storeroom.\n',49,141320,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7758,-12,-42,-3,'A Crystalline Hallway','The crystalline hallway you now gaze upon is quite the marvel to behold in\nthat the walls seem to reflect and refract any and all rays of ambient\nlight.  The dazzling effect is nothing short of breathtaking when viewed in\nthe proper illumination.  The luminescent hallway continues on to the east\nand west.\n',49,141321,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7759,-11,-42,-3,'A Crystalline Hallway','The crystalline hallway you now gaze upon is quite the marvel to behold in\nthat the walls seem to reflect and refract any and all rays of ambient\nlight.  The dazzling effect is nothing short of breathtaking when viewed in\nthe proper illumination.  The luminescent hallway continues on to the east\nand west.\n',49,141321,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7760,-10,-42,-3,'A Crystalline Hallway','The crystalline hallway you now gaze upon is quite the marvel to behold in\nthat the walls seem to reflect and refract any and all rays of ambient\nlight.  The dazzling effect is nothing short of breathtaking when viewed in\nthe proper illumination.  The luminescent hallway curves here and continues\non to the west and southeast.  A large gold-trimmed onyx door rests in the\neastern wall of the corridor.\n',49,141321,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7761,-9,-43,-3,'A Crystalline Hallway','The crystalline hallway you now gaze upon is quite the marvel to behold in\nthat the walls seem to reflect and refract any and all rays of ambient\nlight.  The dazzling effect is nothing short of breathtaking when viewed in\nthe proper illumination.  The luminescent hallway curves here and continues\non to the south and northwest.  A large gold-trimmed onyx door rests in the\nnorthern wall of the corridor.\n',49,141321,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7762,-9,-42,-3,'The Sacred Chapel of the Naiad','You gaze upon a sight truly wondrous to your eyes.  The walls of purest\nmidnight onyx rise high above you on all sides, reaching up into the\ngloom above and out of your sight.  A beautiful stained glass window\nis in the fall wall to the northeast behind an altar on a raised dais.\nTwo sets of pews flank you to the north and east while two large doors\nlead out of this sacred chamber to the south and west.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7763,-9,-41,-3,'Pews','Something about this section of this house of worship strikes you as odd\nin some fashion.  Yes, you can sit here and pray quietly...you can even\nmeditate, but something here is just not quite right.  Perhaps it is the\nfact that everything about you is fashioned out of the purest midnight onyx\nthat seems to sap in any and all light in the surroundings.  Who knows,\nwhatever it is...it is odd.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7764,-8,-42,-3,'Pews','Something about this section of this house of worship strikes you as odd\nin some fashion.  Yes, you can sit here and pray quietly...you can even\nmeditate if you wish, but something here is just not quite right.  Perhaps\nit is the fact that everything about you is fashioned out of the purest\nmidnight onyx that seems to sap in any and all light from surroundings.\nPerhaps it is the various etchings made into the pews.  Who knows, whatever\nit is...it most definitely is unnerving.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7765,-8,-41,-3,'Altar of the Naiad','Dominating your sight is a magnificently intricate and beautiful stained\nglass window in the northeast wall.  Vibrant colors depict a scene of a\nunbelievably beautiful woman with light brown hair and piercing silvery-\nblue eyes frolicking about in a pool of clearest water.  The altar here\nlooks to have been painstakingly carved from a gigantic block of ivory\nand rests firmly upon a raised dais of onyx.  A rather nondescript onyx\ndoor rests in the north wall while the exit from this house of worship\ncan be seen further to the southwest.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7766,-8,-40,-3,'The Saint\'s Outer Chamber','This room is dominated by a gigantic, rectangular crystalline table\nset firmly in the center of the chamber.  A multitude of assorted\nsecular works and sheaves of parchment lie scattered all over the\nsurface of the table and some have even spilled over onto the floor.\nThis appears to be where important policy decisions regarding the\nfollowing of the deity Naiad are made, or perhaps just how to preach\nher teachings.  A pair of onyx doors lead outwards from this chamber,\none set in the west wall and the other in the south one.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7767,-9,-40,-3,'The Saint\'s Living Quarters','This bedchamber is spacious and meticulously well-kept.  Not a single\nobject seems to be out of place and a sense of harmony permeates the\nroom.  A large bed sits up against the west wall and a large onyx door\nrests in the wall opposite it.  A few threadbare tapestries hang from\nthe walls and a few secular articles lie strewn about here and there\non the bed.  The room is perfectly still and the only sound to reach\nyour ears is the gentle whistle of a breeze coming from beneath the\ndoor.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7768,-9,-44,-3,'A Crystalline Hallway','The crystalline hallway you now gaze upon is quite the marvel to behold in\nthat the walls seem to reflect and refract any and all rays of ambient\nlight.  The dazzling effect is nothing short of breathtaking as beams of light\ninterlace and create a wondrous crossfire of illumination.  The luminescent\ncorridor continues on to the north and west, while a large onyx door is\nset in the eastern wall.\n',49,141321,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7769,-8,-44,-3,'The Mess Hall','Long tables run the length of this long and low chamber, most of\nthem covered quite liberally with what is commonly referred to in\nmess halls across The World as \'slop\'.  Obviously some diners were\nso displeased with their meal as to be inclined to attempt impromptu\nart sessions on the onyx walls.  The mess hall continues on to the\nsouth while an onyx door rests in the west wall of this room.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7770,-8,-45,-3,'The Mess Hall','Long tables run the length of this long and low chamber, most of\nthem covered quite liberally with what is commonly referred to in\nmess halls across The World as \'slop\'.  Obviously some diners were\nso displeased with their meal as to be inclined to attempt impromptu\nart sessions on the walls.  The mess hall continues on to the north\nwhile an onyx door rests in the west wall of this room.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7771,-9,-45,-3,'The Kitchen','What you now look upon is a scene of quite contradictory natures\nand opinions.  From here, food preparers either create culinary\nmasterpieces (their opinion) or vile, gut-churning, bile-scaring\nslop (those dining\'s opinion).  Either way, this chamber is what\nis commonly referred to as a kitchen and it has three onyx doors\nleading out from it.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7772,-9,-46,-3,'A Storage Room','You are in what appears to be a room reserved for holding such things as\nfood stores and the like for the outpost\'s inhabitants.  The onyx walls\nare slick with a rime-like moisture and the temperature in here is a bit\nfrigid.  A single onyx door set in the northern wall provides passage out\nof this storeroom.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7773,-10,-46,-3,'Servant\'s Quarters','In stark contrast from what you have possibly seen of the rest of this\noutpost, this chamber seems downright homey, unpretentious and quite\npathologically messy.  Absent are the various tapestries, silk sheets\nand pillows, ornately carved spiral stairwells and the like.  In their\nstead are crude drawings on the walls, tin cups, worn cotten bedding\nand a straw-filled mattress.  It suddenly strikes you that these dwellings\ncould only possibly be the domiciles of the outpost\'s support staff.\nAn onyx door rests in the northeast wall while this scene of squalid\nyet humble living continues on to the north.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7774,-10,-45,-3,'Servant\'s Quarters','In stark contrast from what you have possibly seen of the rest of this\noutpost, this chamber seems downright homey, unpretentious and quite\npathologically messy.  Absent are the various tapestries, silk sheets\nand pillows, ornately carved spiral starewells and the like.  In their\nstead are crude drawings on the walls, tin cups, worn cotton bedding\nand a straw-filled mattress.  It suddenly strikes you that these dwellings\ncould only possibly be the domiciles of the outpost\'s support staff.\nAn onyx door rests in the north wall while this scene of squalid living\ncontinues on to the south.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7775,-10,-44,-3,'A Crystalline Hallway','The crystalline hallway you now gaze upon is quite the marvel to behold\nin that the walls seem to both refract and reflect any and all rays of\nambient light.  The dazzling effect is nothing short of breathtaking as\na dizzying array of beams of light interlace and create a wondrous crossfire\nof illumination.  The luminescent corridor continues on to the east while\nsolid onyx doors rest in the northern, southwestern and southern walls.\n',49,141321,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7776,-10,-43,-3,'Commando Barracks','This long and low chamber stretches out to the west and appears to serve as\nthe living quarters for the commando squad that mans this outpost.  The floor\nis spotlessly clean and there does not seem to be a single mote of dust on\nthe ground or any of the bunks that line each wall.  Folded neatly on each\nbed is a silk blanket accompanied by a silk-covered pillow.  A large door set\nin the southern wall provides egress from this barracks room.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7777,-11,-43,-3,'Commando Barracks','This long and low chamber stretches out to the east and appears to serve as\nthe living quarters for the commando squad that mans this outpost.  The floor\nis spotlessly clean and there does not seem to be a single mote of dust on\nthe ground or any of the bunks that line each wall.  Folded neatly on each\nbed is a silk blanket accompanied by a silk-covered pillow.  A delicate\nlooking onyx spiral staircase leads upwards through a hole in the ceiling.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7778,-11,-45,-3,'Assassin Barracks','This long and low chamber stretches out to the north and appears to serve as\nthe living quarters for the outpost\'s assassin enclave.  The floor is\nspotless and there does not to seem to be a single mote of dust on the\nground or any of the bunks that line each wall.  Folded neatly on each bed is\na silk blanket accompanied by a silk-covered pillow.  A large door set in the\nnortheastern wall provides for egress in that direction.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7779,-11,-44,-3,'Assassin Barracks','This long and low chamber stretches out to the south and appears to serve as\nthe living quarters for the outpost\'s assassin enclave.  The floor is\nspotless and there appears to be nary a single mote of dust on the ground or\nany of the bunks that line each wall.  Folded neatly on each bed is a silk\nblanket accompanied by a silk-covered pillow.  A delicate looking spiral\nstairwell hewn out of obsidian leads upwards through a hole in the ceiling.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7780,-14,-42,-2,'Entrance to the Shadow Arena','Nothing in particular about this room strikes you as odd aside from\nthe fact that it is shaped, unnervingly accurate in proportion, like\nan octagon.  Large panels of onyx make up the walls of this eight-sided\nchamber and an onyx spiral staircase leads down through a hole in the\nfloor.\n',49,141320,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7781,-14,-42,-3,'The Shadow Arena','Darkness rules supreme in this chamber of the arena of stealth and\nshadows.  The walls, ceiling and floor of this room are constructed out\nof huge panels of the purest midnight onyx...so pure in substance that\nyour surroundings seem to almost suck in any and all light...perhaps\nthe walls are magical in nature.  Strange shadows coalesce, shift and\ndisappear at the edges of your vision.  The arena of shadows continues\nto the west and south while an onyx spiral staircase leads upwards\nthrough a hole in the ceiling.\n',49,175144,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7782,-14,-43,-3,'The Shadow Arena','Darkness rules absolutely supreme in this chamber of the arena of\nstealth and shadows.  The walls, ceiling and floor of this room are\nconstructed out of huge panels of the purest midnight onyx...so pure\nin substance that your surroundings almost seem to suck in any and\nall ambient light...perhaps the substance is mystical in nature.\nStrange shadows coalesce, shift and then disappear without a trace at\nthe edges of your vision.  The arena of shadows and darkness appears\nto continue in most possible directions.\n',49,175144,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7783,-14,-44,-3,'The Shadow Arena','Darkness rules absolutely supreme in this chamber of the arena of\nstealth and shadows.  The walls, ceilings and floor of this room are\nconstructed out of huge panels of the purest midnight onyx...so pure\nin substance that your surroundings almost seem to suck in any and\nall ambient light...perhaps the onyx is mystical in nature.  Strange\nshadows coalesce, shift and then disappear without a trace at the edges\nof your vision.  The arena of shadows and darkness appears to continue\non to the north and west.\n',49,175144,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7784,-15,-44,-3,'The Shadow Arena','Darkness rules supreme in this chamber of the arena of stealth and\nshadows.  The walls, ceiling and floor of this room are constructed out\nof huge panels of the purest midnight onyx...so pure in substance that\nyour surroundings seem to almost suck in any and all light...perhaps\nthe onyx is mystical in nature.  Strange shadows coalesce, shift and\nthen disappear without a trace at the edges of your vision.  The arena\nof shadows and darkness appears to continue on in most possible\ndirections from this place.\n',49,175144,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7785,-16,-44,-3,'The Shadow Arena','Darkness rules supreme in this chamber of the arena of stealth and\nshadows.  The walls, ceiling and floor of this room are constructed out\nof huge panels of the purest midnight onyx...so pure in substance that\nyour surroundings seem to almost suck in any and all light...perhaps\nthe onyx is mystical in nature.  Strange shadows coalesce, shift and\nthen disappear without a trace at the edges of your vision.  The arena\nof shadows and darkness appears to continue on to the north and east.\n',49,175144,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7786,-16,-43,-3,'The Shadow Arena','Darkness rules supreme in this chamber of the arena of stealth and\nshadows.  The walls, ceiling and floor of this room are constructed out\nof huge panels of the purest midnight onyx...so pure in substance that\nyour surroundings seem to almost suck in any and all light...perhaps\nthe onyx is magical in nature.  Strange shadows coalesce, shift and\nthen disappear without a trace at the edges of your vision.  The arena\nof shadows and darkness appears to continue in most possible\ndirections.\n',49,175144,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7787,-16,-42,-3,'The Shadow Arena','Darkness rules supreme in this chamber of the arena of stealth and\nshadows.  The walls, ceiling and floor of this room are constructed out\nof huge panels of the purest midnight onyx...so pure in substance that\nyour surroundings seem to almost suck in any and all light...perhaps\nthe walls are magical in nature.  Strange shadows coalesce, shift and\nthen disappear without a trace at the edges of your vision.  The arena\nof shadows and darkness continues to the south and east.\n',49,175144,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7788,-15,-42,-3,'The Shadow Arena','Darkness rules supreme in this chamber of the arena of stealth and\nshadows.  The walls, ceiling and floor of this room are constructed out\nof huge panels of the purest midnight onyx...so pure in substance that\nyour surroundings seem to almost suck in any and all light...perhaps\nthe walls are magical in nature.  Strange shadows coalesce, shift and\nthen disappear in and out of the edges of your vision.  The arena of\nshadows continues in almost all directions.\n',49,175144,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7789,-15,-43,-3,'The Heart of Darkness','The chamber you now rest your gaze upon stretches downwards into a\ndarkness so deep as to be virtually impenetrable.  An almost palpable\ndarkness hangs thickly in the air and the panels of the onyx walls\naround you add to the gloom by unnaturally leeching off the room\'s\nillumination.  The hairs on the nape of  your neck rise as you begin\nto sense the unnaturally seductive call of the shadows...the warmth\nand comfort of the darkness closing in on all sides.\n',49,142376,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7790,-15,-43,-4,'The Heart of Darkness','The chamber that you now rest your gaze upon stretches upwards to a\nceiling barely visible high above your head.  An almost palpable darkness\nhangs thickly in the air and the onyx walls add to the gloom by\nunnaturally leeching off the room\'s illumination.  The hairs on the nape\nof your neck rise as you begin to sense the unnaturally seductive call\nof the shadows...the warmth and comfort of the darkness closing in on\nall sides.  The shadows are slightly darker high overhead in another\nchamber akin to this one.\n',49,142376,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7791,-12,-49,0,'End of a Jungle Trail','This faint trail has been pretty much overgrown by the jungle.  The\nway southeast has been completely overgrown and you cannot force\nyour way through any of the surrounding brush.  To the west is a faint\ntrail cutting through the jungle.\n',49,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7792,-11,-50,0,'A Silent Clearing','Except for the changing weather overhead and the passing of the\nsun, moon and stars...this clearing seems to be stuck in time...\npreserved and almost sacrosanct in a way.  You can hear an animal\ncry from nearby but this particular clearing in the jungle appears\ndevoid of any of the typical jungle fauna.  Something about the air\nhere leads you to believe this particular spot has mostly been\nundisturbed over the ages.\n',49,167072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7793,-12,-50,0,'A Silent Clearing','Except for the changing weather overhead and the passing of the\nsun, moon and stars...this clearing seems to be stuck in time...\npreserved and almost sacrosanct in a way.  You can hear an animal\ncry out from nearby but this particular clearing in the jungle\nappears to be devoid of any of the typical jungle fauna.  Something\nabout the air here leads you to believe that this particular spot\nhas mostly been undisturbed over the ages.\n',49,167072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7800,40,-37,3,'Watchtower On The Southern Wall','  The watchtower affords you one of the better views of the fortress,\nwhich extends out some distance to the north before vanishing into the\nfog.  You can just make out the western and eastern walls in the murk.  A\nfew staggering Drow are given away by their movement atop the walls.  To\nthe south, the horizon melds the fog and the ground into a vague,\nindistinguishable haze.  The structure of the watchtower has partially\ncollapsed, and the stonework has fallen into the stairwell.\n',48,172044,21,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(7801,58,5,-1,'Within the Crevice','  Directly before you lies the empty air of an impassable crevasse.  You\nstand upon an outcropping of rock, which juts from the southern wall of\nthe fissure.  Above, a sturdy bridge affords a method of traversal.\nNatural handholds in the bridge\'s structural timbers may be adequate for\nyou to pull yourself up to the top.  To the south, a passage enters into\nthe rock, dimly lit only by some source of illumination deep within the\ntunnel.\n',48,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,3,72,0,'',NULL),
(7802,58,4,-1,'A Natural Tunnel in the Rock','  This natural tunnel through solid rock extends out of doors to the north,\nand southward toward a dim light.  It\'s fairly difficult to move in here.\n',48,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,3,72,0,'',NULL),
(7803,58,3,-1,'Large Chamber in the Rock','  Contrasting the tight confines of the entry passage, this chamber is\nperhaps 60 feet across and roughly circular.  The walls are natural rock,\npolished smooth and ornately decorated with characters belonging to some\nunknown symbology.  The unbroken plane of the wall gradually breaks into a\nturbulent, jagged ceiling, and the flickering light from meager torches\nplays hide-and- seek with the recesses of the rock.  Vague patterns are\nvisible through the layer of dust upon the floor, spiraling delicately\ntoward the room\'s center.\n',48,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,720,0,'',NULL),
(7804,0,0,0,'Pet Room','  Some in cages others allowed to roam free this is Tarl\'s storage\narea for his trapped and trained animals.  Each appears to be well\ngroomed and fed with a healthy coat about them.  The room itself\nappears for the most part neat and tidy as very few animal droppings\ncan be seen in either the cages or on the floor.\n',54,166075,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7805,34,59,0,'Hides and Herbal Storeroom','   Newly opened, this division of the company is run by Tuvar.  Recently\nretired from the trapping trade, Tuvar agreed to move back to town with\nhis family as long as he could open this division of the company.  Tuvar\ndeals in hides, skins, herbal ingredients and other organic commodities\nalong with the occasional bit of fabric.\n',56,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(7822,10,36,-3,'A Hollowed Out Branch','  It is so dark in here, that even with your light source, you can\nbarely make out your hand stretched out in front of you.  Pebbles and\ndirt crunch loudly beneath your weight as you move.  You can feel a slight\nbreeze filtering through from the leaves above.\n',101,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,1,45,0,'',NULL),
(7823,11,37,-3,'A Hollowed Out Branch','  The branch continues on to a dead-end and apparently the main trunk\nof a tree.  There is nothing here but a small spider\'s web spun in\nthe twigs and leaves above.  The empty carcasses of small worms and\ninsects litter the area beneath it.  The sound of water, lapping\nagainst the trunk you are in, is the apparent reason for the\nmoisture in the air and dampness at your fingertips.\n',101,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,1,30,0,'',NULL),
(7824,11,37,-2,'The Great Oak','  You stand before what has to be the widest oak tree you have ever\nseen.  The top of the oak lays behind you, effectively blocking\nyour path in that direction.  A tattered web at your feet show signs of\nboth decay and repair.  Giggling can be heard from somewhere\nnearby.\n',101,139264,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7825,11,38,-2,'The Great Oak','  Walking along the width of this oak it finally begins to curve\nround.  To the west lies the felled top, its charred edges frayed and\nsplit from the sheer force of the lightening bolt that struck it.\nYears of battering elements have just begun decaying its solid trunk.\n',101,139264,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7826,12,39,-2,'The Great Oak','  A small glade to the east blossoms with wildflowers and crab\ngrass that grabs the base of the tree.  The shaded grass is the\nperfect place for an afternoon picnic or a romantic interlude.\nSmall saplings reach toward the sky in search of freedom from\nthis solitary place.  The surrounding foliage is impenetrable and\noppressing.\n',101,139264,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7827,13,38,-2,'The Great Oak','  A split down the center of the trunk is charred black and debris from\nthe blast is scattered about the ground.  Inside the trunk huge pieces\nof splintered wood are piled high, effectively blocking any passage\nexcept by the smallest of creatures.\n',101,139264,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7828,13,37,-2,'A Giant Oak','  This side of the tree is covered with ivy climbing along the trunk\nand stretching to the top.  Bushes and vines overgrown nearby push their\nway forward through the grass and small trees, trying to gain a\nstronghold.\n',101,139264,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7829,12,38,-2,'Inside a Giant Trunk','  The hollowed out trunk has been ravaged by vegetation and insects\nalike attempting to claim this place as their own.  The ground is\nlittered with jumbled footprints that have been pressed into the soft\nash and soot, some of them yours.  The height of what is left of the\ntree effectively blocks much of the outside elements from penetrating\nhere.  The tattered shards of wood, some blackened, some splintered,\nhave been violently mangled by the awesome force that struck here.\n',101,139264,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7830,14,38,-2,'A Quiet Glade','  Soft grass and tiny wildflowers spring up from the ground, and\nthe saplings give this alcove a youthful feel.  Devoid of the\ndestruction nearby, it is evidence of the renewal of nature\'s cycles.\n',101,139264,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7831,12,36,-2,'A Giant Oak','  This side of the tree is littered with felled branches and\novergrown brush.  The ground is soft and muddy where it meets with\nthe softly rushing water that flows south and disappears beneath\nthe wall of vegetation.\n',101,139264,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7832,12,38,-1,'Atop a Trunk','  You hold on for dear life as you balance on the thin rail of wood\nyou climbed.  The devastation of the tree looks even worse from up here,\nand provides only splinters for your hands to grasp should you begin\nto fall.  Blocked only by the larger trees, you can see over most of\nthe solid hedge rows in all directions, but the southern view is the\nbest.\n',101,139264,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7833,44,-31,3,'A Gigantic Rock','On all sides of this monstrous boulder set in the middle of the stream\nis rushing water that steadily moves downstream and disappears over\na cliff nearby to the east.  A tall, forbidding rock wall looms overhead\na little further upstream.\n',48,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7834,43,-30,3,'In the Mountain\'s Shadow','This appears to be the point where the stream emerges from the mountain\nand some underwater spring.  Looming high overhead is the forbidding\nvisage of a sheer rockface and further travel upstream appears impossible.\nA gigantic rock lying in midstream lies nearby to the southeast.\n',48,131072,52,0,0,0,10,8,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7835,45,-31,3,'A Clear Mountain Stream','Water rushes all around you, steadily moving further downstream to\nthe east.  What appears to be a large boulder set in midstream lies\nnearby to the west and a sheer rockwall looms above it in the\ndistance.\n',48,131072,52,0,0,0,10,8,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7836,46,-32,3,'Atop a Breathtaking Waterfall','The view from here is majestic to say the least.  Directly below you,\nthe water plummets...crashing at the base of the falls with a thunderous\nroar.  Somewhat nearby to the north or northeast is what appears to be\na glittering metal dome half-buried into the side of the mountain.  Far\nto the southeast is what looks like a rolling savannah and you can\nbarely make out tiny specs roving around on the grasslands.  A little\nfurther upstream is what appears to be a gigantic boulder set amidst\nthe water.\n',48,139264,58,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7837,46,-32,2,'A Breathtaking Waterfall','A thunderous roar fills your ears as you look about and cannot help\nbut notice the sheer beauty of your surroundings.  A torrential downpour\nof water cascades from overhead, crashing majestically nearby below.\nThe rockwall behind the sheet of water is slick and wet, but affords\na few handholds here and there.\n',48,139264,58,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7838,-19,-15,0,'Horse Stable','  This part of the stable is slightly messier than the southern part of\nthe stables but it still looks comfortable.  Obviously, the owner is making\nhis employees try to improve this part for the comfort of the horses and\nthe customers.\n',11,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,180,0,'',NULL),
(7839,17,54,-1,'A Small Path South of the Tundra','  Barren trees, dead from the cold chill of winter run rampantly\nin all directions.  The ground here has turned into a murky brown\ncolor where devil weeds grow in clumps.\n',88,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7840,17,53,-1,'A Small Path South of the Tundra','  Barren trees, dead from the cold chill of winter run rampantly\nin all directions.  The ground here has turned into a murky brown\ncolor where devil weeds grow in clumps.\n',88,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7841,17,52,-1,'A Small Path South of the Tundra','  Barren trees, dead from the cold chill of winter run rampantly\nin all directions.  The ground here has turned into a murky brown\ncolor where devil weeds grow in clumps.\n',88,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7842,17,51,-1,'A Small Path South of the Tundra','  Barren trees, dead from the cold chill of winter run rampantly\nin all directions.  The ground here has turned into a murky brown\ncolor where devil weeds grow in clumps.\n',88,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7843,-50,-36,0,'The Mages Arena','  You stand upon a large dirt field which seems surprisingly clean.  As you look\naround, you seem to be within a large arena, completely surrounded by spectator\nstands.  You can hear the sounds of combat in the distance, and see various\nwarriors and gladiators either dueling to settle differences, or just sparring\nfor practice.\n',17,161828,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(7844,-51,-36,0,'The Mages Arena','  You stand upon a large dirt field which seems surprisingly clean.  As you look\naround, you seem to be within a large arena, completely surrounded by spectator\nstands.  You can hear the sounds of combat in the distance, and see various\nwarriors and gladiators either dueling to settle differences, or just sparring\nfor practice.\n',17,161828,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
