(8412,-8,4,0,'A Derelict Slot Machine','<k>  You are at a large derelict slot machine.  The lights have long\nsince gone dead and every once shiny surface has been scratched to\ndullness.  The handle has been broken off, probably sharpened and used\nas a shiv by some unknown vagrant.  A large jagged hole has been cut\ninto the machine at the base, presumably to remove whatever coins may\nhave remained.<1>\n',-1,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8415,-9,3,0,'A Makeshift Boxing Ring','<k>  A large ring has been marked with rocks and slot machine parts.  Scuff\nmarks and <1><r>blood<1><k> stains on the floor indicate the obvious purpose of this ring.<1>\n',-1,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8416,-8,6,0,'Pile Of Corpses','<r> Blood<1> <k>splatters the walls and sits in fetid pools upon the\nfloor.  A gagging stench of rotting corpses fills the air and refuses\nto circulate in this corner room.  A pile of rotting corpses occupies\nnearly all available space, and worse yet they are stinking dirty\nvagrant corpses, covered in the finery of the streets - wretched\ntattered clothing pillaged from garbages and corpses citywide.  One\ncorner of the room is covered in scorch marks, as if someone tried to\nburn the corpses.<1>\n',-1,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8417,-8,5,0,'Pile Of Junk','<k>  This room is a virtual bum\'s paradise of collected garbage.  Pilfered\nbits of wood and steel, broken bottles, scrapped equipment, bones and paper,\ndirty torn cloth and many other sundry items have been stored here for\nsafekeeping.<1>\n',-1,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8418,-10,1,1,'Manager\'s Office','<k>  Not altogether large, the manager\'s office is quite well decorated\nwith plush furniture and outrageous pictures on the walls.  Like all the\nother rooms a hazy smoke lingers in the room with a pleasant smell\nwhich seems to cause you to feel light headed and slightly dizzy.  The\nonly exit to the room appears to be a small door to the north which leads\nto the bouncers lounge area.<1>\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(8419,-9,1,1,'Top of the Stairs','<k>  You are standing at the top of a small spiral staircase which\ndescends down to the abandoned Golden Treasure Casino.  The room you\nstand in is fairly bare and plain, a large sign is posted on the south\nwall.  Although the casino below has long since gone out of business,\nthe lounge to the north remains, albeit in a somewhat sleazier state.\nYou can hear a slow seductive music coming from the end of the hall\nbut the smoke and haze blocks out anything else.<1>\n',-1,393353,32,0,0,0,0,0,12,100,0,'',NULL),
(8420,-8,1,1,'A Small Gaming Room','<k>  A small table rest at the center of the room with several chairs\nsurrounding it.  The walls themselves are stained with blood and\nale from many fights which have started from unhappy gamblers.  A\nsingle door to the north leads to another gaming room and appears\nto be the only exit.<1>\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(8421,-10,2,1,'Bouncer\'s Lounge','<k>  Littered with moderately decent lounge furniture and a small table this\nis the room for the bouncers to take breaks in or hold private meetings.\nLike all the rooms of the lounge a hazy smoke lingers in the room giving\nyou a slight buzz.  A door to the north leads to the bar area and a small\ndoor to the south leads to the Manager\'s Office.<1>\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(8422,-9,2,1,'A Smoky Hallway','<k>  This small hallway is filled with a pleasant smelling smoke from the many\ndrugs the patrons of the lounge are offered.  The walls are fairly bare and\nthe floor is made of wood polished to a high gloss from the numerous patrons\nthat visit the lounge.  To the north of you lies the main room to the Golden\nTreasure Lounge and to the south of you is the staircase leading back down to\nthe abandoned Casino.<1>\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,12,100,0,'',NULL),
(8423,-8,2,1,'A Small Gaming Room','<k>  A small table rest at the center of the room with several chairs\nsurrounding it.  The walls themselves are stained with blood and\nale from many fights which have started from unhappy gamblers.  A\ndoor to the north leads to lounge while a door to the south leads to\nanother gaming room.<1>\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(8424,-10,3,1,'Behind the Bar','<k>  Shelves line the wall to the west and a rickety bar stands between you\nand the main room of the lounge.  The bar continues to the north while a\nsmall door to the south leads to the bouncers lounge area.<1>\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(8425,-9,3,1,'Main Room Next to the Bar','<k>  Tables and chairs are scattered across the floor while patrons are served\nwhatever is their pleasure by the bar maids.  A thick smoky haze lingers\nin the air of the room giving you a feeling of light headedness.  Slow\nseductive music is played by the minstrel on the stage and a woman dances for\nthe entertainment of certain guests.  A small hallway moves away from you to\nthe south and leads out of the lounge while a long bar runs to the west of\nyou and the room continues to the north and east.<1>\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(8426,-8,3,1,'Main Room','<k>  Tables and chairs are scattered across the floor while patrons are served\nwhatever is their pleasure by the bar maids.  A thick smoky haze lingers\nin the air of the room giving you a feeling of light headedness.  Slow\nseductive music is played by the minstrel on the stage and a woman dances for\nthe entertainment of certain guests.  A small door is to the south of you and\nthe room continues to the north and west.<1>\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(8427,-10,4,1,'Behind the Bar','<k>  Shelves line the wall to the west and a rickety bar stands between you\nand the main room of the lounge.  The bar continues to the south while a\nsmall opening in the bar to the east allows access to the main room.<1>\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(8428,-9,4,1,'Main Room Near to the Stage','<k>  Tables and chairs are scattered across the floor while patrons are served\nwhatever is their pleasure by the bar maids.  A thick smoky haze lingers\nin the air of the room giving you a feeling of light headedness.  Slow\nseductive music is played by the minstrel on the stage and a woman dances for\nthe entertainment of certain guests.  The stage is directly to the north of\nyou and the main room continues to the east and south.  The bar is to the west\nof you and a small opening through it allows access to behind the bar.<1>\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(8429,-8,4,1,'Main Room Near to the Stage','<k>  Tables and chairs are scattered across the floor while patrons are served\nwhatever is their pleasure by the bar maids.  A thick smoky haze lingers\nin the air of the room giving you a feeling of light headedness.  Slow\nseductive music is played by the minstrel on the stage and a woman dances for\nthe entertainment of certain guests.  The stage is directly to the north of\nyou and the main room continues to the west and south.<1>\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(8430,-9,5,1,'Stage of the Golden Treasure Lounge','<k>  A minstrel plays seductive music while a woman dances for the pleasure of\nthe audience.  Incense burners line the edge of the stage providing a smoky\nhaze to the room which induces a drugged state to encourage the patrons to\npurchase more drugs of some type.  The main room of the lounge is to the\nsouth and southeast while the stage extends farther to the east.<1>\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,14,100,0,'',NULL),
(8431,-8,5,1,'Stage of the Golden Treasure Lounge','<k>  A minstrel plays seductive music while a woman dances for the pleasure of\nthe audience.  Incense burners line the edge of the stage providing a smoky\nhaze to the room which induces a drugged state to encourage the patrons to\npurchase more drugs of some type.  The main room of the lounge is to the\nsouth and southwest while the stage extends farther to the west.  A small\ncurtain to the north of the stage leads to a dressing room for the dancers\nand bar maids.<1>\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,14,100,0,'',NULL),
(8432,-8,6,1,'Dressing Room','<k>  Tightly cramped this little room is used by the bar maids and the stage\ndancers to dress in.  Different seductive outfits hang from pegs on the\nwalls while a small stand holds perfumes and paints for the performers and\nbar maids.  A thin curtain to the south is all that separates this room\nfrom the lounge stage.<1>\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(8433,-9,1,-1,'Wide hallway','Before you looms a large hallway filled with luxurious furniture,\npolished and well kept. A chandelier, made only from the finest crystals this\nregion has to offer sparkles brightly off the mounted torches along the wall.\nThe constraints of the torches seem to be made out of carved ivory, it seems\nthe casino is doing very well by the looks of this room alone.  Dozens of\nportraits hang off the smooth white marble walls, each one has been specially\ndesigned with its own wooden frame.  A thin sheet of glass has been placed over\nthem for preservation.  A plush red carpet, as wide as the room itself leads down\nthe hallway where two sturdy doors can be seen.\n',-1,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8434,-9,2,-1,'Wide Hallway','   A large red carpet is seen here running in a northern-southern hallway.\nAn antique cherry wood table is here flush against the east wall dressed\nwith tiny brass trinkets.  Mounted wooden torches flicker off the marble\nwalls casting shadows around you.  Two very large doors stand here, one\nleads east and the other west.\n',53,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8435,-8,2,-1,'Accounting Office','  An oval shaped room built into small cells hold hundreds of coins and\ngold plated treasures which can only be viewed through a small opening in\nthe marble walls binded with thick iron bars.  Piled high on a flat desk lies\na small pile of talens.\n',53,131241,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8436,-10,1,-1,'Clerks Office','  This is a tiny office where much of the casino\'s transactions take\nplace.  A wooden counter, no more then three feet high contains two metallic\ncasings atop, each one on opposing ends reading IN-BOX and OUT-BOX.  A well\nrounded desk is placed just behind the counter piled with documents and\nother various files.  A wastebasket is filled with what looks like inked\nscrolls jeering out just above its rim.  Several proclamations are tacked\nto the walls, one is even signed by the King of Grimhaven himself.\n',53,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8437,-9,3,-1,'Wide Hallway','   A red carpet is seen here running in a northern-southern direction.  A\nfew antique tables and chairs have been placed here to admire.  A small brass\nplaque affixed to the eastern wall reads something in tiny lettering.  Mounted\ntorches flicker off the marble walls casting shadows around here causing you\nglance around the room as if someone was there watching you.\n',53,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8438,-8,3,-1,'Small Cell','   This cell hold many talens and various trinkets the good folks of\nGrimhaven have gambled away at the casino\'s tables.  A plaque is seen high\non the northern wall.\n',53,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(8439,-7,3,-1,'Small Cell','  The cells hold many talens and various junk items the casino took as\npayment from folks would couldn\'t pay their debts.  A small plaque is seen here\non the eastern wall.\n',53,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(8440,-7,2,-1,'Small Cell','   A small cell holds special pieces of weapons and armor that price well\non the market.  These items get shipped back to the armour for a fixed price\nat a higher cost and made to profit the casino.\n',53,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(8441,-8,1,-1,'Small Cell','   Warm furs and the like are seen here hung on shelves and racks.  The casino\nprofits not only from the poor but the rich as well.\n',53,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(8442,-10,2,-1,'Storage Room',' The room appears to be a storage space for the casino\'s machinery.  Large\nmetallic type components litter the floor by a dusty toolshed.  Five slots\nmachines sit on a workmens bench, aged and damaged.  Only a single machine\nwhich looks intact sits along the western wall.  It glints a brassy shine off\nthe mounted torches that flicker from a small breeze entering the room.\n',53,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8443,-9,4,-1,'Wide Hallway','  A plush red carpet, as wide as the room itself is seen here running in a\nnorthern-southern direction.  Torches waver slightly from a small gust of wind\nthat wanders in from the south casting shadows off the marble walls.  This room\nwould be empty if not for a hard wooden bench that sits along the eastern wall.\n',54,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8444,-10,3,-1,'Interrogation Room','  This square shaped room is very pleasent.  The potted vegetation\nthat surrounds you makes you feel right at home despite the wanted signs\nthat have been tacked to the walls.  Two large ferns dangle off the ceiling\nover a metal desk thats piled with inked scrolls and documents on seedy\nindividuals that enter the casino.  A portrait hangs off the west wall\nwhere a lock cell can be seen leading north.\n',54,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8445,-10,4,-1,'Cramped Cell','   A small cell well kept is here used for holding criminals till the city\'s\nofficials can take over.  A large bed sits flushed against the north wall\ndressed in cotten linen.  Fresh lettering can be seen on the wall.\n',54,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8446,-9,5,-1,'Hallways End','  The hallway ends here before a massive door made from cast iron.  The\nroom is spotless, not a single drop of dust can be seen on the antique\nfurnishings that have been carefully placed.  Mounted high above the northern\nwall is a very large portrait of the casino\'s owner.  Its gold frame takes up\nmuch of the wall and probably weighs just as much as it looks.  Two oversized\nbronze vases sit on either side of the door filled with foxfire dyed in a\nhaze of purple.\n',54,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8447,-8,5,-1,'Owner\'s Suite','A large decorative chamber stands before you to which you cannot\nbelieve.  The room itself is like some great lost treasure filled with\nobjects of great wealth glittering all around you.  Your heart swells\nwith greed as you spot a chestnut vanity overloaded with sweet smelling\nperfumes, diamond studded jewels and large onyx-rings.  This is immense!\nIts elven crafted woodframe made from solid oak insets an oversized fur\nmattress.  Centering the room is a stained glass table adorned with brass-\nsilvery trinkets.  A nightstand harbors a few tattered books, probably\nantiques too, that lie near a small round crystal sphere.  Red tapestries,\nmade from fine silk drape the walls that circle the rooms interior.\n',0,131241,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8448,-8,4,-1,'Guest Room','   A small but well placed room showered in luxurious bedeck surrounds you.\nThis room was made to entertain guest of the casino\'s owner.  A small round table\nfit to seat two stands besides a woodframed bed.  Foxfire can be seen within a\nlarge bronze vase along the rear wall near a comfortable couch.\n',54,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8449,-7,4,-1,'Stall Room','   A bathroom is here carved from marble.  A stonewash basin sits atop a\ncounter filled with clear liquid by a small woven basket of soap.  A bronze\nchain dangles off a wooden bucket in the north corner of the room used for\nshowering.\n',54,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8450,-7,5,-1,'Dining Room','  Several pillars of white marble can be seen here forming a rectangle in\nthis great hall.  Glancing upwards to where the pillars touch the ceiling you see\nsomeone has made a painstaking task of painting an awesome replica of a dense\nforest.  Four armored statues, placed in separate corners of the room each\nface a large wooden table that is centered in the room.  This chamber was made\nto hold conferences with regard to renovations to the casino at first, now\npolitical debates and other official matters are held here.\n',54,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8500,52,-38,0,'A Small Hill','Standing atop this hill, the view of the surrounding land is somewhat\nbreathtaking.  As far as the eye can see, rolling grassland spreads out before\nyou.  Interspersed with the field of greens and the light yellow of sun-dried\ngrass, you can make out the occasional copse of trees and a slight\nswell of a hill far off in the distance.  Much closer however are hills to\nboth the east and south as well as a copse of trees nearby to the southeast.\n',50,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8501,53,-38,0,'A Small Hill','Standing atop this hill, the view of the surrounding land is somewhat\nbreathtaking.  As far as the eye can see, rolling grassland spreads out before\nyou.  Interspersed with the field of greens and the light yellow of sun-dried\ngrass, you can make out the occasional copse of trees and a slight\nswell of a hill far off in the distance.  Much closer however are hills to\nthe west and southwest as well as a small copse of trees directly to the\nsouth.\n',50,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8502,54,-38,0,'Veldt','As far as the eye can see, rolling grassland spreads out before you.\nInterspersed with the field of greens and the light yellow of sun-dried\ngrass, you can make out the occasional copse of trees and a slight\nswell of a hill far off in the distance.\n',50,131072,42,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8503,55,-38,0,'Veldt','As far as the eye can see, rolling grassland spreads out before you.\nInterspersed with the field of greens and the light yellow of sun-dried\ngrass, you can make out the occasional copse of trees and a slight\nswell of a hill far off in the distance.\n',50,131072,42,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8504,56,-38,0,'A Watering Hole','The blue of the water is a shocking contrast to the perpetual field of\nyellow that is the sprawling expanse of savannah around you.  This small\npool of water is surrounded by a muddy ring, clear evidence that many\nbeasts - both predator and prey - use this watering hole for sustenance.\n',50,131072,42,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8505,57,-38,0,'Veldt','As far as the eye can see, rolling grassland spreads out before you.\nInterspersed with the field of greens and the light yellow of sun-dried\ngrass, you can make out the occasional copse of trees and a slight\nswell of a hill far off in the distance.\n',50,131072,42,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
