(8512,64,-38,0,'A Grassy Gulch','This gully resembles a gentle depression in the ground more than any\ngorge or ravine.  Dried grass is everywhere, creating a field of yellow\nas far as they eye can see -- which is not too far considering where\nyou are standing.  The gully continues on to the southwest.\n',50,131072,42,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8513,65,-38,0,'Veldt','As far as the eye can see, rolling grassland spreads out before you.\nInterspersed with the field of greens and the light yellow of sun-dried\ngrass, you can make out the occasional copse of trees and a slight\nswell of a hill far off in the distance.\n',50,131072,42,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8514,66,-38,0,'A Small Hut','This small, pitiful hovel of a hut seems to be constructed mainly of\nsticks and grass held together by a generous slathering of dried mud.\nThe floor of this domicile is littered with small, inconsequential\nliving things and the occasional piece of feces.  A flimsy \'door\' rests\nin the east \'wall\' of the hut.\n',50,131081,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,84,0,'',NULL),
(8515,67,-38,0,'A Small Clearing','The rolling land of the veldt is interrupted by this small clearing.\nAnimal footprints and feces dot the dirt about your feet, clear evidence\nof the presence of wildlife.  Two miserable looking thatched huts \'stand\'\nnearby - one to the south and the other to the west.\n',50,131073,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8516,68,-38,0,'Veldt','As far as the eye can see, rolling grassland spreads out before you.\nInterspersed with the field of greens and the light yellow of sun-dried\ngrass, you can make out the occasional copse of trees and a slight\nswell of a hill far off in the distance.\n',50,131072,42,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8517,52,-39,0,'Cave Opening','Half-hidden amongst the surrounding hills and sparse treeline, a small\ncavity can be seen in the ground.  From the looks of it, the aperture\nappears to extend deeper down into the earth.\n',50,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8518,53,-39,0,'Copse of Trees','Stark contrast to the rolling plains of the veldt, this cluster of trees\nstands out against the horizon and provides cool shade for wandering\nbeasts who wish to get out of the scorching sun.  Gnarled and twisted roots\nextend everywhere around you, evidence that the animals are not the only\nlife on the savannah that struggles to eke out whatever sustenance it can\nfrom the earth.  A set of low, rolling hills lie to the north and west\nwhile a dark fissure in the ground can be spotted nearby to the west as well.\n',50,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8519,54,-39,0,'Veldt','As far as the eye can see, rolling grassland spreads out before you.\nInterspersed with the field of greens and the light yellow of sun-dried\ngrass, you can make out the occasional copse of trees and a slight\nswell of a hill far off in the distance.\n',50,131072,42,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
