(8557,58,-41,0,'A Dirt Trail on the Veldt','This is a small dirt road somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof veldt you find yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this rather\nunassuming path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A soft wind sweeps\nacross the savannah, bringing the faint odor of dried grass to your nostrils.\nA lake lies sprawled out nearby to the southeast and a small copse of trees\nis to the northwest.  The trail continues on to the southwest and northeast,\nwhile you can makeout what appears to be a large mass of stones to the south.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8558,59,-41,0,'Veldt','As far as the eye can see, rolling grassland spreads out before you.\nInterspersed with the field of greens and the light yellow of sun-dried\ngrass, you can make out the occasional copse of trees and a slight\nswell of a hill far off in the distance.\n',50,131072,42,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8559,60,-41,0,'A Dirt Trail by the Lake','This is a small dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof veldt you find yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this\nrather unremarkable path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A soft wind\nsweeps across the savannah, bringing the faint odor of dried grass to your\nnostrils.  What looks to be a lake lies spread out to the south and the\ntrail continues onward to the east and northwest.  In the distance, you can make\nout what seems to be a jumble of rocks to the southwest.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8560,61,-41,0,'A Dirt Trail by the Lake','This is a small dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof savannah you find yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this\nrather unremarkable path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A soft wind\nsweeps across the veldt, bringing the faint odor of dried grass to your\nnostrils.  A set of low, rolling hills can be made out far to your east while\nwhat appears to be a lake spreads out to your south.  A gully extends off into\nthe distance to your north and the trail continues on to your east and west.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8561,62,-41,0,'A Dirt Trail on the Veldt','This is a small dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof veldt you find yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this\nrather unremarkable path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A soft wind\nsweeps across the savannah, bringing the faint odor of dried grass to your\nnostrils.  A set of low, rolling hills can be seen a bit distant in the\nsoutheast while you can barely make out what appears to be a mass of water\nto your southwest.  The dirt path continues onward to the west and east.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8562,63,-41,0,'A Dirt Trail on the Veldt','This is a small winding dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling\nexpanse of plains you find yourself in.  Dirt and a few loose rocks mark this\nrather unremarkable path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A soft wind\nsweeps across the veldt, bringing the faint odor of dried grass to your\nnostrils.  A set of low, rolling hills can be seen not too far off to the\neast and southeast, and the dirt path ambles on to the east and west.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8563,64,-41,0,'A Trail Amongst the Hills','This is a small winding dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling\nexpanse of plains.  Dirt and a few loose stones mark this rather unremarkable\npath as it leads off into the grasslands.  A soft wind sweeps across the\nsurrounding savannah, bringing the faint odor of dried grass to your\nnostrils.  Low, rolling hills can be seen nearby to the south and east,\nwhile the path ambles onward to the southeast and west.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8564,65,-41,0,'Hills','Standing atop this hill, the view of the surrounding land is somewhat\nbreathtaking.  Off in the distance you can make out a patch of trees or two\nas well as what appears to be water speckling the grasslands.  Somewhat\ncloser is a winding dirt trail to the west and what appears to be a thatched\nhut or two off to the northeast.\n',50,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
