(8587,54,-43,0,'Copse of Trees','Stark contrast to the rolling plains of the veldt, this cluster of trees\nstands out against the horizon and provides cool shade for wandering\nbeasts who wish to get out of the scorching sun.  Gnarled and twisted roots\nextend everywhere around you, evidence that the animals are not the only\nlife on the savannah that struggles to eke out whatever sustenance it can\nfrom the earth.  A jagged line of stones can be seen not too far off to\nthe east.\n',50,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8588,55,-43,0,'Veldt','As far as the eye can see, rolling grassland spreads out before you.\nInterspersed with the field of greens and the light yellow of sun-dried\ngrass, you can make out the occasional copse of trees and a slight\nswell of a hill far off in the distance.\n',50,131072,42,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8589,56,-43,0,'A Dirt Trail by the Ruins','This is a small dirt path somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof veldt you find yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this rather\nunassuming path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A soft wind sweeps\nacross the savannah, bringing the faint aroma of dried grass to your\nnostrils.  A small copse of trees can be seen nearby to the west while the\ntrail winds both northeast and south.  A jagged wall of crumbled stones\nblocks passage to the east.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8590,57,-43,0,'Northwest Corner of Ruins','You stand amidst the rubble of what apparently used to be a tower of\nwhatever structure this complex of jumbled masonry used to be.  The cause\nof this tower\'s eventual demise was most probably the ravages of time\nand the elements.  What remains of a crumbled stone wall blocks passage to\nthe north and west.\n',50,131072,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8591,58,-43,0,'A Clearing in the Rubble','Standing in the middle of an open space cleared of debris, the contrast\nbetween this and the rest of the complex of ruins is readily noticeable.\nGone is the chaotic jumble of stones, twisted metal and rotten wood.  In its\nplace is a relatively smooth surface borders by neat piles of debris on\nall sides.  You note that smack dab in the middle of the clearing is a\nneatly arranged pile of rubble in the shape of a circle.\n',50,131072,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8592,59,-43,0,'A Shimmering Lake','Deep blue water surrounds you on all sides as you wade into the lake.  So\ncrystalline is the liquid that you can make out the lake bottom and the\ngreen plantlife that flourishes underwater.  As a soft underwater current\ngently shifts, you make out what appears to be bones on the lake floor....\n',50,131072,51,0,0,0,0,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
