(8607,57,-44,0,'A Collapsed Wall','You stand atop the rubble of a crumbled section of wall.  A few portions of\nthe wall remain standing, but for the most part the ramparts appear to have\nbeen torn down my the ravishes of Father Time over the ages.  A quick glance\naround reveals the same devastating effects of time as the crumbled ruins\nsprawl out before you on most sides.\n',50,131072,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8608,58,-44,0,'A Clearing in the Rubble','Standing in the middle of an open space cleared of debris, the contrast\nbetween this and the rest of the complex of ruins is readily noticeable.\nGone is the chaotic jumble of stones, twisted metal and rotten wood.  In its\nplace is a relatively smooth surface borders by neat piles of debris on\nall sides.\n',50,131072,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8609,59,-44,0,'A Jagged Pile of Stones','As you survey your immediate surroundings, the unnatural arrangement\nof the debris in this section of the ruins piques your interest.  Unlike\nmost of the rest of the ruins, the rubble here is arranged in an oddly\nordered pile of stones.  The formation appears to be a pyramid, the fallen\nmasonry arranged with a decent modicum of precision - for what purpose you\ncannot seem to discern.  What remains of a stone wall obstructs passage\nto the north and east.\n',50,131072,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
