(8641,57,-46,0,'Entrance to the Ruins','The rolling grasslands of the veldt come to an abrupt halt here.  Crumbled\nruins extend to the northeast, quite a contrast from the teeming life\nand fresh atmosphere of the savannah.  Jumbled stones litter the ground,\nthe jagged edges of the cracked masonry smoothed now after years of\nerosion.  Upon surveying the surrounding area, it looks like a path can\nbe picked through the rubble to the northeast to go further into the\ncrushed and broken rubble.\n',50,131076,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8642,58,-46,0,'Amidst a Sea of Rubble','Strewn all about is a sea of rubble.  Making movement difficult, the\nsheer amount of miscellaneous evidence of architecture in a state of\nruin is quite astounding in itself.  Mixed in with crumbled masonry\nand dirt, you can make out the occasional bit of rotted wood and\ntwisted metal.  What remains of a stone wall blocks passage to the\nsouth and west.\n',50,131072,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8643,59,-46,0,'A Jumbled Mass of Stones','An unnatural formation greets your eye as you survey the surroundings.\nUnlike other parts of this ruined complex, the rubble here is arranged\nin a strangely ordered jumble of stones.  Resembling roughly an\nequilateral triangle, the fallen masonry has been arranged most carefully -\nfor what purpose you cannot seem to discern.  What remains of a stone\nwall obstructs passage to the east and south.\n',50,131072,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
