(8674,64,-48,0,'A Grassy Hill','Standing atop this hill, the view of the surrounding land is somewhat\nbreathtaking.  As far as the eye can see, rolling grassland spreads out before\nyou.  Interspersed with the field of greens and the light yellow of sun-dried\ngrass, you can make out the occasional copse of trees and a slight\nswell of a hill far off in the distance.\n',50,131072,42,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8675,52,-39,-1,'Inside the Cave Mouth','Smooth walls of rock form the walls of this cave, timeworn and ancient.\nThe floor seems as level as the walls are smooth, perhaps the effect\nof countless years of treading feet.  This cavern appears to be\ninhabited, seeing as there are random signs of habitation lying about.\nFaint etchings can be made out on some of the cave walls, interrupted\nonly by the presence of tunnels leading off in other direcitons.\n',50,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,105,0,'',NULL),
(8676,52,-38,-1,'A Small Cave','You are now in what appears to be more a oversized recess than what\ncould be termed a cave.  The walls and ceiling of rock are separated\nonly by a few lengths and the space inbetween is quite cramped.  A strong\nodor seems to be emanating from a dark but shallow hole in the\nnorthwest corner of the chamber.\n',50,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,5,90,0,'',NULL),
(8677,51,-40,-1,'A Narrow Fissure','Darkness surrounds you on all sides, as the walls of this fissure\nprovide passage deeper into this network of caves.  Rifts in the rock\nallow for passage at both ends of this tunnel.\n',50,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,3,95,0,'',NULL),
(8678,53,-40,-1,'A Large Cave','This cavern seems larger than the grotto to the northwest.  The floor is\nequally as smoothed out as well, lending credence to the thought that\nthis network of caves has been inhabited for quite some time.  Faint\netchings can be made out on some of the cave walls.\n',50,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8679,50,-40,-1,'A Cavernous Chamber','Surrounded on all sides by rock, this chamber\'s vast size borders on\nwhat would be considered awe-inspiring.  Even though underground, the\nsheer spaciousness of the cave makes you think for a minute that you\nare out in the open air of the surface world.  A wafting smell of rancid\nodors quickly dispels any such thoughts.  A gaping fissure in the\neast wall of this chamber appears to be the only egress from here.\n',50,139272,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,135,0,'',NULL),
(8680,58,-43,-1,'A Dark Shaft','Darkness surrounds you on all sides as the walls of this narrow vertical\ntunnel seem to almost creep in on you.  Hand and footholds in the dark\ngranite allow you to carefully make your way through here.  Some loose\nrubble can be seen overhead while more darkness beckons you from\nbelow.\n',50,173068,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(8681,58,-43,-2,'Bottom of a Dark Shaft','You are at the bottom of what appears to be a narrow shaft leading\nupwards.  There is substantially more room in here than above, room\nenough for several beings to actually walk around without difficulty.\nA fine layer of dust blankets the floor, ample evidence of the rather\nundisturbed nature of this chamber.  A set of titanium doors rests\nin the southern wall.\n',50,173068,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,105,0,'',NULL),
(8682,58,-44,-2,'An Ancient Burial Crypt','As you look about you, you cannot help but marvel at the morbid beauty\nof this crypt.  Carved in sharp relief on every possible surface of this\nchamber are gargoyles, devils and demons all doing unspeakable acts to\nhapless humanoids.  Not much else adorns this room besides the sculpted\nwalls except for a single faded tapestry on the east wall.\n',50,173068,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,105,0,'',NULL),
(8683,59,-44,-2,'Treasure Room','Small and nondescript, this room would catch nary a second glance if\nnot for its contents.  As you search about for baubles of value, you notice\nthe slight aroma of brine coming from the direction of a shimmering\nred light in the eastern wall.\n',50,173069,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,105,0,'',NULL),
(8684,69,-44,0,'A Small Dirt Trail','This is a small dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof savannah you find yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this\nrather unassuming path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A gentle wind\nsweeps across the veldt, bringing the faint odor of dried grass to your\nnostrils.  The trail continues on to the northeast and west.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8685,70,-43,0,'A Small Dirt Trail','This is a small dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof savannah you find yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this\nrather unassuming path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A gentle wind\nsweeps across the veldt, bringing the faint odor of dried grass to your\nnostrils.  The trail ambles on to the north and southwest.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8686,70,-42,0,'A Small Dirt Trail','This is a small dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof savannah you find yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this\nrather unassuming path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A gentle wind\nsweeps across the veldt, bringing the faint odor of dried grass to your\nnostrils.  The trail extends further to the north and south.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8687,70,-41,0,'A Small Dirt Trail','This is a small dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof savannah you find yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this\nrather unassuming path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A gentle wind\nsweeps across the veldt, bringing the faint odor of dried grass to your\nnostrils.  The trail winds northeast and continues on to the south.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8688,71,-40,0,'A Small Dirt Trail','This is a small dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof veldt you find  yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this rather\nunremarkable path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A soft wind sweeps\nacross the plains, bringing the faint aroma of dried grass to your nose.\nThe trail continues on to the north and southwest.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8689,71,-39,0,'A Small Dirt Trail','This is a small dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof veldt you find  yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this rather\nunremarkable path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A soft wind sweeps\nacross the plains, bringing the faint aroma of dried grass to your nostrils.\nThe trail ambles onwards to the north and south.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8690,71,-38,0,'A Small Dirt Trail','This is a small dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof veldt you find  yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this rather\nunremarkable path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A soft wind sweeps\nacross the plains, bringing the faint aroma of dried grass to your nostrils.\nThe trail ambles onwards to the north and south.\n',50,131076,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8691,71,-37,0,'A Small Dirt Trail','This is a small dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof veldt you find  yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this rather\nunremarkable path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A soft wind sweeps\nacross the plains, bringing the faint aroma of dried grass to your nostrils.\nThe trail ambles onwards to the north and south.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8692,71,-36,0,'A Small Dirt Trail','This is a small dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof veldt you find  yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this rather\nunremarkable path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A soft wind sweeps\nacross the plains, bringing the faint aroma of dried grass to your nostrils.\nThe trail ambles onwards to the north and south.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8693,71,-35,0,'A Small Dirt Trail','This is a small dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof veldt you find  yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this rather\nunremarkable path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A soft wind sweeps\nacross the plains, bringing the faint aroma of dried grass to your nostrils.\nThe trail continues off to the northwest and south.\n',50,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8694,70,-34,0,'A Small Dirt Trail','This is a small dirt trail somewhere in the midst of the sprawling expanse\nof veldt you find  yourself in.  Loose dirt and a few stones mark this rather\nunremarkable path as it leads off into the grasslands.  A soft wind sweeps\nacross the plains, bringing the faint aroma of dried grass to your nostrils.\n',50,131076,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8700,38,66,-3,'North End of the Garden','  A blackened wrought-iron gate leads to <o>Amber Castle<z> to the north.\nThick <g>bushes<z> flank the path here, which leads south into the center\nof the gardens.  South of the garden you can also see the high walls of\nthe <o>hospital<z>.\n',56,131072,16,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8701,37,65,-3,'Northwest Corner of the Gardens','  A short, wide <g>tree<z> grows here with a <r>red<z>,<r> spiny fruit<z> hanging from it.\nAround the base of the tree are several <o>orange flowers<z> with black centers.\nThe grassy ground leads south, southeast, or east from here -- where you\nspot a beautiful marble fountain.\n',56,131072,16,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8702,38,65,-3,'The Royal Botanical Gardens','  This is the center of the garden.  While there are not as many trees or\nflowers here, you have a good view of what is in the gardens overall.  To the\nnorth is the edge of the gardens, and a gate leads to <o>Amber Castle<z> north of\nthat.  You can go in any direction except northwest or northeast, where there\nis a fence bordering the gardens.\n',56,131072,16,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8703,39,65,-3,'Northeast Corner of the Gardens','  Several tiny, yet colorful, <r>flowers<z> line the fence here.  A <p>chipmunk<z> runs\naround near the fence gathering <d>berries and nuts<z> fallen from the trees.  To\nthe north you can see Amber Castle through the trees.  You can go west, south,\nor southwest into other parts of the garden.\n',56,131072,16,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8704,37,64,-3,'Western Entrance to the Gardens','  The gardens stretch to the east, north, and northeast, and a <d>gate<z> opens to\nthe south onto a small stone path.  Glorious <G>trees and strange flowers<z> bloom\nhere, unlike anywhere else in the realms.  The flora here is able to exist\ndespite the year round cold temperatures.\n',56,131072,16,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8705,38,64,-3,'The Royal Botanical Gardens','  Several interesting <b>bushes<z> are here <b>with small, bright blue flowers<z>.  They\nhave been trimmed and pruned well and seem to be thriving despite the cold\ntemperatures.  The grass leads in any direction except to the south, where\na fence borders a stone path.\n',56,131072,16,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8706,39,64,-3,'Eastern Entrance to the Gardens','  The gardens stretch to the west, north, and northwest, and a gate opens to\nyour south onto a small stone path.  Glorious <G>trees and strange flowers<z> bloom\nhere, unlike anywhere else in the realms.  The flora here is able to exist\ndespite the year round cold temperatures.\n',56,131072,16,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8707,36,63,-3,'Stone Road by the North Tower','  This is a simple stone road that runs alongside the <o>hospital<z>, which stands\nto the southeast.  To the east, on the north side of the path, you can see an\nentrance to the <G>Royal Botanical Gardens<z>.  There is a staircase here leading\nup onto the town walls.  The road also leads south.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8708,37,63,-3,'Stone Road by the Hospital','  This is a simple stone road that runs alongside the <o>hospital<z>, which stands\nto the south.  A gate to the north leads into the impressive <G>Royal Botanical\nGardens<z>, and the path runs west and east.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8709,38,63,-3,'Stone Road by the Hospital','  This is a simple stone road that runs alongside the <o>hospital<z>, which stands\nto the south.  To the east and west, on the north side of the road, you can\nsee entrances to the <G>Royal Botanical Gardens<z>.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8710,39,63,-3,'Stone Road by the Hospital','  This is a simple stone road that runs alongside the <o>hospital<z>, which stands\nto the south.  A gate to the north leads into the impressive <G>Royal Botanical\nGardens<z>, and the path runs west and east.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8711,40,63,-3,'Stone Road by the Hospital','  This is a simple stone road that runs alongside the <o>hospital<z>, which stands\nto the southwest.  You can see the docks through a fence to the southeast.\nThe road leads south, or to the west where you can see the Royal Botanical\nGardens.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8712,41,63,-3,'Travel Office','  On a table in the center of the room are several brochures with paintings\nof warmer places on them.  The walls also have <d>paintings<z> of warm beaches and\nthe jungles far off to the southwest of this town.  There are also some faux\n<c>blueprints<z> of the various traveling ships that come through Amber\'s port.\n',56,139273,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8713,42,63,-3,'Amber Shipping Office','  This building houses the main office of Cobra Shipping Ltd., the\nlargest organized shipping firm in all the realms.  The shipping\noffice is in a state of constant turmoil, with people coming and\ngoing at all hours of the day or night, both to drop off things for\nshipment to another city or to pick up merchandise which arrived on\nthe latest caravan.  The room itself is tastefully done in light\n<o>wood paneling<z>, with a hard oak floor.  A large counter in the center\nof the room serves as a drop off and pick up point for merchandise.\nA door south leads onto the boardwalk, and a tiny bell rings each\ntime a customer enters or exits.\n',56,139273,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8714,36,62,-3,'Stone Road by the Hospital','  This is a simple stone road that runs alongside the <o>hospital<z>, which stands\nto the east.  To the north you see a staircase that must lead up to the town\nwalls.  The path also runs south.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8715,40,62,-3,'Stone Road by the Docks','This is a simple stone road that runs alongside the <o>hospital<z>, which stands\nto the west.  There is a small entrance to the dock shop area to the east,\nnoted by a wooden sign with <r>Amber Boardwalk<z> painted on it in red letters.\nThis road runs north and south.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8716,41,62,-3,'North End of the Docks','The wooden planks of the boardwalk lead east to a shop at the end of the\npier or south to where the boat docks are.  There is a small exit to a stone\nroad to the west, and a travel store to the north.  During the day there\nare huge numbers of people milling around, and even the evening invites\nseveral people, though generally of a more rowdy nature.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8717,42,62,-3,'North End of the Docks','  This is the end of the north part of the docks.  The boardwalk continues\nwest, and the frigid ocean water is east.  There is a door to the north\nleading to a shipping office.  A sign above the door proclaims that it is\nCobra Shipping Limited, the largest shipping outfit in the realms.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8718,33,61,-1,'Attallal Boulevard by the Northwest Tower','  The white <c>moonstone tiles<z> here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in reality.\nThere is a staircase here that leads up onto the town walls.  The road leads\nsouth or east.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8719,34,61,-1,'Attallal Boulevard','  The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in reality.\nJust south of here is a store that sells spell components.  The road leads\neast or west where you can see a staircase leading to the town walls.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8720,35,61,-3,'Attallal Boulevard','  The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in reality.\nJust south of here is the weaponer.  To the east you see a massive <o>hospital<z>\ncomplex.  The road leads west, or east where it changes to the stone blocks\nof Cascade Avenue.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8721,36,61,-3,'North Cascade Avenue','  The slate slabs that compose the road here are spaced so that a\ntemperature change will not crack or deform them.  On the east side of the\npath a side entrance to the <o>hospital<z> invites sick or wounded citizens.  To\nthe north a simple stone path leads around the <o>hospital<z>, and to the south\nyou can see Cascade Plaza off a short distance.  The <c>moonstone<z> tiles of\nAttallal Boulevard are visible to the west, where the road leads around\ntown along the tall granite walls.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8722,40,61,-3,'Stone Road by the Docks','  This is a simple stone road that runs alongside the <o>hospital<z>, which stands\nto the west.  Through a fence to the east you can see the docks.  The road\nruns south or north.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8723,41,61,-3,'The Docks','The wooden planks of the boardwalk run north and south.  To the north you\ncan see a few stores at the end of the dock, and to the south you can see\nseveral ships that have come in to port.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8724,42,61,-3,'The Deck of a Merchant Ship','  This ship is flying faded <d>white sails<z> with a <R>red cross<z> marking it.  It\nsways slightly with the waves, but it is not overwhelming.  A small bridge\nleads off the stern to the south, or you might walk to the bow of the ship\nto the east.  A hatch leads down into the boat.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8725,43,61,-3,'The Deck of a Merchant Ship','  This ship is flying faded <d>white sails<z> with a <R>red cross<z> marking it.  It\nsways slightly with the waves, but it is not overwhelming.  Some ropes\ncreak as they strain to keep the masts in line.  The stern is to the west\nof here.  Off the bow of the ship you see the frigid ocean.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8726,33,60,-1,'Attallal Boulevard','  The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in\nreality.  Just east of you is a store that sells spell components.  The\nroad runs south and north, where you can see a staircase that must lead\nup onto the town walls.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8727,34,60,-1,'Shemaesin\'s Components','  Shelves throughout the store are filled with jars and bags of\ninteresting items for use in magical spells.  You do not dare touch any\nof these items without the intent to purchase, as the owner of the store\nhas wards protecting his merchandise.  A row of <c>glowing blue spheres<z>\nrotate around the ceiling, which casts an eerie light throughout the\nstore.\n',56,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8728,35,60,-3,'Lebanull\'s Weapons','  The owner of this store is obviously very interested in implements of\ndeath.  Several twisted, ancient looking <d>weapons are on display here<z>.\nThe weapons seem to be of the highest quality, and you are sure that\nLebanull will value his merchandise appropriately.\n',56,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8729,36,60,-3,'North Cascade Avenue','  The road here is made of shale slabs spaced so that they will not crack\nif there is a temperature change.  The tall walls of the <o>hospital<z> border\nthe road on the east side.  To the west is the weaponer.  The path leads\nnorth and south, where you can see Cascade Plaza nearby.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8730,40,60,-3,'Stone Road by the Docks','This is a simple stone road that runs alongside the <o>hospital<z>, which\nstands to the west.  Through a fence to the east you can see the docks.\nJust south of here is the grand main entrance to the docks, and the path\nalso continues north around the <o>hospital<z>.  A cold wind is channelled\nbetween the dock wall on one side and the <o>hospital<z> wall on the other\nside, and you are forced to wrap your clothing tighter around you.\n',0,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8731,41,60,-3,'The Docks','The wooden planks of the boardwalk lead north and south, or to the east\nwhere a ship is docked.  To the south is the main entrance of the docks,\nand also several more ships.\n',0,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8732,42,60,-3,'A Boarding Dock','  A <o>sign<z> next to a small bridge leading out to a docked ship states that\nthis is boarding dock one.  The boardwalk leads west towards the town, or\nyou could follow the bridge out to the merchant ship docked there.\n',56,139264,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8733,33,59,-1,'Attallal Boulevard','  The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in\nreality.  Just east of here is a commodity store.  The road leads north\nor south, where you can make out the western town gates.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8734,34,59,-1,'T\'agn Commodity Exchange','  Crates of commodities are piled behind the main desk of this store.\nSeveral non-valuable metals are strewn about the room waiting to be packaged.\nEvery day a flux of commodities is brought through here by merchant sailors.\n',56,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8735,35,59,-3,'Omniman\'s Armors','  This is a well stocked store, <y>specializing in harder armors<z> rather than\nthe <d>clothing and<z> which is <d>dealt with upstairs<z>.  All of the wares\nhere are well oiled and polished to seem as enticing as possible to\ncustomers.  A large scimitar is held to the back wall by metal braces --\nit looks intimidating but on closer examination you see that it is rather\nflimsy and obviously just for decoration.  On it, in blue, is engraved:\n<b>Omniman\'s<z>.  An exit east leads into the streets of the town.\n',56,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8736,36,59,-3,'North Cascade Avenue','  You are just north of Cascade Plaza.  The road here is made of slate\nslabs spaced so that they will not crack if there is a temperature change.\nThe tall walls of the <o>hospital<z> rise to the northeast.  East of you is a\nrepair shop, and to the west is a two story building that sells armor and\nclothing.  The road also leads north.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8737,37,59,-3,'Amber Repair Company','  There is a huge grinding whetstone here, as well as several very large\nfiles used to keep any type of weapon in maximum possible shape.  A hammer\nand <y>fire<z> are on one side of the room to beat metal into shape, and you see\na table with a sewing kit for cloth items.  Downstairs is the sharpener\'s\nshop, and to the west is Attallal Boulevard.\n',56,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8738,38,59,-3,'Before the Amber Memorial Hospital','  This is the large entrance to <d>Amber Memorial<z>.  You are awed by the sheer\nsize of this building.  Surely, this is the largest <o>hospital<z> the realms have\never seen, and it must provide superior medical care for those in need.  To\nthe south is Frost Way, and a glass door leads north into the <o>hospital<z>.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8739,39,59,-3,'The Complete Sailor','  Model <c>boats<z> rest on shelves around the room, and an assortment of ropes,\nhooks, anchors, and other sailing materials are strewn about.  A counter\non the west side of the shop has a small <g>abacus<z> on it to calculate\ntransactions.\n',56,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8740,40,59,-3,'Main Entrance to the Docks','This area is generally bustling with activity as merchants load and\nunload ships and bring their goods to and from town.  The road leads\nnorth and south.  To the west is a boat shop, which supplies the ships\nthat you can see docked east of here.  A massive <o>hospital<z> rises above\nthe other buildings of the town, and it is to the northwest of here.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8741,41,59,-3,'The Docks','This is a busy area of the docks, as the main entrance is to the west\nof here.  The salty sea breeze makes your hair sticky and you wrap your\nclothes tighter to fend of the chilly wind.  Merchants, dock workers,\nand rogues carry their goods up and down the docks and into the town,\nwhich is to the west.  The planks of the boardwalk run north and south.\nSeveral ships are docked, and they rock in time with the soothing crash\nof waves.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8742,42,59,-3,'On the Deck of a Small Ship','Due to the small size of this ship, the waves have a great effect on\nthe stability of the decks.  You sway around and several sailpoles swing\ntoo much for comfort.  The deck continues east to the bow, and there is\na hatch in the floor here that leads into the ship.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8743,43,59,-3,'On the Deck of a Small Ship','  Due to the small size of this ship, the waves have a greater effect on\nthe stability of the decks.  You sway around and several sailpoles swing\ntoo much for comfort.  The deck continues west to the stern.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8744,33,58,-1,'The Western Town Gates','  The impressive black steel gates of the town loom over you to the west.\nEast of here runs Frost Way, with its lavish <b>blue tiles<z>, and north and\nsouth is Attallal Boulevard, which runs around the perimeter of the western\nhalf of town.  The road here, and all along Attallal Boulevard, is made of\na <c>white moonstone<z> with a bluish sheen.  The colors of the roads make\neverything seem very ethereal and dreamlike.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8745,34,58,-1,'Western Frost Way','  This road is paved with <b>lapis lazuli<z> and runs from the west town gates\nto the docks on the east side of town.  You marvel at the beauty of the\ntiles and can hardly believe that anyone would spend the time to cut this\nbeautiful blue stone and use it for a road.  To the south is a restaurant,\nwith a bar on the second floor.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8746,35,58,-3,'Western Frost Way','  This road is paved with <b>lapis lazuli<z> and runs from the west town gates\nto the docks on the east side of town.  You marvel at the beauty of the\ntiles and can hardly believe that anyone would spend the time to cut this\nbeautiful blue stone and use it for a road.  To the south is the town bank.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8747,36,58,-3,'Cascade Plaza','  You stand in the middle of this large arctic city.  The bustle of the\ninhabitants around you looks like water flowing through this frozen place.\nNortheast of here, a massive <o>hospital<z> rises above the other buildings.  To\nthe southeast you can see the police station.  North of you, along Cascade\nAvenue, are most of the utility stores.  To the west, along Frost Way, are\na few food stores.  The inn is to the southwest, at the corner of the\nwestern city walls and the wall of the residential district.  The road\nnamed after the center plaza also runs south of here, until it reaches\nAttallal Boulevard against the residential district wall.  By following\n<b>Frost Way<z> to the east, one comes to the important town docks, where\nmerchants and pirates of all sorts come to rest or to sell and buy goods.\n',56,131073,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8748,37,58,-3,'Eastern Frost Way','  This road is paved with <b>lapis lazuli<z> and runs from the west town gates to\nthe docks on the east side of town.  You marvel at the beauty of the tiles\nand can hardly believe that anyone would spend the time to cut this gorgeous\nblue stone and use it for a road.  Northeast of here the huge <o>hospital<z> rises\nabove the other buildings.  Immediately west is Cascade Plaza.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8749,38,58,-3,'Eastern Frost Way','  This road is paved with <b>lapis lazuli<z> and runs from the west town gates to\nthe docks on the east side of town.  You marvel at the beauty of the tiles\nand can hardly believe that anyone would spend the time to cut this gorgeous\nblue stone and use it for a road.  The massive <o>hospital<z> is to the north, and\nthe police station is to the south.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8750,39,58,-3,'Eastern Frost Way','  This road is paved with <b>lapis lazuli<z> and runs from the west town gates to\nthe docks on the east side of town.  You marvel at the beauty of the tiles\nand can hardly believe that anyone would spend the time to cut this gorgeous\nblue stone and use it for a road.  You see the massive <o>hospital<z> to the\nnorthwest of here.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8751,40,58,-3,'Main Entrance to the Docks','This area is generally bustling with activity as merchants load and unload\nships and bring their goods to and from town.  Attallal Boulevard, with its\nbluish moonstone tiles, leads to the south.  To the west is a <b>lapis lazuli<z>\ntiled road which leads to Cascade Plaza.  To the northwest you see a massive\n<o>hospital<z> standing above the other buildings of the town.  The road also\ncontinues north.  To the east is the busy dock area, and you can see several\nships have come in to port.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8752,41,58,-3,'The Docks','This is a busy area of the docks, as the main entrance is to the west\nof here.  You can see the <b>blue stone of Frost Way<z> to the west.  The salty\nsea breeze makes your hair sticky and you wrap your clothes tighter around\nyou to fend off the chilly wind.  Dock workers and merchants swarm around\nyou, carrying crates and other goods up and down to the ships and into\ntown to be sold and one of the many fine stores.  The boardwalk runs\nnorth, south, and out to a docked ship to the east.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8753,42,58,-3,'A Boarding Dock','  A <o>sign<z> next to a small bridge leading out to a docked ship states that\nthis is boarding dock two.  The boardwalk leads west towards the town, or\nyou could follow the bridge north out to the small ship docked there.  To\nthe east lies a large pier which extends out into the Amber Bay.\n',56,139264,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8754,33,57,-1,'Attallal Boulevard','  The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in\nreality.  Just east of here is a restaurant, with a bar on the second story.\nThe road also leads north and south.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8755,34,57,-1,'Dantrang\'s Delicious Dining','  This restaurant is packed with loud customers and fast moving waiters\nand waitresses.  The decor is mostly stained wood than is worn from\nyears of use; wine and beer stains cover most eating surfaces, and\nyou note a puddle of <R>Dantrang\'s Famous Barbecue Sauce<z> on a table near\nwhere you are.  Exits lead north or west, both out to the streets.  An\naged staircase leads upstairs to the bar area.\n',56,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8756,35,57,-3,'Second Bank of Amber','The atmosphere in the bank is completely different from that of the\nstreets outside -- exits east and north lead there.  Instead of a cold,\nbiting wind there is a stagnant scent of coins passing hands and piles\nof records being organized.  The tellers politely wait for customers to\nbring withdrawl and deposit slips to the windows that line the southwest\nwall, and patrons are shuffled through with a great amount of efficiency\nbut with a complete absence of real emotion.  Even the decor is listless,\nwith simple wooden paneling that has an unnatural shine and a thin rug\nthat does not make walking any more pleasant.\n',-1,174265,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,7,'',NULL),
(8757,36,57,-3,'South Cascade Avenue','  You are just south of Cascade Plaza.  The road here is made of slate\nslabs spaced so that they will not crack if there is a temperature change.\nWest of you is the stagnant bank office.  East of you is the <b>police station<z>,\nalthough there is no door from here -- you think you see one further south.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8758,37,57,-3,'The Police Station','There is a staircase leading upstairs here.  The office is continually\nbusy as law enforcement agents are dispatched to solve any problems within\nAmber or the nearby frontier.  The office continues east, southeast, and\nsouth.\n',-1,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8759,38,57,-3,'The Police Station','The busy police station is always in action.  Crimes throughout the town\nare quickly stomped out, ambassadors from the dwarven mines are kept safe,\nand any backup supplies for the frontier are all provided here.  To the\nnorth is <b>Frost Way<z>, and to the east you can see a deputy sheriff\'s office.\nTo the west you can see a staircase leading upstairs.  South and southwest\nthe office continues.\n',-1,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8760,39,57,-3,'The Deputy\'s Office','  This is where a deputy is always on duty.  He does most of the work\nhere, as the High Sheriff is only called on for the most important tasks.\nA <y>painting on the wall<z> depicts Galek and Logrus in battle.  There are also\nseveral plaques to prove that the officer working here is distinguished\nand has many years of experience.  The main office is to the west, and\na door leads south into the High Sheriff\'s office.\n',56,139273,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8761,40,57,-3,'Attallal Boulevard','The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in\nreality.  You can see the docks through a tall wooden fence on the east\nside of the road.  The path itself runs north and south.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8762,41,57,-3,'The Docks','  The wooden planks of the boardwalk lead north and south.  To the north\nis the main entrance area of the docks, and several ships.  To the\nsoutheast you can see a docked ship rocking in the waves.  Further south\non the boardwalk you can see a run down store of some sort.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8763,42,57,-3,'The Deck of a Pirate Ship','This is a large, stable ship.  The sails are a <c>light blue color<z>, and\nif it were not for the obvious black flag flying now this boat would be\ndifficult to spot out on the seas.  The deck leads east to the bow, and\na hatch here leads down into the ship.  A small bridge leads back to the\nboardwalk south of here.\n',0,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8764,43,57,-3,'The Deck of a Pirate Ship','  This is a large, stable ship.  The sails are a <c>light blue color<z>, and\nif it were not for the obvious black flag flying now this boat would be\ndifficult to spot out on the seas.  The deck leads west to the stern of\nthe ship.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8765,33,56,-3,'Attallal Boulevard','  The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in\nreality.  The main lobby of the town inn is to the east, and you can see\nbellhops waiting to show people up to their rooms inside.  The road\nfollows the massive town walls to either the north or the south.  To the\nsouth you can also see the wall of the residential district.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8766,34,56,-3,'The Cold Comfort Inn','  This inn is open to the outside on the ground floor and deserves its\nname.  The rooms for rent are generally comfortable though, and in warmer\nparts of the inn.  To the west and south are exits to Attallal Boulevard,\nand to the east you see a staircase leading up to some of the hotel rooms.\n',56,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8767,35,56,-3,'Grand Staircase to Rooms','  The wooden walls here are covered with thick insulating tapestries,\nand a <B>warm rug<z> nestles your feet.  Glass-covered lamps line the walls\nto guide you up the staircase that leads up to some rooms.  A cool breeze\ndrifts in from the hotel lobby to the west.\n',56,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8768,36,56,-3,'South Cascade Avenue','  The stone tile road runs north to Cascade Plaza or south to Attallal\nBoulevard and the residential district.  A door to the east allows\nentrance to the police station.  Above you an enclosed walkway leads\nfrom the inn on the west side over to the second floor of the police\nstation.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8769,37,56,-3,'The Police Station','The busy police station is always in action.  Crimes throughout the\ntown are quickly stomped out, ambassadors from the dwarven mines are\nkept safe, and any backup supplies for the frontier are all provided\nhere.  To the west through a door is Cascade Avenue.  There is a\nstaircase to the north, leading upstairs.  The office also continues\nnortheast and east.\n',-1,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8770,38,56,-3,'Amber Tax Office','This somber room serves as the office of the Royal tax collector, where all\ntaxes are received and tallied.\n',-1,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8771,39,56,-3,'The High Sheriff\'s Office','  The High Sheriff only bothers with the most important duties rather than\nall of the petty crimes in town.  There is still much to be done, and his\nrole has taken on a political aspect with the strengthening relations with\nthe dwarven mines to the north of the tundra.  A door leads north into the\ndeputy\'s office.  A small, dirty <r>red rug<z> is under the table where the\nsheriff would rest his feet.\n',56,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8772,40,56,-3,'Attallal Boulevard','The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in\nreality.  You can see the docks through a tall wooden fence on the east\nside of the road.  The entrance to the docks are nearby to the north; the\nroad also goes south where it meets the wall of the residential district.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8773,41,56,-3,'South End of the Docks','  This is the end of the boardwalk.  A dock leads out east to a ship in\nport, and the wooden walkway also leads north to the central dock area.\nTo the south is a seedy tattoo shop where drunken visiting sailors might\nhave women, skulls and knives drawn their arms and chests.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8774,42,56,-3,'A Boarding Dock','  This is the southern most point of the docking area.  A <o>sign<z> next to\na small bridge leading out to a ship flying pirate flags states that this\nis dock three.  The boardwalk also leads west, where you can also see a\nrun down store of some sort.  To the south sits a tiny shop, a carved\ntrappers guild logo set into the wood of the door.\n',56,139264,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8775,33,55,-3,'Attallal Boulevard in the Southwest Corner','  The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in\nreality.  The massive granite city wall to the west, and the solid wall\nof the residential district to the south, form a corner here.  To the\nnortheast rests the town inn, which has entrances both to the north,\nand to the east of this corner.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8776,34,55,-3,'Attallal Boulevard','  The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in\nreality.  To the north is the main lobby of the town inn.  The road\ncontinues west and east, along the wall of the residential district\nthat lies to the south.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8777,35,55,-3,'Attallal Boulevard','  The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in\nreality.  The inn is to your north, but there is no entrance from here.\nThe road follows the wall of the residential district that borders the\nsouth side of the street, which runs east and west.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8778,36,55,-3,'Entrance to the Residential District','  South of you are the impressive steel gates that lead into the\nresidential district.  You can see townfolk walking around from their\nhouses and to the few stores through the gates.  Running west to east\nhere are the <c>bluish moonstone tiles<z> of Attallal Boulevard.  North of\nhere, Cascade Avenue runs into the central plaza of town.  A dividing\nwall separates the main town from the residential area, keeping out\nany pirates or other drunken sailors, and the gates lead through this\nwall.  You note that guards keep a sharp eye on those who enter and\nexit the residential district.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8779,37,55,-3,'Attallal Boulevard','  The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in\nreality.  The road runs east and west, from whence you can see the\nentrance to the residential district, which is the only way through\nthe dividing wall on the south side of the road.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8780,38,55,-3,'Attallal Boulevard','The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in\nreality.  To the north a door leads into a government office.  The road\nruns west and east along the edge of the wall dividing the main town\nfrom the residential area that lies to the south.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8781,39,55,-3,'Attallal Boulevard','  The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in\nreality.  The road leads west and east along the wall that divides the\nmain town area and the residential district that lies to the south.  To\nthe east you see a bend in the road north as it leads toward the entrance\nto the docks, and to the west you see an entrance to the police station\non the north side of the road.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8782,40,55,-3,'Attallal Boulevard by the East Tower','The <c>white moonstone<z> tiles here have a bluish sheen to them.  Following\nthis boulevard feels very dreamlike, yet the biting cold keeps you in\nreality.  The wooden wall dividing the town from the dock area is to the\neast, and it leads north to the main entrance into the loading area for\nships.  To the south is a caravan marshalling yard by the East Tower, and\nAttallal Boulevard continues to the west.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8783,41,55,-3,'The Tattoo Store','  This seedy joint caters to the drunk sailors that come into port\nthroughout the year.  The equipment used to make tattoos does not look\nvery safe, and the walls have several dirty and misaligned paintings.\nA <d>counter<z> lines the south wall, and has various tattooing implements\nand garbage all over it.  An exit north leads directly onto the docks.\n',56,139273,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8784,34,57,-2,'Hotel Room 2','  This room has a few carvings made of metal on the tables and shelves.\nSmall, sturdy clothing is neatly folded on a dresser.  This is where the\ndwarven ambassador is staying in Amber while he is on his mission of peace\nhere.  The growing ties between the town and the dwarven mines keep him\nbusy.  A door leads south into the hotel corridor.\n',56,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8785,35,57,-2,'Hotel Room 1','  This room has some nice decorations in it of a dwarven flavor.  Military\ngear is neatly placed in strategic positions so that the guards that live\nhere might prepare for emergencies very quickly.  There is a door to the\nsouth leading into the hotel corridor.\n',56,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8786,37,57,-2,'Stairs Down to Police Station','  A staircase leads down here, or you might wish to follow the plain wood\nfloor to a guard station to the south.  You can hear the busy police office\nbelow you.  The mayor\'s office is through a door to the east.\n',56,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8787,34,56,-2,'Hotel Hallway','  You are just south of a hotel room, and you see another down the hall to\nyour east.  A <g>green rug<z> covers the floor to keep you warm in this heated\ncorridor.  A window on the west wall looks out to the town walls and\nAttallal Boulevard below.\n',56,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8788,35,56,-2,'Hotel Hallway','  You are in a heated hallway.  To the north is a hotel door, and to the\nwest is a hallway leading to another room.  On the east side of the room\nis a door marked \'<r>Authorized Personnel Only<z>\' and you are curious as to\nwhat is behind it.  A green rug lines the floor for extra warmth.\n',56,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8789,36,56,-2,'Connecting Passage','This passage connects the inn to the police station, and through windows\nin the north and south walls you can see Cascade Avenue below you.  People\nbusily scurry through the streets during the day.  Doors lead west and east.\n',-1,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8790,37,56,-2,'Guard Post','  Guards are usually here on duty, posted to defend someone in the hotel\nwhich lies through a door to the west.  To the north you can see a\nstaircase leading down.  The floor here is uncovered wood, and it is quite\na plain room.\n',56,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8791,42,57,-4,'In a Pirate Ship','  The interior of this ship is very bare here, and a sturdy looking door\non the east wall seems to protect something of more value.  The hull of\nthe ship is obviously quite strong, despite many years of corrosion by\nthe sea waters.  A few <o>wooden crates<z> lie around, and a hatch leads up\nand out to the deck, but it is otherwise bare.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8792,43,57,-4,'Mezzo One-Eye\'s Chamber','  This is a dark room, and black tapestries hang from the walls.  Several\n<d>embroidered pillows<z> lie on the floor in the corner of the room, obviously as\ndecoration rather than as a place to rest.  A sturdy door exits the room to\nthe west.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8793,42,59,-4,'In a Small Ship','  The interior of this ship is quite plain, and rather messy.  Boxes and\nbroken furniture are strewn about.  There is a door to the east, and a\nhatch leads to the deck above you.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8794,43,59,-4,'Jahya\'s Quarters','  This room is much more lavish than the entrance to the interior of the\nship, which lies through a door to the west.  A rug lies on the floor,\nkeeping bare feet warm.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8795,42,61,-4,'In a Merchant Ship','  The inside of this ship is quite warm.  Tapestries line the walls, which\ndampens sounds.  There is a plush rug on the ground, with salt and dirt\nstains covering it from years of use.  A screen door leads to the east,\nand a hatch above you leads to the deck of the ship.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8796,43,61,-4,'Lenge\'s Quarters','  There several tapestries and rugs hanging from the walls in this room.\nIt is a comfortable atmosphere.  You can see that the owner of this place\nenjoys collecting trinkets from all over The World.  A screen door to the\nwest exits the room.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8797,34,57,0,'Dantrang\'s Bar','  You are upstairs from the dining room.  Alcohol and other beverages are\nserved here.  Many of the patrons here are visiting sailors, who enjoy\ngetting drunk in their time off.\n',56,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8798,35,59,-2,'Omniman\'s Clothing','  This store deals with <g>softer clothing and leather armor<z>.\nDownstairs is the armor shop, which tends to the harder vestments\nbetter built for battle.\n',56,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8799,37,59,-4,'Amber Repair -- Sharpening Division','  There are several industrial sized implements for sharpening and\nblunting weapons here, and they are very noisy.  You cannot escape the\ngrinding and chiseling noises that the sharpeners make for most of the\nhours of the day.  You hear more noise, mostly a high pitched\nmetal-on-metal sound from the repair shop upstairs.\n',56,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8800,35,64,-2,'The North Tower','  Through the windows in the tower wall here, you can see <o>Amber Castle<z>\nto the north, and the vast tundra to the west.  The large granite blocks\ncomposing the walls would resist anything that might wish to attack the\ntown from the tundra, and they also make a good platform to bombard\nopponents with missiles.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8801,36,64,-2,'The North Tower','  Through the windows in the tower wall here, you can see <o>Amber Castle<z>\nto the north, and the vast tundra to the west.  The large granite blocks\ncomposing the walls would resist anything that might wish to attack the\ntown from the tundra, and they also make a good platform to bombard\nopponents with missiles.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8802,35,63,-2,'The North Tower','  There is an exit from the granite tower to the town walls south of here.\nThe large grey blocks forming the walls would resist anything that might wish\nto oppose the town from the tundra.  There is a staircase leading down to the\neast.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8803,36,63,-2,'Stairs Down to a Stone Road','  Stairs lead down to Attallal Boulevard here.  The granite blocks\ncomposing the walls are sturdy protection from attack by intruders from\nthe tundra.  There is a way out of the tower onto the city walls to the\nwest.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8804,42,55,-3,'Wolfsteen\'s Companions','  Cramped from top to bottom with tools and devices used to trap\nanimals this is obviously some sort of pet shop.  A large room can\nbe seen off to one side with a thick gate blocking its opening.\nA large sign is posted to one side of the gate.\n',60,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8805,32,62,0,'The Northwest Tower','  Through the windows of the stout granite tower you can see miles of\ntundra north and west.  The impressive walls would easily withstand a\nferocious assault.  To the southeast you can see a staircase leading\ndown to Attallal Boulevard.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8806,33,62,0,'The Northwest Tower','  Through the windows of the stout granite tower you can see miles of\ntundra north and west.  The impressive walls would easily withstand a\nferocious assault.  To the east is an arch leading to the open air town\nwalls.  To the south is a staircase leading to the ground level.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8807,34,62,0,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the air, and make a good platform to bombard\nattackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  An archway to the west leads into the\nnorthwest tower, and the wall continues east.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8808,35,62,0,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the air, and make a good platform to bombard\nattackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  An arch leads into a tower to the north\nand the wall continues to the west.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8809,32,61,0,'The Northwest Tower','  Through the windows of the stout granite tower you can see miles of\ntundra north and west.  The impressive walls would easily withstand a\nferocious assault.  To the south is an arch leading to the open air\ntown walls.  To the east is a staircase leading down to ground level.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8810,32,60,0,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the air, and make a good platform to bombard\nattackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  An archway to the north leads into the\nnorthwest tower, and the wall continues south.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8811,32,59,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  The path\non the wall continues north and south.  This is a wonderful vantage point\nfrom which to view the inside of the town.  From here you can see into\nboth the main market area and into the residential district in the section\nof town partitioned off on the south side.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8812,32,58,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  The path\non the wall continues north and south.  This is a wonderful vantage point\nfrom which to view the inside of the town.  From here you can see into\nboth the main market area and into the residential district in the section\nof town partitioned off on the south side.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8813,32,57,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  The path\non the wall continues north and south.  This is a wonderful vantage point\nfrom which to view the inside of the town.  From here you can see into\nboth the main market area and into the residential district in the section\nof town partitioned off on the south side.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8814,32,50,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the air, and make a good platform to bombard\nattackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  An archway leads south into the southwest\ntower, and the wall continues north.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8815,32,49,-2,'The Southwest Tower','  You can see clearly onto the tundra through windows in the strong granite\ntower.  The walls are sturdy enough to withstand almost any assault from\nthe frigid ground to the west.  To the east is a staircase leading down\nto the street level, and an archway north leads onto the open air town\nwalls.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8816,32,48,-2,'The Southwest Tower','  You can see clearly onto the tundra through windows in the strong granite\ntower.  The walls are sturdy enough to withstand almost any assault from\nthe frigid ground to the west.  To the northeast is a staircase leading\ndown to the street level.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8817,33,48,-2,'The Southwest Tower','  You can see clearly onto the tundra through windows in the strong granite\ntower.  The walls are sturdy enough to withstand almost any assault from\nthe frigid ground to the west.  To the east is an archway leading onto the\nopen air walls.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8818,34,48,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the air, and make a good platform to bombard\nattackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  An archway to the west leads into the\nsouthwest tower, and the wall continues east.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8819,35,48,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  This is a\nwonderful vantage point the residential district in the section to the north.\nYou see several houses there, and during the day citizens are busy running\nerrands in the streets.  The path on the wall leads east or west.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8820,36,48,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  This is a\nwonderful vantage point the residential district in the section to the north.\nYou see several houses there, and during the day citizens are busy running\nerrands in the streets.  The path on the wall leads east or west.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8821,37,48,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  This is a\nwonderful vantage point the residential district in the section to the north.\nYou see several houses there, and during the day citizens are busy running\nerrands in the streets.  The path on the wall leads east or west.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8822,38,48,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the air, and make a good platform to bombard\nattackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  An archway to the east leads into the\nsoutheast tower, and the wall continues west.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8823,39,48,-2,'The Southeast Tower','  Through the windows of this sturdy granite tower you can see the forest\nsouth of town.  The walls are designed to repel any attack from that\ndirection, and make a good platform to bombard attackers from.  To the\nnorth is a staircase leading down to ground level, and an archway to the\nwest leads to the open air walls.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8824,40,48,-2,'The Southeast Tower','  Through the windows of this sturdy granite tower you can see the forest\nsouth of town.  The walls are designed to repel any attack from that\ndirection, and make a good platform to bombard attackers from.  To the\nnorthwest is a staircase leading down to ground level, and an archway to\nthe east leads to an open air area used for observation of the docks\nto the northeast.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8825,41,48,-2,'Observation Area of the Town Walls','  The walls of Amber stand atop a cliff overlooking Amber Bay to\nthe northeast, and this vantage point also allows you to look out over the\nbirch forest to the south.  When you look north into the biting winds, you\ncan see the docks, where several ships are in port.  The vantage is a good\nspot to view any arriving boats from as it looks over the entire bay.  An\narchway to the west leads into the southeast tower.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8826,33,61,0,'A Staircase','  A staircase leads down from the granite tower to street level.  The stout\nwalls would be able to easily resist ferocious assault from the tundra.\nThe height of the walls gives an even better tactical advantage in case\nof an attack.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8827,33,49,-2,'Stairs Down to the Residential District','  A staircase leads down from the strong granite tower to the street level.\nThis tower and all of the walls are designed to withstand a ferocious\nassault from the tundra if necessary.  A chill wind blows through briefly,\nand you are glad that there is at least some guard from the icy wind in\nhere.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8828,39,49,-2,'Stairs Down to the Residential District','  The staircase here leads down to the street level.  The strong granite\nblocks composing this tower could repel even the most ferocious attack\nfrom the forest south of town.  A chill wind blows through for a moment\nand you are thankful for the walls of this tower.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8829,40,49,-2,'The Southeast Tower','  Through the windows of this sturdy granite tower you can see the <g>forest<z>\nsouth of town.  The walls are designed to repel any attack from that\ndirection, and make a good platform to bombard attackers from.  An archway\nleads out onto the top of the wall to the north, and to the west is a\nstaircase leading down to ground level.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8830,32,58,-1,'The Western Town Gates','  The impressive black steel gates of Amber loom over you to the east.\nThrough the gates you can see the <c>moonstone tiles<z> of the perimeter road.\nAbove you and on each side of the gate, thick, sturdy, granite walls stand\nagainst intruders.  A trail leads west to the punishing winds of the tundra.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8831,36,54,-3,'Resguard Station Between Town and Residential District','  You are in the guarded area between the Amber town to the north and the\nresidential district to the south.  On both the east and west side of the\npath are guard stations, where sheriffs keep an eye on those who wish\nto travel into the residential area.  You can see townfolk busily moving\nbetween houses and to a few shops through the gate to the south of you,\nand through the gate into the main town area you see a seedier lot of\npedestrians and some guards keeping the peace.\n',56,139273,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8832,38,57,-2,'The Mayor\'s Office','  This is where the mayor works during her long days.  It is mostly in\ncomplete disarray due to the frenetic pace of political activity occuring\ndue to the meetings with the dwarven ambassador from the mines to the north\nof town.  To the east is the secretary\'s desk, and you see the mayor\'s own\ndesk to the southeast.  Some chairs have been set up to the south for\nmeetings.  A door leads out of the office to the west.\n',56,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8833,38,56,-2,'Conference Area','  This area is the cleanest part of the office.  It has been set up to\nallow a private dialogue between the mayor and any ambassadors to discuss\ntreaties or trade agreements and the like.  Currently, it is used for the\ntalks with the dwarven ambassador from the mines to the north of town.  To\nthe east is the mayor\'s desk, and to the northeast is the desk of the\nsecretary.  To the north you see the door out of the office.\n',56,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8834,39,57,-2,'Secretary\'s Desk','The mayor\'s secretary displays a valiant effort to keep the mayor\norganized at all times, yet it is evidently very difficult in the current\npolitical climate.  A painting of Cascade Plaza is on the east wall.  To\nthe west you can see the door that exits the office.  To the south is the\nmayor\'s own disorganized desk, and to the southwest a few chairs have been\nset up for meetings.\n',-1,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8835,39,56,-2,'The Mayor\'s Desk','  This area of the office is in extreme disarray.  The mayor is obviously\nbusy with her political dialogue with the dwarven ambassador from the mines\nto the north of town.  Not only is she pressured to achieve a fair and\nuseful treaty with the dwarves, but she must be a perfect representative\nas the first female mayor in the realms.  To the north is her secretary\'s\ndesk, and the exit from the office is to the northwest.  Directly west is\na cleared area with a few chairs set up for meetings.\n',56,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8836,39,56,-4,'Secret Vault','  This is a small, cramped vault with granite walls and floor.  The stone\nof the walls and floor is very rough, obviously just intended for the\npractical use of keeping thieves like yourself from digging in from the\nside, rather than for aesthetic purposes.  The only exit is a small\n<o>trapdoor<z> above you.\n',56,139272,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8837,40,51,-4,'Secret Cult Basement','  The shroud of darkness that lies in this room is impenetrable.  You\nnearly puke up your guts from the stench and the atmosphere of evil.\nThrough broken floorboards above you a flicker of <o>candelight<z> is the\nonly source of brightness, and as soon as that light enters this room\nit is banished as if by Logrus himself.\n',56,172040,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8838,0,0,0,'Outside the Amber Church','  The Amber church doors are here, waiting for pious travelers and\ntownfolk to visit at any time to repent or talk to the priests for\nguidance.  The symbol of the Order of Serpents is proudly displayed\nabove the doors, which are also engraved with a mass of twisted\n<g>serpentine forms<z>.  To the north you see the gates that lead into the\nmain Amber town area.  Also to the north is access to the streets\nof the residential district.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8839,41,55,-4,'A Dank Storage Room','  The dim light from a store through a <g>grate<z> in the ceiling sends shafts\nof light to the moist dirt floor in this room.  Dust and dirt scatters the\nlight, making the room feel old and unused although the ground seems well\ntrodden.  It is only with further light sources that you notice a passage\ncarved into the dirt leading west.  The passage is off to the side of the\nroom and completely shadowed except for your light source.  Only silence\nemanates from it.\n',56,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(8840,40,55,-4,'A Dirt Passage','  The moist dirt walls could be dug through with the right equipment.  To\nthe east you see some faint shafts of light framed by floating dust that\nare streaming down through a grate in the ceiling.  To the west is more\ndark passageway, and it is eerily silent.\n',56,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(8841,39,55,-4,'A Silent Fence','  Your footsteps are completely silent here, as is everything else.  It\nis extremely dark except for some very <y>dim yellow glowing rods<z> stuck into\nthe dirt walls near the ceiling.  Down the passage to the east you can\nmake out some light, but you are not sure from where it is emanating.  A\ncounter has been built into the west wall on a platform area so that it\nis impossible to look behind the counter.\n',56,175292,13,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(8842,40,56,-4,'A Cold, Secret Room','  The west wall of this room is carved from granite blocks, and you\ncan make out a small crack where you might be able to pull open the\nwall.  The rest of the room has walls of packed dirt that is cold\nfrom the frigid weather.  The room is actually quite large despite\nthe small exit to the west and the obvious difficult nature of\ndigging into this ground.\n',56,163880,13,0,0,0,0,0,12,100,0,'',NULL),
(8843,36,53,-3,'Entrance to the Town','  You are just south of the guarded path between the Amber town and\nthe residential area that you are currently in.  This is the main\ncrossroad of the residential district, with River Street to the east,\nRedland Crescent to the west, and the Amber Church to the south.  The\nsymbol of the Order of Serpents is proudly displayed above the doors\nto the church, and a mass of twisted <g>serpentine forms<z> are engraved\nupon them.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8844,37,54,-3,'Eastern Resguard Station','  The wind in this room is almost completely cut off, due to the fact that\nit is contained within the walls of the residential district.  It serves\nas a room for the guards for the residential district, also known as the\nResguard by Amber citizens.  It is bare and has stone walls and floor.\nThe only exit is to the west, which leads to the space between the gates\nof the residential wall.\n',56,139273,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8845,35,54,-3,'Western Resguard Station','  The wind in this room is almost completely cut off, due to the fact that\nit is contained within the walls of the residential district.  It serves\nas a room for the guards for the residential district, also known as the\nResguard by Amber citizens.  It is bare and has stone walls and floor.\nThe only exit is to the east, which leads to the space between the gates\nof the residential wall.\n',56,139273,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8846,34,54,-3,'A Signmaker\'s Home','  This small studio is the home of Amber\'s most prominent signmaker.\nThe inhabitant has apparently applied his skills to his home as\nthe decorations consist mostly of wood paneling which has been\ncarved, engraved or painted.  On the west wall is a mural of\nguardsmen defending the gates of the northern frontier from an\ninvasion of goblins.  On the east Amber Castle has been painted\nin perfect detail.  The exit is a door to the south.\n',56,139272,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8847,33,54,-3,'The Moyel\'s House','  The first thing that you notice as you step in to this comfortable home\nis the delicious smell of homemade chicken soup wafting from the kitchen.\nVarious religious manuals and tomes line the walls of the eclectic chaos\nthat the local moyel and his wife call their home.  Several beautiful\npictures adorn the walls.  An expensive glass case holds a <y>golden\nobject<z>.  A door on the south wall leads outside.\n',56,139273,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8848,38,54,-3,'The Signmaker\'s Workshop','  This area is strewn with all types of tools, building materials, paints\nand varnishes.  On the west wall is a <o>large tool cabinet<z> and to the\neast building materials lie in a jumbled heap.  Against the back wall\nis the workbench where most of the construction takes place.  It is\nlittered with scraps of wood and metal and its original color has been\nobscured by years of paint splatters.  At the far end a few finished works\nhave been neatly stacked awaiting delivery.\n',56,139272,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8849,39,54,-3,'An Extravagant House','  This extravagant house is very peculiar.  The eastern side of the room\nappears to be the work of a madman.  Splotches of <r>random color<Z> have been\n<g>thrown<z> onto the wall and various <y>objects<z> lie strewn about the floor.  To\nthe west the room suddenly changes to a more organized approach.  The wall\nis a beautiful black and white swirl while various books have been stacked\nperfectly on the floor.  The northern wall is nothing but a massive <d>mural<z>\nof a great being.  Some painting tools and <c>buckets of paint<z> sit on the\nfloor at the feet of the picture.\n',56,132105,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8850,34,53,-3,'Redland Crescent','  Houses to the north and south are the places where two of the finest\ncraftsmen in the realms have come to stay in their retirement.  To the\nnorth is the most famous signmaker\'s home, and a bold marble sign\nengraved with the house number stands in front of it.  To the south is\nthe tastefully decorated home of the finest blacksmith ever to walk the\nrealms, and a steady line of smoke almost always drifts from his chimney.\nThe street itself leads east to the main entrance of the residential area\nor west further down the crescent.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8851,33,53,-3,'Bend in Redland Crescent','  The street turns here, going both east and south.  It\nstretches for a short distance south before terminating near the city\nwalls -- east heads toward the entrance to the residential district.\nA house on the north side of the street has a <b>six pointed star<z> painted\nit in blue.  You can faintly smell chicken soup from the house as well.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8852,35,53,-3,'Redland Crescent','  Just east of here is the entrance to the residential district.  You\nare currently on the more opulent road within the residential area.  It\nis said that the mayor lives at the end of this road.  Several other\nupscale houses line the curved road as it winds near the city walls to\nthe west.\n',56,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8853,40,54,-3,'Marshalling Yard','  This hard packed dirt area just inside the east gate of Amber is where\ncaravans assemble prior to their departure from town.  To north can be\nAttallal Boulevard and to the east the road heads into the base of the East\nTower through an archway closed by a portcullis.  The wall surrounding the\nresidential district prevents you from going south or west.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8854,37,53,-3,'River Street','  You are just east of the main entrance into the residential district,\nstanding on the less upscale road.  Further along this street there is\na post office and a general store, as well as the signmaker\'s shop.  While\nthis street is more downscale, it is still a clean, safe neighborhood\nalthough there is one house at the end of the road that is rumored to\nbe a haunted house -- right across from the bard hostel.  Those houses\ncan be found further down the street that leads east.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8855,38,53,-3,'River Street','  During the day this area of the residential district has a large volume\nof traffic due to the general store that is directly south of here.  You\nhear some faint sawing from the <o>signmaker\'s workshop<z> to the north.  People\nstream from east to west along this street, many of them heading toward\nthe main market area of the Amber town.  You see a post office to the\neast further along the road.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8856,39,53,-3,'River Street','  The post office is directly east of here, but most of the daily foot\ntraffic is to the west, where the Amber general store and the signmaker\'s\nworkshop are.  Further west is the guarded area that leads into the\nmain town.  The street leads south where you see several houses, including\na rather impressive mansion at the end of the street.  There is another\nhouse on the north side of the road.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8857,40,53,-3,'Amber Branch Post Office','  The Amber branch of the post office is rather quiet.  Not much\nmail travels all the way to this part of The World, but what does\nget sent here is generally important.  Due to the fact that there\nis not much activity here, it is very well kept up and neat.  No\npapers litter the floor and a pen with fully inked quill is always\navailable.  You see the streets of the residential district to\nthe west.\n',57,172537,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8858,33,52,-3,'Redland Crescent','  This is a well kept up road on the west side of the Amber residential\ndistrict.  <c>Turquoise colored grass<z> lines each side of the road, and on\nthe west side the strong granite town walls prevent any movement that\nway.  On the east side of the road you see a house, but there is no\nentrance from this side.  The house is made of red bricks and is in\nfairly good condition.  There is a cul-de-sac to the south, along with\nanother house, and to the north you see a bend in the road.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8859,34,52,-3,'Khelfenn\'s Home','  In his prime, the resident of this home was the finest blacksmith in all\nthe lands.  It was rumored that he made several powerful weapons and items\nof armor, but most of those stories seem to just be myths.  A worn, yet\nstill strong, shaping hammer hangs above a <y>fireplace<z>.  Evidently this\nblacksmith was extremely successful because his house is beautiful.  The\ndecor is simple, yet still comfortable and rich.  Deep <R>reds<z> and <g>greens<z> are\nthe primary color scheme, with <B>royal blue<z> curtains on the windows.  A\nsturdy mahogany door with a brass doorknob leads onto Redland Crescent\nto the north.\n',57,139272,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8860,42,53,-3,'Outside the East Gate of Amber','  You are just outside the East Gate of the City of Amber.  The large\nblack steel gate is to the northeast, set into the base of the East\nTower, which surrounds you to the north and west.  To the east, beyond a\nrocky beach, lies the wind blown waters of a large bay.  A road leads south\nalong the shore, between the beach to the east and a cliff upon which sits\nthe city wall to the west.\n',57,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8861,38,52,-3,'Amber General Store','  Shoppers scurry around busily to buy any supplies they need for their\nlives around the house.  This store is placed in the center of the\nresidential district for maximum traffic, and there is certainly a\nlarge crowd here every day.  Any sort of small item that you forgot to\nbring with you can be found here.  To the north you see the streets of the\nresidential area, and more people are walking around those streets during\nthe day.\n',57,172537,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8862,39,52,-3,'River Street','  This part of River Street is decidedly odd.  On the east side of the\nroad is a house with faded polka dots.  Someone must have payed a great\ndeal of money to get that by the housing authorities.  To the south you\ncan see some more tastefully decorated homes at the end of the street.\nNorth of here is the Amber post office, and the general store is nearby\nin that direction as well.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8863,40,52,-3,'Droppa\'s Home','  This house has a strange decor of jester hats and multicolored clothing.\nOn a rack on the wall you see three juggling balls, a <r>red<z>, a <g>green<z>, and a\n<b>blue<z> one.  A pair of <d>curly-toed shoes<z> rests in front of the kitchen area.\nEverything in the house is garish and bright.  On the wall you see a\npicture of a young fool dancing and juggling in a tavern of some sort.\nThe wallpaper is <r>red<z> and <y>yellow<z> vertical stripes.  You see a polka dotted\ndoor that leads out to the street on the west side of the home, but you\nare almost afraid to grab the large red doorknob.\n',57,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8864,33,51,-3,'End of Redland Crescent','  This is a cul-de-sac at the end of the road.  On the east side of\nthe street is a neat house painted grey with white trim.  A <o>welcome\nmat<z> sits in front of the door.  To the west the road is bordered\nby the tall, strong granite town walls.  You can follow the street further\nnorth where you can see more houses.  A path south leads to a staircase\nwhich seems to allow access up onto the town walls.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8865,34,51,-3,'Amber House','  This is a tastefully decorated home, and it is obvious that no children\nlive here because it has several delicate items of furniture.  A painting\nof a distinguished woman on a <b>blue background<z> is nailed to a wall.  The\nfloor is covered by a <r>red rug<z> that matches <r>red curtains<z>.  A window east\nlooks onto the side of the Amber church, and a window south looks onto\nthe path by the strong granite city walls.  A wooden door on the west side\nof the house leads into the streets of the Amber residential district.\n',57,139272,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8866,35,52,-3,'Northwest Corner of the Amber Church','  A massive hanging snake altar is above an raised area that lies to\nthe southeast.  The center of this church is to the east, and the exit\nto the northeast.  The massive serpent form gathers the congregations\nattention, and those who worship from the center of the church stare\nat the snake like they are communing with it telepathically.  To non-\nbelievers this church is frightening, yet to those who follow the\nsnake\'s way it is of purest spirit.  There are only a few small windows\nnear the top of the church, and <r>red stained glass<z> fills these curious\neye-shaped openings.\n',57,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8867,36,52,-3,'Doors out of Amber Church','  Two <o>carved oak doors<z> lead out to the north.  The main church area is to\nthe south, and you can see a massive hanging serpent symbol hanging from\nthe ceiling where priests preach during the days.  From here you can see\nits <r>red staring eyes<z> and vicious fangs.  When a particularly fervent\ncongregation is required the priests will open windows near the top of\nthe church to funnel wind through the snake\'s mouth, creating an ominous\nhiss that drives the masses into a pitched frenzy of devotion.  Even the\ndoors are carved with the sinewy coils of serpents of all kinds, and as\nyou stare at them you become momentarily caught in their hypnotic dance.\n',57,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8868,37,52,-3,'Northeast Corner of the Amber Church','  A massive hanging snake altar is above an raised area that lies to\nthe southwest, south of the center of the church that is immediately\nin that direction.  The carved exit doors are to the west.  The massive\nserpent form gathers the congregation\'s attention, and those who\nworship from the center of the church stare at the snake like they are\ncommuning with it telepathically.  To non-believers this church is\nfrightening, yet to those who follow the snake\'s way it is of the\npurest spirit.  There are only a few small windows near the top of\nthe church, and <r>red stained glass<z> fills these curious eye-shaped\nopenings.\n',57,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8869,38,51,-3,'The House of Bards','  Simple, yet extravagant, this home is obviously shared by several people.\nThis house serves as a temporary home for the traveling bards who wander\nthe lands.  Rumor has it that it was a Bard who discovered the power of\nthe Pattern.  Henceforth, Bards have always been welcome in the town of\nAmber and have been granted this home in gratitude for the help they once\ngave to the Royal Family.\n',57,139272,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8870,39,51,-3,'End of River Street','  This is the end of River Street in the residential area of Amber.\nThree houses line the end of the street, and all are completely\ndifferent.  To the south is a luxurious mansion that attracts your\nattention immediately.  To the west is a house with a sign depicting\na <d>silver harp<z> on a <b>blue background<z> hanging outside the front door,\nand to the east is a house that is beginning to get run down.  It\nis dark on the inside and from what you can see through dusty\nwindows and worn curtains makes it seem almost like a haunted house.\nThe road leads north to more houses and towards the main town, and\na small path leads southwest toward the southern town walls.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8871,40,51,-3,'Cult House','  This house is creepy and dark.  The walls have strange symbols painted\nin some sort of red paste.  The source of light comes from flickering\ncandles rather than bright lamps, and this casts shadows dancing on\nthe floor and walls.  Some of the decorations are bizarre carved\nstatues of gargoyles and skulls, and these cast the most frightening\nsilhouettes, especially enlarged and in motion on the walls.\n',57,139272,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8872,35,51,-3,'Southwest Corner of the Amber Church','  A massive hanging snake altar is above an raised area that lies to\nthe southeast.  The center of this church is to the east, and the exit\nto the northeast.  The massive serpent form gathers the congregation\'s\nattention, and those who worship from the center of the church stare\nat the snake like they are communing with it telepathically.  To non-\nbelievers this church is frightening, yet to those who follow the\nsnake\'s way it is of purest spirit.  There are only a few small windows\nnear the top of the church, and <r>red stained glass<z> fills these curious\neye-shaped openings.\n',57,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8873,36,51,-3,'Center of the Amber Church','  This is the best place from which one may view the massive hanging\nserpent altar which is to the south.  From this vantage it almost\nseems like the snake\'s eyes are judging you, and prompting you to\ntake up a weapon and fight for the Order\'s cause.  During much of the\nweek religious Amber citizens can be found here, praying to this\nserpent and listening to the wisdom of the priests.  The main church\nhall extends east, west, and north, and a few stairs lead up to the\naltar area to the south where religious heads stand during service.\nThe exit from the church is further to the north.\n',57,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8874,37,51,-3,'Southeast Corner of the Amber Church','  A massive hanging snake altar is above an raised area that lies to\nthe southwest.  The center of this church is to the west, and the exit\nto the northwest.  The massive serpent form gathers the congregation\'s\nattention, and those who worship from the center of the church stare\nat the snake like they are communing with it telepathically.  To non-\nbelievers this church is frightening, yet to those who follow the\nsnake\'s way it is of purest spirit.  There are only a few small windows\nnear the top of the church, and <r>red stained glass<z> fills these curious\neye-shaped openings.\n',57,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8875,39,50,-3,'A Well Furnished Amber House','  You are dazzled by the riches contained in this house as you walk in.  The\nfloors are covered with lush carpets that makes you feel like you are walking\non a grassy plain.  Exquisite tapestries cover all four walls depicting scenes\nof a large banquet making you feel like you are actually in the picture.  Many\nglass cases are placed around the room displaying the treasures acquired by\nthe rich owner of the house.\n',57,139272,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8876,36,50,-3,'Altar in the Amber Church','  The <d>impressive altar<z> draws everyone\'s attention and flirts with their\nminds like a dancing cobra ready to strike.  The symbol of the Order of\nSerpents hangs from the ceiling, suspended by a coil of silk rope.  During\nspecial ceremonies wind is tunnelled through the top part of the church\nthrough the mouth of the snake symbol which causes it to emit a faint\nhiss.  This sound generally throws the masses into a religious frenzy\nand the congregation screams for their deities to assist in defeating the\nblasphemous ranks of the other factions.  To the north two small steps\nlead out into the masses.  Up here under the snake charm, on the east\nside of the main dais where the holy books are placed during service,\na wooden panel carved with serpentine forms is positioned.  Priests\nwill prostrate themselves before this panel and pray to their deities.\n',57,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8877,37,50,-3,'Backroom in the Amber Church','  This warm room has no windows yet the air is strangely fresh and smells\nfaintly of roses.  The walls are covered in rather terrifying murals of\nserpents writhing in hypnotic frenzy.  You see movement out of the corners\nof your eyes yet when you turn to look it is simply a painted snake grinning\nwith bared fangs.  On the west side of the room a panel engraved with more\nsnake carvings seems to be a door out of here, if you can find a key for\nits tiny lock.\n',57,139272,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8878,33,49,-3,'Staircase up to the Town Walls','  You are under the southwest tower of the mighty granite town walls.  A\npath leads north onto the southern part of Redland Crescent, and a crude\ndirt path meant to only be traveled by guards leads east along the wall.\nA granite staircase leads up.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8879,39,49,-3,'Staircase up to the Town Walls','  You are under the southeast tower of the mighty granite town walls.  A\ncrude dirt path meant to only be traveled by guards leads west along the\nwall to the west, and a granite staircase leads up onto the walls.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8880,32,56,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  The path\non the wall continues north and south.  This is a wonderful vantage point\nfrom which to view the inside of the town.  From here you can see into\nboth the main market area and into the residential district in the section\nof town partitioned off on the south side.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8881,32,55,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  The path\non the wall continues north and south.  This is a wonderful vantage point\nfrom which to view the inside of the town.  From here you can see into\nboth the main market area and into the residential district in the section\nof town partitioned off on the south side.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8882,32,54,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  The path\non the wall continues north and south.  This is a wonderful vantage point\nfrom which to view the inside of the town.  From here you can see into\nboth the main market area and into the residential district in the section\nof town partitioned off on the south side.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8883,32,53,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  The path\non the wall continues north and south.  This is a wonderful vantage point\nfrom which to view the inside of the town.  From here you can see into\nboth the main market area and into the residential district in the section\nof town partitioned off on the south side.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8884,32,52,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  The path\non the wall continues north and south.  This is a wonderful vantage point\nfrom which to view the inside of the town.  From here you can see into\nboth the main market area and into the residential district in the section\nof town partitioned off on the south side.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8885,32,51,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  The path\non the wall continues north and south.  This is a wonderful vantage point\nfrom which to view the inside of the town.  From here you can see into\nboth the main market area and into the residential district in the section\nof town partitioned off on the south side.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8886,34,49,-3,'Path Along the Southern Wall','  This is a simple dirt path along the southern town wall.  It runs\nwest, where there is a granite staircase leading onto the walls,\nor east further along the wall.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8887,35,49,-3,'Path Along the Southern Wall','  This is a simple dirt path that runes east to west along the\nsouthern town wall.  You see a granite staircase leading up to\nthe top of the walls a short way west.  The back of the Amber\nChurch is to the northeast.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8888,36,49,-3,'Path Along the Southern Wall','  This is a simple dirt path that leads east and west along the\ntall granite town walls that lies on the south side of the path.\nOn the north side of the trail is the back of the Amber Church.\nFrom here you can see an opening near the room of the church wall\nthat is closed from the inside by a wooden door.  It is used to\nlet air through the church on certain religious occasions.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8889,37,49,-3,'Path Along the Southern Wall','  This is a simple dirt path that runs east to west along the\nsouthern town wall.  You see a granite staircase leading up to\nthe top of the walls a short way east.  On the north side of the\ntrail you see the Amber Church.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8890,38,49,-3,'Path Along the Southern Wall','  This is a simple dirt path along the southern town wall.  It runs\neast, where there is a granite staircase which leads up to the walls,\nor west.  A trail north leads to River Street.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8891,33,50,-3,'Path Near Redland Crescent','  Just north of here is the end of Redland Crescent.  You see a\nhouse there.  To the south is a granite staircase leading up onto\nthe town walls.  The path has some grass on it near the street to\nthe north, but it fades to plain dirt to the south.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8892,38,50,-3,'Path by River Street','  This is a plain dirt path that is meant only for guards and other\ntown officials.  It forms an easy trail between River Street to the\nnortheast and the town walls to the south.  On the north side of the\npath is the House of Bards, and on the east side is a nicely\ndecorated house.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8893,40,50,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  The path\non the wall continues northeast and to the south is an archway leading\ninto the southeast tower.  This is a wonderful vantage point from which to\nview the inside of the town.  From here you can see into the residential\ndistrict in the section of town partitioned off on the south side.  Looking\noutward to the east, you can see the wall sits at the edge of a high cliff,\nbeyond which are the frigid waters of Amber Bay.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8894,41,51,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  The path\non the wall continues north and southwest.  This is a wonderful vantage\npoint from which to view the inside of the town.  From here you can see\ninto the residential district in the section of town partitioned off on the\nsouth side.  Looking outward to the east, you can see the wall sits at the\nedge of a high cliff, beyond which are the frigid waters of Amber Bay.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8895,41,52,-2,'On the Town Walls','  The town walls are open to the frigid air, and make a good platform to\nbombard attackers from.  The strong granite blocks composing the wall would\nwithstand ferocious assaults.  A wind blows from the inside of the town to\nthe outside, caused by the slightly warmer air within the walls.  The path\non the wall continues south, and to the north is an archway leading into\nthe East Tower.  This is a wonderful vantage point from which to view the\ninside of the town.  From here you can see into the residential district in\nthe section of town partitioned off on the south side.  Looking outward to\nthe east, you can see the wall sits at the edge of a high cliff, beyond\nwhich are the frigid waters of Amber Bay.\n',57,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8896,41,53,-2,'The East Tower','  Through the windows of the stout granite tower you can see a the board\nexpanse of Amber Bay to the east.  The impressive walls would easily\nwithstand a ferocious assault.  To the south is an archway leading to the\nopen air town walls.\n',57,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8897,41,54,-2,'The East Tower','  Through the windows of the stout granite tower you can see the port\ndistrict to the north, and the roofs of the residential district to the\nwest.  The impressive walls would easily withstand a ferocious assault.\nA staircase descends to the ground level.\n',57,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8898,42,54,-2,'The East Tower','  Through the windows of the stout granite tower you can see the broad\nexpanse of Amber Bay to the east.  To the north stretches the port\ndistrict, and to the south you have a view of a road stretching alongside\nthe base of the cliffs toward the gate below you.  The impressive walls\nwould easily withstand a ferocious assault.\n',57,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8899,41,54,-3,'Inside the East Tower','  You are inside the base of the East Tower of Amber.  The thick walls of\nthis tower, and the black steel gate, provide protection to the town from\nassault by sea.  To the west, through an archway protected by a portcullis\nlies a marshalling yard for the caravans that use this exit from the town.\nTo the southeast lies the gate itself.  A stairway along the wall leads up\nto the top of the tower and from there out onto the wall.\n',57,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(8902,1,21,-1,'Small Trail in a Sparse Forest','  This is a small trail connecting the main part of Haon-Dor\nforest and a thin area of the forest which lies north of here.\nThe trees are not as tall and the sparse tree cover above\nallows a partial view of the sky.  The ground is like a\ncushion of leaves and the only indication of civilization\nare the presence of numerous footprints.  A well traveled path\ncan just be made out to the west of here through the foliage,\nand a smaller path to the south.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8903,2,21,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest, the trees are not as\ntall and the sparse tree cover above allows a partial view of the\nsky.  The ground is like a cushion of leaves and the only indication\nof civilization are the presence of numerous footprints.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8904,1,22,-1,'Inside a Small Tent','  With no apparent purpose, it looks like this tent was forgotten\nhere by an adventurer in a hurry to leave, but it still serves as\nshelter for those that are willing to defy the mystery of this\nforest.  A small hole in the east side of the tent provides a nice\nview of the trail southeast of here.\n',63,131072,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8905,2,22,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree cover\nabove allows a partial view of the sky.  While it appears to lack any\ncivilization, burned twigs reveal what once was a firepit, probably\nused to provide light and keep the travelers warm and safe from\nanimals during the night.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8906,3,22,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  The area is well\ntravelled despite the absence of anything interesting.  Fruits\nof various types can be found spoiling here even though there\nare no fruit bearing trees around.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8907,1,23,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  A small tent is\nsouth of here contrasting with the scenario.  While it appears\nto be here for a long time, the tent is still in good condition,\nas if someone has been looking after it.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8908,2,23,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  The area is well\ntravelled despite the absence of anything interesting.  Fruits\nof various types can be found spoiling here even though there\nare no fruit bearing trees around.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8909,3,23,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  The area is well\ntravelled despite the absence of anything interesting.  Fruits\nof various types can be found spoiling here even though there\nare no fruit bearing trees around.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8910,1,24,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  The area is well\ntravelled despite the absence of anything interesting.  Fruits\nof various types can be found spoiling here even though there\nare no fruit bearing trees around.  A break in the thicker\nundergrowth to the west allows passage to a visible well\ntraveled path there.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8911,2,24,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  The area is well\ntravelled despite the absence of anything interesting.  Fruits\nof various types can be found spoiling here even though there\nare no fruit bearing trees around.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8912,3,24,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  The area is well\ntravelled despite the absence of anything interesting.  Fruits\nof various types can be found spoiling here even though there\nare no fruit bearing trees around.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8913,1,25,-1,'Sparse Forest Before a Large Tree','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  The area is well\ntravelled despite the absence of anything interesting.  Fruits\nof various types can be found spoiling here even though there\nare no fruit bearing trees around.  A particularly large tree stands to\nthe northeast, standing out from the surrounding landscape.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8914,2,25,-1,'Sparse Forest Near a Large Tree','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  The area is well\ntravelled despite the absence of anything interesting.  Fruits\nof various types can be found spoiling here even though there\nare no fruit bearing trees around.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8915,3,25,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  The area is well\ntravelled despite the absence of anything interesting.  Fruits\nof various types can be found spoiling here even though there\nare no fruit bearing trees around.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8916,4,25,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  The area is well\ntravelled despite the absence of anything interesting.  Fruits\nof various types can be found spoiling here even though there\nare no fruit bearing trees around.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8917,1,26,-1,'Sparse Forest Near a Large Tree','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  The area is well\ntravelled despite the absence of anything interesting.  Fruits\nof various types can be found spoiling here even though there\nare no fruit bearing trees around.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8918,2,26,-1,'Inside a Large Tree','  Stairs have been cut into the massive trunk of the tree here,\nallowing easy climbing upwards.  East of here is the counting room.\nA stick hangs looking missplaced on the side of the trunk.\n',63,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,70,0,'',NULL),
(8919,3,26,-1,'The Counting Room','  This is the room where the workers count their fruits.  A large\ndesk sits on the east wall with a few baskets nearby.  There is\nalso a graph hanging on the south wall with the performance of\nthe past few seasons.\n',63,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,70,0,'',NULL),
(8920,4,26,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  The area is well\ntravelled despite the absence of anything interesting.  Fruits of\nvarious types can be found spoiling on the ground here, even\nthough there are no fruit bearing trees around.  There\'s a small\nspring of clear water east of here.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8921,5,26,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  A small spring of\nclear water is here and several scuffs and marks around it indicate\nprevious use.  The ground around the spring is sort of muddy, but\nthe roots of the trees and shrubs quickly suck up the excess water.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8922,1,27,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree cover above allows\na partial view of the sky.  Several fruit bearing trees rest north of here.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8923,2,27,-1,'Inside a Large Tree','  Stairs have been cut into the massive trunk of the tree here,\nallowing easy climbing upwards.  Southeast of here is the counting\nroom.\n',63,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,70,0,'',NULL),
(8924,3,27,-1,'Under a Tree House','  The ceiling here is the floor of the tree house above.  It\'s a\nmix of smooth wood and broken twigs.  The only way up there is by\nclimbing the tree.  There is a hole on the floor allowing passage\nto the fruit\'s storage room in the cave below.\n',63,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,70,0,'',NULL),
(8925,4,27,-1,'Sparse Forest Outside a Cave Opening','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  Several fruit\nbearing trees rest north of here, while to the east you see the\nentrance to a cave.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8926,5,27,-1,'A Cave Opening','  The forest opens up, revealing an entrance to a cave in the\nground.  The vegetation is even more sparse then it is in the rest\nof the forest, only a few shrubs can be seen here.  A trapdoor is\non the ground to keep the animals out of the cave, as well as the\npresence of unexpected outsiders.\n',63,131072,41,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8927,6,27,-1,'Sparse Forest','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  A small spring of\nclear water is here and several scuffs and marks around it indicate\nprevious use.  The ground around the spring is sort of muddy, but\nthe roots of the trees and shrubs quickly suck up the excess water.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8928,1,29,-1,'Sparse Forest with Fruit Bearing Trees','  Several fruit bearing trees stand on this side of the forest,\nbut it\'s obvious that they don\'t belong to this forest.  All the\nfruits had been harvested but a few others are spoiling on the\nground.  The passage to the north and east is blocked by a dense\nstand of trees and shrubs.  A well traveled path is just visible\nthrough the foliage to the west.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8929,1,28,-1,'Sparse Forest with Fruit Bearing Trees','  Several fruit bearing trees stand on this side of the forest,\nbut it\'s obvious that they don\'t belong to this forest.  All the\nfruits had been harvested but a few others are spoiling on the\nground.  A well traveled path is just visible to the west through\nthe foliage.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8930,2,28,-1,'Sparse Forest with Fruit Bearing Trees','  Several fruit bearing trees stand on this side of the forest,\nbut it\'s obvious that they don\'t belong to this forest.  All the\nfruits had been harvested but a few others are spoiling on the\nground.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8931,3,28,-1,'Sparse Forest with Fruit Bearing Trees','  Several fruit bearing trees stand on this side of the forest,\nbut it\'s obvious that they don\'t belong to this forest.  All the\nfruits had been harvested but a few others are spoiling on the\nground.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8932,4,28,-1,'Sparse Forest with Fruit Bearing Trees','  Several fruit bearing trees stand on this side of the forest,\nbut it\'s obvious that they don\'t belong to this forest.  All the\nfruits had been harvested but a few others are spoiling on the\nground.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8933,5,28,-1,'Sparse Forest Outside a Cave Opening','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  Several fruit\nbearing trees stand west of here, while to the south you see\nthe entrance to a cave.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8934,6,28,-1,'Sparse Forest Near a Cave','  This is a thin part of Haon-Dor forest and the sparse tree\ncover above allows a partial view of the sky.  There\'s small\nspring of clear water south of here.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8935,3,27,0,'A Tree House','  This simple construction is made of wood foraged from the trees\naround, making it hard to notice the building through the thick\nfoliage.  The house is used as an observation post from where the\nsentries can see the entire area, the forgotten tent far to the\nsouth, the two springs east of here and the several fruit bearing\ntrees from where the inhabitants get their sustenance.\n',63,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,70,0,'',NULL),
(8936,1,25,-2,'Inside a Cave','  After a whole day harvesting the fruits, this is where the\nworkers come to rest.  There\'s a cushion of leaves sitting on the\nwest side of the room and a candle next to it.  The smell of spoiled\nfruits in the air is nauseating, but the people that live here\nare probably used to it.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(8937,2,25,-2,'Inside a Cave','  After a whole day harvesting the fruits, this is where the\nworkers come to rest.  There\'s a cushion of leaves sitting on the\nwest side of the room and a candle next to it.  The smell of spoiled\nfruits in the air is nauseating, but the people that live here\nare probably used to it.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(8938,1,26,-2,'Inside a Cave','  After a whole day harvesting the fruits, this is where the\nworkers come to rest.  There\'s a cushion of leaves sitting on the\nwest side of the room and a candle next to it.  The smell of spoiled\nfruits in the air is nauseating, but the people that live here\nare probably used to it.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(8939,2,26,-2,'Common Area','  A lamp is hanging from the ceiling providing light.  There is a\nportrait of the worker\'s chief on the northeast corner and a big\nclock on the southeast corner to make sure the harvesting\nschedule will be accomplished.  A table is in the middle of the\nroom so the workers can get together after the harvesting.  The\nresidential caves are along the north, south and west sides.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(8940,3,26,-2,'Access Tunnel','  This tunnel connects the residential caves where the workers\nlive to the forest where they work.  Even being underground, the\nwalls and floor are clean and smooth.  There is a lamp hanging in\nthe west wall providing light.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(8941,4,26,-2,'Access Tunnel','  This tunnel connects the residential caves where the workers\nlive to the forest where they work.  Even being underground, the\nwalls and floor are clean and smooth.  There is a lamp hanging in\nthe west wall providing light.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(8942,5,26,-2,'Bend in the Tunnel','  This tunnel connects the residential caves where the workers\nlive to the forest where they work.  Even being underground, the\nwalls and floor are clean and smooth, a small pile of debris against the\neast wall is the only thing that seems out of place.  There is a lamp\nhanging on the south wall providing light.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(8943,1,27,-2,'Inside a Cave','  After a whole day harvesting the fruits, this is where the\nworkers come to rest.  There\'s a cushion of leaves sitting on the\nwest side of the room and a candle next to it.  The smell of spoiled\nfruits in the air is nauseating, but the people that live here\nare probably used to it.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(8944,2,27,-2,'Inside a Cave','  After a whole day harvesting the fruits, this is where the\nworkers come to rest.  There\'s a cushion of leaves sitting on the\nwest side of the room and a candle next to it.  The smell of spoiled\nfruits in the air is nauseating, but the people that live here\nare probably used to it.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(8945,3,27,-2,'Silo Cave','  This cave is used to storage the fruits harvested by the workers\nwhen they couldn\'t be traded for other goods in Grimhaven.  The\nair is dry and cold so the fruits can stay fresh longer.  The walls\nare smooth and a lamp rests in the corner next to a calendar with\ndrawings marking the correct dates to harvest the fruits and the\nstorage limit of each one of them.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(8946,5,27,-2,'Access Tunnel','  This tunnel connects the residential caves where the workers live\nto the forest where they work.  Even being underground, the walls\nand floor are clean and smooth.  There is a lamp hanging in the\nwest wall providing light.  A trapdoor is in the ceiling keeping\nthe animals out as well as the presence of unexpected outsiders.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(8947,2,26,0,'The Tree Canopy','  The foliage is thick and the leaves are small and bright green.\nIt\'s not easy to keep the balance standing on top of the twigs,\nthe air is chilly and windy up here, shaking the leaves and cracking\nthe twigs.  Despite your presence, birds land near singing a song\nthat echoes through the vegetation.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8948,3,26,0,'The Tree Canopy','  The foliage is thick and the leaves are small and bright green.\nIt\'s not easy to keep the balance standing on top of the twigs,\nthe air is chilly and windy up here, shaking the leaves and cracking\nthe twigs.  Despite your presence, birds land near singing a song\nthat echoes through the vegetation.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8949,2,27,0,'The Tree Canopy','  The foliage is thick and the leaves are small and bright green.\nIt\'s not easy to keep the balance standing on top of the twigs,\nthe air is chilly and windy up here, shaking the leaves and cracking\nthe twigs.  Despite your presence, birds land near singing a song\nthat echoes through the vegetation.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8950,-5,38,-1,'Far Corner of the Encampment','  For some reason, the traders seem to avoid this area as much as possible.\nThe ground here is clean and untrodden aside from the occasional wary guard\'s\nfootprint.  You stand under a huge, wood and iron cage which has no hole with\nwhich to peer in, only a locked ramp which can be lowered from the base of the\ncage.  Blood seeps from the entrance of the cage.\n',64,131080,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,72,0,'',NULL),
(8951,-4,38,-1,'A Patch of Well-Worn Earth','  Little care goes into the maintenance of this part of the camp.  The grass\nhas been beaten to the dirt by the numerous paws and hoofs of the animals\nthat are exercised here daily.  A large, iron cage holding a beast of \nunimaginable terror lies to the west.\n',64,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8952,-5,37,-1,'A Firepit Surrounded by Large Stones','  This firepit appears to be the main gathering place for the traders at this\ncamp.  Bottles and other debris lay on the ground, evidence of wild nights\nheld at this spot.  A huge cage is visible just north of here.\n',64,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8953,-4,37,-1,'A Patch of Well-Worn Earth','  Little care goes into the maintenance of this part of the camp.  The grass\nhas been beaten to the dirt by the numerous paws and hoofs of the animals\nthat are exercised here daily.  A lone flower grows here standing in defiance\nbetween the small tent to the east, and the firepit to the west.  The fact\nthat it stands leads to thought of protective magics.  A large, iron cage\nholding a beast of unimaginable terror lies to the northwest.\n',64,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8954,-3,37,-1,'In a Small Tent','  Spartan doesn\'t quite describe this small, cold tent.  What little comfort\nthere is residing in this tiny living space finds itself in the form of a\npillow and a blanket placed neatly beside the oil lamp.  These traders have\ncome up here looking to make some talens at the arena but with such dismal\nliving conditions, one can\'t help but wonder how any of them could have even\nwhat little cheer they have left.\n',64,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8955,-5,36,-1,'A Makeshift Stable','  The smell creeping out from the hay covering the ground feels nearly caustic\nto your nose and eyes.  Obviously not used to being outside the sandy expanses\nof the desert, the traders came badly prepared for this area and there\'s no \ndoubt that this is the same hay that had been laid out when they first arrived\nand likely hasn\'t been cleaned since.  Luckily, the open, roofless stable has \ngranted the unforseen benefit of releasing the nauseating stench and gracefully\nallowing free passage to all the disgusting insects that call this place home.\n',64,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8956,-4,36,-1,'A Carpeted Path Through the Camp','  Numerous carpets and rugs have been placed on the ground here in a vain\nattempt to lower the amount of mud let into the tents.  Alas, puddles of water\nhave found their way into small depressions along the carpeted walkway and it\nwould appear the mud is winning the battle.\n',64,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8957,-3,36,-1,'A Noisy Animal Enclosure','  Surprisingly unlike the majority of the camp, this area is kept relatively\nclean.  The animals appear to live in more comfort than the traders\nthemselves, and they seem content to pass their feelings of gratitude on to\nthe traders in the form of incessant, irrepressible noise at all hours of the\nday.  Such a collection of animals both exotic and fierce should be expected\nof a zoo, yet here they are, living in a tent, restrained by a wooden\nfence to await sport at the arena.\n',64,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8958,-5,35,-1,'A Calm Pool in the Lake','  The clean, flat surface of this particular pool coupled with the water\'s\nabsolute transparency give this area a calming feeling to say the least.\nThe cold, crisp waters look inviting for any that wish to swim, while the\nplant-life growing around this shady pool lend it a rich, spicy scent.\n',64,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8959,-4,35,-1,'A Carpeted Path Through the Camp','  Numerous carpets and rugs have been placed on the ground here in a vain\nattempt to lower the amount of mud let into the tents.  Alas, puddles of water\nhave found their way into small depressions along the carpeted walkway and it\nwould appear the mud is winning the battle.\n',64,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8960,-3,35,-1,'Inside the Spacious Tent','  This messy tent appears to be the main shelter for the traders of the camp.\nCarpets and pillows lie strewn about the room in a hap-hazard pattern \nproviding the little comfort the traders actually have here.  The northern\nhalf of the tent has been sectioned off by a sturdy wooden fence with a gate\nto contain the animals being brought to the arena.\n',64,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8961,-2,35,-1,'In a Small Tent','  Spartan doesn\'t quite describe this small, cold tent.  What little comfort\nthere is residing in this tiny living space finds itself in the form of a\npillow and a blanket placed neatly beside the oil lamp.  These traders have\ncome up here looking to make some talens at the arena but with such dismal\nliving conditions, one can\'t help but wonder how any of them could have even\nwhat little cheer they have left.\n',64,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8962,-6,34,-1,'On a Crystal Clear Mountain Lake','  Before you lies one of the most beautiful lakes you\'ve ever seen.  It is\nsurrounded by lush evergreen trees and you spot members of the local \nwildlife sipping its refreshing waters by the shore.  In the southwest corner\na rumbling waterfall bestows its enchanted water upon the river below.\n',64,131072,29,0,0,0,3,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8963,-5,34,-1,'On a Crystal Clear Mountain Lake','  Before you lies one of the most beautiful lakes you\'ve ever seen.  It is\nsurrounded by lush evergreen trees and you spot members of the local \nwildlife sipping its refreshing waters by the shore.  In the southwest corner\na rumbling waterfall bestows its enchanted water upon the river below.\n',64,131072,29,0,0,0,3,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8964,-4,34,-1,'A Carpeted Path Through the Camp','  Numerous carpets and rugs have been placed on the ground here in a vain\nattempt to lower the amount of mud let into the tents.  Alas, puddles of water\nhave found their way into small depressions along the carpeted walkway and it\nwould appear the mud is winning the battle.\n',64,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8965,-3,34,-1,'Outside a Large Pavilion Tent','A large rug covers the ground in front of the large pavilion tent to the\nnorth.  Inside you hear sounds one would expect only from a zoo or a king\'s \nmenagerie, and the noise is near deafening.  Muddy footprints of many\nshapes and sizes dot the rug in many places along with lumps of what is\nhoped to be mud.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8966,-2,34,-1,'A Carpeted Path Through the Camp','  Numerous carpets and rugs have been placed on the ground here in a vain\nattempt to lower the amount of mud let into the tents.  Alas, puddles of water\nhave found their way into small depressions along the carpeted walkway and it\nwould appear the mud is winning the battle.  The camp seems to continue to \nthe west while a muddy path cuts through the forest to the east.\n',64,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8967,-6,33,-1,'Atop a Cascading Waterfall','  You are now nearly at the edge of the mighty waterfall.  Roaring water\ntumbles over and between rocks both tiny and titanic before making its \nthundering descent to the river below.  From this vantage point, you can see\nthe desceptively slow curve of the Serpent River as it leads the raging current\nwhile racing to its destination.\n',64,131076,29,0,0,0,6,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8968,-5,33,-1,'On a Crystal Clear Mountain Lake','  Before you lies one of the most beautiful lakes you\'ve ever seen.  It is\nsurrounded by lush evergreen trees and you spot members of the local \nwildlife sipping its refreshing waters by the shore.  In the southwest corner\na rumbling waterfall bestows its enchanted water upon the river below.\n',64,131072,29,0,0,0,3,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8969,-4,33,-1,'A Strange Corner of the Lake','  There is something unnatural about this particular section of the lake.\nMaybe it\'s the nearly complete lack of vegetation, the smell of freshly dug\nearth, or...  the barely discernable seam you just spotted a few feet off the\nshore where ripples seem to crash into invisible walls repeatedly.  Though\nthe phenomenon could be caused by some sub-aquatic means, something tells you\nthere\'s more to this than meets the eye...\n',64,131072,28,0,0,0,0,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8970,-3,33,-1,'A Carpeted Path Through the Camp','  Numerous carpets and rugs have been placed on the ground here in a vain\nattempt to lower the amount of mud let into the tents.  Alas, puddles of water\nhave found their way into small depressions along the carpeted walkway and it\nwould appear the mud is winning the battle.\n',64,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(8971,-2,33,-1,'A Plush-Looking Tent','  This tent provides a total and complete contrast to the others.  Where\nthe others lacked in comfortability, this one makes up for it with sheer\nlavishness.  Expensive carpets cover the floor and a large pillow rests in one\ncorner to serve as a bed.  Oil lamps cover the ground here providing enough\nlight to bring back the reality that lingers on the other side of the tent\'s\nflap.\n',64,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8972,-4,33,-2,'An Uncomfortably Warm Cavern','Mesmerizing wave after mesmerizing wave of orange rolls over the walls of\nthis cramped cavern providing the only source of light.  The heat becomes\nalmost unbearable as drowning in your own sweat becomes an almost real \nconcern.\n',64,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(8973,-5,38,0,'Inside the Large, Iron Cage','  This cage doesn\'t get cleaned out very often.  The smell is almost too much\nto bear, and seems to emanate from something else beside the natural effects\nthe inhabitant has placed on the ground, but more from the inhabitant itself.\nThe only light that shines into this cage stabs down from in between the\nbars covering the roof.  The floor is lined with hay in an effort to keep\nthe beast semi-content, while in one corner, it would appear the beast has his\nown idea of decoration.\n',64,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(8974,-5,35,-2,'Bottom of the Pool','  Immersed in waters so clean and clear, it\'s as if you\'ve entered an entirely\ndifferent world.  Above you rays of light pierce the mirrored surface\nof the pool in an effort to bathe the floor below in its ambience.  A pile\nof rocks provide shelter for the fish that inhabit the lake in one corner\nof the deep pool while sand coats the rest of the bottom covered in \nbeautiful, flowing aquatic plants.\n',64,131072,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9000,-10,-1,-1,'Interrogation Chamber','  This high security room is dedicated to the fine art of interrogation that\nonly the torturers are trained to perform.  This is where new \'subjects\'\nare brought to be broken.  Rusty, blood covered shackles hang from the wall\nin the far corner.  Splatters of blood mark the walls and the floor, showing\njust how much the torturers enjoy their job.  A sign hangs on the wall above\nthe shackles, while a tapestry hangs on the east wall\n',65,135304,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9001,-9,-1,-1,'End of the Hall','  This appears to be the end of a dim hallway.  Torches light the\nhall, creating shadows that dance on the walls.  A fairly strong aroma of\nblood fills the air around you.  Every once in a while you can hear\nwhat sounds to be like a soft, weak moan from somewhere nearby.  A large\ntapestry with the symbol of the Cult hangs on the western wall.\n',65,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9002,-8,-1,-1,'Hallway','Torches attached to the walls light the hallway.   The crackling\ntorch flames create shadows that dance on the walls.\nYou can sometimes make out weak moans coming from somewhere\nnearby.  The hall continues to the east and west.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9003,-7,-1,-1,'Hallway','Torches attached to the walls light the hallway.  The crackling\ntorch flames create shadows that dance on the walls.\nOn the northern wall a crest of Logrus hangs.  To the west, you can\nsee further down the hallway, lit by torchlight.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9004,-10,-2,-1,'Containment Chamber','  This damp, dark chamber is used to keep those who have been\ninterrogated.  Shackles are attached to the walls to ensure any hope\nof escape is futile.  Spies have their uses in the Garrison, and that is\nto make sure they give all the information they have to the Cult before\nthey die...which is usually a short period of time after they are brought\nhere.  A large pit in the center of the room has been dug for additional\ncontainment space.\n',65,393224,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9005,-9,-2,-1,'Main Hall','Torches attached to the walls light the hallway.  The crackling\ntorch flames create shadows that dance on the walls.\nThe Main Hall continues to the east, and a grand Waiting Room\nlies to the south.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9006,-8,-2,-1,'T in the Main Hall','Torches attached to the walls light the hallway.  The crackling\ntorch flames create shadows that dance on the walls.\nThis is a T in the Main Hall.  Exits continue to the west, east, and\nsouth to the Main Hall.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9007,-7,-2,-1,'Main Hall','Torches attached to the walls light the hallway.  The crackling\ntorch flames create shadows that dance on the walls.\nA dark hall leads to the south.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9008,-10,-3,-1,'Containment Chamber','  This damp, dark chamber is used to keep those who have been\ninterrogated.  Shackles are attached to the walls to ensure any hope\nof escape is futile.  Spies have their uses in the Garrison, and that is\nto make sure they give all the information they have to the Cult before\nthey die...which is usually a short period of time after they are brought\nhere.  A large pit in the center of the room has been dug for additional\ncontainment space.\n',65,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9009,-9,-3,-1,'Waiting Room','  When word of new spies being captured gets to the officials of\nthe Cult, this is where they come to rest before having an audience.\nPlush, soft chairs and a bench occupy the room to make their stay\nas pleasant as possible.\n',65,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9010,-8,-3,-1,'Main Hall','Torches attached to the walls light the hallway.  The crackling\ntorch flames create shadows that dance on the walls.\nYou can see further down the hall to the north and south.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9011,-7,-3,-1,'Entrance Hall','  This hall is dimly lit by the dancing flames of torches attached\nto the walls.  In addition to the torches, various pieces of Cult\nmemorabilia hang from the walls.\n',65,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9012,-10,-4,-1,'Containment Chamber','  This damp, dark chamber is used to keep those who have been\ninterrogated.  Shackles are attached to the walls to ensure any hope\nof escape is futile.  Spies have their uses in the Garrison, and that is\nto make sure they give all the information they have to the Cult before\nthey die...which is usually a short period of time after they are brought\nhere.  A large pit in the center of the room has been dug for additional\ncontainment space and a sturdy looking cell door lies to the southeast.\n',65,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9013,-9,-4,-1,'Conference Room','  A large wooden table sits in the middle of the room, occupying\na great deal of space.  This is where any discussions about the\ninformation acquired in the Interrogation Chamber are held.\n',65,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9014,-8,-4,-1,'Main Hall','Torches attached to the walls light the hallway.  The crackling\ntorch flames create shadows that dance on the walls.\nThe hall continues to the north and south.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9015,-7,-4,-1,'Entrance Hall','  This hall is dimly lit by the dancing flames of torches attached\nto the walls.  In addition to the torches, various pieces of Cult\nmemorabilia hang from the walls.\n',65,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9016,-10,-2,-2,'Containment Pit','  This damp, dark pit is used to keep those who have been interrogated.\nShackles are attached to the walls to ensure any hope of escape is futile.\nSpies have their uses in the Garrison, and that is to make sure they give\nall the information they have to the Cult before they die...which is usually\na short period of time after they are brought here.\n',65,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9017,-10,-3,-2,'Containment Pit','  This damp, dark pit is used to keep those who have been interrogated.\nShackles are attached to the walls to ensure any hope of escape is futile.\nSpies have their uses in the Garrison, and that is to make sure they give\nall the information they have to the Cult before they die...which is usually\na short period of time after they are brought here.\n',65,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9018,-8,-5,-1,'Main Hall','Torches attached to the walls light the hallway.  The crackling\ntorch flames create shadows that dance on the walls.\nTo the south, the hall appears to come to an end.  The Main Hall\ncontinues to the north.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9019,-7,-5,-1,'Stair Landing','The stairs reach from the dark foyer here to the trapdoor above.\nVarious Cult memorabilias adorn the walls and a poster hanging on the west \nwall was meant to grab attention.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9020,-9,-5,-1,'Cell Entry','  This carefully guarded room is the entry way to the containment chambers.\nThe spies who are brought here learn to regret their occupation choice.\nA sign hangs on the wall to the south while cell doors are both to the\nnorthwest and southeast.\n',65,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9021,-8,-6,-1,'End of Main Hall','  This appears to be the end of the hallway.  A heavy cell door is to\nthe northwest.  To the southeast, a wooden door awaits.  Every now and\nagain, you believe you can hear faint, muffled moans coming from\nsomewhere nearby.\n',65,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9022,-7,-6,-1,'Interrogator\'s Chamber','  This is where the Interrogator stays when she has idle time.  A\nregal four-posted bed sits along the northern wall.  Bloody leather\nuniforms hang from a clothes rack beside the bed, the source of the\nblood smell that permeates the chamber.  Occasionally, the Interrogator\nwill bring a \'subject\' or two to her chambers with her when she\'s in the\nmood for \'extracurricular activities\'.  A small onyx nightstand sits beside\nthe bed, on it are extra tools of the trade.  Shackles hang from the wall to\nthe west, to keep her occasional guests in their place.  A sign hangs on\nthe wall to the west.  To the south the back of a bookshelf sits acting\nas a door.\n',65,135176,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9023,-10,-4,-2,'Containment Pit','  This damp, dark pit is used to keep those who have been interrogated.\nShackles are attached to the walls to ensure any hope of escape is futile.\nSpies have their uses in the Garrison, and that is to make sure they give\nall the information they have to the Cult before they die...which is usually\na short period of time after they are brought here.\n',65,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9024,-7,-7,-1,'Interrogator\'s Office','  This is the office of the Garrison Interrogator.  Shelves filled with\ncountless books on torture and pain line the walls in all directions.  A\nblack onyx desk sits in the far corner and a single lit candle illuminates\nthe room.  The taint of blood in the air drives you to believe there is\nmore to this quaint office than there appears to be.  A wooden door has\nbeen set into the northwest wall.  A plaque hangs on the east wall above\nthe desk.\n',65,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9025,0,0,0,'Guest Room 1','  Plain and small, this guest room is pretty unimpressive.\nA single-sized bed is pushed into the corner, and a small\nchest is at the foot for clothes and such.  You get the feeling\nthat this room is for the \"less important\" guests.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9026,0,0,0,'Antechamber 1','  You stand in a room that is attached to the guest suite, used \nmostly for lounging, meetings, or for the guest\'s entourage.  A\nlong sofa sits against the southern wall, with a wooden table on\neach end.  A hand-made braided rug covers the wooden floors, and\na thick wooden door that exits into the main hallway is to the east.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9027,0,0,0,'Landing','  At the top of the staircase is a sturdy, wooden-floor landing.\nContinuing straight to the south is a dimly lit hall, luminated\nby torches set in sconces that are attached to the walls.  To the\neast is an empty corridor and to the west is a door.  The stairs \nlead back down.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9028,0,0,0,'Corridor','  Set aside from the hallway, this corridor is mostly empty,\nexcept for a place to sit and a window.  A large, dusty tapestry\nhangs on the wall to the north.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9029,0,0,0,'Guest Room 2','  This is an average-sized room, filled with various pieces\nof furniture.  A rather large bed rests in the far corner, and\na wooden wardrobe sits against the western wall.  A few \npaintings hang from the walls, and a hand-woven rug covers\nthe wooden floor.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9030,0,0,0,'Antechamber 2','  You stand in a room that is attached to the guest suite, used \nmostly for lounging, meetings, or for the guest\'s entourage.  A\nlong sofa sits against the southern wall, with a wooden table on\neach end.  A hand-made braided rug covers the wooden floors, and\na thick wooden door that exits into the main hallway is to the east.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9031,0,0,0,'Hall','Torches affixed to sconces light up this long hallway.\nA door to the west can be seen, and an empty corridor to\nthe east.  The hall continues to the south and appears to\nbe lined with more doors. \n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9032,0,0,0,'Servant\'s Quarters','  This average-sized room is the living quarters of the\nservants who work on this floor of the Garrison.  It is a\nplain simple room, the only furniture occupying it are the\nbeds and clothes chests.  Nevertheless, this room is kept\nneat and tidy.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9033,0,0,0,'Guest Room 3','  This is an average-sized room, filled with various pieces\nof furniture.  A rather large bed rests in the far corner, and\na wooden wardrobe sits against the western wall.  A few \npaintings hang from the walls, and a hand-woven rug covers\nthe wooden floor.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9034,0,0,0,'Antechamber 3','  You stand in a room that is attached to the guest suite, used \nmostly for lounging, meetings, or for the guest\'s entourage.  A\nlong sofa sits against the southern wall, with a wooden table on\neach end.  A hand-made braided rug covers the wooden floors, and\na thick wooden door that exits into the main hallway is to the east.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9035,0,0,0,'Hall','   Torches affixed to sconces light up this long hallway.\nA door to the west as well as the east can be seen.  The\nhall continues to the south and to the north.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9036,0,0,0,'Library','This huge room is filled with books of every kind.  Shelves\nrun the length of each wall and are filled from end to end\nwith endless information.  From children\'s stories to the\narguments of Theology, this place is a information-seeker\'s\ndream.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9037,0,0,0,'Guest Room 4','  This large, awe inspiring room is filled with the finest\nluxuries.  A beautiful bed rests in the farthest corner, with\nthe finest silk blankets and huge fluffy pillows.  Beautiful\nhand-crafted tapestries cover the walls, life-like sculptured\npewter figurines dance on the surface of a wooden table, and\na large wooden wardrobe stands against the wall.  This is \ndefinitely a room saved for the most important of guests.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9038,0,0,0,'Antechamber 4','  You stand in a room that is attached to the guest suite, used \nmostly for lounging, meetings, or for the guest\'s entourage.  A\nlong sofa sits against the southern wall, with a wooden table on\neach end.  A hand-made braided rug covers the wooden floors, and\na thick wooden door that exits into the main hallway is to the east.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9039,0,0,0,'Hall','   Torches affixed to sconces light up this long hallway.\nA door to the west as well as the east can be seen.  The\nhall continues to the south and to the north.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9040,0,0,0,'Library','This huge room is filled with books of every kind.  Shelves\nrun the length of each wall and are filled from end to end\nwith endless information.  From children\'s stories to the\narguments of Theology, this place is a information-seeker\'s\ndream.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9041,0,0,0,'Hall','  Torches affixed to sconces light up this long hallway.\nAn empty corridor lies to the east.  The hall continues to the\nsouth and to the north.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9042,0,0,0,'Corridor','Set aside from the hallway, this corridor is mostly empty,\nexcept for a place to sit.  A painted portrait of a stern-looking man hangs on the wall to the east. \n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9043,0,0,0,'End of Hall','  To the north, a long hallway lit up by torches affixed to\nsconces can be seen.  There is a door to the east.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9044,0,0,0,'Captain\'s Quarters','  This is the room the Captain uses when he has time\nto himself.  A large stone fireplace warms the room and\nprovides illumination.  A meager bookshelf rests on the\nfloor against the wall and a very comfortable looking\ncouch sits to the side of it.   Through the dancing shadows\ncreated by the firelight, a door to the south can be seen.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9045,0,0,0,'Captain\'s Quarters','  This is the living quarters of the Captain.  A plain, \nunmade bed takes up a generous amount of space.\nVarious other items are strewn about, giving the room\na well lived-in look.  An exit can be seen to the north.\n',0,9,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9046,0,0,0,'9046','Empty\n',0,0,60,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9050,-1,5,1,'Secret Staircase','  A creaky wooden staircase leads down to the hidden storage room below.\nIt also serves as the primary means of travel between the first and\nsecond floor for the cleaning staff.  The room is completely empty and\nbarren except for the torch on the wall and a barrel in the corner.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,4,'',NULL),
(9051,-1,4,1,'A Utility Room','  Brooms, slop buckets, scrub brushes and other cleaning apparatuses\nfill this room to capacity.  It looks like it once was a bedroom, hence\nthe broken bed frame left dusty and discarded in the corner, but is now\nbeing used by the cleaning staff due to the increased traffic the\ncathedral has received recently.  There\'s a desk in the corner covered\nwith work assignments and assorted notes.  A wooden door to the west\nleads you back to the Colonnade Balcony.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9052,-1,3,1,'Head Priest\'s Private Chambers','  The Head Priest comes to this room to rest and relax.  A simple cot in\nthe corner suggests he sleeps here as well.  A bookcase on the far wall\nshowcases his vast thirst for knowledge.  Most are leather bound and\nsome are latched shut with a small book lock.  What interests you more\nhowever is the crude quill and manuscript that rests on a table next to\nhis reading chair.  A door leads you back out to the balcony.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9053,-1,2,1,'Papal Suite','  This is the room where high ranking clergy from around the realm are\nlodged and made to feel at home.  It is lavishly decorated as befits any\nself respecting clergyman.  Humility has no place here.  The walls are\npaneled and recessed.  Wonderful paintings adorn every available spot.\nOne in particular catches your attention.  Looking around you notice the\nfloor is covered with cozy looking rug made out of bearskin.  Fine\nfurniture decorates the room as well.  The church is obvious in it\nattention to detail regarding their guests comfort.  The room continues\nto your south and there is a <o>wooden door<z> to your west.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9054,-1,1,1,'Papal Suite','  This room stretches into the one to the north.  Opulence abounds.  The\namount of coinage that must have been spent on the artwork alone is\noutrageous.  Of course, the church always likes to claim some worthy\nartisan donated it on their deathbed as an act of penance.  Your sure\nthe townsfolk would probably be very upset if they knew where all their\ntithe money went.  Suddenly it comes to you that you probably have no\nbusiness here, but before you head back north to leave, you notice the\neerie <r>red<z> glow the stained glass window casts across the room.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9055,-2,1,1,'East Steeple Tower','  Barrel vaulted ceilings make this room spacious and roomy.  The floors\nare polished smooth due to the heavy traffic this area receives and\n<o>torches<z> adorn the walls as very little light reaches this part of\nthe cathedral.  A stone staircase carved into the rock gives you the\nchoice of either going downstairs in the direction of the entryway or\norphanage, and going upstairs will continue your trek to the Steeple\npinnacle itself.  North leads you to the Colonnade balconies where you\ncan watch Mass from a reserved distance and west leads you into the\nglorious Rose Window room.  It seems awfully quiet upstairs.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9056,-3,1,1,'<Y>Rose Window<z>','  The stained glass window before you is awe inspiring.  The tracery\ninvolved probably took the designers thousands of man hours to complete.\nThe window is round and has a circumference of twenty feet.  Within it,\nyou can piece together a <p>story<z>.  The stone balcony north of you\nlooks down upon the Nave where the congregation worships.  You can go\neither east or west.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9057,-4,1,1,'West Steeple Tower','  Barrel vaulted ceilings make this room spacious and roomy.  The floors\nare polished smooth due to the heavy traffic this area receives and\n<o>torches<z> adorn the walls as very little light reaches this part of\nthe cathedral.  A stone staircase carved into the rock gives you the\nchoice of either going downstairs in the direction of the entryway or\nthe monk sanctuary, and going upstairs will continue your trek to the\nSteeple pinnacle itself.  North leads you to the Colonnade balconies\nwhere you can watch Mass from a reserved distance and east leads you\ninto the glorious Rose Window room.  It seems awfully quiet upstairs.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9058,-5,1,1,'Deacon Quarters','  This is a large room where the cathedrals various clerics and deacon\'s\nshare quarters together.  Beds line the walls on one side, and small\nchests lie at the foot of each bed to hold each clergymans personal\nbelongings.  Simple decorations make this room feel comfortable and\nwarm.  A long rug that stretches into the other room keeps everyone\'s\nfeet warm come winter.  The only thing different in this end of the long\nroom is the magnificent stained glass window in the south wall.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9059,-5,2,1,'Cleric Quarters','  This is a large room where the cathedrals various clerics and deacons\nshare quarters together.  Beds line the walls on one side, and small\nchests lie at the foot of each bed to hold each clergyman\'s personal\nbelongings.  Simple decorations make this room feel comfortable and\nwarm.  A long rug that stretches into the other room keeps everyone\'s\nfeet warm come winter.  A door leads back out to the balcony.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9060,-5,3,1,'The Cathedral Library','  Books are scattered all over the place as you enter this room.  The\nchurch librarian seems to be in the middle of reorganizing the whole\nroom.  If the place wasn\'t such a mess it would be a very nice place to\nspend the day reading something spiritual and uplifting.  However, that\nday is unlikely to arrive for a long time.  A door leads back out to the\nbalcony.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9061,-5,4,1,'Altar Boy\'s Quarters','  This room is small and cramped.  Very little space has been allocated\nto the out of luck altar boys.  Tiny cots fill the room leaving hardly\nany room to navigate.  The only exception to this is the far end of the\nroom where a larger than normal cot is.  A plaque over the boys cot\nreads, <Y>\"Sr.  Altar Boy\"<z>.  In addition, another one below it reads,\n<R>\"I rule, you guys drool!\"<z>.  He must think an awful lot of himself.\nA door leads to the balcony.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9062,-5,5,1,'Monk Guildmaster\'s Bedroom','  Here the Master finds solace and rest.  Unlike most people, he finds\nno comfort in a bed or a cot, a straw mat provides that particular need.\nThe room is small and comfortable.  But most importantly, and considered\nin the original design of the church, is the fact that no noise enters\nthis room.  If there was one safe place in the city where one could rest\nin peace and quiet, it would be here.  A picture of a grasshopper is the\nonly wall decoration.\n',67,173560,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9063,-4,5,1,'Monk Guildmaster\'s Meditation Room','The Guildmaster visits this room daily for extended periods of time.  A\nstraw mat placed in the center of the room is one of the few material\ncomforts he affords himself.  A chop block that has suffered years of\nabuse at the Master\'s lethal hands sits discarded in the corner.  A\npicture of a praying mantis is the only decoration to adorn the bare\nwalls\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9064,-2,5,1,'Kitchen','  Your sense of smell is assaulted when you enter this room.  The food\npreparations for the entire church happen here.  Boxes are stacked up to\nthe ceiling with non-perishables on one of the walls and a long\ncountertop supported by wooden posts is in the middle of the room.  A\nfirepot with numerous utensils, pots, and pans is in the far corner.  A\nmischievous rodent scurries about looking for morsels and scraps to feed\nitself with.  A single torch keeps the room lit.  A door south leads to\nthe Colonnade Balcony.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,4,'',NULL),
(9065,-4,4,1,'West Colonnade Balcony','  A magnificent stone balcony dominates this room.  Like most of the\ncathedral it is made out of  <k>limestone<z> chiseled from the rock\nquarries in the far southern reaches of the realm.  Below you is the\nNave, where the congregation worships.  Above you the vaulted arches\nthat make this cathedral known throughout the land soar to great\nheights.  Extraordinary artistry and workmanship is everywhere.  A door\nleads somewhere.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9066,-3,4,1,'Above the Altar','You are just above the altar of the Grimhaven Church, the room continues\noverhead but your path is blocked by a catwalk made of rope.  The\ninstability of the bridge makes attempting to climb onto it from\nbelow suicidal.\n',67,139273,34,0,0,0,0,-1,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(9067,-2,4,1,'Colonnade Balcony','  A magnificent stone balcony dominates this room.  Like most of the\ncathedral it is made out of  <k>limestone<z> chiseled from the rock\nquarries in the far southern reaches of the realm.  Below you is the\nNave, where the congregation worships.  Above you the vaulted arches\nthat make this cathedral known throughout the land soar to great\nheights.  Extraordinary artistry and workmanship is everywhere.  A door\nto the north leads to the kitchen and another opposite from the balcony\nleads elsewhere.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9068,-2,3,1,'Colonnade Balcony','  A magnificent stone balcony dominates this room.  Like most of the\ncathedral it is made out of  <k>limestone<z> chiseled from the rock\nquarries in the far southern reaches of the realm.  Below you is the\nNave, where the congregation worships.  Above you the vaulted arches\nthat make this cathedral known throughout the land soar to great\nheights.  Extraordinary artistry and workmanship is everywhere.  A door\nleads somewhere.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9069,-2,2,1,'Colonnade Balcony','  A magnificent stone balcony dominates this room.  Like most of the\ncathedral it is made out of  <k>limestone<z> chiseled from the rock\nquarries in the far southern reaches of the realm.  Below you is the\nNave, where the congregation worships.  Above you the vaulted arches\nthat make this cathedral known throughout the land soar to great\nheights.  Extraordinary artistry and workmanship is everywhere.  A door\nleads somewhere.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9070,0,0,0,'East Attic Landing','  The top of the steeple tower is almost within reach.  One more flight\nof stairs and your there.  There is a door with a bright yellow\n<Y>sign<z>, marked <R>WARNING!<z> nailed into it to your north.  If you\nlook closely you can see some small writing on the sign.  Below you can\nhear the sounds of people hustling about.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9071,-4,2,1,'West Colonnade Balcony','  A magnificent stone balcony dominates this room.  Like most of the\ncathedral it is made out of  <k>limestone<z> chiseled from the rock\nquarries in the far southern reaches of the realm.  Below you is the\nNave, where the congregation worships.  Above you the vaulted arches\nthat make this cathedral known throughout the land soar to great\nheights.  Extraordinary artistry and workmanship is everywhere.  A door\nleads somewhere.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9072,-4,3,1,'West Colonnade Balcony','  A magnificent stone balcony dominates this room.  Like most of the\ncathedral it is made out of  <k>limestone<z> chiseled from the rock\nquarries in the far southern reaches of the realm.  Below you is the\nNave, where the congregation worships.  Above you the vaulted arches\nthat make this cathedral known throughout the land soar to great\nheights.  Extraordinary artistry and workmanship is everywhere.  A door\nleads somewhere.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9073,0,0,0,'West Attic Landing','  The top of the steeple tower is almost within reach.  One more flight\nof stairs and your there.  There is a door with a bright yellow\n<Y>sign<z>, marked <R>WARNING!<z> nailed into it to your north.  If you\nlook closely you can see some small writing on the sign.  Below you can\nhear the sounds of people hustling about.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9074,0,0,0,'Parapet Wall','  The low wall around the cathedral protects you from plummeting to the\nstreet below you, which would result in your certain death.  The walkway\nis narrow and serves as a means of accessing the elevated heights of the\ncathedral in case of repairs.  You could probably see the different\nsections of street from way up here if you squinted your eyes a little.\n',67,131072,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9075,0,0,0,'The Attic','<k>  The attic before you stretches away into the gloomy darkness.\nShadows dance upon the walls from the flickering <o>flame<z> of a small\ncandle perched in the wall.  A wooden rail is here to protect you from a\ndebilitating if not fatal  fall to the crowded Nave below.  This area is\nfilled with boxes and crates.  An abundance of cobwebs make the room\nfeel spooky indeed.  It\'s difficult to find your way amongst all this\nchaos.\n',67,131084,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9076,0,0,0,'The Attic','<k>  The attic before you stretches away into the gloomy darkness.\nShadows dance upon the walls from the flickering <o>flame<z> <k>of a\nsmall candle perched in the wall.  A wooden rail is here to protect you\nfrom a debilitating if not fatal  fall to the crowded Nave below.  This\narea is filled with boxes and crates.  An abundance of cobwebs make the\nroom feel spooky indeed.  It\'s difficult to find your way amongst all\nthis chaos.<z>\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9077,0,0,0,'The Attic','<k>  The attic before you stretches away into the gloomy darkness.\nShadows dance upon the walls from the flickering <o>flame<z> <k>of a\nsmall candle perched in the wall.  A wooden rail is here to protect you\nfrom a debilitating if not fatal  fall to the crowded Nave below.  This\narea is filled with boxes and crates.  An abundance of cobwebs make the\nroom feel spooky indeed.  It\'s difficult to find your way amongst all\nthis chaos.<z>\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9078,0,0,0,'The Attic','<k>  The attic before you stretches away into the gloomy darkness.\nShadows dance upon the walls from the flickering <o>flame<z> <k>of a\nsmall candle perched in the wall.  A wooden rail is here to protect you\nfrom a debilitating if not fatal  fall to the crowded Nave below.  This\narea is filled with boxes and crates.  An abundance of cobwebs make the\nroom feel spooky indeed.  It\'s difficult to find your way amongst all\nthis chaos.  Where was that door?<z>\n',67,131084,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9079,0,0,0,'The Attic','<k>  The attic before you stretches away into the gloomy darkness.\nShadows dance upon the walls from the flickering <o>flame<z> <k>of a\nsmall candle perched in the wall.  A wooden rail is here to protect you\nfrom a debilitating if not fatal  fall to the crowded Nave below.  This\narea is filled with boxes and crates.  An abundance of cobwebs make the\nroom feel spooky indeed.  It\'s difficult to find your way amongst all\nthis chaos.<z>\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9080,0,0,0,'The Attic','<k>  The attic before you stretches away into the gloomy darkness.\nShadows dance upon the walls from the flickering <o>flame<z> <k>of a\nsmall candle perched in the wall.  A wooden rail is here to protect you\nfrom a debilitating if not fatal  fall to the crowded Nave below.  This\narea is filled with boxes and crates.  An abundance of cobwebs make the\nroom feel spooky indeed.  It\'s difficult to find your way amongst all\nthis chaos.<z>\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9081,0,0,0,'<R>A<z> <Y>Dangerous<z> <R>Catwalk<z>','<k>   You are not sure if you can maintain your balance on this flimsy\nrope bridge.  You could maybe get better balance if you lean against the\nnorth steeple wall, but your footing is precarious at best.  If you\nhurry, you can get to the other side.  It wouldn\'t be good for your\nhealth if you lost your balance and fell.<z>\n',-1,131084,21,300,9066,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9082,0,0,0,'Upper North Steeple Tower','  The North Steeple Tower has always been blocked from the general\npublic due to the dangerous access to the roof it provides.  What used\nto be a small supply room used by the builders of this church has now\nbeen turned into a bedroom.  Dirty clothes and scraps of food litter the\nground.  The stench assails your nostrils.  It doesn\'t look like this\nroom has been cleaned in quite awhile.  A ladder leading up to a\ntrapdoor is here.  The door going to the dangerous catwalk is to your\nsouth.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9083,0,0,0,'Parapet Wall','  The low wall around the cathedral protects you from plummeting to the\nstreet below you, which would result in your certain death.  The walkway\nis narrow and serves as a means of accessing the elevated heights of the\ncathedral in case of repairs.  You could probably see the different\nsections of street from way up here if you squinted your eyes a little.\n',67,131072,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9084,0,0,0,'Overlooking West Main Street & Commonwealth Lane','  This vantage point is magnificent.  Looking around you can see all the\nhard work that went into building this monument to the Almighty.  The\ngraceful, arched shaped flying buttresses that support the awesome\nweight of this structure sweep down to the street level.  Stone\ngargoyles are perched here protecting the church from evil, so legend\nhas it, but also to serve as gutters, diverting the water runoff and\npreserving the exterior from the elements.  From here you can look down\nupon the little people of our fair city.  You can probably see what\'s\ngoing on down below at the other corners of the church as well.\n',67,131072,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9085,0,0,0,'Parapet Wall',' The low wall around the cathedral protects you from plummeting to the\nstreet below you, which would result in your certain death.  The walkway\nis narrow and serves as a means of accessing the elevated heights of the\ncathedral in case of repairs.  A sturdy oak door leads back into the\nattic.  You could probably see the different sections of street from way\nup here if you squinted your eyes a little.\n',67,131072,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9086,0,0,0,'Overlooking Center Square','  This vantage point is magnificent.  Looking around you can see all the\nhard work that went into building this monument to the Almighty.  The\ngraceful, arched shaped flying buttresses that support the awesome\nweight of this structure sweep down to the street level.  Stone\ngargoyles are perched here protecting the church from evil, so legend\nhas it, but also to serve as gutters, diverting the water runoff and\npreserving the exterior from the elements.  From here you can look down\nupon the little people of our fair city.  You can probably see what\'s\ngoing on down below at the other corners of the church as well.\n',67,131072,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9087,0,0,0,'Parapet Wall',' The low wall around the cathedral protects you from plummeting to the\nstreet below you, which would result in your certain death.  The walkway\nis narrow and serves as a means of accessing the elevated heights of the\ncathedral in case of repairs.  You could probably see the different\nsections of street from way up here if you squinted your eyes a little.\n',67,131072,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9088,0,0,0,'Parapet Wall',' The low wall around the cathedral protects you from plummeting to the\nstreet below you, which would result in your certain death.  The walkway\nis narrow and serves as a means of accessing the elevated heights of the\ncathedral in case of repairs.  You could probably see the different\nsections of street from way up here if you squinted your eyes a little.\n',67,131072,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9089,0,0,0,'Overlooking North Main & Oak Street','  This vantage point is magnificent.  Looking around you can see all the\nhard work that went into building this monument to the Almighty.  The\ngraceful, arched shaped flying buttresses that support the awesome\nweight of this structure sweep down to the street level.  Stone\ngargoyles are perched here protecting the church from evil, so legend\nhas it, but also to serve as gutters, diverting the water runoff and\npreserving the exterior from the elements.  From here you can look down\nupon the little people of our fair city.  You can probably see what\'s\ngoing on down below at the other corners of the church as well.\n',67,131072,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9090,0,0,0,'Parapet Wall','  The low wall around the cathedral protects you from plummeting to the\nstreet below you, which would result in your certain death.  The walkway\nis narrow and serves as a means of accessing the elevated heights of the\ncathedral in case of repairs.  You could probably see the different\nsections of street from way up here if you squinted your eyes a little.\nA concealed door is here.\n',67,131072,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9091,0,0,0,'Overlooking Oak Street & Commonwealth Lane','  This vantage point is magnificent.  Looking around you can see all the\nhard work that went into building this monument to the Almighty.  The\ngraceful, arched shaped flying buttresses that support the awesome\nweight of this structure sweep down to the street level.  Stone\ngargoyles are perched here protecting the church from evil, so legend\nhas it, but also to serve as gutters, diverting the water runoff and\npreserving the exterior from the elements.  From here you can look down\nupon the little people of our fair city.  You can probably see what\'s\ngoing on down below at the other corners of the church as well.\n',67,131072,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9092,0,0,0,'<R>Top of the North Steeple Tower<1>','<r>  This room is covered in BLOOD! Flesh, scraps and bones litter every\ncorner.  Unlike the other steeple towers, there is no view.  All the\nwindows have been boarded up to prevent anyone from down below seeing\nthe ghastly atrocities that are performed here.  A pile of rubble blocks\nwhat looks to be the way out to the roof.  You\'re not sure however that\nif you find a way through it if you will be able to go back.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(9093,0,0,0,'Roof of the Cathedral','  A strange wind buffets you where you stand.  You are so high up now\nthat to fall would mean certain death.  The city down below is abuzz\nwith activity but what concerns you most right now is the nasty snarl\ncoming from the other side of the roof.  The mass or rubble behind you\nis shaped and formed in such a way as to prevent passage back into the\nchurch.  The sharp jagged edges of the rocks would surely cut you to\nshreds.  You can\'t help but feel the strange mixture of energy and power\nradiating from the south in a way that disrupts the normal course of\nlife and its mysteries as you know them.  You might be in trouble.\n',67,141636,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9094,0,0,0,'Roof of the Cathedral','  The wind has abated a little.  Although the weather is as it usually\nis this time of year.  It almost feels as if you are near the eye of a\nstorm.  It could also be the strange electrical crackling sound you hear\nall around that makes every hair on your body stand on end as well.  The\ncity down below is abuzz with activity.  A strange pulsating glow\nemanates from the south.\n',67,141632,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9095,0,0,0,'Roof of the Cathedral','  The source of the strange sound and odd glow comes from this room.\nEverywhere you look is crammed with miscellaneous parts and tools of a\ncurious design and nature.  A large, jet black, oval arch inscribed with\nglowing red runes into it dominates the center of this end of the roof.\nYou can see the back side of the east and west steeple towers from here.\n',67,141632,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9096,0,0,0,'Top of the West Steeple Tower','  Wow!  The view up here is incredible.  From here you can see most of\nthe southern part of the city.  Center Square is to your right and\nappears to show a lot of activity but it is hard to tell from this far\naway.  Various shops and buildings fill your sights to the south.  You\ncan make out the tips of the treetops of a huge forest to your west.\nThe steps behind you will bring you back to the attic level of the\nchurch.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9097,0,0,0,'Top of the East Steeple Tower','  Wow!  The view up here is incredible.  From here you can see most of\nthe southern part of the city.  Center Square is to your lower right and\nit\'s filled with people today.  Various shops and buildings fill your\nsights to the south.  To your east you can see the towers of the King\'s\ncastle.  The steps behind you will bring you back to the attic level of\nthe church.\n',67,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9098,0,0,0,'Parapet Wall','The low wall around the cathedral protects you from plummeting to the\nstreet below you, which would result in your certain death.  The walkway\nis narrow and serves as a means of accessing the elevated heights of the\ncathedral in case of repairs.  The North Steeple wall blocks your\npassage to the east.  You could probably see the different sections of\nstreet from way up here if you squinted your eyes a little.  In the\ndistance you hear a frightful snarl.\n',67,131072,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9099,0,0,0,'Parapet Wall',' The low wall around the cathedral protects you from plummeting to the\nstreet below you, which would result in your certain death.  The walkway\nis narrow and serves as a means of accessing the elevated heights of the\ncathedral in case of repairs.  The North Steeple wall blocks your\npassage to the west.  You could probably see the different sections of\nstreet from way up here if you squinted your eyes a little.  In the\ndistance you hear a frightful snarl.\n',67,131072,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9100,0,0,0,'Overlooking the Ocean on a Slippery Dock','Surf sprays wildly, soaking the rickety dock that juts out over the water.\nAs the ocean crashes to the south and west, the poorly constructed dock\nwobbles and shakes, threatening to collapse at anytime.  The rising\nvapors enshroud everything in a nebulous haze.\n',-1,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9101,0,0,0,'Overlooking the Ocean on a Slippery Dock','Surf sprays wildly, soaking the rickety dock that juts out over the water.\nAs the ocean crashes to the south and east, the poorly constructed dock\nwobbles and shakes, threatening to collapse at anytime.  The rising\nvapors enshroud everything in a nebulous haze.\n',-1,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9102,0,0,0,'On a Slippery Dock','The dock wobbles and shakes indicating doubtable safety of structure.  The\nocean crashes to the west creating a thick obscuring mist.\n',-1,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9103,0,0,0,'On a Slippery Dock','The dock wobbles and shakes indicating doubtable safety of structure.  The\nocean crashes to the east creating a thick obscuring mist.\n',-1,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9104,0,0,0,'On a Slippery Dock','The dock wobbles and shakes indicating doubtable safety of structure.  The\nocean crashes to the west creating a thick obscuring mist.\n',-1,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9105,0,0,0,'On a Slippery Dock','The dock wobbles and shakes indicating doubtable safety of structure.  The\nocean crashes to the east creating a thick obscuring mist.\n',-1,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9106,0,0,0,'On a Slippery Dock','The dock trembles slightly, it seems almost secure.  It is very hard to\nsee through the mist, but you can hear the sounds of village life to\nthe north.  The ocean crashes to the west.\n',59,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9107,0,0,0,'On a Slippery Dock','The dock trembles slightly, it seems almost secure.  It is very hard to\nsee through the mist, but you can hear the sounds of village life to\nthe north.  The ocean crashes to the east.\n',59,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9108,0,0,0,'End of a Slippery Dock','This is the end of a slippery dock.  To the north you can hear the sounds\nof villagers, the smells wafting towards you are mixed, perfume of lush\ntropical growth, and an acrid odor found only in decrepit places long\nneglected and filthy.  The beach extends to the northwest, the ocean\ncrashes to the west.\n',59,131076,54,0,0,0,0,0,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9109,0,0,0,'End of a Slippery Dock','This is the end of a slippery dock.  To the north you can hear the sounds\nof villagers, the smells wafting towards you are mixed, perfume of lush\ntropical growth and an acrid odor, found only in places long neglected\nand filthy.  The ocean crashes to the east.\n',59,131076,54,0,0,0,0,0,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9110,0,0,0,'A Beach Enveloped in Mist','The crunch under your feet indicates the presence of many shells.  Each\ncrash of the surf sends up fine droplets of spray, adding to the thickness\nof the fog.  Tropical plants abound somewhere, rustling leaves can be\nheard, their aromas fragrant and delightful fill your head.  The occasional\nshadow of what must be a surfer can be seen riding the dangerous waves.\nOff in the distance you can hear the sounds of the village, slow and lazy.\n',59,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9111,0,0,0,'A Lazy Village','Islanders loll in unhappy bewilderment, their huts lean precariously about.\nTropical plants grow sadly in few places, refuse is strewn all over.  You\ncan just make out a rickety looking dock to the south.\n',59,131072,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9112,0,0,0,'A Lazy Village','Islanders loll in unhappy bewilderment, their huts lean precariously about.\nRefuse is strewn all over.  To the south you can just make out the end of a\nrickety looking dock.\n',59,131072,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9113,0,0,0,'Hut of an Island Witchdoctor','Glass baubles hang from the ceiling, herbs dry hanging between them.\nThings seem in good order here.  The hut seems only slightly dangerous, old\nfish bones are swept into a neat pile in the corner.\n',59,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9114,0,0,0,'A Beach Enveloped in Mist','The crunch under your feet indicates the presence of many shells.  Each\ncrash of the surf sends up droplets of fine spray, adding to the thickness\nof the fog.  Tropical plants abound somewhere, rustling leaves can be\nheard, fragrant aromas delight your senses.  The occasional shadow of what\nmust be a surfer can be seen riding the dangerous waves.  The sounds of a\nlazy village seem loud.\n',59,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9115,0,0,0,'A Lazy Village','Islanders loll in unhappy bewilderment, their huts lean precariously about.\nTropical plants grow sadly in a few places, refuse is strewn all over.\n',59,131072,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9116,0,0,0,'The Center of a Lazy Village','This is the center of a lazy village.  Islanders and their bedraggled\nchildren loll about in bewilderment.  No one here seems happy, expending\nonly the effort to grumble and occasionally fight.  Old fish bones are\nscattered about, decaying in the humid air, a delightful snack for the\nventuresome.  Around the village, huts lean in various states of\nprecariousness.  Thick odorous vapors fill the air.\n',59,131072,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9117,0,0,0,'A Lazy Village','Islanders loll in unhappy bewilderment, their huts lean precariously about.\nTropical plants grow sadly in a few places, refuse is strewn all over.\n',59,131076,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9118,0,0,0,'A Beach Enveloped in Mist','The beach is pretty smooth, you occasionally kick a shell.  The sounds\nfilling your ears are of villagers talking, children crying, and an\noccasional bird screeching to make known its presence.  The air is thick\nwith fog, but you can just make out some of the lush greenery inland.  A\nshort walk to the east leads into the village, but the odors emanating from\nit, in sharp contrast to the nature here, make this a dubious journey.\n',59,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9119,0,0,0,'A Lazy Village','Islanders loll in unhappy bewilderment, their huts lean precariously about.\nTropical plants grow between the huts, there is refuse strewn all over.\n',59,131076,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9120,0,0,0,'A Lazy Village','Islanders loll about in unhappy bewilderment, their huts lean precariously\nabout.  There are tropical plants here, but not many.  Refuse is strewn all\nover, the air is thick with fog.\n',59,131072,43,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9121,0,0,0,'The Hovel of an Island King','The hovel of an island king is cluttered with old decaying fish bones .  The\nroof sags dangerously in the center, threatening collapse.\n',59,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(9122,0,0,0,'Before an Ancient Banyan Tree','This tree is huge!  Towering over 70 feet above you, branches covered in\nheart shaped leaves send down shoots that will eventually root in the\nground and form new trunks.  There is a hard pathway under the tree to the\nnortheast.  A lazy village is to the west.\n',59,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9123,0,0,0,'Under an Ancient Banyan Tree','You are walking under an ancient banyan tree.  Roots reach down from the\nlimbs of the tree.  There are some narrow pathways between the roots.  In\nall its seeming seclusion, the path is hardened by use.\n',59,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9124,0,0,0,'Under an Ancient Banyan Tree','You are walking under an ancient banyan tree.  Roots reach down from the\nlimbs of the tree.  There are some narrow pathways between the roots.  In\nall its seeming seclusion, the path is hardened by use.\n',59,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9125,0,0,0,'Under an Ancient Banyan Tree','You are walking under an ancient banyan tree.  Roots reach down from the\nlimbs of the tree.  There are some narrow pathways between the roots.  In\nall its seeming seclusion, the path is hardened by use.\n',59,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9126,0,0,0,'Under an Ancient Banyan Tree','You are walking under an ancient banyan tree.  Roots reach down from the\nlimbs of the tree.  There are some narrow pathways between the roots.  In\nall its seeming seclusion, the path is hardened by use.\n',59,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9127,0,0,0,'A Nasty Smugglers Hideout','A place for smugglers to trade in illicit goods, there is a long bar along\nthe southern wall, chairs are scattered about.  The entrance to a smugglers\nhideout is to the north.\n',59,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(9128,0,0,0,'Under an Ancient Banyan Tree','You are walking under an ancient banyan tree.  Shoots reach down from the\nlimbs of the tree, rooting in to the ground.  The pathway is hardened by\nuse and stops short near the base of a shoot that almost reaches the\nground.\n',59,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9129,0,0,0,'Under an Ancient Banyan Tree','You are walking under an ancient banyan tree.  Shoots reach down from the\nlimbs of the tree, rooting in to the ground.  The pathway is hardened by\nuse and stops short near the base of a shoot that almost reaches the\nground.\n',59,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9130,0,0,0,'Under an Ancient Banyan Tree','You are walking under an ancient banyan tree.  Roots reach down from the\nlimbs of the tree.  There are some narrow pathways between the roots.  In\nall its seeming seclusion, the path is hardened by use.\n',59,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9131,0,0,0,'Under an Ancient Banyan Tree','The roots of an ancient banyon tree grow close together here.  The main\nstructure of the tree is decayed, it seems to be supported by the younger\nouter roots.  The path is hardened here and seems to go under a crumbling\nroot at the base of the tree.\n',59,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9132,0,0,0,'Entrance to a Nasty Smugglers Hideout','This is the entrance to a nasty smugglers hideout.  The walls are made of\ncrumbling dirt, held in place by the roots of the ancient banyon tree above.\nThere is a rudely constructed door to the east, another room to the south.\nA root dangles above over the entrance.\n',59,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(9133,0,0,0,'A Nasty Smugglers Private Quarters','Exotic rugs hang on the root structure, covering the dirt walls.  Strange\nand beautiful treasures are scattered about the room.  A large mahogany bed\nstands in the eastern corner.  There is a rudely constructed door to the\nwest.\n',59,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9134,0,0,0,'An Island Path','This path leads through heavy growth.  Strange plants are abundant, a\nbeautiful masquerade, these plants could be deadly.  To the south,\nsounds of a village, to the north, the promise of bliss.\n',59,131076,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9135,0,0,0,'An Island Path','This path leads through heavy growth, strange plants are abundant.\nWelcoming flowers scent the humid air, insects and birds, accompanied\nonly by the distant crashing of the ocean serenade you.  You feel peaceful\nhere, relaxed.\n',59,164016,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9136,0,0,0,'An Island Path','This path leads through heavy growth, strange plants are abundant.  From\nthe south come blissful sounds of nature, from the north a strange din, not\nall together pleasant.\n',59,131076,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9137,0,0,0,'Before an Island Pavilion','This path leads through heavy growth, strange plants are abundant.  To the\nnorthwest is the entrance to a pavilion, there is a sign above the\nentrance.  From the south come the sounds of nature, blissful and calming.\n',59,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9138,0,0,0,'Entrance to Barmek\'s Delicatescent','You are at the entrance to Barmek\'s Delicatescent.  This place is odd, the\nplates look stunning till you take another glance.  The tables are laden\nwith a Barmecidal feast.\n',59,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(9139,0,0,0,'Inside Barmek\'s Delicatescent','This place is odd, the plates look stunning till you take another glance.\nThe tables are laden with a Barmecidal feast.\n',59,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(9140,0,0,0,'Inside Barmek\'s Delicatescent','This place is odd, the plates look stunning till you take another glance.\nThe tables are laden with a Barmecidal feast.\n',59,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(9141,0,0,0,'A Low Stage in Barmek\'s Delicatescent','This is a low stage where the nightly entertainment takes place.\n',59,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(9142,0,0,0,'Inside Barmek\'s Delicatescent','This place is odd, the plates look stunning till you take another glance.\nThe tables are laden with a Barmecidal feast.\n',59,131084,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(9143,0,0,0,'Inside Barmek\'s Delicatescent','This place is odd, the plates look stunning till you take another glance.\nThe tables are laden with a Barmecidal feast.  There is a door to the east.\n',59,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(9144,0,0,0,'The Kitchen at Barmek\'s','The kitchen is spotless.  There are no signs of food preparation to be seen\nanywhere.  There are doors to the east and the west.\n',59,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(9145,0,0,0,'A Narrow Seawall','The seawall stretches to the east.  The ocean whips around you, spraying\nfine mist throughout the air.  There is a door to the west.  It is very\nhard to see.\n',59,131076,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9146,0,0,0,'A Narrow Seawall','The seawall stretches to the east and the west.  The ocean whips around\nyou, spraying fine mist throughout the air.  It is very hard to see.\n',59,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9147,0,0,0,'A Narrow Seawall','The seawall stretches to the east and the west.  The ocean whips around\nyou, spraying fine mist throughout the air.  It is very hard to see.\n',59,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9148,0,0,0,'A Narrow Seawall','The seawall stretches to the west.  The ocean whips around you, spraying\nfine mist throughout the air.  It is very hard to see.\n',59,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9150,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','You amble along the path, abundant foliage brushes you, the warm buzz\nof hidden insects whisper quietly.  The ocean can be heard crashing to\nthe south, salting the air with its lightly blowing breezes.\n',59,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9151,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','You amble along the path, abundant foliage brushes you, the warm buzz\nof hidden insects whisper quietly.  The ocean can be heard crashing to\nthe south, salting the air with its lightly blowing breezes.\n',59,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9152,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','You amble along the path, abundant foliage brushes you, the warm buzz\nof hidden insects whisper quietly.  The ocean can be heard crashing to\nthe south, salting the air with its lightly blowing breezes.  To the\nnortheast the trees gain height as the path moves inland.\n',59,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9153,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','You stumble over the roots and leaves of the rich tropical plants hanging\nover the trail.  The smell of the ocean drifts saltily through the jungle\nfrom the south.\n',59,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9154,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','You amble along the path, abundant foliage brushes you, the warm buzz\nof hidden insects whisper quietly.  The trees gain height as the path\nmoves inland.\n',59,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9155,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','A refreshing warm breeze tousles your hair.  Plants line the sandy path.  A\ndull roar, the ocean crashes in the distance.\n',59,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9156,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','A refreshing warm breeze tousles your hair.  Plants line the sandy path.  A\ndull roar, the ocean crashes in the distance.\n',59,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9157,0,0,0,'A Windwhipped Beach','The beach is obscured by mist.  The jubilant ocean throws spray all around\nas it assaults the shoreline, the salty breeze blowing merrily across the\nsand.\n',59,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9158,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','You traipse through the jungle, the varied flora brushes against you.  The\nwarble of island wildlife, the rustling of leaves, fill the fragrant air.\n',59,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9159,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','You walk along a heavily overgrown path.  Tropical plants invade the trail,\ncausing progress to be slow.  The path seems to widen slightly to the\nnortheast, and meanders casually to the south.\n',59,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9160,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','Tall trees tower above you, their branches a host to sounds and scents\nthat waft down to tickle your senses.  Light filtered by the abundant\ngreenery, casts emerald rays about the trail.\n',59,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9161,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','A refreshing warm breeze tousles your hair.  Plants line the now sandy\npath.\n',59,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9162,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','A refreshing warm breeze tousles your hair, fine droplets of water dampen\nyou as the oceans spray blows into the jungle.  A few plants line the sandy\npath.  The ocean crashes off to the east.\n',59,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9163,0,0,0,'A Windwhipped Beach','The beach is obscured by mist.  The jubilant ocean throws spray all around\nas it assaults the shoreline, the salty breeze blowing merrily across the\nsand.\n',59,131076,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9164,0,0,0,'A Mist Enshrouded Beach','The beach is obscured by mist.  The jubilant ocean sprays all around, the\nwind whips salty drops into your eyes, nose and mouth.  From the east comes\nthe heady scent of tropical plants.\n',59,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9165,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','You walk along a heavily overgrown path.  Tropical plants hang over the\ntrail, slowing your movement through this wild place.\n',59,131076,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9166,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','A lovely lagoon can be seen to the north, fragrant lotus flowers bloom\nprofusely.  Birds cheerily chirp in the distance, the peaceful drone of\nflying insects lulls you.\n',59,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9167,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','Tall trees tower above you, their branches a host to sounds and scents that\nwaft down to tickle your senses.  Light filtered by the abundant greenery\ncasts emerald rays about the trail.\n',59,131076,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9168,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','Tall trees tower above you, their branches a host to sounds and scents\nthat waft down to tickle your senses.  Light filtered by the abundant\ngreenery, casts emerald rays about the trail.  The path thins to the south,\nto the east the path borders the inland forests.\n',59,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9169,0,0,0,'A Lush Jungle Path','The path is lushly bordered by the tall trees and thick tropical flora\nof the inland forests.  The heavy musk of exotic flowers, mingle\ndeliciously with a cacophony of tropical wildlife, a dreamy sweet\nnectar to the spirit.\n',59,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
