(9296,0,0,0,'A Rocky Cape','Sharply jutting rocks create a dangerous path.  The ocean breezes blow\nacross the narrow cape.\n',59,131072,50,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9297,0,0,0,'A Rocky Cape','Sharply jutting rocks create a dangerous path.  Immediately to the\nnorth is a soggy rice paddy, the cape continues narrowly to the west.\n',59,131072,50,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9298,0,0,0,'A Rocky Cape','Sharply jutting rocks create a dangerous path.  The ocean breezes blow\nacross the narrow cape.\n',59,131072,50,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9299,0,0,0,'A Rocky Cape','Sharply jutting rocks create a dangerous path.  The ocean breezes blow\nacross the narrow cape.\n',59,131072,50,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9300,52,-5,0,'Road through the Badlands','   You are on a hard dirt road that snakes off into the distance.  All\naround you are scraggly bushes, upshoots of rock, and seemingly bottom-\nless crevices.  The road continues into the Badlands to the north, while\nsouthwest of here lies an ancient pass through the Sympathians.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9301,52,-4,0,'Road through the Badlands','   You are on a hard dirt road that snakes off into the distance.  All\naround you are scraggly bushes, upshoots of rock, and seemingly bottom-\nless crevices.  The road continues into the Badlands to the north, and out\nof the Badlands to the south.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9302,53,-4,0,'Off the Road through the Badlands','   You are in the brush off the side of the dirt road that runs though\nthe Badlands.  The uneven ground is made of broken stone and sand.  The\nbrush seems passable to the north and east.  The road lies to the west\nand northwest.  Your sight to the northeast is blocked by a huge outcropping\nof rock which seems impassable.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9303,54,-4,0,'The Badlands','   You are in the harsh environment known to many as the Badlands.  Because\nof the rock and gravel surface of the land, hardly anything will grow here.\nAll around you are scraggly bushes and huge outcroppings of rock, which\nsurround you in almost all directions.  To the north you see a huge rock\nformation that towers over you.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9304,52,-3,0,'Road through the Badlands','   You are on a hard dirt road that snakes off into the distance.  All\naround you are scraggly bushes, upshoots of rock, and seemingly bottom-\nless crevices.  The road continues into the Badlands to the north, and out\nthe Badlands to the south.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9305,53,-3,0,'Off the Road through the Badlands','   Although you are not to far from the hard dirt road that passes though\nthe Badlands, the brush and rocks have already prevented passage to the\nnortheast, east, and southeast.  You can see the road that leads to and\nfrom the badlands to the west, and a towering formation of rock to your\neast.  The Badlands continue to the north and south.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9306,55,-3,0,'The Badlands','   You are in the harsh environment that is know to many as the Badlands.\nLittle can grow here due to the rocky, broken surface of the land.  All\naround you are scraggly bushes, and large outcroppings of rock.  The\nBadlands continue to the northeast, east, and southwest.  A large formation\nof rock towers over you to the north.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9307,56,-3,0,'The Badlands','   You are in the harsh environment know to many as the Badlands.  All\naround you are large outcroppings of stone, blocking all passage except\nto the north and west.  A predominant formation of rocks lies to your\nnorthwest.  This area seems to have even less growth, and the terrain\nis slowly becoming harder and harder to pass.  To the east is a large,\nodd looking mound.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9308,52,-2,0,'Road through the Badlands','   You are on a hard dirt road that snakes off into the distance.  All\naround you are scraggly bushes, upshoots of rock, and seemingly bottom-\nless crevices.  The road continues into the Badlands to the northeast, and\nout of the Badlands to the south.  The brush and the rocks seem to thin\nto the north and west.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9309,53,-2,0,'Off the Road through the Badlands','   Although you are not to far from the road that travels across the\nBadlands, you are already surrounded by brush and outcroppings of rock\nthat halt your movement.  To the southeast a large formation of rocks\ntower above you.  The Badlands continue to the northeast and south,\nand the hard dirt road lies to the north and east.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9310,56,-2,0,'The Badlands','   Large rocks shoot up all around you as you find yourself now deep\ninto the heart of what are know as the Badlands.  The large rock formations\nto the east and west prevent any passage except in northern, and southern\ndirections.  The terrain is very bare and seems to be even more dry and\ncracked.  As you look off to the north, you wonder if these Badlands ever\nend.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9312,52,-1,0,'Overlooking the Road','   You stand looking down at the Badlands Road that stretches out\nas far as you can see.  The little terrace you are standing on seems\nto be swept clean, yet there are no signs of anyone else but you\nbeing there.  A small path leads east down to the road.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9313,53,-1,0,'Road through the Badlands','   You are on a hard dirt road that snakes off into the distance.  All\naround you are scraggly bushes, upshoots of rock, and seemingly bottom-\nless crevices.  The road continues though the Badlands to the northeast and\nsouthwest.  To the southeast you see a large outcropping of rocks that\nseem to be impassable.  The rocks and brush seem to thin to the north,\nnorthwest, and west.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9314,54,-1,0,'Off the Road through the Badlands','   Although you are not far from the road that travels across the\nBadlands, the rocks and heavy brush have already made travel difficult.\nThe rock to the north curves around a small crag that lies to the northeast.\nTravel to the south is blocked by an enormous outcrop of rock.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9315,55,-1,0,'Between the Rocks and a Crag','   The jagged rocks and scraggly brush of the Badlands surround you in\nevery direction.  To the north is a small crag that prevents passage.\nYour sight to the south is blocked by an enormous outcrop of rock that\nseems to be unclimbable.  The road can be seen to the west.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9316,56,-1,0,'Before the Rocks and the Crag','   The rocks and brush of the Badlands surround you in every direction.\nThe rocky ground and mild climate prove to make travel difficult.  A crag\nto the northwest and an outcrop of rock to the southwest block your path.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9317,57,-1,0,'The Badlands','   The rocks and brush of the Badlands surround you in every direction.\nThe rocky ground and mild climate prove to make travel here difficult.\nThe path continues toward the road to the north, and deeper into the\nBadlands to the west and southwest.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9318,52,0,0,'Off the Road through the Badlands','  To the southeast you can see the Badlands Road stretching\nacross the barren landscape.  The ground slopes gently away to\nthe west and becomes rougher.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9319,53,0,0,'On the Edge of the Road through the Badlands','  The road cuts through the empty landscape just to the southwest\nof where you are standing.  To the north you can make out the\nmouth of an enormous canyon that stretches for leagues to the northeast.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9320,54,0,0,'Near a Bend in the Badlands Road','   You are on a hard dirt road that snakes off into the distance.  All\naround you are scraggly bushes, upshoots of rock, and seemingly bottom-\nless crevices.  The road continues though the Badlands to the north and\nsouthwest.  There is a small crag to the east that seems to be impassable.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9321,56,0,0,'Before the Road and Near a Crag','   Although you are not far from the road that travels across the\nBadlands, the tortured terrain make passage difficult.  To the west\nis a small crag.  The hard dirt road lies to the north.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9322,57,0,0,'The Badlands','   Jagged rocks and heavy brush surround you in almost every direction.\nThis tortured environment and the mild climate make travel here difficult.\nThe Uneven ground to the east seems impassable.  The badlands open up more\nto the south and southwest.  The hard dirt road that leads through the\nBadlands lies to the north.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9323,54,1,0,'Bend in the Road through the Badlands','   You are on a hard dirt road that snakes off into the distance.  All\naround you are scraggly bushes, upshoots of rock, and seemingly bottom-\nless crevices.  The road continues to the east and south as it avoids a small\ncrag that lies to the southeast.  To the northwest you can see a vast\ncanyon that seems to go off into the horizon.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9324,55,1,0,'Near a Bend in the Badlands Road','   You are on a hard dirt road that snakes off into the distance.  All\naround you are scraggly bushes, upshoots of rock, and seemingly bottom-\nless crevices.  All of these things give you an eerie sense on desolation.\nThe road continues to the west and east.  There is a small bend in the\nroad to the east due to a small crag that lies directly south.  To the\nnorthwest is a vast canyon that seems to stretch off to the horizon.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9325,56,1,0,'Road through the Badlands','   You are on a hard dirt road that snakes off into the distance.  All\naround you are scraggly bushes, upshoots of rock, and seemingly bottom-\nless crevices.  All of these things give you an eerie sense of desolation.\nThe road continues to the northeast and west.  The harsh terrain of the\nBadlands seems to thin a bit to the south.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9326,57,1,0,'Off the Road through the Badlands','   Although you are not far from the hard dirt road that leads through\nthe Badlands, the uneven, rocky ground has already made travel difficult.\nThe road lies to the north and west, while the Badlands thin out to the\nsouthwest and south.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9327,56,2,0,'Off the Road through the Badlands','   Although you are not far from the hard dirt road that leads through\nthe Badlands, the jagged, uneven, rocky surface of the area has made\ntravel impossible.  To the east and south lies the road.  To the north\nis a vast canyon that seems to stretch off into the horizon.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9328,57,2,0,'Near A bend in the Badlands Road','   You are on a hard dirt road that leads through the Badlands.  The road\nprovides a clear path through this desolate environment.  The uneven, rocky\nground makes travel off the road difficult.  The only plant life visible\nare scraggly, dried brush that grow between the enormous upshoots of rock.\nThe road continues to the northeast and southwest.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9329,58,2,0,'Bend in the Badlands Road','   Even though you are not far from the road that travels through the\nBadlands, the heavy brush and large rocks make passage difficult.  The\nground is covered with broken rock and the remains of scraggly brush.\nThe hard dirt road is to the north and west.  A vast, mist shrouded\ncanyon lies far to the northwest.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9330,57,3,0,'Off the Road through the Badlands','   Even though you are not far from the road that travels through the\nBadlands, the heavy brush and large rocks make passage difficult.  The\nground is covered with broken rock and the remains of scraggly brush.\nThe hard dirt road is to the east and south.  A vast, mist shrouded\ncanyon lies to the northwest.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9331,58,3,0,'Bend in the Road through the Badlands','   You are on a hard dirt road that leads through the Badlands.  The road\nprovides a clear path through this desolate environment.  The uneven, rocky\nground makes travel off the road difficult.  The only plant life visible\nare scraggly, dried brush that grow between the enormous upshoots of rock.\nThe road continues to the north and southwest.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9332,58,4,0,'On the Road Before a Small Bridge','   You are on a hard dirt road that leads through the Badlands.  The road\nprovides a clear path through this desolate environment.  The uneven, rocky\nground makes travel off the road difficult.  The only plant life visible\nare scraggly, dried brush that grow between the enormous upshoots of rock.\nThere is a bridge that crosses a small crag to the north.  The road continues\nto the south.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9333,58,5,0,'On a Small Bridge','  You are on a small bridge that crosses a small crevice.  Strong planks\nof timber are used in its construction, and they make a curiously hollow\nTHUNK as you step.  The bridge continues to the north, and the road\ncontinues to the south.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9334,58,6,0,'On a Small Bridge','   You are on a small bridge that crosses a small crag.  The bridge is\nmade out of timber that must have been imported from the Haon-Dor, or\nArden forests.  The bridge seems well built and will sustain your weight.\nThe bridge continues to the south, and the road continues to the north.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9335,58,7,0,'Before a Bridge','   You are on a hard dirt road that leads through the Badlands.  The road\nprovides a clear path through this desolate environment.  The uneven, rocky\nground makes travel off the road difficult.  The only plant life visible\nare scraggly, dried brush that grow between the enormous upshoots of rock.\nThe road continues to the north and south.  There is a bridge which\ncrosses a small crag to the south.  You can see a vast, mist shrouded\ncanyon to the east.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9336,58,8,0,'Road through the Badlands','   You are on a hard dirt road that leads through the Badlands.  The road\nprovides a clear path through this desolate environment.  The uneven, rocky\nground makes travel off the road difficult.  The only plant life visible\nare scraggly, dried brush that grow between the enormous upshoots of rock.\nThe road continues to the north and south.  You can see a vast, mist\nshrouded canyon to the west.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9337,57,8,0,'Off the Road through the Badlands','   Even though you are not far from the road that travels through the\nBadlands, the heavy brush and large rocks make passage difficult.  The\nground is covered with broken rock and the remains of scraggly brush.\nTo the east is the hard dirt road.  A vast, mist shrouded canyon lies\nto the west.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9338,57,9,0,'Off the Road through the Badlands','   Even though you are not far from the road that travels through the\nBadlands, the heavy brush and large rocks make passage difficult.  The\nground is covered with broken rock and the remains of scraggly brush.\nTo the east is the hard dirt road.  A vast, mist shrouded canyon lies\nto the west.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9339,58,9,0,'Road through the Badlands','   You are on a hard dirt road that leads through the Badlands.  The road\nprovides a clear path through this desolate environment.  The uneven, rocky\nground makes travel off the road difficult.  The only plant life visible\nare scraggly, dried brush that grow between the enormous upshoots of rock.\nThe road continues to the north and south.  You can see a vast, mist\nshrouded canyon to the west.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9340,58,10,0,'Road through the Badlands','   You are on a hard dirt road that leads through the Badlands.  The road\nprovides a clear path through this desolate environment.  The uneven, rocky\nground makes travel off the road difficult.  The only plant life visible\nare scraggly, dried brush that grow between the enormous upshoots of rock.\nThe road continues to the north and south.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9341,52,11,-2,'Off the Road through the Badlands','   Even though you are not far from the road that travels through the\nBadlands, the heavy brush and large rocks make passage difficult.  The\nground is covered with broken rock and the remains of scraggly brush.\nTo the east is the hard dirt road.  A vast, mist shrouded canyon lies\nto the southwest.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9342,51,11,-2,'The Badlands','   The Badlands surround you.  Heavy brush is the only plant life growing\non this uneven, rocky ground.  Broken stones, gravel and the decayed\nremains of scraggly brush cover the ground in this desolate place.  To\nthe south is a vast, mist shrouded canyon.  A network of cliffs and\nledges leads down into the canyon to the west.  The road that travels\nthrough the Badlands lies to the east.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9343,50,11,-2,'Before the Cliffs to the Canyon','   The Badlands surround you.  Heavy brush is the only plant life growing\non this uneven, rocky ground.  Broken stones, gravel and the decayed\nremains of scraggly brush cover the ground in this desolate place.  A\nlarge pile of rocks blocks any passage to the west.  A vast, mist\nshrouded canyon lies to the south.  A large network of cliffs and ledges\nleads down into the canyon.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9344,58,11,0,'Versilard\'s Highway Near the Badlands','   You are on a hard dirt road that leads through the Badlands.  The road\nprovides a clear path through this desolate environment.  The uneven, rocky\nground makes travel off the road difficult.  The only plant life visible\nare scraggly, dried brush that grow between the enormous upshoots of rock.\nThe road continues to the north and south.\n',53,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9345,50,11,-3,'The Cliffs','   You are on a large cliff and ledge network that leads to the canyon\nfloor below.  The weathered rock surface makes for good handholds, and\nyou find the climb rather easy.\n',53,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9346,51,11,-3,'The Cliffs','   You are on a large cliff and ledge network that leads to the canyon\nfloor below.  The weathered rock surface makes for good handholds, and\nyou find the climb rather easy.\n',53,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9347,51,11,-4,'The Cliffs','   You are on a large cliff and ledge network that leads to the canyon\nfloor below.  The weathered rock surface makes for good handholds, and\nyou find the climb rather easy.\n',53,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9348,50,11,-4,'The Cliffs','   You are on a large cliff and ledge network that leads to the canyon\nfloor below.  The weathered rock surface makes for good handholds, and\nyou find the climb rather easy.\n',53,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9349,50,11,-5,'The Cliffs of the Canyon','   You are on a large cliff and ledge network that leads to the canyon\nfloor below.  The weathered rock surface makes for good handholds, and\nyou find the climb rather easy.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9350,51,-2,0,'Off the Road through the Badlands','   Although you are not to far from the hard dirt road that travels into\nand out of what are known as the Badlands, the ground had already become\nlittered with brush and upshoots of rock that impede any travel to the north\nand south.  The Badlands continue to the east, and a large formation of\nrocks can be seen to the southwest.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9351,50,-2,0,'The Badlands','   You are almost completely surrounded by upshoot of rock that seem\nto jet up from everywhere.  The ground is composed of gravel and weathered\nchips of the rocks that enclose you.  To the east lies the road that travels\nacross the Badlands.  As you gaze to the south you see an enormous\noutcrop of stone.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9352,50,-3,0,'Before a Large Rock Formation','   You are completely surrounded by large upshoots of stones that seem to\nblock all passages except to the north and west.  The area around you\nis almost bare of vegetation.  A huge rock formation lies to the south, and\nyou can pick out trails up its sides.  It looks to be bigger than any building\nin Grimhaven!\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9353,50,-3,1,'Bottom of a Large Rock Formation','   You have climbed onto one of the large rock formations that litter the\nBadlands.  The wind and rain have weathered the stone into easy handholds.\n',53,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9354,49,-3,0,'Before a Large Rock Formation','   You are completely surrounded by upshoots of rock that block almost\nall passage except to the west and east.  All most nothing grows here due\nthe the rocky nature of the soil.  To the south is a large rock formation\nthat seems to be more accessible to the east.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9355,49,-3,1,'On a Rock Formation','   A vein of rock juts out from the formation and blocks any further\nmovement across the face of the cliff.  You can see a ledge above you\nthat seems to be within easy reach.\n',53,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9356,49,-3,2,'On a Ledge','   You scramble onto the narrow ledge and peer over the side.\nWHOOPS! You scramble to grab your equipment before it falls over the\nside.  Above and below you are more small ledges that may allow\nyou to continue on the rock\'s face.\n',53,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9357,49,-3,3,'Stony Outcrop','   You have finally reached the top of the outcrop.  As you look\naround you see the broken ground of the Badlands to the northeast\nand a dirt road winding its way through them.  To the north lies\nthe entrance to a massive canyon, while to the south you can trace\na path to more civilized regions.\n   The view is impressive, but there are no other ways to go but back\nto the bottom of the outcrop.\n',53,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9358,48,-3,0,'Before Two Enormous Boulders','   Large stones jet up everywhere, the path has become even more narrow.\nThe passage is open to the north between two enormous boulders.  A large\nrock formation can be seen to the east.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9359,48,-2,0,'Between Two Enormous Boulders','   You Squeeze yourself between the two huge boulders that are on the east\nand west.  The rocks seem to be smooth and worn from constant travel.\nThe boulders seem to split apart to the north and the south.  You can see\na towering formation of rock to your southwest.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,3,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9360,48,-1,0,'Before Two Enormous Boulders','  The Badlands all around you have opened up into a small clearing.\nThe rocks and brush have given way to a grassy meadow filled with\nvegetation.  The sound of running water draws your attention to a\nsmall stream that flows nearby to the northwest.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9361,47,-1,0,'Before a Massive Boulder','   Before you sits a tremendous boulder.  You wonder what could\nhave been strong enough to move it here.  It sits blocking the\npath to the south.  To the north, a stream bubbles along towards\nthe northeast corner of the clearing.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9362,50,-1,0,'Base of a Massive Boulder','   You come face to face with one of the largest rocks you\'ve ever\nseen.  You crane your neck back to look for the top, but all you see\nis more and more rock.  You shudder to think what you would look\nlike if it shifted and fell on you.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9363,47,0,0,'Southwest Corner of Clearing','   Cutting across the meadow is a sparkling stream.  It looks\nas if you will have to jump it to move onward.\n',53,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9364,48,0,0,'Grassy Knoll','   You climb to the top of a small hill and peer around this\nunusual clearing.  A stream cuts its way across the Badlands\ntowards the mouth of a canyon to the northeast.  The water has\ncreated an oasis of vegetation in the barren surroundings.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9365,49,0,0,'Southeast Corner of Clearing','   There is a fine edge of grass here as the Badlands oasis ends\nand the rocky scrub takes over.  Looking around the plush meadow\nto the north and west makes you want to roll someone over in the\nclover.  A massive boulder blocks the way to the south and trails\nlead off towards the east and southeast.\n',53,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9366,50,0,0,'Narrow Rocky Path','   The path is covered with rocks ranging from pebbles to small\nboulders.  You have to squeeze your way around some of the larger\nones.  To the southwest, two huge boulders rise above the surrounding\noutcrops.  The path smoothes out to the east.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9367,51,0,0,'Off the Badlands Road','   The path seems to become smoother towards the east, and the\nground is getting higher in that direction.  To the west a large\noutcropping of rock fills your view.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9368,47,1,0,'Western Edge of the Meadow','   The meadow expands in every direction but westward where the\nrocky soil prevents any new growth.  There is the sound of running\nwater to the south and east.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9369,48,1,0,'Center of the Badland Oasis','   The small stream that forms the heart of the glade runs\nswiftly from southwest to northeast, nearly cutting the meadow in\ntwo.  The banks overhang the cool water and as you look, fish dart\nbetween the rocks that make up the stream bed.  A pool has formed behind\na bend in the stream that looks deep enough to swim in.  In the far\nbank a family of rats has dug several holes.\n',53,164016,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9370,49,1,0,'Edge of a Meadow','   The dry grass you have been walking through gets thicker, greener\nand taller towards the west.  You hear the sound or rushing water\nfrom the north and west.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9371,47,2,0,'Northwest Corner of Clearing','   The meadow becomes Badlands here.  Dry, yellow grass and scrubby\nplants grudgingly give way to the barren earth.\n',53,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9372,48,2,0,'Northern Edge of a Meadow','   The meadow ends abruptly as the grasses begin to dry out from\nlack of water.  The Badlands take over again to the north.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9373,49,2,0,'Northeast Corner of Clearing','   A large crack lets a fast flowing stream to go underground.  The\nopening seems just large enough for you to squeeze your way down into\nits depths.  To the west, a meadow has grown out of the Badlands making\nan oasis.  The barren rocky soil of the Badlands continues to the north,\nand a large canyon can be seen to the northeast.\n',53,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9374,49,2,-1,'Sliding Down an Underground River','   Arrgh...  You did not count on the crack that lead the swift\nwaters of the stream underground to be so steep.  You have no choice\nbut to go with the flow....  and that would be down!\n',53,131080,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(9375,49,2,-2,'Sliding Down an Underground River','   Arrgh...  The swirling waters drag you even further down, and\nthe incline is to steep for you to stop yourself.  You have no choice\nbut to go with the flow...  and that would be down!\n',53,131080,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(9376,49,2,-3,'A Slight Incline in the Underground River','   The underground river has slowed enough for you to make a quick\ndecision: GET OUT QUICK TO YOUR SOUTH, OR CONTINUE TO BE SUCKED IN\nBY THE RIVER TO YOUR WEST\n',53,131080,29,0,0,0,5,3,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9377,48,2,-3,'Sliding Down an Underground River to Your Doom','   Thats it, you have had it...  there is no way to stop yourself from\nfalling deeper and deeper into the darkness of the underground river.\nAll you can do is await the terrible fate that is store for you.\n',53,131080,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9378,48,2,-4,'Sliding Down an Underground River','   WOW, how long will it take you to actually reach the bottom?  Well,\nthe answer will hit you in a second.  You close your eyes as you see\nwhere the river stops going down and begins to flow out into a large\ncanyon.\n',53,131080,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9379,48,2,-5,'Outlet to the Canyon River','   The underground river pours out a hole in the wall to the east.\nThe force of the water pushes you toward it.\n',53,131080,29,0,0,0,5,1,0,150,0,'',NULL),
(9380,49,1,-3,'Narrow Ledge near the Underground River','   You found a small ledge near the south side of the underground\nriver.  The river pours out of a hole in the center of the ceiling,\nand continues to flow with great force to the west.  The face of the\nrock to the east seems to be smoother then the rest of the rock\nthat surrounds you.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9381,50,1,-3,'Underground Tunnel','   You are in a very narrow, round tunnel.  The surface of the tunnel\nis very smooth and gives the appearance of being worn and weathered.\nThe face of the rock to the west is particularly smooth and shiny.\nThe tunnel continues to the south at a slight decline down.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9382,50,0,-3,'Stone Stairs','   You on a set of natural looking stairs that could have been caused by\nthe flow of water some hundreds of years ago.  The smooth stairs lead up\ninto the darkness of a tunnel, and down to what seems to be the ground\nof the canyon.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9383,47,4,-5,'Bottom of a Natural Stone Stairs','   You are standing just inside a circular tunnel with smooth, almost\npolished walls.  You can see some natural looking stair lead up into\nthe darkness of a tunnel.  To the east is the floor of the canyon.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9384,48,4,-5,'Before a Tunnel in the Canyon','   The high walls of the canyon enclose you in every direction.  The\nsmooth, rocky canyon floor give you the impression that this canyon\nonce held a great river.  The solid, weatherbeaten rock surface shows\nthe true age of the canyon, which must have existed for hundreds of\nthousands of years.  The canyon is completely bare of any plant life.\nA small tunnel leads into the side of the canyon to the west.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9385,49,4,-5,'The Canyon Floor','   The high walls of the canyon enclose you in every direction.  The\nsmooth, rocky canyon floor give you the impression that this canyon\nonce held a great river.  The solid, weatherbeaten rock surface shows\nthe true age of the canyon, which must have existed for hundreds of\nthousands of years.  The canyon is completely bare of any plant life.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9386,49,3,-5,'Just North of the Canyon River','   The canyon floor is smooth from the constant erosion of the small\nriver that lies before you.  The river travels at a very fast speed,\nand the water seems very clear.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9387,49,2,-5,'The Canyon River','   This clear blue river flows at a very fast pace.  While it is small, it\nhas quite a strong current, that could cause problems for even the most\nexperienced of rafter.  Many men have been found on shore after traveling\nthis river, perhaps you should have thought twice before getting on it.\nThis river is fed from a small hole in the canyon wall to the west.\n',53,131072,29,0,0,0,5,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9388,49,1,-5,'Just South of the Canyon River','   The canyon floor is smooth from the constant erosion of the small\nriver that lies before you.  The river travels at a very fast speed,\nand the water seems very clear.  The canyon wall lies to the south.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9389,50,1,-5,'Just South of the Canyon River','   The canyon floor is smooth from the constant erosion of the small\nriver that lies before you.  The river travels at a very fast speed,\nand the water seems very clear.  The canyon wall lies to the south.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9390,49,3,0,'The Badlands Near an Unusual Clearing','   The harsh terrain of the Badlands seems to begin to thin out a bit.\nTo the south you can see an unusual clearing open up into a meadow of\nflowing wild grasses.  The stony surface of the Badlands prevents any\nof this vegetation to grow any further to the north.  You are once again\nsurrounded by upshoots of rock to the east and west.  The path to the\nnorth is blocked by heavy brush.\n',53,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(9391,49,4,0,'Before a Stony Pass','   The Badlands surround you and make almost all passage impossible.\nThe heavy brush and sharp upshoots of rock border the path to the east\nand west.  A large outcrop of stone allows you to travel over these\nobstacles.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(9392,49,4,1,'On a Stony Pass','   This Stony walkway, that rises above the imperfections of the Badlands,\nis smooth and worn from use.  From here you can get a good view of what is\nto come.  To the north you can see a small clearing.  To the south you can\nsee some heavy brush and large upshoots of rock.  As your gaze turns toward\nthe northeast, your mouth drops open to the sight of an enormous canyon\nthat seems to stretch off into the horizon.  The Stony Pass continues to\nthe northwest.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9393,48,5,1,'On a Stony Pass','   The Stony Pass rises above all the imperfections of the Badlands to\ncreate a smooth worn surface on which you can travel to the northern\npart of the Badlands.  To the south you see heavy brush and jagged rocks\nthat may impede your progress.  To the north is a small clearing.  As your\ngaze meets the northeast, you gasp in awe at the sight of an enormous\ncanyon that seems to go off into the horizon.  The Stony Pass gives way\nto the terrible Badlands just below your current position.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9394,48,5,0,'Just Before a Stony Pass','   Before you stands a Stony Pass that rises above the obstacles of the\nBadlands to create a make-shift land bridge.  It is worn from use and is\neasily climbable.  To the north the Badlands open up into a clearing.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9395,47,6,0,'A Clearing in the Badlands','   The rocks and brush of the Badlands have become more separated to form\na small clearing.  The gravel ground has been compacted by heavy use.\nThe clearing opens up more to the north and northeast.  To the west you\ncan see a Stony Pass rise above the terrain of the Badlands.\n',53,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9396,48,6,0,'Entrance to a Small Clearing','   Before you is a small clearing where the brush and the rocks of the\nBadlands have separated to make the terrain more passable.  The clearing\nopens more to the north, and a Stony Pass lies to your south.\n',53,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9397,49,6,0,'A Clearing in the Badlands','   The rocks and heavy brush of the Badlands have given way to a small\nclearing.  The gravel ground has been compacted due to heavy use.  The\nclearing opens up to the west, northwest, and north.  A Stony Pass that\nrises above the terrain of the Badlands can be seen to the southwest.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9398,49,7,0,'A Clearing in the Badlands','   The rocks and heavy brush of the Badlands have given way to a small\nclearing.  The gravel ground of the clearing is compacted giving the sign\nof heavy use.  The clearing opens up to the north, east, and south.\nA Stony Pass rises above the terrain of the Badlands to the southwest.\nA opening to a small cave can be seen to the northwest.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9399,48,7,0,'A Clearing in the Badlands','   You are in the middle of a small flat clearing.  The rocks and brush\nof the Badlands have thinned out to make easy passage.  The clearing\nopens all around you.  To the north you can see the entrance to a small\ncave, and to the south you can see a Stony Pass that rises above the\nterrain of the Badlands.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9400,47,7,0,'A Clearing in the Badlands','   The harsh terrain of the Badlands has given away to a small clearing.\nThe clearing continues to the northeast, east, southeast, and south.\nTo the southeast you can see a Stony Pass that rises above the imperfections\nof the badlands to create a make-shift land bridge that seems to lead to the\nsouth.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9401,48,8,0,'A Clearing in the Badlands Before a Cave','   The rocks and heavy brush of the Badlands have given way to a small\nclearing.  The gravel ground of the clearing is compacted due to heavy\ntravel.  The clearing opens up to the south, southwest, and southeast.\nThe harsh terrain of the Badlands can be seen far to the east.  There is\nan opening to a small cave in the rock to the north.  It is tall enough\nfor a human to easily walk in and out of the opening.  Very defined scratch\nmarks give away that this is not a natural cave.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9402,49,8,0,'A Clearing in the Badlands','   The rocks and heavy brush of the Badlands have given way to a small\nclearing.  The gravel ground of the clearing is compacted due to heavy\ntravel.  The clearing opens up to the west, southwest, and south.\nTo the west you can see the opening to a small dark cave.  The Badlands\ncontinue to the east.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9403,50,8,0,'The Badlands Before a Small Clearing','   The Badlands once again surround you.  The jagged rocks, and barely\nliving brush give you a strange feeling of desolation and solitude.\nThe ground is covered with chips of rock and sand.  To the north and\nsouth, large outcroppings of rock block all hopes of passage.  The\nBadlands continue to the east.  To the west you see a small clearing.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9404,48,9,0,'Just Inside a Small Cave','   This is the entrance to a small cave that has been carved into the\nside of an enormous upshoot of rock.  The walls are very jagged, and\nvery defined gashes can be seen where the tools where used to chip\naway at the rock.  The ceiling is just high enough for a human to stand\ncomfortably.  The ground is of packed dirt that has been carefully\nflattened to cover the stone underneath.  The cave continues north,\nnortheast, and east.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9405,49,9,0,'A Small Cave','   You are in a small cave that opens up to the north, northwest,\nand west.  The cave walls are covered with huge gouges that give the\nsign that this cave is not natural.  The ground if of hard dirt, and\nthe ceilings are just high enough for you to stand comfortably.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9406,49,10,0,'A Small Cave','   You are in a small cave that opens up to the northwest, west, south-\nwest, and south.  The cave walls are covered with huge gouges that give\nthe sign that this cave is not natural.  The ground is of hard dirt,\nand the ceilings are just high enough for you to stand comfortably.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9407,48,10,0,'Center of a Small Cave','   This is the center of the small cave.  It seems as though someone\nhas been here recently.  There is a still warm campfire here, and two\nbedrolls that are carelessly left unrolled in the dirt.  The cave\nentrance can be seen to the south, and the cave opens up in all other\ndirections.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9408,47,10,0,'A Small Cave','   You are in a small cave that opens up to the north, northeast, and\neast.  The cave walls are covered with huge gouges that give the sign\nthat this cave is not natural.  The ground is of hard dirt, and the\nceiling is just high enough for you to stand comfortably.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9409,47,11,0,'A Small Cave','   You are in a small cave that opens up to the south, southeast, east\nand northeast.  The cave walls are covered with huge gouges that give the\nsign that this cave is not natural.  The ground is of dirt, and the\nceiling is just high enough for you to stand comfortably.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9410,48,11,0,'A Small Cave','  You are in a small cave that opens in almost every direction.  The\ncave walls are covered with huge gouges that give the sign that this\ncave is not natural.  The ground is covered with hard dirt, and the\nceiling is just high enough for you to stand comfortably.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9411,48,12,0,'A Small Cave','   You are in a small cave that opens up to the southwest and south.\nThe cave walls are covered with huge gouges that give the sign that\nthis cave is not natural.  The ground is covered with hard dirt, and\nthe ceilings are just high enough for you to stand comfortably.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9412,46,11,-2,'The Badlands','   The Badlands surround you.  Heavy brush is the only plant life growing\non this uneven, rocky ground.  Broken stones, gravel and the decayed\nremains of scraggly brush cover the ground in this desolate place.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9413,47,11,-2,'The Badlands','   The Badlands surround you.  Heavy brush is the only plant life growing\non this uneven, rocky ground.  Broken stones, gravel and the decayed\nremains of scraggly brush cover the ground in this desolate place.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9414,48,11,-2,'The Badlands','   The Badlands surround you.  Heavy brush is the only plant life growing\non this uneven, rocky ground.  Broken stones, gravel and the decayed\nremains of scraggly brush cover the ground in this desolate place.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9415,49,11,-2,'The Badlands','   The Badlands surround you.  Heavy brush is the only plant life growing\non this uneven, rocky ground.  Broken stones, gravel and the decayed\nremains of scraggly brush cover the ground in this desolate place.  A\nlarge pile of rocks blocks any passage to the east.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9416,46,12,-2,'The Badlands','   The Badlands surround you.  Heavy brush is the only plant life growing\non this uneven, rocky ground.  Broken stones, gravel and the decayed\nremains of scraggly brush cover the ground in this desolate place.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9417,47,12,-2,'The Badlands','   The Badlands surround you.  Heavy brush is the only plant life growing\non this uneven, rocky ground.  Broken stones, gravel and the decayed\nremains of scraggly brush cover the ground in this desolate place.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9418,48,12,-2,'The Badlands','   The Badlands surround you.  Heavy brush is the only plant life growing\non this uneven, rocky ground.  Broken stones, gravel and the decayed\nremains of scraggly brush cover the ground in this desolate place.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9419,49,12,-2,'The Badlands','   The Badlands surround you.  Heavy brush is the only plant life growing\non this uneven, rocky ground.  Broken stones, gravel and the decayed\nremains of scraggly brush cover the ground in this desolate place.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9420,50,10,-5,'Before the Canyon Cliffs','   The high walls of the canyon enclose you in every direction.  The\nsmooth, rocky canyon floor give you the impression that this canyon\nonce held a great river.  The solid, weatherbeaten rock surface shows\nthe true age of the canyon, which must have existed for hundreds of\nthousands of years.  The canyon is completely bare of any plant life.\nThere are a series of cliffs and ledges to the north that lead\nup into the Badlands.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9421,51,10,-5,'The Canyon Floor','   The high walls of the canyon enclose you in every direction.  The\nsmooth, rocky canyon floor give you the impression that this canyon\nonce held a great river.  The solid, weatherbeaten rock surface shows\nthe true age of the canyon, which must have existed for hundreds of\nthousands of years.  The canyon is completely bare of any plant life.\nYou can see a series of cliffs and ledges to the northwest that\ncould lead out of the canyon.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9422,49,9,-5,'The Canyon Floor','   The high walls of the canyon enclose you in every direction.  The\nsmooth, rocky canyon floor give you the impression that this canyon\nonce held a great river.  The solid, weatherbeaten rock surface shows\nthe true age of the canyon, which must have existed for hundreds of\nthousands of years.  The canyon is completely bare of any plant life.\nYou can see a series of cliffs and ledges to the north that\nmay lead out of the canyon.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9423,50,9,-5,'The Canyon Floor','   The high walls of the canyon enclose you in every direction.  The\nsmooth, rocky canyon floor give you the impression that this canyon\nonce held a great river.  The solid, weatherbeaten rock surface shows\nthe true age of the canyon, which must have existed for hundreds of\nthousands of years.  The canyon is completely bare of any plant life.\nYou can see a series of cliffs and ledges to the north that\nmay lead out of the canyon.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9424,51,9,-5,'The Canyon Floor','   The high walls of the canyon enclose you in every direction.  The\nsmooth, rocky canyon floor give you the impression that this canyon\nonce held a great river.  The solid, weatherbeaten rock surface shows\nthe true age of the canyon, which must have existed for hundreds of\nthousands of years.  The canyon is completely bare of any plant life.\nYou can see a series of cliffs and ledges to the northwest\nthat may lead out of the canyon.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9425,52,9,-5,'The Canyon Floor','   The high walls of the canyon enclose you in every direction.  The\nsmooth, rocky canyon floor give you the impression that this canyon\nonce held a great river.  The solid, weatherbeaten rock surface shows\nthe true age of the canyon, which must have existed for hundreds of\nthousands of years.  The canyon is completely bare of any plant life.\nA large rocky area prevents passage to the south.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
