(9462,48,8,-5,'The Canyon Floor','   The high walls of the canyon enclose you in every direction.  The\nsmooth, rocky canyon floor give you the impression that this canyon\nonce held a great river.  The solid, weatherbeaten rock surface shows\nthe true age of the canyon, which must have existed for hundreds of\nthousands of years.  The canyon is completely bare of any plant life.\nA large rock formation blocks any passage to the southeast.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9463,57,-3,0,'Entrance to the Mound','   You are in a large burial mound that was most likely built by\nthe savages of ages past.  The stale air stings your lungs as you\nbreath.  The walls are bare packed dirt, and are covered with\nnumerous primitive paintings.  The floor is damp and muddy, strewn\nwith what look to be foot prints.  You can see the exit to the mound\nto the west, while the mound opens up to the east.\n',53,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
