(9485,59,-2,-2,'A Long Corridor','   A long hallway stretches out before you.  The walls are very\nsmooth and flat.  Unlike the rest of the mound, the walls are\ncompletely bare, and there is no dust upon the floor.  The air\nis no longer stale.  The hallway continues to the east and south.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9486,60,-2,-2,'A long Corridor','   A long hallway stretches out before you.  The walls are very\nsmooth and flat.  Unlike the rest of the mound, the walls are\ncompletely bare, and there is no dust upon the floor.  The air\nis no longer stale.  The hallway continues to the east and west.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9487,61,-2,-2,'The End of the Corridor','   A long hallway stretches out before you.  The walls are very\nsmooth and flat.  Unlike the rest of the mound, the walls are\ncompletely bare, and there is no dust upon the floor.  The air\nis no longer stale.  The hallway comes to an end at a large bronze door\non the wall the east.  The hallway continues to the west.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9489,62,-2,-2,'The Crypt','  You are in a large crypt.  The scattered remains of bodies litter\nthe floor, and stains of blood cover the walls.  A large coffin\nlies in the middle of the room.  A large bronze door leads out\nof the crypt to the west.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9490,59,-3,-2,'A Long Corridor','   A long hallway stretches out before you.  The walls are very\nsmooth and flat.  Unlike the rest of the mound, the walls are\ncompletely bare, and there is no dust upon the floor.  The air\nis no longer stale.  The hallway continues to the north and south.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9491,59,-4,-2,'A Long Corridor','   A long hallway stretches out before you.  The walls are very\nsmooth and flat.  Unlike the rest of the mound, the walls are\ncompletely bare, and there is no dust upon the floor.  The air\nis no longer stale.  The hallway continues to the north and east.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9492,60,-4,-2,'A Long Corridor','   A long hallway stretches out before you.  The walls are very\nsmooth and flat.  Unlike the rest of the mound, the walls are\ncompletely bare, and there is no dust upon the floor.  The air\nis no longer stale.  The hallway continues to the east and west.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9493,61,-4,-2,'A Long Corridor','   A long hallway stretches out before you.  The walls are very\nsmooth and flat.  Unlike the rest of the mound, the walls are\ncompletely bare, and there is no dust upon the floor.  The air\nis no longer stale.  The hallway continues to the west.  There is a\nsmall trapdoor in the ceiling here.\n',53,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9500,-37,46,-1,'A Path Through Some Short Grass','  This is a light track along which appears to be small well kept grass.  \nThe grass is short and smooth.  There is no indication of footprints or \nanimal tracks.  Apart from the eerie loneliness felt here this track \nmakes one feel somewhat peaceful and calm.  The path continues to the \nnorth towards a small village or to the south into the mountain forests.\n',70,131072,6,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9501,-37,47,-1,'A Light Clearing Before a Stone Bridge','  This clearing has been made by scores of travelers passing through \nhere.  Around the clearing there is well kept up grass and the area \nseems well foliated.  Where the grass was it has been trampled into \nloose dirt by years of overuse.  Near the edge of the clearing it \nbecomes paved with cobblestones leading to a small bridge over a creek \nto the north.\n',70,131072,6,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9502,-37,48,-1,'A Stone Bridge Across the Meijin Creek','  You are standing on a bridge that is wide enough to fit a horse and cart \nbut apparently wasn\'t designed for that purpose.  This cobblestone bridge \nstands over a small creek which seems shallow, but obviously deep enough \nfor people to construct a bridge to help in their travels.  Though the creek \nseems safe enough the water looks icy cold and swimming or falling in it \nwould be a bad idea.  There seems to be an unnatural amount of mist cloaking \nthe bridge which covers your sight of everything surrounding the bridge.  Just\nfaintly visible to the north is the top of a large structure while a clearing\ncan be seen to the south.\n',70,131072,3,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9503,-37,49,-1,'A Stone Bridge Across the Meijin Creek','  You are standing on a bridge that is wide enough to fit a horse and cart \nbut apparently wasn\'t designed for that purpose.  This cobblestone bridge \nstands over a small creek which seems shallow, but obviously deep enough \nfor people to construct a bridge to help in their travels.  Though the creek \nseems safe enough the water looks icy cold and swimming or falling in it \nwould be a bad idea.  There seems to be an unnatural amount of mist cloaking \nthe bridge which covers your sight of everything surrounding the bridge.  Just\nfaintly visible to the north is the top of a large structure while the bridge\ncontinues to the south.\n',70,131072,3,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9504,-37,50,-1,'The Southern Plaza in Zutanjin Village','  You are standing in what appears to be a central plaza in the small \nZutanjin village.  The villagers jostle around you on their way to a temple \nwhich is standing directly to the north.  Receiving strange looks from the \nvillagers you decide it would be best not to linger in any place for to long \nas it is obvious that you are an outsider.  Surrounding the plaza are a few \nshops and houses of the villagers.  In the centre of this plaza there is a \nstatue of a warrior sheathing his sword with some runes inscribed at the \nbottom.  Looking for relief from the glares of the people you see a bridge \ncrossing the Meijin creek then leading into the wilderness to the south.\n',70,131072,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9505,-37,54,-1,'The Northern Plaza in Zutanjin Village','  This plaza is directly behind a small temple, which seems to be the centre \nof the village.  The plaza here is very dirty and dark, it seems the villagers\ndont travel behind the temple very often and as a result this plaza has become\na centre of criminal activity in the village.  A few shady eyes glance at you \nfrom the shadows, thinking that you will be attacked you break eye contact and\nfeel it would be best to leave this area immediately.  Strangely, there are \ncrates and boxes stacked here and since you have not noticed this in the \nvillage so far you think that this must also be a place of storage for local \nshops and the temple.\n',70,131072,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9506,-35,52,-1,'The Eastern Plaza in Zutanjin Village','  You seem to be standing in a market plaza of Zutanjin.  There are closed \nshops on one side of the plaza, perhaps closed due to a religious holiday, and\non the other side there is a wall of a small temple.  Making their way through\nthe plaza are the small number of villagers that are out trading and bringing \ntheir goods to the open market area.\n',70,131072,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9507,-39,52,-1,'The Western Plaza in Zutanjin Village','  You seem to be standing in a market plaza of Zutanjin.  There are closed \nshops on one side of the plaza, perhaps closed due to a religious holiday, and\non the other side there is a wall of a small temple.  Making their way through\nthe plaza are the small number of villagers that are out trading and bringing \ntheir goods to the open market area.\n',70,131072,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9508,-36,50,-1,'The Southern Path Around a Small Temple','  This is a southern plaza in Zutanjin.  You are standing on a small path that\nskirts around a small temple that is the centre of the village.  The path here\nis loosely covered in gravel that has come from a nearby creek.  To the north \nof this plaza is a small temple while to the south is a creek that leads out \nto the wilderness beyond.\n',70,131072,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9509,-38,50,-1,'The Southern Path Around a Small Temple','  This is a southern plaza in Zutanjin.  You are standing on a small path that\nskirts around a small temple that is the centre of the village.  The path here\nis loosely covered in gravel that has come from a nearby creek.  To the north \nof this plaza is a small temple while to the south is a creek that leads out \nto the wilderness beyond.\n',70,131072,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9510,-38,54,-1,'The Northern Path Around a Small Temple','  You are standing directly behind a small temple in the village Zutanjin.  \nThe light in this part of town is particularly poor and lends itself to \ncriminal activity.  You hear some low mumblings and occasionally a growl or \ngrunt.  This appears to be a storage area of Zutanjin as there are crates and \nboxes stacked against the back wall of the temple.\n',70,131072,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9511,-36,54,-1,'The Northern Path Around a Small Temple','  You are standing directly behind a small temple in the village Zutanjin.  \nThe light in this part of town is particularly poor and lends itself to \ncriminal activity.  You hear some low mumblings and occasionally a growl or \ngrunt.  This appears to be a storage area of Zutanjin as there are crates and \nboxes stacked against the back wall of the temple.\n',70,131072,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9512,-35,53,-1,'The Eastern Path Around a Small Temple','  This part of heavily trodden pathway is the market place of a small \nvillage.  For a market place this plaza is strangely quiet, there are no \nvendors selling their goods or rowdy crowds haggling prices.  The buildings \nthat occupy this plaza seem to be shops which unfortunately appear closed, \nperhaps for a religious  holiday.  To the west there is a small temple where \nthe local villagers come to worship.\n',70,131072,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9513,-35,51,-1,'The Eastern Path Around a Small Temple','  This part of heavily trodden pathway is the market place of a small \nvillage.  For a market place this plaza is strangely quiet, there are no \nvendors selling their goods or rowdy crowds haggling prices.  The buildings \nthat occupy this plaza seem to be shops which unfortunately appear closed, \nperhaps for a religious  holiday.  To the west there is a small temple where \nthe local villagers come to worship.\n',70,131072,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9514,-39,51,-1,'The Western Path Around a Small Temple','  This part of heavily trodden pathway is the market place of a small \nvillage.  For a market place this plaza is strangely quiet, there are no \nvendors selling their goods or rowdy crowds haggling prices.  The buildings \nthat occupy this plaza seem to be shops which unfortunately appear closed, \nperhaps for a religious  holiday.  To the east there is a small temple where \nthe local villagers come to worship.\n',70,131072,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9515,-39,53,-1,'The Western Path Around a Small Temple','  This part of heavily trodden pathway is the market place of a small \nvillage.  For a market place this plaza is strangely quiet, there are no \nvendors selling their goods or rowdy crowds haggling prices.  The buildings \nthat occupy this plaza seem to be shops which unfortunately appear closed, \nperhaps for a religious  holiday.  To the east there is a small temple where \nthe local villagers come to worship.\n',70,131072,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9516,-37,51,-1,'A Temple Entryway','  This is the entrance to a small temple in Zutanjin.  Villagers come \neveryday to train and worship here.  The local plazas all have their \ncentre as the temple as does the entire village.  To the north is the\nDojo Floor, or training area.  To the west is a small storage room while\nto the east appears to be a small dressing area.  A pair of simple doors\nlie to the south and most likely exit the temple.\n',70,131084,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9517,-37,53,-1,'A Shrine of the Zutanji','  You are standing in a small alcove at the back of a small temple.  The few \ncandles that provide light for the shrine cast elongated shadows from the \nmany onyx idols that make up the shrine.  Peering through the darkness caused \nby the alcove you are just able to make out what appears to be a large statue\nof a humanoid warrior.\n',70,131080,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9518,-37,52,-1,'The Dojo Floor','  Hard cloth mats cushion your step on the floor here in the Dojo.  This is \nwhere students of the temple and villagers come to train in martial arts \nunder their sensei.  Judging by the mishape of the mats you can tell that the\nstudents often hit the mat very hard.  This part of the dojo is in the centre \nof the temple, the walls skirting the temple are made of bamboo that is taken \nfrom a nearby glade.\n',70,131080,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9519,-36,52,-1,'The Dojo Floor','  Hard cloth mats cushion your step on the floor here in the Dojo.  This is \nwhere students of the temple and villagers come to train in martial arts \nunder their sensei.  Judging by the mishape of the mats you can tell that the\nstudents often hit the mat very hard.  This part of the dojo is in the centre \nof the temple, the walls skirting the temple are made of bamboo that is taken \nfrom a nearby glade.\n',70,131080,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9520,-38,52,-1,'The Dojo Floor','  Hard cloth mats cushion your step on the floor here in the Dojo.  This is \nwhere students of the temple and villagers come to train in martial arts \nunder their sensei.  Judging by the mishape of the mats you can tell that the\nstudents often hit the mat very hard.  This part of the dojo is in the centre \nof the temple, the walls skirting the temple are made of bamboo that is taken \nfrom a nearby glade.\n',70,131080,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9521,-38,53,-1,'The Dojo Floor','  Hard cloth mats cushion your step on the floor here in the Dojo.  This is \nwhere students of the temple and villagers come to train in martial arts \nunder their sensei.  Judging by the mishape of the mats you can tell that the\nstudents often hit the mat very hard.  This part of the dojo is in the centre \nof the temple, the walls skirting the temple are made of bamboo that is taken \nfrom a nearby glade.\n',70,131080,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9522,-38,51,-1,'A Temple Storage Room','  This is a plain room, devoid of everything but a thick layer of dust.  This \nroom was obviously designed for storage but apparently this temple has little\nneed for anything more then the basic neccessities each person requires.\n',70,131080,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9523,-36,53,-1,'The Sensei\'s Training Floor','Different from the rest of the temple dojo there are martial arts training \ntools built on the ground here.  Obviously this is where the temple master \nteaches the best of his students.  Such students being the elite have sworn \nthemselves to vows of silence and starvation in their persuit of the highest \nlevel of physical excellance.  To this extent there are no material luxuries \nat all, just a plain dirt floor with a few planks of wood for the students to \ntrain on.\n',0,131080,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9524,-36,51,-1,'A Small Dressing Area','  Looking little different then the rest of the temple a few simple\nscreens provide a small bit of privacy for the students and villagers.\nHere they remove their normal garments and prepare for training or worship.\nThe Temple Entryway is to the west while the Dojo Floor is visible to the\nnorth and northwest.\n',70,131080,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9525,5,-6,-1,'Lift between the Theater Basement','  This room appears to be made entirely of wood, except the ceiling\nwhich is open into a dark shaft above you.  The north wall is featureless, \nas is the east, other than a loop of rope running through a crude pulley \non the floor up into the darkness above.  There are gates to the south and \nwest.  A sign hangs from the rope.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,5,360,0,'',NULL),
(9526,5,-7,-1,'Ancient Graffiti Covered Hallway','  A hallway in an ancient basement below the theater.  The walls of \nthe basement are graffiti covered and look as if they predate the \nrest of the theater, perhaps even the city.  This hallway continues \nto the south with a door to the west and a gate to the north.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(9527,5,-8,-1,'An Ancient Graffiti Covered Hallway','  A hallway in an ancient basement below the theater.  The walls of \nthe basement are graffitti covered and look as if they predate the\nrest of the theater, perhaps even the city.  This hallway continues\nto the south, north and west.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(9528,5,-9,-1,'Base of the Stairs','  The base of the spiral stair case in an ancient basement below\nthe theater.  The stairs lead up to the south side of the stage.\nThe walls of the basement are graffiti covered and look as if\nthey predate the rest of the theater, perhaps even the city.\nThis hallway continues to the north and there is a door to the west.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(9530,4,-6,-1,'Set Design','  Combined with and overflowing into Prop Design, this is the largest\nroom in the theater basement.  There is a pile of lumber stacked against\nthe north wall and a bunch of rolled up canvas backdrops leaning\nin the northwest corner.  There is a gate on the east wall and the\nroom is open to the prop builder\'s area to the south.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(9531,4,-7,-1,'Prop Builders','  Messy, cramped and visually dominated by the Set Designer\'s area to the\nnorth, the prop builder\'s area could be easily be over looked.  There\nis a desk in front a set of deep shelves to the west and a workbench\nto the east.  The room is open to the Set Designer\'s area to the north\nand there is a door to the south.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(9532,4,-8,-1,'Ancient Graffiti Covered Hallway','  A hallway in an ancient basement below the theater.  The walls of\nthe basement are graffiti covered and look as if they predate the\nrest of the theater, perhaps even the city.  There is a small rope\nhanging from the center of the hallway here.  This hallway continues\nto the east and west with doors to the north and south.  Oddly the\nceiling in this room is about twenty inches lower then the rest of\nthe surrounding hallways and rooms.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,8,80,0,'',NULL),
(9533,4,-9,-1,'Dressing Room','  All of the available wall space in this room, from the waist high \nshelf to the ceiling, is some form of polished metal mirror.  From \nthe level of cleanliness and general state of disrepair, it\'s safe \nto say the stars don\'t use this room.  There are doors to the north \nand south.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9534,4,-10,-1,'Storage Room','  Covered in dust and spider webs, it\'s doubtful that anything with\nas few as two legs has visited this room in years.  There are some\nmolding and rotten backdrops stacked against the west wall, the east\nsouth walls are covered with sagging shelves filled with objects that\nhave long since faded into obscurity.  There is a door to the north.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9535,3,-6,-1,'Diva\'s Dressing Room','  At first brush, this room is much better kept than the rest.  But it\nis decaying like the rest of the basement, it just has a fresher coat\nof paint.  The north wall has a nice, if old, couch.  To the south is a\nlarge wardrobe and a beat up trunk.  The east wall is dominated by a\npolished metal mirror and a low table with a huge spray of flowers \nacross it.  There is a door to the west.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9536,3,-7,-1,'Wardrobe','  Musty and nearly empty, this Wardrobe would disappoint anyone\nwith childish dress up fantasies.  There is a large trunk near the\neast wall, a wardrobe to the north and a small stool in the\ncenter of the room.  There are doors on the south and west walls.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(9537,3,-8,-1,'Ancient Graffiti Covered Hallway','  A hallway in an ancient basement below the theater.  The walls of\nthe basement are graffiti covered and look as if they predate the\nrest of the theater, perhaps even the city.  This hallway continues\nto the east and west with doors to the north and south.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(9538,3,-9,-1,'Makeup Room','  A mostly barren room, it is brightly lit and has polished metal\nmirrors on every available wall surface.  In the center of the room\nis a large chair with a table and a small chest to one side.  There \nis a door to the north and the west.\n',73,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(9539,3,-10,-1,'Star\'s Dressing Room','  Neat, tidy and lacking almost any character, the star\'s dressing\nroom is not as shabby as some of the rest of the rooms in the\nbasement...  just plain.  There is a couch on the south wall, a trunk\nto the north and a small table in front of a polished metal mirror\nto the east.  There is a door to the west.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(9540,2,-6,-1,'Ancient Graffiti Covered Hallway','  A hallway in an ancient basement below the theater.  The walls of\nthe basement are graffiti covered and look as if they predate the\nrest of the theater, perhaps even the city.  This hallway continues\nto the south and west with a door to the east.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(9541,2,-7,-1,'Ancient Graffiti Covered Hallway','  A hallway in an ancient basement below the theater.  The walls of\nthe basement are graffiti covered and look as if they predate the\nrest of the theater, perhaps even the city.  This hallway continues\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(9542,2,-8,-1,'Ancient Graffiti Covered Hallway','  A hallway in an ancient basement below the theater.  The walls of\nthe basement are graffiti covered and look as if they predate the\nrest of the theater, perhaps even the city.  This hallway continues\nto the north, south and east with a door to the west.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(9543,2,-9,-1,'Ancient Graffiti Covered Hallway','  A hallway in an ancient basement below the theater.  The walls of\nthe basement are graffiti covered and look as if they predate the\nrest of the theater, perhaps even the city.  This hallway continues\nto the north and south with a door to the east.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9544,2,-10,-1,'Ancient Graffiti Covered Hallway','  A hallway in an ancient basement below the theater.  The walls of \nthe basement are graffiti covered and look as if they predate the \nrest of the theater, perhaps even the city.  This hallway continues \nto the north and west with a door to the east.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(9545,1,-6,-1,'Base of the Stairs','  The base of the stair case in an ancient basement below \nthe theater.  The stairs lead up to the north side of the lobby.  \nThe walls of the basement are graffiti covered and look as if \nthey predate the rest of the theater, perhaps even the city.\nThis hallway continues to the east and there is a door to the south.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(9546,1,-7,-1,'Kitchen','  Here is where all the food is prepared for the cast and the crew.\nIn the center is a large fire pit with a spit and several hooks for\nhanging pots.  Around the perimeter of the room are various shelves\nand benches for food preparation.  There is an open archway to the \nsouth and a door to the north.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(9547,1,-8,-1,'Commissary','  The only room that looks like its been renovated or at least kept\nin decent shape.  The kitchen is visible through a small arch to the \nnorth and there is a door to the east.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9548,1,-9,-1,'Manager\'s Office','  A dirty looking little cube with posters of past stars and long\nfaded glories on the walls.  There is a door to the south.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(9549,1,-10,-1,'Base of the Stairs','  The base of the stair case in an ancient basement below \nthe theater.  The stairs lead up to the south side of the lobby.  \nThe walls of the basement are graffiti covered and look as if \nthey predate the rest of the theater, perhaps even the city.\nThis hallway continues to the east and there is a door to the\nnorth.\n',73,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9550,0,0,0,'<C>Water Training<Z>','  As you exit the portal you are instantly confronted by a deep pool, you \nguess that violent tsunami\'s and the like have swept across this watery \nexpanse many a time.  This must be where the master magicians of water come \nto practice.\n',74,139585,52,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9551,0,0,0,'<R>Fire Training<Z>','  As you exit the portal you find yourself in an arid land.  A land as such \nthat it would not be overly effected by sporadic blasts of heat.  On closer \ninspection of the sand on the ground you notice random slivers of glass here \nand there.  You surmise that the academy must have some powerful masters in \nthe manipulation of fire\n',74,139585,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9552,8,-1,-1,'<p>Arena Entrance<Z>','  Looking up you once again see the large veins of opal along the ceiling, \nthese must run throughout the whole of the academy, most likely covered in \nfancy decorations elsewhere, but uncovered in the basement where the looks of a \nroom are not important.  There is two portals in this room, one going to the \nmage arena and the other to the emergency room of the hospital just north of \nthe academy incase of a mishap.\n',74,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9553,0,0,0,'<C>Air Training<Z>','  Woah!!!  You find yourself suspended in mid air, and wait to fall...  Five \nminutes later you realise that you arent going to, and kick yourself for your \nstupidity.  This must be where the flightly magicians of air practice their \nmagical arts.\n',74,139585,65,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9554,0,0,0,'<k>Earth Training<Z>','  As soon as you exit the portal you notice that you are on a large plateau of \nsolid rock, although the ground around you does have the sporadic crater from \na misplaced meteor or two.  Not to mention a deep crack in the ground most \nlikely created by a mage calling forth hot magma.\n',74,139585,61,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9555,0,0,0,'<R>Mage Arena<Z>','  After exiting the portal you find yourself in an arena, blessed by the gods \nin such a way that death here will not actually cost you your life but \ninstead your honour and everything else you wagered upon yourself.  You notice \na sign in the northwestern corner.\n',74,155649,41,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9556,7,-2,-1,'<p>Work Station<Z>','  A pulsating tube runs along the ceiling, entering the room from the southeast \nand running completely across the room to the northwest corner.  The tube \nthen runs down the wall and stops above a large couch.  On the end of the \ntube is a large opal.  The opal and the couch are positioned so one could \neasily rest upon upon the couch while holding and charging the opal.  There \nis a sign placed above the couch.\n',74,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9557,8,-2,-1,'<p>Training Room Entrance<Z>','  The first thing you notice upon entering the room is the four large colored  \nportals.  Each has been placed in a seperate corner of the room.  You begin \nto wonder just where these portals could lead to.\n',74,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9558,9,-2,-1,'<p>Work Station<Z>','  A pulsating tube runs along the ceiling, entering the room from the southwest \nand running completely across the room to the northeast corner.  The tube \nthen runs down the wall and stops above a large couch.  On the end of the \ntube is a large opal.  The opal and the couch are positioned so one could \neasily rest upon upon the couch while holding and charging the opal.  There \nis a sign placed above the couch.\n',74,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9559,0,0,0,'<p>Confiscation Room<z>','  You stand surrounded in confiscated items, taken from various mages and \nplaced here.  You have no idea what some of the items in the room are,  but \nyou suspect that a lot of them are dangerous practical jokes.  Basically the \nkind of stuff you would find confiscated at any schooling facility, only \nthese items are mostly magical in nature.\n',74,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9560,6,-3,-1,'<p>Twist in Hallway<Z>','  The first thing you notice upon entering the room is the large vein like \nlines upon the ceiling, made from the blackest of opal you have ever seen and \nyet glowing with their own inner light.  You know there must be something \nspecial about them, but what that is you are unsure of.  Unlike upstairs, it \nseems that cleanliness is not as important here.  No longer do you see the \nsplendor of the floors above, instead you see simple rooms designed for \nworking in without embelishments.  You get the feeling that you are where the \ntrue mages of the academy work for the sheer pleasure of working, and \ntherefore have no need of fanciful items to make their work look more \nspectacular.\n',74,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9561,7,-3,-1,'<p>Western Hallway<Z>','  The first thing you notice upon entering the room is the large vein like \nlines upon the ceiling, made from the blackest of opal you have ever seen and \nyet glowing with their own inner light.  You know there must be something \nspecial about them, but what that is you are unsure of.  Unlike upstairs, it \nseems that cleanliness is not as important here.  No longer do you see the \nsplendor of the floors above, instead you see simple rooms designed for \nworking in without embelishments.  You get the feeling that you are where the \ntrue mages of the academy work for the sheer pleasure of working, and \ntherefore have no need of fanciful items to make their work look more \nspectacular.  To the east is a large door.\n',74,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9562,8,-3,-1,'<p>Power Generator<Z>','  As you enter the room you see vein like lines of opal upon the ceiling \nconverging to the center of the room from the north, east, south, and west.  \nLarger tube like lines can also be seen converging on the center from the \nnortheastern, northwestern, southeastern, and southwestern corners.  \nFollowing the tubes and veins with your eyes to the center of the room you \nnotice the largest opal powerstone you have ever seen.  Beside the powerstone \nis a sign.\n',74,139593,32,50,9562,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9563,9,-3,-1,'<p>Before a Guard Station<Z>','  The first thing you notice upon entering the room is the large vein like \nlines upon the ceiling, made from the blackest of opal you have ever seen and \nyet glowing with their own inner light.  You know there must be something \nspecial about them, but what that is you are unsure of.  Unlike upstairs, it \nseems that cleanliness is not as important here.  No longer do you see the \nsplendor of the floors above, instead you see simple rooms designed for \nworking in without embelishments.  You get the feeling that you are where the \ntrue mages of the academy work for the sheer pleasure of working, and \ntherefore have no need of fanciful items to make their work look more \nspectacular.  To the east you spy a guard post, and a large door to the west.\n',74,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9564,10,-3,-1,'<p>Guard Post<Z>','You stand in a simple guard post.  If it weren\'t for the large veins of opal \nupon the ceiling and the fact that a guard is casually playing with a small \nfireball, you would swear you were no longer in the academy.\n',-1,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9565,6,-4,-1,'<p>Hallway<Z>','  The first thing you notice upon entering the room is the large vein like \nlines upon the ceiling, made from the blackest of opal you have ever seen and \nyet glowing with their own inner light.  You know there must be something \nspecial about them, but what that is you are unsure of.  Unlike upstairs, it \nseems that cleanliness is not as important here.  No longer do you see the \nsplendor of the floors above, instead you see simple rooms designed for \nworking in without embelishments.  You get the feeling that you are where the \ntrue mages of the academy work for the sheer pleasure of working, and \ntherefore have no need of fanciful items to make their work look more \nspectacular.  To the south you spy a guard post.\n',74,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9566,7,-4,-1,'<p>Work Station<Z>','  A pulsating tube runs along the ceiling, entering the room from the northeast \nand running completely across the room to the southwest corner.  The tube \nthen runs down the wall and stops above a large couch.  On the end of the \ntube is a large opal.  The opal and the couch are positioned so one could \neasily rest upon upon the couch while holding and charging the opal.  There \nis a sign placed above the couch.\n',74,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9567,8,-4,-1,'<p>Southern Hallway<Z>','  The first thing you notice upon entering the room is the large vein like \nlines upon the ceiling, made from the blackest of opal you have ever seen and \nyet glowing with their own inner light.  You know there must be something \nspecial about them, but what that is you are unsure of.  Unlike upstairs, it \nseems that cleanliness is not as important here.  No longer do you see the \nsplendor of the floors above, instead you see simple rooms designed for \nworking in without embelishments.  You get the feeling that you are where the \ntrue mages of the academy work for the sheer pleasure of working, and \ntherefore have no need of fanciful items to make their work look more \nspectacular.  To the north is a large door.\n',74,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9568,9,-4,-1,'<p>Work Station<Z>','  A pulsating tube runs along the ceiling, entering the room from the northwest \nand running completely across the room to the southeast corner.  The tube \nthen runs down the wall and stops above a large couch.  On the end of the \ntube is a large opal.  The opal and the couch are positioned so one could \neasily rest upon upon the couch while holding and charging the opal.  There \nis a sign placed above the couch.\n',74,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9569,10,-4,-1,'<p>Well Lit Cell<Z>','  You stand in a well lit cell, designed as such that a prisoner would be hard \npressed to hide from their captures.  A horrid stench assaults your nostrils, \nconfusing you, for the room is one of the cleanest cells you have ever seen \nbefore, only marred by the large claw marks along the walls.\n',74,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9570,6,-5,-1,'<p>Guard Post<Z>','  You stand in a simple guard post.  If it wasnt for the large veins of opal \nupon the ceiling and the fact that a guard is levitating you would swear you \nwere no longer in the academy.\n',74,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9571,7,-5,-1,'<p>Rest Room<Z>','  The Room before you has been designed for the utmost comfort and relaxation.  \nTables have been placed sporadically throughout the room and are surrounded \nby many comfortable chairs.  The comfort of the room brings many mages on \ntheir breaks to this room, perfectly within earshot of the guards to the west \nif the need for assistance should ever present itself.\n',74,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9572,8,-5,-1,'<p>Turn in the Hallway<Z>','  The first thing you notice upon entering the room is the large vein like \nlines upon the ceiling, made from the blackest of opal you have ever seen and \nyet glowing with their own inner light.  You know there must be something \nspecial about them, but what that is you are unsure of.  Unlike upstairs, it \nseems that cleanliness is not as important here.  No longer do you see the \nsplendor of the floors above, instead you see simple rooms designed for \nworking in without embellishments.  You get the feeling that you are where\nthe true mages of the academy work for the sheer pleasure of working, and \ntherefore have no need of fanciful items to make their work look more \nspectacular.\n',74,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9573,9,-5,-1,'<p>Bottom of A Great Staircase<Z>','  Looking at the huge staircase before you, you cant help but notice that what \nwas once a marble staircase is now one made of black opal.  Not only that but \nthe ceiling and surrounding halls appear to be made from the same material.  \nUnlike elsewhere in the academy that you have seen thus far, it seems that \ncleanliness is not as important.  No longer do you see the splendor of the \nfloors above, instead you see simple rooms designed for certain uses without \nembelishments.  You get the feeling that you are where the true mages of the \nacademy work for the sheer pleasure of working, and therefore have no need of \nfanciful items to make their work look more spectacular.  A gentle force tugs \nyou upward gently, oddly enough there is no secondary force beckoning you onward \ninto the darkness ahead.\n',74,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9574,6,-6,-1,'<p>Guard Room<Z>','  This room seems to dull your wits with its total lack of decoration.  The \nwall to the south being slightly cracked is the only form of decoration in \nthe room, if you can call cracks decorations.  Small bones layer the floor, \nthe only remains of what looks to be rats.\n',74,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9575,0,0,0,'Overlooking a Concealed Trail','  This tiny ledge is overlooking the concealed trail leading to the bandit camp.\nA stealthy person here could keep a close eye on anyone entering or leaving the\nhidden canyon. The trail below can be seen to the east or north.\n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9576,0,0,0,'A Path Along a Thin Ledge','  This path is precariously narrow, a mountainous rock wall to your south, and\na fifty foot fall into the canyon to your north.  The path continues to the\nsouthwest.  This position, however, does give you an incredible view of the \ncamp below, though it is so well concealed as to be nearly invisible. It is no \ndoubt used as a lookout point. \n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9577,0,0,0,'A Path Along a Thin Ledge','  This path is precariously narrow, a mountainous rock wall to your south, and\na fifty foot fall into the canyon to your north.  The path continues to the\nwest and northeast.  This position, however, does give you very nice view of \nthe camp below, though it is so well concealed as to be nearly invisible.\n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9578,0,0,0,'A Path Along a Thin Ledge','  This path is precariously narrow, a mountainous rock wall to your south, and\na fifty foot fall into the canyon to your north.  The path continues to the\neast and west.  This position, however, does give you very nice view of the \ncamp below, though it is so well concealed as to be nearly invisible.\n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9579,0,0,0,'A Path Along a Thin Ledge','  This path is precariously narrow, a mountainous rock wall to your south, and\na fifty foot fall into the canyon to your north.  The path continues to the\neast, and you can climb back down to the campsite from the ledge to the north-\nwest.  This position however, does give you fairly nice view of the camp below,\nthough it is so well concealed as to be nearly invisible.\n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9580,0,0,0,'Hanging From a Cliff Ledge','  You are above a fifty foot drop of nearly sheer cliff. You have a pretty good\nview of the canyon below you, and the entire campsite is almost completely\nundetectable. There is a thin ledge on the cliff face to your southeast.\n',75,131072,35,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9581,0,0,0,'At the Base of a Cliff','  Behind the tent is nothing more than a small flat rock, but it appears like it\nmight be a place to start climbing the canyon cliff face.  There appears to be a\nledge about fifty feet above you, and looks like it will take some considerable\nclimbing skill to reach it. The rip in the back of the tent to the north is\nclearly visible from here.\n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(9582,0,0,0,'Inside a Tent','  This tent is slightly grungy, although surprisingly well constructed and\nclean.  There are a number of personal belongings here, enough to suggest this\ntent is shared by two or three people. \n',75,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,75,4,'',NULL),
(9583,0,0,0,'Inside a Tent','  This tent is slightly grungy, although surprisingly well constructed and\nclean.  There are a number of personal belongings here, enough to suggest this\ntent is shared by two or three people. \n',75,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,75,0,'',NULL),
(9584,0,0,0,'A Pathway in a Hidden Campsite','  This tiny campsite has been carefully hidden from prying eyes.  There are a\nnumber of tents scattered about seemingly at random.  The cloth of then tents\nare painted to blend in with the surrounding mountainside, and the trails are\nall carefully constructed to be invisible from the lip of the canyon, which is\nabout thirty to fifty feet above you.  There are tents to the south and east of\nyou, and southeast appears to be the center of the camp.\n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9585,0,0,0,'Inside a Tent','  This tent is slightly grungy, although surprisingly well constructed and\nclean.  There are a number of personal belongings here, enough to suggest this\ntent is shared by two or three people. \n',75,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,75,0,'',NULL),
(9586,0,0,0,'A Pathway in a Hidden Campsite','  This tiny campsite has been carefully hidden from prying eyes.  There are a\nnumber of tents scattered about seemingly at random.  The cloth of then tents\nare painted to blend in with the surrounding mountainside, and the trails are\nall carefully constructed to be invisible from the lip of the canyon, which is\nabout thirty to fifty feet above you.  There are tents to the south, east and\nwest of you, and north appears to be the center of the camp. The path continues\nsoutheast.\n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9587,0,0,0,'The Center of a Hidden Campsite','  This tiny campsite has been carefully hidden from prying eyes.  There are a\nnumber of tents scattered about seemingly at random.  The cloth of then tents\nare painted to blend in with the surrounding mountainside, and the trails are\nall carefully constructed to be invisible from the lip of the canyon, which is\nabout thirty to fifty feet above you.  This appears to be the center of camp,\nand there is a large fire pit here, as well as a number of places to sit around\nthe fire. There are tents to the north, east, and west, and paths lead away\nfrom the fire to the south, northeast, and northwest.\n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9588,0,0,0,'Inside a Tent','  For a tent in the middle of the mountains, this one is marvelously luxurious.\nDecorations adorn the large canvas shelter, and considering the difference\nbetween this tent and the others of the campsite, you would say this is the\nhome, however temporary, of someone fairly important. A glass shaving mirror\nhangs from one tent post. The center of the camp is visible out the flap to the\nsouth.\n',75,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,75,0,'',NULL),
(9589,0,0,0,'A Pathway in a Hidden Campsite','  This tiny campsite has been carefully hidden from prying eyes.  There are a\nnumber of tents scattered about seemingly at random.  The cloth of then tents\nare painted to blend in with the surrounding mountainside, and the trails are\nall carefully constructed to be invisible from the lip of the canyon, which is\nabout thirty to fifty feet above you.  There are tents to the north and west of\nyou, and a trail leads northwest into the center of camp.\n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9590,0,0,0,'Inside a Tent','  This tent is slightly grungy, although surprisingly well constructed and\nclean.  There are a number of personal belongings here, enough to suggest this\ntent is shared by two or three people. \n',75,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,75,0,'',NULL),
(9591,0,0,0,'Inside a Tent','  This tent is slightly grungy, although surprisingly well constructed and\nclean.  There are a number of personal belongings here, enough to suggest this\ntent is shared by two or three people. \n',75,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,75,0,'',NULL),
(9592,0,0,0,'A Pathway in a Hidden Campsite','  This tiny campsite has been carefully hidden from prying eyes.  There are a\nnumber of tents scattered about seemingly at random.  The cloth of then tents\nare painted to blend in with the surrounding mountainside, and the trails are\nall carefully constructed to be invisible from the lip of the canyon, which is\nabout thirty to fifty feet above you.  There are tents to the south and east of\nyou, and southeast appears to be the center of the camp.  A twisted trail leads \neast into a crevice.\n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9593,0,0,0,'A Secluded Meadow','  The tiny path opens into an incredibly beatiful little meadow here.  The\nground is covered with soft grass, which has either been mown recently or has \nbeen used to pasture horses.  There is a small spring bubbling to one side of\nthe meadow. Despite being sunken thirty to fifty feet below the rest of the\nrock face, a good amount of sun reaches the meadow, making for a very pleasant\nlittle spot.\n',75,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9594,0,0,0,'A Fork in the Path','  The hidden path suddenly widens here, forking to the northeast and west.  The \ntrail is so perfectly hidden and twisty that you can barely spot it even a few \nfeet ahead or behind of you.  The path has leveled out, and if you judge your \ndistances correctly, you could estimate that the tiny canyon you are in is \nabout thirty to fifty feet below the rest of the mountain face, and no doubt \ninvisible from anywhere above.  Due to the nature of these trails, it is\nimpossible to see what lies down either fork.\n',75,131076,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9595,0,0,0,'A Concealed Path','  This hidden path is incredibly hard to navigate, and although you guess that \nit would be possible to very carefully lead a horse through this veritable \ncrevice, you can not imagine why anyone would want to do so.  The trail is so\nperfectly hidden and twisty that you can barely spot it even a few feet ahead or\nbehind of you.  The path has leveled out, and if you judge your distances\ncorrectly, you could estimate that the tiny canyon you are in is about thirty \nto fifty feet below the rest of the mountain face, and no doubt invisible from \nanywhere above.  The trail continues southeast and northwest.\n',75,131072,25,100,9595,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9596,0,0,0,'A Concealed Path','  This hidden path is incredibly hard to navigate, and although you guess that \nit would be possible to very carefully lead a horse through this veritable \ncrevice, you can not imagine why anyone would want to do so.  The trail is so\nperfectly hidden and twisty that you can barely spot it even a few feet ahead or\nbehind of you.  The path has leveled out, and if you judge your distances\ncorrectly, you could estimate that the tiny canyon you are in is about thirty \nto fifty feet below the rest of the mountain face, and no doubt invisible from \nanywhere above.  The trail continues east and northwest.\n',75,131072,25,100,9596,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9597,0,0,0,'A Concealed Path','  This hidden path is incredibly hard to navigate, and although you guess that \nit would be possible to very carefully lead a horse through this veritable \ncrevice, you can not imagine why anyone would want to do so.  The trail is so\nperfectly hidden and twisty that you can barely spot it even a few feet ahead or\nbehind of you.  The path is also very clearly sloped, heading downward into the\nsurrounding mountain face to the west, and up to the southwest.\n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9598,0,0,0,'A Concealed Path','  This hidden path is incredibly hard to navigate, and although you guess that \nit would be possible to very carefully lead a horse through this veritable \ncrevice, you can not imagine why anyone would want to do so.  The trail is so\nperfectly hidden and twisty that you can barely spot it even a few feet ahead or\nbehind of you.  The path is also very clearly sloped, heading downward into the\nsurrounding mountain face to the northeast, and up to the south.\n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9599,-33,-19,0,'A Concealed Path','  You stand just inside a gate that has been carefully constructed to look like\nthe walls of the mountain pass.  The gate has opened to reveal a trail that has\nbeen so well concealed, it is barely visible even with the false wall open.\nThe trail slopes downwards, quickly sinking below the level of the surrounding \nland.  The end result is you cannot discern or even guess where the trail\nleads, just that it heads north from here.\n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9600,0,0,0,'Captain\'s Quarters','  This room is filled with maps and a small porthole can be seen level to\nthe Captain\'s bunk.  The musty odor in here accosts your nose, obviously,\nthis Captain isn\'t one for personal hygiene.  There are a series of what\nseems to be scalps piled atop a chest here giving evidence that the\n\"beloved\" Captain engages in much more that just \"safe passage\" to the Fog\nIslands.  A door to the south most likely supplies access to the rest of\nthe ship.\n',74,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,4,70,0,'',NULL),
(9601,0,0,0,'Moldy Storage Room','  A rancid odor fills the room and you notice mushrooms growing out of a\npile of unknown substance in the corner.  A puddle has accumulated here, its\nsource not readily apparent.  An opening in the east wall apparently is the\nonly exit from the room.\n',74,139272,32,0,0,0,0,-1,4,70,0,'',NULL),
(9602,0,0,0,'Storage area','  The first thing that you notice about this room is that it insignificantly\nsmaller than the rooms to the south.  The air here is particularly rancid\nand the walls seem to soak up any light that creeps in.  Doors are set to\nthe north and south, the hardware on the southern appearing to be quite rusty.\n',74,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,4,70,0,'',NULL),
(9603,0,0,0,'Dusty Storage Room',' A carpet of dust covers the floor of this room.  You can see footprints\nleading towards a stack of crates strapped to the side of the wall.  Extra\nsails are piled upon the floor, providing an excellent nest for the water\nrats.  The only exit from this area appears to be to the west.\n',74,139272,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,70,0,'',NULL),
(9604,0,0,0,'Below Decks','  A small flickering lantern hangs from the ceiling in this area of the ship\nallowing passengers and crew to move about, but the pitch-covered timber\nrunning horizontally across the width of the ship eagerly absorbs most of\nits light.  Various crates of wares are stacked and secured in dimly lit are\nof the ship.  Clear passage through the various ship\'s workings can be seen to\nthe east, south, and southeast.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9605,0,0,0,'Towards the Bow of the ship','  A small flickering lantern hangs from the ceiling in this area of the ship\nallowing passengers and crew to move about, but the pitch-covered timber\nrunning horizontally across the width of the ship eagerly absorbs most of\nits light.  A door is set into the north wall while the ship appears to\ncontinue to the east, west, and south.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9606,0,0,0,'Below Decks','  A small flickering lantern hangs from the ceiling in this area of the ship\nallowing passengers and crew to move about, but the pitch-covered timber\nrunning horizontally across the width of the ship eagerly absorbs most of\nits light.  Barrels of what might be called water, definitely not \"fresh\",\npossibly drinkable, along with other supplies and tack apparently are stored\nin this area of the ship.  Clear passage through the various ship\'s workings\ncan be seen to the south, west\nand southwest.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9607,0,0,0,'Below Decks','  A small flickering lantern hangs from the ceiling in this area of the ship\nallowing passengers and crew to move about, but the pitch-covered timber\nrunning horizontally across the width of the ship eagerly absorbs most of\nits light.  Various crates of wares are stacked and secured in dimly lit are\nof the ship.  Clear passage through the various ship\'s workings can be seen\nleading in several directions.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9608,0,0,0,'Amid Ship','  The ships mast extends through this room, a sign nailed into it, complete\nwith dried scalps hanging by three-pronged hooks.  The mast creaks with the\npush of the wind on its sails overhead, while the muffled shouts of the crew\nat work can be heard as well.  Clear passage through the ships workings are\nvisible in several directions, while a bit of fresh air can be detected to\nthe southwest and a bit of light filters into the room from the southeast.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9609,0,0,0,'Below Decks','  A small flickering lantern hangs from the ceiling in this area of the ship\nallowing passengers and crew to move about, but the pitch-covered timber\nrunning horizontally across the width of the ship eagerly absorbs most of\nits light.  Barrels of what might be called water, definitely not \"fresh\",\npossibly drinkable, along with other supplies and tack apparently are stored\nin this area of the ship.  Clear passage through the various ship\'s workings\ncan be seen leading in several directions.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9610,47,45,-3,'Moss Covered Dock','  You are standing on a small, moss-covered dock that runs east to west.  To\nthe west the dock has almost completely collapsed into the cold waters of the\nsea and the coastline is just within reach through the shallow waters.  The\ndock to the east is just as badly damaged with several of the dock boards\nmissing, rotted or cracked forcing you to keep your eyes cast downwards as\nyou move along.\n',74,139520,31,0,0,0,0,-1,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9611,48,45,-3,'End of a Moss Covered Dock','  You are standing on a small, moss-covered dock that runs east to west.  To\nthe west the dock has almost completely collapsed into the cold waters of the\nsea, the coastline just barely visible.  The dock to the east ends suddenly\nwhere the sea has washed it away.  Scuff marks and other recent damage to the\nremaining dock hint that some vessel or vessels still uses the dock though.\n',74,139520,31,0,0,0,0,-1,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9612,0,0,0,'Next to the Ship\'s Hatch','  To the west is the ship\'s only apparent hatch.  The main thing you notice\nabout this ship is its smell.  The air is thick with moisture and the smell\nof rot and decay.  The shine and wear of the floor makes you wonder about the\nage and seaworthiness of this craft.  A ghastly smell seems to emanate from\nthe south of you while several clear passages through the ships workings can\nbe seen in other directions.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9613,0,0,0,'Below Decks','  A small flickering lantern hangs from the ceiling in this area of the ship\nallowing passengers and crew to move about, but the pitch-covered timber\nrunning horizontally across the width of the ship eagerly absorbs most of\nits light.  For some reason this area of the ship appears to be fairly clear\nof any cargo.  Clear passage through the various ship\'s workings can be seen\nleading in several directions.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9614,0,0,0,'Poker Game','  Situated near a dirty porthole, apparently the only one in this part of the\nship, a large crate has been cleared off to act as a table with several\nsmaller ones placed around it as make-shift chairs.  A hooded candelabra,\nsupport by thick chains, hangs from the timber frame, throwing down a perfect\ncircle of light during the night that sways with the pitch of the boat.\nSmoke hangs thick and anxiety fills the air.  Any smuggler would agree that\npoker is a great way to pass the time and take all of your money.  Clear\npassage through the various ships workings, cargo and tack lead in several\ndirections.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9615,0,0,0,'Slave Pen','  The stench of death and disease is almost unbearable in this area of the\nship, where apparently slaves are kept or punished.  Luckily, there are no\n\"commodities\" filling the iron manacles that are bolted to the floor here.\nThere is a large stain that runs across the floorboards and splatters up onto\nthe west and south wall.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9616,0,0,0,'Before the Sleeping Quarters','  A small flickering lantern hangs from the ceiling in this area of the ship\nallowing passengers and crew to move about, but the pitch-covered timber\nrunning horizontally across the width of the ship eagerly absorbs most of\nits light.  To the south a door leads to what you would guess are the\nsleeping quarters.  Clear passage through the various ship\'s workings can be\nseen leading in several directions.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9617,0,0,0,'Below Decks','  A small flickering lantern hangs from the ceiling in this area of the ship\nallowing passengers and crew to move about, but the pitch-covered timber\nrunning horizontally across the width of the ship eagerly absorbs most of\nits light.  Various crates and boxes are stacked and secured in this area of\nthe ship.  Clear passage through the various ship\'s workings can be seen\nleading in several directions while a sturdy looking door can be seen to the\nsouth.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9618,0,0,0,'Sleeping Area','  First come first serve here, if you need a place to rest grab a cot now.\nWith this crew and the rest of the \"passengers\" you\'d probably do well to put\nsomeone on guard, no one wants to wake up with their throat cut.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9619,0,0,0,'Sleeping Area','  First come first serve here, if you need a place to rest grab a cot now.\nWith this crew and the rest of the \"passengers\" you\'d probably do well to put\nsomeone on guard, no one wants to wake up with their throat cut.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9620,0,0,0,'Storage Area','  Sacks of dry goods sit here atop wooden slats, most of them have holes from\nthe water rats.  Curiously, this is one of the few rooms below decks that is\ndry.  A door can be seen to the north while the room continues to the south.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9621,0,0,0,'Sleeping Area','  First come first serve here, if you need a place to rest grab a cot now.\nWith this crew and the rest of the \"passengers\" you\'d probably do well to put\nsomeone on guard, no one wants to wake up with their throat cut.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9622,0,0,0,'Smuggler\'s Sleeping Area','  This spot is saved for the smugglers, who sleep here in shifts while\nkeeping an eye on the cargo.  There is trash everywhere and clothes all\naround.  One especially large pile lies against the south wall.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9623,0,0,0,'Supply Room','  Shelves filled with food and repair supplies line every wall of this room.\nBoxes are stacked two high and you can see that they are labeled but it\'s\ndifficult to make out the writing.\n',74,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9624,0,0,0,'Small Room','  This room is very small and is probably used for any \"special\" cargo that\nmust be kept secret from those not part of the crew.  A small lockable panel\nto the north conceals a passageway to the sleeping area beyond.\n',74,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,2,50,0,'',NULL),
(9625,0,0,0,'<g>Kelp Forest<1>','<g>  Thick strands of <o>k<g>e<o>l<g>p wave gently with the flowing of the <b>ocean<g>.  Movement\nis difficult and it would be easy to become hopelessly entangled.  The water\nis warm and almost cozy, but the occasional wave of <1><C>frigid<1><g> water from the\nominious <k>darkness<g> below can be felt.\n',78,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(9626,0,0,0,'<o>Crow\'s Nest<1>','<o>  Eroded and decaying wood make up what is left of this crow\'s nest.  The\ntop end of the mast, where a flag would have been, is missing, with nothing\nbut a jagged stump left.  Thick strands of <g>k<o>e<g>l<o>p surround the crow\'s nest,\nblocking visibility in all directions.  A trapdoor leads the way down the mast\ninto <k>darkness<o>.\n',78,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(9627,0,0,0,'<o>Ship Mast<1>','<k>  Wooden <o>pegs<k> protrude from the mast forming a ladder for riggers and\nlookouts to move about.  Tattered <W>sails<1><k> drift slowly in the water, wrapping\naround the mast, tangling up in the old rigging and mingling with the <o>k<g>e<o>l<g>p<1><k>.\n',78,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9628,0,0,0,'<o>Starboard Deck<1>','<k>  The <o>rotted boards<k> below you look none too sturdy, but the ship must have\nbeen well constructed, as no visible holes or missing boards are visible.  A\nshort railing blocks access off the ship and beyond that a wall of <g>k<o>e<g>l<o>p<k>\nencases the ship in a cocoon of darkness.  What was once a large arbalest is\nmounted on the deck here, but is now a decomposed testiment to brigandry.\n',78,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9629,0,0,0,'<o>Starboard Deck<1>','<k>  The <o>rotted boards<k> below you look none too sturdy, but the ship must have\nbeen well constructed, as no visible holes or missing boards are visible.  A\nshort railing blocks access off the ship and beyond that a wall of <g>k<o>e<g>l<o>p<k>\nencases the ship in a cocoon of darkness.  What was once a large arbalest is\nmounted on the deck here, but is now a decomposed testiment to brigandry.\n',78,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9630,0,0,0,'<o>Starboard Deck<1>','<k>  The <o>rotted boards<k> below you look none too sturdy, but the ship must have\nbeen well constructed, as no visible holes or missing boards are visible.  A\nshort railing blocks access off the ship and beyond that a wall of <g>k<o>e<g>l<o>p<k>\nencases the ship in a cocoon of darkness.  What was once a large arbalest is\nmounted on the deck here, but is now a decomposed testiment to brigandry.\n',78,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9631,0,0,0,'<o>Fore Deck<1>','<o>  The prow of the ship has been mounted with a huge intricately carved naked\nwoman.  A mane of <r>red hair<o> blows back as if in a stiff breeze, large breasts\nwith perky nipples poke out, leading the way, and broad shapely hips emerge\nfrom the very bow of the ship, carved with great mastery.  A heavy <k>iron<o> plow\nof the sort used for ramming has been fitted to the ship below the carving.\n',78,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9632,0,0,0,'<o>Center Deck<1>','<o>  The <k>rotted boards<o> below you look none too sturdy, but the ship must have\nbeen well constructed, as no visible holes or missing boards are visible.  The\nfore deck lies to the west.\n',78,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9633,0,0,0,'<o>Center Mast<1>','<o>  A thick, scarred mast leads upwards into <k>darkness<o>.  The mast appears\nto be heavily stained with <r>blood<o> that even the constant pressure of the ocean\ncan\'t wash away.  Heavy <w>iron<o> leg and arm shackles have been set into the mast.\nThe center deck of the ship lies in all directions.  The fore of the ship\nappears to lie to the west.\n',78,139588,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9634,0,0,0,'<o>Center Deck<1>','<o>  The <k>rotted boards<o> below you look none too sturdy, but the ship must have\nbeen well constructed, as no visible holes or missing boards are visible.  The\nfore deck lies to the west.  A set of steep stairs leads below decks.\n',78,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9635,0,0,0,'<o>Aft Deck<1>','<o>  A large knobbed wheel is mounted here, used to control the ships rudder.\nThe deck is slightly raised, allowing a better view of the ship and the\nsurrounding water.  A thick curtain of <g>k<o>e<g>l<o>p blocks visibility off the ship,\nbut at one time this would have been a good spot to direct a battle.\n',78,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9636,0,0,0,'<o>Port Deck<1>','<k>  The <o>rotted boards<k> below you look none too sturdy, but the ship must have\nbeen well constructed, as no visible holes or missing boards are visible.  A\nshort railing blocks access off the ship and beyond that a wall of <g>k<o>e<g>l<o>p<k>\nencases the ship in a cocoon of darkness.  What was once a large arbalest is\nmounted on the deck here, but is now a decomposed testiment to brigandry.\n',78,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9637,0,0,0,'<o>Port Deck<1>','<k>  The <o>rotted boards<k> below you look none too sturdy, but the ship must have\nbeen well constructed, as no visible holes or missing boards are visible.  A\nshort railing blocks access off the ship and beyond that a wall of <g>k<o>e<g>l<o>p<k>\nencases the ship in a cocoon of darkness.  What was once a large arbalest is\nmounted on the deck here, but is now a decomposed testiment to brigandry.\n',78,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9638,0,0,0,'<o>Port Deck<1>','<k>  The <o>rotted boards<k> below you look none too sturdy, but the ship must have\nbeen well constructed, as no visible holes or missing boards are visible.  A\nshort railing blocks access off the ship and beyond that a wall of <g>k<o>e<g>l<o>p<k>\nencases the ship in a cocoon of darkness.  What was once a large arbalest is\nmounted on the deck here, but is now a decomposed testiment to brigandry.\n',78,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9639,0,0,0,'<o>Cargo Hold<1>','<o>  Many chests, barrels and canvas sacks are stacked up along the walls. Heavy\nhooks have been set into the ceiling and the walls to hang sacks and other\ngoods from.\n',78,139592,30,0,0,0,0,-1,20,90,0,'',NULL),
(9640,0,0,0,'<o>Galley<1>','<k>  Pots<o> and <k>pans<o> hang from hooks on the walls.  A large oven sits in\none corner and numerous cabinets have been built into the walls.\n',78,139592,30,0,0,0,0,-1,20,90,0,'',NULL),
(9641,0,0,0,'<o>Mess Hall<1>','<o>  Rows of narrow benches and tables fill the room.  Although mostly rotted,\nthe tables appear to have not been treated well in the past.  Carvings, scorch\nmarks and missing chunks mar the parts that have not eroded away.\n',78,139592,30,0,0,0,0,-1,20,90,0,'',NULL),
(9642,0,0,0,'<o>Bunk Room<1>','<o>  Rows of narrow cots fill this room.  Bedsheets and clothing float about in\nthe water.  Crew members only spent their sleeping hours here and as such their\nis little adornment or furniture.\n',78,139592,30,0,0,0,0,-1,20,90,0,'',NULL),
(9643,0,0,0,'<o>Below Decks<1>','<k> Murky<o> water impairs visibility, while pieces of furniture,\nwood, torn cloth and other debris float in and out of the room.  This\nnarrow hallway continues eastwards while doors lie both north, south\nand west.\n',78,139592,30,0,0,0,0,-1,20,90,0,'',NULL),
(9644,0,0,0,'<o>Below Decks<1>','<k>  Murky<o> water impairs visibility, while pieces of furniture, wood, torn\ncloth and other debris float in and out of the room.  A steep set of stairs\nlead upwards to the main deck.  This narrow hallway continues westwards while\ndoors lie both north and south.\n',78,139592,30,0,0,0,0,-1,20,90,0,'',NULL),
(9645,0,0,0,'<o>Cargo Hold<1>','<o>  Many chests, barrels and canvas sacks are stacked up along the walls. Heavy\nhooks have been set into the ceiling and the walls to hang sacks and other\ngoods from.\n',78,139592,30,0,0,0,0,-1,20,90,0,'',NULL),
(9646,0,0,0,'<o>Captain\'s Quarters<1>','<r>  Stately mahogany boards cover the walls, stolen from some far off mansion\nand poorly remounted.  Frames mounted on the walls must have once held\npaintings that are now only a memory.  Various shattered and tarnished\ntreasures lie strewn about, gaudy loot from a lifetime of robbery.\n',78,139592,30,0,0,0,0,-1,20,90,0,'',NULL),
(9647,0,0,0,'<o>First Mate\'s Room<1>','<b>  Blue wallpaper with a gaudy <c>p<b>a<c>t<b>t<c>e<b>r<c>n<b> give this room a more subdued, regal\nlook than the rest of the ship.  A <o>rusty chandelier<b> hangs from the ceiling,\ntreasure from some long past plundering.  A large <r>mahogany<1> desk dominates part\nof the room, now rotten and falling apart.  A once beautiful armoire stands\nagainst another wall, doors long missing.\n',-1,139592,30,0,0,0,0,-1,20,90,0,'',NULL),
(9648,0,0,0,'<k>Cramped Bilge<1>','<k>  Disgustingly <o>filthy<k> water would make visibility impossible here if it weren\'t\nso cramped to begin with.  A thick sludge of unknown material lines the floor.\n',78,139592,30,0,0,0,0,-1,1,60,0,'',NULL),
(9649,0,0,0,'<k>A Plush Coffin<1>','<r>This coffin has been outfitted in plush red velvet with plenty of\nsoft padding.  A large <W>cream white<1><r> silk pillow is sewn into\nthe velvet at one end.  The dimensions of the coffin are huge, as if\nsized for a very corpulent man, an ill-fated couple or perhaps even a\nnoble surrounded by treasures.  Oddly, a shiny <Y>golden<1><r> door\nhandle has been installed on the inside.<1>\n',-1,139273,32,0,0,0,0,-1,1,36,0,'',NULL),
(9650,0,0,0,'A Strange Island in the Fog','  You are surrounded by an impossibly dense fog.  From what you can\nsee, the island is covered in an extremely thick layer of vegetation,\noffering excellent cover for predators.  You hear the muffled sounds\nof ocean waves crashing.  Your sense of direction is completely\nobliterated and you feel compelled to stay where you are.\n<w>A large wraith-like man shrouded in tattered brown robes is here.<z>\n',198,393281,60,40,9651,1,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9651,0,0,0,'On Soft Ground Deep in the Fog','  You feel a soft, mushy ground under your feet although the fog here\nis so dense that you cannot see the ground, or even your outstretched\nhand. Your sense of direction is completely obliterated and you feel\ncompelled to stay where you are. You hear the faint lapping of water.\n',198,131137,60,40,9652,1,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9652,0,0,0,'On a Boat Deep in the Fog','  A dense, disorienting fog smothers your senses. You think that you\nfaintly hear the light splashing of water and feel the slight swell\nof the boat under you as it moves gently across the water.\n',198,131137,60,40,9653,1,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9653,0,0,0,'On a Boat Deep in the Fog','  A dense, disorienting fog smothers your senses. You think that you\nfaintly hear the light splashing of water and feel the slight swell\nof the boat under you as it moves gently across the water. Occasionally\nyou believe that you hear the screeching of seagulls.\n',198,131137,60,40,9654,1,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9654,0,0,0,'On a Boat Near a Remote Island','  An impossibly dense fog lays mysteriously to the east. To the west you see\nthe eastern coast of an island that seems shaped like a C, with the open part\nnear your ship.\n',198,131137,60,40,9655,1,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9655,0,0,0,'On a Boat in an Island Cove','  Surrounding you on all sides of the cove is beach, and then a dense\ngreen rain forest.  The mouth of the cove, and beyond it the vast fog-covered\nocean, is off to the east.  You are able to see down to the bottom of this\nshallow area through crystal clear turquoise water, all the way to a white\nsilt floor.  A cool breeze arrives from the direction of the ocean.\nTo the west is a small islet in the center of the cove.\n',198,131137,60,40,27571,1,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9656,0,0,0,'On a Boat in an Island Cove','  Surrounding you on all sides of the cove is beach, and then a dense\ngreen rain forest.  The mouth of the cove, and beyond it the vast fog-covered\nocean, is off to the east.  You are able to see down to the bottom of this\nshallow area through crystal clear turquoise water, all the way to a white\nsilt floor.  A cool breeze arrives from the direction of the ocean.\nTo the west is a small islet in the center of the cove.\n<w>A large wraith-like man shrouded in tattered brown robes is here.<z>\n',198,131137,60,40,9657,1,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9657,0,0,0,'On a Boat Near a Remote Island','  An impossibly dense fog lays mysteriously to the east. To the west you see\nthe eastern coast of an island that seems shaped like a C, with the open part\nnear your ship.\n',198,131137,60,40,9658,1,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9658,0,0,0,'On a Boat Deep in the Fog','  A dense, disorienting fog smothers your senses. You think that you\nfaintly hear the light splashing of water and feel the slight swell\nof the boat under you as it moves gently across the water. Occasionally\nyou believe that you hear the screeching of seagulls.\n',198,131137,60,40,9659,1,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9659,0,0,0,'On a Boat Deep in the Fog','  A dense, disorienting fog smothers your senses. You think that you\nfaintly hear the light splashing of water and feel the slight swell\nof the boat under you as it moves gently across the water.\n',198,131137,60,40,9660,1,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9660,0,0,0,'On Soft Ground Deep in the Fog','  You feel a soft, mushy ground under your feet although the fog here\nis so dense that you cannot see the ground, or even your outstretched\nhand. Your sense of direction is completely obliterated and you feel\ncompelled to stay where you are. You hear the faint lapping of water.\n',198,131137,60,40,13179,1,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9701,-30,-35,0,'A Jungle Path','  Just slightly more then a game path this hard packed trail is\nalmost overgrown with thick lush vegetation.  From all about you\ncome the calls of exotic birds and unseen animals while little but\ndim threads of light are able to penetrate the thick canopy overhead.\nThe heat and humidity are almost unbearable and the littlest effort makes\nyou break out in a heavy sweat.  Considering the thick vegetation about\nyou, it appears back to the southeast is your only option.  The path\ndoes continue to the north, but it seems as if a wall of vegetation\nhas almost magically sprung up to bar the path.  Maybe with some work\nthough the path can be opened back up.\n',65,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(9702,-29,-36,0,'A Jungle Path','  Just slightly more then a game path this hard packed trail is\nalmost overgrown with thick lush vegetation.  From all about you\ncome the calls of exotic birds and unseen animals while little but\ndim threads of light are able to penetrate the thick canopy overhead.\nThe heat and humidity are almost unbearable and the littlest effort makes\nyou break out in a heavy sweat.  Considering the thick vegetation about\nyou, your choices for movement are strictly limited to either one way or\nanother down the path.\n',65,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
