(9791,15,-87,-1,'Minotaur\'s Lair','You have wandered into the heart of some beast\'s lair.  Some dark liquid\ndrips from the ceiling, collecting into a small dark pool in the middle\nof the lair.  Bones, humanoid and otherwise, are strewn all about.  You\nfeel that you should get away from this place while you still are able.\nThe echo of the dripping liquid is maddening.\n',55,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9792,14,-88,-1,'Catacombs','This is a simple part of the catacombs below the ruined castle.  The walls\nare made of very ancient, crumbling rock.  It seems as if it could cave-in\nany minute.  The stench of rotten flesh is very strong here, coupled with\na damp smell.  You hear water dripping in the distance, or is it somewhere\nclose by?\n',55,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9793,13,-87,-1,'Catacombs','This is a simple part of the catacombs below the ruined castle.  The walls\nare made of very ancient, crumbling rock.  It seems as if it could cave-in\nany minute.  The stench of rotten flesh is very strong here, coupled with\na damp smell.  You hear water dripping in the distance, or is it somewhere\nclose by?\n',55,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9794,15,-89,-1,'Catacombs','This is a simple part of the catacombs below the ruined castle.  The walls\nare made of very ancient, crumbling rock.  It seems as if it could cave-in\nany minute.  The stench of rotten flesh is very strong here, coupled with\na damp smell.  You hear water dripping in the distance, or is it somewhere\nclose by?\n',55,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9795,15,-86,-1,'A Prize-Keep','This is a very non-descript corner of the cavern.  It is blocked off by\nsolid granite on three sides and has a door made of huge bones in the\nsouthern wall.  It seems to be used as a prize-keep by some large beast.\n',55,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(9899,39,-34,2,'Arch Mage\'s Personal Study','Rather peaceful compared to the magical ridden rooms below this\nstudy is packed wall to wall with history tomes and other boring\nbooks.  Leaflets of parchment lie scattered about either in small\nstacks or half bound tomes being prepared to be made into books.\nNothing of any interest seems to adorn the walls or ceiling other\nthen the plain building materials used in their construction.  A\nsimple tile floor is oddly warm, most likely by magic, and an odor\nof ink and parchment drifts throughout.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(9900,41,-28,1,'Main Gate','  You are underneath what appears to be the gatehouse.  The walls are slick with\nthe ichor of red and black blood that seems to slowly seep out of the arrow\nholes.  The gate lies in splintered shards strewn all about.  A deep sense of\nforeboding slowly creeps over you, almost paralyzing you with an irrational\nsense of fear.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9901,41,-29,1,'Inside the Main Gate','  You stand just inside the main gate, ankle deep in what appears to be a sea\nof blood.  The pool of crimson stretches to the east and west, as well as to the\nsouth where you catch glimpses of a huge engine of war standing in the road.\n',55,163848,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9902,41,-27,1,'Outside the Main Gate','  A shimmering veil of light hangs before you, stretching upwards to the\nunfathomable reaches of the cavern ceiling.  Hints of a gateway to the south can\nbe glimpsed through the pulsating wall of light.  A granite block is anchored\nfirmly in the ground.\n',55,163848,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9903,42,-29,1,'Wall Road','  You stand amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of black liquid break the\nplacidity of the almost perfect red surface.  Floating in the liquid are gory\nreminders of battles fought long ago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand\nyears of warfare, a severed limb floats by and brushes up against your leg.  You\nsee a steel door to the north set in the fortress wall, and to the south a\nnameless building still stands.  The sea of crimson extends to the east and\nwest.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9904,40,-29,1,'Wall Road','  You stand amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of a more viscous black\nliquid break the placidity of the almost perfect red surface.  Drifting about in\nthe liquid are gory reminders of battles fought long ago.  As you survey the\naftermath of a thousand years of  warfare, a severed arm floats by and gently\nnudges your leg.  A steel door rests in the fortress wall to the north while a\ncrumbling building stands to the south.  The sea of crimson extends to the  east\nand west.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9905,43,-29,1,'Wall Road','  You stand amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of black liquid break the\nplacidity of the almost perfect red surface.  Floating in the liquid are gory\nreminders of battles fought long ago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand\nyears of blood-letting, a disembodied head bumps up against your leg and stares\nhorrifically up at you.  The fortress wall towers over you to the north and an\nsteel door rests in the wall of a nameless building to the south.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9906,44,-29,1,'Wall Road','  You stand amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of black liquid break the\nplacidity of the almost perfect red surface.  Floating in the liquid are gory\nreminders of battles fought long ago.  As you survey the aftermath of a\nthousands years of warfare, a  severed leg brushes up against your leg.  The\nfortress wall towers over you to the north and east while the sea of crimson\nextends further to the west and south.  A steel door is set in the fortress wall\nto the northeast.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9907,44,-30,1,'Wall Road','  You stand amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of black liquid break the\nmorbid serenity of the almost perfect red surface.  Drifting in the liquid are\ngory reminders of battles fought long ago.  As you survey the aftermath of a\nthousand years of warfare, an unidentifiable limb from some exotic creature\njabs you in the leg.  The fortress wall stands to the east and a simple building\nremains standing to your west.  The sea of crimson continues to the north and\nsouth.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9908,44,-31,1,'Wall Road','  You stand ankle deep amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Eddies of a more viscous\nblack liquid swirl about, disturbing the placidity of the almost perfect red\nsurface.  Carried about by the swirls are gory epithets of battles fought ages\nago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand years of warfare, a limbless\ntrunk drifts by and almost topples you.  This appears to be an intersection of\nsorts, with passage leading off in all directions.  The crimson tide continues\non to the north, south, and west.  You notice a crumbled section of wall to the\neast.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9909,44,-32,1,'Wall Road','  You stand amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of black liquid break the\nplacidity of the almost perfect red surface.  Floating in the liquid are gory\nreminders of battles fought long ago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand\nyears of warfare, a severed foot bumps your calf gently.  An obsidian wall\nstands menacingly to your west and the crumbled ruins of a section of the\neastern wall lies to the east.  The sea of crimson stretches to the north and\nsouth.  The stench of death wafts to through the air from the south.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9910,44,-33,1,'Wall Road','  You stand amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of black liquid lazily form\ngrotesque patterns in the almost perfect red surface.  The sight of what lies in\nthe middle of your path brings bile to your mouth.  Stacked haphazardly in the\nblood are hundreds of corpses, each unique in its condition of rot and\nassortment of missing limbs.  The stench of death and decay assaults your\nnostrils, causing a wave of nausea to sweep through your body.  The fortress\nwall stands to the east, casting a pall over the grisly scene while a obsidian\nbuilding stands to the west.  Passage along the side of the orgiastic display of\ncadavers is possible to even more pools of crimson to the north and south.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9911,44,-34,1,'Wall Road','  You stand amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of black liquid break the\nplacidity of the almost perfect red surface.  Floating in the liquid are gory\nreminders of battles fought long ago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand\nyears of warfare, a severed arm floats by you and gets entangled in\nyour legs.  As you disentangle yourself from the offending limb, you take in\nyour surroundings.  The fortress wall towers over you to the east, casting a\nshadow over the obsidian walled building to the west.  The sea of crimson\ncontinues to the north and south.  You notice the heavy stench of death coming\nfrom the north.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9912,44,-35,1,'Wall Road','  You stand amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of black liquid break the\nplacidity of the almost perfect red surface.  Floating in the liquid are gory\nreminders of battles fought long ago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand\nyears of warfare, a severed foot bumps into your leg.  The fortress walls tower\nover you to the east, casting a pall over the obsidian walled building that\nstands to the west.  The sea of crimson continues on to the north and south.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9913,44,-36,1,'Wall Road','  You stand ankle deep amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Eddies of a more viscous\nblack liquid swirl about, disturbing the placidity of the almost perfect red\nsurface.  Carried about by the swirls are gory epithets of battles fought long\nago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand years of warfare, a disembodied\nhead brushes up  against your calf and stares horrifically up at you.  The\nfortress walls loom to the east and south while the sea of crimson extends to\nthe north and west.  A steel door is set in the crumbling tower to the\nsoutheast.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9914,43,-36,1,'Wall Road','  You stand ankle deep amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Eddies of a more viscous\nblack liquid swirl about, disturbing the placidity of the almost perfect red\nsurface.  Carried about by the swirls are gory epithets of battles fought long\nago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand years of warfare, a severed leg\ngrazes your leg.  Passage to the east and west is possible via the sea of\ncrimson while the fortress wall stands to the south and an obsidian wall blocks\npassage to the north.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9915,42,-36,1,'Wall Road','  You stand amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of black liquid break the\nplacidity of the almost perfect red surface.  Floating in the liquid are gory\nremains of a thousand years of warfare.  As you survey the aftermath of a battle\nfought ages ago, a limbless trunk hunkers into your legs, almost bowling you\nover.  The fortress wall stands to the south while an obsidian walled building\nlies to the north.  The crimson path continues on to the east and west.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9916,41,-36,1,'Wall Road','  You stand amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of black liquid break the\nplacidity of the almost perfect red surface.  Drifting about in the liquid are\ngory remains of battles fought long ago.  As you survey the aftermath of a\nthousand years of warfare, a severed arm floats by and bumps into your leg.  The\nfortress wall stands solidly to the south while a wall of obsidian restricts\nmovement to the north.  The gruesome crimson path continues on to the east and\nwest.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9917,40,-36,1,'Wall Road','  You stand ankle deep amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Eddies of a  thicker\nblack liquid sluggishly swirl about, disturbing the placidity of the almost\nuniform red surface.  Carried about by the dark current are gory epithets of\nbattles fought ages ago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand years of\nwarfare, a mass of what appears to be entrails entangles itself in your legs.\nFighting down the rising sensation of nausea, you look about for an exit to\nthis grisly place.  The fortress wall towers over you to the south, casting a\nshadow over the obsidian walled building to the north.  The sea of crimson\ncontinues on to the east and west.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9918,39,-36,1,'Wall Road','  You stand amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of black liquid break the\nplacidity of the almost perfect red surface.  Floating in the liquid are gory\nremains of battles fought long ago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand\nyears of warfare, a severed leg bumps into your leg.  Fighting down nausea, you\nnotices that the sea of blood continues to the east and west.  The crumbled\nremains of a section of the fortress wall lie to the south, and an obsidian\nwalled building can be seen to the north.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9919,38,-36,1,'Wall Road','  You stand ankle deep amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Eddies of a more viscous\nblack liquid swirl about, disturbing the placidity of the almost perfect red\nsurface.  Carried about by the swirls are gory epithets of battles fought long\nago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand years of warfare, a limbless\ntrunk bumps into you, almost toppling you over.  To the west, the fortress wall\nappears to have been torn asunder by some mad deity of war, rubble lying strewn\nall about.  Ruins of what used to be the southwestern tower of the fortress lie\nto the southwest.  To the south, you can see a portion of the wall that is still\nstanding.  The sea of crimson continues on to the north and east.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9920,38,-35,1,'Wall Road','  You stand amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of black liquid break the\nplacidity of the almost perfect red surface.  Floating in the liquid are gory\nreminders of battles fought long ago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand\nyears of warfare, a severed arm drifts by and catches on your leg.  The fortress\nwall towers over you to the west and an obsidian walled building stands to the\neast.  The sea of crimson extends to the north and south.  You feel a slight tug\non your legs pulling you northwards, almost like a sluggish tide in this\nmottled red and black miasma.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9921,38,-34,1,'Whirlpool','  You stand knee deep in a pool of crimson blood.  There is a slight whirlpool\neffect as the sticky red liquid slowly drains downwards into some unknown\ncursed abyss.  The fortress wall stands as a silent guardian of sorts over this\nspectacle while an obsidian walled building stands to the east.  By walking up\nagainst the wall to the west, passage to the north and south is possible.\n',55,163848,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9922,38,-33,1,'Wall Road','  You stand amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of black liquid break the\nplacidity of the almost perfect red surface.  Floating in the liquid are gory\nreminders of battles fought long ago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand\nyears of warfare, an unidentifiable body part drifts on by.  The fortress wall\ntowers over you to the west and an obsidian walled building stands solidly to\nthe east.  The trail of crimson continues to the north and south.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9923,38,-32,1,'Wall Road','  You stand ankle deep amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Eddies of a more viscous\nblack liquid swirl about, disturbing the placidity of the almost perfect red\nsurface.  Carried about by the swirls are gory epithets of battles fought long\nago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand years of warfare, a disembodied\nhead bumps into your leg and gazes horrifically up at you.  As you fight down\nthe urge to empty your stomach, you notice the stench of death and decay\nwafting in from the north.  The fortress wall looms to the west, casting a pall\nover the obsidian walled building standing to the east.  The sea of crimson\ncontinues to the north and south.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9924,38,-31,1,'Wall Road','  You stand ankle deep amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Eddies of a more viscous\nblack liquid swirl about, disturbing the placidity of the almost perfect red\nsurface.  Carried about by the swirls are gory epithets of battles fought ages\nago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand years of slaughter, a severed\ntorso drifts by and almost topples you.  This appears to be an intersection of\nsorts, with passage leading off to the north, south and east.  The fortress wall\nstands solidly to your west, casting a bit of shadow over you.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9925,38,-30,1,'Wall Road','  You stand ankle deep in a sea of crimson blood.  Swirls of black liquid break\nthe placidity of the almost perfect red surface.  Floating in the liquid are\ngory reminders of a thousand years of warfare.  As you survey the aftermath of\nbattles fought long ago, innards from some unknown beast entangle your legs,\nalmost causing you to trip and fall.  The fortress wall looms over you to the\nwest while you notice a jumbled mass of masonry to your east.  The crimson sea\nextends off to the north and south.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9926,38,-29,1,'Wall Road','  You stand in the middle of a gory scene of gothic proportions.  Disembodied\nheads, limbs, and other unidentifiable body parts have been piled up in the\nmiddle of your path by some unknown undertaker.  The stench of rotting flesh\nassaults your senses as you survey your surroundings.  A tower looms before you\nto your northwest while there is enough room around the jumbled mass of\ncadavers for passage to the east and south.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9927,39,-29,1,'Wall Road','  You stand ankle deep amidst a sea of crimson blood.  Eddies of a more viscous\nblack liquid swirl about, disturbing the placidity of the almost perfect red\nsurface.  Carried about by the swirls are gory epithets of battles fought long\nago.  As you survey the aftermath of a thousand years of warfare, something warm\nand wet slaps up against your leg.  The fortress wall looms over you to the\nnorth and the crumbled remains of a building lie to the south.  The sea of\ncrimson extends further to the east and west.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9928,42,-28,1,'Eastern Gate House','  You stand in the eastern gate house\'s bottom floor.  Arrow slits line both the\nwestern and northern walls.  Soft, pulsating light pours forth from the holes in\nthe northern walls, casting a bit of illumination over the crimson pool of\nliquid that covers the entire floor.  Upon closer inspection of the room, you\nnotice four sharp-edged stones that are half-submerged in the pool.  A spiderweb\nof cracks lines the ceiling, giving the entire room an air of impending doom\nand possible ruin from a collapsed ceiling.  A steel door can be seen to the\nsouth and a stone ladder leads upwards through a hole in the ceiling.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9929,42,-28,2,'Top of the Eastern Gate House','  You stand inside the top floor of the eastern gatehouse.  A huge gaping hole\nin the ceiling allows you to look out upon the vast expanse of the cavern\nceiling.  Resting solidly and half-buried by the dust that blankets the entire\nroom, is what would best be described as a boulder.  Steel doors rest in both\nthe eastern and western walls, while exit downwards is via a stone ladder that\npeeks through a hole in the floor.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9930,41,-28,2,'Gatekeeper\'s Office','  You stand in the middle of a large room relatively left unscathed by any\nwarfare over the years.  The furnishings of the room rest virtually untouched\nall about the room.  Some strange machinery rests by the southern portion of the\nroom while a tattered swathe of cloth still hangs from the northern wall.  A\nstone table rests in the middle of the room, still cluttered with various items\nnow blanketed in dust.  Steel doors rest in the eastern and western walls of\nthis room.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9931,40,-28,2,'Top of the Western Gate House','  You stand inside the top floor of the western gatehouse.  The ceiling has long\nago collapsed and rubble litters the floor.  Through the gaping hole in the\nceiling you can make out the cavern\'s ceiling in the distance.  On the north\nwall, a dilapidated stretch of cloth hangs in tatters.  Dust hangs heavily in\nthe air and over the entire room\'s contents.  Steel doors rest in both the\neastern and western walls, while exit downwards is via a stone ladder that\npeeks through a hole in the floor.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9932,40,-28,1,'Western Gate House','  You stand in the western gate house\'s bottom floor.  Arrow slits line both the\neastern and northern walls.  Soft, pulsating white light pours forth from the\nholes in the northern wall, casting a bit of illumination on a few stones that\nrest like islands in the ocean of blood covering the floor.  A steel door can be\nseen to the south, and a stone ladder leads upwards through a hole in the\nceiling.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9933,43,-28,2,'On The Northern Wall','  You are standing atop the northern wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled battlements\nyour view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets the area.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9934,44,-28,2,'On The Northern Wall','  You are standing atop the northern wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled battlements\nyour view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets the area.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9935,45,-28,1,'Base of the Northeastern Tower','  You stand inside the base of the stronghold\'s northeastern tower.  Rotting\nbits of wood float in the ankle deep pool of blood that swamps the room.  A\ncrumbling stone staircase leads upwards while a steel door stands in the\nsouthwestern corner of the room.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9936,45,-29,2,'On The Eastern Wall','  You are standing atop the eastern wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled battlements\nyour view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets the area.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9937,45,-30,2,'On The Eastern Wall','  You are standing atop the eastern wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled battlements\nyour view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets the area.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9938,39,-28,2,'On the Northern Wall','  You are standing atop the northern wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled battlements\nyou can almost make out a battle raging off in the distance, but your view is\nquickly obscured by the grey mist that blankets the area.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9939,38,-28,2,'On The Northern Wall','  You are standing atop the northern wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled battlements\nyour view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets the area.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9940,37,-28,1,'Base of the Northwestern Tower','  You stand inside the base of the stronghold\'s northwestern tower.  Rotting\nbits of wood float in the ankle deep pool of blood that swamps the room.  A\ncrumbling stone staircase leads upwards while a steel door stands in the\nsoutheastern corner of the room.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9941,37,-29,2,'On The Western Wall','  You are standing atop the western wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled battlements\nyour view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets the area.\n',55,163848,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9942,37,-30,2,'Narrow Section On The Western Wall','  You are standing atop a crumbling portion of the western wall.  The stones\nbeneath you creak unnaturally as only eldritch forces woven into the masonry\nhold this section of wall together.  Looking westwards over the shattered\nbattlements, your view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets the\narea.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(9943,37,-32,2,'On The Western Wall','  You are standing atop the western wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled battlements\nyour view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets the area.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9944,37,-31,2,'On The Western Wall','  You are standing atop the western wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled battlements\nyou can make out a monstrous siege tower looming in the mist.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9945,37,-33,2,'On The Western Wall','  You are standing atop the western wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled battlements\nyou can barely make out what appears to be a war torn battlefield.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9946,37,-34,2,'On The Western Wall','  You are standing atop the northern wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled battlements\nyour view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets the area.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9947,45,-28,2,'Top of the Northeastern Tower','  You stand inside the northeastern tower of the stronghold.  The rivers of\nblood so prevalent throughout the rest of the fortress are not present here.\nDust however seems to hold court in this space, as the entire room is covered\nin an inch-thick layer of fine soot.  Time-worn steel doors rest in the western\nand southern walls of the tower while a crumbling stone staircase leads\ndownwards.  Through arrow slits that line the walls you can catch glimpses of\ndrifting white mist outside.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9948,37,-28,2,'Top of the Northwestern Tower','  You stand inside the northwestern tower of the stronghold.  The rivers of\nblood so prevalent throughout the rest of the fortress are not present here.\nDust however seems to hold court in this space, as the entire room is covered\nin an inch-thick layer of fine soot.  Time-worn steel doors rest in the eastern\nand southern walls of the tower while a crumbling stone staircase leads\ndownwards.  Through a gaping hole set high in the north wall you can barely make\nout what appears to be the cavern ceiling.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9949,45,-34,2,'On The Eastern Wall','  You are standing atop the eastern wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking eastward out over the crumbled\nbattlements you can barely make out what appears to be a huge engine of war.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9950,45,-35,2,'On The Eastern Wall','  You are standing atop the eastern wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Look eastwards out over the crumbled\nbattlements your view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets the\narea.\n',55,163849,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9951,45,-36,2,'On The Eastern Wall','  You are standing atop the eastern wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking eastwards out over the crumbled\nbattlements your view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets the\narea.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9952,45,-37,2,'Top of the Southeastern Tower','  You stand inside the southeastern tower of the stronghold.  The rivers of\nblood so prevalent throughout the rest of the fortress are not present here.\nDust, however, seems to hold court in this space, as the entire room is covered\nin an inch-thick layer of fine soot.  Time-worn steel doors rest in the western\nand northern walls of the tower while a crumbling stone staircase leads\ndownwards.  Through a large fissure in the south wall you can make out through\nthe mist the back wall of the cavern.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9953,45,-37,1,'Base of the Southeastern Tower','  You stand inside the base of the stronghold\'s southeastern tower.  Rotting\nbits of wood float about in the ankle deep pool of blood that swamps the room.\nA crumbling stone staircase leads upwards while a steel door stands in the\nnorthwestern corner of the room.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9954,44,-37,2,'On The Southern Wall','  You are standing atop the southern wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled battlements\nyour view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets the area.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(9955,43,-37,2,'On The Southern Wall','  You are standing atop the southern wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled battlements\nyour view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets the area.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(9956,42,-37,2,'Narrow Section On The Southern Wall','  You are standing atop a crumbling portion of the southern wall.  The stones\nbeneath you creak unnaturally as only eldritch forces woven into the masonry\nhold this section of wall together.  Looking southward over the shattered\nbattlements, your view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets the\narea.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(9957,41,-37,2,'On The Southern Wall','  You are standing atop the southern wall of the fortress.  The stones are slick\nwith blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled battlements\nyou can barely make out what appears to be a huge engine of war.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(9958,40,-37,2,'On The Southern Wall','  You are standing atop the southern wall of the fortress.  The stones are\nslick with blood, almost treacherously so.  Looking out over the crumbled\nbattlements your view is obscured by an unnatural grey mist that blankets\nthe area.  Directly above you is a watchtower, its structure of rock and\nmortar largely reduced to rubble - perhaps from an ancient assault, but\nmost likely due to the inexorable, levelling fist of time.  A fresh trail\nof blood is spattered upon the jumble of rock leading up to the\nwatchtower.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,8,96,0,'',NULL),
(9959,45,-31,1,'Hole in the Eastern Wall','  You stand atop the rubble of a crumbled section of wall.  A few portions of\nthe wall remain standing, but for the most part the ramparts appear to have\nbeen torn down by some long forgotten weapon of war.  A quick glance around\nreveals bits and pieces of a battle waged eons ago, but the bones of the\ncombatants have long since decayed and their dust lies everywhere.  You can spy\na road to the west through the open areas in the surrounding rubble.  The still-\nexisting wall towers to your north while more rubble lies to the south.\n',55,163848,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9960,45,-32,1,'Hole in the Eastern Wall','  You stand amidst the rubble of a crumbled section of wall.  A few portions of\nthe wall remain upright, but for the most part the ramparts appear to have been\ntorn asunder by some long forgotten weapon of war.  A quick glance around\nreveals bits and pieces of a battle waged eons ago, but the bones of the\ncombatants have long since decayed and their dust lies everywhere.  You can spy\na road to the west through the open areas in the surrounding rubble.  To the\nsouth, a section of the eastern wall that remains standing casts a shadow over\nyou and more rubble lies to the north.\n',55,163848,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9961,39,-37,1,'Breach in the Southern Wall','  You stand atop the rubble of a crumbled section of wall.  A few portions of\nthe wall remain standing, but for the most part the ramparts appear to have\nbeen torn down by some long forgotten weapon of war.  A quick glance around\nreveals bits and pieces of a battle waged eons ago, but the bones of the\ncombatants have  long since decayed and their dust lies everywhere.  You can spy\na road to the north through the open areas in the surrounding rubble.\n',55,163848,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9962,38,-37,1,'Circle of Stones','  You stand amidst a circle of stones, the remains of the top of the\nsouthwestern tower.  Interestingly enough, the formation of the rubble appears\nto be too precise in its arrangement.  Amongst the debris, you can barely make\nout a few crushed helmets and a few other miscellaneous reminders of the\nviolence the took place in this doomed fortress eons ago.  The only visible\npassage from this room is through a small opening in the western portion of the\nring.\n',55,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9963,37,-37,1,'Tower Ruins','  You stand among the rubble of what apparently used to be the southwestern\ntower of the fortress.  The cause of this structure\'s eventual demise remains\nunknown.  Whether it was the passing of time or an invaders mining effort, the\nresult was the same.  Large stones lie strewn about, making passage to the\nnorth, west or south  impossible.  You see a small opening in the remains of the\neastern wall and a road is visible to the northeast.\n',55,163848,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9964,37,-36,1,'Breach in the Western Wall','  You stand atop the rubble of a crumbled section of wall.  A few portions of\nthe wall remain standing, but for the most part the ramparts appear to have\nbeen torn down by some long forgotten weapon of war.  A quick glance around\nreveals bits and pieces of a battle waged eons ago, but the bones of the\ncombatants have long since decayed and their dust lies everywhere.  You can spy\na road to the east through the open areas in the surrounding rubble.  It appears\na path can be picked over the jumbled stones to the north.\n',55,163848,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9965,37,-35,1,'Breach in the Western Wall','  You stand atop the rubble of a crumbled section of wall.  A few portions of\nthe wall remain upright, but for the most part the ramparts appear to have been\nripped asunder by some long forgotten weapon of war.  A quick glance around\nreveals bits and pieces of a battle waged eons ago, but the bones of the\ncombatants have long since decayed and their dust lies everywhere.  Half-buried\nin the mass of broken rock is what appears to be a gargantuan pot of some sort.\nYou can spy a road to the east through the open areas in the surrounding\nrubble.  It appears that access to the south is possible by picking your way\nover the jumbled mass of stones.\n',55,163848,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9967,41,-30,1,'Huge Battering Ram','  You stand here gaping in awe at the sight of what stands here before you in\nthe crimson tide.  A titanic battering ram lies here abandoned in the middle of\nthe road.  Through the mist, you can make out what appears to be an open area to\nthe south.  A steel door marred with deep furrows lies to the west.\n',55,163848,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9968,41,-31,1,'T\'ir Na Z\'goth Square','  You stand in the middle of a square that has been transformed over the eons\ninto something far different from what it was once intended for.  Corpses and\ndisembodied limbs are stacked high, rotting and decaying in the still air while\na brackish water slowly trickles out of the fountain in the middle of the\nsquare.  The stink of death is overwhelming here, causing a wave of nausea to\nsweep through your body.  As you glance down at the sea of crimson you are\nstanding in, trying desperately to avoid the gruesome sight of the cadavers,\ngrisly images behind the surface of the water grin back at you.  This place is\ncursed and the soldiers who waged war here doomed to remain in this unliving\nhell.  To the north, you can make out what appears to be a huge engine of war.\nAn obsidian archway lies to the south, a sense of malicious evil emanating from\nits opening.  The crimson sea of blood continues on to the east and west.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9969,42,-31,1,'F\'al Enlil Road','  You stand ankle deep in a sea of crimson blood.  Grisly remains of battles\nfought ages ago drift about in the liquid, swirling about with a darker, more\nviscous fluid that sluggishly creates patterns in the crimson.  Faces of\nlong-dead warriors leer obscenely back at you from under the surface, spirits\nnever laid to rest and consigned to an unliving hell.  A crumbling building lies\nto the north while an obsidian wall blocks passage to the south.  The sea of\ncrimson continues on to the east and west.  You notice a heavy stench of death\nand decay coming from the west.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9970,43,-31,1,'F\'al Enlil Road','  You stand ankle deep in a sea of crimson blood.  Grisly remains of battles\nfought ages ago drift about in the liquid, swirling about with a darker, more\nviscous fluid that sluggishly creates patterns in the crimson.  Visages of\nlong-dead warriors leer obscenely back at you from under the surface, spirits\nnever laid to rest and consigned to an unliving hell.  A crumbling building lies\nto the north while an obsidian wall blocks passage to the south.  The sea of\ncrimson continues on to the west and you can make out what appears to be an\nintersection of sorts to the east.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9971,40,-31,1,'F\'al Enlil Road','  You stand ankle deep in a sea of crimson blood.  Grisly remains of battles\nfought ages ago drift about in the liquid, swirling about with a darker, more\nviscous fluid that sluggishly creates patterns in the crimson.  Visages of\nlong-dead warriors leer obscenely back at you from under the surface, spirits\nnever laid to rest and consigned to an unliving hell.  The stone wall of a\nbuilding lies to the north while an sheet of obsidian blocks passage to the\nsouth.  The sea of crimson continues on to the east and west.  You detect a\noverpowering stench of death and decay coming from the east.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9972,39,-31,1,'F\'al Enlil Road','  You stand ankle deep in a sea of crimson blood.  Grisly remains of battles\nfought ages ago drift about in the liquid, swirling about with a darker, more\nviscous fluid that sluggishly creates patterns in the crimson.  Visages of\nlong-dead warriors leer obscenely back at you from under the surface, spirits\nnever laid to rest and consigned to an unliving hell.  A demolished building\nlies to the north, unreachable through the jumble of stone obstructing your\npath to it.  An obsidian wall blocks passage to the south while the sea of\ncrimson continues to the east and west.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9973,40,-30,1,'Spider Pens','  As you attempt to enter this building, thick ropy strands of some unknown\norigin obstruct your path.  Looking around, you notice that the entire room is\nfilled by these silky white strands and also that the floor is marred by many\ndeep slashes in the stone.  Decomposing bodies wrapped in a thin white film hang\nsuspended in the air, supported by strands hanging from the ceiling high above\nyour head.  Out of the corner of your eye, you think you can spot dark shadows\nin the corners of the room, but dismiss it as nothing.  A steel door rests in\nthe eastern wall.\n',55,163848,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9974,42,-30,1,'Back Room of the Barracks','  You stand in the back section of a long building.  Stone resting places line\nthe walls, still crackling with eldritch fire imbued upon them eons ago.  The\nwalls of this room are crumbled and the endless warfare waged has taken its\ntoll.  The room is littered with various items of war, all in states of\ndisrepair.  The room continues on to the east.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9975,43,-30,1,'Drow Warrior Barracks','  You stand at one end of a long, narrow building.  Amazingly, this construct\nhas withstood the tests of time and warfare and remains relatively intact.  What\nappear to be resting places crafted of stone line the walls, the stones still\ncrackling with vestiges of eldritch fire.  The room continues of to the west\nwhile a steel door stands in the north wall.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9976,39,-30,1,'Demolished Building','  You stand among the ruins of some unknown building of the past.  Cracked and\nbroken stones lie strewn about all around you, making movement around this area\nsomewhat difficult.  Underneath all of the rubble you can make out what appears\nto be suits of armor and other weapons of war apparently crushed by the\ncollapsing building.  Exit from this doomed building is only possible by picking\nyour way through the rubble to the west.\n',55,163848,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9977,39,-32,1,'Elite Guards\' Barracks','  The obsidian walls of this long room are bathed in an even darker hued\nliquid.  A dark sticky fluid seems to continually drip down the glassy surface,\npooling on the floor.  Stone beds line the walls and are also covered by the\nvile ebony fluid.  The room opens up to the east.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9978,40,-32,1,'Elite Guards\' Barracks','  The obsidian walls of this long room are bathed in an even darker hued\nliquid.  A dark sticky liquid seems to continually drip down the glassy surface.\nStone beds line the wall and are also covered with the vile ebony liquid.  The\nroom continues on to the east while exit from this room is through a steel door\nset in the east wall.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9979,41,-32,1,'Entrance to the Keep of Endless Night','  You stand in an archway made entirely of obsidian.  Sinister light glints off\nthe hard glassy surface of your surroundings, sending beams of eerie light all\nabout the room.  The entire area has a  sinister feel to it, almost as if the\nwalls were emanating a sense of evil.  Along with this sense of dread, sadness\nseems inexplicably to hang in the air.  Steel doors rest in the walls to the\nnorth and south while a large room can be seen to the south.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9980,42,-32,1,'High Priestess\' Quarters','  This room is devoid of any furnishings save a single slab of obsidian lying\nin the middle of the room.  A thick layer of dust blankets the room, evidence\nthat this chamber has remained undisturbed by mortal feet treading its area.  An\nintricately carved obsidian door rests in the southern wall.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9981,43,-32,1,'High Priestess\' Inner Sanctum','  You stand in the middle of an intricate web of spiritual power.  A sense of\nevil and wickedness overcomes you as the walls themselves seem to close in and\nattempt to transform your perception of  reality.  Unholiness rules supreme in\nthis sanctum of cruelty and malefic power.  Huge obsidian columns support an\narched ceiling high above your head.  A great feeling of foreboding overcomes\nyou as you realize that your presence somehow desecrates this most unholy of\nplaces.\n',55,163976,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9982,39,-33,1,'Fortress Armory','  You stand in an imposing room of metal fused to rock.  The entire chamber is\nin essence a jumbled mass of obsidian rock and fused metal, this unholy union\nof The World elements undoubtedly caused by an unbearable mystical heat eons\nago.  There is a steel door set in the eastern wall.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9983,40,-33,1,'Dark Hallway','  You stand in a narrow hallway that is barely illuminated by a gently\nthrobbing green glow coming from an open area to the east.  The obsidian walls\nof this hall are cold and slick to the touch.  There is a steel door set in the\nwestern wall as well as one set in the southern wall.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9984,41,-33,1,'Central Courtyard','  You stand in the middle of a large courtyard.  Glowing green fungus growing on\nthe walls illuminate the area with a pulsating emerald light.  A fountain in\nthe center of the courtyard bubbles and boils, giving off steam and an\nunnaturally putrid odor.  A gargantuan ebony archway can be seen to the north\nwhile a steel door set in the south wall affords passage in that direction.\nShadowed hallways can be seen to the east and west.\n',55,163848,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9985,42,-33,1,'Dark Hallway','  You stand in a narrow hallway barely illuminated by a gently throbbing green\nglow coming from an open area to the west.  The obsidian walls of this hall are\ncold and slick to the touch.  Ornately engraved doors of obsidian rest in the\nnorthern and eastern walls.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9986,43,-33,1,'Shrine of C\'ime En\'lith','  You stand in a chamber where maleficence and unconscionable evil hold court.\nDarkness and doom radiate from the pitch black walls and the ebony artifacts\nlying about.  Unspeakable acts of evil and cruelty have been performed in this\nsanctum to C\'ime En\'lith, patron deity of this degenerate race of drow.  The\nmost striking of the shrine\'s contents appears to be a massive sacrificial\naltar standing by the eastern wall.  An intricately carved door of obsidian\nstands in the western wall.\n',55,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9987,39,-34,1,'Arch Mage\'s Inner Sanctum','  Unnatural power crackles and snaps in the air of this sanctum.  An aura of\nevil seems to resonate from every surface of this unnatural room.  Lines of\npower and force zigzag across the surface of the pitch-black walls and floor.\nYour head spins from the heady sense of malefic power, the voice of vile\ncorruption whispering in your head caressing you like a dark mistress.  Night\nand day magic rules supreme in this inner sanctum of dark sorcery.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9988,40,-34,1,'Storage Room','  You stand in a large, but plain and decrepit room.  Huge metal casks still\nline the wall but remain empty, probably having been in this barren state for\nages.  Dust lies heavily on everything in the chamber and a steel door rests in\nthe north wall.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9989,41,-34,1,'The Chamber of Dusk','  The chamber you now stand in is dark and has a gloomy pallor about it.  The\nwalls seem to barely reflect any illumination whatsoever, lending to the\ndarkness that seems ready to encompass everything.  A set of huge steel doors\nstand in the east wall while a lone steel door rests in the north wall.  From\nthe south, an almost palpable darkness seems to creep in from the pitch black\ngloom beyond an open archway.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9990,42,-34,1,'The Chamber of War','  You stand in the middle of a room far different in a way than any other in\nthe keep.  Not present are the smooth, slick obsidian walls so common within the\nkeep\'s confines.  In their stead stand rough hewn and jagged shards of obsidian,\na savage display of architecture at its basest level.  Thrown together\nhaphazardly, the walls themselves give off an aura of primal fury, a sense of\nbarbarous malediction.  The lone bit of furnishing in this room is a single\ngargantuan obsidian table set firmly in the middle of the chamber.  A pair of\nsteel doors stand solidly in the west wall.\n',55,163976,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9991,43,-34,1,'WarMaster\'s Quarters','The room you stand in is vastly different from anything else in this dark and\naugust keep.  Not present are the harsh lines and auras of death.  In their stead\nis a sense of sensuous abandon - a far cry from the WarMaster\'s own stern\npersonage.  The obsidian walls and ceiling of this room are a dark and\nforbidding, but the general ambiance differs.  The remains of swathes of cloth\nhang from the walls in tatters, one of the room\'s few furnishings.  A steel door\nis set in the southern wall.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9992,39,-35,1,'Arch Mage\'s Quarters','  The stink of rotting flesh and other unmentionable substances hangs in the air\nin this most depraved of quarters.  Darkness seems to pulsate from the very\nwalls, obsidian night cloaking the room.  Countless containers of varying sizes\nand shapes line the room, resting in alcoves crudely carved into the ebony\nstones of the wall.  The only exit from this chamber appears to be an\nintricately carved door made of a ruby-like substance that hangs suspended in\nthe eastern wall.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9993,40,-35,1,'Dark Corridor','  You stand in a shadowed hallway that is barely illuminated by a violently\npulsating red glow streaming in from the east.  The obsidian walls of this hall\nare cold and slick to the touch.  An intricately chiseled door made from some\nruby-like substance hangs suspended in the western wall.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9994,41,-35,1,'Fane of Endless Night','  The chamber you stand in stretches upwards to a ceiling barely visible high\nabove your head.  An almost palpable darkness hangs thickly in the air and the\nobsidian walls add to the gloom by unnaturally leeching off the room\'s\nillumination.  The hairs on the nape of your neck rise as you sense a union of\narcane might and unholy power.  A raised dais covers the southern portion of the\nchamber while you notice some strange patterns engraved in the ebony marble\nbeneath your feet.  Shadowed hallways lead off to the east and west while slight\nillumination creeps in from an archway to the north.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9995,42,-35,1,'Dark Corridor','  You stand in a shadowed hallway that is barely illuminated by a violently\npulsating red glow coming from the west.  The obsidian walls of this hall are\ncold and slick to the touch.  An intricately chiseled door made entirely of a\nruby-like substance rests solidly in the eastern wall.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9996,43,-35,1,'WarMaster\'s Office','  Spartan would be an apt word to describe this chamber.  The only things that\ngrace this room are a huge onyx table resting in the middle of the floor and a\nmass of bones that hangs suspended in the air unnaturally above the table.  On\nthe east wall you see the remains of a tattered banner hanging there, and a\nthick layer of dust blankets the entire room\'s contents.  An intricately carved\ndoor made of a ruby-like substance affords passage to the west while a\nsolid steel door rests in the north wall.\n',55,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9997,36,-31,2,'Top of the Siege Tower \"Doom\"','  You stand on the top of a this tower, an engine of war of monstrous\nproportions.  The wooden planks beneath your feet thrum as if imbibed with a\nmagical sustaining force.  As you survey your surroundings, you can make out\nwhat appears to be a battle raging all around the tower, but your view is\nquickly obscured by a thick mist that covers the area.  A metal plank leads off\nto the east and rests on the fortress wall while a set of steps leads down into\nthe belly of this huge tower.\n',55,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9998,36,-31,1,'Base of the Siege Tower \"Doom\"','You stand deep within the bowels of the siege tower, the only exit from this\nchamber is a set of stairs leading upwards through a small hole in the ceiling.\nThis room is devoid of all furnishings, simply because the warring faction that\nuses this warmonger needs no amenities in the endless battles they wage - so\nset in their warlike ways that Spartan accommodations suit them.  Narrow arrow\nslits line the walls all around, affording little view of what might transpire\noutside.  Peeking through the slits, you catch glimpses of ghostly figures waging\nand endless war outside the tower\'s confines.\n',55,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(9999,41,-26,1,'Standing in a Cave Before an Ancient Fortress','  A thick, white mist hangs heavily in the air.  The dampness of the haze clings\nto you and visibility is rendered to almost nothing.  Through patches of the\nunnatural fog, you can make out some of the caves contents.  Your senses reel as\nyour mind attempts to fathom the dimensions of the cave you now stand in.  All\nabout you, the cave walls seem hundreds of feet away one instant, but right at\nyour fingertips the next.  The ceiling of this ensorcered cavern hangs\nunbelievable high above you, yet obsidian stalactites hover just a few feet\nabove your head.  As the mist parts again, you can make out what appears to be a\nhuge, crumbling fortress sprawled out to the south.  As you look upon this dark\nand decrepit bastion, a sensation of dread courses through your body.  Weird\nmagics and strange blue witchfire run along the edges of the walls, crackling\nand licking along the tops of the crenelations.  Passage to the south can be\nmade by picking a path carefully through the stalagmites rising from the cave\nfloor.  An ancient set of steps leads up out of the cave to the north.\n',55,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10000,39,-26,1,'A Dirt Path','You are traveling along a dirt path that has many deep ruts in it.  Nearby\nto the southeast you can see a line of mountains and even nearer to the\nnortheast you notice a creeping white mist issuing forth from the ground.\n',64,131076,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10001,39,-27,1,'A Dirt Path','You are traveling along a dirt path that has many deep ruts in it.  Nearby\nto the southeast you can make out a line of mountains.  A mysterious white\nfog can be made out nearby to the northeast and what appears to be a\nwinding, mountain trail begins to the south.\n',64,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10002,39,-28,1,'A Mountain Trail','This appears to be the beginning of a trail leading through the mountains\nto the east.  While surveying everything about you, you cannot help but\nnotice a few strange metal flecks spread out along the trail.  A worn\ndirt path lies to the north and the trail continues to wind amongst the\nrocks to the southeast.\n',64,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10003,40,-29,1,'A Mountain Trail','Even though the elevation here is not very extreme, you sense that the\nsurrounding atmosphere is noticeable thinner than the surrounding\ncountryside\'s air.  Strange metal flakes lie strewn about in the dirt at\nyour feet.\n',64,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10004,41,-29,1,'A Mountain Trail','The trail winds about further to the southeast where you can make out\nwhat appears to be a small cliff, possible a rockslide in the distance.\nPassage to the west along the path seems clear.  Curiously, the metal\nflakes and fragments that have been found strewn all about the other\nsections of the trail seem to be absent here.\n',64,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10005,42,-30,1,'Base of a Small Cliff','Passage along this mountain trail has been blocked off it seems by a\nrockslide or two over the years.  A steep wall of jagged stones form\na sort of cliff which might prove to be scaleable given the climber\nexhibits sufficient skill.  As you survey the task at hand, a few\ndecent-sized stones come tumbling down from above - testament to how\ntreacherous climbing this loose \'cliff\' might prove to be.\n',64,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10006,42,-30,2,'Top of a Small Cliff','You are atop a large jumble of stones.  From this high vantage, you can\nsee a winding mountain trail below you towards the west.  A narrow fissure\nin the mountainside provides passage to the northeast.  Curiously enough,\na creeping white mist can be seen in the distance slowly making its way\nacross the mountainside to the north.\n',64,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10007,43,-29,2,'A Narrow Rift in the Stone','You stand between two gargantuan walls of stone.  Some primordial force\neons ago split the mountain in twain here, creating a passage that leads\nto the valley to the east.  The summit of a large mass of stones can be\nseen to the west.\n',64,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,4,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10008,44,-29,2,'Standing Atop a Rocky Crag','High above the valley to the east, you look out upon your surroundings\nfrom a vantage point on this rocky crag.  Below you is a gargantuan dome\nof gleaming metal surrounded by forests.  A deep furrow which appears\nsomewhat scorched leads up to the dome while a meandering stream can be\nspotted farther to the southeast.  A rock ledge to the south might\nprovide a better panorama of the surrounding terrain.  A narrow path\nalongside the cliff face leads off to the north.\n',64,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10009,44,-29,1,'Base of the Cliff','Here at the base of the mountain, your perspective of the surrounding\nterrain is much different.  The only things visible are the forest nearby\nto the northeast, the mountains looming to the west and the strange dome\nof gleaming metal to the south.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10010,44,-28,2,'A Treacherous Cliffside Path','Broken rocks lie all about making passage along this cliffside trail\na hazardous undertaking even without the cruel wind whipping alongside\nthe mountain face.  The footing seems quite loose and the path is\ndangerously narrow and the forest below seems distant.  Even farther off\nin the distance to the northeast, you can make out what appears to be\ndry, cracked and barren land.\n',64,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10011,45,-27,2,'A Treacherous Cliffside Path','The footing here seems quite loose and the path is dangerously narrow.\nPassage along this cliffside trail is a hazardous undertaking even\nwithout a cruel wind whipping at you - howling ferociously as it beats\nagainst the mountain\'s face.  Below you a thick green forest is visible\nand even farther off to the northeast you can make out what appears to\nbe dry, cracked and barren land.\n',64,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10012,44,-30,2,'A Protruding Rock Ledge','Looking all about, you cannot help but marvel at the breathtaking\nview at hand.  Off to the northeast is a remarkably dense sea of\ntrees, the blanket of greenery broken up here and there by strange\nscorched patches and an occasional glint of metal.  What draws your\ngaze away from the forest is a gargantuan dome of metal hundreds of\nfeet below you.  From this distance you can make out some markings\nalong the surface and think you can spot what appear to be windows\nFrom this vantage point, you can make out a deep furrow in the ground\nleading away from the dome and stretching out to the east while the\nforest continues on to the south.\n',64,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10013,45,-28,1,'A Clearing Before the Forest','Trees line the entire east side of this clearing and a faint trail seems\nto lead off in that direction.  Curiously, to the northeast is a barren\npatch of earth while a mountain looms ominously to the west.  What catches\nyour attention though is the massive metal dome nearby to the south that\nappears to come right out of the mountainside.\n',64,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10014,46,-27,1,'A Circle of Scorched Earth','This strange tract of land poses a mystery to you.  In every direction,\nlife teems in greens and golds...but this blasted circle of scorched\nearth appears devoid of any hint of life.  The dirt in some places here\neven seems to have been heated to the point of becoming glass.  A large\njumble of broken rocks lies nearby to the north and a winding trail\nthrough some trees extends to the south and northeast.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10015,46,-28,1,'A Faint Trail in the Woods','All about you is dense foliage and towering trees.  The chirping of various\nbirds and other forest noises can be heard coming from all around.  The\ntrail you are on seems rarely traveled and the woodlands appear to be\nslowly reclaiming it by growing back in place.  A clearing in the trees\ncan be seen nearby to the west while the forest trail winds off to the\nsoutheast.  The woods appear even denser to the east.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10016,46,-26,1,'A Jumble of Stones','All about you shattered and cracked stones of various shapes and size.\nLooking upwards you can make out what looks to be a ledge, if indeed it\ncould be called that seeing as not much remains.  Mixed in among the\nrubble at your feet are various rusted pieces of metal and quite a few\nunidentified bones and skull fragments.  Curiously, to the south is an\narea of scorched earth in a roughly circular shape.  Beyond it a forest\nteems with life, very much like the forest that lies to the east.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10017,46,-26,2,'A Crumbling Ledge','The cliffside trail here seems to have succumbed to the debilitating\nravishes of time.  A dangerously narrow section of the path yet remains,\na mere handwidth of rock along the mountainface.  As you take a peek\nbelow, you notice a large jumble of broken stones directly beneath this\ncrumbled section of the cliffside.\n',64,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10018,47,-26,1,'A Faint Trail in the Woods','Lofty trees and dense underbrush surround you on all sides and a thick,\nwoodsy aroma fills the air.  The trail you are on seems quite short and\nprobably is just a short segment of a longer route.  A sea of towering\ntrees loom in the distance to the northeast and southeast while a pile\nof stones is to the west.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10019,47,-25,2,'A Treacherous Cliffside Path','The footing here seems quite loose and the path is dangerously narrow.\nPassage along this cliffside trail is a hazardous undertaking even\nwithout the wind whipping at you and howling ferociously as it pools\nand eddies against the mountain\'s face.  Below you to your east you can\nsee a thick green forest and even farther off to the northeast a dry,\ncracked and barren land can be spotted.\n',64,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10020,46,-24,2,'A Blank Rock Wall','The narrow path winding around the side of the mountain clearly comes\nto an abrupt halt here.  It appears that whoever carved the trail out\nof the solid rock either lost interest in continuing it, or perhaps\nthis spot is indeed the end of the trail.  Scoping out the wall, you\nalmost write it off as being completely blank but then notice a small\nfaded inscription carved into its face.\n',64,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,21,'',NULL),
(10021,48,-25,1,'Standing Amidst a Sea of Trees','The forest here is densely packed with towering trees that reach high\ninto the sky.  Equally dense underbrush make picking your way around the\nwoodland giants a taxing endeavor and you strive to avoid the numerous\nnicks, bruises and cuts such a task will involve.  A gentle wind rustles\nthrough, bringing on it a thick woodsy aroma and the sound of birds\nchirping somewhere in the distance.  Peeking through the trees, you catch\nglimpses of a nightmarish land of broken earth far in the distance to\nthe northwest.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10022,49,-26,1,'A Clearing of Light and Dark','Something bizarre goes on in this woodland clearing and the foggiest notion\nas to what it is seems beyond your grasp.  The ground all around you seems\nunsettled and whole trees lie fallen, having been uprooted by some unknown\nforce.  A deathly calm lies over this area and the silence is almost more\nthan you can handle.  A sea of trees, not to mention apparent normalcy,\nlie nearby to the south and northwest.  Off in the distance, you can make\nout what appears to be a nightmarish land of broken, barren ground to\nthe northeast.\n',64,164992,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10023,49,-27,1,'Standing Amidst a Sea of Trees','The forest here is densely packed with lofty trees that reach high into\nthe sky.  Equally dense underbrush makes picking your way around the woodland\ngiants a taxing endeavor and you strive to avoid the numerous bruises,\nnicks and cuts such a task will involve.  A gentle wind rustles through the\ntrees, bringing on it the sound of birds chirping somewhere in the distance\nand a thick, woodsy aroma.  A faint forest trail leads off to the southwest\nand the woods continue on to the west.  Clearings can be seen nearby to\nthe north and east.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10024,48,-27,1,'Standing Amidst a Sea of Trees','The forest here is densely packed with towering trees that reach high\ninto the sky.  Equally dense underbrush makes picking your way around the\nwoodland giants a taxing endeavor and you strive to avoid the numerous\ncuts, nicks and bruises such a task will involve.  A gentle wind rustles\nthrough the trees, bringing on it the sound of birds chirping somewhere\nin the distance and a thick, woodsy aroma.  A faint forest trail leads\noff to the northwest and south while the woods continue on to the east.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10025,48,-28,1,'A Faint Trail in the Woods','The winding trail through the woods seems to come to an end here, seeing\nas the path simply leads up to a massive oak tree and does not pick up\nagain beyond it.  A variety of forest noises assails yer hearing and a\nwoodsy odor fills the air.  A sea of trees lies on all sides while a\nwinding forest trail leads off to the southwest.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10026,47,-28,1,'Standing Amidst a Sea of Trees','The forest here is densely packed with towering trees that reach high\ninto the sky.  Equally dense underbrush makes picking your way around the\nwoodland giants a taxing endeavor and you strive to avoid the numerous\nnicks, cuts and bruises such a task will involve.  A gentle wind rustles\nthrough here, bringing on it a thick woodsy aroma and the sound of birds\nchirping somewhere in the distance.  Peeking through the trees, you catch\nglimpses of a winding trail to the east, south and west.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10027,47,-29,1,'A Faint Trail in the Woods','All about you is dense foliage and towering trees.  The chirping of various\nbirds and other forest noises can be heard coming from all around.  The\ntrail you are on seems rarely traveled and the woodlands appear to be\nslowly reclaiming it by simply growing back in place.  The woods seem even\nmore dense nearby to the north while the forest trail winds off to the\nnortheast and northwest.  Through the trees to the southwest you can make\nout glimpses of a large metallic dome somewhere nearby.  A large pile of\nrubble to the southeast effectively blocks passage in that direction off.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10028,50,-27,1,'A Clearing in the Woods','Here at the edge of the forest, your perspective of the surrounding terrain\nis much different.  The only things visible are the forest nearby to the\nwest and some barren patches of earth to the south.  Far off to the southwest\nyou can make out what appears to be a gargantuan dome of metal.\n',64,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10029,50,-28,1,'A Barren Patch of Earth','Surveying all the lies around you, the only thing about your immediate\nsurroundings that seems noteworthy is the lack of greenery and life.\nThe forest nearby to the northwest and even the forest clearing directly\nnorth stand out in stark contrast to this patch of barren earth.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10030,51,-28,1,'Atop the Northern Rim of the Crater','You are on the northern lip of what appears to be a long and deep crater in\nthe countryside.  The earth below is scorched and in some places has been\ntransformed into glass by a raging inferno in the past.  Peering down into\nthe crater, you note that the furrow extends from somewhere nearby to the\nnortheast and ends at the base of a titanic dome of metal firmly planted\ninto face of the mountain southwest of your current position.  The crater\nrim continues on to the southwest while some greenery can be spotted to\nthe northwest.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10031,50,-29,1,'Atop the Northern Rim of the Crater','You are on the northern lip of what appears to be a long and deep crater\nin the countryside.  The earth below is scorched and in some places has been\ntransformed into glass by some raging inferno in the past.  Peering down into\nthe crater, you note that the furrow extends from somewhere in the\nnortheast and ends at the base of a hulking dome of metal firmly embedded\nin the mountain slightly southwest of your current position.  The crater\nrim continues to the northeast and you make out a steep path amongst the\nrocks leading down towards the crater floor.  A jumbled mass of stones lie\nnearby to the southwest.\n',64,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10032,49,-30,1,'Standing Atop of Pile of Stones','This section of the crater rim seems to have succumbed to the effects of\nthe wind and rain, having crumbled and fallen down to the crater floor\nbelow.  Surveying the footing afforded by this heap of rubble, you note that\npassage down is treacherous but possible.  The north rim of the crater\nremains intact and lies to the northeast.\n',64,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10033,49,-30,0,'A Jagged Jumble of Stones','Shattered and cracked stones lie all about you in various shapes and\nsizes.  Mixed in among the rubble at your feet are various rusted pieces of\nmetal and the occasional wood fragment.  Stepping back to survey the pile\nin its entirety, you can visualize a path to the top.  Looming ominously\nnearby to the southwest is a gargantuan dome of gleaming metal.\n',64,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10034,50,-29,0,'A Scorched Furrow of Dirt','Here on the crater floor, the hulking dome of metal absolutely dominates\nyour view to the southwest.  Seemingly embedded in the mountainside, it\nbeckons...a gleaming bubble beneath the looming visage of the mountain.\nA pile of rubble to the southwest marks where the ravishes of time have\nbegun to erode the crater\'s rims, but a path to the top can be picked out\nof the crater wall to the north.\n',64,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10035,51,-28,0,'A Scorched Furrow of Dirt','Here at the crater floor, the gigantic dome of gleaming metal nearby to\nthe southwest dominates the panorama.  Of course, that is not hard to\naccomplish seeing as it basically is all that can be seen besides the\nsteep crater walls.  Looking southwards, you note that ascent to the\nrim is possible.\n',64,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10036,51,-28,1,'Atop the South Rim of the Crater','You are on the lip of what appears to be a long and deep crater in the\ncountryside.  The earth below is scorched and in some places has been\ntransformed into glass by superheating.  Peering down into the crater, you\nnote that the furrow extends from somewhere to the northeast and ends at\nthe base of a hulking dome of metal firmly embedded in the mountain to the\nwest.  The crater rim continues to the northeast and southwest while you\nspot a steep path among the rocks leading down towards the crater floor.\nLofty tree tops are visible to the south and a forest clearing can be seen\nnearby to the east.\n',64,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10037,50,-29,1,'Atop the South Rim of the Crater','You are on the lip of what appears to be a long and deep crater.  The earth\nbelow is scorched and in some places has been superheated to the point of\nbecoming molten glass.  Peering down into the crater bottom, you note that\nit stretches from a hulking dome of metal to the west all the way into the\ndistance to the northeast.  You can pick you way across the top of the crater\nrim to the northeast and a spot of green plantlife can be spotted to the\nsouth.  Lofty tree tops are visible to the east.\n',64,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10038,51,-29,1,'Standing Amidst a Sea of Trees','This copse of woods is densely packed with towering trees that reach high\ninto the sky.  Equally dense underbrush makes picking you way around the\nwoodland giants a taxing endeavor and you strive to avoid the numerous\nnicks, cuts and bruises such a task will involve.  A gentle wind rustles\nthrough here, bringing on it a thick woodsy aroma and the sound of farm\nanimals somewhere to the southeast.  A small garden lies to the southwest\nwhile some sort of crater rim lies to the north and west.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10039,50,-30,1,'A Small Garden','You are at the edge of what appears to be a small garden of sorts.  Row\nupon row of greenery grows in an orderly fashion all about you, some of\nwhich is unrecognizable to you.  The garden continues on to the southwest\nand a campsite can be seen to the southeast.  A line of trees lies to the\nnortheast and the earth seems to drop away somewhere off to the north.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10040,51,-31,1,'A Cluttered Campsite','Calling this patch of Terra Firma a \'cluttered campsite\' is erring on the\ngenerous side.  Surveying your surroundings, you quickly come to the\nconclusion that \'prime ganked domicile\' might be a more fitting description.\nVarious assorted bits of garbage, metal and scrap lie strewn all about in a\nhaphazard fashion.  A large tent stands erected to the east while a field\nof debris lie north of the tent.  A small garden is off to the northwest\nand the campsite continues on to the south.\n',64,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10041,52,-31,1,'A Large Tent','This large tent seems to be the central planning area of the surrounding\ncamp.  Maps and other assorted material either lie strewn all about in a\nhaphazard fashion or are tacked to the tent walls.  Large flaps in the\nnorth and west walls allow for passage out of this tent.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10042,52,-30,1,'A Field of Debris','You stand amidst a field of twisted metal and scorched earth.  The air about\nyou is smoky, causing your eyes to tear.  Looking about you spot the\nsources of the irritant in the many smoking heaps of charred debris lying\nhere and there.  A large tent stands erected to the south and what appears\nto be some sort of grazing area lies to the north.\n',64,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10043,52,-29,1,'A Grazing Field','You stand in the middle of a large grazing field.  Various animals can be\nheard nearby voicing their displeasure at your presence.  This is somewhat\nof an open field, with only a low wire fence to the east and west.  A forest\nclearing lies to the north and a field of wreckage and debris is to the\nsouth.  Tall trees loom nearby to the northwest.\n',64,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10044,52,-28,1,'A Forest Clearing','Here at the edge of the woods, your perspective of the surrounding terrain\nis much different.  The only things visible nearby is a sea of trees to the\nsouthwest, some sort of grazing field to the south, and the rim of what\nappears to be a crater to the north and west.\n',64,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10045,52,-27,1,'Atop the South Rim of the Crater','You are on the lip of a somewhat long and deep crater.  The earth below\nyou is scorched and in some places has been superheated to the point of\nbecoming molten glass.  Peering down into the crater bottom, you note that\nit stretches from nearby to the northeast all the way to a hulking dome\nof metal to the south.  You can pick your way across the top of the\ncrater rim to the southwest and a spot of green plantlife can be spotted\nto the south.\n',64,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10046,48,-31,0,'At the Foot of the Dome','The sheer size of the metallic dome that dominates the surroundings and\ncasts a pall over the landscape is astounding to say the least.  Towering\nhigh above you, it almost appears as if the dome was attempting to reach\ninto the heavens...but is firmly embedded in the side of the mountain\nthat looms even higher nearby to the west.  Upon closer inspection you note\nthat the giant half-sphere is not as pristine and smooth as it appeared\nto be from a distance.  Whole sheets of metal along its surface are missing\nand scorch marks pock the surface.  It appears possible that this gigantic\nconstruct was cast out of sky, falling from the clouds until it finally\ncame to a violent rest in the side of this mountain.  A gigantic crimson\nand green gate directly before you seems to be the only visible means\ninside this enormous orb.\n',64,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10047,47,-31,0,'A Large Empty Chamber','Whatever this chamber was originally intended for, its use has become that\nof a dust museum.  A moderately thick layer of dust covers every single\nflat surface in the room.  Footsteps can be seen in the blanket of dust on\nthe floor.  More importantly, some of the footprints seem significantly\nlarger than those of a normal human.  Hallways to both the north and south\ncurve off somewhere, no doubt running along the inside of the dome\'s curved\nboundaries.  Bright light and a low murmur of voices can be heard coming\nfrom an open doorway to the west.  A large crimson and green gate leads out\nof this metal dome through the east wall.\n',64,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,108,0,'',NULL),
(10048,46,-30,0,'A Long Curving Hallway','This long, curving hallway seems to run the length of the dome\'s rim.  The\nwalls, floor and ceiling seem to be constructed out of the same metallic\nalloys that do not match anything you have ever encountered before.  What\ndoes seem almost as strange is the presence of circular windows set in the\neastern wall when they were not visible from the outside.  The hallway curves\naround further to the northwest.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,108,0,'',NULL),
(10049,45,-29,0,'A Long Curving Hallway','This long, curving hallway seems to run for most of the length of the dome\'s\nrim.  The walls, floor and ceiling seem to be constructed out of the same\nbizarre alloys found throughout the rest of the dome.  A large, sliding door\npanel in the northwest wall seems to be the only possible exit from here\nbesides the hallway which curves off to the southeast.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,108,0,'',NULL),
(10050,44,-28,0,'A Huge Storage Room','The ceiling of this gigantic chamber is so high that you can barely make\nout just where it is above you.  This colossal room appears to have served\nthe purpose of being a storage area of sorts, possibly for weapons of war\nand suits of battle armor.  Now it lies empty except for a few odd pieces\nof mismatched equipment scattered about in a haphazard fashion.  A sliding\ndoor panel in the southeast wall leads out of this huge storage room while\nan oversized opening in the west wall leads to another chamber.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,1000,0,'',NULL),
(10051,43,-28,0,'A Huge Storage Room','The ceiling of this gigantic chamber is so high that you can barely make\nout just where it is above you.  This colossal room appears to have served\nthe purpose of being a storage area of sorts, possibly for weapons of war\nand suits of battle armor.  Now it lies empty except for a few odd pieces\nof mismatched equipment scattered about in a haphazard fashion.  An\noversized opening in the east wall leads into another chamber.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,1000,0,'',NULL),
(10052,46,-32,0,'A Long Curving Hallway','This long, curving hallway seems to run for most of the length of the dome\'s\nouter rim.  The walls, floor and ceiling seem to be constructed out of the\nsame metallic alloys found throughout the rest of the dome.  What seems\nstrange is the presence of a row of circular windows set in the eastern\nwall, when they were not visible from the outside.  The hallway curves\naround further to the southwest.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,108,0,'',NULL),
(10053,45,-33,0,'A Long Curving Hallway','This long, curving hallway seems to run for most of the length of the\nmetallic dome\'s outer rim.  Everything around you seems to be constructed\nout of the same bizarre alloys that you have never come across in the\npast.  A large sliding door panel in the southwest wall seems to be the\nonly possible exit from here besides the hallway which curves off to the\nnortheast.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,108,0,'',NULL),
(10054,44,-34,0,'A Collapsed Storage Room','This chamber obviously was quite spacious and roomy at one time but\napparently is not so now.  It is quite obvious that the original design\nspecifications did not call for a section of a mountainside to serve as\nthe southwest wall of this storage room.  A sliding door panel in the\nnortheastern wall leads out of this storage chamber.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,1000,0,'',NULL),
(10055,46,-31,0,'A Security Checkpoint','Unlike the empty chamber to the east, this room looks like it sees daily\nusage.  Not a single speck of dust is anywhere in sight and various boxes\nand stacks of battle equipment line the walls.  A large sliding panel\nemblazoned with some writing on it affords passage to the west.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,108,0,'',NULL),
(10056,45,-31,0,'Staging Area','Smooth metallic walls of some bizarre allow pen in the vast chamber that\nyou are now in.  Half-empty boxes and other paper goods are strewn across\nthe floor and give this room a cluttered appearance.  A spiral staircase\nleads upwards through a hole in the ceiling while open doorways afford\npassage to the north, south, southwest and northwest.  A sliding door panel\nin the east wall opens out towards the security checkpoint.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,108,0,'',NULL),
(10057,45,-30,0,'Elite Cadre Barracks','Row upon row of bunk beds line the walls of this room.  What makes you\ntake another glance around the room is the fact that the beds are\nsignificantly larger than bunks normal-sized humans would sleep in.  Lacking\nin the layout of this barracks room are the foot lockers so common to the\ntypical barracks.  Oddly enough, there seem to be large fist-shaped dents\nin the walls and traces of blood speckled all over the floor.  An open\ndoorway to the south leads back out to the main staging area.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,10,108,0,'',NULL),
(10058,45,-32,0,'An Equipment Room','You are in a room that appears to be reserved primarily for the storage\nof general supplies and other miscellaneous pieces of equipment.  Huge\nmetal casks line the walls but remain empty, probably having been the first\nperishable supplies consumed.  Numerous empty boxes lie scattered about on\nthe floor mixed in with random articles of garbage here and there.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,6,108,0,'',NULL),
(10059,44,-30,0,'Warriors\' Barracks','Row upon row of bunk beds line the walls of this room.  At the foot of\neach bunk lies a foot locker and some personal belongings of the various\nwarriors.  Other than the bunks and lockers, this chamber is relatively\nbereft of furnishings.  An open doorway to the southeast leads back to the\nmain staging area.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,10,108,0,'',NULL),
(10060,44,-32,0,'A Compressed Chamber','The tight confines of this room do not seem to be the architect of this\ncomplex\'s intent or doing.  What makes this clear immediately is the fact\nthat the whole southwestern wall of this chamber appears to be part of\na mountainside, complete with some shrubbery.  The floor and walls of this\nroom come to an abrupt halt and the metal edges that meet to join with\nthe mountain appear rough-edged and uneven.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,108,0,'',NULL),
(10061,49,-31,1,'A Small Garden','You are in the middle of what appears to be a small garden of sorts.  Row\nupon row of greenery grows in an orderly fashion all about you, some of\nwhich is unrecognizable to you.  You can see a cluttered campsite to the\nsouth and southeast.  This garden appears to continue on to the northeast.\n',64,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10062,49,-32,1,'A Cluttered Campsite','Calling this patch of terra firma a \'cluttered campsite\' is erring on the\ngenerous side.  Surveying your surroundings, you quickly come to the\nconclusion that \'major FUBAR locale\' might be a more fitting description.\nVarious assorted bits of trash, metal and scrap lie strewn all about in a\nhaphazard fashion.  The campsite continues eastward and a small garden\nlies to the north.  The sound of running water can be heard coming from\nthe southwest.\n',64,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10063,50,-32,1,'A Cluttered Campsite','Calling this patch of terra firma a \'cluttered campsite\' is erring on the\ngenerous side.  Surveying your surroundings, you quickly come to the\nconclusion that \'disaster area\' might be a more fitting description.\nVarious assorted bits of metal, scrap and trash lie strewn all about in a\nhaphazard fashion.  The campsite continues to the east and west, and a\nsmall garden lies to the northwest.\n',64,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10064,51,-32,1,'A Cluttered Campsite','Calling this patch of terra firma a \'cluttered campsite\' is erring on the\ngenerous side.  Surveying your surroundings, you quickly come to the\nconclusion that \'disaster area\' might be a more fitting description.\nVarious assorted bits of metal and scrap lie strewn all about in a\nhaphazard fashion.  A large tent stands erected to the southeast while\nthe sound of running water can be heard coming from the south.\n',64,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10065,52,-33,1,'A Large Tent','The interior of this tent belies its appearance from the outside.  For\nsome reason the word \'pavilion\' comes to mind as you look all about at\nthis spacious covered expanse.  Two rows of foldout cots line either side\nof the long tent and a few foot lockers are scattered here and there.\nA large flap at one end allows for exit to the northwest.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10066,51,-33,1,'A Bend in the Stream','Shallow blue water surrounds you on all sides as you wade about in the\nstream.  The liquid is so crystalline that you can make out the streambed\nand all the various forms of underwater life that thrive there.  A small\ncopse of trees lies to the south while the stream continues on to the\nsoutheast and southwest.  What appears to be a campsite is nearby to the\nnorth.\n',64,131072,29,0,0,0,15,8,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10067,51,-34,1,'A Small Copse of Trees','Stark contrast to the stream that surrounds it on all sides, this cluster\nof trees stands out against the horizon and provides cool shade for\nwandering crocodiles and other semi-aquatic beasts who wish to get out\nof the sun.  Gnarled and twisted roots extend everywhere around you,\ndisappearing into the wetland that makes up this little patch of land\namidst the water.  A cluttered campsite can be spotted nearby to the north.\n',64,131072,27,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10068,52,-34,1,'End of a Mountain Stream','Deep blue water surrounds you on all sides as you wade about in the\nstream.  The liquid is remarkably clear, yet you still can\'t make out the\nstreambed.  Gigantic stones lie all about and it appears the stream\ndisappears somewhere underneath them.  You can feel a slight tugging of\na current pulling you downwards but nothing too extreme.  A copse of trees\nlies nearby to the west while what appears to be a campsite is nearby to\nthe northwest and north.\n',64,131072,29,0,0,0,15,7,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10069,50,-34,1,'A Mountain Stream','Shallow blue water surrounds you on all sides as you wade about in the\nstream.  The liquid is so crystalline that you can make out the streambed\nand all the various forms of underwater life that thrive there.  A bend\nin the stream lies to the northeast and what appears to be a campsite\nlies a little farther to the north.\n',64,131072,29,0,0,0,15,6,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10070,49,-34,1,'A Mountain Stream','Shallow blue water surrounds you on all sides as you wade about in the\nstream.  The liquid is so crystalline that you can make out the streambed\nand all the various forms of underwater life that thrive there.  A large\nrock lies in the middle of the stream west of you while a gigantic dome\nof gleaming metal can be seen in the distance to the northwest.\n',64,131072,29,0,0,0,15,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10071,48,-33,1,'A Mountain Stream','Shallow blue water surrounds you on all sides as you wade about in the\nstream.  The liquid is so crystalline that you can make out the streambed\nand all the various forms of underwater life that thrive there.  A large\nrock lies in the middle of the stream south of you while a cluttered\ncampsite can be seen to the northeast.\n',64,131072,29,0,0,0,15,8,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10072,48,-34,1,'A Large Rock in the River','Standing atop this rock affords you a nice vantage point over the\nsurrounding terrain.  A mountain stream runs to northwest and east of\nthis rock and a campsite can be seen nearby to the northeast.  A bit\nfurther to the northwest is a monstrous dome of gleaming metal and\nbeyond that is a range of mountains that extends a bit to the west as\nwell.  Almost directly north and in the distance, you can make out what\nappears to be a forest.\n',64,131072,27,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10073,47,-32,1,'A Mountain Stream','Shallow blue water surrounds you on all sides as you wade about in the\nstream.  The liquid is so crystalline that you can make out the stream\nbottom and all the various underwater life growing there.  Nearby to the\nnorth is a gigantic dome of gleaming metal and a mountain range looms\nominously to the west.\n',64,131072,29,0,0,0,15,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10074,47,-33,1,'A Mountain Stream','Shallow blue water surrounds you on all sides as you wade about in the\nstream.  The liquid is so crystalline that you can make out the streambed\nand all the various forms of underwater life thriving there.  Nearby to the\nnorth lies a gigantic dome of gleaming metal while a mountain range looms\nominously to the west.\n',64,131072,29,0,0,0,15,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10075,46,-32,1,'A Mountain Stream','Deep blue water surrounds you on all sides as you wade about in the stream.\nSo crystalline is the liquid that you can make out the stream bottom far\nbelow.  As a soft undercurrent gently shifts the sand at the stream bottom,\nyou make out what appear to be bones on the streambed...\n',64,131072,29,0,0,0,15,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10076,46,-32,0,'Under the Surface','Inky water surrounds you, chilling you to the bone with its coldness.\nFaint flickerings of light can be seen coming from above, or rather,\nthe direction in this dark environ that appears to be \'up.\' A small\nopening in the rock to the southwest appears to provide passage in\nthat direction.\n',64,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10077,45,-33,0,'An Underwater Tunnel','Inky water surrounds you, chilling you to the bone with its coldness.\nThe current here seems to be almost at a standstill and narrow confines\nof this underwater tunnel do not afford much room for movement.  A small\nfissure in the rock allows for movement to the northeast while this\ntunnel continues on to the west.\n',64,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,3,96,0,'',NULL),
(10078,44,-33,0,'An Underwater Tunnel','Inky black water surrounds you, chilling you to the bone with its\ncoldness.  The current here seems to be almost at a standstill and the\nnarrow confines of this underwater tunnel do not afford much room for\nmovement.  A few faint shimmerings of light can be spotted from above\nwhile this tunnel continues on to the east.\n',64,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,3,84,0,'',NULL),
(10079,44,-33,1,'An Underground Beach','You stand upon the shore of what appears to be a subterranean beach of\nsorts.  The sand beneath you is black, and you suspect that it is merely\ngranite that has slowly been broken down into granules over the eons.\nLooking about this cavern you note two darkened tunnels leading away\nin the north and west walls while the chill water washes up the \'shore\'\nand swirls all about you.\n',64,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,84,0,'',NULL),
(10080,44,-32,1,'A Narrow Fissure','Looking about, you note that you are between two walls of granite set\nrather closely together.  Some primordial force ages ago split the cave\nwall in twain, creating passage to darkened caverns to the northwest\nand south.\n',64,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,84,0,'',NULL),
(10081,43,-31,1,'A Cramped Cave','This cramped cave appears to have been naturally formed.  Throughout the\nages the granite walls have been slowly smoothed and are covered with\na strange sticky substance.  Littered all about the floor are strange\nunrecognizable bits of metal and other garbage.  Passage out of this\ncave appears to be possible to the southeast.\n',64,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,84,0,'',NULL),
(10082,43,-33,1,'A Dank Tunnel','Darkness surrounds you on all sides, as the granite walls of this\ntunnel provide passage deeper into this network of caverns.  Rifts in\nthe rock allow for passage to the east and southeast.\n',64,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,84,0,'',NULL),
(10083,44,-34,1,'A Small Alcove','You are now in what appears to be more an oversized recess than what\ncould be dubbed a cave.  The walls and ceiling of granite are not\nseparated by much and the space between is quite cramped.  A strong\nodor seems to be emanating from a dark but shallow hole in the\nsoutheast corner of the alcove.\n',64,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,84,0,'',NULL),
(10084,45,-31,1,'The Throneroom','This room appears to have been converted into a makeshift throneroom of\nsorts.  A large crimson chair sits atop a dais in the middle of the floor\nwhile a spiral staircase leads down through a hole in the corner of the\nroom.  A large tapestry spans the entire length of the west wall while a\ncrimson banner hangs from the wall opposite it.\n',64,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,108,0,'',NULL),
(10085,48,-30,1,'The Boneyard','The woods seem darker and somehow more sinister here and for some reason\neerily silent.  The sounds usually heard in woodland environs is oddly\nabsent here, almost as if the local wildlife shuns this ground.  The trees\nthat surround you on all sides appear devoid of life and the ground is\nlittered with fallen branches and dead leaves.  A pile of rubble nearby to\nthe northwest strikes you as being out of place here.\n',64,164864,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10086,48,-31,1,'The Boneyard','The woods seem darker and more sinister here, and for some reason...eerily\nsilent.  The sounds normally heard in woodland environs is oddly absent here,\nalmost as if the local wildlife shuns this ground.  The trees that surround\nyou on all sides appear devoid of life and the ground is littered with\nfallen branches and dead leaves.  The earth looks like its been disturbed\nrecently and a small mound of soil is visible peeking out from under some\ndead branches.\n',64,164864,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10090,48,-31,0,'Six Feet Underground','This dark hole in the ground you currently find yourself in is both\ndank and putrescent.  The stench of rotting flesh fills your nostrils,\noverwhelming your sense of smell and it almost forces you to retch.\n',64,164872,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,84,0,'',NULL),
(10100,7,40,-2,'The Western Entrance to Northern Haon-Dor Forest','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional\nrut or tree-root trips you up.  An archway of light to the west yields bright\ncontrast to the gloom of the forest.  You realize that what causes it is the\nsunlight shining in from the rolling hills on the western edge of the forest.\n',56,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10101,8,40,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional\nrut or tree-root trips you up.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10102,9,39,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional\nrut or tree-root trips you up.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10103,10,39,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional\nrut or tree-root trips you up.  A small game path leads south of here.  You\nmight be able to follow it.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10104,11,39,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.  You stand at another bend on the dark forest path.\nWell aware of the quantity of life that must flourish in this forest, you still\ncan\'t shake the feeling that something more intelligent is watching you.  While\nyou hear nothing over the constant bird calls and woodland noises, and see\nnothing out of the ordinary in the brush, you are virtually certain that there\nis much more here than meets the eye.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10105,12,40,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.  Bends in the path in both visible directions prevent\nyou from seeing far in either direction.  Your sixth sense tells you that you\nare being watched, but whether it is by some curious squirrel or by something\nmore malignant you do not know.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10106,13,40,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor',' All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.\n',56,164016,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10107,14,40,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.  A rustling noise from overhead catches your\nattention and you quickly look upward, but whatever it was watching you that\nrevealed its position, it was quick enough to camouflage itself before you\ncould spot it.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10108,15,40,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10109,16,40,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10110,17,41,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10111,18,41,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.  The forest trail broadens out here, as if it has\nseen a bit more traffic then the rest.  It also appears to be one of the densest\nparts of the forest - you can see absolutely nothing above you but darkness due\nto the tree\'s thick vegetation.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(10112,19,41,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.  From above you, you hear a bit of commotion, but by\nthe time you look upwards, it has stopped.  You continue to watch for a short\ntime, and then you notice a small squirrel packing acorns into an overstuffed\nhole high up in a tree.  Occasionally an acorn will roll out and rustle the\nleaves as it falls, but the commotion you heard previously was much louder.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10113,20,40,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10114,21,40,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.  Something here seems oddly strange.  But what?  The\ntrees look perfectly ordinary, the trail shows nothing of interest.  You are at\na loss.  Then it hits you - there are no animals in sight.  The rest of the\nforest is filled with bird cries and rustling leaves as critters scamper about.\nAll about you is strangely devoid of any animal life.  It\'s enough to make it\nseem spooky.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10115,22,40,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.  The trail continues running from east to west.  To\nthe east, the vegetation begins to thin out quite a bit and the trail gradually\nbecomes more bright in that direction.  You surmise you are near one of the\nexits to Haon-Dor.  Some crickets chirp in the thicket just off the path and a\nsquirrel watches you quietly from one of the branches overhead.  Strangely, you\nfeel as if more then just the squirrel is watching.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10116,23,40,-2,'The Eastern Entrance to Northern Haon-Dor Forest','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.  An archway of light to the east yields bright\ncontrast to the gloom of the forest.  You realize that what causes it is the\nsunlight shining in from the rocky foothills on the eastern edge of the forest.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10117,16,39,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10118,16,38,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.  The trail narrows somewhat here as vegetation\nencroaches upon the well-trod path trying to reclaim it.  The oak forest all\nabout you is very dense here and it is difficult to see very far into the gloom\nthat surrounds you.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10119,15,37,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10120,15,36,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','  All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other\nforest noises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog\nthat surrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.  The main path continues north-south, while a\nsecondary path proceeds east from here.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10121,15,35,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.  You stand on a path, deep in the heart of the\nHaon-Dor forest.  As elsewhere, there is very little to see other than the tall\ntrees, various forms of greenery and occasional small animals - most of whom\nwould be rather difficult to chase down.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10122,14,34,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.  As you enter, a fierce scurrying can be heard from\none of the nearby bushes.  You cautiously poke into it to check it out and\ndiscover a small warren of rabbits - most of whom take one look at you and\nimmediately dive for a nearby hole and safety.  One, however, seems to have been\ncaught further from protection then he would have liked, glances at you, and\nruns off west down a small game path.  You doubt you could catch him though.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10123,14,33,-2,'The Forest Trail in Northern Haon-Dor','All about you is dense foliage.  The chirping of various birds and other forest\nnoises can be heard coming from all about you.  The thick white misty fog that\nsurrounds you and emanates from the forest itself adds to the mystique and\ngloom.  The trail you are on seems fairly well traveled - being the only path\nthrough the forest.  It is a mix of sand, mud, and gravel and an occasional rut\nor tree-root trips you up.  South of here the trail ends in dense brush\nbut there is a slight opening of the brush to the west.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10124,16,36,-2,'Secondary Trail','You are on a thin sand and gravel path that stretches through the mysterious\nnorthern Haon-Dor forest.  The trees overhead completely obscure the sky and\nonly a short distance off to either side of the trail, thick brambles prevent\nall passage.  The trail looks moderately well traveled, being the only means\nof passage through the forest.  This is a small secondary trail that branches\noff from the main trail to the west.  It is almost completely overgrown and in\na few years will probably no longer exist having been reclaimed by the forest\nthat is all around you.  You note that a few of the twigs that pass near the\npathway have been snapped off and some ferns underfoot show signs of crushing.\nSomething came through here, and it seems to have been rather recent.\n',56,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10125,17,36,-2,'A Small Clearing in the Forest','This secluded spot is only a short distance off from the main trail in Northern\nHaon-Dor.  You can see an overgrown, but passable, pathway in the northwest\ncorner of the clearing that leads back to the trail.  The clearing itself is\nroughly 200 feet on a side.  Small scrub grass lies underfoot and a few logs\nlie scattered about providing a place to sit.  There is also a ring of rocks\nencircling a blackened area on the ground, and you surmise that an occasional\ntraveler has made his campfire here.   This is the northwest corner of the\nclearing.  There is a small path out of the clearing and back to the trail to\nthe west, and the clearing extends to the south and east from here.\n',56,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10126,18,36,-2,'A Small Clearing in the Forest','This secluded spot is only a short distance off from the main trail in Northern\nHaon-Dor.  You can see an overgrown, but passable, pathway in the northwest\ncorner of the clearing that leads back to the trail.  The clearing itself is\nroughly 200 feet on a side.  Small scrub grass lies underfoot and a few logs\nlie scattered about providing a place to sit.  There is also a ring of rocks\nencircling a blackened area on the ground, and you surmise that an occasional\ntraveler has made his campfire here.\n',56,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10127,17,35,-2,'A Small Clearing in the Forest','This secluded spot is only a short distance off from the main trail in Northern\nHaon-Dor.  You can see an overgrown, but passable, pathway in the northwest\ncorner of the clearing that leads back to the trail.  The clearing itself is\nroughly 200 feet on a side.  Small scrub grass lies underfoot and a few logs\nlie scattered about providing a place to sit.  There is also a ring of rocks\nencircling a blackened area on the ground, and you surmise that an occasional\ntraveler has made his campfire here.\n',56,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10128,18,35,-2,'A Small Clearing in the Forest','This secluded spot is only a short distance off from the main trail in Northern\nHaon-Dor.  You can see an overgrown, but passable, pathway in the northwest\ncorner of the clearing that leads back to the trail.  The clearing itself is\nroughly 200 feet on a side.  Small scrub grass lies underfoot and a few logs\nlie scattered about providing a place to sit.  There is also a ring of rocks\nencircling a blackened area on the ground, and you surmise that an occasional\ntraveler has made his campfire here.\n',56,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10129,13,34,-2,'On the Gamepath','It took a bit of work to open this bramble-filled path up so that it was\npassable to you.  Overhanging branches and thorns off to the side scrape at\nyour exposed skin, and the going is far from easy.  The bushes are so thick,\nyou can hardly see in any direction at all.  Even behind you where you just\ncleared a path seems to close up immediately - the brush you pushed aside to\nallow you entrance falls back into place sealing your exit.  Logic dictates\nthat the gametrail continues from here, since gametrails generally connect two\nplaces where animals have need to journey between and there is absolutely\nnothing here.  However, the seemingly impassable vegetation laying all around\nyou does a good job of defying logic.\n',56,131076,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10130,12,34,-2,'Forest Glade around a Small Pond','You are in a large, natural clearing in the forest.  At the edge of the\nclearing, as elsewhere in the forest, dense vegetation blocks your entrance.\nThe glade itself is quite big.  Underfoot, low shrub grass and ferns rise up to\nyour ankles, while overhead, the few trees that grow in the glade create an\nimpenetrable canopy of leaves.  An occasional bush or small shrub provides\nshelter or protection and this seems to be a fairly secure place to rest and\nrecuperate if need be.  The main feature of the glade, however, is the pond\nwhose waters look quite inviting.  You barely can discern a gamepath leading\neast from here.\n',56,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10131,12,35,-2,'Forest Glade around a Small Pond','You are in a large, natural clearing in the forest.  At the edge of the\nclearing, as elsewhere in the forest, dense vegetation blocks your entrance.\nThe glade itself is quite big.  Underfoot, low shrub grass and ferns rise up to\nyour ankles, while overhead, the few trees that grow in the glade create an\nimpenetrable canopy of leaves.  An occasional bush or small shrub provides\nshelter or protection and this seems to be a fairly secure place to rest and\nrecuperate if need be.  The main feature of the glade, however, is the pond\nwhose waters look quite inviting.\n',56,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
