(10168,14,42,-1,'The Pathway of the Revered Elm','Elm trees are a place of peace and sanctuary for all elves who will always\ntry and have at least one such tree nearby them.  The platform that you are now\nupon encircles the elm tree and rests entirely on its massive limbs.  This\nplatform, like those comprising the other walkways, is connected to its\nneighbors by vine rope bridges, although these seem to have been made more\ndurable and steady by the inclusion of sinewy fibers taken from what the elf\nhunters bring back to feed the village with.  A certain solemn quiet surrounds\nthe walkway as it is a place of respect for the elves, but the ever-present\nforest noises of its animals still intrudes here.\n',56,164016,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10169,14,44,0,'The Elven Leader\'s Branch','A sturdy branch juts out high up on the revered elm tree.  A short distance\naway from the trunk of the tree, a platform, like those that comprise the main\nvillage below, supports a large house which must be the home of the current\nelven leader.  Vines run up and down the tree and a few have been woven into a\nsturdy ladder for easy passage of the venerable leader from his home to his\nbeloved tree and people below.  You are perched precariously on this branch\nsome 500 feet above the forest floor far below you.  You briefly consider the\ndanger you are in, but quickly shake it off as being nonproductive.  A much\nmore stable footing presents itself to you east of here where the elven leader\'s\nhouse is, or you can go back down to the village proper by means of a vine rope\nladder.\n',56,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10170,15,44,0,'The Elven Leader\'s Branch','A sturdy branch juts out high up on the revered elm tree.  A short distance\naway from the trunk of the tree, a platform, like those that comprise the main\nvillage below, supports a large house which must be the home of the current\nelven leader.  Vines run up and down the tree and a few have been woven into a\nsturdy ladder for easy passage of the venerable leader from his home to his\nbeloved tree and people below.  The leader\'s home stands on the south side of\nthis platform where a doorway leads inside.  You now stand on a balcony that\nlooks out over the forest to the north and east.  At the platform\'s western\nedge, a branch of the elm tree leads back toward the trunk of the tree where\nyou note a ladder leads downward.\n',56,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10171,14,43,0,'The Elven Leader\'s Home','This is one corner room of Gersard, the elven leader\'s house.  It is fairly\nspacious for the lifestyles of the elves, and yet it still seems rather small.\nIn fact, you can make out the entire layout from where you stand.  The\nnortheast room appears to be a combination foyer and reception area.  West of\nthat is a den for Gersard\'s study.  South of that in the southwest corner is\nGersard\'s Spartan bedroom, and just east of that is a kitchen.  The house is of\nwooden construction and is simply furnished and decorated with natural\nornamentation, largely plants and a few things you\'d call \"pretty rocks.\"\nGersard\'s study is as simple as the rest of his house.  Archways lead east into\nthe living room and foyer or south into Gersard\'s bedroom from here.\n',56,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10172,15,43,0,'The Elven Leader\'s Home','This is one corner room of Gersard, the elven leader\'s house.  It is fairly\nspacious for the lifestyles of the elves, and yet it still seems rather small.\nIn fact, you can make out the entire layout from where you stand.  The\nnortheast room appears to be a combination foyer and reception area.  West of\nthat is a den for Gersard\'s study.  South of that in the southwest corner is\nGersard\'s Spartan bedroom, and just east of that is a kitchen.  The house is of\nwooden construction and is simply furnished and decorated with natural\nornamentation, largely plants and a few things you\'d call \"pretty rocks.\"\nThis entryway is where Gersard greets and entertains official guests to the\nelven village.  The wooden walls are simply decorated.  A stout door leads\nnorth out of the house, while archways lead west into Gersard\'s study and south\ninto the kitchen area.\n',56,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10173,14,42,0,'The Elven Leader\'s Home','This is one corner room of Gersard, the elven leader\'s house.  It is fairly\nspacious for the lifestyles of the elves, and yet it still seems rather small.\nIn fact, you can make out the entire layout from where you stand.  The\nnortheast room appears to be a combination foyer and reception area.  West of\nthat is a den for Gersard\'s study.  South of that in the southwest corner is\nGersard\'s Spartan bedroom, and just east of that is a kitchen.  The house is of\nwooden construction and is simply furnished and decorated with natural\nornamentation, largely plants and a few things you\'d call \"pretty rocks.\"\nFor a room that Gersard spends a third of his time in, it lacks character.  The\nwooden walls have no ornamentation and nothing but the few pieces of furniture\nyou see about you can be found.\n',56,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10174,15,42,0,'The Elven Leader\'s Home','This is one corner room of Gersard, the elven leader\'s house.  It is fairly\nspacious for the lifestyles of the elves, and yet it still seems rather small.\nIn fact, you can make out the entire layout from where you stand.  The\nnortheast room appears to be a combination foyer and reception area.  West of\nthat is a den for Gersard\'s study.  South of that in the southwest corner is\nGersard\'s Spartan bedroom, and just east of that is a kitchen.  The house is of\nwooden construction and is simply furnished and decorated with natural\nornamentation, largely plants and a few things you\'d call \"pretty rocks.\"\nGersard\'s kitchen is equipped with a few basic necessities.  Archways lead\nnorth to the reception area, or west into the bedroom.\n',56,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10175,11,43,-1,'The Elven Druid Monastery','The monastic temple that the elven druids have erected is in honor to the\nrevered elm tree that they worship.  Like all druid monasteries, it is open\nair, but has a few shrines to protect anything that needs it from the elements.\nThe whole monastery is supported by the branches of the elm and there is an\naltar off on the western side of the monastery.\n',56,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10176,11,42,-1,'The Elven Druid Monastery','The monastic temple that the elven druids have erected is in honor to the\nrevered elm tree that they worship.  Like all druid monasteries, it is open\nair, but has a few shrines to protect anything that needs it from the elements.\nThe whole monastery is supported by the branches of the elm and there is an\naltar off on the western side of the monastery.\n',56,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
