(10199,0,0,0,'Overlooking the Forest','  The window provides an excellent view of the forest from here.  Your vantage\npoint allows you to make out the tops of some of the smaller forest trees below\nyou, while an unobstructed view of the branches of the larger ones is also\npossible.  A few birds nests are visible to the careful observer and on\noccasion, a hawk or sparrow will fly by.  The largest trees of the forest tower\nhigh above you even here, high up in one of the trees and the foliage from\nthem, while less dense then at the forest floor, is still enough to prevent you\nfrom seeing out of the forest into the lands beyond.\n',56,139586,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10200,11,59,-1,'A Wooded, Rocky Trail','You are on a dirt trail that winds through the rocky foothills northeast of the\nHaon-Dor forest.  Small rocks jut through the ground and evergreen and oak trees\ncan be seen in large enough numbers that you would become quickly lost were you\nto leave the path.  In the distance to the west, the boundary of the Haon-Dor\nforest can be made out, while to the east, lies a barren plain.\n',56,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10201,12,59,-1,'A Wooded, Rocky Trail','You are on a dirt trail that winds through the rocky foothills northeast of the\nHaon-Dor forest.  Small rocks jut through the ground and evergreen and oak trees\ncan be seen in large enough numbers that you would become quickly lost were you\nto leave the path.  In the distance to the west, the boundary of the Haon-Dor\nforest can be made out, while to the east, lies a barren plain.\n',56,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10202,13,60,-1,'A Wooded, Rocky Trail','You are on a dirt trail that winds through the rocky foothills northeast of the\nHaon-Dor forest.  Small rocks jut through the ground and evergreen and oak trees\ncan be seen in large enough numbers that you would become quickly lost were you\nto leave the path.  In the distance to the west, the boundary of the Haon-Dor\nforest can be made out, while to the east, lies a barren plain.\n',56,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10203,14,60,-1,'A Thin Trail across the Tundra','A wide, featureless plain spreads out before you.  Short, stubby crabgrass\nprotrudes through the surface in clumps scattered about.  A mountain range\nlines the horizon to the north and east, while little can be seen to the west.\nA bitterly cold wind seems to sweep down from over the mountains.  The trail you\nare on is only discernible by faint wagon tracks on the ground and the absence\nof crabgrass.  You could easily lose it if you are not careful, but it appears\nthe trail goes southeast and west.\n',-1,393216,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10204,15,59,-1,'A Thin Trail across the Tundra','A wide, featureless plain spreads out before you.  Short, stubby crabgrass\nprotrudes through the surface in clumps scattered about.  A mountain range\nlines the horizon to the north and east, while little can be seen to the west.\nA bitterly cold wind seems to sweep down from over the mountains.  The trail you\nare on is only discernible by faint wagon tracks on the ground and the absence\nof crabgrass.  You could easily lose it if you are not careful, but it appears\nthe trail goes east and northwest.\n',56,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10205,16,59,-1,'A Thin Trail across the Tundra','A wide, featureless plain spreads out before you.  Short, stubby crabgrass\nprotrudes through the surface in clumps scattered about.  A mountain range\nlines the horizon to the north and east, while little can be seen to the west.\nA bitterly cold wind seems to sweep down from over the mountains.  The trail you\nare on is only discernible by faint wagon tracks on the ground and the absence\nof crabgrass.  You could easily lose it if you are not careful, but it appears\nthe trail goes northeast and west.\n',56,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
