(10236,12,42,-2,'Frontier Wall','This scaffolding is partially protected by the thick timbers forming the\npalisade, although your upper body and head are still exposed when you stand\nupright.  The timbers themselves are encrusted with a hardened, black resin\nthat must be used to ward off fires.  You have a clear view over the palisade,\nand a bowman would have no difficulty firing down on any attacking force\nfoolish enough to rush the wall.\n',56,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10237,7,46,-3,'Access Trail','This utilitarian trail runs parallel to the wall and allows for rapidly\nreinforcing one area of the wall should it need to be defended.  The frontier\nwall sits on a low earthen embankment.  Thick timbers form the palisade, and a\nscaffold has been erected near the top of the wall where the defenders are able\nto see and fire over the top with a moderate amount of protection.  A small\nladder climbs up to the scaffolding from here.\n',56,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10238,8,45,-3,'Access Trail','This utilitarian trail runs parallel to the wall and allows for rapidly\nreinforcing one area of the wall should it need to be defended.  The frontier\nwall sits on a low earthen embankment.  Thick timbers form the palisade, and a\nscaffold has been erected near the top of the wall where the defenders are able\nto see and fire over the top with a moderate amount of protection.  A small\nladder climbs up to the scaffolding from here.\n',56,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
