(10240,11,42,-3,'Access Trail','This utilitarian trail runs parallel to the wall and allows for rapidly\nreinforcing one area of the wall should it need to be defended.  The frontier\nwall sits on a low earthen embankment.  Thick timbers form the palisade, and a\nscaffold has been erected near the top of the wall where the defenders are able\nto see and fire over the top with a moderate amount of protection.  A small\nladder climbs up to the scaffolding from here.\n',56,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10241,20,69,-1,'Common Room','A musty wood smoke smell lingers in the air, undoubtedly from the fire kept\nburning at all times for warmth and light.  The barracks\' walls are wooden\nlogs coated in some black resin you don\'t recognize but undoubtedly present\nto prevent fires.  The barracks displays the pride and attentiveness to detail\nrequired in the crack troops defending the frontier tinged with the neglect\nfound in a bored soldier on guard duty.  A door in the south wall leads\noutside.  Thin wooden walls partition the common room from the sleeping\narea of the barracks although open archways allow easy access.  A small,\nbarred and shuttered window looks out through the wall of the barracks.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(10242,19,70,-1,'Barracks','A musty wood smoke smell lingers in the air, undoubtedly from the fire kept\nburning at all times for warmth and light.  The barracks\' walls are wooden\nlogs coated in some black resin you don\'t recognize but undoubtedly present\nto prevent fires.  The barracks displays the pride and attentiveness to detail\nrequired in the crack troops defending the frontier tinged with the neglect\nfound in a bored soldier on guard duty.  A sturdy wooden door in the west\nwall bears the inscription \"Armory\".\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(10243,20,70,-1,'Barracks','A musty wood smoke smell lingers in the air, undoubtedly from the fire kept\nburning at all times for warmth and light.  The barracks\' walls are wooden\nlogs coated in some black resin you don\'t recognize but undoubtedly present\nto prevent fires.  The barracks displays the pride and attentiveness to detail\nrequired in the crack troops defending the frontier tinged with the neglect\nfound in a bored soldier on guard duty.  A small, barred and shuttered window\nlooks out through the wall of the barracks.\n',0,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(10244,19,69,-1,'Barracks','A musty wood smoke smell lingers in the air, undoubtedly from the fire kept\nburning at all times for warmth and light.  The barracks\' walls are wooden\nlogs coated in some black resin you don\'t recognize but undoubtedly present\nto prevent fires.  The barracks displays the pride and attentiveness to detail\nrequired in the crack troops defending the frontier tinged with the neglect\nfound in a bored soldier on guard duty.  A wooden door on the west wall\nhas a plaque with the words \"Captain\'s Quarters\" on it.  A small, barred and\nshuttered window looks out through the wall of the barracks.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(10245,18,70,-1,'Armory','Assorted replacement weapons and armor are stored here for disbursement to the\ntroops in times of defense.  The wood smoke smell of the barracks is less\npronounced here as this room is little used.  There are sturdy wooden doors in\nthe east and west wall.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(10246,18,69,-1,'Captain\'s Quarters','A musty wood smoke smell lingers in the air, undoubtedly from the fire kept\nburning at all times for warmth and light.  The barracks\' walls are wooden\nlogs coated in some black resin you don\'t recognize but undoubtedly present\nto prevent fires.  The barracks displays the pride and attentiveness to detail\nrequired in the crack troops defending the frontier tinged with the neglect\nfound in a bored soldier on guard duty.  There are doors in both the east and\nwest walls.  A small, barred and shuttered window looks out through the walls\nof the barracks.\n',56,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(10247,19,58,-1,'Tundra','A wide, featureless plain spreads out before you.  Short, stubby crabgrass\nprotrudes through the surface in clumps scattered about.  A mountain range lines\nthe horizon to the north and east, while little can be seen to the west.  A\nbitterly cold wind seems to sweep down from over the mountains.\n',56,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10248,15,70,-1,'Small Cemetery Plot','The flattened training ground shows fewer signs of marching feet here.  In fact,\nthere are even spots where the clumps of snow that dot the region lies pristine\nand untouched.  A certain amount of revered awe overcomes you in this place for\nthe sacrifices made by the defenders of this barren outpost.\n',56,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10249,16,70,-1,'Training Ground','A flat part in the mountain pass serves as a convenient parade ground for\nkeeping the skills of the border guards maintained.  The barracks are east of\nhere, while on the south side of the training ground, two trails wind through\nthe boulders.\n',56,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10250,17,70,-1,'Training Ground','A flat part in the mountain pass serves as a convenient parade ground for\nkeeping the skills of the border guards maintained.  The barracks are east of\nhere, while on the south side of the training ground, two trails wind through\nthe boulders.  There is a door leading east into the barracks.\n',56,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10251,15,69,-1,'Training Ground','A flat part in the mountain pass serves as a convenient parade ground for\nkeeping the skills of the border guards maintained.  The barracks are east of\nhere, while on the south side of the training ground, two trails wind through\nthe boulders.\n',56,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
