(10257,16,67,-1,'Signal Point Overlook','A winding trail through the boulders leads you south to this outcropping of rock\non the very edge of the mountain range.  You realize your journey has also led\nyou up about 100 feet, as you can see the frontier trail lying some distance\nbelow you.  From this vantage point, the guard towers of Amber can barely be\nmade out to the southeast and a clear view out over the tundra to the southwest\nall the way to the great forest of Haon-Dor presents itself.\n',56,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10258,17,63,-1,'Tundra','A wide, featureless plain spreads out before you.  Short, stubby crabgrass\nprotrudes through the surface in clumps scattered about.  A mountain range lines\nthe horizon to the north and east, while little can be seen to the west.  A\nbitterly cold wind seems to sweep down from over the mountains.\n',56,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10259,19,63,-1,'The Base of the Mountains','You stand on a tundra plain where it abuts the eastern mountains.  The\nsnowcapped mountains stretch high overhead, and the way through them is\nimpassable at this point.  In the other direction, the featureless tundra\nstretches out.  An occasional clump of crabgrass protrudes through the surface\nand clumps of snow dot the landscape.\n',56,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
