(10300,12,54,-5,'Boarded Up Passage','The tunnel is blocked here by a barricade constructed of boards.  The\nbarricade appears to have been hastily constructed as though the builders\nfeared for their lives while putting it in place.  A sign has been painted\nin crimson directly in the center of the obstacle.\n',62,139272,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10301,12,55,-5,'Top of the Shaft','This is the top of a vertical mine shaft.  Driven into the walls are the\nrusted remains of spikes.  By their regularity, it appears that they once\nheld a ladder fixed in place against the wall.  On the ceiling is a broken\npulley.  To the south is a boarded barricade, preventing further access\nsouth.  The shaft continues its steep descent towards the heart of the\nmountain below.\n',62,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,7,72,0,'',NULL),
(10302,12,55,-6,'Vertical Shaft','The mine shaft here is completely vertical.  You find yourself wishing for\na ladder or some rope to help prevent a drop into the murky depths of the mine.\n',62,131080,15,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(10303,12,55,-7,'A Narrow Ledge','A sixteen inch shelf here allows a bit of a respite from clinging to the\nmine walls.  Sound carries funny here.  Is that the echoing of your heart\nbeating you hear?\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(10304,12,55,-8,'Bottom of the Shaft','  This is the bottom of the shaft.  The murky darkness barely allows you to\nsee anything.  However, as you gaze closer, you can see how this was once\na working mine.  Grooves have been worn into the floor from the constant\npassage of carts heavily laden with the riches of the mountain.  This point\nin the mine appears to have been the collection point for the ores and\ntrailings to be taken out of the mountain.  In the corner lies the remains\nof a lift.  There is a tunnel leading deeper into the mountain from here.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,7,60,0,'',NULL),
(10305,13,56,-8,'Mine Shaft','This tunnel has been hewn out of the mountain in a fairly unorganized\nmanner.  It has been cut cleanly, but does not conform to a straight path.\nIt is as though the miners tunneling this shaft were following a twisting\ntrail of some kind.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,6,62,0,'',NULL),
(10306,14,55,-8,'Mine Shaft','The tunnel continues to twist about here.  On the walls are flecks and tiny\nribbons of gold streaking and dotting the dark corridor.  The vein of gold\nmust have been very rich for the dwarves to leave this much gold behind them\nas they tunneled further into the heart of the mountain.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,6,61,0,'',NULL),
(10307,14,56,-8,'Junction in the Shaft','At this junction three tunnels come together.  This is a fairly large area\nfor inside a mine.  You feel it is a little easier to breath here with the\nwalls a little further apart.  On the north wall some miner took the time\nto carve a design into the rock.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,8,75,0,'',NULL),
(10308,13,56,-8,'Mine Shaft','  The tunnel continues to twist about here.  On the walls are flecks and tiny\nribbons of gold streaking and dotting the dark corridor.  The vein of gold\nmust have been very rich for the dwarves to leave this much gold behind them\nas they tunneled further into the heart of the mountain.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,6,61,0,'',NULL),
(10309,14,56,-7,'Poorly Worked Tunnel','Here you see something uncharacteristic of dwarven craftsmanship, a rather\nroughly hewn tunnel in the mine which has been to this point cut quite cleanly\nand smoothly out of the mountain.  Debris and trailings litter the floor.\nThe walls are rough and sharp edges loom for the clumsy.  Evidence that\nthis may have been a rich find is found in the gemstones which remain\nuntaken from the walls.  Some stones look as though they would come out of\nthe wall with just a little encouragement.  You find yourself contemplating\njust what could have led the dwarves to abandon this mine?\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,8,72,0,'',NULL),
(10310,13,57,-8,'Mine Shaft','  The tunnel continues to twist about here.  On the walls are flecks and tiny\nribbons of gold streaking and dotting the dark corridor.  The vein of gold\nmust have been very rich for the dwarves to leave this much gold behind them\nas they tunneled further into the heart of the mountain.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,6,62,0,'',NULL),
(10311,14,58,-8,'Lost in the Mines','  The mine here has the feeling of some sort of warren.  Tunnels branch off in\nseemingly random directions.  It is as though the miners were chasing an elusive\nprey with their picks and sledges forging the trail.  A faint green haze casts\ndim illumination, but the source of this verdant haze is indiscernible.  The\nclose confines of the walls cause sounds to carry in unusual ways.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,6,62,0,'',NULL),
(10312,13,58,-8,'Lost in the Mines','  The mine here has the feeling of some sort of warren.  Tunnels branch off in\nseemingly random directions.  It is as though the miners were chasing an elusive\nprey with their picks and sledges forging the trail.  A faint green haze casts\ndim illumination, but the source of this verdant haze is indiscernible.  The\nclose confines of the walls cause sounds to carry in unusual ways.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,7,72,0,'',NULL),
