(10328,15,57,-7,'Lost in the Mines','  The mine here has the feeling of some sort of warren.  Tunnels branch off in\nseemingly random directions.  It is as though the miners were chasing an elusive\nprey with their picks and sledges forging the trail.  A faint green haze casts\ndim illumination, but the source of this verdant haze is indiscernible.  The\nclose confines of the walls cause sounds to carry in unusual ways.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,7,66,0,'',NULL),
(10329,16,57,-7,'Lost in the Mines','  The mine here has the feeling of some sort of warren.  Tunnels branch off in\nseemingly random directions.  It is as though the miners were chasing an elusive\nprey with their picks and sledges forging the trail.  On the north wall is the\nsolitary remains of a torch bracket.  The torch has long since decayed, but the\nbracket is still in decent shape.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,7,67,0,'',NULL),
(10330,14,56,-7,'Lost in the Mines','  The mine here has the feeling of some sort of warren.  Tunnels branch off in\nseemingly random directions.  It is as though the miners were chasing an elusive\nprey with their picks and sledges forging the trail.  A faint green haze casts\ndim illumination, but the source of this verdant haze is indiscernible.  The\nclose confines of the walls cause sounds to carry in unusual ways.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,6,80,0,'',NULL),
(10331,16,58,-7,'Supply Station','This looks like a typical supply closet for standard mining supplies.  There\nare hooks on the wall for miners to store extra helmets.  On the north wall\nis a locker where miners could store their larger items.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,8,78,0,'',NULL),
(10332,15,57,-7,'Rough Tunnel','  This tunnel is rather roughly hewn out of the mountain.  Debris and trailings\nlitter the floor, making passage tedious.  The walls are rough and sharp edges\nseem to jut out in the most awkward angles.  Evidence of the richness of this\nmine is apparent from the traces of riches left behind untaken.  Gold flecks the\nwalls, and gemstones sparkle in all the corners.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,6,60,0,'',NULL),
(10333,16,56,-7,'Rough Tunnel','  This tunnel is rather roughly hewn out of the mountain.  Debris and trailings\nlitter the floor, making passage tedious.  The walls are rough and sharp edges\nseem to jut out in the most awkward angles.  Evidence of the richness of this\nmine is apparent from the traces of riches left behind untaken.  Gold flecks the\nwalls, and gemstones sparkle in all the corners.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,6,60,0,'',NULL),
