(10336,15,57,-7,'Rough Tunnel','  This tunnel is rather roughly hewn out of the mountain.  Debris and trailings\nlitter the floor, making passage tedious.  The walls are rough and sharp edges\nseem to jut out in the most awkward angles.  Evidence of the richness of this\nmine is apparent from the traces of riches left behind untaken.  Gold flecks the\nwalls, and gemstones sparkle in all the corners.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,6,62,0,'',NULL),
(10337,15,58,-7,'Rough Tunnel','  This tunnel is rather roughly hewn out of the mountain.  Debris and trailings\nlitter the floor, making passage tedious.  The walls are rough and sharp edges\nseem to jut out in the most awkward angles.  The echoing of sounds from the\nnorth seem to indicate that the tunnel widens soon.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,6,66,0,'',NULL),
(10338,15,59,-7,'Inside a Natural Cavern','  The cavern appears to be unaltered by any artificial means.  The walls are\ncompletely smooth, worn with age.  Stalagmites and stalactites jut out from the\nfloor and ceiling like stone teeth in some large giant\'s mouth.  A gentle breeze\ncan be felt stirring the icy air; although its source is impossible to determine\nfrom here.  To the south is a rough opening into a mine tunnel.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10339,15,60,-7,'Center of the Cavern','  The source of the icy breeze is evident, as you notice the hole appearing\nclose overhead.  The narrow hole appears to be some sort of natural opening.  It\nappears to be possible to climb up into it if you step on the stalagmite\ndirectly below the opening.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10340,16,60,-7,'Inside a Natural Cavern','  The cavern appears to be unaltered by any artificial means.  The walls are\ncompletely smooth, worn with age.  Stalagmites and stalactites jut out from the\nfloor and ceiling like stone teeth in some large giant\'s mouth.  A gentle breeze\ncan be felt stirring the icy air; although its source is impossible to determine\nfrom here.  A thin stream of icy water slowly trickles to the east.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10341,14,60,-7,'Inside a Natural Cavern','  The cavern appears to be unaltered by any artificial means.  The walls are\ncompletely smooth, worn with age.  Stalagmites and stalactites jut out from the\nfloor and ceiling like stone teeth in some large giant\'s mouth.  A gentle breeze\ncan be felt stirring the icy air; although its source is impossible to determine\nfrom here.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10342,15,61,-7,'Inside a Natural Cavern','  The cavern appears to be unaltered by any artificial means.  The walls are\ncompletely smooth, worn with age.  Stalagmites and stalactites jut out from the\nfloor and ceiling like stone teeth in some large giant\'s mouth.  A gentle breeze\ncan be felt stirring the icy air; although its source is impossible to determine\nfrom here.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10343,15,60,-6,'Rock Chimney','  This is a narrow, cramped room.  The walls are very close.  With a little\nstretching you can reach both walls and shimmy up or down from here.\n',62,131080,15,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10344,15,60,-5,'Rock Chimney','  This is a narrow, cramped room.  The walls are very close.  With a little\nstretching you can reach both walls and shimmy up or down from here.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10345,15,60,-4,'Rock Chimney','  This is a narrow, cramped room.  The walls are very close.  With a little\nstretching you can reach both walls and shimmy up or down from here.\n',62,131080,15,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10346,15,60,-3,'Rock Chimney','  This is a narrow, cramped room.  The walls are very close.  With a little\nstretching you can reach both walls and shimmy up or down from here.\n',62,131080,15,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10347,15,60,-2,'Bend in the Chimney','  The chimney has an abrupt turn here.  It continues downwards and to the\nnorthwest.  You are still hanging in the air by your grip on the walls with\nyour hands and feet, so be careful!\n',62,131080,15,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10348,14,61,-2,'Bend in the Chimney','  The chimney has bent here, giving a place free from the worries of gravity to\nrest.  This narrow shaft continues up and to the southeast.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10349,14,61,-1,'Rock Chimney',' This is a narrow, cramped room.  The walls are very close.  With a little\nstretching you can reach both walls and shimmy up or down from here.\n',62,131080,15,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10350,14,61,0,'Rock Chimney',' This is a narrow, cramped room.  The walls are very close.  With a little\nstretching you can reach both walls and shimmy up or down from here.\n',62,131080,15,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10351,14,61,1,'Precarious Purchase','  The air is crisp up here on the mountain.  Below is a crack in the mountain\nleading into its depths.  The ledge you are standing on is only a couple feet\nwide.  As you peer over the edge you kick a small pebble over.  It seems to fall\nforever as you wait to hear it hit the bottom, but you never do hear it hit.\nFar to the north you can see the polar ice fields.  In the distance to the\nsouthwest you can make out a vast forrest.\n',62,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10352,15,61,1,'On a Ledge','  The ledge you are standing on is only a couple feet wide.  As you peer over\nthe edge you kick a small pebble over.  It seems to fall forever as you wait to\nhear it hit the bottom, but you never do hear it hit.  Far to the north you can\nsee the polar ice fields.  In the distance to the southwest you can make out a\nvast forrest.  To the west the ledge continues, and to the southeast is a narrow\npath along the mountain.\n',62,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10353,16,60,1,'A Narrow Ravine','  The path here is inside a narrow canyon.  There is barely room to walk two\nabreast.  The walls of the ravine reach high overhead and allow very little\nlight to enter.\n',62,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10354,16,60,0,'A Narrow Ravine','  The path here is inside a narrow canyon.  There is barely room to walk two\nabreast.  The walls of the ravine reach high overhead and allow very little\nlight to enter.\n',62,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10355,17,61,0,'A Faint Trail','  The trail here is not much of a trail, rather a suggestion of slightly easier\npassage through the boulder strewn field on the mountain.  It is tricky to find\nstable footing on all these loose rocks.  They shift and slip with every step.\n',62,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10356,18,62,0,'A Faint Trail','  The trail here is not much of a trail, rather a suggestion of slightly easier\npassage through the boulder strewn field on the mountain.  It is tricky to find\nstable footing on all these loose rocks.  They shift and slip with every step.\n',62,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
