(10368,17,60,-14,'Inside a Well','  It is difficult to see much in the black depths of the well.  All light seems\nto be absorbed by the black rock.  The walls are quite slick, and it is rather\ndifficult to find purchase to prevent tumbling into the black depths.  A rusty\nchain is suspended in the middle of the room continuing into the rooms above and\nbelow.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10369,17,60,-15,'Near the Bottom of the Well','  The rasping sounds of a rusty chain scraping on rock is heard here.  This\nseems to indicate that the vast well is not bottomless.  The slick rock is still\ndifficult to get a steady grip on the smooth surface.\n',62,131080,15,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10370,17,60,-16,'Bottom of the Well','  You find yourself at the bottom of a vast shaft.  Looking upwards it is\nimpossible to tell how tall the opening will reach.  A rusty chain idly swings\nin the center, slowly tracing a circle on the floor through its gentle pendulous\nmotion.  To the east the passage of water has carved a small cavern out of the\nrock.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10371,18,60,-16,'Small Cavern','  It is apparent that water through the passage of time has carved this cavern\nfrom the living rock of the mountain.  The walls are very smooth and show\nstriations tracing the history of the water\'s travels through the mountain.\nIt feels that this cavern is incredibly ancient.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10372,19,59,-16,'Small Cavern','  It is apparent that water through the passage of time has carved this cavern\nfrom the living rock of the mountain.  The walls are very smooth and show\nstriations tracing the history of the water\'s travels through the mountain.\nIt feels that this cavern is incredibly ancient.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10373,19,60,-16,'Dry Riverbed',' Once a river flowed here, but now only the sandy trace of its passage remains.\nAt one time an earthquake or other cataclysm must have changed its course.  The\nriver followed a strange course through the mountain, twisting and turning its\nway through the mountain.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(10374,18,60,-16,'Dry Riverbed',' Once a river flowed here, but now only the sandy trace of its passage remains.\nAt one time an earthquake or other cataclysm must have changed its course.  The\nriver followed a strange course through the mountain, twisting and turning its\nway through the mountain.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(10375,19,61,-16,'Dry Riverbed',' Once a river flowed here, but now only the sandy trace of its passage remains.\nAt one time an earthquake or other cataclysm must have changed its course.  The\nriver followed a strange course through the mountain, twisting and turning its\nway through the mountain.\n',62,131080,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
