(10600,33,37,0,'Trail alongside the Lake','  Wide enough to fit only a draft horse, this trail is slighty overgrown with \ngrass and small brush.  It follows the lake around its perimeter, there is not \nmuch room to veer off the trail since the lake borders one side and the forest \nthickens and rises sharply up the mountains on the other.  A narrow game trail\nseems to wind north through the underbrush and rock and rubble of the mountain.\n',90,139584,25,0,0,0,0,-1,5,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10601,34,37,0,'Trail Alongside the Lake','  Wide enough to fit only a draft horse, this trail is slighty overgrown with \ngrass and small brush.  It follows the lake around its perimeter, there is not \nmuch room to veer off the trail since the lake borders one side and the forest \nthickens and rises sharply up the mountains on the other.\n',90,139584,25,0,0,0,0,-1,5,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10602,35,37,0,'Trail Alongside the Lake','  Wide enough to fit only a draft horse, this trail is slighty overgrown with \ngrass and small brush.  It follows the lake around its perimeter, there is not \nmuch room to veer off the trail since the lake borders one side and the forest \nthickens and rises sharply up the mountains on the other.\n',90,139584,25,0,0,0,0,-1,5,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10603,36,37,0,'Trail Alongside the Lake','  Wide enough to fit only a draft horse, this trail is slighty overgrown with \ngrass and small brush.  It follows the lake around its perimeter, there is not\nmuch room to veer off the trail since the lake borders one side and the forest \nthickens and rises sharply up the mountains on the other.  At this point the\ntrail crosses a rocky streambed of fast moving water and you are careful to\nwatch every step.  The small powerful stream seems to be an outlet for the lakes\noverflow which flows down a steep mountain face north of here to empty out \nelsewhere.  You try to follow the waters flow downwards but it is quickly lost\nfrom sight as it moves through the underbrush and rubble of the mountainside.\n',90,139588,25,60,23274,1,0,-1,5,-1,0,'',NULL),
