(10635,41,34,0,'Before the Fishing Dock','  Green grass stands tall here.  To your west you see the fishing dock that \nbegins right beneath your feet.  A strange smell wafts in from the cool \nbreeze from the west.  The slight lapping of the water against the pylons \nwhich the dock stands gives you a relaxed and soothing feeling.\n',90,139584,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10636,33,33,0,'Dirt Path','  As you enter deeper into the forest the initial feeling of foreboding begins \nto disappear as you realize the magnificence of this ancient copse.  The air \nflees through the leaves and branches as the wind blows steadily from the west.\nThings here seem supremely calm and you feel safe.\n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10637,34,33,0,'Lakeside Forest','  Trees here alongside the lake are sparse, branches have been trimmed back\nto help reduce the amount of foliage that falls onto the trail in the autumn\nmonths.  According to the Lake Elf legend, once a year the goddess of the\nLake,  Eldathial, will make herself in the form of a mortal elf and walk the\nTrail alongside the lake.  During the autumn festival it is considered a great\nomen for a adolescent elf to see the Goddess\'s footprints in the sand.\n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
