(10653,41,32,0,'Arden Lake','  As you gaze across its surface, the calm, deep blue-green waters of Arden \nLake confer a sense of peace and tranquility.  This lake is the home of the \nLake Elf Goddess, Eldathial.  Arden Lake is a deep lake that reaches a depth \nof four hundred feet in two distinct places.  The remainder of the lake ranges \nfrom twenty-five to one hundred feet more than ten feet from the shoreline.\n',90,139584,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10654,33,31,0,'Dirt Path','  Several buildings can be seen to the south but they blend extremely well into\nthe natural topiary behind them.  You can see the impressions of little feet\nin the dirt below yours.  There are several bones piled along side each of the\nshacks.  You realize these bones are an offering to the goddess of the lake\nwho provides the Lake Elves with the fish they harvest for food.\n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10655,34,31,0,'Campsite in the Forest','  A circle of charred stones is the center of this area.  Old timber smolders \nfrom the previous occupants, this must be the center of an outdoor patrol of \nsome sort.  The foliage here is dense providing adequate coverage from the \nelements and sufficient cover to go undetected..\n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10656,35,31,0,'Dirt Path','  Several buildings can be seen to the south but they blend extremely well into \nthe natural topiary behind them.  You can see the impressions of little feet \nin the dirt below yours.  There are several bones piled along side each of the \nshacks.  You realize these bones are an offering to the goddess of the lake \nwho provides the Lake Elves with the fish they harvest for food.\n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10657,36,31,0,'Before the Great Hall of the King','  Two great doors stand open showing the inside of the Great Hall to the \nsouth.  There is a sign posted above the doors and an emblem of a green and \nblue scaled mermaid is emblazoned on both doors.  You can smell the smoke \neminating from the fire-pits burning inside.\n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10658,37,31,0,'Dirt Path','  Several buildings can be seen to the south but they blend extremely well into \nthe natural topiary behind them.  You can see the impressions of little feet \nin the dirt below yours.  There is several bones piled along side each of the \nshacks.  You realize these bones are an offering to the goddess of the lake \nwho provides them with the fish they harvest for food.\n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
