(10663,42,31,0,'Arden Lake','  As you gaze across its surface, the calm, deep blue-green waters of Arden \nLake confer a sense of peace and tranquility.  This lake is the home of the \nLake Elf Goddess, Eldathial.  Arden Lake is a deep lake that reaches a depth \nof four hundred feet in two distinct places.  The remainder of the lake ranges \nfrom twenty-five to one hundred feet more than ten feet from the shoreline.\n',90,139584,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10664,36,30,1,'Sanctuary','  Before you is an altar to pray to the goddess of the Lake.  Slow burning \nincense and candles convey a feeling of serenity and peace.  The smoke of \nthe incense is almost intoxicating and you feel completely and utterly \nrelaxed.\n',90,139592,32,0,0,0,0,0,15,200,0,'',NULL),
(10665,33,30,0,'Fisherman\'s Settlement','  This is a simple house that can hold between 2-3 elves, the typical lake elf\nfamily unit.  Although this house does not cater to the creature comforts that\nmay be found in other elven territories, this house is immaculate.  There is a\nsimple wood stove in the middle of the room that empties its smoke into the\ncylindrical roof above.  There is an innovative but simple method of air\ncirculation that the lake elves have discovered which allows the fire to be\nfed while driving the smoke out.  Fishing nets line the wall by the entrance\nand there are simple beds and furniture neatly placed about.\n',90,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10666,34,30,0,'Fisherman\'s Settlement','  This is a simple house that can hold between 2-3 elves, the typical lake elf \nfamily unit.  Although this house does not cater to the creature comforts that \nmay be found in other elven territories, this house is immaculate.  There is a \nsimple wood stove in the middle of the room which empties its smoke into the \ncylindrical roof above.  There is an innovative but simple method of air \ncirculation that the lake elves have discovered which allows the fire to be \nfed while driving the smoke out.  Fishing nets line the wall by the entrance \nand there are simple beds and furniture neatly placed about.\n',90,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10667,35,30,0,'Private quarters of the Royal Family','  Hidden away from the main chamber this room is for private meetings or for\na place of peace for any of the royal family members.  This room is plain and\nquiet.\n',90,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(10668,36,30,0,'Hall of King Loranth-gil','  This timber framed building rises up 30 feet to an innovative ventilation\nsystem of cross-hatched boards and pulleys.  There is a great firepit in\nthe middle of the room and tables and chairs are stacked against each wall\ncovered in silk to remain hidden.  The Hall of Loranth-gil is a beautifully\nconstructed and decorated.  Plants and vines cover the walls so completely\nthat the illusion of being outdoors is given.\n',90,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(10669,37,30,0,'Study of Loranth-gil','  Stacked high with ancient books of the histories of the Lake elves this\nstudy is one of the few libraries in the world.  As you peruse the shelves \nyou see many books that catch your interest.  As you reach for the case a \nsharp jolt flies up your arm, the bookcase has been warded to keep the books \naway from the hands of the indiscriminating.\n',90,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,10,200,0,'',NULL),
(10670,38,30,0,'Ring of Huge Elm Trees','  Here, in a perfect circle, stand a number of ancient elm trees.  Within the \nring of trees lies a perfectly round and smooth piece of white granite.  You \ncan actually feel the pulsating magic that emanates from this stone.  The wind \ncoming off the lake rustles the leaves in these gigantic trees, but aside from \nthat you notice that is it strangely silent here.\n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10671,39,30,0,'Before a Gigantic Elm','  With a width of about twenty-five feet this ancient elm tree rises well above\nthe canopy of the forest.  It seems all of the surrounding trees reach out \ntowards this matriarch of the forest and most of upper branches of the canopy \nseems to be intertwined.  You think that you can make out a platform high above\nbut the lack of light makes it difficult for you to be sure.  Giant knots the \nsize of a goblin\'s head sporadically stick out throughout the breadth and \nlength of the tree.\n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10672,40,30,0,'Arden Lake','  As you gaze across its surface, the calm, deep blue-green waters of Arden \nLake confers a sense of peace and tranquility.  This lake is the home of the \nLake Elf Goddess, Eldathial.  Arden lake is a deep lake that reaches a depth \nof four hundred feet in two distinct places.  The remainder of the lake ranges \nfrom twenty-five to one hundred feet more than ten feet from the shoreline.\n',90,139584,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
