(10676,42,29,0,'Arden Lake','  As you gaze across its surface, the calm, deep blue-green waters of Arden \nLake confers a sense of peace and tranquility.  This lake is the home of the \nLake Elf Goddess, Eldathial.  Arden lake is a deep lake that reaches a depth \nof four hundred feet in two distinct places.  The remainder of the lake ranges \nfrom twenty-five to one hundred feet more than ten feet from the shoreline.\n',90,139584,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10677,43,29,0,'Arden Lake','  As you gaze across its surface, the calm, deep blue-green waters of Arden \nLake confers a sense of peace and tranquility.  This lake is the home of the \nLake Elf Goddess, Eldathial.  Arden lake is a deep lake that reaches a depth \nof four hundred feet in two distinct places.  The remainder of the lake ranges \nfrom twenty-five to one hundred feet more than ten feet from the shoreline.\n',90,139584,29,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10678,42,28,0,'Waterfall','  Rising hundreds of feet into the air and crashing down right in front of\nyou.  The waterfall sends up a huge plume that coats everything with dew.\nThe sound here is almost deafening and the misty haze cuts down on visibility\nsignificantly.  To one side of the falls is a cliff that is covered with \nmosses and ferns.\n',90,139584,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10679,43,28,0,'Waterfall','  Rising hundreds of feet into the air and crashing down right in front of\nyou.  The waterfall sends up a huge plume that coats everything with dew.\nThe sound here is almost deafening and the misty haze cuts down on visibility\nsignificantly.  To one side of the falls is a cliff that is covered with\nmosses and ferns.\n',90,139584,29,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10680,39,30,1,'Platform high in the trees','  A sturdy, yet very well concealed platform has been constructed high in the \nelm trees that surround the lake.  Large rails with a lattice framework line \nthe wooden runaway and the dizzying height of the platforms is accented by the \nfact that every fifth board is missing, forcing you to look down while you\ntravel along.\n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10681,36,34,-1,'Beneath the lake','  You have entered a pit below the surface of the lake, it is pitch black here.\nIt\'s virtually impossible to see and the only way that you can  navigate is by\nfeel alone.\n',90,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10682,36,33,-1,'Underwater cavern.','  You follow the walls along this underwater passageway; the water is \ndefinitely getting colder the farther in you travel.\n',90,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10683,35,32,-1,'Underwater cavern.','  You follow the walls along this underwater passageway; the water is \ndefinitely getting colder the farther in you travel.\n',90,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10684,34,31,-1,'Underwater cavern.','  You follow the walls along this underwater passageway; the water is \ndefinitely getting colder the farther in you travel.\n',90,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10685,33,30,-1,'Underwater cavern.','  You follow the walls along this underwater passageway; the water is \ndefinitely getting colder the farther in you travel.\n',90,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10686,32,29,-1,'Underwater cavern.','  You follow the walls along this underwater passageway; the water is \ndefinitely getting colder the farther in you travel.\n',90,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10687,32,28,-1,'Underwater cavern.','  You follow the walls along this underwater passageway; the water is \ndefinitely getting colder the farther in you travel.\n',90,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10688,32,27,-1,'Underwater cavern.','  You follow the walls along this underwater passageway; the water is \ndefinitely getting colder the farther in you travel.\n',90,139584,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10689,32,27,0,'Cave deep within the mountain.','  Buried deep within the bowels of this mountain a huge cave has been gutted \nout and transformed into a home for Shorenjin the Ancient.  Deep gashes in \nthe wall give evidence to the dragon\'s temperment.  The air here is extremely \nhumid.  Far, towards the top of the cavern are gigantic stalactites that \nglisten with moisture.  There is a periodic rumble that moves the pools of \nwater that have gathered on the floor.  A feeling of great evil hangs in the \nair and every nerve in your body tells you that it is not safe to be here.\n',90,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,500,0,'',NULL),
(10690,38,30,1,'Crows nest high in the trees.','  The walkway continues on east to west, off of the northside railing there is \na small crows nest that overlooks the lake, providing a decent view through \nthe trees to the north.  The crows\' nest is camouflaged by the natural foliage \nwhose growth that been directed around the railing with small vines and rope.  \n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10691,37,30,1,'Walkway high in the trees.','  As the walkway continues here you see that the high branches of the elm \ntrees have been carefully pruned and directed to make a hallway of sorts,  \nas the branches and leaves create a half-moon shaped hallway above your head.  \nHere and there are spy-holes that have been cut through the branches to let \nin light and give a view to the outside.\n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10692,37,31,1,'Platform in the tree','  This portion of the walkway has actually been cut into on of the ancient \nelm trees towering in from below.  The craftsman that created the path through \nthis tree must have been a master, since you cannot make out any damage that \nhas occurred to the tree itself.  It seems as if the tree opened itself up to \nallow for the placement of boards to run through it.  The inner wood of the \ntree is smooth and unblemished.\n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10693,36,31,1,'Walkway in the trees','  The foot-walk continues north and east here, again the branches and natural \nfoliage all around have been bent to create a sparse ceiling of leaves to \nprotect from the elements.  Along each side of this walkway are crossbows that \nhave been mounted to the railing.  Strapped to the support pole immediately \nbelow the crossbow is a quiver of arrows.\n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10694,36,32,1,'Walkway in the trees','  The  foot-walk continues north to south here, again the branches and natural \nfoliage all around have been bent to create a sparse ceiling of leaves to \nprotect from the elements.  Along each side of this walkway are crossbows that \nhave been mounted to the railing.  Strapped to the support pole immediately \nbelow the crossbow is a quiver of arrows.\n',90,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10695,36,33,1,'Room in the trees','  Unlike the walkway intersection to the south this room here has been \nphysically carved out of this trees  The walls show sign of chopping and are \nsplintered and black with soot.  The smell of the sap the tree bleeds here in \na futile effort to heal itself gives the room a powerful sickly, sweet odor.  \nThere are fish bones and torn netting strewn on the floor in here and a \nmakeshift bed of pine boughs lies in the corner.  Whoever created this place \nseems to not have had much respect for this ancient elm.\n',90,139592,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,10,0,'',NULL),
(10696,33,38,0,'A Game Trail Overlooking a Steep Path','  Standing on this narrow game trail a steep treachous looking path moves\nalmost straight down the side of the mountain.  The game trail seems to\nmove southwards as the northern path grows to narrow and overgrown for \npassage.  You can see that the forest begins to clear away towards the south \nto some large clear area.  In the distance you can see the beginnings of \nanother set of foothills leading even farther up to a lone peak.  At the \nbottom of the foothills a cliff forms a waterfall that is hundreds of feet \nhigh.  The air is sweet with the smell of flowers and thick with moisture.\n',90,139584,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10697,33,38,-1,'Path Up the Mountain','  This path up the side of the mountain is made of loose gravel and rock, it \nis very steep and footing is treacherous.   Each side of the path is cluttered \nwith huge boulders that tower above you  and thick vegetation that hide the \nlittle critters that live here.  The wind here is strong and it chills you to \nthe bone.  The air here is definitely thinner which makes it harder to breathe.\n',90,139584,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10698,33,38,-2,'Forest Trail','  Here lies a trail up to a decent sized mountain to the south.  Up to this \npoint the landscape in this area has been relatively flat, however, the trail\nleading south goes almost straight up.  To the northwest an almost solid wall\nof ferns conceals a narrow passage through a small crevice in the rock.\n',90,139584,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10700,51,-113,4,'Cliff Ledge','  Standing upon this cliff ledge you can look out over the sea to the west.\nA large opening in the cliff face is to the east.  The only other way off this\nledge is to bet your life on the faith of your climbing skills and attempt to\nscale the cliff face below you.\n',69,131080,25,0,0,0,0,0,8,700,0,'',NULL),
(10701,52,-113,4,'Natural Tunnel','  This tunnel appears to be a natural formation through the rock of the\nmountain.  It slopes downward to the east and you can feel and smell a\nsalty breeze to the west.  The floor is layered with numerous rocks but\nthe ceiling appears to range from eight to fifteen feet in height.\n',69,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10702,53,-113,4,'Natural Tunnel','  This tunnel appears to be a natural formation through the rock of the\nmountain.  It slopes downward to the east and you can feel and smell a\nsalty breeze to the west.  The floor is layered with numerous rocks but\nthe ceiling appears to range from eight to fifteen feet in height.\n',69,131080,33,0,0,0,5,2,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10703,54,-113,4,'Natural Tunnel','  This tunnel appears to be a natural formation through the rock of the\nmountain.  It slopes downward to the east and you can feel and smell a\nsalty breeze to the west.  The floor is layered with numerous rocks but\nthe ceiling appears to range from eight to fifteen feet in height.\n',69,131080,33,0,0,0,5,2,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10704,55,-113,4,'Natural Tunnel','  This tunnel appears to be a natural formation through the rock of the\nmountain.  It slopes downward to the east and you can feel and smell a\nsalty breeze to the west.  The floor is layered with numerous rocks but\nthe ceiling appears to range from eight to fifteen feet in height.\n',69,131080,33,0,0,0,7,5,6,100,0,'',NULL),
