(10706,57,-113,4,'Natural Tunnel','  This tunnel appears to be a natural formation through the rock of the\nmountain.  It slopes downward to the east and you can feel and smell a\nsalty breeze to the west.  The floor is layered with numerous rocks but\nthe ceiling appears to range from eight to fifteen feet in height.\n',69,131080,33,0,0,0,15,2,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10707,58,-113,4,'Natural Tunnel','  This tunnel appears to be a natural formation through the rock of the\nmountain.  It slopes downward to the east and you can feel and smell a\nsalty breeze to the west.  The floor is layered with numerous rocks but\nthe ceiling appears to range from eight to fifteen feet in height.\n',69,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10708,59,-113,4,'Cavern Ledge','  You are overlooking a large cavern.  You can either go down to the cavern\nfloor or move west into a natural tunnel where you can feel a salty breeze.\n',69,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10709,59,-113,3,'A Large Cavern','  You are standing in a large cavern with a small pond at the center.  About\nhalfway up the west wall you can see a small ledge and a tunnel appears to\nbegin at the south wall.  Overhead you can see a large hole in the roof of the\ncavern that may have been the source of water in this room.  When the water\nlevel was higher, water would have flowed out of the cavern down the\ntunnel to the south.  You can either travel down the tunnel to the south or\nclimb up to the ledge on the west wall.\n',69,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(10710,59,-114,3,'Dark Tunnel','   You are in a dark tunnel.  Since the walls are very smooth you\ndeduce that at one time an underground river must have run through\nthis tunnel.\n',69,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10711,59,-115,3,'Dark Tunnel','   You are in a dark tunnel.  Since the walls are very smooth you\ndeduce that at one time an underground river must have run through\nthis tunnel.\n',69,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10712,59,-116,3,'Dark Tunnel','   You are in a dark tunnel.  Since the walls are very smooth you\ndeduce that at one time an underground river must have run through\nthis tunnel.  While the main tunnel leads north and south a\nsmaller branch leads to the east.\n',69,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10713,60,-116,3,'Dark Tunnel','   You are in a dark tunnel.  Since the walls are very smooth you\ndeduce that at one time an underground river must have run through\nthis tunnel.  The ceiling has collapsed to the east completely blocking\nthe path.\n',69,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10714,59,-117,3,'Dark Tunnel','   You are in a dark tunnel.  Since the walls are very smooth you\ndeduce that at one time an underground river must have run through\nthis tunnel.\n',69,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10715,58,-118,3,'Dark Tunnel','   You are in a dark tunnel.  Since the walls are very smooth you\ndeduce that at one time an underground river must have run through\nthis tunnel.\n',69,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10716,58,-119,3,'Dead End','   The tunnel stretches on to the north but ends suddenly to the\nsouthwest in a blank wall.  You notice that the air feels fresher\nto the southwest for some reason.\n',69,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10717,57,-120,3,'Dimly Lit Tunnel','   You are in a dimly lit tunnel which continues to the southwest.\nYou deduce that an underground river must have once run this tunnel\nsince the walls appear very smooth.  There is a large stone door set in the\nsoutheast wall, while the tunnel ends in a blank wall to the northeast.\nThe air towards the south seems slightly fresher for some reason.\n',69,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10718,58,-121,3,'Path to the Mines','This is the king\'s personal path to the mines.  It connects the Keep\nabove to the mines below and allows the King to keep a watchful eye on the\nCitadel\'s main commodity.  There are large stones door set in the\nnorthwest and southeast walls.\n',-1,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10719,56,-121,3,'Dimly Lit Tunnel','   You are in a dimly lit cave.  Due to the fact that the walls are\nextremely smooth you deduce that an underground river must have once run\nthrough this tunnel.\n',69,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10720,55,-122,3,'Dark Room','   You are in a small dark room.  There is a large gaping hole in the\nfloor.  While the tunnel continues to the northeast it dead ends in all\nother directions.  The only thing to catch your eye is the strange\nblankness of the wall to the southeast.\n',69,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10721,56,-123,3,'Base of a Small Tower','   You are at the base of a small tower.  There is a staircase leading\nup and a strange tapestry on the northwest wall.  The only sources of\nlight you can locate are small glowing balls attached to the wall.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,4,'',NULL),
(10722,53,-123,3,'Base of a Small Tower','   You are at the base of a small tower.  There is a staircase\nleading upward and a secret door in the south wall.  The room is\nlit by glowing balls of light.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,4,'',NULL),
(10723,52,-123,3,'Prison Cell','   As you enter the cell you quickly take note of the decayed corpses\nand skeletons which line the walls.  Some have been literally hung on\nthe wall itself while others are slouched against its base.  All of the\ncorpses appear as if they were mutilated while they were chained and\nhelpless.  From what little evidence that is left you discover that the\ncorpses are from numerous races and that some are even those of\nwomen and children.  You can see a cell door to the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(10724,51,-123,3,'Torture Chamber','   As you enter the room you fight to keep down what little food is left\nin your stomach.  The stench of the room alone is overpowering yet\nthe sight is even worse.  At first glance the walls appear to be made\nof a deep crimson brick unlike the black brick the rest of the keep is\nconstructed of.  But upon further examination you discover that the\nwalls are literally coated in layers of dried blood.  You can see the\nruined remains of what appear to have been ghastly torture devices\nscattered about the room.  There are pieces and body parts of\nnumerous races thrown about the room while one corpse still hangs\nupon a rack in the far corner.  There is a steel door to the southeast.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10725,51,-124,3,'Prison Cell','   As you enter the cell you quickly take note of the decayed corpses and\nskeletons which line the walls.  Some have been literally hung on the wall\nitself while others are slouched against its base.  All of the corpses appear\nas if they were mutilated while they were chained and helpless.  From what\nlittle evidence that is left you discover that the corpses are from numerous\nraces and that some are even those of women and children.  You can see a\ncell door to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(10726,52,-124,3,'Dungeon Hallway','   You are in what appears to be a dungeon hallway.  You notice several\ntrails of what seems to be blood running along the floor and walls.  The\nstench of human waste and death lingers in the air while ghostly moaning\ncan be heard from all directions.  You notice cell doors to the\nnorth and west and a steel door to the northwest.  Feelings of dread\nemanate from the steel door.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10727,53,-124,3,'Office','   You are standing in a small cramped office.  The only contents of the\nroom are a small desk and a chair.  Actually you are glad that is all that\nis in the room since if anything was present you might not fit.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,4,'',NULL),
(10728,54,-124,3,'Storage','   You are standing among a huge mound of very large chests.  They\nare mostly smashed and splintered while their contents lie scattered\nover the floor.  It appears as though anything worth any value has long\nbeen pilfered from the room.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10729,55,-124,3,'Storage','   This appears to have once been a storage room for all of the\nkeeps extra stuff.  The room is in utter chaos with broken and\nshredded items stern everywhere within the room.  You can hear\nthe constant movement of rodents as they move among their treasure\nhoard.  To the south you see a door.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10730,56,-124,3,'Hallway','   You are in damp stone hallway.  It appears to be in the cellar of some\nlarge structure.  The hall oddly dead ends to the north, but if you look\nclosely you can see footprints which seem to pass through the wall.  You\nhear the echo of dripping water all around you and the air seems slightly\nstale as though this area has been unused for some time.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,4,'',NULL),
(10731,57,-124,3,'Food Storage Room','   This appears to have once been a storage room for food stores.\nThe stench of spoiled food is unbelievable and nothing appears\nsalvageable.  You notice that the room continues to the east and\nthere is a small door to the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10732,58,-124,3,'Meat Storage','   This is where the meat must have been stored.  There is large\npieces of rancid meat hanging from hooks in the ceiling.  You notice that\nnot all of the meat appears to be from animals.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10733,51,-125,3,'Base of a Tower','   You are at the base of a tower.  There is large door in the\neast wall while a set of stairs wind upwards.  The stairwell is lit\nby glowing balls of light attached to the walls.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10734,52,-125,3,'Dungeon Hallway','   You are in what appears to be a dungeon hallway.  You notice several\ntrails of what seems to be blood running along the floor and walls.  The\nstench of human waste and death lingers in the air while ghostly moaning\ncan be heard from all directions.  There is cell door to the south, a steel\ndoor to the east and a door to the west.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10735,53,-125,3,'Guard\'s Station','   You are standing in a room which is well lit by torches.  You\nsee a large desk in the center of the room, a large table off the side,\nand a small chest in the corner.  What used to be deck of playing\ncards lays upon the table completely rotted.  You notice a steel door\nto the west, through which you can hear ghostly moaning!\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10736,54,-125,3,'Hallway','   You are in damp stone hallway.  It appears to be in the cellar of some\nlarge structure.  You hear the echo of dripping water all around you and the\nair seems slightly stale as though this area has been unused for some time.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10737,55,-125,3,'Hallway','   You are in damp stone hallway.  It appears to be in the cellar of some\nlarge structure.  You hear the echo of dripping water all around you and the\nair seems slightly stale as though this area has not been used in some time.\nYou can see a small door to the north and a wood door to the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10738,56,-125,3,'Hallway','   You are in damp stone hallway.  It appears to be in the cellar of some\nlarge structure.  You hear the echo of dripping water all around you and the\nair seems slightly stale as though this area has been unused for some time.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10739,57,-125,3,'Hallway','   You are in damp stone hallway.  It appears to be in the cellar of some\nlarge structure.  You hear the echo of dripping water all around you and the\nair seems slightly stale as though this area has been unused for some time.\nYou notice a small door to the north and an opening in the wall to the\neast.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10740,58,-125,3,'Base of a Tower','  You are at the base of a tower.  There is large portal in the\nwest wall while a set of stairs wind upwards.  The stairwell is lit\nby glowing balls of light attached to the walls.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10742,52,-126,3,'Prison Cell','   As you enter the cell you quickly take note of the decayed corpses\nand skeletons which line the walls.  Some have been literally hung on\nthe wall itself while others are slouched against its base.  All of the\ncorpses appear as if they were mutilated while they were chained and\nhelpless.  From what little evidence that is left you discover that the\ncorpses are from numerous races and that some are even those of\nwomen and children.  You can see a cell door to the north.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(10743,53,-126,3,'Hallway','You are in damp stone hallway.  It appears to be in the cellar of some\nlarge structure.  You hear the echo of dripping water all around you and the\nair seems slightly stale as though this area has been unused for sometime.\nThere is a large portal to the south.\n',-1,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10744,54,-126,3,'Among the Racks','   These are the racks that were once used to store the keeps\nsupple of wine and mead.  Large kegs line one wall while racks for\nwine storage are at the other side of the room.  Many of the racks\nare overturned with their contents laying smashed upon the floor.\nThere is a mild stench of fermented fruit within the room.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10745,55,-126,3,'Wine Cellar','   At one time this must have been the keeps wine cellar.  Large vats\nare placed throughout the room while the racks for storage are to the west.\nYou see numerous kegs and wine presses within the room.  While the stench of\nfermented wine is very strong it barely keeps your attention from the sound\nof rodents moving within the walls.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10746,57,-126,3,'Weapons and Armor Store Room','   This appears to have been a weapons and armor storage room.  There is\nbroken weaponry and a mixture of smashed and broken armor all over\nthe floor.  You see pieces of plate mail, scraps of leather, and fragile\nslivers of obsidian.  It is very doubtful that anything is left that can\nbe used.  There is a small door to the west and a heavy door to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10747,58,-126,3,'Treasure Chamber','  Appearing to have escaped the destruction that devastated the rest of the\nKeep this room appears fairly neat and tidy.  Several small chests of\nobsidian are stacked throughout the room looking entirely too heavy to\nmove.  Unless you know what you are looking for its unlikely you\'ll\nfind anything useful.  The only exit from the room is a doorway to\nthe west displaying a heavy door to seal the room.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10748,53,-127,3,'Base of a Large Tower','   You are at the base of a large tower.  The room is lit by glowing\nballs attached to the walls.  You can see a dark hallway to the north and the\nstaircase leads upward.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10749,56,-127,3,'Base of a Large Tower','   You are at the base of a large tower.  The room is lit by glowing\nballs attached to the walls.  You can see a dark hallway to the north and\nthe staircase leads upward.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10750,51,-123,4,'General\'s Quarters','   Small but tidy, the general\'s room is decorated by several tattered and\nworn plaques and awards.  The corpse of the general lies slouched in the\ncorner in a complete suit of rusted and smashed armor.  The corpse has\nbeen kept warm in the afterlife by a large dented shield which lies over his\nbody.  Across the room lies the right arm of the skeleton which still holds\nthe broken remains of a mighty broad sword.  You can see a door to the\nsoutheast.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(10751,52,-123,4,'Royal Advisor\'s Quarters','   The royal advisor\'s room looks to have once been a small orderly room\nwith numerous maps, globes, documents, and books, all of which are\nneeded by an advisor so that he may fulfill his job adequately.  All of these\nthings now lie about the room destroyed.  The advisor\'s corpse is pinned to\nthe wall by a broken shaft of a very ornate staff, while the bed and other\nfurnishings of the room have all been smashed and burned in one corner.\nYou can see a door to the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(10752,53,-123,4,'In a Small Tower','   Fortunately the walls of this small tower are completely lit by the glowing\nballs of light which line the stairwell.  The stairs continue both up and down\nfrom the landing which you stand upon, but it is impossible to determine\nwhat lies around then bend either way.  It appears as if this tower has seen\nlittle use for many decades, and even then the wear on the stone of the stair\ntreads appear as if few people were permitted to use this tower.  You see a\npainting on the southeast wall of the tower.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,4,'',NULL),
(10753,56,-123,4,'In a Small Tower','   Fortunately the walls of this small tower are completely lit by the glowing\nballs of light which line the stairwell.  The stairs continue both up and down\nfrom the landing which you stand upon, but it is impossible to determine\nwhat lies around then bend either way.  It appears as if this tower has seen\nlittle use for many decades, and even then the wear on the stone of the stair\ntreads appear as if few people were permitted to use this tower.  You see a\npainting on the southwest wall of the tower.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,4,'',NULL),
(10754,57,-123,4,'Headmaster\'s Quarters','   This room is small but adequate furnished with a small dresser,\nnight stand, and trunk.  The trunk is at the foot of a small bed which is\ncomplete with corpse.  Unlike the other corpses found in the keep the\nheadmaster appears to have died of starvation as he locked himself into his\nroom.  The contents of the room are few, but they are in a neat orderly\nfashion.  There is a door to the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10755,58,-123,4,'Servant\'s Quarters','   This room of the keep is tightly packed with cots and small trunks.\nAs you sift through the destroyed garments and useless trinkets you decide\nthat this must have been the servants quarters for men.  More than one of\nthe cots is still occupied by the corpse of a servant who must have been\nmurdered in his sleep.  You can see a door to the southwest.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(10756,51,-124,4,'Commander\'s Quarters','   Murdered in his sleep you can see the Commander of the Royal Guard\nlying within his bed.  Although he slept with his weapon, his armor lies\nscattered about the room, neither must have helped him and now both are\nrusted scraps of metal.  It appears that the commander was a simple man\nas there are only a small cot and dresser in this room.  You can see a door\nto the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(10757,52,-124,4,'End of a Hallway','   Acting as the main access way for this floor of the keep, this hallway is\nrelatively clear of obstructions and is quite large.  At one time their was a\nmodest runner of blue carpet on the floor, but it has long since faded and\nbecome unraveled.  You can see brackets for torches lining the walls, but\nthey all appear empty.  There are doors to the north, northwest, and west.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10758,53,-124,4,'Hallway','   Acting as the main access way for this floor of the keep, this hallway is\nrelatively clear of obstructions and is quite large.  At one time their was a\nmodest runner of blue carpet on the floor, but it has long since faded and\nbecome unraveled.  You can see brackets for torches lining the walls, but\nthey all appear empty.  There is a door to the east and the hallway continues\nto the west.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10759,54,-124,4,'To the Left of a Large Throne','   You are standing next to a large detailed obsidian throne, which is\nlaced with steel edging.  The feeling of something extremely evil emanates\nfrom the throne.  You can see a large pool of dried blood upon the throne\nitself, and numerous bloody footprints on the thrones footrest.  To the\nnorthwest you see a large tapestry which is partly torn from its hanging.\nYou notice a small plain door behind the tapestry, but you can\'t seem to\nbudge the door open.  You see a door to the west, while the room continues\nto the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,4,'',NULL),
(10760,55,-124,4,'To the Right of a Large Throne','   You are standing next to a large detailed obsidian throne, which is\nlaced with steel edging.  The feeling of something extremely evil emanates\nfrom the throne.  You can see a large pool of dried blood upon the throne\nitself, and numerous bloody footprints on the thrones footrest.  To the\nnortheast you see a large tapestry which is partly torn from its hanging.\nYou notice a small plain door behind the tapestry, but you can\'t seem to\nbudge the door open.  You see a door to the east, while the room continues\nto the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,4,'',NULL),
(10761,56,-124,4,'Hallway','   Acting as the main access way for this floor of the keep, this hallway is\nrelatively clear of obstructions and is quite large.  At one time their was a\nmodest runner of blue carpet on the floor, but it has long since faded and\nbecome unraveled.  You can see brackets for torches lining the walls, but\nthey all appear empty.  There is a door to the west and the hallway\ncontinues to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10762,57,-124,4,'End of a Hallway','   Acting as the main access way for this floor of the keep, this hallway is\nrelatively clear of obstructions and is quite large.  At one time their was a\nmodest runner of blue carpet on the floor, but it has long since faded and\nbecome unraveled.  You can see brackets for torches lining the walls, but\nthey all appear empty.  There are doors to the north, northwest, east, and to\nthe south.  The hallway continues to the west.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10763,58,-124,4,'Maids Quarters','   You are in a small room which is filled with numerous cots pushed\nclosely together.  Many of the beds have trunks at the foot of them, but\nmost of them appear to be smashed.  By the size and type of torn garments\nthrown about the room you determine that this must have been the maids\nquarters.  Off to one corner of the room you can see what is left of a\ncorpse.  There is a door to the west.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(10764,51,-125,4,'In a Tower','   The stairway of this tower seems to have been very well decorated\nat one time.  There are numerous slashed paintings of what appear to\nbe royal personages lining the walls which appear to have been\npainted in splendid colors.  Also you find yourself walking on what\nwas once a rich plush carpet.  Glowing balls of light help you to see\nthat the stairwell continues both up and down from this point.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,4,'',NULL),
(10765,52,-125,4,'Stacks','   What at one time were nice and orderly stacks are now a librarians\nnightmare.  Many of the books are strewn about the floor, and turn to\ndust as you tread on them.  A similar fate awaits the books you touch\non the shelves.  While the main room of the library is to the east, the\nstacks continue to the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10766,53,-125,4,'Library','   Although at one time this room appeared to have been neat and\norderly it now lies in shambles.  Several of the writing desks in this\nsection have been overturned while others have been outright\nsmashed to splinters.  Stacks of paper can be found scattered about\nthe room, many of which appear to be maps of the keep.  The library\ncontinues to the south, the stacks are to the west and a door is to the\neast.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10767,54,-125,4,'Throne Room','   You are standing in what was once an elaborate throne room.  As you\nlook around all that can now be found in the room is shredded tapestries,\nslashed paintings, broken tables and smashed chairs.  It appears as if a\ngreat struggle took place within this room.  Among the debris you notice\nmany splintered pieces of bone from the people who died here.  A grave\nsense of dread hangs over you as you stand in this part of the keep, you\nfind yourself constantly scanning the room for its source.  You see a door\nto the west and a large obsidian door to the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10768,55,-125,4,'Throne Room','   You are standing in what was once an elaborate throne room.  As you\nlook around all that can now be found in the room is shredded tapestries,\nslashed paintings, broken tables and smashed chairs.  It appears as if a\ngreat struggle took place within this room.  Among the debris you notice\nmany splintered pieces of bone from the people who died here.  A grave\nsense of dread hangs over you as you stand in this part of the keep, you\nfind yourself constantly scanning the room for its source.  You see a door\nto the east and a large obsidian door to the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10769,56,-125,4,'Dining Hall','   This is the great dining hall of the keep.  A long table runs the length\nof the room.  You see the remains of a large feast on the table which\nappears to have rotted before it was ever touched by guests.  In many\nplaces large chunks of the table are missing or great notches have been\nplaced in the table top.  A large rusted axe is completely embedded in one\nsection of the table.  You can see a large fireplace in the west wall, along\nwith a door also to the west.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10770,57,-125,4,'Dining Hall','   This is the great dining hall of the keep.  A long table runs the length\nof the room.  You see the remains of a large feast on the table which\nappears to have rotted before it was ever touched by guests.  In many\nplaces large chunks of the table are missing or great notches have been\nplaced in the table top.  A large rusted axe is completely embedded in one\nsection of the table.  There is a door to the north.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10771,58,-125,4,'In a Tower','   This appears to be an access tower for the keep servants as you see\nmany rotted bits of food, dropped scraps of cloth, or broken buckets upon\nthe stairs.  The stairs are well lit by the glowing balls of light attached to\nthe walls and continue both up and down.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10772,51,-126,4,'Study','   Although small the room is packed with ancient books and tomes.\nUnfortunately being left unpreserved for such a long period has left\nthe books dry and brittle to the touch.  To touch them would risk their\ndestruction.  Your eyes are drawn to the corpse of the librarian\nslouched across his desk at the center of the room with his skull\nsmashed in.  He seems to be grasping some ancient tome, but it also\ntoo brittle to touch.  A large worn tapestry hangs to the north depicting\na simple map of the general keep.  There is a door to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,4,'',NULL),
(10773,52,-126,4,'Stacks','   What at one time were nice and orderly stacks are now a librarians\nnightmare.  Many of the books are strewn about the floor, and turn to\ndust as you tread on them.  A similar fate awaits the books you touch\non the shelves.  While the main room of the library is to the east, the\nstacks continue to the north.  There is a door to the west.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10774,53,-126,4,'Library','   Although at one time this room appeared to have been neat and\norderly it now lies in shambles.  Several of the writing desks in this\nsection have been overturned while others have been outright\nsmashed to splinters.  Stacks of paper can be found scattered about\nthe room, many of which appear to be maps of the keep.  The library\ncontinues to the north, the stacks are to the west and a door is to the\neast.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10775,54,-126,4,'Antechamber','   Used for formal greeting of guest and ambassadors, this large room\nwas at one time very richly decorated with gifts and tokens from\nforeign realms.  Most have been destroyed or desecrated beyond use.\nA large tower stairway can be seen to the southwest, a large obsidian\ndoor can be seen to the north, and a door can be seen to the west as\nwell.  There is a large stone door to the south which appears to lead\nout of the keep, but some force seems to be baring it shut.  Overhead\nbalconies of the upper levels can be seen overlooking this room.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(10776,55,-126,4,'Antechamber','   Used for formal greeting of guest and ambassadors, this large room\nwas at one time very richly decorated with gifts and tokens from\nforeign realms.  Most have been destroyed or desecrated beyond use.\nA large tower stairway can be seen to the southeast, a large obsidian\ndoor can be seen to the north, and a door can be seen to the east as\nwell.  There is a large stone door to the south which appears to lead\nout of the keep, but some force seems to be baring it shut.  Overhead\nbalconies of the upper levels can be seen overlooking this room.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(10777,56,-126,4,'Dining Hall','   This is the great dining hall of the keep.  A long table runs the length\nof the room.  You see the remains of a large feast on table which\nappears to have rotted before it was ever touched by guests.  In many\nplaces large chunks of the table are missing or great notches have been\nplaced in the table top.  There is a door to the west.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10778,57,-126,4,'Dining Hall','   This is the great dining hall of the keep.  A long table runs the length\nof the room.  You see the remains of a large feast on the table which\nappears to have rotted before it was ever touched by guests.  In many\nplaces large chunks of the table are missing or great notches have been\nplaced in the table top.  You can see a large fireplace in the east wall,\nalong with a large swinging door also to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10779,58,-126,4,'Kitchen','   It appears as if a whirlwind struck this part of the keep.  You find\nmutilated corpses scattered about the room.  A large fireplace used for\ncooking can be seen in the west wall, within which you find the remains\nof a burnt corpse lying among a pile of smashed pots.  Numerous kitchen\nutensils lie strewn across a large oak table at the center of the room.  There\nis a large swinging door to the west.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10780,53,-127,4,'In a Large Tower','   This was probably the main access tower for guests and dignitaries of\nthe keep.  It would be possible to walk three persons abreast within this\nlarge tower stairwell.  You can tell that it must have seen quite a bit of use\nby the worn treads of the stairs and the smooth wood of the handrail.  The\ntower is lit by numerous glowing balls of light attached to the walls.  By\nthe light of these balls you can see that the stairs continue both up and\ndown from this landing.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10781,56,-127,4,'In a Large Tower','   This was probably the main access tower for guests and dignitaries of\nthe keep.  It would be possible to walk three persons abreast within this\nlarge tower stairwell.  You can tell that it must have seen quite a bit of use\nby the worn treads of the stairs and the smooth wood of the handrail.  The\ntower is lit by numerous glowing balls of light attached to the walls.  By\nthe light of these balls you can see that the stairs continue both up and\ndown from this landing.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10782,53,-123,5,'In a Small Tower','  Fortunately the walls of this small tower are completely lit by the\nglowing balls of light which line the stairwell.  The stairs continue both up\nand down from the landing which you stand upon, but it is impossible to\ndetermine what lies around the bend either way.  It appears as if this tower\nhas seen little use for many decades, and even then the wear on the stone of\nthe stair treads appear as if few people were permitted to use this tower.  A\nstone on the south wall seems to catch your attention.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,4,'',NULL),
(10783,56,-123,5,'In a Small Tower','   Fortunately the walls of this small tower are completely lit by the\nglowing balls of light which line the stairwell.  The stairs continue both up\nand down from the landing which you stand upon, but it is impossible to\ndetermine what lies around the bend either way.  It appears as if this tower\nhas seen little use for many decades, and even then the wear on the stone of\nthe stair treads appear as if few people were permitted to use this tower.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10784,52,-124,5,'Princess\'s Closet','  Standing among the tattered remains of countless silk dresses you realize\nthat the princess did not lack for fine clothes.  A large wardrobe stands\nagainst the east wall.  As you look closer you notice a scuff mark in the\nshape of an arc directly in front of the wardrobe.  The princess\'s bedroom is\nto the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10785,53,-124,5,'Prince\'s Study','   The prince\'s study is occupied by a large oak desk, a small liquor cabinet,\ntwo plush chairs, and the decayed corpse of what looks to be the prince\nhimself.  You see a trail of smeared blood which runs in a very organized\npattern from stone to stone on the north wall.  A large tapestry depicting the\nprincess is on the west wall.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,4,'',NULL),
(10786,54,-124,5,'Guest Study','   This room is for guest and ambassadors to meet or relax when not in\naudience with the king.  There are numerous chairs, sofas, and tables\nthroughout the room, along with a couple of bookshelves filled with books\nfor the pleasure of guests.  Besides the general state of decay that the room\nis in, most things in this room are still intact.  The room continues to the\nsouth and there is a doorway to the east leading to the guest dining room.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10787,55,-124,5,'Guest Dining Hall','   A scaled down version of the keeps dining hall this room is for small\nnon-formal dinners with guest and ambassadors.  A long cherry table runs\nthe length of the room and is bare of any objects.  The room continues to\nthe south and there is a doorway set into the west wall leading to the guest\nstudy.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10788,56,-124,5,'Guest Quarters','   Simply furnished with a bed, chest, table and chair, this appears to be one\nof the guest rooms of the keep.  Most of the furnishings are smashed and\nthe guest\'s possessions lie scattered about the room.  You notice many\ntrinkets of dwarven make among the debris.  The corpse of the dwarven\nambassador is pinned to the wall by his own great battle axe.  There lies\na door to the southeast.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10789,57,-124,5,'Guest Quarters','   Simply furnished with a bed, chest, table and chair, this appears to be one\nof the guest rooms of the keep.  Most of the furnishings are smashed and\nthe guest\'s possessions lie scattered about the room.  You notice many\ntrinkets of shadow make among the debris.  The corpse of the ambassador\nfrom the ancient land of the shadow lies against the far wall with a look of\nabsolute terror frozen on his face.  A door lies to the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10790,51,-125,5,'In a Tower','   The stairway of this tower seems to have been very well decorated at one\ntime.  There are numerous slashed paintings of what appear to be royal\npersonages lining the walls which appear to have been painted in splendid\ncolors.  Also you find yourself walking on what was once a rich plush\ncarpet.  Glowing balls of light help you to see that the stairwell continues\nboth up and down from this point.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,4,'',NULL),
(10791,52,-125,5,'Princess\'s Room','   The highlight of this room is a large bed with a shredded silk canopy over\nit.  As you step closer you notice that the rotted corpse of the princess lies\nin the bed.  Appearing very peaceful, the princess looks to have died in her\nsleep from a massive chest wound.  There is a bloody trail of footprints\nleading up to the west wall.  There is a solid oak door to the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,4,'',NULL),
(10792,53,-125,5,'Prince\'s Room','   Elegantly furnished with a good sized bed and large wardrobe, this is the\nprince\'s bedroom.  Off to the side of the room you can see two smashed\nchairs, both of which were once covered with plush upholstery of crimson\nvelvet.  You can see a trail of dried blood leading to the north.  There is a\nsolid oak door to the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10793,54,-125,5,'Guest Study','   This room is for guest and ambassadors to meet or relax when not in\naudience with the king.  There are numerous chairs, sofas, and tables\nthroughout the room, along with a couple of bookshelves filled with books\nfor the pleasure of guests.  Besides the general state of decay that the room\nis in, most things in this room are still intact.  The room continues to the\nnorth and there is a door to the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10794,55,-125,5,'Guest Dining Hall','   A scaled down version of the keeps dining hall this room is for small\nnon-formal dinners with guest and ambassadors.  A long cherry table runs\nthe length of the room and is bare of any objects.  The room continues to\nthe north and there is a door to the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10795,56,-125,5,'Guest Quarters','   Simply furnished with a bed, chest, table and chair, this appears to be one\nof the guest rooms of the keep.  Most of the furnishings are smashed and\nthe guest\'s possessions lie scattered about the room.  You notice many\ntrinkets of halfling make among the debris.  The corpse of the halfling\nambassador lies against the far wall with his small skull crushed.  There\nis a door to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10796,57,-125,5,'Hallway','   This hallway provides access to the guest wing on this level of the keep.\nThere are numerous torch brackets lining the wall, but most of them are\neither empty or hold the stub of burned out torches.  A faded green runner\ncan be found on the floor of the hallway.  The hallway continues to the\nsouth, there are doors to the west, northwest, and to the north.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10797,58,-125,5,'In a Tower','   This appears to be an access tower for the keep servants as you see\nmany rotted bits of food, dropped scraps of cloth, or broken buckets upon\nthe stairs.  The stairs are well lit by the glowing balls of light attached to\nthe walls and continue both up and down.  There is a door to the west.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10798,52,-126,5,'Princess\'s Waiting Room','   Draped with blood soaked silk hangings, this room is the waiting room for\nthose calling on the princess.  You see a large plush sofa to one side of the\nroom, but its cushions are slashed and covered with dried blood.  You see\na solid oak door to the north.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10799,53,-126,5,'Prince\'s Waiting Room','   Simply furnished with a small bench and two chairs, both broken, this room\nacts as a waiting room for those wishing to speak to the prince.  As with\nmany of the rooms in the keep, you notice blood smeared across the walls\nof the room and bones littering the floor.  There is a solid oak door to the\nnorth.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10800,54,-126,5,'Balcony','   Overlooking the keep\'s antechamber on the ground floor, this second\nfloor balcony is surrounded by a fragile wood railing.  Hanging from the\nrailings you see numerous flags and tapestries depicting the different crests\nof the royal family.  Most are tattered and hanging in shreds.  The balcony\nextends to the east and there is a door to the north.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10801,55,-126,5,'Balcony','   Overlooking the keep\'s antechamber on the ground floor, this second\nfloor balcony is surrounded by a fragile wood railing.  Hanging from the\nrailings you see numerous flags and tapestries depicting the different crests\nof the royal family.  Most are tattered and hanging in shreds.  The balcony\nextends to the west and there is a door to the north.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10802,56,-126,5,'Guest Quarters','   Simply furnished with a bed, chest, table and chair, this appears to be one\nof the guest rooms of the keep.  Most of the furnishings are smashed and\nthe guest\'s possessions lie scattered about the room.  You notice many\ntrinkets of elven make among the debris.  The corpse of the elven\nambassador lies against the far wall.  It appears he died in a great battle.\nThere is a door to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10803,57,-126,5,'Hallway','   This hallway provides access to the guest wing on this level of the keep.\nThere are numerous torch brackets lining the wall, but most of them are\neither empty or hold the stub of burned out torches.  A faded green runner\ncan be found on the floor of the hallway.  The hallway continues to the\nnorth and there is a door to the west.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10804,53,-127,5,'In a Large Tower','   This was probably the main access tower for guests and dignitaries of\nthe keep.  It would be possible to walk three persons abreast within this\nlarge tower stairwell.  You can tell that it must have seen quite a bit of use\nby the worn treads of the stairs and the smooth wood of the handrail.  The\ntower is lit by numerous glowing balls of light attached to the walls.  By\nthe light of these balls you can see that the stairs continue both up and\ndown from this landing.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10805,56,-127,5,'In a Large Tower','   This was probably the main access tower for guests and dignitaries of\nthe keep.  It would be possible to walk three persons abreast within this\nlarge tower stairwell.  You can tell that it must have seen quite a bit of use\nby the worn treads of the stairs and the smooth wood of the handrail.  The\ntower is lit by numerous glowing balls of light attached to the walls.  By\nthe light of these balls you can see that the stairs continue both up and\ndown from this landing.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10806,53,-123,6,'In a Small Tower','  Fortunately the walls of this small tower are completely lit by the\nglowing balls of light which line the stairwell.  The stairs continue both up\nand down from the landing which you stand upon, but it is impossible to\ndetermine what lies around the bend either way.  You notice a large tapestry\ncovering the southeast wall.  It appears as if this tower has seen little use\nfor many decades, and even then the wear on the stone of the stair treads\nappear as if few people were permitted to use this tower.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10807,56,-123,6,'In a Small Tower','   Fortunately the walls of this small tower are completely lit by the\nglowing balls of light which line the stairwell.  The stairs continue both up\nand down from the landing which you stand upon, but it is impossible to\ndetermine what lies around the bend either way.  You notice a large tapestry\non the southwest wall.  It appears as if this tower has seen little use for\nmany decades, and even then the wear on the stone of the stair treads\nappear as if few people were permitted to use this tower.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10808,52,-124,6,'King\'s Bedroom','   The only furnishings of this room are a large bed and wardrobe.  This is\nroom is used only for the sleeping quarters for the king.  His study is to the\neast and the room continues to the south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10809,53,-124,6,'King\'s Study','   Besides a large oak desk and two large chairs, you see a large bookshelf\nto the north of the room which is oddly hanging about a half an inch off\nthe floor.  The top of the desk has been broken in two and brittle pieces\nof paper lie strewn about the room.  The corpse of the king, complete in his\narmor, has been thrown across the top of his desk.  It appears, by the many\nbroken bones, that the king died from a long and hard fought battle.  The\nking\'s bedroom is to the west and a door can be seen to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10810,54,-124,6,'Royal Study','   A large table sets in the middle of this room surrounded by numerous\nplush chairs.  This is the royal study where the royal family meets to hold\nconferences or where the king and his advisors meet to discuss important\nstate affairs.  A large tapestry hangs in the northwest corner of the room.\nTo the west you notice a door and the room continues to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10811,55,-124,6,'Royal Study','   A large table sets in the middle of this room surrounded by numerous\nplush chairs.  This is the royal study where the royal family meets to hold\nconferences or where the king and his advisors meet to discuss important\nstate affairs.  A large tapestry hangs in the northeast corner of the room.\nTo the east you notice a door while a large fireplace dominates the southern\nwall of the room.  The room continues to the west.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10812,56,-124,6,'Queen\'s Study','   Arranged perfectly the furniture of this room has seen little use.  A large\ndesk and chair are the main furnishings in the room.  You can see a\nbookshelf to the north which oddly hangs about a half inch off the floor\nand a door to the west.  The queen\'s bedroom is to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10813,57,-124,6,'Queen\'s Bedroom','   Apparently seeing little use, the queen\'s bed and a small night stand are\nthe only furnishings visible in this room.  Although faded and ripped the\nsilk canopy of the bed is much too lavish to have been anything but simply\nfor show.  The queen\'s study is to the west while the room continues to\nthe south.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10814,51,-125,6,'In a Tower','   The stairway of this tower seems to have been very well decorated at one\ntime.  There are numerous slashed paintings of what appear to be royal\npersonages lining the walls which appear to have been painted in splendid\ncolors.  Also you find yourself walking on what was once a rich plush\ncarpet.  Glowing balls of light help you to see that the stairwell continues\nboth up and down from this point.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,4,'',NULL),
(10815,52,-125,6,'King\'s Room','   It is here that the king meets guest on an informal basis.  The remains of a\nset of chairs and small table can be seen to one side of the room.  The\ncorpse of one of the king\'s squires lays on the floor at the northern end of\nthe room.  Dressed in rotted leather and wielding only a small dagger the\nsquire appears to have died protecting his king.  A painting on the west wall\ndepicts the king looking out over his kingdom from atop a tower.  The king\'s\nbed room is to the north and the king\'s closet is to the east.  You can see a\nsolid door to the southeast.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,4,'',NULL),
(10816,53,-125,6,'King\'s Closet','   Hanging from rotted wood hangers to either side of you are the tattered\nremains of the kings lavish wardrobe.  You see numerous silk outfits in\nthe royal colors of the king.  The king\'s room is to the west and a small\ndoor can be seen to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10817,54,-125,6,'Royal Dining Room','   This is the dining quarters for the royal family and their personal\nguests.  A long table, which is coated in a heavy layer of dust, runs the\nlength of the room.  The table is surrounded by numerous high-backed\nchairs.  You can see a door to the west and the room continues to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10818,55,-125,6,'Royal Dining Room','   This is the dining quarters for the royal family and their personal\nguests.  A long table, which is coated in a heavy layer of dust, runs the\nlength of the room.  The table is surrounded by numerous high-backed\nchairs.  A large fireplace sits coldly to the north of the room.  You can\nsee doors to the east and south.  The room continues to west.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10819,56,-125,6,'Queen\'s Closet','   Hanging from rotted wood hangers to either side of you are the tattered\nremains of the queen\'s lavish wardrobe.  You see numerous silk gowns\nseparated by seasonal colors.  The queen\'s room is to the west and a\ndoor can be seen to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10820,57,-125,6,'Queen\'s Apartment','   This is the room where the queen and her ladies pass the time each day.\nA large spinning wheel lies destroyed to the east of the room.  The queen\nand one of her ladies lie slouched over a table at the center of the room\nbludgeoned to death.  The queen\'s closet is to the west and her bedroom\nis to the north.  A curtain covers an opening to the south while a solid oak\ndoor can be seen to the southwest.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,4,'',NULL),
(10821,58,-125,6,'In a Tower','   This appears to be an access tower for the keep servants as you see\nmany rotted bits of food, dropped scraps of cloth, or broken buckets upon\nthe stairs.  The stairs are well lit by the glowing balls of light attached to\nthe walls and continue both up and down.  You notice that the path to\nthe west wall seems to be free of debris.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,4,'',NULL),
(10822,52,-126,6,'Squires\' Quarters','   The two small beds are overturned in this room and among them you find\nthe bloody corpse of one of the king\'s squires.  He appears to have fought\nbravely to the end with only a small dagger for a weapon.  Unfortunately\nhis trusty dagger must have finally failed him since you find it broken off\nat the hilt.  Two chest are smashed open, leaving useless trinkets and\nrotted clothes scattered about the room.  The king\'s waiting room is to the\neast.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10823,53,-126,6,'King\'s Waiting Room','   Simply furnished with a small bench and two chairs, both broken, this room\nacts as a waiting room for those wishing to speak to the king.  As with\nmany of the rooms in the keep, you notice blood smeared across the walls\nof the room and bones littering the floor.  There is a solid door to the\nnorthwest and the squire\'s quarters are to the west.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(10824,54,-126,6,'Balcony','   Overlooking the keep\'s antechamber on the ground floor, this third floor\nbalcony is surrounded by a fragile wood railing.  You become dizzy from\nthe height of the balcony as you look over the edge.  Hanging from the\nrailings you see numerous flags and tapestries depicting the different crests\nof the royal family.  Most are tattered and hanging in shreds.  The balcony\nextends to the east and the king\'s waiting room is to the west.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10825,55,-126,6,'Balcony','   Overlooking the keep\'s antechamber on the ground floor, this third floor\nbalcony is surrounded by a fragile wood railing.  You become dizzy from\nthe height of the balcony as you look over the edge.  Hanging from the\nrailings you see numerous flags and tapestries depicting the different crests\nof the royal family.  Most are tattered and hanging in shreds.  You see an\noak door to the north of the balcony while the balcony extends to the west\nand the queen\'s waiting room is to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10826,56,-126,6,'Queen\'s Waiting Room','   Draped with blood soaked silk hangings, this room is the waiting room for\nthose calling on the queen.  You see a large plush sofa to one side of the\nroom, but its cushions are slashed and covered with dried blood.  There is\na solid oak door to the northeast and a door to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10827,57,-126,6,'Ladies\' Quarters','   The two small beds are overturned in this room and among them you find\nthe bloody corpse of one of the queen\'s ladies.  She appears to have been\nbrutally beaten to death as she huddled in the corner fearing for her life.\nTwo chest are smashed open, leaving useless trinkets of jewelry and rotted\nsilk gowns scattered about the room.  The queen\'s waiting room is to the\nwest, and a thin curtain covers an opening in the north wall.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10828,53,-127,6,'In a Large Tower','   This was probably the main access tower for guests and dignitaries of\nthe keep.  It would be possible to walk three persons abreast within this\nlarge tower stairwell.  You can tell that it must have seen quite a bit of use\nby the worn treads of the stairs and the smooth wood of the handrail.  The\ntower is lit by numerous glowing balls of light attached to the walls.  By\nthe light of these balls you can see that the stairs continue both up and\ndown from this landing.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10829,56,-127,6,'In a Large Tower','   This was probably the main access tower for guests and dignitaries of\nthe keep.  It would be possible to walk three persons abreast within this\nlarge tower stairwell.  You can tell that it must have seen quite a bit of use\nby the worn treads of the stairs and the smooth wood of the handrail.  The\ntower is lit by numerous glowing balls of light attached to the walls.  By\nthe light of these balls you can see that the stairs continue both up and\ndown from this landing.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10830,53,-123,7,'Atop a Small Tower','   You are standing atop a small tower that borders the battlements of the\nkeep.  The view from this spot is extremely good.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10831,56,-123,7,'Atop a Small Tower','   You are standing atop a small tower that borders the battlements of the\nkeep.  The view from this spot is extremely good.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(10832,54,-124,7,'Battlements','   You are standing on the battlements of keep.  It is here that the guards\nkeep a look out for advancing armies.  It appears that a large scale battle\ntook place here, as you can see numerous corpses and rusted pieces of\narmor laying about.\n',69,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10833,55,-124,7,'Battlements','   You are standing on the battlements of keep.  It is here that the guards\nkeep a look out for advancing armies.  It appears that a large scale battle\ntook place here, as you can see numerous corpses and rusted pieces of\narmor laying about.\n',69,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10834,51,-125,7,'Atop the King\'s Tower','   This covered tower room provides views of the surrounding area for the\nking.  The king comes here to look over his citadel and surrounding lands.\nYou can see vast distances in any direction.  A set of stairs leads down.\n',69,131073,2,0,0,0,0,0,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10835,54,-125,7,'Battlements','   You are standing on the battlements of keep.  It is here that the guards\nkeep a look out for advancing armies.  It appears that a large scale battle\ntook place here, as you can see numerous corpses and rusted pieces of\narmor laying about.\n',69,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
