(10840,53,-127,7,'Atop a Large Tower','   You are standing atop a large tower that borders the battlements of the\nkeep.  The view from this spot is incredible.\n',69,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10841,56,-127,7,'Atop a Large Tower','   You are standing atop a large tower that borders the battlements of the\nkeep.  The view from this spot is incredible.\n',69,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10842,56,-126,3,'Hallway','   You are in damp stone hallway.  It appears to be in the cellar of some\nlarge structure.  You hear the echo of dripping water all around you and the\nair seems slightly stale as though this area has been unused for some time.\nThere is a large portal to the south and a small door to the east.\n',69,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10843,51,-113,3,'Cliff Face','  Either you are floating on air or your climbing skills are superb.  This\nshear cliff face has very few handholds, but a rush of adrenaline keeps you\ngoing as you look down at the jagged rocks covering the beach below.\n',69,139264,35,0,0,0,0,0,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10844,51,-113,2,'Cliff Face','  Either you are floating on air or your climbing skills are superb.  This\nshear cliff face has very few handholds, but a rush of adrenaline keeps you\ngoing as you look down at the jagged rocks covering the beach below.\n',69,139264,35,0,0,0,0,0,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10845,51,-113,1,'Cliff Face','  Either you are floating on air or your climbing skills are superb.  This\nshear cliff face has very few handholds, but a rush of adrenaline keeps you\ngoing as you look down at the jagged rocks covering the beach below.\n',69,139264,35,0,0,0,0,0,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10846,51,-113,0,'A Rocky Beach','  This beach is covered with very sharp jagged pieces of rock which have\nfallen from the cliff face above you.  A stormy sea is to the west.  This\nspot appears to have the best climbing surface, although it is poor at best,\nif you wish to attempt scaling the cliff face above you.\n',69,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,15,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10847,51,-114,0,'A Rocky Beach','  This beach is covered with very sharp jagged pieces of rock which have\nfallen from the cliff face above you.  A stormy sea is to the west.  A rock\nslide to the south has blocked the path along the beach.\n',69,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,15,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10848,51,-112,0,'A Rocky Beach','This beach is covered with very sharp jagged pieces of rock which have\nfallen from the cliff face above you.  A stormy sea is to the west.\n',0,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,15,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10849,51,-111,0,'A Rocky Beach','  This beach is covered with very sharp jagged pieces of rock which have\nfallen from the cliff face above you.  A stormy sea is to the west.  The\nbeach dead ends to the north in a shear rock wall polished smooth by the\nstormy winds of the sea.\n',69,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,15,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10899,0,0,0,'Lava Pool','   You have just landing in pool of hot steaming LAVA!  As you attempt to\nreach the edge you realize that there are notches carved into the side of the\npool for people to sit in!  This must be where Mithros comes to rest and\nrelax after a long day of world creation.\n',0,131081,49,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10900,-27,-28,1,'Fox\'s Den',' Around you the thick earthen walls are at least dry, if cold.\nOnly the one small opening above you can be seen which is able to\nbe concealed with a few pieces of scrub brush.  The floor of the\nden is dry fine dirt littered with a few bones picked clean of all\nmeat.\n',75,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,144,0,'',NULL),
(10901,-18,-21,0,'A Crushed Stone Road','   You stand in the middle of a road of crushed stone.  The road continues\nto the east, where you see a major intersection, and to the northwest, forced\nto detour by a large rock immediately to the west.  Fields of tall grass\nprevent passage to the north and south.\n',63,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10902,-19,-20,0,'A Crushed Stone Road','   You stand in the middle of a road made of crushed stone.  The road\ncontinues to the southeast and southwest, forced from its east/west\npath by a large rock, which lies directly to your south.\n',63,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10903,-20,-21,0,'A Crushed Stone Road','   You stand in the middle of a road of crushed stone.  The road\ncontinues to the northeast and up the mountain side.  A large rock\nlies immediately to the east.\n',63,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10904,-20,-21,1,'Switchback Road','   You stand on a road carved into the granite face of the mountain,\nwhich lies to your west.  The road continues south along the side of\nthe mountain, and down to the plains below.  A steep drop-off prevents\npassage to the east.\n',63,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10905,-20,-22,1,'Switchback Road','   You stand on a road carved into the granite face of the mountain,\nwhich lies to your west.  The road continues north and south along the\nside of the mountain.  A steep drop-off prevents passage to the east.\nA large clump of brush stands against the mountain to the west.\n',63,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10906,-20,-23,1,'Switchback Road','   You stand on a road carved into the granite face of the mountain,\nwhich lies to your west.  The road continues north and up along the\nface of the mountain.  A steep drop-off prevents passage to the east.\n',63,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10907,-20,-23,2,'Switchback Road','   You stand on a road carved into the face of the mountain, which lies\nto your south and west.  The road continues down and east along the\nmountain side.  A steep drop prevents movement to the north.\n',63,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10908,-19,-23,2,'Switchback Road','   You stand on a road carved into the face of the mountain, which lies\nto your south.  The road continues west and up along the mountain side.\nA steep drop prevents movement to the north and east.\n',63,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10909,-19,-23,3,'Switchback Road','   You stand on a road carved into the side of a mountain, which lies\nto the south.  The road continues down and southeast along the face of\nthe mountain.  A steep drop-off prevents passage to the north, east and west.\n',63,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10910,-18,-24,3,'Switchback Road','   You stand on a road carved into the side of a mountain, which lies\nto the south and west.  The road continues northwest along the face of\nthe mountain and southeast into a mountain pass.  A steep drop-off\nprevents passage to the north and east.\n',63,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10911,-17,-25,3,'Mountain Pass','   You stand at the eastern end of a mountain pass.  A cold wind whips\nthrough the pass, causing you to shiver and hope you aren\'t caught here\nin bad weather.  High mountain peaks loom to the northwest and southwest.\nThe road continues northwest down the eastern slope of the mountains and\nwest into the pass.  A steep drop prevents passage to the north, east and\nsouth.\n',63,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10912,-18,-25,3,'Center of the Pass','   You stand in the center of a high mountain pass.  A cold breeze whips\nthrough the pass, causing you to shiver and hope you aren\'t caught here\nin bad weather.  Tall, snow-covered peaks loom to the north and south.\nThe pass continues to the east and west.\n',63,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10913,-19,-25,3,'Mountain Pass','   You stand at the western end of a mountain pass.  A cold wind whips\nthrough the pass, causing you to shiver and hope you aren\'t caught here\nin bad weather.  High mountain peaks loom to the northeast and southeast.\nThe road continues down the western slope of the mountain, into a large\nvalley you see to your west, and east into the pass.\n',63,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10914,-19,-28,2,'Poacher\'s Campsite',' Concealed within a tight circle of rock the campsite is virtually\ninvisible from the valley outside.  Fist sized rocks coat the floor\nof the little campsite, crushed into smaller pebbles in several places.\nThe rocks are a sickly deep red color from the large amounts of blood\nwhich coats the ground all about you.  The stench from the rotting flesh\nis almost unbearable and you can\'t imagine any civilized person who could\npossibly stand to sit or sleep in the camp.  Off to one side you spot a\nhuge hole dug into the rock and decipher that the majority of the stench\nis coming from the hole.  Some scrub brush has been gathered from the valley\nbelow to provide a screen for the opening in the rock to the northwest.\n',75,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,15,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10915,-29,-23,2,'A Small Cabin','  You are standing in the middle of a small cabin.  The walls of the\ncabin are made of rough cut logs, and the floor and roof from pine\nboards.  There is a door to the southeast.\n',63,131084,32,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(10916,-21,-22,1,'Cave Entrance','  You stand in the entrance to a cave on the side of the mountain.\nSome light filters through the large clump of brush which blocks the\nentrance to the east.  The cave itself continues northwest into the\ngloom.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(10917,-22,-21,1,'A Cave in the Mountain','   You stand in the back of a mountain cave.  There is barely enough\nroom to stand in this small area, which has evidently been used by some\nanimal as den.  A few bones lie scattered about and there is a musky\nsmell to the place.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(10918,-26,-25,2,'A Mountain Stream','  You are in the middle of a swiftly flowing mountain stream.  The water is\ndeep and cold, and numerous rocks make this stream treacherous.  The banks\naround you are too high to climb, but there is a bridge above you and maybe\nyou can climb its support pillars.  The stream flows from the northwest\ninto a lake to the southeast.\n',63,131072,29,0,0,0,15,8,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10919,-21,-30,2,'High Mountain Pass','   You stand in a pass between two large peaks, one to the north and one to the\nwest.  A large mountain valley, ringed by trees with a lake in the middle, lies\nto the northwest.  The center of the pass, which lies to the south, has been\nblocked by an avalanche.  Something tells you it will be a while before you are\nable to proceed any further in this direction.\n',63,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10920,-19,-25,2,'Road Above the Tree Line','   You stand above the tree line on the side of a range of tall mountains.\nA road made of crushed stone descends from the pass above you toward the\nfloor of the valley to the west.  The plant life is minimal, consisting\nmainly of moss and lichen.\n',63,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10921,-19,-26,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You stand above the tree line on the western slope of a range of tall\nmountains.  A series on unclimbable, snow covered peaks are to the east\nand south.  The hillside slopes westward toward the center of the valley.\nPlant life this high up is minimal, consisting mainly of moss and lichen.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10922,-20,-24,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You stand above the tree line on the southwestern slope of a range of\ntall mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the north and east.\nThe mountain side descends to the west-southwest toward the center of the\nvalley.  Plant life is minimal at this altitude, consisting mainly of moss\nand lichen.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10923,-20,-25,2,'Road through a Pine Forest','   You are standing in the middle of a road made of crushed stone, which\nascends to the east toward a mountain pass and descends to the west toward\nthe valley floor.  Tall evergreens, mostly pine, surround you on all sides.\nYou can see a fair distance between the trunks of the trees, as there is\nvery little ground clutter.  Birds flutter back and forth overhead, and\nthe occasional small animal can be seem darting between the trees.\n',63,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10924,-20,-26,2,'A Pine Forest','   You stand in the middle of a forest of evergreens, mostly pine, but\nincluding some aspen and birch.  The ground slopes upward to the south\nand east, and downward toward the valley floor to the west.\nVisibility is surprisingly good between the trunks of the trees, due to\nthe absence of the clutter that normally marks a forest floor.  Instead,\nthe ground is carpeted with the fragrant needles of the pines around you.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10925,-20,-27,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You are standing above the tree line on the northwest slope of a range\nof high mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the east and\nsouth.  To the west-northwest, the hillside slopes downward toward the\nvalley floor.  There is very little plant life at this altitude, mainly\njust some moss and lichen.  This lack of plantlife makes the pile of\nbrush to the southeast oddly out of place.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10926,-21,-23,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You stand above the tree line on the southwestern slope of a range of\ntall mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the north and east.\nThe mountain side descends to the west-southwest toward the center of the\nvalley.  Plant life is minimal at this altitude, consisting mainly of moss\nand lichen.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10927,-21,-24,2,'A Pine Forest','   You stand in the middle of a forest of evergreens, mostly pine, but\nincluding some aspen and birch.  The ground slopes upward to the north\nand east, and downward toward the valley floor to the south and west.\nVisibility is surprisingly good between the trunks of the trees, due to\nthe absence of the clutter that normally marks a forest floor.  Instead,\nthe ground is carpeted with the fragrant needles of the pines around you.\nDownhill to the southwest, you can see a lake through the trees.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10928,-21,-25,2,'On a Crushed Stone Road','   You stand in the middle of a road of crushed stone at the eastern end of\na mountain valley.  The temperature here on the floor of the valley is\nsurprisingly warm, the high peaks shielding you from the worst of the\nweather.  To either side of the road lies a lush alpine meadow.  Pine\nforests, which lie immediately to your north and east, ring the valley.  A\nmountain <B>lake<1> lies immediately to your west.  The road climbs upwards toward\nthe pass to the east and curves northwest to follow the shore of the lake.\n',63,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10929,-21,-26,2,'An Alpine Valley','   You are standing in a field of tall grass at the eastern end of a\nmountain valley.  Tall, snow-covered mountains ring the valley on all sides.\nA band of pine forests cover the hillsides, but most of the valley floor\nis an open meadow.  There is an east-west road immediately north of you, and\na <B>lake<1> to the northwest.\n',63,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10930,-21,-27,2,'A Pine Forest','   You stand in the middle of a forest of evergreens, mostly pine, but\nincluding some aspen and birch.  The ground slopes upward to the south\nand east, and downward toward the valley floor to the north and west.\nVisibility is surprisingly good between the trunks of the trees, due to\nthe absence of the clutter that normally marks a forest floor.  Instead,\nthe ground is carpeted with the fragrant needles of the pines around you.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10931,-21,-28,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You are standing above the tree line on the northwest slope of a range\nof high mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the east and\nsouth.  To the west-northwest, the hillside slopes downward toward the\nvalley floor.  There is very little plant life at this altitude, mainly\njust some moss and lichen.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10932,-22,-22,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You stand above the tree line on the southwestern slope of a range of\ntall mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the north and east.\nThe mountain side descends to the west-southwest toward the center of the\nvalley.  Plant life is minimal at this altitude, consisting mainly of moss\nand lichen.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10933,-22,-23,2,'A Pine Forest','   You stand in the middle of a forest of evergreens, mostly pine, but\nincluding some aspen and birch.  The ground slopes upward to the north\nand east, and downward toward the valley floor to the south and west.\nVisibility is surprisingly good between the trunks of the trees, due to\nthe absence of the clutter that normally marks a forest floor.  Instead,\nthe ground is carpeted with the fragrant needles of the pines around you.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10934,-22,-24,2,'On a Crushed Stone Road','   You stand in the middle of a road of crushed stone at the northeastern\nend of a mountain valley.  The temperature here on the floor of the valley is\nsurprisingly warm, the high peaks shielding you from the worst of the weather.\nThe road runs through a lush alpine meadow, following the shore of a mountain\n<B>lake<1> immediately to the south.  Pine forests, which lie immediately to your\nnorth and east, ring the valley.  The road continues along the shore of the\nlake to the west and southeast.\n',63,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10935,0,0,0,'A Mountain Lake','   This small lake is filled with the deepest, bluest, cleanest, clearest\nwater you think you have ever seen.  Looking into its depths, you can see\nno hint of its bottom.  Dark shadows deep in the depths are probably fish,\nbut light doesn\'t penetrate deep enough to be sure.  Sticking your finger\ninto the water, you discover it is also ice cold, fed by the melting snows\non the mountains surrounding this valley.  You don\'t think it would be\npleasant to stay in this water for long.\n',0,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10936,-22,-26,2,'An Alpine Meadow','   You are standing in a field of tall grass at the eastern end of a\nmountain valley.  Tall, snow-covered mountains ring the valley on all sides.\nA band of pine forests cover the hillsides, but most of the valley floor\nis an open meadow.  There is a lake to your north and west.\n',63,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10937,-22,-27,2,'An Alpine Meadow','   You are standing in a field of tall grass at the southeastern end of a\nmountain valley.  Tall, snow-covered mountains ring the valley on all sides.\nA band of pine forests cover the hillsides, but most of the valley floor\nis an open meadow.  There is a lake to your northwest.\n',63,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10938,-22,-28,2,'A Pine Forest','   You stand in the middle of a forest of evergreens, mostly pine, but\nincluding some aspen and birch.  The ground slopes upward to the south\nand east, and downward toward the valley floor to the north and west.\nVisibility is surprisingly good between the trunks of the trees, due to\nthe absence of the clutter that normally marks a forest floor.  Instead,\nthe ground is carpeted with the fragrant needles of the pines around you.\nA gamepath climbs the hillside from the northwest to the south.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10939,-22,-29,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You are standing above the tree line on the northwest slope of a range\nof high mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the east and\nsouth.  To the west-northwest, the hillside slopes downward toward the\nvalley floor.  There is very little plant life at this altitude, mainly\njust some moss and lichen.  A small game trail traverses the slope from\nthe north to the southeast.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10940,-23,-22,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You stand above the tree line on the southern slope of a range of\ntall mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the north.  The\nmountain side descends south toward the center of the valley.  Plant life\nis minimal at this altitude, consisting mainly of moss and lichen.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
