(10956,-25,-22,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You stand above the tree line on the southern slope of a range of\ntall mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the north.  The\nmountain side descends south toward the center of the valley.  Plant life\nis minimal at this altitude, consisting mainly of moss and lichen.  You can\nhear the sound of running water from the west.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10957,-25,-23,2,'A Pine Forest','   You stand in the middle of a forest of evergreens, mostly pine, but\nincluding some aspen and birch.  The ground slopes upward to the north, and\ndownward toward the valley floor to the south.  Visibility is surprisingly\ngood between the trunks of the trees, due to the absence of the clutter that\nnormally marks a forest floor.  Instead, the ground is carpeted with the\nfragrant needles of the pines around you.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10958,-25,-24,2,'On a Crushed Stone Road','   You stand in the middle of a road of crushed stone on the northern side\nof a mountain valley.  The temperature here on the floor of the valley is\nsurprisingly warm, the high peaks shielding you from the worst of the weather.\nThe road runs through a lush alpine meadow.  A lake lies to the southeast, and\nthere is a small knoll directly south.  Pine forests, which lie immediately\nto your north, ring the valley.  The road continues along the shore of the\nlake to the east and  curves toward a bridge to the southwest.  A thicket of\nbushes lies to the west.\n',63,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10959,-25,-25,2,'Campsite','   This small knoll just off the road along the shore of the lake appears to\nhave been used quite regularly as a campsite.  Several blackened rings of\nstones show where fires were built recently, and the grass is flattened from\ntents and bedrolls.  The lake is immediately to the south and east, with the\nroad running past to the north and the west.  Passage to the southwest is\nprevented by the steep banks of a swift mountain stream.\n',63,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10960,0,0,0,'A Mountain Lake','   This small lake is filled with the deepest, bluest, cleanest, clearest\nwater you think you have ever seen.  Looking into its depths, you can see\nno hint of its bottom.  Dark shadows deep in the depths are probably fish,\nbut light doesn\'t penetrate deep enough to be sure.  Sticking your finger\ninto the water, you discover it is also ice cold, fed by the melting snows\non the mountains surrounding this valley.  You don\'t think it would be\npleasant to stay in this water for long.\n',0,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10961,-25,-27,2,'An Alpine Meadow','   You are standing in an alpine meadow on the southern side of the valley\nfloor.  A mountain lake surrounds you to the north and east.  A pine forest\nlies to your south and the meadow continues to the west.\n',63,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10962,-25,-28,2,'A Pine Forest','   You stand in the middle of a forest of evergreens, mostly pine, but\nincluding some aspen and birch.  The ground slopes upward to the south and\ndownward toward the valley floor to the north.  Visibility is surprisingly\ngood between the trunks of the trees, due to the absence of the clutter that\nnormally marks a forest floor.  Instead, the ground is carpeted with the\nfragrant needles of the pines around you.  You can just make out a lake\nthrough the trees to the northeast.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10963,-25,-29,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You are standing above the tree line on the northern slope of a range of\nhigh mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the south.  To the\nnorth, the hillside slopes downward toward the valley floor.  There is very\nlittle plant life at this altitude, mainly just some moss and lichen.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10964,-26,-22,2,'A Mountain Stream Above the Tree Line','   You stand above the tree line on the southern slope of a range of\ntall mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the north.  The\nmountain side descends south toward the center of the valley.  Plant life\nis minimal at this altitude, consisting mainly of moss and lichen.  A small\nmountain stream, feed by the melting snows on the peaks to the north, flows\ndownhill to the southwest.\n',63,131072,29,0,0,0,0,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10965,-26,-23,2,'A Pine Forest','   You stand in the middle of a forest of evergreens, mostly pine, but\nincluding some aspen and birch.  The ground slopes upward to the north, and\ndownward toward the valley floor to the south.  Visibility is surprisingly\ngood between the trunks of the trees, due to the absence of the clutter that\nnormally marks a forest floor.  Instead, the ground is carpeted with the\nfragrant needles of the pines around you.  You hear the sound of running\nwater to the west.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10966,-26,-24,2,'Berry Thicket','   Thickets of wild berry bushes dot the meadow floor all around you.  Wildlife\nabounds in this area, using the thorny bushes for both food and shelter.  You\ncan hear running water to the west, and there is a bridge to the south.  The\nsteep banks of a mountain stream prevent passage to the southwest.\n',63,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10967,-26,-25,3,'A Stone Bridge','  You stand in the middle of a bridge constructed of large blocks of stone.\nThe bridge is about 20 feet wide and 120 feet long, spanning the gorge of\na mountain stream.  A crushed stone road stretches to the northeast and\nsouthwest.  There are thickets of bushes to the north and west, and to the\nsoutheast, you can see a mountain lake.\n',63,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10968,-26,-26,2,'An Alpine Meadow','   You are standing in an alpine meadow on the floor of a mountain valley.\nA mountain lake stretches out to your east and the meadow continues to the\nsouth.  A road runs through the meadow to your north and west, and you see\na thicket of bushes across the road to the northwest.  The steep banks of\na mountain stream prevent passage to the northeast.\n',63,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10969,-26,-27,2,'An Alpine Meadow','   You are standing in an alpine meadow on the floor of the mountain valley.\nThe meadow continues to the north, east and west.  A pine forest lies to\nyour south and a mountain lake lies to the northeast.  A road passes the\nmeadow on the northwestern side.\n',63,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10970,-26,-28,2,'A Pine Forest','   You stand in the middle of a forest of evergreens, mostly pine, but\nincluding some aspen and birch.  The ground slopes upward to the south and\ndownward toward the valley floor to the north.  Visibility is surprisingly\ngood between the trunks of the trees, due to the absence of the clutter that\nnormally marks a forest floor.  Instead, the ground is carpeted with the\nfragrant needles of the pines around you.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10971,-26,-29,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You are standing above the tree line on the northern slope of a range of\nhigh mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the south.  To the\nnorth, the hillside slopes downward toward the valley floor.  There is very\nlittle plant life at this altitude, mainly just some moss and lichen.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10972,-27,-22,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You stand above the tree line on the southern slope of a range of\ntall mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the north.  The\nmountain side descends south toward the center of the valley.  Plant life\nis minimal at this altitude, consisting mainly of moss and lichen.  You can\nhear the sound of running water from the south and east.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10973,-27,-23,2,'A Stream through a Pine Forest','  You stand in the shallows of a swift moving mountain stream which runs\nthrough the forest here.  The stream enters from uphill to your northeast and\nexits downhill to the south.  The stream is only about 3 feet deep, so it is\neasily waded, but the water is really cold.\n',63,131072,29,0,0,0,45,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10974,-27,-24,2,'A Mountain Stream','  This stream gets faster and deeper the further down the hillside you go.\nAt this point, the banks are still shallow enough that you can climb out if\nyou have to, but you don\'t think that will be the case for long.  Pine forest\nsurrounds you to the north and west, and there are berry thickets to the south\nand east.  The stream flow downhill from the north toward a bridge to the\nsoutheast.\n',63,131072,29,0,0,0,30,8,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10975,-27,-25,2,'Berry Thicket','   Thickets of wild berry bushes dot the meadow floor all around you.  Wildlife\nabounds in this area, using the thorny bushes for both food and shelter.  You\ncan hear running water to the north, and there is a bridge to the east.  The\nsteep banks of a stream prevent passage to the northeast.\n',63,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10976,-27,-26,2,'On a Crushed Stone Road','   You stand in the middle of a road of crushed stone on the western end\nof a mountain valley.  The temperature here on the floor of the valley is\nsurprisingly warm, the high peaks shielding you from the worst of the weather.\nThe road runs through a lush alpine meadow, leading from a bridge to the\nnortheast toward a canyon to the west.  Pine forests, which lie immediately to\nyour southwest, ring the valley.  A thicket of bushes lies to the north.\n',63,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10977,-27,-27,2,'An Alpine Meadow','   You are standing in an alpine meadow in the southwestern corner of the\nvalley.  A pine forest lies to your south and west, and the meadow continues\nto the east.  A road runs past on the northern side of the meadow.\n',63,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10978,-27,-28,2,'A Pine Forest','   You stand in the middle of a forest of evergreens, mostly pine, but\nincluding some aspen and birch.  The ground slopes upward to the south\nand west, and downward toward the valley floor to the north and east.\nVisibility is surprisingly good between the trunks of the trees, due to\nthe absence of the clutter that normally marks a forest floor.  Instead,\nthe ground is carpeted with the fragrant needles of the pines around you.\nOne large clump of brush does catch your eye though to the southwest\nnear a mound of rock and dirt.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10979,-27,-29,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You are standing above the tree line on the northern slope of a range of\nhigh mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the south and west.\nTo the north, the hillside slopes downward toward the valley floor.  There is\nvery little plant life at this altitude, mainly just some moss and lichen.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10980,-28,-23,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You stand above the tree line on the southeastern slope of a range of\ntall mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the north and west.\nThe mountain side descends to the east-southeast toward the center of the\nvalley.  Plant life is minimal at this altitude, consisting mainly of moss\nand lichen.  You can hear running water to the east.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10981,-28,-24,2,'A Pine Forest','   You stand in the middle of a forest of evergreens, mostly pine, but\nincluding some aspen and birch.  The ground slopes upward to the north\nand west, and downward toward the valley floor to the south and east.\nVisibility is surprisingly good between the trunks of the trees, due to\nthe absence of the clutter that normally marks a forest floor.  Instead,\nthe ground is carpeted with the fragrant needles of the pines around you.\nYou can hear the sound of running water to the east.  To the northwest,\nyou can see a small cabin nestled between two tall mountains.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10982,-28,-25,2,'An Alpine Meadow','   You stand in the middle of a field of tall grass at the western end of a\nmountain valley.  There are pine trees to the north and a thicket of bushes to\nthe east.  A road winds through the valley to your south and west.  You can\nhear the sound of running water from the northeast.  To the west, the walls\nof the valley begin to rise steeply, forming a canyon.\n',63,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10983,-28,-26,2,'On a Crushed Stone Road','   You stand in the middle of a road of crushed stone on the western end\nof a mountain valley.  The temperature here on the floor of the valley is\nsurprisingly warm, the high peaks shielding you from the worst of the\nweather.  To the west, the sides of the valley rise steeply, forming the\nwalls of a canyon.  A pine forest lies to the south, and to the east is the\nvalley floor.  The road continues to the east and northwest.\n',63,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10984,-28,-27,2,'A Pine Forest','   You stand in the middle of a forest of evergreens, mostly pine, but\nincluding some aspen and birch.  The ground slopes upward to the south\nand west, and downward toward the valley floor to the north and east.\nVisibility is surprisingly good between the trunks of the trees, due to\nthe absence of the clutter that normally marks a forest floor.  Instead,\nthe ground is carpeted with the fragrant needles of the pines around you.\n',63,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10985,-28,-28,2,'Above the Tree Line','  You stand above the tree line on the northeastern slope of a range of\ntall mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the south and west.\nThe mountain side descends to the east-northeast toward the center of the\nvalley.  Plant life is minimal at this altitude, consisting mainly of moss\nand lichen.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10986,-29,-24,2,'Above the Tree Line','   You stand above the tree line on the southeastern slope of a range of\ntall mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the north and west.\nThe mountain side descends to the east-southeast toward the center of the\nvalley.  Plant life is minimal at this altitude, consisting mainly of moss\nand lichen.  The ground slopes downward into a canyon to the south.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10987,-29,-25,2,'On a Crushed Stone Road','   You stand in the middle of a road of crushed stone on the western end\nof a mountain valley.  The temperature here on the floor of the valley is\nsurprisingly warm, the high peaks shielding you from the worst of the\nweather.  The walls of the valley begin to rise steeply around you, forming\na canyon.  The canyon continues to the south and west and opens into the\nvalley floor to the east.  The road continues west and southeast.\n',63,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10988,-29,-26,2,'Front of the Canyon','   You are standing at the front of a canyon at the western end of a\nmountain valley.  The canyon wall, which lies to your south, is still\npassable at this point, but rises more steeply further to the west.  The\ncanyon continues to your north and west.  To the east is the valley floor.\nYou can see a road running north and east of you.\n',63,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10989,-29,-27,2,'Above the Tree Line','  You stand above the tree line on the northeastern slope of a range of\ntall mountains.  Unclimbable, snow-covered peaks loom to the south and west.\nThe mountain side descends to the east-northeast toward the center of the\nvalley.  Plant life is minimal at this altitude, consisting mainly of moss\nand lichen.  A hillside descends into a canyon to the north.\n',63,131072,25,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10990,-30,-25,2,'Before the Cliffs','   You are standing on a road of crushed stone at the back of a canyon.\nHigh granite cliffs loom to the north and west.  The canyon continues to\nthe south and east.  The road continues to the east, and to the west, you\nsee the entrance to a tunnel into the mountain.\n',63,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10991,-30,-26,2,'Back of a Canyon','   You are standing at the back of a canyon.  High granite cliffs prevent\nfurther progress to the south and west.  The canyon continues to the north and\neast.  You can see a road north of you.\n',63,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10992,-31,-25,2,'Tunnel Entrance','   You are standing in the entrance of a tunnel into the side of the\nmountain.  A lot of effort was expended carving this tunnel out of solid\nrock.  The tunnel is framed every ten feet with thick wooden braces, to\nprevent cave-ins.  The tunnel continues to the west, and a road runs east\ninto a canyon.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(10993,-24,-25,1,'Bottom of the Lake','   You are at the bottom of this mountain lake.  The water is very clear\nand you can clearly see the muddy bottom around you, as well as the\nsurface above.  A variety of underwater plant life grows here, providing\nfood and shelter for the fish.  The water is very cold.\n',63,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10994,-23,-25,1,'Bottom of the Lake','   You are at the bottom of this mountain lake.  The water is very clear\nand you can clearly see the muddy bottom around you, as well as the\nsurface above.  A variety of underwater plant life grows here, providing\nfood and shelter for the fish.  The water is very cold.\n',63,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10995,-23,-26,1,'Bottom of the Lake','   You are at the bottom of this mountain lake.  The water is very clear\nand you can clearly see the muddy bottom around you, as well as the\nsurface above.  A variety of underwater plant life grows here, providing\nfood and shelter for the fish.  The water is very cold.\n',63,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10996,-24,-26,1,'Bottom of the Lake','   You are at the bottom of this mountain lake.  The water is very clear\nand you can clearly see the muddy bottom around you, as well as the\nsurface above.  A variety of underwater plant life grows here, providing\nfood and shelter for the fish.  The water is very cold.  There is a\nlarge pile of sticks lying against the bank to the southeast.\n',63,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(10997,-23,-27,1,'A Muddy Tunnel','   You find yourself in a narrow underwater tunnel dug into the mud of\nthe side of the lake.  A pile of sticks blocks the tunnel to the northwest\nand the tunnel continues to the east.  This tunnel appears to have been\ndug by some kind of animal.\n',63,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,3,40,0,'',NULL),
(10998,-22,-27,1,'A Bend in a Muddy Tunnel','   You are at a bend in an underwater tunnel dug through the mud.  The\ntunnel continues to the west, and to the north it curves upward into an\nair pocket.  This tunnel is very narrow and appears to have been dug by\nan animal.\n',63,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,3,40,0,'',NULL),
(10999,-22,-26,1,'A Muddy Cave','   You are in a roughly hemispherical cave dug in the mud.  Some light\nenters the room through small cracks in the ceiling.  The floor of the\ncave is covered with sticks and leaves.  A few shells and the bones of\nsome fish lie scattered about.\n',63,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(11000,0,0,0,'A Path of Gold','You are on a path of peculiar cobblestones -- this pavement appears to be\ncovered with gold flecks.  After the initial shock of this exorbitant and\nlavish pavement, you peer around and take stock of your surroundings.  You\ncatch your breath when you realize that this road and everything nearby is\nfloating miles up in the sky.  The glittering path continues to the west\nwhere you can see a city in the distance.  A wooded area lies nearby to the\nnorthwest and some verdant glades are off to the southwest.\n',67,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11001,0,0,0,'A Path of Gold','You are on a path of glittering gold cobblestones.  After the initial\namazement regarding how the roads in this mystical land are paved, you\nscan your surroundings and catch your breath in amazement.  It appears that\nthe ground you tread and everything surrounding it is floating on a thick\nwhite cloud miles up in the sky.  The glittering path continues to the west\nwhere you can see a walled city looming in the distance.  A wooded area lies\nnearby to the northwest and some verdant grassland is off to the southwest.\n',67,139264,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11002,0,0,0,'A Path of Gold','You are on a well-worn path of glittering gold cobblestones which winds its\nway to the southwest and continues to the east as well.  A dense mist seems\nto emanate from the woods west of here.  Just above the treetops you catch\nglimpses of a crystalline castle floating above a walled city.\n',67,139264,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11003,0,0,0,'A Path of Gold','You are on a well-worn path of glittering gold-flecked cobblestones which\nwinds its way to the northeast and ends somewhere to the west at the gates\nof a walled city.  A grassy hillock and what, at this distance, looks like\na decrepit old shed are nearby to the southwest.  A sickeningly sweet aroma\nwafts towards you from a dim and mist-filled stand of trees to the north.\nThe woodlands grows especially dense on the north side of the path here,\neffectively blocking any travel in that direction.\n',67,139264,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11004,0,0,0,'Outside a Huge Crystalline Gate','The glittering path of gold-flecked cobblestones ends here at the feet of\na monstrous crystalline gate.  The walls of this city rise high into the\nsky to either side of the gate and two minarets as well as a floating\ncrystalline castle can be seen above the walls from here.  A grassy hillock\nrises gently from the earth south of you and a verdant glade can be seen to\nthe southwest.  Clearings before the city walls are both north and west of\nyou and the glittering path winds off to the east.\n',67,139264,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11005,0,0,0,'A Grassy Hillock','Atop this grassy knoll your perspective of your surroundings is slightly\ndifferent from what you would be able to drink in visually down in the glade\nto the southwest or west.  The walls of the city to the northwest are in full\nview.  Straining your eyes, you can almost make out some details about the\ntwin minarets lancing towards the sky as well as the crystalline castle that\nhovers over the city.  On a different, more plain note, you spot a small\nshack nearby to the south.\n',67,139264,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11006,0,0,0,'A Verdant Glade','Green grass and small plants surround you on all sides as you take a look\nabout this glade teeming with life.  You catch your breath as you notice a\nhole in the earth a few feet ahead of where you are now.  As you head over\nto inspect it you realize that the hole seems to pass completely through\nthis gigantic floating piece of earth.  Peering down through the hole you can\nmake out a gleaming dome of metal extremely far off below you.  A clearing\njust outside the city wall is north of you and a grassy hillock gently rises\nout of the earth to the east.\n',67,139264,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11007,0,0,0,'A Clearing Outside the Walls','This clearing lies in the shadow of the towering city walls northwest of\nyou.  Taking a moment to survey your current environs, you notice a variety\nof abnormally large flowers growing here amidst the waist-high grass.  A\nnauseatingly sweet aroma fills the air here and a light buzzing can be heard\ndroning somewhere nearby.  A verdant glade lies to the south and a titanic\ncrystalline gate in the city wall can be seen nearby to the north.\n',67,139264,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11008,0,0,0,'A Clearing Outside the Walls','This clearing lies in the shadow of the towering city walls northwest of\nyou.  Taking stock of your situation, you notice a variety of abnormally\nlarge flowers growing here amidst the waist-high grass.  A sickly sweet aroma\nfills the air here and a light buzzing can be heard droning somewhere\nnearby.  A roiling white mist seeps out from a dark, shadowy copse of trees\nto the east.  A titanic crystalline gate in the city wall can be seen south\nof here.\n',67,139264,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11009,0,0,0,'A Murky Forest','The trees here tower high above and you can barely make out the lofty forest\nceiling.  A thick, roiling mist swirls about the trees, licking and curling\nat your feet.  The murky woodland continues to the north and a clearing\nbefore a city wall can be seen through the trees to the west.  Through the\nhazy mist you catch glimpses of something glittering to the east.\n',67,139264,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11010,0,0,0,'A Murky Forest','The tree here tower high above you and it is a strain to try to make out the\nlofty forest ceiling above.  A thick, roiling white mist swirls about the\ntrees, licking and curling at your feet.  The murky woodland continues to the\neast and south while a barren plot of earth can be spotted to the north.\nDead leaves rustle underfoot as you stir restlessly in the bizarre environs.\nA sickeningly sweet aroma wafts in from a colossal tree to the northeast.\n',67,139264,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11011,0,0,0,'At the Foot of a Giant Heartwood Tree','Unlike the other trees nearby, this one stands alone here.  The mist that is\neverpresent in the murky woods to the south and southwest is also here,\nforming strange patterns as it swirls about the base of this truly mammoth\nheartwood tree.  The sickeningly sweet aroma here is strong, on the verge of\nbeing overpowering and it seems to be coming from higher up in the tree.\n',67,139264,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11012,0,0,0,'High Up in the Heartwood Tree','The surrounding landscape looks much different from your vantage point here\namong the branches higher up in the heartwood tree.  Dominating the view is\na glittering city to the west, complete with a crystalline castle floating\nmajestically above it.  Nearer to your position is a dark forest and a light\nmist can be seen seeping out from the woods\' edges.  A nauseatingly sweet\nsmell overpowers your senses and you catch yourself before you plummet to\nthe ground below.  The offensive odor seems to be coming from a large\nhoneycomb arrangement in the northeast branches of this magnificent tree.\n',67,139264,35,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11013,0,0,0,'Inside the Main Gate of Cimea','The pavement beneath your feet looks to be constructed of a multitude of\ntiny thumb-sized tiles patiently laid together in a tight formation.  Your\nheart skips a beat for a brief moment as the pavement disappears from under\nyou for a split second, and visible momentarily is the ground thousands of\nfeet below.  Before you can even blink, the tiles are back in place but\ncrackling with emerald-colored tendrils of power.  Shaken by this fearsome\nand fantastic terrain you currently tread upon, you quickly survey the exits\nfrom here and note that streets lead off to the northwest, northeast and\nsouthwest.  A caved-in building sits in ruins to the north.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11014,0,0,0,'Amadis Street','The ground beneath you is paved with countless little tiles laid together\nin a tight formation.  What sends a shiver down your spine is the fact that\nthe pavement disappears for a split second every now and then, revealing\nthe ground thousands of feet below.  This strange disappearing effect does\nnot seem to faze the locals at all, seeing as it does not even cause the\nfaintest of reactions on anyone\'s countenance.  A spacious-looking shop with\na complete set of knight\'s armor hanging over the doorway lies to the west.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11015,0,0,0,'Amadis Street','This street, paved with numerous colorful tiles disappears for a split\nsecond, only to reappear before you have time to even blink in surprise.\nThe locals of this bustling metropolis do not appear to be disturbed even\nthe slightest by the bizarre pavement, their blank inexpressive faces\ntestament to that.  A large shop with a set of crossed claymores hanging\nover the doors lies to the east.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11016,0,0,0,'Amadis Street','This bustling section of pavement seems to be the intersection of the\nimportant thoroughfares of this bustling metropolitan area.  Street peddlers\nattempt to hawk their wares and a steady din fills the air.  The paved tiles\nbeneath your feet are crackling intensely with an emerald-colored energy\nbut the ground does not fade or disappear, much to your relief.  Activity\nin this section of town seems to be busiest in front of a store to the south.\nAs the crowd parts for a moment, you catch a glimpse of the storefront\'s\nwindow and note a vast variety of different wares inside.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11017,0,0,0,'Faunus Street','This thoroughfare runs along the inside of the city wall which towers high\nabove you to the northeast.  This a wide, clean street that rises gently as\nit runs to the east.  The unmistakable aroma of grilled meat reaches your\nnose and the plume of smoke being spit out by a chimney mark the building\nto the south as the source of succulent meats.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11018,0,0,0,'Faunus Street','This thoroughfare runs along the inside of the city wall which rises high\nabove you to the northeast.  This is a wide, clean street that dips gently\ndownwards as it runs to the west.  Looking directly overhead, you can see\nthe bottom of a cloud which, by your estimation, is supporting the\ncrystalline castle you spotted from afar.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11019,0,0,0,'Faunus Street','This thoroughfare runs along the inside of the city wall that looms over you\nto the northeast.  This is a wide, clean street and a towering minaret to the\neast reaches up into the heavens.  A doorway at the base of the minaret seems\na perfect point of entry.  A huge, but crude-looking structure with a single\nlarge granite club hanging over the doorway is to the west.  The street\ncontinues on to both the southeast and northwest.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11020,0,0,0,'Faunus Street','This thoroughfare runs along the inside of the city wall which rises high\ninto the sky above you to the northeast.  This is a wide, clean street that\ndips gently downwards as it runs to the south.  A towering minaret stands\nbefore you to the north and a floating crystalline castle hovers in the air\neven further up in the atmosphere.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11021,0,0,0,'Faunus Street','This thoroughfare runs along the inside of the city wall which rises high\nabove you to the east.  This is a wide, clean street that rises gently as it\nruns to the north.  A squat but opulent looking building with three hammers\nin a triangle formation hanging over the front door is to the northwest.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11022,0,0,0,'Cortege Avenue','The street you are now on runs along the inside of the city wall which\ntowers high above you to the south.  The avenue is broad and relatively clean\nfor such a much-used thoroughfare in this floating metropolis.  A rather\nplain-looking residence is north of you and the avenue dips gently as it runs\nto the west.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11023,0,0,0,'Cortege Avenue','The street you are now on runs along the inside of the city wall which rises\nhigh above you to the southwest.  This avenues is broad and relatively clean\nfor such an oft-traveled thoroughfare, and rises gently as it runs to the\neast.  Looking overhead to the north, you can spot the bottom of a cloud\nwhich, by your estimation, is supporting the crystalline castle you spotted\nfrom afar.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11024,0,0,0,'Cortege Avenue','The street you are now on runs along the inside of the city wall that looms\nover you to the southwest.  The avenue is broad and relatively clean for such\nan oft-traveled street in this floating metropolitan jungle.  A towering\nminaret to the west reaches up towards the heavens and a doorway at the base\nseems a perfect point of entry if you so desired to take a peek at the\nland beyond the walls.  A rather plain-looking residence is directly opposite\nfrom the minaret.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11025,0,0,0,'Cortege Avenue','The street you are now on runs along the inside of the city wall which looms\nhigh above your head to the southwest.  It is wide and relatively clean for\nsuch a well-traveled pathway in this bustling floating metropolis.  A\ntowering minaret stands before you to the south and a floating crystalline\ncastle hovers in the air high above you.  The avenue rises gently as it runs\nto the north.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11026,0,0,0,'Cortege Avenue','The street you are now on runs along the inside of the city wall which looms\nhigh above your head to the west.  It is wide and relatively clean for such\na well-traveled avenue in this bustling metropolis.  An elegant wooden\nstructure to the southwest causes you to pause and spend a moment to drink\nin the precise, natural lines of the architecture.  It almost seems as if the\nentire building was shaped out of a small copse of interlocking trees.  The\navenue dips gently downwards as it runs to the south.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11027,0,0,0,'Zank\'s Chophouse','This place is reputed to serve the best assortment of meat in the known\nworld, but from the looks of this place, that claim is a tad hard to\nbelieve.  The room is filled with an oily smoke that fills your lungs with\na burning sensation and your eyes begin to tear uncontrollably.  From what\nyou can make out of this place through the smoke, it looks like there are\nabsolutely no seats or tables in this funky joint.  A door in the north\nwall provides an escape route from this smoke-filled chophouse.\n',67,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11028,0,0,0,'The Ogre Embassy','At first glance this building appears nothing more than a low-rent hovel,\nand compared to some of its neighboring buildings it is just that.  However,\nwhat sets this place apart from most of the locations in this cloud city\nis the fact that it is the official embassy for the ogre delegation of The\nWorld.  The floor is littered with an assortment of rusted pieces of armor\nand weapons.  A large wooden desk and chair in one corner of the room seem\nto be the only intact furnishings in here.  Shattered chairs and tables lie\nstrewn all about the floor in a haphazard fashion.  Perhaps there was some\nsort of scuffle here, but odds are all the wanton destruction was merely the\nside effect of drunken ogres not using what few brain cells they have.  Well,\nat least they will have an abundant supply of firewood if it ever gets cold.\nA large wooden door in the east wall of the embassy leads back out to the\nstreet.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11029,0,0,0,'Boodle\'s Curio Shop','As you take in all the wondrous objects sitting on the shelves that line\neach of this shop\'s four walls, you cannot help but wonder how any one store\ncould assemble such a varied collection of paraphernalia.  A door set in the\nnorth wall affords passage out of this compulsive shopper\'s nightmare.\n',67,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11030,0,0,0,'Siva\'s Assemblage of Arms','You have entered a large shop which contains an assortment of finely crafted\nand maintained weapons of every make and model imaginable.  Looking about the\nstore you note a few exotic weapons that you fail to recognize, piquing your\ncuriosity.  Behind the counter is a back room from which you hear the\nrepetitive strikes of a hammer and anvil, no doubt forging a new weapon of\ndestruction to be sold to a potential buyer like yourself.\n',67,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11031,0,0,0,'The Dwarven Embassy','At first glance the interior of this building appears more like the forge of\na blacksmith than what is supposed to be the official embassy of The World\'s\ndwarven population.  Set in the north wall, a blazingly hot fire burns and\nspits out flaming embers onto the floor nearby.  The temperature in here is\nswelteringly hot and rivulets of sweat stream down your body.  Various pieces\nof armor and articles of war are piled up in one corner of the room.  The\nonly features of the room that would hint that this is indeed the official\nhome of the dwarven delegation is a low marble table and a intricately\ncarved marble plaque deeming it so.  A sturdy marble door in the southeast\nwall provides passage back out onto the street.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11032,0,0,0,'The Elven Embassy','You look about you in awe because it seems that whoever shaped this wooden\nstructure had an unbelievable rapport with nature and the myriad of trees\nthat intertwined themselves in order to create a watertight shelter here.\nEvery single piece of furniture in this chambers appears to be a living\nplant or tree of some sort.  Glowing orchids hang from the ceiling of tree\nbranches above and help illuminate the arranged assortment of shaped plant-\nfurniture.  A heady woodsy aroma fills the air and washes over you, bringing\nabout a sense of peace and tranquility to your soul.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11033,0,0,0,'Alexander\'s Armour Shop','You stand within the roomy confines of a shop that contains just about\nevery variation of protective gear in existence.  Armor and shields hang from\nthe walls in convenient groupings of type, style and size.  The smell of\noiled metal is strong here, reminding you of the smell of a battlefield.\nBehind the counter is a back room from which the sound of a hammer and\nanvil can be heard, no doubt pounding out the dents in a newly acquired\ncuirass or some such.\n',67,174269,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11034,0,0,0,'A Ruined Building','You are now within the confines, if indeed this roofless structure could be\ncalled that, of a crumbling building of some antiquity.  The architecture\nappears out of place with the styles on display throughout the rest of this\nfloating metropolis.  The premises are barren of any furnishings, testament\nto the effects of time and the avarice of self-serving looters.  A single,\nempty window gazes out at the street outside.  An empty doorway as well as\nnumerous holes in the south wall leads out to the walkway beyond.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11035,0,0,0,'A Homely Domicile','In stark contrast from what you have seen of the rest of the city, this\nresidence seems downright homely and unpretentious in its simplicity.  Absent\nare the extravagant statues of gold, emerald goblets and ornately carved\nmarble basins.  In their stead are tin cups, worn cotton bedding and a straw-\nfilled mattress.  It suddenly strikes you that, in a way, this crib shows\nmore taste and refinement than the pleasure palaces and mansions that seem\nquite plentiful in other areas of the city.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11036,0,0,0,'A Homely Domicile','In stark contrast from what you have seen of the rest of the city, this\nhouse seems downright homely and unpretentious in its simplicity.  Absent\nare statues of platinum, diamond utensils and silk-covered furniture.  In\ntheir stead are tin pots, simple fur rugs and plain wooden furnishings.\nSomehow, this non-extravagance somehow seems to show more taste and\nrefinement.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11037,0,0,0,'Amadis Street','This thoroughfare, paved with a multitude of colorful tiles disappears for\na split second, only to reappear underneath your feet before you have time to\neven blink in surprise.  The local denizens of this cloud city appear to be\nunfazed by the pavement\'s strange behavior and continue about their daily\nbusiness as usual.  Rowdy voices spill out from a tavern to the east while a\nstrange star-shaped structure remains silent to the south.  A long, narrow\nbuilding is to the southwest and a guard post to the northeast provides a\nperfect vantage point for the guardians watching those who use the crystal\nstaircase to the northwest.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11038,0,0,0,'At the Foot of a Crystalline Staircase','Tilting your head back, you look up the length of the crystal staircase and\nsee that it disappears into a thick white cloud not to far above you.  The\nsteps are wide and the staircase spirals upwards.  A bustling city street,\ncomplete with throngs of people and a steady buzz of activity is to the\nsoutheast.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11039,0,0,0,'The Three-Legged Man Tavern','The atmosphere in this joint is one of merriment and drunken pleasure.  The\ndin of a multitude of voices is bordering on being unbearably loud but is\ntolerable for now.  Wooden tables and chairs all around you are filled with\ndrunken patrons knocking back ales by the barrelful.  A long, mahogany-wood\nbar sits by the north wall and an astounding variety of bottles line the\nwall behind it.  A sign in the northeast corner announces that the second\nlevel of this tavern serves as an inn and a wooden staircase in the same\ncorner leads upwards.  You notice a loud commotion along the eastern wall and\ncloser inspection reveals a row of eyeholes, most of which are already in\nuse by some of the alehouse\'s male patrons.\n',67,141801,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11040,0,0,0,'The Musidora Inn','You stand at the front desk of the Inn.  Scoping out the room, it appears to\nbe decorated in a way to give off the impression of being warm and secure.\nYou can see a long hallway of doors, apparently the rooms of the Inn, where\nmany a traveler has rested his or her tired bones.  A wooden staircase in\nthe northeastern corner of the room leads back down towards the tavern and\nrowdy voices can be heard downstairs chanting what sounds like \'Yeehaw\'.\nTruly befuddling.\n',67,172221,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11041,0,0,0,'The Stargazer Observatory','The lighting in this chamber is dim and you nearly trip over something on\nthe floor but catch yourself in time.  All along the wall are maps of the\nsurrounding landscape down below and some of realms even farther away, and\nin some cases extremely distant.  You wonder at this since every map, even\nthose of the distant realms, seem to be drawn from a perspective of being\nhigh up in the sky.  A crystalline ladder leads down through a hole in the\nfloor.\n',67,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11042,0,0,0,'Chamber of a Thousand Oriels','You stare all about in wonder at this vast chamber and the amazing number of\nwindows looking out from here.  It looks as if this chamber is low enough\nthat it in effect hangs below the cloud that supports the rest of the cloud\ncity.  Looking through some of the windows, you see enhanced images of the\nsurrounding countryside in fine detail.  What normally would be out of sight\nis now visible to you through the mystical windows covering every square\ninch of wall here in stark detail.  A crystalline ladder leads up through a\nhole in the floor.  A strobe effect of colors pours into the room from the\nnortheast and southeast.\n',-1,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11043,0,0,0,'The Northeast Spire','You are now inside the base of the city\'s northeastern spire.  The walls on\nall sides seem to be constructed out of giant, solid blocks of marble\nstacked and joined almost seamlessly.  You look closer and note a faint\nflickering of emerald-lightning traveling the length of the seams between\neach and every stone.  A marble staircase leads up and out to the top of the\nspire and a door resting in the western wall leads back out onto the street.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11044,0,0,0,'Atop the Northeast Spire','The view from atop this spire is breathtaking to say the least.  Your vantage\npoint here allows you to look over the city that lies sprawled out to the\nsouthwest.  Hovering on a cloud above the city and reflecting any and all\nlight near it in a rapturous and blinding display is a crystalline castle.\nSlightly to the southeast is a dark, gloomy forest and a verdant swathe of\ngrassland lies southwest of that.  Looking even further away from this\nmagnificent floating city you can see the rest of The World thousands of\nfeet below.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11045,0,0,0,'The Southwest Spire','You are now inside the base of the city\'s southwestern spire.  The walls\non all side seem to be constructed out of solid blocks of marble stacked and\njoined almost seamlessly.  You look closer and note a faint flickering of\nemerald-lightning traveling the length of the seams between each stone.\nA marble staircase leads up and out to the top of the spire and a door\nresting in the east wall leads back out onto the street.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11046,0,0,0,'Atop the Southwest Spire','The view from atop this spire is breathtaking to say the least.  Your vantage\npoint here allows you to look over the city that lies sprawled out to the\nnortheast.  Hovering on a cloud above the city, reflecting any and all light\nnear to it in a rapturous and blinding display is a crystalline castle.\nFar to the west is a dark, gloomy forest while a verdant swath of grassland\nlies somewhat closer to the southeast.  Looking even further in the distance,\nyou think you can make out a huge sprawling city to the west.  A stairway\nleads downwards into the spire.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11047,0,0,0,'A Murky Forest','The trees tower high above your head here and it strains your neck as well\nas your eyes when you try to gauge the distance to the lofty forest ceiling.\nA thick, roiling white mist swirls about the trees, licking and curling at\nyour feet.  The murky woodland continues west of you and a colossal tree\nstands alone in a clearing to the north.\n',67,139264,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11048,0,0,0,'A Barren Tract of Timberland','The land here is broken and barren, devoid of any hint of plantlife.  The\nground beneath you seems soft and somewhat moist.  You decide to examine it\nfurther and note that the moistness you noticed is in actuality a sticky\ncrimson liquid welling up from the soil.  It is then that you are aware of a\naroma in the air that you have grown accustomed to during your adventures\nabroad in The World -- the smell of blood.  A thick, white mist seeps out\nfrom around the trunks of some trees at the south end of this clearing.\n',67,139264,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11049,0,0,0,'A Verdant Glade','You are surrounded on all sides by green grass and abnormally large flowers.\nA gentle wind rustles through, causing the grass to undulate and sway in\na mesmerizing fashion.  You snap out of the stupor brought about by the\ninherent peacefulness and beauty of nature and scan the landscape nearby.\nThis grassy clearing continues on to the north and a grassy hillock rises\ngently out of the earth to the northeast.  A small, insignificant looking\nshack sits innocently at the eastern end of this glade.\n',67,139264,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11050,0,0,0,'A Small Shack','This small, pitiful hovel of a shack seems to be constructed mainly of\nsticks, grass and what appears to be sections of a beehive, all held\ntogether by generous slatherings of a dried crimson mud.  The floor of this\nhumble domicile is littered with small, inconsequential living effects and\nthe occasional piece of feces.  A flimsy door made of giant leaves interwoven\nrests in what serves as the west wall of this shack.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,108,0,'',NULL),
(11051,0,0,0,'Surrounded by a Hazy Mist','The only thing visible here is the crystal staircase you are now on.  A\nthick, soupy white mist surrounds you on all sides and reduces your field\nof vision to only a few feet in all directions.  The spiraling staircase\ndisappears into the clouds further above and below you.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11052,0,0,0,'A Luxuriant Antechamber','You are now surrounded by luxuriant decadence at its most extreme.  Priceless\nsilks hang from the crystalline walls, an obscene clash of garish colors.\nThe floor is carpeted by countless thick fur rugs and diamond-studded\nchandeliers hang from the ceiling.  A large golden gate rests firmly in the\nnorthwest wall of this antechamber and a set of gilded gold doors rest in\nthe wall opposite the gate.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(11053,0,0,0,'A Dim Corridor','You are now in a dim, narrow hallway that is barely illuminated by a soft,\ngentle light filtering in through the crystalline walls of this castle\nfloating up in the sky.  The floor is spotlessly clean and a luxuriant\nantechamber can be seen nearby to the west.  A door emblazoned with an\nemerald-green triangle rests in the north wall.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11054,0,0,0,'A Dim Corridor','You are now in a dim, narrow hallway that is barely illuminated by soft,\ngentle rays of light that filter in beams through the crystalline walls of\nthis floating citadel.  The floor is spotlessly clean and the hallway\ncontinues on to the east and west.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11055,0,0,0,'A Dim Corridor','You are now in a dim, narrow hallway that is barely illuminated by soft,\ngentle rays of light that filter in beams through the crystalline walls of\nthis floating citadel.  The floor is spotlessly clean and the hallway takes\na bend to the southeast.  A non-descript looking door rests in the southwest\nwall of the corridor.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11056,0,0,0,'A Dim Corridor','You are now in a dim, narrow hallway that is barely illuminated by soft,\ngentle rays of light that filter in beams throughout the crystalline walls\nof this floating castle.  The floor is spotlessly clean and the corridor\ncurves to the northwest.  A door emblazoned with a small, emerald-green\nsquare is set in the west wall of the corridor.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11057,0,0,0,'A Dim Corridor','You are now in a dim, narrow hallway that is barely illuminated by soft,\ngentle rays of light that filter in beams through the crystalline walls\nof this floating citadel.  The corridor ends here at the foot of a door\nto the south emblazoned with an emerald-green square about two-thirds of\nthe way up.  The dim corridor leads off to the north.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11058,0,0,0,'A Dim Corridor','You are now in a dim, narrow hallway that is barely illuminated by the\ngentle light that filters though the crystalline walls of this keep.  The\nfloor is spotlessly clean and a luxuriant antechamber can be seen nearby\nto the north.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(11059,0,0,0,'A Dim Corridor','You are now in a dim, narrow hallway that is barely illuminated by the\nsoft, gentle light that filters through the crystalline walls of this\nfloating citadel.  The floor is spotlessly clean and the hallway continues on\nto the north and south.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(11060,0,0,0,'A Dim Corridor','You are now in a dim, narrow hallway that is barely illuminated by the soft,\ngentle light that filters in through the crystalline walls of this floating\ncitadel.  The floor is spotlessly clean and the hallway takes a bend to the\nsoutheast.  A non-descript looking door rests in the northeast wall of the\ncorridor.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(11061,0,0,0,'A Dim Corridor','You are now in a dim, narrow hallway that is barely illuminated by a soft,\ngentle light that filters in through the crystalline walls of this floating\ncastle.  The corridor curves to the northwest and continues  on to the east.\nA door emblazoned with an emerald-green circle is set in the north wall of\nthe hall.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(11062,0,0,0,'A Dim Corridor','You are now in a dim, narrow hallway that is barely illuminated by a soft,\ngentle light that filters in through the crystalline walls of this floating\ncastle.  The corridor ends here at the foot of a door to the east emblazoned\nwith an emerald-green oval.  Another door bearing the same symbol, only\nsmaller, rests in the north wall.  The dim corridor leads off to the west.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(11063,0,0,0,'Sentry Post','This guard room is very spartan in appearance.  The crystalline walls of this\nroom are smooth and encompass a small area, giving this post an almost\nclaustrophobic sense.  An open doorway looks out into a luxuriant antechamber\nto the northeast.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11064,0,0,0,'Barracks of the Imperial Cadre','This long and low chamber stretches out to the north and appears to serve as\nthe living quarters for the cloud city\'s elite imperial guard.  The floor is\nspotless and there does not seem to be a single mote of dust on the ground or\nany of the bunks that line each wall.  Folded neatly on each bed is a silk\nblanket accompanied by a silk-covered pillow.  A large door set in the south\nwall of this barracks room leads back out to the hallway.  A crystalline\nladder leads up through a hole in the ceiling near the back of the room.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11065,0,0,0,'A Vast Throneroom','The scene here is a prime example of imperial decadence and the extravagant\nexcesses of those who wield power in this realm.  Lush silk-covered furniture\nis arranged along the walls and solid platinum tables rest in front of them.\nThe center of the floor is clear and provides space for any entertainment\nthe imperial court might choose to bring in to amuse their ruler.  The\nceiling of the throneroom lies high above your head and a raised golden dais\nto the southeast is the resting place of a gigantic diamond throne.  A set\nof gilded golden doors rests firmly in the northwest wall.\n',67,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11066,0,0,0,'A Vast Throneroom','The scene here is a prime example of imperial decadence and the extravagant\nexcesses of those who wield power in this realm.  Lush silk-covered furniture\nis arranged along the walls and solid platinum tables rest in front of each\ncluster of chairs.  The center of the floor is clear and provides ample room\nfor any entertainment the imperial court might choose to bring in to amuse\ntheir ruler.  The ceiling of the throneroom lies high above your head and\na mammoth diamond throne sits on a raised golden dais nearby to the south.\nA non-descript crystal door is visible from behind a silken tapestry in the\nnortheast wall.\n',67,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11067,0,0,0,'A Vast Throneroom','The scene here is a prime example of imperial decadence and the extravagant\nexcesses of those who wield power in this realm.  Lush silk-covered furniture\nis arranged along the walls and solid platinum tables rest in front of each\ncluster of chairs.  The center of the floor is clear and provides ample\nspace for any entertainment the imperial court might choose to bring in to\namuse their ruler.  The ceiling of the throneroom lies high above your head\nand a gigantic diamond throne sits high on a  raised golden dais nearby to\nthe east.  A non-descript crystal door is visible from behind a silken\ntapestry in the southwest wall.\n',67,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11068,0,0,0,'The Emperor\'s Dais','The section of the throne room you are now in is raised a few feet off the\nthe floor.  The dais is circular and sitting squarely in the center is a\nlarge diamond throne.  The floor here is golden, and judging from the\ncountless dents, depressions and footprints, the dais seems to be one solid\nblock of gold.  Your vantage point allows you to look out over the throneroom\nand you can see a set of gilded golden doors at the far northwestern wall of\nthe room.  A thick, intricately detailed tapestry hangs directly behind the\nthrone.\n',67,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11069,0,0,0,'Prince Coel\'s Bedroom','This room is spacious but the floor is dominated by an enormous bed lying\nin the middle of the floor.  You notice that the sheets of the bed seem to\nbe undulating gently.  Elegant tapestries hang from the crystalline walls,\na pleasant contrast to the various assorted weapons and shields arranged\nalongside them.  Heaped in one corner of the bedchamber is a pile of\nclothing.  A single door in the east wall here provides passage back out\nto the hallway.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11070,0,0,0,'The Imperial Vault','This chamber is small but oddly enough seems to hold a vast store of wealth\nand precious baubles.  The crystalline walls of this vault are darkened and\nan extremely thick crystalline safe door rests in the south wall.\n',67,172040,32,0,0,0,0,0,5,120,0,'',NULL),
(11071,0,0,0,'A Storage Room','You are in what appears to be a room reserved for holding such things as\nfood stores and the like for the castle\'s inhabitants.  The crystalline walls\nare slick with a rime-like moisture and the temperature in here is a bit\nfrigid.  A single crystal door set in the south wall provides passage out\nof this storeroom.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11072,0,0,0,'Princess Isis\' Boudoir','This chamber is spacious and has a decidedly feminine touch to it.  Soft\npastel colors abound, from the bedsheets covering a broad bed in one\ncorner of the room to the elegant tapestries hanging from the walls.  A\nbasin rests along the east wall and a full-length mirror stands next to\nit on the floor.  A single door set in the south wall provides passage out\nof the bedchamber back towards the corridor.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11073,0,0,0,'A Meditative Sanctum','This bedchamber is spacious and meticulously well-kept.  Not a single\nobject seems out of place and a sense of harmony permeates the room.\nA large bed sits up against the east wall and an open bay window to the\nsouth exits out onto a balcony overlooking the surrounding landscape.\nBeautiful tapestries hang from the walls and an especially large one\noccupies the entire north and east walls, creasing a bit in the corner.\nThe room is perfectly still and the only sound to reach your ears is the\ngently rustle of a curtain by the balcony flapping softly in the wind.\nA single large crystalline door rests firmly in the crystalline west\nwall.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(11074,0,0,0,'The Empress\' Balcony','The view here is breathtakingly magnificent.  Looking out across the sky,\nthe aerial metropolis brings to mind an image of a delicate lily floating\non the surface of a pond.  The pond in this case being the endless blue\nexpanse, and of course the city being the lily.  Some stout-looking vines\ngrowing on the side of the balcony might possibly allow you to climb\ndown from this perch.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11075,0,0,0,'A Tableau of Decadence','The stench of sweat permeating this room and almost causing you to\nblanch is the first thing about this bedchamber that registers with\nyour senses.  Holding your breath and taking a look at your surroundings,\nyou wonder how any person could possible find restful sleep in this\noddly furnished room.  Sitting squarely in the center of the floor is a\nhuge four-poster bed complete with manacles and an equally broad mirror\nhanging from the ceiling.  Next to the bed is some sort of wooden table\nwith handholds on one end.  You suspect that this device is used to flog\nsomeone.  Hanging from one corner of the room, right in front of a huge\ntapestry, are two chains hanging from the ceiling.  The chains are about\ntwo arms lengths apart and you suspect that their purpose is also for\nsome perverse sport.  An open bay window to the east exits out towards a\nbalcony overlooking the floating city below.  Crystalline doors in the\nnorth and west walls provide other passage from this chamber of sadistic\npleasures.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11076,0,0,0,'The Emperor\'s Balcony','The view here is breathtakingly magnificent.  Looking out across the sky,\nthe aerial metropolis floating upon a cloud brings to mind an image of a\ndelicate lily floating on the surface of a pond.  The pond in this case\nbeing the endless blue expanse, and of course the city being the lily.  Some\nstout-looking vines growing on the side of the balcony might possibly allow\nyou to climb down from this perch.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11077,0,0,0,'Desade\'s Stateroom','This room is dominated by a gigantic, circular crystalline table set\nfirmly in the center of the chamber.  A multitude of assorted maps and\nsheaves of parchment lie scattered all over the surface of the table and\nsome have even spilled over onto the floor.  This appears to be where\nimportant policy decisions for the city are made.  An intricately detailed\ntapestry hangs in the northwest corner of the room and a door is set in\nthe east wall.  A large, emerald-green curtain hangs along the north wall.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11078,0,0,0,'Guard Quarters','This long and low building appears to serve as the quarters for the cloud\ncity\'s guard force.  The floor is spotless and there does not seem to be a\nsingle mote of dust on the floor or on any of the bunks that line each wall.\nFolded neatly on each bed is a simple fur blanket as well as a goose-down\npillow.  A large door set in the northeast wall of the barracks leads back\nout to the street.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11079,0,0,0,'Sentry Post','This guard room is very spartan in appearance.  Rough hewn walls of granite\nencompass a small area, giving this post an almost claustrophobic sense.\nAn open doorway leads back out onto the street to the southwest.  Tacked\nhere and there on the wall are crude, poorly painted pictures.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,5,120,0,'',NULL),
(11080,0,0,0,'At the Top of a Crystalline Staircase','You are now atop a crystalline staircase that extends downwards into a bank\nof clouds below.  A large aquamarine gate is set firmly in the crystalline\ncastle wall southeast of you.  Scanning all around, a sense of awe washes\nover your body as you look out towards the northwest and west.  Visible even\nfrom this height is a city sprawled out in the distance and a thick, green\nforest north of it.\n',67,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11081,0,0,0,'In the Air Above the Throneroom','You are relatively high up in the air near the ceiling of the throne room.\nA golden chandelier hangs from the ceiling and the crystalline walls around\nyou reflect and refract its light in gentle beams.  Far below you, the\nimperial court looks much different.  From this perspective it resembles the\ninside of a lavish doll-house more than anything else.\n',67,139273,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11082,0,0,0,'In the Air Above the Throneroom','You are relatively high up in the air near the ceiling of the imperial\nthrone room.  A golden chandelier hangs from the ceiling and the crystalline\nwalls all around you reflect and refract its light in gentle beams.  From\nthis perspective, the imperial court far below you looks much different.\n',67,139273,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11083,0,0,0,'In the Air Above the Throneroom','You are relatively high up in the air near the ceiling of the imperial\nthrone room.  A golden chandelier hangs from the ceiling and the crystalline\nwalls all around you reflect and refract its light in gentle beams.  From\nthis perspective, the imperial court far below you looks much different.\n',67,139273,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11084,0,0,0,'In the Air Above the Dais','You are relatively high up in the air near the ceiling of the imperial\nthrone room.  A golden chandelier hangs from the ceiling and the crystalline\nwalls all around you reflect and refract its light in gentle beams.  From\nthis perspective, the imperial court below looks much different.  A shining,\ndiamond throne rests far below in the middle of a golden dais.  Crackling\nwith a green mystical energy, is some sort of barrier field in the wall\nto the southeast.\n',67,139273,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11085,0,0,0,'An Oft-Changing Tableau','This room is like no other you can think of having ever had the pleasure of\nexperiencing.  All about you different scenes flash in and out of existence,\neach one displaying a section of The World for a scant few seconds, only to\nbe replaced by another, and another.  This relentless slide show of sorts is\nhaving a disorienting effect on you and even the ground has been replaced by\na myriad of clashing images.  The only point of sanity remaining in this mad\njumble of colors and forms is a stable rectangular outline to the southwest.\n',67,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11086,0,0,0,'An Oft-Changing Tableau','This room is like no other you can think of having ever had the pleasure, or\ndispleasure, of experiencing.  All about you different scenes flash in and\nout of existence, each one displaying a section of The World for a scant few\nseconds, only to be replaced by another, and then another.  This relentless\nslide show from hell is having a disorienting effect on you, and even the\nground has been usurped by an endless parade of clashing images.  The only\nanchor of sanity remaining in this mad jumble of colors and forms is a stable\nrectangular outline to the northwest.\n',67,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11087,0,0,0,'The Hive','A deafening buzz assaults your sense of hearing and washes over you almost\nlike a palpable wave.  As you slowly grow accustomed to the overpowring din\nsurrounding you, you become uncomfortably aware of the now-familiar sickeningly\nsweet odor filling your nostrils.  Controlling the urge to retch you take\nstock of your surroundings and note that the smell appears to be originating\nfrom the honey free-flowing from every hole in the honeycomb matrix that\nserves as this hive\'s walls.  You begin to lose your footing in the pools of\nsweet nectar on what must be the floor but catch yourself in time.  A round\nhole in the southwest corner of the hive seems to be the only exit back out\ninto the branches of the heartwood tree.\n',67,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11088,0,0,0,'A Fiery Pentacle','Unnatural power crackles and snaps in the air of this mystical sanctum.\nAn aura of maleficence seems to resonate from every surface of this\nsupernatural chamber.  Lines of power and force zigzag across the surface\nof the floor, joining together in the shape of a pentagram.  You head\nthrobs from the crushing pressure you feel weighing down on you from the\nsheer amount of mystical energy in here.\n',67,139273,32,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(11089,0,0,0,'Hanging From a Balcony','What looked to be thick, sturdy vines during your initial descent now seem\nto merely be a few strands of ivy.  You wonder just how long the vines will\nbe able to support your weight.\n',67,139264,21,20,11090,1,0,0,0,-1,20,'',NULL),
(11090,0,0,0,'High Up in the Clouds','You cannot see much around you due to the thick, white mist that surrounds\nyou on all sides.  As the wind shifts, you catch a glimpse of what is above\nand below you.  Above, there appears to be a city floating on a sea of\nclouds, while below is a gleaming dome of metal lodged firmly in a\nmountainside.\n',67,139264,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11091,0,0,0,'Lower in the Sky','You are a few hundred feet up in the sky and have a clear view of the\nsurrounding countryside.  Directly below you appears to be some sort of\nmetallic dome lodged firmly into a mountainside while a little northwest\nof that a steady stream of thick, white mist seems to be coming out of\na dark hole in the ground.  Broken, barren earth stretches for quite a\ndistance to the northeast while  some open, grassy country lies somewhere\noff to the southeast.\n',67,139264,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11092,0,0,0,'Office of the Imperial Cadre','This office appears spartan in furnishings but makes up for it with the\nmess covering the floor.  Littered all about are crumpled wrappings,\npossibly from packaged items.  A large platinum desk sits in one corner\nof the room with a wooden chair.  A crystalline ladder disappears down into\na hole in the floor.\n',67,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(11100,0,-31,-1,'Top of a Dark Stair','This is the top of a dark stairway.  There is a constant flow of water\nrunning down the red metal stairs.  The walls are made of the same red\nmetal and have runes etched into them.  A ladder made of roots from a\nswamp tree leads up to the swamp.  Unfortunately a large pile of rubble\nhas collapsed sealing the stairs passage downward.\n',-1,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,3,150,0,'',NULL),
(11101,0,0,0,'On a Dark Stair','There is a constant flow of water running down the red metal stairs.  The\nwalls are made of the same red metal and have runes etched in them.  You\nget the feeling this could be the stairway to hell.  Stairs lead up\nand down into the darkness.\n',65,139400,56,0,0,0,0,0,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(11102,0,0,0,'On a Dark Stair','There is a constant flow of water running down the red metal stairs.  The\nwalls are made of the same red metal and have runes etched in them.  You\nget the feeling that this could be the stairway to hell.  Stairs lead up\nand down into the darkness.\n',65,139400,56,0,0,0,0,0,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(11103,0,0,0,'On a Dark Stair','There is a constant flow of water running down the red metal stairs.  The\nwalls are made of the same red metal and have runes etched in them.  You\nget the feeling this could be the stairway to hell.  Stairs lead up and\ndown into the darkness.\n',65,139400,56,0,0,0,0,0,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(11104,0,0,0,'On a Dark Stair','There is a constant flow of water running down the red metal stairs.  The\nwalls are made of the same red metal and have runes etched in them.  You\nget the feeling this could be the stairway to hell.  Stairs lead up\nand down into the darkness.\n',65,139400,56,0,0,0,0,0,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(11105,0,0,0,'On a Dark Stair','There is a constant flow of water running down the red metal stairs.  The\nwalls are made of the same red metal and have runes etched in them.  You\nget the feeling this could be the stairway to hell.  Stairs lead up\nand down into the darkness.\n',65,139400,56,0,0,0,0,0,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(11106,0,0,0,'In a Dark Tunnel','This is a narrow tunnel.  The water from the stairs above has pooled\nhere and is eight inches deep and smells horrible.  The air is humid and\nhot, you could almost swim through the room.  The red metal walls and\nceiling are strangely void of any runes.  Stairs lead up into the darkness.\nThe tunnel continues to the southwest.\n',65,139272,56,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(11107,0,0,0,'In a Dark Tunnel','This is a narrow tunnel.  Water is flowing into this room from the\nnortheast and out to east.  The air is hot and humid, you could almost\nswim through the room.  The red metal walls and ceiling are strangely\nvoid of any runes.  The tunnel leads the northeast and the east.\n',65,139272,46,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(11108,0,0,0,'In a Dark Tunnel','This is a narrow tunnel.  Water is flowing in from the west and down the\nstairs.  The air is humid and hot, you could almost swim through the room.\nThe red metal walls and ceiling are strangely void of any runes.  The tunnel\nleads to the west and stairs descend into the darkness.\n',65,139272,46,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(11109,0,0,0,'On a Dark Stair','There is a constant flow of water running down the red metal stairs.  The\nwalls are made of the same red metal and have runes etched in them.  You\nget the feeling this is the stairway to hell.  Stairs lead up and\ndown into the darkness.\n',65,139400,56,0,0,0,0,0,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(11110,0,0,0,'On a Dark Stair','There is a constant flow of water running down the red metal stairs.  The\nwalls are made of the same red metal and have runes etched into them.  You\nget the feeling this is the stairway to hell.  Stairs lead up and down\ninto the darkness.\n',65,139400,56,0,0,0,0,0,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(11111,0,0,0,'Landing on a Dark Stair','This is a wide landing on a dark stair.  The water from the red metal\nstairs flows down into a drain built into the floor.  A strange red moss\ngrows around the grate and glows lightly.  The runes on the red metal\nwalls, floor and ceiling glow brightly.  Stairs lead up and the landing\nruns to the southwest.\n',65,139400,56,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(11112,0,0,0,'At the Bottom of a Dark Stair','The landing comes to a sudden end.  It appears that whomever was digging\nthe stairway gave up.  The runes on the red metal walls, floor and ceiling\nare glowing brightly.  A mere spec of dust lies on the floor.  The only\nway out from this place is to the northeast.\n',65,139272,50,0,0,0,0,0,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(11113,0,0,0,'Entrance to the Temple of the Ryoken','This is a small dark room.  The walls are made of a strange red metal and\nappear to be bleeding.  The floor is covered in a thick soggy carpet that\nis red from the walls.  Whenever you move you can feel the carpet grasping\nat your feet.  A solid looking door leads south and a trap door leads up.\n',65,139272,50,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(11114,0,0,0,'In the Temple of the Ryoken','This is a small dark room.  The walls are made of a strange red metal and\nappear to be bleeding.  The floor is covered in a thick soggy carpet that\nis red from the walls.  Whenever you move you can feel the carpet grasping\nat your feet.\n',65,139272,50,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(11115,0,0,0,'In the Temple of the Ryoken','This is a poorly lighted room.  The ceiling glows with a pale red light.\nThe walls are made of a strange red metal and appear to be bleeding.  The\nfloor is covered in a thick, soggy carpet that is stained red from the\nwalls.  Whenever you move you can feel the carpet grasping at your feet.\nArchways lead to the north and the west.\n',65,139273,50,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(11116,0,0,0,'In the Temple of the Ryoken','This is a poorly lighted room.  The ceiling glows with a pale red light.\nThe walls are made of a strange red metal and appear to be bleeding.  The\nfloor is covered in a thick, soggy carpet that is stained red from the\nwalls.  Whenever you move you can feel the carpet grasping at your feet.\nArchways lead to the west and south.\n',65,139273,50,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL);
