(11181,0,0,0,'In the Church of the Ryoken','This is a dark room with a red metal floor.  Deep grooves have been cut\ninto the red metal floor and seem to lead to the east.  The moans of\npraying Ryoken can be hear from all around.\n',65,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11182,0,0,0,'In the Church of the Ryoken','This is a dark room with a red metal floor.  Deep grooves have been cut\ninto the red metal floor and seem to lead to the southeast.  The moans\nof praying Ryoken can be heard from all about.\n',65,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11183,0,0,0,'In the Church of the Ryoken','This is a dark room with a red metal floor.  Deep grooves have been cut\ninto the red metal floor and seem to lead to the southeast.  The moans\nof praying Ryoken can be heard from all around.\n',65,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11184,0,0,0,'In the Church of the Ryoken','This is a dark room with red metal floors.  Deep grooves have been cut\ninto the red metal floor and seem to lead to the southeast.  The moans\nof praying Ryoken can be heard from all around.\n',65,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11185,0,0,0,'In the Church of the Ryoken','This is a dark room with a red metal floor.  Deep grooves have been cut\ninto the red metal floor and seem to lead to the east.  The moans of\npraying Ryoken can be hear from all around.\n',65,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11186,0,0,0,'Bottom of a Red Metal Stair','This is the bottom of a red metal stair.  Stairs made from a dull red metal\nlead upwards.  Deep grooves have been cut into the red metal floor and\nseem to lead to the southeast.  The moans of praying Ryoken can be heard\nall around you.\n',65,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11187,0,0,0,'In the Church of the Ryoken','This is a dark room with a red metal floor.  Deep grooves have been cut\ninto the floor and seem to lead to the southeast.  The moans of praying\nRyoken can be heard from all around.\n',65,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11188,0,0,0,'In the Church of the Ryoken','This is a dark room with a red metal floor.  Deep grooves have been cut\ninto the red metal floor and seem to lead to the southeast.  The moans of\npraying Ryoken can be hear from all around.\n',65,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11189,0,0,0,'In the Church of the Ryoken','This is a dark room with a red metal floor.  Deep grooves have been cut\ninto the red metal floor and seem to lead to the east.  The moans of\npraying Ryoken can be hear from all around.\n',65,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11190,0,0,0,'Ryoken Guest Quarters','This is part of the luxurious guest quarters of the Ryoken.  Many\ninstruments of pain line these walls.  Bottles containing parts of various\nguests line one wall.  Cries of pain and whimpers of fear can be heard\ncoming from the west and south.\n',65,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11191,0,0,0,'Ryoken Guest Quarters','This is part of the luxurious guest quarter of the Ryoken.  Tall poles\nof a strange red metal have been placed in the floor.  Each pole starts\nwith a wide base and narrows to a dangerous point.  Several guests have\nbeen impaled on these poles.  You notice that with every step you take\nthe guests scream in pain and slide a little further down the pole.\n',65,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11192,0,0,0,'Bottom of a Blood Covered Stair','This is a brightly lighted landing.  Stairs covered in layers of blood\nlead up.  Cries of pain and whimpers of fear can be hard coming from the\nnorth.  A thin trickle of blood flows from out from under a door to the\nnorth.  A second door leads to the west.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11193,0,0,0,'Ryoken Guest Quarters','This is part of the luxurious guest quarters of the Ryoken.  Several lucky\nguests already occupy this room.  A once proud elf lies on a table in the\ncenter of the room.  A hulking ogre sits in the corner whimpering with\na whining voice about his fate.  A halfling is here to see if he can grow\ntaller.\n',65,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11194,0,0,0,'Ryoken Guest Quarters','This is the waiting room for guests of the Ryoken.  Several large cages\nline the walls.  A pair of eyes looks out at you as you scan the room.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11195,0,0,0,'Office of the Ryoken Interrogator','This is a spacious office.  The carpet is soft and comforting.  Many\ncharts line the walls.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11196,0,0,0,'Ryoken Guest Quarters','This is part of the luxurious guest quarters of the Ryoken.  Various\ninstruments for self mutilation lie spread out on a large red metal table.\n',65,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11197,0,0,0,'Ryoken Guest Quarters','This is part of the luxurious guest quarters of the Ryoken.  There are\nchains hanging from the walls to help you stretch out and relax.  A\nlarge table covered with poisoned spikes is here so you can lie down.  A\nlarge sign has been posted of the door to the south.\n',65,139272,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11198,0,0,0,'Incinerator','This is the incinerator room.  This place is unbelievably hot.  What are\nyou doing in here?\n',65,139275,62,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11199,0,0,0,'Spymaster\'s Lair','This is the resting place of the hideous Ryoken Spymaster.  Here in this\ndark, damp room she plots to take over The World.  With one such as this\nagainst it, how can The World survive?\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11200,0,0,0,'A Dark Stair','This is a short dark stairway.  It stretches only eight steps down and ends\nin a tiny landing.  A door has been set into the west wall.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(11201,0,0,0,'A Large Office','This is the office of the Ryoken Spymaster.  In this room she passes out\nassignments to her minions and berates them for their rare failures.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11202,0,0,0,'Reception Room','This is a well lighted room.  The walls are covered in large murals of\nthe many treacherous deeds of the Ryoken.  A door leads to the north and\nanother leads to the east.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11203,0,0,0,'Astral Walkway','This is an area of mists and voids.  A slim pathway extends across space\nand time.  It ends in a place much like the one where it began.  A door\nleads to the west at one end of the bridge.  While at the other end of the\nbridge a door leads to the east.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11204,0,0,0,'Entrance to the Inner Sanctum of the Ryoken','This small room is made entirely of astral matter.  The walls, ceiling and\nfloor shift constantly in swirling clouds of gray and white.  A door appears\nto be floating in the air to the west and an archway leads to the east.\n',65,139273,60,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11205,0,0,0,'A Narrow Hall','This is a narrow, stone hallway.  Stones from every type of rock in existence\nhave been used in this tall, yet narrow hallway.  A wide arch opens to the\nsouth.\n',65,131081,55,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(11206,0,0,0,'A Narrow Hall','This is a narrow, stone hallway.  Stones from every type of rock in existence\nhave been used in this tall, yet narrow hallway.\n',65,131081,55,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(11207,0,0,0,'A Narrow Hall','This is a narrow, stone hallway.  Stones from every type of rock in existence\nhave been used in this tall, yet narrow hallway.\n',65,131081,55,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(11208,0,0,0,'Storage Room','This is the room where the food for the High Lord and his minions is stored.\nThe bodies of many people from many races have been stacked here.  All the\nbodies are in a state of suspended animation.  A door of magically clear\ncrystal has been set into the south wall.\n',65,139273,60,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11209,0,0,0,'Quarters of a Ryoken General','This room shines with a light the color of pure gold.  The walls and floor\nare covered in the trophies of the Ryoken General.  Everything from the\nswords of paladins to the heads of elven kings can be found here.  Upon\ncloser examination of these items you discover they are all illusions.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(11210,0,0,0,'A Wide Hallway','This is a wide hallway with a low ceiling.  The walls, ceiling and floor\nhave all been made from a strange red metal.  A door has been set into the\nwest wall.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,15,100,0,'',NULL),
(11211,0,0,0,'A Grand Hallway','This is a grand hallway.  Rows of statues line the walls.  The walls,\nceiling and floor have been made from a single piece of pure platinum.\n',65,131081,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11212,0,0,0,'A Wide Hallway','This is a wide hallway with a low ceiling.  The walls, ceiling and floor\nhave all been made from a strange blue metal.\n',65,140297,55,0,0,0,0,0,15,100,0,'',NULL),
(11213,0,0,0,'Food Preparation Room','This is the room where all the meals for the High Lord and his minions are\nprepared.  A door made of magically clear crystal leads to the north.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11214,0,0,0,'Quarters of a Ryoken General','This room is completely void of furniture.  The walls are made of a dull\nred metal and have no markings on them.\n',65,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(11215,0,0,0,'A Wide Hallway','This is a wide hallway with a low ceiling.  The walls, ceiling and floor\nhave all been made from a strange red metal.  A door has been set into the\nwest wall.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,15,100,0,'',NULL),
(11216,0,0,0,'A Grand Hallway','This is a grand hallway.  Rows of statues line the walls.  The walls,\nceiling and floor have been made from a single piece of pure platinum.\n',65,131081,55,0,0,0,0,0,100,100,0,'',NULL),
(11217,0,0,0,'A Wide Hallway','This is a wide hallway with a low ceiling.  The walls, ceiling and floor\nhave all been made from a strange blue metal.  An archway leads to the east.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,15,100,0,'',NULL),
(11218,0,0,0,'A Sterile Room','This room is completely clean.  Not a single particle of dust is here.\nA door leads to the north and an archway leads west.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11219,0,0,0,'Quarters of a Ryoken General','This room is filled with gray vapors.  You cannot see more than a foot in\nfront of you.  There are no detectable walls here only a door in what must\nbe the east wall.\n',65,140297,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11220,0,0,0,'A Wide Hallway','This is a wide hallway with a low ceiling.  The walls, ceiling and floor\nhave all been made from a strange red metal.  A door has been set into the\nwest wall.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,15,100,0,'',NULL),
(11221,0,0,0,'A Grand Hallway','This is a grand hallway.  Rows of statues line the walls.  The walls,\nceiling and floor have been made from a single piece of pure platinum.\n',65,131081,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11222,0,0,0,'A Wide Hallway','This is a wide hallway with a low ceiling.  The walls, ceiling and floor\nhave all been made from a strange blue metal.  A door has been set into the\neast wall.\n',65,140297,55,0,0,0,0,0,15,100,0,'',NULL),
(11223,0,0,0,'Servant\'s Quarters','This is the room were the servants of the High Lord are allowed to come\nand rest.  There are no furnishings in this room.  A door has been set into\nthe west wall.\n',65,140297,55,0,0,0,0,0,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(11224,0,0,0,'End of a Wide Hall','This is a wide hallway with a low ceiling.  The walls, ceiling and floor\nhave all been made from a strange red metal.  A door has been set into the\nsouth wall.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(11225,0,0,0,'A Wide Hallway','This is a wide hallway with a low ceiling.  The walls, ceiling and floor\nhave all been made from a strange red metal.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,15,100,0,'',NULL),
(11226,0,0,0,'A Grand Hallway','This is a grand hallway.  Rows of statues line the walls.  The walls,\nceiling and floor have been made from a single piece of pure platinum.\nTo the south is the entrance to the a throne room.\n',65,131081,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11227,0,0,0,'End of a Wide Hallway','This is the end of a wide hallway with a low ceiling.  The walls, ceiling\nand floor have all been made from a strange blue metal.  A large door leads\neast.\n',65,140297,55,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(11228,0,0,0,'Servant\'s Hallway','This hallway is used by the servants of the High Lord.  The walls, ceiling\nand floor are all made from a strange blue metal.  A door has been set into\nwest wall.  An archway leads to the south.\n',65,140297,55,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(11229,0,0,0,'Room of Records','This dusty room is filled with wall to wall shelves.  The shelves extend\nfrom the floor to the vaulted ceiling.  Scrolls of all sizes and ages fill\nthe shelves.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11230,0,0,0,'High Lord\'s Chamber','This is the private retreat of the High Lord.  Here he can be himself and\nbe alone with his thoughts or share the company of a female companion.\nA portal made of mystical energies hovers in the east wall.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11231,0,0,0,'Throne Room of the Ryoken High Lord','This is the Throne Room of the Ryoken High Lord.  Here he keeps his court,\ndeclares his commands and hears the pleas of his followers.  Huge murals\ncover the walls and ceiling.  A small metal door leads to the east.  A\nportal of mystical energies floats to the west.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11232,0,0,0,'Dining Room','This is the dining room used by the High Lord and his Minions.  The room\nis brightly lit and looks to be spotlessly clean.  Doors lead to the west\nand the east.\n',65,139273,55,0,0,0,0,0,15,100,0,'',NULL),
(11233,0,0,0,'Servant\'s Hallway','This hallway is used by the servants of the High Lord.  The walls, ceiling\nand floor are all made from a strange blue metal.  A door has been set into\nthe west wall.  An archway leads to the north.\n',65,140297,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11234,0,-31,0,'Small Clearing','This small clearing at the end of the road is all that separates the mighty\njungle south of here and the swamp to the north.  Mother nature does not seem\ncontent with this situation, as a jungle vine or two extend across the ground\nencroaching on this clearing.\n',65,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11235,0,0,0,'The Incinerator','This is the incinerator.  Flames lick about you, scorching your skin.\nYou could already be dead bit a worse fate awaits you in the pit below.\n',68,131085,57,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(11236,0,0,0,'Descent into the Pit','As you fall your hands desperately try to grip the smooth, red metal walls.\nYour mind races as you imagine the terrors awaiting you below.\n',68,131080,57,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(11237,0,0,0,'The Dark Pit of Ryoken','As your recover from your fall you look around.  The walls are made of a\nsmooth red metal and are probably unclimbable.  The walls suddenly become\nunimportant as you become more aware of your surroundings.  You sense that\nthis is the home of something evil and that you might not be alone.  The\nhair on the back of your neck begins to rise.\nBlood and filth flow into a grate on the floor.\n',68,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(11238,0,0,0,'Descent into the Pit','As you fall your hands madly try to gain hold on the smooth walls.  Your\nmind races and you try to imagine the terrors awaiting below.\n',68,131080,58,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(11239,0,0,0,'The Incinerator','This is the incinerator.  Flames lick about you, scorching your skin.\nYou could already be dead but a worse fate awaits you in the pit below.\n',68,131080,62,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(11240,0,0,0,'Sewage Drain','Blood and filth flow in from the grate above.  The muck is chest deep to a\nhalfling.  Filth and the remains from the demons previous meals float about\nthe room and into a small grate to the north.\n',68,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,2,130,0,'',NULL),
(11241,0,0,0,'Sewage Tunnel','This is a small sewage tunnel.  The filth almost reaches the top of the\ntunnel leaving a tiny space to breath.  The tunnel runs north and south.\n',68,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,2,30,0,'',NULL),
(11242,0,0,0,'Sewage Junction','This is a junction of sewage pipes.  Filth flows into the room from dozens\nof small tunnels, including one in the ceiling.  The filth flows into the\ndrain in the floor.  Thick iron bars block entrance to the drain.  The\nonly tunnels that are not filled with sewage are the one to the south and\nthe one above, which is blocked by a grate.\n',68,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,30,0,'',NULL),
(11243,0,0,0,'Narrow Sewage Tunnel','This is a narrow sewage tunnel that runs up and down.  Filth flows into\nthe tunnel from above and down over the walls.  Rungs have been bolted\ninto the walls.  The filth flows out through a grate in the floor.  Air\nand light seems to come from the grate above.\n',68,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,30,0,'',NULL),
(11244,0,0,0,'Dark Corridor','This is a dark corridor.  Thick cobwebs hide much of the passage but do\nnot hinder movement.  The floor is littered with dust and bones of long\ndead adventurers.\n',68,139272,50,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11245,0,0,0,'End of a Dark Corridor','This is the end of a dark corridor.  Thick cobwebs clog the corridor.  Bones\nof long dead adventurers litter the floor and are covered in a thick dust.\n',68,139272,50,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11246,0,0,0,'End of a Dark Corridor','This is the end of a dark corridor.  Thick cobwebs clog the corridor.  Bones\nof long dead adventurers litter the floor and are covered in a thick dust.\n',68,139272,50,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11247,0,0,0,'Dark Corridor','This is part of a dark corridor.  Thick cobwebs clog the corridor.  Bones\nof long dead adventurers litter the floor and are covered in a thick dust.\nA strange malevolent aura of power seems to come from the north.\n',68,139272,50,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11248,0,0,0,'Demon\'s Lair','This is the end of a dark corridor.  Thick cobwebs lie crushed on the floor.\nDemolished bones of the dead are scattered every where.  The walls are covered\nin scorch marks and blood.  A feeling of fear fills your bones.\n',68,139272,50,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11300,0,0,0,'Dirt Road','  You are standing on a dirt road that runs east to west.  The road looks\nit has been heavily traveled in recent times.  To the north you can see a\nfaint trail that has been lightly concealed in brush.\n',66,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11301,0,0,0,'Concealed Path','  You are traveling along a trail which is partially obscured by twigs and\nbranches.  There are a number of boot-prints in the dust.  Directly south\nis a substantial-looking east-west road.\n',66,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11302,21,14,-3,'Rough, Dirty Path','  This is a rough and dirty path through the low brush.  Decomposing plant\nmatter along the path gives the area a slightly putrid smell.  In the distance\nto the north you can see a rock outcropping at the base of rising hills.\n',66,131072,60,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11303,21,15,-3,'End of the Path','  A path disappearing to the south ends here at your feet.  The dense scrub\nmakes it virtually impossible to move in any other direction.  Hills rising\ninto a mountain range are visible to the northeast, and an outcropping of\nrock extends like a finger from the base of the nearest hill, intersecting\nthe path.\n',66,131072,60,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11304,21,15,-4,'Inside the Entrance to the Rock Formation','  This room is very small and the walls and floor are composed of solid\nrock.  Above is a hole through which fresh air flows, contrasted with\nthe dankness emanating from a twisting tunnel south.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(11305,21,14,-4,'Twisting Passage Through a Cave','  This is a twisting passage that proceeds through solid rock.  All about\nare rock shards, as if some unknown deity had picked up the mountain and\nshaken it about.  Stale air emanates from the northeast.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11306,22,15,-4,'Twisting Passage Through a Cave','  You are on a twisting passage cut through solid rock.  The passage is\nrather featureless, if you don\'t consider faint bloodstains on the walls\nvery noteworthy.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11307,23,15,-4,'Twisty Passage Through a Cave','  The passage is filled with flickering shadows from the torches here.\nThe walls are quite featureless, and exits disappear into the blackness in\nboth directions.  A dank, musty smell emanates from one of the exits.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11308,24,16,-4,'Little Twisty Passage Through a Cave','  This is a lovely little passage which seems to have been cut through solid\nrock.  The floor is completely devoid of dust, dirt or rock fragments, as if\nsomeone has swept the room recently.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11309,25,15,-4,'Tiny Alcove','  This is a tiny alcove branching off from the main passage.  The room is\nwell kept and nearly filled by the simple, but dominating furnishings.  The\nonly exit returns you from whence you came.\n',66,139276,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11310,25,17,-4,'Twisting Passage Deep in the Mine','  The passage changes in depth rapidly here, sloping steeply upward to the\nsouthwest and downward to the north.  The walls have huge gashes in\nthem where valuable minerals have been forcibly removed.  A dank, musty\nodor emanates from the north exit.  It smells a bit like rotting\nrefuse mixed with a strong smell of sweat, but you really can\'t put your\nfinger on what its source might be.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11311,25,18,-4,'Wide Passage in the Mine','  You are in the center of a passage through what is obviously a mine.  The\npath forks here, with an upsloping, narrowing exit south, and descending\npassages northeast and southeast.  There is a putrid smell pervading the\nroom and it seems to increase in intensity to the northeast.  You can hear\nnoises in the distance, but from here you cannot determine their source.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11312,26,17,-4,'South Fork of the Mine','  This is the south fork of what must be an old abandoned mine.  The walls\nhere are crumbling from lack of maintenance and the ceiling is held up by\nrotting wooden posts.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11313,27,17,-4,'South Fork of the Mine','  This is the south fork of an ancient mine.  The walls here are dry and the\nsoil is flaking and eroding from decades of neglect.  The eastern wall,\nhowever, is a solid blockade of smooth granite.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11314,27,17,-3,'Rubble Filled Cave','  This underground cave must be the result of recent seismic activity.\nYour movement is slowed by the piled-up rock and dirt; surprisingly large,\nflat segments of shattered rock and wooden posts virtually block passage\nin several places.  This certainly doesn\'t look like a safe place to be.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11315,28,18,-3,'Rubble Filled Cave','  This underground cave must be the result of recent seismic activity.\nYour movement is slowed by the piled-up rock and dirt; surprisingly large,\nflat segments of shattered rock and wooden posts virtually block passage\nin several places.  This certainly doesn\'t look like a safe place to be.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11316,29,18,-3,'Rubble Filled Cave','  This underground cave must be the result of recent seismic activity.\nYour movement is slowed by the piled-up rock and dirt; surprisingly large,\nflat segments of shattered rock and wooden posts virtually block passage\nin several places.  This certainly doesn\'t look like a safe place to be.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11317,30,19,-3,'Rubble Filled Cave','  This underground cave must be the result of recent seismic activity.\nYour movement is slowed by the piled-up rock and dirt; surprisingly large,\nflat segments of shattered rock and wooden posts virtually block passage\nin several places.  This certainly doesn\'t look like a safe place to be.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11318,30,20,-3,'Rubble Filled Cave','  This underground cave must be the result of recent seismic activity.\nYour movement is slowed by the piled-up rock and dirt; surprisingly large,\nflat segments of shattered rock and wooden posts virtually block passage\nin several places.  This certainly doesn\'t look like a safe place to be.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11319,30,21,-3,'Rubble Filled Cave','  This underground cave must be the result of recent seismic activity.\nYour movement is slowed by the piled-up rock and dirt; surprisingly large,\nflat segments of shattered rock and wooden posts virtually block passage\nin several places.  This certainly doesn\'t look like a safe place to be.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11320,31,22,-3,'Rubble Filled Cave','  This underground cave must be the result of recent seismic activity.\nYour movement is slowed by the piled-up rock and dirt; surprisingly large,\nflat segments of shattered rock and wooden posts virtually block passage\nin several places.  This certainly doesn\'t look like a safe place to be.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11321,31,23,-3,'Rubble Filled Cave','  This underground cave must be the result of recent seismic activity.\nYour movement is slowed by the piled-up rock and dirt; surprisingly large,\nflat segments of shattered rock and wooden posts virtually block passage\nin several places.  This certainly doesn\'t look like a safe place to be.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11322,31,23,-2,'Rubble Filled Cave','  This underground cave must be the result of recent seismic activity.\nYour movement is slowed by the piled-up rock and dirt; surprisingly large,\nflat segments of shattered rock and wooden posts virtually block passage\nin several places.  A cool breeze can be felt from the west.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11323,30,23,-2,'Entrance to Rubble Filled Cave','  This underground cave must be the result of recent seismic activity.\nYour movement is slowed by the piled-up rock and dirt; surprisingly large,\nflat segments of shattered rock and wooden posts virtually block passage\nin several places.  Directly to the west you can see the beginning of a\nroad, and the cave continues forebodingly to the east.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11324,29,23,-2,'A Rough Road','  This rough road is made of dirt and loose stones.  You see a large forest off\nto the north, and a huge cliff off to the east.  Parts of the cliff have\nbeen damaged by what seems to have been an avalanche, and there is rubble\nfrom rock fragments and roots scattered everywhere.\n',66,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11325,29,20,-3,'Remnant of the Maze','  This room has remarkably stout and smooth walls, quite unlike the rubble\nyou have trudged through previously.  This is an entirely intact corner of the\nmaze that existed before the earthquake!  It may be all of the labyrinth\nthat remains undamaged.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11326,29,21,-3,'Remnant of the Maze','  This is a remnant of the fabled Logrus Maze, natural wonder of The World.\nUnfortunately the maze turns west here and is totally blocked by crumbled\nand shattered boulders, undoubtedly due to an earthquake of some sort.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11327,0,0,0,'Secret Path Along the Rocks','This masterfully concealed path roughly parallels the trail to the west.  A rock\nformation prevents the trail from going any further.\n',0,140288,24,300,11302,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11328,0,0,0,'Crevice in the Rock Outcropping','  You are standing at the mouth of a crevice within the rock outcropping.\nThe floor of the crevice is hard-packed dirt and it seems to extend for a\nshort distance before disappearing into solid rock.  There is a small hut\nconstructed in the center of the crevice, preventing you from following it\nfurther into the rock.\n',66,139264,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11329,0,0,0,'Interior of Hut','  This is the hut of Luipol, the master thief and scout for hire.  The room\nis sparse and dimly lit, and the ceiling is quite low.  The back of the\nhut is open and slopes down to an underground room to the east, from which\nyou can see a soft glow.  A door leads to the outdoors.\n',66,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11330,0,0,0,'Burrow','  The ceiling of the hut is now solid earth - this is a Hobbit burrow, or at\nleast as much as could be excavated before hitting solid rock!  This room is\nwell-kept and the light from the single lamp plays upon the granite walls.\n',66,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11331,0,0,0,'Narrow Crawl Space','  This is a narrow crawlspace between the rear of the hut and the crevice.\nIt must be intended as an escape route, as no self-respecting Hobbit would\nhave only a single entryway to his abode.  Since the rear of the hut is\nflush with the ground at your feet, you can walk west up the roof towards\nthe front.  A very small crack leads into the solid rock to the north.\n',66,139264,24,0,0,0,0,0,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11332,0,0,0,'Empty Air in Front of the Hut','  Wow, that hut was small.  It took you like, no time at all to walk right\noff the front of the house and into the empty air.  There\'s ground beneath\nyou and nice, solid hut just out of reach to the east.\n',66,139264,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11333,0,0,0,'Crack in the Rock','  This is an extremely small crack in the rock.  There is barely enough room\nfor you and your belongings.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,1,100,0,'',NULL),
(11334,0,0,0,'Crack in the Rock','  This is an extremely small crack in the rock.  There is barely enough room\nfor you and your belongings.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,1,100,0,'',NULL),
(11335,0,0,0,'Crack in the Rock','  This is an extremely small crack in the rock.  There is barely enough room\nfor you and your belongings.  The air temperature seems to change inversely with\nrespect to the depth of the shaft.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,1,100,0,'',NULL),
(11336,0,0,0,'Crack in the Rock','  This is an extremely small crack in the rock.  There is barely enough room\nfor you and your belongings.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,1,100,0,'',NULL),
(11337,0,0,0,'Crack in the Rock','  This is an extremely small crack in the rock.  There is barely enough room\nfor you and your belongings.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,1,100,0,'',NULL),
(11338,0,0,0,'Crack in the Rock','  This is an extremely small crack in the rock.  There is barely enough room\nfor you and your belongings.  At your feet, the crack seems to widen slightly.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,1,100,0,'',NULL),
(11339,0,0,0,'Bottom of the Shaft','  You are at the bottom of a long shaft.  It is extremely cold and the air\npierces your lungs.  There are no footprints or other markings of any kind,\nonly rock and dirt surround you.  A stone door inscribed with a single ancient\nrune indicate a passage east.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(11340,0,0,0,'Featureless Hall','  This is a featureless hall extending east and west.  The walls are polished\nsmooth and the ceiling rises to the east.  A stone door lies west.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(11341,0,0,0,'Featureless Hall','  This is a largely featureless east-west hall.  The granite walls are\npolished smooth and the ceiling here is very high.  The floor is totally clear\nof rock fragments, and the outlines of steps are apparent if you follow the\nhall as it descends to the east.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,400,0,'',NULL),
(11342,0,0,0,'Featureless Hall','  This is a largely featureless east-west hall.  The granite walls are\npolished smooth and the ceiling here is very high.  The floor is totally clear\nof rock fragments, and well-defined steps descend eastward.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,400,0,'',NULL),
(11343,0,0,0,'Anteroom','  This room is very large and circular.  The walls are solid granite polished\nto a perfect mirror finish, and the ceiling is presumably so high that it\ncannot be seen.  A hall enters from the west with inset, descending steps\nthat vanish into the perfectly cleared floor.  A gigantic door is set into\nthe northeastern wall, and it is adorned by a single, huge rune.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,500,0,'',NULL),
(11344,0,0,0,'Heart of the Mountain','  This is the heart of the mountain range which divides the lands of Logrus\nfrom the rest of The World.  The room is huge but is without features or\nmarkings.  It is clear by the stale smell of the air that this room has not\nbeen found by explorers in a long time.  A huge door leads southwest.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,500,0,'',NULL),
(11345,31,19,-1,'South Fork of the Mine','  This is the west end of the south fork of an abandoned mine.  The walls\nare totally stripped of any mineral wealth they once had.  There is a great\ndeal of silt and dry wood fragments littering the floor here.  Passage west\nis completely blocked by a stout granite wall.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11346,32,18,-1,'South Fork of the Mine','  This is the west end of the south fork of an ancient mine.  The walls here\nare totally stripped of any mineral wealth they once had.  High above there\nseem to be many small entrances to the tunnel, too small for passage but\nentirely too big to be unnoticed.  The passage steepens greatly southeast.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11347,33,17,-1,'Top of a Steep Incline','  You are standing at the top of a incline which slopes steeply to the east.\nThere is evidence that water used to run through this passage, as sediment and\ndirt make your footing very unsure.  If you aren\'t careful you may slide down\nthe incline.\n',66,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,30,'',NULL),
(11348,33,21,-6,'Shore of the Underground River','  You are on a small shore of pebbles, bordering a swiftly moving underground\nriver to the north.  At your back is nothing but solid rock.\n',66,131080,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11349,34,17,-1,'On an Incline','  You are on an incline which slopes steeply downward to the east.  The walls\nare eroded from what must have been rushing water at one time.  Sediment\nprobably deposited as the water trickled to a stop makes your footing quite\ntreacherous.  If you aren\'t careful you may slide down the incline.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,30,'',NULL),
(11350,43,17,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  Northeast is a large pit, the result of a cave-in.  The edges\nof the pit look treacherous.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11351,35,17,-1,'At the Bottom of an Incline','  You are at the bottom of an incline which terminates over a large pool of\nwater.  The walls of the incline look weathered and eroded, probably from\na large quantity of fast-moving water at some point in time.  If indeed there\nwas a underground river here, where you are standing must have been the top\nof a magnificent waterfall which exited into the pool.  There is a lot of\nloose dirt and small rocks which have been deposited here, and the precipice\nis quite steep, so mind your step!\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,30,'',NULL),
(11352,42,16,0,'Crack in the Solid Rock','  You are in a narrow crack in the otherwise solid granite rock of the\nmountain.  To the north you can see a room filled with rubble.  The crack\nnarrows so that you cannot continue south.  Your nose detects the slightest\ntrace of ozone, and you notice a faint haze blanketing the room.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(11353,36,17,-1,'Above the Pool','  You are in thin air above a large pool.  At the south side of the pool is\nwhat appears to be the only way out of the water - a small passage leading\nsouthwest out of the room.  To your east is a steep incline to which you\nare probably longing for physical contact.\n',66,131080,57,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11354,36,17,-2,'In the Pool','  You are in a pool of water.  The water is slightly brackish and is shallow\nenough to stand in.  There is a depression in the west wall of the room\nwhich makes the pool\'s capacity slightly larger than you originally expected,\nand it looks a wee bit deeper there.  You can exit the pool to a passage south.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11355,34,16,-1,'Relief Tunnel','  This seems to be a relief tunnel for the dry waterway that is through the\nhole to the north.  It would appear that when the water got too high it\nwas diverted through this tunnel instead of proceeding down the waterfall.\nThis passage is small and you can easily steady yourself as you walk.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11356,35,15,-1,'Relief Tunnel','  This is a tunnel which may have been used to transport water at one time,\nas evidenced by the silt deposits on the walls and floor.  It is small\nenough that you may easily steady yourself by contact with the walls, even\nthough it is quite steep here.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11357,35,15,-2,'Relief Tunnel','  This is a tiny tunnel which slopes upward quite steeply.  It is small\nenough that you may easily steady yourself by holding on to the walls,\nhowever.  The tunnel also leads through a small hole east, and northeast\nthere are sounds of lapping water.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11358,36,16,-2,'At the Pool\'s Edge','  You are on the edge of a large pool that fills the room except for the\nsmall ledge upon which you stand.  The water looks a bit brown, as if it\nhas been standing for a long time and accumulated some particulates.  A\ncliff-like configuration is above the pool which must have been at one time\na massive waterfall.  To the southwest is a tunnel which might have been a\nsort of water bypass, evident by all the silt and pebbles at your feet here.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11359,35,17,-2,'A Sheltered Depression','  This part of the pool is in a sheltered depression in the cliff wall.\nThe walls here are unyielding, with years of lime deposits covering any\nporosity in the rock.  You could not climb out of the water here.  Below\nyou the water seems to be quite deep, in contrast with the main pool.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11360,35,17,-3,'Under the Pool Surface','  Your feet are resting on the solid floor of the pool about fifteen feet\nbelow the surface of the water.  The drop-off looks very severe; in fact,\nif you cannot swim back up the way you came you are unlikely to be able to\nhoist yourself back up to the main pool.  This part of the pool extends to\nthe north into total darkness.\n',66,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11361,35,18,-3,'Debris in the Pool','  This must have been the exit for the pool as it is the lowest point you\nhave seen so far.  Unfortunately, waterlogged bits of debris and large rocks\nhave totally plugged the descending passage and prevented the water from\nflowing - this is probably why the water is so brackish.\n',66,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11362,36,15,-2,'Small Hole in the Mountain','  The tiny passage leading northward must have been created by a recent\nearthquake.  Your progress is slowed by piles of rock, dirt and fragments of\nwood.  Tunnels leading both west and east seem to open up a bit.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(11363,37,16,-2,'Small Hole in the Mountain','  This tiny passage must have been created by a recent earthquake.  Your\nprogress is slowed by piles of rock, dirt and fragments of wood.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(11364,38,17,-2,'Small Hole in the Mountain','  This tiny passage must have been created by a recent earthquake.  Your\nprogress is slowed by piles of rock, dirt and fragments of wood.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(11365,38,17,-1,'Small Hole in the Mountain','  This tiny passage must have been created by a recent earthquake.  Your\nprogress is slowed by piles of rock, dirt and fragments of wood.  Northeast is\na larger room which is completely filled with debris.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(11366,39,18,-1,'Sinkhole','  You are inside a sinkhole which is filled with debris that has fallen\nfrom above.  Large pieces of rock and wooden post fragments make this room\nvery difficult to traverse.  You might be able to squeeze through a tiny\nhole leading southwest.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11367,39,18,0,'Inside the Mountain','  This room is filled with rubble and debris.  Large sections of the walls\nhave splintered and fallen down, presumably from a strong earthquake.  There\nis a large sinkhole in the floor here.  To the west is a passage leading\nout of the mountain to a narrow rock pass.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11368,38,18,0,'Split in the Rock','  You are standing in a deep split which extends some distance to the\nsouthwest.  The sides of the split are steep and rise high into the sky.\nTo the east is a narrow entrance to a mountain passage.  You notice\nscattered bits of rock and clumps of dirt on the passage floor.\n',66,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11369,40,18,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  Looking south, you see that the ceiling has collapsed and a\nhuge boulder has fallen into the room from above.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11370,40,19,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  To the north and northwest, the passage ends in solid granite.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11371,41,19,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  An impassable jumble of debris blocks your passage east.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11372,41,18,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  Your way is totally blocked northeast and southwestwards, but\nthe passage is fairly clear to the southeast.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11373,41,17,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  Directly west lies a huge boulder which appears to have\ncrashed through the eroded ceiling, and travel southwards becomes impossible\ndue to a solid granite wall.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11374,42,17,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  The way south is blocked by a stout granite wall, but it seems\nto be cracking in places.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11375,42,18,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  A huge pile of earth, rock and splinters of wooden posts lie\nnorth.  There certainly is no way to get over it, as it extends from\nfloor to ceiling.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11376,43,18,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  East lies a large pit, the result of a cave-in.  The edges of\nthe pit look treacherous.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11377,43,19,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  Movement west is prohibited by a huge pile of debris extending\nfrom floor to ceiling, and at your feet is the lip of a large pit dominating\nthe area southeast.  The edges of the pit look dangerous.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11378,44,19,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  A solid granite wall blocks the way to the north.  South is a\nlarge pit.  It might be advisable to use some care when moving about the pit.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11379,45,19,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  Southwest lies a large pit, the result of a severe cave-in.\nThe edge of the pit looks dangerous.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11380,45,18,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  There is a large pit west, and its edges look treacherous.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11381,45,17,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  A huge pit lies northwest, and you can just see the edge of\na section of wall extending from the edge of the pit to its floor.  Perhaps\nyou might be able to slide down.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11382,46,17,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11383,46,18,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11384,47,18,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with rubble and debris.  Large sections of the walls\nhave splintered and fallen down, presumably from a strong earthquake.  There\nis a passage continuing west, and a rocky overgrown trail begins to the east.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11385,48,18,0,'An Overgrown Rocky Trail','  This narrow, rocky trail is seldom used and has mostly been reclaimed by\nthe local vegetation.  The mighty Sympathian Mountains loom to the\nwest, and this trail follows the gully through the foothills.  Immediately to\nthe west stands a tall, rock cliff, in which you see a man-made entrance\nleading into the mountain.  Where the road meets the entrance, the mortar\nis crumbled and the stones have fallen out of place.\n',66,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11386,44,18,0,'Absence of Ground Over a Pit','  The solid ground is no longer directly under your feet, as you are now\nsupported by a twenty-foot column of air.  How long you may continue to\nmaintain your position relative to the rubble-filled floor of the pit\nbelow may be uncertain.\n',66,131080,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11387,44,18,0,'The Cold Hard Ground of the Pit','  You are within a pit, the result of severe seismic activity combined with\na weak localized ground structure.  The cave-in has deposited chunks of rock\nand dirt on the floor here.  The pit walls are very sheer, and you are unable\nto scale them to reach the edge twenty feet above.  Fortunately, some large\nfragments of flat granite have wedged themselves into the floor and the\nsoutheast wall, affording a makeshift ramp with which you may be able\nto extract yourself.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11388,26,19,-4,'North Fork of the Mine','  This shaft of the old, abandoned mine descends steadily eastbound.  The\nwalls are crumbling with age, but there is evidence of heavy trafficking\nif you scrutinize the floor.  A smell you simply cannot define drifts in\nfrom the northeast.  You simply know it smells BAD.  Seemingly strange\na magical looking rune mars the northwest wall.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11389,27,20,-4,'North Fork of the Mine','  You are traversing a passage which extends southwest and east for some\ndistance before changing direction.  The walls are showing signs of erosion\nand a piece of dirt falls onto your head from a chink in the ceiling.  A\nparticularly offensive odor wafts into the room from the east corridor.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11390,28,20,-4,'North Fork of the Mine','  This part of the mine shaft seems to have been particularly hard hit by\nthe recent seismic activity.  Part of the south wall has collapsed into a\nlarge pile of dirt and large rocks litter the floor like polka-dots.  There\nare sounds nearby that are foreign to your ears, and a very pervasive smell\nhits your nostrils and makes you wince.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11391,29,20,-4,'North Fork of the Mine','  The passage turns here, with exits leading west and southeast.  There is\na large hole in the floor through which the most indescribably disgusting\nodor emanates.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11392,30,19,-4,'North Fork of the Mine','  You are following the northernmost shaft of the abandoned mine.  In the\ndistance to the east you can see the passage split in a \"Y\".  A particularly\noffensive odor is detectable here, most strongly near the northwestern exit.\nFortunately, it is just overwhelmed by the smells of cooking meat from\nthe other direction.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11393,29,20,-5,'Humid Corridor','  You are at the beginning of a corridor extending out to the northeast.  Your\nnose is assaulted by an acrid odor wafting into the room from somewhere down\nthe passage, and you feel some humidity in the air.  Above is another passage.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11394,30,21,-5,'Narrow Humid Corridor','  The corridor narrows here to pass through a section of solid rock.  The smell\nis absolutely unbearable here combined with the high humidity.  You can glimpse\nthe anchor-point of a makeshift bridge to the east.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(11395,31,21,-5,'Edge of Chasm','  You are standing at the edge of a thirty-foot wide chasm across which is\nsuspended a rickety wooden-slat bridge.  The bridge is the only way across the\nchasm, and west leads through a narrow passage in rock.  You can hear the\nsound of fast-moving water nearby, but you scarcely notice since your senses\nsingularly concentrate on the terrible smell emanating from the north.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11396,31,22,-5,'Wooden Bridge Across the Chasm','  You are standing on the rotted slats of a wooden bridge.  The bridge is held\ntogether with knotted rope that looks badly decomposed - perhaps traversing it\nwasn\'t the best idea?  Far below, a fast-moving river burbles and splashes\nthrough the chasm.  A dim torchlight is visible on the other side of the chasm\nto the north, and you wish you could ignore the terrible odor coming from\nthat same direction.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11397,31,23,-5,'Edge of Chasm','  You are standing at the edge of a thirty-foot wide chasm across which is\nsuspended a rickety wooden-slat bridge.  The bridge is the only way across\nthe chasm.  Many footprints lead from the bridge to a short hallway northeast\nthrough the dirt floor.  You can scarcely breathe due to the incredible\nrotting smell emanating from the hallway.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11398,32,24,-5,'Official-Looking Stone Office','  This room looks as it has been hewn from the solid stone of the\nmountain.  The ceiling is about 20 feet high, and the floor is polished\ngranite.  The dominant feature of the room, however, is the massive pile of\nrotting flesh and bone which graces the corner of the room.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11399,31,19,-4,'Long Hall','  This is the west end of a large hall.  It has been reinforced with stout\nwooden posts, and the floor is hard-packed dirt.  The smell of cooking meat\nwafts in from the southern passage.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11400,31,18,-4,'Mess Hall','  This is a large room which must be used for feeding large number of\nravenously hungry individuals.  The ceiling is quite high and the walls\nare reinforced.  If the inhabitants here take fighting seriously, it\nis apparent they give equal weight to their gluttonous tendencies!\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11401,32,19,-4,'Long Hall','  You are in a large hall which has been reinforced with stout wooden posts.\nThe floor is hard-packed dirt, and judging from the footprints in the dust, it\nreceives a lot of traffic.  The main passage turns slightly north here, and a\nsmaller passage branches off to the east.  From the west your nose detects\nthe smells associated with a kitchen.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11402,33,20,-4,'Long Hall','  You are in a large hall which has been reinforced with stout wooden posts.\nThe floor is hard-packed dirt, and judging from the footprints in the dust, it\nreceives a lot of traffic.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11403,33,19,-4,'Crawlway','  You are traversing a crawlway that appears to parallel the main hall.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,3,40,0,'',NULL),
(11404,34,20,-4,'Long Hall','  You are in a large hall which has been reinforced with stout wooden posts.\nThe floor is hard-packed dirt, and judging from the footprints in the dust, it\nreceives a lot of traffic.  A small crawlway leads southwest.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11405,35,20,-4,'Long Hall','  You are in a large hall which has been reinforced with stout wooden posts.\nThe floor is hard-packed dirt, and judging from the footprints in the dust, it\nreceives a lot of traffic.  Another large hall branches off to the north.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11406,35,21,-4,'Large Hall','  You are traversing a large hall which turns sharply.  Directly south is the\nmain hall.  You can see a torchlight to the west.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11407,34,21,-4,'Entrance to Barracks','  You are standing at the entrance to several barracks.  The largest by far is\nthe central one directly north, and two smaller rooms flank to either side.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11408,36,20,-4,'Long Hall','  You are in a large hall which has been reinforced with stout wooden posts.\nThe floor is hard-packed dirt, and judging from the footprints in the dust, it\nreceives a lot of traffic.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11409,37,22,-2,'Long Hall','  You are in a large hall which has been reinforced with stout wooden posts.\nThe floor is hard-packed dirt, and judging from the footprints in the dust, it\nreceives a lot of traffic.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11410,38,22,-2,'Long Hall','  You are in a large hall which has been reinforced with stout wooden posts.\nThe floor is hard-packed dirt, and judging from the footprints in the dust, it\nreceives a lot of traffic.  A strong-looking steel door is set into a cutout in\nthe northeast wall.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11411,39,22,-2,'Long Hall','  You are in a large hall which has been reinforced with stout wooden posts.\nThe floor is hard-packed dirt, and judging from the footprints in the dust, it\nreceives a lot of traffic.  A narrow corridor leads south.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11412,39,21,-2,'Narrow Corridor Through Rock','  This is a corridor cut through the solid rock.  The floors, walls and ceiling\nare smooth and there are no sharp corners or edges.  You can hear the sounds\nof weapons and grunts of combat nearby.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11413,39,20,-2,'Narrow Corridor Through Rock','  This is a corridor cut through the solid rock.  The floors, walls and ceiling\nare smooth and there are no sharp corners or edges.  You can hear the sounds\nof weapons and grunts of combat nearby.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11414,38,19,-2,'Training Room','  This is a large natural cavern in the rock, perfectly suited for its\npresent usage as a combat training ground.  The air is musty with the smells\nof physical exertion, and you can see the fading stains of blood on the floor\nwhere the combat training became particularly intense.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11415,40,22,-2,'Long Hall','  You are in a large hall which has been reinforced with stout wooden posts.\nThe floor is hard-packed dirt, and judging from the footprints in the dust, it\nreceives a lot of traffic.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11416,41,23,-2,'Long Hall','  This is the east end of a large hall.  It has been reinforced with stout\nwooden posts, and the floor is hard-packed dirt.  Judging by the footprints\nin the dust, it appears to receive a lot of traffic.  The hall gives way\nto another, poorly maintained passage above.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11417,41,23,-1,'North Fork of the Mine','  This northern shaft of the mine merges with a larger passage below.  You\ncan detect noises from the hall but cannot hear enough to identify them.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11418,44,23,-2,'Junction of the Mine Passages','  You are standing at the intersection of two passages.  The southern corridor\nappears recently excavated, in contrast to the eroding condition of the tunnel\nin which you stand.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11419,43,21,-1,'North Fork of the Mine','  This shaft of the old, abandoned mine descends steadily westbound.  The\nwalls are crumbling with age, and you surmise that despite its condition,\nthe passage is heavily used, as the boot prints in the dust catch your eye.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11420,44,20,-1,'Entrance to the Mine','  This is the entrance to an abandoned mine, evidence given by the ragged\nappearance of the rock walls exhausted of mineral value.  The solid granite\nwall that lies east gives way to a dilapidated and collapsing pass northwest.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11421,45,20,-1,'Low Passage Through a Cave','  This passage is rather wide but the ceiling is only about five feet from the\nfloor.  Looking southeast you can see a lot of debris from earthquake damage,\nbut this room seems much more structurally sound.  There is a solid granite wall\nwhich blocks the passage from continuing west.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11422,46,19,-1,'Cave-In','  Ploink!  You are hit in the head by a stone falling from the room above.\nThis room is full of dirt and rock which formerly comprised a ceiling.  A\npassage begins in the room above, and a low passage leaves northwest.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11423,46,19,0,'Rubble Filled Passage Through the Mountain','  This room is filled with debris due to involuntary remodeling by a natural\ndisaster.  It is roughly polygon-shaped with walls jutting into the room at\nright angles.  The walls that are standing are flat sheets of rock,\nreinforced with stout wooden posts.  Others lie broken on the floor amid\nthe rubble.  There is a big hole in the floor, and bits of dirt shake loose\nfrom the edges of the holes and fall as you walk about the room.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,30,'',NULL),
(11424,32,18,-4,'Kitchen','  This is a kitchen, although it seems rather poorly equipped.  Its primary\npurpose seems to be the cooking of large quantities of meat, with pots and\npans and large knives adorning the walls, and a large fire burning in a\nstone furnace in the center of the room.\n',66,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11425,30,22,-6,'Underground River','  The bottom of the chasm here is filled with fast-moving water.  If you have\nthe means to levitate, you might be able to reach the wooden bridge above.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,15,1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11426,29,22,-6,'Subterranean River','  You are shoulder-deep in a swift underground river flowing through a chasm.\nThe chasm narrows slightly as it makes a slight turn here, increasing the\nspeed of the water flow.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,15,1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11427,28,23,-6,'Subterranean River','  You are shoulder-deep in a swift underground river flowing through a chasm.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,30,8,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11428,27,24,-6,'Subterranean River','  You are shoulder-deep in a swift underground river flowing through a chasm.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,30,8,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11429,26,25,-6,'Subterranean River','  You are shoulder-deep in a swift underground river flowing through a chasm.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,30,8,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11430,25,26,-6,'Subterranean River','  Your feet just touch the pebble-lined bottom of the bed of this underground\nriver, but the water is high enough to reach your shoulders.  The river extends\nupstream through a large grotto, and a long beach parallels the south bank.\nDownstream, the river flows into a large chasm with steep walls.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,30,8,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11431,31,22,-6,'Subterranean River','  You are shoulder-deep in a swift underground river flowing through a chasm.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,15,1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11432,32,22,-6,'Subterranean River','  You are shoulder-deep in a swift underground river flowing through a chasm.\nAlong the south side of the cavern it appears notches have been carved\ninto the rock almost like a ladder.  It would seem one could attempt\nto scale the wall to the bridge overhead.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,15,1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11433,33,22,-6,'Subterranean River','  All the water of the river disappears through a huge grating that is firmly\nset into a rock wall to the east.  You could haul yourself out of the water\nonto a beach of pebbles south, or swim back upstream to the west.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11434,33,22,-4,'Kobolds\' Barracks','  This is the part of the barracks reserved for the kobold force.  Kobolds\nhave no particularly bad habits to speak of, but simply cannot stand the\npersonal hygiene of the orcs.  They also live in mortal fear of an ogre\nbreaking wind, so they insist on their own partitioned place to rest and sleep.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11435,34,22,-4,'Orcs\' Barracks','  This is the largest barracks room, and it belongs to the orcs.  The orcs\nrefuse to associate with ogres on a non-military level, and while they have\nbeen heard to murmur about the company of \"one of those feeble little kobolds,\"\ntheir unusual and distinctive body odor always announces their presence\nbefore any compromising situation can develop.  In short, kobolds insist on\nseparate rooms and will have nothing to do with the orcs.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11436,35,22,-4,'Ogres\' Barracks','  This is the section of the barracks that is reserved for the ogres.  The\nogres are not adverse to sharing their beds with their comrades (in fact,\nthey are most eager to share with anyone who will acquiesce), but they quite\nliterally snore more loudly than Baeron, man of the mountain himself.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11437,39,23,-2,'Armory','  This is a makeshift armory.  The room is structurally sound and the\nsteel door stoutly mounted.  But oddly, there don\'t seem to be any weapons or\narmor here.  Perhaps you could donate some of your equipment to the cause;\njust leave it on the floor on your way out.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11438,24,27,-6,'Subterranean River','  You are in a swift moving subterranean river, flowing through a large grotto.\nThe water is high enough to reach your shoulders, but you may be able to\nreach a beach on the south bank.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,30,8,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11439,23,28,-6,'Subterranean River','  You are in a swift moving subterranean river, flowing through a large grotto.\nThe water is high enough to reach your shoulders, but you may be able to\nreach a beach on the south bank.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,30,8,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11440,22,29,-6,'Subterranean River','  You are in a swift moving subterranean river, flowing through a large grotto.\nThe water is high enough to reach your shoulders, but you may be able to\nreach a beach on the south bank.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,30,8,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11441,21,30,-6,'Subterranean River','  You are in a swift moving subterranean river, flowing through a large grotto.\nThe water is high enough to reach your shoulders, but you may be able to\nreach a beach on the south bank.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,30,8,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11442,21,30,-6,'Subterranean River','  You are in a swift moving subterranean river, flowing through a large grotto.\nThe water is high enough to reach your shoulders, but you may be able to\nreach a beach on the south bank.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,30,8,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11443,20,31,-6,'Subterranean River','  The water reaches your shoulders here, and you take this advantage to survey\nthe large grotto that extends far downstream.  A long beach parallels the\nriver along its south bank.\n',66,131080,29,0,0,0,30,8,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11444,19,33,-6,'Subterranean River','  You are totally submerged in an underground river which pulls you southward.\n',66,131080,30,0,0,0,30,2,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11445,19,34,-6,'Subterranean River','  You are totally submerged in an underground river which pulls you southward.\n',66,131080,30,0,0,0,30,2,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11446,20,33,-5,'A Stream in Arden','  This is a deep pool fed by the stream inflow from the east.  High banks\nborder the pool in all other directions, but the north and south banks seem\nto offer enough handholds for you to pull yourself out of the water.  You feel\na strong suction at your feet.\n',66,131076,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11447,19,31,-6,'Subterranean Beach','  This beach parallels the underground river that flows through the grotto.  The\nsand is comprised of fine white sand interspersed with small pebbles.  Strange\nthin tracks are patterned across and down the beach.\n',66,131080,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11448,20,30,-6,'Subterranean Beach','  This beach parallels the underground river that flows through the grotto.  The\nsand is comprised of fine white sand interspersed with small pebbles.  Strange\nthin tracks are patterned across and down the beach.\n',66,131080,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11449,21,29,-6,'Subterranean Beach','  This beach parallels the underground river that flows through the grotto.  The\nsand is comprised of fine white sand interspersed with small pebbles.  Strange\nthin tracks are patterned across and down the beach.\n',66,131080,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11450,21,29,-6,'Subterranean Beach','  This beach parallels the underground river that flows through the grotto.  The\nsand is comprised of fine white sand interspersed with small pebbles.  A huge\npile of bones and rotting matter sits in the center of the beach here, like\nleftovers from a gruesome meal.\n',66,131080,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11451,23,27,-6,'Subterranean Beach','  This beach parallels the underground river that flows through the grotto.  The\nsand is comprised of fine white sand interspersed with small pebbles.  Strange\nthin tracks are patterned across and up the beach.\n',66,131080,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11452,23,27,-6,'Subterranean Beach','  This beach parallels the underground river that flows through the grotto.  The\nsand is comprised of fine white sand interspersed with small pebbles.  Strange\nthin tracks are patterned across and up the beach.\n',66,131080,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11453,24,26,-7,'Hole in the Sand','  You are standing in a hole in the sandy beach.\n',66,131080,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11454,32,22,-5,'Over the Chasm on a Ladder','  If not for the carved ladder in the south wall you would fall to\nthe turbulent waters below.  The safety of a bridge can be seen just\nto the west or you can navigate the ladder downwards.\n',66,131080,35,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11455,30,22,-5,'Over the Chasm','  You have stepped off the bridge and into the freedom of the air.  For just a\na moment, you contemplate an avian lifestyle - carefree, unlimited by the\nshackles of the earth, but then you notice the turbulent waters far below and\nsnap back into reality.\n',66,131080,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11456,37,15,-2,'South Fork of the Mine','  This is the south fork of what must be an abandoned mine.  The walls have\nbeen ravaged with horrid tears and gouges from the attempts to harvest\nvaluable minerals and gems.  Sometime recently, however, someone has buttressed\nup the walls and ceiling with new timber supports.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11457,38,15,-2,'South Fork of the Mine','  This is the south fork of what must be an abandoned mine.  The walls have\nbeen ravaged with horrid tears and gouges from the attempts to harvest\nvaluable minerals and gems.  Sometime recently, however, someone has buttressed\nup the walls and ceiling with new timber supports.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11458,37,14,-2,'South Fork of the Mine','  This is the south fork of what must be an abandoned mine.  The walls have\nbeen ravaged with horrid tears and gouges from the attempts to harvest\nvaluable minerals and gems.  Sometime recently, however, someone has buttressed\nup the walls and ceiling with new timber supports.  A strange glowing hall\nleads south.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11459,40,16,-2,'South Fork of the Mine','  This is the south fork of what must be an abandoned mine.  The walls have\nbeen ravaged with horrid tears and gouges from the attempts to harvest\nvaluable minerals and gems.  Sometime recently, however, someone has buttressed\nup the walls and ceiling with new timber supports.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11460,41,16,-2,'South Fork of the Mine','  This is the south fork of what must be an abandoned mine.  The walls have\nbeen ravaged with horrid tears and gouges from the attempts to harvest\nvaluable minerals and gems.  Sometime recently, however, someone has buttressed\nup the walls and ceiling with new timber supports.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11461,40,15,-2,'South Fork of the Mine','  This is the south fork of what must be an abandoned mine.  The walls have\nbeen ravaged with horrid tears and gouges from the attempts to harvest\nvaluable minerals and gems.  Sometime recently, however, someone has buttressed\nup the walls and ceiling with new timber supports.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11462,41,16,-2,'South Fork of the Mine','  This is the south fork of what must be an abandoned mine.  The walls have\nbeen ravaged with horrid tears and gouges from the attempts to harvest\nvaluable minerals and gems.  Sometime recently, however, someone has buttressed\nup the walls and ceiling with new timber supports.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11463,44,18,-2,'South Fork of the Mine','  This is the south fork of what must be an abandoned mine.  The walls have\nbeen ravaged with horrid tears and gouges from the attempts to harvest\nvaluable minerals and gems.  Sometime recently, however, someone has buttressed\nup the walls and ceiling with new timber supports.  To the east, the cavern\nhas completely collapsed, preventing movement in that direction.  A\nrelatively new tunnel leads north.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11464,41,15,-2,'Medic\'s Room','  This room is where the battle-weary and the injured seek aid to their\ninjuries.  After a hard day of scouting, marauding and looting, the invading\nforces must insure they can repeat their activities on the next by keeping\nin good health.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11465,39,15,-2,'Glowing Passage','  You are in a strange, glowing passage.  You can hear a slight humming rise\nand fall in pitch in concert with the intensity of the light.  The glow itself\nseems to emanate from beyond the ethereal surface of the walls.\n',66,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11466,40,15,-2,'Glowing Passage','   You are in a strange, glowing passage.  You can hear a slight humming rise\nand fall in pitch in concert with the intensity of the light.  The glow itself\nseems to emanate from beyond the ethereal surface of the walls.\n',66,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11467,40,14,-2,'Study of the Magus','  This room is glowing with an ethereal light.  There are manuals and books\non magic usage and conjuring lying about.  The air smells of an acrid smoke\nand a strong ozone; the hair on your arms stands straight up and salutes.\nObviously this is a room of powerful magic, perhaps you\'d think twice about\ntangling with its master.\n',66,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11468,44,19,-2,'Access Tunnel','  This is a long, straight tunnel.  Judging by the condition of the wall\nsupports, it was only recently excavated.  Nearby to the south the passage\ndead ends into another tunnel, and far to the north you can see a large\ncorridor.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11469,44,20,-2,'Access Tunnel','  This is a long, straight tunnel.  Judging by the condition of the wall\nsupports, it was only recently excavated.  The tunnel exits into other\npassages at both ends.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11470,44,21,-2,'Access Tunnel','  This is a long, straight tunnel.  Judging by the condition of the wall\nsupports, it was only recently excavated.  Nearby to the north it joins up\nwith a large passage, and a ways to the south you can see it terminate into\nanother corridor.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11471,44,22,-2,'Access Tunnel','  This is a long, straight tunnel.  Judging by the condition of the wall\nsupports, it was only recently excavated.  Far in the distance to the south,\nyou can see it dead-end into another tunnel, and immediately north is\nanother perpendicular passage.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11472,42,18,-1,'Inside the Pile','  This is a small hollow inside a huge pile of rubble and debris.  It\'s nice\nand warm in here, and it occurs to you that it would be an ideal hideout for\nthose who would ambush travelers through this area.  A large wooden post\nwedged into the pile controls access in and out of the hollow.\n',66,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11473,25,20,-4,'Orc Magi\'s Cave','  Set into the mountain side this little niche of a cave is surprisingly\nwarm.  From floor to ceiling and sometimes even on the floor and ceiling\nthemselves magical runes and notes can be seen.  Several different\nwooden benches and tables have been anchored into the walls and on many\nof them are the ghastly remains of experiments.  High overhead you can\njust make out a pinpoint of light which must be a tiny natural cavern\nwhich vents the smokes from the many small fires about the room.  The\nonly exit from the room appears to be a tiny concealable door in the\nsoutheast wall.\n',78,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11800,0,0,0,'A Small Office',' This is a fairly small room.  Its ceiling was probably at one\ntime fully vaulted but now due to what took place here in\nGrimhaven, the aftershocks have brought down timbers from the\nabove rooms that spear through the ceiling.  A single faded and\ntorn banner hangs down the center of this room.  The stone floor\nand stone walls have large gouges.  An archway leads out to the east.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11801,0,0,0,'An Entryway',' It would seem that this is some sort of entryway.  The stone walls and\nstone floor have splintered and cracked as if lightning struck this very\nsite.  To the south, a hallway stretches deeper into the shabby building.\nThere is an archway to the west, and a cave-in to the north you can make\nout the faint outline of where a door once was.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11802,0,0,0,'A Hallway',' The dusty hallway runs in all directions here.  Whatever force shook the\nearth, it was strong enough to uplift the stone floor and crack it easily.\nLarge roots pierce through the cracks in the floor.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11803,0,0,0,'Mess Hall',' You are in the north-east corner of a huge mess hall.  Rows of wooden tables\nand chairs once stood here from what you recall, now all that remains are\npiles of timber.  To the west, a small archway leads out of this room.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11804,0,0,0,'A Cracked Hallway',' A dull cracked hallway turns here from the north to the west.  In the\nsouthwest corner of this room a faded banner still hangs on the wall.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11805,0,0,0,'Metal Stairway','  The wooden floor below you has been weakend by what ever force took place\nhere in Grimhaven.  Fastened to the stone walls, the staircase trembles as\nyou set foot on it.  Glancing upwards you can see a cave-in has occurred\nleaving the entrance unusable.  Downward leads into a darkend pit.  To the\neast a hallway is seen.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11806,0,0,0,'Mess Hall',' You are in the north-east corner of a huge mess hall.  Rows of wooden tables\nand chairs once stood here from what you recall, now all that remains are\npiles of timber.  To the west, a small archway leads out of this room.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11807,0,0,0,'Mess Hall',' You are in the north-east corner of a huge mess hall.  Rows of wooden tables\nand chairs once stood here from what you recall, now all that remains are\npiles of timber.  To the west, a small archway leads out of this room.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11808,0,0,0,'Mess Hall',' You are in the north-east corner of a huge mess hall.  Rows of wooden tables\nand chairs once stood here from what you recall, now all that remains are\npiles of timber.  To the west, a small archway leads out of this room.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11809,0,0,0,'Cobwebed Kitchen','  Foul odors insult your taste buds as you survey this cobwebed scene.\nAlthough its quite apparent that this room was used as a kitchen, you find it\ndisgusting to think that someone at one time actually ate the food that was\ncreated here.  Basically, the place is filthy.  To the south, an archway leads\nout.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11810,0,0,0,'A Small Bedroom',' This bedroom is covered in dust and broken gizmos.  East provides a means of\nescape from this clutter.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11811,0,0,0,'A Office',' This small room was used as someone\'s office at one time.  You can tell\nthe stone floor was thick at one time, it has been uprooted by a strong force.\nTo the north, an archway provides an exit.  To the south another pathway is\nseen.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11812,0,0,0,'Training Yard',' This was the Warrior training yard, which is surrounded by a broken wooden\nfence.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11813,0,0,0,'A Narrow Hallway',' This short, north-south hallway is quite narrow.  It runs from a high\narchway to the north.  The floor has been uprooted and has broken off in\nseveral pieces.  To the east, you can see an office of some sort.  To the west\nanother pathway is seen.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11814,0,0,0,'A Small Latrine',' This is a small, <g>moldy<1> latrine.  You are overwhelmed by the\nstench of this place.  It seems all of the city uses this latrine daily.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11815,0,0,0,'A Small Office',' This is a small office with cracked stone walls and an uprooted floor.  An\nexit to the west leads back to a hallway.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11816,0,0,0,'Bottom of a Stairwell',' You are at the bottom of a metal stairwell, which stretches into the\ndarkness above.  The stone floor here is cracked, and degrades into\ndirt as a tunnel stretches to the east.\n',80,131084,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11817,0,0,0,'A Dirt-walled Tunnel',' You are inside a dirt-walled tunnel, which runs from east to west.  The\nwalls and ceiling are held up by wooden support beams that are quite old.\nTo the south, a small side tunnel juts off into darkness.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11818,0,0,0,'A Dirt-walled Tunnel',' You are inside a narrow, dirt-walled tunnel.  The walls and ceiling are\nsupported by ancient wooden beams.  There is an archway where the tunnel\nends to the east and a cell to the south.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11819,0,0,0,'An Armory',' It\'s quite clear this room is used as an armory.  Death Knights and other\nofficials use this room as a means of storage as well.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11820,0,0,0,'A Dull Cell',' This is a cold cell.  The walls are cracked and dull grey in color.  Since\ntheres no use for prisoners, the cell door has been removed.  Dried blood\npermeates the splintery rock crevices.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11821,0,0,0,'A Damp, Musty Tunnel',' You are inside a damp, musty tunnel which runs from the north to the south.\nThe tunnel floor is rather muddy here, and you can smell human waste nearby.  A\nwooden archway leads to the west, while the tunnel another leads south.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11822,0,0,0,'Crypt',' This is a small crypt housed for the undead.  The dirt floor is covered\nwith junk, while the walls and support beams are rotting away and caving in.\nA wooden archway leads out to the east.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11823,0,0,0,'A Damp, Musty Tunnel',' You are inside a damp, musty tunnel which runs from the north to the south.\nThe tunnel floor is rather muddy here, and you can smell human waste nearby.\nTrails of fresh blood lead in all directions.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11824,0,0,0,'Crypt',' This is a small crypt housed for the undead.  The dirt floor is covered\nwith junk, while the walls and support beams are rotting away and starting to\ncave-in.  A wooden archway leads out to the west.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11825,0,0,0,'Crypt',' This is a small crypt housed for the undead.  The dirt floor is covered\nwith junk, while the walls and support beams are rotting away and starting to\ncave-in.  A wooden archway leads out to the east.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11826,0,0,0,'Crypt',' This is a small crypt housed for the undead.  The dirt floor is covered\nwith junk, while the walls and support beams are rotting away and starting to\ncave-in.  A wooden archway leads out to the east.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11827,0,0,0,'A Damp, Musty Tunnel',' You are inside a damp, musty tunnel which runs from the north to the south.\nThe tunnel floor is rather muddy here, and you can smell human waste nearby.\nTrails of fresh blood lead in all directions.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11828,0,0,0,'Crypt',' This is a small crypt housed for the undead.  The dirt floor is covered\nwith junk, while the walls and support beams are rotting away and starting to\ncave-in.  A wooden archway leads out to the west.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11829,0,0,0,'Vampires Retreat',' If ever there was a remnant of Grimhaven, this splotched room would be it.\nVarious portraits of the Arch Vampire himself hang off the discolored walls.\nThe ground is a sandy <R>russet<1> color, probably imported from an unholy\nplace.  The pillars of wood used to support this room have been recently\nreplaced with new ones.  You can\'t imagine that the Arch Vampire could live in\nsuch a small room or even accustomed to sharing his crypt with others.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11830,0,0,0,'Hospital Waiting Room',' You are in the Hospital waiting room.  There was a small stairway here that\nlead up to the second floor, it has collapsed to the ground.  A hallway leads\neast into a hallway.  A stone statue sits here.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11831,0,0,0,'Hospital',' This is an intersection leading through the hospital.  Stone arrows and\nlong shafted stone spears pierce and decorate the walls around you.  You can\ngo east into the Examination Room, southeast into the Operating Room, or\nsouth into the Intensive Care Unit.  To the north a small opening is seen.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11832,0,0,0,'Intensive Care Room',' Perhaps at one time long ago the people of Grimhaven came here to heal their\nwounds when other clerical means failed.  What now seems this hospital is made\nfor is for death swiftly and painlessly.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11833,0,0,0,'Supply Room',' You find yourself standing in a small supply room, which is more like a\nlarge closet.  There is very little in the way of supplies here, except\nfor some rotted linens stacked up on dusty shelves.  The only exit is back\nsouth.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11834,0,0,0,'Operating Room',' Long gone are of the days when the Grimhaven Doctor cured the people of this\ncity.  What lives here now is what no man should face alone.  A putrid smell\ncomes from a pool of thick <g>green residue<1> thats used as a well for the\nthe mistress that crawls these dark corridors.  Four white marble pillars\nbrace the ceiling for support.  The air is dry and stale.\n',80,135176,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11835,0,0,0,'Examination Room',' Upon entering this room your heart stands still.  Cosmos and worlds swirl\nthrough the very threshold you have stepped upon!  Space fills itself with\nnebulae, shooting stars and black holes that flow by you as a slow moving\nriver would carry a leaf.  Your head spins with excitement and terror tearing\nat your sense of logic.\n',80,164017,60,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11836,0,0,0,'Short Hallway',' You are standing in a dark musty hallway that runs north-south.  An eerie\nslithering sound echoes north and south of you.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11837,0,0,0,'Entrance to the Health Spa',' The walls in this entryway are covered with black draperies.  You smell a\nfaint sense of incense, putrid.  There is a small opening to the north.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11838,0,0,0,'Dressing Room',' This room has broken benches on either side of the room.  This room was used\nwhere one could store his or her clothing before entering the sauna which\nstill lies to the north.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11839,0,0,0,'Sauna',' This room is cold and damp.  The cold rising from the floor chills your\nbones.  Your nostrils with the aroma of incense, made from rotting flesh.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11840,0,0,0,'Alchemist Room',' A wide array of colored glass lie shattered at your feet.  The tidy shelves\nthat once lined this room now lie refuse to small rodents.  Small crates\ntoppled over along the northern wall is filled with personable items that once\nbelonged to the alchemist.  It seems at least some warning was given that\nallowed the shop keeper to prepair for before the catastrophe you see\naround you.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11841,0,0,0,'Entry Hall',' This north-south passage connects the entry way with the rest of the academy.\nWhat ever magic was saved during the catastrophe it was enough to keep the\nacademy magically lit.\n',80,131085,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11842,0,0,0,'Secretary Station',' This was the office of the Mage\'s secretary.  The walls on the east and west\nare filled with sketches of all the great mystic\'s who ran this academy.  It\namazes you that the academy still stands as you remembered it.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11843,0,0,0,'Intersection',' You are at an intersection.  Hallways go north, south, east, and west from\nhere.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11844,0,0,0,'Narrow Hallway',' This hallway runs east-west and is in poor shape.  It is probably so worn\ndown from the numerous students that once ran here to their classes.  There\nis a classroom to the south.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11845,0,0,0,'Turn in the Hallway',' The hallway turns from east to north here.  Strange smells waft in from the\nnorth.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11846,0,0,0,'Passageway',' This passage runs north-south.  The walls here have been inscribed with\nmystical runes that emit with a soft glow.  The passageway is extremely\nwell built and solid.  There is an archway to the west leading to a small\nlaboratory.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11847,0,0,0,'Laboratory',' This lab from what you recall had several work tables but only one is seen\nhere.  There are broken bottles scattered all over the room.  A pool of water\nis in the center of the room has a mystical vapor rising through the air.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11848,0,0,0,'Passageway',' This passage runs north-south.  The walls here have been inscribed with\nmystical runes that emit with a soft glow.  The passageway is extremely\nwell built and solid.  There is an archway to the west and to the north.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11849,0,0,0,'Laboratory',' This lab is scattered with debris and refuse.  There are broken bottles\nscattered all over the room.  A firepit in the center of the room burns\nfiery-red.  The walls show many scorch marks upon them.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11850,0,0,0,'Alchemist\'s Office',' This was the office of the head alchemist.  Faded portraits and grim covered\nclothing lie in a mass heap here.  It appears the alchemist made haste here\nand left his belongings behind.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11851,0,0,0,'Classroom',' This classroom is barren yet still the air seems unnaturally charged.  The\nseating for the students that once filled this room have been reduced to dust.\nA few tiny specks of metal catch your eye amidst the rubble here.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11852,0,0,0,'Hallway',' This hallway extends north, south and west.  There is a large sign on the\neast wall written in the Common Language.  A walkway leads south into a\nclassroom.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11853,0,0,0,'Classroom',' This classroom is barren yet still the room seems unnaturally charged.  The\nseating for the students that once filled this room have been reduced to dust.\nA few tiny specks of metal catch your eye amidst the rubble here.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11854,0,0,0,'Hallway','  This east-west hallway is slightly warmer than other parts of this hall.  To\nthe south is a classroom.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11855,0,0,0,'Classroom',' This classroom is unusual, yet still the room seems unnaturally charged.\nStrange pillars of rock, much like stalagmites surround a heap of dust where\nthe students chairs once sat.  There is a large chart on the south wall and\nsoil and dirt has been scattered across the floor.  A few tiny specks of metal\ncatch your eye amidst the rubble here.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11856,0,0,0,'Grand Hallway',' This Grand Hallway runs north and south.  A minor hall runs east from here.\nTo the south is some sort of waiting room.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11857,0,0,0,'Receptionist Chamber',' This room was a waiting area for those who wished to seek the Head Mage of\nGrimhaven.  There is an archway to the south with a small sign on it.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11858,0,0,0,'Head Mage\'s Chamber',' This was the chamber of the famous Head Mage of Grimhaven.  It was well known\nthat this mage had instructed more pupils than any other mage in the land.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11859,0,0,0,'Grand Hallway',' This plush hallway runs north-south.  The carpeting is very worn from all\nthe students who had traveled this hall many times when class was called.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11860,0,0,0,'Narrow Hallway',' This plush hallway runs north-south.  The carpeting is very worn from all\nthe students who had traveled this hall when classes were called.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11861,0,0,0,'Grand Hallway',' This plush hallway runs north-south.  The carpeting is very worn\nfrom all of the students that once traveled it.  There is a small\nlibrary to the east.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11862,0,0,0,'Small Library',' This library is completely in ruins.  Bookcases have been toppled over and\nvandalized.  Only a handful of leather bound books that have managed to\nsurvive what ever took place here lie on the ground.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11863,0,0,0,'Small Library',' This library is completely in ruins.  Bookcases have been toppled over and\nvandalized.  Only a handful of leather bound books that have managed to\nsurvive what ever took place here lie on the ground.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11864,0,0,0,'Grand Hallway',' This plush hallway runs north-south.  The carpeting is very worn from all of\nthe students that once traveled it.  A small storage area is to the north.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11865,0,0,0,'Storage Area',' This is a part of the Academy that was often used for storage.  Cobwebs and\njunk litters the ground.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11866,0,0,0,'Entryway To Palace',' You are standing under a large stone archway.  There is a pathway to the\nnorth and a plush lawn to the south.  The palace looms over you casting an\neerie shadow on you.  It looks like the palace took much of the damage when\nthe catastrophe hit, much of its stonewalls have either crumbled or fallen.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11867,0,0,0,'Palace Foyer',' This is a large dusty foyer with faded chipped murals on the ceiling.\nAn alcove leads to the west.  There is a small pathway to the east and a\npassage to the north.  Another path leads south to the Entryway.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11868,0,0,0,'Back Passage',' This room is small and cramped.  You see a stairway going down to the north.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11869,0,0,0,'Top of Staircase',' You are standing at the top of a unstable staircase.  It seems to be darker\nbelow you.  Something stirs from the depths of the staircase for a moment,\nwhat follows is an unsettling silence.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11870,0,0,0,'Alcove',' This tiny alcove is completely dark, and quite small.  There is a small\nport hole in the west wall and a passage to the east leading to the foyer.\nAnother passage leads north.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11871,0,0,0,'Staircase',' You are at the base of a large staircase.  There are several cloak-hooks on\nthe west and east walls.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11872,0,0,0,'Entrance Hall',' This is a musty long hallway leading through the palace.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11873,0,0,0,'Dining Room',' This room is a large unused dining area.  The highlight of the room is a\nlarge cobwebed infested oaken dining table in the center of the room.  A\ndangling swinging door rest lazily on the ground to the east.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11874,0,0,0,'Servant\'s Quarters',' This room looks like it was used for housing a few servants.\nLong moth eaten aprons still hang on wooden dowels here.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11875,0,0,0,'Kitchen',' This kitchen has not been used in quite some time.  Large cracks and\nblood stains mar the walls.  Broken plates that were probably expensive at\nonce time lie shattered at your feet.  You can imagine all the good food\nthat was prepared here at one time.  There lingers the smell of the dead\nhere now.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11876,0,0,0,'The Business Office','  This was once the main business office for the palace.  It looks like it\nhas been plundered.  Many of the crates have been torn open or left to\nrot.  There is not much decoration to the room except for a faded\npicture of the King\'s father hanging prominently on the wall.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11877,0,0,0,'Bottom of Staircase',' You are at the bottom of a staircase.  It is damp and smells of mold\ndown here.\n',80,139628,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11878,0,0,0,'Dark Passage',' This passage leads west and north.  At one time this passage served the\nguards with a place of rest when the Captain of the Guard wandered the\ncompound\'s making sure all was well in Grimhaven.  In days long past even\nthe royal subjects used these corridors to meet with scrupulous scum to\nplot out devious deeds.  Even lovers that were never meant to be lavished\nlustfully in their infidelities down here.  Every sense of emotion or\naction of sin can best describe these stone walls.  An iron circle is\nseen here on the ground.\n',80,139624,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11879,0,0,0,'Dark Passage',' At one time this passage served the guards with a place of rest when the\nCaptain of the Guard wandered the compound\'s making sure all was well in\nGrimhaven.  In days long past even the royal subjects used these corridors\nto meet with scrupulous scum to plot out devious deeds.  Even lovers that\nwere never meant to be lavished lustfully in their infidelities down here.\nEvery sense of emotion or action of sin can best describe these stone\nwalls.\n',80,139624,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11880,0,0,0,'Main Passage',' A strong sense of evil flows through you here.  Its grip is chilling\nunlike nothing you\'ve ever felt before.  Something tragic must have\nhappend here to generate such a feeling that has taken root in your bones.\nThe passageway runs north-south on a paved stone floor.  Another iron\ncircle is seen here on the ground.\n',80,143849,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11881,0,0,0,'Dark Passage',' At one time this passage served the guards with a place of rest when the\nCaptain of the Guard wandered the compound\'s making sure all was well in\nGrimhaven.  In days long past even the royal subjects used these corridors\nto meet with scrupulous scum to plot out devious deeds.  Even lovers that\nwere never meant to be lavished lustfully in their infidelities down here.\n',80,139624,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11882,0,0,0,'Wine Cellar',' This is where the wine and ale were kept.  You can still tell from the\nodor that overcomes you.  There is a empty wine rack on the east wall.\n',80,139624,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11883,0,0,0,'Corridor',' This corridor is full of dust and dirt.  There are footprints on the\nfloor.\n',80,139560,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11884,0,0,0,'Storage Hold',' This area once held lots of equipment, crates, and bottles.  You can tell\na door once stood here that leads north back into the corridor.\n',80,139624,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11885,0,0,0,'Cheese Room',' This is the room in which the royal cheese is stored.  It smells of mold\nand mouse droppings.\n',80,139560,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11886,0,0,0,'Road Through Park',' The hillside flourished with vegetation at one time.  A blanket of ash\ncovers the ground all around you.  Now that the park has been burned to\nthe ground, you can view its surroundings easily.  Dragon tracks can be\nseen here.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11887,0,0,0,'Road Through Park',' The ground is deep with black ash.  To the south you notice a small piece\nof wood sticking out of the ground.  Dragon tracks lead in all directions.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11888,0,0,0,'Northwest Corner',' An ancient Elm tree amazingly still stands here amidst the smoldering\nash.  What ever magic the tree retains was strong enough to resist the\nflames that devoured the park around you.  The heat here is more intense\nas if a dragon unleashed its mighty breath seconds before your arrival.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11889,0,0,0,'Road Through Park',' The scent of not only ash but death and decay carries swiftly on the\nwinds.  The park has been consumed in flames leaving only a layer of deep\nash for you to travel on.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11890,0,0,0,'Broken Down Cabin',' A large piece of wood jagged and scorched stands upright within the thick\nash ground.  You gather this piece of wood was part of the cabin that\nstood here at one time.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11891,0,0,0,'Playground',' A blanket of ash covers the ground all around you.  Now that the park has\nbeen burned to the ground, you can view its surroundings easily.  Dragon\ntracks can be seen here.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11892,0,0,0,'Broken Down Cabin',' A large piece of wood jagged and scorched stands upright within the thick\nash ground.  You gather this piece of wood was part of the cabin that\nstood here at one time.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11893,0,0,0,'Road Through the Park',' A blanket of ash covers the ground all around you.  Now that the park has\nbeen burned to the ground, you can view its surroundings easily.  Dragon\ntracks can be seen here.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11894,0,0,0,'Cobblestone Path',' The cobblestone is completely invisible under thick layered ash, yet you\ncan still feel them beneath your footing.  Pathways lead in all\ndirections.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11895,0,0,0,'Cobblestone Path',' The cobblestone is completely invisible under thick layered ash, yet you\ncan still feel them beneath your footing.  It seems dragons are not the\nonly living creatures thriving here.  You can tell something has been\nburrowing in the ash.  Small rows of lines formed along the ashy pathways\nlead in all directions.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11896,0,0,0,'Cobblestone Path',' The cobblestone is completely invisible under thick layered ash, yet you\ncan still feel them beneath your footing.  It seems dragons are not the\nonly living creatures thriving here.  You can tell something has been\nburrowing in the ash.  Small rows of lines formed along the ashy pathways\nlead in all directions.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11897,0,0,0,'Cobblestone Path',' The cobblestone is completely invisible under thick layered ash, yet you\ncan still feel them beneath your footing.  It seems dragons are not the\nonly living creatures thriving here.  You can tell something has been\nburrowing in the ash.  Small rows of lines formed along the ashy pathways\nlead in all directions.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11898,0,0,0,'Northeast Corner',' The cobblestone is completely invisible under thick layered ash, yet you\ncan still feel them beneath your footing.  It seems dragons are not the\nonly living creatures thriving here.  You can tell something has been\nburrowing in the ash.  Small rows of lines formed along the ashy pathways\nlead in all directions.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11899,0,0,0,'Southwest Corner',' A blanket of ash covers the ground all around you.  Now that the park has\nbeen burned to the ground, you can view its surroundings easily.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11900,0,0,0,'Mallards Rest',' Once long ago lady Jezebel Mallard\'s name echoed throughout the realm\nwhen L\'yrel first appeared before the people of Grimhaven.  It was here,\nbesides a willow tree the once grew here that her body was buried by a bed\nof wildflowers.  All that remains here now is an ashy pathway.  How\nironic.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11901,0,0,0,'Cobblestone Path',' The park has been reduced to ash.  Beneath your footing you can still\nfeel the hard cobblestones leading through the park.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11902,0,0,0,'Cobblestone Path',' The park has been reduced to ash.  Beneath your footing you can still\nfeel the hard cobblestones leading through the park.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11903,0,0,0,'Cobblestone Path',' The park has been reduced to ash.  Beneath your footing you can still\nfeel the hard cobblestones leading through the park.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11904,0,0,0,'Cobblestone Path',' The park has been reduced to ash.  Beneath your footing you can still\nfeel the hard cobblestones leading through the park.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11905,0,0,0,'Southeast Corner','  You\'ve come to the southeast end of the park.  Several large Oak trees,\nstill stand here encircling a small glass gazebo.  A powerful spell must\nhave been placed here by the rangers before their demise.  The trees\nthemselves are not as old as the Elm tree that stands in the northwest\ncorner but almost as old.\n',80,131076,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11906,0,0,0,'Gazebo',' Ferns, violets and birds of paradise fill the rooms interior.  Creeping\nvines work outward and upward along the walls and ceiling.  Its plant\nlife, although cluttered, makes the gazebo seem like a dark silent jungle.\nCentered upon a golden anvil rest a crystal figure of a winged dragon.\n',80,131085,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11907,0,0,0,'Cobblestone Path',' The park has been reduced to ash.  Beneath your footing you can still\nfeel the hard cobblestones leading through the park.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11908,0,0,0,'Cobblestone Path',' The park has been reduced to ash.  Beneath your footing you can still\nfeel the hard cobblestones leading through the park.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11909,0,0,0,'Cobblestone Path',' The park has been reduced to ash.  Beneath your footing you can still\nfeel the hard cobblestones leading through the park.\n',80,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(11910,0,0,0,'Theater Entrance',' You are standing in the lobby of a haunted looking theater.  A torn faded\nred carpet extends to the north and south.\n',80,131084,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11911,0,0,0,'Theater Lobby',' You are standing in the lobby of a haunted looking theater.  A passageway\nleads to the east deeper into the theater.  To the south, a large\nstaircase landing sits.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11912,0,0,0,'Staircase Landing',' You are at the bottom of a wide staircase.  Above you, you can see that a\ncave-in blocks your way up.  The railing on the staircase is made of\nthick, white marble which has been severed in three places.  Dust and the\nstench only the dead carry wafts through the air.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11913,0,0,0,'Theater Seats',' A row of theater seats is seen here.  The seats are covered in blood and\na dozen fully clothed skeletons have been positioned in them.  A shabby\nfaded carpet leads through the rows of seats towards center stage and\ncomes to rest before the orchestra pit.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11914,0,0,0,'Theater Seats',' A row of theater seats is seen here.  The seats are covered in blood and\na dozen fully clothed skeletons have been positioned in them.  A shabby\nfaded carpet leads through the rows of seats towards center stage and\ncomes to rest before the orchestra pit.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11915,0,0,0,'Theater Aisle',' This aisle slopes downward from west to east at a slight angle.  The\naisle extends from the lobby all the way down to a cobwebed stage.  You\nsee velvet seats to the left and right as you face the stage, many of\nwhich has skeleton remains still seated in them.  You can\'t help but think\nthat these poor souls who died, died while watching a performance the\ntheater was giving at the time.  Immediately to the east is the stage.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11916,0,0,0,'Theater Seats',' A row of theater seats is seen here.  The seats are covered in blood and\na dozen fully clothed skeletons have been positioned in them.  A shabby\nfaded carpet leads through the rows of seats towards center stage and\ncomes to rest before the orchestra pit.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11917,0,0,0,'Stage Left',' You are standing on a worn cobwebed stage.  The floor here is made of\nthick wooden boards, in some places you can see where mice have gnawed\nthrough the wood.  A few drops of dried faded paint can be seen on floor.\nAs you look to the west, you see the ghastly skeletons seated in their\nseats.  To the south, you see a small opening where the performers make\ntheir dramatic entrances.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11918,0,0,0,'Off Stage',' You are just off-stage.  There is a opening to the north that leads to\nstage left.  To the east you see a small dressing room.  To the northeast,\nyou see backstage.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11919,0,0,0,'Dressing Room','  This is where the performers came to prepare their appearance for\ntheater.  The room is small and still smells of cosmetics.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11920,0,0,0,'Backstage',' This cluttered passage is where once the hustle and bustle of the\nperformance arts was most strained.  There are various props and sets\nleaning up against the wall covered in dust and cobwebs.  To the\nsouth, you see a small dressing room.  To the north is the prop room.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11921,0,0,0,'Prop Room',' This is where the props were stored between performances.  Most of the\nprops are in large, wooden boxes with some canvas back-drops leaning up\nagainst the walls.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11922,0,0,0,'Storage Room',' This room appears to be a storage room for many sets and props that did\nnot fit in the prop room.  To the south you see the prop room.  To the\nnorth is a green room.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11923,0,0,0,'The Green Room',' This room is colored green, and has several chairs strewn about.  This\nis where the performers sit, while awaiting their entrance.  To the south\nyou see a bunch of props.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11924,0,0,0,'Off Stage',' You are just off-stage.  There is an opening to the south that\nleads to a stage right.  To the east, you see a small waiting area.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11925,0,0,0,'Stage Right',' You are standing on a worn cobwebed stage.  The floor here is made of\nthick wooden boards, in some places you can see where mice have gnawed\nthrough the wood.  A few drops of dried faded paint can be seen on floor.\nAs you look to the west, you see the ghastly skeletons seated in their\nseats.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11926,0,0,0,'Center Stage',' You are standing on center stage of the theater.  The floorboards here\nhave rotted away leaving only a single plank of wood to stand upon.\nGlancing out into the audience, you can see the ghastly expressions\nof the skeletons that are seated in the theater.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11927,0,0,0,'Theater Lobby',' You are standing in the theater lobby.  At one time this theater\nrepresented the best performances anywhere, now what remains is a\nrun down shack housed for the spirits that wander these halls.\nAn entryway can be seen east that leads to the theater.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11928,0,0,0,'Staircase Landing',' A large dusty marble staircase is here.  All that remains of it\nare large chipped chunks of marble that once lead up to the room\nabove.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11929,0,0,0,'Theater Aisle',' This aisle slopes downward from west to east at a slight angle.  The\naisle extends from the lobby all the way down to a cobwebed stage.  You\nsee velvet seats to the left and right as you face the stage, many of\nwhich has skeleton remains still seated in them.  You can\'t help but think\nthat these poor souls who died, died while watching a performance the\ntheater was giving at the time.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11930,0,0,0,'Theater Seats','  The best seats in the theater can be found right where you\'re standing.\nThough the theater hasn\'t been used in ages the seats still retain\nthe soft velvet feel.  There are only a handful of rotted corpses\nsitting in these seats, from their attire you gather that they\nmust have been important people at one time.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11931,0,0,0,'Theater Seats','  The best seats in the theater can be found right where you\'re standing.\nThough the theater hasn\'t been used in ages the seats still retain\nthe soft velvet feel.  There are only a handful of rotted corpses\nsitting in these seats, from their attire you gather that they\nmust have been important people at one time.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11932,0,0,0,'Theater Seats','  The best seats in the theater can be found right where you\'re standing.\nThough the theater hasn\'t been used in ages the seats still retain\nthe soft velvet feel.  There are only a handful of rotted corpses\nsitting in these seats, from their attire you gather that they\nmust have been important people at one time.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11933,0,0,0,'Theater Seats','  The best seats in the theater can be found right where you\'re standing.\nThough the theater hasn\'t been used in ages the seats still retain\nthe soft velvet feel.  There are only a handful of rotted corpses\nsitting in these seats, from their attire you gather that they\nmust have been important people at one time.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11934,0,0,0,'Theater Seats','  The best seats in the theater can be found right where you\'re standing.\nThough the theater hasn\'t been used in ages the seats still retain\nthe soft velvet feel.  There are only a handful of rotted corpses\nsitting in these seats, from their attire you gather that they\nmust have been important people at one time.\n',80,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11935,0,0,0,'A Slot Machine',' You are at a large broken dust covered slot machine.\nA large stool is in front of the machine.  Hairline cracks\ntravel along the surface of the walls, they crumble\nat your touch.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11936,0,0,0,'A Slot Machine',' You are at a large broken dust covered slot machine.\nA large stool is in front of the machine.  Hairline cracks\ntravel along the surface of the walls, they crumble\nat your touch.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11937,0,0,0,'A Slot Machine',' You are at a large broken dust covered slot machine.\nA large stool is in front of the machine.  Hairline cracks\ntravel along the surface of the walls, they crumble\nat your touch.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11938,0,0,0,'A Slot Machine',' You are at a large broken dust covered slot machine.\nA large stool is in front of the machine.  Hairline cracks\ntravel along the surface of the walls, they crumble\nat your touch.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11939,0,0,0,'The Blackjack Table',' For many moons the townsfolk of Grimhaven once came to this spot\nto make a quick fortune.  Looking at your surroundings you discover\nsomething odd about the table in front of you which has been\nsplintered in two and lies sprawled upon the dust covered floor.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11940,0,0,0,'A Slot Machine',' You are at a large broken dust covered slot machine.\nA large stool is in front of the machine.  Hairline cracks\ntravel along the surface of the walls, they crumble\nat your touch.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11941,0,0,0,'The Casino Fire Table',' A large table sits here splintered in two.  At one time this\nspot was used as a recreational facility for the people of\nGrimhaven.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11942,0,0,0,'The Casino Gin Table',' A large table sits here splintered in two.  At one time this\nspot was used as a recreational facility for the people of\nGrimhaven.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11943,0,0,0,'The Casino Floor',' This is the main floor of the casino that once bustled with\neveryday activity.  Run down slot machines and various crap\ntables line the floor of the room around you.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11944,0,0,0,'A Large Craps Table',' A large table sits here splintered in two.  At one time this\nspot was used as a recreational facility for the people of\nGrimhaven.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11945,0,0,0,'The Roulette Wheel',' A large roulette wheel lies against the north wall, pined to it\nis a small carcass of what resembles a hobbit.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11946,0,0,0,'A Slot Machine',' You are at a large broken dust covered slot machine.\nA large stool is in front of the machine.  Hairline cracks\ntravel along the surface of the walls, they crumble\nat your touch.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11947,0,0,0,'A Slot Machine',' You are at a large broken dust covered slot machine.\nA large stool is in front of the machine.  Hairline cracks\ntravel along the surface of the walls, they crumble\nat your touch.\n',80,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11948,0,0,0,'Wide hallway',' Before you looms a large hallway filled with sparse furniture.\nA chandelier, made only from the finest crystals this region\nhas to offer no longer sparkles with the same glow it once held.\nThe constraints of ivory once used as a fitting for the torches\nhave long since been plundered by thugs and thieves.  Dozens of\nportraits hang off the gouged faded white marble walls, each one\nhas been either torn from its casing or splotched over with paint.\nA shaggy red carpet, as wide as the room itself leads\ndown the hallway where an entryway can be seen.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11949,0,0,0,'Clerks Office',' This is a tiny office where much of the casino\'s transactions took\nplace.  A wooden counter, no more then three feet high contains two metallic\ncasings atop, each one on opposing ends reading IN-BOX and OUT-BOX.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11950,0,0,0,'Wide hallway',' Before you looms a large hallway filled with sparse furniture.\nA chandelier, made only from the finest crystals this region\nhas to offer no longer sparkles with the same glow it once held.\nThe constraints of ivory once used as a fitting for the torches\nhave long since been plundered by thugs and thieves.  A shaggy red\ncarpet, as wide as the room itself leads up and down the hallway.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11951,0,0,0,'Storage Room',' The room appears to be a storage space for the casino\'s\nmachinery.  Large metallic type components litter the floor\nby a dusty toolshed.  Five slots machines sit on a workmens\nbench, aged and damaged.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11952,0,0,0,'Accounting Office',' An oval shaped room built into small cells holds skeletal remains\nwhich can only be viewed through a small opening in the marble walls\nbinded with thick iron bars.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11953,0,0,0,'Small Cell',' Cold and damp, the cell only contains the skeletal remains\nof a small carcass.  Hairline cracks run along the surface\nof the wall as if a deep impact shook the earth at one time.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11954,0,0,0,'Small Cell',' Cold and damp, the cell only contains the skeletal remains\nof a small carcass.  Hairline cracks run along the surface\nof the wall as if a deep impact shook the earth at one time.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11955,0,0,0,'Small Cell',' Cold and damp, the cell only contains the skeletal remains\nof a small carcass.  Hairline cracks run along the surface\nof the wall as if a deep impact shook the earth at one time.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11956,0,0,0,'Small Cell',' Cold and damp, the cell only contains the skeletal remains\nof a small carcass.  Hairline cracks run along the surface\nof the wall as if a deep impact shook the earth at one time.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11957,0,0,0,'Wide hallway',' Before you looms a large hallway filled with sparse furniture.\nA chandelier, made only from the finest crystals this region\nhas to offer no longer sparkles with the same glow it once held.\nThe constraints of ivory once used as a fitting for the torches\nhave long since been plundered by thugs and thieves.  A shaggy red\ncarpet, as wide as the room itself leads up and down the hallway.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11958,0,0,0,'Interrogation Room',' This square shaped room was once used to interrogate suspicious\ntownsfolk of cheating in the casino.  All that remains here now is\njust a hallow room filled with debris.  Though The World has moved\non, you can still see wanted signs hanging from the walls.\nA small dusty cell is seen north of here.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11959,0,0,0,'Cramped Cell',' A small cell is here once used for holding criminals\ntill the city\'s officials could come in and take over.\nIf this cell was used today, death would come quick and\neasy from the death knights that roam the city now.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11960,0,0,0,'Wide hallway',' Before you looms a large hallway filled with sparse furniture.\nA chandelier, made only from the finest crystals this region\nhas to offer no longer sparkles with the same glow it once held.\nThe constraints of ivory once used as a fitting for the torches\nhave long since been plundered by thugs and thieves.  A shaggy red\ncarpet, as wide as the room itself leads up and down the hallway.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11961,0,0,0,'Hallways End',' The hallway ends here before a large opening east of you.\nOn the floor is a massive door made from cast iron rusting\naway, you make a guess and tell that this door probably stood\nupright that lead into the room east of you.  Mounted high above\nthe northern wall is a very large and faded portrait of the\ncasino\'s owner.  Its frame that was once made of gold plundered\nas well, takes up much of the wall.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11962,0,0,0,'Owner\'s Suite',' A large empty chamber stands before you.  The room itself was\nmade to house treasures of wealth at some time but like the\nrest of the casino, it\'s been looted by thieves.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11963,0,0,0,'Guest Room',' Barren and bare this room like much of the casino has\nbeen looted by thieves and thugs.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11964,0,0,0,'Stall Room',' A bathroom is here made from marble.  The stone marble has\nbeen damaged from vandals and slabs of it have been removed,\nprobably by thieves and sold at a price.  A stonewash basin\nstill sits atop a counter filled with green liquid.  A bronze\nchain dangles off a wooden bucket in the north corner of the\nroom used for showering.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(11965,0,0,0,'Dining Room',' Several pillars of white marble can be seen here forming a rectangle in\nthis great hall.  Glancing upwards to where the pillars touch the ceiling\nyou see someone has made a painstaking task of painting an awesome replica\nof a dense forest.  This chamber was made to hold conferences with regard\nto renovations to the casino.\n',80,139720,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(12000,0,0,0,'Center Square','  You are in the center of a large forgotten city once called Grimhaven.\nAn east-west road meets with a north-south road overrun with debris and\nleads through a grassland terrain.  The plaza is wide and deathly silence\nsurrounds you.\n',81,164017,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12001,0,0,0,'North Main Street',' This was a well maintained, north-south road running through a\nlarge city.  To the east existed a large palace at one time, all\nthat remains now is a large pile of rock and a crumbling wall\nwhich it hid behind.  To the west yet another pile of rubble,\nthough all you can make out on the dusty rock blocks that lie at\nyour feet are words that echo in your mind of a time you knew so\nlong ago.  South lies the center of this forgotten city.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12002,0,0,0,'East King\'s Way',' This was a wide and clean street at one time which slopes gently\ndownwards as it runs to the east.  To the north is a high crumbled wall,\nbehind which is a shattered palace.  To the south is a fence where a\ncharred park is seen.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12003,0,0,0,'South Main Street',' This is a wide, north-south road is overrun with weeds.  To the east lies a\nlarge charred park, while to the west appears to be a boarded up marketplace.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12004,0,0,0,'West King\'s Way',' This wide street probably once a well used road is filled with debris\nand tall grass.  To the north you see a large collapsed church, and to the\nsouth was a once popular tavern.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12005,0,0,0,'East King\'s Way',' This was a wide and clean street at one time which slopes gently\ndownwards as it runs to the east.  To the north is a high crumbled\nwall, behind which is a shattered palace.  To the south is a fenced off\ncharred park.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12006,0,0,0,'East King\'s Way',' This was a wide and clean street at one time and slopes gently\ndownwards as it runs to the east.  To the north a gate probably\nonce stood in the high crumbled wall that lead into the palace.\nThe archway appears unsteady but allows entrance to the north.\nTo the south, a path leads into a charred park.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12007,0,0,0,'East King\'s Way',' This was a wide and clean street at one time which slopes gently\ndownwards as it runs to the east.  To the north is a high crumbled wall,\nbehind which is a shattered palace.  To the south is a fenced off charred\npark.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12008,0,0,0,'Front Lawn',' You are in front of what used to be very large palace.  Obviously,\na very important person lived here at one time.  There is a large\narchway to the north.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12009,0,0,0,'Park Entrance',' The road begins to widen and slope downward towards a hillside.  What\nwas once a small part of greenery in the lands Grimhaven has now become\na place of dread.\n',81,131072,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12010,0,0,0,'East King\'s Way',' The road is level here, it runs beside a crumbled palace wall\nto the north, and a fence along the south.  The road is overrun\nwith grass and portions of stonework which probably fell from\nthe palace.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12011,0,0,0,'East King\'s Way',' The land here is filled with chip\'s of stonework that have fallen\nfrom the collapsed palace which lies north of you.  From what you\nrecall, you remember clearly how the spires of its roof sailed\nupwards into the skies.  But that time has changed, now what\nremains is a ghost town from a past shadowing this present.\nTo the south, a rotted splintery high fence blocks your entrance\nto a charred park.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12012,0,0,0,'East King\'s Way',' This east-west road is wide and dirty.  South of here is a crumbled wall of a\nlarge building.  An office building appears to have once stood to the north.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12014,0,0,0,'East King\'s Way',' This east-west road is wide and dirty.  To the north a narrow\nroad leads you into a very shady area of city.  To the south\nappears to be where the proud Mage Academy once stood before\nit was cast in ruins.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12015,0,0,0,'Park Avenue',' You are on a very dirty and uneven road.  The cobble stones that\nonce laid here have been torn asunder by a powerful blast of some\nkind.  From what you recall, this was once a good part of town.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12016,0,0,0,'An Entry Way',' You are in an entrance to the Mage\'s Academy.  North of here lies\nKing\'s Way while a small dusty passage leads east.  This room\nappears to have been used as a shop at one time.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12017,0,0,0,'East King\'s Way',' This east-west road is wide and dirty.  To the north is a darkened\nentrance to the Grimhaven Hospital, or what\'s left of it.  To the\nsouth is the entrance to the Mage\'s Academy.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12018,0,0,0,'Hospital Reception',' You are standing in the entrance to the Grimhaven Hospital.  The facilities\nhere are inadequate, but they will have to do.  To the north is what looks\nlike the waiting room, and to the south you see King\'s Way.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12019,0,0,0,'Entry Hall',' You are in the entrance to the Mage\'s Academy, or what\'s left of it.\nTo the west a passageway is seen and another exit leads south.\nNorth of here lies King\'s Way.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12020,0,0,0,'East King\'s Way','  This east-west road is wide, a perfect spot to rest in within\nthe tall lush grass.  Sloping downwards, it extends east from here.\nTo the north lies a large structure once known as the Grimhaven\nHospital.  To the south the Mage\'s Academy appears to be in ruins.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12021,0,0,0,'East King\'s Way',' This east-west road is wide, a perfect spot to rest in within\nthe tall lush grass.  Sloping downwards, it extends east from here.\nTo the north lies a large structure once known as the Grimhaven\nHospital.  To the south the Mage\'s Academy appears to be in ruins.\nYou see Perimeter road east of here, or what\'s left of it.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12022,0,0,0,'Perimeter Road',' This road goes around the outer perimeter of Grimhaven, and lies\nbetween the huge city walls and the city.  The walls are made of\nlarge stones held together with large amounts of mortar, and have\nlong out lived their use.  It looks easy to scale these walls now that\nhave been subdued by an unknown force.  Pieces of the wall lie\neverywhere.  Looking westwards, you see King\'s Way while east of here\nis one of the gates of the city, or is that a gate you see?\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12023,0,0,0,'The East Gate of Grimhaven',' You are just inside of what use to be the gates of the city\nof Grimhaven.  You are fairly near the edge of the plateau upon\nwhich the city of Grimhaven was built upon.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12024,0,0,0,'Perimeter Road',' This road goes around the outer perimeter of Grimhaven, and lies\nbetween the huge city walls and the city.  The walls are made of\nlarge stones held together with large amounts of mortar, and have\nlong out lived their use.  It looks easy to scale these walls now\nthat have been subdued by an unknown force.  Pieces of the wall lie\neverywhere.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12025,0,0,0,'Perimeter Road',' This road goes around the outer perimeter of Grimhaven, and lies\nbetween the huge city walls and the city.  The walls are made of\nlarge stones held together with large amounts of mortar, and have\nlong out lived their use.  It looks easy to scale these walls now\nthat have been subdued by an unknown force.  Pieces of the wall lie\neverywhere.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12027,0,0,0,'West King\'s Way',' This wide street probably once a well used road is filled with\ndebris and tall grass.  To the north you see a large collapsed\nchurch.  The pathway slopes gently east here.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12028,0,0,0,'West King\'s Way',' This wide street probably once a well used road is filled with\ndebris and tall grass.  To the north you see a large collapsed\nchurch, looks as if the church doors have been ripped open by\nsomething massive.  To the south is a street that is lined with\nvacant shops.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12029,0,0,0,'An Entryway',' This was the main entrance to the church.  You see the main\ncollapsed sanctuary to the north, and partically collapsed\nhallways to the east and west.  You see a large door on the\nsouth wall.  This church was constructed by the Brotherhood of\nGalek with the permission of the king of Grimhaven; the\nBrotherhood uses it as a place of worship and as a monument\nand centerpiece to disseminate the teachings of Galek.\n',81,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12030,0,0,0,'Branish Way',' You are on the north part of Branish Way.  King\'s Way is to the\nnorth of here and there are boarded up shops to the east and west.\nSouth leads down towards Market Road.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12031,0,0,0,'West King\'s Way',' This wide street probably once a well used road is filled with\ndebris and tall grass.  To the north you see a large collapsed\nchurch.  The street which slopes gently downwards as it runs to\nthe east.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12032,0,0,0,'West King\'s Way',' This wide street probably once a well traveled road is filled with\ndebris and tall grass.  It slopes gently to the east along the\ncluttered rubble of stone that lie in sections here.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12033,0,0,0,'West King\'s Way',' You are at the intersection of King\'s Way and Commonwealth Lane.\nTo your northeast is a collapsed church.  To the southeast is a\nvacant market district.  To the northwest is a shattered threshold,\nyou remember it was once the bank in Grimhaven; southwest is a\nlarge leveled building.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12034,0,0,0,'Collapsed Ruins',' From what you recall this was the monk entrance that lead from\nCommon Wealth into the church.  A large jagged hole to the south\nleads to West Kingsway.  Another passage travels north through a\ntight squeeze, it appears much of the roofing has caved-in there.\n',81,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12035,0,0,0,'Commonwealth Lane',' This is an uneven north-south road running through a large city.\nTo the west, a large building sits.  To the east was once a popular\nmage store.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12036,0,0,0,'West King\'s Way',' This wide street probably once a well used road is filled with\ndebris and tall grass.  It slopes gently to the east along the\ncluttered rubble of stone that lie in sections here.  To the north-\nwest was once the proud Grimhaven First Kingdom Bank.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12037,0,0,0,'Commonwealth Lane',' This was once a well maintained road that ran through the city.  Choked\nweeds and underbrush now serves as a passageway for the living dead.\nTo the west you clearly remember the Bank of Grimhaven that once stood\nthere, now its just a pile of rubble.\n',81,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12038,0,0,0,'West King\'s Way',' This wide street probably once a well used road is filled with\ndebris and tall grass.  It slopes gently to the east along the\ncluttered rubble of stone that lie in piles here.  The wall\nbuilt by the casino yet stands, though crumbled and torn it has\nsurvived whatever took place here in Grimhaven.  To the south\nappears to have been a guild of somesort, what remains is a\ncollapsed ruin now.  There is a large faded sign here.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12040,0,0,0,'West King\'s Way',' This wide street probably once a well used road is filled with debris\nand tall grass.  It slopes gently to the east along the cluttered rubble\nof stone that lie in sections here.  To the south was a large building,\nits completely in ruins.  North of here is the Golden Treasure Casino, not\ncompletely caved-in, a pathway can be seen leading into it.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12041,0,0,0,'The Entrance to the Golden Treasure Casino',' You are standing in the entrance to the one proud Golden Treasure.\nThe first thing you notice is the long rows of rust covered slot\nmachines to your east and west.  Further into the casino you can make\nout three or four tables located in the center of the room.  An\ninconspicuous spiral staircase seems to lead upwards but a cave-in\nprevents passage that way.  A strange wooden panel below you looks\nlike it can be opened.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12042,0,0,0,'West King\'s Way',' You are at the west end of King\'s Way.  To the west is Perimeter Road.  To\nthe north is a shattered wall of the casino while south is a crumbled,\nstonework wall of a large leveled building.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12043,0,0,0,'Perimeter Road',' This road goes around the outer perimeter of Grimhaven, and lies\nbetween the huge city walls and the city.  The walls are made of\nlarge stones held together with large amounts of mortar, and have\nlong out lived their use.  It looks easy to scale these walls now\nthat have been subdued by an unknown force.  Pieces of the wall lie\neverywhere.  Looking eastwards, you see King\'s Way while west of\nhere is one of the gates of the city, or is that a gate you see?\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12044,0,0,0,'Perimeter Road',' This road goes around the outer perimeter of Grimhaven, and lies between\nthe huge city walls and the city.  The walls are made of large stones held\ntogether with large amounts of mortar, and have long out lived their use.\nIt looks easy to scale these walls now that have been subdued by an\nunknown force.  Pieces of the wall lie everywhere.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12045,0,0,0,'Perimeter Road',' This road goes around the outer perimeter of Grimhaven, and lies between\nthe huge city walls and the city.  The walls are made of large stones\nheld together with large amounts of mortar, and have long out lived their\nuse.  It looks easy to scale these walls now that have been subdued by an\nunknown force.  Pieces of the wall lie everywhere.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12046,0,0,0,'West Gate of Grimhaven',' You are just inside of what use to be the gates of the city of Grimhaven.\nYou are fairly near the edge of the plateau upon which the city of\nGrimhaven was built upon.  A swirling mass of color lies here in place of\nthe city\'s gates.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12048,0,0,0,'North Main Street',' This was a well maintained, north-south road running through a large\ncity.  To the east existed a large palace at one time, all that remains now\nis a large pile of rock and a crumbling wall which it hid behind.  To\nthe west yet another pile of rubble, though all you can make out on the\ndusty rock blocks that lie at your feet are words that echo in your mind\nof a time you knew so long ago.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12049,0,0,0,'North Main Street',' This was a well maintained, north-south road running through a large\ncity.  To the east existed a large palace at one time, all that remains\nnow is a large pile of rock and a crumbling wall which it hid behind.  To\nthe west yet another pile of rubble, though all you can make out on the\ndusty rock blocks that lie at your feet are words that echo in your mind\nof a time you knew so long ago.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12050,0,0,0,'Collapsed Ruins',' This was once the main entrance of an orphanage.  Long ago it was\nadministered by the missionaries of The Brotherhood of Galek.  The sight of\nyour surroundings nauseates you with a feeling to run from this place.\nWhat could have happend to Grimhaven?\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12051,0,0,0,'North Main Street',' This was a well maintained, north-south road running through a large\ncity.  To the east existed a large palace at one time, all that remains\nnow is a large pile of rock and a crumbling wall which it hid behind.  To\nthe west yet another pile of rubble, though all you can make out on the\ndusty rock blocks that lie at your feet are words that echo in your mind\nof a time you knew so long ago.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12052,0,0,0,'North Main Street',' This was a well maintained, north-south road running through a large\ncity.  To the east existed a large palace at one time, all that remains\nnow is a large pile of rock and a crumbling wall which it hid behind.  To\nthe west yet another pile of rubble, though all you can make out on the\ndusty rock blocks that lie at your feet are words that echo in your mind\nof a time you knew so long ago.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12053,0,0,0,'North Main Street',' This was once a well maintained north-south road that lead through the\ncity.  To the west another passage can be seen amidst the rubble and\nthick foliage.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12054,0,0,0,'Walkway',' A walkway that use to lead into the great palace of Grimhaven is overrun\nwith debris, large portions of the palace walls and thick foliage.  The\nlarge door that once barred entrance into the castle yet stands, though\ncharred and cracked it\'s a wonder it survived.  Small creature\'s you\'ve\nnever encountered scurry off beneath the cluster of rocks that form aside\nthe palace door.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12055,0,0,0,'North Main Street',' This was once a well maintained north-south road that lead through the\ncity.  To the east lies a large stone structure of a building that once\nstood there.  To the west reveals a small housing of some sort - though\nalmost collapsed and in ruins a large gaping hole on its side allows\nentrance to it.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12056,0,0,0,'Oak Lane',' The is brittle road, now reduced to nothing more then dust leads\neast-west through this forgotten city.  To the south lies a large\ncrumbling wall that once belonged to this city\'s church community.  To the\nnorth lies a desolate resident home.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12057,0,0,0,'Inside a Very Dirty House',' This house is just off of Oak Lane in what was a good part of Grimhaven.\nIt is extremely dirty.  Broken religious icons are shattered all over the\nmusty floors and all the furniture that once belonged here has been\ncharred as if some great fire passed over them.\n',81,131080,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(12058,0,0,0,'North Main Street',' This road is overrun with thick underbrush and long stemmed weeds.\nTo the east, two large doors have been torn asunder by a powerful\nforce and barely hang on its hinges.  Though the building to the\neast has fallen, a small passage can still be seen.  On the\nground you can see a sign of some sort.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12059,0,0,0,'North Main Street',' This road is overrun with thick underbrush and long stemmed weeds.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12060,0,0,0,'An Entryway',' This is a small entryway before a large opening to the west.  This\nbuilding is made of solid stone, and doesn\'t ventilate very well.\nA hallway stretches to the east, while an archway provides escape to the\nsouth.\n',81,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(12061,0,0,0,'Collapsed Ruins',' From what you recall this room was where the wayward children of\nGrimhaven gathered for their meal\'s.  The wreckage of is beyond word\'s -\npaning the room you can see where large tables and chairs once stood,\nmuch of which is now piled with large portion\'s of roofing.  You also take\nnotice of skeletal remains of small bodies under the debris that\nsurrounds you.  From what you see you imagine these children under table\'s\nsearching for cover in the few moment\'s that ended their lives.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12062,0,0,0,'North Main Street',' The wide, north-south road you are on is cluttered with debris and\nfoliage.  A small side-street runs westward towards some homes that have\nbeen vacant a long long time.  To the east lies large rock formations\nwhere part of a building once stood.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12063,0,0,0,'Perimeter Road',' This road goes around the outer perimeter of Grimhaven, and lies between\nwhat use to be called the lush Haon-Dor forest and this forsaken city.\nThe wall\'s are still standing somewhat - in some area\'s you can see where\nit has fallen.  Creeping vines have formed over the once proud wall that\nwas held together with large stones and large amounts of mortar.  It\nsickens you how did this ever happen in the first place...\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12064,0,0,0,'Briar Way',' This small weeded road runs east to west.  To the west seems like a\ndead-end and to the east lies North Main Street.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12065,0,0,0,'Under a Watchtower',' You are standing underneath a partially collapsed watchtower of\nGrimhaven.  You can see just north of you where the city\'s gates once\nstood.  The gates have been torn from the city walls and now lie on the\nweeded ground beneath you.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12066,0,0,0,'North Gate of Grimhaven',' You are just inside of what use to be the gates of the city of\nGrimhaven.  You are fairly near the edge of the plateau upon which the\ncity of Grimhaven was built upon.  A swirling mass of color lies here in\nplace of the city gates.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12067,0,0,0,'Perimeter Road',' This road goes around the outer perimeter of Grimhaven, and lies between\nthe huge city walls and the city.  The walls are made of large stones held\ntogether with large amounts of mortar, and have long out lived their use.\nIt looks easy to scale these walls now that they have been subdued by an\nunknown force.  Pieces of the wall lie everywhere.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12070,0,0,0,'Collapsed Ruins',' This was the home of wayward boys and girls of this town.  Long ago\nchildren would sleep here in their bedding\'s cuddled up with whatever the\ngood citizens of Grimhaven could give.  All that remains are broken pieces\nof wooden toys scattered around the room.  A few rag doll\'s have seemed to\nmanage to survive whatever took place here so long ago but other then\nthat, your memory of this place leaves you only with the soft echoing\nlaughter that once filled this room.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12071,0,0,0,'Collapsed Ruins',' This use to be a long narrow hallway that ran east to west.  You can tell\nno one has passed over this threshold in a long time.  In fact, your\nfootprint\'s are the only visible signs of life you seen so far within the\nthick pungent grass.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12072,0,0,0,'Collapsed Ruins',' This aisle leads you from the entrance of the church to the altar.  You\nsee broken pews to the east and the west.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12073,0,0,0,'Collapsed Ruins',' This room once belonged to the orphanage where children came to play.\nMuch of the ground covering consist of lush green grass.  You can tell\nthat no one has been active in here for many seasons by its untamed\ncondition with the exception of the roof which has collapsed in along the\nnorthern part of the room.  A ghostly laughter echos softly in your ear\nas if it was a thousand miles away, perhaps it\'s the voices of the dead\nchildren that once played here in a time you knew so long ago.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12074,0,0,0,'Collapsed Ruins',' You are in a small church pew that has been destroyed and partially\ndecayed.  The aisle to the west leads back to the main altar while to your\nnorth more shattered pews are seen.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12075,0,0,0,'Collapsed Archway',' The condition of this room resembles the architectural structure of an\nalcove.  At one time pews to the church once stood in this very place but\nlike most of what you see around you the toll of what took place here has\nleft much in ruins creating pathways where none were before.  Above you a\nlarge gaping hole is seen allowing ventilation into the room.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12076,0,0,0,'Collapsed Archway',' The condition of this room resembles the architectural structure of an\nalcove.  At one time pews to the church once stood in this very place but\nlike most of what you see around you the toll of what took place here has\nleft much in ruins creating pathways where none were before.  Above you a\nlarge gaping hole is seen allowing much ventilation into the room.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12077,0,0,0,'Altar of Grimhaven',' The main altar of Grimhaven is a centerpiece once praised for its\nbeauty.  Many travelers from all walks of life came here to pray before\nwhat deity they had even though it conflicted with the teachings of Galek.\nIt was well known that the priest enjoyed the company of those in other\nreligions, thus it was proclaimed that this church would allow all to\nenter and leave with some sort of seed left instilled within them.  Much of\nthe ground covering runs smoothly with small grassy mounds and creeping\nvines crawl through a large opening above you.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12078,0,0,0,'Alcove Behind the Altar',' Standing behind the altar you can make out the outline of a door that\nonce stood just north of you.  Fresh air sweeps in from a large opening\njust above you.  To the you can see the main altar chamber.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12079,0,0,0,'Back Passage',' This passage was once the threshold before the head priest\'s chambers\nwhich leads west.  A large hole in the ceiling allows the air to filter in\nabove you and a passage way leads east and back south.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12080,0,0,0,'Collapsed Ruins',' This use to be a long narrow hallway that ran east to west.  You can tell\nno one has passed over this threshold in a long time.  In fact, your\nfootprint\'s are the only visible signs of life you seen so far within the\nthick pungent grass.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12081,0,0,0,'Collapsed Ruins',' You are in a small church pew that has been destroyed and partially\ndecayed.  The aisle to the east leads back to the main altar while to your\nnorth more shattered pews are seen.  Above you a large gaping hole is seen\nallowing much ventilation into the room.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12082,0,0,0,'Collapsed Archway',' The condition of this room resembles the architectural structure of an\nalcove.  At one time pews to the church once stood in this very place but\nlike most of what you see around you the toll of what took place here has\nleft much in ruins creating pathways where none were before.  Above you a\nlarge gaping hole is seen allowing much ventilation into the room.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12083,0,0,0,'Collapsed Archway',' The condition of this room resembles the architectural structure of an\nalcove.  At one time pews to the church once stood in this very place but\nlike most of what you see around you the toll of what took place here has\nleft much in ruins creating pathways where none were before.  Above you a\nlarge gaping hole is seen allowing ventilation into the room.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12084,0,0,0,'Priest\'s Chamber',' This was once the home of the Cleric Guildmaster of Grimhaven.  Like\nmost of what\'s left of the church small grassy mounds spread out around\nyou east and south.  Though the walls remain intact you can vaguely see\na small amount of soot on them.  A large gaping hole above you allows the\nair to creep in chilling you to the bone.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12085,0,0,0,'Room of Remembrance',' This room was once the shrine to all noble men who died in battle.\nThe shrine has long been gone and probably came to rest underneath the\ngrassy mounds under your footing.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12086,0,0,0,'Collapsed Ruins',' This is a long narrow hallway that runs east to west.  The roofing\nabove you has several holes punctured in it allowing the air to\nsweep through the area.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12087,0,0,0,'Collapsed Ruins',' You manage to squeeze through the moss covered wooden beams that cross\nyour path.  A large crack above you provides a look up to the open\nskies.  The pathway continues north and south.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,1,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12088,0,0,0,'Collapsed Ruins',' You manage to squeeze through the moss covered wooden beams that cross\nyour path.  A large crack above you provides a look up to the open\nskies.  The pathway continues north and south.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12089,0,0,0,'Collapsed Ruins',' You manage to squeeze through the moss covered wooden beams that cross\nyour path.  A large crack above you provides a look up to the open\nskies.  The pathway continues north and south.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12090,0,0,0,'Grandmaster Monk\'s Lair',' This was the home to the Grandmaster Monk of Grimhaven.  At one\ntime you recall that the Grandmaster dedicated his life in aid to\nothers.  You can only wonder what was his action at the time when\nGrimhaven fell beneath the dreaded sight you see before you now.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12091,0,0,0,'Perimeter Road',' This road goes around the outer perimeter of Grimhaven, and lies between\nthe huge city walls and the city.  The walls are made of large stones\nheld together with large amounts of mortar, and have long out lived their\nuse.  It looks easy to scale these walls now that have been subdued by an\nunknown force.  Pieces of the wall lie everywhere.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12092,0,0,0,'Perimeter Road',' This road goes around the outer perimeter of Grimhaven, and lies between\nthe huge city walls and the city.  The walls are made of large stones held\ntogether with large amounts of mortar, and have long out lived their use.\nIt looks easy to scale these walls now that have been subdued by an\nunknown force.  Pieces of the wall lie everywhere.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
