(12181,0,0,0,'Market Road',' You are at the west end of a vacant shopping district in Grimhaven.\nImmediately to your west is Commonwealth Avenue.  North and south of you\nexisted shops at one time, these shops have long been vacant and boarded\nup.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12182,0,0,0,'Market Road',' This part of Market Road seems oddly quiet.  North and south of you\nexisted shops at one time, these shops have long been vacant and boarded\nup.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12183,0,0,0,'Market Road',' This was the center of Grimhaven\'s Trading District.  There are all\nsorts of vacant boarded up shops in all directions.  Market Square is\nimmediately to your east.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12184,0,0,0,'Market Square',' This was the center of Grimhaven\'s Trading District.  There are all\nsorts of vacant boarded up shops in all directions.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12185,0,0,0,'Market Road',' This part of Market Road seems oddly quiet.  Market Square is immediately\nto your west with the road continuing eastward.  To the north lies a\ncollapsed shop of some sort.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12186,0,0,0,'Market Road',' You are at the eastern edge of Grimhaven\'s vacant shopping district.\nImmediately to your north was the famous Roaring Lion Inn, its in ruins\nnow.  To the east is Main Street and west Market Road continues.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12187,0,0,0,'Branish Way',' This was once the heart of the busy marketplace of Grimhaven.\nMarket square is directly south of you and a boarded up armory is to your\nwest.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12188,0,0,0,'Branish Way',' Immediately to your west was Grimhaven\'s finest weaponsmith, it too has\nbeen boarded up and sealed.  Market Square is to the north.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12189,0,0,0,'End of Branish Way','  You are at the end of a vacant shopping street.  To the west is an\nabandoned donation area and to the east you hear the sound of the wind\nhowling softly.  South of here, are the narrow, twisty alleys of\nGrimhaven\'s slums.  It seems the alleyways have been cut off by a cave-in.\n',81,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12200,0,0,0,'Path Before the Gates',' You are standing on a high crumbled plateau of which Grimhaven was built upon.\nThe road here slopes downward along a steep incline that opens up before\na market place of some sort.  Far north you can see the vast forest of\nHaon-Dor stretch out over the horizon.  To the east mountain peaks are seen\njutting up to the heavens.  A narrow ledge can be seen heading north\nand south skirting the outer walls of Grimhaven.  A swirling mass of color stands\nhere acting as a forcefield between you and the inner city.  Perhaps there is\nanother way in?\n',82,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12201,0,0,0,'West Stone Road',' You are standing on a road that extends to the east on what seems to be a\ngreat market place.  The pathway lead here is well traveled judging by\nthe many tracks that tread back and forth.  Glancing to the east, you can\nsee that the road is laced with small white pebbles most likely used to\nkeep the weeds and grass from flourishing.  Large oak trees arranged along\nthe east road create a natural splintery archway above your head that\nprovides shade and some protection from the elements.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12202,0,0,0,'A Narrow Ledge',' Dense brush covers this surrounding landscape.  Prickly bushes and\nthick wooded trees tighten around a narrow muddy trail that leads\nnorth to south.  Above you, you can see outer walls of Grimhaven\ntower just above the foundation it was built upon.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
