(12222,0,0,0,'A Narrow Ledge',' Dense brush covers this surrounding landscape.  Prickly bushes and\nthick wooded trees tighten around a narrow muddy trail that leads\nback northeast.  Above you, you can see outer walls of Grimhaven\ntower just above the foundation it was built upon.  The wall here\nis covered with <g>moss<1> and fungi.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12223,0,0,0,'<b>Waterdeep Ave North<1>',' Waterdeep Ave runs north to south here aside some residential homes\nshops.  The road here is extremely muddy at all times and the neighborhood\nis a bit shady compared to the rest of the of settlement.  An open market\nplace lies east of you.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12224,0,0,0,'<b>Waterdeep Ave North<1>',' Waterdeep Ave runs north to south here aside some residential\nhomes and shops.  The road here is thick with mud, probably due\nto the waterboys that run back and forth fetching water from\nan open well in the center of town and returning to the Water\nPurifying shop located on the north end of Waterdeep.  An odd\nshop lies west of you where a small sign can be seen tacked\nto the wooden entrance.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12225,0,0,0,'<b>Waterdeep Ave North<1>',' Waterdeep Ave runs north to south here aside some residential\nhomes and shops.  The road here is thick with mud, probably due\nto the waterboys that run back and forth fetching water from\nan open well in the center of town and returning to the Water\nPurifying shop located on the north end of Waterdeep.  To the\neast lies a small dwelling establishment.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12226,0,0,0,'<b>Waterdeep Ave North<1>',' Waterdeep Ave runs north and south along a muddy road.  A\nfactory lies east of you, inside strange sounds softly creep out.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12227,0,0,0,'<b>Waterdeep Ave North<1>',' You\'ve reached the northen end of Waterdeep.  Small puddles of water\nfill in the places where townfolks have left their footprints.  A\nsmall shop lies east of you.  Above its entrance is a small sign.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12228,0,0,0,'<b>Waterdeep Ave South',' Waterdeep avenue runs north to south here aside some residential homes\nand shops.  The road here is thick with mud, probably due to the waterboys\nthat run back and forth fetching water from an open well in the center of\nthe settlement and returning to the Water Purifying shop located on the\nnorth end of Waterdeep.  To the east lies a open market place.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12229,0,0,0,'<b>Waterdeep Ave South',' Waterdeep avenue runs north to south here aside some residential homes.\nThe road here is extremely muddy at all times and the neighborhood is a bit\nshady compared to the rest of the of settlement.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12230,0,0,0,'<b>Waterdeep Ave South',' Waterdeep avenue runs north to south here aside some residential\nhomes.  The road here is extremely muddy at all times and the\nneighborhood is a bit shady compared to the rest of the settlement.\nHousing units for the poor can be seen from here east of you.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12231,0,0,0,'<b>Waterdeep Ave South',' Waterdeep Ave runs north to south here aside some residential\nhomes.  The road here is extremely muddy at all times and the\nneighborhood is a bit shady compared to the rest of the settlement.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12232,0,0,0,'<b>Waterdeep Ave South',' Waterdeep Ave runs north to south here aside some residential\nhomes.  The road here is extremely muddy at all times and the\nneighborhood is a bit shady compared to the rest of the settlement.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12233,0,0,0,'Small Dwelling',' Despite the location of this abode, the dwelling is warm and\na few expensive antiques are seen.  This space is large enough\nto hold a family of four used as a living quarters.  Two large clumsy\nbeds fit neatly back to back along the west wall between a\nnightstand that separates them.  An alcove in the north wall\nhas been readily made as a washing unit, you can see two\nbamboo pipes jut through wall extending from the Water Purifying\nroom thats located next door.\n',82,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(12234,0,0,0,'Water Purifying Shop',' A small shop is filled with pottery, small vials, skins and\nvirtually every type of container ever imaginable used to hold\nwater.  Four bamboo pipes jut through the south wall distributing\nfresh sparking water into a large wooden bucket.\n',82,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(12235,0,0,0,'Water Purifier',' A strange device sits here shielded by a chainlink fence.\nSmall bamboo pipes jut through the north and south walls\nseemingly carrying water to both ends of the complex.\n',82,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(12236,0,0,0,'Trouts Supply Shop',' Trouts shop is an oddity among shopkeepers anywhere in the lands.\nFrom the jaws of a great white shark to the full skeletal remains\nof a Saberfish guardian, pieces of numerous species hang and line\nthese inner walls from top to bottom.  Also known for his expertise\nin tailoring various armors, Trout greets you with a smile.\n',82,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(12237,0,0,0,'Open Market Vendor',' A wheelcart filled with tiny sculptures of pumice and other various\nitems can be seen here.  Rare items are sometimes bought and sold here.\nThe merchant keeps a careful eye on you and his wares.\n',82,172528,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12238,0,0,0,'Open Market Vendor',' Precious pearls and other trinkets are bought and sold here.\nRare items of course is the merchants specialty when it\ncomes to pearls.  She greets you with a warm smile.\n',82,172528,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12239,0,0,0,'Open Market Vendor',' Potions and scrolls written on rice paper decorate this merchants\nwheelcart.  On his counter you can see a small space where a glass\ncabinate holds a few rare items made by the merchant himself.\nHe keeps a watchfull eye on you and his wares.\n',82,172528,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12240,0,0,0,'Open Market Vendor',' You have ventured into an open market where merchants peddle\naway their wares.  Food items and trinkets to charms of all kinds\nlay sprawled on a wheelcart built by the merchant himself.\nHe keeps a careful eye on you and his goods.\n',82,172208,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12241,0,0,0,'West Stone Road',' Stone road runs east to west here and bustles heavily with activity.\nYou can see that the road is laced with small white pebbles most\nlikely used to keep the weeds and grass from flourishing.  Large\noak trees placed along the this road create a natural splintery\narchway above your head that provides shade and some protection\nfrom the elements.  Merchants have settled here selling their\nwares on this open market street.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12242,0,0,0,'West Stone Road',' You are standing on a open market road running through West Stone road.\nThe road here bustles heavily with activity from a merchant who has set\nup his wheelcart selling his wares.  You can see that the road is laced\nwith small white pebbles most likely used to keep the weeds and grass from\nflourishing.  Large oak trees placed along the this road create a natural\nsplintery archway above your head that provides shade and some protection\nfrom the elements.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12243,0,0,0,'Walton Ave North',' This avenue runs north and south.  The forest road is wide and leaves\nlitter the dirt floor.  The avenue is still under construction, you can\nsee where townsfolks have marked their claim to the lands by using wooden\nstakes and rope tieing off their boundaries.  Though there are few housing\nunits here, they probably belong to merchants that have accumulated enough\ntalens to build a humble home.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12244,0,0,0,'Walton Ave North',' This avenue runs north and south.  The forest road is wide and leaves\nlitter the dirt floor.  The avenue is still under construction, you can\nsee where townsfolks have marked their claim to the lands by using wooden\nstakes and rope tieing off their boundaries.  Though there are few housing\nunits here, they probably belong to merchants that have accumulated enough\ntalens to build a humble home.  A horrible smell wafts in from the west\nand a small shop lies east.\n',82,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
