(12435,44,-46,0,'In a Small Fjord','  There are shear rock cliffs on both sides of you.  The water\ncontinues to the northwest and to the southeast.  You see many\nboulders overhead that appear as if they could fall at any time\n',71,131072,28,0,0,0,25,7,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12436,44,-46,1,'On a Cliff Face','  At this point the distance to the ocean surface is not that far, but\nrocks below discourage your hopes of being safe should you fall.  There\nis a small opening to the east that would allow for one person to move\nthrough.\n',71,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(12437,45,-46,1,'In a Tunnel','  After a brief walk from the opening in the cliff face you find yourself\nat what appears to be a dead end.  As you look closer you see what appears\nto be a stone doorway concealed in the northeastern corner of the room.\n',71,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,500,0,'',NULL),
(12438,46,-45,1,'Kassdedra\'s Lair','  In contrast to the cave entrance you just moved through, the bright\nlight coming from the hole in the ceiling of this cavern temporarily\nblinds you.  As your eyes slowly adjust you see that this is an enormous\ncavern.  Off to one side of the cavern, sheltered by a large overhang,\nyou see a small garden surrounding a moderate sized pool of water.  The\npool is fed by a small waterfall which flows from the cavern wall, provided\na beautiful, soothing back ground noise.  A large stone fire pit rest next\nto the pool.  The smoke from any fire is drawn up through a natural crack\nin the cavern wall and is probably diffused before it every reaches the sky.\n',71,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,500,0,'',NULL),
