(13712,-20,24,-2,'A Large Cave','  This large cave is home to a fair sized pond, which is directly west.\nRivulets of <b>water<1> flow in from the east and join the pond, providing a very\nslight supply of fresh <b>water<1> from the river outside.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13713,-20,23,-2,'A Large Cave','  This large cave is home to a fair sized pond, which is directly west.  The\nwater looks rather murky and probably does not circulate much.  The air is damp\nand chilly, and the ground is quite muddy.  Water slowly drips down from roots\nhanging off the dirt ceiling, adding even more mud to the pond.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13714,-21,24,-3,'Waterfilled Tunnel','<b>  The water that fills this tunnel is extremely <k>dark<b> and <o>murky<b>.\nThe ground is covered in a fine layer of <o>silt<b> and <w>ash<b>.  The ceiling here\nis oddly smooth and upon closer inspection does not seem to be made of rock.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13715,-20,24,-3,'Waterfilled Tunnel','<b>  The water that fills this tunnel is extremely <k>dark<b> and <o>murky<b>.\n<g>Vegetation<b> fills the cracks between the rocks on the walls and ceiling.\nThe ground is covered in a fine layer of <o>silt<b> and <w>ash<b>.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13716,-19,24,-3,'Waterfilled Tunnel','<b>  The water that fills this tunnel is extremely <k>dark<b> and <o>murky<b>.\nThe ground is covered in a fine layer of <o>silt<b> and <w>ash<b>.  A faint rippling\nin the water above you would indicate that the surface is not far.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13717,-19,24,-2,'Murky Pool','<b>  The walls are rocky and jagged here and are formed from a natural lava\ntube, that seems to come to an end here.  A <k>dark<b> and <o>murky<b> pool occupies\nthe room and seems rather deep.  The tube leads off to the east.\n',85,139592,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(13718,-18,24,-2,'Lava Tube','<k>  The walls of this tunnel are hard and jagged.  Various types of <g>moss<k>\ngrow and flourish in the cracks and corners.  <W>Splotches<k> of bat guano\nmark the walls and ground in places and the occasional <w>spider web<k> can be\nseen.  The ground is rocky and difficult to walk on, indicating that this\narea is most likely uninhabited by anything other than rodents and vermin.\nThe tube seems to run diagonally upwards towards <C>fresh air<k> and the\nfreedom of the surface world and downwards into the bowels of the <o>earth<k>.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(13719,-18,24,-3,'Lava Tube','<k>  The walls of this tunnel are hard and jagged.  Various types of <g>moss<k>\ngrow and flourish in the cracks and corners.  <W>Splotches<k> of bat guano\nmark the walls and ground in places and the occasional <w>spider web<k> can be\nseen.  The ground is rocky and difficult to walk on, indicating that this\narea is most likely uninhabited by anything other than rodents and vermin.\nThe tube seems to run diagonally upwards towards <C>fresh air<k> and the\nfreedom of the surface world and downwards into the bowels of the <o>earth<k>.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(13720,-17,24,-3,'Lava Tube','<k>  The walls of this tunnel are hard and jagged.  Various types of <g>moss<k>\ngrow and flourish in the cracks and corners.  <W>Splotches<k> of bat guano\nmark the walls and ground in places and the occasional <w>spider web<k> can be\nseen.  The ground is rocky and difficult to walk on, indicating that this\narea is most likely uninhabited by anything other than rodents and vermin.\nThe tube seems to run diagonally upwards towards <C>fresh air<k> and the\nfreedom of the surface world and downwards into the bowels of the <o>earth<k>.\nThere is a small natural alcove to the south.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(13721,-17,23,-3,'Collapsed Tunnel','<k>  Large beams hold up this tunnel which was obviously not created naturally.\nAt one point it must have continued to the east, but it is now collapsed\nunder the pressure of all the <o>earth<k> above it.  You notice that one of the\nbroken beams in the rubble pile has axe marks around the broken end; perhaps\nthe tunnel was collapsed intentionally.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,58,0,'',NULL),
(13722,-17,24,-4,'Lava Tube','<k>  The walls of this tunnel are hard and jagged.  Various types of <g>moss<k>\ngrow and flourish in the cracks and corners.  <W>Splotches<k> of bat guano\nmark the walls and ground in places and the occasional <w>spider web<k> can be\nseen.  The ground is rocky and difficult to walk on, indicating that this\narea is most likely uninhabited by anything other than rodents and vermin.\nThe <C>air<k> is <b>chilly<k> here, reminding you how far away you are from the <y>warmth<k>\nand safety of the surface world.  The dark abyss of the underworld awaits\nyou below.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(13723,-17,24,-5,'Lava Tube','<k>  The walls of this tunnel are hard and jagged.  Various types of <g>moss<k>\ngrow and flourish in the cracks and corners.  <W>Splotches<k> of bat guano\nmark the walls and ground in places and the occasional <w>spider web<k> can be\nseen.  The ground is rocky and difficult to walk on, indicating that this\narea is most likely uninhabited by anything other than rodents and vermin.\nThe <C>air<k> is <b>chilly<k> here, reminding you how far away you are from the <y>warmth<k>\nand safety of the surface world.  The dark abyss of the underworld awaits\nyou below.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(13724,-17,25,-6,'Tunnel of Garbage','<k>  The walls here have been cut away by something, leaving them rough and\nunfinished, particularly on the west side.  Various debris covers the ground\nand is piled against the walls.  Old <b>water<k> skins, broken <w>pick axes<k> and\nother digging tools, some half eaten <G>mushrooms<k> and an oddly shaped saddle\nwith broken stirrups.  This must have been a waste area at one time, but it\ndoes not seem to have been visited for quite some time.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13725,-17,24,-6,'Lava Tube','<k>  The walls of this tunnel are hard and jagged.  The <C>air<k> is very <b>cold<k>\nhere and extremely <b>moist<k>.  A cold sweat clings to your body, chilling\nyou to the <W>bone<k>.  The <g>moss<k> growing on the walls here is abundant and\nprospering in the saturated environment.  Small puddles of <b>water<k> cover\nthe rocky floor making the footing here very treacherous.  The glistening\nblack rocks are sharp and seem to hint murder to anyone who should be so\nunlucky as to fall.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(13726,-16,25,-6,'Carved Tunnel','<k>  The walls here have been cut away by something, leaving them rough and\nunfinished.  The ground has also been cut away somewhat providing a fairly\neven walking surface.  The ceiling is a few feet lower here than in the lava\ntube to the south.  The tunnel comes to an end to the west.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13727,-16,24,-6,'Lava Tube','<k>  The <C>air<k> is very <b>cold<k> here and extremely <b>moist<k>.  The <g>moss<k>\ngrowing on the walls here is abundant and prospering in the saturated\nenvironment.  Small puddles of <b>water<k> cover the rocky floor making the\nfooting here very treacherous.  The ground is relatively flat here as most\nof the rocks appear to have been chipped down by something.  The lava tube\ncontinues to the south and a low tunnel has been carved to the north.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(13728,-16,23,-6,'Lava Tube','<k>  The <C>air<k> is very <b>cold<k> here and extremely <b>moist<k>.  The <g>moss<k> growing on the\nwalls here is abundant and prospering in the saturated environment.  Small\npuddles of <b>water<k> cover the rocky floor making the footing here very\ntreacherous.  The ground is relatively flat here as most of the rocks appear\nto have been chipped down by something.  The tube widens into a large cave\ndirectly to the east and also comes to a split north of here.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(13729,-15,23,-6,'Wet Cavern','<k>  The <C>air<k> is very <b>cold<k> here and extremely <b>moist<k>.  The <g>moss<k> growing on the\nwalls is abundant and prospering in the saturated environment.  Large drops\nof <b>water<k> fall from the ceiling constantly making it feel like rain.  Large\npuddles have formed on the ground concealing most of it.  The cavern walls\nappear to have been chiseled away somewhat, widening the area.  A lava tube\nheads off to the west and the rest of the cavern is east and south.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(13730,-15,22,-6,'Wet Cavern','<k>  The <C>air<k> is very <b>cold<k> here and extremely <b>moist<k>.  The <g>moss<k> growing on the\nwalls is abundant and prospering in the saturated environment.  Large drops\nof <b>water<k> fall from the ceiling constantly making it feel almost as if it\nwere raining.  Large puddles have formed on the ground concealing most\nof it.  The cavern walls appear to have been chiseled away somewhat, widening\nthe area.  The blackness continues to the north and east.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(13731,-14,23,-6,'Wet Cavern','  The <C>air<1> is very <b>cold<1> here and extremely <b>moist<1>.  The <g>moss<1> growing on the\nwalls is abundant and prospering in the saturated environment.  Large drops\nof <b>water<1> fall from the ceiling constantly making it feel almost as if it\nwere raining.  A lava tube leads downward, although you can make out no\nhand or foot holds.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(13732,-14,22,-6,'Wet Cavern','<k>  The <C>air<k> is very <b>cold<k> here and extremely <b>moist<k>.  The <g>moss<k> growing on the\nwalls is abundant and prospering in the saturated environment.  Large drops\nof <b>water<k> fall from the ceiling constantly making it feel almost as if it\nwere raining.  Large puddles have formed on the ground concealing most of it.\nThe cavern walls appear to have been chiseled away somewhat, widening the\narea.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(13733,-15,25,-6,'Access Tunnel','  This tunnel makes a loop around a large column.  The column is wrapped from\nfloor to ceiling in very thick <o>copper<1> cable.  At various points around the\ncolumn there are small gauges mounted.  In some spots the <o>copper<1> cable has\nbeen burned black.  A strand of <o>copper<1> leads from the wall to the center of\nthe ceiling where an odd lamp is mounted.  It all seems very unusual and\nyou suspect that there is some kind of magic at work here.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13734,-14,27,-6,'Access Tunnel','  This tunnel is roughly hewn and confining.  A ladder with steel rungs leads\ndownwards from here.  The tunnel continues to the south.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13735,-14,26,-6,'Access Tunnel','  This tunnel makes a loop around a large column.  The column is wrapped from\nfloor to ceiling in very thick <o>copper<1> cable.  At various points around the\ncolumn there are small gauges mounted.  In some spots the <o>copper<1> cable has\nbeen burned black.  A strand of <o>copper<1> leads from the wall to the center of\nthe ceiling where an odd lamp is mounted.  It all seems very unusual and\nyou suspect that there is some kind of magic at work here.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
