(13738,-14,23,-8,'Vertical Lava Tube','  The walls of this lava tube are rocky, but the rocks themselves are\nfairly smooth.  Unexpectedly, there is no growth here, nor any sign of life\nof any kind.  The tube continues in darkness above and below.\n',85,139592,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,15,'',NULL),
(13739,-13,27,-8,'A Thin Vertical Shaft','  Thick <g>green<1> and <r>red<1> algae cover the sides of this thin shaft leading upwards.\nIt appears to have been formed naturally, as a stress fracture or perhaps it\nis a very small lava tube.  Whatever the case, there is no way to tell with\nthe abundance of <g>plant<1> life concealing the walls.\n',85,139592,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,15,'',NULL),
(13740,-16,26,-8,'Beneath A Massive Fan','  The floor here is actually a <o>screen<1> that stretches from wall to wall.\nIt\'s a bit springy, but stable enough.  A massive fan unlike any you have\nseen before occupies the space above this area.  A hatch is built into the\nfloor here.\n',85,139592,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13741,-16,25,-8,'Beneath A Massive Fan','  The floor here is actually a <o>screen<1> that stretches from wall to wall.\nIt\'s a bit springy, but stable enough.  A massive fan unlike any you have\nseen before occupies the space above this area.\n',85,139592,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,15,'',NULL),
