(13755,-16,26,-9,'Under A Hatch In The Screen','  The ground is covered in <k>sludge<1> in all directions, but is much more shallow\nhere than to the east.  The <k>sludge<1> is predominately composed of <o>sand<1> and\n<o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>, some of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.\nThe entire western wall is composed of thinly spaced vertical slats made out\nof some type of non-rusting <w>metal<1>.  There seems to be some sort of hatch\nbuilt into the <o>screen<1> above you.  A <w>metal<1> ladder is attached to the wall\nand leads up and through the hatch.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13756,-16,25,-9,'<w>Next To The Vents','  The ground is covered in <k>sludge<1> in all directions, but is much more shallow\nhere than to the east.  The <k>sludge<1> is predominately composed of <o>sand<1> and\n<o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>, some of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.\nThe entire western wall is composed of thinly spaced vertical slats made out\nof some type of non-rusting <w>metal<1>.  There seems to be some sort of hatch\nbuilt into the <o>screen<1> on the ceiling to the north.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13757,-16,24,-9,'<w>Next To The Vents','  The ground is covered in <k>sludge<1> in all directions, but is much more shallow\nhere than to the east.  The <k>sludge<1> is predominately composed of <o>sand<1> and\n<o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>, some of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.\nThe entire western wall is composed of thinly spaced vertical slats made out\nof some type of non-rusting <w>metal<1>.  The ceiling is a finely meshed <o>rusty\nscreen<1> which must filter out larger debris on the level above you.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13758,-15,26,-9,'Under A Rusty Screen','  The ground is covered in <k>sludge<1> in all directions, but is much more shallow\nhere than to the east.  The <k>sludge<1> is predominately composed of <o>sand<1> and\n<o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>, some of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.\nThere seems to be some sort of hatch built into the <o>screen<1> to the west.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13759,-15,25,-9,'Under A Rusty Screen','  The ground is covered in two feet deep <k>sludge<1> in all directions.  It is\npredominately composed of <o>sand<1> and <o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>,\nsome of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.  All of it seems to be relatively fine\ngrain, except for the plant life which probably originated here in the <k>sludge<1>.\nThe ceiling is a finely meshed <o>rusty screen<1> which must filter out larger\ndebris on the level above you.  The <k>sludge<1> continues in all directions.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13760,-15,24,-9,'Under A Rusty Screen','  The ground is covered in two feet deep <k>sludge<1> in all directions.  It is\npredominately composed of <o>sand<1> and <o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>,\nsome of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.  All of it seems to be relatively fine\ngrain, except for the plant life which probably originated here in the <k>sludge<1>.\nIt is piled up particularly high next to the wall, similar to a snow drift or\nsand dune.  The ceiling is a finely meshed <o>rusty screen<1> which must filter\nout larger debris on the level above you.  The area seems to come to a corner\nto the west.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13761,-14,26,-9,'Under A Rusty Screen','  The ground is covered in two feet deep <k>sludge<1> in all directions.  It is\npredominately composed of <o>sand<1> and <o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>,\nsome of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.  All of it seems to be relatively fine\ngrain, except for the plant life which probably originated here in the <k>sludge<1>.\nIt is piled up particularly high next to the wall, similar to a snow drift or\nsand dune.  The ceiling is a finely meshed <o>rusty screen<1> which must filter\nout larger debris on the level above you.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13762,-14,25,-9,'Under A Rusty Screen','  The ground is covered in two feet deep <k>sludge<1> in all directions.  It is\npredominately composed of <o>sand<1> and <o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>,\nsome of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.  All of it seems to be relatively fine\ngrain, except for the plant life which probably originated here in the <k>sludge<1>.\nThe ceiling is a finely meshed <o>rusty screen<1> which must filter out larger\ndebris on the level above you.  The <k>sludge<1> continues in all directions.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13763,-14,24,-9,'Under A Rusty Screen','  The ground is covered in two feet deep <k>sludge<1> in all directions.  It is\npredominately composed of <o>sand<1> and <o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>,\nsome of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.  All of it seems to be relatively fine\ngrain, except for the plant life which probably originated here in the <k>sludge<1>.\nThe ceiling is a finely meshed <o>rusty screen<1> which must filter out larger\ndebris on the level above you.  No reasoning for this is apparent and the\nscreen is too fine to see through.  A tunnel heads off to the south.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13764,-13,26,-9,'Under A Rusty Screen','  The ground is covered in <k>sludge<1> in all directions, but is much more shallow\nhere than to the east.  The <k>sludge<1> is predominately composed of <o>sand<1> and\n<o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>, some of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.  The\nceiling is a finely meshed <o>rusty screen<1> which must filter out larger debris\non the level above you.  The <k>sludge<1> is piled particularly high next to the\nnorth wall which seems to have partially collapsed.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13765,-13,25,-9,'Under A Rusty Screen','  The ground is covered in two feet deep <k>sludge<1> in all directions.  It is\npredominately composed of <o>sand<1> and <o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>,\nsome of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.  All of it seems to be relatively fine\ngrain, except for the plant life which probably originated here in the <k>sludge<1>.\nThe ceiling is a finely meshed <o>rusty screen<1> which must filter out larger\ndebris on the level above you.  The <k>sludge<1> continues in all directions.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13766,-13,24,-9,'Under A Rusty Screen','  The ground is covered in two feet deep <k>sludge<1> in all directions.  It is\npredominately composed of <o>sand<1> and <o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>,\nsome of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.  All of it seems to be relatively fine\ngrain, except for the plant life which probably originated here in the <k>sludge<1>.\nIt is piled up particularly high next to the wall, similar to a snow drift or\nsand dune.  The ceiling is a finely meshed <o>rusty screen<1> which must filter\nout larger debris on the level above you.  No reasoning for this is apparent\nand the screen is too fine to see through.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13767,-12,26,-9,'Under A Rusty Screen','  The ground is covered in <k>sludge<1> in all directions, but is much more shallow\nhere than to the east.  The <k>sludge<1> is predominately composed of <o>sand<1> and\n<o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>, some of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.  The\nceiling is a finely meshed <o>rusty screen<1> which must filter out larger debris\non the level above you.  The <k>sludge<1> is piled particularly high in the corner.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13768,-12,25,-9,'Under A Rusty Screen','  The ground is covered in two feet deep <k>sludge<1> in all directions.  It is\npredominately composed of <o>sand<1> and <o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>,\nsome of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.  All of it seems to be relatively fine\ngrain, except for the plant life which probably originated here in the <k>sludge<1>.\nIt is piled up particularly high next to the wall, similar to a snow drift or\nsand dune.  The ceiling is a finely meshed <o>rusty screen<1> which must filter\nout larger debris on the level above you.  This seems to be the eastern-most\nedge of this area.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13769,-12,24,-9,'Under A Rusty Screen','  The ground is covered in <k>sludge<1> in all directions, but is much more shallow\nhere than to the east.  The <k>sludge<1> is predominately composed of <o>sand<1> and\n<o>dirt<1> but there are also chunks of <g>algae<1>, some of it glowing a pale <G>green<1>.  The\nceiling is a finely meshed <o>rusty screen<1> which must filter out larger debris\non the level above you.  The <k>sludge<1> is piled particularly high in the corner.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,3,3,0,60,15,'',NULL),
(13770,-14,23,-9,'Lava Tube','  The walls of this lava tube are rocky, but the rocks themselves are\nfairly smooth.  The ground is covered in an ankle deep <o>slushy <g>goo<1> composed\nof <g>moss<1>, <o>mud<1> and bits of various debris.  The tube continues directly\nupwards into darkness and widens to the north.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,15,'',NULL),
(13771,-13,27,-9,'A Filthy Pit','  This pit is dominated by a tremendous amount of <o>garbage<1>.  Old fish <W>bones<1>,\nrotting carcasses of dead animals, <G>glowing algae<1>, old worn out clothing and a\nfair amount of unidentifiable decomposed matter.  The weight of all this trash\nseems to have partially collapsed the south wall.  A thin <g>algae<1> choked\nvertical shaft heads upwards.\n',85,139592,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,15,'',NULL),
(13772,-14,23,-7,'Vertical Lava Tube','  The walls of this lava tube are rocky, but the rocks themselves are\nfairly smooth.  Unexpectedly, there is no growth here, nor any sign of life\nof any kind.  The tube widens into a large cavern above you and continues\nin darkness below.\n',85,139592,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,15,'',NULL),
(13773,-13,27,-7,'Top Of A Vertical Shaft','  Slimy <g>moss<1> covers the wall around this area, thriving on the humid\natmosphere.  A narrow shaft leads downwards.  Bits of debris are scattered\naround the shaft.  It appears that this naturally created shaft is being\nutilized as a garbage dump.  A tunnel has been carved out of the rock to\nthe north.\n',85,139592,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,15,'',NULL),
(13774,-13,28,-7,'A Crudely Carved Tunnel','  The walls and ceiling have been chiseled away and <o>wooden<1> supports put\nup to form this tunnel.  The work was done shabbily, as if this area wasn\'t\ngoing to be used often, or perhaps only temporarily.  There appears to be\nsome sort of hole or pit to the south and this tunnel makes a turn to the\nnorth.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13775,-13,29,-7,'A Crudely Carved Tunnel','  The walls and ceiling have been chiseled away and <o>wooden<1> supports put\nup to form this tunnel.  The work was done shabbily, as if this area wasn\'t\ngoing to be used often, or perhaps only temporarily.  The tunnel widens to\nthe west, into a better maintained area.  This crude tunnel continues\nto the south.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13776,-14,26,-7,'Observation Platform','  This narrow platform overlooks a wide area to the south.  The upper half\nof the area (level with this platform) is dominated by a massive steel fan.\nEach blade of the mighty fan must be nearly fifty feet long and each blade\nperhaps fifteen feet wide at its widest edge.  Many large vents cover the\nceiling above the fan.  Steps lead down to the lower area.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13777,-14,27,-7,'Before A Heavy Steel Door','  This tunnel looks well built.  The stone floor has been worn smooth from\nuse and care has been taken to make the walls fairly smooth and free of\njagged edges.  A sturdy ladder with steel rungs leads up through a narrow\nhole in the ceiling.  A heavy steel door is mounted in the south wall.  It\nhas a large wheel attached to it that controls four steel rods that fit\ninto holes in the wall.  This door was made to be very secure.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,160,0,'',NULL),
(13778,-14,28,-7,'A Tunnel','  This tunnel looks well built.  The stone floor has been worn smooth from\nuse and care has been taken to make the walls fairly smooth and free of\njagged edges.  The tunnel comes to a T to the north and continues to the\nsouth.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13779,-14,29,-7,'A Tunnel','  This tunnel looks well built.  The stone floor has been worn smooth from\nuse and care has been taken to make the walls fairly smooth and free of\njagged edges.  It continues off to the west and south.  A less inviting\ntunnel leads east.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13780,-15,27,-7,'Storage Area','  Large amounts of equipment are hanging from racks on the walls and from\na large support column in the center of the room.  Various digging and\nmining tools are present, as well as helmets, rough leather protective\nclothing, boots, a few unused wheelbarrows, buckets and medical supplies.\nThere is also a large supply of food and provisions here, most of which\nis in ready to eat form, no cooking required.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13781,-15,28,-7,'Barracks','  This large open area serves as the primary living area for the inhabitants\nof these caves and tunnels.  Rows of beds line the walls and lead off to\nthe west and there is a cluster of beds in the center.  Various pieces of\nclothing strewn about, as well as water skins, cups and digging tools.  The\nfloor is dirty almost to the point of appearing to be made of earth instead\nof stone.  Whoever lives here either does not believe that cleanliness is\nnext to godliness, or does not care much for godliness.  Some sort of\nstorage area/locker room is to the south.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13782,-15,29,-7,'A Tunnel','  This tunnel looks well built.  The stone floor has been worn smooth from\nuse and care has been taken to make the walls fairly smooth and free of\njagged edges.  The tunnel comes to a T to the east and opens up somewhat to\nthe west.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13783,-16,27,-7,'Barracks','  This large open area serves as the primary living area for the inhabitants\nof these caves and tunnels.  Rows of beds line the walls and lead off to\nthe north and there is a cluster of beds in the center.  Various pieces of\nclothing strewn about, as well as water skins, cups and digging tools.  The\nfloor is dirty almost to the point of appearing to be made of earth instead\nof stone.  Whoever lives here either does not believe that cleanliness is\nnext to godliness, or does not care much for godliness.  Some sort of\nstorage area/locker room is to the east.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13784,-16,28,-7,'Barracks','  This large open area serves as the primary living area for the inhabitants\nof these caves and tunnels.  Rows of beds line the walls and lead off to\nboth the east and south, as well a cluster of beds in the center.  There\nare various pieces of clothing strewn about, as well as water skins, cups\nand digging tools.  The floor is dirty almost to the point of appearing to\nbe made of earth instead of stone.  Whoever lives here either does not\nbelieve that cleanliness is next to godliness, or does not care much for\ngodliness.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13785,-16,29,-7,'A Tunnel','  The floor of this tunnel is worn smooth and gets a lot of use.  A stone door\nto the north has \'<w>Headmaster<1>\' engraved in it.  A large room or cavern opens\nup to the south and the tunnel continues both east and west.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13786,-16,30,-7,'Headmaster\'s Office','  This may be the Headmaster\'s office, but it doesn\'t look like much office\nwork gets done here.  A comfortable sleeping mat lies against the back wall,\nnext to a large pile of crumpled dirty clothing.  Two large barrels sit next\nto another wall.  You notice that they both have spigots attached and you\ncome to the conclusion that they are extremely large beer kegs.  An old\nbeat up table cluttered with various objects is in the center of the room.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13787,-17,29,-7,'A Tunnel','  The tunnel to the west seems to be somewhat less used that this part.  Bits\nof debris litter the floor around the northen exit and the tunnel leads back\nto the east.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13788,-17,30,-7,'Debris','  This room is cluttered with a huge assortment of debris.  All sorts of\n<g>c<b>o<g>l<b>o<g>r<b>e<g>d<1> rocks and stones, shells, <W>bones<1>, a raft or two, broken fishing rods\nand many unidentifiable things.  Anything here that may have once been\nuseful is now water damaged beyond repair.  You feel as though you could\nstand here for days sorting through this trash and never grow bored.  An\neven larger heap of refuse lies to the north.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13789,-17,31,-7,'Debris','  This pile of garbage nearly reaches to the ceiling.  It is composed of\na wide variety of items, all of which appear to have spent some time\nunderwater.  The stench of brine and decay is overwhelming.  A hole has\nbeen dug into the side of the pile.  It looks like it might be the lair\nof some trash loving animal.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13790,-18,29,-7,'A Tunnel','  Rock chips and <o>mud<1> cover the narrow floor of this roughly hewn tunnel.\nThe jagged rock walls glisten with dampness and small amounts of <g>moss<1> have\nbegun take hold in the cracks.  As you gaze up at the tiny stalactites that\nare forming on the ceiling a twinge of animal terror runs through you at the\nthought of all the tons of rock and <o>earth<1> above your head.  Footprints\nin the <o>mud<1> lead off both east and west.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13791,-19,29,-7,'Turn In The Tunnel','  Rock chips and <o>mud<1> cover the narrow floor of this roughly hewn tunnel.\nThe jagged rock walls glisten with dampness and small amounts of <g>moss<1> have\nbegun take hold in the cracks.  The tunnel makes an abrupt turn here,\nobviously the result of some careful planning by its creators.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13792,-19,30,-7,'A Tunnel','  Rock chips and <o>mud<1> cover the narrow floor of this roughly hewn tunnel.\nThe jagged rock walls glisten with dampness and small amounts of <g>moss<1> have\nbegun take hold in the cracks.  As you gaze up at the tiny stalactites that\nare forming on the ceiling a twinge of animal terror runs through you at the\nthought of all the tons of rock and <o>earth<1> above your head.  Footprints\nin the <o>mud<1> lead off both north and south.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13793,-19,31,-7,'A Tunnel','  Rock chips and <o>mud<1> cover the narrow floor of this roughly hewn tunnel.\nThe jagged rock walls glisten with dampness and small amounts of <g>moss<1> have\nbegun take hold in the cracks.  As you gaze up at the tiny stalactites that\nare forming on the ceiling a twinge of animal terror runs through you at the\nthought of all the tons of rock and <o>earth<1> above your head.  Footprints\nin the <o>mud<1> lead off both north and south.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13794,-19,32,-7,'A Tunnel','  Rock chips and <o>mud<1> cover the narrow floor of this roughly hewn tunnel.\nThe jagged rock walls glisten with dampness and small amounts of <g>moss<1> have\nbegun take hold in the cracks.  As you gaze up at the tiny stalactites that\nare forming on the ceiling a twinge of animal terror runs through you at the\nthought of all the tons of rock and <o>earth<1> above your head.  Footprints\nin the <o>mud<1> lead off both north and south.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13795,-19,33,-7,'A Branch In The Tunnel','  Rock chips and <o>mud<1> cover the narrow floor of this roughly hewn tunnel.\nThe jagged rock walls glisten with dampness and small amounts of <g>moss<1> have\nbegun take hold in the cracks.  A smaller, rougher tunnel branches off to the\nnorth and the main thoroughfare runs south-northeast.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13796,-19,34,-7,'A Tunnel With <w>Steel Rails','  This tunnel is composed of hard packed <o>dirt<1> and the occasional large rock.\nIt is short, wide and very roughly cut.  The floor, however, is very level\nand a pair of <w>steel rails<1> mounted on <o>wooden planks<1> lead the way north.  From\nthe lack of use that is evident, you suspect that this tunnel was used only\nto transport mining tools and raw materials to and from the tunnels to the\nsouth as they were being dug.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13797,-19,35,-7,'A Tunnel With <w>Steel Rails','  This tunnel is composed of hard packed <o>dirt<1> and the occasional large rock.\nIt is short, wide and very roughly cut.  The floor, however, is very level\nand a pair of <w>steel rails<1> mounted on <o>wooden planks<1> lead the way north\nand south.  From the lack of use that is evident, you suspect that this\ntunnel was used only to transport mining tools and raw materials to and from\nthe tunnels to the south as they were being dug.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13798,-19,36,-7,'A Bend In A Tunnel With <w>Steel Rails','  This tunnel is composed of hard packed <o>dirt<1> and the occasional large rock.\nIt is short, wide and very roughly cut.  The floor, however, is very level\nand a pair of <w>steel rails<1> mounted on <o>wooden planks<1> make a smooth bend,\nleading off to the northwest and south.  From the disused look of this area\nyou suspect that it was used only to transport mining tools and raw materials\nto and from the tunnels to the south as they were being dug.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13799,-20,37,-7,'A Tunnel With <w>Steel Rails','  This tunnel is composed of hard packed <o>dirt<1> and the occasional large rock.\nIt is short, wide and very roughly cut.  The floor, however, is very level\nand a pair of <w>steel rails<1> mounted on <o>wooden planks<1> lead the way northwest\nand southeast.  From the lack of use that is evident, you suspect that this\ntunnel was used only to transport mining tools and raw materials to and from\nthe tunnels to the south as they were being dug.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13800,-21,38,-7,'A Bend In A Tunnel With <w>Steel Rails','  This tunnel is composed of hard packed <o>dirt<1> and the occasional large rock.\nIt is short, wide and very roughly cut.  The floor, however, is very level\nand a pair of <w>steel rails<1> mounted on <o>wooden planks<1> make a smooth bend,\nleading off to the northwest and southeast.  From the disused look of this\narea you suspect that it was used only to transport mining tools and raw\nmaterials to and from the tunnels to the south as they were being dug.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13801,-20,39,-7,'A Tunnel With <w>Steel Rails','  This tunnel is composed of hard packed <o>dirt<1> and the occasional large rock.\nIt is short, wide and very roughly cut.  The floor, however, is very level\nand a pair of <w>steel rails<1> mounted on <o>wooden planks<1> lead the way north\nand southwest.  From the lack of use that is evident, you suspect that this\ntunnel was used only to transport mining tools and raw materials to and from\nthe tunnels to the south as they were being dug.  It looks like there is some\nsort of staging area to the north.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13802,-20,40,-7,'A Staging Area','  This tunnel is composed of hard packed <o>dirt<1> and the occasional large rock.\nIt is short, wide and very roughly cut.  The floor, however, is very level\nand a pair of <w>steel rails<1> mounted on <o>wooden planks<1> lead off to the\nsouth.  Some unused <w>rails<1> and <o>planks<1> are stacked against the wall,\napparently discarded.  From the look of things this is probably where\nequipment was stored temporarily and transported south in carts on the <w>rails<1>.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13803,-19,41,-7,'A <k>Dark<1> Cavern','  This cavern is massive.  The walls are rocky and ascend into oblivion\nabove.  Except for the adjacent walls, everything is enshrouded in darkness.\nStanding in the center of the cavern is a tall tower made from <w>granite<k> blocks.\nIt looks like a toy, nearly lost in the all encompassing abyss around you.\nFrom the very top of the mysterious tower is the faintest gleam of <W>light<k>.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13804,-19,40,-7,'A <k>Dark<1> Cavern','  This cavern is massive.  The walls are rocky and ascend into oblivion\nabove.  Except for the adjacent walls, everything is enshrouded in darkness.\nStanding in the center of the cavern is a tall tower made from <w>granite<k> blocks.\nIt looks like a toy, nearly lost in the all encompassing abyss around you.\nFrom the very top of the mysterious tower is the faintest gleam of <W>light<k>.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13805,-19,39,-7,'A <k>Dark<1> Cavern','  This cavern is massive.  The walls are rocky and ascend into oblivion\nabove.  Except for the adjacent walls, everything is enshrouded in darkness.\nStanding in the center of the cavern is a tall tower made from <w>granite<k> blocks.\nIt looks like a toy, nearly lost in the all encompassing abyss around you.\nFrom the very top of the mysterious tower is the faintest gleam of <W>light<k>.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13806,-18,41,-7,'A <k>Dark<1> Cavern','  This cavern is massive.  The walls are rocky and ascend into oblivion\nabove.  Except for the adjacent walls, everything is enshrouded in darkness.\nStanding in the center of the cavern is a tall tower made from <w>granite<k> blocks.\nIt looks like a toy, nearly lost in the all encompassing abyss around you.\nFrom the very top of the mysterious tower is the faintest gleam of <W>light<k>.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13807,-18,40,-7,'Inside A Tower','  The inside of this tower is completely bare.  There are no furnishings or\nadornments of any kind.  A wide <w>stone<k> staircase spirals upwards.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13808,-18,39,-7,'A <k>Dark<1> Cavern','  This cavern is massive.  The walls are rocky and ascend into oblivion\nabove.  Except for the adjacent walls, everything is enshrouded in darkness.\nStanding in the center of the cavern is a tall tower made from <w>granite<k> blocks.\nIt looks like a toy, nearly lost in the all encompassing abyss around you.\nFrom the very top of the mysterious tower is the faintest gleam of <W>light<k>.\nAn open entrance to the north leads inside.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13809,-17,41,-7,'A <k>Dark<1> Cavern','  This cavern is massive.  The walls are rocky and ascend into oblivion\nabove.  Except for the adjacent walls, everything is enshrouded in darkness.\nStanding in the center of the cavern is a tall tower made from <w>granite<k> blocks.\nIt looks like a toy, nearly lost in the all encompassing abyss around you.\nFrom the very top of the mysterious tower is the faintest gleam of <W>light<k>.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13810,-17,40,-7,'A <k>Dark<1> Cavern','  This cavern is massive.  The walls are rocky and ascend into oblivion\nabove.  Except for the adjacent walls, everything is enshrouded in darkness.\nStanding in the center of the cavern is a tall tower made from <w>granite<k> blocks.\nIt looks like a toy, nearly lost in the all encompassing abyss around you.\nFrom the very top of the mysterious tower is the faintest gleam of <W>light<k>.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13811,-17,39,-7,'A <k>Dark<1> Cavern','  This cavern is massive.  The walls are rocky and ascend into oblivion\nabove.  Except for the adjacent walls, everything is enshrouded in darkness.\nStanding in the center of the cavern is a tall tower made from <w>granite<k> blocks.\nIt looks like a toy, nearly lost in the all encompassing abyss around you.\nFrom the very top of the mysterious tower is the faintest gleam of <W>light<k>.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13812,-18,40,-6,'Inside A Tower','  The inside of this tower is completely bare of furnishings.  Strange <r>r<p>u<c>n<b>e<g>s<k>\nof various colors twinkle from the walls.  They are all interconnected and\nencircle the tower completely.  An impalpable tingle runs through your body as\nyou pass through the level of the <r>r<p>u<c>n<b>e<g>s<k>.  The wide staircase spirals upwards\nand downwards.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13813,-18,40,-5,'A Magical Prison','  The purpose of the <r>r<p>u<c>n<b>e<g>s<k> below become clear when you see the contents\nof this room.  The only person who would live here would be a prisoner and\nthey must prevent escape.  These sparse living quarters must be the sole\npurpose for this tower.  A wide <w>stone<k> staircase is the only exit and very\nthin windows peer outwards in the eight cardinal directions.  A poorly made\nbed stands against one wall, next to it, similarly constructed desk, chair and\nrotting book shelf.  A visible groove has been worn into the floor around the\nstaircase, presumably a result of the constant pacing the prisoner who resides\nhere.  A <p>mystical circle<k> is drawn on the floor in one half of the room.\nIt glows a bright <b>bluish<k>-<p>purple<k> and radiates power and energy.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13814,-16,39,-7,'A Tunnel','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The stone floor has been worn smooth and there is a notable\nlack of <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<k>, however it is somewhat dirty.  It widens into\na large rough cavern to the northwest.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13815,-15,39,-7,'A Tunnel','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The stone floor has been worn smooth and there is a notable\nlack of <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<k>.  Although not as well travelled as the thoroughfare\nto the east, this tunnel gets its share of use.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13816,-14,39,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<k> floor has been worn smooth and there is a notable\nlack of <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<k>.  The thoroughfare continues to the north and\neast, but dwindles into a mere path to the west.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13817,-13,39,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<k> floor has been worn smooth and there is a notable\nlack of <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<k>.  This is obviously a main thoroughfare.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13818,-12,39,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<k> floor gives away to <o>dirt<k> and <o>mud<k> to the north where\nwide ruts in the <o>dirt<k> lead into darkness.  An imposing <w>iron<k> gate, bearing\nan equally imposing <w>iron <k>lock, bars passage to the south.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13819,-11,40,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<k> floor gives away to <o>dirt<k> and <o>mud<k> to\nthe north where wide ruts in the <o>dirt<k> lead into darkness.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13820,-10,39,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<k> floor has been worn smooth and there is a notable\nlack of <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<1>.  This is obviously a main thoroughfare.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13821,-9,39,-7,'An Intersection Of Tunnels','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<1> floor has been worn smooth and there is a notable\nlack of <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<k>.  This is obviously a main thoroughfare.  Another\nintersection lies directly east and the main tunnel heads west.  A smaller\nless used tunnel breaks off to the south.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13822,-8,39,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<k> floor has been worn smooth and there is a notable\nlack of <w>cobwebs<1> and <g>moss<1>.  This main thorough fare leads north and west.  A\nstable of some sort is to the east.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13823,-7,39,-7,'Corral Ready Room','  This looks like a storage room for riding equipment.  Saddles and other\nriding paraphernalia hang from the walls.  The saddles are odd affairs,\nhaving an unusually large amount of straps and prods.  You can\'t imagine\nwhat would make such complexity necessary.  A wide gate to the south provides\npassage through a wall of thick <w>metal<k> bars and a well travelled thoroughfare\nlies west.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13824,-8,38,-7,'Steeder Corral','  Everything about this den inspires mortal terror in your heart.  The floor\nis rocky and difficult to walk on, making you feel immediately out of place.\nThe ceiling recedes into near darkness, but dark vague shapes can be seen\nmoving about slowly.  The sharp rocks glisten wetly, prepared to puncture\nthe skin of the unwary.  Several cocooned corpses are stuck to the walls,\nmost of which are humanoid in form.  In one corner a large cocoon has a bumpy\nshape, as if it contained eggs.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13825,-7,38,-7,'Steeder Corral','  Everything about this den inspires mortal terror in your heart.  The floor\nis rocky and difficult to walk on, making you feel immediately out of place.\nThe ceiling recedes into near darkness, but dark vague shapes can be seen\nmoving about slowly.  The sharp rocks glisten wetly, prepared to puncture\nthe skin of the unwary.  A large <w>grey<k> fuzzy object is lodged next to a rock\nprotruding from the wall.  On closer inspection you see that it is a withered\nhumanoid corpse in a web cocoon!\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13826,-13,38,-7,'Slave Quarters','  This sections is marginally nicer than the other parts of the slave quarters.\nBodily excesses seem to be mostly confined to a hole in the corner and the\nsleeping mats are more <g>moss<k> that <o>dirt<k>.  The stench is still nearly unbearable,\nbut it\'s a lot easier to control the gag reflex.  This is where the more\nobedient, intelligent slaves are kept.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13827,-12,38,-7,'Slave Quarters','  This rough niche is dirty and smelly.  The floor is mostly composed of <o>mud<k>\nand trampled bits of <g>moss<k>.  The whole area reeks of <y>urine<k>, <o>feces<k> and the\ninevitable decay of death.  There is no furniture in sight, giving the\nimpression that this area is for gathering slaves before taking them out to\nwork in the farms and other areas.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13828,-11,38,-7,'Slave Quarters','  This narrow tunnel is dirty and smelly.  The floor is mostly composed of <o>mud<k>\nand trampled bits of <g>moss<k>.  The whole area reeks of <y>urine<k>, <o>feces<k> and the\ninevitable decay of death.  What might be called sleeping mats lie in the mud,\nmade out of <g>moss<k> but looking more like packed <o>mud<k>.  <w>Iron<k> loops protrude\nfrom the walls at intervals.  The slaves are not allowed even the minimal\nfreedom of roaming this small domain.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13829,-10,38,-7,'Slave Quarters','  This narrow tunnel is dirty and smelly.  The floor is mostly composed of <o>mud<k>\nand trampled bits of <g>moss<k>.  The whole area reeks of <y>urine<k> and <o>feces<k>.  What\nmight be called sleeping mats lie in the mud, made out of <g>moss<k> but looking\nmore like packed <o>mud<k>.  <w>Iron<k> loops protrude from the walls at intervals.  The\nsmell of death wafts in from the south.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13830,-10,37,-7,'Torture Chamber','  The sight and smell of this room would make any human being gag in disgust.\nThe slaves that are kept here are of the worst sort: they do not easily give\nup their freedom and still wish for better days.  This room represents either\nthe end of their lives or the beginning of their passive career as an obedient\nslave.  The <o>muddy<k> floor is tinged with <r>red<k> that can only be <r>blood<k>.  <w>Iron<k>\nchains descend from the ceiling from which slaves are hung suspended from\ntheir hands, feet and sometimes neck.  Bodies are left rotting in the corners\nand some have been ravaged by the other slaves for cannibalistic nourishment\nor carnal pleasures.  You shudder to think of the evils that have occurred in\nthis room.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13831,-18,34,-7,'A Tunnel','  Rock chips and mud cover the narrow floor of this roughly hewn tunnel.\nThe jagged rock walls glisten with dampness and small amounts of moss have\nbegun take hold in the cracks.  Small stalactites are forming on the ceiling\nas <b>water<1> drips off the rocks.  Footprints in the mud lead off both\neast and southwest.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13832,-17,34,-7,'Under A <w>Silver<1> Arch','  Rock chips and <o>mud<1> cover the narrow floor of this roughly hewn tunnel.\nBrilliant <w>silver<1> streaks mingle among the jagged rocks of the walls\nand ceiling forming an arch over the tunnel.  Small stalactites are forming\non the ceiling as <b>water<1> drips down.  Footprints in the mud lead off\nboth east and west.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13833,-16,34,-7,'Under A <w>Silver<1> Arch','  Rock chips and <o>mud<1> cover the narrow floor of this roughly hewn tunnel.\nBrilliant <w>silver<1> streaks mingle among the jagged rocks of the walls\nand ceiling forming an arch over the tunnel.  Small stalactites are forming\non the ceiling as <b>water<1> drips down.  Footprints in the mud lead off\nboth east and west.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13834,-15,34,-7,'A Tunnel','  The floor is very <o>muddy<1> here and the rich deep scent of <o>earth<1> fills\nthe air.  The <o>mud<1> originates from the northeast, from a section of the\ntunnel that is cut out of <o>dirt<1> instead of stone.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13835,-14,35,-7,'A Muddy Tunnel','<o>  This section of the tunnel runs through raw earth.  Thick wooden beams\nsupport the walls and ceiling at regular intervals.  Roots dangle down from\nthe ceiling, dripping <b>water<1> slowly into the muddy mess that serves\nas a floor.  As muddy as this area is, you have to wonder if it is terribly\nsafe to travel through.  The tunnel returns to <k>stone<1> to the southwest and\nthis tunnel of mud continues to the east.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13836,-13,35,-7,'A Muddy Tunnel','<o>  This section of the tunnel runs through raw earth.  Thick wooden beams\nsupport the walls and ceiling at regular intervals.  Roots dangle down from\nthe ceiling, dripping <b>water<1> slowly into the muddy mess that serves\nas a floor.  As muddy as this area is, you have to wonder if it is terribly\nsafe to travel through.  The mud continues east and west.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13837,-12,36,-7,'A Tunnel','  The floor is very <o>muddy<1> here and the rich deep scent of <o>earth<1> fills\nthe air.  The <o>mud<1> originates from the southwest, from a section of the\ntunnel that is cut out of <o>dirt<1> instead of stone.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13838,-11,36,-7,'A Tunnel','  Rock chips and <o>mud<1> cover the narrow floor of this roughly hewn tunnel.\nThe jagged rock walls glisten with dampness and small amounts of <g>moss<1> have\nbegun take hold in the cracks.  Small stalactites are forming on the ceiling\nas <b>water<1> drips off the rocks.  Footprints in the <o>mud<1> lead off both\neast and west.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13839,-10,36,-7,'A Tunnel Of <G>Glowing<1> <g>M<p>o<g>s<p>s','  Thick <g>green<1> and <p>purple<1> <g>m<p>o<g>s<p>s<1> covers the floor and walls here and thickens to\nthe east.  It gives off a very faint <G>glow<1> that adds a sinister gleam to the\nwet rocks that poke out of the <g>m<p>o<g>s<p>s<1>.  The <G>glow<1> is brighter to the east\nand diminishes to the west.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13840,-9,36,-7,'A Tunnel Of <G>Glowing<1> <g>M<p>o<g>s<p>s','  Thick <g>green<1> and <p>purple<1> <g>m<p>o<g>s<p>s<1> covers the entire tunnel here, giving\noff a <G>glow<1> that is almost as bright as <y>daylight<1>.  The <G>glow<1> diminishes\nboth north and west.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13841,-9,37,-7,'A Tunnel Of <G>Glowing<1> <g>M<p>o<g>s<p>s','  Thick <g>green<1> and <p>purple<1> <g>m<p>o<g>s<p>s<1> covers the floor and walls here and thickens to\nthe east.  It gives off a very faint <G>glow<1> that adds a sinister gleam to the\nwet rocks that poke out of the <g>m<p>o<g>s<p>s<1>.  The <G>glow<1> is brighter to the south\nand diminishes to the north.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13842,-9,38,-7,'A Tunnel','  Rock chips and <o>mud<1> cover the narrow floor of this roughly hewn tunnel.\nThe jagged rock walls glisten with dampness and small amounts of <g>moss<1> have\nbegun take hold in the cracks.  Small stalactites are forming on the ceiling\nas <b>water<1> drips off the rocks.  Footprints in the <o>mud<1> lead off to the\nsouth.  To the north another larger tunnel runs perpendicular to this one.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13843,-13,41,-7,'<g>Moss Farm<1>','  This farm supplies much of the raw material that the surrounding inhabitants\nuse.  Because no natural light is available this deep into the earth, the\nonly possible growth is <o>fungus<k> and <b>moss<k>.  As a result there is an immense\nvariety of <p>moss<k> growing here.  Each strain has been carefully selected and\ncrossbred to fulfill certain needs of the community.  Much of the <c>moss<k> is soft\nand velvety, providing material for clothing, while some strains are more\nrugged and can be used for clothing reinforcement.  Thick fluffy <r>moss<k> is used\nfor sleeping pallets, cushions and carpets.  Heavy rough <o>moss<k> is braided into\nrope.  Bristly tough <y>moss<k> make good scrubbing tools and floor mats to wipe\nboots off.  A few types of <g>moss<k> are edible and serve to liven up the usual\nfair of <g>mushroom<k> derived foods.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13844,-12,41,-7,'<y>Moss Farm<1>','  This farm supplies much of the raw material that the surrounding inhabitants\nuse.  Because no natural light is available this deep into the earth, the\nonly possible growth is <o>fungus<k> and <p>moss<k>.  As a result there is an immense\nvariety of <c>moss<k> growing here.  Each strain has been carefully selected and\ncrossbred to fulfill certain needs of the community.  Much of the <r>moss<k> is soft\nand velvety, providing material for clothing, while some strains are more\nrugged and can be used for clothing reinforcement.  Thick fluffy <o>moss<k> is used\nfor sleeping pallets, cushions and carpets.  Heavy rough <y>moss<k> is braided into\nrope.  Bristly tough <g>moss<k> make good scrubbing tools and floor mats to wipe\nboots off.  A few types of <b>moss<k> are edible and serve to liven up the usual\nfair of <g>mushroom<k> derived foods.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13845,-13,40,-7,'<o>Moss Farm<1>','  This farm supplies much of the raw material that the surrounding inhabitants\nuse.  Because no natural light is available this deep into the earth, the\nonly possible growth is <o>fungus<k> and <c>moss<k>.  As a result there is an immense\nvariety of <r>moss<k> growing here.  Each strain has been carefully selected and\ncrossbred to fulfill certain needs of the community.  Much of the <o>moss<k> is soft\nand velvety, providing material for clothing, while some strains are more\nrugged and can be used for clothing reinforcement.  Thick fluffy <y>moss<k> is used\nfor sleeping pallets, cushions and carpets.  Heavy rough <g>moss<k> is braided into\nrope.  Bristly tough <b>moss<k> make good scrubbing tools and floor mats to wipe\nboots off.  A few types of <p>moss<k> are edible and serve to liven up the usual\nfair of <g>mushroom<k> derived foods.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13846,-12,40,-7,'<r>Moss Farm<1>','  This farm supplies much of the raw material that the surrounding inhabitants\nuse.  Because no natural light is available this deep into the earth, the\nonly possible growth is <o>fungus<k> and <r>moss<k>.  As a result there is an immense\nvariety of <o>moss<k> growing here.  Each strain has been carefully selected and\ncrossbred to fulfill certain needs of the community.  Much of the <y>moss<k> is soft\nand velvety, providing material for clothing, while some strains are more\nrugged and can be used for clothing reinforcement.  Thick fluffy <g>moss<k> is used\nfor sleeping pallets, cushions and carpets.  Heavy rough <b>moss<k> is braided into\nrope.  Bristly tough <p>moss<k> make good scrubbing tools and floor mats to wipe\nboots off.  A few types of <c>moss<k> are edible and serve to liven up the usual\nfair of <g>mushroom<k> derived foods.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13847,-11,41,-7,'<g>Mushroom Farm<1>','  This farm supplies much of the food and materials for the surrounding\ninhabitants.  Since no natural light is available this deep into the earth,\nthe only possible growth is <o>fungus<k> and <g>moss<k>.  As a result, there is an immense\nvariety of <o>mushrooms<k> growing here, carefully selected to fulfill every purpose\nin daily life.  <r>Mushrooms<k> of all sizes and colors provide food.  Squat wide\n<y>mushrooms<k> are leveled off and serve as tables or chairs.  Wide thin <b>mushroom<k>\ntops are used for cushioning under a <g>moss<k> sleeping pallet, or to sit on.  Some\n<g>mushrooms<k> produce a very hard but flexible shell that can be used for armor.\nObviously, the cultivation of <p>mushrooms<k> is taken very seriously here.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13848,-10,41,-7,'<b>Mushroom Farm<1>','  This farm supplies much of the food and materials for the surrounding\ninhabitants.  Since no natural light is available this deep into the earth,\nthe only possible growth is <o>fungus<k> and <g>moss<k>.  As a result, there is an immense\nvariety of <r>mushrooms<k> growing here, carefully selected to fulfill every purpose\nin daily life.  <y>Mushrooms<k> of all sizes and colors provide food.  Squat wide\n<b>mushrooms<k> are leveled off and serve as tables or chairs.  Wide thin <g>mushroom<k>\ntops are used for cushioning under a <g>moss<k> sleeping pallet, or to sit on.  Some\n<o>mushrooms<k> produce a very hard but flexible shell that can be used for armor.\nObviously, the cultivation of <r>mushrooms<k> is taken very seriously here.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
