(13851,-14,40,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<1> floor has been worn smooth from use and the are\nabsent of both <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<k>.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13852,-14,41,-7,'A Main Throughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<1> floor has been worn smooth from use and the are\nabsent of both <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<k>.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13853,-14,42,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<1> floor has been worn smooth from use and the are\nabsent of both <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<k>.  The tunnel widens even further to the\nnorth and you see side passages that have the look of habitation.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13854,-14,43,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  This area has the look of long term inhabitation.  The <w>stone<k> floor is worn\nsmooth and has a fair number of slabs laid into it, apparently to repair\ndamage from constant use.  A wide entry way framed with <w>granite<k> beams leads\nto the east and has two very large <w>stone<k> axes crossing above it.  A town square\nof sorts lies directly north.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13855,-13,43,-7,'Sparse Barracks','  Many tidy sleeping mats line the walls, each of which has a large locker\nat its head and pegs in the walls to hang weapons and shields from.  The\nfloor is quite clean, obviously swept daily and the mats are well used but\nin good repair.  No tables are present as the soldiers do their fraternizing\nin the communal area of the settlement, or in the field.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13856,-12,43,-7,'Sparse Barracks','  Many tidy sleeping mats line the walls, each of which has a large locker\nat its head and pegs in the walls to hang weapons and shields from.  The\nfloor is quite clean, obviously swept daily and the mats are well used but\nin good repair.  The entire east wall is devoted to holding spare weapons of\nvarious kinds.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13857,-13,42,-7,'Sparse Barracks','  Many tidy sleeping mats line the walls, each of which has a large locker\nat its head and pegs in the walls to hang weapons and shields from.  The\nfloor is quite clean, obviously swept daily and the mats are well used but\nin good repair.  An area has been cleared away in the center of the room,\nprobably for light sparring and wrestling.  No tables are present as the\nsoldiers do their fraternizing in the communal area of the settlement, or\nin the field.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13858,-14,44,-7,'A Communal Area','  This large open cavern is a common area for the local inhabitants.  A crudely\nconstructed <w>stone<k> fountain occupies the center of the cavern and fills it with\nthe sharp tangy odor of fresh mineral <b>water<k>.  Hand crafted <w>stone<k> benches\nand tables surround the fountain, their proximity lending a communal feel\nto the whole setup.  A <w>stone<k> anvil and hammer are mounted above an entrance to\nthe west and the thoroughfare leads south and northeast.  A smaller forbidding\ntunnel heads to the northwest.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13859,-16,44,-7,'Raw Materials Storage','  Various types of metals, minerals and gemstones are piled up into sorted\nstacks here.  A central area has been cleared out to make room for dwarves\nthat chip off the non-valuable stone.  When the ore is ready for further\nprocessing, it is taken south and put into the grinding and polishing machine.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13860,-15,44,-7,'Entrance To The Forge','  This large forge is where metals, minerals and gemstones of the underdark\nare processed for shipment or forged into useful items.  Raw materials are\ndumped into a pile to the west, where the stone and granite are chipped off\nto reveal as much of the underlying valuable material as possible.  They are\nthen moved into a large cylinder that rotates, slowly breaking the last pieces\nof stone off.  Once the material is as pure and polished as possible, it is\neither shipped off to other places for commerce, or fashioned into equipment\nat the forge to the south.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13861,-16,43,-7,'Grinding And Polishing Machine','  A large dented iron cylinder lies on its side here, supported by four wooden\nlegs.  One end has a hatch that is opened with a wheel and the other side has\ncrank attached.  Ore is put into the cylinder, which is turned slowly.  The\nore grinds together, causing the remaining bits of stone to come off and\neventually be reduced to powder.  The underlying material also becomes slightly\npolished as a result.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13862,-15,43,-7,'The <R>Forge<1>','  This is where all of the finishing work is done on the equipment constructed\nby the dark dwarves.  Stones and gems are hand polished or cut by diligent\ncraftsmen, armor plates are sewn onto clothing and metals are melted down and\nreshaped in the monstrous <R>forge<1>.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13863,-13,45,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<k> floor has been worn smooth from use and the are\nabsent of both <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<k>.  A wide common area lies to the southwest.\nThe thoroughfare leads east into a residential area and a smaller tunnel\nbranches north.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13864,-12,45,-7,'Residential Area','  The air here is cool and dry.  The walls are immaculately clean and well\npolished.  The ceiling has been shaped into an elegant curving arch.  The\nfloor has been expertly cobbled with deep <r>crimson<k> stones that give off a faint\nlight.  A splendidly crafted <w>granite<k> door to the northeast is mounted in a\n<w>granite<k> frame that is nothing short of breathtaking.  The delicate carvings\ncapture your eye and you can only imagine the amount of effort put into them.\nThe double doors to the north have a detailed images of a dwarven warriors\ncarved into each one.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13865,-12,46,-7,'The <1><b>Governor\'s<o> Home','  This beautifully furnished abode serves as both a home to the <1><b>governor<k>\nand his family as well as an office where day to day affairs are handled.\nEverything in this room has been hand made by the best craftsmen available\nand out of the best materials.  Elaborately carved images of several warriors\ncover the walls, perhaps the same warriors from whom the <1><b>governor<k> is\ndescended from.  An unassuming door leads north into what is probably the\nprivate section of the home and a pair of doors are set into the south wall\nas well.<1>\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13866,-12,47,-7,'The <1><b>Governor\'s<o> Home','  Although still quite beautiful and costly, the private section of the\n<1><b>governor\'s<k> home lacks the extravagant adornment of his office.  The family\nlives together in one large room.  Living space is at a premium in the\nunderdark and since dark dwarves spend the majority of time training and\nworking, larger homes would be unnecessary.<1>\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13867,-11,46,-7,'A Homestead','  Sleeping quarters, a small kitchen, a pantry and some storage lockers are\nall that compose this homestead.  What little there is here is very high\nquality and neatly kept.  Despite their small homes, the dark dwarves take\ngreat pride and luxury in what they do have.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13868,-11,45,-7,'Residential Area','  The air here is cool and dry.  The walls are immaculately clean and well\npolished.  The ceiling has been shaped into an elegant curving arch.  The\nfloor has been expertly cobbled with deep <r>crimson<k> stones that give off a faint\nlight.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13869,-10,45,-7,'Residential Area','  The air here is cool and dry.  The walls are immaculately clean and well\npolished.  The ceiling has been shaped into an elegant curving arch.  The\nfloor has been expertly cobbled with deep <r>crimson<k> stones that give off a faint\nlight.  A splendidly crafted <w>granite<k> door to the north is mounted in a\n<w>granite<k> frame that is nothing short of breathtaking.  The delicate carvings\ncapture your eye and you can only imagine the amount of effort put into them.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13870,-10,46,-7,'A Luxuriant Home','  Thick carpeting of moss covers the floor and a large fur mat from some\nunidentified underdark wildlife lies at the entrance.  The walls and ceiling\nhave been chipped and filed to be perfectly level, and then polished to\nperfection.  What little furniture there is, is expertly crafted and ornately\ncarved.  This plush home must belong to one of the more successful denizens\nof the area.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13871,-9,45,-7,'Residential Area','  The air here is cool and dry.  The walls are immaculately clean and well\npolished.  The ceiling has been shaped into an elegant curving arch.  The\nfloor has been expertly cobbled with deep <r>crimson<k> stones that give off a faint\nlight.  A splendidly crafted <w>granite<k> door to the northeast is mounted in a\n<w>granite<k> frame that is nothing short of breathtaking.  The delicate carvings\ncapture your eye and you can only imagine the amount of effort put into them.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13872,-8,46,-7,'A Homestead','  Sleeping quarters, a small kitchen, a pantry and some storage lockers are\nall that compose this homestead.  What little there is here is very high\nquality and neatly kept.  Despite their small homes, the dark dwarves take\ngreat pride and luxury in what they do have.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13873,-8,44,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<k> floor has been worn smooth and there is a notable\nlack of <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<k>.  This is obviously a main thoroughfare.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13874,-8,43,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<k> floor has been worn smooth and there is a notable\nlack of <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<k>.  This is obviously a main thoroughfare.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13875,-8,42,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<k> floor has been worn smooth and there is a notable\nlack of <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<k>.  An acrid scent emanates from the dwelling to the\nwest.  It smells sort of like <o>ale<k>, but not quite.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13876,-9,42,-7,'<g>Mushroom <o>Ale<g> Brewery<1>','  This cave is dominated by a mass of brewing apparatus.  It all looks very\ncomplicated and well worn, but also well crafted and sturdy.  Several large\ncasks line the north wall and a deep trough where fresh <g>mushrooms<k> are held\nhas been carved into the south wall.  It seems that brewing <o>ale<k> from <g>mushrooms<k>\nwould be impossible, but a large vat of freshly brewed <g>mushroom<o> ale<k> awaits\nyour tasting.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13877,-10,42,-7,'<g>Mushroom <o>Ale<g> Brewery Storage Room<1>','  More casks are stacked here, some of which appear to be quite old, as if\nthe <g>mushroom<o> ale<k> was being aged before consumption.  A few crates of\n<g>mushrooms<k> are here, also being aged before use.  Some spare parts for the\nbrewery are stored here as well as some exotic looking tools, but there is\nlittle else of interest.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13878,-8,41,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<k> floor has been worn smooth and there is a notable\nlack of <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<k>.  This is obviously a main thoroughfare.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13879,-8,40,-7,'A Main Thoroughfare','  The ceiling is enshrouded in darkness and the walls of this wide tunnel are\nvery far apart.  The <w>stone<k> floor has been worn smooth and there is a notable\nlack of <w>cobwebs<k> and <g>moss<k>.  This is obviously a main thoroughfare.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13880,-13,46,-7,'A Small Access Tunnel','  This tunnel is short and narrow, providing only single file travel.  It\nmust lead to some commonly used portion of the underdark that is not easily\naccessible from the main tunnel, perhaps an area to harvest food or hunt.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13881,-14,47,-7,'A Small Access Tunnel','  This tunnel is short and narrow, providing only single file travel.  It\nmust lead to some commonly used portion of the underdark that is not easily\naccessible from the main tunnel, perhaps an area to harvest food or hunt.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13882,-14,48,-7,'<w>An Iron Door<1>','  This access tunnel comes to an abrupt halt here, at an iron door.  There\ndoesn\'t appear to be a door handle or keyhole of any sort.  This must be\na semi-permanent barrier constructed by the dark dwarves.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13883,-15,45,-7,'A <r>Cobbled<1> Tunnel','  This tunnel is large and well traveled.  It provides the primary route of\ntravel to and from the wild underdark, used by miners, travelers and soldiers.\nThe floor is paved with <r>red cobblestones<1> loosely fitted together, providing\na solid, level path.  The dark dwarf settlement lies to the southeast and\nthe tunnel continues west towards the underdark.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13884,-16,45,-7,'A <r>Cobbled<1> Tunnel','  This tunnel is large and well traveled.  It provides the primary route of\ntravel to and from the wild underdark, used by miners, travelers and soldiers.\nThe floor is paved with <r>red cobblestones<1> loosely fitted together, providing\na solid, level path.  The dark dwarf settlement lies to the east and the\ntunnel continues west towards the underdark.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13885,-17,45,-7,'A <r>Cobbled<1> Tunnel','  This tunnel is large and well traveled.  It provides the primary route of\ntravel to and from the wild underdark, used by miners, travelers and soldiers.\nThe floor is paved with <r>red cobblestones<1> loosely fitted together, providing\na solid, level path.  The dark dwarf settlement lies to the east and the\ntunnel continues northwest towards the underdark.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13886,-18,46,-7,'A Cave-In','  The <r>cobbled<1> tunnel comes to an abrupt end here.  The ceiling has collapsed,\nshowering tons of rock and dirt into the tunnel, completely blocking it off.\nThe settlement requires travel to and from the underdark to survive, so the\ntunnel won\'t be blocked off for long.  Until it is cleared, there will be no\negress.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13887,-18,24,-2,'A Small Dirt Tunnel','  This tunnel runs through the earth, supported only by roots and the a few\nlarge rocks.  The ground is <o>muddy<1> and <b>water<1> flows in from the east and out\nto the west.  The <o>dirt<1> walls are patterned with brush marks from the hair of\npassing animals.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(13888,-17,25,-2,'A Steep Slope','  The ground slopes upward at a steep angle here.  A small amount of <b>water<1> runs\ndown the slope and leaves southwest down a small tunnel.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13889,-17,25,-1,'A Steep Slope','  The ground slopes downward at a steep angle here.  Rivulets of <b>water<1> dribbles\ndown the rocky slope, splashing in some spots.  A large cave is to the east.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13890,-16,26,-1,'A Large Cave','  This dark cave reeks of a heavy musky scent.  The dirt floor is packed down\nfrom use and dark <o>brown<1> animal hair is all over.  You can tell that this cave\nis populated by a fair number of some type of animal.  Dim light marks the exit\nto the southeast.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13891,-16,25,-1,'The Center Of A Large Cave','  This is the center of a large cave.  It reeks of heavy musk and there is\n<o>brown<1> animal hair all over.  A dim light marks the exit to the east.\nRivulets of <b>water<1> run in from the east and leave west, towards a steep\ndrop to a lower level.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13892,-16,24,-1,'A Large Cave','  This dark cave reeks of a heavy musky scent.  The dirt floor is packed down\nfrom use and dark <o>brown<1> animal hair is all over.  You can tell that this cave\nis populated by a fair number of some type of animal.  A large humanoid (ogre?)\n<W>skull<1> pokes out of the ground, half buried in the dirt.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13893,-15,25,-1,'A Large Cave','  This dark cave reeks of a heavy musky scent.  The dirt floor is packed down\nfrom use and dark <o>brown<1> animal hair is all over.  You can tell that this cave\nis populated by a fair number of some type of animal.  Rivulets of <b>water<1> flow\ndownslope to the west.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13894,-15,24,-1,'A Large Cave','  This dark cave reeks of a heavy musky scent.  The dirt floor is packed down\nfrom use and dark <o>brown<1> animal hair is all over.  You can tell that this cave\nis populated by a fair number of some type of animal.  Dim light marks the exit\nto the north.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13895,-14,26,-1,'Before A Larger Cave','  The cave widens out into a much larger area to the southwest.  A heavy musky\nscent wafts in from the larger cave and is somewhat dissipated by a light cool\nbreeze coming from the east.  Rivulets of <b>water<1> run down slope southwest.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13896,-14,27,-1,'A <r>Bloody<1> Cave','  Dried <r>blood<1> covers the floor and walls of this cave.  Some of it appears\nto be fresh and it glistens wetly on the walls and forms small pools between\nthe rocks on the floor.  This must be a feasting place of the beasts that\ninhabit this lair.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13897,-13,27,-1,'A Cave Full Of <W>Bones<1>','  Numerous <W>bones<1> litter the floor of this area, some of which still have chunks\nof <o>meat<1> left on them.  Many are stained with <r>blood<1> and others are crushed\ninto many pieces.  Some of the <W>bones<1> are obviously human and you can make out\nsome scraps of clothing.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13898,-13,26,-1,'A Small Damp Cave','  Rivulets of <b>water<1> run deeper into the cave to the west.  You notice a hunk\nof old shriveled flesh caught on a rock just before the tunnel leading\nnorthwest.  A cold breeze blows in from the southeast and you can hear the\nsplashing of the river from that direction.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13899,-11,24,-2,'Entrance Of A Small Cave','  This small cave has been tunneled into the river bank by some large animal,\nto be used as a lair.  The ground slopes downwards to the west and <b>water<1>\nsplashes in from the river and runs in rivulets into the cave.  A cold wind\nblows in from the east making it quite chilly here.\n',85,139592,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13900,0,0,0,'Maza\'s Slave Pen','  A foul <o>mud<1> composed of old rotted flesh, decomposed <W>bones<1> and <w>gravel<1> cover\nthe floor.  The stench here is a nearly unbearable odor of decay.  The living\nconditions, if they can be called that, are despicable.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13901,0,0,0,'Slave Pen','  A foul <o>mud<1> composed of old rotted flesh, decomposed <W>bones<1> and <w>gravel<1> cover\nthe floor.  The stench here is a nearly unbearable odor of decay.  The living\nconditions, if they can be called that, are despicable.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13902,0,0,0,'Maza\'s Slaves','  Being one of the more popular slave traders in the area, Maza specializes\nin fixed price and small quantity slave orders.  Although the quality is not\nas great as some of the other traders, the prices are always low and the\nslaves are always available.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13903,0,0,0,'Stone Stairs','  Wide stairs lead upwards to the <r>Merchant Ring<1> section of <w>Yautepec<1>.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(13904,0,0,0,'Stone Stairs','  Wide stairs lead upwards to the <r>Merchant Ring<1> section of <w>Yautepec<1>.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
