(14087,0,0,0,'<g>Guard Walk<1>','  This path affords a view of the entire city of <w>Yautepec<1>.  From this vantage\npoint, the guards can spot any trouble that arises and keep tabs on visiters\nwalking along the <r>Merchant Ring<1> or in the <o>Slave Market<1>.  The path encircles\nabout half of the city, providing enough angle to view everything.  A wide\nstone staircase leads down.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14088,0,0,0,'<g>Guard Walk<1>','  This path affords a view of the entire city of <w>Yautepec<1>.  From this vantage\npoint, the guards can spot any trouble that arises and keep tabs on visiters\nwalking along the <r>Merchant Ring<1> or in the <o>Slave Market<1>.  The path encircles\nabout half of the city, providing enough angle to view everything.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14089,0,0,0,'<g>Guard Walk<1>','  This path affords a view of the entire city of <w>Yautepec<1>.  From this vantage\npoint, the guards can spot any trouble that arises and keep tabs on visiters\nwalking along the <r>Merchant Ring<1> or in the <o>Slave Market<1>.  The path encircles\nabout half of the city, providing enough angle to view everything.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14090,0,0,0,'<g>Guard Walk<1>','  This path affords a view of the entire city of <w>Yautepec<1>.  From this vantage\npoint, the guards can spot any trouble that arises and keep tabs on visiters\nwalking along the <r>Merchant Ring<1> or in the <o>Slave Market<1>.  The path encircles\nabout half of the city, providing enough angle to view everything.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14091,0,0,0,'Entrance of <w>Yautepec<1>','  The main gate of the city lies to the south, while a wider walkway lies to\nthe north.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14092,0,0,0,'Guard Barracks','  Although sparse by illithid standards, these barracks are as well appointed\nas a wealthy human merchants home would be.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14093,0,0,0,'Entrance of <w>Yautepec<1>','  Guard barracks have been carved out of stone to the west.  The main gate of\nthe city lies to the south.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14094,0,0,0,'Guard Barracks','  Although sparse by illithid standards, these barracks are as well appointed\nas a wealthy human merchants home would be.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14095,0,0,0,'Entrance of <w>Yautepec<1>','  Guard barracks have been carved out of stone to the west.  The main gate of\nthe city lies to the south.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14096,0,0,0,'Gate of <w>Yautepec<1>','  A very heavy portcullis has been built directly into the surrounding stone\nhere, to limit access to and from the city.  As the sole entrance to <w>Yautepec<1>,\nit is very heavily guarded and under constant watch.  A large contingent of\nguards is always on hand to search arriving merchants and to thwart any\npossible invasions or slave uprisings.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14097,0,0,0,'Entrance Tunnel','  This tunnel provides access to and from the <o>Slave Market<1>.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14098,0,0,0,'Entrance Tunnel','  This tunnel provides access to and from the <o>Slave Market<1>.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14099,0,0,0,'Stone Stair Spiral','  This wide set of stairs spirals up from the <o>Slave Market<1> to the <g>Guard\nWalk<1>, near the city gates.  A tunnel leads to the <o>Slave Market<1> to the north.\n',105,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14100,29,-37,0,'A Faint, Fading Path','  This path winds along a sloping terrain covered with heather and sage, with\npatches of lavender casting its <p>violet<1> hues among the <g>green<1> of the sage and the\n<k>grey<1> of the heather.  The path is partially overgrown with weeds and wild\nflowers, and you see it continue in the distance, but very faintly...\n',83,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14101,29,-38,0,'Farther Along the Path','  You stumble on the erratic patches of weeds and brush as you continue along\nthe path.  To each side of the path are small bushes with <r>blood-red berries<1>\npeeking out from beneath the scrubby leaves.  You hear the titterings of small\nanimals as you disturb the peace with the fall of your footstep.\n',83,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14102,29,-36,0,'Faint Trail','  This path winds along a sloping terrain covered with heather and sage, with\npatches of lavender casting its <p>violet<1> hues among the <g>green<1> of the sage and the\n<k>grey<1> of the heather.  The path is partially overgrown with weeds and wild\nflowers, and you see it continue in the distance, but very faintly...\n',83,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14103,29,-39,0,'A Stony Creekbed','  As you pass over the remains of a once bubbling brook, you observe the beauty\nof the different color smooth pebbles and notice that some of them are aligned\nby color, as if some small child was playing by the bank one day long ago...\n',83,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14104,30,-38,0,'A Dead End','  The path dwindles off to nonexistence as you start to plow your way through\nhigh weeds.  All around you hear the buzzing of honey bees and the rustling of\ntall grass blowing in the wind.\n',83,139272,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14105,29,-40,0,'A Curve in the Path','  As the path gently curves around to the east, you behold a breathtaking view\nfrom the summit of the hill on which you are standing.  Below you spreads a\n<B>vast body of glistening blue water<1>, and along the shore is the ruin of what\nonce must have been an awe-inspiring palace.  The landscape gently slopes down\ntowards the sea, and the high grasses of the hills gradually become less wild\nas you come to the edge of what was once civilization.\n',83,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14106,30,-40,0,'A Downward Slope','  The path winds its way down the gentle slope as you continue to follow it\neast towards the sea.  At your feet scurry small animals that have been routed\nfrom the underbrush by your disturbing footsteps.  The air smells of salt as a\nswift breeze wafts its way up the windward side of the hill.\n',83,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14107,31,-40,0,'The Foot of the Hill','  You have reached the bottom of the path that leads to the sea.  All around you\nsee overgrown vegetation that was apparently once domesticated, but has now\ngone wild.\n',83,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14109,32,-40,0,'The Shoreline','  You have reached the rocky shoreline that runs to the north.  To the south,\nthe shore becomes less harsh and gradually turns into a beach.  Off in the\ndistance to the east, you see the prow of a galleon protruding out of the calm\nwater.\n',83,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14110,32,-41,0,'The Shoreline','  You stumble over sharp rocks as you continue traversing the shoreline.  You\nfeel the sea mist as the waves crash against the rocks and splash up into the\nair.  The scent of sea salt assails your nostrils, and you notice a large\nseagull flying overhead.\n',83,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14111,32,-39,0,'The Shoreline','  The terrain becomes treacherous as you pick your way along the rocky path.\nThe waves crash violently against the rocks and spray all over the surrounding\nareas.\n',83,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14112,32,-42,0,'A Rocky Beach','  This is the beginning of the transition from the harsh shoreline to a sandy\nbeach.  All around your feet lie smooth pebbles and pieces of broken shells,\nand you notice the pattern left on the sand by the undulating currents of the\ntide.\n',83,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14113,32,-38,0,'The North Shore','  The path becomes impassable here as giant rocks loom up above your head.  You\nfeel a chill breeze as the cliffs create a vortex through which the wind blows\nnot as gently as it did on the more southern shore.\n',83,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14114,32,-43,0,'The South Beach','  You have reached the southern end of the shoreline, or at least that part of\nthe shoreline that is fully accessible to most travelers.  On the sand you see\na veritable plethora of tracks, made by the small feet of birds and various\nsea-creatures.  Here you see that the waves have made small undulating patterns\non the sand, and all around your feet lie all kinds of different sea shells.\nSouth and east from here stretches the mighty <B>Myrian Ocean<1>.\n',83,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14115,33,-43,0,'The Shallows','  You are in knee-deep water looking out over the beautiful seascape.  You have\nto struggle to keep your footing as you feel the tide begin to pull you out\ntowards the open water.  The current is strong here, and you realize that\nextreme caution must be observed if you chose to go out deeper into the water.\nA beach can be reached west of here, while south and east the ocean stretches\noff to the horizon.\n',83,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14116,34,-43,0,'Deep Water','  You have to swim to keep your head above water as you continue east through\nthe sea.  Your feet are about 5 feet from the sea floor, and the current is\nbecoming much stronger as you go further and further out into the sea.  The\nmighty <B>Myrian Ocean<1> stretches away south of here.\n',83,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14117,35,-43,0,'Underwater','  The powerful undertow has pulled you below the surface of the water.  If you\nlook up, you can see the surface about 7 feet above your head, but for some\nreason you cannot swim up to get a breath of air.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14118,36,-44,0,'A Greater Depth','  You have sunk down even lower in the water as the current drags you with it.\nIf you are unable to swim, or cannot breath underwater, you are out of luck.\nAll around you see the undersea life, and you watch intently as fish swim by\nyour head with out hesitation.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14119,37,-45,0,'Deeper Down and Farther Out','  As you continue on a southerly course, the water gets deeper and deeper, and\nbecomes increasingly difficult to reach the surface.  But the beautiful view of\nyour surrounding more than makes up for the danger that you are risking.  All\naround you sway fronds of underwater plant life, and darting in and around them\nare small, brightly colored fishes, searching for food.  The fish in this area\nlook harmless, but looks can be deceiving.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14120,38,-46,0,'A Sub-aquatic Garden','  You are swimming through an underwater garden of multi-colored seaweeds and\nkelps.  The hues are breathtaking,  and you have never before seen something\nthat compares  to the beauty of this place.  It is like a fairy world, and the\npeace that the water creates soothes your mind and opens your eyes to the\nwonder of the deep.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14121,38,-47,0,'An Underwater Path','  You have reached the beginning of a mysterious underwater path that leads\nsouth away from the shore.  You consider that it is highly unusual for there to\nbe a path here at all, and think it even stranger that it appears to be paved\nwith small, multi-colored pebbles.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14122,39,-45,0,'The Entrance to a Sub-aquatic Cave','  You are swimming before the opening of a small cave that apparently reaches\nfar into the mass of rock that it was cut from by the sometimes harsh currents\nand tectonic forces.  As you peer inside the dark cavern, you can see that it\nwould not be prudent to enter without a light of some sort.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14123,37,-47,0,'A School of Fish','  As you swim along you accidentally collide with a large school of small,\n<g>green<1> and <y>yellow<1> striped fish.  They look harmless enough, so you don\'t pay\nthem much mind.  You admire the scenery as you swim through the beautiful\nreef-like area.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14124,40,-45,0,'The Cave','  This area is totally dark and filled with thick, underwater plant-life.  It\nseems to be colder here than it was in the open water, and there is distinct\nair of evilness that pervades the cave.\n',83,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(14125,38,-48,0,'The Path Widens','  As you continue along the underwater path, you realize that it becomes\ngradually wider and more marked.  To each side of the path, you notice\nartfully placed underwater vegetation, and begin to think that nature could\nnever have placed them there without the help of skillful hands...\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14126,38,-49,0,'Farther Along the Path','  The path continues on south without altering its course in the slightest.  You\nwonder how the pebbles on the road keep from getting displaced, and guess that\nsome kind of magic force is protecting the path.  You see a large stone to the\nright side of the road, and you can barely make out an inscription on its\nsmooth side.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14127,38,-50,0,'Coral Road','  The small path turns into a larger road as you pass the road marker.  You see\nthat instead of being paved with small pebbles, the road is now covered with\n<R>crushed, red coral<1>, creating a beautiful effect against the blue cast of the\nother surroundings.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14128,38,-51,0,'An Air Pocket','  You have inadvertently stepped into a pocket of air that has been magically\nplaced around this section of the road.  The sea-people of Kalysia have many\nfriends above the water, and it was necessary to place magically sustained air\nbubbles periodically along the path to enable those who wish to visit the\nopportunity.\n',83,131085,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14129,38,-52,0,'Coral Road','  You continue on the north and south route of Coral Road.  Everywhere you look\nyou see endless beauty of form and color, and the peace of your environment\nnearly overwhelms you.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14130,38,-53,0,'Coral Road','  You continue along the russet-colored path.  The water is crystal clear, and\neverything looks surreal in the pale blue light.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14131,38,-54,0,'Coral Road','  The <R>red coral<1> of the path creates an interesting contrast with the white sand\nas you continue on your way.  To either side of the road are various shells,\npebbles, and bones from small marine animals.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14132,38,-55,0,'A Decision','  Here the road branches off to the south, while the main road continues\nnorth and southeast.  You must make a decision that may affect your\njourney indefinitely.  There is no marker or sign that indicates where\nthe southern way leads, so if you choose that way you must be prepared\nfor anything...\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14133,38,-56,0,'A Small Path','  This path runs north and south and has no definite or indicated destination.\nYou see that the way is not paved, but is merely cleared of vegetation and\nother maritime objects that could be considered obstacles.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14134,38,-57,0,'A Small Path','  You continue along the small path as it runs north and south through the\ncrystal clear water.  The way is slightly sinister in its surroundings, and\nthere is not the typical feeling of calm that generally accompanies the rest of\nthe sub-marine realm.  You notice a small rock to the left of the path, and you\nsee that it is inscribed with words that are partially weathered and difficult\nto make out.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14135,38,-58,0,'A Small Path','  The path is very narrow here, forcing you to brush up against the plants as\nyou continue along your way.  You notice that the water is rather dark, and you\nconsider that it might be wise to carry a light before you go on.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14136,38,-59,0,'Tunnel entrance','  You are at the entrance to a tunnel that leads below a huge network of marine\nvegetation.  The path is basically clear here, but it is very dark, and looks\nas if no one has been this way for years...\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14137,38,-60,0,'The Tunnel','  You shiver unconsciously as you pass through the dark entryway.  To both the\nleft and right, it is impossible to penetrate the thick barrier of underwater\nfoliage.  Your only way lies to the north or south, so you can either escape\nthe darkness to the north, or continue on your way into the dark hole...\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14138,38,-61,0,'The Tunnel','  If you have an ounce of claustrophobia, this is not the place for you.  It\nalmost looks like the fronds of vegetation that make up the walls of the tunnel\nare closing in and trying to swallow anything that tries to pass by them...\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14139,38,-62,0,'The Lair','  You have reached the lair of a Sea-Hag, and you instantly feel the evilness\nexuding from the very walls of her den.  Along the walls, live, animated\nvegetation stretch their slimy fingers out as if to grasp you and to never let\nyou go.  You shiver uncomfortably at the sight.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14140,39,-56,0,'Coral Road','  The road begins to dip down as you continue to travel along the path.  You\nnotice a slight change in temperature as the path leads you to greater depths.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14141,40,-57,0,'Coral Road','  You continue along the russet-colored path.  The water is crystal clear, and\neverything looks surreal in the pale blue light.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14142,41,-58,0,'An Air Pocket','  This is another bubble created and sustained by the magic of the mer-people.\nThis area was created to allow the overworld dwellers to travel in safety\nthrough the sea.  Rest here and regain your mana.\n',83,131085,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14143,42,-59,0,'Coral Road','  You continue along the russet-colored path.  The water is crystal clear, and\neverything looks surreal in the pale blue light.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14144,43,-60,0,'Coral Road','  You have come to the easternmost end of the Coral Road.  To the southeast, it looks\nas if the path just disappears, but you realize that this cannot be the case...\n',83,131085,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14145,31,-43,0,'A Trail Farther Up The Shore','  This area is slightly more inland than the beach, but it is still very sandy,\nbut sand was carried here by the wind, not by the tide.   Patches of coarse\ngrass thrust up from the light, porous earth, and you see tracks that were made\nby some strange animal heading west...  \n',102,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14146,30,-43,0,'A Narrow Trail','  As you follow the tracks of some unidentifiable animal, you must make your\nway slowly and with much effort, for weeds and other obstacles make traveling\ndifficult here.  If you stand on the tips of your toes, you can just make out\nthe ruins of what used to be some sort of huge structure rising above the \nlevel of the overgrown plant-life.  \n',102,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14147,29,-43,0,'A Trail','  The path is easier to follow here than it is to the east, and you continue to\nwonder what kind of animal kept the trail open at all.  The weeds are very high\nat this point, obstructing any further view to either side of the path.  \n',102,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14148,30,-44,0,'A Small Animal Trail','  You can see tiny footprints in the sandy earth as you follow this almost\nundetectable path.  The undergrowth is very thick here, and almost impassable.\n',102,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14149,30,-45,0,'A Hole in the Hill','  Many would have to crawl to gain access to this very closed in space.  You \nsmell a musty scent, and you wonder what type of animal inhabits this place.  \n',102,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,40,0,'',NULL),
(14150,28,-43,0,'The Opening to a Clearing','  The trail opens into a small clearing of weeds, but far larger than the\nclearing itself is the huge pile of stone rubble that clearly used to be a\nstructure of some sort.  Sadly, the place looks like it was abandoned hundreds\nof years ago, and left to fall to ruin as the weathering affects of wind and \nwater took their toll.  \n',102,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14151,27,-43,0,'Among the Rubble','  You are among the huge blocks of stone that were once part of an imposing\nwall.  All around your feet grow ugly, invading weeds, twisting their way among\ncracks in the stones, and choking out all forms of domesticated plant-life that\nstill struggle to exist.  \n',102,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14152,27,-42,0,'Before a Solitary Door','  You are before the only entrance left standing to the interior of the \nruined structure.  The dilapidated structure looms up before you, and you \nfeel dwarfed by the sheer massiveness of the arched door frame.  You notice \na weathered inscription on a large boulder which fills the door frame.  \n',102,393224,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,4,'',NULL),
(14153,27,-41,0,'A Long Corridor','  This hallway is huge and extremely dusty.  You stifle a sneeze as your\nfootsteps stir up dust particles that have long lain undisturbed.  On the \nwalls hang moth-eaten and faded tapestries, but you can still see that at \nanother time, they must have been magnificent.  You notice that the walls \nare remarkably sound, and realize that some strong magic must be on the \nplace to keep it standing for as long as it has.  An arched doorway to the \nsouth appears to be an exit from this place, but a large boulder sits in\nthe doorway.  You notice a strange inscription carved into the boulder.     \n',102,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,180,4,'',NULL),
(14154,26,-37,0,'A Small Bedroom','  Once probably furnished with simple but well constructed furniture the \nbedroom now lies empty of anything other then rotted and decayed debris.\nA small door sits in the south wall as the only apparent exit.\n',102,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14155,27,-40,0,'The Southern End of a Grand Hall','  This room is simply gargantuan in its size.  The high vaulted ceilings span\nfar above your head, and flying buttresses adorn the tall windows.  The ceiling\nmust have been a magnificent gold at one time, but now only flakes of the gold\nplate remain to tell the tale.  On the floor, you notice a large, round symbol.\nIt appears to be in the exact center of the room.  \n',102,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(14156,27,-39,0,'The Center of a Grand Hall','  This is the northern sector of the Hall.  To the north you see a large,\nraised platform made from a dense, white stone.  It appears to be some sort of\naltar or the seat of authority for this structure.  The stone blocks of the \nlarge, round platform are in perfect shape.  \n',102,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(14157,26,-40,0,'The Southwestern Corner of a Grand Hall','  You have reached the the southwestern corner of the great hall.  The stones\nthat make up the walls here are slightly weathered, and upon the far north wall\nyou see by the mark left that a huge tapestry once hung there.  \n',102,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(14158,28,-38,0,'The Northeastern Corner of a Grand Hall','  This is the easternmost extreme of the huge hallway.  To the west, you see\nthe broad expanse of floor that leads to  the other end of the hall, and you\nmarvel at the craftsmanship of the builders.  To the north is a small doorway\nthat stands partially open.  It is dark inside.  \n',102,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(14159,27,-38,0,'The Dais','  You are in the center of a large, round stone platform.  All around the side\nof the dais, curved steps of smooth marble lead down to the hard, slick floor.\nYou can tell by the sound of your footsteps on the rock that the platform is\nbuilt solidly and without a break.  This floor-work was crafted by a skilled\nartisan, you surmise.  \n',102,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(14160,28,-37,0,'The Weaponry','  You have reached a weapons chamber in the ruined structure.  It is a little \nodd that there would be a weaponry opening out from what appears to be temple, \nbut nevertheless that is the only thing this place could have been.  All along\nthe walls are remnants of ancient looking, antiquated swords and battle-axes,\nas well as nearly disintegrated halberds and war-hammers.  It looks as if they\nwould crumble if you even breathed on them, much less touched them.  \n',102,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14161,28,-40,0,'The Southeastern Corner of a Grand Hall','  You are in the easternmost end of the grand hall.  Against the wall are piles\nof rubble and heaps of dust, and you see motes of dust swirling in the air\nbefore you as well.  This place looks as if it has not been disturbed for many\nyears.  \n',102,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(14162,28,-39,0,'The Eastern End of a Grand Hall','  You are at the easternmost end of the vast hall.  Dust and debris litter the\nfloor, and dust swirls through the air as your footsteps disturb the peace of\nthe chamber.  You hear a scurrying of little furry feet.  \n',102,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(14163,26,-39,0,'The Western End of a Grand Hall','  This is the westernmost end of the massive hall.  Debris lies scattered about\nthe floor here, and dust flies up in your face as you disturb the peace of the\nhall with your footsteps.  \n',102,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(14164,26,-38,0,'The Northwestern Corner of a Grand Hall','  You have reached the far northwestern corner of the vast hall.  You see\nnothing particularly special about your surroundings, but you feel a cold draft\ncoming from the east.  To the north a door lies its locking mechanism long ago\nrusted into a useless state.  \n',102,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(14165,27,-37,0,'The Treasure Chamber','  As you walk through the door, you detect a hint of the smell of rotting\nleather, and dust flies up about the room as your commotion disturbs the peace.\nAll around you are wooden shelves, plated with gold and silver; you can see\nthat in another time they must have been breathtaking.  On the floor rots the\nlasts vestiges of what used to be a rich, beautiful carpet, but the beauty is\nlong gone, and the rug is now frayed nearly beyond recognition.  \n',102,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14166,44,-61,0,'A Precipice','  You are standing on the edge of a high sub-aquatic cliff, and you behold the\nawesome spectacle laid out before your eyes as you gaze downwards.  You are\nstanding on the boundaries of Kalysia, the land of the Sea-People.\n',83,131085,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14167,44,-61,-1,'The Foot of the Cliff','  You have reached the bottom of the precipice, and you see the Coral Road\ncontinue to the east.  Also to the east, you see a huge gateway made of\n<R>brilliant red coral<1>, studded with what appear to be diamonds and <G>emeralds<1> of\nenormous size.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14168,45,-61,-1,'The End of Coral Road','  You have reached the end of the road that leads eastwards to Kalysia, the\ntown of the Sea-People.  Just a few yards to the east stands the beautiful\nfront gate of the town.  As the walls of the sub-marine valley provide adequate\nprotection from foes should they choose to attack from the sides, the coral\nwall that encircles the town is superfluous, but it is also incredibly\nbeautiful.  In fact, the entirety of your surroundings suggests the love of the\nvisually divine.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14169,46,-61,-1,'The Gate To Kalysia','  You are beneath the imposing front gate of the beautiful town of Kalysia.\nAbove your head spans the vast sea of blue water, and you see all kinds of\nsea-life swimming or floating through the deep.  Eastward lies the town, and to\nyour west leads the Coral Road upward over the precipice.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14170,47,-61,-1,'Inside the Gate','  You are inside the front gate that opens to the underwater town of Kalysia.\nThis place is very peaceful, and lacks the normal bustle of every day town life\nabove the sea.  To the left and right you see dwellings and such, made mainly\nof different and vivid colors of coral.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14171,48,-61,-1,'Anemone Avenue','  You are on the main street that runs through the town all the way to the\npalace.  The smooth road is paved with cemented sediments, speckled here and\nthere with the <R>red coral<1> of Coral Road.  On each side of the street sway tall\naquatic trees, the like of which has never been seen in any other place but\nKalysia.  You see dwellings and places of business all around you.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14172,49,-61,-1,'Anemone Avenue','  You continue on your way as you take the central road of Kalysia.  The way\nleads east and west, and you see it join with Coral Road just outside the town\ngate.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14173,50,-61,-1,'An Intersection','  You have reached the intersection that joins Anemone Avenue with Conch\nStreet.  If you go south, you will find the Hospitality Center, and farther on\nare some other buildings.  To the north lies a garrison and the gatehouse.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14174,51,-61,-1,'Anemone Avenue','  You are on the main street running east and west from the front gate of\nKalysia.  The way is paved with <R>red coral<1>, and bordering the road are colorful\nfronds of marine plant-life.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14175,50,-60,-1,'North Conch Street','  You are on Conch Street, north of the first intersection from the front gate\nof Kalysia.  Further on down the street, you see a large building constructed\nmostly of <R>red coral<1>, and another large structure directly across from it.  The\nstreet runs north and south.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14176,50,-62,-1,'South Conch Street','  You are on the southern end of the first north/south road from the town gate.\nTo the southwest you see a large, octagonal building that is well lit, and you\nsense a strong feeling of peace emanating from its walls.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14177,50,-63,-1,'South Conch Street','  This wide, pleasant street runs north and south through Kalysia, and is\nbordered by odd but pleasing aquatic plant life.  The street itself is paved\nwith sand and bits of <R>red coral<1>.  To the west you see the Hospitality Center.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14178,49,-63,-1,'Entrance to the Hospitality Center','  You are before a large, octagonal building made entirely of <P>vivid purple\ncoral<1>.  Lights shine brightly from the round windows, and the door is standing\nwide open to welcome you.  There is a large sign swaying on its hooks in the\nwater above your head.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14179,48,-63,-1,'The Hospitality Center','  You are just within the front doorway of the center for the welcoming of\nvisitors to Kalysia.  In this building, the oxygen level of all rooms is\nsustained by the magic force placed on it.  To the west is the lobby, and to\nyour north and south are private rooms with locked doors.\n',83,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14180,48,-62,-1,'The Public Relations Committee Staffroom','  This room is dominated by a huge oblong table that stretches from one end of\nthe room to the other.  There are papers scattered everywhere on the floor, and\nit looks like this place could use a little cleaning.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14181,48,-64,-1,'The Public Relations Committee Chairperson\'s Office','  This office is simply filled with stacks of white paper, and crumpled balls\nof used tissue litter the large wooden desk that dominates the small room.  The\nroom is lit by a large orb of glowing light, and a window looks out into the\nsea.\n',83,131209,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14182,47,-63,-1,'The Lobby','  You are at the far east end of the lobby of the Hospitality Center.  Before\nyou spans a vast floor made out of a strange material that you cannot quite\nidentify.  At the far west end of the lobby is the information desk, and\ncomfortable chairs are strategically placed around the beautiful fountain the\noccupies the center of the room.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14183,46,-63,-1,'The Center of the Lobby','  You are in the middle of the huge, airy lobby.  A <k>large grey marble fountain<1>\ndominates the center of the area, and many chairs are placed about the rim of\nthe water.  The information desk is to the west.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14184,45,-63,-1,'The Information Desk','  You are directly in front of the main desk of the Hospitality Center of\nKalysia.  There is a bell cord hanging off to one side, and various books and\nlogs are scattered over the desk.\n',83,164025,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14185,46,-62,-1,'Entrance to the North Wing','  You are at the entrance to the north wing of the Hospitality center.\nNear the center of the room a large carved set of stairs descends to the\nnorth wing below.  An inscription carved in italics has been placed on\nthe first step.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14186,46,-64,-1,'The Entrance to the South Wing','  You are at the entrance to the south wing of the Hospitality center.\nNear the center of the room a large carved set of stairs descends to the\nnorth wing below.  An inscription carved in italics has been placed on\nthe first step.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14187,46,-64,-2,'A Corridor','  This is a short hallway that stretches on for about 15 feet and ends at a set\nof double doors.  The hall is empty as far as you can tell, and in the corners\nof the room float small orbs of light that give off a rather eerie cast.\nA large carved set of stairs spiral upwards out of the room.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14188,46,-62,-2,'The Hallway','  You are in the hallway of the northern wing of the visitor\'s center.  There\nare a few doors in this hallway, and at the far end you can see a faint glow.\nA large carved staircase leads upwards out of the room.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14189,46,-61,-2,'The Hallway','  The hall stretches a long way to the north, and you can detect a faint glow\ncoming from the end of the corridor.  To your east is a closed door.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14190,47,-61,-2,'Storage Room','  You are overwhelmed by a cloud of dust as you open the door.  A faint musty\nsmell lingers in the air, and various types of cleaning implements lean against\nthe walls.  Also, spare chairs and a desk or two take up space in the small,\ncramped room.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14191,46,-60,-2,'The Hallway','  You continue along the hallway as you make your way towards the eerie glow at\nthe end of the corridor.  You dodge a large chair that is sitting right in the\nmiddle of the hall for no apparent reason.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14192,46,-59,-2,'The Hallway','  You are near the northern end of the hallway, and the glow becomes brighter\nas you move towards it.  The hall is beginning to get a little stuffy, and a\nstrange warmth is starting to fill the area.  To your west is a door.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14193,45,-59,-2,'An Empty Room','  The only thing you see here is a lot of dust and sand particles.  There is no\nlight in here like the rest of the area\'s in this building, and you think that\na little strange...\n',83,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14194,46,-58,-2,'The Northern End of the Hallway','  You have reached the very end of the long hallway.  To the direct north is a\ndoor that is partially cracked, and through the crack shines an eerie dull\nglow...\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14195,46,-57,-2,'A Brightly Lit Room','  You are nearly blinded by the fierce light as you step into the room.  But\nmore unusual than the light itself is the source of the light.  In the far\nnorth west corner of the room stands a brightly glowing, beautifully carved\ngold mirror.  You hear a faint humming sound.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14196,46,-65,-2,'A Set of Double Doors','  You have reached the doors that end the southern corridor.  The doors are\nmassive in size, and the dark, smooth wood is carved with intricate designs and\nstrange runic characters.  Above the doors is a bas-relief carved in the form\nof a beautiful deity that you are certain you have seen before...\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14197,46,-66,-2,'The Grand Ballroom','  You are standing at the entrance to a huge room with high vaulted ceilings\nand gilded walls.  The elegance of the place dazzles you, and you just stare at\nthe intricate decorations that adorn the walls and ceiling.  The room is\ntotally bare of furniture, but a sparkling fountain occupies the center of the\nroom.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14198,46,-67,-2,'South towards the Fountain','  You are about 20 feet to the south of the doors, and 30 feet away from the\nfountain in the center of the room.  The smooth floor spans out hundreds of feet\nbefore you in each direction, but the fact that there are no furnishings in the\nroom serves to make the area look even larger.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14201,46,-68,-2,'The Fountain','  You are before a huge marble fountain that shoots fresh water 10 feet into\nthe air.  Other smaller streams of water arch out to the sides and fall into\nthe wide basin.  The water seems to be a strange shade of <b>blue<1>.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14202,47,-67,-2,'The Northeast Corner','  You are at the northeast corner of the Grand  Ballroom.  In the center of the\nroom you see the large marble fountain, and all around you spans the spacious\nfloor.  This room is remarkably free of dust and cobwebs, but that is not so\nstrange as this building is underwater.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14203,45,-67,-2,'The Northwest Corner','  You are at the northwest corner of the Grand Ballroom of the Hospitality\nCenter.  You can see that the town of Kalysia spared no expense when building\nthis visitor\'s area, and you are very impressed with the beauty and elegance\nthat surrounds you.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14204,47,-68,-2,'The East Wall','  You are before the extreme eastern wall of the Grand Ballroom.  The fountain\ndominates the center of the room, but the overall bareness of the room serves\nto accentuate the spaciousness of the area.  The floor stretches out to the\nwest about 80 feet, and the smooth floor gleams in the eerie light of the\nglowing orbs that float in the corners of the room.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14205,45,-68,-2,'The West Wall','  You are in the middle of the west sector of the Grand Ballroom.  The wall\nreaches up about 50 feet to the huge, gilded ceiling, and the floor stretches\nout from your feet a great distance to the east.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14206,46,-69,-2,'The Southern Wall','  You are at the far wall opposite the double doors that lead out into the\nlobby.  To the north the fountain bubbles continuously, and to the left and\nright the floor spans out quite a few feet.  The high ceiling looms above your\nhead, making you feel like you are very small and insignificant.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14207,47,-69,-2,'The Southeastern Corner','  This is the southeastern corner of the Grand Ballroom.  You do not notice\nanything remarkable about this section of the room except that it is very clean\nand well-kept.  You see no dust or cobwebs laying or hanging about, but  when\nyou consider that this building is underwater, that does not come as such a big\nsurprise.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14208,45,-69,-2,'The Southwest Corner','  You are at the southwest corner of the Grand Ballroom.  The area is\nremarkably clean and free of dust and cobwebs, but upon reflection you realize\nthat since the building is underwater, that is not so strange an attribute.\n',83,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14209,50,-59,-1,'North Conch Street','  You are on the north side of Kalysia, on the first road from the town gate.\nTo the west you see the barracks of the town guard, and to the east is the\nmess-hall.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14210,51,-59,-1,'Entrance to the Mess-hall','  You see a large, flat-roofed building made of the <R>red coral<1> that comprises\nmost of the building material of Kalysia.  The double doors to the east are\nhigh and arched, and there are stone steps leading up to them.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14211,49,-59,-1,'Entrance to the Guardhouse','  You are before the entrance to the barracks of the town guard of Kalysia.  The\nbuilding is long and flat-roofed, and is constructed of <R>red coral<1>.  The tall\ndoorway looms above your head, and you notice that the double-doors are open wide.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14212,52,-59,-1,'The Mess-hall','  You are in the mess-hall for the town guard of Kalysia.  The room is large\nand bare of furniture except for long, rectangular tables with benches drawn up\nto them.  To the north is the kitchen.\n',83,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(14213,52,-58,-1,'The Kitchen','  You have entered the kitchen area of the mess-hall.  You nothing out of the\nordinary here--kitchen utensils hanging from the ceiling, waist-high counters\nlining the walls.  You notice that there are no ovens in this particular\nkitchen, however.\n',83,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(14214,48,-59,-1,'The Guardhouse','  You are in the barracks provided for the town-guard of Kalysia.  The ceiling\nis rather low here in the main room, and the lighting is a bit dim, but you can\nstill see your surroundings perfectly if you carry a light.\n',83,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,10,70,0,'',NULL),
(14215,48,-60,-1,'The Bunkroom','  This main room of the barracks is totally filled with bunks of a uniform size\nand the same <k>grey color<1>.  There are no bedclothes on the bunks, and no pillows,\nwhich you think a little odd.  The room is spotlessly clean and free of\nclutter, and everything is straight and in order.\n',83,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,10,70,0,'',NULL),
(14216,50,-58,-1,'North Conch Street','  You are on the first street that runs north and south through the town east\nof the front gate.  Lining this pleasant street are colorful sub-aquatic plants\nand trees, and the street itself is paved with small pieces of <R>red coral<1>.\nFarther north you see an intersection.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14217,50,-57,-1,'The Corner of Conch and Dolphin','  The road makes a \'T\' here as Conch Street terminates at the wall of the basin\nthat contains the town.  Running east and west is Dolphin Boulevard, the wall\nroad on the north side of Kalysia.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14218,51,-57,-1,'Dolphin Boulevard','  This street runs east and west along the north edge of town by the basin\nwall.  On the left side of the street is the craggy surface of the wall, and on\nthe right side are various dwellings of the inhabitants of Kalysia.  Aquatic\nplants line the edge of the road.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14219,49,-57,-1,'Dolphin Boulevard','  You are following Dolphin Boulevard, the street that runs east and west along\nthe northern edge of the town.  The basin wall blocks movement to the north,\nbut to the south is a small bare area.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14220,52,-57,-1,'Dolphin Boulevard','  This street runs east and west along the basin wall on the north side of the\ntown.  On the left hand side of the street is the rugged surface of the wall\nitself, blocking all movement to the north, and to the right of the road are\ngently swaying aquatic plants.  The road is paved with chunks of <R>red coral<1>\nmixed in with the <w>white sand<1> of the sea-floor.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14221,49,-58,-1,'An Empty Lot','  You have made your way to an area that has been left to itself for some time,\napparently.  The lot is behind the barracks of the town guard, and looks like\nit has been roughly used recently, for training or some other violent activity.\nThe ground is sandy with errant chunks of coral lying here and there.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14222,53,-57,-1,'Corner of Dolphin and Templeway','  At this point in the road, Dolphin Street meets up with Templeway, which is\nobviously the road that leads to the temple.  The road is very well taken care\nof, and there is a total absence of litter and refuse.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14223,53,-58,-1,'Templeway','  Templeway runs north and south through the central part of Kalysia, and by\nits name, it can be construed that somewhere along this road lies the temple of\nKalysia.  The way is paved with <R>red coral<1> and <w>white sand<1>, and bordering the\nstreet are colorful aquatic plants.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14224,55,-57,-1,'Dolphin Boulevard','  You are on Dolphin Boulevard, the road that runs the northern perimeter of\nKalysia.  To the left is the basin wall, obstructing all movement to the north,\nand on the right sway tall fronds of colorful underwater plants.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14225,55,-57,-1,'Dolphin Boulevard','  You are on Dolphin Boulevard, the road that runs the northern perimeter of\nKalysia.  To the left is the basin wall, obstructing all movement to the north,\nand on the right sway tall fronds of colorful underwater plants.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14226,56,-57,-1,'Dolphin Boulevard','  You are on Dolphin Boulevard, the street that follows the northern perimeter\nof Kalysia.  To the north, the road is bordered by the basin wall, obstructing\nall movement in that direction.  To the south sway tall fronds of colorful\nunderwater plants.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14227,0,0,0,'Corner of Dolphin and Sand','  You have reached the intersection of Dolphin Boulevard and Sand Street.  To\nthe north is the basin wall, blocking all movement in that direction, and to\nthe south, Sand Street runs across the east side of Kalysia.\n',0,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14228,57,-58,-1,'Sand Street','  Sand Street is a beautiful road paved with <R>red<1> and <P>purple<1> coral, and bordered\nby tall aquatic plants that wave gently in the water current.  Farther down the\nstreet you see various structures that appear to be houses, and you notice a\nglowing light coming from the southeast.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14229,57,-59,-1,'Sand Street','  You are on North Sand Street, the last street running north and south from\nthe front gate of Kalysia.  Farther down the way you see archway of tall marine\nplant-life, and you also notice an odd glow coming from the southeast.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14230,57,-60,-1,'Sand Street','  This road runs north and south through the eastern end of Kalysia.  The way\nhere is covered with brilliant <R>red<1> and <P>purple<1> coral, with patches of <w>white sand<1>\nhere and there.  The road is covered by a canopy of tall aquatic plants, and\nyou notice the beauty of your surroundings as you make your way through the\ntunnel-like path.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14231,57,-61,-1,'Intersection of Sand and Anemone','  You have reached the intersection of Sand Street and Anemone Avenue, the\nstreet that leads east from the town gate.  There are tall plants swaying in\nthe current, and the way is paved with <R>red<1> and <P>purple<1> coral.  Sand Street\nruns north and south, and Anemone Avenue continues west into the town.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14232,52,-61,-1,'Anemone Avenue','  You are on the main street running east from the front gate of Kalysia.  The\nway is paved with <R>red coral<1>, and colorful fronds of marine plant life border\nthe road.  To the south you see a small building, and to the north are other\nstructures that appear to be homes of the inhabitants.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14233,53,-61,-1,'The Intersection of Anemone and Templeway','  You have reached the second intersection that lies east of the town gate.\nAnemone Avenue continues running east and west, and Templeway intersects it,\nleading north and south.  To the north on Templeway stands a huge building\nwith tall columns of marble guarding the entrance.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14234,52,-62,-1,'Entrance to the Salty Dog','  You are at the entrance to the Salty Dog, the main eating establishment in\nKalysia.  To the west is a large set of double doors, and above the doors is an\ninscription carved in the frame.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14235,51,-62,-1,'The Salty Dog','  The Salty Dog is a place where the inhabitants of Kalysia come for good food\nand social interaction.  Throughout the room are large wooden tables and\nbenches, and a glowing orbs float in all corners of the room.  Stacks of what\nappear to be odd types of dishes are on a few of the tables.  You feel very\nwelcome here, as it is very hospitable.\n',83,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(14236,51,-63,-1,'The South End of the Salty Dog','  You are farther inside the Salty Dog, and to the south is the extreme\nsouthern wall of the establishment.  A glowing orb floating near the ceiling\ncast a strange light throughout the room.\n',83,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(14237,53,-60,-1,'Templeway','  You are on Templeway, the road that leads north and south through central\nKalysia.  The way is paved with <R>red coral<1> and <w>white sand<1>, and is bordered by\ntall, colorful aquatic plants.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14238,53,-59,-1,'Templeway','  You are on Templeway, the road that leads north and south through central\nKalysia.  The way is paved with <R>red coral<1> and <w>white sand<1>, and is bordered by\ntall, colorful aquatic plants.  Directly to the east is the Temple of Kalysia,\na huge structure with tall marble pillars guarding the entrance.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14239,54,-59,-1,'Entrance to the Temple of Kalysia','  You are before the huge structure of the Temple of Kalysia, and you feel\ndwarfed by the massive size of the marble pillars that stand by the entrance.  A\nlarge set of double doors hang on tarnished brass hinges to the east, and you\nsee an ornate inscription on the door frame.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14240,55,-59,-1,'The Temple','  This room is simply gargantuan in size.  The ceiling spans high above your\nhead and creates a very open environment for the worshiping of the deities.\nThe room is basically empty of furniture except for a large altar in the\ncenter of the room.  A large pair of double doors stand in the western wall,\nand the Temple extends to the north, south and east.\n',83,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,10,200,0,'',NULL),
(14241,55,-59,0,'Near the Ceiling','  You are in danger of floating back down to the floor as you peer around the\ntop of the room.  The ceiling is very near your head here--you could touch it\neasily.  A glowing orb floats in the very highest part of the domed roof; it\ncasts a strange aura about the room.\n',83,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(14242,56,-59,-1,'The Eastern End of the Temple','  Near to you here is the eastern wall of the temple.  The wall itself is made\nof granite, and the massiveness of it astounds you.  On the wall is writing done\nin an ornate, italic print, and is lit by a glowing ball floating near.\n',83,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(14243,55,-60,-1,'The Southern End of the Temple','  You are very near the southern wall of the Temple of Kalysia.  Written on the\nwall are large, ornate words carved in an italic print.  A glowing ball lights\nthe area with its eerie magic.\n',83,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(14244,55,-58,-1,'The Northern End of the Temple','  You have reached the northern end of the Temple of Kalysia.  Very near to you\nstands the north wall, and you notice an inscription carved on it in ornate,\nitalic figures.\n',83,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(14245,53,-62,-1,'Templeway','  This street runs north and south through the very center of the beautiful\ntown of Kalysia.  The way is paved with <R>red<1> and <P>purple<1> coral, and lovely\nunderwater plants line the street.  To the east you see a small building that\nappears to be some kind of shop.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14246,54,-61,-1,'Anemone Avenue','  You are on the street that runs east and west straight from the town gate.\nThe way is paved with chunks of <R>brilliant red coral<1>, and lovely aquatic plants\nline the street.  All around you see the houses of the inhabitants of Kalysia,\nand you marvel at the beauty of your surroundings.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14247,55,-61,-1,'Anemone Avenue','  This street runs east and west through the central part of the town of\nKalysia, and is paved with porous chunks of <R>brilliant red coral<1>.  The fronds of\nthe plants that line the way float by you as you continue down the road.  To\nthe south, you see a small building that seems to be a little out of place on\nthis grand street.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14248,56,-61,-1,'Anemone Avenue','  This street runs east and west through the very center of the town.  To the\nwest you see the road stretch out before you all the way to the town gate, and\nto the east you see an intersection.  The way is paved with <R>bright red coral<1>,\nand colorful marine plant-life borders the street.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14249,55,-62,-1,'The Butchery','  You notice a <r>faint tinge of red<1> in the room as you make your way through the\nslightly jagged doorway.  All around the room you see freshly slaughtered\ncarcasses of fish and other marine animals, and you shudder at the gruesome\nsight.  On the far wall from the door is a large, square counter, and above it\nis a large sign stating the prices of the various products available.\n',83,166077,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14250,54,-62,-1,'The Weaponry','  This is the only shop in Kalysia that is totally devoted to the art of\nweaponry.  On the walls hang various models of the types of weapons that are\navailable to the customer, and a long counter stands against the far east wall.\n',83,174269,30,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(14251,53,-64,-1,'Corner of Templeway and Urchin','  This intersection lies on the extreme south side of the town, and connects\nTempleway, which runs north and south, with Urchin Street, which follows an\neasterly path.  The junction is wide with plenty of room for traffic to pass\nthrough unhindered.  The streets here are paved with the same <B>red coral<1> that\ncovers most of the roads throughout Kalysia.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14252,53,-63,-1,'Templeway','  This street runs north and south through the very center of the beautiful\ntown of Kalysia.  The way is paved with <R>red<1> and <P>purple<1> coral, and lovely\nunderwater plants line the street.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14253,54,-64,-1,'Urchin Street','  This street runs east and west through the south end of Kalysia.  The way is\npaved with <r>dirty, red chunks of coral<1>, and bits of slime and kelp litter the\nroad.  There is an eerie light that is cast here by the beams of light coming\nfrom the adjacent dwellings, and you feel a vague sense of foreboding as you\ntraverse the street.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14254,52,-64,-1,'Urchin Street','  Urchin Street is on the south end of town, and is the home to many of the\nmore unsavory members of Kalysian Society.  It is darker here than in other\nparts of town, and you feel a bit uneasy making your way down the street.  To\nthe north you see a small, seedy looking building.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14255,52,-63,-1,'Jank\'s Tavern','  As you walk through the small, cramped doorway, you immediately notice the\nshabby furnishings of the small main room.  There are a few round, wooden\ntables scattered about haphazardly, and broken benches lean against the wall to\nthe east.  There are no windows, but the room is lit by two of those strange\norbs of light that can be found throughout the town.  These, however, appear to\nbe very old, as their light is very dim and wavy.\n',83,166077,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14256,51,-64,-1,'Urchin Street','  This street is not nearly as clean as the rest of the roads in the town, and\nthere is also a noticeable absence of light in this part of town.  The way\nitself is paved with <r>dirty, faded red coral<1>, with pieces of kelp and slime\nmixed in with the sand.  The water seems to contain a high amount of silt, and\nthe visibility is not nearly as clear as in other parts of Kalysia.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14257,50,-64,-1,'Corner of Conch and Urchin','  You have reached the junction of Conch street, which runs north and south\nthrough the west end of town, and Urchin street, which goes east and west along\nthe south basin wall.  The intersection is wide with plenty of room for traffic\nto pass unhindered.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14258,56,-64,-1,'Urchin Street','  You are on the road that runs east and west through the south side of town.\nTo the direct south is the southern basin wall, blocking all movement in that\ndirection, and to the north is a run down building about the size of a shack.\nThe way is paved with <r>dirty red coral<1>, and silt stirs as you disturb the water\nwith your movement.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14259,56,-63,-1,'An Abandoned Hovel','  You have made your way to an old abandoned shack that looks like it has been\nleft alone for a very long time.  The crumbling walls are made of <p>faded purple\ncoral<1> and are covered with <k>black slime<1>.  There are no lights in this room other\nthan what feeble light shines in through the single window.\n',83,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,6,80,0,'',NULL),
(14260,55,-64,-1,'Urchin Street','  You are on the road that runs east and west through the south side of town.\nTo the direct south is the southern basin wall, blocking all movement in that\ndirection.  The way is paved with <r>dirty red coral<1>, and silt stirs as you\ndisturb the water with your movement.  A disreputable shack stands to the\nnorth,\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14261,0,0,0,'Corner of Sand and Urchin','  You are on the corner of Sand Street, which runs north and south through the\neast end of the town, and Urchin Street, which runs east and west.\n',0,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14262,57,-63,-1,'Sand Street','  You make your way down the street that runs north and south through the\neastern end of Kalysia.  The path is covered with colorful coral and patches of\nwhite sand, and tall aquatic plants line the road.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14263,57,-62,-1,'Sand Street','  You make your way down the street that runs north and south through the\neastern end of Kalysia.  The path is covered with colorful coral and patches of\nwhite sand, and tall aquatic plants line the road.\n',83,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14264,54,-63,-1,'A Rundown Hovel','  This small dwelling has surely seen better days.  The crumbling walls\nare made of <p>faded purple coral<1> and you wonder how long it will be\ntill they turn to dust.  There are no lights in this room other than what\nfeeble light shines in through the single window.\n',83,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,6,80,0,'',NULL),
(14265,55,-63,-1,'A Disreputable Shack','  Upon entering this building, you immediately get the feeling you\'re in\na place you probably shouldn\'t be.  Situated in one of the worst parts of\ntown, this is a place where people on the wrong side of the law go to\nacquire things that they probably shouldn\'t have.\n',83,174269,30,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(14270,0,0,0,'A Small Storage and Preparation Room','  Once long ago this small room apparently was a storage room for any\ntools or supplies for those who worked in, or visited, the catacombs on a \nregular basis.  Also it served as a location where the bodies of the dead \nwhere brought to be cleansed and prepared for entombment into the catacombs.\nThe last this room was used though was ages ago and anything which might \nhave been stored here has long since turned to dust.  The only exit to the\nroom seems to be through a rotting wooden door to the south.\n',109,131148,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14271,0,0,0,'The Upper Catacombs','  Within the upper regions of the catacombs, the Gnomes Center of Knowledge \nplaced the dead of their common brethren.  Those monks, warriors, or even\nsometimes thieves, who had earned the right to be buried beneath the center.\nMost of the tombs were simple and lacking any major embellishments.  Simply\nbeing a place of rest on holy ground for those deserving.  This section of \nthe Catacombs was spared the full wrath of Lixlor as he was first confronted\nwithin the Center itself, and later within the lower catacombs where he was\nlater imprisoned.  Various side tunnels lead off of this one as they enter \nthe private tombs of different individuals.  A rotting wooden door sits\nto the north while the main tunnel seems to move to the southwest from here.\n',109,131144,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(14272,0,0,0,'The Upper Catacombs','  Within the upper regions of the catacombs, the Gnomes Center of Knowledge \nplaced the dead of their common brethren.  Those monks, warriors, or even\nsometimes thieves, who had earned the right to be buried beneath the center.\nMost of the tombs were simple and lacking any major embellishments, simply\nbeing a place of rest on holy ground for those deserving.  This section of \nthe catacombs was spared the full wrath of Lixlor as he was first confronted\nwithin the Center itself, and later within the lower catacombs where he was\neventually imprisoned.  Various side tunnels lead off of this one as they \nenter the private tombs of different individuals.  The main tunnel seems to \nmove to the northeast and southeast from here.\n',109,131144,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(14273,0,0,0,'The Upper Catacombs','  Within the upper regions of the catacombs, the Gnomes Center of Knowledge \nplaced the dead of their common brethren.  Those monks, warriors, or even\nsometimes thieves, who had earned the right to be buried beneath the center.\nMost of the tombs were simple and lacking any major embellishments, simply\nbeing a place of rest on holy ground for those deserving.  This section of \nthe catacombs was spared the full wrath of Lixlor as he was first confronted\nwithin the Center itself, and later within the lower catacombs where he was\neventually imprisoned.  Various side tunnels lead off of this one as they \nenter the private tombs of different individuals.  A set of narrow stairs\nlead downward from here and once continued upwards as well, but apparently\nwere destroyed and covered over.  The main tunnel seems to move to the \nnorthwest.\n',109,131144,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(14274,0,0,0,'A Dusty Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those warriors deserving of a burial beneath\nthe center this tomb is simple and bare.  Each warrior was wrapped in burial\ncloth and laid within a shallow niche in the wall.  The niche was then sealed\noff with a thick, but brittle, layer of dried mud.  Several of these niches \nnow lie open and exposed, and strangely it appears as if they were opened\nby someone within the niche itself!  The main tunnel can be seen to the \nsoutheast.\n',109,131144,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14275,0,0,0,'A Dusty Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those warriors deserving of a burial beneath\nthe center this tomb is simple and bare.  Each warrior was wrapped in burial\ncloth and laid within a shallow niche in the wall.  The niche was then sealed\noff with a thick, but brittle, layer of dried mud.  Several of these niches \nnow lie open and exposed, and strangely it appears as if they were opened\nby someone within the niche itself!  The main tunnel can be seen to the \nsouthwest.\n',109,131144,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14276,0,0,0,'A Dusty Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those warriors deserving of a burial beneath\nthe center this tomb is simple and bare.  Each warrior was wrapped in burial\ncloth and laid within a shallow niche in the wall.  The niche was then sealed\noff with a thick, but brittle, layer of dried mud.  Several of these niches \nnow lie open and exposed, and strangely it appears as if they were opened\nby someone within the niche itself!  The main tunnel can be seen to the west.\n',109,131144,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14277,0,0,0,'A Dusty Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those warriors deserving of a burial beneath\nthe center this tomb is simple and bare.  Each warrior was wrapped in burial\ncloth and laid within a shallow niche in the wall.  The niche was then sealed\noff with a thick, but brittle, layer of dried mud.  Several of these niches \nnow lie open and exposed, and strangely it appears as if they were opened\nby someone within the niche itself!  The main tunnel can be seen to the \nnorthwest.\n',109,131144,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14278,0,0,0,'A Rancid Smelling Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those thieves wealthy enough to buy a burial \nbeneath the center this tomb is fairly plain.  Each thief was wrapped in \nburial cloth soaked in perserving oils and laid within a niche cut into the\nstone.  The niche was then sealed off with wooden planks.  Several of these\nniches now lie open and exposed, and strangely it appears as if they were \nopened by someone within the niche itself!  The main tunnel can be seen to\nthe south.\n',109,131144,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14279,0,0,0,'A Rancid Smelling Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those thieves wealthy enough to buy a burial \nbeneath the center this tomb is fairly plain.  Each thief was wrapped in \nburial cloth soaked in perserving oils and laid within a niche cut into the\nstone.  The niche was then sealed off with wooden planks.  Several of these\nniches now lie open and exposed, and strangely it appears as if they were \nopened by someone within the niche itself!  The main tunnel can be seen to\nthe west.\n',109,131144,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14280,0,0,0,'A Rancid Smelling Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those thieves wealthy enough to buy a burial \nbeneath the center this tomb is fairly plain.  Each thief was wrapped in \nburial cloth soaked in perserving oils and laid within a niche cut into the\nstone.  The niche was then sealed off with wooden planks.  Several of these\nniches now lie open and exposed, and strangely it appears as if they were \nopened by someone within the niche itself!  The main tunnel can be seen to \nthe north.\n',109,131144,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14281,0,0,0,'A Simple Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those monks worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb is plain and organized.  Each monk was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a wooden coffin, and then \nplaced within a niche cut into the stone.  The niche was then sealed off \nwith masonary blocks.  Several of these niches now lie open and exposed, \nand strangely it appears as if they were opened by someone within the niche \nitself!  The main tunnel can be seen to the west.\n',109,131144,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14282,0,0,0,'A Simple Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those monks worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb is plain and organized.  Each monk was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a wooden coffin, and then \nplaced within a niche cut into the stone.  The niche was then sealed off \nwith masonary blocks.  Several of these niches now lie open and exposed, \nand strangely it appears as if they were opened by someone within the niche \nitself!  The main tunnel can be seen to the northeast.\n',109,131144,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14283,0,0,0,'A Simple Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those monks worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb is plain and organized.  Each monk was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a wooden coffin, and then \nplaced within a niche cut into the stone.  The niche was then sealed off \nwith masonary blocks.  Several of these niches now lie open and exposed, \nand strangely it appears as if they were opened by someone within the niche \nitself!  The main tunnel can be seen to the north.\n',109,131144,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14284,0,0,0,'A Simple Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those monks worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb is plain and organized.  Each monk was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a wooden coffin, and then \nplaced within a niche cut into the stone.  The niche was then sealed off \nwith masonary blocks.  Several of these niches now lie open and exposed, \nand strangely it appears as if they were opened by someone within the niche \nitself!  The main tunnel can be seen to the northwest.\n',109,131144,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14285,0,0,0,'The Lower Catacombs','  Within the lower regions of the catacombs, the Gnomes Center of Knowledge \nplaced the dead of their special brethren.  Those clerics, scholars, and \ngnights who had earned the right to be buried beneath the center in specially\nprepared tombs and burial vaults.  This section of the catacombs was greatly\neffected by the full wrath of Lixlor as he battled to ellude his impending\nimprisonment.  Many of the tunnels have collapsed and various doorways are\nnow blocked by piles of earth and rubble as Lixlor\'s magic shook the very \nfoundation of the Center.  The main tunnel appears to move north from here\nwhile there are rotting wooden tomb doors to the west and south.\n',109,139596,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14286,0,0,0,'The Lower Catacombs','  Within the lower regions of the catacombs, the Gnomes Center of Knowledge \nplaced the dead of their special brethren.  Those clerics, scholars, and \ngnights who had earned the right to be buried beneath the center in specially\nprepared tombs and burial vaults.  This section of the catacombs was greatly\neffected by the full wrath of Lixlor as he battled to ellude his impending\nimprisonment.  Many of the tunnels have collapsed and various doorways are\nnow blocked by piles of earth and rubble as Lixlor\'s magic shook the very \nfoundation of the Center.  The main tunnel apparently moved both north and\nsouth from here at one time, but the passage to the north now lies blocked \nby a large cave-in.  The cave-in has blocked the door to the west as well\nbut a rotting wooden tomb door is still accessible to the southeast.\n',109,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14287,0,0,0,'The Lower Catacombs','  Within the lower regions of the catacombs, the Gnomes Center of Knowledge \nplaced the dead of their special brethren.  Those clerics, scholars, and \ngnights who had earned the right to be buried beneath the center in specially\nprepared tombs and burial vaults.  This section of the catacombs was greatly\neffected by the full wrath of Lixlor as he battled to ellude his impending\nimprisonment.  Many of the tunnels have collapsed and various doorways are\nnow blocked by piles of earth and rubble as Lixlor\'s magic shook the very \nfoundation of the Center.  The main tunnel appears to have moved south from\nhere at one time but has been blocked by a large cave-in which also blocks\nthe rotting wooden tomb doors to the east and west.  The tomb doors to the\nnorth and southwest are luckily still accessible.\n',109,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(14288,0,0,0,'A Small Burial Vault','  Used to house the bodies of those clerics worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb is quite splendid.  Each cleric was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a marble coffin, and then \nplaced upon marble piers about the vault.  Several of these coffins now lie\nopen as if their lids were thrown off by those within.  An archway to the \neast seems to lead to an entry of some type.\n',109,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(14289,0,0,0,'An Entry to the Vaults of the Clergy','  Used to house the bodies of those cleric worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center these vaults are quite splendid.  Each cleric was wrapped in \nburial cloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a marble coffin, and \nthen placed upon marble piers about the vault.  This room was created for the \nceremonies which were performed for the cleric\'s passing.  Archways to the \neast and west seem to lead to the vaults themselves while a rotting wooden \ntomb door is set in the north wall.\n',109,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(14290,0,0,0,'A Small Burial Vault','  Used to house the bodies of those clerics worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb is quite splendid.  Each cleric was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a marble coffin, and then \nplaced upon marble piers about the vault.  Several of these coffins now lie\nopen as if their lids were thrown off by those within.  An archway to the \nwest seems to lead to an entry of some type while a large pile of rubble to\nthe north is visible where a portion of the wall collapsed during the battles\nthat took place here in the lower catacombs.\n',109,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(14291,0,0,0,'A Decorated Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those gnights worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb is highly decorated.  Each gnight was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a stone coffin, and then \nplaced within a specially prepared marble lined niche.  The niche was then \nsealed off with marble masonary blocks.  Several of these niches now lie open \nand exposed, and strangely it appears as if they were opened by someone within\nthe niche itself!  A rotting wooden tomb door is visible to the east while\na collapsed portion of the wall to the north has left an opening which appears\nto lead into another tomb north of here.\n',109,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(14292,0,0,0,'A Decorated Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those gnights worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb is highly decorated.  Each gnight was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a stone coffin, and then \nplaced within a specially prepared marble lined niche.  The niche was then \nsealed off with marble masonary blocks.  Several of these niches now lie open \nand exposed, and strangely it appears as if they were opened by someone within\nthe niche itself!  A rotting wooden tomb door is visible to the northwest while\na large pile of rubble to the south is visible where a portion of the wall \ncollapsed during the battles that took place here in the lower catacombs.\n',109,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(14293,0,0,0,'A Decorated Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those gnights worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb is highly decorated.  Each gnight was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a stone coffin, and then \nplaced within a specially prepared marble lined niche.  The niche was then \nsealed off with marble masonary blocks.  Several of these niches now lie open \nand exposed, and strangely it appears as if they were opened by someone within\nthe niche itself!  To the east once stood a tomb door, but it is now buried\nbeneath a mountain of earth and rubble.  A similar but not quite as large\npile of rubble can be seen to the northeast as well.  To the south a collapsed\nportion of the wall has left an opening which appears to lead into another tomb\nsouth of here.\n',109,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(14294,0,0,0,'A Decorated Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those gnights worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb is highly decorated.  Each gnight was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a stone coffin, and then \nplaced within a specially prepared marble lined niche.  The niche was then \nsealed off with marble masonary blocks.  Several of these niches now lie open \nand exposed, and strangely it appears as if they were opened by someone within\nthe niche itself!  Against the northern wall a coffin lid stands in an upright,\nalmost doorlike pose, while a rotting wooden tomb door to the northwest appears\nto be an exit to this tomb.\n',109,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(14295,0,0,0,'A Decorated Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those gnights worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb is highly decorated.  Each gnight was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a stone coffin, and then \nplaced within a specially prepared marble lined niche.  The niche was then \nsealed off with marble masonary blocks.  Several of these niches now lie open \nand exposed, and strangely it appears as if they were opened by someone within\nthe niche itself!  To the east once stood a tomb door, but it is now buried\nbeneath a mountain of earth and rubble.  To the north a collapsed portion of \nthe wall has left an opening which appears to lead into another tomb north of \nhere.\n',109,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(14296,0,0,0,'A Decorated Tomb','  Used to house the bodies of those gnights worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb is highly decorated.  Each gnight was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a stone coffin, and then \nplaced within a specially prepared marble lined niche.  The niche was then \nsealed off with marble masonary blocks.  Several of these niches now lie open \nand exposed, and strangely it appears as if they were opened by someone within\nthe niche itself!  To the west once stood a tomb door, but it is now buried\nbeneath a mountain of earth and rubble.  A coffin lid stands upright against\nthe southern wall almost in a doorlike pose.  To the north a strange panel \nshaped area of the wall has been polished smooth and an inscription carved \nupon its surface.\n',109,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,90,4,'',NULL),
(14297,0,0,0,'A Looted Burial Vault','  Used to house the bodies of those scholars worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb was once grand indeed.  Each scholar was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a crystal coffin, and then \nlaid upon onyx piers about the room.  Strangely several of these coffins now\nlie open as if their inhabitants had thrown off the lids to break free.  Other\nsmall containers and chests about the room once housed copies of the works \nthese great scholars completed.  Unfortunately these now lied smashed and \ndestroyed, their contents looted by vandals or those seeking power.  An arched\nopening in the wall to the east seems to lead to an entry of some sort while\nsome occurance has left a hole through the wall to the south.\n',109,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(14298,0,0,0,'A Small Entry Chamber','  Used to house the bodies of those scholars worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb was once grand indeed.  Each scholar was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a crystal coffin, and then \nlaid upon onyx piers in the adjacent vaults.  Various containers about the room\nonce held copies of the works created by these great scholars to aid them in\nthe afterlife.  Unforunately all of these now lie smashed and looted as vandals\nor seekers of power have destroyed them.  An arched opening in the wall to the\nwest leads to one of the burial vaults.  A similar archway once stood to the\neast as well, but is now buried beneath a mound of rubble and earth.  A tomb\ndoor made of wood sits in the south wall slowly rotting into nothingness.  It\nwould appear the door leads back to the main passage of the catacombs.\n',109,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(14299,0,0,0,'A Desecrated Burial Vault','  Used to house the bodies of those scholars worthy enough of a burial beneath \nthe center this tomb was once grand indeed.  Each scholar was wrapped in burial\ncloth soaked in perserving oils, encased within a crystal coffin, and then \nlaid upon onyx piers about the room.  Strangely several of these coffins now\nlie open as if their inhabitants had thrown off the lids to break free.  Other\nsmall containers and chests about the room once housed copies of the works \nthese great scholars completed.  Unfortunately these now lied smashed and \ndestroyed, their contents looted by vandals or those seeking power.  All about\nyou ancient arcane phrases have been carved or marked upon the walls and seem\nto give off an eerie chill.  This is the chamber, and eventual prison, that\nLixlor used to launch his attack against the center.  An arched opening once\nstood in the wall to the west, but now lies buried beneath a mountain of rubble\nand earth.  To the south a panel shaped portion of the wall has been polished\nsmooth and clean with one simple inscription carved into it.\n',109,142792,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,90,4,'',NULL),
(14300,-32,-25,2,'Tunnel Through the Mountains','  You are in the middle of a tunnel carved out of solid rock.  The tunnel\nis framed every ten feet with thick wooden braces, to prevent cave-ins.\nTo the east, you see the tunnel entrance.  The tunnel continues to the\nsouthwest.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(14301,-33,-26,2,'Tunnel Through the Mountains','  You are in the middle of a tunnel carved out of solid rock.  The tunnel\nis framed every ten feet with thick wooden braces, to prevent cave-ins.\nThe tunnel continues to the south and the northeast.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(14302,-33,-27,2,'Tunnel Through the Mountains','  You are in the middle of a tunnel carved out of solid rock.  The tunnel\nis framed every ten feet with thick wooden braces, to prevent cave-ins.\nThe tunnel continues to the north and south.  There is a crack in the\ntunnel wall to the east.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,4,'',NULL),
(14303,-33,-28,2,'Tunnel Through the Mountains','  You are in the middle of a tunnel carved out of solid rock.  The tunnel\nis framed every ten feet with thick wooden braces, to prevent cave-ins.\nThe tunnel continues to the north and south.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(14304,-33,-29,2,'Tunnel Through the Mountains','  You are in the middle of a tunnel carved out of solid rock.  The tunnel\nis framed every ten feet with thick wooden braces, to prevent cave-ins.\nThe tunnel continues to the north, and to the southwest you see an\nentrance to the tunnel.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(14305,-34,-30,-1,'Tunnel Entrance','  You are in the entrance to a tunnel carved out of solid rock.  The\ntunnel is framed every ten feet with thick wooden braces, to prevent\ncave-ins.  The tunnel continues deeper into the mountain to the\nnortheast, and opens out into the foothills to the west.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(14306,-35,-30,-1,'A Road Through the Hills','  You are in the middle of a road that runs through a range of low\nrolling hills.  To the east, a range of tall, snow-covered mountains\ndominates the horizon.  A swiftly flowing creek separates the road from\nan wide prairie to the west.  The way north is blocked by an escarpment.\nThe road enters a tunnel to the east, and continues down the valley to\nthe southeast, along the creek.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14307,-36,-31,-1,'Road Through the Vale','  You are in the middle of a road that runs through a vale between low\nrolling hills.  To the east, a range of tall, snow-covered mountains\ndominates the horizon.  A swiftly flowing creek separates the road from\nan wide prairie to the west.  The road continues to the northeast and the\nsouth.  A ford crosses the creek to the west.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14308,-36,-32,-1,'Road Through the Vale','  You are in the middle of a road that runs through a vale between low\nrolling hills.  To the east, a range of tall, snow-covered mountains\ndominates the horizon.  A swiftly flowing creek separates the road from\nan wide prairie to the west.  The road continues to the north and the\nsouth.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14309,-36,-33,-1,'Road Through the Vale','  You are in the middle of a road that runs through a vale between low\nrolling hills.  To the east, a range of tall, snow-covered mountains\ndominates the horizon.  To the west, a small pipeweed patch lays in the\nlowlands along a creek, beyond which a wide prairie extends to the\nhorizon.  The road continues to the north and the south.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14310,-36,-34,-1,'Road Through the Vale','  You are in the middle of a road that runs through a vale between low\nrolling hills.  To the east, a range of tall, snow-covered mountains\ndominates the horizon.  A fence separates the road from a small farm,\nwhich lies to the west between the road and the creek.  The road\ncontinues to the north and the south.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14311,-36,-35,-1,'Road Through the Vale','  You are standing in the middle of a road that runs through a vale\nbetween low rolling hills.  A stone wall separates the road from an\norchard, which lies on the hillside to the east.  A fence separates the\nroad from a small farm, which lies to the west between the road and the\ncreek.  The road continues to the north and the south.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14312,-36,-36,-1,'Road Through the Vale','  You are in the middle of a road that runs through a vale between low\nrolling hills.  A stone wall separates the road from an orchard, which\nlies on the hillside to the east.  A fence separates the road from a\nsmall farm, which lies to the west between the road and the creek.  A\nstorage shed lies to the south.  The road continues to the north and the\nsouthwest.  There is a gate in the wall to the east.\n',76,131076,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14313,-37,-37,-1,'Road Through the Vale','  You are in the middle of a road that runs through a vale between low\nrolling hills.  At this point, the road runs between two farms, one\nuphill to the south, and one downhill to the north, along the creek.\nFences separate the farms from the road, and prevent movement in those\ndirections.  A storage shed lies to the east.  The road continues to the\nnortheast and the west.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14314,-38,-37,-1,'Road Through the Vale','  You are in the middle of a road that runs through a vale between low\nrolling hills.  At this point, the road runs between two farms, one\nuphill to the south, and one downhill to the north, along the creek.\nFences line the sides of the road, with an iron gate to the north and a\nwooden gate to the south, providing access into the yards of the two\nfarms.  The road continues to the east and the west.\n',76,131076,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14315,-39,-37,-1,'Road Through the Vale','  You are in the middle of a road that runs through a vale between low\nrolling hills.  At this point, the road runs between two farms, one\nuphill to the south, and one downhill to the north, along the creek.\nFences separate the farms from the road, and prevent movement in those\ndirections.  The road continues to the east and the west.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14316,-40,-37,-1,'Road Through the Vale','  You are in the middle of a road that runs through a vale between low\nrolling hills.  To the north lies a wooden building, with a door in the\nwall facing you.  To the south, you see the side of a small home.  The\nroad continues to the east and the west.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14317,-41,-37,-1,'Road Through the Vale','  You are in the middle of a road that runs through a vale between low\nrolling hills.  To the north, Whitehawk creek flows over a dam, powering\na water wheel attached to the wooden building to the northeast.  The creek\nflows onward to the west, in a southwesterly direction.  To the south, a\nwrought iron fence separates you from a small flower garden.  The road\ncontinues to the east and southwest.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14318,-42,-38,-1,'Outside the North Gate','  You are on a stone road, just outside the north gate to a small shire.\nWhitehawk creek runs alongside the road to the north and west of you.\nThe shire is protected by a stout wooden wall, which runs east and west\nat this point.  The gate into the shire is directly to your south.  To\nthe east, a passage leads through a wrought iron fence, into a small\nflower garden.  The road continues to the northeast.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14319,-32,-27,2,'A Ledge in a Natural Cave','  You are on a ledge overlooking a large natural cave.  The cave stretches\ninto the distance to the east and south, the walls are beyond the range of\nyour light.  The floor of the cave is some distance below you, and you\ncannot see any way off the ledge, except through the crack in the wall to\nthe west.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,4,'',NULL),
(14320,-35,-36,-1,'Inside the Orchard Gate','  You are just inside the gate of a fruit orchard.  Fruit trees of\nseveral different types, including apple, cherry and peach, stand in neat\nrows, marching up the hillside to the east.  The orchard continues to the\nnorth, east and south.  A stone wall separates the orchard from a road,\nwhich lies just downhill to the west.  There is a gate in the wall to the\nwest.\n',76,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14321,-35,-35,-1,'In the Northwest Corner of the Orchard','  You are in the northwest corner of a fruit orchard.  Fruit trees of\nseveral different types, including apple, cherry and peach, stand in neat\nrows, marching up the hillside to the east.  The orchard continues to the\neast and south.  A stone wall separates the orchard from a road, which\nlies just downhill to the west, and the hills to the north.\n',76,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14322,-35,-37,-1,'In the Southwest Corner of the Orchard','  You are in the southwest corner of a fruit orchard.  Fruit trees of\nseveral different types, including apple, cherry and peach, stand in neat\nrows, marching up the hillside to the east.  The orchard continues to the\nnorth and east.  A shed, with a door in the middle of the wall, stands to\nthe west.  A stone wall separates the orchard from the hills to the south.\n',76,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14323,-34,-36,-1,'In the Center of the Orchard','  You are in the center of a fruit orchard.  Fruit trees of several\ndifferent types, including apple, cherry and peach, stand in neat rows,\nmarching up the hillside to the east, and downhill to the west.  The\norchard continues to the north, east, south and west.\n',76,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14324,-34,-35,-1,'On the Northern Edge of the Orchard','  You are on the northern edge of a fruit orchard.  Fruit trees of\nseveral different types, including apple, cherry and peach, stand in neat\nrows, marching up the hillside to the east, and downhill to the west.\nThe orchard continues to the east, south, and west.  A stone wall\nseparates the orchard from the hills to the north.\n',76,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14325,-34,-37,-1,'On the Southern Edge of the Orchard','  You are on the southern edge of a fruit orchard.  Fruit trees of\nseveral different types, including apple, cherry and peach, stand in neat\nrows, marching up the hillside to the east, and downhill to the west.\nThe orchard continues to the north, east, and west.  A stone wall\nseparates the orchard from the hills to the south.\n',76,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14326,-33,-36,-1,'On the Eastern Edge of the Orchard','  You are on the eastern edge of a fruit orchard.  Fruit trees of several\ndifferent types, including apple, cherry and peach, stand in neat rows,\nmarching down the hillside to the west.  The orchard continues to the\nnorth, south and west.  A stone wall separates the orchard from the hills\nto the east.  Tall, snow-covered mountains dominate the horizon beyond\nthe wall to the east.\n',76,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14327,-33,-35,-1,'In the Northeast Corner of the Orchard','  You are in the northeast corner of a fruit orchard.  Fruit trees of\nseveral different types, including apple, cherry and peach, stand in neat\nrows, marching down the hillside to the west.  The orchard continues to\nthe south and west.  A stone wall separates the orchard from the hills to\nthe north and east.  Tall, snow-covered mountains dominate the horizon\nbeyond the wall to the east.\n',76,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14328,-33,-37,-1,'In the Southeast Corner of the Orchard','  You are in the southeast corner of a fruit orchard.  Fruit trees of\nseveral different types, including apple, cherry and peach, stand in neat\nrows, marching down the hillside to the west.  The orchard continues to\nthe north and west.  A stone wall separates the orchard from the hills to\nthe south and east.  Tall, snow-covered mountains dominate the horizon\nbeyond the wall to the east.\n',76,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14329,-36,-37,-1,'In a Stone Storage Shed','  You are inside a small storage shed.  The walls are made of stones\nneatly stacked and mortared together.  The roof is made of wooden planks,\nnailed to cross-beams above your head.  The only exit is the door in the\nmiddle of the east wall.  There are some vents under the eaves of the\nroof, but they are too small for you to get through.  This shed is used\nfor storage of tools used in the orchard, with fresh picked fruit also\nstored here in season.  The air inside the shed is cool and dry, the\nperfect conditions for preventing spoilage.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,96,0,'',NULL),
(14330,-37,-36,-1,'Inside a Farmer\'s Burrow','  You find yourself in the middle of a medium sized Hobbit burrow, built\ninto the center of a small hillock.  The walls, floor and ceiling are\nmade of wood, if you hadn\'t seen the outside, you would never know you\'re\nin a home below ground and not a free-standing house.  The room itself is\nabout 20 feet square, the six foot high ceiling forces the taller among\nyou to walk slightly bent over.  All the activities of the family take\nplace in this one room.  The front part is the living area, with a eating\narea along the northern wall, a kitchen in the back to the east, and\nplaces for sleeping along the wall to the south.  Round windows look out\nto the north, east, and south.  There is a round door in the western wall.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,72,0,'',NULL),
(14331,-38,-36,-1,'In the Farmyard','  You are at the southern end of the yard in the center of a small farm.\nThe ground is hard packed dirt, with the tracks of numerous animals and\nhumanoids.  To the east is a small hillock, with a round door in the\nmiddle.  To the west is some kind of animal pen, with a sliding gate in\nthis side.  A fence, with a wooden gate in it, separates the farmyard\nfrom a road to the south.  The yard continues to the north.\n',76,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14332,-39,-36,-1,'A Muddy Animal Pen','  Yuck, what a disgusting place.  The ground in this pen is covered with\nthick brown mud, or at least you hope it\'s mud.  The smell is terrible, a\nmixture of rotting food, animal waste and sweaty animals.  You can\'t wait\nto get out of here so you can breathe again.  A fence runs around the pen\nto the east, south and west.  A barn forms the northern boundary.  There\nis a door in the side of the barn, and a sliding gate in the fence to the\neast.\n',76,131072,27,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14333,-39,-35,-1,'In the Barn','  You find yourself inside a small wooden barn.  The place smells of warm\nanimal and dry grass.  Animal stalls line the western wall.  Fodder for the\nanimals is kept in the northeast corner, the southeast corner is used to\nstore the farm tools.  Doors lead out to the north, east, and south.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14334,-38,-35,-1,'In the Farmyard','  You are at the northern end of the yard in the center of a small farm.\nThe ground is hard packed dirt, with the tracks of numerous animals and\nhumanoids.  A fence, with a wooden gate in it, separates the farmyard\nfrom a pasture to the north.  To the east lies a small garden.  A wooden\nbarn, with a large door in it, stands to the west.  The yard continues to\nthe south.\n',76,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14335,-37,-35,-1,'In the Garden','  Vegetable plants of all types surround you, each type in its own neat\nstraight row.  A quick glance shows you corn, tomatoes, carrots, lettuce,\nand several others that you can\'t immediately identify.  This garden is\nobviously well tended, there are no weeds, and the plants all appear very\nhealthy.  A fence separates the garden from the road to the east and the\npasture to the north.  A small hillock, with a window in it, stands to\nthe south.  The garden opens into the farmyard to the west.\n',76,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14336,-37,-34,-1,'In a Pasture','  You are at the eastern end of this rolling, grassy area along the banks\nof a swiftly flowing creek.  Thick green grass provides food for the\nanimals, which are allowed to freely roam this area, contained by the\nfence which runs along the northern, eastern and southern sides.  Beyond\nthe fence to the east, you see a north-south road.  To the north, a small\npipeweed patch lies in the lowlands along a creek, beyond which a wide\nprairie stretches to the horizon.  Beyond the fence to the south you see a\ngarden.  The pasture continues to the west.\n',76,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14337,-38,-34,-1,'In a Pasture','  You are in the middle of this rolling, grassy area along the banks\nof a swiftly flowing creek.  Thick green grass provides food for the\nanimals, which are allowed to freely roam this area, contained by the\nfence which runs along the northern, and southern sides.  The creek lies\nbeyond the fence to the north, and to the south, a wooden gate provides\naccess to the farm yard.  The pasture continues to the east and west.\n',76,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14338,-39,-34,-1,'In a Pasture','  You are at the western end of this rolling, grassy area along the\nbanks of a swiftly flowing creek.  Thick green grass provides food for\nthe animals, which are allowed to freely roam this area, contained by\nthe fence which runs along the northern, western and southern sides.\nThe creek lies beyond the fence to the north, and opens into a small pond\nto the west.  A small barn, with a door in the center, stands to the\nsouth.  The pasture continues to the east.\n',76,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14339,-40,-36,-1,'Waterford Mill','  The inside of the mill is quite crowded, and not near as big inside as\nit appears from the outside.  From the inside, you can see there is no\nsecond story, the open beams above provide the space for the mill\nmachinery.  Large millstones in the center of the room, powered by the\nflow of water across the water wheel, crush grain into flour.  The\nincoming grain is stored along the eastern wall, with the processed flour\nalong the western wall.  A loading door to the north provides access to\nthe millpond, allowing the grain to be moved by barge.  There is a wooden\ndoor in the southern wall.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14340,-39,-38,-1,'Inside a Farmer\'s Burrow','  You find yourself in the middle of a medium sized Hobbit burrow, built\ninto the center of a small hillock.  The walls, floor and ceiling are\nmade of wood, if you hadn\'t seen the outside, you would never know you\'re\nin a home below ground, and not a free-standing house.  The room itself\nis about 20 feet square, the six foot high ceiling forces the taller\namong you to walk slightly bent over.  All the activities of the family\ntake place in this one room.  The front part is the living area, with a\neating area along the southern wall, a kitchen in the back to the west,\nand places for sleeping along the wall to the north.  Round windows look\nout to the north, west, and south.  There is a round door in the eastern\nwall.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,96,0,'',NULL),
(14341,-38,-38,-1,'In the Farmyard','  You are at the northern end of the yard in the center of a small farm.\nThe ground is hard packed dirt, with the tracks of numerous animals and\nhumanoids.  To the west is a small hillock, with a round door in the\nmiddle.  To the east is some kind of animal pen, with a sliding gate in\nthis side.  A fence, with a iron gate in it, separates the farmyard from\na road to the north.  The yard continues to the south.\n',76,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14342,-37,-38,-1,'A Muddy Animal Pen','  Yuck, what a disgusting place.  The ground in this pen is covered with\nthick brown mud, or at least you hope it\'s mud.  The smell is terrible, a\nmixture of rotting food, animal waste and sweaty animals.  You can\'t wait\nto get out of here so you can breathe again.  A fence runs around the pen\nto the east, north and west.  A barn forms the southern boundary.  There\nis a door in the side of the barn, and a sliding gate in the fence to the\nwest.\n',76,131072,27,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14343,-37,-39,-1,'In the Barn','  You find yourself inside a small wooden barn.  The place smells of warm\nanimal and dry grass.  Animal stalls line the eastern wall.  Fodder for the\nanimals is kept in the northwest corner, the southwest corner is used to\nstore the farm tools.  Doors lead out to the north, west, and south.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14344,-38,-39,-1,'In the Farmyard','  You are at the southern end of the yard in the center of a small farm.\nThe ground is hard packed dirt, with the tracks of numerous animals and\nhumanoids.  A fence, with a wooden gate in it, separates the farmyard\nfrom a pasture to the south.  To the west lies a small garden.  A wooden\nbarn, with a large door in it, stands to the east.  The yard continues to\nthe north.\n',76,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14345,-39,-39,-1,'In the Garden','  Vegetable plants of all types surround you, each type in its own neat\nstraight row.  A quick glance shows you corn, tomatoes, carrots, lettuce,\nand several others that you can\'t immediately identify.  This garden is\nobviously well tended, there are no weeds, and the plants all appear very\nhealthy.  A fence separates the garden from the hillside to the west and\nthe pasture to the south.  A small hillock, with a window in it, stands to\nthe north.  The garden opens into the farmyard to the east.\n',76,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14346,-39,-40,-1,'In a Pasture','  You are at the western end of this rolling, grassy area in the\nfoothills of the Parnithian range.  Thick green grass provides food for\nthe animals, which are allowed to freely roam this area, contained by the\nfence which runs along the northern, western and southern sides.  A\ngarden lies to the north, and pasture continues to the east.\n',76,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14347,-38,-40,-1,'In a Pasture','  You are in the center of this rolling, grassy area in the foothills of\nthe Parnithian range.  Thick green grass provides food for the animals,\nwhich are allowed to freely roam this area, contained by the fence which\nruns along the northern, and southern sides.  A gate to the north provides\naccess to the farm yard.  The pasture continues to the east and west.\n',76,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14348,-37,-40,-1,'In a Pasture','  You are at the eastern end of this rolling, grassy area in the\nfoothills of the Parnithian range.  Thick green grass provides food for\nthe animals, which are allowed to freely roam this area, contained by\nthe fence which runs along the northern, eastern and southern sides.\nA small barn, with a door in the center, stands to the north.  The\npasture continues to the west.\n',76,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14349,-37,-33,-1,'In a Pipeweed Patch','  You find yourself in a low, somewhat swampy area along the banks of a\ncreek, which lies immediately to your north and west.  Neat rows of a\nbroadleaf plant, which you recognize as pipeweed, have been planted in\nthe wet ground.  A road runs by the patch to the east, and to the south,\na fence separates you from a pasture.\n',76,131072,27,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14350,-42,-42,0,'Village Square','You are in the middle of the Waterford village square, which lies at the\nintersection of Orchard Lane and Vineyard Road.  The village church\nstands to the northeast, and the community meeting hall lies to the\nsoutheast.  To the northwest stands the imposing building housing the\nGrimhaven Embassy, while to the southwest, you see an Inn.  Orchard Lane\ncontinues north and south, while Vineyard Road continues to the east and\nwest.  There is a door into the church to the northeast.\n',76,164017,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14351,-42,-41,0,'Orchard Lane','  You are on Orchard Lane, the main north-south road within Waterford.\nTo the east lies the village church, to the west the Grimhaven Embassy.\nThe village square lies to the south and the road continues north.  There\nis a door to the west.\n',76,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14352,-42,-40,0,'Orchard Lane','  You are on Orchard Lane, the main north-south road within Waterford.\nTo the east lies a small shop, from which the aroma of fresh baked bread\nemanates, to the west lies the Grimhaven Embassy.  There is a door to the\neast into the shop, and the road continues north and south.  A <Y>sign<1> hangs\nbeside the door.\n',76,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14353,-42,-39,0,'Inside the North Gate','  You are on Orchard Lane, just inside the north gate of Waterford.  The\nshire is protected by a stout wooden wall, which runs east and west just\nto the north of you.  The gate out of the shire is directly to your north.\nSmall, round doors lead to hobbit burrows, which lie to the east and west,\nand the road continues south toward the center of the village.\n',76,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14354,-42,-43,0,'Orchard Lane','  You are on Orchard Lane, the main north-south road within Waterford.\nTo the east lies the community meeting hall, to the west lies an inn.\nThe village square lies to the north, and the road continues south.\nThere are doors to the east and west.\n',76,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14355,-42,-44,0,'Orchard Lane','  You are on Orchard Lane, the main north-south road within Waterford.\nTo the east lies a small hobbit burrow, to the west lies an inn.  There\nis a round door into the burrow to the east, while the road continues\nnorth.  A bridge lies to the south.\n',76,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14356,-41,-42,0,'Vineyard Road','  You are on Vineyard Road, the main east-west road within Waterford.\nThe village church lies to the north, and the community meeting hall to\nthe south.  To the west lies the village square.  The road continues\neast.  There is a door to the south.\n',76,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14357,-40,-42,0,'Vineyard Road','  You are on Vineyard Road, the main east-west road within Waterford.\nThe office of the Shiriff lies to the north, and the office of the\nBurgermeister to the south.  The road continues east and west.  There are\ndoors to the north and south.\n',76,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14358,-39,-42,0,'Inside the East Gate','  You are on Vineyard Road, the main east-west road within Waterford,\njust inside the east gate to the village.  The stout wooden wall to your\neast surrounds the village.  A small hobbit burrow lies to the north, and\na small shop lies to the south.  The east gate itself is just to the\neast, and the road continue to the west.  There are doors to the north\nand south.\n',76,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14359,-43,-42,0,'Vineyard Road','  You are on Vineyard Road, the main east-west road within Waterford.\nThe Grimhaven Embassy lies to the north and an inn to the south.  The\nvillage square is to your east and the road continues to the west.  There\nare doors to both the north and south.\n',76,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14360,-44,-42,0,'Vineyard Road','  You are on Vineyard Road, the main east-west road within Waterford.\nThe Grimhaven Embassy lies to the north and an inn to the south.  You see\na bridge to the west and the road continues to the east.\n',76,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14361,-43,-41,0,'Foyer','  You are in the foyer of the Grimhaven Embassy.  The place is ornately\ndecorated, it was obviously designed to emphasize the wealth and power of\nthe Kingdom of Grimhaven.  The walls are white plaster with gold leaf\ntrim.  Large velvet curtains, red with gold trim, frame all the doors.\nThe floor is polished marble, with the Grimhaven Coat of Arms inlaid in\nthe center.  Doors to the south and east open out into the village, while\ndoors to the north and west lead deeper into the building.  There is a\nbrass plaque above the door to the west, and a sign beside the door to\nthe north.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14362,-44,-41,0,'Office of the Ambassador','  You are in the office of the Grimhaven Ambassador to the Shire.  The\noffice is both ornately decorated, as befits a man of the Ambassador\'s\nrank, and functional, as you would expect of the career diplomat who holds\nthis important post.  The walls are the same white plaster with gold leaf\ntrim that was found in the lobby, but the floor is polished hardwood\ninstead of marble.  Bookcases frame both the window in the west wall and\nthe wooden door in the north wall.  A fireplace stands alone on the south\nwall.  A variety of plaques and certificates hang on the east wall.\nThere are doors to the east and north.\n',76,131084,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14363,-44,-40,0,'A Studio Apartment','  This room is the personal apartment of the Ambassador.  While not as\nornate as the rest of the embassy, everything in the room is of high\nquality and immaculate cleanliness.  There is a door in the southern wall.\n',76,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14364,-43,-40,0,'Embassy Office','  This office is typical of that of bureaucrats everywhere.  The walls are\npainted a pale \"puke\" green and the floor is made of tile, the color of\nwhich emphasizes the dirt rather than hiding it.  A long counter divides\nthe room into two sections, the waiting area where you are in the front,\nand the clerk\'s working area in the back.  Your side of the counter is\nbare, without even a chair to sit on while you wait for the clerk to get\nto you.  Several large desks and numerous filing cabinets take up most of\nthe space behind the counter.  A small sign sits on the counter and there\nis a large poster on the back wall.  There is a door to the south.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14365,-43,-39,0,'Inside a Hobbit Burrow','  You find yourself in the middle of a small sized hobbit burrow, built\ninto the center of a small hillock.  The walls, floor and ceiling are\nmade of wood, if you hadn\'t seen the outside, you would never know you\'re\nin a home below ground and not a free-standing house.  The room itself is\nabout 15 feet square, the six foot high ceiling forces the taller among\nyou to walk slightly bent over.  All the activities of the family take\nplace in this one room.  The front part is the living area, with a eating\narea along the northern wall, a kitchen in the back to the west, and\nplaces for sleeping along the wall to the south.  There is a round door\nin the eastern wall.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,72,0,'',NULL),
(14366,-40,-44,-1,'Crawlspace','  You are in a crawlspace under the meeting hall.  A first glance, this\nplace doesn\'t appear to have been visited in a long time, maybe since the\nhall was built.  Cobwebs hang from the ceiling, which is only about three\nand a half feet tall.  The walls are of stone block construction and\nappear quite sturdy.  The floor is made of dirt, and is covered with a\nlayer of dust.  A flimsy wooden ladder leads up to the trapdoor in the\nceiling, and the room continues to the northwest.\n',76,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,42,0,'',NULL),
(14367,-41,-43,-1,'Crawlspace','  You are in a crawlspace under the meeting hall.  A first glance, this\nplace doesn\'t appear to have been visited in along, time, maybe since the\nhall was built.  Cobwebs hang from the ceiling, which is only about three\nand a half feet tall.  The walls are of stone block construction and\nappear quite sturdy.  The floor is made of dirt, and is covered with a\nlayer of dust.  The room continues to the southeast, and a hole has been\nknocked in the wall to the east.\n',76,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,42,0,'',NULL),
(14368,-40,-43,-1,'A Small Stone Room','  You are in a small room built of stone block.  Based on the route you\ntook to get here, you figure you are under the Burgermeister\'s office.\nThe room is fairly small, the ceiling is only about three and a half feet\ntall.  The floor is just packed earth.  The corners of the room are piled\nwith dirt, as though someone has been digging here recently.  A hole has\nbeen knocked in the western wall.\n',76,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,42,0,'',NULL),
(14369,-39,-43,-1,'Guildmaster\'s Office','  You are in the cozy office of the new Grandmaster of the Thieves\nGuild.  The office has features that give it a warm, homey feeling,\nincluding oak paneled walls, and a hardwood floor, which has been lowered\nto allow adequate headroom for the taller members of the guild.  Cabinets\ncontaining many of Guildmaster\'s treasures line the walls.  A large\nfireplace has been added, its chimney cunningly concealed in that of the\nshop above this room.  The exit to the room is to the west, opened by\npushing the block on the wall.\n',76,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,80,0,'',NULL),
(14370,-41,-41,0,'Among the Pews','  You are at the back of the Waterford village church, among the pews.\nThe inside of this small wooden building is Spartan and plain, as befits a\npoor country parish.  The walls are bare wood covered with a thin coat\nof whitewash.  Leaded glass windows, once colorful but now dulled by years\nworth of grime, admit barely enough light to see by.  The altar is to the\nnortheast, and the door out of the church is to the southwest.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14371,-40,-40,0,'At the Altar','  You are at the front of the Waterford village church, next to the altar.\nThe inside of this small wooden building is Spartan and plain, as befits a\npoor country parish.  The walls are bare wood covered with a thin coat\nof whitewash.  Leaded glass windows, once colorful but now dulled by years\nworth of grime, admit barely enough light to see by.  The pews lie to the\nsouthwest.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14372,-41,-40,0,'Village Bakery','  You are in the bakery for the village.  The smell of fresh baked bread\nand pastry fills the air, making your stomach rumble and your mouth\nwater.  There is a door to the west.\n',76,164028,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14373,-41,-39,0,'Inside a Hobbit Burrow','  You find yourself in the middle of a small sized hobbit burrow, built\ninto the center of a small hillock.  The walls, floor and ceiling are\nmade of wood, if you hadn\'t seen the outside, you would never know you\'re\nin a home below ground and not a free-standing house.  The room itself is\nabout 15 feet square, the six foot high ceiling forces the taller among\nyou to walk slightly bent over.  All the activities of the family take\nplace in this one room.  The front part is the living area, with a eating\narea along the northern wall, a kitchen in the back to the east, and\nplaces for sleeping along the wall to the south.  There is a round door\nin the western wall.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,72,0,'',NULL),
(14374,-40,-41,0,'Office of the Shiriff','  This small stone office belongs to the High Shiriff, the chief law\nenforcement officer of Waterford Shire.  The first thing you notice is\nthat there are none of the things you are used to seeing in jails, no\ncells, no wanted posters, no bars on the doors or windows, and no\nprisoners.  The single room is plain, but very clean.  The floor is\nstone, and the ceiling to only 6 feet high, forcing humans and ogres to\nwalk with bent knees.  There is a single door to the south.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,96,0,'',NULL),
(14375,-39,-41,0,'Inside a Hobbit Burrow','  You find yourself in the middle of a small sized hobbit burrow, built\ninto the center of a small hillock.  The walls, floor and ceiling are\nmade of wood, if you hadn\'t seen the outside, you would never know you\'re\nin a home below ground and not a free-standing house.  The room itself is\nabout 15 feet square, the six foot high ceiling forces the taller among\nyou to walk slightly bent over.  All the activities of the family take\nplace in this one room.  The front part is the living area, with a eating\narea along the western wall, a kitchen in the back to the north, and\nplaces for sleeping along the wall to the east.  There is a round door in\nthe southern wall.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,72,0,'',NULL),
(14376,-43,-43,0,'Entry to the Dancing Bear','  You are in the entry way to the Dancing Bear Inn and Tavern.  The walls\nare made of a dark, hand-polished wood, and the floor is slate.  The\nceiling is at a rather comfortable height of 8 feet.  Doors open out into\nthe street to the north and east, to the south you see the reception\ndesk of the inn, and to the west a pair of swinging doors lead into the\ntavern.  <y>A sign stands beside the door to the bar.<1>\n',76,131084,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14377,-44,-43,0,'Dancing Bear Tavern','  This place exudes a warm, homey feeling, the perfect place to come have\na drink with friends and forget your cares for a while.  The walls of the\nroom are paneled in dark, hand-polished wood, and the floor is made of\nplanks of the same wood.  Smoke from the fire and dozens of hobbit pipes\nfills the room with aromatic scents, and obscures the ceiling.  A long\nbar stands by the northern wall.  Tables and comfortable chairs take up\nmost of the floor space.  A pair of swinging doors lead east into the\nentry to the inn, and a sliding glass door to the south leads out onto\nthe deck.  A sign hangs on the wall behind the bar.\n',76,164024,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14378,-44,-44,0,'Deck of the Dancing Bear Tavern','  Wow, what a view!  The Silverstone river flows along the southern edge\nof the deck from east to west, and Whitehawk Creek flows along the\nwestern edge from north to south.  The deck is built onto the back of the\ninn/tavern, just above the point where they meet.  Looking south across\nthe Silverstone, you can see and open, arid plain, with the edge of a\ndesert just visible on the horizon.  Looking west across the creek, you\nsee a rolling grassland, extending all the way to the horizon.  The deck\nis built of wood, with benches along the edge, and tables and stools\ntaking up most of the floor space, for those who prefer fresh air and\nsunshine to the dark, smoke-filled air of the tavern, which lies through\na sliding glass door to the north.\n',76,164020,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14379,-43,-44,0,'Reception Desk','  Before you stands the reception desk of the Dancing Bear Inn.  The\nwalls of the room are made of dark paneling, with the floor made of\nplanks of the same wood.  The room is warm, and slightly smoky.  A set\nof stairs behind the desk leads up to the private rooms above.  To the\nnorth is the entry way.\n',76,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14380,-41,-43,0,'Back of the Meeting Hall','  You are at the back of the Waterford Shire Community Meeting Hall.\nThis large, open room is designed to hold the entire population of the\nShire, when they get together to hold town meetings and celebrations.\nThe building is of wood frame construction, and the floor of the room is\nmade of tile.  Wide doors open onto the street to the north and west, and\nthe room continues to the southeast.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14381,-40,-44,0,'Front of the Meeting Hall','  You are at the front of the Waterford Shire Community Meeting Hall.\nThis large, open room is designed to hold the entire population of the\nShire, when they get together to hold town meetings and celebrations.\nThe building is of wood frame construction, and the floor of the room is\nmade of tile.  The room continues to the northwest.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14382,-41,-44,0,'Inside a Hobbit Burrow','  You find yourself in the middle of a small sized hobbit burrow, built\ninto the center of a small hillock.  The walls, floor and ceiling are\nmade of wood, if you hadn\'t seen the outside, you would never know you\'re\nin a home below ground and not a free-standing house.  The room itself is\nabout 15 feet square, the six foot high ceiling forces the taller among\nyou to walk slightly bent over.  All the activities of the family take\nplace in this one room.  The front part is the living area, with a eating\narea along the northern wall, a kitchen in the back to the east, and\nplaces for sleeping along the wall to the south.  There is a round door in\nthe western wall.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,72,0,'',NULL),
(14384,-40,-43,0,'Office of the Burgermeister','  This small, plain office is occupied by the leader of the Hobbit\ncommunity here in the Shire.  Since hobbits are too independent to\npermit much in the way of government, this room really just serves as a\nplace where people can come and ask the advice of the Burgermeister, who\nis widely considered to be the wisest member of the hobbit race.  The\nroom itself is made of stone, and the low ceiling reflects the height of\nthe occupant.  There is a single door to the north.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14385,-39,-43,0,'Waterford Trading Post','  You are in a shop unlike that you have ever seen before.  Items of\nevery description line the shelves and display cases of this small,\ncluttered room.  You can discern no rhyme or reason to the order or\nplacement in which items are stored, it looks like things have been\ndropped or cast aside seemingly at random.  The only way you are going to\nfind anything is to ask the proprietor.  <y>There is a sign on the counter.<1>\nThere are doors in the north and south walls.\n',76,164024,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14386,-39,-44,-1,'Loading Dock','  You are on a small square, wooden dock along the banks of the\nSilverstone river.  Boxes, bales, bags and crates of various sizes make\nit difficult to navigate here, but the are a few clear aisles left.  To\nthe north, a door leads into the back of a small shop.  There is access\nto the river from both the eastern and southern sides of the dock.  The\nback of a wooden building prevents passage to the west.\n',76,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14387,-38,-42,0,'Outside the East Gate','  You are on a dusty path, just outside the east gate to a small shire.\nThe shire is protected by a stout wooden wall, which runs north and south\nat this point.  The gate to the west leads through the wall into the\nshire.  To the north, a small hobbit burrow lies alongside the wall, with\na round door facing the road.  To the south, a pipeweed patch lies in the\nlowlands along the river bank.  The path continues to the east.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14388,-37,-42,-1,'On a Dusty Path','  You are in the middle of a dusty path, which runs through a series of\nlow hills.  The hills to the north show signs of cultivation, and a\npipeweed patch lies in the lowlands along the river to the south.  A\nshort way to the west you can see a wall, with the roofs of a small shire\npoking over the top.  The path continues to the east and west.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14389,-36,-42,-1,'On a Dusty Path','  You are in the middle of a dusty path, which runs through a series of\nlow hills.  The hills to the north show signs of cultivation, and a\npipeweed patch lies in the lowlands along the river to the south.  A ways\nto the west you can see a wall, with the roofs of a small shire poking\nover the top.  A stone building is built into the hillside to the east.\nThe path continues to the southeast and west.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14390,-35,-43,-1,'On a Dusty Path','  You are in the middle of a dusty path, which runs through a series of\nlow hills.  A stone building is built into the side of the hill to the\nnorth and east.  There is a wooden door in the wall to the north.  A\nriver parallels the road immediately to the south.  A pipeweed patch lies\nin the lowlands along the river to the west.  The path continues to the\nsoutheast and northwest.\n',76,131076,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14391,-34,-44,-1,'On a Dusty Path','  You are in the middle of a dusty path, which runs through a series of\nlow hills, paralleling a river.  A stone building is built into the side\nof the hill to the north.  A wide, swift flowing river prevents passage\nto the south.  You can hear a loud roaring sound in the distance to the\neast.  The path continues to the northwest and a rock ledge leads along\nthe river to the east.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14392,-33,-44,-1,'On a Rock Ledge','  You are on a rock ledge, which runs along a rocky cliff face parallel\nto a wide, swiftly flowing river.  The cliffs prevent passage to the\nnorth, and the river prevents passage to the south.  You can hear a loud\nroaring sound a short ways to the east.  The ledge continues to the east\nand west.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14393,-32,-44,-1,'Beside Silverstone Falls','  You are on a rock ledge beside the base of the mighty Silverstone\nFalls.  The loud roaring of the falls makes conversation here difficult.\nTall cliffs of solid rock prevent further passage to the north and east.\nA wide pool at the base of the falls lies to the south.  The falls\nthemselves are just to the southeast.  The ledge continues to the west.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14394,-31,-45,-1,'Behind Silverstone Falls','  This small passage lies just behind Silverstone Falls.  The falls are\nto the west.  A rock ledge disappears into the waterfall to the\nnorthwest, and the passage continues to the northeast.  The walls of the\npassage are smooth, it appears that this tunnel was created by running\nwater at some time in the distant past.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(14395,-30,-44,-1,'An Underground Passage','  You are in a narrow passage, worn by water and time through solid\nrock.  A load roaring sound comes from further down the passage to the\nsouthwest.  The passage opens into a cave to the northwest.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(14396,-31,-43,-1,'In a Cave','  You are in the southeast corner of a large cave, which stretches off\ninto the darkness to the north and west.  Stalagmites cover the cave\nfloor, indicating that this cave was formed by running water long ago.\nThe ceiling of the cave is lost in the gloom.  The cave is cool and\nslightly damp.  There is an acrid smell which you can\'t quite place.  A\npassage leads off to the southeast.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,410,0,'',NULL),
(14397,-32,-43,-1,'In a Cave','  You are in the southwest corner of a large cave, which stretches off\ninto the darkness to the north and east.  Stalagmites cover the cave\nfloor, indicating that this cave was formed by running water long ago.\nThe ceiling of the cave is lost in the gloom.  The cave is cool and\nslightly damp.  There is an acrid smell which you can\'t quite place.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,410,0,'',NULL),
(14398,-32,-42,-1,'In a Cave','  You are in the northwest corner of a large cave, which stretches off\ninto the darkness to the south and east.  Stalagmites cover the cave\nfloor, indicating that this cave was formed by running water long ago.\nThe ceiling of the cave is lost in the gloom.  The cave is cool and\nslightly damp.  There is an acrid smell which you can\'t quite place.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,410,0,'',NULL),
(14399,-31,-42,-1,'In a Cave','  You are in the northeast corner of a large cave, which stretches off\ninto the darkness to the south and west.  Stalagmites cover the cave\nfloor, indicating that this cave was formed by running water long ago.\nThe ceiling of the cave is lost in the gloom.  The cave is cool and\nslightly damp.  There is a strong acrid smell, which makes think of a\nlarge reptile.  An alcove lies to the east.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,410,0,'',NULL),
(14400,-30,-42,-1,'In a Dragon\'s Lair','  You are in an alcove off a large cave.  A raised ledge at the back of\nthe alcove provides a dry bed for the dragon.  Numerous bones lie\nscattered about the alcove, remains of the dragon\'s last visitors.  The\nodor in here is fairly obnoxious, the acrid stink of a large reptile\nmixed with smell of decayed animal matter.\n',76,133128,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,410,0,'',NULL),
(14401,-35,-42,-1,'Entry of the Silverstone Winery','  This small stone room is the entryway into the Silverstone Winery and\nVineyard.  Plaques dot the walls, showing the awards the winery has won\nover the years.  A wooden door to the south leads out to a path.  An iron\ngate to the north leads into the vineyard.  A metal door to the east\nleads deeper into the building.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14402,-34,-42,-1,'Wine Processing Room','  This is the room where the grapes are made into wine.  Several large\npresses occupy the center of the room, and a number of wooden tubs sit\nalong the walls.  Spare wine bottles and casks are stacked about\nhaphazardly.  Doors lead out of the room to the east, west and south.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14403,-34,-43,-1,'Winery Office','  This small office is where the master vintner oversees the operation of\nthe winery and vineyard.  The place is cluttered, with papers scattered\neverywhere.  The walls and floor are made of stone, with a wooden roof.\nA single door leads north into the winery.\n',76,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14404,-33,-42,-1,'Winery Storage Cave','  This medium sized natural cave is used by the winery for storage.  This\npart of the cave seems to be used for general storage, you see cases of\nempty new wine bottles, and stacks of small wine casks.  The cave is cool\nand dry.  A stone door leads west into the winery, and the cave continues\nto the south.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14405,-33,-43,-1,'Wine Aging Cave','  You are in the back of the winery storage cave, where the processed\nwine is stored and aged.  Large wooden barrels line the walls, and cases\nof bottled wine are neatly stacked in the center of the floor.  The cave,\nwhich is cool and dry, continues to the north.\n',76,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(14406,-37,-41,-1,'In the Vineyard','  You are at the western end of the vineyard.  Trellises line the\nhillside, with well-tended grape vines of numerous types almost\ncompletely covering them.  A stone wall runs around the vineyard,\nseparating it from the hillsides to the north, south and west.  The\nvineyard continues to the east.\n',76,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14407,-36,-41,-1,'In the Vineyard','  You are in the center of the vineyard.  Trellises line the hillside,\nwith well-tended grape vines of numerous types almost completely covering\nthem.  A stone wall runs along the north side of the vineyard, separating\nit from the hillside.  The stone winery building lies to the south.  The\nvineyard continues to the east and west.\n',76,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14408,-35,-41,-1,'In the Vineyard','  You are in the center of the vineyard.  Trellises line the hillside,\nwith well-tended grape vines of numerous types almost completely covering\nthem.  A stone wall runs along the north side of the vineyard, separating\nit from the hillside.  An iron gate leads into the stone winery building\nto the south.  The vineyard continues to the east and west.\n',76,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14409,-34,-41,-1,'In the Vineyard','  You are in the center of the vineyard.  Trellises line the hillside,\nwith well-tended grape vines of numerous types almost completely covering\nthem.  A stone wall runs along the north side of the vineyard, separating\nit from the hillside.  The stone winery building lies to the south.  The\nvineyard continues to the east and west.\n',76,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14410,-33,-41,-1,'In the Vineyard','  You are at the eastern end of the vineyard.  Trellises line the\nhillside, with well-tended grape vines of numerous types almost\ncompletely covering them.  A stone wall runs around the vineyard,\nseparating it from the hillsides to the north, south and east.  The\nvineyard continues to the west.\n',76,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14411,-42,-45,0,'Bridge Over the Silverstone River','  You are in the middle of a wide, stone bridge that spans the\nSilverstone River.  The bridge is made of large blocks of a polished\nsilvery stone, and is obviously of dwarven construction.  A stairway\nleads down the southern bridge pillar to the river 30 feet below.  A\nbrass plaque is affixed to the pillar beside the stairway.  A street\nleads north into a small shire, and a trail leads south into an arid\nplain.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14412,-42,-46,0,'On a Dusty Trail','  This trail isn\'t much more than a pair of ruts made by the wheels\nnumerous wagons in the hard packed dirt surface of the plain.  There is a\nlittle bit of green here, next to the river, but the further south you\ngo, the more arid it gets.  Even this close to the river, the vegetation\nis stunted and scraggly.  To the north, the trail crosses a bridge into a\nsmall shire.  To the south, the trail continues across the plain.\n',76,131076,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14413,-42,-47,0,'On a Dusty Trail','  This trail isn\'t much more than a pair of ruts made by the wheels\nnumerous wagons in the hard packed dirt surface of the plain.  There is a\nlittle bit of green here, close to the river, but the further south you\ngo, the more arid it gets.  Even this close to the river, the vegetation\nis stunted and scraggly.  The trail continues north and south.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14414,-42,-48,0,'On a Dusty Trail','  This trail isn\'t much more than a pair of ruts made by the wheels\nnumerous wagons in the hard packed dirt surface of the plain.  The dirt\nis dry and cracking due to lack of moisture, and what little vegetation\nyou see is stunted and scraggly.  Further south, it appears even more\narid.  The trail continues to the north and southwest.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14415,-43,-49,0,'On a Dusty Trail','This trail isn\'t much more than a pair of ruts made by the wheels\nnumerous wagons in the hard packed dirt surface of the plain.  The dirt\nis dry and cracking due to lack of moisture, and what little vegetation\nyou see is stunted and scraggly.  Further south, it appears even more\narid.  The trail continues to the northeast, and to the southwest the trail\ndisappears into a broad desert.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14416,-45,-42,0,'Bridge Over Whitehawk Creek','  You are in the middle of a wide, stone bridge that spans Whitehawk\nCreek.  The bridge is made of large blocks of a polished silvery stone,\nand is obviously of dwarven construction.  A street leads east into a\nsmall shire, and a road leads west.  It is possible to climb down to\nthe water below.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14417,-46,-42,0,'Norman\'s Road','  You are on the southern part of Norman\'s Road.  The road itself is made\nof carefully hewn granite cobblestones meticulously maintained, although\nsome weeds and moss grows up between a few of the rocks here and there.\nA rolling open grassland borders the road to the south and west, and a\nfield of grain lies to the north.  The road continues to the east and \nnorthwest.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14418,-47,-41,0,'Norman\'s Road','  You are on the southern part of Norman\'s Road.  The road itself is made\nof carefully hewn granite cobblestones meticulously maintained although\nsome weeds and moss grows up between a few of the rocks here and there.\nA rolling, open plain borders the road to the south and west, and a field\nof grain lies to the north and east.  The road runs northwest and southeast.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14419,-48,-40,0,'Norman\'s Road','  You are on the southern part of Norman\'s Road.  The road itself is made\nof carefully hewn granite cobblestones meticulously maintained although\nsome weeds and moss grows up between a few of the rocks here and there.\nA rolling, open grassland borders the road to the south and west, and a\nfield of grain lies to the east.  The road runs north and southeast.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14420,-48,-39,0,'Norman\'s Road','  You are on the southern part of Norman\'s Road.  The road itself is made\nof carefully hewn granite cobblestones meticulously maintained although\nsome weeds and moss grows up between a few of the rocks here and there.\nA rolling, open grassland borders the road to the west, and a wide prairie\nlies to the east.  The road continues north and south.\n',76,131076,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14421,-48,-38,0,'Norman\'s Road','  You are on the southern part of Norman\'s Road.  The road itself is made\nof carefully hewn granite cobblestones meticulously maintained although\nsome weeds and moss grows up between a few of the rocks here and there.\nA wide prairie borders the road to the east, and an open, rolling\ngrassland lies to the west.  The road continues north and south.\n',76,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
