(14489,-53,-44,-1,'On the Silverstone River','  You are in the middle of the Silverstone River.  This broad, swift\nflowing stream runs from the Parnithian Mountains westward to the Agorian\nSea.  The river takes its name from the silvery stones that can be found\nupon its banks.  The river is about 150 feet wide, and over 15 feet\ndeep.  Looking northeast, you see an open grassland, which extends to\nthe horizon.  To the southwest you can see a broad, arid plain.  The\nriver continues upstream to the southeast and downstream to the\nnorthwest.\n',76,131072,29,0,0,0,30,7,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14490,-54,-43,-1,'On the Silverstone River','  You are in the middle of the Silverstone River.  This broad, swift\nflowing stream runs from the Parnithian Mountains westward to the Agorian\nSea.  The river takes its name from the silvery stones that can be found\nupon its banks.  The river is about 150 feet wide, and over 15 feet\ndeep.  Looking north, you see an open grassland, which extends to the\nhorizon.  To the southwest you can see a broad, arid plain.  The river\ncontinues upstream to the southeast and downstream to the west.\n',76,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14491,-55,-43,-1,'On the Silverstone River','  You are in the middle of the Silverstone River.  This broad, swift\nflowing stream runs from the Parnithian Mountains westward to the Agorian\nSea.  The river takes its name from the silvery stones that can be found\nupon its banks.  The river is about 150 feet wide, and over 15 feet\ndeep.  The banks of the river are high enough here that you cannot see\nwhat is beyond them from your viewpoint on the river\'s surface.  The\nriver continues upstream to the east and downstream to the west.\n',76,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14492,-56,-43,-1,'On the Silverstone River','  You are in the middle of the Silverstone River.  This broad, swift\nflowing stream runs from the Parnithian Mountains westward to the Agorian\nSea.  The river takes its name from the silvery stones that can be found\nupon its banks.  The river is about 150 feet wide, and over 15 feet\ndeep.  The banks of the river are high enough here that you cannot see\nwhat is beyond them from your viewpoint on the river\'s surface.  The\nriver continues upstream to the east and downstream to the northwest.\n',76,131072,29,0,0,0,30,7,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14493,-57,-42,-1,'On the Silverstone River','  You are in the middle of the Silverstone River.  This broad, swift\nflowing stream runs from the Parnithian Mountains westward to the Agorian\nSea.  The river takes its name from the silvery stones that can be found\nupon its banks.  The river is about 150 feet wide, and over 15 feet\ndeep.  The banks of the river are high enough here that you cannot see\nwhat is beyond them from your viewpoint on the river\'s surface.  The\nriver continues upstream to the southeast and downstream to the\nnorthwest.\n',76,131072,29,0,0,0,30,7,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14494,-58,-41,-1,'On the Silverstone River','  You are in the middle of the Silverstone River.  This broad, swift\nflowing stream runs from the Parnithian Mountains westward to the Agorian\nSea.  The river takes its name from the silvery stones that can be found\nupon its banks.  The river is about 150 feet wide, and over 15 feet\ndeep.  The banks of the river are high enough here that you cannot see\nwhat is beyond them from your viewpoint on the river\'s surface.  The\nriver continues upstream to the southeast and downstream to the west.\nDownstream to the west, a highway bridge spans the river.\n',76,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14495,-59,-41,-1,'On the Silverstone River','  You are in the middle of the Silverstone River.  This broad, swift\nflowing stream runs from the Parnithian Mountains westward to the Agorian\nSea.  The river takes its name from the silvery stones that can be found\nupon its banks.  The river is about 150 feet wide, and over 15 feet\ndeep.  The banks of the river are high enough here that you cannot see\nwhat is beyond them from your viewpoint on the river\'s surface.  Far\nabove your head, a bridge carrying a major highway spans the river.  The\nriver continues upstream to the east and downstream to the west.\n',76,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14496,-60,-41,-1,'Silverstone River Delta','  The Silverstone River begins to spread out here, as it flows into the\nAgorian Sea.  The banks of the ravine begin to tumble away as the you\nnear the shore of the sea.  The delta fans out to the northwest and\nsouthwest, although the main channel is still to the west.  The river\ncontinues upstream to the east, where a bridge carrying the coastal\nhighway across the river can be seen.\n',76,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14497,-61,-40,-1,'Northern Channel of the Silverstone River Delta','  The Silverstone River spreads out here, as it flows into the Agorian\nSea, which stretches out to the west of you.  You are in the northernmost\nchannel, which flows northwest into the sea.  The seashore stretches to\nthe north before you, far in the distance, you can see a white city along\nthe sea.  The delta continues to the south, and the river flows from the\nsoutheast.\n',76,131072,29,0,0,0,30,7,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14498,-61,-41,-1,'Main Channel of the Silverstone River Delta','  The Silverstone River spreads out here, as it flows into the Agorian\nSea, which stretches out to the west of you.  You are in the main\nchannel, which flows west into the sea.  The delta continues to the north\nand south, and the river flows from the east.\n',76,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14499,-61,-42,-1,'Southern Channel of the Silverstone River Delta','  The Silverstone River spreads out here, as it flows into the Agorian\nSea, which stretches out to the west of you.  You are in the southernmost\nchannel, which flows southwest into the sea.  The seashore stretches to\nthe south before you.  The delta continues to the north, and the river\nflows from the northeast.\n',76,131072,29,0,0,0,30,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14500,0,0,0,'On the Silverstone River','  You are in the middle of the Silverstone River.  This broad, swift\nflowing stream runs from the Parnithian Mountains westward to the Agorian\nSea.  The river takes its name from the silvery stones that can be found\nupon its banks.  The river is about 150 feet wide, and over 15 feet\ndeep.  Looking north, you see an open grassland, which extends to the\nhorizon.  To the south you can see a broad, arid plain.  The river\ncontinues upstream to the east and downstream to the northwest.\n',76,131072,29,0,0,0,30,7,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(14501,0,0,0,'On the Silverstone River','  You are in the middle of the Silverstone River.  This broad, swift\nflowing stream runs from the Parnithian Mountains westward to the Agorian\nSea.  The river takes its name from the silvery stones that can be found\nupon its banks.  The river is about 150 feet wide, and over 15 feet\ndeep.  Looking north, you see an open grassland, which extends to the\nhorizon.  To the south you can see a broad, arid plain.  The river\ncontinues upstream to the east and downstream to the northwest.\n',76,131072,29,0,0,0,30,7,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15100,13,33,-2,'Lesser Traveled Path in Haon-Dor','  This path is barely a path.  The foliage has been arranged to prevent\ndistant eyes from seeing the path into the woods.  A diversion which kept\ntravelers of the Haon-Dor trail from observing the heart of the forest.\nThe sky is completely blocked off by the overhanging branches.  The small\npath continues south at a moderate descent through a break in the brush or\nyou can go east to return to the main trail.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15101,10,25,-3,'Underfloor Storage','  This is where the parishable items are stored for the pygmies.  Food\nthat can rot in the hot sun is maintained a little longer by the cool\ndirt that this cellar is dug into.  It also serves as a place to hide, if\nthe need be.\n',86,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15102,13,32,-2,'Lesser Traveled Path in Haon-Dor','  Pushing your way through the dense brush, you notice that this path\nparallels the Haon-Dor trail.  Unnatural brush to the east has been placed\nto hinder vision from the main trail.  The fallen leaves from the trees\nquiet your footfalls as you pick your way among the foliage.  There is a\nsmall opening in the path to the southwest as well as to the north where\nthe path seems to climb a a bit deeper into the forest.  Only the sounds\nof your heartbeat and the small animals moving in the dense underbrush can\nbe heard above the awesome silence of the forest.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15103,12,31,-2,'Lesser Traveled Path in Haon-Dor','  The narrow path is quite constrained and is nearly impossible to traverse.\nYou notice that there are a multitude of small humanoid footprints in the\nsoft ground.  The heavy grass and leaves covering the forest floor have been\nworn away to leave a narrow rut.  The path continues to the northeast and to\nthe southwest.  The light ground fog obscures your vision and amplifies noises\nheard in the distance.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15104,11,30,-2,'Lesser Traveled Path in Haon-Dor','  The narrow path is quite constrained and is nearly impossible to traverse.\nYou notice that there are a multitude of small humanoid footprints in the\nsoft ground.  The heavy grass and leaves covering the forest floor have been\nworn away to leave a rut.  The path appears to widen a bit to the west,\nwhile to the northeast it seems to vanish into the fog blanketed forest.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15105,10,30,-2,'Trail Head','  Abundant trees and brush constrict your movement in all directions except\nfor two.  A vague path to the east can be seen.  To the southwest the forest\nappears to thin out slightly.  Giant trees felled by time litter the area.\nThe light fog and moss hanging from the trees give the impression of flying\nspirits out to wreak havoc on anyone who dare enter their domain.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15106,9,29,-2,'Clearing in the Forest of Haon-Dor','  Standing on the edge of an abrupt treeline, you see a village to the\nsouth, encircled by a makeshift fence.  From this distance you cannot\nmake out details of the village.  The village sits on the northern end\nof a grassy meadow.  The break in the trees allows you to see the large\nplateau to the far south.  To the northeast the trail enters the deep\nforest.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15107,9,28,-2,'North of Village','  The fence blocking your way south is composed of thorns and vines from\nthe forest.  Quite capable of keeping out the small animals, you doubt that\nit would stand up to anything larger than a horse.  You see just past the\nfence into the village.  Approximately ten yurts are built in a circle,\nradiating out from a central larger structure.  There might be an entrance\neast or west.  To the north is the path into the forest treeline.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15108,10,28,-2,'Northeast Path Around Pygmy Village','  Peering into the village, pygmies stare back at you with fear in\ntheir eyes.  The fence continues southeast and to the west.  You\nnotice that the dwellings in the village are built mostly out of\nvines and debris from the forest.  The larger structure in the center\nis the only one made with a wooden frame.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15109,11,27,-2,'Northeast Path Around Pygmy Village','  You are on a path that skirts the outside of the village.  The\nthorns and vines are much less dense here.  A number of sticks are\nfashioned together to form a gate to the southwest.  A stray stone or\nspear flies over the fence from the unhappy warriors inside.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,10,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15110,12,26,-2,'Eastern Path Around Pygmy Village','  You are on a path that skirts the outside of the village.  The\npath is the only direction of travel around the village.  To the south,\na yurt is positioned to hold up the fence.  From this vantage point\nyou can see the larger building in the middle is taller on the west\nside than the east.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15111,13,25,-2,'Eastern Path Around Pygmy Village','  The path following the fence changes direction here.  Due south\nor northwest, the path outlines the village.  Looking at the structures\nit would seem that these buildings have been here for some time.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15112,13,24,-2,'Eastern Path Around Pygmy Village','  The path follows the fence to the north and southwest.  Looking\nat the structures inside the village, it is apparent that time has taken\nits toll.  To the west, just on the other side of the fence, is a covered\nplatform.  The forest to the east is quite dense and impossible to see\nfive feet into.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15113,12,23,-2,'Southeast Path Around Pygmy Village','  You are on a path that skirts the outside of the village.  The\npath is the only direction of travel around the village.  To the north,\njust on the other side of the fence, is a covered platform.  Life\nsounds from animals are plentiful from the forest to the east.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15114,11,22,-2,'Southside Path Around Pygmy Village','  You are on a path that skirts the outside perimeter of the village.\nTo the nearby west you see an entrance to the village.  Northeast the\npath continues around the village.  Just on the other side of the fence\nto the north, is another yurt.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15115,10,22,-2,'Southside Path Around Pygmy Village','  Directly west is the entrance to the village.  The fence to your\nnorth thins a bit, but still warrants second thought of crossing as\nthe thorns are still quite abundant.  From this point you can see\nthe small maze of paths in the village.  Winding between yurts, the\npiles of forest debris, and disappearing behind the main hall, the paths\nare very well used.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15116,9,22,-2,'Southern Entry to Pygmy Village','  The fence has given way to the main path into the village.  To\nthe north you see a small well, and behind it a much larger structure.\nThe path west and east follow the village perimeter out to the forest.\nWell groomed and kept clean of trash this is the most widely used path\nby the pygmies.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15117,8,22,-2,'Southside Path Around Pygmy Village','  Directly east is the entrance to the village.  The fence to your\nnorth thins a bit, but still warrants second thought of crossing as\nthe thorns are still quite abundant.  From this point you can see\nthe small maze of paths in the village.  Winding between yurts, the\npiles of forest debris, and disappearing behind the main hall, the paths\nare very well used.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15118,7,22,-2,'Southside Path Around Pygmy Village','  You are on a path that skirts the outside perimeter of the village.\nTo the nearby east you see an entrance to the village.  Northwest\nthe path continues around the village.  On the other side of the fence\nto the north, is a yurt.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15119,6,23,-2,'Southwestern Path Around Pygmy Village','  You are on a path the skirts the outside of the village.  The path\nis the only direction of travel around the village.  To the north,\njust on the other side of the fence, is a covered platform.  To the west\nis a rocky impassable plateau that stretches southwest of here.  Upon\nthe plateau to the southwest is a walled city.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15120,5,24,-2,'Western Path Around Pygmy Village','  The path follows the fence to the north and the southeast.  Looking\nat the structures inside the village, it is apparent that time has taken\nits toll.  To the east, just on the other side of the fence, is a covered\nplatform.  The impassable rocky plateau to the west is quite ominous.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15121,5,25,-2,'Western Path Around Pygmy Village','  The path outside the fence that skirts the village perimeter changes\ndirection here.  Due south or northeast are your options.  Looking into\nthe village, the structures appear to have been here for quite some time.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15122,6,26,-2,'Northwestern Path Around Pygmy Village','  You are on a path that skirts the outside of the village.  The\npath is the only direction of travel around the village.  From this\nvantage point you can see the large structure in the middle is taller\non the west side than the east.  To the west is an impassable rocky\nplateau, several thick bits of brush along the base of its vertical\nrise.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15123,7,27,-2,'Northwestern Path Around Pygmy Village','  You are on a path that follows the fence to the northeast\nand southwest.  Looking at the structures inside the village, you can\nsee the decay from time and the forest taking a toll on all of the\nyurts.  To the west is an impassable rocky plateau.  A large flock\nof birds cover the sky to the north as they rise from the canopy of\nthe Haon-Dor.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15124,9,23,-2,'Pygmy Village','  Directly behind the well to the north is the center of the village.\nThis hub of the village is where the pygmy people conduct all their\nbusiness.  The trade of food, water, weapons and knowledge are the only\nworries that these people have.  To the nearby east and west are smaller\nyurts, possibly used for storage.  South is the main entrance to the\nvillage.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15125,8,28,-2,'Northern Path Around Pygmy Village','  Peering into the village, pygmies stare back at you with fear in\ntheir eyes.  The fence continues southwest and to the east.  You\nnotice that the dwellings in the village are built mostly out of\nvines and debris from the forest.  The larger structure in the center\nis the only one with a wooden frame.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15126,10,23,-2,'Pygmy Village','  You are on a path in the Pygmy village.  To the east is a well kept\nyurt.  The perimeter fence blocks your passage south.  You see the\nsouthern entrance to the village to your west.  Nearby to the north you\nsee the community hall.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15127,11,23,-2,'Tidy Yurt','  You are standing inside a six foot, domed hut.  Made with sticks, vines\nand debris from the forest, it provides more than adequate protection from\nthe elements.  As long as someone continuously repairs the roof.  The pygmies\nare not particular where they sleep nor do they need anything much more\nthan a blanket in this temperate weather.\n',86,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15128,10,24,-2,'Pygmy Village','  You are on a path in Pygmy village.  To the north is door to the\ncommunity hall.  There is a lookout platform nearby to the east and the\nperimeter fence lies to the south.  You see a round stone water well to\nthe west.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15129,11,24,-2,'Pygmy Village','  You are on a path in in Pygmy village.  To the east is the lookout\nplatform, built from logs in the forest, it is fashioned from the ancient\ntrees lashed together.  The path turns north and to the nearby west you\nsee the water well.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15130,12,25,-2,'Worn Down Yurt','  This round thatched dwelling is in a state of decay.  There\nare patches of the wall falling apart.  The domed roof has partially\nfallen in.  Sticks and debris litter the dirt floor.  Small pockets of\nwater are spread about the floor from the rain dripping in through\nthe leaky overhead.  The northern area of the round walls have separated\nfrom the rest of the yurt.\n',86,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15131,10,25,-2,'Community Hall','  Standing inside the community hall, the pygmies gather here to learn from\nthe teachings of Berardinis.  This is also where they store their food and\na majority of the weapons.  A door south leads into the village.  To the\nwest a door leads into another room of the hall.  There are no furnishings\nto speak of, save a occasional blanket.  There is a light dust floating in\nthe air as if dirt had been kicked up from the floor.\n',86,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15132,9,24,-2,'Before the Community Hall','  The path approaches a round stone well from the south, splits and\ncontinues on its way to the east and west.  The well has a bucket\nattached to a rope and pulley system to access the water.  The community\nhall before you to the north is by far the largest building of all in the\nvillage.  The western side of the hall is much taller, possibly having two\nlevels.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15133,11,25,-2,'Pygmy Village','  You are on a path in Pygmy village.  To the east is a well used yurt.\nIt is falling down and unkempt.  The community hall to the west allows\nno entrance here.  The path runs north to the perimeter fence and south\naround the hall.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15134,11,24,-1,'Lookout Platform','  This platform built out of logs from the forest, is quite sturdy.\nStanding upon it you can see over all the huts in the village and into\nthe forest.  To the southwest you can see the city built upon the\nplateau.  To the near northwest the windows in the second story of the\ncommunity hall are visible as well as anyone inside.  The thatched roof\nprovides shelter from the elements and also extra armor from an\nair attack, should there be any.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15135,8,24,-2,'Pygmy Village','  You are on a path in Pygmy village.  A door to the north leads into\nthe community hall.  You see a stone water well to the east and nearby\nto the west is a lookout platform and to the south is the perimeter\nfence.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15136,11,26,-2,'Pygmy Village','  You are on a path in Pygmy village.  The village perimeter fence\nis to your east as well as north and permits no passage.  The path turns\nwest here and also runs to the south.  The hall to the southwest displays\na heavy support structure made from the trees in the forest.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15137,10,26,-2,'Pygmy Village','  You are on a path in Pygmy village.  A small gate to the northeast\nblocks your way to the perimeter path.  The path east skirts the outside\nof the hall.  To the nearby west you see a possible entrance to the hall.\nThe hall to the south is completely walled off.  To the north is the side\nof a well kept yurt, however there is no entry from this direction.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15138,9,26,-2,'Pygmy Village','  You are on a path in Pygmy village.  The path runs east and west.\nTo the north is a narrow  path that is only traveled by one person.\nThe hall to the south is most impressive compared to the array of yurts.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15139,9,27,-2,'Pygmy Village','  You are on a narrow path in Pygmy village.  This path runs east into\na smaller yurt, and south to the unnamed path.  There are only one set of\nfootprints in the soft dirt of this path.  The fence to the north marks\nthe northern edge of the village.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15140,10,27,-2,'Tetrarch\'s Yurt','  This yurt is the sleeping place of the leader of the pygmies.  When not\nhere, he is with the Ancient Berardinis, learning of The World and its\nmystical powers.  The Tetrarch also teaches the pygmies what he learns.\nThe only offerings this yurt has is a blanket upon the floor and a roof\nthat does not leak.\n',86,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15141,8,26,-2,'Pygmy Village','  You are on a path in Pygmy village.  There is a door to the south,\nallowing entrance to the community hall.  The path west skirts the\noutside of the hall.  To the east the path runs along the backside\nof the hall.  The perimeter fence to the north blocks your way.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15142,7,26,-2,'Pygmy Village','  You are on a path in Pygmy village.  The village perimeter fence\nto your west and north permits no passage.  The path turns east here\nand also runs to the south.  The hall to the southeast stands above your\nhead.  You see that there are windows in the north and west side of the\nsecond story.  No movement in the second story is visible from this angle.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15143,9,25,-2,'Community Hall','  Standing inside the community hall, the pygmies gather here to learn from\nthe teachings of Berardinis.  This room is not decorated and has no windows.\nDoors north and south lead out into the village.  The ceiling is made from\nlogs laid side by side.  One log does not appear to fit correctly.  There is\na drawing in the soft dirt at your feet.\n',86,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15144,7,25,-2,'Pygmy Village','  You are on a path in Pygmy village.  The path north and south skirts\nthe outside wall of the hall.  The hall to your east blocks your way.\nThe perimeter fence to the west also blocks your way.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15145,8,25,-1,'SafeHaven','  Four windows on each wall of this haven allow one to stand anywhere\nin the room and view the surrounding terrain.  In the center of the room\nis the ornate chair of the Ancient Magus Berardinis.  His age forced his\nretirement from adventuring but his magical prowess has kept him alive to\ndiscover an inner self.  He teaches the Tetrarch of the pygmies basic magic\nand life lessons learned from the hard life of a battle mage.  Upon further\ninspection of the windows, three of them look normal.  The west window is\nthe only one that does not look right.  Shimmering, twisted images attack\nyour senses from this direction.\n',86,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15146,7,24,-2,'Pygmy Village','  You are on a path in Pygmy village.  To the west is a lookout\nplatform, built from logs in the forest, it looks like a miniature\nfortress.  The path runs north around the walls of the hall.  To the\nnearby east you see the water well.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15147,7,24,-1,'Lookout Platform','  This platform is built from logs in the forest, and is quite sturdy.\nStanding upon it you can see over all the huts in the village and into the\nrocky plateau to the west.  To the southwest you can see the city built upon\nthe plateau.  To the near northeast the windows in the second story of the\ncommunity hall are visible as well as any occupant inside.  The thatched\nroof above your head provides shelter from the elements and also extra\nprotection from an air attack, should there be any.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15148,8,23,-2,'Pygmy Village','  You are on a path in the Pygmy village.  To the west is a yurt.\nThe perimeter fence blocks your passage south.  You see the\nsouthern entrance to the village to your east.  Nearby to the north\nyou see the community hall.\n',86,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15149,7,23,-2,'Yurt','  You are standing inside a six foot, domed hut.  Made with sticks, vines\nand debris from the forest, it provides more than adequate protection from\nthe elements.  As long as someone continuously repairs the roof, the pygmies\nwill not get wet if it rains.  The yurt is not decorated and only a few\nblankets litter the floor.\n',86,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15150,6,-21,-1,'Fishing Boat Docks','  These small docks are designed specifically for Keirk\'s chartered fishing\nboat.  Passengers wait here for the boat to return from trips and to gather\nbefore boarding.\n',86,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15152,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined. It is so detailed they seem to \nwrithe. The path underfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine.  The tunnel\ncontinues in a downward slope.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15153,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined. It is so detailed they seem to \nwrithe.  The path underfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine.  The tunnel\ncontinues in a downward slope.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15154,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined. It is so detailed they seem to \nwrithe.  The path underfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine.  The tunnel\ncontinues in a downward slope.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15155,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined. It is so detailed they seem to \nwrithe.  The path underfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine.  The tunnel\ncontinues in a downward slope.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15156,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined.  It is so detailed they seem to \nwrithe.  The path underfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine.  The path\ncontinues to the north.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15157,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined. It is so detailed they seem to\nwrithe. The path underfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine that inclines\nso sharply to the northwest.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15158,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined. It is so detailed they seem to\nwrithe. There are words carved into the stone as well, perhaps explaining\nwhat the writhing serpents depict. The path underfoot is smoothed to a\nglossy shine that inclines slightly to the west. To the northeast is a\nsteep incline and to the southeast a steep decline.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15159,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined. It is so detailed they seem to\nwrithe. The path underfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine.  A slight decline\nleads to the east. All other directions seem to be level.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15160,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. The indepth\ncarvings on the walls seem to writhe with life.  The path underfoot is\nsmoothed to a glossy shine.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15161,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. The indepth\ncarvings on the walls seem to writhe with life.  The path underfoot is\nsmoothed to a glossy shine.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15162,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined. It is so detailed they seem to\nwrithe. The path underfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine.  The distant\nsound of water dripping can be heard somewhere to the northwest.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15163,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined. It is so detailed they seem to\nwrithe. The path underfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine.  The sound of\nwater dripping can be heard coming from the north.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15164,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined. It is so detailed they seem to\nwrithe. The path underfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15165,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined, there are some words in the\nmidst of the design. It is so detailed they seem to writhe.  The path\nunderfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine. Water drips loudly to the east.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15166,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined. It is so detailed they seem to\nwrithe. The path underfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine. A warm glow\ncomes from an alcove to the south.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15167,0,0,0,'<r>An Alcove in the Tunnels of Red Stone<1>','The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined. It is so detailed they seem to\nwrithe. The path underfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15168,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined. It is so detailed they seem to\nwrithe. The path underfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine. There is a\nbreeze blowing from some place north of here.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15169,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. Great care has\nbeen taken to carve intricate designs in the walls of the tunnel. The\ndesign consists of serpents intertwined. It is so detailed they seem to\nwrithe. The path underfoot is smoothed to a glossy shine. There is a gilt\nframed doorway to the north. A small window above the door is open,\nallowing the breeze to blow into the tunnels.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15170,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnels deeply polished walls appear to be dug into marble. There is\nlittle carved stone ere, the marbling is rich enough to catch attention. There is\na rich scent wafting from somewhere north. The path underfoot is smoothed to\na glossy shine.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15171,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnels deeply polished walls appear to be dug into marble. There is\nlittle carved stone here, the marbling is rich enough to catch attention. There is\na rich scent wafting from the north. The path underfoot is smoothed to a\nglossy shine. Wide steps have been cut into the northern end of the tunnel.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15172,0,0,0,'<r>A Round Room in the Red Stone Tunnels<1>','  This is a perfectly circular room. The red marble walls glow deeply from\nregular polishing. Along the ceiling is a border of serpents intertwined,\nthey seem to be in some kind of trance of worship. The floor is composed of\na rich black onyx. There are steps leading down towards the south, a tunnel\nleads out in a southeastern direction.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15173,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnels deeply polished walls appear to be dug into marble. There is\nlittle carved here, the marbling is rich enough to catch attention. There is\na rich scent wafting from the northwest. The path underfoot is smoothed to\na glossy shine. Wide steps have been cut into the northern end of the tunnel.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15174,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnels deeply polished walls appear to be dug into marble. There is\nlittle carved here, the marbling is rich enough to catch attention. There is\na rich scent wafting from somewhere northwest. The path underfoot is smoothed\nto a glossy shine.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15175,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnels deeply polished walls appear to be dug into marble. It is\nnearly solid in color with very little veining. The highly buffed surface\nis almost reflective. High ceilings lend an almost airy feel to the tunnel,\nbut the walls are close enough together to be a constant reminder that\nthis place is underground.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15176,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnels deeply polished walls appear to be dug into marble. It is\nnearly solid in color with very little veining. The highly buffed surface\nis almost reflective. High ceilings lend an almost airy feel to the tunnel,\nbut the walls are close enough together to be a constant reminder that \nthis place is underground. The tunnel becomes even more narrow to the\nnortheast.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15177,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. The walls have\nbeen buffed to a glossy shine. You see yourself reflected in them from every\nangle. The echoes resulting from the highly vaulted ceiling seem to go\non and on, resounding throughout the tunnel.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15178,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. The walls have\nbeen buffed to a glossy shine. Staring into them produces a reflection\nof yourself. The highly vaulted ceiling produces maddening echoes from\nany footsteps or other movements. The path drops steeply down to the\nsouthwest.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15179,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. The indepth\ncarvings on the walls seem to writhe with life. To the southwest the\ntunnel is narrowed and somewhat constricting. The path underfoot is\nsmoothed to a glossy shine.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15180,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. The stone here\nis smooth and unblemished. Red pebbles of various shades are loosely scattered\non the ground to make up the pathway.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15181,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. The stone here\nis smooth and unblemished. Red pebbles of various shades are loosely scattered\non the ground to make up the pathway.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15182,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel ends abruptly at the north end. The stones on the ground are of\nvarious shades of red pebbles.  They seem to have been carefully laid out and\naffixed in some kind of pattern.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15183,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. The stone here\nis smooth and unblemished. Red pebbles of various shades are loosely scattered\non the ground to make up the pathway.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
