(15189,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. The stone here\nis smooth and unblemished. Red pebbles of various shades are loosely scattered\non the ground to make up the pathway.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15190,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. The stone here\nis smooth and unblemished. Red pebbles of various shades are loosely scattered\non the ground to make up the pathway.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15191,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel ends abruptly at the north end. The stones on the ground are of\nvarious shades of red pebbles.  They seem to have been carefully laid out and\naffixed in some kind of pattern.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15192,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. The stone here\nis smooth and unblemished. Red pebbles of various shades are loosely scattered\non the ground to make up the pathway.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15193,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The tunnel is in the depths of a mass of deep red stone. The stone here\nis smooth and unblemished. Red pebbles of various shades are loosely scattered\non the ground to make up the pathway. There is a glossy red door on the on\nthe southern wall of the tunnel.\n',115,131084,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15194,0,0,0,'<r>A Narrow Stairwell<z>','   The stairwell is of extremely narrow proportions. It seems to have been\ndesigned to keep intruders from entering in large numbers. The steps are\nbarely ample in width for the placement of a large foot. Directly to the\nnortheast runs a tunnel, a door is located in the north wall.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(15195,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','   The walls of the tunnel have been artfully crafted, millions of sparkling\nred rubys are set in a most natural way. The warm glow of the rubys combined\nwith the rich luster of polished red marble floors exude wealth and comfort.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15196,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','   The walls of the tunnel have been artfully crafted, millions of sparkling\nred rubys are set in a most natural way. The warm glow of the rubys combined\nwith the rich luster of polished red marble floors exude wealth and comfort.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15197,0,0,0,'<r>A Meeting Room<z>','   This meeting room seems to be carved into a solid bed of red marble. The\nwalls, floors and ceiling are one continuous polished marble piece. A large\nmahogany table fills the center of the room, mahogany chairs, with red velvet\ncushions are spaced comfortably around the table. A huge ruby is embedded in\nthe ceiling, a reddish light enfuses the room through this stone.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15198,0,0,0,'<r>A Tunnel of Red Stone<z>','  The walls of the tunnel have been artfully crafted, millions of sparkling\nred rubys are set in a most natural way. The warm glow of the rubys combined\nwith the rich luster of polished red marble floors exude wealth and comfort.\nThere is an imposing door set in the eastern wall.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15199,0,0,0,'<r>A Richly Garnished Office<z>','   This is a tidy office, decorated in extreme elegance and style. A large \ndesk of mahogany is centered on the rich red carpeting. Three detailed \npaintings, framed in mahogany, grace the walls. In the corners are statues \ncarved from red marble.\n',115,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15200,0,-42,-2,'A Vaulted Chamber','  You are in a chamber carved from the stone with an exit opening southward\ninto the main section of the ruins.  A rusty iron ladder is bolted to the\nnorth wall leading to a wooden trapdoor in the ceiling.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(15201,0,-42,-1,'A Stone Hallway','  A fairly large stone hallway stretches east to west.  You see the faint\noutline of a trapdoor where the north wall meets the floor.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,75,0,'',NULL),
(15202,-1,-42,-1,'A Large Stone Chamber','  You have entered some kind of large stone chamber.  The ceiling here is at\nleast twenty feet tall, and large doorways have been cut into the east, south,\nand west walls.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(15203,1,-42,-1,'A Bend in the Hallway','  The fairly large stone hallway takes a bend here.  A short passage travels\nnorth, and a longer hallway stretches to the west.  You smell a mildly awful\nstench wafting in from the north.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,75,0,'',NULL),
(15204,1,-41,-1,'Before a Large Gate','  This section of the stone hallway is in bad shape.  Bits of debris lie\nscattered here and there creating small piles in places.  Slime molds of\nvarious colors grow along the floor and walls.  A smaller passageway extends\nto the west, and a large rusty iron gate has been built to limit entry to a\nlarger passage to the north.  A strong stench of rotten garbage attacks your\nsenses through the gate making you gag.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,70,0,'',NULL),
(15205,0,-41,-1,'A Dead End','  This smaller stone passage dead ends to the west where it looks like\nconstruction has been halted in any attempt to expand in that direction.\nChunks of stone chipped from the walls dot the floor along with small\npiles of organic refuse.  You occasionally hear a tiny rustle or a squeak\nas you attempt to survey your surroundings.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,65,0,'',NULL),
(15206,1,-40,-1,'A Rotting Garbage Dump','  Mounds of stinking garbage fill this section making progress further north\nimpossible.  The steaming dripping stink seems to cling to your skin and\ngear.  The sheer amount of refuse filling the place and the depth of the\ndecay suggest that this place must have been used as a dump for half a\ncentury or more.  Small cave dwelling insects and maggots crawl through the\nmounds adding to the rate of decomposition.  There is a small crack in the\nstone floor with dim light coming up through it.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15207,-2,-42,-1,'A Stone Hallway','  A fairly large stone hallway stretches east and west.  You notice from the\namount of unmolested dust and dirt on the ground that this passage is not\noften used.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,75,0,'',NULL),
(15208,-3,-42,-1,'A Rubble Filled Hall','  A fairly large stone hallway stretches east and northwest.  The area is hard\nto travel in due to variously sized pieces of rock laying on the ground.  You\nhope your light holds out, as this would be a great place to turn an ankle.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(15209,-1,-43,-1,'A Stone Hallway','  A fairly large stone hallway stretches north and south.  This passage is\nrelatively clean and the stone has been rubbed smooth, seemingly from recent\nand high volume of traffic.  Stone archways carved into the sides lead east\nand west.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,75,0,'',NULL),
(15210,-2,-43,-1,'A Pantathian Lair','  This rather smallish cavern seems to serve as living quarters for a number of\nthe lizard\'s families.  Straw mats are strewn in the corners with small useless\npieces of pottery you suppose are used for meals.  The place smells well lived\nin, in fact it reeks like a filthy animal cage.  You doubt the inhabitants here\nwould care much for your snooping around in their home.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,65,0,'',NULL),
(15211,-1,-44,-1,'A Stone Hallway','  A fairly large stone hallway stretches north and south.  This passage is\nrelatively clean and the stone has been rubbed smooth, seemingly from recent\nand high volume of traffic.  Stone archways carved into the sides lead east\nand west.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,75,0,'',NULL),
(15212,-2,-44,-1,'A Pantathian Lair','  This rather smallish cavern seems to serve as living quarters for a number of\nthe lizard\'s families.  Straw mats are strewn in the corners with small useless\npieces of pottery you suppose are used for meals.  The place smells well lived\nin, in fact it reeks like a filthy animal cage.  You doubt the inhabitants here\nwould care much for your snooping around in their home.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,65,0,'',NULL),
(15213,-1,-45,-1,'A Large Stone Chamber','  You have entered some kind of large stone chamber.  The ceiling here is at\nleast twenty feet tall, and large doorways have been cut into the south\nand west walls.  A long hallway extends through a stone arch to the north,\nand a thick rusty door has been set in the east wall.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(15214,-2,-45,-1,'A Stone Hallway','  A fairly large stone hallway stretches east and north-west.  This passage is\nrelatively clean and the stone has been rubbed smooth, seemingly from recent\nand high volume of traffic.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,75,0,'',NULL),
(15215,-1,-46,-1,'A Storage Room','  From the looks of the contents herein, you surmise that this room is used\nby the Pantathians for storage.  Piles of scrap rusty metal, wood, and\nother useless debris litter the area in unorganized mounds.  You can\'t\nimagine what use any of this stuff might have, but figure they must dump\nhere the junk that at least doesn\'t stink or decompose.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,65,0,'',NULL),
(15217,-3,-44,-1,'A Stone Hallway','  A fairly large stone hallway stretches north and south-east.  This passage\nis relatively clean and the stone has been rubbed smooth, seemingly from\nrecent and high volume of traffic.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,75,0,'',NULL),
(15218,-3,-43,-1,'A Stone Hallway','  A fairly large stone hallway stretches south.  A stone archway has been dug\nthrough the stone to the west leading into a fairly large chamber beyond.\nThere are pieces of eggshell laying on the ground here seemingly tracked onto\nthe stone floor from the west.  There is also a thin layer of dirt covering\nparts of the stone mixed in with the fragments of shell.  This is the first\ntime you\'ve seen dirt on the bare stone since entering the ruins.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15219,-4,-43,-1,'A Pantathian Hatchery','  This rather large room has been filled with dirt matching that outside the\nentrance to the lizard ruins.  Small mounds of dirt lie as if something has\nbeen buried in them.  Straw and bits of strange fungus cover the mounds keeping\nthem warmed by their decay.  Paths of packed down dirt cross back and forth in\nrows edging up to the mounds.\n',109,131080,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,70,0,'',NULL),
(15220,-5,-43,-1,'A Pantathian Hatchery','  This rather large room has been filled with dirt matching that outside the\nentrance to the lizard ruins.  Small mounds of dirt lie as if something has\nbeen buried in them.  Straw and bits of strange fungus cover the mounds keeping\nthem warmed by their decay.  Paths of packed down dirt cross back and forth in\nrows edging up to the mounds.\n',109,131080,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15221,-4,-44,-1,'A Pantathian Hatchery','  This rather large room has been filled with dirt matching that outside the\nentrance to the lizard ruins.  Small mounds of dirt lie as if something has\nbeen buried in them.  Straw and bits of strange fungus cover the mounds keeping\nthem warmed by their decay.  Paths of packed down dirt cross back and forth in\nrows edging up to the mounds.\n',109,131080,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,70,0,'',NULL),
(15222,-5,-44,-1,'A Pantathian Hatchery','  This rather large room has been filled with dirt matching that outside the\nentrance to the lizard ruins.  Small mounds of dirt lie as if something has\nbeen buried in them.  Straw and bits of strange fungus cover the mounds keeping\nthem warmed by their decay.  Paths of packed down dirt cross back and forth in\nrows edging up to the mounds.\n',109,131080,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,70,0,'',NULL),
(15223,-4,-41,-1,'A Rubble-Filled Dead End','  This section of hallway is filled with large pieces of rock and debris.\nThe hall continues on to the south-east where the fallen rocks are more\nsparse.  The only other exit visible in the room looks like it used to\ncontinue westward but has now caved in making progress impossible.\nFrom the looks of the walls and ceiling surrounding the cave-in, you\'d\nguess it was brought down on purpose.  Marks from what looks like some kind\nof pick-axe are left where chunks of the ceiling have fallen in.  You notice\na tiny \'gap\' between two very large boulders in the rubble blocking any\nprogress further west.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(15224,-5,-41,-1,'An Isolated Chamber','  You see here a stand alone chamber blocked off from the main area by a\nmajor cave-in.  Large fallen stone boulders have cut off all escape.  From the\nlooks of the large pick marks on the ceiling, it almost appears that this\nchamber was purposefully buried for some reason.  Thick layers of unmolested\ndust covers the rubble strewn floor.  Apparently, no living creature has\nstepped foot here for centuries.  Very dim light comes through a small gap\nbetween two very large boulders that help to block any progress east through\nthe cave-in.  A rusted iron grate lies embedded in the floor.\n',109,139272,56,0,0,0,0,0,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(15225,-5,-41,-2,'A Smooth Vertical Tunnel','  This passageway is more like a vertical chute than a tunnel.  The walls here\nare of smooth stone with no visible hand holds and look impossible to climb.\nIf you are here, you are flying..  hopefully not down at a high rate of speed.\nA rusted iron grate is embedded in the ceiling of stone above your head.\n',109,139272,57,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15226,-5,-41,-3,'A Small Natural Tunnel','  You are in a small tunnel that seems to have been formed naturally in the\nstone.  Stalagmites from mineral deposits rise from the floor to meet their\nbrothers reaching down from above.  This cavern is fairly small in size\nmaking you almost have to crawl to get through.  The presence of the\nstalagmites make the quarters even more cramped.\n',109,139272,56,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(15227,-4,-42,-3,'A Small Natural Tunnel','  You are in a small tunnel that seems to have been formed naturally in the\nstone.  Stalagmites from mineral deposits rise from the floor to meet their\nbrothers reaching down from above.  This cavern is fairly small in size\nmaking you almost have to crawl to get through.  The presence of the\nstalagmites make the quarters even more cramped.\n',109,139272,56,0,0,0,0,0,4,65,0,'',NULL),
(15236,0,-43,-1,'A Pantathian Lair','  This rather smallish cavern seems to serve as living quarters for a number of\nthe lizard\'s families.  Straw mats are strewn in the corners with small useless\npieces of pottery you suppose are used for meals.  The place smells well lived\nin, in fact it reeks like a filthy animal cage.  You doubt the inhabitants here\nwould care much for your snooping around in their home.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,65,0,'',NULL),
(15237,0,-44,-1,'A Pantathian Lair','  This rather smallish cavern seems to serve as living quarters for a number of\nthe lizard\'s families.  Straw mats are strewn in the corners with small useless\npieces of pottery you suppose are used for meals.  The place smells well lived\nin, in fact it reeks like a filthy animal cage.  You doubt the inhabitants here\nwould care much for your snooping around in their home.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,65,0,'',NULL),
(15238,0,-45,-1,'A Small Primitive Lab','  You have entered some kind of large stone chamber that seems to serve as\nsome kind of primitive laboratory.  Dark stains of dried blood spatter\nthe floor and walls.  Various implements lie equally stained here and there\nresting where you imagine they were last used and discarded.  The place isn\'t\nvery organized making you wonder how any work here is actually accomplished.\nA thick rusty door has been set in the west wall, and an archway has been\ncut in the east leading out.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,10,70,0,'',NULL),
(15239,1,-45,-1,'A Short Stone Hallway','  This is a short stone hallway leading from a stone archway to the west\nto doorway cut into the stone to the north.  In the doorway is hung an\nextremely dirty ragged curtain fashioned of heavy animal skins.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,20,70,0,'',NULL),
(15240,1,-44,-1,'A Large Stone Lair','  This seems to be the lair of a relatively important person within the lizard\nrealm.  A rugged attempt at decorating is evident with pieces of engraved\nmetal fastened to the walls as well as painted designs on the floor.\nThe area is fairly large and the ceiling has been carved to a height of\nabout fifteen feet -- rather vaulted for what you\'ve seen of Pantathian\nliving quarters.  In a doorway to the south is hung an extremely dirty ragged\ncurtain of heavy animal skins.\n',109,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,20,180,0,'',NULL),
(15242,-4,-43,-2,'In a Hole','  You are in a dirt hole, now devoid of all dirt.\n',109,131080,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,35,0,'',NULL),
(15243,-5,-43,-2,'In a Hole','You are in a dirt hole, now devoid of all dirt.\n',109,131080,54,0,0,0,0,0,1,35,0,'',NULL),
(15244,-4,-44,-2,'In a Hole','You are in a dirt hole, now devoid of all dirt.\n',109,131080,54,0,0,0,0,0,1,35,0,'',NULL),
(15245,-5,-44,-2,'In a Hole','You are in a dirt hole, now devoid of all dirt.\n',109,131080,54,0,0,0,0,0,1,35,0,'',NULL),
(15250,-6,20,-1,'Forest Trail Leading Up a Small Mountain','There is thick brush here and a few small trees next to the fence to the\nsouth.  The dirt path is strewn with pebbles and weeds.  Past the fence to\nthe south you can barely see the walls of Grimhaven.  The east and west are\nflanked by the mighty trees of the Haon-Dor forest, and the path continues\nnorth, sloping upwards.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15251,-6,21,-1,'Forest Trail Leading Up a Small Mountain','Whoever made this path needed to turn it slightly so as to move around a\ndense stand of trees.  The ground is littered with pebbles and weeds.  You\ncan see a fence to the south, but trees surround every other side.  The path\nslopes up to the northwest and down to the south.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15252,-7,22,-1,'Forest Trail Leading Up a Small Mountain','The trees of the Haon-Dor forest surround you, and little light is able to\nstream through the high leaves and dense branches.  The pebble strewn path\nleads up to the north and down to the southeast with a gentle slope.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15253,-7,23,-1,'Forest Trail Leading Up a Small Mountain','There is a break in the forest leading to a clearing west of you, and the\npebble strewn path leads gently up to the north or down to the south.  The\ntrees of the Haon-Dor block movement east.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15254,-7,24,-1,'Forest Trail Leading Up a Small Mountain','The trees of the Haon-Dor forest block movement east or west.  The pebble\nand weed strewn path leads up the gently sloping mountain to the northwest,\nor down to the south.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15255,-8,25,-1,'Forest Trail Leading Up a Small Mountain','The Haon-Dor forest prevents passage north or south, but a small dirt trail\nleads down the gentle slope to the southeast, or to the west.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15256,-9,25,-1,'Forest Trail Leading Up a Small Mountain','There is forest surrounding the entire western and southern sides of the\npebble strewn trail, which leads up the mountain to the north or to the\neast.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15257,-8,25,-2,'Forest Trail Leading Up a Small Mountain','The dense Haon-Dor lies to your east while the pebble strewn path leads up\nthe mountain to the northeast or down to the south.  To the west you can\nhear water flowing through the manzanita bushes.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(15258,-7,26,-2,'Forest Trail Leading Up a Small Mountain','The trees flanking you to the east and west are thinner here.  The dirt\npath leads southwest or north into a large clearing.  Beyond the clearing\nto the north you can see the peak of the mountain, and a small waterfall\nflowing down the side of it.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15259,-8,29,-2,'Corner of a Camp by a River','Across the swift river to the west is a higher bank that you could not climb\nup to from the level of the water.  There seems to be a break in the trees\nthere and you think you might see motion among the oak and pine there.  To\nthe southeast is a cookfire used to cook meats, which are cut from game.  The\nanimals are gutted and skinned on wooden racks that you see to the east.\nSouth of you the clearing continues along the riverbank.  South and east of\nyou there is a break in the treeline which must lead to a path down the\nhillside.  To the north past the trees you see the origin of the river: a\nwaterfall on the mountainside caused by pooled rainwater.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15260,-7,29,-2,'A Small Camp on the Mountainside','This seems to be the part of the camp where freshly killed animals are hung\nand their skins dried.  To the south you see the center of the camp where\na cooking grill is placed for all the campers to eat.  To the east the\nclearing stretches a bit further and then is stopped by a wall of trees.  To\nthe west you can see a river cutting off the clearing.  The source of the\nriver is a waterfall further up the mountainside.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15261,-6,29,-2,'Northeast Corner of a Small Camp on the Mountainside','This is where newly slaughtered animals are gutted and skinned.  To the west\nthere is more area to undertake this task.  Southwest of you is the center\nof the camp, where a cookfire is used to grill meats for the ragtag crew of\ncampers in the clearing.  To the north and east is forest.  Far to the north\nbeyond the trees you can see the peak of the forest and you can barely view\na waterfall that must run down the mountainside to the west of here.  South\nand west you see a break in the forestline where a path must lead down the\nhill.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15262,-5,29,-2,'On the Edge of a Small Camp on the Mountainside','The dirt ground of the clearing is covered with moss and larger stones here,\nand some of the biggest rocks seem to be used as makeshift chairs.  The whole\narea must be an impromptu meeting place, perhaps to stay out of the sun\nduring hot summer days.  To the west you can see some racks used to hang\nnewly killed game.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15263,-8,28,-2,'A Camp by a River','The west side of the swift river is bounded by a high bank and dense foliage.\nA waterfall further up the mountain, beyond the trees bordering the clearing,\nis the source of the rapids.  East of you is the center of the camp, where\na grill is used to cook meats to feed the worn campers.  To the northeast\nyou see racks used to hang freshly slaughtered game, where it may be gutted\nand skinned.  The clearing leads south as well, and you see a break in the\ntreeline as you follow it east.  The break must lead to a path leading down\nthe hillside.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15264,-7,28,-2,'Center of a Small Camp on the Mountainside','To the north and northeast you see freshly slaughtered animals hanging from\nwooden racks.  The meat is obviously cooked here in the center of the camp\nto feed the tattered inhabitants of the clearing.  To the east, at the edge\nof the camp nearby, is the Haon-Dor forest.  The west side of the camp is\nbordered by a swift river that originates from a waterfall further northwest\nup the mountainside.  To the south you see a path cut into the forest that\nleads downhill.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15265,-6,28,-2,'A Small Camp on the Mountainside','Tall trees line the east, but there is a way northeast to a more shaded part\nof the clearing.  To the north you see some racks used to hold carcasses\nwhile they are gutted and skinned after being caught.  To the west is a\ncookfire where meats are grilled for the pathetic looking campers.  Further\nwest you can barely see a river, which flows from a waterfall that is\nsituated further up the mountainside.  To the southeast you see a break in\nthe treeline where a path must lead down the hill.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15266,-8,27,-2,'Corner of a Camp by a River','A swift river flows to the west that originates further up the mountain at\na waterfall beyond the trees to the north.  A cookfire is used to grill meats\nin the center of the camp to the northeast.  There is a break in the treeline\nto the east that permits a dirt path to travel through the forest down the\nhillside to the south.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15267,-7,27,-2,'Entrance to a Small Camp on the Mountainside','There is a clearing in the forest here approximately thirty by forty feet.\nIt serves as a camp for some bedraggled looking people.  To the north you\nsee some wooden racks holding freshly slaughtered animals, and a fire in the\ncenter of the camp with a cooking grill over it.  The clearing stretches\neast and then ends at the forest line.  To the west the clearing is bounded\nby a swift river flowing down the mountainside, and you see its origin to\nthe north and slightly west: a waterfall caused by pooled rainwaters.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15268,-6,27,-2,'Southeast Corner of a Small Camp on the Mountainside','The dense oak and pine of the Haon-Dor forest lie east and south, blocking\nyour movement.  A short way north you see some wooden racks holding some\nslaughtered game corpses, which appear to be cooked on a grill to the\nnortheast in the center of the camp.  Far to the west you see that the\nclearing is confined by a swift river that originates further up the\nmountain at a waterfall.  There is a break in the treeline to the west that\nprobably leads to a path down the hillside.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15269,-9,24,-1,'Northwest Corner of a Clearing in a Forest','The oak and pine trees of the Haon-Dor prevent movement north, while thick\nbrush stymies passage west, from whence you hear the rush of a river.  A\nshort way to the south you can see a rickety wooden tower that barely rises\nabove the treetops.  To the southeast you see a break in the trees that leads\nto a path which wanders north up the mountain or south down it.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15270,-8,24,-1,'Northeast Corner of a Clearing in a Forest','Tall pines and thick branching oaks prevent passage north or east.  The\nclearing leads west and south, and distantly to the southwest you see a tall\nwooden tower that barely rises above the treeline.  To the south you can\nsee a break in the treeline that seems to lead to a trail up and down the\nmountainside.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15271,-9,23,-1,'A Clearing in a Forest','To the east you see a break in the treeline that allows passage to a trail\nleading up the mountain north or down to the south.  South of you is a tall,\nrickety tower.  You hear the roar of a river running to the west, through the\nbrush and trees.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15272,-8,23,-1,'Clearing in a Forest by a Trail','A dirt trail lies to the east, which leads up or down the mountainside.  The\nclearing stretches north, south and west, and the only structure of note is\na rickety looking tower to the southwest, which rises above the oaks and even\nthe tall pine bordering the clearing.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15273,-9,22,-1,'Southwest Corner of a Clearing in a Forest','Your passage south is blocked by the dense oak and pine trees of the Haon-Dor\nforest, and thick brush prevents you from going west, from whence you hear\nthe rush of a river.  To the northeast you see a break in the trees leading\nto a path up and down the mountainside.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15274,-8,22,-1,'Southeast Corner of a Clearing in a Forest','Passage east and south is prevented by dense oaks and pines.  The clearing\nstretches north, and to the west you see a tall wooden tower that reaches\neven above the trees.  The treeline is broken to the north where you would\nbe able to exit the clearing and follow an adjoining trail up or down the\nmountainside.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15275,-11,31,-1,'Clearing in a Dense Forest','The foliage here is extremely thick and you can\'t pass any further.  Through\nthe brush east you can see a swift river; a steep dirt bank leads down to it,\nalthough it\'s impossible to get to from here due to the trees blocking it.\nThe only direction you can pass is to the south.\n',89,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15276,-12,30,-1,'Corner of a Clearing in a Dense Forest','There is barely enough room to move around here; dense foliage still blocks\nthe small clearing.  The forest is too thick to move in any direction but\neast, from whence you can faintly hear a river.\n',89,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15277,-11,30,-1,'A Clearing West of a River','There is a river down a steep bank to the east, mostly blocked by tall trees.\nYou can see a large clearing on the other side of the river, lower than this\nside.  The foliage has been cleared enough for passage north, west or south.\nYou can make out a blue tent to the west, but it is so covered by vines and\nbushes that you need to be close to view it.  One of the trees on the eastern\nbank is tied to a complex looking wheel apparatus, and is roped near the top.\n',89,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,5,'',NULL),
(15278,-11,29,-1,'A Clearing in a Dense Forest','You can barely make your way through the foliage here; hardly enough of it\nhas been removed to allow movement.  Trees west and south prevent you from\ngoing further in those directions, while brush and a steep bank down to a\nriver is east.  You could forge your way north.  There is a tangled mess of\nivy between two trees to the south.\n',89,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15279,-12,28,-1,'A Small Forest Clearing','This is the northwest corner of a small clearing.  There is animal blood on\nthe ground, and this seems to be a secret hideaway to store poached game.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15280,-11,28,-1,'A Small Forest Clearing','This appears to be where slaughtered animals are stored, and perhaps hid from\nsomebody.  There is a tangled mess of ivy between two oaks to the north.\n',89,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15281,-12,27,-1,'A Small Forest Clearing','The forest is cleared out here and seems to be where poachers are hiding\nslaughtered game.  Southeast you can see a river flowing through the woods.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15282,-10,26,-2,'A Small Forest Clearing by a River','There is blood smeared on the dirt ground here.  The clearing seems to be\nused to hide game killed by poachers.  To the south is a swift flowing river.\n',89,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15283,-9,22,0,'Top of a Rickety Spytower','Your vantage above the treetops allows you to see the north gates of\nGrimhaven to the south.  Through a window east you can see the vast expanse\nof the Haon-Dor, north you can make out the arena, and to the west you see\na river directly beside the oak and pines.  The river originates further up\nthe mountainside at a waterfall and flows downhill to the west side of\nGrimhaven.\n',89,131080,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15284,0,0,0,'Inside a Small Tent','The tent is dark, with no windows.  It is made of a tough blue cloth, and\ndirt covered in pine needles serves as a floor.  You can hear a river very\nfaintly to the east.\n',89,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(15285,-7,32,-2,'A Small Waterfall on a Mountainside','You are at the base of the waterfall, which forms a river running south down\nthe mountainside.  Directly south the water has formed a small beach in the\nforest, while the main river runs southwest.  The top of the waterfall is\nframed by moss and brightly colored small flowers.  You see no way to get\nup to the level of the pool that must lie above.\n',89,131072,29,0,0,0,44,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15286,-7,31,-2,'A Dirt Shoreline in the Haon-Dor','To the north you can hear the sound of water rushing, while all other\ndirections are blocked by thick oak and pine trees.  The ground is wet and\ncovered by soft pine needles and emerald moss.  It seems like a nice place\nto rest.\n',89,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15287,-8,31,-2,'On a Swift Flowing River','You can hear the rushing sound of a waterfall from the northeast, where the\nriver evidently flows from.  Trees line both sides of the river, which leads\nsouthwest down the mountainside.\n',89,131072,29,0,0,0,44,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15288,-9,30,-2,'On a Swift Flowing River','The river bends south here, due to some larger rocks on the western bank.  You\nare prevented passage anywhere but the river by dense oak and pine trees.\nFrom the northeast you hear the faint sound of a waterfall further up the\nmountainside.\n',89,131072,29,0,0,0,44,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15289,-9,29,-2,'On a Swift Flowing River','You are able to forge your way to a shore east, which seems to be on the\nedge of a forest clearing.  The western bank is steep and the foliage too\ndense to make way in that direction.  The river runs from the north downhill\nto the south through the dense trees.\n',89,131072,29,0,0,0,44,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15290,-9,28,-2,'On a Swift Flowing River','You are able to forge your way to a shore east, which seems to be on the\nedge of a forest clearing.  The western bank is steep and the foliage too\ndense to make way in that direction.  The river runs from the north downhill\nto the south through the dense trees.\n',89,131072,29,0,0,0,44,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15291,-9,27,-2,'On a Swift Flowing River','You are able to forge your way to a shore east, which seems to be on the\nedge of a forest clearing.  The western bank is steep and the foliage too\ndense to make way in that direction.  The river runs from the north downhill\nto the south through the dense trees.\n',89,131072,29,0,0,0,44,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15292,-9,26,-2,'On a Swift Flowing River','The east and west banks are thick with oak and pine trees and other brush,\npreventing passage.  The river flows swiftly from north to south, downhill.\n',89,131072,29,0,0,0,44,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15293,-9,25,-2,'A Bend on a Swift Flowing River','As the river bends, it also widens, which causes the current to flow less\nvigorously.  The east bank is studded with oaks, pines, and a thick manzanita\nbush.\n',89,131072,29,0,0,0,0,3,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(15294,-10,25,-2,'A Bend on a Swift Flowing River','As the river bends, it also widens, which causes the current to flow less\nvigorously.  There is an opening in the forest to the north.  The river flows\nfrom the east and turns south here.\n',89,131072,29,0,0,0,44,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15295,-10,24,-2,'A Bend on a Swift Flowing River','As the river bends, it also widens, which causes the current to flow less\nvigorously.  The river flows from the north and turns east here.\n',89,131072,29,0,0,0,44,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15296,-9,24,-2,'A Bend on a Swift Flowing River','As the river bends, it also widens, which causes the current to flow less\nvigorously.  The eastern side has dense forest and you cannot find a way\nthrough the foliage.  The river flows from the west and runs south, down the\nmountainside.\n',89,131072,29,0,0,0,44,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15297,-9,23,-2,'On a Swift Flowing River','The east and west banks are thick with oak and pine trees and other brush,\npreventing passage.  The river flows swiftly from north to south, downhill.\n',89,131072,29,0,0,0,44,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15298,-9,22,-2,'On a Swift Flowing River','The east and west banks are thick with oak and pine trees and other brush,\npreventing passage.  The river flows swiftly from north to south, downhill.\n',89,131072,29,0,0,0,44,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15299,-9,21,-2,'On a Swift Flowing River','The east and west banks are thick with oak and pine trees and other brush,\npreventing passage.  The river flows swiftly from north to south, downhill--\n',89,131072,29,0,0,0,44,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15300,0,0,0,'<o>Sewage<1>','<k>  There is nothing here but <o>excrement<k> and <y>urine<k>.  You can\'t breathe,\nyou can\'t see, you can do nothing but gag and choke.\n',96,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,1000,0,'',NULL),
(15301,-49,4,0,'Dirt Road','  This simple road runs south into what appears to be a small village.  A\nlarge two story building is to the southeast and a small stable is just\nsouth and west.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15302,-50,3,0,'Stable','  The ground here is <o>muddy<1> and trampled, with <y>clumps of hay<1> strewn\nabout.  This is where visitors tie down their mounts.  It looks like\nit could be a bit cramped, but it\'s warm and dry.  A storage area for\ngear is off to the south and the town\'s saloon is across the road.\n',96,131080,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15303,-49,3,0,'Dirt Road','  A small stable opens up to the west and the side of a big building\nblocks the way to the east.  The road continues to the south and north.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15304,-47,3,0,'<o>The Saloon\'s Bar<1>','<k>  An alcohol laden bar is on the northern wall, stocked with many fine\n(and some not so fine) liquid refreshments.  The look of things here gives\na pretty good handle on what the most common local hobby is.\n',96,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15305,-46,3,0,'<o>Saloon<1>','<k>  This corner of the saloon is particularly dark and smoky, the walls\nare barely visible much less any distinguishing features.  A vague light\noff to the southwest may or may not be the saloon entrance.  It smells of\nstale beer and tobacco smoke.\n',96,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15306,-50,2,0,'Storage Area','  This small area is where visitors secure their gear for the duration.\nThere are crude wooden shelves built into the west and south walls.  No\nlocks are required here; the locals generally do not steal from each other\nand those that do meet swift (and usually violent) justice.  A stable is to\nthe north and you can see the ever popular saloon just across the road to\nthe east.\n',96,131080,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15307,-49,2,0,'Dirt Road','  A storage area extension of the stable is to the west and the side\nof a big building blocks the way to the east.  The road begins to open\nup to the south, which appears to be the center of this little village.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15308,-47,2,0,'<o>Saloon<1>','<o>  The ceiling here is quite low and the wooden floor is not level; it\nbecomes apparent that this building is not of top quality construction.  It\nis rather dark and smoky making the room look larger than it is.  A\nstaircase is on the east side of the room and the bar is to the north.\n',96,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15309,-46,2,0,'<o>Saloon Stairs<1>','<o>  These stairs lead up to the rooms, where undoubtedly some behind\nclosed doors reveling takes place.  Egress may be found to the west and a\nbar is to the northwest for those so inclined.<1>\n',96,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15310,-45,2,0,'Outhouse','<o>  This room obviously gets a lot of use.  The air is warm and stuffy\nand it smells extremely foul in here.  There are some crude carvings\non the wall.<1>\n',96,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(15311,-49,1,0,'Dirt Road','  Some low steps lead up to the front porch of a saloon to the east.\nThe road splits into a T to the south.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15312,-48,1,0,'Saloon Entrance','  Before you lies the local source of entertainment, a beat up old saloon\nthat attracts ranchers and and cattlehands from the surrounding prairie.\nTwo wide swinging doors lead into the saloon directly to the northeast and\nthe porch extends to the east.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15313,-47,1,0,'Saloon Porch','  A large overhang makes <k>shade<1> for this part of the saloon\'s porch.\nThis looks like a good place to just sit back and watch the local traffic\ngo by.  A wooden rail blocks passage to the south and east.  The porch\ncontinues to the west.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15314,-46,1,0,'Bushes','<g>  It seems that this area serves as an alternate to the outhouse in times\nof need.  It doesn\'t smell too great.  There\'s a few broken bottles and\nother trash lying about.\n',96,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15315,-45,1,0,'Dirt Path','  This small path leads to an outhouse to the north.  There is a slight\nopening in the bushes to the west.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15316,-52,0,0,'Dirt Road','  The cobblestone road from the west meets hard packed earth here.\nThe dirt road leads off to the east, where some buildings can be seen\nthrough the trees.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15317,-51,0,0,'Dirt Road','  A door leading into a modest sized building lies to the south.  A\nhand-painted wooden sign is hung on the door, reading \'Sheriff\'.  The\nroad continues to both the east and the west.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15318,-50,0,0,'Dirt Road','  Thick undergrowth blocks the way to the north and a wooden building\nis to the south.  The road continues to the west and opens up to the\neast.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15319,-49,0,0,'Village Square','  This is the center of a small village.  A large saloon is to the\nnortheast, up some low stairs.  A general store is to the south and the\nroad continues to the north, west and east.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15320,-48,0,0,'Dirt Road','  Low wooden steps lead up to a saloon to the north.  The road opens\nup to the west and narrows to the east.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15321,-47,0,0,'Dirt Road','  A wooden rail blocks access to the saloon\'s porch to the north.  The\nroad narrows to the east.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15322,-46,0,0,'Dirt Road','  The edge of this small village is off to the east, while the center\nof town is to the west.  A large saloon is to the north.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15323,-45,0,0,'Dirt Road','  The road ends here, but a small dirt path leads to a small building\nto the north.  You can see mountains off in the distance to the east.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15324,-51,5,0,'Dirt Road','  The cobblestone from the west dwindles off to hard packed earth.\nThe forest seems to thin to the southeast and some buildings can seen\nin that direction.  The main road is to the west and the dirt road\nleads off to the east.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15325,-51,-1,0,'Sheriff\'s Office','  From the look of things the Sheriff probably spends more time in the\nsaloon or on the range than he does here.  A foot locker sits in the corner\nwhere weapons and other dangerous objects are stored while their owners\ntake some time out in the cell, to the east.\n',96,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15326,-50,-1,0,'Dirty Prison Cell','<k>  The floor is hard packed dirt.  There is a smell of <g>mold<k>, <y>urine<k> and\n<g>v<y>o<g>m<y>i<g>t<k> pervading the area.  It doesn\'t look like a nice place to spend\nthe night, but most people who end up here aren\'t in the condition to\nnotice.  The cell continues to the south.\n',96,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15327,-50,5,0,'Dirt Road','  There appears to be a small village to the south and southeast.\nThick forest and undergrowth block passage to the north.  The road\ncontinues to the southeast.\n',96,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15328,-49,-1,0,'General Store','  Saddles, rope, hard tack and other items of use to ranchers are\ndisplayed here.  Sparse on luxury and heavy on utility, this store\nmakes a tidy profit providing needed items locally that would normally\nbe gotten from Brightmoon, a long ride to the south.  The shop\'s\nproprietor is no where to be seen.\n',96,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15329,0,0,0,'<o>Under an Outhouse<1>','<k>  This hole is about half full of <o>excrement<k> and <y>urine<1><k>.  The stench is\nastoundingly awful.  A small hole above thankfully leads back out.\n',96,131080,28,300,15329,0,0,5,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15330,-50,-2,0,'Dirty Prison Cell','<k>  It reeks of the stench of <y>urine<k>.  Dark stains on the wall indicate\nthat this is where the cell\'s inhabitants relieve themselves if they can\'t\nwait until morning, which appears to be quite often.\n<1>',96,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15333,-46,4,1,'<o>Dirty Bedroom<1>','<k>  This room seems to be a bit of a mess.  An <o>old pair of boots<k> lie\ndiscarded in a corner, empty and broken bottles are scattered about\nrandomly and it smells of <o>booze<k> and <g>v<y>o<g>m<y>i<g>t<k>.\n',96,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15334,-47,3,1,'<o>Bedroom<1>','  There is some hiking gear piled into a corner.  The room seems to be\nfairly tidy and clean.  It is probably being rented by a traveler or\nadventurer heading northwards to <g>Mordant\'s Deep<1>.\n',96,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15335,-46,3,1,'<o>Upstairs Hallway<1>','<o>  The hallway ends here.  \'<w>Room 101<o>\' is written on the sign above the\ndoor to the west and \'<w>Room 102<o>\' is to the north.  Stairs leading down\nare to the south.\n',96,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15336,-47,2,1,'<o>Plain Bedroom<1>','  This windowless room is very small and sparse, containing only the\nnecessities.\n',96,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15337,-46,2,1,'<o>Saloon Upstairs<1>','<o>  Stairs lead back down into the main room of the saloon.  The air is\na bit more clear here, but smoke wafts up from below and dissipates in\nthis area.  A door is to the west, with a small hand-written sign above it,\nproclaiming \'<w>Room 100<o>\'.  A hallway leads to the north.\n',96,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15338,-47,3,-1,'Cellar','  A particularly large spider web occupies the northwest corner here.\nWhat sort of spider could make a web that large?\n',96,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15339,-46,3,-1,'Cellar','  Maybe long ago this was a wine cellar.  It\'s hard to tell now, with\neverything covered in <o>dust<k> or <g>mold<k>.\n',96,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15340,-47,2,-1,'Cellar','<k>  A large <b>puddle of water<k> has gathered in this corner, it is at least\nankle deep.  A few pinpoints of <w>light<k> shine through the floor boards\nabove.\n',96,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15341,-46,2,-1,'Cellar','  A large vertical beam is here, supporting the saloon, above.  It\'s\ndark and creepy down here.  Darkness is all around, but there is a\nwall to the east and a thin shaft of <w>light<k> to the south.\n',96,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15342,-46,1,-1,'Cellar Stairs','  The cellar is dank, musty and dark.  There is <g>mold<k> growing on the\nstone walls, <b>puddles of water<k> on the <o>dirt floor<k> and cobwebs in the\ncorners.  Stairs lead upward and the darkness extends to the north.\n',96,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15343,-17,21,-3,'Portal Room','  Many portals are here to serve as egress from Peel\'s Office.\n',1,139273,60,0,0,0,0,0,25,120,0,'',NULL),
(15344,0,0,0,'<o>Inside the <1><w>Grimhaven<1><o>-<1><W>Brightmoon<1><o> trolley<1>','<o>Comfortable benches are lined up here, providing rest for passengers.\nYou may step off the trolley to the north, when you have reached your\ndestination.\n',-1,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15345,6,-21,0,'A Fishing Shop','  This small hut is setup as a fishing shop, for those that wish to fish \nthe nearby Kranor river.  A large variety of rods, poles, lures and baits\nhang on the walls.\n',42,141320,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15346,8,-1,-1,'Grimhaven Portal Room','A round stone platform occupies most of the floor in this room.  This is\na magical focal point for allowing transportation via portals.\n',0,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(15347,0,0,0,'Brightmoon Portal Room','A round stone platform occupies most of the floor in this room.  This is\na magical focal point for allowing transportation via portals.\n',0,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(15348,73,-10,-1,'Logrus Portal Room','A round stone platform occupies most of the floor in this room.  This is\na magical focal point for allowing transportation via portals.\n',0,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(15349,0,0,0,'<o>Inside of Keirk\'s Fishing Boat<1>','  The deck of this boat is barren, leaving plenty of room for fishermen and\ntourists.  The rail to the north has several braces built into it to hold\nfishing poles.\n',2,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15350,3,-30,0,'<k>A Large Damp Cave Opening<Z>','<k>  The walls of this cave seem to have been carved out fairly recently.\nIt doesn\'t take a dwarf to tell the workmanship is poor and it looks\nas though it was done in a great deal of hurry.  Northwest of the cave\nmouth is a poor looking road, and the cave continues to the southeast.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15351,4,-31,0,'<k>A Rough Hewn Cave<Z>','<k>   Small rocks and chunks of dirt lie strewn about the floor and large\nroots dangle from the walls and ceiling.  Deep gouges and furrows line\nthe floor and walls at irregular intervals.  A good bit of light filters\nin here from the nearby cave mouth and the floor drops drastically as\nthe cave descends down.<z>\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(15352,4,-31,-2,'<k>A Dark Damp Cave<Z>','   This part of the cave is fairly humid and the ceiling is pretty low.  The\nrough hewn walls jut out at odd angles here and there, casting ominous\nshadows that make it hard to tell if there could be something lurking there.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,77,0,'',NULL),
(15353,5,-31,-2,'<k>A Dark Damp Cave<Z>','   This part of the cave is fairly humid and the ceiling is pretty low.  The\nrough hewn walls jut out at odd angles here and there, casting ominous\nshadows that make it hard to tell if there could be something lurking there.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(15354,6,-31,-2,'<k>A Dark Damp Cave<Z>','   This part of the cave is fairly humid and the ceiling is pretty low.  The\nrough hewn walls jut out at odd angles here and there, casting ominous\nshadows that make it hard to tell if there could be something lurking there.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,70,0,'',NULL),
(15355,9,-31,-2,'<k>A Dan<Z><g>k<k> St<Z><o>o<k>rag<Z><g>e<k> Ro<Z><g>o<k>m<Z>','   Several different varieties of <g>mold<Z> and <g>mildew<z> grow on remnants\nof <w>cloth sacks<Z> and <o>leather pouches<Z> stuffed into small carved out cubby\nholes.  Humanoid bodyparts varying in length and thickness also litter\nthe area.  Stains from dried <r>blood <Z>dot the floor and walls and bits of hair\nstill attached to skin are caked on a few of them.  The only way out of\nhere is through a door on the north wall was obviously destroyed quite\nsome time ago.<Z>\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,50,0,'',NULL),
(15356,5,-30,-2,'<k>A Dark Humid Cave<Z>','   Small stalactites and stalagmites break up the otherwise nondescript\nfloor and ceiling of the area.  Pockets of steam drift along the roof of\nthe cavern slowly dissipating, making the air very thick with moisture.\n',112,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,75,0,'',NULL),
(15357,6,-30,-2,'<k>An Oddly Shaped Junction<Z>','   Strange looking footprints span the length and width of the immediate\narea.  The cavern walls are noticeably smoother here, as if this part of\nthe cave was already existing.  A warm fiery glow is reflected off a few of\nthe walls\' outcroppings, seeming to come from the small cave west of\nhere.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(15358,7,-30,-2,'<k>An Oddly Shaped Junction<Z>','   Strange footprints and scratchmarks cover the floor and even the walls\nin some places.  Stringy roots covered with clumps of dirt dangle from the\nceiling and even the walls in some places.  The air here is not as laden\nwith moisture as the surrounding tunnels are, and you can see a faint\nglow from a large cavern a short distance away.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(15359,9,-30,-2,'<k>A Gr<Z><g>i<k>my K<o>i<k>tc<k>h<Z><g>e<k>n<Z>','   Steam severely obscures everything in here.  The floor is very slick\nwith a gray pasty liquid that smells of spoiled meat.  A few of the\nstalactites on the floor have been filed down to serve as tables.  There\nis a small storage area to the south and a large cavern north of here.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,90,0,'',NULL),
(15360,4,-29,-2,'<k>A <Z><r>Hot<k> Humid Cave<Z>','   Moisture covers everything from the walls and floor all the way to\nthe odd rock formations of the place.  Stalactites and stalagmites\nabound here.  Rivulets of water cascade down the uneven surface of the\ncavern walls and the floor, dotted with pointy mineral deposits, is coated\nin a thin layer of a <o>yellow-<w>white<Z> slime near the bubbling pools of water.\n',112,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15361,7,-29,-2,'<k>An Oddly Shaped Junction<Z>','   The well traveled floor of this cave section has been littered with\nsmall bits of leather and cloth.  The individual footprints become less\ndistinguishable and distinct paths become more prominent at this point.\nSmall symbols have been painted the walls, apparently with <r>blood<Z>.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(15362,8,-29,-2,'<k>The Southern End of a Large Cave<Z>','   This is a large open cavern with few distinguishing features.  The\nceiling is about twenty feet high and is covered with long pointy\nstalactites.  Along the wall where it meets the floor are several small\nholes dug into the earth.  Southwest and west of here there is a large\njunction of caves and the cavern extends off in a northerly direction.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(15363,9,-29,-2,'<k>Southern End of a Large Cave<Z>','  This is a large open cavern with few distinguishing features.  The\nceiling is about twenty feet up and is covered with long pointy stalactites.\nAlong the wall where it meets the floor are several small holes dug\ninto the earth.  South of here is what could pass for a kitchen and the\ncavern extends off in a northerly direction.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(15364,5,-28,-2,'<k>A <Z><r>Hot<k> Humid Cave<Z>','   Moisture covers everything from the walls and floor all the way to\nthe odd rock formations of the place.  Stalactites and stalagmites\nabound here.  Rivulets of water cascade down the uneven surface of the\ncavern walls and the floor, dotted with pointy mineral deposits, is coated\nin a thin layer of a <o>yellow-<w>white<Z> slime near the bubbling pools of water.\n',112,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15365,6,-28,-2,'<k>A Dark Humid Cave<Z>','   Small stalactites and stalagmites break up the otherwise nondescript\nfloor and ceiling of the area.  Pockets of steam drift along the roof of\nthe cavern slowly dissipating, making the air very thick with moisture.\n',112,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15366,8,-28,-2,'<k>A Large Cavern<Z>','  This is a large open cavern with few distinguishing features.  The\nceiling is about twenty feet high and is covered with long pointy\nstalactites.  Along the wall where it meets the floor are several small\nholes dug into the earth.  The large cavern extends north and south from\nhere.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(15367,9,-28,-2,'<k>A Large Cavern<Z>','  This is a large open cavern with few distinguishing features.  The\nceiling is about twenty feet high and is covered with long pointy\nstalactites.  Along the wall where it meets the floor are several small\nholes dug into the earth.  The large cavern extends north and south from\nhere.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(15368,7,-27,-2,'<k>The Hatching Chamber<Z>','  A small roundish chamber with a very low ceiling, this has been set\naside for hatching young.  The walls and floor are smooth and the uneven\nceiling has been smoothed over as best as possible.  Shallow depressions\nsparsely populate the floor, mostly next to the walls.  North of here\nis where the young are raised after they\'re hatched.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15369,8,-27,-2,'<k>A Large Cavern<Z>','  This is a large open cavern with few distinguishing features.  The\nceiling is about twenty feet high and is covered with long pointy\nstalactites.  Along the wall where it meets the floor are several small\nholes dug into the earth.  The large cavern extends north and south from\nhere.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(15370,9,-27,-2,'<k>A Large Cavern<Z>','  This is a large open cavern with few distinguishing features.  The\nceiling is about twenty feet high and is covered with long pointy\nstalactites.  Along the wall where it meets the floor are several small\nholes dug into the earth.  The large cavern extends north and south from\nhere.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(15371,7,-26,-2,'<k>The Hatchling\'s Chamber<Z>','  This is a low chamber with smooth walls.  The dirt and rocks have\nbeen cleared away to make it a bit more habitable for the young.  Wisps\nof steam rise from cracks in the floor making this room a little more\nthan comfortably warm.  A smaller roundish chamber lies to the south and\na large cavern is to the east.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(15372,8,-26,-2,'<k>The Northern End of a Large Cavern<Z>','   This is a large open cavern with few distinguishing features.  The\nceiling is about twenty feet high and is covered with long pointy\nstalactites.  Along the wall where it meets the floor are several small\nholes dug into the earth.  The cavern extends southward from here and\nthere is a large rock on the west wall partially covering a tunnel.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(15373,9,-26,-2,'<k>The Northern End of a Large Cavern<Z>','   This is a large open cavern with few distinguishing features.  The\nceiling is about twenty feet high and is covered with long pointy\nstalactites.  Along the wall where it meets the floor are several small\nholes dug into the earth.  Southwest and west of here there is a large\njunction of caves and the cavern extends off in a northerly direction.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(15374,4,-31,-1,'<k>A Dark Sloping Cave<Z>','   Small rocks and chunks of dirt lie strewn about the steeply sloping\nfloor and stringy roots dangle from the walls and ceiling.  Deep gouges\nand furrows line the floor and walls at irregular intervals.  Dim light\nfaintly filters in through the upper caves and the floor drops drastically\nhere as the cave descends down.\n',112,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(15375,0,0,0,'Fore Deck','The bow of the ship tapers to a concrete point, sure to breach\nthe hull of any enemy ship.  Adorning the bow is a dragon head\nmade of gold.  Its bared teeth and horizon fixed eyes spark fear\nin any sailor that sees the vessel approach.\n',0,178676,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15376,0,0,0,'Mid Deck','The midsection of the longboat is covered in clinker planks.\nThe lightweight material and excellent construction make for\na ship of deadly speed.  A mast with a square white sail lufts\nabove, and a hatch descends into the oarsmen hull.\n',0,139584,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15377,0,0,0,'Aft Deck','  The striking simplicity of the warship is layed out ahead. An oak tiller runs\nbelow deck to the rudder.  Behind the\ntiller, the hull comes to a point adorned by a golden dragon head.  The hull\nitself is composed of two layers of clinker planks, making for a light frame.\nLines are lashed on one end to cleats fastened to the hull, and on the other\nend to the four corners of the square sail ahead.\n',0,139584,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15378,0,0,0,'Mast','A rope ladder scales the mast from the deck below to the crow\'s nest\nabove.  A square sail can be heard lufting in the wind that blows\ngently from every direction. \n',0,178676,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15379,0,0,0,'Crow\'s Nest','From this vantage point the view stretches off towards the horizon.\nCertainly, an enemy ship could be seen from here, but also the\nforeign shore can be spotted for a quick hit and run attack during\nthe night.\n',0,178676,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15380,0,0,0,'Fore Drummer Station','The drummer stands in the bow\'s hull to beat the rhythm for the\noarsmen to accelerate the longboat during an attack.  A goat skin\ncovers the barrel of a drum.\n',0,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15381,0,0,0,'Oarsmen Hull','Benchs stripe the bowels of the warship with space for fifty slaves\nto man the oars.  The hull wall planks contain oar holes next to each\nbench for the labour of sweat.  A foul stench impregnates the room.\n',0,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15382,0,0,0,'Aft Drummer Station','The drummer stands in the stern\'s hull to beat the rythym for the\noarsmen to back the longboat during an attack.  A goat skin\ncovers the barrel of a drum.\n',0,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15400,12,18,-1,'Center of a Large Corn Field','   You are now somewhere around the middle of a large corn field.  By winter\nit lies quite barren, but after long hours of toil a beautiful transformation\ntakes place.  In the spring planting begins, and soon afterward tiny green\nshoots sprout up and with back breaking labor they grow until the corn is\nformed, ripens, and eventually is harvested.\n',92,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15401,12,19,-1,'Center of a Large Corn Field','   You are now approximately in the center of a large corn field.  You are\nsurrounded by long rows of corn which stretch out from you in all directions.\nThere is something almost magical about this place, and the way that the\ncorn properly planted and tended for grows up on its own providing food for\nany willing to harvest it.\n',92,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15402,13,19,-1,'Center of a Large Corn Field','   You are now approximately in the center of a large corn field.  You are\nsurrounded by long rows of corn which stretch out from you in all directions.\nHere however it appears as if something has totally destroyed any hopes for\na crop this year.  Throughout this area bits of corn plants lie ravaged as\nif torn to shreds by ravenous beasts.\n',92,131072,60,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15403,13,18,-1,'Center of a Large Corn Field','You are now approximately in the center of a large corn field.\nSurrounding you on all sides are long rows of corn which stretch out\nfrom you for a longs way.  A gentle breeze blows and everything seems\nquiet and at peace here.\n',-1,131072,60,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15404,11,20,-1,'Northwestern Corner of a Corn Field','   A cornfield surrounds you in all directions save to the north where\nincredibly thick brush blocks your path.  The corn here does not seem to be\nextremely healthy.  Soon after the corn here is planted in the spring, the\nshoots sprout up, and are cared for with the same arduous labor as the rest\nof the field, and yet they plants simply don\'t turn out too well.  Large trees\nto the north might be blocking some of the light, or perhaps it is the soil\nthat is the problem here.\n',92,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15405,12,20,-1,'Northern Edge of a Corn Field','   A cornfield surrounds you in all directions save to the north where\nincredibly thick brush blocks your path.  The corn here does not seem to be\nextremely healthy.  Soon after the corn here is planted in the spring, the\nshoots sprout up, and are cared for with the same arduous labor as the rest\nof the field, and yet they plants simply don\'t turn out too well.  Large trees\nto the north might be blocking some of the light, or perhaps it is the soil\nthat is the problem here.\n',92,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15406,13,20,-1,'Northern Edge of a Corn Field','   A cornfield surrounds you in all directions save to the north where\nincredibly thick brush blocks your path.  The corn here does not seem to be\nextremely healthy.  Soon after the corn here is planted in the spring, the\nshoots sprout up, and are cared for with the same arduous labor as the rest\nof the field, and yet they plants simply don\'t turn out too well.  Large trees\nto the north might be blocking some of the light, or perhaps it is the soil\nthat is the problem here.\n',92,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15407,14,20,-1,'Northeastern Corner of a Corn Field','   At a corner of a fairly large corn field, you cannot help but be impressed\nat just how straight the rows are, and just how square the edges are.  This\nwas a job extremely well done.  No hired help could possibly have been pushed\ninto such craftsmanship.  This field is clearly a labor of love, and one that\nthe owner must take great pride in.  The corn field stretches off to the south\nand west, while a split rail fence protects the field to the north and east.\n',92,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15408,14,19,-1,'Eastern Edge of a Corn Field','   You are on the eastern edge of a cornfield.  Though it is obscured by\nthe forest that surrounds you, you think that you can see what looks like a\ncountry farm house off to the east.  To the west there isn\'t much around you but\ncorn.  It looks as if to the south there is a gate providing passageway in and\nout of this field.  To the east is a split rail fence, and beyond it a thick\nimpassable forest.\n',92,139264,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15409,14,18,-1,'Eastern Edge of a Corn Field','  You are on the eastern edge of a cornfield.  There is a wide gate to the east\nthat protects the corn, while allowing passageway for people certainly, and\nperhaps even a horse drawn cart could fit through when it is opened all the\nway.  Off to the east the dense trees obscure the view, but it looks as if\nthere is some kind of building in that direction.  To the west corn stretches\nout until it meets the darkness of a surrounding forest.\n',92,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15410,14,17,-1,'Southeastern Corner of a Corn Field','  This is the southeastern corner of a large corn field.  The rows on the\nsoutherly part of this area meander slightly.  The rest of the rows however\nlie along a straight course.  Corn stretches off to the north and west until\nit meets tall trees.  To the south there is a fence, and beyond it a forest.\nTo the east a fence protects this field from the creatures that might come\nfrom the extremely dense and almost impassable brush.\n',92,139264,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15411,13,17,-1,'Southern Edge of a Corn Field','  Perhaps the most amazing thing about this section of the corn field is\nthat here there are noticeable imperfections.  The rows aren\'t exactly\nstraight, but seem to bend a bit back and forth.  The mistakes here are small\nand confined to the southern edge of the field.  It is as if this exception\nproves that the cornfield was made by regular people who did the job well\nand with pride.  The field stretches off in all directions save to the south\nwhere a fence separates it from the forest.\n',92,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15412,12,17,-1,'Southern edge of a Corn Field','  Perhaps the most amazing thing about this section of the corn field is\nthat here there are noticeable imperfections.  The rows aren\'t exactly\nstraight, but seem to bend a bit back and forth.  The mistakes here are small\nand confined to the southern edge of the field.  It is as if this exception\nproves that the cornfield was made by regular people who did the job well\nand with pride.  The field stretches off in all directions save to the south\nwhere a fence separates it from the forest.\n',92,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15413,11,17,-1,'Southwestern Corner of a Corn Field',' You are at the southwest corner of a corn field.  To the south and west a\nfence lends protections against hungry forest animals.  To the north long\nstraight rows of corn stretch into the distance, and to the east there are\nmore long rows of corn.\n',92,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15414,11,18,-1,'Western Entrance of a Corn Field','   You are at the western entrance to a corn field.  To the west lies a\nfence and a gate designed to keep animals out of the cornfield.  Long\nstraight rows of corn stretch out before you to the east, and you can only\nimagine the kind of damage that rabbits and the like could do were the gate\nto be left open.\n',92,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15415,11,19,-1,'Western Edge of a Corn Field','   Long straight rows of corn stretch out from you to the east, while to\nthe west a split rail fence protects the field from any forest creatures\nlooking for a tasty snack.  The forest here has been cut back considerably\nfrom the edge of the field, perhaps in order to expand it by the next\nseason or so.\n',92,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15420,15,18,-1,'Path Through the Brush','   Surrounding the path on both sides are dense brush.  It appears that you may\nbe able to beat a path through to the north and northeast, however the only\nthing visible in those directions is more brush.  Off to the west lies a corn\nfield seemingly chopped out of the forest which surrounds you.  To the east\nthere appears to be some sort of civilization, two buildings are visible,\nthough the view is obscured by the dense foliage.\n',92,131076,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15421,16,18,-1,'Path Through the Brush','   The dense foliage of this area has been hacked back into a temporary\nsubmission.  Every rain seems to give this dense growth new life however,\nand it is only a matter of time before the path will have to be cleared\nout or risk being choked off.  To the east there are buildings visible,\nand to the west a large corn field spreads out in a clearing surrounded by\na great forest.\n',92,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15422,17,18,-1,'Path Near a Farm','   The dense foliage indigenous to this area has been mostly cleared away, and\nyou can clearly see a farmhouse to the southeast, and a barn to the northeast.\nThrough the thick brush you can also make out a cornfield to the west.  To the\neast however nothing really catches your eye.  In fact the path you are now on\nsoon ends to the east in forest which stretches as far as the eye can see.\n',92,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15423,18,18,-1,'Path Beside a Farm','   This is one end of the path between the cornfield and the farm house and\nbarn.  To the south is a large cheerful looking log cabin.  It appears big enough\nto house quite a family of ten or more comfortably.  To the north sits a red\nbarn large enough to hold the essentials of farming life.\n',92,131076,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15424,18,19,-1,'Inside a Barn','   The air inside this barn is hot, humid, and filled with smells.  The hay scent\nisn\'t really so bad compared to the smells emanating from the stalls which are\nin constant need of mucking out.  Those foul smelling areas must be what\'s\nattracting flies.  The buzzing of flies around this place adds a constant low\ndrone to the otherwise quiet area.  A few tools line the walls, and there is\nsome hay around for feeding animals.  The barn extends to the north while\nstall doors line the walls to the east and west.  To the south a large barn\ndoor separates the barn from the outdoors.\n',92,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(15425,18,20,-1,'Inside a Barn','  The smells in this part of the barn aren\'t so terribly bad.  It is still just\nas stifling though, and to say it doesn\'t smell good, is indeed a major\nunderstatement.  More tools lie are stored around here, and there is a large\nspot set aside to store what would be some sort of cart.  It is impossible\nto be totally sure because it isn\'t here at the present time.  Only a clear\npatch of dirt marks its place.  Above your head is a trap door, to the east\nand west lie stalls, and to the south is the rest of the barn.\n',92,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(15426,19,20,-1,'Small Stall','   This stall is pretty nice really.  It looks clean, covered with hay, and  it\ndoesn\'t even smell that bad.  It appears that this stall must not be in use\nright now.  It\'s the only way possible that it could be this nice.  This\nactually wouldn\'t be that bad of a place to rest.  Perhaps this place might\nbe used for spending the night for someone passing through and willing to do\na few hours worth of work in exchange for a roof and perhaps a meal.\n',92,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(15427,17,20,-1,'Small Stall','   This is a small area without a lot of room.  This small stall could be set\nup to house a farm animal no larger than a pony.  It hasn\'t been used in a\nlong time however.  Spiderwebs cover the corners of this stall, turning them\nfrom mere pieces of wood into deadly traps for unwary flies.\n',92,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(15428,19,19,-1,'Large Stall','   Whew, what a smell.  This stall is clearly in dire need of mucking out.  Horse\nmanure covers most of the floor here, and gives off an odor that is anything\nbut fragrant.  In addition to the wonderful smell it gives off the manure also\nseems to be attracting flies.  That aside, this is a fairly nice spacious\narea.  It could easily and comfortably hold a large farm animal such as a\nhorse.  This area is enclosed by walls on three sides, and a stall door to the\nwest.\n',92,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(15429,17,19,-1,'Large Stall','  This is a large stall set up for the care and housing of a horse, or some\nsimilar animal such as a pony.  There is an odor about this place that\nsuggests that it was either recently used, or has been left uncleaned for a\nlong period of time.  The floor of this area appears to be fairly clean, as\nif the place is indeed cleaned if not quite often enough.  To the east a\nstall door separates this area from the rest of the barn.\n',92,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(15430,18,17,-1,'Large Dining Room','  This is a room that invites you to take off your coat and relax for a\nwhile.  The main room of a farm house, it is set up to be usefull for\nalmost everything besides sleeping.  Eating a delicious home cooked\nmeal, talking, or just relaxing around the fire, whatever you want to\ndo seems to be just fine here.\n',92,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(15431,18,16,-1,'Children\'s Area','  Wow, there must be a lot of kids in this family, because this is quite\na large area, with all kinds of stuff separated into maybe ten or fifteen\ndifferent areas.  To the north is the large main room, while to the south\nlies a smaller bedroom.\n',92,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(15432,18,15,-1,'Master Bedroom','   Not really a room, this little division of the cabin is snug and cozy.  With\nlong hard days of working a farm there probably isn\'t time for much besides\neating, working, and going to bed.  To the north a small dividing wall is set\nup with a door for privacy.\n',92,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(15433,15,19,-1,'Thick Forest With Heavy Brush','  All around you are trees and brush.  Tall trees blot out the sky.  Thick\nbrush makes quiet passage impossible for all but the most stealthy and\nlearned in forest lore.  Vision too is obscured by the brush, making it\nalmost impossible to detect anything at a distance without the use of other\nsenses.  There is no possible way to proceed to the north or to the west, but\nthere are enough breaks in the growth to force passage to a clearer path to\nthe south, or deep into brush to the east.\n',92,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15434,16,19,-1,'Deep Inside Heavy Brush','   Passage is made difficult here by the dense brush that surrounds you.  When\nyou try to move, thorns tear into your sides, and you are forced to push away\nsmall trees in order to get anywhere.  It appears as though you can force\npassage into more heavily overgrown areas to the east and west.  To the\nsouthwest is a clearer path.  To the north heavy brambles block passage, and\nin the other directions passage appears to be simply impossible.\n',92,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15435,17,19,-1,'Thick Forest With Heavy Brush','   You are deep inside a heavily overgrown area.  Thorns line the sides of\nthis path creating narrow lanes of safety.  Branches of young trees seem\nready to trip or smack into the unwary traveler.  Passage is possible to\nthe south into a clearer area, and into more heavy brush to the west, but the\nheavy thorns render movement to the north and east impossible.\n',92,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15437,16,20,-1,'Small Path Through the Woods','   There is something ominous lurking in these woods.  The forest is intensely\nthick, and seems to press in upon you from all sides.  The present path is\nhardly worthy of that name.  It is merely the only way possible through these\nwoods, and is covered with small trees.  Not only does the forest seem to\npress in, but it is unnaturally dark here.  Something seems to be hiding,\nwaiting, ready to strike.\n',92,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15438,17,21,-1,'Small Path Near a Clearing','This area is intensely dark.  The tall trees in this area are extremely\nefficient at catching every last glimmer of light.  No matter the weather\nor time this area is so dark that the clearing to the east sends in light\nas if from the end of a tunnel.\n',92,131076,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15439,18,21,-1,'A Beautiful Flower Filled Clearing','   Mostly covered in grass and clover, this field also contains hundreds, or\nperhaps even thousands of beautiful wildflowers.  In the sunshine on a clear\nblue day this would be one of the most awesome sights you can imagine.  Even\non a cold rainy day there is something charming about this scene of nature in\nits finest.\n',92,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15440,19,21,-1,'A Beautiful Flower Filled Clearing','   This clearing is full of lush grass, beautiful wildflowers and rich clumps\nof clover.  Bees fly around among the flowers and buzz past you, but like\neverything else here in this valley they seem lazy and peaceful.  Thick forests\nsurround you, and you occasionally manage to catch a glimpse of something\nrustling around in the brush nearby.  There is no path to enter into the forest\nthough, and the only way to proceed is to the west into more of the meadow.\n',92,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15441,10,18,-1,'Just Outside a Corn Field','   The current path which is wide enough for a cart or perhaps a carriage\ndramatically widens to the east.  A large corn field lies just beyond a small\ngate to the east.  To the northwest the path winds its way deep into the\ncenter of the Haon-Dor.\n',92,131076,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15442,9,19,-1,'Path Through the Woods','   To the west this path leads through a forest that grows a bit lighter.\nTo the southeast there is some type of clearing.  About this place there\nare noises of flies, mosquitoes, and large spiderwebs lain as traps for the\nunwary insect.\n',92,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15443,8,19,-1,'Path Through Haon-Dor','   The current path is small and only moderately traveled.  Most of the traffic\nthrough these parts appears to be done by foot because the vegetation has\nbeen almost completely worn away only in a very narrow area.  Evidence of\noccasional carts or carriages exists though, but such traffic is rare and\nmarks from such passage are few.\n',92,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15444,7,18,-1,'Path Through Haon-Dor','   The current path is small and only moderately traveled.  Most of the traffic\nthrough these parts appears to be done by foot because the vegetation has\nbeen almost completely worn away only in a very narrow area.  Evidence of\noccasional carts or carriages exists though, but such traffic is rare and\nmarks from such passage are few.\n',92,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15445,18,20,0,'Hay Loft','   The floor of this loft is made of sturdy boards that look as if they were\nplaced here fairly recently.  The color is still light, and they only make\nsmall creaking sounds when weight is put upon them.  This area is covered\nwith hay, and has some air flowing from around the window to the south.  It\ndoesn\'t smell bad at all, and seems to be quite a comfortable place.\n',92,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,78,0,'',NULL),
(15446,0,0,0,'Thin Air Inside a Well','   Now you\'ve really done it.  Maybe you should look before you leap next time.\nYou find yourself hurtling downwards towards the bottom of the well, which\nincidentally is a bit deeper than you thought at first inspection.  You can\'t\nhelp but notice as you are hurtling along here towards the bottom of the\nwell that there is a rope here leading up to the top of the well.  You can\nonly hope that it is long enough to reach the bottom.\n',92,131072,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15447,0,0,0,'Bottom of a Well','  After that nice trip you just had, you find yourself at the bottom of a\nwell.  You would probably need to fly to make it out of here, because the sides\nof this well are coated with slime, and appear to be unclimbable.  The south\nwall is totally caved in at the bottom, filling much of this area with\nrubble.\n',92,131072,27,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15448,0,0,0,'Small Cave','  You are now in a small cave.  The ceilings are low making these quarters\nvery cramped.  Water trickles down rocks making the only natural noises in\nthis otherwise silent area.  The cave quickly narrows down to a crack to the\nsouth, while to the east and west are solid rock walls coming up to meet\nthe ceiling.  To the north there is a great pile of rubble, the apparent result\nof a recent landslide.\n',92,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(15450,0,0,0,'Ledge Before a Waterfall','The forest comes to an abrupt end as the ground plunges into emptiness, giving\nway to the ravishing waters from the waterfall northwest of here.  Its intense \nroar blocks most of the forest sounds one would normally hear here.  The hazy mist of \nspray makes visibility difficult but also makes the trees around even greener\nthan in the rest of Haon-Dor forest.  A narrow trail leads into the forest.\n',0,140608,26,0,0,0,0,-1,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15451,0,0,0,'Narrow Trail Through Haon-Dor','  Tall and thick pine trees surround this narrow path that winds its way\naround a small mountain, the vegetation closing in tightly.  The many trees\nand dense undergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest. \nA light breeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air. \nThe ground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional\nbranch, rut or tree root tripping the unwary.  A soft, rumbling sound echoes\nthrough the trees. \n',-1,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15452,0,0,0,'Narrow Trail Through Haon-Dor','  Tall and thick pine trees surround this narrow path that winds its way around\na small mountain, the vegetation closing in tightly.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  A light\nbreeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The ground\nis a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional branch, rut or\ntree root tripping the unwary.\n',-1,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15453,0,0,0,'Narrow Trail Through Haon-Dor','  Tall and thick pine trees surround this narrow path that winds its way around\na small mountain, the vegetation closing in tightly.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  A light\nbreeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The ground\nis a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional branch, rut or\ntree root tripping the unwary.\n',-1,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15454,0,0,0,'Narrow Trail Through Haon-Dor','  Tall and thick pine trees surround this narrow path that winds its way around\na small mountain, the vegetation closing in tightly.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  A light\nbreeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The ground\nis a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional branch, rut or\ntree root tripping the unwary.\n',-1,139584,26,0,0,0,0,-1,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15455,0,0,0,'Deep in the Haon-Dor Forest','   Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  Various\nwildlife inhabits this forest, well known for its abundance of game resources.\nA light breeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The\nground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional branch,\nrut or tree root tripping the unwary.\n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15456,0,0,0,'Deep in the Haon-Dor Forest','   Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  Various\nwildlife inhabits this forest, well known for its abundance of game resources.\nA light breeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The\nground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional branch,\nrut or tree root tripping the unwary.\n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15457,0,0,0,'Deep in the Haon-Dor Forest','Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  Various\nwildlife inhabits this forest, well known for its abundance of game resources.\nA light breeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The\nground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional branch,\nrut or tree root tripping the unwary.  A well traveled path can be seen east of\nhere.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15458,0,0,0,'Deep in the Haon-Dor Forest','  Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  A small mountain lies to the west,\nbut its face is too steep here to allow passage.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  Various\nwildlife inhabits this forest, well known for its abundance of game resources.\nA light breeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The\nground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional branch,\nrut or tree root tripping the unwary.\n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15459,0,0,0,'Deep in the Haon-Dor Forest','  Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  Various\nwildlife inhabits this forest, well known for its abundance of game resources.\nA light breeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The\nground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional branch,\nrut or tree root tripping the unwary.\n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15460,0,0,0,'Deep in the Haon-Dor Forest','   Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  Various\nwildlife inhabits this forest, well known for its abundance of game resources.\nA light breeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The\nground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional branch,\nrut or tree root tripping the unwary.  A well traveled path can be seen through\nthe foliage east of here.\n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15461,0,0,0,'Deep in the Haon-Dor Forest','  Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  A small mountain lies to the west,\nbut its face is too steep here to allow passage.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  Various\nwildlife inhabits this forest, well known for its abundance of game resources.\nA light breeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The\nground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional branch,\nrut or tree root tripping the unwary.\n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15462,0,0,0,'Deep in the Haon-Dor Forest','  Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  Various\nwildlife inhabits this forest, well known for its abundance of game resources. \nA light breeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air. \nThe ground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional\nbranch, rut or tree root tripping the unwary. \n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15463,0,0,0,'Deep in the Haon-Dor Forest','Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  Various\nwildlife inhabits this forest, well known for its abundance of game resources.\nA light breeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The\nground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional branch,\nrut or tree root tripping the unwary.  A well traveled path can be seen east of\nhere.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15464,0,0,0,'Deep in the Haon-Dor Forest','  Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  A small mountain lies to the\nwest, its face too steep here to allow passage.  The high grounds stall the\nbreeze, the air is damp and still.  A small clearing can be seen through the\nvegetation to the south.  The ground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and\nleaves, and it gets a little more humid here.  Several footprints of different\nsizes and shapes are noticeable on the humid ground. \n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15465,0,0,0,'Deep in the Haon-Dor Forest','   Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  Various\nwildlife inhabits this forest, well known for its abundance of game resources.\nA light breeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The\nground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional branch,\nrut or tree root tripping the unwary.\n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15466,0,0,0,'Deep in the Haon-Dor Forest','   Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  Various\nwildlife inhabits this forest, well known for its abundance of game resources.\nA light breeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The\nground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional branch,\nrut or tree root tripping the unwary.\n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15467,0,0,0,'Deep in the Haon-Dor Forest','Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  Various\nwildlife inhabits this forest, well known for its abundance of game resources.\nA light breeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The\nground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, with an occasional branch,\nrut or tree root tripping the unwary.  A well traveled path can be seen east of\nhere.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15468,0,0,0,'Deep in the Haon-Dor Forest','Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  A small mountain lies to the west,\nits face too steep here to allow passage.  The many trees and dense\nundergrowth block sight of all but the nearest parts of the forest.  Various\nwildlife inhabits this forest, well known for its abundance of game resources.\nA light breeze blows through, bringing different forest scents to the air.  The\nground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and leaves, and it gets a little more\nhumid here.  Several footprints of different sizes and shapes are noticeable on\nthe humid ground.\n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15469,0,0,0,'Before a Small Clearing in Haon-Dor','  Tall and thick pine trees are all around.  The undergrowth isn\'t as abundant\nhere as in other areas of the forest.  A gentle damp breeze comes in from the\nclearing to the south.  The ground is a mixture of sand, mud, gravel and\nleaves, and it gets more humid here.  Several footprints of various sizes and\nshapes are noticeable on the humid ground. \n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
