(15700,9,46,-3,'By a Wall, Just Beyond the Frontier','The mountain pass narrows toward the northeast, but a small flat region exists\nbetween the wall and where the trail forces travelers to walk single file again.\nThe wall itself is of thick timbers probably hauled at great expense from the\nHaon-Dor and Arden forests.  In layout, the wall curves in such a way as to seem\nto funnel things toward the gate, but in fact you realize that this is done so\nas to provide the maximum amount of room on the wall able to fire at whatever is\nattacking the gate itself.  The palisade sits atop an earthen embankment that\nwas created by digging a deep trench just outside the wall.  The trench plus\nembankment plus palisade makes the wall practically double the height.  You\nrealize with a chill that the region you now stand upon represents a carefully\nplanned killing-zone.  The trench is about four feet deep and six feet wide and\nruns the entire length of the wall.\n',95,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15701,20,69,-1,'Frontier Wall - Outside the Gate','The mountain pass narrows toward the northeast, but a small flat region exists\nbetween the wall and where the trail forces travelers to walk single file again.\nThe wall itself is of thick timbers probably hauled at great expense from the\nHaon-Dor and Arden forests.  In layout, the wall curves in such a way as to seem\nto funnel things toward the gate, but in fact you realize that this is done so\nas to provide the maximum amount of room on the wall able to fire at whatever is\nattacking the gate itself.  The palisade sits atop an earthen embankment that\nwas created by digging a deep trench just outside the wall.  The trench plus\nembankment plus palisade makes the wall practically double the height.  You\nrealize with a chill that the region you now stand upon represents a carefully\nplanned killing-zone.  The trench is about four feet deep and six feet wide and\nruns the entire length of the wall\n',95,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15702,11,44,-3,'Just Beyond the Frontier','The mountain pass narrows toward the northeast, but a small flat region exists\nbetween the wall and where the trail forces travelers to walk single file again.\nThe wall itself is of thick timbers probably hauled at great expense from the\nHaon-Dor and Arden forests.  In layout, the wall curves in such a way as to seem\nto funnel things toward the gate, but in fact you realize that this is done so\nas to provide the maximum amount of room on the wall able to fire at whatever is\nattacking the gate itself.  The palisade sits atop an earthen embankment that\nwas created by digging a deep trench just outside the wall.  The trench plus\nembankment plus palisade makes the wall practically double the height.  You\nrealize with a chill that the region you now stand upon represents a carefully\nplanned killing-zone.  The trench is about four feet deep and six feet wide and\nruns the entire length of the wall.\n',95,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15703,10,46,-3,'Just Beyond the Frontier','Blistering winds sweep through the mountain pass, blowing snow around and\neffectively blinding you.  You stumble through the thick dunes of ice and\nsnow.  Passage northwest is blocked by the sheer face of a mountain.  To the\nsouth you can vaguely make out a high wooden wall.\n',95,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15704,11,45,-3,'Just Beyond the Frontier','Blistering winds sweep through the mountain pass, blowing snow around and\neffectively blinding you.  You stumble through the thick dunes of ice and\nsnow.  Passage southeast is blocked by the sheer face of a mountain.  To the\nwest you can vaguely make out a high wooden wall.\n',95,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15705,10,47,-3,'Just Beyond the Frontier','Blistering winds sweep through the mountain pass, blowing snow around and\neffectively blinding you.  You stumble through the thick dunes of ice and\nsnow.  To the northwest the sheer face of a mountain prevents passage.\n',95,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15706,11,46,-3,'Just Beyond the Frontier','Blistering winds sweep through the mountain pass, blowing snow around and\neffectively blinding you.  You stumble through the thick dunes of ice and\nsnow.\n',95,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15707,12,45,-3,'Just Beyond the Frontier','Blistering winds sweep through the mountain pass, blowing snow around and\neffectively blinding you.  You stumble through the thick dunes of ice and\nsnow.  To the southeast the sheer face of the mountain prevents passage.\n',95,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15708,11,47,-3,'Just Beyond the Frontier','Blistering winds sweep through the mountain pass, blowing snow around and\neffectively blinding you.  You stumble through the thick dunes of ice and\nsnow.  To the north the sheer face of a mountain prevents passage.\n',95,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15709,12,46,-3,'Just Beyond the Frontier','Blistering winds sweep through the mountain pass, blowing snow around and\neffectively blinding you.  You stumble through the thick dunes of ice and\nsnow.  To the southeast the sheer face of the mountain prevents passage.\n',95,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15710,12,47,-3,'Just Beyond the Frontier','Blistering winds sweep through the mountain pass, which narrows to the\nnortheast.  Gusts of wind cause whirlwinds of snow to blow around, effectively\nblinding you, and causing you to stumble through the thick dunes of ice and\nsnow.\n',95,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15711,13,46,-3,'By a Cave Entrance Just Beyond the Frontier','Blistering winds sweep through the mountain pass, blowing snow around and\neffectively blinding you.  You stumble through the thick dunes of ice and\nsnow.  You see the dark form of a cave leading into the mountainside east of\nhere.\n',95,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15712,14,46,-3,'A Cold Cave Entrance','Freezing winds create a howling sound as they blow across the cave opening\nthat lies to the west.  You are protected from the fierce gusts here, but the\nchill is omnipresent.  The cave leads further south or southeast, following\nmysterious trails on broken bones.\n',95,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,20,350,0,'',NULL),
(15713,14,45,-3,'A Cold Cave','From the north you hear a faint howling noise caused by fierce winds blowing\nacross a cave opening there.  The chill of the tundra reaches even into the\ncave, making your thoughts drift to warmer places that you have visited.  The\nfloor is littered with broken bones.\n',95,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,20,350,0,'',NULL),
(15714,15,45,-3,'Back of a Cold Cave','From the northwest you hear a faint howling noise caused by fierce winds blowing\nacross a cave opening there.  The chill of the tundra reaches even into the\ncave, making your thoughts drift to warmer places that you have visited.  The\nfloor is littered with broken bones.\n',95,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,20,350,0,'',NULL),
(15715,13,48,-3,'Arctic Trail','This is part of the arctic trail winding its way through the mountains.  The\ntrail heads northeast into the polar ice world beyond the civilized realms\nor southwest toward the frontier.  The trail is of slippery, ice-covered\nrock and at this point the only view available is snow capped mountains.  A\nbitterly cold wind whips down the path and there is nothing to provide relief\nor cover from it.  Northeast of here lies a frozen plain stretching away\nfrom the mountains southwest.\n',95,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15716,14,51,-3,'The Frozen Plains','The plains extend for many miles to the north and east, causing you to lose\nbearing and wander aimlessly.  Cold winds buffet you from every side, and throw\nsnow into the air, blinding you.  A large dune has formed to the west,\npreventing you from traveling in that direction.\n',95,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15717,14,50,-3,'The Frozen Plains','The plains extend for many miles to the north and east, causing you to lose\nbearing and wander aimlessly.  Cold winds buffet you from every side, and throw\nsnow into the air, blinding you.  A large dune has formed to the west,\npreventing you from traveling in that direction.\n',95,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15718,14,49,-3,'The Frozen Plains','The plains extend for many miles to the north and east, causing you to lose\nbearing and wander aimlessly.  Cold winds buffet you from every side, and throw\nsnow into the air, blinding you.  A large dune has formed to the west,\npreventing you from traveling in that direction.\n',95,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15719,14,48,-3,'The Frozen Plains','The plains extend for many miles to the north and east, causing you to lose\nbearing and wander aimlessly.  Cold winds buffet you from every side, and throw\nsnow into the air, blinding you.  A large dune has formed to the west and south,\npreventing you from traveling in those directions.\n',95,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15720,15,51,-3,'The Frozen Plains','The plains extend for many miles to the north and east, causing you to lose\nbearing and wander aimlessly.  Cold winds buffet you from every side, and throw\nsnow into the air, blinding you.  A large dune has formed to the west, and the\nchill wind is so strong to the north, that you cannot travel in either of\nthose directions.  A sheer mountain face blocks passage to the southeast.\n',95,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15721,15,49,-3,'The Frozen Plains','The plains extend for many miles to the north and east, causing you to lose\nbearing and wander aimlessly.  Cold winds buffet you from every side, and throw\nsnow into the air, blinding you.\n',95,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15722,15,48,-3,'The Frozen Plains','The plains extend for many miles to the north and east, causing you to lose\nbearing and wander aimlessly.  Cold winds buffet you from every side, and throw\nsnow into the air, blinding you.  A large dune has formed to the south, and the\nwinds are so strong to the east, that you cannot travel in those directions.\n',95,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15723,16,52,-3,'By a Cave in the Mountainside in the Frozen Plains','The plains extend for many miles to the north and east, causing you to lose\nbearing and wander aimlessly.  Cold winds buffet you from every side, and throw\nsnow into the air, blinding you.  The fierce winds are so strong that you\nare able only to travel southwest along a mountain face, or south into what\nseems to be a small cave opening into the mountainside.\n',95,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15724,16,51,-3,'A Cave in the Mountainside','This is barely a nook in the side of the mountain, and provides little cover\nfrom the howling winds and freezing ice in the frozen plains to the north.  What\nseems to be frozen solid body parts are sparsely thrown throughout the cave,\nthough more might be hidden under small snow drifts.  You see a rusted manacle\nin one corner.\n',95,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,20,600,0,'',NULL),
(15725,16,49,-3,'The Frozen Plains','The plains extend for many miles to the north and east, causing you to lose\nbearing and wander aimlessly.  Cold winds buffet you from every side, and throw\nsnow into the air, blinding you.  A large dune has formed to the south, and the\nwinds are so strong to the east, that you cannot travel in those directions.  To\nthe north is a sheer mountain face.\n',95,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15726,15,50,-3,'Base of the Mountain','   The mountain stands here majestically, telling a timeless and wordless\ntale of nature.  Although a bleak and desolate place, you sense the enormous\nenergy that nature holds in such holy places.  The frozen plains stretch north\nand east, and the mountain seems to have no peak--it just disappears into the\nclouds.  Winds howl around you, and snow and small ice chunks sting your face.\nA few yards away a ledge can be spotted that runs along the mountain in a steep\nslope.\n',95,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15900,-47,36,0,'<o>Clearing With a Well<z>','<p>  The rising mountains to the east cast shadows over the surrounding landscape.\nUnlike the nearby road, this area is not so well kept.  The cobbled road has\nbeen badly marked by time and even the grass has given no mercy.  Large cracks\nin the stones give places for weeds and other such plants to show their cruelty.\nTowards the center the granite cobblestones have been ripped up for the placing\nof a well.  Not many signs of travel can be found here.<z>\n',100,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15901,0,0,0,'<b>Inside The Well<z>','<B>  The stones that make up this well look very dry and dirty.  The few\nfootholds that can be found hold well under the weight.  Down below, the\nwell continues into its dark path.  The way up provides a scene of the\nsky above.  Not much room is available in here due to the closeness of\nthe walls.  A way downwards can be easily followed through the protruding\nrocks.  While a few grip holds at the top of the well allow an easy passage\nout.<z>\n',100,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,4,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15902,0,0,0,'<B>Deeper Into The Well<z>','<c>  The well at this level appears very old but not as dirty.  The water\nthat once filled this well has left a noticeable waterline on the walls.\nThe sky up above is no longer viewable but the darkness below still holds\nstrong in its place.  Foot holds and what few protruding rocks that can be\nfound lead upwards and downwards.<z>\n',100,131080,35,0,0,0,0,0,3,240,0,'',NULL),
(15903,0,0,0,'<B>Deeper Into The Well<z>','<c>  The stones here seem very new and not much decay shows on them.\nDarkness creeps into the room from above and below.  The protruding rocks\nand foot holds have increased in this room to the point of creating an\nentire ledge.  A small pathway of stone gives access to a path leading\ndownwards.  The way upwards can be followed due to the protruding rocks.\nA few drops of sand seem to be stuck on the walls here.<z>\n',100,131080,35,0,0,0,0,0,3,240,0,'',NULL),
(15904,0,0,0,'<B>Bottom Of The Well<z>','<o>  At the bottom of the well the scene is anything but bare.  The walls\nhere show many signs of age and use.  The mortar shows even more.  The\nupwards view is dark while the downwards view shows a pit of sand.  The\npit on the floor gently sucks downwards allowing a possible way even\nfurther into the well.<z>\n',100,131080,33,60,15905,1,0,0,5,240,0,'',NULL),
(15905,0,0,0,'<k>A Cavern Of Stone<z>','<z>  The walls here are of solid stone and are covered in dirt and sand.\nThe ground is a mixture of rock and sand while a hole in the ceiling\ndrips sand every now and then.  A path heading east leads deeper into the\ncavern while the way south leads into a cave.\n',100,131080,33,200,15905,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(15906,0,0,0,'<k>A Cavern Of Stone<z>','<z>  The floor is covered in rock and sand while the walls appear to be the\nsame.  The ceiling rises far above the floor overlooking the rest of the\ncavern.  The air here seems a little foul to the southeast while a sweeter\nsmell drifts in from the south.  To the west a gentle sifting sound\ndrifts in from time to time.  The south and southeast directions lead\ndown slopes that quickly drop to one of the lower levels here while the\nway east and west lead to other sections of the cavern.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(15907,0,0,0,'<k>A Massive Cavern<z>','<z>  This massive cavern stretches in almost every direction.  The floor has\nmuch sand on it and the northern wall is layered with dirt and dust.  An\nuneasy smell drifts into this room from the south while the fresh air\nbattles it from above.  The way east and west lead into other sections of\nthe cavern while the southern paths lead down slopes to the next level.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,221,0,'',NULL),
(15908,0,0,0,'<k>A Large Cavern<z>','<z>  This section of the cavern appears to be the northeastern section.  The\nceiling, like in the rest of the cavern, is well above the floor.  The few\nwalls that are in touching distance are craggy and dirty.  The floor is\nalmost engulfed by sand from the slopes to the south and southwest.  The\nair is very sweet with a very dry taste to it.  Slopes lead downwards to\nthe south and southwest.  The way west and southeast lead into other\nsections of the cavern.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,198,0,'',NULL),
(15909,0,0,0,'<k>A Dark Cave<z>','<z>  The ceiling of this cave rises about six feet above the floor while the\nwalls close in on themselves.  Not much elbow room is given by the walls\nof this room.  The sand on this floor appears odd in its positioning.  The\nwalls here are very clean and smooth while a gentle light pulsates to the\nsouthwest.  The way south leads deeper into the cave while the way north\nleads out.  Another possible exit lies to the southwest towards the light.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,74,0,'',NULL),
(15910,0,0,0,'<k>An Open Cavern<z>','<z>  The cavern opens up quite well here.  The ceiling rises well above your\nhead and what walls there is in close proximity allow for lots of movement.\nThe air is a mixture of sweet, salty, and dry.  The ground has bits of\nsand towards the west along with a little bit of dirt to the southeast.\nThe way west leads towards a downwards slope that quickly falls downwards.\nThe way southeast leads into the mouth of a cave while the cavern\ncontinues to the northwest.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,278,0,'',NULL),
(15911,0,0,0,'<o>A Mysterious Den<z>','<c>  This room would appear to be someone\'s den.  Dirt, sand, and small\nmarks line the floor in patterns.  The walls in here are extremely smooth\nand clean while the ceiling, a mere eight or so feet above the floor, is\ncracked and spotted with protruding rods.  A few objects in the room catch\nyou eye.  The main one being a rather large looking spike attached to the\nsouthern wall.  The way northeast leads into cave while the way east does\nalso.<z>\n',100,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,5,101,0,'',NULL),
(15912,0,0,0,'<k>Deeper Into The Cave<z>','<z>  The walls in this room are rough and dirty.  The ceiling is roughly six\nor so feet above the floor and is even more dirty than the walls.  The\nfloor is dotted with splotches of sand and rock with the occasional dirt\npile.  The way north leads towards the mouth of the cave while the way\nsoutheast leads deeper into the cave.  A small beam of light creeps in\nfrom the west.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,76,0,'',NULL),
(15913,0,0,0,'<k>Inside the Mouth of the Cave<z>','<z>  This section of the cave appears to be the mouth of the cave.  The\nceiling here rises quickly from the floor and the walls open up to allow\nfor much movement.  The dirt in this room is both sparse and thinly\nlayered.  A foul stench is in the air but is partially subdued by the open\ncavern air coming from the northwest.  The way southwest leads deeper\ninto the cave while the path northwest allows freedom.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,203,0,'',NULL),
(15914,0,0,0,'<k>A Room Of Rock<z>','<z>  It is easy to tell that this room was cut out of the very rock of which\nit is encased in.  The walls, floor, and ceiling are perfectly boxed and\nsmooth.  On the northern wall there appears to be an odd upside-down V\ndesign.  The floor shows sign of very little use.  This room is clean of\nsand and dirt.  The marks on the northern wall let in just enough light to\nbe noticed but not enough to make a difference.\n',100,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,3,55,0,'',NULL),
(15915,0,0,0,'<k>A Cave Of Stone<z>','<z>  The walls here are a little dusty but very old.  The ceiling is riveted\nby rocky spikes and clumps of dirt fall onto the floor every now and then.\nThe floor has a few specks of sand but mostly its covered in dirt and rock.\nThe way northwest leads into another section of the cave while the way\neast leads deeper into the cave.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,5,66,0,'',NULL),
(15916,0,0,0,'<k>A Cave Of Rock<z>','<z>  This cave stretches to the east and west.  The walls are dirty and\ncracked.  The ceiling rises about six feet above the ground and is pitted\nby rock spikes and stalactites.  Dirt and a little debris cover the floor.\nThe way east darts deeper into the cave while the way west leads into\nanother section of the cave.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,3,76,0,'',NULL),
(15917,0,0,0,'<k>A Cave Of Rock<z>','<z>  This section of the cave seems to close in on you from every direction.\nThe ceiling and walls are both dirty and cracked.  Dirt lines the floors\nand a foul stench lingers in the air here.  An uneasy feeling accompanies\nthis scene almost as if you were being watched by someone or something.\nThe way east and west both lead deeper into the cave.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,3,63,0,'',NULL),
(15918,0,0,0,'<k>A Cave Of Rock<z>','<z>  This bend in the cave has a foul stench to it.  The walls are splotched\nwith a gray matter that mixes rather oddly with the dirt.  The ceiling is\nmarked by stalactites and the floor seems to be gently cracked.  The way\nwest leads straight into another section of the cave while the way\nnortheast bends gently as it goes further into the rock.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,5,88,0,'',NULL),
(15919,0,0,0,'<o>A Dry Beach<z>','<c>  This beach seems to have been long dry.  The water that once fed this\nbeach to the south would seem to be long dead.  The sand is still golden\nand is of a fine grain.  A stench drifts in from the east while a salty\nsmell drifts in from the south.  The beach continues to the east while the\nlong dead river bed lies to the south and southeast.  A pair of slopes\nlifts up towards the north and northeast.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,226,0,'',NULL),
(15920,0,0,0,'<o>A Beautiful Subterranean Beach<z>','<c>  This would seem to be the center of what was once a beautiful subterranean\nbeach.  The sand is of a beautiful golden color and stretches in all\ndirections from here.  A foul stench seems to be in the air of this room\nwhile a salty smell wafts in from the south and southwest.  The beach\ncontinues to the east and west.  A river bed to the south and southwest\nhelp drown the stench a little but not much.  Slopes rise upwards in the\nnorthern directions.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,244,0,'',NULL),
(15921,0,0,0,'<o>A Dry Beach<z>','<c>  This once beautiful beach has been long dry by now.  The sand has\ngently formed a solid mass to the south while the sand to the north has\nstayed broken.  The ceiling rises far above the ground here and a rancid\nstench accompanies the darkness from the west.  Slopes rise upwards to\nthe northwest, north, and east.  The beach continues to the west while\nwhat would be the river bed lies to the southwest.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,241,0,'',NULL),
(15922,0,0,0,'<o>A Dead River Bed<z>','<c>  The ground here is a deep brown and is fractured horribly.  A wall\nrises to your west blocking passage in that direction.  The sand to the\nnorth and northeast gently creep in from those directions while the river\nbed stretches to the east and south.  In the distance to the south\nwhat appears to be a cave of some sorts looms out of the darkness.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,258,0,'',NULL),
(15923,0,0,0,'<o>A Long Dead River Bed<z>','<c>  This long dead river bed seems to carry a history with it.  Cracks and\nother markings line the ground.  The darkness above stretches far above\nthe ground.  To the southwest a cave looms out of the darkness.  The\nriver bed continues to the west and southwest and the sandy beaches creep\nin from the northern directions.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,284,0,'',NULL),
(15924,0,0,0,'<o>Before A Cave<z>','<c>  The river bed that spans the ground here reaches off in all walk able\ndirections.  Cracks line the floor and sand spots can be seen here and\nthere.  The walls here show sign of age and use while the air keeps a\nconstant salty flavor flowing in.  To the south a cave beckons entrance\nwhile the river bed flows to the north and northeast.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,180,0,'',NULL),
(15925,0,0,0,'<k>Inside A Cave<z>','<z>  This would be cave appears to be the product of palatial drifting under\nthe ground.  Cracks scar the floor and all the walls while a rather large\nrip in the rock to the east provides an open path.  A foul stench drifts\nin from the southeast.  A small river bed travels north to east here.\nThe way southeast seems to be a product of time.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,63,0,'',NULL),
(15926,0,0,0,'<k>Deeper In A Cave<z>','<z>  This section of the cave seems to open up a little more.  The walls\nare cracked and the ceiling is covered in dust.  Drops of sand dot the\nground here and there.  A gentle breeze flows in from the western wall\nthrough a rather large rip.  The way southwest leads towards a bend in\nthe cave while the way east leads deeper into the rock.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,73,0,'',NULL),
(15927,0,0,0,'<k>Deeper Into The Rock<z>','<z>  From west to east the walls go from cracked and rocky to clean and\nsmooth.  The ceiling gently rises as it travels and the air seems to\nbecome a little more ancient smelling.  A breeze gently flows in from the\nwest bringing with it a light layer of dust.  The cave gently bends to\nthe southeast and the way west leads deeper into the rock.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,86,0,'',NULL),
(15928,0,0,0,'<k>A Bend In The Cave<z>','<z>  Very little passage room is given here.  The walls seem to close in on\neach other in a tight formation while the ceiling hangs low.  A foul\nstench lingers in this room for a little then drifts off to the northeast\nand northwest.  Cracks and rips scar the walls here.  To the northeast a\nway deeper into the cave opens up while the way northwest seems to lead\ntowards the front of the cave.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,2,52,0,'',NULL),
(15929,0,0,0,'<k>Deeper In The Rock<z>','<z>  Below the layers of dust on these walls there seems to be a nice\ngleam.  The ceiling drops back down towards the south while the walls\nopen up to allow plenty of room.  Dust covers most of the room but only\nin a thin layer.  To the south the way goes deeper into the rock while\nthe way northwest leads back into the outskirts of the cave.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,74,0,'',NULL),
(15930,0,0,0,'<p>Before A Hallway<z>','<r>  The walls begin to open up quite a bit here.  The ceiling rises far\nabove the ground and an odd breeze drifts in from the north and south.\nDebris covers the floor in places.  The temperature here is unnaturally\nwarm for this depth but seems very comfortable.  The air is very humid\nhere and water drops pry at the walls.  The way north leads deeper into\nthe rock while the way south leads into what would be a stone hallway.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,122,0,'',NULL),
(15931,0,0,0,'<p>A Beautiful Hallway<z>','<r>  The blocks that make up this hallway are intricately detailed and\npainted.  Parts of the walls have collapsed leaving deep scars in the\nbeautiful artwork while a few blocks of the ceiling seem missing.  Dust\ncovers almost everything in this room.  A breeze from the south brings\nthe smell of battles long lost.  The way north provides escape to the\nfront of the hallway while the way south leads towards a massive gate.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,133,0,'',NULL),
(15932,0,0,0,'<k>A Plain Section Of Cave<z>','<z>  The scene here is very bleak and bare.  The floor, ceiling, and walls\nare rocky but not much else.  Little light, nor much living life, has\ntouched this place in a long time it would seem.  To the south the cave\ncontinues while a pit welcomes you to the east.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,76,0,'',NULL),
(15933,0,0,0,'<o>A Spherical Pit<z>','<c>  A rather large pit dominates this room.  Towards the center of the pit\nis a black hole that seems to provide passage to the lower section.  The\nwalls are very smooth and gently circular.  The ceiling is somewhat dome\nlike and is as smooth as the walls.  The way west and southwest provide\naccess to the rest of the cave from here.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,144,0,'',NULL),
(15934,0,0,0,'<k>Deeper Into The Rock<z>','<z>  The ceiling quickly rises towards the north and northeast.  The walls\nopen up giving plenty of moving room.  The floor here is badly cracked\nand small dots of sand show here and there.  A warm breeze flows in from\nthe south.  To the north and south the cave continues while a pit scars the\nfloor to the northeast.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,5,53,0,'',NULL),
(15935,0,0,0,'<k>A Path Through The Rock<z>','<z>  The ceiling hangs rather low here and the walls give very little\nshoulder room.  Cracks scar every part of this area.  A hole in the\nground here allows water to bubble up.  To the north the cave continues.\nA warm draft of air sweeps the room from all but the north.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,2,46,0,'',NULL),
(15936,0,0,0,'<C>The Room Of Teaching<z>','<B>  This room is rather massive and cluttered.  All sorts of teaching\nsupplies are scattered all over the place.  Documents are piled into\ncorners and books remain in oddly stacked piles.  The floor is tiled with\nmetal and onyx and the walls are the same.  The ceiling is made of stone\nand rises a good twenty feet above the ground.  A trapdoor in the floor\nprovides escape from this cluttered mess.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(15937,0,0,0,'<p>A Common Room Of Living<z>','<r>  From the ceiling to the floor the walls have been delicately painted to\nshow an awe inspiring scene.  The ceiling is very clean while the floor\nis a bit dirty.  The walls have been carved from a massive stone block\nalong with the floor and ceiling.  To the south an open doorway leads\ninto another common room of living while the way east seems to lead into\na chapel of some kind.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,5,120,0,'',NULL),
(15938,0,0,0,'<p>A Room Of Worship<z>','<r>  The first thing that stands out about this room is how clean it is.\nThe walls have all been cleaned and smoothed out and even the floor has\nbeen waxed and polished to get rid of that rough surface.  The ceiling is\nas clean as the rest of the room.  Those who are faithful come here to\ngive there praise and love to there deity.  To the southeast and west are\nopen doorways to a pair of common rooms of living.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(15939,0,0,0,'<p>A Common Room Of Living<z>','<r>  This room seems to be a common room of living.  The walls have been\ncut from a single piece of stone along with the floor and ceiling.\nThe wall to the south has an odd granite block protruding from it.\nThe floor is rather dirty here and the walls look like they could use a\nnice cleaning.  To the north an open doorway leads to another common room\nof living.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,5,120,0,'',NULL),
(15940,0,0,0,'<k>A Room Of Carved Stone<z>','<z>  The walls, floor, and ceiling here are constructed of carved stone\nblocks.  Detail covers everything even the hole in the ceiling.  The floor\nis very clean and the walls seem to have been recently polished.  A meshy\nlayer of moss covers a hole in the southern wall.\n',100,173244,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(15941,0,0,0,'<p>A Common Room Of Living<z>','<r>  The walls here haven\'t been cleaned in ages.  From the floor to the\nceiling the walls are covered in dirt and dust.  Hay lies strewn all over\nthe room while a few broken pens lie here and there.  The ceiling is\ncovered in spider webs and the floor is covered in debris.  A doorway in\nthe northwest wall provides escape from this ungodly scene.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,3,120,0,'',NULL),
(15942,0,0,0,'<p>Western Dead End Of A Grand Hallway<z>','<r>  The hallway becomes a sudden dead end here.  In all directions but\neast the path is blocked by stone blocks.  The walls are made up of the\nsame carved stone that seems to be used throughout this place while the\nnorthern wall seems odd.  The ceiling is a perfect parallel of the floor\nright down the block settings.  The way east leads to the center of\nthe hallway.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(15943,0,0,0,'<p>A Grand Hallway<z>','<r>  The ceiling rises a few feet above the ground giving well enough head\nway here while what few walls are here are well places allowing a lot of\nextra room.  The floor consists of perfect squared off blocks while the\nceiling mimics this design perfectly.  To the east and west the hallway\ncontinues.  The way south branches off from the main hallway into a small\nroom.  A meshy patch of moss covers a hole in the northern wall.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(15944,0,0,0,'<p>Eastern Dead End Of A Grand Hallway<z>','<r>  The hallway suddenly gives way to a dead end here.  The floor seems\nto have been recently cleaned and swept.  The ceiling, like the rest of\nthe room, is made up of that same odd stone that makes up the rest of the\nhallway.  The walls here are a perfect box except for a granite block on\nthe north wall.  The way west leads to the center of the hallway.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(15945,0,0,0,'<p>A Small Forward Room<z>','<r>  This branch off of the main hallway looks almost as well designed as\nthe hallway itself.  The walls are comprised of many perfectly cut small\nblocks.  The ceiling has giving way to a pure slab of rock while the\nfloor is made up of intricately cut stone pieces.  A doorway in the\nsoutheast wall has been cut into the stone blocks themselves.  The\nsouthwestern wall appears somewhat odd compared to the rest.<z>\n',0,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(15946,0,0,0,'<R>A Guard Room<z>','<p>  To the northeast the room appears to be common stone while to the\nsoutheast the room appears to be metal.  A few military objects sit in\nthe room here and there along with a few normal items.  The walls to the\nsoutheast and northeast seem peculiar.  The floor here shows many signs\nof use.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(15947,0,0,0,'<B>A Message Room<z>','<c>  The walls here are stone to the northwest and metal in all the\nothers.  The ceiling and floor mimic this pattern perfectly.  The stone\nthat makes up the northwestern section of this room appears to be common\nstone while the metal that makes up the rest of the room doesn\'t appear\nto be a natural metal.  A door in the northwest wall has been carved\nfrom the stone itself while a door in the southwest wall has been cut\nfrom the metal.  A piece of paper has been attached to the eastern wall.<z>\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,3,120,0,'',NULL),
(15948,0,0,0,'<k>A Room Of Metal<z>','<z>  The ceiling of this room is made up of carved metal with a trapdoor in\nthe center.  The floor is tiled with onyx that has been cut to a perfectly\nsmooth and flat surface.  The walls are made up of the same metal that\ncovers the ceiling.  An intricate design has been carved into the southern\nwall while a hairline crack seems to have been carved into the northwestern\nwall.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(15949,0,0,0,'<k>A Massive Cave In<z>','<z>  To the south a massive gate towers over the scene here.  What was\nonce a set of imposing guard towers are now destroyed to either side of\nthe gate.  The ceiling has collapsed onto the gate both blocking passage\nand destroying it.  The walls show heavy signs of battle while the air\naccompanies it.  The floor is nothing but breaks, rips, and pits now due\nto the debris that fell from above.\n',100,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,2,489,0,'',NULL),
(15950,0,0,0,'Northern Coastal Highway','A large highway runs north and south here, following the coast of the\nAgorian Sea northwards into the wilderness.  Large fields of grain block\nall passage to the east, while the sea itself blocks the west.  To the\nnorthwest, a spire topped building juts from a rocky cliff overlooking\nthe ocean.  To the south lies the northern gatekeep of the town of\nBrightmoon.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15951,0,0,0,'Outside a Towering Library','  To the northwest looms a huge building.  Its two spiked spires shoot into\nthe sky, and overlook the Agorian sea to the west.  A set of polished steel\ndoors serve as an entrance into the building.  To the east lie many golden\nfields of grain and pasture.  To the south you can see the high wall which\nsurrounds the city of Brightmoon.  \n',129,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15952,0,0,0,'Library Corner','  This room is swathed in a thick blanket of tangible quiet.  Tapestry adorned\nwalls stand proudly, muting loud noises into a soft buzz.  Vaulted stone\nceilings rise above, decorated with gold designs and patterns.  The bare floor\nis made of a cold unyielding white marble. \n',129,167100,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15953,0,0,0,'Library Walkway','  To call this ample passage a walkway seems like an understatement at best. \nGleaming stone walls stand proudly, magnifying even the slightest sound into a\nmighty crescendo.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated with gold\ndesigns and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white\nmarble. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15954,0,0,0,'Library Walkway','  To call this ample passage a walkway seems like an understatement at best. \nGleaming stone walls stand proudly, magnifying even the slightest sound into a\nmighty crescendo.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated with gold\ndesigns and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white\nmarble. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15955,0,0,0,'Library Walkway','  To call this ample passage a walkway seems like an understatement at best. \nGleaming stone walls stand proudly, magnifying even the slightest sound into a\nmighty crescendo.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated with gold\ndesigns and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white\nmarble. A sliding door leads to a courtyard to the north.  \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15956,0,0,0,'Library Walkway','  To call this ample passage a walkway seems like an understatement at best. \nGleaming stone walls stand proudly, magnifying even the slightest sound into a\nmighty crescendo.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated with gold\ndesigns and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white\nmarble. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15957,0,0,0,'Library Study Hall','  The stillness of the surrounding air provides a place for people to pursue\nquiet contemplation.  Tapestry adorned walls stand proudly, muting loud noises\ninto a soft buzz.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated with gold\ndesigns and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white\nmarble. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15958,0,0,0,'Library Study Hall','  The stillness of the surrounding air provides a place for people to pursue\nquiet contemplation.  Tapestry adorned walls stand proudly, muting loud noises\ninto a soft buzz.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated with gold\ndesigns and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white\nmarble.  A stained glass window rests on the east wall. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15959,0,0,0,'Corner of a Small Courtyard','  A feeling of calm pervades the still air of this verdant garden.  Perfumed\nflowery scents waft about the air.  The sky peeks in from above, bounded on all\nsides by the towering walls of the library.  Small bushes and flowers grow\nalong a well manicured walkway.  \n',129,131072,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15960,0,0,0,'A Small Courtyard','  A feeling of calm pervades the still air of this verdant garden.  Perfumed\nflowery scents waft about the air.  The sky peeks in from above, bounded on all\nsides by the towering walls of the library.  Small bushes and flowers grow\nalong a well manicured walkway.  Sliding doors to the east and south lead\ninto the library. \n',129,131072,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15961,0,0,0,'Library Foyer','  The entryway in the southeast corner unfolds magnificently into a voluminous\nlobby.  Gleaming stone walls stand proudly, magnifying even the slightest\nsound into a mighty crescendo.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated\nwith gold designs and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding\nwhite marble.  The interior of this room looks like the antithesis of\ndelicate, but still maintains a pure presentation of splendor.  A\nmagnificently polished set of steel doors lie to the southeast.  A sliding\ndoor leads to a courtyard to the west. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15962,0,0,0,'Library Walkway','  To call this ample passage a walkway seems like an understatement at best. \nGleaming stone walls stand proudly, magnifying even the slightest sound into a\nmighty crescendo.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated with gold\ndesigns and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white\nmarble. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15963,0,0,0,'Library Study Hall','  The stillness of the surrounding air provides a place for people to pursue\nquiet contemplation.  Tapestry adorned walls stand proudly, muting loud noises\ninto a soft buzz.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated with gold\ndesigns and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white\nmarble. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15964,0,0,0,'Library Study Hall','  The stillness of the surrounding air provides a place for people to pursue\nquiet contemplation.  Tapestry adorned walls stand proudly, muting loud noises\ninto a soft buzz.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated with gold\ndesigns and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white\nmarble. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15965,0,0,0,'Corner of a Small Courtyard','  A feeling of calm pervades the still air of this verdant garden.  Perfumed\nflowery scents waft about the air.  The sky peeks in from above, bounded on all\nsides by the towering walls of the library.  Small bushes and flowers grow\nalong a well manicured walkway.  \n',129,131072,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15966,0,0,0,'Corner of a Small Courtyard','  A feeling of calm pervades the still air of this verdant garden.  Perfumed\nflowery scents waft about the air.  The sky peeks in from above, bounded on all\nsides by the towering walls of the library.  Small bushes and flowers grow\nalong a well manicured walkway.  \n',129,131072,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(15967,0,0,0,'Library Walkway','  To call this ample passage a walkway seems like an understatement at best. \nGleaming stone walls stand proudly, magnifying even the slightest sound into a\nmighty crescendo.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated with gold\ndesigns and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white\nmarble. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15968,0,0,0,'Library Walkway','  To call this ample passage a walkway seems like an understatement at best. \nGleaming stone walls stand proudly, magnifying even the slightest sound into a\nmighty crescendo.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated with gold\ndesigns and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white\nmarble. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15969,0,0,0,'Library Study Hall','  The stillness of the surrounding air provides a place for people to pursue\nquiet contemplation.  Tapestry adorned walls stand proudly, muting loud noises\ninto a soft buzz.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated with gold\ndesigns and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white\nmarble. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15970,0,0,0,'Library Staircase','  A giant spiraling marble staircase corkscrews into the air in the middle of\nthis room.  Vaulted stone ceilings flank the edges of where the staircase\ndisappears above.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white marble. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15971,0,0,0,'Library Study Hall','  The stillness of the surrounding air provides a place for people to pursue\nquiet contemplation.  Tapestry adorned walls stand proudly, muting loud noises\ninto a soft buzz.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated with gold\ndesigns and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white\nmarble.  A stained glass window rests on the south wall. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(15972,0,0,0,'Library Study Hall','  The stillness of the surrounding air provides a place for people to pursue\nquiet contemplation.  Tapestry adorned walls stand proudly, muting loud noises\ninto a soft buzz.  Vaulted stone ceilings rise above, decorated with gold\ndesigns and patterns.  The bare floor is made of a cold unyielding white\nmarble. \n',129,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
