(16100,-10,39,-1,'A Paved Road','  It seems someone has widened the narrow path.  The road is made of tightly\nfitted yellow stones.  It continues to the west while to the east is a narrow\npath.  To the south is a large forest.  The tree-line has been moved back\nquite a bit from the road.  In the distance to the west you see a tower\nflying a white banner.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16101,-11,39,-1,'A Paved Road','  The road is made of tightly fitted yellow stones.  It continues to the\nnorthwest and east.  To the south is a large forest.  The tree-line has been\nmoved back quite a bit from the road.  In the distance to the west you see a\ntower flying a white banner.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16102,-12,40,-1,'A Paved Road','  The road is made of tightly fitted yellow stones.  It continues to the\nwest and southeast.  To the south is a large forest.  The tree-line has been\nmoved back quite a bit from the road.  In the distance to the west you see a\ntower flying a white banner.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16103,-13,40,-1,'A Paved Road','  The road is made of tightly fitted yellow stones.  It continues to the\nnorthwest and east.  To the south is a large forest.  The tree-line has been\nmoved back quite a bit from the road.  In the distance to the west you see a\ntower flying a white banner.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16104,-14,41,-1,'A Paved Road','  The road is made of tightly fitted yellow stones.  It continues to the\nwest and southeast.  To the south is a large forest.  The tree-line has been\nmoved back quite a bit from the road.  In the distance to the west you see a\ntower flying a white banner.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16105,-15,41,-1,'A Paved Road','  The road is made of tightly fitted yellow stones.  It continues to the\nsouthwest and east.  To the south is a large forest.  The tree-line has been\nmoved back quite a bit from the road.  To the west you see a tower flying a\nwhite banner.  To the southwest is a small settlement enclosed by tall wooden\nstakes.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16106,-16,40,-1,'A Paved Road','  This is a very well constructed road made of tightly fitted yellow stones.\nIt continues to the west and northeast.  To the south is a large forest.\nThe tree-line has been moved back quite a bit from the road.  To the south is a\nwall made of tall wooden stakes.  To the northwest you see a tower flying a\nwhite banner.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16107,-17,40,-1,'A Paved Road','  This is a very well constructed road made of tightly fitted yellow stones.\nIt continues to the west and east.  A dirt path branches off the road to the\nnorth and south.  You see a tower to the north flying a white banner.  To\nthe south is a closed gate.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16108,-18,40,-1,'A Paved Road','  This is a very well constructed road made of tightly fitted yellow stones.\nIt continues to the west and east.  To the south is a wall made of tall\nwooden stakes.  To the northeast you see a tower flying a white banner.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16109,-19,40,-1,'A Paved Road','  This is a very well constructed road made of tightly fitted yellow stones.\nIt continues to the west and east.  To the south is a wall made of tall\nwooden stakes.  To the northeast you see a tower flying a white banner.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16110,-20,40,-1,'A Paved Road','  This is a very well constructed road made of tightly fitted yellow stones.\nIt continues to the west and east.  To the south is a large forest.  The\ntree-line has been moved back quite a bit from the road.  To the northeast\nyou see a tower flying a white banner.  To the southeast is a small\nsettlement enclosed by a wall made of tall wooden stakes.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16111,-21,40,-1,'A Paved Road','  This is a very well constructed road made of tightly fitted yellow stones.\nIt continues to the southwest and east.  To the south is a large forest.\nThe tree-line has been moved back quite a bit from the road.  In the distance\nto the east you see a tower flying a white banner.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16112,-22,39,-1,'A Paved Road','  The road is made of yellow stones.  If you look closely, you can make out\nsome cracks in the mortar.  It continues to the west and northeast.  To the\nsouth is a large forest.  In the distance to the east you see a tower flying\na white banner.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16113,-23,39,-1,'A Paved Road','  The road is made of yellow stones.  If you look closely, you can make out\nsome cracks in the mortar.  It continues to the northwest and east.  To the\nsouth is a large forest.  In the distance to the east you see a tower flying\na white banner.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16114,-24,40,-1,'A Paved Road','  The road is made of yellow stones.  If you look closely, you can make out\nsome cracks in the mortar.  It continues to the southwest and southeast.  To\nthe south is a large forest.  In the distance to the east you see a tower\nflying a white banner.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16115,-25,39,-1,'A Paved Road','  The road is made of yellow stones.  If you look closely, you can make out\nsome cracks in the mortar.  It continues to the west and northeast.  To the\nsouth is a large forest.  In the distance to the east you see a tower flying\na white banner.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16116,-17,41,-1,'Dirt Path','  You are on a dirt path.  The gatekeep of a large tower is to the north of\nthe path.  To the south is an intersection in the main road.  The path seems\nto be very well traveled.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16117,-17,42,-1,'Killing Ground Between the Gates','  This is a small area between the outer and inner gates of the tower.\nTotally disguised as part of the thick walls of the tower as seen from\nthe outside, it makes the perfect trap for any invading force should they\nbreach the outer gates.  The tower gates lie to the north and south.\n',103,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16118,-17,43,-1,'Courtyard','  This wide open area is the parade ground of the tower.  This is where the\ntroops gather to receive accommodations, rebukes, punishments and hear\nstirring speeches given by their commander.  To the east is a large stable\nwhere mounts of all kinds can be kept.  North is the entrance to the tower.\n',103,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16119,-16,43,-1,'Stable','  The sweet scent of manure invades your sense of smell the minute you step\ninto the stable.  There are stalls of all shapes and sizes in this room.\nEnough varieties to accommodate most of the animals used as mounts.\n',103,139432,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16120,-18,44,-1,'Barracks','  The barracks was built to hold at most one hundred soldiers.  It is a very\nlarge room with good ventilation.  Plain and simple, without much decoration,\nas it should be since it was made to house soldiers.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16121,-17,44,-1,'Stairwell','  This is the main hallway and intersection of the tower.  Captured banners\nand other trophies are displayed here for all to see.  The staircase is in\nthe southwest corner of the room.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16122,-16,44,-1,'Mess Hall','  Tables are placed in neat rows across the room with benches on both\nsides.  Even though the mess hall is large, it cannot hold all the\noccupants of the tower all at once forcing the soldiers to eat in shifts.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16123,-18,45,-1,'Barracks','  The barracks was built to hold at most one hundred soldiers.  It is a very\nlarge room with good ventilation.  Plain and simple, without much decoration,\nas it should be since it was made to house soldiers.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16124,-17,45,-1,'Armory','  This room functions as the armory and storage room.  Everything appears\nto be pretty well organized.  The northwest corner of the room is reserved\nfor the foodstuffs.  In the northeast corner are barrels of oil and water\nused during sieges.  Racks of weapons and armors fill the rest of the room.\nNestled beside every rack is a pile of neatly stacked quivers bristling\nwith arrows.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16125,-16,45,-1,'Barracks','  The barracks was built to hold at most one hundred soldiers.  It is a very\nlarge room with good ventilation.  Plain and simple, without much decoration,\nas it should be since it was made to house soldiers.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16126,-17,46,-1,'Latrine','  The smell of the latrine is not as bad as is expected of a place filled\nwith humanoids.  It is all due to the cleaning servants and an efficient\nsewage disposal system.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16127,-18,44,0,'Laboratory','  The acrid smell of sulphur permeates your nose.  Did someone just throw a\nfireball in here?  Maybe it was just an experiment gone bad.  Various\ncontraptions lie on the floor.  You have a feeling you should not touch\nanything in here.  Something bad might happen.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16128,-17,44,0,'Stairwell','  This is the main hallway and intersection of the tower.  Captured banners\nand other trophies are displayed here for all to see.  The staircase is in\nthe southwest corner of the room.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16129,-16,44,0,'Altar','  This is the altar room.  Servants, soldiers, and officers alike come\nhere to pray to their deities and put their minds at rest.  A raised\ndais with a stone altar rests in the center of the room.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16130,-18,45,0,'Mage\'s Quarters','  This room is very large and spacious.  Books of all kinds ranging from\nanatomy to theories of mathematics lie on the floor in piles.  A small table\nwith a scrying device on top of it is in the center of the room.  An unmade\nbed rests in the northwest corner.  Either a very distracted individual or a\nslovenly pig lives here.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16131,-17,45,0,'Captain\'s Quarters','  This room acts as both office and sleeping quarters for the commander\nof the troops residing in the tower.  A desk filled with neatly stacked\npapers faces the door.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16132,-16,45,0,'Cleric\'s Quarters','  This sparsely furnished room resembles a monk\'s cell.  A pallet lies\nin the center of the room.  The walls are bare except for the mural on\nthe north wall.  A small window with a soft glowing aura surrounding it\nallows fresh air to enter the room.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16133,-17,46,0,'Latrine','  The smell of the latrine is not as bad as is expected of a place filled\nwith humanoids.  It is all due to the cleaning servants and an efficient\nsewage disposal system.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16134,-18,44,1,'On Top of the Tower','  Fierce winds constantly rake the top of the tower attempting to pluck\na soldier from it.  From this vantage point, a good view of the surrounding\narea is available.  To the south is a large forest.\n',103,139584,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16135,-17,44,1,'On Top of the Tower','  Fierce winds constantly rake the top of the tower attempting to pluck\na soldier from it.  From this vantage point, a good view of the surrounding\narea is available.  To the south is a large forest.  North lies a sparsely\nwooded plain which eventually coalesces into a larger forest.\n',103,139584,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
