(16138,-17,45,1,'On Top of the Tower','  Fierce winds constantly rake the top of the tower attempting to pluck\na soldier from it.  From this vantage point, a good view of the surrounding\narea is available.  To the south is a large forest.  North lies a sparsely\nwooded plain which eventually coalesces into a larger forest.\n',103,139584,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16139,-16,45,1,'On Top of the Tower','  Fierce winds constantly rake the top of the tower attempting to pluck\na soldier from it.  From this vantage point, a good view of the surrounding\narea is available.  To the south is a large forest.\n',103,139584,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16140,-19,38,-1,'Backyard','  This is the backyard of the kitchen.  A pile of firewood lies in the\nnortheast corner.  A well is dug into the ground in the center of the yard.\nTo the west and south are the walls separating the trading post from the\nforest.  North is the back-room of the tavern.  You can see into the smoky\nroom through a window.  To the east is a door leading to the kitchen.\n',103,139264,21,0,0,0,0,0,3,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16141,-18,39,0,'Private Dining Room','  This is a large dining room above the tavern.  Built and funded by rich\nmerchants who wanted a private meeting place to discuss business above the\nhubbub of the commoners, it is richly furnished.  A cozy fireplace is built\ninto the north wall for use during cold nights.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16142,-18,39,-1,'Silver Cup Tavern','  This establishment is the only other building in the settlement made of\nstone other than the tower to the north.  Like most taverns and inns in\nsmall villages, it is a gathering place for the locals to learn the latest\nnews of the outside world from the travelers who stop by.  A staircase\nin the southwest corner leads up to a private dining room.  A door to the\nsouth apparently leads to the kitchen from the heavy traffic of servants\ngoing in and out.  To the west is the back room of the tavern.\n',103,172216,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16143,-17,39,-1,'Dirt Path','  You are on a dirt path that runs through a small settlement.  It continues\nto the south.  To the west is a large building with a sign hanging from it.\nA building to the east has the look of a warehouse.  To the north is a gate\nthat allows access out of the settlement.  The path seems to be very well\ntraveled.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16144,-16,39,-1,'Lisa\'s Food Supplies','  You are standing in a large well swept room devoid of any dust at all.\nThe back of the room is filled with crates stacked neatly together.  Workers\nbusily fill empty crates with foodstuffs bought from local farmers and\ntraveling merchants.  Suddenly, you notice how clean your travel worn\nclothes are.  It seems like the dust and grime were left outside when you\nwalked into the warehouse.\n',103,172216,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16145,-18,38,-1,'Kitchen','  This is a large kitchen.  Pots, pans, and other kinds of cooking tools\nhang from two ropes strewn across the room within easy reach of the cook.\nA large table is set up in the middle of the room for chopping up foodstuffs.\nA row of cabinets parallel to the table is affixed to the ceiling.  A large\nfireplace is built into the center of the west wall of the kitchen.  There\nare four brick ovens, two on each side of the fireplace.  A window facing\nthe road to the east helps ventilate the room.  Exits to the north and west\nleads out of the kitchen.\n',103,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16146,-17,38,-1,'Dirt Path','  You are on a dirt path that runs through a small settlement.  It continues\nto the north.  There are two buildings, one on each side of the path built\nagainst the walls enclosing the settlement.  The smell of roast and fresh\nbaked bread wafts from a window to the west.  A door gives access to the\nbuilding to the east.  To the south is a gate that leads out of the\nsettlement.  The path seems to be very well traveled.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16147,-16,38,-1,'Fencing Post','  Squeezed in between the wall of the compound and the building to the\nnorth, this small room was built after the rest of the compound was\ncompleted.  Unkempt and dirty with plaster peeling from the walls, its\na wonder anyone would stay in such a place.\n',103,131272,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,60,0,'',NULL),
(16148,-17,37,-1,'Dirt Path','  You are on a small dirt path.  It continues south into a large forest.  To\nthe north are the gates to a small trade post enclosed by a wall made of tall\nwooden stakes.  The road seems to have once been very well traveled, but\nthe surrounding vegetation is slowly consuming its presence.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16149,-19,39,-1,'Backroom','  A layer of smoke from the fireplace covers the room.  The warmth from\nthe fire makes this room a natural place for the locals to gather on\ncold rainy nights.  There\'s a window just above you here.\n',103,139272,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16150,-24,-51,0,'A Sinkhole in the Trail','  You feel warm air coming from a large sinkhole in the trail which\nhas a slight odor of sulfur in it.  The sinkhole has what looks like a\npath running along it into the depths of the earth.  It appears that with\na little caution you should be able to traverse the trail downwards.\n',103,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16151,-24,-51,-1,'On a Path in a Sinkhole','  Hot air with a hint of sulfur raises out of the hole around you into The\nworld above.  The walls here are made of dirt with a faint yellow tint.\nThe path you are on continues down into darkness or up into the light of\nThe World.\n',103,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16152,-24,-51,-2,'On a Path in a Sinkhole','  Hot air with a hint of sulfur raises out of the hole around you into\nThe World above.  The walls here are made of dirt with a faint yellow tint.\nThe path you are on continues down into darkness or up into the light of\nThe World.  You see a glimmer of light coming from below.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(16153,-24,-51,-3,'In a Cavern at the Bottom of a Sinkhole','  The sinkhole from above ends abruptly here as it met a solid mass of\nobsidian it could no longer penetrate.  Appearing man made a cavern has\nbeen carved into the obsidian leading down into the earth below.  The light\nof the sky can just barely be seen above you, while below you can just make\nout the light from a flickering torch.  The path is traversable upwards or\nyou can follow the cavern path as it slopes gently downwards.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(16154,-24,-51,-4,'At the Bottom of a Cavern','  This is a small room at the bottom of a sloping cavern.  A crude stone\ndoor lies on the south wall.  A gently sloping cavern leads up.  You feel\na cool breeze coming from above while a large amount of heat comes from\nbehind the door.  Two torches rest in the east and west walls keeping this\nroom lit.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(16155,-24,-52,-4,'Next to a Guard Post','  The passage here was carved out of solid obsidian.  The passage is\nextremely hot, and the heat seems to be coming from the south.  To the west\nyou see a small guard post, while to the south is the start of a tunnel.\nOn the north wall there is a crude stone door.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16156,-25,-52,-4,'A Guard Post','  This guard post is set up as the first line of defense against any\ninvaders from the surface and is carved from the surrounding obsidian.\nThere is a set of bunks set against the north wall for any guards posted\nhere to sleep on, and a bench set up next to a window in the east wall.\nThe window allows the guards to watch the tunnel without those in the\ntunnel being able to see them.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(16157,-24,-53,-4,'Along a Stone Tunnel','  The passage here is carved out of the surrounding obsidian.  The passage\nis lit by a red glow coming from the east which may have something to do\nwith the wave of heat emanating from that direction.  You think you hear\nwhat sounds like rushing water coming from the east as well.  The walls\nare angled to reflect the light down the passage to the north.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(16158,-23,-53,-4,'Along a Stone Tunnel','  A bright red glow is coming from a lava stream to the south.  The heat\nhere is almost unbearable.  The walls here are made from polished obsidian\nto reflect the glow along the passage to the west keeping the whole\npassage lit.  There is a bridge spanning the stream to the south allowing\npassage across the stream.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16159,-23,-54,-4,'On a Bridge Over a Stream of Lava','  The thunder of rushing water comes to your ears.  The only thing wrong is\nthat the liquid is not water, but lava.  The bridge you stand on is over a\nlava stream moving as fast as a river.  The bridge is only five feet above\nthe lava and the heat coming from the lava is extreme.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(16160,-23,-55,-4,'Along a Stone Tunnel','  A bright red glow is coming from a lava stream to the north, making the\nheat here almost unbearable.  The walls here are made from polished obsidian\nthat reflect the glow along the tunnel to the west to keep the whole\npassage lit.  There is a bridge spanning the stream to the north allowing\npassage across the stream.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(16161,-24,-55,-4,'Along a Stone Tunnel','  A deep red glow comes from the east and west.  Westward you see a slow\nmoving lava stream crossable by a stone bridge while to the east the\npassage you are in continues.  A sound similar to rushing water can\nalso be heard coming from the east and to the west a large gate is\nvisible.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16162,-25,-55,-4,'On a Bridge Before a Gate','  The bridge you stand on crosses a slow moving lava stream.  The light\nfrom the stream baths the surrounding area in a bright glow.  The heat\ncoming from the stream is causing you to sweat profusely.  Set in the west\nwall is a large gate made from obsidian while to the east is a passage\nthrough the obsidian leading back to the outside world.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16163,-26,-55,-4,'Entrance to a Small Outpost','  Set in the east wall is a large stone gate while to the west is a huge\ncavern.  Contained in the cavern is an outpost with a small keep on the far\nwestern side.  A red glow coming from the west lights this room along with\na glow coming from beyond the gate.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16164,-27,-55,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running in a circle about the outpost.  Along the path an\noccasional small building can be spotted.  Off to the west you see a small\nkeep but your way is blocked by a huge lake of lava.  To the east is a\ntunnel leading to a gate while to the north and south the path continues.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16165,-27,-56,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running through the whole outpost.  Around you you see an\noccasional small building off the path.  The path runs in a circle around\nthe outpost.  Off to the northwest you see a small keep.  To the south a\ncave-in has blocked the passage through a small tunnel.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16166,-27,-54,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running about the outpost with an occasional small\nbuilding set just back from its edge.  The path continues to the north and\nthe south, but is blocked to the west by a lake of lava.  Beyond the\nlake you can see a small keep.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16167,-27,-53,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running about the outpost with an occasional small\nbuilding set just back from its edge.  The path continues to the north and\nthe south, but is blocked to the west by a lake of lava.  Beyond the\nlake you can see a small keep.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16168,-27,-52,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running about the outpost with an occasional small\nbuilding set just back from its edge.  The path continues to the north and\nthe south, but is blocked to the west by a lake of lava.  Beyond the\nlake you can see a small keep.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16169,-27,-51,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running about the outpost with an occasional small\nbuilding set just back from its edge.  The path continues to the south and\nthe west where you can see a small keep.  To the north a door appears to\nlead into a small building.  Passage to the southwest is blocked by a lake\nof lava.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16170,-27,-50,-4,'In a Small Home','  This home appears to belong to a rather militant person.  The walls are\nlined with weapons and armor.  There is a mat spread out on the floor to\nserve as a bed.  There is a metal table sitting in the center of the room\nand a lava filled hole at the back of the room.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,8,96,0,'',NULL),
(16171,-28,-51,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running through the outpost.  Around you you see an\noccasional small building off the path which runs in a circle around\nthe whole outpost.  Off to the west you see a small keep.  To the west and\neast the path continues.  To the south passage is blocked by a large\nlava lake.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16172,-29,-51,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running through the outpost.  Around you can be seen an\noccasional small building off the path, which runs in a circle around\nthe whole outpost.  Off to the west you see a small keep along the\ncontinueing path, which also moves farther to the east.  To the south is\na door leading into what looks like a holy building of some sorts.  Along\nthe sides of the building you see a large lava lake.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16173,-29,-52,-4,'Temple of the Flame','  This room\'s walls are made of fire.  There are pews lined up facing a\nlarge altar.  The ceiling is made of some red metal and shaped to focus the\nlight in the room on the altar.  Long tapestries hang on the wall behind\nthe altar.  The altar is most likely dedicated to a deity of fire.  There is\na door in the north wall leading back to the outpost.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,30,180,5,'',NULL),
(16174,-30,-50,-4,'In a Small Home','  This house looks more like barracks than a house.  There are two rows of\nbunks on the east and west walls.  A large table is in the center of the\nroom and six foot lockers line the north wall.  A strange red glow emits\nfrom a hole in the floor along the north wall.  On the south wall is a door\nleading back to the outpost.\n',103,131081,61,0,0,0,0,0,8,96,0,'',NULL),
(16175,-30,-51,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running through the outpost.  Around you you see an\noccasional small building off the path which runs in a circle around\nthe whole outpost.  Off to the west you see a small keep.  To the west and\neast the path continues.  To the south passage is blocked by a large lava\nlake.  There is a door to the north leading into a small building.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16176,-31,-51,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running through the outpost.  Around you you see an\noccasional small building off the path which runs in a circle around\nthe whole outpost.  Off to the southwest you see a small keep.  To the\nsouth and east the path continues.  To the southeast passage is blocked\nby a large lava lake.  There is a door to the west that leads into a\nsmall building.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16177,-32,-51,-4,'In a Small Home','This house is kept neat and tidy.  There is a large table on the south\nwall, and a large bed along the north wall.  There is a set table sitting\nin the center of the room and a small lava filled hole along the back wall.\nThere is an open chest filled with toys in the northwest corner.\n',0,131081,61,0,0,0,0,0,8,96,0,'',NULL),
(16178,-31,-52,-4,'On a Bridge Over a Lava Stream','  This is a bridge over a lava stream coming off of a large lava lake from\nthe east.  The stream splits a little to the west forming a moat around the\nkeep to the west.  The bridge exits to a path through the outpost to the\nnorth and south sides.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16179,-31,-53,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost',' This path seems to run throughout the outpost.  Occasionally a small\nbuilding can be seen off the path which continues north and south.  A\nsmall path branches off to the west leading to the keep, while to the east\na large lake of lava halts all movement.  Along the path to the north it\nseems a bridge of some sorts spans a stream of lava.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16180,-31,-54,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running through the outpost.  Around you you see an\noccasional small building off the path which runs in a circle around\nthe whole outpost.  Off to the west you see a small keep.  To the north and\nsouth the path continues.  To the east is a door leading into a small\nbuilding.  Off to the sides of the building you see a large lava lake.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16181,-30,-54,-4,'In a Small Home','  This house appears to be just large enough for one person.  There is a\nsmall cot lying along the north wall.  A hole in the floor filled with\nlava is along the east wall.  A messy table rests on the floor in the\ncenter of the room.  Objects lie scattered all over the floor with no\norder what so ever.\n',103,131081,61,0,0,0,0,0,8,96,0,'',NULL),
(16182,-31,-55,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running through the outpost.  Around you you see an\noccasional small building off the path which runs in a circle around\nthe whole outpost.  Off to the northwest you see a small keep.  To the\nnorth and south the path continues.  To the east passage is blocked by\na large lava lake.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16183,-31,-56,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running through the outpost.  Around you you see an\noccasional small building off the path which runs in a circle around\nthe whole outpost.  Off to the northwest you see a small keep.  To the\nnorth and east the path continues.  The northeast the way is blocked\nby a large lava lake.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16184,-30,-56,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running through the outpost.  Around you you see an\noccasional small building off the path which runs in a circle around\nthe whole outpost.  Off to the northwest you see a small keep.  To the\neast and west the path continues.  The way to the north is blocked by\na large lava lake.  To the south is a door that leads into a small building.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16185,-30,-57,-4,'In a Small Home','  This house is home to a small family.  There are two beds in the room,\nthe larger one rests in the southwest corner while the smaller one lies\nalong the east wall.  There is a curtain hanging from the ceiling near the\nlarger bed.  A small table lies in the northeast corner and a hole in the\nfloor is in the southeast.  There is a red glow coming out of the hole.\n',103,131081,61,0,0,0,0,0,8,96,0,'',NULL),
(16186,-29,-56,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running through the outpost.  Around you you see an\noccasional small building off the path which runs in a circle around\nthe whole outpost.  Off to the northwest you see a small keep.  To the\neast and west the path continues.  To the north passage is blocked by\na large lava lake.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16187,-28,-56,-4,'On a Path Through the Outpost','  This is a path running through the outpost.  Around you you see an\noccasional small building off the path which runs in a circle around\nthe whole outpost.  Off to the north west you see a small keep.  To the\neast and west the path continues.  To the north passage is blocked by\na large lava lake.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(16188,-32,-53,-4,'A Hall Before a Small Keep','  This hall is lit by a sickly red glow coming from a lava moat to the\nwest.  The moat is crossable by a bridge made from pure obsidian.  Off to\nthe west you see a small keep.  To the east contained in a huge cavern is\nan outpost.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(16189,-33,-53,-4,'On a Bridge Before a Small Keep','  This bridge crosses a moat of lava.  To the west is a small keep and to\nthe east is a huge cavern containing a small outpost.  The lava flowing in\nthe moat provides ample light for the surrounding area.  The sickly red glow\ncoming from the moat pulsates off you skin and armor making you feel\nsick to your stomach.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16190,-34,-53,-4,'Next to the Guard Posts Before a Small Keep','  This room is lit by two torches set in the entrances of two guard posts,\none on the north and one on the south.  To the east is a hallway leading\ninto the outpost.  The path to the west leads into a small keep made from\nobsidian bricks.  The path to the west is blocked by a portcullis.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16191,-35,-53,-4,'Entrance to a Small Keep','  This is the entrance to the small keep.  There is a set of stairs to the\nwest leading into the keep itself, but they appear to dead end into a\ntrapdoor in the ceiling.  There is a portcullis to the east leading to\nthe outpost grounds.  Two torches are set in the north and south walls to\nkeep this room lit.  The walls here are made from bricks of obsidian\nheld together by pumice mortar.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16192,-34,-52,-4,'A Guard Post','  This guard post has two bunks, one on the east wall and one on the west.\nThe room is lit by a lava moat that the guard post was built over.  There\nis no north wall to the room and the floor drops off right into the moat.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(16193,-34,-54,-4,'A Guard Post','  This guard post has two bunks, one on the east wall and one on the west.\nThe room is lit by a lava moat that the guard post was built over.  There\nis no south wall to the room and the floor drops off right into the moat.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(16194,-35,-54,-3,'A Guard Post','This guardpost houses two of the keep\'s commander\'s personal guards.\nThere is a doorway to the north allowing easy sight and access to the\nhallway.  There are two bunks against the south wall for the guards to\nsleep on.  The room is lit by two torches set in the east and west walls.\n',0,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(16195,-35,-53,-3,'A Hallway in a Small Keep','  This is the east end of a short hallway running through this keep.  Set\nin the floor here is a trapdoor.  Off to the west you can see that the\nhallway ends in a door.  To the south you can see a guard post of sorts.\nThe walls here are made from bricks of obsidian held together by pumice\nmortar.  The hallway is lit by two torches set on the north wall.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,6,120,0,'',NULL),
(16196,-36,-53,-3,'A Hallway in a Small Keep','  This is the middle of a short hallway running through this keep.  To the\nwest you see the hallway deadends into a door, while to the east the\nhallway deadends at a trapdoor in the floor.  The walls here are made from\nobsidian bricks held together by mortar made from pumice.  The hallway is\nlit by two torches set in the north and south walls.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16197,-37,-53,-3,'At the End of A Hallway in a Small Keep','  This is the west end of the hall in this keep.  A sturdy stone door rests\nin the west wall, while the hall continues east leading out of the keep.\nThe walls here are made from obsidian bricks kept together by pumice\nmortar.  This part of the hall is lit by two small torches set in the\nnorth and south walls.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16198,-38,-53,-3,'Outpost Commander\'s Room','  This is both an office and sleeping area.  An orderly desk sits in the\ncenter of the room.  Behind the desk is a well made bed.  The room is lit\nby two pools of lava in the northeast and southeast corners.  A large\nsolid obsidian door rests in the east wall.  The floor in the room is\nhighly polished stone.  The walls and ceiling have been carved out from\nthe surrounding obsidian.\n',103,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(16199,0,0,0,'Fire Vault','  This room is made from fire.  The walls are fire, the ceiling is fire,\nand the floor is fire.  The floor is made of some type of solid fire, but\nthe ceiling and walls are not.\n',103,175273,62,0,0,0,0,0,5,120,0,'',NULL),
(16200,37,62,-3,'Operating Room','  Here is the main operating room where the Master Surgeon of Amber works.\nIt is well lit and unbelievably clean.  If he\'s not too busy, perhaps\nhe might cure whatever ailment you may have.  A door leads south.\n',105,207021,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16201,38,62,-3,'Pharmacy','  Welcome to the Amber pharmacy.  This little shop has the drugs you will\nneed to get better.  On the floor is a broken vial with green liquid coming\nfrom it.  YUCK!  You see an exit south.\n',105,166077,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16202,39,62,-3,'Staff Lounge','  This lounge is quite comfortable.  So, this is where the staff just kicks\nback and relaxes.  You notice very few people here, if any.  Well, guess\nthe staff doesn\'t get much of a break here.  A window is set in the northern\nwall.  A screen lies to the south.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16203,37,61,-3,'Emergency Entrance','  This is the emergency entrance of Amber Memorial.  Here is where\nthe very ill come in hopes that they may be cured.  A black marble\nfloor extends to the east towards a foyer.  Doors are seen to the\nnorth and south.  A staircase to the north of the room leads up\nand down.  To the west are glass doors leading back out onto Amber.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16204,38,61,-3,'Main Foyer','  This is the grand foyer.  It is huge and its black marble floor extends\nin all directions.  Hallways lead to the south and west.  Doors lie to your\nnorth, east, and southeast.\n',105,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16205,39,61,-3,'Grand Conference Room','  The conference room is quite large.  This is where the staff meets to\ndiscuss administrative topics about the hospital.  To the north is a\nscreen and a door leads westward back to the foyer.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16206,37,60,-3,'Emergency Room','  This emergency room is for those patients in need of urgent care.  Not\nto be confused with near-death experiences which are handled by the\nIntensive Care Unit of this hospital.  The room has a dirty appearance\nto it due to the high activity that goes on here.  A door lies to the\nnorth.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,19,'',NULL),
(16207,38,60,-3,'Amber Memorial\'s Main Lobby','  You are now standing in the grand lobby of Amber Memorial Hospital,\nAmber\'s great hospital and perhaps the largest in the land.  The lobby\nis huge with vaulted ceilings and is quite spacious.  The black marble\nfloor is sparkling clean.  To the north, you see a large foyer.  To the\nsouth is a glass door leading towards the town of Amber.\n',105,131084,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16208,39,60,-3,'Small Chapel','  This is a small non-denominational chapel built into the hospital\nfor those to pray for their loved ones.  Perhaps your deity may help\nyou out if you have been good.  Scattered around the room are\nnumerous statues of deities throughout the land.  A door leading back\nto the foyer is to the northwest.\n',105,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16209,37,62,-2,'Labor & Delivery','  This place looks like a disaster zone.  There must be a lot of activity\nthat goes on here.  Is there a baby boom on Sneezy?  Here, expecting\nmothers come and wait until they are ready to deliver.  A door lies to the\nsouth and the room continues to the east.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16210,38,62,-2,'Delivery Room','  Here is where new babies are born in Amber.  The room is quite large\nin order to handle the large amounts of people who can be in here at\none time.  By the looks of things, it seems that this room has been\nused a lot lately.  A door leads to the east and the room continues\nto the west.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16211,39,62,-2,'Observation Room','  This is where newly-borns are put under observation until they are ready\nto be taken home.  A large glass window is to the south.  A door lies to\nthe west.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16212,37,61,-2,'2nd Floor of Hospital','  This is the second floor of the hospital.  A black marble hallway leads\nto the east.  A staircase leads up and down.  Doors are to the north and\nsouth.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16213,38,61,-2,'Hallway','  This hallway has a black marble floor that stretches to the east\nand west.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16214,39,61,-2,'East End of Hallway','  This is the east end of the hallway.  This is where family members can\nlook at their newly-born through the window to the north.  To the south\nappears to be some sort of lounge.  The hallway expands westward.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16215,37,60,-2,'OB/Gyn Examination Room','  This is where gynecological exams and prenatal checks are given.  The\nair is quite chilly in here.  Curtains are set up in here to screen\noff the patient from others who may enter the room.  There are doors\nto the east and north.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16216,38,60,-2,'Doctor Short\'s office','  This office is huge.  It has been well decorated.  On the wall are\nvarious paintings and some degrees showing the qualifications of this\ndoctor.  Looking around, you notice some strange papers on a desk.\nA door lies to the west.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16217,39,60,-2,'Lounge and Snack Area','  This lounge was set up for visitors to wait here and relax.  It\nlooks quite inviting.  A window to the south looks out upon the\nfair city of Amber.  To the north is a hallway.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16218,37,62,-1,'Block 301','  This room is enclosed by padded walls all around it.  The room is\nextremely dark and damp.  Mold is noticed on the floor and walls.\nWhat human being could live in here, it\'s too unsanitary for even\na sewer rat.  There is a padded door with a slit in it to the\nsoutheast.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16219,38,62,-1,'Block 302','  This room is enclosed by padded walls all around it.  The room is\nextremely dark and damp.  Mold is noticed on the floor and walls.\nWhat human being could live in here, it\'s too unsanitary for even\na sewer rat.  There is a padded door with a slit in it to the south.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16220,39,62,-1,'Block 303','  This room is enclosed by padded walls all around it.  The room is\nextremely dark and damp.  Mold is noticed on the floor and walls.\nWhat human being could live in here, it\'s too unsanitary for even\na sewer rat.  There is a padded door with a slit in it to the\nsouthwest.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16221,37,61,-1,'Psychiatric Ward','  You have reached a poorly lit floor.  This is the psychiatric floor\nof Amber.  Here, the mentally insane go.  A sign is posted on the west\nwall.  To the east, you make out a desk.  A staircase leads up and down.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16222,38,61,-1,'Guard Desk','  This is where the guard watching this floor sits.  It\'s a large room\nconnecting many smaller ones.  The poor lighting here gives you an eerie\nfeeling.  Padded doors with slits on them lie to the northwest, north,\nnortheast, southwest, south, and southeast.  A large oaken door lies to\nthe east.  Westwards is a staircase.\n',105,131084,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16223,39,61,-1,'Doctor Krueger\'s Office','  Here you see a well-lit office.  This is where the head psychiatrist\nworks.  This room has no windows and only a door to the west leads\nout.  The room is quite plain and very few objects are present.\nPerhaps that\'s a good thing considering who this doctor is dealing with.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16224,37,60,-1,'Block 304','  This room is enclosed by padded walls all around it.  The room is\nextremely dark and damp.  Mold is noticed on the floor and walls.\nWhat human being could live in here, it\'s too unsanitary for even a\nsewer rat.  There is a padded door with a slit in it to the northeast.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16225,38,60,-1,'Block 305','  This room is enclosed by padded walls all around it.  The room is\nextremely dark and damp.  Mold is noticed on the floor and walls.\nWhat human being could live in here, it\'s too unsanitary for even a\nsewer rat.  There is a padded door with a slit in it to the north.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16226,39,60,-1,'Block 306','  This room is enclosed by padded walls all around it.  The room is\nextremely dark and damp.  Mold is noticed on the floor and walls.\nWhat human could live in here, it\'s too unsanitary for even a sewer\nrat.  There is a padded door with a slit in it to the northwest.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16227,37,62,0,'Staff Sleeping Area','  This room is for the staff of this floor.  They sleep here so that they\nmay be immediately called when needed.  The room looks plain, but you\nwonder how often anyone ever sleeps here anyways.  There is a door to the\nsoutheast.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16228,38,62,0,'Recovery Room 1','  This room is for those patients who have undergone treatment, but still\nneed to be under close observation due to their condition.  It\'s comforting\nto know that an excellent staff is only a shout away.  A window on the\nnorth wall looks out upon the beautiful Botanical Gardens of Amber.\nA door leads to the south.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16229,39,62,0,'Spare Operating Room','  This room is used as a spare operating room, just in case it\'s needed.\nAlthough not as equipped as the main trauma room, it\'s still quite\nsufficient to heal a needed person.  A door leads south.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16230,37,61,0,'Intensive Care Floor','  Welcome to the Intensive Care Unit.  Here, doctors try to save those\nwho are near death.  This floor is always prepared for the worst case\nscenario.  It is highly clean and well supplied.  The floor continues\nto the east while a staircase leads downward.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16231,38,61,0,'Center of ICU','  This is the center of the ICU.  Here, one is connected to most of the\nfloor.  During times of emergencies, this room can be highly congested.\nDoors are to the northwest, north, southwest, and south.  To the east,\nthere is a large room.  A staircase lies to the west.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,17,'',NULL),
(16232,39,61,0,'Trauma Room','  This room is where newly flown-in patients are quickly taken care of.\nOnly the best of care is given here.  The staff here is trained to work\nmiracles and bring people back from near-death experiences.  Doors lie\nto the north and south.  A room lies to the west.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16233,37,60,0,'Discussion Room','  This discussion room is used by the ICU staff to brainstorn and\ndiscuss treatment options for those under their care.  It\'s also used\nfor just kicking back and relaxing on their free time, whenever that\nmay be.  You see a door to the northeast.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16234,38,60,0,'Recovery Room 2','  This room is used for patients who have undergone treatment, but because\nof their condition, they still need to be under observation.  It\'s\ncomforting to know that an excellent staff is only a shout away.  A window\nto the south looks out upon the docks of Amber.  A door lies to the north.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16235,39,60,0,'Supply Room','  This is the supply room for the ICU.  It is the most supplied room in\nthe hospital.  If you can\'t find it here, it probably doesn\'t exist.\nThen again, someone may have taken it.  A door lies to the north.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16236,37,62,-4,'Private Laboratory','  This is the private laboratory of the pathologist, Dr.  Dimento.  He\nlikes to run his own tests to speed up his work.  You notice black soot\nmarks on the walls.  A door leads eastward.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16237,38,62,-4,'Autopsy Room','  This room is where the pathologist down here does his many autopsies.\nThe room is dark and cold.  You notice doors to the west and south\nof you.  A large oak door lies to the east.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16238,39,62,-4,'Dr Dimento\'s Office','  This is the private office of the pathologist, Dr.  Dimento.  It is here\nthat he lives his solitary life.  After all, who is crazy enough to visit\nhim.  His office is decorated with silk wallpapering and Persian rugs.\nObviously, this guy makes good money.  A door leads back out to the west.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,4,'',NULL),
(16239,37,61,-4,'Basement','  You have reached the basement of the hospital.  No one ever comes down\nhere for obvious reasons.  It\'s cold, dark, and damp.  But you know that\nsomeone has to come down here.  Doors lie to the south and east.  A\nstaircase leads upwards.  A sign is posted here.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL);
INSERT INTO `room` VALUES (16240,38,61,-4,'Cold Room','  This room is freezing.  Much colder than the other rooms.  This is where\nthey keep the many bodies that must undergo autopsies.  The room extends\nto the east and south.  A door leads north and west.\n',105,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16241,39,61,-4,'Cold Room','  This room is freezing.  It is much colder than the rest.  This is where\nthey keep the many bodies which must undergo autopsies.  The room extends\nto the west and southwest.  You feel immense heat coming from an iron door\nto the south.  Something is written on the door.\n',105,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16242,37,60,-4,'Laboratory','  This laboratory is where they do general tests for patients throughout\nthe hospital.  If a test must be done, the technician in here does it\nand sends the results to the doctors above.  A door lies to the north.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16243,38,60,-4,'Cold Room','  This room is freezing.  It\'s much colder than the rest.  This is where\nthey keep the bodies that must undergo autopsies.  The room extends to the\nnorth and northeast.\n',105,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16244,39,60,-4,'Incinerating Room','  This is the incinerating room.  When bodies are done being examined and\nthey are not claimed by anyone for proper burial, they are exhumed here.\nThe room is very warm and a welcome relief from the cold rooms outside.\nA door leads northward.\n',105,131080,55,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16245,38,62,1,'Roc\'s Nest','  On the roof here is a huge nest expanding in all directions.  The nest\nconsists of huge limbs and other material.  In it, you notice some bones\nthat look like they came from a caribou.  A railing blocks your path to\nthe west and north.  To the south lies a door.  The roof continues towards\nthe east.\n',105,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16246,39,62,1,'Large Landing Pad','  Painted on the roof here is a gigantic circle with an X on it.  It\nlooks like this is a landing pad of some sort.  But for what??\nRailings are to your north and east to prevent a possible fall.  The\nroof continues to the west and south.\n',105,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16247,38,61,1,'Roc Rider\'s Quarters','  This is where the person who flies the Roc lives.  It is a modest\nabode.  Especially for one who risks his life to fly that thing.\nOn the walls are many certificates from the hospital commending him\nfor his service.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16248,39,61,1,'Roof of the Hospital','  You are now on the roof of the hospital.  You feel a swift, cold\nbreeze run past your cheeks.  The view of Amber from up here is breath-\ntaking.  There are railings here to the east and south to prevent you\nfrom accidently falling off the roof.  The roof continues to the north.\n',105,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16249,40,62,-4,'Secret Stash','  You have found the secret stash of the pathologist, Dr.  Dimento.  So,\nthis is the guy who has been stealing supplies and money from the hospital.\nThis little room is quite small and is used as a secret storage chamber.\nYou see a bookshelf with a misplaced anatomy book to the west.\n',105,131080,12,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,4,'',NULL),
(16250,0,0,0,'A Dark Walkway','A narrow decrepit stone path leads north and south from here.  \nThe path is decaying and in a state of disrepair.  Large weeds have \nsprung up between the stones, completely obscuring the path.\nTo the north a decaying structure creaks and \ngroans. The large wooden building, although still showing hints of \nits past prestige, appears ready to crumble into rubble at any moment.  \nOminous looking trees tower above the path, blotting out light and \nmuffling noise.  The wind whips through the trees and rattles the structure \nto the north. \n',-1,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16251,0,0,0,'Decayed Smoking Room','The fragmented remains of oak furniture lie scattered about the \nroom.  The walls are caked with dried blood and deep gouge \nmarks.  Along the west wall a brick fireplace has collapsed into a \nlarge pile of rubble.  Spindly cobwebs cling to everything and mix\nwith the dust to make breathing difficult.  A large carpet has been\npushed into the southwest corner and appears as if something has\nbeen using it as a nest.  Large cracked eggshells, the size of a \nlarge pony, are lying near the nest.\n',-1,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16252,0,0,0,'Littered Room','  This room was once an extravagantly decorated waiting room.  \nNow, years of neglect and abuse have left it filthy and decayed.  \nShredded tatters of paintings and tapestries cling to the wooden \nwalls.  A large chandelier lies on the floor shattered into tiny \nfragments.  A heavy layer of dusts covers everything in this room.  \nIn the northwest corner what was once a freestanding candlestick \nlies on the floor, snapped in two.  Large shuffling footprints lead \nto the north.  \n',137,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16253,0,0,0,'Decayed Foyer','  The fragmented remains of oak furniture lie scattered about this \nroom.  In the southeast corner, large blankets and furs \nhave been made into a makeshift nest.  Inside the nest is an \nimmense broken egg.  The shattered fragments of a large wall \nmirror are scattered about the floor.  A large window along the \nsouth wall has been boarded up with planks.    \n',137,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16254,0,0,0,'Dining Hall','Oddly, this room is in perfect condition.  A beautiful oak dining table,\nwith twelve matching chairs, sits in the center of the room.  Silver place\nsettings, fine china, and crystal goblets have been set before each chair.  \nCarefully placed in the center of each place setting is a gold embroidered \nnapkin. Fine silk tapestries adorn the walls, depicting gardens, forests, \nand other scenic settings.  A large crystal chandelier hangs high above\nthe table.  A large wall size mirror has been set into the south wall.  The\nlight strumming of a harp can be heard coming from an unknown source. \n',-1,172360,22,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16255,0,0,0,'Dark Hallway','  The remnants of a large chandelier lie scattered about the floor.  In\nthe center of the room the floor has bucked inward, as if a great \nweight landed there.  Shreds of tattered tapestries cling to the \ndecaying walls.  In the northwest corner of the room a strange \nsymbol has been carved into the floor.  Crimson candle wax spirals \nout from the center of the symbol like bony fingers.  What looks to be a\nflesh colored piece of yarn is pinned to the wall.  A strange green \nglow emanates from this corner of the room.\n',137,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16256,0,0,0,'Decayed Library','  The shredded remains of leather bound tomes lie scattered about the\nroom.  In the southeast corner thousands of pages have been torn from \nbooks and piled together to form a litter.  The pages are soaked with \nurine and covered with dung.  Large shelves have been set into the walls,\nand presumably were once filled with books.  Most of the shelves have \nbeen hacked, clawed, and smashed into pieces.  Shards of broken egg shells\nlie scattered about the floor.\n',137,172360,22,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16257,0,0,0,'Scorched Room','This room is completely empty and a strong mineral smell hangs in the \nair.  The walls, ceiling, and floor have been scorched by an extreme heat, \nand are covered with a sticky white substance.  Most of the boards used \nto construct the room were warped by the heat.  Throughout the room, \nlarge red scales are littered about the floor.  Long gouge marks streak\nacross the floor.  Lying in the corner is a large leather strap.  \n',-1,172360,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16258,0,0,0,'Dark Hallway','  The smell of rotting wood permeates the air.  The floorboards and walls \nare in an extreme state of disrepair.  The wood has become so \nwaterlogged and decayed that it crumbles under the slightest pressure.  \nBroken bits of glass are strewn about the hallway.  A decayed piece of \ncloth lies strewn across the center of the room.  The rotting carcass of a \nlarge rat is festering with maggots in the southwest corner.\n',137,164168,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16259,0,0,0,'Children\'s Playroom','  The faded remnants of children\'s paintings adorn the walls.  Somebody\nhas taken to adding to the once happy depictions by inserting assorted\nundead creatures into the pictures.  Small broken toys are littered about\nthe floor.\n',137,172360,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16260,0,0,0,'Cooking Area','The kitchen is one of the few rooms in this decaying structure that is in\ngood condition.  A large cooking fire blazes in the center of the room, over\nwhich a black pot has been set.  Against the west wall is a long counter upon\nwhich serving bowls have been placed.  A wooden spice rack sits on the counter,\nand is overflowing with various spices.  The door of the pantry in the\nnorthwest corner sits crookedly on its hinges.\n',-1,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16261,0,0,0,'Dark Hallway','  The decayed hallway ends to the north.  Set into the north wall is a\nshattered floor length mirror.  Into the back frame of the mirror, a\nstrange symbol has been etched, along with words written in an archaic\nlanguage.  \n',137,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16262,0,0,0,'Sleeping Quarters','    This room was once a bedroom for the servants.  Piles of animal dung, \nfur, and rotting food suggest that it was quite recently used as a\nmakeshift kennel.  Small wooden crates, which appear to have been used to\ncage animals for extended periods of time, align the southern wall.  The air\nin this room smells of animals and fecal matter.  Small strands of fur cling\nto everything in the room.    \n',137,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16263,0,0,0,'Dark Path','  A newly constructed cobblestone path extends from the back of a large \nwooden structure.  The cobblestones have been carefully placed and \ncrafted, so that the path is sturdy.  Large trees overhang the path, \nblotting out much of the sky.  To the southeast a large wooden building \nlooks as if it will collapse at any moment.  To the north the path leads \naway from the structure. To the southeast is the back wall of the house\'s\nkitchen.  A loose wall panel covers a crack in the wall of the pantry to the\nsoutheast.\n',137,172352,22,0,0,0,0,-1,7,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16264,0,0,0,'Tool Shed','  What was once a caretaker\'s shed for the nearby mansion, has decayed \ninto an unsteady pile of rotting boards.  Large cobwebs hang from what \nremains of the walls and ceilings.  Large weeds sprout up from between \nthe floorboards.  The dark outlines of gardening tools, which were once \nused to care for the estate grounds, are spotted across the walls.  A large \nlog rests against the north wall.\n',137,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16265,0,0,0,'Crypt','  A large mausoleum, built from solid black marble, has been looted and \ndefiled.  A marble casket lies toppled in the corner, where a \ndecaying corpse lies sprawled out on the floor.  Strange etchings \nhave been carved into the leathery flesh of the corpse.  \nSpindly vines creep up the wall, interlocking in the center of the ceiling.  \n',137,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16266,0,0,0,'Small Garden','  This small area once served as a scenic garden for the residents of the \nestate.  Now, it has been overrun by rodents and weeds.  A moss-covered \nmarble statue has fallen over and lies broken on the ground.  A large \nburrow has been dug underneath the statue.  A small log leans against a\nwall to the south.\n',137,139584,22,0,0,0,0,-1,25,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16267,0,0,0,'Weed-Infested Garden','  A large fountain sits in the center of this part of the garden.  The \nfountain basin is partially full of stagnant water.  The skeleton of a \nhumanoid creature is decaying in the basin.  The bones of the skeleton \nhave been stripped clean of their flesh, and look to have been recently \npolished.  The plants around the fountain have been neglected, and are \ngrowing out of control.  A dark looking crypt is to the south.  \n',137,172352,22,0,0,0,0,-1,25,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16268,0,0,0,'Large Office','This large room has been turned into a makeshift office.  A large oak \ndesk has been placed against the back wall, which is littered with papers \nand books.  Various rotting animal corpses have been placed throughout \nthe room.  Several skeletons have been strung up from the ceiling and \ndance and jiggle like a marionettes.    \n',-1,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16269,0,0,0,'Narrow Hallway','This narrow hallway runs north to south.  The floorboards beneath you \nare decayed and incapable of supporting much weight. A light breeze wafts\nthrough the gaps in the decayed ceiling above.  Large cobwebs drape\nacross the hallway and glisten when the lights hit them.  The dried \ncarcass of a long snake lies against the west wall, covered by swarming \nand writhing maggots.\n',-1,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16270,0,0,0,'Master Bedroom','Unlike other rooms in this decaying mansion, this room has been \nwell kept.  The furniture has been recently constructed and is clean.  \nA large map dominates the entire northern wall.  The walls and floor \nglisten with water, presumably from a recent cleaning.  A light smell of\nfresh lemon scent permeates the room.  \n',-1,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16271,0,0,0,'Decaying Room','  This room appears to have once been an elegant, yet small bedroom.  \nYears of neglect have left the room in a state disrepair and decay.  Thick \ncobwebs glaze the walls and ceilings.  Broken bits of bones and scales \nare scattered about the room.  The smell of rotting flesh hangs in the air, \nmaking breathing an unpleasant experience.  \n',137,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16272,0,0,0,'Narrow Hallway','The house creaks and groans constantly.  A light breeze blows in \nfrom the north, howling eerily as it moves past you.  A strange pair of \nfootprints are on the ceiling, leading to the south.  The walls are covered \nwith cobwebs and riddled with mouse holes.  \n',-1,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16273,0,0,0,'Decaying room','This room appears to have once been an elegant, yet small, bedroom.  \nYears of neglect have left the room in a state disrepair and decay.  Thick \ncobwebs glaze the walls and ceilings.  Broken bits of bones and scales \nare scattered about the room.  The smell of rotting flesh hangs in the air, \nmaking breathing an unpleasant experience.  \n',-1,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16274,0,0,0,'Servants\' Bedroom','This room is noticeably smaller than the rest.  The broken remains of a \nsmall bed lie scattered about the floor.  A large tree branch has crashed \nthrough the ceiling above, letting in a breeze of fresh air that \nmoans continuously.  Dusty cobwebs dominate the room.  \n',-1,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16275,0,0,0,'Narrow Corridor','This narrow hallway runs north to south.  The floorboards beneath you \nare decayed and incapable of supporting much weight.  A light breeze wafts\nthrough the gaps in the decayed ceiling above.  Large cobwebs drape \nacross the hallway and glisten when the lights hit them.  Suspended in a \nweb, about two feet off the ground, are the dried remains of a large rat.  \n',-1,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16276,0,0,0,'Child\'s Playroom','Although this room was once the playroom for generations of children, \nit is now a place of death and decay.  Assorted bones and rotting body \nparts litter the room.  The walls and ceiling are splattered with numerous \nlayers of dried blood.  The wood floor is covered with many bloody foot \nand hand prints that almost appear to have been orchestrated into some \nsort of sadistic artwork.  \n',-1,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16277,0,0,0,'Small Playroom','  This section of the attic has been turned into a gruesome playroom.  \nSmall toy figures have been constructed out of bones and rotting flesh.  \nLittle torture devices have been crafted out of wood and straw.  The \nfigures have been placed in the devices in a vicious depiction of pain and \nagony.  \n',137,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16278,0,0,0,'Attic','A musty smell hangs in the air of this room.  Large rodent droppings \nlitter the floor.  The support-beams holding up the ceiling are splintering \nand are beginning to buckle under the weight of the roof.  A large tree \nlimb has crashed through the roof.  The walls creak and moan \nconstantly, sounding as if they will crumble at any moment.  The floor \nglistens with water, presumably from a recent rain that leaked through\nthe roof.  \n',-1,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16279,0,0,0,'Makeshift Bedroom','  Assorted skinned animal furs have been piled in the southeast corner of\nthis room, making a bed.  A large puddle of wax lies next to the bed, \nhaving long since burned to its core.  The floor boards are splintered and \ndo not appear able to support much weight.  The smell of mildew hangs\nin the air.  A large fungus has sprouted on the south wall.  \n',137,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16280,0,0,0,'Attic','A musty smell hangs in the air of this room.  Large rodent droppings \nlitter the floor.  The support beams holding up the ceiling are splintering \nand are beginning to buckle under the weight of the roof.  The walls\ncreak and moan constantly, sounding as if they will crumble at any \nmoment.  The floor glistens with water, presumably from a recent rain \nthat leaked through the roof.  \n',-1,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16281,0,0,0,'Stuffy Attic','Unlike other parts of the attic, the air here is deathly still.  A faint\ngrunting noise can be heard coming from all directions.  The decayed floorboards\nare splintered and crumbling, and do not appear as if they can support\nmuch weight.  A breeze wafts in from above, where holes and cracks\nhave formed in the roof.  \n',-1,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16282,0,0,0,'Small Study','Several glass tubes, beakers, and buckets of liquid have been assembled \nhere, each representing various stages of some mad experiment.  \nDiscarded body parts have been left throughout the room, and are being \nquickly devoured by hordes of teeming maggots.  \n',-1,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16283,0,0,0,'Stuffy Attic','  The floorboards in this room are splintered and crumbling, and do not \nappear to be capable of supporting much weight.  A strange fungus is \ngrowing up the walls, fanning itself out in small veins resembling bony \nfingers.  The floor is slick with water, presumably caused by a leaky roof \nand the recent rains.  A small pile of animal bones has been amassed in \nthe northeast corner.  Large rodent droppings lie scattered about the \nfloor.  \n',137,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16284,0,0,0,'Attic','  The floorboards in this room are splintered and crumbling, and do not \nappear to be capable of supporting much weight.  A strange fungus is \ngrowing up the walls, fanning itself out in small veins resembling bony \nfingers.  The floor is slick with water, presumably caused by a leaky roof \nand the recent rains.  A small pile of animal bones has been amassed in \nthe northeast corner.  Large rodent droppings lie scattered about the \nfloor.  \n',137,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16285,0,0,0,'Small Laboratory','A long table has been butted up against the west wall of this room.  A\nmummified corpse has been placed on the table and looks as if various\nexperiments have been performed on it.  The head of the corpse has been\nsevered and is resting in a large metal tray.  From the state of the corpse, \nit appears that rodents have been gnawing at the decayed flesh.  A\nstrange chemical smell hangs in the air.  \n',-1,172360,32,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16286,0,0,0,'Small Platform','A large platform, carved into the rock foundation of the house above, is \nthe halfway point of the stairwell.  Large stairs cut into the rock lead up \nand down.  Judging by the smooth surface of the stairs and the platform, \na highly skilled craftsman designed this area.  The rock-face is still \nperfectly smooth and polished, suggesting that it is well cared for.\nSome tattered carpet hangs through a hole in the decaying wood of the ceiling.\n',-1,172360,13,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16287,0,0,0,'Polished Tunnel','A large tunnel has been carved into a strange black rock.  The floors, \nwalls, and ceilings are perfectly smooth and are so well polished they act \nas mirrors.  The air in here is surprising fresh and cold.  \n',-1,172360,13,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16288,0,0,0,'Polished Tunnel','A large tunnel has been carved into a strange black rock.  The floors, \nwalls, and ceilings are perfectly smooth and are so well polished they act \nas mirrors.  The air in here is surprising fresh and cold.  \n',-1,172360,13,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16289,0,0,0,'Polished Tunnel','A large tunnel has been carved into a strange black rock.  The floors, \nwalls, and ceilings are perfectly smooth and are so well polished they act \nas mirrors.  The air in here is surprising fresh and cold.  The tunnel \nappears to open up to the east.  \n',-1,139592,13,0,0,0,0,-1,25,100,0,'',NULL),
(16290,0,0,0,'Ghostly Market','Just off the main entrance, this is prime market real estate.  Odd items, \nincluding various body parts in different stages of decay, are on display at \nethereal booths.\n',-1,139592,13,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16291,0,0,0,'Ghostly Market','This appears to be the entrance to an underground market.  To the west,\na passage leads away from the market.  To the north, east, and south are\ncollections of ghostly tables and booths displaying macabre wares. \nAlthough the rock floor and ceiling are of a high quality, and \ncompletely smooth, the constant hustle and bustle of the marketplace has \nsullied the rock to a dull gray.  \n',-1,139592,13,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16292,0,0,0,'Ghostly Market','Just off the main entrance, this is prime market real estate.  Odd items,\nincluding various body parts in different stages of decay, are on display at\nethereal booths.\n',-1,172360,13,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16293,0,0,0,'Ghostly Market','Small translucent tables and booths have been set up to market assorted \ngoods and trinkets.  However, this market does not dabble in the ordinary\ntypes of merchandise.  Rather, the displays hold assorted organic items, \nwhich generally consist of some sort of pickled, dried, or freshly \nharvested body part.\n',-1,172360,13,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16294,0,0,0,'Center of a Ghostly Market','  A small clearing has been left empty by the vendors and merchants.  \nSmall tables and chairs have been placed here for those who have grown \nweary from haggling.  The air here is oddly still and quiet.  \n',137,172360,13,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16295,0,0,0,'Ghostly Market','Small translucent tables and booths have been set up to market assorted goods\nand trinkets.  However, this market does not dabble in the ordinary types of\nmerchandise.  Rather, the displays hold assorted organic items, which generally\nconsist of some sort of pickled, dried, or freshly harvested body part.\n',-1,172360,13,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16296,0,0,0,'Outskirts of a Ghostly Market','Perhaps because it lies at the back corner, this spot lacks the densely\npacked tables and displays that populate the rest of the market.  A cool\ndraft blows down off the rock face to the east, keeping this area\npleasantly cool.\n',-1,172360,13,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16297,0,0,0,'Before a Large Set of Marble Doors','  This area is clear of merchants.  To the east a large pair of marble doors \nis set into the black rock wall.  The wall is smooth and reflects the \nactivity of the market.  A cold blast of air runs down the rock face and \ngushes out to the west.  Etched into the doors are sketches and symbols.  \nThe decaying carcass of an elven merchant has been strung across the \ntop of the doors.  \n',0,172360,13,0,0,0,0,-1,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(16298,0,0,0,'Outskirts of a Ghostly Market','Perhaps because it lies at the back corner, this spot lacks the densely\npacked tables and displays that populate the rest of the market.  A cool\ndraft blows down off the rock face to the east, keeping this area\npleasantly cool.\n',-1,172360,13,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16299,0,0,0,'Conservatory','The ceiling of this room was once a retractable dome \nthat served as a conservatory from which an eager astrology \nstudent could view the heavens.  The dome has long since \nsplintered and now offers no protection from the elements.  \nThe remnants of a large telescope lie scattered about the \nfloor, shattered into miniscule pieces.  Large piles of garbage \nand waste have been strewn about the conservatory.  A large\nrodent nest lies in the northeast corner of the room.  \n',-1,172360,26,0,0,0,0,-1,25,120,0,'',NULL),
(16300,14,-18,0,'A Freshly Made Path','This small pathway is freshly made with the immediate surrounding\nvegetation cleared. The grass has been cut low to permit travel on any part\nof the new clearing. To the south a large white tent can be seen\nbehind rows of colorful carts.\n',133,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16301,14,-19,0,'Beneath a Cloth Covered Archway','This small pathway is freshly made with the immediate surrounding\nvegetation cleared. The grass has been cut low to permit travel on any part\nof the new clearing. To the south a large white tent can be seen\nbehind rows of colorful carts. The sun is blocked by a canvas\ncovering with small slits cut into it to permit airflow. Vision\nto the east and west is blocked by large colorful carts.\n',133,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,9,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16302,10,-20,0,'A Small Pathway','This small pathway is freshly made with the immediate surrounding\nvegetation cleared. The grass has been cut low to permit travel on any part\nof the new clearing. To the east the pathway continues between some \ncarts and the perimiter of a large tent. To the north a small cart\nis designed to house beasts. To the southwest is a generic cart that looks \nto be for storage.\n',133,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
