(16371,7,-35,-2,'<G>Deep In The Thick Jungle<1>','  <g>This section of the jungle seems especially damp.  A strange\ngloominess hangs around the air here.  The animal activity seems\nto decrease to the east.  You are almost sure you are not alone in\nthe jungle, as a couple of eyes flash for a second from a nearby\nvine bush.<1>\n',108,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16372,7,-35,-1,'<G>Deep Among The Trees<1>','  <g>Wild jungle trees entangle around you and compete to reach the top.  Many\nbranches of vine rope bridges seem to come together and form wider and\nstronger bridges to the east.  From above, you can clearly make out several\ntracks below you.  There seems to be a few shadows behind some trees and\nbushes around you.<1>\n',108,131072,58,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16373,8,-35,-2,'<G>Deep In The Thick Jungle<1>','  <g>This section of the jungle seems especially damp.  A strange gloominess\nhangs around the air here.  The animal activity seems to decrease to the\neast.  You are almost sure you are not alone in the jungle, as a couple of\neyes flash for a second from a nearby vine bush.<1>\n',108,131072,45,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16374,8,-35,-1,'<G>Deep Among The Trees<1>','  <g>Wild jungle trees entangle around you and compete to reach the top.  Many\nbranches of vine rope bridges seem to come together and form wider and\nstronger bridges to the east.  From above, you can clearly make out several\ntracks below you.  There seems to be a few shadows behind some trees and\nbushes around you.<1>\n',108,131072,58,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16375,8,-36,-2,'<G>Deep In The Thick Jungle<1>','  <g>This section of the jungle seems especially damp.  A strange gloominess\nhangs around the air here.  The animal activity seems to decrease to the\neast.  You are almost sure you are not alone in the jungle, as a couple of\neyes flash for a second from a nearby vine bush.<1>\n',108,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16376,8,-36,-1,'<G>Deep Among The Trees<1>','  <g>Wild jungle trees entangle around you and compete to reach the top.  Many\njungle branches of vine rope bridges seem to come together and form wider\nand stronger bridges to the east.  From above, you can clearly make out\nseveral tracks below you.  There seems to be a few shadows lurking behind\nsome trees and brushes around here.  The traces of several ancient <r>ruins<g>\nappear south of a long <c>river<g> behind the trees to your south.<1>\n',108,131072,58,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
