(16382,10,-35,-1,'<G>Deep Among The Trees<1>','  <g>Wild jungle trees entangle around you and compete to reach the top.  Many\njungle branches of vine rope bridges seem to come together and form wider\nand stronger bridges to the east.  From above, you can clearly make out\nseveral tracks below you.  There seems to be a few shadows lurking behind\nsome trees and bushes around you.<1>\n',108,131072,58,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16383,5,-32,-2,'<G>Jungle Trail Along The Canyon Walls<1>','  <g>The jungle seems to grow thinner to the east from here.  To the north you\ncan see the high walls of the canyon that surround the grand misty valley.\nThe view to the south is clearer inbetween the tops of the trees.  The\nground level of the jungle is slowly rising to the east and you can see\nseveral recently made tracks on the trail.<1>\n',108,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16384,6,-32,-2,'<G>Along The Walls Of The Canyon<1>','  <g>The earth beneath you is inclining upwards to the east, though the trees\nof the jungle are growing thinner that way.  You can see the sharp canyon\nwalls of the valley to the north and east, from between the tree tops.\nSeveral paw tracks of some group of animals are scattered around.<1>\n',108,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16385,7,-34,-1,'<G>Above A Cliff Looking On The Jungle<1>','  <g>The hills seem to have come to a stop south of you.  You are high on\ntop of a cliff and to the south you can see the huge jungle with a large\nsection of it collapsed at a point and obscuring the view beyond it.\nYou can make out the canyon walls to the north and the hills seem to go\nonward to the east and connect with the walls of the canyon.  To the far\nsouth, the remains of ancient <r>ruins<g> are clearly visible behind a <c>river<g>\nsouth of the jungle.<1>\n',108,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16386,11,-35,-2,'<G>Before A Collapsed Section Of The Jungle<1>','  <g>Despite the many collapsed trees lying before you, this section of the\njungle is gloomier than the other parts.  Many vine trees seem to have\ncollapsed together to form what looks like a wall.  The trees have been\ncleared and are showing a distinct trail going under the collapsed mess.\nThis section of the jungle seems totally inactive and silent.<1>\n',108,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16387,7,-33,-2,'<G>At The Foot Of The Hills<1>','  <g>You seem to be at the foot of some of the southern hills of the jungle.\nThe walls of the canyon is not that far north but it looks like the jungle\nto the south is closer to you than the canyon walls to the north.  There\nare several claw marks over the trees in this section of the jungle.<1>\n',108,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16388,7,-33,-1,'<G>Over the Hills Near the Jungle<1>','  <g>You can clearly see the huge jungle south and west of you.  The sharp\nedges of the wall of the canyon surrounding this valley go around the\nnorth and all the way from the far west.  The hills seem to extend to\nseveral miles to the east, and you can spy some sort of movement there\namong the trees.  The remains of ancient <r>ruins<g> lie south far beyond the\ntrees of the jungle.<1>\n',108,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16389,7,-32,-2,'<G>At The Foot Of The Hills<1>','  <g>The walls of the canyon are now very clear and distinct between the thin\ntrees.  You can see the sharp incline in the hills to the east and the slow\ndecline in the trail to the west.  Some sort of wild movement seems to be\noccuring between the trees on top of the hills.<1>\n',108,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16390,7,-32,-1,'<G>Over The Hills<1>','  <g>For the first time you feel a breeze of wind between the jungle trees.\nYou can see the tip of the canyon wall north and east of you.  The jungle\nto the south looks huge and you can see a clear distinct collapsed\nsection of it that obscures what\'s behind it.  To the far south beyond\nthe jungle, you can see ancient <r>ruins<g> with a long <c>river<g> running across\nit.\n',108,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16391,8,-34,-1,'<G>Over The Hills Near The Jungle<1>','  <g>You seem to be standing atop a high cliff looking over the jungle to the\nsouth of here.  You can make out the walls of the canyon to the north and\nthe hills in between.  There seems to be wild activities occuring between\nthe trees among the hills.  There remains of ancient <r>ruins<g> are visible\nfar south beyond a <c>river<g> south of of the jungle.<1>\n',108,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16392,8,-33,-1,'<G>Center Of The Hills<1>','  <g>You can see the skies clearly between the trees here.  The canyon wall\ngoes around north of you.  The large gloomy jungle lingers to the south of\nyou and there are the remains of ancient <r>ruins<g> far beyond the <c>river<g> south\nof it.  Many trees here have been broken down.  Signs of wild activity are\nscattered all over the trees here.  Several paw tracks run in all directions\nand seem to come out of no where.<1>\n',108,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16393,8,-32,-1,'<G>Over The Hills Near The Canyon Wall<1>','  <g>The jungle is growing less and less damp to the east.  North of you is\nthe sharp edge of the canyon wall blocking your way.  The hills extend in\nall other directions.  You can make out the thick jungle to the far south\nand the remains of ancient <r>ruins<g> extend beyond a long <c>river<g>.  There seems\nto be some sort of activity around these hills.\n',108,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16394,9,-34,-1,'<G>Over The Hills Near The Jungle<1>','  <g>The walls of the canyon to the north seem to stop here.  You can see\nover the cliff, the large jungle extending to the south and beyond it\nthe remains of the ancient <r>ruins<g> far behind a long flowing <c>river<g>.  A section\nof the jungle is collapsed and is blocking the view beyond it.  Several\nhills merge together to the west and northwest of you.  There is a faint\ntrail to the east that ends at what looks to be a cave in the walls of\ncanyon.<1>\n',108,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16395,10,-34,-1,'<B>Cave Entrance<1>','  <b>You are before a gloomy looking cave.  Several tracks lead inside\nthe cave and seem to go under a large thicket of vines blocking the\ncave entrance.  You can see the jungle hills to your west merging\nbetween the grand walls of the canyon and the huge jungle.<1>\n',108,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16396,10,-33,-1,'<B>Inside A Damp Cave<1>','  <b>The cave floors feels wet, damp and warm.  Several vines have grown\nfrom inside to the outside over the thicket covering the exit.  The\ncave looks like it is or was occupied by some sort of reptilian animal\nwhich enjoys the warmth of the tunnels.  The floor of the cave looks\ncrude and has many scattered stones lying about it.<1>\n',108,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,5,400,0,'',NULL),
(16397,10,-32,-1,'<B>Dead End<1>','  <b>The cave seems to end here.  There are several long dry bushes of grass\nlying here with dried <r>blood<b> over them.  They seem to be emitting a\ndisgusting odor that is increasing the already heavy stench in the room.\nSeveral claw marks are scattered around the cave walls.  The cave tunnels\nseem to be wide enough for a large creature to maneuver around comfortably.<1>\n',108,131080,56,0,0,0,0,0,7,700,0,'',NULL),
(16398,9,-32,-1,'<G>Over The Hill Near The Canyon Wall<1>','  <g>North of you is the sharp edge of the canyon wall surrounding this\nvalley.  It totally blocks the way to the north and east.  There is a huge\njungle south of the hills south of you, and beyond it is a long flowing\n<c>river<g> before some ancient <r>ruins<g>.  Several activities blur between\nthe trees on the hills below your level.<1>\n',108,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16399,9,-33,-1,'<G>Over The Hills Near The Canyon Wall<1>','  <g>The walls of the canyon take a sharp turn to the south here and totally\nblocks the jungle hills from going east.  You can make out the jungle to\nthe south and many jungle hills rolling down from the mountain range.  The\nancient remains of some <r>ruins<g> appear beyond a flowing <c>river<g> far south\nof the jungle.  Several activities seem to be occuring on the hills at the\nfeet of the canyon wall.<1>\n',108,131072,47,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16450,0,0,0,'<W>Tiled Sewers<z>','  Smooth, white, marble tiles line the floor, ceiling  and walls of this\nroom just like all others in this sewer.  Each tile is spotless, and the\nfloor in this room slopes steeply to the south.  A few drainage pipes jut\nout of the tiles but nothing seems to flow out of them.\n',110,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,3,43,0,'',NULL),
(16451,0,0,0,'<W>Tiled Sewers<z>','  The ceiling in this part closes in as the floor slopes up to the north,\nand down to the south.  The tiles are dry, and smooth, yet allow enough\ntraction to walk up the slope.\n',110,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,63,0,'',NULL),
(16452,0,0,0,'<W>Drainage Pipe<z>','  The pipe here ends in a large valve hatch, that would possibly open if\nthere was ever any water in the sewers.  East leads back up the pipe and\ninto the sewer system.\n',110,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,3,43,0,'',NULL),
(16453,0,0,0,'<W>Drainage Pipe<z>','  This large, seemingly unused, drainage pipe is just big enough to allow\nsomeone to squeeze into.  Sloping down to the west the pipe becomes even\nsmaller.  To the east leads back into the sewers.\n',110,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,3,43,0,'',NULL),
(16454,0,0,0,'<W>Tiled Sewers<z>','  The floor slopes up to the east from here, and to the west, a large\ndrainage pipe can be seen.  Smaller pipes protrude from the walls and a\nfew from the ceiling of this room, yet the whole place is completely dry.\n',110,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,53,0,'',NULL),
(16455,0,0,0,'<W>Tiled Sewers<z>','  The floor in this room slopes downward to the west, and up to the east.\nPipes on both the north and south walls jut out, and yet they seem to be\nunused.  The tiles in this room, like in the rest of the sewers,  are\nshiny white, and free from any filth.\n',110,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,5,63,0,'',NULL),
(16456,0,0,0,'<W>Tiled Sewers<z>','  This seems to be the sewer junction, with the floor sloping down to the\nwest, and up to the east, north, and south.  Here, as in the rest of the\nsewer, the tiles are pristine, and free of any filth.  Along each corner,\nexcept to the southeast, pipes poke out, although seemingly unused.\n',110,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16457,0,0,0,'<W>Tiled Sewers<z>','  The ceiling in this part closes in as the floor slopes up to the east,\nand down to the west.  The tiles are dry, and smooth, yet allow enough\ntraction to walk up the slope.\n',110,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,63,0,'',NULL),
(16458,0,0,0,'<W>Tiled Sewers<z>','  Smooth, white, marble tiles line the floor, ceiling, and walls of this\nroom just like all others in this sewer.  Each tile is spotless, and the\nfloor in this room slopes steeply to the west.  A few drainage pipes jut\nout of the tiles but nothing seems to flow out of them.\n',110,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,3,43,0,'',NULL),
(16459,0,0,0,'<W>Tiled Sewers<z>','  The ceiling in this part closes in as the floor slopes up to the south,\nand down to the north.  The tiles are dry, and smooth, yet allow enough\ntraction to walk up the slope.\n',110,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,4,63,0,'',NULL),
(16460,0,0,0,'<W>A Valve Room<z>','  The walls, floor and ceiling of this room are covered in the same white\nmarble tiles as in the rest of the sewers.  To the northwest two large,\nhinged tiles make a simple, but hard to see, entrance into this small water\nrelease room.  In the center of the room is a water release hatch in case\nthe sewers ever do fill up with too much water.\n',110,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(16461,0,0,0,'<W>Tiled Sewers<z>','  Smooth, white, marble tiles line the floor, ceiling,  and walls of this\nroom just like all others in this sewer.  Each tile is spotless, and the\nfloor in this room slopes steeply to the north.  A few drainage pipes jut\nout of the tiles but nothing seems to flow out of them.  One large pipe\nseems to be out of place in this room, and even looks a little damp.\n',110,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,3,43,0,'',NULL),
(16462,0,0,0,'<W>A Water Drain Pipe<z>','  The walls of the pipe, while free of water, are close enough together to\nallow you to shimmy up and down.  Like the rest of the sewer, this pipe is\nclean, and completely free of water of any kind.\n',110,131080,35,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(16463,0,0,0,'A Water Drain Pipe Outlet','  The walls and floor of this room are tiled in smooth, white marble.  To\nthe southeast there seems to be some sort of natural cave formation.\nRunning across the floor from the southwest to the northeast, you\ncan just spot a thin crevice.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,40,0,'',NULL),
(16464,0,0,0,'A Narrow Crevice','  While thin at the top, this crevice widens at the bottom, allowing\nenough room to squeeze through.  To the southwest the crevice ends in a\nnarrow cave, while downward the crevice continues to open up.  The rock\nhere is somewhat jagged, like it was broken, but it does give some decent,\nif sharp, hand holds.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(16465,0,0,0,'A Narrow Cave','  The cave here narrows, and turns to the northeast, where you can see a\nthin crevice.  Made of the same hard rock, this cave seems to be naturally\nsmooth.  To the east you can see a tunnel sloping into this area.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16466,0,0,0,'A Sloping Passage','  The tiles of the sewer end in the northwest part of this tunnel, and the\nwalls here are made of a smooth, hard rock.  While to the west the tunnel\nslopes downward into another cave formation.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16467,0,0,0,'An Entrance to a Flawless Tunnel','  This room is lined in flat, dark marble, fit together so seamlessly it\ncan only be called flawless.  Curving downward in a deep slope this\ncircular tunnel continues on.  To the southwest is a door fit with the\nsame flawless construction, so flawless even that when it is closed, it is\nimpossible to see.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16468,0,0,0,'A Smooth Cave','This cave, while looking natural, is extremely smooth, and is somewhat\nspherical in shape.  The floor is free of any debris.  Any noise you make \nechoes back perfectly, and creates an eerie atmosphere.\n',-1,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16469,0,0,0,'A Natural Cave System','  This looks to be some sort of naturally formed cave system.  The rock is\nhard, and jagged in some places, but over all the area is traversable.  In\nthe ceiling a large crevice runs southwest to northeast, and smaller,\ntunnels branch off to the north, east, and southwest.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16470,0,0,0,'A Damp Tunnel','  This tunnel seems to be the first sign of moisture you\'ve seen in the\nwhole area.  The walls are slick to the touch, and the air is noticeably\nhumid.  To the west leads back to drier tunnels, while east you can see\nsome sort of glowing moss formations.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16471,0,0,0,'<g>A Moss Covered Passage<z>','  Thriving in these damp tunnels some strain of glowing moss had made this\nplace its home.  Covering the walls, floor and ceiling the moss is\neverywhere.  As you walk across it, it squishes like a sponge full of\nwater.  West leads to a damp, but moss free tunnel, and south the moss\nseems present, but scraped off of large parts of the cave.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16472,0,0,0,'A Sloping Cave','  Sloping from the northeast, down into a cave to the south, the floor of\nthis tunnel is worn smooth.  A channel, running down the middle of the\ntunnel, although free of water, seems to have been formed from it.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16473,0,0,0,'A Rough Cut Hollow','  Here, you can see that this cave has been enlarged with the use of metal\ntools or some other type of sharp objects.  Deep, rough scratch marks line\nthe far wall, and to the north moss encroaches.  The floor is littered with\nbroken rock, and bits of dried moss.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16474,0,0,0,'A Collapsed Cave','  A channel, possibly formed from water, runs into this cave from the\nnorth and ends where the floor of the cave has collapsed.  A ring of rock\noverhangs the collapsed portion of this cave, and seems somewhat unstable.\nAlthough it should be possible to climb down in a few spots along the\nedge.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16475,0,0,0,'A Flawless Tunnel','  This room is lined in a flat, dark marble, with its walls curving up\nto form a circular tunnel.  Winding in steeply from above and back upon\nitself this tunnel does not look like it was designed for travel.  More\nlikely it was meant to carry water at some point in time.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16476,0,0,0,'A Flawless Tunnel','  Lined with perfectly fitted flat, black marble, this circular tunnel\nwinds its way to the south and to the northeast.  Your footsteps echo\noddly off the curved surface of the floor, as you continue on your way.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16477,0,0,0,'A Collapsed Tunnel','  Here the marble tunnel, while being fit together with craftsmanship\nunseen before, is not quite perfect.  Underminded from below it seems to\nhave fallen in, creating a passage leading downward into a hole in its\nfloor.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16478,0,0,0,'A Caved in Tunnel','  Made out of perfectly fitting flat, black marble, this seems to be the\nend of a finely crafted tunnel.  To the west the tunnel began to curve\noff in another direction, but it is caved in and covered with rubble,\nmaking it impassable.  To the south, there is a large crack in the wall\npossibly formed from the same event that caused the cave in to the west.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16479,0,0,0,'<c>A Rubbled Pool<z>','  This cave is full of rubble, probably from the collapse of its ceiling.\nAn underground stream may have once flowed through here but all that is\nleft now is a small pool of water.  A large crack runs down the north side\nof the cave, while too small to move through, you can possibly make out a\ncave on the other side.\n',110,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16480,0,0,0,'A Tunnel Junction','  The excavation marks in this tunnel seem to be more like what someone\nwould see in a mining or rough excavation tunnel.  Although this part of\nthe tunnel has a decent sized hole in its ceiling, and the floor is\nlittered with strange flat, black marble tiles, it seems safe enough now.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16481,0,0,0,'An Abandoned Tunnel','  Rough marks line the east side of this tunnel, consistant with the marks\nleft with some type of mining pick, or other digging tools.  From the\nlooks of it though, whoever was digging this tunnel abandoned it.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16482,0,0,0,'A Smooth Tunnel','  The walls of this tunnel have been worked smooth, and shaped large\nenough to allow unrestricted movement.  To the south the tunnel looks to\nchange direction again, and northeast rubble can be seen on the tunnel\nfloor.  The eastern wall seems to be rather thin, probably more of a\nsupport than a wall.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16483,0,0,0,'A Smooth Sloping Tunnel','  The walls of this tunnel have been worked smooth, and shaped large\nenough to allow unrestricted movement.  To the south the tunnel looks to\nchange direction again, and north rubble can be seen on the tunnel floor.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16484,0,0,0,'A Convergence of Two Smooth Tunnels','  Two smoothed tunnels branch off to the north, and northeast, and from\nhere it can be seen that the wall separating them on this end is rather\nthin, left more as a support than a wall.  To the south the smoothed\ntunnel continues.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16485,0,0,0,'A Recent Floor Excavation','  Here it can seen that the floor was purposely excavated from above\ndropping this tunnel down into the tunnel below it.  To the north more\nexcavation continues.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16486,0,0,0,'A Strange Tunnel','  This strange tunnel seems to be made out of an unknown type of rock, or\nmetal, the surface is smooth, and circular shape, like a pipe.  Also,\nstrange enough, any sound made within the tunnel is absorbed, instead of\nbeing echoed.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16487,0,0,0,'A Branching Tunnel','  Branching off from the main tunnel which enter from the southeast, two\ntunnels, lead away to the northeast, and to the south.  Tiny pebbles line\nthe floor which slopes up to the northeast, and down to the south.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16488,0,0,0,'A Strange Cave','  This spherical shaped cave has one entrance to the north.  Made out of a\nstrange metal, or rock, it seems to unnaturally absorb any sound made\nwithin it.  On the floor, there seems to be a good number of lightly etched\nrunes of some type.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16489,0,0,0,'A Curved Tunnel','  This large, curving tunnel winds off to the southwest and southeast.\nThe walls and floor are smooth, and free of dust, like it has been\ntraveled recently.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16490,0,0,0,'A Sloped Tunnel','  The floor of this tunnel slopes smoothly up to the north and to the\ndown south.  The walls are close, and the ceiling is high above your head.\nSmall pebbles present on the floor make travel difficult, although the\nwalls have enough small hand holds to allow someone to traverse this area\nwithout serious harm.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16491,0,0,0,'A Branching Tunnel','  The main tunnel leading in from the northeast branches off to the south,\nand to the northwest.  A couple pebbles line the floor, but other than\nthat this area is empty.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16492,0,0,0,'A Widening Tunnel','  This tunnel winds in from the northwest, and begins to curve back to the\neast but seems to have been caved in or left unfinished.  There is a small\ntunnel leading to the south though.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16493,0,0,0,'A Strange Tunnel','  This tunnel is quite strange.  It is devoid of any rocks, dust, or\ndebris normally found in underground tunnels, and is made of a rock or\npossibly metal of a kind not found above ground.  The whole thing is\nperfectly circular, and even seems to absorb sound instead of echoing it.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16494,0,0,0,'A Tunnel Junction','  This junction serves to connect three branching tunnels.  One that slopes\nupward to the north, and another, curving tunnel to the southeast.  While\nto the west there is a strange and unnerving tunnel.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16495,0,0,0,'A Natural Hollow','  This part of the tunnel system seems to have been naturally formed.  The\nwalls, floor and ceiling are smooth, but non-uniform, giving support to\nthe idea that this cave was not excavated.  Small glowing mosses speckle\nthe walls and give off an eerie glow.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16496,0,0,0,'A Tunnel Junction','  This room seems to be formed because of, not for, the connection of the\nthree tunnels leading to it.  The ceiling being excavated to allow passage\nto and from some tunnel above this room, while the tunnel to the east\nactually seems rather small compared to the tunnel leading southwest.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16497,0,0,0,'A Small Branch Tunnel','  This tunnel has a rather low ceiling, and looks like a quickly excavated\nconnection tunnel more than anything else.  Curving roughly to the north\nit begins to open up into another tunnel.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(16498,0,0,0,'A Strange Cave','  Made out of some unknown metal, or rock, this cave is quite unnerving.\nAll sound made within it is not echoed as with other natural and man\nmade caves.  Except for the entrance to the northwest the cave is\ncompletely spherical in shape.  Etched along the walls at about eye level\nis a series of fine, wispy runes.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16499,0,0,0,'A Curved Tunnel','  This large, curving tunnel winds off to the northeast and northwest.\nThe walls and floor are smooth, and free of dust, like it has been\ntraveled recently.\n',110,131080,61,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16625,0,0,0,'The Mouth of an Ancient, Desert Canyon','  The sand slowly mixes in with rock as it enters the ancient canyon.  Dark\nshadows are cast throughout the deep slash in the rock known as the Sandworm\nTrough.  Rough winds course through the canyon accompanied by howls and groans\nwhile night and day seemingly meld into one as the walls overlap and rise\nfar into the sky.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16626,0,0,0,'The Mouth of an Ancient, Desert Canyon','  The sand slowly mixes in with rock as it enters the ancient canyon.  Dark\nshadows are cast throughout the deep slash in the rock known as the Sandworm\nTrough.  Rough winds course through the canyon accompanied by howls and groans\nwhile night and day seemingly meld into one as the walls overlap and rise\nfar into the sky.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16627,0,0,0,'A Cramped, Winding Path Through the Canyon','  Stone walls smoothed by centuries of wind and sand running along their\nsurfaces form the canyon known as the Sandworm Trough.  In places, the red\nrock has fallen victim to crude carvings and paintings of a diminutive people\nusually crowded around a sandworm or other such beast.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16628,0,0,0,'A Cramped, Winding Path Through the Canyon','  Stone walls smoothed by centuries of wind and sand running along their\nsurfaces form the canyon known as the Sandworm Trough.  In places, the red\nrock has fallen victim to crude carvings and paintings of a diminutive people\nusually crowded around a sandworm or other such beast.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16629,0,0,0,'A Cramped, Winding Path Through the Canyon','  Stone walls smoothed by centuries of wind and sand running along their\nsurfaces form the canyon known as the Sandworm Trough.  In places, the red\nrock has fallen victim to crude carvings and paintings of a diminutive people\nusually crowded around a sandworm or other such beast.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16630,0,0,0,'A Cramped, Winding Path Through the Canyon','  Stone walls smoothed by centuries of wind and sand running along their\nsurfaces form the canyon known as the Sandworm Trough.  In places, the red\nrock has fallen victim to crude carvings and paintings of a diminutive people\nusually crowded around a sandworm or other such beast.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16631,0,0,0,'A Cramped, Winding Path Through the Canyon','  Stone walls smoothed by centuries of wind and sand running along their\nsurfaces form the canyon known as the Sandworm Trough.  In places, the red\nrock has fallen victim to crude carvings and paintings of a diminutive people\nusually crowded around a sandworm or other such beast.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16632,0,0,0,'A Cramped, Winding Path Through the Canyon','  Stone walls smoothed by centuries of wind and sand running along their\nsurfaces form the canyon known as the Sandworm Trough.  In places, the red\nrock has fallen victim to crude carvings and paintings of a diminutive people\nusually crowded around a sandworm or other such beast.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16633,0,0,0,'A Cramped, Winding Path Through the Canyon','  Stone walls smoothed by centuries of wind and sand running along their\nsurfaces form the canyon known as the Sandworm Trough.  In places, the red\nrock has fallen victim to crude carvings and paintings of a diminutive people\nusually crowded around a sandworm or other such beast.  A small path breaks\naway from the main flow of the canyon to the east.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16634,0,0,0,'A Cramped, Winding Path Through the Canyon','  Stone walls smoothed by centuries of wind and sand running along their\nsurfaces form the canyon known as the Sandworm Trough.  In places, the red\nrock has fallen victim to crude carvings and paintings of a diminutive people\nusually crowded around a sandworm or other such beast.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16635,0,0,0,'A Cramped, Winding Path Through the Canyon','  Stone walls smoothed by centuries of wind and sand running along their\nsurfaces form the canyon known as the Sandworm Trough.  In places, the red\nrock has fallen victim to crude carvings and paintings of a diminutive people\nusually crowded around a sandworm or other such beast.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16636,0,0,0,'The Sandworm\'s Eye','  A small pear shaped hole has been forced through the rock here by powerful\nwinds and time.  Now what is left is the natural archway leading through\nthe canyon known as the Sandworm\'s Eye.  Shadows seem to bend as all light\npulls itself towards the eye.  The change in the light\'s direction causes\na slight sensation of disorientation as you no longer know if you\'re still\nheading south since the light should be coming in an eastern or western\ndirection.  The sketches that have been placed throughout the canyon seem to\nbe densely placed around the hole.\n',138,139592,40,0,0,0,0,-1,3,40,0,'',NULL),
(16637,0,0,0,'A Sharp Curve in the Canyon','  Even more of the strange drawings adorn the walls in this part of the canyon\nas it tightly curves like some wild beast such as that by which it received\nits name.  To the north, the almost unnatural formation of rock known as the\nSandworm\'s Eye casts its gutless shadow upon the rock face to the south\nevery sunset.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16638,0,0,0,'An Abrupt Dead-End','  The canyon narrows off to a dead end here.  A painting larger than the\nrest covers the otherwise blank surface of the eastern wall depicting a short\nstocky man with arms raised and a spear stuck in the sand.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16639,0,0,0,'A Steep Rocky Hill','  This hill climbs steeply up to where a tunnel seems to follow the same\ndirection as the previous one.  Rocks, each the size of an ogre\'s skull\nlay strewn over the hill from a recent slide.  Sand and gravel covers each\nrock making each step across them treacherous at best.  Numerous prints\nshow that many others have travelled this same path.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16640,0,0,0,'A Tunnel Burrowing Through the Side of the Canyon','  Light reflects off mineral deposits inside this cave creating an unearthly\neffect.  Daylight, even starlight glows through as if magic is involved in this\nsomehow.  Sand different from that of the desert covers the floor marked\nby the footprints of others who have wandered this path before.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16641,0,0,0,'A Tunnel Burrowing Through the Side of the Canyon','  Light reflects off mineral deposits inside this cave creating an unearthly\neffect.  Daylight, even starlight glows through as if magic is involved in this\nsomehow.  Sand different from that of the desert covers the floor marked\nby the footprints of others who have wandered this path before.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16642,0,0,0,'A Tunnel Burrowing Through the Side of the Canyon','  Light reflects off mineral deposits inside this cave creating an unearthly\neffect.  Daylight, even starlight glows through as if magic is involved in this\nsomehow.  Sand different from that of the desert covers the floor marked\nby the footprints of others who have wandered this path before.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16643,0,0,0,'Atop the Sandworm\'s Eye','  Standing some forty yards above the canyon floor, the Sandworm\'s Eye is just\nas impressive from above as it is from below.  Here you can see just how\nbeautiful nature\'s architecture can be.  Colours ranging from deep browns\nto soft pinks adorn the walls of the cavern in swirling patterns, bearing\ntestament to the chaotic dance of the sands throughout time.  Shadows protest\nagainst the sun creeping out from beneath outcroppings and ledges in an attempt\nto veil this spectacle.  Nature truly is an artist.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16644,0,0,0,'A Smooth Trail Covered in Sand','  With its easy, slow curve, this trail is a relief compared to the hard,\nrugged terrain the departing traveller has faced, or a deceptive ploy inviting\nnew players in the canyon\'s game of hardship.  A faint tinge of salt can be\ndetected in the air and the sound of crashing waves emanates with great\npitch in their attempt to further carve the already magnificent canyon.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16645,0,0,0,'A Smooth Trail Covered in Sand','  With its easy, slow curve, this trail is a relief compared to the hard,\nrugged terrain the departing traveller has faced, or a deceptive ploy inviting\nnew players in the canyon\'s game of hardship.  A faint tinge of salt can be\ndetected in the air and the sound of crashing waves emanates with great\npitch in their attempt to further carve the already magnificent canyon.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16646,0,0,0,'A Smooth Trail Covered in Sand','  With its easy, slow curve, this trail is a relief compared to the hard,\nrugged terrain the departing traveller has faced, or a deceptive ploy inviting\nnew players in the canyon\'s game of hardship.  A faint tinge of salt can be\ndetected in the air and the sound of crashing waves emanates with great\npitch in their attempt to further carve the already magnificent canyon.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16647,0,0,0,'A Smooth Trail Covered in Sand','  With its easy, slow curve, this trail is a relief compared to the hard,\nrugged terrain the departing traveller has faced, or a deceptive ploy inviting\nnew players in the canyon\'s game of hardship.  A faint tinge of salt can be\ndetected in the air and the sound of crashing waves emanates with great\npitch in their attempt to further carve the already magnificent canyon.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16648,0,0,0,'A Smooth Trail Covered in Sand','  With its easy, slow curve, this trail is a relief compared to the hard,\nrugged terrain the departing traveller has faced, or a deceptive ploy inviting\nnew players in the canyon\'s game of hardship.  A faint tinge of salt can be\ndetected in the air and the sound of crashing waves emanates with great\npitch in their attempt to further carve the already magnificent canyon.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16649,0,0,0,'Before a Large Boulder','  Looking out from behind this boulder at a beautiful beach of white sand\nand water the color of pale sapphire leaves nothing but disappointment at the\ninaccessibility of the shore.  Perhaps one day the boulder will be moved.\n',138,139584,40,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16700,0,0,0,'Cramped Attic','This humble attic space is striking in its stark simplicity. Slanting ceilings meet with the floor, precluding any wall decorations or other adornments. Absent of windows, the room would be pitch black if not for the blinding portal pulsing in the center. Surrounding the portal are scattered various sundry items used to ready again the battle torn.',0,139529,29,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16701,0,0,0,'Galek Armory','Bloodstains on the worn wooden flooring give off the stench of the battlefield. This armory supplies the Galekian warriors with various equipment for the righteous battle. The room is grimy, dirty and worn out from overuse and abuse. Containers of all sorts are haphazardly arranged, but the dominant feature of the room is a blindingly bright portal.',0,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16702,0,0,0,'Private Room','This room directly above the barracks was once used for storage, but has been\nconverted to a tasteful foyer of a private apartment.  The room is scrubbed\nclean and from the south wafts the mixed smells of a rumpus room.  Overhead, a\nlarge trapdoor leads to a bedroom.  Hung on most of the walls are thick\ntapestries depicting some of the legendary battles of old.  An uncovered window\non the east wall is a reminder of the frigid weather outdoors.',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16703,0,0,0,'Cozy Bedroom','This small bedroom is warm and snug, with large pelts of baanta covering and\ninsulating the walls and ceiling.  The floor is weathered hardwood and covered\nin a thick rug.  Tiny magical lights cling to the furry ceiling, emanating a\nfaint cinnamon scent and casting a soft, ambient glow about the room.  A large\ntrapdoor in the corner leads down to the foyer.',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16704,0,0,0,'Private Lounge','This informal room is meant for relaxation, comfort and entertainment.  There are cushions of varying colors and textures affixed to the walls with steel pegs and braided rope.  The floor has been completely covered in a fuzzy padding, and rugs are tossed on the floor, overlapping one another in an array of blue and gold.  Blankets are pinned to the ceiling and gold film lanterns hang from the pins.  Through an open doorway to the north, the foyer is visible.',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16705,0,0,0,'<o>A Raven\'s Nest<z>','High above the park, at the top of a <G>tree<z>, rests a rather large <o>raven\'s\nnest<z>.  The larger branches have become intricately woven with the smaller and\nflimsier branches making it a cozy place to nest.  Small strips of <k>nightmare\nwool<z> and <k>black mesh<z> have been tucked here and there to keep out the\nelements and unexpected guests.  Scattered chunks of <r>ruby<z>, <W>diamond<z>,\n<r>molten<z> and <B>sapphire<z> are firmly embedded into the floor while long\nstrands of <k>spider silk<z> are draped from the top of the nest.  In the middle\nof the floor, an intricate <k>carving<z> is displayed.  Amazingly, no\n<k>feathers<z> can be found.\n',0,139529,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16706,0,0,0,'A Comfortable Barn','This simple but comfortable barn has several stalls to rest in and hay strewn about the floor. A soft light emanates from a few small hurricane lanterns perched on ledges around the room. The walls are kept clean and smooth and are painted a dark reddish-brown.',0,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16707,0,0,0,'A Ramshackle Backroom','Despite cobwebs this cozy nook appears lived in, although not well  cared for.\nFurniture has been spread around this space without any  apparent semblance of\norder.  Reams of paper and parchment have been  strewn about the floor, making\nit difficult to see the wooden flooring  beneath. Pulsing golden sigils outline\na door to the south.\n',0,139528,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16708,0,0,0,'Unfinished Bungalow On Stilts','The stench from the dump below is so pervasive, anyone with less than a stomach\nof steel may be overcome by nausea.  A red code enforcement sign is posted on\nthe wall, giving an unsettling impression about the safety of the structure.\nLayers of carpet and animal hides cover the floors, walls and ceiling in an\nattempt to keep out the smell of rotten eggs and spoiled fish.  A trapdoor in\nthe floor with a rope leads down to the dump.\n',0,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(16709,0,0,0,'The Great House','This is hidden home is warm reminder of another world for it holds the memories\nof a time long past. The walls are made of exotic dark woods that are richly\nengraved by the best artisans. Beams of sunlight pour though the glass ceiling\nbringing your attention to the beautiful red flowers that stem from a flower\nbed. The south wall is made of solid granite that has been worn smooth by the\npassage of water. Native plants have been placed throughout this room in\ncolorful ceramic vase\'s and are fed from streams beneath the grassy floor.\nSitting quietly you can hear the subtle sounds of water moving beneath.\n',0,139593,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(16710,0,0,0,'Old Weapons Cache','What looks to be an old weapons cache is now an apartment bedroom. \nThe remnants of the cache still remain in the few decaying equipment racks.\nOn each wall hangs a mural depicting battles of lands far away.  A padded cot\nwith a fur blanket rests in the corner awaiting a weary traveler. The heavy oak\ndoor to the east is the only entrance to the room.\n',0,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(16711,0,0,0,'A Simple Apartment','If four walls and a roof were what solely defined an apartment, this would be an\nextremely well-defined one. It is devoid of any personality, accentuated by the\nbare walls and floor. A simple bed sits in one corner and <p>a couch<z> is\npushed up against a wall.\n',0,139273,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16712,0,0,0,'Lord Deslok\'s Chamber','This room is dedicated to Deslok, the First Lord of the Serpents.  Every wall is\ncovered with pictures and murals depicting the legendary weapons master who\nruled for 40 years and wrote the majority of the doctrine on which the order\nitself was formed.  The floor has many scuff marks - some of them curve in a\nserpentine fashion.  There is a doorway to the west and a trapdoor in the floor.\n',0,139529,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16713,0,0,0,'Spine\'s Chamber','The walls and floors of this room are spotless and incredibly clean.  Although\nnot as lavish as the Chamber of Lord Deslok, it\'s still a fine room with many\nadornments of victory and glory.  The lower tiered leaders of the faction use\nthis room for many purposes such as sleeping, storage, and more often than not -\nas the master planning and organization location.  To the west is a an equipment\nand weapons repair room and to the east is a door leading to an ornate chamber.\n',0,139529,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(16714,0,0,0,'Repair Room','Tools of almost every imaginable type litter the floor and various repair\ndevices are scattered amongst the room.  This room is used by some of the realms\ngreatest blacksmiths to repair the factions powerful weapons and armor.\n',0,139529,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(17100,17,50,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  You have come across a strange dark concealed trail that leads\nsouth away from the tundra.  The air is filled here with a musty odor\nfrom a campfire that smolders at your feet.  Large footprints are seen\nleading in a southern direction.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17101,18,50,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  Barren trees, dead from the cold chill of winter run rampantly\nin all directions.  The ground here is a <o>murky brown<1> color and\ndevil weeds grow in clumps.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17102,18,55,-1,'Just South of the Tundra','  Barren trees, dead from the cold chill of winter run rampantly in all\ndirections.  The ground here is a <o>murky brown<1> color and devil\nweeds grow in clumps along the path.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17103,19,50,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  The wooded area is marked with a rancid smell that emanates\nfrom the ground.  Small twigs that stem from the frost bitten\ntrees branch out in clusters along the dotted plain of tarnished grass.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17104,21,52,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  The wooded area is marked with a rancid smell that emanates\nfrom the ground.  Small twigs that stem from the frost bitten\ntrees branch out and from clusters of bothersome obstacle\'s.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17105,17,49,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  The trail narrows and leaves you barely enough room to\nmaneuver through the dense thorny forest.  You spot something\nshining just south of you.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17106,17,48,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Small stepping stones painted bright <y>yellow<1> lie deep in the\nmud and form a ragged circle.  Thin skeletal trees scatter themselves\nalong the tarnished plain.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,32,'',NULL),
(17107,16,50,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  Tall barren trees grow along this frosty region.  Patches of brown\ngrass have been meshed into the muddy path by something large.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17108,15,50,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  Tall barren trees grow along this frosty region on a small path by\nthe tundra.  Patches of grass grow in clumps on the muddy path.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17109,22,52,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  Tall barren trees grow along this frosty region.  Patches of brown\ngrass have been trampled on by something big recently.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17110,23,52,-1,'In an Open Field North of a Skeletal Forest','  You\'ve come across an open field where tiny fragments of rock blanket\nthe ground.  A <k>stone well<1> can be seen here bulging out of the earth\nchoked with weeds that surround its circular shape.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17111,14,51,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  A rancid smell lingers heavily through the thick skeletal forest.  A\ncarcass of what seems like a small animal is seen protruding under a small\ndirt mound.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17112,13,52,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  Smoke rolls into the sky and casts a dark shroud over the chilled\ntrail from a large campfire seen burning in the underbrush.  Thin barkless\ntrees double in number that camouflage the trail slightly.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17113,12,52,-1,'Northwest Corner of a Skeletal Forest','  A skeletal forest leads in every direction along this path.\nClumps of frost bitten grass cause you more hardships as you travel deeper\ninto its midst.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17114,12,51,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  Thin barren trees waver easily from a strong gust of wind that blows in\nfrom the north.  Small patches of frost lightly cover the dark colored\ngrass within the myriad of trees that stretch out for miles.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17115,13,51,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  A muddy path leads here through the clusters of thin trees that\nrun around you a great distance.  Small mounds of compose litter the\nground and rustle beneath your feet.  Just south of you, you spot a dark\nfigure shifting through the woods with eerie ease.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17116,12,50,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  The trail is completely visible and a jumble of footprints can be seen\nleading in each direction.  The aroma of the woods inflames your nostrils\nwith the smell of pine, mildew, and a scent you can\'t quite make out.\nFallen boughs have toppled over a few small shrubs to your west\nnear a dirt mound.   A large boulder, covered in brittle <g>green\nmoss<1> bulges out of the drenched soaked earth that can possibly be\nused to rest upon.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17117,23,51,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  This trail is hardly visible amidst the staggering number of skeletal trees\nthat blanket the landscape.  A Large boulder, covered in brittle <g>green\nmoss<1> bulges out of the muddy path that can be used to rest upon.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17118,22,51,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  This trail is hardly visible amidst the staggering number of trees\nthat blanket the landscape.  A large boulder covered in brittle <g>green\nmoss<1> bulges out of the muddy path where white coated mushrooms\nsprout.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17119,21,51,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  This trail is hardly visible amidst the staggering number of skeletal\ntrees that blanket the landscape.  A large boulder covered in brittle\n<g>green moss<1> bulges out of the muddy path where a patch of white\ncoated mushrooms sprout.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17120,13,50,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  This trail is hardly visible amidst the staggering number of skeletal\ntrees that blanket the landscape.  A large boulder covered in brittle\n<g>green moss<1> bulges out of the muddy path.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17121,14,50,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  On a disused forgotten trail, you venture through a pasture of low-\nstemmed trees covered in a thick layer of brittle <g>green moss<1>.  Small\nspiders spin cobwebs off the lifeless branches of this skeletal forest\nthat travels as far as the eye can see.  Woodbine leaves litter most of the\nsurrounding area.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17122,14,49,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Thin low-stemmed trees covered in <g>green moss<1> grow in the faded\nearth.  The sodden pasture makes your headway difficult to manage.  There\nis a large campfire here providing warmth from the bitter cold.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17123,15,49,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Small shrubs of wild berries grow within the vast number of skeletal\ntrees that run rampantly all around you.  Woodbine leaves litter most of the\nsurrounding area.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17124,16,49,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Low stemmed trees have been coated with spiderwebs that dress\nthemselves on the lifeless branches of the forest that spans out\nbefore you.  Small groves of wild berries can be seen along this frost\nbitten path.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17125,16,48,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Low-stemmed trees covered in purple-<g>green moss<1> give the muddy\nlandscape character where the earth has faded away into a damp isolated place.\nTiny fireflies swarm lazily around you briefly before moving to the next\nsection of the forest where coated powdered white mushrooms grow.  The\ntreetops form a natural splintery archway here.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17126,16,47,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  The trail steepens here within the vast forest that surrounds you.  Even a\nwell trained adventurer would not travel alone through this path where\nspider webs drape over the seemingly haunted low-stemmed trees that shape\nthemselves into creatures of your own imagination.  The stillness here\nsends chills down your spine in one spot in particular, where a patch of\npowdered mushrooms grow.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17127,20,50,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  The trail leads through a vast forest of skeletal trees that run for miles.\nA large <o>haycock<1> lays upon the ground by a nearby firepit.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17128,21,50,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  Barren boughs lie neatly piled here within the myriad of lifeless trees\nthat run in every direction.  Groves of <y>yellow-stemmed raspberries<1>\ngrow here on the muddy path.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17129,22,50,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  Rising over a <g>moss<1> covered hillside you can see the forest stretch\nout a great distance.  Withered boughs, mixed in with woodbine lay\nscattered along the muddy path.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17130,23,50,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  Deep in the tangled dead forest, a trail barely visible leads through\na pasture of wild raspberries and dead skeletal trees.  A light frost has\nsettled on the ground near a <g>clover patch<1> by tall thickets.  A rancid\nsmell lingers heavily here.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17131,13,49,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Deep in the tangled deed forest, a trail barely visible leads through a\npasture of wild raspberries and dead skeletal trees.  A light frost has settled\non the ground near a <g>clover patch<1> by tall thickets.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17132,18,49,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Deep in the tangled forest, a trail barely visible leads through\na pasture of wild raspberries and dead skeletal trees.  A light frost\nhas settled on the ground by a <g>clover patch<1> near tall thickets.\nA rancid smell lingers heavily here.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17133,19,49,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Deep in the tangled forest, a trail barely visible leads through\na pasture of wild raspberries and dead skeletal trees.  A light frost\nhas settled on the ground by a <g>clover patch<1> near tall thickets.\nA rancid smell lingers heavily here.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17134,17,47,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Deep in the tangled forest, a trail barely visible, leads through\na pasture of wild raspberries and dead trees.  A light frost has\nsettled on the ground by a <g>clover patch<1> near tall thickets.  A\nrancid smell lingers heavily here.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17135,12,49,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Fresh footprints can be seen within the muddy pasture.  A myriad of\nlow-stemmed trees span\'s out over the forest floor a great distance.\n<g>Iceplant<1> slowly creeps towards a east passageway.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17136,23,49,-1,'A Skeletal forest','  Large footprints can be seen on the ground leading through the myriad of\ntrees the run in every direction.  <g>Iceplant<1> begins to creep slowly\nwest overtaking much of the landscape.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17137,12,48,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Large footprints can be seen within the myriad of trees that run\nall around you.  <1>Iceplant<1> begins to grow here over taking much of\nthe ground cover.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17138,22,49,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Large footprints can be seen within the myriad of trees that run\nall around you.  <g>Iceplant<1> begins to grow here over taking much of\nthe ground cover.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17139,21,49,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  The trail leads through a vast skeletal forest filled with iceplant\nand tall thickets.  Small shrubs of wild berries <y>yellow<1>-purple and\n<b>blue<1> scattered themselves within the myriad of trees.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17140,18,47,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  The trail leads through a vast forest filled with iceplant and\ntall thickets.  Small shrubs of wild berries scatter themselves within\nthe myriad of trees.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17141,20,49,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  The trail leads through a vast forest filled with iceplant and\ntall thickets.  Small shrubs of wild berries <y>yellow<1>, purple and\n<b>blue<1> scatter themselves within the myriad of trees.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17142,19,48,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  The trail leads through a sodden pasture where iceplant and tall\nthickets grow within the myriad of trees that stretch out a great\ndistance.  Small shrubs of wild berries <y>yellow<1>, purple and\n<b>blue<1> scatter themselves far across the plain.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17143,23,48,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  The trail leads through a muddy pasture where iceplant and tall\nthickets grow within a myriad of trees that stretches a great distance.\nSmall shrubs of berries, <y>yellow<1>, purple and <b>blue<1> scatter\nthemselves far across the plain.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17144,22,48,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  The trail leads through a muddy pasture of low-stemmed trees\nwhere iceplant and tall thickets grow heavily.  Small shrubs of wild\nberries dot the landscape.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17145,21,48,-1,'In the Skeletal Forest','  The trail leads through a muddy pasture of low-stemmed trees where\nicepant and tall thickets cover much of the surrounding area.  Bright\nvibrant <R>wild berries<1> dot the wooded area.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17146,20,48,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  The dark trail is overgrown with small raspberry shrubs and iceplant\nthat flow into a pool of tall barren trees.  Nestled on a tree limb you\ncan see a faded tinged <o>nest<1> just above your reach.  There is a rancid\nsmell in the air.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17147,20,48,0,'Low-Stemmed Tree','  Up on a tree limb you notice that the <o>nest<1> isn\'t as close as you\nthought.  From here you can see the dark forest around you widen a\ngreat distance.\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17148,20,48,1,'High Above A Treetop','  A small <o>nest<1> dangles from a lifeless tree limb just west of you.\nFrom here you notice a large puff of <k>black smoke<1> rising in the\nsoutheast.\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17149,19,48,1,'On A Western Limb','  You\'ve managed to reach a faded <o>nest<1> on the frail limb.\nIt would be a hard fall if you lose your grasp.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,1,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17150,18,48,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Cluttered in a large neat pile rest a mound of leaves by a withered\ntree.  Spiders spin marvelous webs along the many small bushes that grow\nhere.  There is a horrible smell in the air!\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17151,13,48,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  The barkless trees seem like thin ghosts wavering in the vast\nforest.  Patches of grasslands can be seen here in sections as you\nventure further along this path.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17152,14,48,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Curls of <k>smoke<1> drift and slumber through the low-stemmed trees\nfrom a campfire that smolders within the underbrush.  An occasional\npatch of <W>fungus<1> grows on the few toppled trees that lean against\nlong lifeless limbs and tiny fragments of pebbles lie scattered across the\nplain.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17153,15,48,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  The air seems to lose its frosty bite as you continue through\nthe myriad of low-stemmed trees.  Patches of grass grow in sections\nacross the wide plain.  Carefully keeping your eye on the trail, you\ncatch sight of something located on the base of a tree.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17154,12,47,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Standing just on the edge of a skeletal forest you feel the air begin to\nwarm.  A grassy hillside slopes east of you where a small impassable\nmountain resides that provides a clear shallow stream running through the\nwoods.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17155,15,47,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Up in the distance, you can make out what seems to be a clearing of some\nsort.  Large faded footprints buried deeply into the muddy ground lead\nthrough a cluster of tall skeletal trees.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17156,14,47,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Large dirt hillsides form here like swells of ocean bubbling up out of the\nearth.  A shallow stream that runs south of you carries away small debris\nwith its current.  Large jagged rocks and fallen boughs make the southern\npassageway impassable.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17157,13,47,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  Standing on a hillside you survey your surroundings carefully.  Tall\ndead oak trees have been uprooted here from the constant harsh weather.\nHeaps of compost drift and slumber on the muddy path scattering debris\nin your eyes.  From here you spot a small stream running just south of you\nthrough a heavily wooded area.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17158,15,46,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  The road here is surprisingly dry and well tended considering the\ndamp weather.  The road leads through a valley of swelling hillsides filled\nwith dead oaks, pines and occasional shrubs that dot the landscape.  The air\nhere is crisp and clean, your senses tell you something out of the ordinary\nlingers here.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17159,14,46,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  A well kept road leads through a valley of swelling hillsides filled with\nlarge dead oaks, pines and occasional shrubs that dot the landscape.  The road\nis surprisingly dry considering the damp weather.  You wonder what powerfull\nmagic could linger so long to keep this road dry while the rest of\nthe forest submits the mother nature...Your gut instincts tell you you\'re\nabout to find out.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17160,13,46,-1,'A Skeletal Forest','  A well kept dirt road leads through a valley of swelling hillsides filled\nwith tall thin skeletal trees and shrubs.  In the distance a flock of sparrows\ncan be seen flying above what seems like the tallest tree in the forest.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17161,12,46,-1,'In a Clearing','  The edges of this forest have been formed by dark sweet smelling fir\ntrees that curve round in a ragged semi-circle.  To the west the ground\nhas broken off and drops three hundred feet in a series of crumbling shale\nledges and fractured cliffs.  A clear stream runs out of the woods and\nacross the splintery rock floor where the land has dropped away.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17162,11,46,-1,'On a Crumbling Shale Ledge','  The water descends the shale ledges in a series of small waterfalls\nmade up and any number of rainbow colors.  Below you can see a forest of\nfir trees choked with great elms.\n',120,131072,29,0,0,0,1,5,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17163,11,46,-2,'On a Crumbling Shale Ledge','  Small waves of water lightly tremble over your feet here, making your\ndecent slippery and hard to manage a steady foothold.  Tiny pebbles, sparking\nblue plunge downward into a large grate just below you.\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17164,11,46,-3,'Below a Cliffside','  An iron grate is seen here below the cliffside where water runs far\nbelow a deep dark chasm.  A well-kept dirt road leads through a forest of\ntall skeletal trees and small faded shrubs.\n',120,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17165,12,46,-3,'On a Well Kept Road','  A huge <g>hoary pine tree<1> stands here pulsating with life amidst the\nfir trees the run rampantly around you.  It stands fifty-feet tall with\nlong feathered branches that spreads over the forest floor fourteen feet\nin length.  Another wondrous feat of magic is at work here as you glance\nat the tree.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17166,13,46,-3,'On a Well Kept Road','  The land here has been cleared away where a soft <R>russet<1> colored\nroad leads perfectly through the thin skeletal forest.  The road measures\neighteen feet in length and is free of debris.  Not even a single footprint\nmarks its path.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17167,14,46,-3,'On a Well Kept Road','  The <R>russet<1> colored road is well kept here, only a handfull of\nleaves mark its path.  High above, on a large dead tree a flock of crows\nsit silently watching you intently.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17168,15,46,-3,'On a Well Kept Road','  Over a gentle slope you travel on a wide road where tall slender trees\nwith wide spreading tops fill the landscape.  The road is well kept here,\nonly a handfull of leaves mark its path within the soft <R>russet<1>\ncolored earth.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17169,16,46,-3,'On a Well Kept Road','  Over a hillside you travel through the forest with long slender\ntrunks and wide spreading treetops that fill the landscape.  A well kept\nroad is here, only a handfull of leaves mark its path within the soft\n<R>russet<1> colored earth.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17170,17,46,-3,'On a Well Kept Road','  Over the dirt hillsides you travel through a thorny forest of trees.\nThe road continues east and west here on a well kept <R>russet<1> colored\nroad.  One set of single footprints can be seen here leading nowhere.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17171,17,47,-3,'On a Well Kept Road','  Over the hillside you travel through a forest with long slender trunks\nand wide spreading tops.  A well kept road is here, only a handfull of leaves\nmark its path within the soft <R>russet<1> colored earth.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17172,18,47,-3,'On a Well Kept Road','  Over the hillsides you travel through a forest with long slender trunks\nand wide spreading tops that fill the landscape.  A well kept road is here, only\na handfull of leaves mark its path within the soft <R>russet<1> colored\nearth.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17173,19,47,-3,'On a Well Kept Road','  Over the hillsides you travel through a forest of long slender trunks\nand wide spreading top that fill the landscape.  A well kept road is here,\nonly a handfull of leaves mark its path within the soft <R>russet<1>\ncolored earth.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17174,20,47,-3,'On a Well Kept Road','  Over the hillsides you travel through a forest with long slender trunks\nand wide spreading tops that fill the landscape.  A well kept road is here, only\na handfull of leaves mark its path within the soft <R>russet<1> colored\nearth.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17175,18,46,-3,'Dead End','  Large dirt hillsides form here through a forest of fir trees.\nThe road here is very well kept and leads back west.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17176,21,47,-3,'On a Well Kept Road','  You have come upon the high grounds of the forest, from here you spot a\nsmall clearing.  Further, you spot a campsite surrounded in a fortress of\ntall end-spiked trees, sewn together in mud and woodbine.  A <k>black\nshroud of smoke<1> curls through the air from a large firepit at the\ncenter of the camp.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17177,22,47,-3,'A Small Clearing','  You have entered a small clearing in the forest.  The grass and\nweeds that succeed in growing here have been trampled down by the frequent\nuse of the path.  The trees to the south give this spot an empty and\nabandoned feeling.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17178,22,46,-3,'Near the Small Clearing','  You can barely walk through the many dead branches that litter the\nground.  Like hardened bones, the branches crack and shifts beneath\nyou.  A tree limb grabs hold of your sleeve as you struggle to find a\nclear spot to step.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17179,22,48,-3,'Near the Small Clearing','  The surrounding dead bush and forest effectively block any further\npassage in either direction other than the one from which you just\narrived.  This spot is not secluded enough to provide a protected or\nsafe resting place, unless you keep one eye open.\n',120,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17180,23,47,-3,'Before the Gates','  Before you stands a large wooden crudely built archway leading into\na small campsite.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17181,24,47,-3,'Ogre Campsite','  Before you stands an ogre campsite of thatched straw huts that surround a\nfirepit dug deeply into the ground.  A large boar is seen roasting in\nits scorching heat.  The road forks here ending before three large huts,\neach facing the pits blaze.  Tall trees and rough terrain make all other\nexits impassable off the campsites outskirts.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17182,25,47,-3,'Chief Ogre\'s Hut','  This hut is much more simpler than the others.  A sturdy wooden bed\nis seen resting along the northern wall by a black cook stove.\nA small mirror hangs on the western wall with dozens of wood framed\nportraits that decorate the room.  A small oval basin is seen upon a\nwooden pedestal.\n',120,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(17183,24,48,-3,'The Church of Zelpth','  Upon entering the hut, your eyes focus on the few splintery pews\nthat rests along the faithfull oiled floors that shine with its own\nserene inner light.  A black cookstove takes up much space along the\nwestern wall by a small woodstack located in an alcove next to it.  A\nshrine faces the rear wall of the hut.\n',120,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(17184,24,46,-3,'Sorcerers Study','  This room looks larger then is appears from the outside.  A polished oak\ndesk, encrusted with tiny emerald runes running along its trim, sits\ncentered upon the soft <R>russet<1> colored floor.  A large bookcase\nstruggles to support an impressive collection of elven scrolls, maps and\ndiaries.  A basin is set upon a wooden pedestal next to a brick fireplace\non the north side of the hut.\n',120,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(17185,20,51,-1,'A Path North of the Skeletal Forest','  The wooded area is marked with a rancid smell that emanates\nfrom the ground.  Small twigs that stem from the frost bitten\ntrees branch out in clusters along the dotted plain of tarnished grass.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17186,18,46,-2,'Above a Hoary Pine','  The large pine stretches upwards into a wide spreading top.  Slender\ntrunks reach outward off the trees base.\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,3,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17187,18,46,-1,'Above the Treetop','  The cluster of trees make it impossible to see outward clearly.\nSparrows chirp madly in a nearby nest.\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17188,19,47,-2,'Above a Hoary Pine','  The tree extends upwards into a canopy of slender trunks.  Blue birds\nsquawk at you from above.\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,3,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17189,14,46,-2,'On a Frail Limb','  The tree extends upwards in a series of frail limbs.  A flock of crows\nsit silently above you.\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,3,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17190,14,46,-1,'Above the Treetop','  Here you can see the forest span out a great distance.  A small\nand impassable mountain rises over in the west.\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,3,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17191,12,46,-2,'Above a Hoary Pine','  Standing on a slender trunk of the tree you can see the forest span\nout a great distance.  Claw marks can be seen here deeply into the limb.\nThe branches extend far up into a canopy of darkness.\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,3,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17192,12,46,-1,'Above a Hoary Pine','  Large slender trunks extend outward here that shift slightly from a gust\nof wind blowing in from the west.  From here you spot a small impassable\nmountain to the west.\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,3,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17193,12,46,0,'Above a Hoary Pine','  Up further into the cluster of slender trunks you climb into darkened\ncanopy of leaves.  You can hear the sound of buzzing nearby.\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,3,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17194,12,46,1,'In a Treetop','  A buzzing sound can be heard coming from the eastern limb.  Looking\ndown, you can see that you are about fifty feet up! Falling would\nmean a nasty death.\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,4,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17195,12,46,2,'Above a Treetop','  A large wasps nest dangles on a sturdy knotted branch within a canopy\nof clustered leaves that spread far and wide of the great thick trunk\nof the pine.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,5,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17196,14,46,0,'On a Tree Limb','  Standing on a sturdy tree limb you can see the forest span out before you\nfilled with dead lifeless trees.  The tree extends upwards where many\nlimbs offer support.\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17197,14,46,1,'Home of an Owlbear','  A large Owlbear\'s nest is seen along a nearby tree limb just east of you.\nA gust of wind blows in from the north shaking the tree slightly causing the\nleaves to drift silently to the ground.\n',120,131072,4,0,0,0,0,0,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17198,14,47,0,'On a Sturdy Limb','  Sparrows chirp madly as you approach a tinged nest far above your reach.\nFrom here you can see the land spread out a great distance.\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17199,16,49,0,'On a Frail Limb','  Standing on a frail limb you notice a small pile of dead leaves at the\nend of the limb.  You are about five feet up the tree....\n',120,131072,35,0,0,0,0,0,3,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17200,0,0,0,'The Northern Shore of Brightmoon Bay','  You are on the northern shore of the Great Bay of Brightmoon, crystal clear\nwaters stretch to the south far across to the other side of the bay. Southwest\nof here you can see the great Sea Gate, and to the east, the sparkling city of\nBrightmoon is visible.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17201,0,0,0,'The Northern Shore of Brightmoon Bay','  You are on the northern shore of the Great Bay of Brightmoon, crystal clear\nwaters stretch to the south far across to the other side of the bay. Southwest\nof here you can see the great Sea Gate, and to the east, the sparkling city of\nBrightmoon is visible.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17202,0,0,0,'The Western Shore of Brightmoon Bay','  You are on the western shore of the Great Bay of Brightmoon, crystal clear\nwaters stretch to the east far across to the other side of the bay. South-\nwest of here you can see the great Sea Gate, and to the east, the sparkling\ncity of Brightmoon is visible.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17203,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Bay','  Clear water stretches in all directions about you. You can see the white\ntowers of Brightmoon past the eastern shore of this great bay, and to the west\nthe magnificent Sea Gate is visible. The waterfront docks are south of here.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17204,0,0,0,'The Northern Shore of Brightmoon Bay','  You are on the eastern shore of the Great Bay of Brightmoon, crystal clear\nwaters stretch to the north far across to the other side of the bay. West of\nhere you can see the great Sea Gate, and to the southeast, the sparkling\ncity of Brightmoon is visible.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17205,0,0,0,'The Northern Shore of Brightmoon Bay','  You are on the eastern shore of the Great Bay of Brightmoon, crystal clear\nwaters stretch to the north far across to the other side of the bay. West of\nhere you can see the great Sea Gate, and to the southeast, the sparkling\ncity of Brightmoon is visible.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17206,0,0,0,'The Western Shore of Brightmoon Bay','  You are on the western shore of the Great Bay of Brightmoon, crystal clear\nwaters stretch to the east far across to the other side of the bay. South-\nwest of here you can see the great Sea Gate, and to the east, the sparkling\ncity of Brightmoon is visible.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17207,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Bay','  Clear waters stretch in all directions about you. You can see the white\ntowers of Brightmoon past the eastern shore of this great bay, and to the west\nthe magnificent Sea Gate is visible. The waterfront docks are south of here.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17208,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Bay','  Clear waters stretch in all directions about you. You can see the white\ntowers of Brightmoon past the eastern shore of this great bay, and to the west\nthe magnificent Sea Gate is visible. The waterfront docks are south of here.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17209,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Bay','  Clear waters stretch in all directions about you. You can see the white\ntowers of Brightmoon past the eastern shore of this great bay, and to the west\nthe magnificent Sea Gate is visible. The waterfront docks are south of here.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17210,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Bay','  Clear waters stretch in all directions about you. You can see the white\ntowers of Brightmoon past the eastern shore of this great bay, and to the west\nthe magnificent Sea Gate is visible. The waterfront docks are south of here.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17211,0,0,0,'The Eastern Shore of Brightmoon Bay','  You are on the eastern shore of the Great Bay of Brightmoon, crystal clear\nwaters stretch to the north far across to the other side of the bay. West of\nhere you can see the great Sea Gate, and to the southeast, the sparkling\ncity of Brightmoon is visible.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17212,0,0,0,'The Western Shore of Brightmoon Bay','  You are on the western shore of the Great Bay of Brightmoon, crystal clear\nwaters stretch to the east far across to the other side of the bay. South-\nwest of here you can see the great Sea Gate, and to the east, the sparkling\ncity of Brightmoon is visible. South of here is a small maintenance dock.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17213,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Bay','  Clear waters stretch in all directions about you. You can see the white\ntowers of Brightmoon past the eastern shore of this great bay, and to the west\nthe magnificent Sea Gate is visible. The waterfront docks are east of here.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17214,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Docks','  Salty winds whip across these waterfront docks, adding a pleasant tang to the\nair. The docks are made in titanic proportions, and seem to be magnificently\ncrafted to raise and lower seamlessly with the tide. The docks also seem to be\nin very good condition, considering the corrosive nature of the ocean, and the\ngeneral wear and tear from feet and boats. The Sea Gate is visible high in the\nair to the west, and Brightmoon City hugs the bay to the east. A gangplank leads\neast to a low merchant\'s ship.\n',135,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17215,0,0,0,'On the Deck of a Merchant Ship','  This small merchant ship bears blue sails and a flag with the White Flame of\nGalek. The decks have recently been cleaned, but they bear the marks and\nscratches of years of use. This ship creaks softly as the waves rock it against\nthe waterfront docks. A gangplank leads west to the docks.\n',135,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17216,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Docks','  Salty winds whip across these waterfront docks, adding a pleasant tang to the\nair. The docks are made in titanic proportions, and seem to be magnificently\ncrafted to raise and lower seamlessly with the tide. The docks also seem to be\nin very good condition, considering the corrosive nature of the ocean, and the\ngeneral wear and tear from feet and boats. The Sea Gate is visible high in the\nair to the west, and Brightmoon City hugs the bay to the east.\n',135,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17217,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Bay','  Clear waters stretch in all directions about you. You can see the white\ntowers of Brightmoon past the eastern shore of this great bay, and to the west\nthe magnificent Sea Gate is visible. The waterfront docks are south and west of\nhere.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17218,0,0,0,'The Eastern Shore of Brightmoon Bay','  You are on the eastern shore of the Great Bay of Brightmoon, crystal clear\nwaters stretch to the north far across to the other side of the bay. West of\nhere you can see the great Sea Gate, and to the southeast, the sparkling\ncity of Brightmoon is visible.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17219,0,0,0,'The Bottom of a Squat Tower','  This squat, white tower is one of the fortifications of the Brightmoon Sea\nGate. The base of the gate can be used as a small garrison for forces in times\nof war, and from the top of the tower, arrows and other weapons can be used\nagainst invading forces. The tower and Sea Gate are made of a strange type of\nwhite marble, and not a single inch of it is soiled. A ladder leads up to the\ntop of the tower, and the machinery of the Sea Gate is housed in a building\neast of here.\n',135,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(17220,0,0,0,'Inside the Sea Gate','  This huge stone room contains the bowels of the great Brightmoon Sea Gate.\nGears, ropes, pulleys, springs, levers and a multitude of other odd devices make\nup the machinery of this titanic gate that guards Brightmoon Bay from raiders\nand invading armies. You wonder what sort of engineering genius was responsible\nfor this creation. A maintenance dock leads east into the bay, and west of here\nis the bottom of one of the Sea Gate\'s white towers.\n',135,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(17221,0,0,0,'A Small Maintenance Dock','  The dock appears to be placed for access to the Sea Gate, which towers west of\nhere. From here you can see just how marvelous the Sea Gate really is, with its\nhigh marble towers and shining fortifications. It is no wonder that the gate is\na landmark of the western sea. A door west leads into the bowels of the Sea Gate\nand all around you is Brightmoon Bay.\n',135,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17222,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Bay','  Clear waters stretch in all directions about you. You can see the white\ntowers of Brightmoon past the eastern shore of this great bay, and to the west\nthe magnificent Sea Gate is visible. The waterfront docks are east of here, and\nthere is a small maintenance dock west.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17223,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Docks','  Salty winds whip across these waterfront docks, adding a pleasant tang to the\nair. The docks are made in titanic proportions, and seem to be magnificently\ncrafted to raise and lower seamlessly with the tide. The docks also seem to be\nin very good condition, considering the corrosive nature of the ocean, and the\ngeneral wear and tear from feet and boats. The Sea Gate is visible high in the\nair to the west, and Brightmoon City hugs the bay to the east.\n',135,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17224,0,0,0,'On the Deck of a Merchant Ship','  This small merchant ship bears blue sails and a flag with the White Flame of\nGalek. The decks have recently been cleaned, but they bear the marks and\nscratches of years of use. This ship creaks softly as the waves rock it against\nthe Brightmoon waterfront docks. A hatch leads down into the ship\'s galley.\n',135,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17225,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Docks','  Salty winds whip across these waterfront docks, adding a pleasant tang to the\nair. The docks are made in titanic proportions, and seem to be magnificently\ncrafted to raise and lower seamlessly with the tide. The docks also seem to be\nin very good condition, considering the corrosive nature of the ocean, and the\ngeneral wear and tear from feet and boats. The Sea Gate is visible high in the\nair to the west, and Brightmoon City hugs the bay to the east.\n',135,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17226,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Bay','  Clear waters stretch in all directions about you. You can see the white\ntowers of Brightmoon past the eastern shore of this great bay, and to the west\nthe magnificent Sea Gate is visible. The waterfront docks are south and west of\nhere.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17227,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Bay','  Clear waters stretch in all directions about you. You can see the white\ntowers of Brightmoon past the eastern shore of this great bay, and to the west\nthe magnificent Sea Gate is visible. The waterfront docks are south and west of\nhere.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17228,0,0,0,'The Brightmoon Bay','  Clear waters stretch in all directions about you. You can see the white\ntowers of Brightmoon past the eastern shore of this great bay, and to the west\nthe magnificent Sea Gate is visible. The waterfront docks are south and west of\nhere. Fisherman\'s Wharf is visible east of here.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(17229,0,0,0,'Under the Brightmoon Sea Gate','  The air is much cooler beneath this giant gate, which is one of the main\ndefenses of Brightmoon City. The crystal clear waters of Brightmoon Bay offer\nyou a view of a double porticullis contraption. One set that raises from the\nwater, and another that lowers from above, in the gate. When both are open, the\nlargest merchant ship can enter, but when both are closed a lone swimmer would\nhave trouble gaining entrance. The Argorian Sea spreads out west of here, and\nthe Brightmoon Bay is to the east.\n',135,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
