(19000,0,0,0,'Poop Deck','The center of the poop deck has a commanding <o>view<1> of the ship\'s forward\ndecks.  An austerely carved <o>railing<1> runs the length of the stern, saving\ndrunks\nfrom the relentlessly cleansing waters.  The long boom hanging from the main\nmast slowly sways overhead under a shroud of <c>rigging<1>.\n',0,139584,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19001,0,0,0,'Poop Deck','  The starboard poop deck is somewhat less battered than the main deck to the\nfore.  A simple railing is all there is to keep the waters at bay.  The main\nand fore sails tower overhead, patched and stitched in materials gathered from\ndistant lands. \n',0,139584,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19002,0,0,0,'Starboard Deck','  This section of the deck is much more rough, with large gouges in the\ndecking and smears of tar caulking applied hastily.  The railing is chipped,\nand rope has been wrapped around it to protect it and give the crew a better\ngrip.  Tough, tar-coated rope shrouds descend from the top mast and attach to\nthe side of the vessel.\n',0,139584,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19003,0,0,0,'Center Deck','The center deck is dominated by the main mast, which is made of strong\nblackbutt wood and well kept, though weathered.  Unlike the fore mast, the\nmain mast and riggings are devoid of any decorative markings.  The plank\ndecking is a bit rougher here, and the tar caulking is obvious in several\nspots.  The gaff and main boom sport a full sail of dark blue-grey with a\nbrilliant emblem of the rising sun. \n',0,139584,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19004,0,0,0,'Foredeck','  This \'ere is the bow of the ship, lined with a well-smoothed railing of fine\nwood.  The planks are kept well-tidied by the crew in spite of the sea air and\nfowl.  The fore mast and bowsprit are made of dark wood and are marked by small \n<o>inscriptions<1> carved by the mates of the ship.  The jibs are colored red,\norange and yellow to mimic a colorful sunrise.  The <o>figurehead<1> is barely\nvisible here.\n',0,401728,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19005,0,0,0,'Port Deck','  This section of the deck is much more rough, with large gouges in the\ndecking and smears of tar caulking applied hastily.  The railing is chipped,\nand rope has been wrapped around it to protect it and give the crew a better\ngrip.  Tough, tar-coated rope shrouds descend from the top mast and attach to\nthe side of the vessel. \n',0,139584,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19006,0,0,0,'Poop Deck','  The larboard poop deck is somewhat less battered than the main deck to the\nfore.  A simple railing is all there is to keep the waters at bay.  The main\nand fore sails tower overhead, patched and stitched in materials gathered from\ndistant lands. \n',0,139584,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19007,0,0,0,'The Tequila Sunrise Common Room','This room is an example of bright disarray, every inch of every wall covered\nin loot, prizes, defaced portraits of past crew members, scribbled-on maps,\nstuffed fish and other game.  The tiny spots not covered in mementos are\ninscribed with initials or are covered in small <o>scraps of cloth<1> fastened\nwith\nshiny brass nails.\n',0,139592,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(19008,0,0,0,'Crew Quarters','  Pew!  It\'s obvious by the stench that rough, bloodthirsty pirates take their\nleave here.  This room appears to accommodate several crewmembers and their\nloot, and all the dirty, smelly accoutrements of daily life aboard a boat. \nThe bulkheads here are completely covered in marks, notes and scratches.  The\nfloorboards, in the few places you can see them, are stained and scuffed. \n',0,139592,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19009,0,0,0,'Powder Room','  Spotless floorboards and walls greet visitors of the powder room.  This is\nthe domain of the quartermaster, and the crew thinks twice before crossing\nhim.  As such, there are no marks of any kind on any of the bare, carefully\nscrubbed and whitewashed walls.  A thick white rug with four black spots\ncovers most of the floor. \n',0,139592,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19010,0,0,0,'Crew Quarters','  Pew!  It\'s obvious by the stench that rough, bloodthirsty pirates take their\nleave here.  This room appears to accommodate several crewmembers and their\nloot, and all the dirty, smelly accoutrements of daily life aboard a boat. \nThe bulkheads here are completely covered in marks, notes and scratches.  The\nfloorboards, in the few places you can see them, are stained and scuffed. \n',0,139592,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19011,0,0,0,'Captain\'s Cabin','  Beautifully kept flooring and painstakingly and decoratively carved walls set\nthis room apart from the others.  Vibrantly colored panels of the finest silk\nflutter slightly against the bulkhead.  The air smells pleasant here, and light\nfilters in from a <c>window<1> in the stern.\n',0,139592,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19012,0,0,0,'Main Mast & Shroud','  Looking down from the rigging of the main mast, the top deck can be seen\nframed by water.  A small platform is overhead from which the yards can be\naccessed.  Dark sailcloth hangs from them, bearing the emblem of a rising sun. \n',0,139584,58,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19013,0,0,0,'Crow\'s Nest','  This small platform provides both something of a respite from the precarious\nrigging and a vantage point to observe everything around the ship.  The top\nmast runs a bit higher up.  From here one can see two <o>flags<1>, one flying\nfrom\nthe foremast and another directly overhead.\n',0,139584,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19014,0,0,0,'Filthy Brig','The wooden plank here is covered in a thick sludge of dirt, seawater\nand other refuse too disgusting or mingled with other material to identify.  To\nthe north and south are holding cells for those unlucky enough to have crossed\nthe quartermaster and crew.\n',0,139592,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(19015,0,0,0,'Disgusting Cell','A small, filthy cell has been built here to house any crewmember that has\ncrossed the quartermaster or fellow shipmates.  The thick stench of body odor\nand elimination are permanently steeped into every surface.  There are no\ndecorations or furnishings given to prisoners who await their turn to walk the\nplank and meet their partners in crime in Davy Jones Locker.\n',0,139592,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(19016,0,0,0,'Disgusting Cell','A small, filthy cell has been built here to house any crewmember that has\ncrossed the quartermaster or fellow shipmates.  The thick stench of body odor\nand elimination are permanently steeped into every surface.  There are no\ndecorations or furnishings given to prisoners who await their turn to walk the\nplank and meet their partners in crime in Davy Jones Locker.\n',0,139592,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(19024,0,0,0,'The Briny Deep','The underwater river and ocean currents of the world all eventually lead\nto this area of the ocean floor, far below the surface.  A large amount of\njunk that has been lost at sea gathers here.\n',0,139585,53,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19025,0,0,0,'Sandy Beach','  Fine white sand covers this area and is scattered with seaweed, small\npebbles, abandoned seashells and the occasional unidentifiable garbage the\nocean spits up onto the shoreline.  The ocean breeze is strong in both force\nand aroma here, and sometimes a bit of salty water is deposited on the sand. \n',164,139264,54,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19026,0,0,0,'Sandy Beach','  Fine white sand covers this area and is scattered with seaweed, small\npebbles, abandoned seashells and the occasional unidentifiable garbage the\nocean spits up onto the shoreline.  The ocean breeze is strong in both force\nand aroma here, and sometimes a bit of salty water is deposited on the sand. \n',164,139264,54,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
