(19040,0,0,0,'Sandy Beach','  Fine white sand covers this area and is scattered with seaweed, small\npebbles, abandoned seashells and the occasional unidentifiable garbage the\nocean spits up onto the shoreline.  The ocean breeze is strong in both force\nand aroma here, and sometimes a bit of salty water is deposited on the sand. \n',164,139264,54,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19041,0,0,0,'Sandy Beach','  Fine white sand covers this area and is scattered with seaweed, small\npebbles, abandoned seashells and the occasional unidentifiable garbage the\nocean spits up onto the shoreline.  The ocean breeze is strong in both force\nand aroma here, and sometimes a bit of salty water is deposited on the sand. \n',0,139264,54,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19042,0,0,0,'Rocky Beach','  The sand peters out here and turns into a mixture of large, rugged rocks and\nsmall, smooth pebbles.  Bits of dead coral and crushed seashells are sprinkled\namong the rocks, and seaweed clings tightly to the more roughly textured\nrocks.  The ocean spray is regular here, and many of the rocks are perpetually\nslick with seawater. \n',164,139264,54,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19043,0,0,0,'Rocky Beach','  The sand peters out here and turns into a mixture of large, rugged rocks and\nsmall, smooth pebbles.  Bits of dead coral and crushed seashells are sprinkled\namong the rocks, and seaweed clings tightly to the more roughly textured\nrocks.  The ocean spray is regular here, and many of the rocks are perpetually\nslick with seawater. \n',164,139264,54,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19044,0,0,0,'Dock','  Rough blackbutt planks form a study, simple dock here.  Brackets made from\niron sport tiedown rings and await boats to tie up to them.  Barnacles have\ncemented themselves to the weathered piling.  When the water is calm,\nsometimes it\'s possible to see these filter feeders with their feathery legs\nout, catching a microscopic bite to eat. \n',164,139264,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19045,0,0,0,'Dock','  Rough blackbutt planks form a study, simple dock here.  Brackets made from\niron sport tiedown rings and await boats to tie up to them.  Barnacles have\ncemented themselves to the weathered piling.  When the water is calm,\nsometimes it\'s possible to see these filter feeders with their feathery legs\nout, catching a microscopic bite to eat. \n',164,139264,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19046,0,0,0,'Sandy Path','There\'s an obvious path here formed out of compacted sandy dirt and rough-hewn logs. Small rocks and pebbles are tamped down between and around the logs. To the west lies the lagoon and the docks.',164,139264,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19047,0,0,0,'Sandy Path','  There\'s an obvious path here formed out of compacted sandy dirt and\nrough-hewn logs.  Small rocks and pebbles are tamped down between and around\nthe logs.  Tracks from carts are visible along the path, and small vines and\nflowers take purchase in the more hospitable edges along the trail. \n',164,139264,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
