(19158,0,0,0,'Airy Woods','  Trees here are tall and skinny, and lots of scrubby underbrush cling to the\nalternatively spongy and rocky soil.  There are many fallen trees and\nscattered branches, leaves and general detritus blown in from storms. \nBrightly colored birds flit from tree to tree, and occasionally a small animal\nrustles in the bushes. \n',164,139520,46,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19159,0,0,0,'Airy Woods','  Trees here are tall and skinny, and lots of scrubby underbrush cling to the\nalternatively spongy and rocky soil.  There are many fallen trees and\nscattered branches, leaves and general detritus blown in from storms. \nBrightly colored birds flit from tree to tree, and occasionally a small animal\nrustles in the bushes. \n',164,139520,46,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19160,0,0,0,'Sandy Path','  There\'s an obvious path here formed out of compacted sandy dirt and\nrough-hewn logs.  Small rocks and pebbles are tamped down between and around\nthe logs.  Tracks from carts are visible along the path, and small vines and\nflowers take purchase in the more hospitable edges along the trail. \n',164,139264,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19161,0,0,0,'Grassy Dune','  A rocky mixture of dirt and sand encourage the growth of tall, tough grasses\nhere.  Sand still dominates the area, but plant life is more abundant. \nBranches and leaves have been blown from further inland and mix with the sand\nto make the texture of the ground very prickly and uneven.  Small birds have\nmade nests in areas with thicker grasses, and wispy young trees struggle to\ntake root in the sandy soil. \n',164,139264,54,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19162,0,0,0,'Sandy Beach','  Fine white sand covers this area and is scattered with seaweed, small\npebbles, abandoned seashells and the occasional unidentifiable garbage the\nocean spits up onto the shoreline.  The ocean breeze is strong in both force\nand aroma here, and sometimes a bit of salty water is deposited on the sand. \n',0,139264,54,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19163,0,0,0,'Sandy Beach Surrounding a Lake','  Fine white sand covers this area and and is scattered with crushed coral,\nsmall pebbles, abandoned seashells and some odd seaweed here and there.  A\nsmall lake is nearby, and some greenery has taken hold here and there. \n',164,139264,54,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19164,0,0,0,'Sandy Beach Surrounding a Lake','  Fine white sand covers this area and and is scattered with crushed coral,\nsmall pebbles, abandoned seashells and some odd seaweed here and there.  A\nsmall lake is nearby, and some greenery has taken hold here and there. \n',164,139264,54,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19165,0,0,0,'Sandy Path','There\'s an obvious path here formed out of compacted sandy dirt andrough-hewn logs.  Small rocks and pebbles are tamped down between and around\nthe logs.  To the west lies a small freshwater lake, and to the east, a tall\ncathedral.  The path continues to the north and southeast.\n',164,139264,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19166,0,0,0,'Abandoned Cathedral','If there were still pews in this cathedral, this is where the aisles would be. \nThe aisles are marked by lines of rich marble inlaid into the floor, and tall\ncolumns and arches separate this area from the nave.  Richly colored light\nfilters in from the stained glass windows in the nave.\n',0,139528,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(19167,0,0,0,'Abandoned Cathedral','The nave of the cathedral continues up high above the aisles, where you can see\nmany elaborate stained glass windows.  This area is separated from the aisles by\ntall, slender columns faintly decorated with a multicolored glass mosaic, now\nsmudged and dusty.  To the east the destroyed choir area is visible.\n',0,139528,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(19168,0,0,0,'Abandoned Cathedral','If there were still pews in this cathedral, this is where the aisles would be. \nThe aisles are marked by lines of rich marble inlaid into the floor, and tall\ncolumns and arches separate this area from the nave.  This is also where the\nchoir once stood, and a mostly-destroyed latticework is all that is left of the\nmemory.\n',0,139528,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(19169,0,0,0,'Cathedral Courtyard','The cathedral courtyard has been well maintained, though it is obvious that the\ncathedral to the west has long been abandoned.  The courtyard is paved with\nmulticolored bricks and accented with a bright mosaic of inlaid glass in strong, solid\ncolors.  Long marble benches are arranged conveniently for after-services\nenjoyment.  To the east and southeast, a garden is visible.  To the north, the sights and\nsmells of farmland greet visitors.  The courtyard continues to the south.\n',0,139520,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19170,0,0,0,'Garden','The cathedral garden looks old but lovingly tended to, with various flowers\nin many colors, bushes and grasses and even tall, flowering trees.  Small\nbirdbaths and feeders stand behind rounded, smoothed rocks topped with a carved\noak seats.  To the west and southwest are the cathedral courtyards, and to the\nnorth and northeast the sights and smells of farmland greet visitors.   East of\nhere, a wooded area is visible.\n',0,139520,47,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19171,0,0,0,'Airy Woods','  Trees here are tall and skinny, and lots of scrubby underbrush cling to the\nalternatively spongy and rocky soil.  There are many fallen trees and\nscattered branches, leaves and general detritus blown in from storms. \nBrightly colored birds flit from tree to tree, and occasionally a small animal\nrustles in the bushes. \n',0,139520,46,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
