(19179,0,0,0,'Sandy Beach','Fine white sand covers this area and is scattered with seaweed, smallpebbles, abandoned seashells and the occasional unidentifiable garbage the\nocean spits up onto the shoreline.  To the west is a freshwater lake, and to the\neast a tall cathedral is barely visible.\n',164,139264,54,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19180,0,0,0,'Sandy Path','There\'s an obvious path here formed out of compacted sandy dirt andrough-hewn logs.  Small rocks and pebbles are tamped down between and around\nthe logs.  To the west lies a small freshwater lake, and to the east, a tall\ncathedral.\n',164,139264,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19181,0,0,0,'Abandoned Cathedral','If there were still pews in this cathedral, this is where the aisles would be. \nThe aisles are marked by lines of rich marble inlaid into the floor, and tall\ncolumns and arches separate this area from the nave.  Richly colored light\nfilters in from the stained glass windows in the nave.\n',0,139528,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(19182,0,0,0,'Abandoned Cathedral','The entrance to what was once a grand cathedral is large, airy and open.  A\nlarge oak podium and lectern have been built on the southwest wall.  This being\nthe easternmost point of the cathedral, it\'s quite unusual to see the lectern\nhere, but it is presumably to allow those enjoying the service to also enjoy\nseeing the beautiful cathedral courtyard to the east.\n',0,139528,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(19183,0,0,0,'Cathedral Courtyard','The cathedral courtyard has been well maintained, though it is obvious that\nthe cathedral to the west has long been abandoned.  The courtyard is paved with\nmulticolored bricks and accented with a bright mosaic of inlaid glass in\nstrong, solid colors.  Long marble benches are arranged conveniently for\nafter-services enjoyment.   The cathedral entrance is to the west, while to the\neast and northeast, a garden is visible. The courtyard continues to the north.\n',0,139520,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19184,0,0,0,'Garden','The cathedral garden looks old but lovingly tended to, with various flowers in\nmany colors, bushes and grasses and even tall, flowering trees.  Small birdbaths\nand feeders stand behind rounded, smoothed rocks topped with a carved oak seats. To the west and northwest are the cathedral courtyards and to the north, the garden continues. A sandy path is visible to the east and woods stretch on to the northeast.\n',0,139520,47,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(19185,0,0,0,'Sandy Path','  There\'s an obvious path here formed out of compacted sandy dirt and\nrough-hewn logs.  Small rocks and pebbles are tamped down between and around\nthe logs.  Tracks from carts are visible along the path, and small vines and\nflowers take purchase in the more hospitable edges along the trail. \n',164,139264,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
