(19219,0,0,0,'Abandoned Cathedral','The nave of the cathedral continues up here, and enormous stained glass windows\ndominate the room.  Below, the nave continues and the columns that separate the\nnave from the aisles meet up into archways punctuated by smaller stained glass\nwindows, each with a singular but different color.\n',0,139528,57,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(19222,0,0,0,'Abandoned Cathedral','The nave of the cathedral culminates here with a richly decorated fresco\ndecorating the plaster covered timbers that make up the ceiling of the\ncathedral.  Strong, elaborately carved oak makes an elegant veneer over the\ncoarser wood, visible where the veneer has been pecked and nibbled away by\nanimals and insects.  Stained glass windows below fill this area with eerie\ncolored shadows.\n',0,139528,57,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(19223,0,0,0,'Under the Presbytery','This relatively freshly dug tunnel is supported by cobbled together pieces of rusting, rotting old iron-ringed hoop barrels. The tunnel continues up and to the northwest.',0,139272,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(19224,0,0,0,'Under the Substances Shop','This tunnel leads to the cathedral to the southeast, and up via a dirty hatch into the shop where drugs and booze are sold. It looks like the tunnel is supported by old barrels and random pieces of rusty metal, and the walls are lined with driftwood plank.',0,139592,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(20000,0,0,0,'The Tournament Organizer\'s Office','  You are in an enormous and busy office.  The most prominent objects in\nit are a long cluttered desk and a spinning globe of The World.  There is\na tall bulletin board against the west wall containing a lot of Tournament\ninformation.  Other than this board, the walls are totally covered by maps,\ncalendars, and yellow sticky pieces of paper.  On the wall behind the desk,\nwithin easy reach of Fay\'s desk, you see a rack containing various brochures\ndescribing tournament events and how to sign-up.  As you look around, you\nsee the inn above you and additional well lit rooms to your north.  These\nadditional rooms appear to contain trophy cases and equipment.  Maybe you\nshould investigate further.\n',203,166077,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(20001,0,0,0,'Trophy Room','  You are in a brightly lit room bordered on all sides by glass\ntrophy cases of various sizes.  It is here that the special prizes for the\ntournament are available for viewing.  Given the obvious value of the prizes\nin this room, you know the security here must be real tight.  However, unless\nyou really examine the room, you see no trace of the security system.  The\ntrophy room is open for browsing 24 hours a day so take your time looking\naround.  To the south you see the tournament organizer\'s office and the inn.\nTo the north you see a barred vault filled with equipment and treasure.  You\nassume that these are other prizes to be given out at the tournament.  The\nbars on the vault make entrance into the vault unlikely unless you had the\nright key.  However, even though you can\'t enter, you are able to see clearly\ninto it and are in awe at all the treasure it contains.\n',203,166073,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(20002,0,0,0,'Prize Vault','  This is a very secure vault.  The walls are made of a highly polished\nsteel.  You can\'t tell their exact thickness but you imagine that they are\nvery thick indeed.  You can not imagine anyone tunneling into this vault.\nIt makes you feel so safe and secure you wonder if there is a way for you\nto leave your own valuables here for safe-keeping.\n',203,166073,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(20400,45,-130,-4,'Below the Surface of the Janasee River','   You fight to swim back to the surface as the waterfall above\ncontinuously beats down upon you.  Small bits of obsidian and rock\nslash and pummel your body as the current spins you in loops\ndisorienting you.  The swirling water is so saturated with debris\nand dirt it is impossible to see anything of the river bottom\nbelow you.\n',113,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20401,45,-130,-1,'Over a Roaring Waterfall','   If not for the lack of any tangible substance below your feet this would be\na great look out spot as the view up here is spectacular.  Surrounding you on\nall sides are the high cliff walls of the Janasee River Canyon which fade away\nin the distance to the Southeast.  To the northeast you see the high shear\nwalls of the Obsidian Citadel.  Your only exit choices seem to be straight down\nor try and overpower the powerful stream of water that pours from the crevice\nto the north where the life blood of the Janasee River begins.\n',113,131072,15,0,0,0,25,5,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20402,45,-130,-2,'A Roaring Waterfall','   As the water drops to the rivers surface below you it begins to soak you to\nthe bone.  The view from here is not as spectacular as above at the top of the\nfalls but its still quite amazing.  From here you can either attempt to\nnavigate upwards or continue your descent downwards to the rivers surface.\n',113,131072,15,0,0,0,25,5,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20403,45,-130,-3,'Beneath the Falls','  Under the falls you are constantly pounded by the heavy downpour of\nwater from above which threatens to push you under the surface to drown.\nThe Janasee River begins its descent down the canyon to the southeast\nwhile you can attempt to navigate upwards if you have the ability to\nfly somehow.\n',113,131072,8,0,0,0,25,8,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20404,46,-131,-3,'Janasee River','  Cutting its way through the steep Marjiln Mountains the Janasee River\nhas created this deep River Canyon as its current and collection of\ndebris slice through the solid rock.  Ascending towards the sky on both\nsides of the canyon are steep rock cliffs coated with incredibly slick\nice made even slipperier by the thin layer of water on their surface.\n',113,131072,8,0,0,0,25,8,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20405,47,-132,-3,'Janasee River','  Cutting its way through the steep Marjiln Mountains the Janasee River\nhas created this deep River Canyon as its current and collection of\ndebris slice through the solid rock.  Ascending towards the sky on both\nsides of the canyon are steep rock cliffs coated with incredibly slick\nice made even slipperier by the thin layer of water on their surface.\n',113,131072,8,0,0,0,30,8,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
