(20412,54,-139,2,'Janasee River','  Cutting its way through the steep Marjiln Mountains the Janasee River\nhas created this deep River Canyon as its current and collection of\ndebris slice through the solid rock.  Ascending towards the sky on both\nsides of the canyon are steep rock cliffs coated with incredibly slick\nice made even slipperier by the layer of water on their surface.  To\nthe northeast the surface of the eastern branch of the Janasee River\nhas frozen into a steep slope of slick ice that rises in the distance.\nHigh overhead you see a massive stone bridge that spans the canyon.\n',113,131072,8,0,0,0,30,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
