(20427,67,-145,2,'Janasee River','  Cutting its way through the steep Marjiln Mountains the Janasee River\nhas created this deep River Canyon as its current and collection of\ndebris slice through the solid rock.  Ascending towards the sky on both\nsides of the canyon are steep rock cliffs coated with incredibly slick\nice made even slipperier by the layer of water on their surface.  While\nstill just as steep, the cliff walls seem a little shorter and the ice a\nlittle thinner then upstream as though the canyon is descending towards\nwarmer air.\n',113,131072,8,0,0,0,30,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
