(20434,74,-147,2,'Janasee River','  Cutting its way through the foothills of the Marjiln Mountains the\nJanasee River has created this River Canyon as its current and collection\nof debris slice through the solid rock and dirt.  Ascending upwards along\nboth sides of the canyon are steep walls of rock and dirt which force\nyou to follow the river as your only course.\n',113,131072,29,0,0,0,30,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20435,75,-147,2,'Janasee River','  Cutting its way through the foothills of the Marjiln Mountains the\nJanasee River has created this River Canyon as its current and collection\nof debris slice through the solid rock and dirt.  Ascending upwards along\nboth sides of the canyon are steep walls of rock and dirt which force\nyou to follow the river as your only course.\n',113,131072,29,0,0,0,30,6,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
