(20437,78,-144,2,'Janasee River','  Cutting its way through the foothills of the Marjiln Mountains the\nJanasee River has created this River Canyon as its current and collection\nof debris slice through the solid rock and dirt.  Ascending upwards along\nboth sides of the canyon are steep walls of rock and dirt which force\nyou to follow the river as your only course.\n',113,131072,29,0,0,0,30,6,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20438,78,-144,2,'Janasee River','  Cutting its way through the Chaos Plains the Janasee River has created\nthis River Canyon as its current and collection of debris slice through\nthe solid rock and dirt.  Ascending upwards along both sides of the\ncanyon are steep walls of rock and dirt which appear to make following\nthe river canyon your only course.  As the river twist and turns through\nthe plains you find beaches scattered along its path covered with black\nsand, battered pieces of rock and tiny shards of worthless obsidian.\n',113,131072,29,0,0,0,30,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
