(20517,89,-144,1,'Beneath the Surface of Shard Lake','  Just below the surface of Shard Lake your eyes continually adjust\nto the murky waters.  Constant debris swirls around you making it\ndifficult to see clearly.  Besides water and whatever wandering local\ninhabitant swims by there is very little here to take notice of.\n',113,131072,53,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20518,89,-142,0,'Bottom of Shard Lake','  Reaching the small \"bowl\" at the bottom of the lake you are amazed to\nfind it appears if someone either lives here or frequently visits as there\nare paths on the lake bottom, engravings in the rock, and decorative\nobjects placed around the area.  While most of the paths seem to head\nto the north a few head east and northeast as well.\n',113,131072,53,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20519,90,-142,0,'Bottom of Shard Lake','  Reaching the small \"bowl\" at the bottom of the lake you are amazed to\nfind it appears if someone either lives here or frequently visits as there\nare paths on the lake bottom, engravings in the rock, and decorative\nobjects placed around the area.  This particular area seems to be some sort\nof \"camp\" area as you see scattered bones and such from leftover meals\npiled neatly to one side.  While most of the paths seem to head to the\nnorthwest a few head north and south as well.\n',113,131072,53,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20520,90,-141,0,'Bottom of Shard Lake','  Reaching the small \"bowl\" at the bottom of the lake you are amazed to\nfind it appears if someone either lives here or frequently visits as there\nare paths on the lake bottom, engravings in the rock, and decorative\nobjects placed around the area.  While most of the paths seem to head\nto the west a few head south and southwest as well.\n',113,131072,53,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20521,89,-141,0,'A Stone Altar at the Bottom of Shard Lake','  Made of stone and other collected debris you are shocked to see a\nperfect stone altar has been raised to some worshipped being here.\nPathways lead off to the south and easterly directions while engravings\nmark the rocks around you and decorative objects are scattered about the\nsmall bowl here at the bottom of Shard Lake.\n',113,131072,53,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20522,54,-136,3,'Before the Citadel Gate','  Standing out here on the windy ledge you see a massive gate of\nthe Obsidian Citadel bars the path before you.  A narrow path of rock\ncan be seen descending from the keep towards the mountains to the\nsoutheast, and the ledge extends in front of the other Citadel Gate\nto the east.  Looking over the ledge to the west you see way below\nyou the surface of the Janasee River, but at this distance you can\nmake out little besides the fact its water.\n',113,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20523,55,-136,3,'Before the Citadel Gate','  Standing out here on the windy ledge you see a massive gate of\nthe Obsidian Citadel bars the path before you.  A narrow path of rock\ncan be seen descending from the keep towards the mountains to the\nsouth, and the ledge extends in front of the other Citadel Gate to the\nwest.  Looking over the ledge to the east you see below you the frozen\nsurface of the Eastern Janasee River, but at this distance you can\nmake out little besides its white blurry surface.\n',113,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20524,55,-137,3,'High Atop a Mountain Path','  Just below the Gates of the Obsidian Citadel this path meets a\nmassive arching bridge to the southeast which bridges the canyon created\nby the swift waters of the Janasee River.  The path while just wide\nenough for merchants wagons is extremely narrow, which makes the\nCitadel easily defended, considering this appears to be the only\nfeasible approach to the Citadel.  Scraggly brush lines both sides\nof the path where citizens of the Citadel once attempted to \"beautify\"\nthe entrance to their homeland.\n',113,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20525,55,-138,3,'On a Massive Stone Bridge','  Arching across the canyon created by the swift waters of the Janasee\nRiver this bridge was constructed eons ago by the dwarves that once\ninhabitanted these mountains.  But like many civilizations on this\ncontinent magic storms wiped all but a few of these dwarves from the\nsurface.  This bridge and the original stonework of the Obsidian Citadel\nto the north are about all that are left to show of their passing.  The\nbridge arches downward to the southeast side of the canyon or to a narrow\npath to the northwest.\n',113,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20526,56,-139,3,'On a Massive Stone Bridge','  Arching across the canyon created by the swift waters of the Janasee\nRiver this bridge was constructed eons ago by the dwarves that once\ninhabitanted these mountains.  But like many civilizations on this\ncontinent magic storms wiped all but a few of these dwarves from the\nsurface.  This bridge and the original stonework of the Obsidian Citadel\nto the north are about all that are left to show of their passing.  The\nbridge arches downward to the southeast side of the canyon or to a narrow\npath to the northwest.\n',113,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20527,57,-140,3,'High Atop a Mountain Path','  Just below a massive bridge near the Obsidian Citadel this path stretches\nbetween the bridge to the northwest which arches over the canyon created\nby the swift waters of the Janasee River and the Marjiln Mountains to the\neast.  The path while just wide enough for merchants wagons is quite narrow,\nwhich makes the Citadel easily defended, considering this appears to be\nthe only feasible approach to the Citadel.  Scraggly brush lines both sides\nof the path where citizens of the Citadel once attempted to \"beautify\" the\nentrance to their homeland.\n',113,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20528,58,-140,3,'Before the Cavern Gates','  The path ends here before a set of stone gates constructed across a cave\nopening.  The tunnel through the Marjiln mountains used to be kept in decent\nrepair by the Citadel for merchants as well as guards set on regular patrols.\nBut since King Urik\'s curse many things have changed around the Citadel.\nNow only the bravest of merchants traverse the tunnels which are said to\nhave collapsed in areas and are now haunted, but thats a myth of course,\nyou hope.  A guards shanty has been constructed to the north for the few\nguards still set on duty near the tunnels.  A lookout post is to the south\nfor a guard to stand watch over the Janasee River Canyon to make sure no\nenemy forces attempt passage up the river.\n',113,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20529,58,-139,3,'Guards Outpost','  Already small the shanty seems even smaller due to the numerous items the\nguards have carried in to make it slightly more comfortable on chilly winter\ndays.  The building itself while being quickly constructed appears to have\nbeen built to at least be moderately sturdy and warm.  Rough hewn timbers\nstretch from poles to the west across to be embedded into the stone of the\ncliff face to the east.  A roof then stretches across the timbers and any\nholes sealed with some sort of tar residue.  Finally warm thick wool blankets\nhave been draped from the walls to act as a minor insulation.  The only\nexit from the shanty appears to be back to the south.\n',113,131081,12,0,0,0,0,0,12,130,0,'',NULL),
(20530,58,-141,3,'Lookout Over the Janasee River','  Uncomfortably cold this lookout point hangs out over the edge of the Janasee\nRiver Canyon slightly.  Whoever stands here is constantly battered by strong\nfierce winds which rip their way down the canyon from the north.  Despite the\ncold though it is an excellent vantage point to see an enemy that might try to\nmake its way up the river in an attempt to attack the Citadel from below.  A\nsmall path back to the north appears to be the only exit from this spot as\nshear cliffs drop downwards to the west and south and the mountain juts upwards\nto the east in the form of a vertical wall.\n',113,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20531,59,-140,3,'Cavern Entrance Near the Citadel','  At this point most people either feel apprehension and fear or a profound\nemotion of relief.  To the west a set of stone gates are set across the cave\nmouth to restrict passage.  To the east of you looms a dark forbidding hole\ninto the depths of the mountain.  While its size is not that immense its\ndarkness seems to swallow any light you might have.  A bone chilling draft\nof air seems to constantly brush across the back of you neck no matter which\nway you attempt to face.  The rock surrounding you seems to be unearthly cold\nand small patches of ice mar the otherwise slick, damp, clammy surface.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(20532,60,-140,3,'Path through the Caverns','  Moving through the caverns this appears to be the old path used by merchants\nwhen regular trade routes were established to the Citadel.  Many places you\ndiscover that seismic activity has caused sections of the walls to collapse\nforcing you to deter slightly from the path.  The feeling of someone watching\nyou constantly nags at your senses while a bone chilling draft of air\nseems to always be blowing across the back of your neck no matter which\ndirection you face.  The walls themselves are clammy and unearthly cold while\nnarrow trickles of water run down their surface in spots sometimes leaving\nicy patches behind.  Any light sources you attempt to use almost seem dim\nin comparison to their normal illuminance as the caverns seem to greedily\nswallow it up.  Echos occasionally bounce down the caverns, but you are rarely\nable to tell which direction they come from, and more often then not you are\nscared to even guess what the source of the noise was.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,150,0,'',NULL),
(20533,61,-139,3,'Path through the Caverns','  Moving through the caverns this appears to be the old path used by merchants\nwhen regular trade routes were established to the Citadel.  Many places you\ndiscover that seismic activity has caused sections of the walls to collapse\nforcing you to deter slightly from the path.  The feeling of someone watching\nyou constantly nags at your senses while a bone chilling draft of air\nseems to always be blowing across the back of your neck no matter which\ndirection you face.  The walls themselves are clammy and unearthly cold while\nnarrow trickles of water run down their surface in spots sometimes leaving\nicy patches behind.  Any light sources you attempt to use almost seem dim\nin comparison to their normal illuminance as the caverns seem to greedily\nswallow it up.  Echos occasionally bounce down the caverns, but you are rarely\nable to tell which direction they come from, and more often then not you are\nscared to even guess what the source of the noise was.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,12,110,0,'',NULL),
(20534,62,-138,3,'Blocked Passage','  Moving through the caverns this appears to be the old path used by merchants\nwhen regular trade routes were established to the Citadel.  Unfortunately\nseismic activity has caused this portion of the cavern to collapse completely.\nThe feeling of someone watching you still nags at your senses while a bone\nchilling draft of air continues to blow across the back of your neck no matter\nwhich direction you face.  The walls which are still intact are clammy and\nunearthly cold while narrow trickles of water run down their surface in spots\nleaving icy patches behind.  Any light sources you attempt to use almost seem\ndim in comparison to their normal illuminance as the caverns seem to greedily\nswallow it up.  Echos occasionally bounce down the caverns, but you are rarely\nable to tell which direction they come from, and more often then not you are\nscared to even guess what the source of the noise was.  The only clear path\nseems to be to the southwest.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(20535,63,-139,3,'Blocked Passage','  Moving through the caverns this appears to be the old path used by merchants\nwhen regular trade routes were established to the Citadel.  Unfortunately\nseismic activity has caused this portion of the cavern to collapse completely.\nThe feeling of someone watching you still nags at your senses while a bone\nchilling draft of air continues to blow across the back of your neck no matter\nwhich direction you face.  The walls which are still intact are clammy and\nunearthly cold while narrow trickles of water run down their surface in spots\nleaving icy patches behind.  Any light sources you attempt to use almost seem\ndim in comparison to their normal illuminance as the caverns seem to greedily\nswallow it up.  Echos occasionally bounce down the caverns, but you are rarely\nable to tell which direction they come from, and more often then not you are\nscared to even guess what the source of the noise was.  The only clear path\nseems to be to the southeast.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,16,120,0,'',NULL),
(20536,64,-140,3,'Before a Cave-In','   It seems you\'ve stumbled upon yet another result of the seismic activities\nwithin the caverns.  The wall to the southwest, where it appears the path\noriginally led, has been completely blocked by large slabs of earth and rock\nwhich fell from the ceiling above.  It looks as though some poor merchant was\nunlucky enough to be standing under the area at the time as you see the crushed\nremains of a merchants wagon and a skeleton half pinned under the rock.  Your\nonly apparent exit seems to be back towards the northwest.  Maybe you can find\nenough way through from back farther along the path.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,8,130,0,'',NULL),
(20537,63,-141,3,'Before a Cave-In','   It seems you\'ve stumbled upon yet another result of the seismic activities\nwithin the caverns.  The wall to the northeast, where it appears the path\noriginally led, has been completely blocked by large slabs of earth and rock\nwhich fell from the ceiling above.  It looks as though some poor merchant was\nunlucky enough to be standing under the area at the time as you see the crushed\nremains of a merchants wagon and a several crates and barrels of wares crushed\nunder the rock.  Your only apparent exit seems to be back towards the south.\nMaybe you can find enough way through from somewhere back along the path.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,15,130,0,'',NULL),
(20538,63,-142,3,'Narrow Passage through the Caverns','  Extremely narrow this path is slowly becoming non-existant as random seismic\ntremors keep cascading rock and debris down from the walls and tunnel overhead.\nThe path seems moderately clear to the north and south, but large piles of\nrubble block your path to the west and east.  As always in the caverns a bone\nchilling draft of air continually blows across the base of your neck no matter\nwhich direction you face.  Even stranger, it seems that light is almost\nswallowed up by the cavern walls as any of your light sources seem a good deal\ndimmer then usual.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,18,130,0,'',NULL),
(20539,64,-142,3,'A Cluttered Chamber','  Littered with fallen rocks, scraps of different household items, and bones\nof past eaten meals this tiny little chamber appears quite likely to be the\nhome of some inhabitant of the caverns.  Different rocks bare scorch marks\nwhere some candle or other light source was allowed to consume itself into\noblivion.  The bone chilling breeze continues to blow across the base of your\nneck, and your light sources always seem a good deal dimmer then usual.  A\nlarge pile of rubble has managed to accumulate during the recent seismic\nactivities blocking the path to the west.  The wind seems to whirl and eddy\nin the room before being sucked southward through a small stone grate set in\nthe base of the south wall.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,8,130,0,'',NULL),
(20540,60,-142,3,'Makeshift Cell','  Appearing having been hastily constructed this room seems to have been\nconverted from a tiny dead end tunnel into a small cell to hold someone or\nsomething.  Bars of wood planks, broken, rusty spears, and other long scrap\nitems are fastened together into a portcullis to the southeast.  It appears it\ntakes either a very strong individual or someone using a simple winch mechanism\nto the southeast to raise the portcullis should it be closed.  The walls of the\ncell appear basically bare and plain besides some random chips and scratches\nfrom some bored prisoner most likely.  Even here in this tiny chamber the\nstrange bone chilling wind seems to blow across the base of your neck while\nyour light sources seemed a good deal dimmer then usual as if the walls are\nsomehow swallowing the light like some tangible substance.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(20541,61,-143,3,'Barred Passage','  The passage basically ends here as the only visible exit besides back to the\neast is an opening in the northwest wall which a makeshift portcullis seems to\nhave been hastily constructed across.  The portcullis is made of several scrap\nitems, mostly wooden planks, broken, rust spears, and any other long slender\nobjects that could be gathered.  A tiny winch mechanism is here which can be\nused to raise and lower the portcullis, otherwise it would take someone quite\nstrong to raise the portcullis manually.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,4,'',NULL),
(20542,62,-143,3,'Dark Narrow Passage','  Extremely narrow this path is slowly becoming non-existant as random seismic\ntremors keep cascading rock and debris down from the walls and tunnel overhead.\nThe path seems moderately clear to the west, but large piles of rubble block\nyour path in all other directions.  The only break you can find in the dull\nwalls is a small rusty grate set into the base of the east wall.  As always in\nthe caverns a bone chilling draft of air continually blows across the base of\nyour neck no matter which direction you face.  Even stranger, it seems that\nlight is almost swallowed up by the cavern walls as any of your light sources\nseem a good deal dimmer then usual.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(20543,63,-145,3,'Cramped Chamber','  Littered with fallen rocks, scraps of different household items, and bones\nof past eaten meals this tiny little chamber appears quite likely to be the\nhome of some inhabitant of the caverns.  Different rocks bare scorch marks\nwhere some candle or other light source was allowed to consume itself into\noblivion.  A tiny hole appears to have been dug through the south wall but\nit is entirely too small for anything but looking through.  While the most of\nthe air seems to be sucked through the tiny hole the bone chilling breeze\ncontinues to find the base of your neck, but at least it seems your light\nsources are a little bit lighter here, almost to their normal standards.  A\nnarrow path leads back to the north appearing to be your own egress from this\nchamber.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,8,90,0,'',NULL),
(20544,63,-144,3,'Breezy Passage','  Slightly cramped for the space this passage seems to squeeze its way into\na tiny chamber to the south but ends in a blank slab to the north.  A strong\nwind seems to drift to the south as if some escape draws its attention.  The\nwalls to either side of you appear quite solid and small rocks and dust are\nthe only thing that cover the path below your feet.  Even though the strong\nwind blows southward that same bone chilling breeze continues to drift across\nthe base of your neck.  Unfortunately it still seems as if any light you\nattempt to light is swallowed up by the cavern walls themselves.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,12,130,0,'',NULL),
(20545,63,-143,3,'Bend in the Passage','  Winding its way through the caverns this appears to the best passage.  At\none time it was the main throughfare for merchants and ambassadors on their\nway to and from the Obsidian Citadel.  Unfortunately it seems its fallen under\ndisrepair and is slowly being clogged with fallen debris and rocks from all the\nseismic activities within these mountains.  The passage takes a turn at this\npoint exiting to the north and east.  While the south wall seems to be little\nmore then a blank slab you do notice a small rusty grate set in the west wall.\nComing this far you are no longer surprised to feel the bone chilling draft of\nair that is blowing across the base of your neck or that your light sources\nseem a good deal dimmer then their usual standards.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(20546,64,-143,3,'Passage through the Caverns','  Moving through the caverns this appears to be the old passage used by\nmerchants and ambassadors when regular trade routes were established to the\nCitadel.  The feeling of someone watching you still nags at your senses while\na bone chilling draft of air continues to blow across the back of your neck\nno matter which direction you face.  The walls which are still intact are\nclammy and unearthly cold while narrow trickles of water run down their\nsurface in spots leaving icy patches behind.  Any light sources you attempt to\nuse almost seem dim in comparison to their normal illuminance as the caverns\nseem to greedily swallow it up.  Echos occasionally bounce down the caverns,\nbut you are rarely able to tell which direction they come from, and more often\nthen not you are scared to even guess what the source of the noise was.  The\nonly clear path seems to be to the east or west while the north and south\nwalls appear to be solid rock except for one tiny stone grate set into\nthe north wall.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(20547,65,-143,3,'Blocked Passage','  Moving through the caverns this appears to be the old path used by merchants\nwhen regular trade routes were established to the Citadel.  Unfortunately\nseismic activity has caused this portion of the cavern to collapse completely.\nThe feeling of someone watching you still nags at your senses while a bone\nchilling draft of air continues to blow across the back of your neck no matter\nwhich direction you face.  The walls which are still intact are clammy and\nunearthly cold while narrow trickles of water run down their surface in spots\nleaving icy patches behind.  Any light sources you attempt to use almost seem\ndim in comparison to their normal illuminance as the caverns seem to greedily\nswallow it up.  Echos occasionally bounce down the caverns, but you are rarely\nable to tell which direction they come from, and more often then not you are\nscared to even guess what the source of the noise was.  The only clear path\nseems to be to the west.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,14,120,0,'',NULL),
(20548,66,-142,3,'Blocked Passage','  Moving through the caverns this appears to be the old path used by merchants\nwhen regular trade routes were established to the Citadel.  Unfortunately\nseismic activity has caused this portion of the cavern to collapse completely.\nThe feeling of someone watching you still nags at your senses while a bone\nchilling draft of air continues to blow across the back of your neck no matter\nwhich direction you face.  The walls which are still intact are clammy and\nunearthly cold while narrow trickles of water run down their surface in spots\nleaving icy patches behind.  Any light sources you attempt to use almost seem\ndim in comparison to their normal illuminance as the caverns seem to greedily\nswallow it up.  Echos occasionally bounce down the caverns, but you are rarely\nable to tell which direction they come from, and more often then not you are\nscared to even guess what the source of the noise was.  The only clear path\nseems to be to the northeast.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,20,150,0,'',NULL),
