(20555,73,-142,3,'Before a Heavy Gate','  Moving through the caverns this appears to be the old passage used by\nmerchants and ambassadors when regular trade routes were established to the\nCitadel.  The feeling of someone watching you still nags at your senses while\na bone chilling draft of air continues to blow across the back of your neck\nno matter which direction you face.  The walls which are still intact are\nclammy and unearthly cold while narrow trickles of water run down their\nsurface in spots leaving icy patches behind.  Any light sources you attempt to\nuse almost seem dim in comparison to their normal illuminance as the caverns\nseem to greedily swallow it up.  Echos occasionally bounce down the caverns,\nbut you are rarely able to tell which direction they come from, and more often\nthen not you are scared to even guess what the source of the noise was.  While\nthe passage seems clear both to the northeast and northwest, a heavy looking\ngate has been constructed to the northeast possibly making movement in that\ndirection difficult for one without the proper key.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,10,90,0,'',NULL),
(20556,74,-141,3,'Before a Heavy Gate','merchants and ambassadors when regular trade routes were established to the\nCitadel.  The feeling of someone watching you still nags at your senses while\na bone chilling draft of air continues to blow across the back of your neck\nno matter which direction you face.  The walls which are still intact are\nclammy and unearthly cold while narrow trickles of water run down their\nsurface in spots leaving icy patches behind.  Any light sources you attempt to\nuse almost seem dim in comparison to their normal illuminance as the caverns\nseem to greedily swallow it up.  Echos occasionally bounce down the caverns,\nbut you are rarely able to tell which direction they come from, and more often\nthen not you are scared to even guess what the source of the noise was.  While\nthe passage seems clear both to the north and southwest, a heavy looking gate\nhas been constructed to the southwest possibly making movement in that\ndirection difficult for one without the proper key.\n',113,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(20557,74,-140,3,'Warmer Passage through the Caverns','  Moving through the caverns this appears to be the old passage used by\nmerchants and ambassadors when regular trade routes were established to the\nCitadel.  Unfortunately seismic activity has taken its toll on the passage\nas numerous rocks and bits of debris litter the passage floor having fallen\nfrom overhead.  The air in this area seems rather warm for being closed in\nby rock so its probably safe to assume you are fairly close to an outside exit\nof some kind.  Small trickles of water can be seen occasionally racing down\nthe walls to pool and then seep into cracks on the passage floor.  The passage\nseems to continue to the south and northeast.\n',113,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,15,120,0,'',NULL),
(20558,75,-139,3,'Warmer Passage through the Caverns','  Moving through the caverns this appears to be the old passage used by\nmerchants and ambassadors when regular trade routes were established to the\nCitadel.  Unfortunately seismic activity has taken its toll on the passage\nas numerous rocks and bits of debris litter the passage floor having fallen\nfrom overhead.  The air in this area seems rather warm for being closed in\nby rock so its probably safe to assume you are fairly close to an outside exit\nof some kind.  Small trickles of water can be seen occasionally racing down\nthe walls to pool and then seep into cracks on the passage floor.  The passage\nseems to continue to the southeast and southwest.\n',113,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,15,130,0,'',NULL),
(20559,76,-140,3,'Warmer Passage through the Caverns','  Moving through the caverns this appears to be the old passage used by\nmerchants and ambassadors when regular trade routes were established to the\nCitadel.  Unfortunately seismic activity has taken its toll on the passage\nas numerous rocks and bits of debris litter the passage floor having fallen\nfrom overhead.  The air in this area seems rather warm for being closed in\nby rock so its probably safe to assume you are fairly close to an outside exit\nof some kind.  Small trickles of water can be seen occasionally racing down\nthe walls to pool and then seep into cracks on the passage floor.  The passage\nseems to continue to the northwest and southeast.\n',113,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,16,130,0,'',NULL),
(20560,77,-141,3,'Warmer Passage through the Caverns','  Moving through the caverns this appears to be the old passage used by\nmerchants and ambassadors when regular trade routes were established to the\nCitadel.  Unfortunately seismic activity has taken its toll on the passage\nas numerous rocks and bits of debris litter the passage floor having fallen\nfrom overhead.  The air in this area seems rather warm for being closed in\nby rock so its probably safe to assume you are fairly close to an outside exit\nof some kind.  Small trickles of water can be seen occasionally racing down\nthe walls to pool and then seep into cracks on the passage floor.  The passage\nseems to continue to the east and northwest.\n',113,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,16,130,0,'',NULL),
(20561,78,-141,3,'Collapsed Tunnel','  Moving through the caverns this appears to be the old passage used by\nmerchants and ambassadors when regular trade routes were established to the\nCitadel.  Unfortunately seismic activity has taken its toll on the passage\nas numerous rocks and bits of debris litter the passage floor having fallen\nfrom overhead and a large pile of boulders has completely blocked the passage\neast.  You can feel warm fresh air pushing its way through the cracks hinting\nthat the outside awaits on the other side of the boulders, but it looks\ndoubtful anything but a full working crew of dwarves is going to clear the\nboulders aside to reopen the passage.\n',113,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,80,0,'',NULL),
(20562,78,-145,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nobsidian can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.  As you look closer you notice a thin sloping\npath to the south which seems to meander up a recent pile of earth which has\ncollapsed down into the canyon, what luck.  This small tract of land continues\nto the east while the Janasee River is to the north.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20563,79,-145,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nobsidian can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.  This small tract of land continues to the\nwest while the Janasee River is to the north.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20564,58,-137,2,'On a Plateau Before a Wall of Ice',' Standing on this plateau of the glacier you find your only option for an exit\nappears to be back to the west.  A shear slick wall of ice formed by the\nglacier to the northeast blocks passage in all other directions.  Taking a\ncloser look at your surroundings you notice that one spot of the wall seems\nas if someone or something frequently slides down the wall and then proceeds\nwest along the plateau.  Unfortunately the slide is much to steep and slick to\neven consider climbing.  Off to one side you spot what appears to be a small\ncampsite which was recently used.  Otherwise you are surrounded by sleet and\nsnow as the cold glacier freezes the water vapor from the Janasee River to the\nsouthwest.\n',113,131072,11,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20565,78,-145,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nobsidian can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.  This small tract of land continues to the\neast while the Janasee River is to the south.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
