(20567,82,-142,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nobsidian can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.  This small tract of land continues to the\neast and southeast while the Janasee River is to the south.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20568,58,-147,2,'A Cramped Cave','  So small as to only be suited for someone of the smaller races this little\ncave is piled high with little odds and ends making it someones home.  Some\ntiny hides, food stores, and cooking implements line one wall while a little\npile of straw and twigs has been fashioned into a bed on the opposite wall.\nThe wall opposite the opening bears some carvings and paintings from the\nobviously bored inhabitant.  The blocks to the northeast have been stacked and\nhinged perfectly to act as the only door you find in this room.\n',113,131080,13,0,0,0,0,0,5,80,0,'',NULL),
(20569,87,-144,2,'Muddy Beach of Shard Lake','  Underwater probably fifty percent of the time this muddy beach stretches\nalong the edge of the Shard Lake.  Working through the mud with your feet\nyou find worthless shards of obsidian and other pieces of junk which have\nbeen deposited here by the flow of the Janasee and Sedmar rivers which empty\ninto the lake.  High walls normally prohibit you from moving upwards to the\nplains above but you do notice a mud slide to the southwest where the wall\nhas collapsed to a level that the climb upwards might be feasible.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20570,87,-141,2,'Muddy Beach of Shard Lake','  Underwater probably fifty percent of the time this muddy beach stretches\nalong the edge of the Shard Lake.  Working through the mud with your feet\nyou find worthless shards of obsidian and other pieces of junk which have\nbeen deposited here by the flow of the Janasee and Sedmar rivers which empty\ninto the lake.  High walls prohibit you from moving upwards to the plains\nabove but you do notice that mud and rock slides seem to be a frequent\noccurrence here so maybe at some point the wall will collapse to a level that\nthe climb upwards might be feasible.  The beach continues to the north.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20571,87,-140,2,'Muddy Beach of Shard Lake','  Underwater probably fifty percent of the time this muddy beach stretches\nalong the edge of the Shard Lake.  Working through the mud with your feet\nyou find worthless shards of obsidian and other pieces of junk which have\nbeen deposited here by the flow of the Janasee and Sedmar rivers which empty\ninto the lake.  High walls prohibit you from moving upwards to the plains\nabove but you do notice that mud and rock slides seem to be a frequent\noccurrence here so maybe at some point the wall will collapse to a level that\nthe climb upwards might be feasible.  The beach continues to the south and\nnortheast.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
