(20579,89,-148,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nminerals can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.  This small tract of land continues to the\nsouth while the Southern Sedmar River is to the east.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20580,89,-149,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nminerals can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.  This small tract of land continues to the\nnorth while the Southern Sedmar River is to the east.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20581,90,-150,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nminerals can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20582,55,-137,2,'A Tiny Ledge of Ice','  Quite narrow this ledge is probably not the best spot to be at this point.\nThe cold winds which blow off the glacier to the northeast are funneled down\nbetween the mountains and buffet you endlessly.  A narrow path leads back to\nthe east but you are confronted by a shear rock wall to the west.  It might\nbe possible to climb upwards if the slick ice was somehow chipped off the\nrock so you could find hand holds.\n',113,131072,11,0,0,0,0,0,4,-1,4,'',NULL),
(20583,89,-152,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nminerals can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.  This small tract of land continues to the\nsouth   while the Southern Sedmar River is to the west.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20584,89,-153,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nminerals can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.  This small tract of land continues to the\nnorth while the Southern Sedmar River is to the west.  It seems luck would\nseem to bless you, a recent rain has caused the southern face of the canyon to\ncollapse forming a small ravine where water from the plains above flows down\nto the river level.  Tricky but passable, the path up to the plains seems\ntraversable.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20585,56,-137,2,'A Tiny Ledge of Ice','  Quite narrow this ledge is probably not the best spot to be at this point.\nThe cold winds which blow off the glacier to the northeast are funneled down\nbetween the mountains and buffet you endlessly.  A narrow path leads both to\nthe east and west while below you can see a slick ice slide which descends\ndownwards to the Janasee River.  As you watch, a group of penguins happily\nslide downwards to plunge into the icy cold water and disappear swimming\nthrough the waters easily to find their own way back up.\n',113,131072,11,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20586,87,-154,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nminerals can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.  This small tract of land continues to the\nsouth   while the Southern Sedmar River is to the east.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20587,87,-155,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nminerals can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.  This small tract of land continues to the\nnorth   while the Southern Sedmar River is to the east.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20588,86,-156,2,'Rocky Banks of the Southern Sedmar River','  Slightly higher then the rivers surface this piece of land mostly remains\ndry except during the flood seasons.  Large rocks and boulders lie scattered\nabout having fallen from the high shear canyon walls.  Their seems to be no\napparent way to climb the shear walls and reach the plains level above you.\nOccasionally you notice a pile of rocks that might have once been high enough\nto attempt climbing to the top, but they all seem to have toppled downwards\nleaving a last leg of the climb just barely too high for anyone to jump and\nreach the edge of the canyon wall.  You see that this rocky area continues\nto the south while the river continues its course to the east.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20589,86,-157,2,'Rocky Banks of the Southern Sedmar River','  Slightly higher then the rivers surface this piece of land mostly remains\ndry except during the flood seasons.  Large rocks and boulders lie scattered\nabout having fallen from the high shear canyon walls.  Their seems to be no\napparent way to climb the shear walls and reach the plains level above you.\nOccasionally you notice a pile of rocks that might have once been high enough\nto attempt climbing to the top, but they all seem to have toppled downwards\nleaving a last leg of the climb just barely too high for anyone to jump and\nreach the edge of the canyon wall.  You see that this rocky area continues\nto the north while the river continues its course to the east.\n',113,131072,31,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20590,85,-158,2,'Shamans Hut','  Cramped and smelling like mold and plants this little hut is the home of\nthe Shaman who watches over the dam for any dangers that might threaten the\nTerraqu population in this area of the realms.  Small wooden bowls are\nscattered about filled with mixtures of nuts and berries in different stages\nof fermenting for salves and poultices.  A tiny bed of coals lie in a rock\ncircle at the center of the hut giving off no light while a circle has been\ncut out of the center of the roof overhead to allow the smoke to escape.\nYour only exit appears to be through a vine screen to the east.\n',113,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(20591,90,-134,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nminerals can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.  This small tract of land continues to the\nnorth while the Northern Sedmar River is to the east.\n',113,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20592,90,-133,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nminerals can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.  This small tract of land continues to the\nnorth and south while the Northern Sedmar River is to the east.\n',113,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20593,55,-138,2,'Bottom of an Ice Slide','  Incredibly smooth and slick this slope of ice appears to be the slide for\nsome playful creature.  Climbing it is near impossible and the descent\ndownwards does not look at all pleasant as it ends in a nice plunge into the\nicy cold waters of the Janasee River.\n',113,131072,11,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,30,'',NULL),
(20594,56,-138,2,'The Middle of an Ice Slide','  Incredibly smooth and slick this slope of ice appears to be the slide for\nsome playful creature.  Climbing it is near impossible and the descent\ndownwards does not look at all pleasant as it ends in a nice plunge into the\nicy cold waters of the Janasee River.\n',113,131072,11,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,30,'',NULL),
(20595,91,-130,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nminerals can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.  This small tract of land continues to the\nnorth while the Northern Sedmar River is to the east and south.\n',113,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20596,91,-129,2,'River Canyon','  Created when the river varied course slightly this small patch of the canyon\nfloor is covered with debris.  Various sized rocks and worthless fragments of\nminerals can be seen scattered about along with an occasional article of\nclothing, probably from some unlucky traveler who got caught in the river and\ncouldn\'t swim.  The river continues on its way close by while the canyon walls\nkeep you down here at the rivers level.  Occasionally you see where at one\ntime part of the wall might have collapsed offering a way up to plains above,\nbut the flooding and swelling of the river quickly sweep up the fallen rock\nand dirt trapping you once again.  This small tract of land continues to the\nsouth while the Northern Sedmar River is to the east.\n',113,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20597,57,-137,2,'The Top of an Ice Slide','  Incredibly smooth and slick this slope of ice appears to be the slide for\nsome playful creature.  Climbing it is near impossible and the descent\ndownwards does not look at all pleasant as it ends in a nice plunge into the\nicy cold waters of the Janasee River.  Another route which looks a good deal\nmore pleasing is a path to the east and west.\n',113,131072,11,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,30,'',NULL),
(20598,92,-127,2,'Grassy Banks of the Northern Sedmar River','  Covered in a thick layer of lush green grass this small strip of land only\noccasionally floods with waters from the Northern Sedmar River which deposits\nrich minerals and fertilizers into the soil.  Several small trees and plants\nlie scattered about you as well as a few moss coated boulders.  The Northern\nSedmar river lies to your east while the banks to the north appear overgrown\nwith vegetation.  Unfortunately you see no way to reach the plains level above\nyou from this point.\n',113,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20599,92,-126,2,'Overgrown Banks of the Northern Sedmar River','  Covered in a thick layer of lush green grass this small strip of land only\noccasionally floods with waters from the Northern Sedmar River which deposits\nrich minerals and fertilizers into the soil.  Numerous small trees and plants\nlie scattered about you as well as several moss coated boulders.  The Northern\nSedmar river lies to your east while the banks to the south appear slightly\nless overgrown with vegetation.  Unfortunately you see no way to reach the\nplains level above you from this point and any path to the north has long\nsince become completely overgrown with vegetation.\n',113,131072,54,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20600,87,-151,2,'Guard\'s Tent','  Considering the tent\'s interior is fairly sparsely decorated its no wonder\nthat it is tidy and neat.  A small pile of thatch and leaves adorn one corner\nof the tent allowing the guards to take shifts and get a little rest.  A flat\nrock sits to one side where a carved wooden container of some type rests, most\nlikely to supply water or other beverage to the guards.  Apparently someone\nforgot to fill it at the springs recently as it is empty.  The only apparent\nexit to the tent is a flap covered opening.\n',129,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,12,108,0,'',NULL),
(20601,79,-148,2,'Overgrown Path','  While apparently the path may go farther into the forest to the south\nit seems it has been magically closed off by causing the already dense\ngreenery to grow into a solid wall of vegetation.  The sounds of the forest\ncan be heard all about you, but strangely remain unseen.  The path continues\nnorth to the grasslands where it seems to meet a small hardened path.\n',129,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20602,78,-146,2,'Top of a Steep Incline','  Appearing recently picked clean of rubble and debris the trail looks none\nto pleasant to navigate.  Several other paths are visible that have either\ncollapsed or become too cluttered to be of use.  Apparently it seems someone\nhas to keep cleaning or finding new ways to move between the canyon floor\nbelow and the grasslands to the southeast.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20603,79,-147,2,'Beaten Path','  Bordered by the grassy plains to the north and the thick vibrant forest to\nthe south this path apparently gets a good amount of use.  The path itself is\ncomprised of dark rich looking soil compacted and pressed into a hard almost\nrock surface which water pools and is forced to run off of instead of soaking\ninto its depths.  The path continues to the east towards a village of some\nsorts and to the south into the forest.  The path also continues to the\nnorthwest where it appears to drop off into the river canyon north of here.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20604,80,-147,2,'Beaten Path','  Bordered by the grassy plains to the north and the thick vibrant forest to\nthe south this path apparently gets a good amount of use.  The path itself is\ncomprised of dark rich looking soil compacted and pressed into a hard almost\nrock surface which water pools and is forced to run off of instead of soaking\ninto its depths.  The path continues to the east towards a village of some\nsorts and to the west towards a river canyon.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20605,81,-147,2,'Path Near the Village','  Bordered by the grassy plains to the north and the thick vibrant forest to\nthe south this path apparently gets a good amount of use.  The path itself is\ncomprised of dark rich looking soil compacted and pressed into a hard almost\nrock surface which water pools and is forced to run off of instead of soaking\ninto its depths.  To the east a small village rest while the path continues\nback to the west as well.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20606,82,-147,2,'Path Through the Village','  Clean of debris and other clutter the path appears to be well maintained\nas it runs through the small village.  A small line of rocks line both sides\nof the path as it moves along.  A small tent sits just off the path to your\nnorth and the backside of two other tents rest to your east and south.  The\ntent to the east appears to be considerably large and is most likely a\nmeeting tent of some type.  The tent to the south is of a decent size and\nappears to be of a quality which denotes a person of at least minor importance.\nThe path continues southeast farther into the village and back to the west\nwhere the rock lining seems to end, most likely signalling the end of village\ngrounds.  To the northwest the grasslands begin as tall grasses cover\neverything in sight and to the southwest a thick dense forest blocks all\npassage.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20607,83,-148,2,'Junction of Paths','  Clean of debris and other clutter the path appears to be well maintained\nas it runs through the small village.  A small line of rocks line both sides\nof the path as it moves along.  The side of a large tent sits to your north,\nby its immense size compared to the other tents about it you would guess it\nis some sort of meeting tent.  A clear blue expanse of water can be seen\nswirling in a fresh water spring fashion just to your east.  To the southwest\na moderately sized \"two\" tent structure exists with entrance flaps to your\nwest and south.  The path splits here going either northwest, northeast, or\nto the southeast.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20608,84,-149,2,'Path Through the Village','  Clean of debris and other clutter the path appears to be well maintained\nas it runs through the small village.  A small line of rocks line both sides\nof the path as it moves along.  The path seems to widen here a bit with a\nsmall offshoot to the east and the main portion continueing to the northwest\nor southeast.  A clear expanse of water swirls in a spring like fashion just\nto the north of you and a moderately sized tent sits to the west of you.\nThe dense forest which borders the village on the southwest is visible between\nthe tent and a strange \"cage\" contraption to the south.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20609,85,-149,2,'Path Near the Fields','  Clean of debris and other clutter the path appears to be well maintained\nas it runs through the small village.  A small line of rocks line both sides\nof the path as it moves along.  A small gate has been placed in a fence that\nruns across the path to the northeast.  The fence seems to run between the\nback of a tent to your east and a clear spring to your north.  The main path\nthrough the village can be seen to the south and west where it runs just in\nfront of a strange cage like contraption.  Beyond the cage sits the dense\nforest which borders this small village to the southwest.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20610,85,-150,2,'Path Through the Village','  Clean of debris and other clutter the path appears to be well maintained\nas it runs through the small village.  A small line of rocks line both sides\nof the path as it moves along.  The path seems to widen here a bit with a\nsmall offshoot to the north and the main portion continueing to the northwest\nor southeast.  A clear expanse of water swirls in a spring like fashion just\nbeyond the path to the north of here.  A small tent is just off the path to\nthe east while an odd cage like contraption sits to the west.  To the\nsouthwest a thick dense jungle borders the village.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20611,84,-147,2,'Path Through the Village','  Clean of debris and other clutter the path appears to be well maintained\nas it runs through the small village.  A small line of rocks line both sides\nof the path as it moves along.  To the northwest sits a grand tent with a\nset of flaps to its entrance.  By its massive size in comparison to the other\ntents throughout the village you gather this must be a meeting tent of some\nsort.  The path continues both northeast and southwest to a junction, but is\nbordered on the southeast by a small spring.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20612,85,-146,2,'Path Through the Village','  Clean of debris and other clutter the path appears to be well maintained\nas it runs through the small village.  A small line of rocks line both sides\nof the path as it moves along.  The side of a large tent can be seen to the\nwest of here while just slightly north and west sits a good sized tent.\nDirectly north of you is a tent with numerous \"trophies\" and such sitting\nabout it, most likely a gathering spot for hunters.  A small simple tent\nis to the east and has a fence running from the back of it up to the clear\nsprings directly to the south of you.  A gate is set into the fence with\na small offshoot of the path moving southeast towards it.  The main path seems\nto proceed both southwest and northeast of here.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20613,86,-145,2,'Top of a Mud Slide','  Most likely due to recent storms it appears the path here has collapsed\ninto the river canyon below.  This new change is seen by the villages to the\nsouthwest as both a good thing for easier access to the river, and yet a\nthreat to their simple way of life by allowing for the strange beast that\nlive along the river to gain access to their homes.  The grasslands sit to\nthe northwest as well as the southeast.  The back of two different tents\nblocks movement either west or south.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20614,86,-151,2,'Path Near the Village','  Bordered by the village to the northwest and the thick vibrant forest to\nthe southwest this path apparently gets a good amount of use.  The path\nis comprised of dark rich looking soil compacted and pressed into a hard almost\nrock surface which water pools and is forced to run off of instead of soaking\ninto its depths.  To the northwest a small village rest while the path\ncontinues to the south.  The back of a tent sits to your north and the front\nof a simple tent sits to your east.  Running between the two is a stout\nfence with a small gate set at its center.  To the southeast the grassland\nplains can be seen.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20615,86,-152,2,'Beaten Path','  Bordered by the grassy plains to the east and the thick vibrant forest to\nthe west this path apparently gets a good amount of use.  The path itself is\ncomprised of dark rich looking soil compacted and pressed into a hard almost\nrock surface which water pools and is forced to run off of instead of soaking\ninto its depths.  The path continues to the north towards a village of some\nsorts and to the south along a river canyon.  The side of a small plain\nlooking tent sits just to the north of you and a thin narrow offshoot of the\npath also moves to the southeast through some taller then average grasses.\nTo the southwest it appears a small section of the forest has been cleared\nenough to allow passage, but otherwise seems no different then the other\nsurrounding greenery which lies to the west.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20616,86,-153,2,'Beaten Path','  Bordered by a river canyon to the southeast and the vibrant forest to\nthe west this path apparently gets a good amount of use.  The path itself is\ncomprised of dark rich looking soil compacted and pressed into a hard almost\nrock surface which water pools and is forced to run off of instead of soaking\ninto its depths.  The path continues to the north towards a village of some\nsorts and to the south along a river canyon.  A thick wall of tall intertwined\ngrass prevents movement to the northeast and earth drops off into the river\ncanyon just a little ways beyond some tall grasses to the southeast.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20617,86,-154,2,'Beaten Path','  Bordered by a river canyon to the east and the rich vibrant forest to\nthe west this path apparently gets a good amount of use.  The path itself is\ncomprised of dark rich looking soil compacted and pressed into a hard almost\nrock surface which water pools and is forced to run off of instead of soaking\ninto its depths.  The path continues to the north and to the south but a\nthick wall of tall intertwined grass blocks your view to the east where the\nearth drops off into the river canyon below.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20618,86,-155,2,'Beaten Path','  Bordered by a river canyon to the southeast and the rich vibrant forest to\nthe northwest this path apparently gets a good amount of use.  The path\nitself is comprised of dark rich looking soil compacted and pressed into a\nhard almost rock surface which water pools and is forced to run off of instead\nof soaking into its depths.  The path continues to the north and dwindles to\nthe southwest but a thick wall of tall intertwined grass blocks your view to\nthe southeast where the earth drops off into the river canyon below.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20619,87,-153,2,'Next to a Large Tree','  Standing among tall thick grasses a large tree from below and south of\nhere protrudes its limbs through the grasses.  The thick intertwined grasses\nblock your way in all directions except to the northwest where a narrow path\nwinds its way through.  To the east and south you can hear the roar of what\nsounds like rushing water, but unfortunately the grasses block your view so\nyou can\'t be sure.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20620,85,-156,2,'Under a Large Tree','  Standing on a lush rich green pad of grass a large tree spreads its limbs\noverhead.  Tall thick grasses block your way to the east, where you can hear\nthe roar of rushing water, as does a dense forest to your west.  The small\nclearing extends south apparently, and you think maybe you could ascend the\ntree itself given its arrangement of limbs and knots.\n',129,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20621,85,-157,2,'Under a Large Tree','  Standing on a lush rich green pad of grass a large tree spreads its limbs\noverhead.  Tall thick grasses block your way to the east and south, where you\ncan hear the roar of rushing water.  To the west a dense forest again halts all\npassage and the small clearing extends a little farther north before being\nstopped by some light forest.\n',129,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20622,85,-157,3,'Lookout','  Given the several carved branches and worn bark on many of the limbs\nperfect for resting, you assume this is a lookout of some sort.  You\nhave an excellent window through the leaves south and below you into a\nhole set in the top of a small structure.  Another window has been\ngroomed into the concealing leaves down and to the southeast as well.\nYou can easily move back north deeper into the branches of the tree.\n',129,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20623,85,-156,3,'In a Large Tree','  A spiderwork of branches surround you offering numerous places to rest\nor climb.  You view is blocked in most direction by the thick canopy about\nyou.  It would seem you can proceed easily either down to the forest floor\nbelow you or to the south farther out within the branches.\n',129,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20624,85,-155,2,'Forest Edge','  Just barely cleared enough to allow movement this is the outskirts of a\ndense forest to your west.  Various stumps and other cut vegetation mark the\nway where someone or something has harvested the woods of the forest for their\nown use.   The light forest appears to continue to your north while a path\nalong its edge can just be seen to the east.  South of you a grassy clearing\nseems to surround an ancient tree.\n',129,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20625,85,-154,2,'Forest Edge','  Just barely cleared enough to allow movement this is the outskirts of a\ndense forest to your west.  Various stumps and other cut vegetation mark the\nway where someone or something has harvested the woods of the forest for their\nown use.   The light forest appears to continue to your north and south while\na path along its edge can just be seen to the east.\n',129,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20626,85,-153,2,'Forest Edge','  Just barely cleared enough to allow movement this is the outskirts of a\ndense forest to your west.  Various stumps and other cut vegetation mark the\nway where someone or something has harvested the woods of the forest for their\nown use.   The light forest appears to continue to your south while a path\nalong its edge can just be seen to the northeast and east.\n',129,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20627,87,-152,2,'Overlooking a Canyon','  Appearing rather unstable the earth here suddenly drops off into the river\ncanyon below.  The dirt is loose packed and seems to shift and move slightly\nwith each step or movement you make.  Several spots along the edge you see\nareas where the dirt has lost its hold and apparently cascaded into the canyon\nbelow leaving uneven barren earth.  A short distance back from the edge plains\ngrasses begin to take root where they strive and grow into a sea of wavy\nbrownish green.  You can just make out a path through the grasslands to your\nwest.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20628,88,-151,2,'Overlooking a Canyon','  Appearing rather unstable the earth here suddenly drops off into the river\ncanyon below.  The dirt is loose packed and seems to shift and move slightly\nwith each step or movement you make.  Several spots along the edge you see\nareas where the dirt has lost its hold and apparently cascaded into the canyon\nbelow leaving uneven barren earth.  A short distance back from the edge plains\ngrasses begin to take root where they strive and grow into a sea of wavy\nbrownish green.  Off to the west the back of a small plain looking tent can\nbe seen.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20629,88,-150,2,'Overlooking a Canyon','  Appearing rather unstable the earth here suddenly drops off into the river\ncanyon below.  The dirt is loose packed and seems to shift and move slightly\nwith each step or movement you make.  Several spots along the edge you see\nareas where the dirt has lost its hold and apparently cascaded into the canyon\nbelow leaving uneven barren earth.  A short distance back from the edge plains\ngrasses begin to take root where they strive and grow into a sea of wavy\nbrownish green.  To your west a sturdy looking fence sits comprised of numerous\nsharp barbed vines and grasses.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20630,88,-149,2,'Overlooking a Canyon','  Appearing rather unstable the earth here suddenly drops off into the river\ncanyon below.  The dirt is loose packed and seems to shift and move slightly\nwith each step or movement you make.  Several spots along the edge you see\nareas where the dirt has lost its hold and apparently cascaded into the canyon\nbelow leaving uneven barren earth.  A short distance back from the edge plains\ngrasses begin to take root where they strive and grow into a sea of wavy\nbrownish green.  To your west a sturdy looking fence sits comprised of numerous\nsharp barbed vines and grasses while you can move deeper into the plains to the\nnorthwest.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
