(20643,80,-145,2,'Overlooking a Canyon','  Appearing rather unstable the earth here suddenly drops off into the river\ncanyon below.  The dirt is loose packed and seems to shift and move slightly\nwith each step or movement you make.  Several spots along the edge you see\nareas where the dirt has lost its hold and apparently cascaded into the canyon\nbelow leaving uneven barren earth.  A short distance back from the edge plains\ngrasses begin to take root where they strive and grow into a sea of wavy\nbrownish green.  The heart of the grasslands lies to the south.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20644,79,-146,2,'Overlooking a Canyon','  Appearing rather unstable the earth here suddenly drops off into the river\ncanyon below.  The dirt is loose packed and seems to shift and move slightly\nwith each step or movement you make.  Several spots along the edge you see\nareas where the dirt has lost its hold and apparently cascaded into the canyon\nbelow leaving uneven barren earth.  A short distance back from the edge plains\ngrasses begin to take root where they strive and grow into a sea of wavy\nbrownish green.  The heart of the grasslands lies to the east while you can\njust make out a narrow path to the south.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20645,87,-148,2,'On the Plains','  Surrounded by tall vibrant plains grass you feel like you are amid a sea\nof wavy brownish-green dancers with the wind acting as their coordinator.\nThey roll and move in perfect unison appearing to thrive with the life given\nto them by the simplest gust of wind.  The very air seems to delight your\nsenses with its crisp clean fragrance and subtle undertones of life.  Even\nphysically the plains show ample signs of true life with small burrows here\nand there, and the tracks of numerous animals marring the ground beneath your\nfeet.  It seems though that most life seeks the safety of their shelters long\nbefore you arrive where you can feel but not see their ever present eyes\nwatching you.  To the west and south you can just make out a fence made from\nthe vines and grasses while the plains continue to the north and east.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20646,87,-147,2,'On the Plains','  Surrounded by tall vibrant plains grass you feel like you are amid a sea\nof wavy brownish-green dancers with the wind acting as their coordinator.\nThey roll and move in perfect unison appearing to thrive with the life given\nto them by the simplest gust of wind.  The very air seems to delight your\nsenses with its crisp clean fragrance and subtle undertones of life.  Even\nphysically the plains show ample signs of true life with small burrows here\nand there, and the tracks of numerous animals marring the ground beneath your\nfeet.  It seems though that most life seeks the safety of their shelters long\nbefore you arrive where you can feel but not see their ever present eyes\nwatching you.  The plains continue all about you except to the west where\na tightly woven fence of grasses and vines blocks your passage.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20647,87,-146,2,'On the Plains','  Surrounded by tall vibrant plains grass you feel like you are amid a sea\nof wavy brownish-green dancers with the wind acting as their coordinator.\nThey roll and move in perfect unison appearing to thrive with the life given\nto them by the simplest gust of wind.  The very air seems to delight your\nsenses with its crisp clean fragrance and subtle undertones of life.  Even\nphysically the plains show ample signs of true life with small burrows here\nand there, and the tracks of numerous animals marring the ground beneath your\nfeet.  It seems though that most life seeks the safety of their shelters long\nbefore you arrive where you can feel but not see their ever present eyes\nwatching you.  The plains continue all about you except to the west where\na small unremarkable tent blocks your passage and to the northwest where a\nnightmarish looking mud slide awaits.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20648,80,-146,2,'On the Plains','  Surrounded by tall vibrant plains grass you feel like you are amid a sea\nof wavy brownish-green dancers with the wind acting as their coordinator.\nThey roll and move in perfect unison appearing to thrive with the life given\nto them by the simplest gust of wind.  The very air seems to delight your\nsenses with its crisp clean fragrance and subtle undertones of life.  Even\nphysically the plains show ample signs of true life with small burrows here\nand there, and the tracks of numerous animals marring the ground beneath your\nfeet.  It seems though that most life seeks the safety of their shelters long\nbefore you arrive where you can feel but not see their ever present eyes\nwatching you.  The plains continue to the east while you can just make out a\nhard packed path to the south.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20649,81,-146,2,'On the Plains','  Surrounded by tall vibrant plains grass you feel like you are amid a sea\nof wavy brownish-green dancers with the wind acting as their coordinator.\nThey roll and move in perfect unison appearing to thrive with the life given\nto them by the simplest gust of wind.  The very air seems to delight your\nsenses with its crisp clean fragrance and subtle undertones of life.  Even\nphysically the plains show ample signs of true life with small burrows here\nand there, and the tracks of numerous animals marring the ground beneath your\nfeet.  It seems though that most life seeks the safety of their shelters long\nbefore you arrive where you can feel but not see their ever present eyes\nwatching you.  The plains continue to the west and northeast, but your way\nis blocked to the east by a small unremarkable tent structure.  You can just\nmake out a hard packed path to the south.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20650,82,-145,2,'On the Plains','  Surrounded by tall vibrant plains grass you feel like you are amid a sea\nof wavy brownish-green dancers with the wind acting as their coordinator.\nThey roll and move in perfect unison appearing to thrive with the life given\nto them by the simplest gust of wind.  The very air seems to delight your\nsenses with its crisp clean fragrance and subtle undertones of life.  Even\nphysically the plains show ample signs of true life with small burrows here\nand there, and the tracks of numerous animals marring the ground beneath your\nfeet.  It seems though that most life seeks the safety of their shelters long\nbefore you arrive where you can feel but not see their ever present eyes\nwatching you.  The plains continue to the southwest while the back of a small\nunremarkable tent can be seen south of here.  The back of a well made tent\nblocks your way to the east as well.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20651,84,-144,2,'On the Plains','  Surrounded by tall vibrant plains grass you feel like you are amid a sea\nof wavy brownish-green dancers with the wind acting as their coordinator.\nThey roll and move in perfect unison appearing to thrive with the life given\nto them by the simplest gust of wind.  The very air seems to delight your\nsenses with its crisp clean fragrance and subtle undertones of life.  Even\nphysically the plains show ample signs of true life with small burrows here\nand there, and the tracks of numerous animals marring the ground beneath your\nfeet.  It seems though that most life seeks the safety of their shelters long\nbefore you arrive where you can feel but not see their ever present eyes\nwatching you.  The plains continue to the east while the back of a well\nmade tent sits to the south blocking your passage.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20652,85,-144,2,'On the Plains','  Surrounded by tall vibrant plains grass you feel like you are amid a sea\nof wavy brownish-green dancers with the wind acting as their coordinator.\nThey roll and move in perfect unison appearing to thrive with the life given\nto them by the simplest gust of wind.  The very air seems to delight your\nsenses with its crisp clean fragrance and subtle undertones of life.  Even\nphysically the plains show ample signs of true life with small burrows here\nand there, and the tracks of numerous animals marring the ground beneath your\nfeet.  It seems though that most life seeks the safety of their shelters long\nbefore you arrive where you can feel but not see their ever present eyes\nwatching you.  The plains continue to the west while a nasty looking mudslide\nseems to have occurred to the southeast.  Off to the south the back of a\ndecorated tent intrudes onto the plains.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20653,86,-146,2,'In a Tent','  Tidy and neat this small tent appears to be a normal dwelling for a commoner\nof the Simal Village.  The dwellings interior is sparsely furnished with a\nfew simple hides to ward off the chill and a small cookfire.  The tent roof\nstretches upwards at a steep slope to keep the rain water from puddling and\ncollapsing the tent while a small opening has been left near the peak to allow\nsmoke and other foul odors to escape.  The only exit appears to be a simple\nflap covered slit cut into the west side of the tent.\n',129,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,10,108,0,'',NULL),
(20654,83,-145,2,'Chief\'s Tent','  Made from thick good quality hides this is appears to be the personal tent\nfor the chief of the Simal.  The dwellings interior is furnished with several\nthick hides to ward off the chill and a small cookfire.  The tent roof\nstretches upwards at a steep slope to keep the rain water from puddling and\ncollapsing the tent.  A small opening has been left near the peak to allow\nsmoke and other foul odors to escape.  The only exit appears to be a decorated\nhide screen to the east.\n',129,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,10,108,0,'',NULL),
(20655,84,-145,2,'Chief\'s Meeting Tent','  With the numerous mats and other furnishing about the room this apparently\nis the meeting space for the Chief and his advisors.  The hide walls are\ncoated in a thick greasy substance, most likely left over residue from pipe\nsmoking.  Beneath the grease various pictures and other crude paintings adorn\nthe walls, along with an occasional ceremonial piece securely fastened to the\ntent about the room.  A decorated panel seems to separate this space from a\nsmaller one to the west and the exit to the tent is located on the south side\nof the room.\n',129,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,20,120,0,'',NULL),
(20656,85,-145,2,'Hunter\'s Tent','  Smoke lingers in the air making the features of the room rather hazy.\nThrough the cloudy vapor various animals sit crouched about the tents edge\nseemingly on the verge of launching themselves into a frenzied attack.\nSeveral tribal looking Simal dance about the tent\'s perimeter apparently in\nthe midst of some ritual, completely ignoring the animals about them.  What\nis strangely absent though is the sounds that should accompany these images\nas the tent is deathly silent.  Overhead a thin sliver of light adds its ever\nso small contribution to the light which creeps in from the flap covered\nopening to the south.\n',129,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,15,120,0,'',NULL),
(20657,82,-146,2,'In a Tent','  Tidy and neat this small tent appears to be a normal dwelling for a commoner\nof the Simal Village.  The dwellings interior is sparsely furnished with a\nfew simple hides to ward off the chill and a small cookfire.  The tent roof\nstretches upwards at a steep slope to keep the rain water from puddling and\ncollapsing the tent while a small opening has been left near the peak to allow\nsmoke and other foul odors to escape.  The only exit appears to be a simple\nflap covered slit cut into the south side of the tent.\n',129,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,10,108,0,'',NULL),
(20658,83,-146,2,'Meeting Tent','  Bare of any major furnishings this seems to be a meeting tent of some sorts.\nThe ground has been packed down with a few scattered thatch mats thrown down\nto add some comfort for the elder Simal.  The hide of the simple tent structure\nsurrounding this space has been completely covered with numerous paintings\nand sketches, but no objects of any sort adorn the walls.  The tent extends\nto the south and east while a simple flap covered opening has been constructed\ninto the southeast side of the tent.\n',129,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(20659,84,-146,2,'Meeting Tent','  Bare of any major furnishings this seems to be a meeting tent of some sorts.\nThe ground has been packed down with a few scattered thatch mats thrown down\nto add some comfort for the elder Simal.  The hide of the simple tent structure\nsurrounding this space has been completely covered with numerous paintings\nand sketches, but no objects of any sort adorn the walls.  The tent extends\nto the west and southwest.\n',129,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(20660,83,-147,2,'Meeting Tent','  Bare of any major furnishings this seems to be a meeting tent of some sorts.\nThe ground has been packed down with a few scattered thatch mats thrown down\nto add some comfort for the elder Simal.  The hide of the simple tent structure\nsurrounding this space has been completely covered with numerous paintings\nand sketches, but no objects of any sort adorn the walls.  The tent extends\nto the north and northeast.\n',129,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,10,120,0,'',NULL),
(20661,82,-148,2,'Apprentice\'s Tent','  Obviously the tent of some one still in their years of study this tent\ncontains stacks and piles of what appear to be worthless junk.  A small\nmat sits in one corner to act as a sleeping pallet, but otherwise all useable\nspace within tent is occupied with these trinkets and other worthless items.\nSeveral oily stains can be seen along the tents wall, most likely where a flame\nof some sort was pushed too close and began to burn the oils within the cured\nhides.  The only apparent exit seems to be to the east, but with all the piles\nof junk about the room there easily could be more hidden away.\n',129,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,10,108,0,'',NULL),
(20662,83,-149,2,'Shaman\'s Tent','  Crowded with orderly stacks and piles of various odds and ends the tent\nappears to belong to a medicine man or shaman of some type.  Several tubes\nand bundles of dried herbs and other substances lie about the room neatly\nstacked.  A single sleeping mat seems to hint that the shaman has no mate,\nmost likely a result of his duties to the village.  The apparently is just\nthe single flap covered exit to the north, but with the numerous stacks and\npiles about the room another exit could easily be hidden.\n',129,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,10,108,0,'',NULL),
(20663,84,-150,2,'In a Cage','  Littered with bones and other ghastly substances the cage apparently is used\nto contain both beast and civilized prisoners of the village.  A thick reed\nbase and ceiling to the cage prevent anyone from digging their way out of the\nsmall prison.  Bars about the thickness of an elven forearm line the cage and\nare almost as sturdy as solid steel and apparently will hold even the strongest\ncreature.  The only exit appears to be the hinged opening of the cage to the\nnortheast.\n',129,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,8,108,0,'',NULL),
(20664,86,-149,2,'In a Tent','  Tidy and neat this small tent appears to be a normal dwelling for a commoner\nof the Simal Village.  The dwellings interior is sparsely furnished with a\nfew simple hides to ward off the chill and a small cookfire.  The tent roof\nstretches upwards at a steep slope to keep the rain water from puddling and\ncollapsing the tent while a small opening has been left near the peak to allow\nsmoke and other foul odors to escape.  The only exit appears to be a simple\nflap covered slit cut into the west side of the tent.\n',129,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,10,108,0,'',NULL),
(20665,86,-150,2,'In a Tent','  Tidy and neat this small tent appears to be a normal dwelling for a commoner\nof the Simal Village.  The dwellings interior is sparsely furnished with a\nfew simple hides to ward off the chill and a small cookfire.  The tent roof\nstretches upwards at a steep slope to keep the rain water from puddling and\ncollapsing the tent while a small opening has been left near the peak to allow\nsmoke and other foul odors to escape.  The only exit appears to be a simple\nflap covered slit cut into the west side of the tent.\n',129,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,10,108,0,'',NULL),
(20666,86,-147,2,'Path through a Field','  Lined on each side with rock this small path winds its way through the rows\nof cultivated crops about you.  Various irrigation ditches bring the much\nneeded water from the springs south of here to the crops.  To the northwest\na small gate across the path keeps out the various plains animals and the\npath seems to continue through the fields to the south.  Just barely visible\npast the crops to the east is a thick fence made from interwoven vines and\ngrasses which separates the fields from the plains.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20667,86,-148,2,'Path through a Field','  Lined on each side with rock this small path winds its way through the rows\nof cultivated crops about you.  Various irrigation ditches bring the much\nneeded water from the springs south of here to the crops.  To the southwest\nand southeast small gates lie across the path to keep out the various plains\nanimals.  The path seems to continue through the fields to the north.  Just\nbarely visible past the crops to the east is a thick fence made from interwoven\nvines and grasses which separates the fields from the plains.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20668,87,-149,2,'Fenced Pasture','  You stand on one of the many small animal paths that criss cross the pasture\nfields about you.  Grasses about three feet in height sway to and fro and seem\nto provide more then ample grazing grounds for the few animals kept by the\nSimal.  The pastures seems to continue to the south and is bordered by a thick\nfence of interwoven grasses and vines to the east, a gate in the fence sits to\nthe northwest.  The back of a small ordinary looking tent sits off to the west.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20669,87,-150,2,'Fenced Pasture','  You stand on one of the many small animal paths that criss cross the pasture\nfields about you.  Grasses about three feet in height sway to and fro and seem\nto provide more then ample grazing grounds for the few animals kept by the\nSimal.  The pastures seems to continue to the north and is bordered by a thick\nfence of interwoven grasses and vines to the east, a gate in the fence sits to\nthe southwest.  The back of a small ordinary looking tent sits off to the west.\n',129,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20670,84,-148,2,'Tiscal Springs','  Crystal blue in color the springs are a source of pure fresh water for the\nSimal.  The water seems to swirl about in a large lazy circle as it bubbles up\nfrom the springs source below you.  These springs appear to be home to some sort\nof large barbed fish as several of them dart past.  A path around the springs\ncan be seen west, north and south of here while the springs continue to the\nnortheast and east.\n',129,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20671,85,-147,2,'Tiscal Springs','  Crystal blue in color the springs are a source of pure fresh water for the\nSimal.  The water seems to swirl about in a large lazy circle as it bubbles up\nfrom the springs source below you.  These springs appear to be home to some sort\nof large barbed fish as several of them dart past.  A path around the springs\ncan be seen to the west & north.  The springs continue to the southwest and\nsouth while a cultivated field is just visible to the east.\n',129,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20672,85,-148,2,'Tiscal Springs','  Crystal blue in color the springs are a source of pure fresh water for the\nSimal.  The water seems to swirl about in a large lazy circle as it bubbles up\nfrom the springs source below you.  These springs appear to be home to some sort\nof large barbed fish as several of them dart past.  A path around the springs\ncan be seen to the south.  The springs continue to the west and north while\na cultivated field is just visible to the east.\n',129,131072,29,0,0,0,60,5,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20673,85,-148,1,'Below the Surface of Tiscal Springs','  Fighting the lazy yet surprising strong current of the springs the surface\nis just overhead.  Several barbed fish dart about only rarely stopping long\nenough to inspect the intrusion into their home.  Farther below the source of\nthe springs is just barely visible.\n',129,131072,30,0,0,0,60,5,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20674,85,-148,0,'Bottom of Tiscal Springs','  Standing at the bottom of the springs the current is surprisingly strong.\nSeveral small rock bounce and roll about just slightly too heavy to be pushed\ncompletely from their home here on the bottom.  Within a circle of heavy\nboulders can be seen the small pentration into the rock below which supplies\nthe water source of the springs.\n',129,131072,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20750,94,-127,2,'A Lookout Post by the Gates','  Situated between the cleft of two high walls of unscaleable rock this Calthor\nOutpost was the farthest north of its kind for the Calthor Empire.  The outpost\nwas overtaken by the Chaos Winds when they obliterated the Calthor Empire from\nthe map.  Unused by any organized forced in some time the Outpost Yards are now\nbarren of anything of use.  Tall grasses cover the once well kept grounds and \nvarious broken and rusty scraps lies scattered about.  The Yards continue to \nthe north and east while a large brittle looking bronze gate stands across \nthe pass to the southwest.\n',149,131072,41,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20751,94,-126,2,'A Lookout Post above the River','  Situated between the cleft of two high walls of unscaleable rock this Calthor\nOutpost was the farthest north of its kind for the Calthor Empire.  The outpost\nwas overtaken by the Chaos Winds when they obliterated the Calthor Empire from\nthe map.  Unused by any organized forced in some time the Outpost Yards are now\nbarren of anything of use.  Tall grasses cover the once well kept grounds and \nvarious broken and rusty scraps lies scattered about.  The Yards continue to \nthe east and south from this small lookout over the river canyon to the west.\n',149,131072,41,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20752,95,-127,2,'The Outpost Yards','  Situated between the cleft of two high walls of unscaleable rock this Calthor\nOutpost was the farthest north of its kind for the Calthor Empire.  The outpost\nwas overtaken by the Chaos Winds when they obliterated the Calthor Empire from\nthe map.  Unused by any organized forced in some time the Outpost Yards are now\nbarren of anything of use.  Tall grasses cover the once well kept grounds and \nvarious broken and rusty scraps lies scattered about.  The Yards continue to \nthe west, north and northeast.\n',149,131072,41,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20753,95,-126,2,'The Outpost Yards','  Situated between the cleft of two high walls of unscaleable rock this Calthor\nOutpost was the farthest north of its kind for the Calthor Empire.  The outpost\nwas overtaken by the Chaos Winds when they obliterated the Calthor Empire from\nthe map.  Unused by any organized forced in some time the Outpost Yards are now\nbarren of anything of use.  Tall grasses cover the once well kept grounds and \nvarious broken and rusty scraps lies scattered about.  The Yards continue to \nthe west, south and east.\n',149,131072,41,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20754,96,-126,2,'Before the Outpost Cavern','  Situated between the cleft of two high walls of unscaleable rock this Calthor\nOutpost was the farthest north of its kind for the Calthor Empire.  The outpost\nwas overtaken by the Chaos Winds when they obliterated the Calthor Empire from\nthe map.  Unused by any organized forced in some time the Outpost Yards are now\nbarren of anything of use.  Tall grasses cover the once well kept grounds and \nvarious broken and rusty scraps lies scattered about.  The Yards continue to \nthe south and west while a large battered bronze door has been constructed\ninto the rock wall to the southeast.\n',149,131072,41,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20755,97,-127,2,'A Large Cavern','  Once a natural cavern the Calthor legions used magic and might to expand and\nfinish this cavern as part of the Outpost.  The walls were once adorned with\npaintings and tapestries which depicted the might of the Calthor Empire but\nthese have long since withered and worn away, been outright stolen, or simply \ndefaced until they are no longer legible.  A carved set of stone stairs \ngradually climb into the higher portion of the cavern to the southeast.\n',149,131080,56,0,0,0,0,-1,0,210,0,'',NULL),
(20756,98,-128,2,'The Outpost Hall','  Once a natural cavern the Calthor legions used magic and might to expand and\nfinish this cavern as part of the Outpost.  The walls were once adorned with\npaintings and tapestries which depicted the might of the Calthor Empire but\nthese have long since withered and worn away, been outright stolen, or simply \ndefaced until they are no longer legible.  A carved set of stone stairs \ngradually descend into the lower portion of the cavern to the northwest while\nanother smaller set leads upwards to the southeast.  There is a sturdy looking \nbronze door to the north and a plain bronze door to the east.  A horrid smell \nseems to come from beyond a wooden door to the west as well as the passageway \nwhich leads to the southwest.\n',149,131080,56,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(20757,98,-127,2,'A Weapon\'s Storage Room','  Apparently once used to store the Outpost arsenal this small room has been\nconverted into some sort of cage or den for a large beast.  A make-shift bed\nof scrap leather and grasses is situated in the northwest corner of the room\nwhile the opposite corner holds other not so pleasant treasures.  A sturdy\nlooking bronze door bars passage to the south when it is closed and there\nappears to be no other exits.\n',149,131080,56,0,0,0,0,-1,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(20758,99,-128,2,'The Outpost Commander\'s Room','  Once used by the Outpost Commander as their personal quarters the rooms\ncurrent occupant is definitely not from any organized legion.  What was once\na grand desk of polished oak and bronze is now a heap of rubble, numerous \npieces having been stripped for their value or flamiblity.  One large drawer\nof the desk has even been degraded so far as to be used as a chamberpot.  What\nonce might have been a bed is now a pile of burnt ash where an extremely hot\nfire got out of hand.  The remainder of the room is a heap of trash and filth\nnot worth sorting through.  The only apparent exit to the room seems to be a\nplain bronze door to the west.\n',149,131080,56,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(20759,97,-128,2,'The Outpost Kitchen','  Ow!  What a stench!  This was, and seemingly still is, the Outpost Kitchen.\nNumerous pots and rusted utensils lie about the room, those that are still\nusable so coated in filth and grime one would be crazy to handle them.  Many\nof the pots have been melted clean through as a careless cook set them too\nclose to a fire which was entirely too hot for cooking.  What were once \npreperation tables of oak have been smashed and used as fire wood with table\nlegs and large wooden splinters scattered about the room.  Only one small\narea is clear and obivously used to prepare the meals of the Outposts current\ninhabitants.  An opening in the rock wall to the south seems to lead to the\nDining Hall while the only other exit seems to be through a wooden door to\nthe east.\n',149,131080,56,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(20760,97,-129,2,'The Outpost Dining Hall','  Once filled with rows of oak tables for the Outposts Legions to gather at\nthis was the Dining Hall.  The once sturdy tables now lie in heaps as they\nwere apparently broken and smashed for firewood or from large brawls.  Table\nlegs lie scattered about, most broken as they were smashed over someones head.\nThe flat table tops lie on the floor, some piled high with filth and rotting\nscraps of what might be called food, while others are covered in urine and \nfeces.  Passageways through the rock lie to the northeast and north while a \nlarge bronze banded door lies to the south for one to escape this nightmare.\n',149,131080,56,0,0,0,0,-1,0,110,0,'',NULL),
(20761,97,-130,2,'The Outpost Barracks','  An utter disaster area, the once orderly barracks of the Outpost have been\nconverted into a maze of broken beds and furniture.  Foot lockers have been\nsmashed to get at their contents or burned whole for firewood.  The once basic\nstraw filled mattresses have been broken open and used as toilets, leaving\nthem ripe and reaking of waste and feces.  Small cleared spots here and there\ndenote personal sleeping areas for the current inhabitants while the barracks\ncontinues on to the east.  One large pile of heavy looking crates and broken \nfurniture sits against the west wall strangely out of place in its \"stacked\" \narrangement.  A bronze banded door to the north bars passage in that direction\nwhen closed.\n',149,131080,56,0,0,0,0,-1,0,110,0,'',NULL),
(20762,98,-130,2,'The Outpost Barracks','  An utter disaster area, the once orderly barracks of the Outpost have been\nconverted into a maze of broken beds and furniture.  Foot lockers have been\nsmashed to get at their contents or burned whole for firewood.  The once basic\nstraw filled mattresses have been broken open and used as toilets, leaving\nthem ripe and reaking of waste and feces.  Small cleared spots here and there\ndenote personal sleeping areas for the current inhabitants while the barracks\ncontinues on to the west.  A narrow stairway ascends higher into the cavern to\nthe northwest appearing to be the only exit from this disaster.\n',149,131080,56,0,0,0,0,-1,0,110,0,'',NULL),
(20763,99,-129,2,'An Ancient Altar','  Once crafted to honor an ancient deity of the Calthor people the small altar\nis the only semblance of order left within the Outpost.  Due to its holy nature\nnot a word may be uttered in this sacred space.  Perhaps this holy silence has\ncaused enough unease in the Outposts current inhabitants to instill a sense of\nfear into their hearts allowing this Altar to go unharmed.  Two small sets of\nstairs lead gradually downwards to the northwest as well as to the southwest.\n',149,142824,56,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(20764,96,-130,2,'A Cramped Cavern','  Once a storage room for the day to day needs of the Outpost this room appears\nto have been converted into a haphazard daycare, or perhaps prison is a better \nterm.  Anything which might have once been in the room is now smashed, burned,\nor chewed on.  Markings and paintings adorn the wall, drawn with substances\nbest not to dwell on.  A stacked pile of crates and furniture can bar passage \nout of the room to the east and seem to have been arranged purposely for just \nthat reason.\n',149,131080,56,0,0,0,0,-1,6,70,0,'',NULL),
(20800,93,-128,2,'Overlooking a Canyon','  Appearing rather unstable the earth here suddenly drops off into the river\ncanyon below.  The dirt is loose packed and seems to shift and move slightly\nwith each step or movement you make.  Several spots along the edge you see\nareas where the dirt has lost its hold and apparently cascaded into the canyon\nbelow leaving uneven barren earth.  A short distance back from the edge plains\ngrasses begin to take root where they strive and grow into a sea of wavy\nbrownish green.  The grasses die out a little ways to the east as a wall of\nimpassable rock ascends into the Calcathian Mountains.  To the northeast \nsomeone has undergone the tedious work to dig out a brittle looking bronze\ngate from beneath an avalance of rock and dirt.\n',147,131076,41,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20801,93,-129,2,'Overlooking a Canyon','  Appearing rather unstable the earth here suddenly drops off into the river\ncanyon below.  The dirt is loose packed and seems to shift and move slightly\nwith each step or movement you make.  Several spots along the edge you see\nareas where the dirt has lost its hold and apparently cascaded into the canyon\nbelow leaving uneven barren earth.  A short distance back from the edge plains\ngrasses begin to take root where they strive and grow into a sea of wavy\nbrownish green.  The grasses die out a little ways to the east as a wall of\nimpassable rock ascends into the Calcathian Mountains.\n',147,131072,41,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20802,93,-130,2,'Overlooking a Canyon','  Appearing rather unstable the earth here suddenly drops off into the river\ncanyon below.  The dirt is loose packed and seems to shift and move slightly\nwith each step or movement you make.  Several spots along the edge you see\nareas where the dirt has lost its hold and apparently cascaded into the canyon\nbelow leaving uneven barren earth.  A short distance back from the edge plains\ngrasses begin to take root where they strive and grow into a sea of wavy\nbrownish green.  The grasses die out a little ways to the east as a wall of\nimpassable rock ascends into the Calcathian Mountains.\n',147,131072,41,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20803,92,-131,2,'Overlooking a Canyon','  Appearing rather unstable the earth here suddenly drops off into the river\ncanyon below.  The dirt is loose packed and seems to shift and move slightly\nwith each step or movement you make.  Several spots along the edge you see\nareas where the dirt has lost its hold and apparently cascaded into the canyon\nbelow leaving uneven barren earth.  A short distance back from the edge plains\ngrasses begin to take root where they strive and grow into a sea of wavy\nbrownish green.  The grasses continue to the east where they cover the\nfoothills of the Calcathian Mountains in a blanket of vegetation.\n',147,131072,41,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20804,92,-132,2,'Overlooking a Canyon','  Appearing rather unstable the earth here suddenly drops off into the river\ncanyon below.  The dirt is loose packed and seems to shift and move slightly\nwith each step or movement you make.  Several spots along the edge you see\nareas where the dirt has lost its hold and apparently cascaded into the canyon\nbelow leaving uneven barren earth.  A short distance back from the edge plains\ngrasses begin to take root where they strive and grow into a sea of wavy\nbrownish green.  The grasses continue to the east across the plains before\ncoming to the Calcathian foothills beyond.\n',147,131072,41,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
