(20828,89,-154,2,'Overlooking a Canyon','  Appearing rather unstable the earth here suddenly drops off into the river\ncanyon below.  The dirt is loose packed and seems to shift and move slightly\nwith each step or movement you make.  Several spots along the edge you see\nareas where the dirt has lost its hold and apparently cascaded into the canyon\nbelow leaving uneven barren earth.  A short distance back from the edge plains\ngrasses begin to take root where they strive and grow into a sea of wavy\nbrownish green.  The grasses continue to the east where they cover the\nfoothills of the Calcathian Mountains in a blanket of vegetation.  A recent\nstorm seems to have created a new ravine to the north down to the canyon\nfloor below.  While a tricky descent, the sloped ravine is traversable.\n',147,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
