(20847,93,-131,2,'The Calcathian Foothills','  With the plains to the west and the ancient Calcathian mountains, or\n\"Calcat\'s Spine\" as they are often termed, to the east, these are the\nfoothills which lie in between.  Covered in the thick lush plains grasses\nlike the flatlands to the west, the landscape also has several sharp\noutcroppings and ascending walls of rock as it moves upwards into the mountain\nheights.  Unfortunately not far to the east the foothills quickly turn into\nfull fledged mountains where large vertical expanses of rock make progress\nin that direction all but impossible.\n',147,131072,47,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
