(20870,94,-138,2,'Foot of a Rock Slide','  With the plains to the west and the ancient Calcathian mountains, or\n\"Calcat\'s Spine\" as they are often termed, to the east, these are the\nfoothills which lie in between.  Covered in the thick lush plains grasses\nlike the flatlands to the west, the landscape also has several sharp\noutcroppings and ascending walls of rock as it moves upwards into the mountain\nheights.  A small trail, possibly an ancient road, apparently once led\ninto the mountains to the northeast but a massive rock slide has sealed\nthe pass in that direction.\n',148,131072,47,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20871,95,-139,2,'Foot of a Rock Slide','  With the plains to the west and the ancient Calcathian mountains, or\n\"Calcat\'s Spine\" as they are often termed, to the east, these are the\nfoothills which lie in between.  Covered in the thick lush plains grasses\nlike the flatlands to the west, the landscape also has several sharp\noutcroppings and ascending walls of rock as it moves upwards into the mountain\nheights.  A small trail, possibly an ancient road, apparently once led\ninto the mountains to the northeast but a massive rock slide has sealed\nthe pass in that direction.\n',148,131072,47,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20872,94,-144,2,'Foot of a Rock Slide','  With the plains to the west and the ancient Calcathian mountains, or\n\"Calcat\'s Spine\" as they are often termed, to the east, these are the\nfoothills which lie in between.  Covered in the thick lush plains grasses\nlike the flatlands to the west, the landscape also has several sharp\noutcroppings and ascending walls of rock as it moves upwards into the mountain\nheights.  A small trail, possibly an ancient road, apparently once led\ninto the mountains to the southeast but a massive rock slide has sealed\nthe pass in that direction.\n',148,131072,47,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20873,93,-148,2,'Before a Pair of Massive Gates','  With the plains to the west and the ancient Calcathian mountains, or\n\"Calcat\'s Spine\" as they are often termed, to the east, these are the\nfoothills which lie in between.  Covered in the thick lush plains grasses\nlike the flatlands to the west, the landscape also has several sharp\noutcroppings and ascending walls of rock as it moves upwards into the mountain\nheights.  What appears to have been an ancient road begins here and leads to\nthe southeast up to a pair of massive stone gates.\n',148,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20874,89,-158,2,'Overlooking a Dam','  This small lookout spot sits next to a grand natural dam which lies to the\nwest of here.  A window like opening is present through the trees which allows\nsomeone to look at the water which lies at the base of the dam.  The plains\nbegin north of here while the Calcathian Mountains lie to the east.  To the\nsouth all hope of travel seems useless as a thick forest becomes quickly\nimpassable with no apparent game or man-made trails to traverse.\n',148,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20875,95,-137,2,'The Top of a Rock Slide','  Once a road through the Calcathian Mountains, a rock slide has filled \nthe lower portion of the pass.  The slide is traversable to the southeast\nand east yet, but the rock walls of the pass block passage in other \ndirections.  A large pile of rubble and stone sit across the entrance of \nthe pass to the southwest blocking passage back out onto the plains.\n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20876,96,-138,2,'The Top of a Rock Slide','  Once a road through the Calcathian Mountains, a rock slide has filled \nthe lower portion of the pass.  The slide is traversable to the northwest\nand north yet, but the rock walls of the pass block passage in other \ndirections.  A large pile of rubble and stone sit across the entrance of \nthe pass to the southwest blocking passage back out onto the plains.  To \nthe east a windy trail leads up through the larger piles of stone to a \nplateau farther in that direction.\n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20877,96,-137,2,'The Top of a Rock Slide','  Once a road through the Calcathian Mountains, a rock slide has filled \nthe lower portion of the pass.  The slide is traversable to the west\nand south yet, but the rock walls of the pass block passage in other \ndirections.  To the north a windy trail leads up through the larger piles \nof stone to a plateau farther in that direction.\n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20878,96,-136,2,'A Cultivated Plateau','  At one time a barren plateau, small patches of green vegetation has been\nnurtured to life all about the area.  Probably some of the worst possible\nfarmland when compared to the rich fertile soil of the plains to the west,\nit is none the less a flat expanse of rock and soil and relatively safe from\nthe Chaos Winds.  For this fact alone it has been worked and toiled over for\nyears and is just now sprouting the fruits of those labors in any substantial\nquantity.  The plateau continues to the north and east while a small windy\ntrail leads down through a rock slide to the south.\n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20879,97,-136,2,'A Cultivated Plateau','  At one time a barren plateau, small patches of green vegetation has been\nnurtured to life all about the area.  Probably some of the worst possible\nfarmland when compared to the rich fertile soil of the plains to the west,\nit is none the less a flat expanse of rock and soil and relatively safe from\nthe Chaos Winds.  For this fact alone it has been worked and toiled over for\nyears and is just now sprouting the fruits of those labors in any substantial\nquantity.  The plateau continues to the north and west.\n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20880,96,-135,2,'A Cultivated Plateau','  At one time a barren plateau, small patches of green vegetation has been\nnurtured to life all about the area.  Probably some of the worst possible\nfarmland when compared to the rich fertile soil of the plains to the west,\nit is none the less a flat expanse of rock and soil and relatively safe from\nthe Chaos Winds.  For this fact alone it has been worked and toiled over for\nyears and is just now sprouting the fruits of those labors in any substantial\nquantity.  The plateau continues to the south and east.\n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20881,97,-135,2,'A Cultivated Plateau','  At one time a barren plateau, small patches of green vegetation has been\nnurtured to life all about the area.  Probably some of the worst possible\nfarmland when compared to the rich fertile soil of the plains to the west,\nit is none the less a flat expanse of rock and soil and relatively safe from\nthe Chaos Winds.  For this fact alone it has been worked and toiled over for\nyears and is just now sprouting the fruits of those labors in any substantial\nquantity.  The plateau continues to the south and west while a small trail\nwinds its way up to a plateau slightly higher then this one to the northeast.\n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20882,98,-134,2,'A Lookout Plateau','  Too small to be of any agricultural use this plateau does provide a small\nspring which has been used to water the cultivated fields below to the \nsouthwest.  Also it is a perfect lookout point to watch for any aggressive\ncreatures which might seek to feed on the vegetation of the plateau below or\nthe workers who tend it.  Shear rock walls surround the plateau on all sides \nexcept to the southwest and southeast.  To the southwest a small windy trail \nleads downwards to the cultivated plateau in that direction while a large \ncave opening covers the expanse of the wall to the southeast.\n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20883,97,-138,2,'A Cultivated Plateau','  At one time a barren plateau, small patches of green vegetation has been\nnurtured to life randomly about the area.  Probably some of the worst possible\nfarmland when compared to the rich fertile soil of the plains to the west,\nit is none the less a flat expanse of rock and soil and relatively safe from\nthe Chaos Winds.  For this fact alone it has been worked and toiled over for\nyears but has yet to sprout the fruits of those labors in any substantial\nquantity.  A few make-shift dwellings, little more then three sided tents,\nare set about the edges of the plateau.  The plateau continues to the south \nand east while a small trail winds its way down through a rock slide to the \nwest.\n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20884,97,-139,2,'A Cultivated Plateau','  At one time a barren plateau, small patches of green vegetation has been\nnurtured to life randomly about the area.  Probably some of the worst possible\nfarmland when compared to the rich fertile soil of the plains to the west,\nit is none the less a flat expanse of rock and soil and relatively safe from\nthe Chaos Winds.  For this fact alone it has been worked and toiled over for\nyears but has yet to sprout the fruits of those labors in any substantial\nquantity.  A few make-shift dwellings, little more then three sided tents,\nare set about the edges of the plateau.  The plateau continues to the north \nand east.\n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20885,98,-138,2,'A Cultivated Plateau','  At one time a barren plateau, small patches of green vegetation has been\nnurtured to life randomly about the area.  Probably some of the worst possible\nfarmland when compared to the rich fertile soil of the plains to the west,\nit is none the less a flat expanse of rock and soil and relatively safe from\nthe Chaos Winds.  For this fact alone it has been worked and toiled over for\nyears but has yet to sprout the fruits of those labors in any substantial\nquantity.  A few make-shift dwellings, little more then three sided tents,\nare set about the edges of the plateau.  The plateau continues to the south \nand west.\n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20886,98,-139,2,'A Cultivated Plateau','  At one time a barren plateau, small patches of green vegetation has been\nnurtured to life randomly about the area.  Probably some of the worst possible\nfarmland when compared to the rich fertile soil of the plains to the west,\nit is none the less a flat expanse of rock and soil and relatively safe from\nthe Chaos Winds.  For this fact alone it has been worked and toiled over for\nyears but has yet to sprout the fruits of those labors in any substantial\nquantity.  A few make-shift dwellings, little more then three sided tents,\nare set about the edges of the plateau.  The plateau continues to the north \nand west while a large pile of collected brush and branches lie against the \nsoutheast expanse of wall which borders the plateau.\n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20887,99,-140,2,'A Large Cave','  Quite large in size it appears the cave is primarily used as a storage \narea for the refugees.  While large, it is not big enough to house all the\nrefugees so rather then fight over the rights to use the cave it seems the\nrefugees live outside in their simple make-shift dwellings.  One corner of\nof the cave does appears to be kept cleared for an emergency shelter should\nharsh weather come up or something attack the small community.  The cave \ncontinues to the southeast and an opening to the northwest seems to lead \noutside where a large pile of brush and branches lie stacked.\n',150,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(20888,100,-141,2,'A Large Cave','  Quite large in size it appears the cave is primarily used as a storage \narea for the refugees.  While large, it is not big enough to house all the\nrefugees so rather then fight over the rights to use the cave it seems the\nrefugees live outside in their simple make-shift dwellings.  This area of\nthe cave seems to be for long term storage of anything which might later\nbe useful.  Almost all of it is useless junk but one never knows when it\nmight come in handy, especially when living in as primitive conditions as\nthese.  The cave continues to the northwest, which is the only direction \nother then to the southwest where junk is not piled or stacked.\n',150,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(20889,99,-142,2,'A Windy Cave','  Due to the high ceiling overhead and the circular shape of this particular\ncave, the winds which enter from the southwest and are vented through a\nsmall opening near the top of the cave seem to be highly amplified.  Dust\nand debris are constantly caught up in the high speed winds and sucked out\nthrough the small hole overhead.  The walls of the cave are polished smooth\nfrom years of this abrasive action and the size of the cave actually seems \nto be steadily growing.  One abnormal draft of air seems to come from the\nnortheast which is outside the normal pattern.  The cave appears to continue\nto the south and west.\n',150,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,160,0,'',NULL),
(20890,99,-143,2,'A Windy Cave','  Due to the high ceiling overhead and the circular shape of this particular\ncave, the winds which enter from the southwest and are vented through a\nsmall opening near the top of the cave seem to be highly amplified.  Dust\nand debris are constantly caught up in the high speed winds and sucked out\nthrough the small hole overhead.  The walls of the cave are polished smooth\nfrom years of this abrasive action and the size of the cave actually seems \nto be steadily growing.  The cave appears to continue to the north and west.\n',150,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,160,0,'',NULL),
(20891,98,-142,2,'A Windy Cave','  Due to the high ceiling overhead and the circular shape of this particular\ncave, the winds which enter from the southwest and are vented through a\nsmall opening near the top of the cave seem to be highly amplified.  Dust\nand debris are constantly caught up in the high speed winds and sucked out\nthrough the small hole overhead.  The walls of the cave are polished smooth\nfrom years of this abrasive action and the size of the cave actually seems \nto be steadily growing.  The cave appears to continue to the south and east.\n',150,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,160,0,'',NULL),
(20892,98,-143,2,'A Windy Cave','  Due to the high ceiling overhead and the circular shape of this particular\ncave, the winds which enter from the southwest and are vented through a\nsmall opening near the top of the cave seem to be highly amplified.  Dust\nand debris are constantly caught up in the high speed winds and sucked out\nthrough the small hole overhead.  The walls of the cave are polished smooth\nfrom years of this abrasive action and the size of the cave actually seems \nto be steadily growing.  The cave appears to continue to the north and east.\nA rusty gate has been crudely attached to the opening in the cave wall to\nthe southwest.\n',150,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,160,0,'',NULL),
(20893,97,-144,2,'A Narrow Ledge','  Quite dangerous and narrow this ledge is constantly buffeted by strong\nwinds which blow from the south and west coming off the plains.  The ledge\nthankful is clear of any rocks and stones which might cause one to loose\ntheir footing due to the high speed winds which catch up and carry off\nsuch debris.  The ledge continues to the south but stops before a cave\nopening to the northeast where a rusty looking gate has been crudely affixed\nto the cave entrance.  \n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,4,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20894,97,-145,2,'A Narrow Ledge','  Quite dangerous and narrow this ledge is constantly buffeted by strong\nwinds which blow from the south and west coming off the plains.  The ledge\nthankful is clear of any rocks and stones which might cause one to loose\ntheir footing due to the high speed winds which catch up and carry off\nsuch debris.  The ledge continues to the north or a small narrow path leads\ndownwards to the southwest into a narrow fissure.  \n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,4,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20895,96,-146,2,'A Narrow Fissure','  Caused by some seismic occurrence this fissure has been cut through solid\nrock.  The shear rock walls stretch far overhead but are unfortunately just\nbarely far enough apart to hinder any chance to climb up using both walls\nfor support.  The fissure continues to the northwest or a small narrow path\nleads upwards to the northeast where a narrow ledge on the side of the\nmountain is just visible.  \n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,5,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20896,95,-145,2,'A Narrow Fissure','  Caused by some seismic occurrence this fissure has been cut through solid\nrock.  The shear rock walls stretch far overhead but are unfortunately just\nbarely far enough apart to hinder any chance to climb up using both walls\nfor support.  The fissure continues to the southeast, but to the northwest\na pile of boulders appear to block any passage.\n',150,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,5,-1,0,'',NULL),
(20897,99,-135,2,'A Large Cavern','  Circular in shape the cavern has a high ceiling and is cluttered with\nnumerous debris and fallen rock.  A tingle to the air seems to nag at your\nsenses constantly drawing your attention to the eastern area of the cavern.\nA large opening to the northwest appears to be the only apparent exit to \nthe cavern and leads out onto a high plateau.  A regular \"whooshing\" sound\ncomes from that direction.\n',150,131084,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(20898,100,-135,2,'A Large Carved Lair','  Once a small hole in the side of the mountain a creature has clawed or\nused its magic to extract tons of rock to make a large lair for itself.\nThe walls are marred by numerous scratch and claw marks along with several\nblast marks where the rock was literally blown away.  Many of the caves\nfeatures seem similar to those used by dragons.  Unlike many dragons though\nthis lair seems to be lacking in any major treasure horde, strange if its\ninhabitant is a true dragon.  A large opening to the east appears to the\nonly apparent exit to the lair and the pleasant sounds of a bubbling spring\nemanate through the opening.\n',150,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(20899,101,-135,2,'A Secluded Grotto','  With several foreign trees and other vegetation about the area this small \ngrotto is apparently tended by someone for their own pleasures.  Shear rock\nwalls prohibit any chance of climbing out of the tiny grotto and high winds\noverhead would be dangerous for any but the most powerful of fliers.  A large\nopening in the rock face to the west leads into a cave of some sort.  \n',150,139584,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22400,-16,-26,0,'A Bright Tunnel','  Sunlight filters in through the opening to the south, through which you are\nable to glimpse strange, colorful hills.  To the north, the tunnel continues\ninto the darkness...\n',120,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22401,-12,-22,0,'At the Edge of a Vast Forest','  You stand at the edge of a vast forest which stretches to the east.  To the\nwest lies a decaying road.  Apparently this road once continued eastward into\nthe dark woods, but neglect has allowed the forest to create an impassable\nbarrier.  A small tunnel, however, has recently been cut through a colossal\ntree, thus providing passage.\n',120,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22402,-13,-22,0,'Bend in a Decaying Road','  The decaying road you are traveling along bends here, continuing to the\nnorth and to the east.  To the east the road appears to end, blocked by a\ndense forest.\n',120,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22403,-13,-21,0,'Bend in a Decaying Road','  The decaying road you are traveling along bends here, continuing to the\nsouth and to the west.  The road is in extremely poor shape here.  Along\nthe sides of the road lie the bones of many strange creatures, now\nunidentifiable.\n',120,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22404,-14,-21,0,'On A Decaying Road','  The decaying road you are traveling along continues to run east and\nwest.  To the south-east you can see a vast forest, to the north-east a\ndistant village, and to the south-west a range of hills.\n',120,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22405,-15,-21,0,'On a Decaying Road','  The decaying road you are traveling along continues to run east and\nwest.  To the south is a range of small hills.  To the north is a barren,\nforeboding, and very nasty looking wasteland.  Beyond it are some mountains.\n',120,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22406,-16,-21,0,'On A Decaying Road','  The decaying road you are traveling along continues to run east and\nwest.  To the south is a range of small hills.  To the north is a barren,\nforeboding, and very nasty looking wasteland.\n',120,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22407,-17,-21,0,'On A Decaying Road','  The decaying road you are traveling along continues to run east and\nwest.  To the south a small path leads into the hills.  To the north is an\nimpassable wasteland, while westward the road continues toward an unbroken\nchain of mountains.\n',120,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22408,-14,-31,0,'Abandoned Storage Cellar','  Once used by the gnomes for an underground storage cellar this cavern\nis now abandoned, or supposedly.  A small smoldering campsite sits at\nthe middle of the room and makeshift device seems to have been\nconstructed to vent its smoke downwards to some tiny underground\ncrevice.  Old rusty gates sit in the north and northeast walls most likely\nleading into individual storage areas.  To the east it appears a gate\nwas replaced with a patched and battered wooden one.  To the west lies a\nsolid iron door.  It appears to be a specially made gnome door, with an\nequivalent security level of vault.\n',130,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,10,96,0,'',NULL),
(22409,-14,-30,0,'Damp Storage Cellar','  Filthy beyond words the little cellar has been cleared of all stores.\nrickety wooden shelves adorn one wall while in the center of the room\nseveral bedrolls have been laid out and recently used.  A rusty iron\ngate sits in the south wall leading back to the main room of the\nunderground storage cellar.\n',130,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22410,-13,-31,0,'Damp Storage Cellar','  The room while fairly dirty is at least somewhat organized.  A pile\nof debris sits in one corner and a bedroll in the other.  A small\ncrude set of wooden shelves has been repaired to a useable state and\nset to one side.  To the west a repaired wooden gate leads back to\nthe main area of the storage cellar.\n',130,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22411,-13,-30,0,'Dry Storage Cellar','  For some strange reason this area of the cellar seems to be dryer then\nthe rest.  The walls have been lined with hanging faded tapestries to\nhelp keep the area warmer.  A bedroll sits near the far side of the room\nwhile a candle and pillow sit to the other side.  A rusty metal gate is\nset into the southwest wall leading back to the main area of the cellar.\n',130,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(22412,-11,-23,-1,'Outcast Sleeping Area','  Little more then a cluttered cavern with a few cleared spots this appears\nto be where the gnome outcasts sleep.  Once smooth walls are now chipped\nand have collected deposits of minerals and dirt making them almost appear\nrough and completely natural.  The cavern continues to the west.\n',146,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22413,-12,-24,-1,'Tiny Cavern','  Concealed behind a secret panel to the north this tiny cavern appears to\nbe used by one of the outcasts as their personal quarters.  A small bed is\nabout the only furnishing still in one piece.  A weak attempt at cleaning\nappears to have been made to this area as most of the clutter has been\npushed into a small pile and the walls at least roughly brushed clean of\nloose dirt and earth.\n',146,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(22414,-17,-22,0,'On A Dirt Path','  You stand on a north-south dirt path that leads from a decaying road to the\nnorth into a range of small hills to the south.  Strange flowers and berries\ncover the hills.  Some of them would even appear to be kept up...  as if they\nwere farmed!\n',120,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22415,-17,-23,0,'A Dirt Path Among Small Hills','  Rather nondescript, grass-covered hills surround you as the path you are\non twists from the north to the east.  Someone appears to have camped here\nrecently by the side of the road.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22416,-16,-23,0,'A T in the Dirt Path','  The dirt path you are on plunges into a valley between two hills,\nclimbing to the east towards the top of a particularly high crest.  The\nhills here are covered with strange blue flowers that fill the air with a\nsoft, sweet scent.  To the south a dark cave mouth smiles at you.  A dirt\npath climbs up the hill to the south.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22417,-15,-23,0,'On the Ledge of a Cliff, atop a High Hill','  The dirt road you are traveling on ends here before a cliff wall.  From\nthis vantage point you are able to survey most of the surrounding terrain.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22418,-16,-24,0,'Inside the Mouth of a Cave','  Every indication would be that this cave gets used quite often.  The\nfloor of the cave is well worn, and various garbage lies strewn about.  The\ntapestries on the wall could be considered another clue that this is not\nsome chance hole-in-the-wall.  Sunlight filters in to the north, while the\ncave slopes downward to the south.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22419,-16,-25,0,'Deep Inside A Cave','  Various ornaments cover the walls, hinting that this may be a place of some\nimportance.  A stairwell stretches into the darkness below.  The strong odor\nseems to float up from below.  Sheesh! To the south, a tunnel twists out of\nsight.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22420,-16,-25,-1,'Foot of a Grand Staircase','  You are in a small room with archways leading towards hallways to the north,\nsouth and west.  A stairwell stretches up the east wall towards the north.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22421,-15,-25,-1,'A Dark, Musty Passage','  This east-west passage smells of exotic fragrances.  The west wall is\ncovered by a large painting.  The floor is made of a dark stone, with an\nexpensive red carpet running from the west wall to the large metal door on\nthe east wall.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22422,-14,-25,-1,'A Nobleman\'s Quarters','  This large and well-kept room would appear to be the quarters of a rich\nnobleman.  The small furniture would suggest the occupant is under 4 feet\ntall.  There is small bed along the east wall of the room, and a door in\nthe west wall.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22423,-15,-26,-1,'A Small Armory','  You stand a small, square room apparently designed as an armory.  A\nnumber of exotic weapons are racked here and ready.  They would probably\ninterest you more if they weren\'t so damn small.  There  is a door in the\nnorth wall.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22424,-16,-27,-1,'Cluttered Room','  With few actual furnishings, the rooms is still quite cluttered.  It\nappears as if someone hastily unpacked several things with no intentions to\nactually stay long.  Various braziers and other magical apparatus sit\naround the room on rickety stands and boxes.  One small bed sits off to the\nside for the rooms inhabitant and a door provides access to other parts of\nthe cavern to the north.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22425,-16,-26,-1,'A Dark, North-south Passage','  This north-south passage ends in a door on the southern wall.  Rich\ntapestries on the other walls depict gnomes doing various activities.\nThe stone about you has been rubbed smooth over the years as many gnomes\napparently have lived in these caverns.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22426,-17,-26,-1,'A Nobleman\'s Quarters','  This large and well-kept room would appear to be the quarters of a rich\nnobleman.  The small furniture would suggest the occupant is under 4 feet\ntall.  There is small bed along the southern wall of the room, and a door\nin the north wall.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22427,-17,-25,-1,'A Dark, Sinister Passage','  This east-west passage ends in a door on the west wall.  There is an\nadditional door on the southern wall as well, but it looks far less\ninteresting.  Tapestries along the walls depict gnomes laboring to build a\nmighty town, and harvesting strange berries.  A pedestal along the north wall\nholds burning incense.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22428,-18,-25,-1,'A Nobleman\'s Quarters','  This large and well-kept room would appear to be the home of a rich\nnobleman.  The small furniture would suggest the occupant is under 4 feet\ntall.  There is small bed along the southern wall of the room, and a door\nin the east wall.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22429,-16,-24,-1,'A Long North-south Hallway','  You stand in a long north-south hallway that is decorated with tapestries\ndepicting great victories by gnome warriors over humans, dwarves, and elves.\nThere are a few simple statues between the tapestries.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22430,-16,-23,-1,'A Large Meeting Hall','  This immense room would appear to be used by the tiny gnomes to hold\nmeetings.  Rows of tables and chairs fill the room, and a large stage\nrests on the north wall with a podium and many bright banners.  On the east\nwall lies a wooden door, while tunnels stretch to the north, south, and\nwest.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22431,-15,-23,-1,'A Dirty Storage Room','  Crates, barrels, and various containers lie strewn about here.  Pieces of\nrotting food and puddles of stale ale indicate that the gnomes give little\nthought to sanitation.  A mural on the east wall depicts the harvesting of\nstrange flowers by gnomes.  In the center of the west wall lies a wooden door.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22432,-14,-23,-1,'A Dead-end Hallway','  You stand in a long hallway stretching from the east to the west.  The\nfloor is covered with dust.  The east end of the hall is decorated with\ndark green paint, while the west end of the hall is painted with red.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22433,-13,-23,-1,'An Abandoned Hall','  You stand at the west end of an incredibly large hall.  Apparently long\nabandoned, the ceiling has collapsed in the center of the hall.  The\nresulting pile of rubble blocks all passage eastward.  The north and south\nwalls are made of solid stone.  The west wall has a strange green door set\ninto it.  Various garbage lies strewn about in the dirt here.  You smell\nrotting flesh nearby.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22434,-12,-23,-1,'Home of the Outcast Gnomes','  You have chanced upon a secret lair that would appear to be home to exiled\ngnomes.  You are able to deduce this from the well-kept up gnome furniture\naround you, along with the various loot these gnomes have been pillaging from\ntheir kinfolk.  A pile of rubble blocks the exit to the west.  A ladder\nleads up into the ceiling above.  You have the feeling you are not wanted\nhere.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22435,-12,-23,0,'Up into a Tree Stump','You exit from a tree stump, but quickly forget which one it is...\n',120,131080,20,1,22401,1,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22436,-16,-22,-1,'The Main Hall','  This red-carpeted hallway runs north to south, lined by murals depicting\nthe royal line of the gnomes fighting fierce battles against elves,\ndwarves, and humans.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22437,-16,-21,-1,'The Main Hall','  This red-carpeted hallway runs north to south, lined by murals depicting\nthe royal line of the gnomes fighting fierce battles against elves,\ndwarves, and humans.  The smell of luxurious perfume wafts in from an\narchway to the north.  Two large stone doors are set into the east and\nwest walls.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22438,-15,-21,-1,'A Guest\'s Suite','  This luxurious room is decorated in lavish colors, with a soft, plush\nbed and a fine cedar desk.  Beautiful plants adorn the walls, kept alive\nby mysterious means.  The floor is covered with a plush rug, and a stone\ndoor leads out to the west.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22439,-15,-20,-1,'The Gnight\'s Quarters','  A tiny, fluffy bed lies in the center of the room, with strange furniture\nalong the walls.  A large mirror in the east wall is lined by a beautiful oak\nframe, reflecting the exotic colors of the wall tapestries.  There is a\nregal-looking door on the south end of the west wall.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22440,-16,-20,-1,'The Gnight\'s Station','  A large desk dominates the room, apparently way too big for the tiny\ngnome body which commands from it.  Nevertheless, the large map behind the\nthrone depicts a tremendous amount of territory that the gnome gnight\noverlooks.  An archway leads to a hall to the south, while a regal looking\ndoor leads to the east.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22441,-17,-20,-1,'The Outpost Treasure Room','  All the riches of the gnomes lie around you.  You are not very impressed.\nThere is a door on the east wall.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22442,-17,-21,-1,'A Guest\'s Suite','  This luxurious room is decorated in lavish colors, with a soft, plush\nbed and a fine cedar desk.  Beautiful plants adorn the walls, kept alive\nby mysterious means.  The floor is covered with a plush rug, and a stone\ndoor leads out to the east.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22443,-18,-21,-1,'A Damp Cell','  This tiny cell reeks of filth and foulness.  Various bones lie strewn\nabout, and a door set with iron bars blocks escape to the south.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22444,-17,-22,-1,'A Dusty Cell','  This tiny cell reeks of filth and foulness.  Various bones lie strewn\nabout, and a door set with iron bars blocks escape to the west.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22445,-19,-22,-1,'A Musty Cell','  This tiny cell reeks of filth and foulness.  Various bones lie strewn\nabout, and a door set with iron bars blocks escape to the east.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22446,-19,-23,-1,'Inside a Cage','  Carved into the rock itself this room has been lined with steel\ngratework, apparently to keep creatures capable of boring through the\nsurrounding earth from burrowing out.  The ironwork is quite sturdy and\nhas a detailed lock set into its only hinged gate to the east.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22447,-18,-24,-1,'The Sergeant\'s Quarters','  The sergeant of the gnome troops commands from this stately room.  In it\nlies his desk and various paperwork, as well as a bed and a few tiny\nchairs.  A door in the north wall leads out.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22448,-18,-23,-1,'The Gnome Barracks','  This huge room houses a small army.  Bunk beds line the walls, with\nfoot-lockers set in front of them.  Everything is kept nice and tidy.  A\nhallway leads north from the north-west corner of the room.  A heavy piece\nof tattered moleskin conceals a gate set in the west wall.  To the south\nlies a door made of iron while to the east wall a large archway supports an\nopening in the stone.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22449,-17,-23,-1,'A Long East-west Hallway','  Running east to west, this hallway allows quick access between two very\nlarge rooms.  Its stone floor and bare walls are fairly drab and boring.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22450,-18,-22,-1,'In a Hall, Beside the Cells','  To the north, east, and west lie tiny cells.  Here a jailer can sit and\nwatch the prisoners slowly die.  How wonderful.  To the south would appear\nto be a large room.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22451,-16,-23,1,'North Face of a Hill','  You are surrounded by the strangest looking flowers and berries you have\never seen.  In all directions stretch hills covered with similar, sweet\nsmelling plants.  A small trail leads down the hill here, as well as to\nthe north.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22452,-16,-24,1,'Top of a Hill','  The scent of the odd but beautiful flowers is overwhelming.  Intermixed\nwith the flowers are short bushes containing multi-colored berries.  From\nthe top of this hill you are able to catch glimpse of a vast forest to the\neast, as well as some farms and a small village to the south.  The view to\nthe west is blocked by an even larger hill.  A small path runs north and\nsouth here, cutting its way through the foliage.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22453,-16,-25,1,'South Face of a Hill','  This is the south face of a rather large hill.  Below you, the path you\nare on turns into a larger road.  To the north, it weaves its way through\nthe multi-hued plant life.  There is a small collapsed shed nearby which\nlooks very ancient.  Beside it is a water pump.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22454,-16,-27,0,'End of a Gravel Road','  The well-maintained gravel road ends here before a small cave to the\nnorth.  An offshoot of the road degrades into a path, leading up the side\nof the north hill.  To the west, a small farmhouse borders the side of the\nroad.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22455,-16,-28,0,'On A Gravel Road','  You are on a north-south running gravel road that seems to be well\nmaintained.  Hills surround you, covered with strange plants.  A small path\noffshoots from the road, heading toward fenced in fields to the east.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22456,-15,-28,0,'On A Dirt Path','  Colorful fields of strange plants surround you to the north and the\nsouth.  The path you are on leads from a small, round farmhouse in the\neast to a road to the west.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22457,-15,-27,0,'In a Hilly Field','  You stand on a hill among rows of strange bushes and plants.  A short\nfence blocks passage to the north and to the west.  The fields extend to\nthe east, and to the south is a dirt path.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22458,-14,-27,0,'In a Hilly Field','  You stand on a hill among rows of strange bushes and plants.  A short\nfence blocks passage to the north.  The fields extend to the east and\nwest.  To the south is the side of a strange, round farmhouse.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22459,-13,-27,0,'In a Hilly Field','  You stand on a hill among rows of strange bushes and plants.  A short\nfence blocks passage to the north and to the east.  The fields extend to\nthe south and to the west.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22460,-13,-28,0,'In a Hilly Field','  You stand on a hill among rows of strange bushes and plants.  A short\nfence blocks your passage to the east while the fields extend to the\nsouth and to the north.  To the west is the back of a small, round\nfarmhouse.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22461,-14,-28,0,'In a Gnome Farmhouse','  This is the humble home of a hill gnome, who labors hard to harvest the\nexotic plants that give him sustenance.  The house is circularly shaped,\nconsists of one room, and is quite simple in terms of decor.  Other than a\nfew basic furniture items, there is nothing of value here.  A door leads\nout to the west.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22462,-14,-32,0,'Hunter\'s Blind','  Nestle into the shadow of a hill to the north this little blind has been\ncleverly created from various bits of brush and earth.  A thin slot has\nbeen left about gnome height high for the occupant to look out onto the\nclosest area of the wooded hills to the south.  The blind continues to the\neast where an exit is most likely located.\n',120,131076,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22463,-13,-32,0,'Entrance to a Hunter\'s Blind','  Nestled into the shadow of a hill to the north this little blind has\nbeen cleverly created from various bits of brush and earth.  The blind\ncontinues to the west where a hunter could sit for hours to observe the\nwooded hills just southwest of here.  A small low opening to the south\nappears to be the only exit to the blind.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22464,-13,-29,0,'In a Hilly Field','  You stand on a hill among rows of strange bushes and plants.  A short\nfence blocks passage to the south and to the east.  The fields extend to\nthe north and to the west.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22465,-14,-29,0,'In a Hilly Field','  You stand on a hill among rows of strange bushes and plants.  A short\nfence blocks passage southward.  To the east and west, the fields\ncontinue.  To the north lies a small, round farmhouse.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22466,-15,-29,0,'In a Hilly Field','  You stand on a hill among rows of strange bushes and plants.  A short\nfence blocks passage to the south and to the west.  To the east, the\nfields continue, while a path lies to the north.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22467,-16,-29,0,'A Twist in a Gravel Road','  The gravel road bends from the north to the west here.  To the south, a\nnarrow dirt path cuts its way through a fenced in field towards a distant\nfarm house atop a hill.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22468,-17,-29,0,'On A Gravel Road','  The gravel road runs east to west here between small hills.  These hills\nare covered with rows of exotic, multi-colored plants.  An odd farmhouse\nlies atop the hill to the north.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22469,-18,-29,0,'A Twist in a Gravel Road','  The gravel road twists from the east to the south here.  Southward, it\nwinds its way up the side of a steep hill.  To the east, it dips between\ntwo small hills.  A small, round farmhouse lies atop the hill to the west.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22470,-18,-30,0,'Atop A Hill On A Gravel Road','  The gravel road continues down the north and south sides of this steep\nhill.  Far to the south, a small village lies tucked between two hills.\nAll around you, colorful hills stretch as far as your eyes can see.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22471,-17,-30,0,'In a Hilly Field','  You stand on a hill among rows of strange bushes and plants.  A short\nfence blocks passage to the north and to the west.  The fields extend to\nthe south and to the east.  To the east you catch glimpse of a small dirt\npath.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22472,-16,-30,0,'On A Dirt Path','  Colorful fields of strange plants surround you to the east and the west.\nThe path you are on leads from a small, round farmhouse in the south to a\nroad to the north.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22473,-15,-30,0,'In a Hilly Field','  You stand on a hill among rows of strange bushes and plants.  A short\nfence blocks passage to the north and to the east.  The fields extend to\nthe south and to the west.  To the west a small dirt path appears to wind\nits way through the crops.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22474,-13,-33,0,'Edge of a some woody hills','  Standing on a muddy embankment a small path can be seen just to the east\nafter which it appears the ground drops suddenly away into a deep ravine.\nA muddy looking river lies just to the south and to the southeast it\nappears a poorly made bridge has been erected over the river.  West of\nhere the hilly landscape is dotted with several trees creating a small\nwoodlands.  To the north a tall mound of vegetation sits, strangely with\nan opening just barely visible at its base.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22475,-13,-34,0,'Muddy Stream','  Created by the water coming from a shallow pond to the southwest the\nstream is directed along a narrower channel at this point.  To the east\nthe river appears to drop over a cliff face into a ravine.  Passage that\nway though is halted by the combination of a shaky looking bridge and\nseveral small dams, some naturally created and others apparently the work\nof some creature or another.  The hilly landscape to the west is dotted\nwith several trees creating a small woodlands.\n',120,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22476,-15,-31,0,'In a Hilly Field','  You stand on a hill among rows of strange bushes and plants.  A short\nfence blocks passage to the east.  The fields extend to the north and to\nthe south.  To the west is the side of a strange farmhouse.  Some\novergrown brush can be seen to the east.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22477,-16,-31,0,'In a Gnome Farmhouse','  This is the humble home of a hill gnome, who labors hard to harvest the\nexotic plants that give him sustenance.  The house is circularly shaped,\nconsists of one room, and is quite simple in terms of decor.  Other than a\nfew basic furniture items, there is nothing of value here.  A door leads\nout to the north.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22478,-17,-31,0,'In a Hilly Field','  You stand on a hill among rows of strange bushes and plants.  A short\nfence blocks passage to the west.  The fields extend to the north and to\nthe south.  To the east is the side of a strange farmhouse.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22479,-18,-31,0,'On A Gravel Road','  You are standing on a north-south running gravel road.  To the north,\nthe road ascends a steep hill.  To the south, it continues to snake\nbetween hills towards a small village.  To the west is a tiny campsite.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22480,-19,-31,0,'Beside A Tiny Campsite','  Dug into the side of a side of the hill to the west, this campsite\noffers protection from the elements.  To the east lies a gravel road which\ndescends southward.  A small campfire still flickers here, providing some\nwarmth.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22481,-18,-32,0,'On A Gravel Road','  Descending down a valley between two hills, this road would appear to head\ntowards a small village to the south.  To the north, it ascends a steep hill.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22482,-18,-33,0,'On A Gravel Road','  This north-south road descends to a small village to the south.  To the\nnorth it cuts its way upwards, through the valley while some forested\nhills lies to the east.  To the west dense forest and hills block all\npassage.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22483,-18,-34,0,'Outside the Gates of a Gnome Village','  The unmistakable architecture of the gnomes makes the tiny town to the\nsouth incredibly beautiful to behold.  Nestled in a valley, the village\'s\nsolid colors sharply contrast the multi-hued chaos of the exotic plants\ndotting the surrounding country-side.  To the north a gravel road ascends\nout of the valley while to the east lies some forested hills.  To the\nsouth lie the gates of the village and to the west thick forests and hills\nblock all passage.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22484,-17,-32,0,'In a Hilly Field','  You stand on a hill among rows of strange bushes and plants.  A short\nfence blocks passage to the south and west.  The fields extend northward\nand eastward.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22485,-16,-32,0,'In a Hilly Field','  You stand on a hill among rows of strange bushes and plants.  A short\nfence to the south has apparently been broken through by force.  Near the\nbreach in the fence, the bushes and plants have been cut down and\ntrampled.  The fields extend to the east and to the west.  To the north is\nthe back of a small, round farmhouse.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22486,-15,-32,0,'In a Hilly Field','  You stand on a hill among rows of strange bushes and plants.  A short\nfence blocks passage to the south and to the east.  The fields extend\nnorthward and westward.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22487,-17,-33,0,'Tree Covered Hills','  Giving evidence to rich soil below several tall trees and lush\nvegetation dot the landscape about you.  The various forest sounds can all\nbe heard, but the majority of their owners seem to prefer the concealment\nof the surrounding forest over an encounter with a stranger.  Tall\ngrasses, leaves, twigs and other decaying matter cover the earth below you\nand quickly mask the passage of any creatures.  The wooded hills continue\nto the south and east while a road of some sort is just visible to the\nsouth and west.  To the north a short fence blocks your passage.\n',120,131076,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22488,-16,-33,0,'Tree Covered Hills','  Giving evidence to rich soil below several tall trees and lush\nvegetation dot the landscape about you.  The various forest sounds can all\nbe heard, but the majority of their owners seem to prefer the concealment\nof the surrounding forest over an encounter with a stranger.  Tall\ngrasses, leaves, twigs and other decaying matter cover the earth below you\nand quickly mask the passage of any creatures.  The forested hills\ncontinue to the west, east and south.  A short fence to the north would\nappear to normally block your passage, but someone or something has\nbroken through it leaving a gap.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22489,-15,-33,0,'Tree Covered Hills','  Giving evidence to rich soil below several tall trees and lush\nvegetation dot the landscape about you.  The various forest sounds can all\nbe heard, but the majority of their owners seem to prefer the concealment\nof the surrounding forest over an encounter with a stranger.  Tall\ngrasses, leaves, twigs and other decaying matter cover the earth below you\nand quickly mask the passage of any creatures.  The forested hills\ncontinue to the east, west and south, but a short fence blocks your\npassage north.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22490,-14,-33,0,'Tree Covered Hills','  Giving evidence to rich soil below several tall trees and lush\nvegetation dot the landscape about you.  The various forest sounds can all\nbe heard, but the majority of their owners seem to prefer the concealment\nof the surrounding forest over an encounter with a stranger.  Tall\ngrasses, leaves, twigs and other decaying matter cover the earth below you\nand quickly mask the passage of any creatures.  The forested hills\ncontinue to the south and west while the forest edge appears to be just to\nthe east.  North of here a huge mound of vegetation blocks your passage.\nTo the southeast you can just make out a muddy looking stream.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22491,-17,-34,0,'Tree Covered Hills','  Giving evidence to rich soil below several tall trees and lush\nvegetation dot the landscape about you.  The various forest sounds can all\nbe heard, but the majority of their owners seem to prefer the concealment\nof the surrounding forest over an encounter with a stranger.  Tall\ngrasses, leaves, twigs and other decaying matter cover the earth below you\nand quickly mask the passage of any creatures.  The forested hills\ncontinue to the east and north, while a road of some sorts is just visible\nto the west and north.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22492,-16,-34,0,'Tree Covered Hills','  Giving evidence to rich soil below several tall trees and lush\nvegetation dot the landscape about you.  The various forest sounds can all\nbe heard, but the majority of their owners seem to prefer the concealment\nof the surrounding forest over an encounter with a stranger.  Tall\ngrasses, leaves, twigs and other decaying matter cover the earth below you\nand quickly mask the passage of any creatures.  The forested hills\ncontinue to the east, west and north.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22493,-15,-34,0,'Tree Covered Hills','  Giving evidence to rich soil below several tall trees and lush\nvegetation dot the landscape about you.  The various forest sounds can all\nbe heard, but the majority of their owners seem to prefer the concealment\nof the surrounding forest over an encounter with a stranger.  Tall\ngrasses, leaves, twigs and other decaying matter cover the earth below you\nand quickly mask the passage of any creatures.  The forested hills\ncontinue to the east, west and north.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22494,-14,-34,0,'Tree Covered Hills','  Giving evidence to rich soil below several tall trees and lush\nvegetation dot the landscape about you.  The various forest sounds can all\nbe heard, but the majority of their owners seem to prefer the concealment\nof the surrounding forest over an encounter with a stranger.  Tall\ngrasses, leaves, twigs and other decaying matter cover the earth below you\nand quickly mask the passage of any creatures.  The forested hills\ncontinue to the north and west.  A muddy stream is just visible to the\neast and the edge of the forested area can be seen shortly to the\nnortheast.\n',120,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22495,-17,-27,0,'In a Gnome Farmhouse','  This is the humble home of a hill gnome, who labors hard to harvest the\nexotic plants that give him sustenance.  The house is circularly shaped,\nconsists of one room, and is quite simple in terms of decor.  Other than a\nfew basic furniture items, there is nothing of value here.  A door leads\nout to the east.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22496,-19,-29,0,'In a Gnome Farmhouse','  This is the humble home of a hill gnome, who labors hard to harvest the\nexotic plants that give him sustenance.  The house is circularly shaped,\nconsists of one room, and is quite simple in terms of decor.  Other than a\nfew basic furniture items, there is nothing of value here.  A door leads\nout to the east.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22497,-17,-28,0,'In a Gnome Farmhouse','  This is the humble home of a hill gnome, who labors hard to harvest the\nexotic plants that give him sustenance.  The house is circularly shaped,\nconsists of one room, and is quite simple in terms of decor.  Other than a\nfew basic furniture items, there is nothing of value here.  A door leads\nout to the south.\n',120,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22500,-13,-37,-1,'Steep, Downward-sloping Tunnel','  The tunnel around here glows with a life of its own and the moss\ncovering it gives a strong forbidding aura to it.  The walls look more\nsolid upwards yet more slippery.  Strong stenches of decay are seeping\nupwards from below, and the air below is very humid.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22501,-13,-37,-2,'Steep, Downward-sloping Tunnel','  The tunnel is covered with glowing moss that makes it hard to get a\nfirm hold on the sides.  It slides down steeply making it even harder to\nclimb both ways.  The walls of the tunnel are changing from rocky walls\nabove to dirt walls below, though it is hard to tell with all the moss\ncovering the walls of the passage.  You can see a twisting wide passage\nto the north.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22502,-13,-37,-3,'Steep, Downward-sloping Tunnel','  The tunnel is covered with glowing moss that makes it hard to get a\nfirm hold on the sides.  It slides down steeply making it even harder to\nclimb.  You can see a freshly dug passage to the south.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22503,-13,-37,-4,'Steep, Downward-sloping Tunnel','  The tunnel is covered with glowing moss that makes it hard to get a\nfirm hold on the sides.  It slides down steeply making it even harder to\nclimb.  There is a narrow ancient hallway to the east.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22504,-13,-37,-5,'A Sharp Turn in the Tunnel','  The tunnel makes a sharp turn around here.  The glowing moss covering\nthe walls seem to be more concentrated in this area.  The walls are rocky\nand natural unlike the rest of the tunnel above.  The air in here is\nchilly, soothing and cool.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22505,-9,-45,-3,'In a Vertical Tunnel of Dirt','  The tunnel runs straight down with no place to hold on to for support or\nclimbing.  Below, you can see a large shrine covered with blood.  The tunnel\nlooks like it has been made on purpose to kill someone by throwing them on\nthe shrine below.\n',123,131080,34,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22506,-13,-36,-2,'A Wide, Twisting Tunnel','  The passage is large and dirty.  Only the upper walls are covered with\nthe strange glowing moss.  The air in here is humid and warm, the stench\nin here can drive a man insane and it grows stronger to the north.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22507,-13,-35,-2,'A Wide, Twisting Tunnel','  The passage is large and dirty.  Only the upper walls are covered with\nthe strange glowing moss.  The air in here is humid and warm, the stench\nin here can drive a man insane and it grows stronger to the north.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22508,-13,-34,-2,'An Intersection in the Tunnel','  Here the passages come to an intersection.  To the east the tunnel\nis wide and twisting.  To the west the tunnel is narrow.  Several\nfragments, of what seems to be thick bones, litter the area.  The stench\nis hard to tolerate and the ceiling is still covered with glowing moss.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22509,-12,-34,-2,'A Wide, Twisting Tunnel','  The tunnel is wide enough for five ogres to pass together comfortably.\nIt\'s dirty and littered with bones, some are even new and fresh.  There is\nglowing moss all over the ceiling, adding to the room a dark aura with its\npale light.  The tunnel is obviously well used.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22510,-12,-33,-2,'A Wide, Twisting Tunnel','  The tunnel is wide enough for five ogres to pass together comfortably.\nIt\'s dirty and littered with bones, some are even new and fresh.  There is\nglowing moss all over the ceiling, adding to the room a dark aura with its\npale light.  The tunnel is obviously well used.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22511,-11,-33,-2,'A Wide, Freshly Dug Tunnel','  The passage here is very wide and new, and clean relative to the other\nsmelly and dirty passages around here.  Even the glowing moss is piled on\ntop in an organized fashion of their own.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22512,-11,-34,-2,'A Wide, Freshly Dug Tunnel','  The passage here is very wide and new, and clean relative to the other\nsmelly and dirty passages around here.  Even the glowing moss is piled on\ntop in an organized fashion of their own.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22513,-10,-34,-2,'A Twist in a Freshly Dug Tunnel','  The passage here is very wide and new, and clean relative to the other\nsmelly and dirty passages around here.  The tunnel twists to a corner here\nwithout losing any of its organized and relatively clean fashion.  There\nare several piles of bones and rotten torn flesh in the corner, shadowed\nby the pale light of the moss.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22514,-10,-33,-2,'A Wide, Freshly Dug Tunnel','  The wide tunnel is slowly narrowing down to the north.  The glowing\nmoss is also decreasing to the north and giving the northern passage\ndark shadows.  The stench seems on the rise again to the north and the\nsweat and water in the air are making the tunnel very damp and warm.  To\nthe south, the tunnel looks fresh and wide.  There is a narrow tunnel to\nthe east of here that gives off a stench similar to the northern tunnel.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22515,-10,-32,-2,'A Narrow, Freshly Dug Tunnel','  The tunnel here, though narrow, splits into many directions.  The\nglowing moss is piled up together around the ceiling in small piles.  The\nstrong odor of rotting bones and flesh cloud the air in the passage and\nseems to be stronger to the west.  There are several blood traces on the\nfloor.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(22516,-10,-31,-2,'A Narrow, Freshly Dug Tunnel','  The passage here is unbelievably smelly and nauseating.  Several rotten\ncarcasses litter the way and there are traces of blood leading to the north\nand east.  The moss on the ceiling here is slightly glowing a red hue\nalong with its pale blue light.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(22517,-11,-31,-2,'A Narrow, Freshly Dug Tunnel','  The tunnel here is full of smelly odor and rotten stench of decay.\nSeveral bones and rotten torn limbs litter the way .  The glowing moss on\nthe ceiling is casting a dreadful red hue along with its pale blue light,\nadding a haunting look to the scene.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(22518,-12,-31,-2,'A Narrow, Freshly Dug Tunnel','  The stench of blood and rotten flesh linger in the air of the tunnel.\nSeveral blood stains and traces are scattered around.  The glowing moss\non the ceiling is casting a blood red hue along with its pale blue light.\nThe passages branches north and south here.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(22519,-13,-31,-2,'A Narrow, Freshly Dug Tunnel','  Many little piles of rotten flesh are littering the room here, causing a\nstrong stench of decay in the air.  The piles of glowing moss covering the\nceiling have extended slightly downwards along the walls towards the\nrotting blood and flesh.  The walls of the passage look relatively new\nwith respect to the rest of the tunnels.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(22520,-13,-32,-2,'A Narrow, Freshly Dug Tunnel','  The tunnel is wider to the north and narrow to the south.  Several piles\nof glowing moss are scattered across the ceiling.  There is a sick stench\nof decay coming from the northern passage.  The walls to the north look\nrelatively new.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(22521,-13,-33,-2,'A Narrow, Freshly Dug Tunnel','  The tunnel is getting wider to the north.  The glowing moss covering\nthe ceiling has stretched over the walls and is casting a dull green\nlight in this passage.  The tunnel floor is more used to the north and\nhas supported activities by something heavy.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(22522,-14,-33,-2,'A Narrow, Freshly Dug Tunnel','  The tunnels bend here at a right angle.  There is a small branch going\ndownwards from the bend.  The smell of stinking sweat and repulsive odor\nis diffusing from that branch.  The tunnels of the south are narrower\nthan the ones to the east.  There are several piles of green glowing moss\nscattered on the ceiling.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(22523,-14,-34,-2,'A Narrow, Freshly Dug Tunnel','  The tunnels here are new, narrow and freshly dug with some recent\nattempts to widen them.  They are lightly lit by the green glowing moss\nscattered on the ceiling.  There are marks of heavy activities on the\nfloor.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(22524,-9,-33,-2,'A Cave Home','  Littered with various refuse, this small cave would appear to function as\nsomeone\'s living quarters.  There is an incredibly foul stench here, emanating\nfrom a pile of excrement in the corner.  A tunnel leads out to the west.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22525,-11,-32,-2,'A Cave Home','  Piles of bones are highlighted by freshly-torn flesh.  Various excrement\nlies in a heap in the center of the room.  It seems hard to believe that\nsomeone lives here, but you are quite certain that someone, or something,\ndoes.  A tunnel leaves this cave to the east.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22526,-9,-31,-2,'A Cave Home','  It seems obvious that someone lives here.  Or perhaps, something.  Here and\nthere lie bites of torn flesh, and a pile of excrement lies in the corner.  The\nstench is overwhelming.  The cave is rather small, and a tunnel leads out to\nthe west.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22527,-10,-30,-2,'A Cave Home','  Apparently, someone likes living here.  That seems hard to believe as this\nsmall cave is littered with various debris.  Signs of bedding, or what seems\nto be an attempt to make a bed are still visible, although hard to see under\nthe various, freshly severed body parts which litter this abode.  A tunnel\nleads southwards out of the cave.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22528,-12,-30,-2,'A Cave Home','  Apparently the inhabitants of this cave love gnomes.  You can tell that\nby the numerous gnome heads lying in various states of decay throughout the\nroom.  There are several fresh dwarven heads scattered on top of those of\nthe gnomes.  A tunnel leads out of the cave to the south.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22529,-14,-31,-2,'A Cave Home','  This cave home is terrifying.  The room is full of torn limbs and flesh.\nBlood of the bodies has been smeared all over the walls of the cave.  The\nskulls have been laid in the corner in pyramid like piles.  The glowing moss\nhas crept along the ceiling from the outside and is now covering a major\npart of the ceiling in here.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22530,-12,-32,-2,'A Cave Home','  Unlike the other cave homes around this area, this cave home is relatively\nclean.  Although it does have the stinking sweat stench and the various torn\nlimbs, but its not as badly littered as the rest of the cave homes.  There is\na small inscription on the wall.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22531,-13,-38,-3,'A Wide, Freshly Dug Tunnel','  The tunnel goes on to the north and south.  The floor shows signs of\nheavy traffic passing through here.  Signs of struggle are visible on the\nwalls.  The glowing moss is lightly covering the passage ceiling and is\nshining with a pale haunting green light.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22532,-13,-39,-3,'A Wide, Freshly Dug Tunnel','  The tunnel goes on to the east and north.  The floor shows signs of\nheavy traffic passing through here.  Signs of struggle are visible on the\nwalls.  The glowing moss is lightly covering the passage ceiling and is\nshining with a pale haunting green light.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22533,-12,-39,-3,'A Narrow Passage through the Rock','  The passage stretches down to the east through solid rock.  The tunnel\nis obviously not completed yet but it\'s clear too that no work has been\ndone on it in quit a while.  The passage is very narrow here.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(22534,-11,-39,-3,'A Narrow Passage Through the Rock','  The passage stretches down to the east through solid rock.  The tunnel\nis obviously not completed yet but it\'s clear too that no work has been\ndone on it in quit a while.  The passage is very narrow here.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(22535,-10,-39,-3,'A Wide Passage Through the Rock','The passage stretches down to the east through solid rock.  The tunnel\nis obviously not yet completed but it\'s clear too that no work has been\ndone on it in quite a while.  The passage is very narrow here.\n',0,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(22536,-9,-39,-3,'At a Dead End','  The tunnel stops here at a dead end.  The glowing moss covering the\nwhole passage has intensely gathered around the rock walls in the end.\nThere is a small patch of stone on the ceiling that doesn\'t seem to have\nthe moss as heavily concentrated around it.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(22537,-9,-39,-2,'A Run-down Room','  The tunnel is lightly inclined to the south from here.  Several rocks\nlie here at the bottom obscuring the entrance from below.  The passage is\nvery clean with solid walls.  There are some traces of <r>blood<1> here.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22538,-9,-40,-2,'A Tunnel of Smooth Dirt Walls','  The tunnel continues south at a slow inclination and to the north at a\nlight decline.  Decorations of crude runes line the walls, many of them\nare very grotesque and ugly.  A stinking smell of sweat is drifting in\nfrom the passage to the west.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22539,-10,-40,-2,'A Guard Post','  The stench of sweat and alcohol in this room is nauseating.  The walls\nhave some decorative weapons hanged on them, many of which are whips and\nflails.  The room is simple and plain looking.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22540,-9,-41,-2,'A Tunnel of Smooth Dirt Walls','  The tunnel continues south at a slow inclination rate and northwards at\na light decline.  Decorations of crude runes line the walls, many of them\nare very grotesque and ugly.  A stinking smell of sweat is drifting in from\nthe passage to the east.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22541,-8,-41,-2,'A Guard Post','  The stench of sweat and alcohol in this room is nauseating.  The walls\nhave some decorative weapons hanged on them, many of which are whips and\nflails.  The room is simple and plain looking.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22542,-9,-42,-2,'A Tunnel of Smooth Dirt Walls','  The tunnel to the south is slowly inclining, while the northern passage\nis lightly declining.  Decorations of crude runes line the walls, many of\nthem are very grotesque and ugly.  A stinking smell of sweat is drifting in\nfrom the passage to the west.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22543,-10,-42,-2,'A Guard Post','  The stench of sweat and alcohol in this room is nauseating.  The walls\nhave some decorating weapons hanged on them, many which are whips and\nflails.  The room is simple and plain looking.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22544,-9,-43,-2,'A Narrow Hallway','  The passage seems to become a bit narrow to the south and has stopped\nits inclination, but continues declining lightly to the north.  You can\nhear some sounds of activity from the south.  Several sets of tracks are\nclear on the floor here.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(22545,-9,-44,-2,'At the End of a Narrow Hallway','  The hallway to the north ends here.  There is a large door to the south\nwith a crooked sign on it.  The floor here has several large blood stains\ntracing to the doorway.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22546,-9,-45,-2,'Slaves and Prisoners\' Chambers','  The sight of this room is really terrifying.  Blood is smeared all over\nthe walls and torn rotten limbs lie all around the place.  The prisoners\nand slaves must have been stored here like food.  The stench of decay is\nso strong it\'s making it hard to breath the humid air in here.  There is a\ndoor to the north of here.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22547,-10,-45,-2,'Slaves and Prisoners\' Chambers','  The sight of this room is really terrifying.  Blood is smeared all over\nthe walls and torn rotten limbs lie all around the place.  The prisoners\nand slaves must have been stored here like food.  The stench of decay is\nso strong it\'s making it hard to breath the humid air in here.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22548,-10,-46,-2,'Slaves and Prisoners\' Chambers','  The sight of this room is really terrifying.  Blood is smeared all over\nthe walls and torn rotten limbs lie all around the place.  The prisoners\nand slaves must have been stored here like food.  The stench of decay is\nso strong it\'s making it hard to breath the humid air in here.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22549,-10,-47,-2,'Slaves and Prisoners\' Chambers','  The sight of this room is really terrifying.  Blood is smeared all over\nthe walls and torn rotten limbs lie all around the place.  The prisoners\nand slaves must have been stored here like food.  The stench of decay is\nso strong it\'s making it hard to breath the humid air in here.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22550,-9,-46,-2,'Slaves and Prisoners\' Chambers','  The sight of this room is really terrifying.  Blood is smeared all over\nthe walls and torn rotten limbs lie all around the place.  The prisoners\nand slaves must have been stored here like food.  There is a grand\ntapestry hung on the south wall, showing several crude pictures on it.\nThe stench of decay is very strong here but it seems to be a bit stronger\nto the north.  It\'s hard to tell but there is some faint moaning coming\nfrom behind the northern wall.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22551,-8,-47,-2,'Slaves and Prisoners\' Chambers','  The sight of this room is really terrifying.  Blood is smeared all over\nthe walls and torn limbs lie all around the place.  The prisoners and\nslaves must have been stored here like food.  The stench of decay is so\nstrong it\'s making it hard to breath the humid air in here.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22552,-8,-46,-2,'Slaves and Prisoners\' Chambers','  The sight of this room is really terrifying.  Blood is smeared all over\nthe walls and torn rotten limbs lie all around the place.  The prisoners\nand slaves must have been stored here like food.  The stench of decay\nis so strong it\'s making it hard to breath the humid air in here.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22553,-8,-45,-2,'Slaves and Prisoners\' Chambers','  The sight of this room is really terrifying.  Blood is smeared all over\nthe walls and torn rotten limbs lie all around the place.  The prisoners\nand slaves must have been stored here like food.  The stench of decay is\nso strong it\'s making it hard to breath the humid air in here.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22554,-9,-45,-2,'Torture Room','  This room has a chilling aura hanging in the air inside it.  There are\nchains and head crushers fixed through out the walls.  The chains seem\nalive with their own hypnotic energy.  Some corpses are still tied up in\nthem.  A few of the head crushers are oozing red blood from the crushed\nheads left inside them.  In the corner, there is a small altar with a\npool of blood at its base.  It\'s obvious that it has been used to torment\nmany of the prisoners.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22555,-9,-47,-2,'Behind a Secret Passage','  The walls have a very smooth surface here, although the passage is a bit\ndusty and obviously not used that much.  There is a tunnel going down that\nis just old as the room here.  Several faint groans can be heard here from\nthe north behind the tapestry.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22556,-12,-37,-4,'A Narrow Passage though the Rock','  The tunnel runs west to the main cave passage and east through a narrow\nsplit in the solid rock.  The dust and spider webs indicate that its very\nold, although none of the dust and webs seem to be close to the strange\nglowing moss that is covering the top in large piles.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(22557,-11,-37,-4,'A Narrow Passage through the Rock','  The tunnel runs west to the main cave passage and east through a narrow\nsplit in the solid rock.  The dust and spider webs indicate that it\'s very\nold, although none of the dust and webs seem to be close to the strange\nglowing moss that is covering the top in large piles.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(22558,-10,-37,-4,'A Narrow Passage through the Rock','  The tunnel runs west to the main cave passage and east through a narrow\nsplit in the solid rock.  The dust and spider webs indicate that it\'s very\nold, although none of the dust and webs seem to be close to the strange\nglowing moss that is covering the top in large piles.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(22559,-9,-37,-4,'A Turn in the Narrow Tunnel','  The tunnel bends here sharply without affecting the concentration of the\nglowing moss on the ceiling.  The tunnels to the south look ancient, old and\nhaving been dug centuries ago, although they do look wider than the tunnels to\nthe west.  The air seems to be warmer to the south.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(22560,-9,-38,-4,'An Ancient Tunnel of Dirt Walls','  The walls of this tunnel are old and ancient.  Although they are well\nused by someone and are naturally established from volcanic activities of\nthe surface, they are not solid rock and are in fact dirt walls.  The air\nto the south seems to be warmer than the air of the northern tunnel.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22561,-9,-39,-4,'An Ancient Tunnel of Dirt Walls','  The walls of this tunnel are old and ancient.  Although they are well\nused by someone and naturally established from volcanic activities of the\nsurface, they are not solid rock and are in fact dirt walls.  The air to\nthe south seems to be warmer than the air in the northern tunnel.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22562,-9,-40,-4,'An Ancient Tunnel of Dirt Walls','  The walls of this tunnel are old and ancient.  Although they are well\nused by someone and are naturally established from volcanic activities of\nthe surface, they are not solid rock and are in fact dirt walls.  The air to\nthe south seems to be warmer than the air in the northern tunnel.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22563,-9,-41,-4,'An Intersection in the Ancient Tunnel','  Several ancient tunnels intersect here.  The southern passage walls are\nsolid rock, unlike the other passages of the intersection.  To the west and\neast, there are several carved runes along the walls.  Some of the runes\nare covered with blood.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22564,-10,-41,-4,'A Narrow Hallway','  The tunnel branches from the intersection to the east.  The walls are\npretty close together and bend to form a passage to the south.  They are\ncovered with crude runes that are painted with blood.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(22565,-10,-42,-4,'A Beautiful Alcove','  The passage ends here at a small beautiful shrine.  The glowing moss of\nthe ceiling has covered all the walls at the dead end and the floor next\nto them.  The pale green hue emitted by them is radiating the room.\nDespite the runed walls to the north, there is an aura of holiness in\nthe room along with haunting sensation in the area.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22566,-8,-41,-4,'A Narrow Hallway','  The tunnel branches from the intersection to the west.  The walls are\npretty close together and bend to form a passage to the south.  They are\ncovered with crude runes that are painted in blood.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(22567,-8,-42,-4,'A Beautiful Alcove','  The passage ends here at a small beautiful shrine.  The glowing moss of\nthe ceiling has covered all the walls at the dead end and the floor next\nto them.  The pale green hue emitted by the moss is radiating the room.\nDespite the runed walls to the north, there is an aura of divine holiness\nin the room along with the haunting sensation in the area.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22568,-9,-42,-4,'Before the Massive Gates','  Before you are massive gates set with strong hands in solid rock.  The\nglowing moss has gathered around its doors making it look like a fearsome\nwarrior ready for the kill.  Dark sensations of death are flowing from\nbeyond the gates.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22569,-9,-43,-4,'In an Ancient Hallway','  Before you the tunnel is spot clean, without a single speck of dust to be\nseen.  To the north, the massive gates tower in the solid rock walls with\nseveral steel hinges holding it tight.  The air in here is very still and\nwarm, yet the it seems to be getting warmer to the south.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22570,-9,-44,-4,'Inside a Grand Hall','  The tunnels intersect here in a gigantic domed cavern.  You can tell\nthis is a place where many gather and meet.  There is a stalactite in the\ncenter of the hall cut and made flat for someone to stand upon.  Several\nviolet and red tapestries decorate the walls of this huge cavern.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22571,-8,-44,-4,'Guard Barracks','  This room has been built in support of the grand hall to the west.\nSeveral guard backup posts are made here in case of trouble in the grand\nhall.  There are some weapons decorating the walls, though most of them are\nthe brutish club and axe type.  To the north there is an old passage.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22572,-8,-43,-4,'An Old Room','  The room here is very old and full of dust.  There are spider webs on the\nceiling that are carefully avoiding the glowing moss on top.  The room is\nobviously used for storage only.  There are several shelves on the walls\ncarved from the rock itself.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22573,-10,-44,-4,'Guard Barracks','  This room has been built in support of the grand hall to the east.\nSeveral guard backup posts are made here in case of trouble in the grand\nhall.  There  are some weapons decorating the walls, though most of them\nare the brutish club and axe type.  To the north there is an old passage.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22574,-10,-43,-4,'An Old Room','  The room here is very old and full of dust.  There are spider webs on the\nceiling that are carefully avoiding the glowing moss on top.  The room is\nobviously used for storage only.  There are several shelves on the walls\ncarved from the rock itself.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22575,-9,-45,-4,'Before a Massive Altar','  The heat in this room is very intense.  Warm, dark waves of power flow\nfrom the giant, blood covered altar in the center of the room.  Many unholy\nsymbols and prayers are crudely carved on the ivory surface of the altar.\nPools of dried juices of life lie around the feet of the grand altar.\nSeveral magnificent tapestries adorn the eastern and western walls giving\nthe chamber an evil feeling.  At the top, the glowing moss has covered the\nwhole ceiling except for a large hole in its center above the altar.  The\npale blue light from the moss shining over the pools of blood is making\nthe scene more and more terrifying.  To the south, there is a small tunnel.\n',123,131080,35,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22576,-9,-46,-4,'End of the Ancient Halls','  The ancient halls end here.  The glowing moss covering the ceiling is\nshedding a faint, dull green hue on the room.  The piles are scattered\neverywhere except on the southern wall, where they are only lightly spread.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22577,-8,-45,-4,'A Large Cave Home','  It appears to be that this place is home to someone of importance in\nthese caves.  The floor and walls are clean with respect to the rest of the\ntunnels and the corners don\'t look too dusty.  There is a passage here\nleading south.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22578,-8,-46,-4,'A Large Cave Home','  It appears to be that this place is home to someone of importance in\nthese caves.  The floor and walls are clean, with respect to the rest of\nthe tunnels, and the corners don\'t look too dusty.  There is a passage\nhere leading east.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22579,-7,-46,-4,'A Large Cave Home','  It appears to be that this place is home to someone of importance in\nthese caves.  The floor and walls are clean, with respect to the rest of\nthe tunnels, and the corners don\'t look too dusty.  There is a private\nlooking door to the east.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22580,-6,-46,-4,'A Dirty Bedroom','  This can easily be the ugliest room you have ever been in.  The owners\nmust really like their privacy and are aggressive about it.  The room might\nhave been cleaned once in the last decade.  There is a large bed of straw\nin the corner where the owners enjoy themselves.  The stinking odor of urine\nis being emitted from an opposite corner along with the pungent smell of\nsweat.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22581,-10,-45,-4,'A Bend in a Tunnel','  A passage of solid stone extends from the tapestries to the east.  The\npassage is clean, although the air in it is very smelly.  The tunnel bends\naround a corner to the south.  The passage looks like it\'s leading to\nsomeone or someplace important.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22582,-10,-46,-4,'A Great Cavern','  You are before a large wide room.  Several meetings have been held here\nby the looks of the place.  The smell of sweat still lingers in the air\nhere, and the odor of rotten flesh lies about everything in this room.\nThere is a long hallway to the west.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(22583,-11,-46,-4,'A Long Hallway','  The hallway extends from the eastern great cavern of meetings and stops\nat some private door at the west.  The door looks important, in its own\nclumsy way.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22584,-12,-46,-4,'A Ghastly Throne Room','  The sight of this room can make a lady of high born faint in one look.\nDreadful heads of various races at different states of decay adorn the walls\nof this room as trophies to the mighty troll chief.  Near the center of the\neastern wall, a pyramid of skulls lie piled together, acting like a throne\nto the gruesome ruler.  The smell of rotten flesh is intense in the air and\nis even clouding the stinking odor of swear.  Some signs of attempts to\nclean the blood of victims off the floor are apparent, too bad they all\nobviously failed.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22585,-9,-47,-4,'A Large Domed Room','  This room is large and shaped in a conical form.  There are some steps\nleading upwards, but they look like they haven\'t been used in quite a while.\nThere are piles of dust on the east and western walls that haven\'t been\ntouched in centuries, which are a great contrast to the rest of the cavern\nwhich seems to have been used a lot recently.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(22586,-9,-47,-3,'Above an Ancient Sunken Structure','  The ancient stairs are strong and sturdy in spite of their age.  The\nstairs going down are leading to a vast dome shaped chamber.  Looking at\nthe floor from above, there is a pattern of a circle on the floor in the\nchamber below.  Faint light beams are coming from above.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22587,-14,-37,-5,'A Damp, East-west Tunnel','  The passage is old and ancient compared to the tunnels of the main\nentrance.  The strange glowing moss is thriving greatly from the weird\ndampness in the air.  It has covered the walls, ceiling and even the floor\nentirely.  The tunnels go straight east and west with no bending along\nthem.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22588,-15,-37,-5,'A Damp, East-west Tunnel','  The passage is old and ancient compared to the tunnels of the main\nentrance.  The strange glowing moss is thriving greatly from the weird\ndampness in the air.  It has covered the walls, ceiling and even the floor\nentirely.  The tunnels go straight east and downwards to the west.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22589,-15,-37,-6,'A Damp, East-west Tunnel','  The passage is old an ancient compared to the tunnels of the main\nentrance.  The strange glowing moss is thriving greatly from the weird\ndampness in the air.  It has covered the walls, ceiling and even the floor\nentirely.  The tunnels go straight west and upwards to the east.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22590,-16,-37,-6,'A Damp, East-west Tunnel','  The passage is old and ancient compared to the tunnels of the main\nentrance.  The strange glowing moss is thriving greatly from the weird\ndampness in the air.  It has covered the walls, ceiling and even the floor\nentirely.  The tunnels go straight west and east with no bending along.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22591,-17,-37,-6,'A Damp, East-west Tunnel','  The passage is old and ancient compared to the tunnels of the main\nentrance.  The strange glowing moss is thriving greatly from the weird\ndampness in the air.  It has covered the walls, ceiling and even the floor\nentirely.  The tunnels go straight east and downwards to the west.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22592,-17,-37,-7,'A Damp, East-west Tunnel','  The passage is old and ancient compared to the tunnels of the main\nentrance.  The strange glowing moss is thriving greatly from the weird\ndampness in the air.  It has covered the walls, ceiling and even the floor\nentirely.  The tunnels go straight west and upwards to the east.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(22593,-18,-37,-7,'A Damp, East-west Tunnel','  The passage is old and ancient compared to the tunnels of the main\nentrance.  The strange glowing moss is thriving greatly from the weird\ndampness in the air.  It has covered the walls, ceiling and even the floor\nentirely.  The tunnels go straight west and east with no bending along.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(22594,-19,-37,-7,'A Damp, East-west Tunnel','  The passage is old and ancient compared to the tunnels of the main\nentrance.  The strange glowing moss is thriving greatly from the weird\ndampness in the air.  It has covered the walls, ceiling and even the floor\nentirely.  The tunnels go straight east and downwards to the west.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22595,0,0,0,'A Damp, East-west Tunnel','The passage is old and ancient compared to the tunnels of the main entrance. \nThe strange glowing moss is thriving greatly from the weird dampness in the air.\nIt has covered the walls, ceiling and even the floor entirely.  The tunnels go\nstraight west and upwards to the east and to the south you see a large gate.\n',0,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22596,-20,-37,-8,'A Damp East-west Tunnel','  The passage is old and ancient compared to the tunnels of the main\nentrance.  The strange glowing moss is thriving greatly from the weird\ndampness in the air.  It has covered the walls, ceiling and even the floor\nentirely.  The tunnels go straight west and east with no bending along.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22597,-21,-37,-8,'A Cavern Beside a Dark Pool','  Before you is a large, dark underground pool.  The pool seems to be\nproviding all the water and dampness that the glowing moss needs to live\nhere.  The pool seems to continue westwards and down under the rocky wall\nof the end of the tunnel to the west.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22598,0,0,0,'Underwater','The water of the pool is cool and refreshingly chilly.  Darkness and shadows\nsurround you with unknown and undiscovered corners of this ancient pool.  You\ncan see the pool goes on to the west and south.\n',0,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22599,0,0,0,'Underwater','The water of the pool is cool and refreshingly chilly.  Darkness and shadows\nsurround you with unknown and undiscovered corners of this ancient pool.  The\npool extends in multiple directions including upwards.\n',0,131080,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22600,-13,-37,0,'Inside a Glowing Cave','  The cave is chilling and gloomy.  The walls are covered with glowing\nmoss that give it a haunting aura.  The cave tunnel slopes down steeply\ninto the mountain range.  The foreboding silence and haunting glow\ncoming from deep inside makes the tunnel look like it\'s alive.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22601,0,0,0,'Before a Glowing, Eerie Cave','  The path has come to a halt to the south and gave way to a glowing\neerie cave.  The entrance appears foreboding and its looks like the walls\nare glowing.  The air is very humid yet cold around here.  You can see\nnumerous claw marks over the rocks here.\n',0,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22602,-13,-35,0,'A Twist in the Path','  The path stops going east here and goes south.  To the south, there is\nthe range of mountains coming from the west.  The path has many large\ntracks covering it and is slowly drying up to the south.\n',123,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22603,-12,-35,0,'On a Muddy Path','  The road is muddy and damp matching the humidity in the atmosphere.\nWhoever made the path didn\'t do a good job at it.  Several branches and\nthickets have crashed over the way giving the area a dark, ominous look.\nTo the south there is a range of mountains coming from the west.  To the\nnorth the path arches upwards gently to move over a bridge there.\n',123,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22604,-12,-34,0,'On a Bridge Above a Stream','  To the south and north, the path is muddy.  Below you, the stream\nis passing silently, adding to the gloominess of the area.  The bridge\nlooks cracked in every section, but seems to be still intact.\n',123,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22605,-12,-33,0,'Muddy Path','  The path to the south ascends upwards in a gentle arch as it crosses a\nshaky looking bridge built over a muddy river.  Beyond the bridge the path\nseems dark and gloomy.  To the north and east the ground suddenly drops\noff into a ravine while to the west you can just make out the edge of some\nforested hills.  To the southwest lies a muddy stream.\n',123,131076,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22606,-9,-45,-5,'Inside an Unholy Shrine','  Powerful auras radiate the air in here.  Several patches of long ago dried\nblood are scattered around the area.  Ghastly words of terror are inscribed\nupon the jet walls of the shrine.  Demonic pictures of murder are carved on\nthe solid, jet floor.  Several rotten skeletons lie here unburied, in shame.\nA large, wide circle of bones lines the inner circumference of the room.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22607,-9,-47,-5,'Inside a Secret Passage','  The air in here is very hot and unpleasant although not humid.  The tunnel\nwalls are of solid jet and pumice.  There is a long, dark passage to the south\nthat is declining downwards slowly.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22608,-9,-48,-5,'Along a Dark Corridor','  The corridor bends here sharply.  To the west, you can feel the heat\nincreasing as the passage goes down.  The northern tunnel is slightly\ninclined upwards.  Sigils of an ancient language are inscribed along the\nsolid walls of jet.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22609,-10,-48,-5,'Above a Staircase','  Before you stands a grand, jet black staircase heading downwards.  Fumes\nof hot air are flowing upwards from below making the atmosphere hard to\ntolerate.  The tunnel goes slightly upwards to the east.\n',123,131080,49,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22610,-10,-48,-6,'Below a Staircase','  The air here is too hot to tolerate.  There is a large staircase of jet\ngoing up to another tunnel.  Many sigils and runes cover the dazzling,\nsmooth jet surface of the staircase.  There is a corridor going north\nfrom here with a delicate decline along it.  You can hear a faint humming\nat its end.\n',123,172360,49,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22611,-10,-47,-6,'Before a Runed Gate','  The corridor turns sharply to the east here and stops before a grand gate.\nThe doors of the gate are of pure, solid jet and are runed with spidery words\nand ancient sigils of power.  You can hear the humming coming from the doors.\n',123,172361,49,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22612,-9,-47,-6,'On Top of a Staircase','  To the west, a grand runed gate towers above you and the staircase to your\neast.  The staircase are made of smooth jet and are solid hard with many\nrunes and sigils similar to those on the gate.  The staircase runs downwards\nto an even hotter passage.\n',123,172361,49,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22613,-9,-47,-7,'Below a Staircase','  To the north is a smooth jet staircase covered with runes and sigils of\nsummoning magic.  To the south, a dark corridor declines slowly.  Several\nrunes, of similar patterns to those on the staircase, glow with power on\nthe walls of the corridor.\n',123,172361,49,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22614,-9,-48,-7,'Before a Torture Pit','  The room looks like a chamber taken from the nightmare of an innocent\nchild.  Runes and sigils of power are carved everywhere along the smooth,\ngleaming walls of jet of the chamber.  To the west, you can see a red\nportcullis glowing with force and might.  Through it, you can see a huge\npit falling deep down to darkness and oblivion.\n',123,172361,49,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22615,-10,-48,-7,'Above a Torture Pit','  You are at the tip of a large torture pit.  You can see the pit below\nblazing with fire.  It\'s very hot and slippery even this far away from\nthe bottom.  Perhaps it\'s an illusion of the scorching fire, but something\ndark, black is down there between the embers and flames of the inferno.\n',123,172365,35,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22616,-10,-48,-8,'Down a Torture Pit','  You are just beneath the tip of the pits opening.  The inferno waves are\nstrong and way too high for a normal mortal to endure.  You can see the\nvolcanic lava splashing around something big and black down at the bottom\nof the pit.\n',123,172361,64,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22617,-10,-48,-9,'Halfway Down a Torture Pit','  You are half way down a pit of fire.  Flames are exploding upwards at you\nfrom below.  At this point, the flames are only licking you.  Further down\nthe flames roar with scorching heat that sizzles along your skin.\n',123,172361,64,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22618,-10,-48,-10,'In a Demonic Pit','  You are above a small island of hardened jet in the center of the flames.\nAll around you, lava and fire splash in giant waves about the vast circular\nchamber.  At the top, the dark passage, falling down here, starts upwards\nout of the pit.  Flames from the chamber fly up along the tunnel and scorch\nthe ceiling of the upper chamber and the tip of the tube like passage.  You\ncan see the flames dancing with the shadows far above.\n',123,172361,62,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22619,-9,-48,-4,'A Hallway in the Secret Treasury','  You stand a knee deep in a sea of bones.  The vast treasury of the trolls\nhas endured numerous attempts at being breached by many mighty bands of\nadventurers.  The corpses have been piled up here and left to rot in\nshame, some are even new and only half decayed.  Tapestries speak the\nstories of old legends about the ancient trolls in the paintings on them.\nThe sea of bones continues to the west.\n',123,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22620,-10,-48,-4,'A Hallway in the Secret Treasury','  You stand a knee deep in a sea of bones.  The vast treasury of the trolls\nhas endured numerous attempts at being breached by many mighty bands of\nadventurers.  The corpses have been piled up here and left to rot in\nshame, some are even new and only half decayed.  Tapestries speak the\nstories of old legends about the ancient trolls in the paintings on them.\nThe sea of bones continues east and south.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22621,-10,-49,-4,'Treasure Hoard Room','  The sea of bones and corpses end here at a huge hoard of gold.  The\ntreasures of the trolls are all hoarded here together, with enough gold\naround to enable a man to dive in safely.  A thief would cry in pain at it\nand even a paladin would stare at this hoard.  From the grin on the faces\nof some of the skeletons around, you can tell they were not really that\nsad when they died here.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22622,-9,-49,-4,'Secret Chamber','  The secret chamber of the trolls is adorned with the tapestries of the\nancient wars.  Only the most important of all treasures are stored around\nhere.  There are not only many skeletons lying around but also many\nrotten corpses of what looks to be dwarves.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22623,-11,-33,-1,'A Cave Home','  The cave is disgusting and terrifying.  The walls are smeared with blood.\nNumerous heads of unlucky adventurers of several different races are\nadorning the walls of the cave, although you can tell that the preferences\nof the owners is probably gnomes.  Signs of a long abandoned fire pit in\nthe center of the room are visible.  There are fresh body parts littering\nthe cave.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22624,-14,-33,-3,'A Cave Home','  Someone, or something, obviously lives here.  There are signs of bedding\nand a fire pit visible under the stinking, rotten body parts and debris\nlying around the room.  There is a tunnel leaving upwards out of the room.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22625,-22,-37,-8,'A Cool, Natural Cavern','  You are inside a great, ancient cavern formed through the passage of\ncenturies of time.  Strange glowing moss is covering all the round ceiling\nof this great dome and is shedding bright, blue light over the cave.\nBeautiful stalactites protrude from the floor and ceiling of the cavern\nmaking the cave look like a giant open mouth with large fangs.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22626,-23,-37,-8,'A Cool, Natural Cavern','  You are inside a great, ancient cavern formed through the passage of\ncenturies of time.  Strange glowing moss is covering all the round\nceiling of this great dome and is shedding a bright, blue light over the\ncave.  Beautiful stalactites protrude from the floor and ceiling of the\ncavern making the cave look like a giant, open mouth with large fangs.\n',123,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(22627,-47,-24,0,'On a Little Path','  The grass path runs east to a small wooden cabin.  The path looks old and\nnot frequently used.  The farm land about the cabin is not planted and\ntended like the other farm lands in the area.  You can see several cracks\nin the walls of the cabin even from afar.\n',123,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22628,-46,-24,0,'Inside an Old Cabin','  The cabin is very old although it\'s very clean.  The floor is cracked\nin several places and the whole setting shows that the owners are really\npoor.  Numerous holes are visible in the roof from here.  Several\npictures are hung on the wooden walls.\n',123,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22629,-11,-47,-10,'In a Demonic Pit','You are above a small island of hardened jet in the northwestern corner of\nthe flames.  All around you, lava and fire splash in giant waves about the\nvast circular chamber.  At the top, the dark passage, falling down here\nstarts upwards out of the pit.  Flames from the chamber fly up along the\ntunnel and scorch the ceiling of the upper chamber, along with the tip of\nthe tube-like passage.  You can see the flames dancing with the shadows far\nabove.\n',123,172361,62,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22630,-10,-47,-10,'In a Demonic Pit','  You are above a small island of hardened jet north in the flames.  All\naround you, lava and fire splash in giant waves about the vast circular\nchamber.  At the top, the dark passage, falling down here, starts upwards\nout of the pit.  Flames from the chamber fly along the tunnel and scorch\nthe ceiling of the upper chamber, along with the tip of the tube-like\npassage.  You can see the flames dancing with the shadows far above.\n',123,172361,62,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22631,-9,-47,-10,'In a Demonic Pit','  You are above a small island of hardened jet in the northeastern corner\nin the flames.  All around you, lava and fire splash in giant waves about\nthe vast circular chamber.  At the top, the dark passage, falling down\nhere, starts  upwards out of the pit.  Flames from the chamber fly along\nthe tunnel and scorch the ceiling of the upper chamber, along with the tip\nof the tube-like passage.  You can see the flames dancing with the shadows\nfar above.\n',123,172361,62,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22632,-11,-48,-10,'In a Demonic Pit','  You are above a small island of hardened jet west in the chamber of\nflames.  All around you, lava and fire splash and spit in giant wave about\nthe vast circular dome.  At the top, the dark passage, falling down here\nstarts upwards out of the pit.  Flames from the chamber fly up along the\ntunnel and scorch the ceiling of the upper chamber, and the tip of the\ntube-like passage.  You can see the flames dancing with the shadows far\nabove.\n',123,172361,62,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22633,-9,-48,-10,'In a Demonic Pit','  You are above a small island of hardened jet east in the flames.  All\naround you, lava and fire splash and spit in giant waves about the vast\ncircular chamber.  At the top, the dark passage, falling down here, starts\nupwards out of the pit.  Flames from the chamber fly along the tunnel and\nscorch the ceiling of the upper chamber, along with the tip of the\ntube-like passage.  You can see the flames dancing with the shadows far\nabove.\n',123,172361,62,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22634,-11,-49,-10,'In a Demonic Pit','You are above a small island of hardened jet in the southeastern corner\n of the chamber of flames.  All around you, lava and fire splash and spit\nin giant waves about the vast circular chamber.  At the top, the dark\npassage,  falling down here, starts upwards out of the pit.  Flames from\nthe chamber fly up along the tunnel and scorch the ceiling of the upper\nchamber and the tip of the tube-like passage.  You can see the flames\ndancing with the shadows far above.\n',-1,172361,62,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22635,-10,-49,-10,'In a Demonic Pit','  You are above a small island of hardened jet south in the chamber of\nflames.  All around you, lava and fire splash in giant waves about the\nvast circular chamber.  At the top, the dark passage, falling down here,\nstarts upwards out of the pit.  Flames from the chamber fly up along the\ntunnel and scorch the ceiling of the upper chamber and the tip of the\ntube-like passage.  You can see the flames dancing with the shadows far\nabove.\n',123,172361,62,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22636,-9,-49,-10,'In a Demonic Pit','  You are above a small island of hardened jet in the south-eastern corner\nin the flames.  All around you, lava and fire splash and spit in giant\nwaves about the vast circular chamber.  At the top, the dark passage,\nfalling down here, starts upwards out of the pit.  Flames from the chamber\nfly along the tunnel and scorch the ceiling of the upper chamber along\nwith the tip of the tube-like passage.  You can see the flames dancing with\nthe shadows far above.\n',123,172361,62,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22650,2,33,-1,'Inside the Hunting Lodge','  This lodge suffers from years of neglect by the hunters.  The floors\nare filthy and there is dust on almost everything.  Although the lodge is\nwell equipped with the things that a hunter would need, you probably would\nthink twice about using anything in this lodge.  A rickety door leads to\nthe east, half hanging on rusty hinges.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22651,2,32,-1,'Lodge Trail','   This trail has been stamped down by the numerous hunters that use the\nnearby lodges for their hunting enjoyment.  Many of the hunters that come\nhere do not even hunt at all, but rather come for the relaxation that comes\nalong with communing with nature.  The forest opens itself up to the\nsoutheast.  A row of small shacks lies to the northeast along the trail.\nThe path ends abruptly here, allowing the forest to encroach on its\nboundaries.\n',124,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22652,2,31,-1,'Forest Near Lodge Trail','  The forest brush is less predominate here than to the south.\nPerhaps this is due to the main trail through the forest to the\nnorthwest.  The ground cover is stamped down somewhat, but still\nprevalent enough to cause some troubled footing.  The trees have\nsmall mushrooms and lichens growing towards the ground.  The forest\ngets thicker to the south and east, and is so thick to the west\nthat it is not passable.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22653,2,30,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see all the wildlife about you.  Strange\nsounds fill and echo through the thick trees.  Smells of the forest\nfill the air as well.  Thick piles of leaves and broken twigs scatter\nabout on the ground.  The forest is so thick to the south that light\neven struggles to make it past the gnarled branches strewn about\nand the thick underbrush.  The forest opens up to the northeast,\nrevealing a truly beautiful forest.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22654,3,34,-1,'A Hunting Lodge','  This lodge contains only the most necessary equipment.  Serving the\npurpose of both a place to sleep at night, and a place to store the meat,\nthis lodge barely has a free foot of space.  A set of cupboards on the west\nwall are covered with soot and ash.  The fireplace on the north wall has a\npot simmering some sort of stew.  The floors are dirt, and the walls look\nto have been thrown up in a hurry.  A doorway leads to the east.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,200,0,'',NULL),
(22655,3,33,-1,'Lodge Trail','   This trail has been stamped down by the numerous hunters that use the\nnearby lodges for their hunting enjoyment.  Many of the hunters that come\nhere do not even hunt at all, but rather come for the relaxation that comes\nalong with communing with nature.  The forest opens itself up to the\nsoutheast.  A small shack lies to the west, barely standing on its own.\nThe trail ends abruptly here, allowing the forest to encroach on its\nboundaries.\n',124,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22656,3,32,-1,'Forest Near Lodge Trail','  The forest brush is less predominate here than to the south.\nPerhaps this is due to the main trail through the forest to the\nnorthwest.  The ground cover is stamped down somewhat, but still\nprevalent enough to cause some troubled footing.  The trees have\nsmall mushrooms and lichens growing towards the ground.  The forest\ngets thicker to the south.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22657,3,31,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see all the wildlife about you.  Strange\nsounds fill and echo through the thick trees.  Smells of the forest\nfill the air as well.  Thick piles of leaves and broken twigs scatter\nabout on the ground.  The forest continues in all directions.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22658,3,30,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see all the wildlife about you.  Strange\nsounds fill and echo through the thick trees.  Smells of the forest\nfill the air as well.  Thick piles of leaves and broken twigs scatter\nabout on the ground.  The forest continues in all directions, however\nit is too thick to the south to permit passage.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22659,4,35,-1,'A Hunting Lodge','  A tall vaulted ceiling made of pine wood opens this lodge up quite a bit.\nThe walls are vertical paneling also of pine wood.  A thin, overabused rug\nlies on the ground, caked with dirt and needles from the forest that lies\nthrough a door on the east wall.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(22660,4,34,-1,'Lodge Trail','  This trail has been stamped down by the numerous hunters that use the\nnearby lodges for their hunting enjoyment.  Many of the hunters that come\nhere do not even hunt at all, but rather come for the relaxation that comes\nalong with communing with nature.  The forest opens itself up to the\nsoutheast where you see a small pond.  A shack lies to the west, barely\nstanding on its own.\n',124,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22661,4,33,-1,'Forest Near Lodge Trail','  The forest brush is less predominate here than to the south.\nPerhaps this is due to the main trail through the forest to the\nnorthwest.  The ground cover is stamped down somewhat, but still\nprevalent enough to cause some troubled footing.  The trees have\nsmall mushrooms and lichens growing towards the ground.  The forest\ngets thicker to the south, and you see a small pond to the east.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22662,4,32,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see all the wildlife about you.  Strange\nsounds fill and echo through the thick trees.  Smells of the forest\nfill the air as well.  Thick piles of needles and broken twigs scatter\nabout on the ground.  The forest continues in all directions, and a\nsmall pond lies to the northeast.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22663,4,31,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see all the wildlife about you.  Strange\nsounds fill and echo through the thick trees.  Smells of the forest\nfill the air as well.  Thick piles of leaves and broken twigs scatter\nabout on the ground.  The forest continues in all directions.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22664,4,30,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see all the wildlife about you.  Strange\nsounds echo through the thick trees.  Smells of the pine forest fill the\nair as well.  Thick piles of needles and broken twigs scatter about on the\nground.  The forest continues in all directions, however it is too thick to\nthe south to permit passage.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22665,5,35,-1,'Lodge Trail','   This trail has been stamped down by the numerous hunters that use the\nnearby lodges for their hunting enjoyment.  Many of the hunters that come\nhere do not even hunt at all, but rather come for the relaxation that comes\nalong with communing with nature.  The forest opens itself up to the\nsoutheast.  A small shack lies to the west, barely standing on its own.\n',124,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22666,5,34,-1,'Forest Near Lodge Trail','  The forest brush is less predominate here than to the south.\nPerhaps this is due to the main trail through the forest to the\nnorthwest.  The ground cover is stamped down somewhat, but still\nprevalent enough to cause some troubled footing.  The trees have\nsmall mushrooms and lichens growing towards the ground.  The forest\nopens up to the southeast, where you see a small pond.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22667,5,33,-1,'A Small Pond','  The glory of the Haon-Dor extends into the heavens and breaks\nopen to reveal this lush pond to the sun and moon.  Crystal clear\nwater springs up from the ground here, providing water for animals\nand adventurers alike.  The Haon-Dor extends all around except for\nthe east and northeast, where the pond continues.\n',124,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22668,5,32,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see all the wildlife about you.  The\nforest here is oddly quiet, as if animals have vacated the surrounding\narea.  Smells of the pine forest fill the air as well.  Thick piles\nof needles and broken twigs scatter about on the ground.  The forest\ncontinues in all directions, and a small pond lies to the north.\n',124,131076,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22669,5,31,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see wildlife all around you.  Strange\nsounds echo through the thick trees.  Smells of the pine forest\nfill the air, and thick piles of needles and broken twigs\nscatter about on the ground.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22670,5,30,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see all the wildlife about you.  Strange\nsounds echo through the thick trees.  Smells of the forest fill\nthe air as well.  Thick piles of leaves and broken twigs scatter\nabout on the ground.  The forest is so dense to the south that light\nstruggles to make it past the gnarled branches strewn about and\nthe thick underbrush.  The animals do not have problems getting through,\nbut it is too tangled for you to pass.  The forest is less dense\nand passable to the north, northeast and northwest.\n',124,131073,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22671,6,36,-1,'Lodge Trail','   This trail has been stamped down by the numerous hunters that use the\nnearby lodges for their hunting enjoyment.  Many of the hunters that come\nhere do not even hunt at all, but rather come for the relaxation that comes\nalong with communing with nature.  The forest opens itself up to the\nsoutheast.  A small shack lies to the west, barely standing on its own.\n',124,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22672,6,35,-1,'Forest Near Lodge Trail','  The forest brush is less predominate here than to the south.\nPerhaps this is due to the main trail through the forest to the\nnorthwest.  The ground cover is stamped down somewhat, but still\nis prevalent enough to cause some troubled footing.  The trees have\nsmall mushrooms and lichens growing towards the ground.  The forest\nthins to the south, where you see a small pond.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22673,6,34,-1,'A Small Pond','  The glory of the Haon-Dor extends into the heavens and breaks\nopen to reveal this lush pond to the sun and moon.  Crystal clear\nwater springs up from the ground here, providing water for animals\nand adventurers alike.  The Haon-Dor extends all around except for\nthe south and southwest, where the pond continues.\n',124,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22674,6,33,-1,'A Small Pond','  The glory of the Haon-Dor extends into the heavens and breaks\nopen to reveal this lush pond to the sun and moon.  Crystal clear\nwater springs up from the ground here, providing water for animals\nand adventurers alike.  The Haon-Dor extends all around except for\nthe north and west, where the pond continues.\n',124,131072,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22675,6,32,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see all the wildlife about you.  Strange\nsounds fill and echo through the thick trees.  Smells of the forest\nfill the air as well.  Thick piles of needles and broken twigs scatter\nabout on the ground.  The forest continues in all directions, and a\nsmall pond lies through the trees to the north.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22676,6,31,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see wildlife all around you.  Strange\nsounds echo through the thick trees.  Smells of the pine forest\nfill the air, and thick piles of needles and broken twigs\nscatter about on the ground.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22677,6,30,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see all the wildlife about you.  Strange\nsounds echo through the thick trees.  Smells of the forest fill\nthe air as well.  Thick piles of leaves and broken twigs scatter\nabout on the ground.  The forest is so dense to the south that light\nstruggles to make it past the gnarled branches strewn about and\nthe thick underbrush.  The animals do not have problems getting through,\nbut it is too tangled for you to pass.  The forest is less dense\nand passable to the north, northeast and northwest.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22678,7,37,-1,'Lodge Trail','  The forest opens up to allow passing to the south and southwest.\nAlthough still very thick, the brush is not as thick, so as to allow\npassage.  Smells of the forest drift through the trees.  The ground\nis covered in decomposing leaves, broken twigs, and rotting branches.\nThe canopy of the trees does not allow for much light to shine through,\nbut enough light shines through in the day time to allow trouble free\npassage.\n',124,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22679,7,36,-1,'Forest Near Lodge Trail','  The forest brush is less predominate here than to the south.\nPerhaps this is due to the main trail through the forest to the\nnorthwest.  The ground cover is stamped down somewhat, but still\nis prevalent enough to cause some troubled footing.  The trees have\nsmall mushrooms and lichens growing towards the ground.  The forest\ngets thicker to the south.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22680,7,35,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see all the wildlife about you.  Strange\nsounds fill and echo through the thick trees.  Smells of the forest\nfill the air as well.  Thick piles of leaves and broken twigs scatter\nabout on the ground.  The forest continues in all directions, however\nit is too thick to the east to permit passage.  A small pond\nlies to the southwest.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22681,7,34,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see all the wildlife about you.  Strange\nsounds fill and echo through the thick trees.  Smells of the forest\nfill the air as well.  Thick piles of leaves and broken twigs scatter\nabout on the ground.  The forest continues in all directions, however\nit is too thick to the east to permit passage.  A small pond\nlies to the west.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22682,7,33,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see all the wildlife about you.  Strange\nsounds fill and echo through the thick trees.  Smells of the forest\nfill the air as well.  Thick piles of leaves and broken twigs scatter\nabout on the ground.  The forest continues in all directions, however\nit is too thick to the east to permit passage.  A small pond lies to the\nwest.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22683,7,32,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.  It comes\nas no surprise to see wildlife all around you.  You hear the sound of a\nwoodpecker knocking on a tree in the distance.  Smells of the pine forest\nfill the air, and thick piles of needles and broken twigs scatter about on\nthe ground.  To the north, west and south, the forest is less dense and\npassable.  However, to the east the forest has grown far too thick to\npass.  Strange noises, almost of someone giggling can be heard from\nsomewhere, but pinpointing where is impossible.  Trickles of water can be\nheard echoing throughout the forest.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22684,7,31,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.  It comes\nas no surprise to see wildlife all around you.  You hear the sound of a\nwoodpecker knocking on a tree in the distance.  Smells of the pine forest\nfill the air, and thick piles of needles and broken twigs scatter about on\nthe ground.  To the north, west and south, the forest is less dense and\npassable.  However, to the east the forest has grown far too thick to pass.\nStrange noises, almost of someone giggling can be heard from somewhere,\nbut pinpointing where is impossible.  Trickles of water can be heard\nechoing throughout the forest.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22685,7,30,-1,'Deep Within the Haon-Dor Forest','  The Haon-Dor forest is famous for its abundant game resources.\nIt comes as no surprise to see wildlife all around you.  Above\nyou, near the top of a massive pine, is a woodpecker who is\ncreating a hollow knocking sound by slamming its strong beak\non the trunk of the tree.  Small chips of wood fly off to the\nforest floor.  Smells of the pine trees fill the air, and thick\npiles of needles and broken twigs scatter about on the ground.\nTo the north, west and south, the forest is less dense and passable.\nHowever, to the east the forest has grown far too thick to pass.\nStrange noises, almost of someone giggling can be heard from somewhere,\nbut pinpointing where is impossible.  Trickles of water can be\nheard echoing throughout the forest.\n',124,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22686,5,36,-1,'A Hunting Lodge','  The door to this lodge, which lies on the east side of the room,\nis extremely short -- about the right height for a gnome or hobbit.\nThe ceiling is also quite low, which makes it difficult for larger\nraces to walk around but is quite comfortable to the shorter\nhunters who frequent this lodge most often.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,50,0,'',NULL),
(22687,7,38,-1,'A Narrow Trail in the Forest','  This narrow trail appears to have been made by hunters in search of\ngame in the depths of the woods, the Haon-Dor forest being famous for its\nabundant game resources.  Strange sounds fill the air and echo through the\nthick trees.  Smells of the forest fill the air as well.  Thick piles of\nleaves and broken twigs litter the ground around you.  Heavy brush on both\nsides of the trail prevents you from going in any direction but that which\nthe trail leads.\n',125,131076,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22688,6,39,-1,'A Narrow Trail in the Forest','  This narrow trail appears to have been made by hunters in search of\ngame in the depths of the woods, the Haon-Dor forest being famous for its\nabundant game resources.  Strange sounds fill the air and echo through the\nthick trees.  Smells of the forest fill the air as well.  Thick piles of\nleaves and broken twigs litter the ground around you.  Heavy brush on both\nsides of the trail prevents you from going in any direction but that which\nthe trail leads.\n',125,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22689,5,39,-1,'A Narrow Trail in the Forest','  This narrow trail appears to have been made by hunters in search of\ngame in the depths of the woods, the Haon-Dor forest being famous for its\nabundant game resources.  Strange sounds fill the air and echo through the\nthick trees.  Smells of the forest fill the air as well.  Thick piles of\nleaves and broken twigs litter the ground around you.  Heavy brush on both\nsides of the trail prevents you from going in any direction but that which\nthe trail leads.\n',125,131076,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22750,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','This broad road runs south from Brightmoon along the shore of the Agorian Sea\nto the west. The Silverstone River spreads out into a delta before merging with\nthe sparkling blue waters to the southwest. A cool salty mist blows from the \nwest and the sound of crashing waves seems to whoosh from all directions. The \nrocky shoreline continues south as cliffs rise with the road, leaving the sea \nbelow. Although it has become more hazy, to the east lies an arid plain \nfilled with brown grasses and broken earth. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22751,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','This broad road runs south from Brightmoon along the shore of the Agorian Sea\nto the west. The Silverstone River spreads out into a delta before merging with\nthe sparkling blue waters to the southwest. A cool salty mist blows from the \nwest and the sound of crashing waves seems to whoosh from all directions. The \nrocky shoreline continues south as cliffs rise with the road, leaving the sea \nbelow. Although it has become more hazy, to the east lies an arid plain \nfilled with brown grasses and broken earth. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22752,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','This broad road runs south from Brightmoon along the shore of the Agorian Sea\nto the west. The Silverstone River spreads out into a delta before merging with\nthe sparkling blue waters to the southwest. A cool salty mist blows from the \nwest and the sound of crashing waves seems to whoosh from all directions. The \nrocky shoreline continues south as cliffs rise with the road, leaving the sea \nbelow. Through the haze, Brightmoon can be barely seen to the north, and an arid\nplain consisting of nearby grasses and shrubs can be seen to the east.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22753,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','This broad road continues its north-south path along the Agorian Sea. \nDangerously sharp, crumbling cliffs stretch south and westward to a protected \nbeach below. A cool salty mist blows through the air from the west as waves\nwhoosh far below. The city of Brightmoon is barely visible to the north, \nwhile the haze camouflages any clear vision to the east.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22754,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','This broad road continues its north-south path along the Agorian Sea. \nDangerously sharp, crumbling cliffs stretch south and westward to a protected \nbeach below. A cool salty mist blows through the air from the west as waves\nwhoosh far below. The city of Brightmoon is barely visible to the north, \nwhile the haze camouflages any clear vision to the east.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22755,0,0,0,'Bend in the South Coastal Highway','The road makes a slight bend as it sways with the cliffs high above the\ncoastline. Dangerously sharp, crumbling cliffs follow the western side of the\nroad, overlooking a narrow beachline far below. A cool salty mist blows from\nthe west and the sound of crashing waves seem to whoosh from all directions.\nThe haze has completely camouflaged any clear vision to the east.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22756,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','The road continues along a northwest-southeast direction high above the\ncoastline. Dangerously sharp, crumbling cliffs follow the southwestern side of\nthe road overlooking a narrow beachline far below. A cool salty mist blows from\nthe west and the sound of crashing waves seem to whoosh from all directions.\nThe haze has completely camoflauged any clear vision to the east. To the south,\nthe cliff face has eroded deep underneath the edge, creating a large overhang.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22757,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','The road continues along a northwest-southeast direction high above the \ncoastline. Dangerously sharp, crumbling cliffs follow the road to the northwest\nwhile a eroding cliff face continues south. A shabby greenbelt to the south\noffers a better view, where an old wooden fence spans the\nlength along the cliff edge. A cool salty mist blows from the west and the\nsound of crashing waves seem to whoosh from all directions. Haze has completely\nobscured any clear vision to the east.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22758,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','  This broad road continues its north-south stretch along the western \ncoastline. A thin greenbelt runs closer along the coast to the west, likely\noffering a better view of what lies below. Across an open chasm farther to the\nwest, a small peninsula points northward towards Brightmoon.  The haze has\ncompletely camouflaged any clear vision to the east.\n',167,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22759,0,0,0,'Bend in the South Coastal Highway','The road makes a slight bend as it turns with the cliffs high above the\ncoastline. This short section of the highway was built slightly more inland \nthan the rest, since the eroding cliffs were too dangerous to build upon. \nInstead, to the west a thin greenbelt runs along the coast and should offer a\nbetter view of the coastline and beyond. The haze has completely camouflaged \nany clear vision to the east.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22760,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','  This broad road continues its north-south stretch along the western \ncoastline. A thin greenbelt runs closer along the coast to the west, likely\noffering a better view of what lies below. Across an open chasm farther to the\nwest, a small peninsula points northward towards Brightmoon.  The haze has\ncompletely camouflaged any clear vision to the east.\n',167,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22761,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','  This broad road continues its north-south stretch along the western \ncoastline. A thin greenbelt runs closer along the coast to the west, likely\noffering a better view of what lies below. Across an open chasm farther to the\nwest, a small peninsula points northward towards Brightmoon.  The haze has\ncompletely camouflaged any clear vision to the east.\n',167,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22762,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','  This broad road continues its north-south stretch along the western \ncoastline. A thin greenbelt runs closer along the coast to the west, likely\noffering a better view of what lies below. Across an open chasm farther to the\nwest, a small peninsula points northward towards Brightmoon.  The haze has\ncompletely camouflaged any clear vision to the east.\n',167,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22763,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','  This broad road continues its north-south stretch along the western \ncoastline. A thin greenbelt runs closer along the coast to the west, likely\noffering a better view of what lies below. Across an open chasm farther to the\nwest, a small peninsula points northward towards Brightmoon.  The haze has\ncompletely camouflaged any clear vision to the east.\n',167,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22764,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','  This broad road continues its north-south stretch along the western \ncoastline. A thin greenbelt runs closer along the coast to the west, likely\noffering a better view of what lies below. Across an open chasm farther to the\nwest, a small peninsula points northward towards Brightmoon.  The haze has\ncompletely camouflaged any clear vision to the east.\n',167,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22765,0,0,0,'Bend in the South Coastal Highway','  The road makes a slight bend as it turns with the cliffs high above the\ncoastline. This short section of the highway was built slightly more inland \nthan the rest, since the eroding cliffs were too dangerous to build upon. \nInstead, to the west a thin greenbelt runs along the coast offering a better\nview of the coastline and beyond. The haze has completely camouflaged any clear\nvision to the east.\n',167,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22766,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','The road follows a northeast-southwest path along unstable weathered cliffs\nnear the Agorian Sea. Further to the west lies a deep chasm that had created a \nsmall peninsula beyond. A thin greenbelt runs closer along the coast, likely\noffering a better view of what lies below. The haze has completely camouflaged \nany clear vision to the southeast.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22767,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','The road follows a northeast-southwest path along unstable weathered cliffs\nnear the Agorian Sea. Further to the west lies a deep chasm that had created a \nsmall peninsula beyond. A thin greenbelt runs closer along the coast to the\nnorth, likely offering a better view of what lies below. The haze has \ncompletely camouflaged any clear vision to the southeast.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22768,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','The road continues along the dangerously sharp and crumbling cliffs that lie\nto the northwest.  The cliffs drop precipitously to a cove surrounded by a \nrocky beach.  A little to the west, a small peninsula points northward toward \nBrightmoon. The haze has completely camouflaged any clear\nvision to the southeast.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22769,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','The road continues along the dangerously sharp and crumbling cliffs that lie\nto the\nnorthwest. The rocky beach below rests at the south end of a secluded cove that\nopens to the north. A small peninsula begins a little to the west. The haze has\ncompletely camouflaged any clear vision to the southeast.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22770,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','The road continues its northeast-southwest path along dangerously crumbling\ncliffs nearby to the north. A small peninsula begins to jut out to the \nnorthwest. At the bottom of the cliffs is a rocky beach, which lies at the\ncloser end of a secluded cove that opens into the Agorian Sea far to the north.\nThe haze has completely camouflaged any clear vision inland on the southeast \nside of the road.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22771,0,0,0,'Cliffs Above a Rocky Beach','The beautiful sparkling blue waters of the Agorian Sea envelop the senses.\nSlightly out into the waters to the southwest is a small peninsula, the cliffs\nof which fall short of the mainland. This small opening in the sea made a \npleasant and private cove to the southwest below. A simple wooden fence \nprotects those who may wish to lean too far over the crumbling cliff edge. \nThe Coastal Highway is just to the east if you want to continue on your way.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22772,0,0,0,'Cliffs Above a Rocky Beach','The beautiful sparkling blue waters of the Agorian Sea envelop your senses.\nSlightly out into the waters to the southwest is a small peninsula, the cliffs\nof which\nfall short of the mainland. This small opening in the sea made a \npleasant and private cove to the southwest below. That narrow beachline would \nbe a secluded sunbathing location, since a simple wooden fence protects those \nwho may wish to lean too far over the crumbling cliff edge to get a better \nview. The Coastal Highway is just to the east if you wish to continue on your \nway.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22773,0,0,0,'Cliffs Above a Rocky Beach','The beautiful sparkling blue waters of the Agorian Sea envelop your senses.\nSlightly out into the waters to the west is a small peninsula, the cliffs of \nwhich \nfall short of the mainland. This small opening in the sea made a pleasant \nand private cove to the southwest below. That narrow beachline would be a \nsecluded sunbathing location, since a simple wooden fence protects those who \nmay wish to lean too far over the crumbling cliff edge to get a better view. \nThe Coastal Highway is just to the east if you wish to continue on your way.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22774,0,0,0,'Cliffs Above a Rocky Beach','The beautiful sparkling blue waters of the Agorian Sea envelop your senses.\nSlightly out into the waters to the west is a small peninsula, the high cliffs\nof which\nfall short of the mainland. This small opening in the sea made a pleasant \nand private cove to the southwest below. The narrow beachline would be a nice\nsecluded sunbathing location in the summer, since a simple wooden fence \nprotects those who may wish to lean too far over the cliff edge to get a better\nview. The Coastal Highway is just to the east if you wish to continue on your \nway.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22775,0,0,0,'Cliffs Over a Small Cove','The view of the Agorian Sea to the west is somewhat obscured by a \npeninsula that almost touches the mainland to the north. Fresh seawater flows\ninto the cove through the gap. The waters appear to have eroded \nthe cliff face below. Thankfully, a simple wooden fence protects those who may\nwish to lean too far over the crumbling cliff edge. The Coastal Highway is just\nto the east if you wish to continue on your way.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22776,0,0,0,'Cliffs Over a Small Cove','The view of the Agorian Sea to the west is somewhat obscured by a\npeninsula that almost touches the mainland to the north. Fresh seawater flows\ninto the cove through the gap. The waters appear to have eroded\nthe cliff face below. Thankfully, a simple wooden fence protects those who may\nwish to lean too far over the crumbling cliff edge. The Coastal Highway is\nto the east if you wish to continue on your way.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22777,0,0,0,'Cliffs Over a Small Cove','The view of the Agorian Sea to the west is mostly obscured by a\npeninsula that almost touches the mainland to the north. \nA small lighthouse pokes its top over the far side of the peninsula cliff.\nBelow, the cove\nexpands north toward its opening to the sea. A simple wooden fence protects\nthose who may wish to lean too far over the eroded cliff underneath. The\nCoastal Highway to the east offers a paved pathway for a longer journey.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22778,0,0,0,'Cliffs Over a Small Cove','The view of the Agorian Sea to the west is mostly obscured by a\npeninsula that almost touches the mainland to the north.\nA small lighthouse pokes its top over the far side of the peninsula cliff.\nBelow, the cove\nexpands north toward the opening in the sea. A simple wooden fence protects\nthose who may wish to lean too far over the eroded cliff underneath. The\nCoastal Highway to the east offers a paved pathway for a longer journey.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22779,0,0,0,'Cliffs Above a Rocky Beach','The view of the Agorian Sea to the west is mostly obscured by a\npeninsula that almost touches the mainland to the north.\nA small lighthouse pokes its top over the far side of the peninsula cliff.\nThe bottom of the\ncove lies below, opening to a modest beach scattered with rocks fallen from\nthe cliff face. A simple wooden fence protects those who may wish to lean \ntoo far over the crumbling cliff edge. The Coastal Highway to the south and \neast offers a paved pathway for a longer journey.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22780,0,0,0,'Cliffs Above a Rocky Beach','The sharp cliff edge to the north opens to a secluded cove far below. To the\nwest, a thin peninsula begins its fingerlike extension northward. At the tip of\nthe peninsula stands a small lighthouse. Dangerously crumbling cliffs stop any\npassage north, where a small neglected beach lies far below.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22781,0,0,0,'Base of the Peninsula','The sharp cliffs abruptly change direction as the peninsula begins its \nstretch north. A secluded beach and protected cove open up far below. To the\nsouth, a single stone table offers limited rest for weary travelers following\nthe Coastal Highway. The thin peninsula continues northward, where a small\nlighthouse is barely visible through the misty haze. \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22782,0,0,0,'Eastern Edge of the Peninsula','Strong breezes from the west try to blow everything atop the cliffs down into\nthe cove far below. The dangerously sharp, crumbling cliff face has dropped\nmany rocks onto a beach at its base. The cliff edge runs north from here, \nending at a small lighthouse barely visible at the tip. A little further to the\nsoutheast spans the broad Coastal Highway.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22783,0,0,0,'Eastern Edge of the Peninsula','Strong westerly sea breezes try to blow everything atop the cliffs down into\nthe cove far below. The dangerously sharp, crumbling cliff face has dropped\nmany rocks onto a beach at its base. The bay below ends at a small beach \ndirectly to the east, which then fills in the rest of the southern \"bowl\". A \nsmall lighthouse is barely visible to the north. Farther to the south runs the\nbroad Coastal Highway.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22784,0,0,0,'Eastern Edge of the Peninsula','Strong westerly sea breezes try to blow everything atop the cliffs down into\nthe cove far below. The dangerously sharp, crumbling cliff face has dropped \nmany rocks onto a beach at its base. A small lighthouse is barely visible to \nthe north. Farther to the south runs the broad Coastal Highway.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22785,0,0,0,'Eastern Edge of the Peninsula','Strong westerly sea breezes try to blow everything atop the cliffs down into\nthe cove far below. The dangerously sharp, crumbling cliff face has dropped\nmany rocks onto a beach at its base. A small lighthouse stands proudly at the\npeninsula\'s tip to the north in order to provide warning to seafarers of the\ndangers that lie ahead.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22786,0,0,0,'Narrow Stretch of the Peninsula','The peninsula is at its thinnest here. Both the Agorian Sea to the west and \nthe secluded cove to the east are far below. A combination of strong winds\nand crumbling cliffs on either side play with one\'s sense of balance and \nagility. Towards the near-side of the cove below, a thin extension of the rocky\nbeach runs south along the eastern edge of the peninsula. A small lighthouse \nto the north stands proudly in the winds to provide warning to seafarers.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22787,0,0,0,'Narrow Stretch of the Peninsula','The peninsula is at its thinnest here and slopes upward to the north. Both\nthe Agorian Sea to the west and the secluded cove to the east are far below.\nThe combination of strong, salty winds and crumbling cliffs on either side play\nwith one\'s sense of balance. Towards the near-side of the cove, a thin extension\nof the rocky beach runs south along the eastern edge of the peninsula. A \nlighthouse to the north stands proudly in the winds to provide warning to \nseafarers. \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22788,0,0,0,'Before a Weathered Lighthouse','  A lighthouse grips the tip of the eroded peninsula to the north.  It is not as\nsmall as it appeared from farther distances, and must have been a great asset\nto ship captains for generations. Judging from the broken glass windows,\nchipped plaster and scattered grey bricks around its base, one can deduce that\nit has been neglected for some time. No door appears on this side, so maybe\nwalking around it a little may find entrance. As you turn to step away, the\nstrong steady winds continue to weather down this quaint old lighthouse once\nagain, as if to beat it into submission.\n',167,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22789,0,0,0,'Peninsula Cliffs Above a Secluded Cove','A lighthouse grips the edge of the eroded peninsula cliff to the northwest. \nIt stands several stories tall, and must have been a\ngreat asset to ship captains for generations. The tip of the peninsula is \nslightly farther to the north, and a well-protected cove rests far below at the\nbottom of the cliffs to the east.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22790,0,0,0,'Tip of the Peninsula','WOW! You can actually see Brightmoon from here! Strong westerly sea \nwinds pound against anything in their path. A weathered and forgotten \nlighthouse tenatiously grips the tip of the eroded peninsula to the west. The\neastern tip stands higher than any other part of the peninsula, which offers\nthis excellent view. A boarded-up door to the west bars entry into\nlighthouse. A well-protected cove lies far \nbelow to the east, and directly across into the hazy distance runs the \nCoastal Highway.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22791,0,0,0,'Western Edge of the Peninsula','Atop a cliff from the western edge of the peninsula, the Agorian Sea \nencompasses a 180 degree view. The strong, salty winds from the west are\nvery persistent here. The steep cliff face below has\neroded from years of the storms, surf and winds pounding at its side. A small\nlighthouse to the north stands proudly at the peninsula\'s tip in order to \nprovide warning to seafarers. \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22792,0,0,0,'Western Edge of the Peninsula','Atop a cliff from the western edge of the peninsula, the Agorian Sea \nencompasses a 180 degree view. The strong, salty winds from the west are\nvery persistent here. The steep cliff face below has\neroded from years of storms, surf and winds pounding at its side. A small\nlighthouse is barely visible to the north, while the Coastal Highway is  \nfurther south.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22793,0,0,0,'Western Edge of the Peninsula','Atop a cliff from the western edge of the peninsula, the Agorian Sea \nencompasses a 180 degree view. The strong, salty winds from the west are\nvery persistent here. The steep cliff face below has\neroded from years of storms, surf and winds pounding at its side. A small\nlighthouse is barely visible to the north, while the Coastal Highway is  \nfurther south.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22794,0,0,0,'Western Edge of the Peninsula','Atop a cliff from the western edge of the peninsula, the Agorian Sea \nencompasses a 180 degree view. The strong, salty winds from the west are\nvery persistent here. The steep cliff face below has \neroded from years of storms, surf and winds pounding at its side. A small\nlighthouse is barely visible to the north, while the Coastal Highway is a \nlittle further south.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22795,0,0,0,'Western Edge of the Peninsula','Atop a cliff from the western edge of the peninsula, the Agorian Sea \nencompasses a 180 degree view. The strong, salty winds from the west are\nvery persistent here. The steep cliff face below has \neroded from years of storms, surf and winds pounding at its side. A small\nlighthouse is barely visible to the north, while the Coastal Highway is a \nlittle further to the south and east.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22796,0,0,0,'Western Base of the Peninsula','Atop a cliff from the western edge of the peninsula, the Agorian Sea \nencompasses a 180 degree view. The strong, salty winds from the west are\nvery persistent here. The steep cliff face below has \neroded from years of storms, surf and winds pounding at its side. A small\nlighthouse is barely visible to the north, while the Coastal Highway is a \nlittle further to the east.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22797,0,0,0,'Abandoned Rest Area','A single weathered stone table is all that remains of this rest area. Years\npast this must have been a relatively safe place to rest weary feet and \nsaddle-sore butts. A peninsula stretches out to the north here, and at\nthe bottom of the cliffs to the north and east lies a protected cove. The \ncoastal highway is to the south and east, beyond which is just salty haze \nblown in from the Agorian Sea.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22798,0,0,0,'Cliffs Above the Agorian Sea','Atop a cliff from the western edge of the peninsula, the Agorian Sea is a \nbreath of fresh air to the adventurous traveler. The strong, salty winds from \nthe west-northwest are very persistent. The steep cliff face below has eroded\nfrom years of storms, surf and winds pounding at its side. To the east, the\nbroad Coastal Highway continues its trek through the southern lands.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(22799,0,0,0,'South Coastal Highway','This broad road continues northeast-southwest as it passes the base of a \nthin peninsula to the north. The peninsula continues northward from the road\nhere, where grasses blow in all directions in the whirling sea breeze. The \nview of the Agorian Sea must be breathtaking out at the point. The haze is  \nvery thick on the southeast side of the road. \n',-1,393216,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23000,19,-74,-1,'Beneath the Surface','  Beneath the surface the water appears to be cloudy. Plankton contained in the\nwater enriches the sea to sustain life. The salt content makes it difficult to\nhold your eyes open for any length of time.\n',165,131072,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
