(23087,21,-76,-6,'Bottom of the Ocean','  The ocean floor is muddy and movement is very difficult. The water\nis far too cold to do much of anything without suffering extreme\ndiscomfort. The pressure of the water squeezing your muscles\ncauses extreme pain. The floor surprisingly is clear of many\nrocks and debris that would be expected here. A carving of a large\nbeast is etched into the crevice wall.\n',165,142592,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23088,22,-76,-6,'Bottom of the Ocean','  The ocean floor is muddy and movement is very difficult. The water\nis far too cold to do much of anything without suffering extreme \ndiscomfort. The pressure of the water squeezing your muscles \ncauses extreme pain. The floor surprisingly is clear of many\nrocks and debris that would be expected here.\n',165,142592,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23089,20,-76,-6,'A Large Underwater Grotto','  This large cavern has been naturally formed over many years. The walls\nare of dark colored coral and stone. Sponges line the bottom of the ocean\nfloor almost in an organized pattern. Claw marks have been scraped into\nthe walls of the cavern. Old dragon scales litter the floor.\n',165,142592,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23100,0,0,0,'A Small Tunnel','This very porous, small tunnel has been carved from the earth by lava.  The\nheat is intense, making it hard to breathe.  Water trickles down the walls\nthrough the ceiling but never reaches the floor.  The humidity in the air is\nevidence of the water evaporating almost as soon as it enters this room.  The\nwalls of the tunnel seem firm and stable, and scalding to the touch.  The tunnel\ncontinues to the northwest and towards the south.\n',-1,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(23101,0,0,0,'A Small Tunnel','  This very porous, small tunnel has been carved from the earth by lava.  The\nheat is intense, making it hard to breathe.  Water trickles down the walls\nthrough the ceiling but never reaches the floor.  The humidity in the air is\nevidence of the water evaporating almost as soon as it enters this room.  The\nwalls of the tunnel seem firm and stable, and scalding to the touch.  The tunnel\ncontinues to the southeast and to the north.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23102,0,0,0,'A Wide Tunnel','  This wide tunnel is somewhat cooler than you would expect.  The ground is hot\nto the touch, but not scalding.  The air is less humid, making it a lot easier\nto breathe.  Dozens of tiny pebbles are scattered about here indicating no lava\nhas flowed through this tunnel in quite some time.  The ceiling and walls are\nboth still unmarked and smooth.  The tunnel continues into the darkness to the\nnortheast and northwest.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23103,0,0,0,'A Wide Tunnel','  This wide tunnel is somewhat cooler than you would expect.  The ground is hot\nto the touch, but not scalding.  The air is less humid, making it a lot easier\nto breathe.  Dozens of tiny pebbles are scattered about here indicating no lava\nhas flowed through this tunnel in quite some time.  The ceiling and walls are\nboth still unmarked and smooth.  The tunnel continues into the darkness to the\nsoutheast and northwest.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23104,0,0,0,'A Wide Tunnel','  This wide tunnel is somewhat cooler than you would expect.  The ground is hot\nto the touch, but not scalding.  The air is less humid, making it a lot easier\nto breathe.  Dozens of tiny pebbles are scattered about here indicating no lava\nhas flowed through this tunnel in quite some time.  The ceiling and walls are\nboth still unmarked and smooth.  The tunnel continues into the darkness to the\nnorth and southwest.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23105,0,0,0,'A Small Ledge','  A narrow ledge has been carved here by the flowing magma.  The ground seems to\nbe a bit unstable as you can hear the splashes of what sounds like rocks falling\ninto the pit of boiling lava.  An intense sensation of heat can be felt from the\neast.  A narrow tunnel, barely large enough to walk through, leads into darkness\nto the north.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,2,85,0,'',NULL),
(23106,0,0,0,'Above a Pool of Lava','  You are standing in mid-air.  Below you, lava boils up almost touching your\nfeet.  The intensity of the heat in the steam is scalding to the skin and you\nbegin to think of what being burnt to a crisp would feel like.  A small ledge\nis to the east and west.\n',176,131144,64,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23107,0,0,0,'A Small Ledge','  A narrow ledge has been carved here by the flowing magma.  The ground seems to\nbe a bit unstable as you can hear the splashes of what sounds like rocks falling\ninto the pit of boiling lava.  An intense sensation of heat can be felt from the\nwest.  A wide tunnel leads into darkness to the east.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23108,0,0,0,'A Wide Tunnel','  This wide tunnel is somewhat cooler than you would expect.  The ground is hot\nto the touch, but not scalding.  The air is less humid, making it a lot easier\nto breathe.  Dozens of tiny pebbles are scattered about here indicating no lava\nhas flowed through this tunnel in quite some time.  The ceiling and walls are\nboth still unmarked and smooth.  The tunnel continues into the darkness to the\nsoutheast and looks to open up to the west.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23109,0,0,0,'A Wide Tunnel','  The tunnel makes a sharp curve south and east here.  The ground here is very\nporous and quite warm to the touch.  The walls are nice and smooth, though very\nhot.  It is much easier to breathe the air in this tunnel, for it is cooler and\nless humid.  Large chunks of obsidian rest against the wall, remains of the lava\nthat once carved these tunnels.  The tunnel continues east and south into the\ndarkness.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23110,0,0,0,'A Wide Tunnel','  The tunnel seems to be widening as one travels west.  The ground here is very\nporous and quite warm to the touch.  The walls are nice and smooth, though very\nhot.  It is much easier to breathe the air in this tunnel, for it is cooler and\nless humid.  Large chunks of obsidian rest against the wall, remains of the lava\nthat once carved these tunnels.  The tunnel continues east and west into the\ndarkness.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23111,0,0,0,'A Wide Tunnel','  The tunnel seems to be widening as one travels west.  The ground here is very\nporous and quite warm to the touch.  The walls are nice and smooth, though very\nhot.  It is much easier to breathe the air in this tunnel, for it is cooler and\nless humid.  Large chunks of obsidian rest against the wall, remains of the lava\nthat once carved these tunnels.  The tunnel continues east and west into the\ndarkness.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23112,0,0,0,'A Wide Tunnel','The tunnel seems to be widening as one travels west.  The ground here is very\nporous and quite warm to the touch.  The walls are nice and smooth, though very\nhot.  It is much easier to breathe the air in this tunnel, for it is cooler and\nless humid.  Large chunks of obsidian rest against the wall, remains of the lava\nthat once carved these tunnels.  The tunnel continues northeast and west into\nthe darkness.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23113,0,0,0,'A Fork in the Small Tunnel','  The tunnel abruptly forks off into two different directions here.  Both\ntunnels are too dark to make out where they lead.  An overwhelming flow of hot\nair seems to be coming from the tunnel leading northwest.  The air is very humid\nand you feel almost as if you are going to pass out from the heat.  The ground\nis very porous and hard here, another example of the sheer force and power\nbehind a flow of lava.  To the south is another tunnel.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23114,0,0,0,'A Small Tunnel','  This very porous, small tunnel has been carved from the earth by lava.  The\nheat is intense, making it hard to breathe.  Water trickles down the walls\nthrough the ceiling but never reaches the floor.  The humidity in the air is\nevidence of the water evaporating almost as soon as it enters this room.  The\nwalls of the tunnel seem firm and stable, and scalding to the touch.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23115,0,0,0,'A Small Tunnel','  This very porous, small tunnel has been carved from the earth by lava.  The\nheat is intense, making it hard to breathe.  Water trickles down the walls\nthrough the ceiling but never reaches the floor.  The humidity in the air is\nevidence of the water evaporating almost as soon as it enters this room.  The\nwalls of the tunnel seem firm and stable, and scalding to the touch.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23116,0,0,0,'A Narrow Tunnel','  This narrow tunnel is barely large enough to house two people.  The humid air\nand tight spacing provide for a very uncomfortable surrounding.  Thought not\nunbearable, the heat is extremely intense.  Shards of obsidian cover the porous\nflooring making a small maze to navigate this room without having your feet cut\nopen.  The ceiling is very low and like the walls, is smooth as glass.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,3,74,0,'',NULL),
(23117,0,0,0,'A Small Tunnel','  The tunnel forks again here.  From the north, an enormous amount of heat can\nbe felt entering this room.  Sounds of splashing rocks can also be heard to the\nnorth.  The tunnel leading to the southwest seems to be cool and less humid, but\nit is too dark to see what lies in that direction.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23118,0,0,0,'A Small Tunnel','  This very porous, small tunnel has been carved from the earth by lava.  The\nheat is intense, making it hard to breathe.  Water trickles down the walls\nthrough the ceiling but never reaches the floor.  The humidity in the air is\nevidence of the water evaporating almost as soon as it enters this room.  The\nwalls of the tunnel seem firm and stable, and scalding to the touch.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23119,0,0,0,'A Small Tunnel','  This very porous, small tunnel has been carved from the earth by lava.  The\nheat is intense, making it hard to breathe.  Water trickles down the walls\nthrough the ceiling but never reaches the floor.  The humidity in the air is\nevidence of the water evaporating almost as soon as it enters this room.  The\nwalls of the tunnel seem firm and stable, and scalding to the touch.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23120,0,0,0,'A Narrow Ledge','  A narrow ledge has been carved here by the flowing magma.  The ground seems to\nbe a bit unstable as you can hear the splashes of what sounds like rocks falling\ninto the pit of boiling lava.  An intense sensation of heat can be felt from the\nnorth.  To the southwest is a small tunnel leading into darkness.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23121,0,0,0,'A Narrow Tunnel','\nThis narrow tunnel is barely large enough to house two people.  The humid air\nand tight spacing provide for a very uncomfortable surrounding.  Thought not\nunbearable, the heat is extremely intense.  Shards of obsidian cover the porous\nflooring making a small maze to navigate this room without having your feet cut\nopen.  The ceiling is very low and like the walls, is smooth as glass.  Along\nnortheast wall, a small door can be seen.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,5,73,0,'',NULL),
