(23125,0,0,0,'A Bridge of Porous Rock','  Supplying a path across the lava below is a very porous, yet sturdy bridge.\nSteam, from the invading water dripping off the ceiling, rises up surrounding\nyou.  The steam is so thick here, it is virtually impossible to see.  To the\neast and west are pools of lava.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23126,0,0,0,'Above a Pool of Lava','  You are standing in mid-air.  Below you, lava boils up almost touching your\nfeet.  The intensity of the heat in the steam is scalding to the skin and you\nbegin to think of what being burnt to a crisp would feel like.\n',176,131144,64,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23127,0,0,0,'A Small Tunnel','  This very porous, small tunnel has been carved from the earth by lava.  The\nheat is intense, making it hard to breathe.  Water trickles down the walls\nthrough the ceiling but never reaches the floor.  The humidity in the air is\nevidence of the water evaporating almost as soon as it enters this room.  The\nwalls of the tunnel seem firm and stable, and scalding to the touch.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(23128,0,0,0,'A Fork in the Tunnel','  The tunnel splits into two seperate tunnels at this intersection.  The porous\nrock floor has been carved from the flow of lava through the tunnels.  The walls\nare smooth and free of scars.  Though the heat is very intense in this room,\nit is bearable.  The humid and hot air makes it somewhat difficult for you to\nbreathe.  To the east is a pool of molten lava and leading into the darkness\nnortheast and southeast are tunnels.\n',176,131144,49,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
