(23193,0,0,0,'<R>A Small Experiment Room<1>','Upon entering this room, you notice a <B>bright blue<1> rug that covers\nnearly the entire floor.  The walls are black but no decoratins are\nseen.  A small table with many bottles and potions rest against the eastern\nwall.  A cot on the northern wall could be used for sleeping, but from the\nlooks of it, it has not been touched in many days.  A door leading out can\nbe found on the southwestern wall.\n',176,131369,56,0,0,0,0,-1,12,100,0,'',NULL),
(23194,0,0,0,'<Y>A Small Treasure Room<1>','This small room gives off some type of magical arua.  In the center,\non the floor, there appears to be a large hole.  Flames lick up from\nthe edges and swirl in the middle, almost as if there was a portal of\nsome type here.  The ceiling of the room reaches into the darkness\nabove.  The walls are smooth and have the reflective quality of a \nhighly polished mirror, most likely obsidian.  To the north, you can\nsee an exit from this room.\n',176,131072,49,0,0,0,0,-1,2,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23195,0,0,0,'A Plain Bedroom','This room is nearly empty.  All the walls are empty and dirty.  No rugs\nor carpet cover the ground, only sand and dirt can be found.  A small\ncot in the opposite corner is the only furnishings that can be found.  A\nsmall door is on the northwest wall leads out of this depressing room.\n',176,131081,61,0,0,0,0,-1,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(23200,32,47,-2,'Arden Forest Along the South Wall of Amber','  The forest next to the tall granite walls of Amber has been cut back\nso that nothing can creep close to the town without being seen from\nabove.  Scraggly brush covers the ground, and in the winter there is\na light dusting of snow.  To the south is the vast forest -- the tall\nstraight lines of white birch trees make the <o>orange<z> glow of the leaves\nseem brighter.  The forest is in a perpetual fall season due to the\nunusual latitude and climate, with leaves fading to <r>red<z>, <o>orange<z>, and\nthen gold, falling from the branches, and then returning briefly in\nemerald hues before entering the abscission cycle again.  To the west\nis a sharp cliff face which seems to lower somewhere to the south.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
