(23210,32,46,-2,'Arden Forest Near the South Wall of Amber','  You are at the northern edge of the Arden birch forest.  <g>Green<z>, <r>red<z>,\n<o>orange<z>, and gold leaves make a soft, thin layer on the cold ground.\nThe thin white parchment-like bark of the trees makes interesting and\nunique patterns and distorts the tall thin vertical lines of the tree\ntrunks.  All around you see this beautiful forest stretching out,\nalthough to the north the trees thin out and you can see the tall\ngranite walls of Amber.  To the west is a sharp cliff face which seems\nto lower somewhere to the south.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
