(23234,36,44,-2,'Arden Forest','  Your footsteps rustle the dried <o>orange<z> leaves that form a soft mat\non the forest floor.  Tall birch rise around you, holding bright\n<y>yellow<z> leaves aloft like flames on giant torches.  The ground is solid\nfrom the chilly weather, which feels like fall for most of the year.\nThe forest stretches in all directions and you cannot find the end\nof it.  To the east you see a small <b>stream<z> that cuts through the forest.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23235,37,44,-2,'Bend in a Stream in Arden Forest','  A <b>stream<z> runs downhill from the south and turns sharply to the east\nhere.  The cold waters freeze to your clothing and make warm fingers\nstick to metal.  The birch trees of the forest lie on every side of\nthe <b>stream<z>.  To the east a large fallen tree spans the river and\nthe water is forced to flow beneath it.\n',166,131072,29,0,0,0,45,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23237,39,44,-2,'A Stream in Arden Forest','  A <b>stream<z> runs downhill from the west to east here.  The cold waters\nfreeze to your clothing and make warm fingers stick to metal.  The\ntall birch trees of the forest lie on every side of the <b>stream<z>.  Water\nbounces off cold stones that line the edges of the water.  To the west a\nlarge fallen tree spans the river as the water is forced below it.\n',166,131072,29,0,0,0,45,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23238,40,44,-2,'A Pond in Arden Forest','  You are at the bottom of a small hill on the edge of some small mountains,\nwhich are to the east.  The mountain range extends from the north by\nAmber to the distant south.  A pond has formed at the bottom of the hill\ndue to collected rainwater, and a small <b>stream<z>.  The stream flows from\nthe west across the flat forest that stretches in that direction.  In \nbright daylight on a clear day the <o>orange<z> leaves of the birch trees\nreflect off the waters of the pond and create a stunning view.\n',166,131072,29,0,0,0,0,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23239,41,44,-2,'A Pond in Arden Forest','  You are at the bottom of a small hill on the edge of some small mountains,\nwhich are to the east.  The mountain range extends from the north by\nAmber to the distant south.  A pond has formed at the bottom of the hill\ndue to collected rainwater, and a small <b>stream<z>.  The stream flows from\nthe west across the flat forest that stretches in that direction.  To the\neast another small path has been cut through the rock as well by a stream.  \nOnly during a strong rain will water still flow down the path, yet\nit still provides for a simple way through the mountains toward the\neastern coast.  In bright daylight on a clear day the <o>orange<z> leaves\nof the birch trees reflect off the waters of the pond and create a\nstunning view.\n',166,131072,29,0,0,0,0,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23240,32,43,-2,'Arden Forest','  Your footsteps rustle the dried <o>orange<z> leaves that form a soft mat\non the forest floor.  Tall birch rise around you, holding bright\n<y>yellow<z> leaves aloft like flames on giant torches.  The ground is solid\nfrom the chilly weather, which feels like fall for most of the year.\nThe forest stretches in all directions and you cannot find the end\nof it.  A small leaf-strewn <p>trail<z> leads west between two sharp cliff\nfaces.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23241,33,43,-2,'Arden Forest','  Your footsteps rustle the dried <o>orange<z> leaves that form a soft mat\non the forest floor.  Tall birch rise around you, holding bright\n<y>yellow<z> leaves aloft like flames on giant torches.  The ground is solid\nfrom the chilly weather, which feels like fall for most of the year.\nThe forest stretches in all directions and you cannot find the end\nof it.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
