(23255,37,42,-2,'A Stream in Arden Forest','  A <b>stream<z> lazily wanders through the forest, flowing from south to\nnorth.  You can see that it gets much shallower as it heads north.\nThe cold water chills your skin, yet it is not quite cold enough\nto freeze here.  The tall birch trees of the woods lie on the east\nand west the banks of the <b>stream<z>, with their leaves in a perpetual\nautumnal <o>orange<z>.\n',166,131072,29,0,0,0,45,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23256,38,42,-2,'Arden Forest','  Your footsteps rustle the dried <o>orange<z> leaves that form a soft mat\non the forest floor.  Tall birch rise around you, holding bright\n<y>yellow<z> leaves aloft like flames on giant torches.  The ground is solid\nfrom the chilly weather, which feels like fall for most of the year.\nThe forest stretches in all directions and you cannot find the end\nof it.  A <b>stream<z> cuts through the forest to the west of here, running\nsouth to north.  A slight incline leads down to the east.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23257,39,42,-2,'Arden Forest','  Your footsteps rustle the dried <o>orange<z> leaves that form a soft mat\non the forest floor.  Tall birch rise around you, holding bright\n<y>yellow<z> leaves aloft like flames on giant torches.  The ground is solid\nfrom the chilly weather, which feels like fall for most of the year.\nThe forest stretches in all directions and you cannot find the end\nof it.  An slope leads down to the east, and you can see a <b>pond<z>\nat the bottom of the hill to the northeast.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23258,40,42,-2,'A Hill in Arden Forest','  From your vantage at the top of this hill you can see down into the\nglowing <o>orange<z> forest to the west, and also a <b>pond<z> that has formed\nto the north.  Some small mountains cut a line from north to south\non the east side of the hill, and a steep rock face prevents you from\nwalking much farther in that direction.  The slope leads down to the north,\nsouth and west into the forest beyond.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23259,41,42,-2,'A Hill in Arden Forest','  From your vantage at the top of this hill you can see down into the\nglowing <o>orange<z> forest to the west, and also a <b>pond<z> that has formed\nto the north.  Some small mountains cut a line from north to south\non the east side of the hill, and a steep rock face prevents you from\nwalking in that direction.  A strange patch of dense vegetation adorns\nthe face of one section of the rocky wall to the east while the slope leads\ndown to the south and to the west into the forest.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23260,32,41,-2,'Arden Forest','  Your footsteps rustle the dried <o>orange<z> leaves that form a soft mat\non the forest floor.  Tall birch rise around you, holding bright\n<y>yellow<z> leaves aloft like flames on giant torches.  The ground is solid\nfrom the chilly weather, which feels like fall for most of the year.\nThe forest stretches in all directions and you cannot find the end\nof it.  A sharp cliff face shoots up through the ground here, but\nit seems to become much lower further north.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
