(23265,37,41,-2,'A Stream in Arden Forest','  A <b>stream<z> lazily wanders through the forest, flowing from south to\nnorth.  You can see that it gets much shallower as it heads north.\nThe cold water chills your skin, yet it is not quite cold enough\nto freeze here.  The tall birch trees of the woods lie on the east\nand west banks of the <b>stream<z>, with their leaves in a perpetual\nautumnal <o>orange<z>.\n',166,131072,29,0,0,0,45,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23266,38,41,-2,'Arden Forest','  Your footsteps rustle the dried <o>orange<z> leaves that form a soft mat\non the forest floor.  Tall birch rise around you, holding bright\n<y>yellow<z> leaves aloft like flames on giant torches.  The ground is solid\nfrom the chilly weather, which feels like fall for most of the year.\nThe forest stretches in all directions and you cannot find the end\nof it.  A <b>stream<z> cuts through the forest to the west of here, running\nsouth to north.  A slight incline leads up to the east, and the forest\nis oddly quiet and seems hazy to the south.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23267,39,41,-2,'Arden Forest','  Your footsteps rustle the dried <o>orange<z> leaves that form a soft mat\non the forest floor.  Tall birch rise around you, holding bright\n<y>yellow<z> leaves aloft like flames on giant torches.  The ground is solid\nfrom the chilly weather, which feels like fall for most of the year.\nThe forest stretches in all directions and you cannot find the end\nof it.  An incline leads up to the northeast, and the forest\nis oddly quiet and seems hazy to the southwest.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23268,40,41,-2,'Arden Forest','  Your footsteps rustle the dried <o>orange<z> leaves that form a soft mat\non the forest floor.  Tall birch rise around you, holding bright\n<y>yellow<z> leaves aloft like flames on giant torches.  The ground is solid\nfrom the chilly weather, which feels like fall for most of the year.\nThe forest stretches in all directions and you cannot find the end\nof it.  An incline leads up to the north.  Some small mountains bound \nthe east side of the forest at bit farther in that direction.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23269,41,41,-2,'Arden Forest','  Your footsteps rustle the dried <o>orange<z> leaves that form a soft mat\non the forest floor.  Tall birch rise around you, holding bright\n<y>yellow<z> leaves aloft like flames on giant torches.  The ground is solid\nfrom the chilly weather, which feels like fall for most of the year.\nThe forest stretches in all directions and you cannot find the end\nof it.  An incline leads up to the north.  Some small mountains bound \nthe east side of the forest.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23270,32,40,-2,'Arden Forest','  Your footsteps rustle the dried <o>orange<z> leaves that form a soft mat\non the forest floor.  Tall birch rise around you, holding bright\n<y>yellow<z> leaves aloft like flames on giant torches.  The ground is solid\nfrom the chilly weather, which feels like fall for most of the year.\nThe forest stretches in all directions and you cannot find the end\nof it.  A rocky outcropping has formed in the short cliff to the west\nand curves around to the south.  It seems that someone has been using\nit for cover and has made a campsite there.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23271,33,40,-2,'Arden Forest','  Your footsteps rustle the dried <o>orange<z> leaves that form a soft mat\non the forest floor.  Tall birch rise around you, holding bright\n<y>yellow<z> leaves aloft like flames on giant torches.  The ground is solid\nfrom the chilly weather, which feels like fall for most of the year.\nThe forest stretches to the north and you cannot find the end of it.  To\nthe south though lies a hard wall of impassable rock and rubble as the the\nland climbs higher into the mountains.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23272,34,40,-2,'Arden Forest','  Your footsteps rustle the dried <o>orange<z> leaves that form a soft mat\non the forest floor.  Tall birch rise around you, holding bright\n<y>yellow<z> leaves aloft like flames on giant torches.  The ground is solid\nfrom the chilly weather, which feels like fall for most of the year.\nThe forest stretches to the north and you cannot find the end of it.  To\nthe south though lies a hard wall of impassable rock and rubble as the the\nland climbs higher into the mountains.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23273,35,40,-2,'Arden Forest','  Your footsteps rustle the dried <o>orange<z> leaves that form a soft mat\non the forest floor.  Tall birch rise around you, holding bright\n<y>yellow<z> leaves aloft like flames on giant torches.  The ground is solid\nfrom the chilly weather, which feels like fall for most of the year.\nTo the east you see a small <b>river<z> that cuts through the forest.\nThe forest stretches to the north and you cannot find the end of it.  To\nthe south though lies a hard wall of impassable rock and rubble as the the\nland climbs higher into the mountains.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23274,36,40,-2,'End of a <B>Stream<z> in Arden Forest','  A small but fast rushing stream of water flows from above into this \narea, and continues on to the east.  Birch trees in a perpetual state of \nautumn stretch to the north, east and to the west, their white bark set \noff by  the intense <o>orange<z> leaves.\n',166,131072,29,0,0,0,30,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23275,37,40,-2,'Bend in a Stream in Arden Forest','  A shallow <b>stream<z> of water flows from the west to the north here,\nwhere you can see it continues a northward path for some distance.  To \nthe east you see an unusual dark clearing in the woods.  Unfortunately,\nyou become quite waterlogged from the <b>stream<z> because while it is\nshallow, it is moving quite fast at this point in its journey.\n',166,131072,29,0,0,0,30,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23276,38,40,-2,'Strange Clearing in Arden Forest','  The healthy forest seems to withdraw itself from this place.  To the\nwest you see a fast moving <b>stream<z> that runs through the woods.  The \nground here is dry though, and a layer of soot covers it.  Even the air \nseems darker and hazy.  The forest stretches to the north and you cannot \nfind the end of it.  To the south though lies a hard wall of impassable \nrock and rubble as the the land climbs higher into the mountains.\n',166,131076,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23277,39,40,-2,'Arden Forest','  This is the southeast corner of the forest, and the birch trees are\ncut to an end by the edge of the some small mountains to the south,\nwhere a steep rock face juts out of the ground.  Small mosses grow in\nmoist crevices within the rock.  The forest stretches to the north and \nyou cannot find the end of it.  To the south though lies a hard wall of \nimpassable rock and rubble as the the land climbs higher into the mountains.\n\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23278,40,40,-2,'Arden Forest','  This is the southeast corner of the forest, and the birch trees are\ncut to an end by the edge of the some small mountains to the south,\nwhere a steep rock face juts out of the ground.  Small mosses grow in\nmoist crevices within the rock.  The forest stretches to the north and \nyou cannot find the end of it.  To the south though lies a hard wall of \nimpassable rock and rubble as the the land climbs higher into the mountains.\n\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23279,41,40,-2,'Arden Forest','  This is the southeast corner of the forest, and the birch trees are\ncut to an end by the edge of some small mountains to the south and\neast, where steep rock faces jut out of the ground.  Small mosses grow\nin moist crevices within the rock.  The forest stretches to the north and \nyou cannot find the end of it.  To the south though lies a hard wall of \nimpassable rock and rubble as the the land climbs higher into the mountains.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23280,42,44,-2,'Path Through Some Small Mountains','  You are just east of a <b>pond<z> on a trail that cuts through this\npart of a mountain range.  It seems that this small path was cut\nout of the cold rocks by a stream of water, yet only during hard\nrains will the <b>pond<z> to the west overflow enough to produce a\nsmall trickle of rainwater along this path.  The trail leads east\ntowards the coast.\n',166,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23281,43,44,-2,'Path Through Some Small Mountains','  You are on a cramped rocky path that cuts through a narrow part of\nthese small mountains.  After a rainstorm or when snow begins to\nmelt a small trickle of water will run down the grade along the trail\nfrom the west and falls down the steep grade here.  You can see that\nafter running down this precarious slope the trail leads east out\nonto a small beach.\n',166,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23282,43,44,-3,'Path Through Some Small Mountains','  A rocky trail leads up a steep and precarious slope here, and also\neast where can you see that it meets a beach.  The path has many\nsmall, sharp pebbles on it and seems to have been carved by water\nthat ran from uphill and down to the coast to the east.\n',166,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23283,45,44,-3,'Path Through Some Small Mountains','  The north and south borders of this small rocky trail are bounded\nby some cliffs of some small mountains, but water has carved\nthis small path that goes west and east.  To the west you see the\ntrail turn sharply uphill, but to the east you see the pale sands\nof a beach.\n',166,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23284,46,46,-3,'A Chilly Beach','  This is the north end of a small white sand beach.  The air is chilly\nyet the temperature does not fluctuate much during the year due to the\nproximity of the ocean and the protection from the wind provided by the\nmountains that surround the beach.  The soothing crash of the waves to\nthe east lulls you into peaceful thoughts.\n',166,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23285,46,45,-3,'A Chilly Beach','  This is a small white sand beach surrounded on the west side by rocky\ncliffs.  The air is chilly yet the temperature does not fluctuate much\nduring the year due to the proximity of the ocean and the protection\nfrom the wind provided by the mountains that surround the beach.  The\nsoothing crash of the waves to the east lulls you into peaceful thoughts.\nFarther to the east just visible through the mist which hangs over the sea\nis what remains of an old dock.  It would appear the water is not too deep\nbefore what remains of the dock can be accessed.\n',166,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23286,46,44,-3,'A Chilly Beach','  This is a small white sand beach surrounded on the west side by rocky\ncliffs.  The air is chilly yet the temperature does not fluctuate much\nduring the year due to the proximity of the ocean and the protection\nfrom the wind provided by the mountains that surround the beach.  The\nsoothing crash of the waves to the east lulls you into peaceful thoughts.\nA small trail has been cut through the cliffs to the west, and it leads\nup a sharp incline in the near distance.\n',166,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23287,46,43,-3,'A Chilly Beach','  This is the south end of a small white sand beach.  The air is chilly\nyet the temperature does not fluctuate much during the year due to the\nproximity of the ocean and the protection from the wind provided by the\nmountains that surround the beach.  The soothing crash of the waves to\nthe east lulls you into peaceful thoughts.\n',166,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23288,0,0,0,'A Weather-Beaten Shack','  The shack has been constructed from old wooden planks that have\npartially disintegrated from the salty air outside.  The soothing\ncrash of waves from outside calms your mind.  The decor of the\nshack is rather spartan, with little furniture and one one\nsmall window.  The floor creaks when you walk over it.\n',166,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,80,0,'',NULL),
(23289,31,43,-2,'A Path Through the Arden Foothills','  A leaf-strewn trail leads through a rocky protrusion out of the earth,\nstrolling west and east.  The west leads out into some foothills and\nfurther beyond them to the Haon-Dor forest.  To the east you see an\nentrance to Arden forest, with its tall stands of birch trees.  Arden\nis situated in a unique area of the realms where the weather is a\nperpetual autumn, and the leaves of the white-skinned trees flaunt this\nwith their orange and red leaves, bursting with color and energy.  Small\nferns grow in cracks of the rock faces on the sides of the trail.\n',166,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23290,31,40,-2,'Under a Rock Outcropping','  Someone has taken advantage of the natural protection under this\noutcrop in the rock face.  Signs of life are strewn around; ashes\nand coals, areas where leaves have been piled into makeshift beds,\nand some bones from eaten animals.  A few small ferns grow in\ncrevices in the rock.  You can see the tall birch trees of Arden\nforest outside.\n',166,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,10,76,0,'',NULL),
(23291,31,39,-2,'Under a Rock Outcropping','  Someone has taken advantage of the natural protection under this\noutcrop in the rock face.  Signs of life are strewn around; ashes\nand coals, areas where leaves have been piled into makeshift beds,\nand some bones from eaten animals.  A few small ferns grow in\ncrevices in the rock.  You can see the tall birch trees of Arden\nforest outside.\n',166,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,10,80,0,'',NULL),
(23292,32,39,-2,'Under a Rock Outcropping','  Someone has taken advantage of the natural protection under this\noutcrop in the rock face.  Signs of life are strewn around; ashes\nand coals, areas where leaves have been piled into makeshift beds,\nand some bones from eaten animals.  A few small ferns grow in\ncrevices in the rock and to the southeast one large mass seems to \nhave really taken root.  You can see the tall birch trees of Arden\nforest outside.\n',166,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,10,75,0,'',NULL),
(23293,38,44,-2,'Tree Spanning a Stream in Arden Forest','  This moss covered tree provides a dry path over the river below.  The\nsurface is slippery and the way treacherous, with the danger of falling\ninto the cold waters below always apparent.  At both the north and south\nend of the log stretches a massive birch forest.  The river flowing\nbelow finds its way to a pond visible down the gentle hill to the east.\n',166,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(23294,42,42,-2,'Spacious Cavern','  Carved into the rock about you the cavern apparently was once a natural\nformation which has been enlarged and made livable.  A thick screen of\nvegetation backed with cloth to hold it together is the only apparent exit\nto the room.  Markings and sketches adorn the smooth rock walls while\nvarious tables and other experimenting equipment have been firmly attached\nto the walls.  High overhead the blackness envelopes the air making it\nimpossible to see any further.\n',166,139592,33,0,0,0,0,-1,12,140,0,'',NULL),
(23300,0,0,0,'Dark Ant Tunnels','  The walls, floor, and low ceiling here are made of chunks loose dirt.\nThe tunnel is round in shape rather than square like most normal\nconstructions, which makes it somewhat difficult to walk, although the\nsoft nature of the floor aids in stabilizing your steps.  The darkness,\nbizarreness, and uniform nature of this tunnel system is confusing and\nyou are easily lost and disoriented.\n',129,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,12,85,0,'',NULL),
(23301,0,0,0,'Dark Ant Tunnels','  The walls, floor, and low ceiling here are made of chunks loose dirt.\nThe tunnel is round in shape rather than square like most normal\nconstructions, which makes it somewhat difficult to walk, although the\nsoft nature of the floor aids in stabilizing your steps.  The darkness,\nbizarreness, and uniform nature of this tunnel system is confusing and\nyou are easily lost and disoriented.\n',129,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,85,0,'',NULL),
(23302,0,0,0,'Gnome Fungus Farm','  The walls, floor, and low ceiling here are made of loose chunks of dirt.\nThe walls of the tunnel are extremely moist, and small clumps of fungus\nflourish on them.  The fungus is a deep brown color, and smells musty.\nThe way that the gnomes eat is very informal: when hungry, them simply\nfind their way to one of these fungus farms and pull some from a wall.\nFortunately the fungus grows quite quickly, so if a farm is completely\ndepleted of food it will restore itself rapidly.\n',129,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,85,0,'',NULL),
