(23379,0,0,0,'Gnome Fungus Farm','  The walls, floor, and low ceiling here are made of loose chunks of dirt.\nThe walls of the tunnel are extremely moist, and small clumps of fungus\nflourish on them.  The fungus is a deep brown color, and smells musty.\nThe way that the gnomes eat is very informal: when hungry, them simply\nfind their way to one of these fungus farms and pull some from a wall.\nFortunately the fungus grows quite quickly, so if a farm is completely\ndepleted of food it will restore itself rapidly.\n',129,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,85,0,'',NULL),
(23380,0,0,0,'The Queen Ant\'s Chamber','  The queen ant\'s chamber is quite impressive.  The ceiling here is a foot\nor two higher than in most of the tunnels that connect the chamber to the\nrest of the anthill complex.  Ant larvae are strewn throughout the room,\nand drone ants are constantly coming to bring food and trinkets from the\nsurface to their queen.\n',129,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23381,0,0,0,'The Queen Ant\'s Chamber','  The queen ant\'s chamber is quite impressive.  The ceiling here is a foot\nor two higher than in most of the tunnels that connect the chamber to the\nrest of the anthill complex.  Ant larvae are strewn throughout the room,\nand drone ants are constantly coming to bring food and trinkets from the\nsurface to their queen.\n',129,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
