(23783,0,56,-2,'Narrow Damp Tunnel','  This tunnel is barely wide enough for you to walk through.  The walls are\ncovered with a thick slimy substance.  All of a sudden a strong draft blows a\nblast of moist air in your face.  You can make out a dripping sound in the\ndistance.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23784,1,57,-2,'Narrow Damp Tunnel','  You are at the end of a narrow tunnel.  The walls are damp and in the distance\nyou can hear the sound of water dripping.  The tunnel continues to the\nsouthwest.  A trapdoor up leads out into the arena.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23785,-4,56,-2,'Smooth Tunnel','  You are in an underground tunnel about eight feet high and three feet wide.\nThe walls here are very smooth, appearing to be carved out rather than a\nnatural formation.  The air here is cool and crisp.  Darkness surrounds you.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23786,-4,57,-2,'Smooth Tunnel','  You are in an underground tunnel about eight feet high and three feet wide.\nThe walls here are very smooth, appearing to be carved out rather than a\nnatural formation.  The air here is cool and crisp.  Darkness surrounds you.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23787,-5,57,-2,'Smooth Tunnel','  You are in an underground tunnel about eight feet high and three feet wide.\nThe walls here are very smooth, appearing to be carved out rather than a\nnatural formation.  The air here is cool and crisp.  Darkness surrounds you.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23788,-5,58,-2,'Smooth Tunnel','  You are in an underground tunnel about eight feet high and three feet wide.\nThe walls here are very smooth, appearing to be carved out rather than a\nnatural formation.  The air here is cool and crisp.  Darkness surrounds you.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23789,-4,58,-2,'Smooth Tunnel','  You are in an underground tunnel about eight feet high and three feet wide.\nThe walls here are very smooth, appearing to be carved out rather than a\nnatural formation.  The air here is cool and crisp.  Darkness surrounds you.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23790,-4,59,-2,'Smooth Tunnel','  You are in an underground tunnel about eight feet high and three feet wide.\nThe walls here are very smooth, appearing to be carved out rather than a\nnatural formation.  The air here is cool and crisp.  Darkness surrounds you.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23791,-3,59,-2,'Smooth Tunnel','  You are in an underground tunnel about eight feet high and three feet wide.\nThe walls here are very smooth, appearing to be carved out rather than a\nnatural formation.  The air here is cool and crisp.  Darkness surrounds you.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23792,-2,60,-2,'Smooth Tunnel','  You have come to the end of the underground tunnel.  In front of you is a\nflat wall.  It is completely smooth and devoid of any markings.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23793,-1,60,-2,'Large Room','  This is a large room that has been carved into an underground cavern.  The\nceiling slopes up into a dome.  Thick brown carpeting covers the floor.  The\nroom looks like a nice place to stay, as well as looking very lived in.  To\nthe west a small crack in the cave wall leads into the tunnel.  Some writing\nhas been carved into the northern wall.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23794,0,60,-2,'Large Room','  The room here has a musty smell mixed with that of air freshener.  The room\nis nice and warm, feeling like a nice place to rest.  There is thick brown\ncarpeting covering the floor.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23795,-1,59,-2,'Large Room','  You have arrived at a sleeping area.  A small lamp illuminates the room with\na soft glow.  The floor is covered with thick, brown carpeting and assorted\ndecorations hang from the ceiling.\n',124,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23796,0,59,-2,'Large Room','  The floor here is frozen solid.  Several black spots are slowly fading away\nin the middle of the room, all that remains of some mystical gate.  Cold\nseems to emanate from the very center of this room and you feel a strong\nurge to get away.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23797,-1,58,-2,'Arena Vault','  You are in a cold stone vault.  It has been carved into an underground cavern\nand looks like a very safe place to store treasure.  A thick vault door set into\nthe northern wall bars unwanted entry.\n',124,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23798,0,48,-1,'The Arena Sharpening Shop','  You have entered the arena\'s local weapon sharpening shop.  This shop is always\nvery crowded before battles, as the gladiators are always sure to keep their\nweapons as sharp as possible.  In the back of the room is an enormous grinding\nwheel, to the side of it are several razor sharp blades.\n',124,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(23799,-6,48,-1,'The Arena Repair Shop','  This is the famous arena repair shop.  Countless stories have been told of\ndestroyed weapons and armor being restored to brand new quality at this shop.\nAs you look around at the neat, masterfully arranged repair shop, a sense of\nsafety overcomes you.  You realize that this would be the safest place to leave\nyour damaged equipment for the night.\n',124,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(24400,-18,-35,0,'The Main Gate of Gnath','  This is the main gate of the Gnomish town, Gnath.  This is a peaceful\ntown nestled in between two large hills.  The town lies to the south, and\nthe village outskirts are northward, through the gate.  West of here\npassage is blocked by numerous hills and dense forest regions while to the\neast the grounds drops off suddenly and you can just make out a shallow\npond below.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24401,-18,-36,0,'Intersection of Gnath Main and Gnorr Street','  Gnorr Street heads off to the east and west of here, and the main street of\nGnath leads off to the south toward the center of town.  The main gates are to\nthe north.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24402,-18,-37,0,'North Gnath Main','  You are standing on the northern part of the main street of Gnath.  The town\ngate is a little ways off to the north, and south heads off toward the center\nof town.  The bakery is in a building to your east, and the Gemcutters\' Guild\nis to the west.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24403,-18,-38,0,'North Gnath Main','  This is the main street in Gnath.  To the south, the village well can be\nseen.  The village schoolhouse shares a building with the gemcutters\' guild\nto the west.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24404,-18,-39,0,'The Town Well','  This is the center of the town of Gnath.  It is a popular community\ngathering place.  This is where the king\'s heralds deliver his special\nannouncements.  On special occasions the town chief will speak here by the\nwell.  Gnath Main heads off north toward the gate, and off to the south.\nGnee Street crosses from east to west here.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24405,-18,-40,0,'South Gnath Main','  This is the southern part of the main street in Gnath.  To the west is the\nsmith, and to the east is the small Gnath Inn.  To the north, you see the\ntown\'s well, which happens to be a popular meeting place.  Southward you see\nanother east-west street.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24406,-18,-41,0,'Intersection of Gnath Main and Gnickel Way','  This is the southernmost end of Gnath Main where it intersects with the\neast-west street, Gnickel Way.  There are some warrens built into the hill\nto the south.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24407,-19,-41,0,'Gnickel Way','  You are on Gnickel Way, right behind the metalsmith\'s workshop.  You hear\nthe loud clanking of a hammer hitting metal.  There is a wider road to your\neast, that travels northward through town.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24408,-20,-41,0,'Gnickel Way','  This part of Gnickel Way is right behind the tanner\'s workshop.  There is a\nlarge defensive wall made of stone that protects these peaceful citizens from\nall sorts of outside dangers.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24409,-21,-41,0,'Intersection of Gnobleman\'s Lane and Gnickel Way','  This appears to be the southwest corner of town.  The town\'s southern wall\nends where the western hill begins.  There is a big pile of rubble and rocks\nwhere the wall meets the hill.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24410,-17,-41,0,'Gnickel Way','  This part of the street is where it actually turns into a cave, and\nGnickel Way continues a little way as a tunnel in the eastern hill\'s side.\nTo the north, the toymaker\'s workshop is built into the hillside, but\nthere is no entrance on this side.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24411,-16,-41,0,'Gnickel Way','  Gnickel Way is under-ground here.  This part of the street is behind the\ngadgetmaker\'s workshop.  There is no entrance from this side.  This tunnel\nhas almost a dwarven quality to it.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,84,0,'',NULL),
(24412,-15,-41,0,'Intersection of Gnack Lane and Gnickel Way','  This is an underground intersection between two roads on the southeastern\npart of town.  The town temple is in a cavern to the southeast.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(24413,-17,-36,0,'Gnorr Street','  This is a smaller street on the northern end of town.  The town wall on the\nnorth side of the street, and the wall of a building is on the southern side of\nthe street.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24414,-16,-36,0,'Intersection of Gnorr Street and Gnack Lane','  This seems to be the northeastern part of town.  The sturdy town wall meets\nthe side of the eastern hill here.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24415,-19,-36,0,'Gnorr Street','  The town wall is on the northern side of this street, and the wall of a\nbuilding is on the southern end of this street.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24416,-20,-36,0,'Gnorr Street','  The town wall is on the north side of this street.  On the southern side\nis the town\'s schoolhouse.  There is no door to the schoolhouse here, but\nyou do see a small window.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24417,-21,-36,0,'Corner of Gnorr Street and Gnobleman\'s Lane','  This looks like it is the northwest corner of the town.  The town wall ends\nat the western hill.  There is a little pile of rocks and stones against the\nwall here, where it meets the hillside.  Gnorr Street leads off to the east and\nGnobleman\'s Lane heads south from here.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24418,-20,-39,0,'Gnee Street','  This is the main east-west street through the town of Gnath.  The ground\nis packed hard, and it is well travelled.  The schoolhouse is to the north,\nand the tanner is working in his workshop to the south.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24419,-19,-39,0,'Gnee Street','  This is the main east-west street through Gnath.  The ground is packed hard,\nand it is well travelled.  There is a schoolhouse to the north, and the town\'s\nmetalsmith owns a workshop to the south.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24420,-17,-39,0,'Gnee Street','  This is the main east-west street in Gnath.  On the south end of the\nstreet is the small Gnath Inn.  To the north you see the wall of the\nbakery kitchen.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24421,-16,-39,0,'Gnee Street','  This is the eastern end of Gnee Street.  The gadget-maker\'s workshop is to\nthe south of here.  There is a sign above the door.  A north-south street\ntakes a twist here.  The southern end of the street enters a cave to the east,\nand it continues on northward from here.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24422,-21,-37,0,'Gnobleman\'s Lane','  This street runs south along the western hill.  The schoolmaster\'s office\nis to the east, and the entrance to the Governor\'s Mansion opens to the\nwest.  Gnobleman\'s Lane continues off to the south and north of here.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24423,-21,-38,0,'Gnobleman\'s Lane','  Gnobleman\'s Lane follows along the western hill of the town.  There\nis a small schoolhouse to the east.  You can tell that part of the hill\nwas excavated to build this road.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24424,-21,-39,0,'T-Intersection of Gnee Street and Gnobleman\'s Lane','  This street was carved into the side of the western hill.  Gnobleman\'s Lane\ncontinues to the north and south from here, and Gnee Street goes to the east.\nThe Toymaker\'s Workshop has been built into the western hill.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24425,-21,-40,0,'Gnobleman\'s Lane','  You are on Gnobleman\'s Lane, near the southwestern corner of Gnath.  There\nare warrens built into the hillside to the west, and the tanner\'s workshop is\nto your east.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24426,-15,-40,0,'Gnack Lane','  Gnack Lane has been burrowed into the eastern hillside.  The gadget-maker\'s\nworkshop is directly to your west.  It appears to have been literally carved\ninto the rock and earth that is part of the eastern Hill.  It looks like a\ncombination between Dwarven and Gnomish engineering, with wooden supports and\nbeams combined with the Gnomish architecture.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(24427,-15,-39,0,'Gnack Lane','  Gnack Lane emerges from the hillside here, twisting to the northwest.  Gnee\nStreet also emerges here, and heads west toward the center of town.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,84,0,'',NULL),
(24428,-16,-38,0,'Gnack Lane','  This part of the road is more like an alley than a street.  The bakery\'s\nkitchen has a door that opens out here onto Gnack Lane.  It is ideally located\nright across from the town\'s grain storage room, which is built into the\nhillside to the east.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24429,-16,-37,0,'Gnack Lane','  This north-south street is on the east end of town.  It travels along side\nthe eastern hill.  This part of Gnack Lane is behind the Bakery.\n',140,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24430,-14,-42,0,'Entrance to the Temple','  This is the entrance to the temple of the town of Gnath.  This small church\nwas literally carved into the hillside.  The altar is to your southeast.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,102,0,'',NULL),
(24431,-14,-43,0,'A Small Temple','  This is the temple of the Gnome town of Gnath.  It looks like any other\nchurch, except this one is carved into a cavern.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(24432,-13,-42,0,'A Small Temple','  This is the temple of the Gnome town of Gnath.  It looks like any other\nchurch, except this one is carved into a cavern.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(24433,-13,-43,0,'The Temple Altar','  This is where the priest gives his sermons during mass.  There are steps that\nlead up to the altar, which is set a little bit away from the wall of the \ntemple.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(24434,-16,-40,0,'The Gadgetmaker\'s Workshop','  This is the town gadget maker\'s workshop.  Strange gadgets and machines\nclutter this small work area.  On the workbench sits a pile of springs,\nlevers, and other oddities.  Mounted on the wall is a strange object emitting\na ticking sound.\n',140,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24435,-17,-40,0,'Gnath Inn','  Small but cozy this little inn appears recently opened.  Its furnishings\nare cheap and sparse, but still tasteful.  A small desk sits before a tiny\ndoor behind which the inn\'s rooms are most likely located.  A fire burns\nwithin a small hearth along the south wall to warm the inns patrons.\n',140,164029,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,62,0,'',NULL),
(24436,-20,-40,0,'The Tanner\'s Workshop','  This is the tanner\'s workshop.  There are some leatherworking tools sitting\non the workbenches, and there are leather goods on shelves.\n',140,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24437,-19,-40,0,'The Metalshop','  The town smith works in this small shop.  The shelves are all neatly\norganized with various metal works.\n',140,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24438,-20,-37,0,'The Schoolmaster\'s Office','  This small office is where the schoolmaster does his paperwork.  The office\nis very neat and tidy.  On the wall you see a painting with a small caption.\n',140,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24439,-20,-38,0,'A Classroom','  This small classroom is where the older gnome children come to learn.\nComplex equations and symbols are written on a large slate board at the\nfront of the room.\n',140,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24440,-19,-38,0,'A Classroom','  This small classroom is filled with orderly rows of desks.  There is a flat\nboard at the front of the room with some writing on it.  This appears to be the\nclassroom where the younger gnomes come to learn.  There is another classroom\nto the west, and doors to the south and east exit out to the town streets.\n',140,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,65,0,'',NULL),
(24441,-19,-37,0,'The Gemcutters\' Guild','  This is where the master gemcutter teaches his pupils the fine art of\ngemcutting.  There are some complex tools in this room, used to cut complex,\nand beautiful gems.  A display case on the wall shows this guild\'s works.\n',140,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24442,-17,-37,0,'The Bakery','  This is the town bakery.  The counter is lined with fresh bread and\npastries.  Your mouth waters at the wonderful smells!\n',140,172217,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24443,-17,-38,0,'The Baker\'s Kitchen','  This is the kitchen where the Baker bakes his goods.  A beautiful aroma\nfills the room.  There are a few large ovens in which many breads and\npastries are being baked.\n',140,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24444,-15,-37,0,'A Grain Storage Room','  This is the grain storage room for the town of Gnath.  Many sacks of grain\nare piled in this large room.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24445,-14,-37,0,'A Grain Storage Room','  This is the grain storage room for the town of Gnath.  Many sacks of grain\nare piled in this large room.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24446,-15,-38,0,'A Grain Storage Room','  This is the grain storage room for the town of Gnath.  Many sacks of grain\nare piled in this large room.  Immediately to the west is a door that leads\nto the streets of Gnath.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(24447,-14,-38,0,'A Grain Storage Room','  This is the grain storage room for the town of Gnath.  Many sacks of grain\nare piled in this large room.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24448,-22,-37,0,'The Entrance of the Governor\'s Mansion','  This is the entrance to the governor\'s mansion of the town of Gnath.  This\nplace has been cut into the hillside.  A <r>red carpet<1> leads to the west, and\nthere is a door to the east which opens to the town streets.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,84,0,'',NULL),
(24449,-23,-37,0,'The Governor\'s Mansion','  This is the governor\'s mansion for the town of Gnath.  A long, narrow, <r>red\ncarpet<1> leads to the reception to the west, and to the exit to the east.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(24450,-24,-37,0,'The Reception','  This is the reception area for the governor\'s mansion.  It is so well\ndecorated that you almost forget that it is carved into a cavern.  The\ngovernor\'s office is to the south, and the treasurer\'s office is to the\nnorth.\n',140,131081,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,96,0,'',NULL),
(24451,-24,-38,0,'The Governor\'s Office','  This is the office of the Governor of Gnath.  This is where he performs all\nof his governing activities.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,72,0,'',NULL),
(24452,-24,-36,0,'The Treasurer\'s Office','  This is the office of the Treasurer of the town of Gnath.  The furniture\nis elaborate and the room is very nicely decorated.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,72,0,'',NULL),
(24453,0,0,0,'Escape Tunnel','This room was carved into the hillside, and offers an escape in the event of an\nattack from outside. There is a large pile of rocks to the north, and there are\nsigns of relatively recent masonry work to the south.\n',0,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,48,0,'',NULL),
(24454,-17,-38,1,'The End of a Long Tunnel','  This is the eastern end of a long, dark tunnel.  This secret tunnel was\ndesigned and constructed by the Gnome engineers from the town of Gnath so\nthat if the town was ever under serious attack, the citizens could escape\nto safety in the mountains to the west.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24455,-18,-38,1,'A Secret Escape Tunnel','  This secret escape tunnel is cramped and dark.  It travels east and west\nhere.  Gnome engineers from the town of Gnath constructed this tunnel as a\nmeans of escape in case the town is ever under serious attack.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24456,-19,-38,1,'A Secret Escape Tunnel','  This is a secret, east-west escape tunnel.  The Gnome engineers of Gnath\ndesigned it in case the town is ever under serious attack.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24457,-20,-38,1,'A Secret Escape Tunnel','  This small, dark east-west tunnel has a very low ceiling and cramped walls.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24458,-21,-38,1,'The End of a Long Tunnel','This is the end of a long, dark tunnel with very low ceilings.  There is\na small ladder mounted firmly to the west wall.\n',-1,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24459,-21,-38,2,'Inside a Windmill','  You are inside a windmill.  There are complex gears, cables, and belts\nall spinning and rotating in all different directions.  The floor is covered\nwith a thick layer of dust.  The rickety door on the west wall looks like\nit might fall off its hinges soon.\n',140,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,108,0,'',NULL),
(24460,-22,-38,2,'The Foothills','  You are in the foothills of the mountains overlooking a small city down\nto the east.  There is a windmill here, just east of you.  You can climb the\nmountain to the northeast.\n',140,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24461,-18,-34,2,'Steep Rocky Trail','  This extremely steep trail leads up to the mountains in the northwest, and\ndown to the foothills in the southwest.\n',140,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24462,-19,-33,2,'Rocky Mountain Trail','  This mountain trail ascends up a pass to the northwest, and heads down to\nthe foothills to the southeast.\n',140,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24463,-20,-32,2,'Mountain Pass','  This is a rocky mountain trail.  A mountain pass climbs up to the north,\nand the trail descends to the southeast.  You feel miniscule in comparison\nto the large mountain directly to the west.\n',140,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24464,-20,-31,2,'Mountain Pass','  You are high on a pass between two mountain peaks.  There is a peak to the\nnorth and another to the west.\n',140,131072,5,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24465,-22,-39,0,'The Toymaker\'s Workshop','  This workshop has many large pieces of equipment used in the art of\ntoymaking.  On the west wall, you see shelves of finished toys, ready to\nbe sent to the nearby towns of Brightmoon, Grimhaven, and Amber, where\nthey can be sold.  Workbenches line the rest of the walls, and they have\nworks in progress sitting on them.\n',173,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,62,0,'',NULL),
(24466,-23,-39,0,'Gnathan\'s Residence','  Recently built Gnathan\'s small home is both his residence as well as his\nworkshop.  This portion of the small home is where Gnathan lives when not\nworking on his beloved toys.  All about the room small trinkets and items\nGnathan acquired during his life as a trader can be seen.  Each is lovingly\ncared for and firmly secured to the walls.  Three overstuffed chairs sit\nbefore a small hearth where a fire is always burning.  It is here Gnathan\nenjoys sitting with his neice and nephew or other guests who drop in to say \nhi.  On the opposite side of the room is a small cookstove along with a \nkitchen table for his meals.  A secure looking door has been built into the \neastern wall which leads to Gnathan\'s workshop.  Within a shadowy alcove \nwithin the western wall another small door could easily be overlooked.\n',173,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,62,0,'',NULL),
(24467,-24,-39,0,'A Small Home','  Apparently setup for two occupants the little home is neat and tidy.\nOne side of the room has furnishings more suited to a young gnome woman\nwhile the other side is furnished with items more likely in the possession\nof a young gnome male.  A small hearth sits against the far wall and would\nseem to serve as both the kitchen and a place to relax.  Set in a shadowy\nalcove of the eastern wall is a door which could easily be overlooked.  \nThe main entrance to the small home is a door set within the southern wall.\n',173,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,62,0,'',NULL),
(24471,-22,-40,0,'Entrance to the Warrens','  This is the entrance to the west warrens in the Gnomish town of Gnath.  The\nwarrens continue in to the west, and the streets of the Gnath are to the east.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24472,-23,-40,0,'The Warrens','  You are in the west warrens of the town of Gnath.  There is a small home\nimmediately to the south.  The warrens continue on to the west.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24473,-24,-40,0,'The Warrens','  This is the warrens in the western side of the Gnome town of Gnath.  There\nis a small home to the south.  A <r>red banner<1> hangs on the north wall\nnext to a small door.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24474,-25,-40,0,'The Warrens','  These are the small western warrens in the town of Gnath.  There is a small\nhome directly to the south.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24475,-25,-41,0,'A Well-Decorated Home','  This is a small gnome home in the west warrens of the town of Gnath.  The\nhome is very tidy and well kept.  It is so well decorated that you are hardly\naware that this home is an underground cave.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24476,-24,-41,0,'A Tidy Home','  This small home is well kept and neatly organized.  The room is rather plain\nand very few decorations adorn the rock walls.  A <o>large rug<1> lies in the middle\nof the floor.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24477,-23,-41,0,'A Small Home','  This small home has a desk in the corner with many papers piled on it.\nThe occupants must either be explorers or cartographers, because various\nmaps are posted on the walls of this cave.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24478,-18,-42,0,'Entrance to the South Warrens','  This is the entrance to the southern warrens of town.  Many small homes\nare within the caverns to the south, and this cave opens out to Gnickel Way\nto the north.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24479,-18,-43,0,'The Warrens','  These are the southern warrens of town.  There are small homes to the east\nand west.  The entrance is immediately north, and the warrens continue to the\nsouth.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24480,-18,-44,0,'The Warrens','  Most of the living quarters in Gnath are located here in the south warrens.\nThere are homes to the east and west, and there are more to the south.  The\ncave also heads north where it opens up to Gnickel Way.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24481,-18,-45,0,'The Warrens','  The southern warrens are where the majority of the population of Gnath\nreside.  The small homes are built into the caverns in the hills.  There\nis a home to the east, and one to the west.  The southern warrens continue\nsouth from here.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24482,-18,-46,0,'The Warrens','  This is the very southernmost part of the town of Gnath.  There are small\nhomes to the west, south, and east, and the exit from the warrens is to the\nnorth.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(24483,-18,-47,0,'A Messy Home','  This small home is a mess!  There are dirty dishes scattered around on make-\nshift furniture, and there are clothes strewn about the floor.  Empty boxes\nand crates serve the purpose of tables and chairs.  The gnome who lives here\nobviously doesn\'t believe that neatness counts.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24484,-19,-46,0,'The Town Doctor\'s Home Office','  This is the home office of the town doctor.  This area serves as a\nliving room and a waiting room.  The rest of the warrens are to the\neast, an examination room is to the northwest, and the doctor\'s bedroom\nis to the southwest.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24485,-17,-46,0,'A Small Home','  This particular home is neatly organized, with many large oaken bookcases\nlining the walls.  The occupant of this home obviously spends a lot of time\nstudying.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24486,-20,-45,0,'The Examination Room','<W>  The walls of this tiny cavern have been painted white.  The exam room is\nan extension from the rest of the doctor\'s home.<1>\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24487,-20,-47,0,'The Doctor\'s Bedroom','  This is a small, simple bedroom where the doctor sleeps.  It is pretty\nbare.  The waiting room/living room is directly to the northeast.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24488,-19,-45,0,'A Fairly Large Home','  This large home has a higher ceiling than most of the other homes in the\nwarrens.  A <W>large snow leopard skin rug<1> rests in the middle of the room.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,66,0,'',NULL),
(24489,-17,-45,0,'A Tiny Home','  This is a very tiny home carved into the solid rock of the hills surrounding\nthe town.  The occupant of this home has made no effort to decorate this\nplace.  The walls are still dark gray, and there is a small mat before the\ndoor.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,56,0,'',NULL),
(24490,-19,-44,0,'A Trapper\'s Home','  This small home is well-decorated with many various furs and skins.  This\nmust be the home of a skilled trapper or ranger.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24491,-17,-44,0,'An Empty Home','  This small home is completely empty and the walls are totally bare.\nSomeone must have recently moved out of this home.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,58,0,'',NULL),
(24492,-19,-43,0,'<B>A Large Blue Home<1>','  This is a large home carved into the hillside in the south warrens of the\ntown of Gnath.  The <c>walls<1> are painted blue, and the <b>rugs and carpets<1> are a\ndeep, midnight blue.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,56,0,'',NULL),
(24493,-17,-43,0,'An Artist\'s Home','  The walls of this small home are covered with many paintings.  Ceramics are\nplaced throughout the room and on various pieces of furniture.\n',140,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,54,0,'',NULL),
(24494,-21,-37,2,'A Rocky Trail','  This rocky trail leads up the mountain to the northeast, and down to the\nsouthwest.\n',140,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24495,-20,-36,2,'A Rocky Trail','  This trail leads up the mountain to the northeast, and down the mountain\nto the southwest.\n',140,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24496,-19,-35,2,'A Steep Rocky Trail','  The trail here is pretty steep, and it looks like it gets worse to the\nnortheast.  The trail leads down the mountain to the southwest.\n',140,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24497,0,0,0,'In the Shaft of a Well','  The walls are clad in thick, clean tiles.  A gentle draft of fresh air blows\ndownward. The round, barreled shaft continues both above and below.  \n',184,131080,35,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(24498,0,0,0,'In the Shaft of a Well','  The walls are clad in thick, clean tiles.  A gentle draft of fresh air blows\ndownward. The round, barreled shaft continues both above and below.  \n',184,131080,35,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(24499,0,0,0,'At the Top of a Well Shaft','  Clean, thick tiles lines the walls of this circular shaft.  A gentle draft\nof fresh air blows downward.  The shaft makes a sheer descent into the dampness\nbelow. \n',184,131080,35,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(24675,0,0,0,'A Small Game Path','A small dirt trail shoots off from here into the southern forest, fading and\nsometimes disappearing altogether.  It leaves a path only a ranger could follow.\nSeveral trees have been cut down here, and there are many logs piled together. \nThe vegetation here seems less affected by the malady present throughout the\nnorthern forest, yet there is a profound silence here that causes the area to\nfeel even more devoid of life.\n',-1,131072,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24676,0,0,0,'A Small Hut','This simple hut was crudely built, but has been furnished and made into a home.\nA large, comfortable looking stuffed chair rests in a corner, and a small teapot\nhangs from a metal bracket over a cheerful fire in the center of the room. Attached to the walls are shelves stocked full of potions, scrolls, and other assorted items.\n',-1,174489,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(24677,0,0,0,'A Dark Forest','A fell wind rustles through the trees, carrying with it the stench of decay.\nDead leaves and fallen branches litter the ground. The normal signs of life\nexpected to be seen in the wilderness are nowhere to be found, and even the\ntrees seem dead. The forest growth has become thick here, leaving little more\nthan a trail through the forest.\n',-1,139264,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24678,0,0,0,'A Dark Forest','A fell wind rustles through the trees, carrying with it the stench of decay.\nDead leaves and fallen branches litter the ground.  The normal signs of life\nexpected to be seen in the wilderness are nowhere to be found, and even the\ntrees seem dead.  The undergrowth in this area causes the eastern part of the\nforest to become inaccessible.\n',-1,139264,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24679,0,0,0,'A Dark Forest','A fell wind rustles through the trees, carrying with it the stench of decay.\nDead leaves and fallen branches litter the ground.  The normal signs of life\nexpected to be seen in the wilderness are nowhere to be found, and even the\ntrees seem dead.  The undergrowth in this area causes there to be little more\nthan a path through this part of the forest.  A small drawbridge provides\npassage across a ravine to the northeast, and a small hut can be seen on the\nother side.\n',-1,139264,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24680,0,0,0,'A Dark Forest','A fell wind rustles through the trees, carrying with it the stench of decay.\nDead leaves and fallen branches litter the ground.  The normal signs of life\nexpected to be seen in the wilderness are nowhere to be found, and even the\ntrees seem dead.  The forest undergrowth becomes thick here, and completely\nimpassable to the north.\n',-1,139264,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24681,0,0,0,'A Small Clearing','The trees part here, opening into a wide, almost perfect circle.  It is as if\nthe trees avoid this small area.  The only thing that grows here is a thick,\nlustrious green grass.  Light and life touch this part of the forest, and if not\nfor its dark surroundings, it would be a place where elven children might play. \nThere is a sense of peace here, as if something holy and glorious had been done\nhere long ago.\n',-1,172469,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24682,0,0,0,'A Dark Forest','A fell wind rustles through the trees, carrying with it the stench of decay.\nDead leaves and fallen branches litter the ground.  The normal signs of life\nexpected to be seen in the wilderness are nowhere to be found, and even the\ntrees seem dead.  The trees and undergrowth are thick here, barring all passage\nto the south.\n',-1,139264,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24683,0,0,0,'A Dark Forest','A fell wind rustles through the trees, carrying with it the stench of decay.\nDead leaves and fallen branches litter the ground.  The normal signs of life\nexpected to be seen in the wilderness are nowhere to be found, and even the\ntrees seem dead.  Several trees have been cut down here, and there are many logs\npiled together.\n',-1,139264,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24684,0,0,0,'A Dark Forest','A fell wind rustles through the trees, carrying with it the stench of decay.\nDead leaves and fallen branches litter the ground. The normal signs of life expected to be seen in the wilderness are nowhere to be found, and even the trees seem dead.\n  \nThe trees have become extremely thick here, barring all passage to the\nsouth. \n',-1,139264,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24685,0,0,0,'A Dark Forest','A fell wind rustles through the trees, carrying with it the stench of decay.\nDead leaves and fallen branches litter the ground.  The normal signs of life\nexpected to be seen in the wilderness are nowhere to be found, and even the\ntrees seem dead.  A thick stand of trees and shrubs bar passage to the east,\nhowever, what looks to be a small clearing can be seen on the other side.\n',-1,139264,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24686,0,0,0,'A Dark Forest','A fell wind rustles through the trees, carrying with it the stench of decay.\nDead leaves and fallen branches litter the ground.  The normal signs of life\nexpected to be seen in the wilderness are nowhere to be found, and even the\ntrees seem dead.  The western part of the forest is dense here, and all passage\nin that direction becomes impossible.\n',-1,139264,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24687,0,0,0,'A Dark Forest','A fell wind rustles through the trees, carrying with it the stench of decay.\nDead leaves and fallen branches litter the ground.  The normal signs of life\nexpected to be seen in the wilderness are nowhere to be found, and even the\ntrees seem dead.  The forest undergrowth becomes thick here, and completely\nimpassable to the north.\n',-1,139264,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24688,0,0,0,'A Dark Forest','A fell wind rustles through the trees, carrying with it the stench of decay.\nDead leaves and fallen branches litter the ground. The normal signs of life\nexpected to be seen in the wilderness are nowhere to be found, and even the\ntrees seem dead. An earthworks has been contructed here, leaving little more\nthan barren ground and fingers of bleached wood rising up out of the earth.\n',-1,139264,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24689,0,0,0,'The Lair of a Werewolf','  The walls of this section of the cave are covered with large claw marks.\nSmall patches of fur lie here and there near a huge pile of bleached white\nbones.  Dark blood stains on the floor leave clear evidence that something with\na massive appetite returns here, often, to feed upon freshly killed prey.  From\nthe size of the bite marks on some of the bones, it must be a very large\ncreature.  Towards the back of the cave, there seems to be some sort of crevice\nleading out, but it is covered by an earthworks of some kind.\n\n\n',-1,139272,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(24690,0,0,0,'A Small Cave','Here the cave rounds off in a semi-circle. The walls are quite smooth, and the\nfloor is hard packed dirt. Roots cover the ceiling like spiderwebs and a few\nalmost touch the ground.\n',-1,139272,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(24691,0,0,0,'A Small Cave','The passage through the cave continues on and splits off in three directions.\nLarge drag marks on the floor indicate that a fair sized object or animal was\nhauled through here recently. Dark blood stains are splattered across the floor,\nleaving a trail to the east.\n',-1,139272,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(24692,0,0,0,'A Small Cave','From here the cave branches off in two directions. Moving through the room,\nhowever, proves slightly difficult as it seems a part of the cave has collapsed\nto the north. Large boulders and small rocks are scattered on the floor. Roots\ncover the ceiling like spiderwebs and a few almost touch the ground.\n',-1,139272,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(24693,0,0,0,'A Small Cave','A rather diminutive cave has been carved out of the earth here. The walls are\nworn and have been smoothed by time, but there are scratches and claw marks on\nthe ground that look fairly recent. Small leaves and assorted foliage fall to the floor from above every so often. The cave branches off here to the east and\nsoutheast.\n',-1,139272,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(24694,0,0,0,'A Dead Section of Forest','This part of the forest is by far the most decayed, as if the root of this\nsickness lay nearby. The fog shifts and moves here, as if alive, and desiring\nnothing more than to consume everything in its path. Heavy foliage covers the\nground, and further passage through this area is barred by the thick deadwood\nlying in ruins all about.\n',-1,131072,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24695,0,0,0,'A Dead Section of Forest','Some mysterious malady has caused this part of the forest to wither and die.\nBeautiful trees lived here once, but now all that remain are the stark white\nempty shells of deadwood rising up out of the ground. The mist gathers thickly\nhere, forming into an ominous fog.\n',0,131080,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(24696,0,0,0,'A Dead Section of Forest','Some mysterious malady has caused this part of the forest to wither and die.\nBeautiful trees lived here once, but now all that remain are the stark white\nempty shells of deadwood rising up out of the ground. The mist gathers thickly\nhere, forming into an ominous fog.\n',-1,131072,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24697,0,0,0,'A Dead Section of Forest','Some mysterious malady has caused this part of the forest to wither and die.\nBeautiful trees lived here once, but now all that remain are the stark white\nempty shells of deadwood rising up out of the ground. The mist gathers thickly\nhere, forming into an ominous fog. Several of the most rotted trees have\ncollapsed upon themselves, creating a huge pile of deadwood, barring the way\nsouth.\n',-1,131072,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24698,0,0,0,'A Dead Section of Forest','Some mysterious malady has caused this part of the forest to wither and die.\nBeautiful trees lived here once, but now all that remain are the stark white\nempty shells of deadwood rising up out of the ground. The mist gathers thickly\nhere, forming into an ominous fog.\n',-1,131072,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24699,0,0,0,'A Dead Section of Forest','Some mysterious malady has caused this part of the forest to wither and die.\nBeautiful trees lived here once, but now all that remain are the stark white\nempty shells of deadwood rising up out of the ground. The mist gathers thickly\nhere, forming into an ominous fog.\n',0,131072,66,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24700,0,0,0,'A Swamp\'s Edge','  Patches of thick-bladed grass grow here and there in the muck, churned up\ninto decaying heaps in many places.  Tracks tell of the comings and goings \nof many creatures.  Dank and fetid air wafts from a seemingly impenetrable\nforest of twisted, vine-covered trees to the north.\n',183,131072,50,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24701,0,0,0,'A Hot and Humid Swamp','  Huge, vine-strangled trees loom overhead, and the thick mist that swirls\nabout their trunks obscures the ground.  The heavy air is laden with the scent\nof decaying vegetation.\n',183,131072,50,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24702,0,0,0,'A Stagnant Pool in a Swamp','  Huge, vine-strangled trees loom overhead, and the thick mist that swirls\nabout their trunks obscures the ground.  The heavy air is laden with the scent\nof decaying vegetation.  Sporadic burbling sounds draw attention to\noccasional large bubbles that burst when they reach the surface film\nof this stagnant pool.\n',183,131072,52,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24703,0,0,0,'A Stagnant Pool in a Swamp','  Huge, vine-strangled trees loom overhead, and the thick mist that swirls\nabout their trunks obscures the ground.  The heavy air is laden with the scent\nof decaying vegetation.  Sporadic burbling sounds draw attention to\noccasional large bubbles that burst when they reach the surface film\nof this stagnant pool.\n',183,131072,52,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
