(24792,0,0,0,'A Dark Cavern','  This cavern has been carved out of the dirt to allow secrecy\nin the rituals of the shaman that inhabit the small village\nabove the surface. The floor has been packed with stones to \nprovide a more solid walking surface.\n',180,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(24793,0,0,0,'A Dark Cavern','  This cavern has been carved out of the dirt to allow secrecy\nin the rituals of the shaman that inhabit the small village\nabove the surface. The floor has been packed with stones to \nprovide a more solid walking surface.\n',180,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(24794,0,0,0,'A Dark Passageway','  The dirt has been carved away to build this passageway. The walls\nof the passage have small vine-like roots exposed and the dirt is \npacked hard for the most strength. The floor of the passage has had\nsmall stones embeded into the dirt to provide a more solid walkway.\n',180,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(24795,0,0,0,'A Dark Passageway','  The dirt has been carved away to build this passageway. The walls\nof the passage have small vine-like roots exposed and the dirt is \npacked hard for the most strength. The floor of the passage has had\nsmall stones embeded into the dirt to provide a more solid walkway.\n',180,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(24796,0,0,0,'A Dark Passageway','  The dirt has been carved away to build this passageway. The walls\nof the passage have small vine-like roots exposed and the dirt is \npacked hard for the most strength. The floor of the passage has had\nsmall stones embeded into the dirt to provide a more solid walkway.\nA wooden panel embeded between the walls blocks further passage \nnorthward.\n',180,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(24797,0,0,0,'A Dark Passageway','  The dirt has been carved away to build this passageway. The walls\nof the passage have small vine-like roots exposed and the dirt is \npacked hard for the most strength. The floor of the passage has had\nsmall stones embeded into the dirt to provide a more solid walkway.\nA wooden panel blocks exit to the south while dirt walls block\npassage in all other directions.\n',180,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(24798,0,0,0,'A Dark Room Carved in the Dirt','This small room has been decorated with colored stones embedded\ninto the packed dirt walls and floor. The colors of the stones form\na barrier to protect the houngans that use the altar contained in\nthe room. Small traces of blood stain the colored stones on the floor.\nA small curtain of beads provide an exit to this room.\n',0,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(24799,0,0,0,'A Dark Passageway','  The dirt has been carved away to build this passageway. The walls\nof the passage have small vine-like roots exposed and the dirt is \npacked hard for the most strength. The floor of the passage has had\nsmall stones embeded into the dirt to provide a more solid walkway.\n',180,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,80,0,'',NULL),
(24800,0,0,0,'East King\'s Way','This is a wide street which slopes gently downwards as it runs to the east.\nThe gates of the palace have been ruined and lie here lying here on ground.\nTo the north is the smoking remains of the once proud royal palace.\nTo the south, a path leads into a beautiful park.\n',106,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24801,0,0,0,'Burnt Lawn','You are amongst the rubble of the palace.  An archway has crumbled to the\nnorth almost blocking the way.  Huge stone blocks and crushed statues\nlitter the lawn.\n',106,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24802,0,0,0,'Ruined Entrance','You are standing amongst the smoldering remains of the palace.  Walls\nhave crumbled from the heat of the previous fire.  All around you huge blocks\nof stone are lying like a child\'s building blocks.  To the south the arch has\ncollapsed to rubble.  The path to the north is fairly clear.\n',106,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24803,0,0,0,'Ruins','This was once a large foyer.  Now only burnt decorations and crumbled walls\nremain.  Only the wall to the west survived the fire without falling.\n',106,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24804,0,0,0,'Ruins','This was once a tiny alcove.  Now it is filled with rubble of the ruined\ncastle.  The walls of the alcove are surprisingly erect and not badly burned.\n',106,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24805,0,0,0,'Staircase','You are at the base of a large staircase.  The supporting walls seem to\nhave kept it from crumbling.  Though the stairs remain standing they do\nnot appear to be safe.\n',106,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24806,0,0,0,'Top of the Stairs','This is the top of the staircase.  From this vantage point you can see\nthe destruction the fire has wrought on the palace.  Of the once mighty\nstructure, this is the highest point still to survive the destruction.\nRocks shift between your weight as bits of stone break off and fall into\nthe rubble below.\n',106,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24807,0,0,0,'North Main Street','This is a well maintained, north-south road running through a large city.\nTo the east is a small path leading to the ruins of the palace.  To the west\nyou see a large church.\n',106,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24808,0,0,0,'Ruins','This was once a servant\'s walkway.  Now it is filled with rubble and soot.\nThe walls are still standing but have been filled with rubble from the\nfloors above\n',106,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(24809,0,0,0,'Rubble','Empty\n',106,131072,60,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25250,-49,-9,0,'A Wagon Rutted Trail Through the Prairie','  Deep ruts cover the prairie here, the product of countless caravans\nof wagons that have passed this way.  The scars of the numerous\nwagon wheels show the direction of the main trail across the prairie.\nAlthough there is plant growth in the ruts, the indentations made by\nthe wheels are still quite visible leading northwest and southeast.  The\ntrail leads across a metal grate through a fence to the southeast.\n',138,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25251,-50,-8,0,'A Wagon Rutted Trail Through the Prairie','  Deep ruts cover the prairie here, the product of countless caravans\nof wagons that have passed this way.  The scars of the numerous\nwagon wheels show the direction of the main trail across the prairie.\nAlthough there is plant growth in the ruts, the indentations made by\nthe wheels are still quite visible leading northwest and southeast.\n',138,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
