(25290,-51,-9,0,'Surrounded by Prairie','  Thick lush prairie lies in every direction.  Various assorted\nwildflowers and prairie grasses are scattered about along the\nground.  Small patches of worn prairie dot the landscape, the result\nof the grazing animals that use this area to feed.  The vegetation\nflourishes all around.  A campsite is northwest.\n',138,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25291,-50,-9,0,'Surrounded by Prairie','  Thick lush prairie lies in every direction.  Various assorted\nwildflowers and prairie grasses are scattered about along the\nground.  Small patches of worn prairie dot the landscape, the result\nof the grazing animals that use this area to feed.  The vegetation\nflourishes all around.\n',138,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25292,-55,-10,0,'Junction of Fences','  Lush prairie lies all around.  Aside from a glimmer of a distant\nwheat field, and a tower off in the distance, the prairie around\nyou seems to stretch forever.  A well constructed fence, joined\nby a large, sturdy post, connects here.  The fences which stretch\none direction to the north and another direction to the east have\ntiny speckles of white on them.\n',138,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25293,-54,-10,0,'Near a Field of Wheat','  Far to the south a field of wheat sways back and forth with\nthe wind.  It is amazing it can stay upright.  Each\nindividual plant is bursting with copious vegetation.\nA well placed fence blocks your passage south.  The fence is\nmade up of split rails and bears witness to the harsh weather\nthat this area is known for.  Built to keep the grazing animals\naway from the rich harvest, this fence looks capable of doing\njust that.  Aside from the wheat, the only other thing you can\nsee is a lush prairie.\n',138,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25294,-53,-10,0,'Near a Field of Wheat','  Far to the south a field of wheat sways back and forth with\nthe wind.  It is amazing it can stay upright.  Each\nindividual plant is bursting with copious vegetation.\nA well placed fence blocks your passage south.  The fence is\nmade up of split rails and bears witness to the harsh weather\nthat this area is known for.  Built to keep the grazing animals\naway from the rich harvest, this fence looks capable of doing\njust that.  Aside from the wheat, the only other thing you can\nsee is a lush prairie.\n',138,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25295,-52,-10,0,'Near a Field of Wheat','  Far to the south a field of wheat sways back and forth with\nthe wind.  It is amazing it can stay upright.  Each\nindividual plant is bursting with copious vegetation.\nA well placed fence blocks your passage south.  The fence is\nmade up of split rails and bears witness to the harsh weather\nthat this area is known for.  Built to keep the grazing animals\naway from the rich harvest, this fence looks capable of doing\njust that.  Aside from the wheat, the only other thing you can\nsee is a lush prairie.\n',138,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25296,-51,-10,0,'Near a Field of Wheat','  Far to the south a field of wheat sways back and forth with\nthe wind.  It is amazing it can stay upright.  Each\nindividual plant is bursting with copious vegetation.\nA well placed fence blocks your passage south.  The fence is\nmade up of split rails and bears witness to the harsh weather\nthat this area is known for.  Built to keep the grazing animals\naway from the rich harvest, this fence looks capable of doing\njust that.  Aside from the wheat, the only other thing you can\nsee is a lush prairie.\n',138,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25297,-50,-10,0,'Near a Field of Wheat','  Far to the south a field of wheat sways back and forth with\nthe wind.  It is amazing it can stay upright.  Each\nindividual plant is bursting with copious vegetation.\nA well placed fence blocks your passage south.  The fence is\nmade up of split rails and bears witness to the harsh weather\nthat this area is known for.  Built to keep the grazing animals\naway from the rich harvest, this fence looks capable of doing\njust that.  Aside from the wheat, the only other thing you can\nsee is a lush prairie.\n',138,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25298,-49,-10,0,'Junction of Fences','  Tiny bits of rock lie all around.  To the northwest is a lush\nprairie and to the east a unbroken chain of mountains looms.  The\nfences to the east and south are joined here by a sturdy post\nwith some strange writings on it.  Far to the south you can see\na vast field of wheat that sways back and forth with the wind.\n',138,131072,20,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25299,0,0,0,'Inside a tent','  The inside of this tent is furnished with nothing more than a sleeping\nbag and a lantern.  Made of a brown canvas, and weathered\nby the hot sun by day and the dew by night, a faint mix\nof campfire and mildew wafts through your nose.  A moth\nhas eaten a hole through the side of the tent, which gives\nyou a good view of the outside surroundings.\n',138,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(25400,3,-1,0,'Park Entrance','  The road begins to widen and slope downward towards a hillside.  Bright\ntangled flower beds made up of daisies, jasmine and sage brush tremble lightly\nin the breeze.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25401,4,-1,0,'Road Through Park','   The hillside flourishes with vegetation.  Grass grows in thick here,\nplush green.  Tiny rows of flower beds extend all around you, emitting the\nair with a sweet smelling scent.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25402,1,-2,0,'Road Through Park','   The hillside here is plush green and carries the scent of the many\nwildflowers that bloom here.  Just south of you, a small play ground is seen.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25403,1,-5,0,'Southwest Corner','  The hillside flourishes with bright wildflowers that bloom\nin every direction.  A small oak tree grows within the tall lush\ngrass here.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25404,2,-1,0,'Road Through Park','   Small wild flowers tremble lightly from a small gust of wind that blows\nin from the east.  The grass has grown in thick here which makes the underbrush\ncrackle slightly beneath your feet.  To the south you notice a small cabin by a\nlarge Oak tree.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25405,1,-3,0,'Playground','   You\'ve come across a small playground that lies among the wilted dried\nlandscape.  The grass that once grew here has turned brown and brittle.  A\nseesaw that once delighted small children has collapsed to the ground, broken\nin two.  Small pieces of metal that were once the monkey bars now rest at your\nfeet and a small sandbox lays filled with refuge and debris.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25406,2,-2,0,'Cabin in the Park','   A small run-down cabin is here wasting away.  The cabin itself looks rather\nodd since its made from a variety of timber such as pine, oak and cedar.  A door\ncan be seen here leading into the cabin and a ladder leads up into a large tree just beside the cabin.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25407,2,-2,1,'Tree House','   A run down tree house looks to have been vacant for a long time.  Dust\nrises off the rotted floor boards as you make your way through the cramped\nquarters.  Small wooden toys and cloth made dolls dressed in rags can be seen\nhere, obviously this was once a place where children frequently visited.  What\nnow remains is retreat for small bugs and rodents.\n',128,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25408,2,-3,0,'Broken Down Cabin','   Long ago this cabin was once part of the park\'s recreational use.\nWhat once rested upon the polished bookshelves now sits at your feet, burnt\nand illegible.  A map of the town of Grimhaven pinned to the south wall has\nfaded away.\n',128,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,84,0,'',NULL),
(25409,1,-4,0,'Road Through Park','   The road here evens out and extends in every direction.  Here you can see\ncobblestone within grass, though cracked on faded, it still serves as an easier\npath to travel on other then the dirt path.  Small sparrows and wild dogs roam\nthe park, it seems to be a safehaven for all the animals that wander into\nGrimhaven.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25410,2,-5,0,'Cobblestone Path','  Oak trees tower some ten feet above you here in the park with wide\nspreading branches.  Birds chirp above the treeline and a faded cobblestone path\nleads in every direction through the underbrush.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25411,2,-4,0,'Cobblestone Path','   Tall Oak trees grow here along the plush green grass that stems no\nhigher then your calf.  The cobblestone is barely visible under its thick\nunderbrush.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25412,3,-5,0,'Cobblestone Path','   Tall Oak trees and small bushes grow here along the plush green grassy\nsurface.  The grounds are well kept and fresh plots of flowers have been\nweeded recently.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25413,4,-5,0,'Cobblestone Path','  The trees thicken here which gives this path a tropical look.  The\ngrass here is a deep cyan color, it confuses you for a moment.\nWhy this particular shade?  A cobblestone path leads in all directions.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25414,5,-5,0,'Southeast Corner','  You\'ve come to the southeast end of the park.  Several large oak trees,\ntower above you and encircle a small glass gazebo.  The trees themselves\nare not as old as the elm tree that stands in the northwest corner but\nalmost as old.  Hundreds of wild flowers perfume the air here that seem to\nbloom year round.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,10,10,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25415,3,-4,0,'Cobblestone Path','   Massive Oak tree take shape here within the thick underbrush of the\npark.  A cobblestone path, though chipped and faded from use still serves\nas a better route to travel on other then the precarious footholes the park\nhas.  Bright wild flowers dot the landscape.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25416,4,-4,0,'Cobblestone Path','Massive Oak trees with wide spreading tops branch outwards over the many\nwildflowers here.  A cobblestone path leads in all directions.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25417,3,-3,0,'Cobblestone Path','   The grounds here are well kept, the grass has been cut back evenly\nand small plots of flowers have been recently weeded.  The trees have\nbeen trimmed back slightly and shaped creating just the right amount of\nshade.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25418,3,-2,0,'Cobblestone Path','  This is a peacefull spot dotted with flowers and shaded by many trees.\nA large rock formation bulges out of the park\'s thick underbrush.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25419,4,-2,0,'Cobblestone Path','  This spot is dotted with many wildflowers and shaded by trees.  The thick\nunderbrush now reaches up to your knees, if it were not for the cobblestone it\nwould probably slow you down.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25420,5,-1,0,'Northeast Corner','  Wildflowers scatter themselves within the thick foliage of leaves thats\nsettled on the ground.  A cobblestone paths lead south and southwest.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25421,4,-4,-1,'Garden Path','Tall hedges and thickets make this path a tight fit.  The path\nleads in all directions.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,2,87,0,'',NULL),
(25422,5,-2,0,'Mallards Rest','  You\'ve come across a soft glade of plush green grass that ends\nbefore a stone wall.  A willow tree rests here next to a flowerbed\nof wildflowers.  There is a strange silence in the air.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25423,5,-3,0,'Garden Path','  Fresh lawn carpets the path.  A clutter of tall thickets make\nyour passage a tight fit.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25424,4,-3,0,'Gardens Gateway','  The path runs smoothly over a small glade of soft grass dotted with\nwildflowers.  Centered in the glade surrounded by a painted circle of stones\nrest a shrubbery of an Ogre wielding a very large axe.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25425,5,-3,-1,'Garden Path','This spot is filled with large sculpted shrubberies of\nwhat looks like mighty warriors dualing within a circle of brightly\npainted stones.  Underground, the garden shifts its form from a\nbeautiful park to a dark cavern.  Corridors lead in every direction.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25426,1,-1,0,'Northwest Corner','   An ancient Elm tree stands here atop the underbrush that rustles at\nyour feet.  Wildflowers dot the glade\'s landscape and a wooden ladder leads up\ninto the tree\'s branches.  A large dark hole leads down just beneath the Elm.\n',128,131073,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25427,5,-2,1,'Above the Willows treetop','   The thick foliage of the trees canopy makes it difficult to see outward.\nYou can hear the townsfolk just north of you.  Below you spot something\nmetal along the base of the tree.\n',128,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25428,1,-2,1,'Above a Treetop','   Many branches reach upward and out here.  Just to the west you can see South\nMain Street busy with activity.  Sparrows chip madly, filling the air with a\nsymphony of their own.\n',128,131073,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25429,5,-5,-1,'Garden Path','A tall dead oak tree stands within the dried crust of the\nsurface floor.  Devil weeds grow in clumps near a defined\nshrubbery of an Orc guard.  A circle of bright colored stones\ncan be seen here that round sculpture of the image.\n',128,131112,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25430,5,-4,-1,'Garden\'s Path','  You are standing on a dark path where devilweeds grow from the\ndried crust of the surface floor.  A large fountain can be seen here.\n',128,164008,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25431,4,-5,-1,'Garden Path','A constant warm breeze that enters from the east gently brushes\nagainst the devil weeds that flourish over this path.  Here, a wilted\nwillow tree embraces the shoulders of a defined shrubbery.  Small\nwebs cover the shrubbery\'s head and a ring of black stones encircle it.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25432,3,-5,-1,'Garden Path','Along the gardens path you come across another sculpted shrubbery\nof a unicorn that poses in the northeast corner.  The devil weed\ngrows in thick here within the dried crust of the surface floor.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25433,1,-4,1,'Above a Treetop','   Balancing yourself along the treetop you can see the park infested\nwith wild life and bright vibrant flowers.  The perch of the tree limb would\nbe a perfect spot to sit in and daydream all day if it were not for the\nconstant barkings of the wild dogs.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25434,1,-5,1,'Above a Treetop','   Standing on a thick tree limb, you can\'t make out anything through the\ncluster of leaves that block your view.\n',128,132104,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25435,2,-5,-1,'Garden Path','The garden opens wide here.  Dead oak trees stand within the\ndried crust surface of the garden\'s path and devil weeds sprout\nin patches.  Encased in a bright colored circle of stones rests\na shrubbery of a fierce looking wolf.  A wooden bridge crosses here.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25436,1,-5,-1,'Dead End','You have come to a dead end where devil weeds spawn from\nthe dried crust of the surface floor.  A large hole is here leading\ndown.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,1,100,0,'',NULL),
(25437,2,-4,-1,'Shang\'ry Crossing','Standing on the wooden bridge you notice that it arches upward\nslightly giving you a clear view all around.  The bridge leads\nnorth and south towards the park\'s garden.\n',128,131084,22,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(25438,2,-3,-1,'Garden Path','The garden opens widely here revealing a perfect spot to rest in.\nDevil weeds grow between the cracks of the hard surface floor and\na Shrubbery of a Cyclops sits centered in a round circle of stones.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25439,4,-1,1,'Above a Treetop','   From here you see the park stretch a short distance in Grimhaven.  A light\nbreeze gently brushes against you which blows in from the southeast.\n',128,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25440,3,-2,-1,'Garden Path','Devil weed grows here scattered in clumps along the dried surface\nfloor.  A sculpted form of an Amber guard sits centered within a\ncircle of stones here.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25441,2,-2,-1,'Gardens Path','The garden is overrun with devil weed.  Centered within the thick\nunderbrush in a circle of stones rests a life-like image of a\nLizard-man shaped out of a shrub.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25442,1,-2,-1,'Garden Path','The hard, craggy surface houses only weeds and a small bug or two.\nA shrubbery of a Paladin guard rests within a circle of stones\nbeyond the bend of the garden path.\n',128,131080,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25443,2,-5,1,'Above a Treetop','  Here you stand just slightly above the ground on a tree limb.  Scaning\neast you take notice of a small structure surrounded by several trees.\n',128,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25444,3,-4,1,'Above a Treetop','  Here you can see the park stretch out a short distance.  Wild dogs and\nmangy cat\'s become a bothersome bore.\n',128,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25445,4,-5,1,'Above a Treetop','   From here you can see through the parts in the tree as the park unfolds\naround you.  The park is definitely man made, with the exception of the huge\nElm that stands along the Northwest corner.\n',128,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25446,4,-2,-1,'Dirt path','You have come across a small dirt path that leads in all directions.\nPatches of devil-weed grass grow on this plain meshed with the wilted\nflowerbeds.  Strange footprints can be seen here leading in each direction.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25447,5,-2,-1,'Park Library','You\'ve come to an abandoned old library that stands just a few yards\nnorth of you.  Devil-weed grows here at a rapid rate over taking the\nroad and a huge door leads into the library chamber.\n',128,131080,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25448,3,-5,1,'Above a Treetop','  Standing on a tree limb, you notice just south of you a small two-story\nbuilding.  Leaning forward, you can hear voices drift through the air like\nsoft musical notes lingering in the breeze.  Glancing through the parts in the\ntree you can see the park stretch North by Northwest.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25449,4,-3,-1,'Dirt Path','  Devilweeds grow in clumps along the this sodden path.  A\nshallow pit is seen here leading downward into the earth.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25450,1,-1,1,'Halfway Up the Tree','   The light breeze of the wind begins to pick up here.  Deep grooves are\netched into a large branch here resembling claw marks.  The wooden ladder\ncontinues up and back down.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25451,1,-1,2,'Top of the Tree','   You are standing at the top of a huge Elm tree.  Here you have a clear\nview of the park and the Grimhaven palace slightly north of you.\n',128,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25452,5,-1,-1,'Tsarnek Library','You are standing in what looks like a small library with hard redwood\nfloors that run smoothly east and west.  Four rows of bookshelves\nform small paths running north and ending at the rear wall.  A desk,\nmusty from the passing of time, sits along the southeast corner and\nseveral large wooden tables used once for reading are scattered\nthoughout the room.\n',128,131084,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25453,1,-1,-1,'Ranger\'s Retreat','   You have entered what appears to be the home of the Rangers of\nGrimhaven.  A large wooden table dresses the north wall where several small\nchairs have been placed around it.  Embedded within the confines of the tree,\nalong the east wall are two small bunk-beds covered in soot.  In fact the whole\nroom looks like someone has torched it.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,85,0,'',NULL),
(25454,4,-1,-1,'Tsarnek Library','Cathedral ceilings loom above the inner walls leaving you with a\nsense of awe.  Painted within the framework of the ceiling is a\nmural.  You can make out what seems to be the Haon-Dor forest which\nis directly north of Grimhaven.  An elm tree stands vividly in the\nsettings frame.  Several red tapestries drape the walls, imprinted\nwith the logo of a lion head.  Four ivory pillars brace themselves\nagainst the cool surface of the hard redwood floors and nestled\nalong the south wall rests a small polished oak table.\n',128,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25455,3,-1,-1,'Tsarnek Library','Cathedral ceilings loom far above you here.  Painted on the ceiling is\na mural depicting a road made from loose stones.  Painted into the\nframework is a lean man dressed in bright colored clothing.  Several\ntables and chairs line themselves along the north and south wall and\nfour ivory pillars stand against the cool surface of the hard redwood\nfloors.  The corridor leads east and west here.\n',128,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25456,2,-1,-1,'Tsarnek Library','Cathedral ceilings loom high above you here, its mural is colorfully\npainted picturing a muddy path that seems to lead through a jungle\nand into a far off misty valley by a stone arch.  A hard wooden bench\nrests against the north wall facing a small round table.\n',128,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25457,2,-1,-2,'Tsarnek Library','A cathedral ceiling looms far above your head here that has been\npainted in bright colors.  This chamber is barren.\n',128,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25458,2,-1,1,'Above a Treetop','   You are standing on a small tree limb within the trees protective\ncanopy.  Its overhanging branches and leaves block your vision from the hustle\nand bustle that can be heard on East King\'s Way.\n',128,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25459,2,-1,2,'Above a Treetop','   Standing on a frail tree limb you sense that learning how to climb might\ncome in handy in the future.  For the moment you are safe from falling to your\ndeath while in the park.  A small opening in the trees cluster allows you to spot\na road just north of you.\n',128,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25460,5,-1,1,'Above a Treetop','  You are standing on a limb above a treetop.  A light breeze blows in from the\nsouth, chilling you to the bone.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25461,5,-1,2,'Above a Treetop','  You are standing on a sturdy tree limb.  Just north of you voices can be\nheard carried through the air.\n',128,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25462,4,-1,2,'Above a Treetop','You are standing on a tree limb that over looks East King\'s Way, just north\nof you.  From here you can see the Royal Palace as well.\n',0,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25463,5,-2,2,'Above the Willows treetop','   You are standing on a limb of a Willow tree who\'s branch spirals upwards\nand slightly bends west.  A stone wall brushes against the tree\'s eastern side\nhere.  The thick canopy of the tree makes it difficult to see through.\n',128,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25464,5,-3,1,'Above a Treetop','  You are standing on a thick tree limb.  The cluster of leaves make\nit difficult to survey your surroundings.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25465,5,-3,2,'Above a Treetop','  You are standing on a large tree limb.  The cluster of  leaves\nmake it impossible to see outward.  Birds chirp madly as you approach.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25466,4,-4,1,'Above a Treetop','  Standing on a tree limb you see the park blossom all around you.\nBlue birds cry out as you approach a nearby nest.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25467,4,-4,2,'Above a Treetop','  Standing on a thick tree trunk you can see the park blossom with\nbright scented flowers that dot the landscape.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25468,4,-5,2,'Above a Treetop','  Standing on a tree limb you can see the park flourish with\nbright wildflowers that dot the landscape.\n',128,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25469,3,-5,2,'Above a Treetop','  The long slender trunk of the tree supports your weight easily.\nThe chimes of the church can be heard here.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25470,2,-5,2,'Above a Treetop','  Standing above on a tree limb, here you can see the park\nstretch out with bright wildflowers that dot the landscape.\n',128,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25471,2,-4,1,'Above a Treetop','   Small and large tree limbs branch outwards that spiral upwards around the\nbase of the tree.  A colony of fire ants have mad a nest here working briskly\nas they carry off small leaves and compost into their home.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25472,2,-4,2,'Above a Treetop','   Standing on a limb you can peer through the parts in the tree.\nThe park leads eastward and not far north to south.  Wild dogs and mangy cats\ncause a ruckus in a nearby tree all the while causing leaves to drift off\nsilently to the ground.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25473,1,-4,2,'Above a Treetop','  Standing on a tree limb, you can here townfolk to the west of\nyou.  Birds chirp madly all around you followed by a dogs howl.  The\ncluster of leaves makes it difficult to see here.\n',128,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25474,1,-5,2,'Above a Treetop','  You are standing on a large tree limb.  The cluster of leaves\nmakes it difficult to see outward.\n',128,131073,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25475,5,-5,1,'Above a Treetop','  The tree limb supports you easily as you stare into the open\nspace getting a full view of the park.  Small birds chirp madly\nin a nearby tinged nest just above you.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,1,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25476,5,-5,2,'Above a Treetop','  Standing on a tree limb you see the park blossom with bright\nscented flowers.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,1,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25477,3,-3,-1,'Garden Path','Devil weed flourishes over this path.  Centered in a tiny circle\nof stones rest a shrubbery of a half humanoid half frog like creature.\n',128,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,87,0,'',NULL),
(25478,3,-4,-1,'Garden Path','Devil weeds tangle themselves within the dried crust of the\nsurface floor here.  Centered within a circle of stones rest\na shrubbery of a Centaur.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,87,0,'',NULL),
(25479,1,-3,-1,'Garden Path','Devil weed grows in thick along this path.  A large hole is here\nleading downward into a darkened pit.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25480,1,-4,-1,'Dead End','You have come to a dead end in the path.  Devil weeds flourish\nwithin the dried crust of the surface floor and a large hole can\nbe seen leading downward into a darkened pit.\n',128,131080,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25481,1,-4,3,'Above a Treetop','   High above the tree your eyes follow the park that leads eastward that\ncomes to rest against a large stone wall.  A jumble of voices carrying through\nthe air can be heard from South Main Street.\n',128,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25482,1,-5,3,'Above a Treetop','  Standing on a tree limb, here you can see the park spread\nout all around with bright wildflowers that dot the landscape.\n',128,131073,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25483,1,-2,2,'Above a Treetop','   You are standing on a frail limb that could snap at any moment.  Here\nyou can see the past stretch out to the east and south.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25484,2,-2,2,'Above a Treetop','    A sturdy tree trunk twists and bends up and around the tree forming a\nperfect place to sit here.  A small wooden trap door leads downward.\n',128,131080,26,0,0,0,0,0,1,84,0,'',NULL),
(25485,3,-2,1,'Above a Treetop','  You are standing on a small tree limb.  Thick branches enriched with leaves\nmake it difficult to see outward.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25486,3,-2,2,'Above a Treetop','   You are standing on along the treeline just above its wide spreading\ntop.  Here not only can you see the park fully, but also the royal palace.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25487,3,-3,2,'Above a Treetop','   Small sparrow perch themselves on the outer branch of the trees limb.\nThe cluster of leaves make it difficult to view the outskirts of the park.\n',128,131073,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,24,'',NULL),
(25488,3,-3,1,'Above a Treetop','   Standing on a limb you can see that the tree parts here revealing the\npark around you.  It\'s strange that not a grounds keeper can be seen, just\nthe occasional wild life and a lampboy that makes his way around merrily.\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25489,4,-2,1,'Above a Treetop','  You are standing barely on a fail limb thats about to snap at any\nsecond! Better get going before you fall!\n',128,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25490,4,-2,2,'Above a Treetop','  You are standing on a tree limb that branches off west.  From here you\ncan see all the animals and an occasional lamp-boy make his way through the\npark lighting the lamps.\n',128,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25491,5,-4,0,'Gazebo','Ferns, violets and birds of paradise fill the rooms interior.  Creeping\nvines work outward and upward along the walls and ceiling.  Its plant life,\nalthough cluttered, makes the gazebo seem like a dark silent jungle.  Centered\nupon a golden anvil rests a crystal figure of a winged dragon.\n',0,131073,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25492,3,-4,2,'Above a Treetop','  The treetops canopy makes it difficult to see anything here.\n',128,131080,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25493,1,-4,-2,'In a Hole','You are standing in a large acrid smelling pit, small skeletal\nremains lie scattered along the base of the floor.  From the looks\nof the opening you gather that something large has been burrowing\nhere.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25494,1,-3,-2,'In a Hole','  You are standing in a large rancid pit.  small skeletal remains\nlay scattered along the surface floor.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25495,3,-3,-2,'In a Hole','You are standing in a large acrid smelling pit, small skeletal\nremains lie scattered along the base of the floor.  From the looks\nof the opening you gather that something large has been burrowing\nhere.\n',128,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,87,0,'',NULL),
(25496,3,-4,-2,'In a Hole','  You are standing in a large rancid pit, small skeletal\nremains lie scattered along the floor.  From the looks of the\nopening you gather that something large has been burrowing\nhere.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,87,0,'',NULL),
(25497,4,-3,-2,'In a Hole','  You are standing in a shallow rancid pit, a pile if what\nseems like skeletal remains lie neatly stacked against the\nnorth wall.  Large claw marks outline the pits opening.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(25498,1,-5,-2,'In a Hole','  You are standing on a large rancid pit, small skeletal remains\nlay scattered along the floor.  Large claw marks outline the holes\nopening.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(25499,5,-5,-2,'In a Hole','  You are standing in a large rancid pit, small skeletal\nremains lie scattered along the sodden floor.  From the looks\nof the opening you gather that something large has been burrowing\nhere.\n',128,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(25500,-43,-50,0,'On a Dusty Trail','This trail isn\'t much more than a pair of ruts made by the wheels\nof numerous wagons in the hard packed dirt surface of the plain.  The\ndirt is dry and cracking due to lack of moisture, and what little\nvegetation you see is stunted and scraggly.  Further south, it appears\neven more arid.  The trail continues to the northeast, and to the\nsouth the trail disappears into a broad desert.\n',-1,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25501,-43,-51,0,'On a Dusty Trail','  The ground here has become much too hard to bear any tracks, and it isn\'t\nmuch more hospitable for plants.  Some occasional scrub is all that can be\nseen.  A broad plateau stretches to the west, and the trail continues north\nand south.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25502,-43,-52,0,'On a Hardened Dirt Trail','  The ground here has become much too hard to bear any tracks, and it isn\'t\nmuch more hospitable for plants.  Some occasional scrub is all that can be\nseen.  A broad plateau stretches to the west, and the trail continues north\nand south.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25503,-43,-53,0,'On a Hardened Dirt Trail','  The ground here has become much too hard to bear any tracks, and it isn\'t\nmuch more hospitable for plants.  Some occasional scrub is all that can be\nseen.  A broad plateau stretches to the west, and the trail continues north\nand south.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25504,-43,-54,0,'On a Hardened Dirt Trail','  The ground here has become much too hard to bear any tracks, and it isn\'t\nmuch more hospitable for plants.  Some occasional scrub is all that can be\nseen.  A broad plateau stretches to the west, and the trail continues north\nand south.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25505,-43,-55,0,'On a Hardened Dirt Trail','  The ground here has become much too hard to bear any tracks, and it isn\'t\nmuch more hospitable for plants.  Some occasional scrub is all that can be\nseen.  A broad plateau stretches to the west, and the trail continues north\nand south.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25506,-43,-56,0,'A Bend in a Rocky Trail','  Loose pebbles and stones make the footing on this little used trail\nsomewhat tricky.  Fortunately, there are no hills in these parts; the\nplateau extends all around, giving an even more desolate feeling to the\ndry, rocky terrain.  The path curves from the southwest here, then\ncontinues north.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25507,-44,-57,0,'A Bend In a Rocky Trail','  Loose pebbles and stones make the footing on this little used trail\nsomewhat tricky.  Fortunately, there are no hills in these parts; the\nplateau extends all around, giving an even more desolate feeling to the\ndry, rocky terrain.  The path curves from the northeast here, then\ncontinues south.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25508,-44,-58,0,'Near The Edge of The Cliffs','  Vegetation along this quickly fading path has all but ceased.  The only\nsigns of life come from a distant flock of vultures hovering around some\nunseen carcass.  A steep decline is near to the south, and a trail\ncontinues to the north.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25509,-44,-59,0,'At The Edge of The Cliffs','  What remains of the rocky path abruptly gives way to the lip of a\ntremendous cliff.  Stretching out beneath is the unforgiving expanse of the\nAtakaji Desert.  A slight breeze, drained of all moisture, wafts up from\nthe desert floor, warning of oppressive, searing heat.  The view from here\nis stunning; off to the west, amidst rolling dunes, an ancient pyramid\nstabs toward the arid sky.  Not as far off to the southwest, walls of\ngleaming rock protect a small trader\'s outpost from the brutal Atakaji\nwinds.  Someone has carved a crude staircase into the cliffside here.  It\'s\nvery steep, with jagged edges of stone protruding from the sides.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25510,-44,-59,-1,'A Recess in The Cliffs','  This natural inset into the cliffside is perfect for blocking out the\nsun.  The small amount of shade given is just about right to cover one\'s\nface and body.  Some crude steps lead upward through the cliffside.  To the\nwest the heat of the Atakaji Desert roars.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25511,-45,-60,-1,'At The Base of The Cliffs','  This is the edge of the vast desert known as the Atakaji.  A sheer\ncliffside extends off to the northwest and south.  There\'s no way of\ntelling from here how far the rock face stretches.  Many miles, at least.\nThe rock is layered, with shades of red toward the top, about seventy feet\nfrom where you stand, then giving way to shades of gray at the bottom.  The\nonly visible break in the wall is just to the northeast, a sharp recess\noffering a shelter from the desert.  The ground is mostly covered in sand\nhere, although a few rocks rest near the steep crag.  No such features can\nbe seen among the rolling hills of sun-bleached sand to the west and\nsouthwest, however, just to the west sits a stout keep made of white stone,\nand a bit farther to the southwest lies a small village, constructed\nprimarily with the same sort of rock.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25512,-45,-61,-1,'At The Base of The Cliffs',' The desert runs abruptly into the sheer, towering cliffside.  The rock is\nlayered, with shades of red toward the top, about seventy feet from where\nyou stand, then giving way to shades of gray at the bottom.  To the\nnorthwest sits a stout keep made of white stone.  A bit farther to the\nsouthwest lies a small village, apparently constructed primarily with the\nsame sort of rock.  The cliffside extends north and south, blocking your\npassage to the east.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25513,-45,-62,-1,'At The Base of The Cliffs',' The desert runs abruptly into the sheer, towering cliffside.  The rock is\nlayered, with shades of red toward the top, about seventy feet from where\nyou stand, then giving way to shades of gray at the bottom.  To the\nnorthwest sits a stout keep made of white stone.  A bit farther to the\nsouthwest lies a small village, apparently constructed primarily with the\nsame sort of rock.  The cliffside extends straight north and south,\nblocking passage to the east.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25514,-45,-63,-1,'At The Base of The Cliffs','  The desert runs abruptly into the sheer, towering cliff side.  The rock\nis layered, with shades of red toward the top, about seventy feet from\nwhere you stand, then giving way to shades of gray at the bottom.  To the\nnorthwest sits a stout keep made of white stone.  To the west lies a small\nvillage, which is surrounded by a wall cut from the same type of rock.  The\ncliff side cuts sharply here, cutting you off to the east and south, and\nthe walls of the village run directly into the rock face just to the\nsouthwest.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25515,-46,-63,-1,'Desert Outside of Al Abijah','  Waves of heat rise from the white sand at your feet, making an effort of\nsimple acts like standing and walking.  This arid, desolate place offers\nfew signs of life.  An occasional beetle scuttles past, but not even a\ncactus will call the Atakaji home.  It must have been ages ago when the\nland here saw a drop of rain.  The white marble walls of a desert village\nrise twenty feet or so from the desert floor nearby to the southwest.  The\nwalls were once polished and smooth, but they now appear pockmarked by\nyears of relentless sandstorms.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25516,-46,-62,-1,'Outside the Gate of Al Abijah','  An enormous gate of solid bronze is set into the walls of this desert\nvillage, just to the southwest.  The gate, as well as the surrounding\nmarble bulwark, bear the scars of years of abuse by the Atakaji.  A sign\nabove the gate reads, simply, \"Al Abijah\".  It looks as if this could be a\ngood place to gain shelter from the oppressive heat of the open desert.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25517,-46,-61,-1,'The Atakaji Desert','  Waves of heat rise from the white sand at your feet, making an effort of\nsimple acts like standing and walking.  This arid, desolate place offers\nfew signs of life.  An occasional beetle scuttles past, but not even a\ncactus will call the Atakaji home.  It must have been ages ago when the\nland here saw a drop of rain.  A stout keep sits immediately to the\nnorthwest.  The structure is cylindrical, apparently cut from white marble.\nIt rises about thirty feet off the desert floor and looks to be about\neighty feet in circumference.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25518,-46,-60,-1,'The Atakaji Desert','  Waves of heat rise from the white sand at your feet, making an effort of\nsimple acts like standing and walking.  This arid, desolate place offers\nfew signs of life.  An occasional beetle scuttles past, but not even a\ncactus will call the Atakaji home.  It must have been ages ago when the\nland here saw a drop of rain.  A stout keep sits immediately to the west.\nThe structure is cylindrical, apparently cut from white marble.  It rises\nabout thirty feet off the desert floor and looks to be about eighty feet in\ncircumference.  A stout wooden door is set into the tower to the west.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25519,-46,-59,-1,'At The Base of The Cliffs','  The desert runs abruptly into the sheer, towering cliffside.  The rock is\nlayered, with shades of red toward the top, about seventy feet from where\nyou stand, then giving way to shades of gray at the bottom.  Farther to the\nsouthwest lies a small village, apparently constructed with the same sort\nof rock.  The cliffside extends in jagged fashion to the northwest.  Off in\nthe distance, to the west, the tip of a massive pyramid is visible.  A\nstout keep sits immediately to the southwest.  The structure is cylindrical,\napparently cut from white marble.  It rises about thirty feet off the desert\nfloor and looks to be about eighty feet in circumference.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25520,-47,-58,-1,'At The Base of The Cliffs','  The desert runs abruptly into the sheer, towering cliff side.  The rock\nis layered, with shades of red toward the top, about seventy feet from\nwhere you stand, then giving way to shades of gray at the bottom.  Strange\nscratch marks appear on the stones to the north.  To the southwest is a\npyramid, and a small town lies to the southeast.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25521,-47,-59,-1,'The Atakaji Desert','  Waves of heat rise from the white sand at your feet, making an effort of\nsimple acts like standing and walking.  This arid, desolate place offers\nfew signs of life.  An occasional beetle scuttles past, but not even a\ncactus will call the Atakaji home.  It must have been ages ago when the\nland here saw a drop of rain.  A stout keep sits immediately to the south.\nThe structure is cylindrical, apparently cut from white marble.  It rises\nabout thirty feet off the desert floor and looks to be about eighty feet in\ncircumference.  A stout wooden door is set into the tower to the south.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25522,-47,-60,-1,'Inside the Garrison','  The marble walls of this circular building are smooth and featureless.\nFour stout wooden doors are set into the walls in each direction.  The room\nis about 25 feet across, and in the center, a spiral staircase leads\nupwards to an observation deck.  The southwest portion of the room is taken\nup by a rail and trough.  Three iron racks, meant to hold weapons of some\nsort, are set up between the other doors, and a long bench sits just in\nfront of each rack.\n',142,141640,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,250,0,'',NULL),
(25523,-47,-61,-1,'The Atakaji Desert','  Waves of heat rise from the white sand at your feet, making an effort of\nsimple acts like standing and walking.  This arid, desolate place offers\nfew signs of life.  An occasional beetle scuttles past, but not even a\ncactus will call the Atakaji home.  It must have been ages ago when the\nland here saw a drop of rain.  A stout keep sits immediately to the north.\nThe structure is cylindrical, apparently cut from white marble.  It rises\nabout thirty feet off the desert floor and looks to be about eighty feet in\ncircumference.  A stout wooden door is set into the tower to the north.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
