(25561,-52,-58,-1,'The Atakaji Desert Near a Temple','  Just to the west stands an enormous pyramid hewn from white marble.  No\ngrooves or joints can be detected to suggest that the pyramid was made from\nmany blocks of marble, but surely it couldn\'t have been cut entirely from\none slab.  After all, the structure must be at least 300 feet in height.\n',142,131072,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
