(25563,-52,-63,-1,'The Atakaji Desert','   Waves of heat rise from the white sand at your feet, making an effort of\nsimple acts like standing and walking.  This arid, desolate place offers\nfew signs of life, an occasional beetle scuttles past, but not even a\ncactus will call the Atakaji home.  It is so arid that it must have been\nages ago when the land here saw a drop of rain.  Off to the northwest a\npyramid looms and to the southeast is a small town.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25564,-53,-56,-1,'The Base of The Cliffs Near The Pyramid','  The desert runs abruptly into the sheer, towering cliffside.  The rock is\nlayered, with shades of red toward the top, about seventy feet from where\nyou stand, then giving way to shades of gray at the bottom.  Just to the\nsouth stands an enormous pyramid hewn from white marble.  No grooves or\njoints can be detected to suggest that the pyramid was made from many\nblocks of marble, but surely it couldn\'t have been cut entirely from one\nslab.  After all, the structure must be at least 300 feet in height.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25565,-53,-61,-1,'The Atakaji Desert Near a Temple','  Just to the north stands an enormous pyramid hewn from white marble.  No\ngrooves or joints can be detected to suggest that the pyramid was made from\nmany blocks of marble, but surely it couldn\'t have been cut entirely from\none slab.  After all, the structure must be at least 300 feet in height.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25566,-53,-62,-1,'The Atakaji Desert Near a Temple','  Just to the north stands an enormous pyramid hewn from white marble.  No\ngrooves or joints can be detected to suggest that the pyramid was made from\nmany blocks of marble, but surely it couldn\'t have been cut entirely from\none slab.  After all, the structure must be at least 300 feet in height.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25567,-53,-63,-1,'The Atakaji Desert Near the Dunes','  Broad dunes stretch to the south, far too tall to attempt to pass\nthrough.  The desert extends as far as the eye can see.  To the north a\npyramid looms and to the east a town lies.  The dunes are rumored to be the\nhome of some of the worst of all creatures, the sandworms.  What appear to\nbe sunken holes dot the dunes to the south.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(25568,-54,-56,-1,'The Base of The Cliffs Near The Pyramid','  The desert runs abruptly into the sheer, towering cliffside.  The rock is\nlayered, with shades of red toward the top, about seventy feet from where\nyou stand, then giving way to shades of gray at the bottom.  Just to the\nsouth stands an enormous pyramid hewn from white marble.  No grooves or\njoints can be detected to suggest that the pyramid was made from many\nblocks of marble, but surely it couldn\'t have been cut entirely from one\nslab.  After all, the structure must be at least 300 feet in height.\n',142,141632,40,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
