(26858,0,0,0,'The Garden',' The smell of roses and smoke permeates the air.  Divots, boot-marks and\nscattered rose petals cover the ground.  Battered thorn bushes, ten feet tall,\nenclose the area.  Arched openings cut into the bushes long ago permit access to\nother parts of the garden.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(26859,0,0,0,'The Garden','The smell of roses and smoke permeates the air. Divots, boot-marks and scattered\nrose petals cover the ground. Battered thorn bushes, ten feet tall, enclose the\narea. An arched opening in the bushes to the north leads to other parts of the\ngarden.\n',0,131072,26,0,26859,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(26860,0,0,0,'Front Lawn','A grassy lawn expands before a great <o>mansion<1>, its large bronze doors and\nfront steps smeared with darkened blood. Walls of thorns surround the estate,\nkeeping the dark woods at bay. To the east, a <o>gate<1> of woven branches\nprovides inconspicuous passage out of the yard.\n',0,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(26861,0,0,0,'The Garden','  The smell of roses and smoke permeates the air.  Divots, boot-marks and\nscattered rose petals cover the ground.  Battered <o>thorn bushes<1>, ten feet\ntall, enclose the area.  An arched opening in the bushes to the north leads to\nother parts of the garden. \n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(26862,0,0,0,'Bathhouse','A wooden partition divides the interior of this warm stone chamber into two\nparts. It is not high enough to reach the rafters above, nor low enough to meet\nthe floor. A sliding panel in the partition leads into the sauna area to the\nwest and a door in the eastern wall opens up into a courtyard. \n',0,131080,32,120,26862,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26863,0,0,0,'Courtyard','The courtyard is paved with tightly joined flat stones.  To the south are the\ndoors into the mansion.  Two smaller buildings, separate from the main, lie to\nthe west and east.  Steam wafts from the door to the west.  There is a balcony\noverhead, from which hangs a pair of <o>bloodied bloomers<1>.\n',0,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(26864,0,0,0,'Ransacked Servants\' Quarters','These quarters, although simple, show the signs of merciless plunder. All\nsurfaces are littered with shredded cloth and straw from the abused beds.\nSeveral pieces of furniture have been reduced to kindling. The door from the\ncourtyard to the west is still functional, but the brass knob has been smeared\nwith some form of slimy filth.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26865,0,0,0,'Guard Room','Other than the smashed iron door leading to the lounge in the eastern wall and\nthe large pool of blood in the center of the floor, this room appears to have\nbeen preserved from the excessive molestations visited upon the nearby portions\nof the mansion. An intact iron door is in the southern wall.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26866,0,0,0,'Uncomfortable Lounge','There is evidence that people used to gather here in comfort and safety.  For\nexample, elegantly carved doors\nlead into a feast hall to the east, an empty pair of hobbit knickers\npinned to them by rusty knives. \nWalls of finest plaster are cracked from head sized holes.\nA flight of keenly polished \nstairs rises into the atrium above, carpeted by stained trousers and fine\npetticoats.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26867,0,0,0,'Feast Hall','A stage lines the east wall, rising about two feet from the floor. Remnants of\nmeals and broken dishes clutter the corners of this ample hall. Great carved\ndouble doors lead to the west and a swinging door opens up upon the kitchen to\nthe south.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26868,0,0,0,'Caretaker\'s Room','This room is both office and living quarters. It is smoky and stinks of booze. \nThere is an ax planted firmly into the wall, the frame of a broken mirror\nsurrounding it. An iron door leads north and a <c>window<1> faces south where\nthe Kranor River drifts peacefully past.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26869,0,0,0,'Ruined Conference Room','  The southern face of the mansion has been blown open by explosions and now\ngives way to the passing Kranor River.  Opulent wallpaper hangs in shreds\nfrom the walls of this once-circular chamber.  Splinters of glass and wood\ncover everything like fresh down, darkened by <r>pools of clotted blood<1>. \n',0,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26870,0,0,0,'Vandalized Kitchen','The contents of the well appointed pantry have been largely emptied out upon the\nshelves. A <c>window<1> faces south to the serenely passing Kranor River, framed\nby a box of aromatic herbs. Splotches of white flour mark the walls and the\nswinging door that leads into the feast hall to the north.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26871,0,0,0,'Balcony','A courtyard can be seen below the <c>railing<1> of this small balcony. Further north can be seen the tops of the tall thorn hedges of an enclosed  garden. The smell of the forest mingles with acrid smoke. Tied to the stone balustrade is a pair of <o>bloodied bloomers<1> on display to the courtyard below.\r\n',0,131072,21,0,0,0,0,0,3,-1,0,'',NULL),
(26872,0,0,0,'Foyer','This small area has been outfitted as a waiting room. Double doors lead to a\nchamber to the west and a veranda overlooks the center of the mansion to the\neast. A lush carpet covers the floor, trampled but still more comfortable than\nthe bare wood.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26873,0,0,0,'Veranda','The stairs from below land on the south edge of this veranda as it circles an\nopen atrium.  Sailors\' clothing and brassieres hang from the railings.  Passages\nshoot off in all directions towards the outer rooms of the mansion.  A screen\ndoor to the north leads to an outdoor balcony.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26874,0,0,0,'Foyer','This small area has been outfitted as a waiting room. Double doors lead to a\nchamber to the east and a veranda overlooks the center of the mansion to the\nwest. A lush carpet covers the floor, trampled but still more comfortable than\nthe bare wood.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26875,0,0,0,'Foyer','This small area has been outfitted as a waiting room. Double doors lead to a\nchamber to the west and a veranda overlooks the center of the mansion to the\nnortheast. A lush carpet covers the floor, trampled but still more comfortable\nthan the bare wood.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26876,0,0,0,'Solarium',' A fleet of couches and divans are anchored beneath an exquisite <c>solarium<1>.\nOutside, the\nlanguid Kranor River passes slowly by.  Stuffing from the couches is\nscattered about the room like clouds in a sky.  Breathtakingly vandalized\nlandscape\npaintings cover the walls.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26877,0,0,0,'Foyer','This small area has been outfitted as a waiting room. Double doors lead to a\nchamber to the east and a veranda overlooks the center of the mansion to the\nnorthwest. A lush carpet covers the floor, trampled but still more comfortable\nthan the bare wood.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26878,0,0,0,'Bathhouse Sauna','A wooden partition divides the interior of this warm stone chamber into two\nparts. It is not high enough to reach the rafters above, nor low enough to meet\nthe floor. A sliding panel in the partition leads into the bathing area to the\neast. \n',0,131080,32,120,26878,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26879,0,0,0,'Brotherhood of Galek Conference Room','An expanse of silver inlaid white marble stretches from the lofty ceiling to the\nblue tiled floor. \nA <o>target<1> has been mounted on one wall and filled with daggers.\n Stained glass windows have been covered with gauzy silks from distant lands.\nDouble doors grant access to the foyer to the west.\n',0,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26880,0,0,0,'Unaffiliated Conference Room','In spirit, not much appears to have changed here for years. A few of the\nbarbaric trophies on display actually show a thick layer of dust. However, the\nbenign neglect of the old tenants has given way to a calculated & atavistic\nmalignancy. Maps and notes fill the walls, weighing various opportunities to\neither devastate or control regional trade centers. Double doors grant access to\nthe foyer to the west.\n',0,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26881,0,0,0,'Serpent Order Conference Room','This lavishly appointed chamber both reflects upon its <o>original tenants<1>\nand expresses the new direction pursued by the their successors. Trinkets\nboth bawdy and opulent dangle from the masterful plasterwork foliage that\ndecorates the hall. Double doors grant access to the foyer to the east.\n',0,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26882,0,0,0,'Cult of Logrus Conference Room','The once proud <o>murals<1> on the southern wall have been retouched by a most\nvulgar hand. The cabinets are lined with emptied bottles of rum and the shelves\nwith trinkets from distant lands. Double doors grant access to the foyer to the\neast.\n',0,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(26883,0,0,0,'Side Road','  Tall trees arch over the road, forming an almost seamless canopy overhead. \r\nTo the south lies the entrance to a large garden.  In the distance beyond the\r\ngarden an elegant mansion sprouts up from amidst the surrounding vegetation,\r\nits windows smashed. \r\n',0,131076,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(26884,0,0,0,'Side Road','  This is a side road that branches off from the main path through the forest.\nTall trees arch over the road, forming an almost seamless canopy overhead.  Off\nin the distance to the south a wall of thorn bushes can be seen.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(26885,0,0,0,'Center of the Rose Garden','Ringed by battered thorn bushes rising ten feet into the air, there seems\nto be no obvious exit. A large <o>scorched rose bush<1> dominates the center of the\ngarden.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27100,-17,35,-1,'Corner of a Desolate Graveyard','  The quaint sounds of the wilderness are barely audible here, with only a\nharsh silence to fill your ears.  Looking across the shrub covered ground a\ngraveyard, with broken tombstones, beckons.  To the north an iron gate sits\nbetween the graveyard and a small overgrown path.\n',166,131072,41,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27101,-16,35,-1,'Desolate Graveyard','  The forest seems to be held at bay by some unseen force.  Looking closer, you\nsee that the graveyard just seems to stop all forms of life larger than a small\nshrub.  With no grave here, the shrub grass has gotten a firm foothold.\nThere are even some small shrubs taking root.  With the forest sounds oddly\nabsent a gentle breeze is your only link out of this desolate place.\n',166,131072,41,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27102,-15,35,-1,'Desolate Graveyard','  The forest seems to be held at bay by some unseen force.  Looking closer, you\nsee that the graveyard just seems to stop all forms of life larger than a small\nshrub.  With no grave here, the shrub grass has gotten a firm foothold.\nThere are even some small shrubs taking root.  With the forest sounds oddly\nabsent a gently breeze is your only link out of this desolate place.\n',166,131072,41,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27103,-14,35,-1,'Desolate Graveyard','  The forest seems to be held at bay by some unseen force.  Looking closer,\nyou see that the graveyard just seems to stop all forms of life larger than a\nsmall shrub.  A wind eroded gravestone juts upwards from ground, an epitaph\nbarely visible.  The forest seemingly has never been able to reclaim this\nportion of the land, with only shrub grass and weeds existing to cover the\ngrave.  Towards the east you see a grove of willow trees.\n',166,131072,41,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(27104,-13,35,-1,'Edge of a Willow Tree Grove','  The forest seems to be held at bay by some unseen force.  Looking closer,\nyou see that the graveyard just seems to stop all forms of life larger than a\nsmall shrub.  The forest seemingly has never been able to reclaim the land\nhere.  A broken gravestone juts up from the ground before you; a great magical\nforce has smashed this tombstone.  The broken grave is shaded by the branches\nof a large willow tree.\n',166,131072,41,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(27105,-12,35,-1,'Willow Tree Grove','  You have stumbled into a willow grove.  The branches of the trees block out\nmost of the light, leaving the area in a cool shadow.  The shrub grass here has\na reddish tinge that reminds you more of grass you have seen after a large\nbattle, rather than a nice natural color.\n',166,131072,41,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27106,-17,34,-1,'Desolate Graveyard','  The forest seems to be held at bay by some unseen force.  Looking closer, you\nsee that the graveyard just seems to stop all forms of life larger than a small\nshrub.  The forest has never been able to reclaim this portion of land;\nonly shrub grass and weeds cover the grave.  A broken gravestone juts up from\nthe ground before you; a great natural force has smashed it.\n',166,131072,41,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(27107,-16,34,-1,'Desolate Graveyard','  The forest seems to be held at bay by some unseen force.  Looking closer,\nyou see that the graveyard just stops all forms of life larger than a small\nshrub.  The forest has never been able to reclaim this portion of land as\nonly shrub grass and weeds exist here.  A broken gravestone juts up from the\nground before you; a great physical force has smashed it.  A large dark crypt\nlooms to the southeast.\n',166,131072,41,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(27108,-15,34,-1,'Desolate Graveyard','  The forest is held at bay by some unseen force.  Looking closer, you see that\nthe graveyard just seems to stop all forms of life larger than a small\nshrub.  A gravestone juts forth from the ground, the words barely visible;\nthe elements of nature have clearly taken their toll here.  The forest has\nnever been able to reclaim this land as only shrub grass and weeds exist here.\nA large dark crypt looms to the south.\n',166,131072,41,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(27109,-14,34,-1,'Desolate Graveyard','  The forest seems to be held at bay by some unseen force.  Looking closer, you\nsee that the graveyard has stopped all forms of life larger than a small\nshrub.  With no grave here, the shrub grass has gotten a firm foothold.\nThere are even some small shrubs taking root.  The forest sounds are oddly\nabsent, a gently breeze is your only link out of this desolate place.  A large\ndark crypt looms to the south while a willow grove to the east beckons you.\n',166,131072,41,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
