(27114,-15,33,-1,'Crypt','  This room is completely empty.  Only a thick layer of dust covers the floor.\nMaybe in a time long past it was filled with opulent furniture and decorations\nbut only stale air greets you now.\n',166,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27115,-14,33,-1,'Crypt','With the exception of a stone staircase leading down, this room lacks decoration.  Cold dark walls line the \nnorthern and eastern parts of the room, while openings lead south, west and southwest.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27116,-13,33,-1,'Edge of a Willow Tree Grove','  The forest is held at bay by some unseen force.  Looking closer, you see that\nthe graveyard just stops all forms of life larger than a small shrub.  The\nforest has never been able to reclaim this land as only shrub grass and weeds\nexist.  A gravestone juts up from the ground its words are barely visible; the\nelements of nature have clearly taken their toll here.  A large dark crypt\nlooms to the west while a willow grove to the north beckons you.\n',166,131072,41,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(27117,-12,33,-1,'Desolate Graveyard','  The forest is held at bay by some unseen force.  Looking closer, you see that\nthe graveyard just stops all forms of life larger than a small shrub.  There\nare even some small shrubs taking root.  The forest sounds still are oddly\nabsent.  The branches of a large willow tree shade the broken grave.  Towards\nthe north you see a dense grove of willow trees.\n',166,131072,41,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27118,-17,32,-1,'Desolate Graveyard','  The forest is held at bay by some unseen force.  Looking closer, you see\nthat the graveyard just seems to stop all forms of life larger than a small\nshrub.  A wind eroded gravestone juts upwards from ground, an epitaph\nbarely visible.  The forest has never been able to reclaim this portion of\nland.  Only shrub grass and weeds exist to cover the grave.\n',166,131072,41,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(27119,-16,32,-1,'Desolate Graveyard','  The forest is held at bay by some unseen force.  Looking closer, you see\nthat the graveyard just stops all forms of life larger than a small shrub.\nWith no grave here, the shrub grass has gotten a firm foothold.  There are even\nsome small shrubs taking root.  The forest sounds are oddly absent.  A large\ndark crypt looms to the east.\n',166,131072,41,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27120,-15,32,-1,'Crypt','  The rubble blocking the entrance might, in an age past, have been protecting\na great tomb, but now it protects only a dust covered floor.  This room of the\ncrypt is sadly empty.\n',166,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27121,-14,32,-1,'Crypt','  This room is completely empty.  Only a thick layer of dust covers the floor.\nMaybe in a time long past it was filled with opulent furniture and decorations\nbut only stale air greets you now.\n',166,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
