(27147,-12,32,-2,'In The Shallow Grave','  This is a perfect place for a coffin.  Whoever dug this grave has really done\na fabulous job of it.  The walls are almost ruler straight and there is clearly\nan outline of where the coffin should be placed.\n',166,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27148,-17,36,-1,'Overgrown Dirt Path','  This small overgrown path appears to have once been well traveled, but\nis now slowly being consumed by the surrounding vegetation.  Just barely\nvisible to the north is a small trade post while to the south an iron\ngate allows access to a small desolate graveyard.\n',103,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27150,69,-5,0,'<k>The Shaman\'s Hut<z>','  <b>This room is very neat an organized.  Unlike the rest of the camp,\nthere is no mud here.  The floor appears to be made of a polished marble.\nAt the foot of the bed is a small nightstand.  On top of the nightstand\nis a small book and a partially burned candle.  A small rug lies on\nthe floor next to the nightstand.  The rug looks as if it was quickly\nthrown onto the floor.  A strange humming noise emanates from the center\nof the room.<z>\n',160,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,14,100,0,'',NULL),
(27151,69,-5,1,'<r>The War Conference Room<z>','  <r>This room is dominated by a large table in the center of the room.\nInches of dust cover everything in the room.  The billowing clouds of\ndust makes breathing difficult.  Beneath the dust is a wooden floor\nriddled with deep holes and scratches.<z>\n',160,131081,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27152,69,-5,-1,'<r>Shaman\'s Temple<z>','<r>  The air on this room is deathly still.  Your breath turns to a reddish\nvapor when you exhale.  Despite the stillness of the air, your breathe\nseems to radiate toward a small hole in the floor.  The walls in this room\nare covered with strange archaic symbols.  An ominous jet black altar is in\nthe center of the room.  The floor appears to be covered in a sticky red\nsubstance, which radiates out from the altar.<z>\n',160,163849,32,0,0,0,0,0,14,150,0,'',NULL),
(27153,69,-6,0,'<k>A Trash Filled Courtyard<z>','  <y>This appears to have once been a majestic courtyard.  However, it\nhas long since fallen into a state of decay.  The ground is covered\nwith a foul smelling mud.  Debris is scattered everywhere.  To the\nnorth is a small hut, from which a humming noise can be heard.  A\nlarge black crow circles high overhead, as if to warn of your approach.<z>\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27154,69,-7,0,'<k>Mercenary Guard Post<z>','  <k>This appears to have once been a great courtyard.  An immense marble\nstatue of a lone archer taking aim at a distant target, now lays shattered\non the ground.  Garbage litters the entire courtyard.  Everything in sight\nis covered with a foul smelling mud.<z>\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27155,70,-6,0,'<k>Neglected Orchard<z>','  This neglected orchard once supplied the keep with fresh fruit.\nApparently, the current occupants of the keep do not appreciate this\nconstant food source.  The trees are growing out of control.  Rotting\nfruit lies all over the ground.  Small birds flit about, picking at\nthe fruit.  Small fruit flies buzz about.\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27156,68,-6,0,'<b>Natural Spring <z>','  <b>A small natural stream bubbles up from the earth here.  Originally,\nthe stream followed its natural path through the keep to the southwest.\nRecently, somebody attempted to divert the flow of the stream.  To what\nend this was done is unclear, but the stream is now slowly turning the\nkeep into an unnatural swamp.<z>\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27157,68,-7,0,'<k>An Unstable Archer\'s Perch<z>','<k>  Set high in the wall to the south is a perch set into the wall.\nBefore this keep was turned into a trashed filled eyesore, these perches\nwere manned by archers watching the road to the south.  Now these perches\nare merely reminders of the former stature of the keep.<z>\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27158,70,-7,0,'<k>An Unstable Archer\'s Perch<z>','  <k>Set high in the wall above is an archer\'s perch.  The access ladder\nto the perch has long since vanished.  Centuries ago, skilled archers\ndiligently watched the single road into the keep from the perch.  The\nperch is no longer suitable for its intended use.  What is left of it is\nrotted and falling apart.  It is just a bitter reminder of how great this\nkeep once was, and what it has now become.<z>\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27159,69,-8,0,'<k>Before a Wrought Iron Gate<z>','  <k>The path to the north here, ends at an iron gate.  The gate looks as\nif it has been recently attached to the decrepit walls.  The keep to the\nnorth is well camouflaged, and cannot be seen from the south.  Along the\nwall of the keep, archer\'s turrets are visible, but it is impossible to\ndiscern if they are currently manned.  A small overgrown path threads\nits way through the underbrush to the south.<z>\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27160,71,-7,0,'<k>Base of a Rickety Watchtower<z>','  <k>There is a large watchtower standing high over the keep here.  The\nsupport beams of the tower are rotting, and look as if they will crumble\nmomentarily.  About ten feet off the ground, the tower has begun to pull\naway from the wall.<z>\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27161,71,-7,1,'<k>Atop the Southeast Tower','  It appears that the mercenaries still use this tower, despite its\nunstable condition.  The floorboards are rotting and loose.  The roof has\ncompletely eroded in places and provides little shelter.  A small sign\nhangs from the rafters.\n',160,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,12,100,0,'',NULL),
(27162,67,-7,0,'<k>Base of a Partially Rotted Watchtower<z>','  There is a large watchtower standing high over the keep here.  The\nsupport beams of the tower are rotting, and look as if they will crumble\nmomentarily.  About ten feet of the ground, the tower has begun to pull\naway from the wall.\n',160,131072,44,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27163,67,-7,1,'<k>Atop an Unstable Watchtower<z>','  It appears that the mercenaries still use this tower, despite its\nunstable condition.  The floorboards are rotting and loose.  The roof has\ncompletely eroded in places and provides little shelter.  A small sign\nhangs from the rafters.\n',160,131080,22,0,0,0,0,0,12,90,0,'',NULL),
(27164,67,-6,0,'<k>Along a Crumbled Wall<z>','  The wall here has greatly deteriorated.  Large pieces of it have\ncrumbled away where the mortar has failed to hold it in place.  At one\npoint there is a small hole in the wall.  A few wildflowers grow at the\nbase of the wall.\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27165,67,-5,0,'<r>Scorched Earth<z>','  The ground here is charred and barren.  A large impact crater in the\nshape of a circle is here.  The crater itself is about ten feet across\nand about three feet deep.\n',160,163840,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27166,68,-5,0,'<k>Training Grounds<z>','  This was once the training area for the soldiers of the keep.  As they\nhave with everything else in the keep, the mercenaries have destroyed\nwhat they found here.  The remains of training dummies are scattered\nabout.  A toppled archer\'s target lies toppled in the mud.\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27167,70,-5,0,'<r>Scorched Earth<z>','  The ground here is charred and barren.  A large impact crater in the\nshape of a circle is here.  The crater itself is about ten feet across\nand about three feet deep.\n',160,163840,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27168,71,-6,0,'<k>Breached Wall<z>','<g>  A large gapping hole in the wall here has been temporarily plugged\nwith garbage, broken twigs and weapon fragments.  The hole was  originally\nabout ten feet high and six feet wide.  The wall leans into the keep at a\nfrightening angle.<z>\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27169,71,-5,0,'<k>Decayed Wall<z>','<k>  The wall here has greatly deteriorated.  Large pieces of it have\ncrumbled away where the mortar has failed to hold it in place.  At one\npoint there is a small hole in the wall.  A few wildflowers grow at the\nbase of the wall.<z>\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27170,67,-4,0,'<k>Along a Decaying Wall<z>','  The wall here has greatly deteriorated.  Large pieces of it have\ncrumbled away where the mortar has failed to hold it in place.  At one\npoint there is a small hole in the wall.  A few wildflowers grow at the\nbase of the wall.\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27171,68,-4,0,'<k>Camp Prison<z>','  The original inhabitants of the keep used this room as an office.  The\nmercenaries have built shackles into the wall, and now use it for a camp\nprison.  A small desk is against the north wall.  Currently there are\nno prisoners here.  A loose panel in the floor beneath your feet catches\nyour eye.\n',160,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,12,100,0,'',NULL),
(27172,70,-4,0,'<k>Disorganized Bunkhouse<z>','  What was once a comfortable bunkhouse to the keep\'s soldiers, has now\nbecome a cluttered and nauseating room.  Broken pieces of furniture are\nscattered about the room.  Rotting food, covered in roaches and ants is\neverywhere.  Mud has been tracked over everything.\n',160,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,14,100,0,'',NULL),
(27173,71,-4,0,'<k>Intact Wall<z>','  <k>The western wall of the keep is in better shape here than than in\nthe rest of the keep.  Garbage is strewn about here, and the smell of\nrotting food is tremendous.  Small field mice and roaches busily scurry\nabout.  Apparently, the inhabitants of the keep are not very concerned\nwith its appearance.<z>\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27174,70,-4,-1,'<k>Stolen Goods Storage Facility <z>','  This rather large storage facility is mostly empty at the moment.  This\nsecret room is the perfect place to store their stolen contraband.  A\nsmall pile of clothes is in the corner.  Despite the empty current status\nof this room, by the number of signs around the room, it must house\na great deal of contraband at times.\n',160,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,14,85,0,'',NULL),
(27175,69,-4,0,'<r>Bonfire<z>','  A huge bonfire has been started here and is being fed by the camp\ngarbage.  Although the fire is roaring and creating tremendous amounts\nof heat, it is strangely producing no smoke.\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27176,68,-4,-1,'<k>Prison Guard Station<z>','This is the guard station of the keep\'s secret prison.  It is here that\nthey keep the prisoners and hostages that they acquire.  This room has\nrecently been built.  The walls are made of gray stone, as is the floor.\nA lone tapestry on the southwest wall is the only decoration to the room.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(27177,69,-3,-1,'<k>A Small Cell<z>','   This is a small damp cell.  There is a small pile of straw in the corner,\ncovered in mud, that has been used for a bed.  The inhabitants of the cell\nare forced to fight for the bed nightly.  The walls are covered with a gray\nmold and small roaches race across the floor, searching for a meal.\n',160,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(27178,69,-4,-1,'<k>A Small Cell<z>','  This is a small damp cell.  There is a small pile of straw in the corner,\ncovered in mud, that has been used for a bed.  The inhabitants of the cell\nare forced to fight for the bed nightly.  The walls are covered with a gray\nmold.  Small roaches race across the floor, searching for a meal.\n',160,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(27179,68,-5,-1,'<k>A Small Cell<z>','  This is a small damp cell.  There is a small pile of straw in the corner,\ncovered in mud, that has been used for a bed.  The inhabitants of the cell\nare forced to fight for the bed nightly.  The walls are covered with a gray\nmold.  Small roaches race across the floor, searching for a meal.\n',160,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(27180,67,-4,-1,'<k>A Small Cell<z>','  This is a small damp cell.  There is a small pile of straw in the corner,\ncovered in mud, that has been used for a bed.  The inhabitants of the cell\nare forced to fight for the bed nightly.  The walls are covered with a gray\nmold.  Small roaches race across the floor, searching for a meal.\n',160,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(27181,69,-5,-1,'<r>Torture Room<z>','  This is a small room with black walls.  The floor is covered in dried\nblood.  The walls have been splattered with blood.  A small table sits at\nthe center of the table.  Above the table, a small sign is stuck to the\nceiling.<z>\n',160,163848,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(27182,67,-5,-1,'<k>Political Prisoner\'s Cell<z>','  This secret cell is where the important hostages are hidden.  The\nconditions here are deplorable.  Human and rat excrement cover the floor.\nThe room smells of rotting food and flesh.  The walls are covered with\na gray fungus.  Large cobwebs hang from the ceiling.\n',160,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(27183,69,-3,0,'Large Refuse Pile','  Despite the garbage that is scattered throughout the compound, somebody\nhas actually gathered a lot of it here.  The pile is approximately twenty\nfeet high, and about thirty feet wide.  It has been piled up here, and\nis now waiting to be added to the bonfire burning to the west.  Judging\nby the size of this pile, the mercenaries have occupied this keep for\nquite some time.<z>\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,14,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27184,70,-3,0,'Towering Pile of Garbage','  Despite the garbage that is scattered throughout the compound, somebody\nhas actually gathered a lot of it here.  The pile is approximately twenty\nfeet high, and about thirty feet wide.  It has been piled up here, and\nis now waiting to be added to the bonfire burning to the west.  Judging\nby the size of this pile, the mercenaries have occupied this keep for\nquite some time.\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,14,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27185,71,-3,0,'<k>Base of a Watchtower<z>','<k>  Shattered bones have been trampled into the ground here.  The tower\nabove is slowly sinking into the mud.  The main support beam of the\ntower has split, causing the tower to lean heavily to the south.  A few\nbeams have been placed here to brace the tower, in a futile attempt to\nprevent it from toppling.<z>\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27186,71,-3,1,'<k>Ruined Watchtower<z>','<k>  The mercenaries have turned this tower into a small rec room.  A\ndestroyed dart board is placed in the western wall.  A bleached human\nskull rests on one of the beams.<z>\n',160,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,14,100,0,'',NULL),
(27187,68,-3,0,'<k>Small Cemetery<z>','  This is a small private cemetery.  A few grave markers are here and a\npatch of tall black roses grow about the smallest grave.  The only other\napparent vegetation that grows here is a tall barren tree that spreads\nits limbs over the cemetery.\n',160,163840,24,0,0,0,0,0,14,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27188,67,-3,0,'<k>Base of a Large Tree<z>','  A large tree is being utilized as a corner of the wall.  The tree itself\nis a towering oak tree, and it appears that rather than face the daunting\nchallenge of attempting to remove this tree, the builders of the keep\ndecided to build around it.  A large strange root burst through the soil,\nwraps around itself, and vanishes back onto the soil.\n',160,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27189,68,-3,-1,'<k>Small Crypt<z>','  This is a small crypt.  There is a small open casket here, that appears\nto have been pried open.  The walls are jet black, and have deep claw\nmarks in them.  The wind howls through the grave opening above you.\nBeside the thin stream of light from above, the room is dark.\n',160,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(27190,67,-3,1,'Camouflaged Perch','  A small siting perch has been constructed into the tree here.  Although\nit is not visible from below, it offers a panoramic view of most of the\nkeep.  The walls of the keep meet here at the tree, incorporating it as a\ncorner of the wall.\n',160,131072,22,0,0,0,0,0,14,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27191,67,-3,2,'<g>Top of a Large Oak Tree<z>','  The wind howls through the tree top.  From this vantage point, most of\nthe keep can be seen.  Occasionally, the wind stops and the rotting smell\nof the keep rises up.  A large battle field can be seen to the north of\nthe keep.\n',160,131072,24,0,0,0,0,0,5,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27192,67,-3,-1,'Small Underground House','  The roots of this tree have created a natural house here.  The roots\nabove, fan out and form the ceiling.  At the edge of the room they\ncascade down forming walls.  The floor is made out of a smooth marble,\nand is covered by a soft green moss.  Despite the subterranean nature of\nthis dwelling.  The air is surprisingly fresh.  The smell of fresh\nbaked bread hangs in the air.\n',160,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,80,0,'',NULL),
(27193,67,-2,-1,'<k>Small Bedroom<z>','  As in the front room, the walls and ceiling of this room are formed by\nthe roots of the great oak tree above.  The same moss adorns this room\nas in the front room, here it is a deep blue color.  Two small beds are\nagainst the wall, separated by a desk.\n',160,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,5,80,0,'',NULL),
(27194,69,-2,0,'<k>Near a great Battlefield<z>','  A small trench has been dug into the earth here.  The trench is lined\nwith bleached skeletons and broken spears and halberds.  There is a large\nhorse skeleton impaled upon a great spear.  Further to the north, a large\nfield opens opens up.  Long ago, the original inhabitants of this keep\nmade a desperate counter-strike, that terminated to the north.\n',160,131072,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27195,69,-1,0,'<k>Ancient Battlefield<z>','  This large open field is covered by the remains of a great battle.\nBleached bones riddle the field.  Broken weapons lie about the field.\nAt the center of this battle is an immense skeleton of a dragon, embedded\nabout fifteen feet into the ground.  Around this dragon, the earth has\nbeen scorched, and is no longer able to support even the hardiest of weeds.\n',160,163840,26,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27196,70,-10,0,'Overgrown Path','  Once a well used path it seems lack of use has allowed even the minimal\nsurrounding vegetation to overtake the narrow walkway.  Tall grasses and\nscrub brush keep your view focused directly on the path in front of you.\nWhile the path seems to move to the northwest, to the east it moves\nthrough a small iron fence.  Unfortunately it seems several large pieces\nof stonework have fallen across the opening in the fence.\n',167,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27197,69,-9,0,'Overgrown Path','  Once a well used path it seems lack of use has allowed even the minimal\nsurrounding vegetation to overtake the narrow walkway.  Tall grasses and\nscrub brush keep your view focused directly on the path in front of you.\nThe path appears to move to the north and to the southeast.\n',167,131072,36,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27200,-16,1,0,'<w>A Small Cobblestone Path<z>','  Small white cobblestones have been placed together to make a path\nhere.  Between the cobblestones grass grows in thick and lush.  You can\ntell that these stones were laid long ago.  It seems that the grounds\nare well taken care of.  To the north you can see what seems to be a small\niron fence and a large stone building.  A larger path lies to the south.\n',161,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27201,-16,2,0,'<w>Entrance to a Small Cemetery<z>','  Here in the center of the path is a fenced in cemetery, a gate allows\nentrance into it.  You suspect the gate is here to keep dogs and other\nsmall animals from trampling on top of the graves.  Glancing at the\nhinges, you notice a lot of rust.  The latch on the gate seems to also be\nrusted.  You remember how well kept the cobblestones were and wonder why\nthe gate is in such bad condition.  It looks like the gate hasn\'t been\nused in quite some time.\n',161,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27202,-16,3,0,'<w>A Small Cobblestone Path<z>','  The cobblestones here are very dirty.  Leaves cover most of the path,\nit looks as if no one has cleaned this place in quite some time.  You\nbegin to get a strange feeling about this place, as if someone was\nwatching you.  It probably would not be a good idea to visit this place\nafter dark.  To the north you can see a large stone building which\nappears to be a mausoleum.  To the east and west you see trails leading\nalongside a small iron fence.\n',161,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27203,-15,3,0,'<w>Along An Iron Fence<z>','  A small iron fence surrounds the cemetery that stands only four feet\ntall.  You can easily examine the surrounding landscape from where you\nstand.  On the top of each post of the fence, a blackened spike protrudes\nsharply towards the sky.  The grass here is a bright green color and very\nneatly trimmed.  Looking far to the east, you see a large city perched\natop a plateau, probably Grimhaven.  To the northeast an iron fence marks\nthe boundaries of the cemetery.  To the west you can find the entrance of\nthe cemetery.\n',161,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27204,-17,3,0,'<w>Along An Iron Fence<z>','  A small iron fence about four feet in height surrounds the cemetery.\nYou can easily survey the surrounding landscape the lies beyond the\nfence.  On the top of each post the iron fence has is a blackened spike\nprotruding sharply towards the sky.  Far to the west you see a large river\nthat seems to flow very swiftly.  Below you, bright green grass covers the\nground.  An iron fence continues along a pathway that leads northwest,\nand east where the entrance to the cemetery can be found.\n',161,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27205,-14,4,0,'<w>Along An Iron Fence<z>','  A small iron fence surrounds the cemetery that stands only four feet\ntall.  You can easily examine the surrounding landscape from where you\nstand.  On the top of each post of the fence, a blackened spike protrudes\nsharply towards the sky.  The grass here is a bright green color and very\nneatly trimmed.  Looking far to the east, you see a large city perched\natop a plateau, probably Grimhaven.  To the west you see a broken\ntombstone and to the northwest you can see a large pile of dirt.  To the\nsouthwest is an iron fence leading down another pathway.\n',161,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27206,-15,4,0,'<w>A Broken Tombstone<z>','  This tombstone has many cracks on it.  The top half of the tombstone\nhas broken off and has come to rest on the ground.  Your guess is that a\ngang of kids or cult members vandalized this grave, you start to become\nweary of this place.  A small shovel has been thrown aside and some dirt\nhas been removed from the top of the grave site, as if someone or\nsomething had plans to dig it up.  To the north is an empty grave, and to\nthe east is a iron fence.  To the west is the main path leading through\nthe cemetery.\n',161,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27207,-16,4,0,'<w>A Small Cobblestone Path<z>','  The cobblestones here are very dirty.  Leaves seem to cover most of\nthe path as if no one has cleaned this place in quite some time.  You\nbegin to get a strange feeling about this place, as if someone was\nwatching you.  It probably would not be a good idea to visit this place\nafter dark.  To the north you can see a large stone building that you guess\nto be a mausoleum.  To the east and west you can see the tombs of past\nhero\'s.\n',161,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27208,-17,4,0,'<w>The Tomb of An Unknown Mage<z>','  A small tombstone is placed in the ground here atop a grave.  Numerous\ncracks can be seen on the tombstone.  Perched on top of the tombstone\nis a small ankh.  In the upper part, a small spider is spinning a web.\nGazing at the ground, you observe the grass is bright green and the ground\nseems to be pretty solid.  To the east you see a cobblestone path, while\nto the west an iron fence trods down another path.\n',161,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27209,-18,4,0,'<w>Along An Iron Fence<z>','  A small iron fence surrounds the cemetery that stands only four feet\ntall.  You can easily examine the surrounding landscape from where you\nstand.  On the top of each post of the fence, a blackened spike protrudes\nsharply towards the sky.  Far to the west you see a large river that seems\nto flow very swiftly.  Below you, bright green grass covers the ground.\nTo the northeast and east you can see small tombstones.  An iron fence\ntravels southeast along a path.\n',161,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27210,-16,0,-1,'<o>A Damp Passage<z>','  The ground here is slightly damp, just enough to make squishing sounds\nwhen you step.  A gust of cold air rises, chilling you ever so slightly.\nThe walls are braced with two large pillars of wood on each side for\nsupport.  Another large pillar stands upright against the ceiling, making\nyou feel more comfortable than before.  The absence of light makes it too\ndifficult to see anything outside this room.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27211,-17,5,0,'<w>The Tomb of An Infamous Cleric<z>','  A small tombstone sits in the ground here marking a small grave.\nReading the tombstone you conclude this grave belongs to a great cleric\nthat once roamed these parts.  The ground is soft, almost as if the grave\nwas dug just moments ago.  To the north you see a small building.  To the\neast is the main path leading though the cemetery.  A small tombstone can\nbe seen to the south and to the southwest another path trods down\nalongside the iron fence.\n',161,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27212,-16,5,0,'<w>Before A Large Mausoleum<z>','  The cobblestones here are not as dirty as most.  Leaves litter most of\nthe path as if no one has cleaned this place in quite some time.  You\nbegin to get a strange feeling about this place, as if someone was\nwatching you.  It probably would not be a good idea to visit this place\nafter dark.  To the north you see a large stone building with a door on it.\nThe door looks ominous and forboding.  On the west side of the cobbled\npath sits a large tombstone and to the east a grave that has been dug can\nbe found.\n',161,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27213,-15,5,0,'<w>An Empty Plot<z>','  Better watch your step here, a large hole has been dug in the ground.\nGazing into the hole you estimate it is nearly six feet in depth.  A large\npile of dirt sits haphazardly to the right of the hole.  No tombstone has\nbeen placed at the head of this pit yet.  Water trickles down the sides of\nthe pit, leaving little puddles on the bottom.  It seems this grave was dug\nsome time ago.  To the north is a rather small building with a brown door.\nA dirty looking sign is hung just above the door.  To the west is a\ncobblestone path, south is a broken tombstone and to the southeast you see\nan iron fence troding down another path.\n',161,131072,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27214,-15,-2,-1,'<o>A Bend in A Damp Passage<z>','  Another turn in the tunnel makes you feel as if you were lost in a\nmaze.  The puddles of water seem to stream ever so slowly to the north.\nMud covers the walls and the floor, camouflaging the room.  You struggle\nto make headway through the muck which is knee deep.  To the north you\ncan see a wall of solid mud.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27215,-15,-1,-1,'<o>A Damp, Rubble Filled Passage<z>','  The tunnel ends here suddenly.  Tons of rubble and debris cover the\nground, blocking all exits except for the way you entered this room.  The\nground is wet, but no water is seen.  While a slight breeze can be felt, it\nisn\'t as cold as the other caved-in corridors.  It\'s almost as if the water\nhas ran through the rubble and the air has followed its path.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27216,-17,6,0,'<b>A Tool Shed<z>','  Numerous cobwebs line the corners of this small shed.  There are no\nfloor boards here, just dirt.  Roaches and other small insects scavenge\nthe area for food.  Shovels, rakes, and hoes are placed along the\nwestern wall, while many bags of unknown substances are stacked along\nthe eastern wall.  On the northern wall there is a small window with\ndust covered curtains draping over it.  On the southern wall is a\nsmall door that leads back into the cemetery.\n',161,141800,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27217,-16,6,0,'<w>A Large Mausoleum<z>','Four caskets sit on the floor in rows of two\'s.  Along the walls are\nlarge drawers which house the dead, those who aren\'t buried underground.  A\nsmall nameplate has been riveted into each drawer.  Cobwebs line the\ncorners of each wall and dust covers each casket.  The room is very cold\nand the air has an awful odor.  A small trapdoor is seen  behind the\nnorthern-most casket.  A door to the south leads back into the cemetery.\n',0,139272,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27218,-17,0,-1,'<o>A Damp Passage<z>','  The ground here is slightly damp and makes squishing sounds when you\nstep.  Cold frosty weather races through the air chilling you ever so\nslightly.  The walls are braced by two large pillars of wood on both ends\nfor support.  Another very large pillar of wood braces the ceiling.  You\nfeel more comfortable than before.  The absence of light makes it too\ndifficult to see anything outside this room.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27219,-15,-2,-2,'<y>A Muddy Corridor<z>','  The mud here reaches almost to your knees, making it very hard to move.\nThe ceiling and walls both have many support beams keeping it together.\nEven with support from the wood, the small size of this room makes you\nfeel very uncomfortable.  An awful smell seems to come from the south,\nas does a brisk wind.  Small doors can be seen along the east and west\nwalls.\n',161,139272,33,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(27220,-16,6,-1,'<o>Tunnel Under the Mausoleum<z>','  Walls of mud line this small tunnel.  On the ground numerous puddles\nof water can be found.  Cold air races though this passage and sends\na chill down your spine.  Glancing up you see a lot of water spilling\ndown the walls.  Wiping the water from your eyes, you are able to make\nout a small trapdoor on the ceiling.  Limited light makes it to hard for\nyou to tell what is to your east and west.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27221,-17,6,-1,'<o>Bend in a Small Tunnel<z>','  Puddles of water have made the ground very muddy.  The walls have no\nsupport beams, making you weary that is might cave in any second.  Cold\nair races through the tunnel chilling you ever so slightly.  It is too\ndark for you to see out of this room.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27222,-17,5,-1,'<o>Small Tunnel<z>','  Puddles of water have made the ground very muddy.  The walls have no\nsupport beams, making you weary that a cave in might happen at any\nsecond.  Cold air races through the tunnel chilling you ever so slightly.\nIt is too dark for you to see out of this room.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27223,-17,4,-1,'<o>A Fork in a Small Tunnel<z>','  The tunnel splits in two directions here.  Water trickles towards the\nsoutheast while nothing seems to flow to the southwest.  No cold air\ncan be felt from the southwest either.  Mud covers the unsupported\nwalls making you feel very unsafe.  It is too dark for you to tell what\nis outside of this room.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27224,-16,3,-1,'<o>A Damp Passage','  The ground here is slightly damp.  Cold air sweeps through the passage\nchilling you ever so slightly.  The walls have been braced by two large\npillars of wood on both ends of the entrance for support.  You feel safe\nwith the beams intact.  The absence of light makes it too difficult to\nsee anything outside this room.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27225,-18,3,-1,'<o>A Caved-in Section of the Tunnel','  The tunnel has caved-in here.  Small tools used for digging lie\nscattered in the mud.  The tools must have been used to dig a new tunnel,\nbut for some odd reason the digging has stopped.  Something or someone has\nevidently scared them away.  Glancing upwards you notice the ceiling is\nvery unstable here and decide maybe you should leave also.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27226,-16,2,-1,'<o>A Damp Passage','  The ground here is slightly damp and makes squishing sounds when you\nstep.  Cold frosty weather races through the air chilling you ever so\nslightly.  The walls are braced by two large pillars of wood on both ends\nfor support.  Another very large pillar of wood braces the ceiling.  You\nfeel more comfortable than before.  The absence of light makes it too\ndifficult to see anything outside this room.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27227,-15,2,-1,'<o>A Damp Passage','  The ground here is slightly damp and makes squishing sounds when you\nstep.  Cold frosty weather races through the air chilling you ever so\nslightly.  The walls are braced by two large pillars of wood on both ends\nfor support.  Another very large pillar of wood braces the ceiling.  You\nfeel more comfortable than before.  The absence of light makes it too\ndifficult to see anything outside this room.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27228,-15,1,-1,'<o>A Damp Passage','   The ground here is slightly damp and makes squishing sounds when you\nstep.  Cold frosty weather races through the air chilling you ever so\nslightly.  The walls are braced by two large pillars of wood on both ends\nfor support.  Another very large pillar of wood braces the ceiling.  You\nfeel more comfortable than before.  The absence of light makes it too\ndifficult to see anything outside this room.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27229,-15,0,-1,'<o>A Bend in A Damp Passage','  The ground here is slightly damp and makes squishing sounds when you\nstep.  Cold frosty weather races through the air chilling you ever so\nslightly.  The walls are braced by two large pillars of wood on both ends\nfor support.  Another very large pillar of wood braces the ceiling.  You\nfeel more comfortable than before.  The absence of light makes it too\ndifficult to see anything outside this room.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27230,-15,6,0,'<b>The Caretaker\'s Office<1>','  A cluttered desk sits in the corner of this small room.  On the desk,\nyou see a couple of feather tipped pens, and a lot of papers.  A small\nchair is placed in front of the desk.  Just inside the doorway, a set of\nmuddy footprints lead towards the desk.  The walls are empty and dark\nbrown as is the ceiling.  The door on the southern wall has many locks on\nit.\n',161,141352,33,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27231,-14,6,0,'<b>The Caretaker\'s Atrium<1>','  This courtyard is perhaps the only pretty thing in the cemetery.  A\nfew flowers have started to bloom making a colorful sight to see.  A small\nwooden bench has been placed next to a small tree on the eastern side\nof this atrium.  The view from here is fascinating.  Looking to the east\nyou can make out a large city.\n',161,140288,23,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27232,-18,0,-1,'<o>A Damp Passage','  The ground here is slightly damp and makes squishing sounds when you\nstep.  Cold frosty weather races through the air chilling you ever so\nslightly.  The walls are braced by two large pillars of wood on both ends\nfor support.  Another very large pillar of wood braces the ceiling.  You\nfeel more comfortable than before.  The absence of light makes it too\ndifficult to see anything outside this room.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27233,-18,-1,-1,'<o>A Damp Passage','  The ground here is slightly damp and makes squishing sounds when you\nstep.  Cold frosty weather races through the air chilling you ever so\nslightly.  The walls are braced by two large pillars of wood on both ends\nfor support.  Another very large pillar of wood braces the ceiling.  You\nfeel more comfortable than before.  The absence of light makes it too\ndifficult to see anything outside this room.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27234,-15,6,-1,'<o>A Bend in A Small Tunnel','  Puddles of water have collected making the ground very muddy.  The walls\nhave no support beams, making you weary of a collapsed ceiling.  Cold air\nraces through the tunnel chilling you ever so slightly.  It is too dark\nfor you to see out of this room.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27235,-14,5,-1,'<o>A Bend in A Small Tunnel','  Puddles of water have collected making the ground very muddy.  The walls\nhave no support beams, making you weary of a collapsed ceiling.  Cold air\nraces through the tunnel chilling you ever so slightly.  It is too dark\nfor you to see out of this room.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27236,-14,4,-1,'<o>A Bend in A Small Tunnel','  Puddles of water have collected making the ground very muddy.  The walls\nhave no support beams, making you wary of a collapsed ceiling.  Cold\nair races through the tunnel chilling you ever so slightly.  To the west\nyou can see a small nook.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27237,-18,-2,-1,'<o>The Edge of A Murky Pool of Water','  The tunnel takes yet another sharp turn here.  The ground is a lot\nmore soggy than in the previous room.  Cold water rises almost to your\nknees as you tread your way through the mud.  Cold air blows rather\nfierce in this section of the tunnel, kinda like an ocean breeze in mid\nwinter.  Looking to the east you see a small pool of muddy water and to\nthe north is the damp passage under the cemetery.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27238,-17,-2,-1,'<y>Atop A Pool of Muddy Water','  Just as one would suspect, the water here is colder than the air\nitself.  You try to peer down through the water but it\'s so muddy you\nare not able to make out a thing.  Water splashes in your face as you\ntry to make way through this mud filled pool.  To the east and west\nyou can see higher ground.\n',161,139272,8,0,0,0,5,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27239,-16,-2,-1,'<o>The Edge of A Murky Pool of Water','  The ground is a lot more soggy than in the previous room.  Cold water rises\nalmost to you knees as you treed your way through the mud.  Cold air blows\nrather fierce in this section of the tunnel, kinda like an ocean breeze in\nmid winter.  A short ways to the east you see a solid wall of mud, while to the\nwest is a muddy pool of water.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27240,-17,-2,-2,'<y>A Muddy Pool of Water<z>','  Your bones shiver and your body quivers as you swim beneath the muddy\nwater here.  The water here is much colder than that at the surface of the\npool.  On the bottom of the pool you notice a small chest sitting in the\ncorner.  Making your way to the bottom you notice the ground here is almost\nas soft as quick-sand, yet the chest doesn\'t seem to sink at all.  The only\nway out of this icy grave is to try and swim to the surface.\n',161,139272,30,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27241,-15,4,-1,'<o>A Small Nook','  Walls of solid dirt surround you here.  Odd these walls aren\'t muddy\nas the previous.  The ground here seems to have no puddles or standing\nwater either.  Cold air swirls around you leaving you to suspect that the\nonly exit is your east.  Above your head, many small bats dangle from\ntheir feet.  To the east you can see a small passage.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27242,-16,-2,-2,'<r>A Casket Filled Niche','  A small torch serves as light in this dark, mysterious room.  Stacked\nalong all the northern and southern wall are many small caskets, all of\nwhich are empty.  This room is very dry and oddly very warm.  On the eastern\nwall is the door leading out of this chamber.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27243,-14,-2,-2,'<r>A Storage Room','  A few shelves line this empty storage room.  Besides dust and\na broken chair in the middle of the floor, there is nothing here.  A\nfew puddles of water cover the floor, that you guess came through\nthe crack between the door to the west and the floor.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27244,-15,-3,-2,'<y>A Muddy Corridor','  The mud here comes almost to your knees, making it very hard to move.\nThe ceiling and walls both have many support beams keeping it together.\nEven with support from the wood, the small size of this room makes you\nfeel very uncomfortable.  An awful smell seems to come from the south,\nas does a brisk wind.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(27245,-15,-4,-2,'<y>End of A Muddy Corridor','  The mud here comes almost to your knees, making it very hard to move.\nThe ceiling and walls both have many support beams keeping it together.\nEven with support from the wood, the small size of this room makes you\nfeel very uncomfortable.  The smell is at its worst here, and the air is\nstale.  Many panels cover the southern wall.  To the west and the east there\nare small doors.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27246,-14,-4,-2,'<r>An Empty Chamber','  Stale air fills this room of nothingness.  The floor is completely\ndry and no traces of mud can be found.  Evidently no one has used this\nroom in quite some time.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27247,-15,-5,-2,'<p>Shroud\'s Lair<1>','  A transparent floor catches your sight as you enter this room.  The\nthought of falling to your death enters your mind.  Looking downwards\nyou see a place that resembles hell.  Quickly lifting your head, you scan\nthe room.  All the walls are bare asides from the northern wall which\nis covered with several panels.\n',161,139624,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27248,-15,-1,-2,'<y>A Muddy Corridor','  The mud here comes almost to your knees, making it very hard to move.\nThe ceiling and walls both have many support beams keeping it together.\nEven with support from the wood, the small size of this room makes you\nfeel very uncomfortable.  An awful smell seems to come from the south,\nas does a brisk wind.  Above your head is some loosely hanging rubble.\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,8,80,0,'',NULL),
(27249,-16,-4,-2,'<r>A Blood-stained Alcove <1>','  In the center of the room a small table sitting above many small pools\nof blood.  The floor is made of solid granite rocks and is quite hard.\nOn the northern wall, looks to be a weapon rack.  On the western\nwall is a small shrine made of solid jade.  Perched atop a circular box,\nlocated on the southern wall is a book entitled, \"Death\'s Many Forms\".\n',161,139272,13,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27250,0,0,0,'On the Kranor River','You are on the River Kranor.  This wide, flowing river is deep and cold, and\nruns from its spring deep in the Parnithian Mountains all the way to the Myrian\nOcean. \n',-1,131072,29,0,0,0,36,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27251,0,0,0,'On the Kranor River','  You are on the River Kranor.  This wide, flowing river is deep and cold, and\nruns from its spring deep in the Parnithian Mountains all the way to the Myrian\nOcean. \n',204,131072,29,0,0,0,36,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
