(27292,0,0,0,'On the Kranor River','  You are on the River Kranor.  This wide, flowing river is deep and cold, and\nruns from its spring deep in the Parnithian Mountains all the way to the Myrian\nOcean. \n',204,131072,29,0,0,0,36,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27293,0,0,0,'Under the River Kranor','  <o>Silty waters<z> churn about with the current and cut out any light that\nmight come from the sky above.  Something has burrowed into the riverbed of\nthe Kranor here, leaving deep claw marks in the stones and clay.  The tunnel\ncontinues downward.  Upward is the surface of the river.  \n',204,131080,30,0,0,0,15,5,2,250,0,'',NULL),
(27294,0,0,0,'Under the River Kranor','  <o>Silty waters<z> churn about with the current and cut out any light that\nmight come from the sky above.  Something has burrowed into the riverbed of\nthe Kranor here, leaving deep claw marks in the stones and clay.  The tunnel\ncontinues upward and downward.  \n',204,131080,30,0,0,0,15,5,2,250,0,'',NULL),
(27295,0,0,0,'Under the River Kranor','  <o>Silty waters<z> churn about with the current and cut out any light that\nmight come from the sky above.  Something has burrowed into the riverbed of\nthe Kranor here, leaving deep claw marks in the stones and clay.  The tunnel\ncontinues upward and downward.  \n',204,131080,30,0,0,0,15,5,2,250,0,'',NULL),
(27296,0,0,0,'Cave Under the River Kranor','<o>Silty waters<z> churn about with the current and cut out any light that\nmight come from the sky above.  Something has burrowed into the riverbed of\nthe Kranor here, leaving deep claw marks in the stones and clay.  A tunnel\nstretches into the water above, opening here into a cave that continues to the\nnorth, northeast, and east.  \n',0,131080,30,0,0,0,15,1,8,250,0,'',NULL),
(27297,0,0,0,'Cave Under the River Kranor','<o>Silt<z> churns lazily in the chilly waters.  Something carved an\nunderwater cavern from the riverbed of the Kranor here, leaving deep claw\nmarks in the stones and clay.  The cave continues to the west, northwest, and\nnorth. \n',0,131080,30,0,0,0,15,0,8,250,0,'',NULL),
(27298,0,0,0,'Cave Under the River Kranor','<o>Silt<z> churns lazily in the chilly waters.  Something carved an\nunderwater cavern from the riverbed of the Kranor here, leaving deep claw\nmarks in the stones and clay.  The cave continues to the east, southeast, and\nsouth. \n',0,131080,30,0,0,0,15,2,8,250,0,'',NULL),
(27299,0,0,0,'Cave Under the River Kranor','<o>Silt<z> churns lazily in the chilly waters.  Something carved an\nunderwater cavern from the riverbed of the Kranor here, leaving deep claw\nmarks in the stones and clay.  The cave continues to the west, southwest, and\nsouth. \n',0,131080,30,0,0,0,15,3,8,250,0,'',NULL),
(27300,26,-15,0,'Inside The Ruins','  <k>Fallen chunks of shattered stone blocks covered in trailing vines and\nspringy moss, effectively bar the way to the south.  The remains of a\nfountain teeter on the edge of an immense hole to the east where the floor\nhas dropped away.  Noxious smells are coming from whatever lies below in the\ndarkness.  Large stone columns stand to the northeast and the southeast, but\nthere remains enough of the floor to get around them.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27301,27,-14,0,'The Northwest Corner of the Main Hall','  <g>This cavernous room must have been the main hall of the tower before it\ncame to ruin.  Nothing looks very safe, though one can\'t help but want to\nexplore.  A large statue without a head lies on its side near the column to the\nsouthwest.  Fallen chunks of shattered stone block covered in vines and moss\neffectively blocks the path to the north.  To the south the remains of a\nfountain teeter on the western edge of an immense hole in the crumbling\nfloor.  Scuffles and murmurs can be heard in the distance.  An extremely large\nbeetle scuttles from the shadow of a pile of rubble, over some green leafed\nvines and into a crack under a stone.  Vines and weeds cover almost every\nsurface.  A large stone column stands to the southwest but there is a path\naround it.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27302,27,-16,0,'The Southwest Corner of the Main Hall','  <g>This cavernous room must have been the main hall of the tower before it\ncame to ruin.  To the north the remains of a fountain teeter on the western\nedge of an immense dark hole in the crumbling floor.  The air is rank with\noffensive smells.  There is something moving in the foliage.  Across the room\non the far side of the hole to the northeast, a fireplace burns brightly.\nExploring to the southeast is an option even with the crumbling floor as long\nas one stays near the wall.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27303,28,-14,0,'Northwest of the Center in the Main Hall','<g>  A large fireplace is built into the northern wall.  To the south the\nremains of a fountain teeter on the western edge of an immense hole in the\ncrumbling floor.  It smells horrible here, perhaps if you breathe through\nyour mouth it won\'t be so bad.  The leaves rustle as things move among\nthe foliage.  You can see a spiral staircase a ways to the southeast.<z>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27304,28,-17,0,'The West End of the Dining Hall','  <g>Broken planks are in splinters everywhere.  Some of the long trestle tables\nremain intact, but are covered in vines and leaves.  There are insects crawling\nover every surface.  To the west is another mound of ivy covered stone blocks.\nTo the north is an immense hole with the fountain teetering on the western\nedge.  There is a fireplace on the far eastern wall of this large room.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27305,28,-18,0,'The Pantry','  <k>The walls are lined with mostly broken shelves.  The remnants of several\nlarge crates are scattered along the east wall.  One crate looks odd, maybe\nbecause it is the only one intact.  A large spider sits in a delicate web\nnear the ceiling slowly wrapping a beetle in sticky webbing.  The smell from\nthis room is enough to make anyone gag.  Large piles of dung are covered in\nflies and maggots.  Small bones are strewn about.  This must be the refuse\nroom of the gnolls, but from what has been lying about so far, they aren\'t\nreally choosy where they relieve themselves.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,4,'',NULL),
(27306,28,-18,-1,'The Wine Cellar','  <k>The floor is littered with broken bottles and splintered wood.  A few\nbroken barrels with rusty bands lie within a large heap of rubble to the\nnorth.  Bugs are crawling everywhere.  Thick patches of dark mold grow up the\nwest wall.  Dripping water, diverted by moss grown thick and spongy, trickles\ndown the southern wall.  Slimy pools of dark water stand inches deep in several\nlow spots in the room.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,4,'',NULL),
(27307,29,-13,0,'A Study','  <k>These huge windows look like they were originally made to take\nadvantage of the light for reading or studying.  A breeze blows in the\nwindow giving a welcome respite to the fetid air of the ruins.  A hooting\nsound comes from outside in the distance.  A once grand table is almost\ncovered over with vines and moss.  Broken chairs lean drunkenly against\nthe wall.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27308,29,-14,0,'North of the Center of the Main Hall','  <o>This is the mid-point of this huge room.  To the southeast there is a\nlarge stone column encircled with stairs.  The floor has crumbled away to\nthe south leaving a jagged hole, a fountain teeters on the southwestern\nedge.  A swarm of gnats hovers over something in the foliage.  The air is\nputrid and rank with odors.  One fireplace glows with flickering light to the\nnorthwest and another a ways to the east.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27309,29,-17,0,'The East End of the Dining Hall','  <g>Parts of long trestle tables are covered with the vines and leaves.\nSome are actually kind of clean if one doesn\'t count the claw marks\nand gouges, or the occasional bug that scurries across them.  It must\nhave been the dining hall of the tower before it came to ruin.  A large\nfireplace sits within the east wall.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27310,29,-18,0,'West End of the Kitchen','  <o>This large room is hot and muggy.  There is a huge fireplace set\nalong the south wall.  A big black pot hangs from a metal swing arm\nset over the fire, its contents boiling.  The smell combined with the\nputrid air is sickening.  Bones litter the floor.   Bugs are swarming\neverywhere.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27311,30,-14,0,'Northeast of the Center in the Main Hall','  <g>This room is huge.  Fallen chunks of shattered stone covered in vines\nand moss are scattered around.  Something in the foliage rustles nearby.\nThere is a circular stone stairway to the south leading up into the tower.\nA fat rat streaks by, running from one pile of rubble to another.  The\nfoliage next to a vine covered stone is quivering.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27312,30,-15,0,'A Circular Stone Stairway','<k>This stairway is cut into the side of a huge pillar of stone, winding\naround and upwards to disappear into the ceiling.    There is no handrail\nand it is hard to tell if there ever was one.  The stairs themselves seem to be\nintact for the most part, only a few of the steps seem to be chipped.  A\nlarge beetle scuttles quickly up the broad middle column.  It loses its\nfooting and falls to a stair.  After a moment it scurries straight for the\nedge and falls off out of sight in the rubble and weed strewn floor.  To the\nwest lies the crumbling floor, the remains of a fountain seem to teeter on\nthe western edge.<1>\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27313,30,-18,0,'The Middle of a Huge Kitchen','  <o>This large room is hot and muggy.  Three huge fireplaces are set\nalong the southern wall.  There are fires burning in two of them.  A big\nblack pot hanging from a metal swing arm has steam rising from it.  The\nsmell combined with the putrid air is sickening.  Bones litter the floor.\nBugs are swarming everywhere.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27314,31,-13,0,'A Storage Room','  <k>This room has several bundles of rags lying about within the foliage\nwhich has grown here.  This must be the sleeping lair for the Gnolls.\nWhile it smells rank and musky it looks surprisingly clean.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27315,31,-14,0,'Northeast Corner of the Main Hall','  <g>This room is huge.  Fallen chunks of shattered stone covered in vines\nand moss are scattered around.  Better be careful here it looks dangerous.\nThere is a circular stone stairway to the southwest leading up into the\ntower.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27316,31,-15,0,'East End of the Main Hall','  <g>This room is huge.  Fallen chunks of shattered stone covered in vines\nand moss are scattered around.  Better be careful here it looks dangerous.\nThis room is a bit cleaner than the others in the main hall.  The smell of\nincense is coming from the east.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27317,31,-17,0,'A Hallway','  <o>This room is a long hallway that connects the kitchen area with the\nMeditation Hall.  Several large moss covered stones are half blocking the\nroom at the end but there is enough room to pass by them to the northeast.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27318,31,-18,0,'The East End of a Huge Kitchen','  <o>This large room is hot and muggy.  There is a huge fireplace in the\nsouth wall.  It is not being used but two more to the west have something\ncooking in big black pots.  The smell combined with the putrid air is\nsickening.  Bones litter the floor.  Bugs are swarming everywhere.  A\nhallway leads north.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27319,32,-16,0,'The Meditation Hall','  <k>This room is almost clear of vines and weeds.  Several small alcoves\nare set within the walls.  Each has a small bench.  Incense wafts from a\nlarge altar to the east.  Strange <r>symbols<z> <k>and markings have been drawn\non the floor and on the walls.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27320,27,-17,0,'A Closet','  <k>This small room has a very large crack running down the wall and across\nthe floor.  There is a small dark hole in the floor where one of the stones\nis missing.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27321,26,-15,1,'A Storage Room','  <k>Mostly broken shelves line the walls.  The smell from this room is\nenough to make anyone gag.  Large piles of dung are covered in flies and\nmaggots.  Small bones are scattered about.  This must be the refuse room\nfor the hobgoblins.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27322,27,-14,1,'A Closet','  <k>The floor is strewn with broken shelves and pottery.  Several pallets\nof brightly colored cloth are scattered about.  The room is very dirty and\nsmells fetid and rank.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27323,27,-15,1,'End of a Long Hall on the Second Floor','  <o>Barrels made of wood and banded with metal are stacked along the\nwalls lining both sides of the hall.  The floor has a visible indentation\nin the stone down the center of the hall where many feet have trod.  There\nare more barrels stacked in the hall to the east.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(27324,27,-16,1,'A Hot and Muggy Room','  <k>The dampness of this room make the lingering odor even worse.  The\nslimy walls drip with moisture.  There are several small fires burning with\npots of water boiling.  For the room to be this moist these pots must boil\nmost night and day.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27325,28,-13,1,'Student Dormitory','  <k>The iron rail bedsteads along the walls are still intact.  Instead of\ncontaining the down or straw filled mattresses which the young novice\nused while studying here, there are remnants of once bright colored cloth\nin dirty bundles.  The air is rank and foul smelling.  The room continues\nto the east.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27326,28,-14,1,'A Workroom','  <o>Several scarred tables are in this room.  Broken glass and pottery\ncovers the floor.  Several moldy books are lying open on the dirty floor.\nPieces of broken furniture are stacked in the corner.  The room continues\nto the east.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27327,28,-15,1,'A Long Hall on the Second Floor','  <k>There are places on the wall that are a slightly lighter shade of dirt\nwhere tapestries have been pulled down.  They were most likely used to\nmake a few the many sleeping pallets seen about.  The floor has a visible\nindentation in the stone down the center of the hall where many feet have\ntrod.  Some barrels are stacked along the wall.  You can see more barrels\nto the west.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27328,28,-16,1,'A Laboratory','   <k>A long worktable stands against the north wall.  It has quite a\nfew intact bottles on it.  The south wall is lined with shelves some are\nbroken.  The floor is littered with broken vials and bottles.  Small bunches\nof herbs still hang from the lower rafters here and there.  A cracked\nmortar lies next to its chipped pestle under a table in the middle of the\nroom.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(27329,29,-13,1,'Student Dormitory','  <k>The iron rail bedsteads along the walls are still intact.  Instead of\ncontaining the down or straw filled mattresses which the young novice\nused while studying here, there are remnants of once bright colored cloth\nin dirty bundles.  The air is rank and foul smelling.  The room continues\nto the west.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27330,29,-14,1,'A Workroom','  <o>Several scarred tables are in this room.  Broken glass and pottery\ncovers the floor.  Several moldy books are lying open on the dirty floor.\nPieces of  broken furniture are stacked in the corner.  The room continues\nto the west.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27331,29,-15,1,'A Long Hall on the Second Floor','  <k>There are places on the wall that are a slightly lighter shade of dirt\nwhere tapestries have been pulled down.  The were most likely used to\nmake a few the many sleeping pallets you\'ve seen.  The floor has a visible\nindentation in the stone down the center of the hall where many feet have\ntrod.  You see some barrels down the hall to the west.  A circular stone\nstaircase is to the east.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27332,29,-16,1,'A Collapsed Bedroom','  <k>The ceiling seems to have fallen in on this room.  Judging from the\namount of rubble in the room perhaps the walls from the room above now\nreside here too.  You can see a path through the crumbled stones to the\nwest and the north.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,40,0,'',NULL),
(27333,30,-14,1,'North Hall','  <k>There are chunks of stone chipped from several places in the walls.\nScraps and gouges line the walls as well.  The floor has a visible\nindentation in the stone down the center of the hall where many feet\nhave trod.  A large circular stone staircase lies to the south.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(27334,30,-15,1,'Circular Stone Staircase on the Second Floor','  <o>The air is rank with odors.  You can see down the hallway to the\nwest some barrels are stacked along the wall at the far end.  The stair\ncircles a column both up and down from here.  A large torch burns on\nthe wall to the east.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27335,30,-16,1,'South Hall','  <k>There are places on the wall that are a slightly lighter shade of dirt\nwhere tapestries have been pulled down.  They were most likely used to\nmake a few of the many sleeping pallets you\'ve seen.  The floor has a\nvisible indentation in the stone down the center of the hall where many\nfeet have trod.  A large circular stone staircase lies to the north.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27336,31,-14,1,'A Tranquil Chamber','  This room gives you a sense of inner peace.  This room doesn\'t seem to\nhave been touched by the hobgoblins or anyone in quite a while.  The floor\nis thick with dust.\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(27337,31,-16,1,'A Sleeping Chamber','  <o>The remnants of a blue wall hanging are still suspended from the\nstone walls.  Pallets of bright colored cloth and straw are everywhere\nabout the room, which smells musty and rank.  Thick cobwebs hang in the\ncorners stretched from the high ceiling overhead.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27338,31,-14,2,'A Supply Room','  <o>The unbroken shelves in this room are stacked with an assortment of\nitems.  One shelf holds some leather satchels, another some lanterns, while\nanother has a stack of torches and there is one that has an assortment of\nrocks.  A person can\'t help but wonder what the rocks are for.  This must\nbe the supply room of the hobgoblins.  Some crates are stacked in the\ncorner.  Pieces of a broken crate are strewn about.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27339,30,-13,2,'A Sleeping Room','  <o>There are scraps of tattered wall hangings of a yellowish color upon\nthe walls.  There are pieces of dirty armor stacked in a heap.  A weapon\nrack sits here.  Some broken swords are standing in the corner.  The\nhobgoblins must now use this room as an armory.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27340,30,-14,2,'The East End of the Hallway on the Third Floor','  <k>A cook fire burns in the middle of the room.  The smell of the meat\ncooking is unappetizing.  Some barrels are lined along the wall.  A large\ncircular stone staircase is to the south.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27341,30,-15,2,'Circular Stone Staircase on the Third Floor','  <k>The air is rank and musty.  Several of these top stairs are almost half\ngone.  There are scrape marks on stair steps as if someone were hacking\nat them with something.  You have to step over a fresh pile of dung as you\ngo.  Thick mold lines the center column, but is worn away on the steps\nthemselves.  The inner edge of the stairs is slick with slime.  Better watch\nthe footing here.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27342,29,-14,2,'A Hallway on the Third Floor','  <k>A torn tapestry flutters slightly when anyone passes by.  The stone\nwalls and flooring are cracked and caked with dirt and grime.  Cobwebs\nreside in the corners and edges of the ceiling.  There is a visible pathway\non the flagstones beneath your feet.  Many people have traversed these\nhalls.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27343,29,-15,2,'The Library','  <o>Ripped and torn books litter the floor with various pages strewn\neverywhere.  Some of the ceiling high bookshelves have managed to remain\nintact.  Several chairs are still in good condition if one doesn\'t count\nthe padding  that is coming out of the rent fabric here and there.  Several\ncolorful bundles of rags are in the corner making a row of pallets.  The air\nsmells musky and dank.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27344,28,-13,2,'A Sleeping Chamber','  <k>Faded wall coverings of green and gold hang from the walls.  The\nremains of a large once canopied bed is along the north wall.  Several\npallets of bright colored cloth are here and there on the floor.  This must\nbe a sleeping lair of the hobgoblins.  The room is musky and dirty.  A\nfireplace stands along the north wall.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27345,28,-14,2,'End of a Hall','  <k>The hallway ends here.  It looks as though this room is used as a\npractice area.  A target has been drawn on the wall.  A few broken spears\nhave been thrown in to the corner.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27346,28,-15,2,'A Sleeping Chamber','  <k>A broken shelf leans drunkenly against the western wall.  Several\ncrates are stacked here.  A few bundles of rags have been scattered about.\nThis looks like its now used as a sleeping lair for the hobgoblins.  The\nroom smells musky and dank.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27347,29,-14,3,'Laboratory of the High Mage','  <k>A large part of the original western wall has been filled in carelessly\nwith mortar and broken chunks of stone.  The trailing vines growing up the\nwall are doing their part in holding it all together.  The rest of the wall\nis scorched and scarred, perhaps from a spell gone wrong.  There are a few\nshelves still standing, littered with broken vials.  Several moldy tomes lie\nrotting amid the clutter.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(27348,30,-14,3,'Library','  <k>The wall to the east is missing quite a few stones.  Vines are climbing\neverywhere.  In some places they are so thick they have almost replaced the\nwalls.  Toward the west the vines have been cut back.  The remains of a few\nbooks are scattered around.  Some moldy tomes rest on the unbroken shelves\nthat stand against the northern wall.<1>\n',163,131080,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27349,30,-15,3,'Circular Stone Staircase at the Top of the Tower','  <g>Almost all of this top floor has crumbled to ruin.  There are a couple\nof rooms to the north that are somewhat intact.  Green leafy vines cover\neverything.  Some are growing through the cracks in the masonry so much that\nit looks like they are pulling the stones from their mortar casings.  You can\nsee the walls of the city of Grimhaven to the northwest.<1>\n',163,131072,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27500,0,0,0,'Northwest Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches to the south of here.  There is a slight\ngradient down towards the east, and there seems to be a raised area of this\nisland to the south and west of you.  Over the tops of the trees to the\nsoutheast you can see a cove with an islet in the center of it.  Distantly to\nthe southeast, you think you see a faint tendril of smoke rising through the\ngreen leaves.  The stout trunks and vines of the rain forest are too dense to\nsee through to the south and southwest.  To the north is a massive ocean\ncovered in impossibly thick fog, and waves occasionally smash against the\nrocky cliffs of the northern coast of this island.  Marine birds float\nlazily in the currents of salty air.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27501,0,0,0,'North Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches south of here, and a vast fog-covered ocean\nextends to the north.  The forest is thick with leaves, trunks, and vines,\nand the air is dense with animal sounds.  A gradient leads upwards to the\nwest, and several roots and vines protruding from the moist earth would aid\nyou in climbing up that way.  South of here the forest splits into to levels,\none above which can be reached by climbing up the hill to the west, and one\nbelow which you are now on.  Mist clings to the cliff face to the south, and\ncasts an eerie and chill presence upon the island.  The waves of the ocean to\nthe north occasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of the northern coast\nof this island, and marine birds are forced to temporarily flee their rocky\nperches or be crushed against the jagged stones of the coast.  You are glad\nto be above the dangerous looking waters, although the rain forest does not\nseem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27502,0,0,0,'North Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches south of here, and a vast fog-covered ocean\nextends to the north.  The forest is thick with leaves, trunks, and vines,\nand the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves of the ocean to the north\noccasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of the northern coast of this\nisland, and marine birds are forced to temporarily flee their rocky perches\nor be crushed against the jagged stones of the coast.  You are glad to be\nabove the dangerous looking waters, although the rain forest does not\nseem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27503,0,0,0,'North Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches south of here, and a vast fog-covered ocean\nextends to the north.  The forest is thick with leaves, trunks, and vines,\nand the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves of the ocean to the north\noccasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of the northern coast of this\nisland, and marine birds are forced to temporarily flee their rocky perches\nor be crushed against the jagged stones of the coast.  You are glad to be\nabove the dangerous looking waters, although the rain forest does not\nseem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27504,0,0,0,'North Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches south of here, and a vast fog-covered ocean\nextends to the north.  The forest is thick with leaves, trunks, and vines,\nand the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves of the ocean to the north\noccasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of the northern coast of this\nisland, and marine birds are forced to temporarily flee their rocky perches\nor be crushed against the jagged stones of the coast.  You are glad to be\nabove the dangerous looking waters, although the rain forest does not\nseem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27505,0,0,0,'North Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches south of here, and a vast fog-covered ocean\nextends to the north.  The forest is thick with leaves, trunks, and vines,\nand the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves of the ocean to the north\noccasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of the northern coast of this\nisland, and marine birds are forced to temporarily flee their rocky perches\nor be crushed against the jagged stones of the coast.  You are glad to be\nabove the dangerous looking waters, although the rain forest does not\nseem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27506,0,0,0,'Northeast Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches southwest of here, and a vast fog-covered\nocean extends to the north and east.  The forest is thick with leaves,\ntrunks, and vines, and the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves\nof the ocean to the north occasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of\nthe northeastern coast of this island, and marine birds are forced to\ntemporarily flee their rocky perches or be crushed against the jagged\nstones of the coast.  You are glad to be above the dangerous looking\nwaters, although the rain forest does not seem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27507,0,0,0,'Northwest Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches southeast of here, and a vast fog-covered\nocean extends to the north and west.  The forest is thick with leaves,\ntrunks, and vines, and the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves\nof the ocean to the north occasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of\nthe northwestern coast of this island, and marine birds are forced to\ntemporarily flee their rocky perches or be crushed against the jagged\nstones of the coast.  You are glad to be above the dangerous looking\nwaters, although the rain forest does not seem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27508,0,0,0,'Northwest Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches out to the west and east, and a vast fog-\ncovered ocean extends to the north and west.  To the southeast, the moist\nearth drops away sharply and allows you to see over the top of the forest\nand into a cove at the center of the island.  The cliff to the southeast\nseems too precarious to navigate despite the vines and roots growing out\nof it.  The forest is thick with leaves, trunks, and vines, and the air is\ndense with animal sounds.  The waves of the ocean to the north occasionally\nsmash against the rocky cliffs of the northewestern coast of this island,\nand marine birds are forced to temporarily flee their rocky perches or be\ncrushed against the jagged stones of the coast.  You are glad to be above\nthe dangerous looking waters, although the rain forest does not seem much\nmore inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27509,0,0,0,'Northwest Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches out to the north and west, and a vast fog-\ncovered ocean extends to the north and west.  To the southeast, the moist\nearth drops away sharply and allows you to see over the top of the forest\nand into a cove at the center of the island.  The cliff to the southeast\nseems too precarious to navigate despite the vines and roots growing out\nof it.  The forest is thick with leaves, trunks, and vines, and the air is\ndense with animal sounds.  The waves of the ocean to the north occasionally\nsmash against the rocky cliffs of the northewestern coast of this island,\nand marine birds are forced to temporarily flee their rocky perches or be\ncrushed against the jagged stones of the coast.  You are glad to be above\nthe dangerous looking waters, although the rain forest does not seem much\nmore inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27510,0,0,0,'Base of a Cliff in a Rain Forest','  To the west a tall, sharp cliff rises menacingly out of the moist earth\nof a dense green rain forest.  The forest itself stretches in all other\ndirections, and its suprising density makes it impossible to see far.  Leaves\nand vines twist around you and seem to grab at you like soft hands.  From\nwithin the forest come occasional hollers and thrashing of the underbrush.\nA swarm of gnats buzzes around your head, and a bead of sweat drips from\nyour eyelid.  During the day, the canopy of leaves provides a welcome\nrespite from the intense sun, though it is impossible to evade the\nsweltering heat entirely.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27511,0,0,0,'A Rain Forest','  You are in the depths of a rain forest -- you cannot tell exactly how\nfar in you are due to the amazing density of the foliage.  The leaves\nare so thick that even in the height of the afternoon no light is able\nto penetrate through the trees to the ground.  All about you are twisted\nvines and sounds of creatures walking, climbing, and thrashing about the\nbrush.  The humid air sticks to you and seems to suffocate you.  Sweat\nis barely permitted to escape your pores to cool your body.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27512,0,0,0,'A Rain Forest','  You are in the depths of a rain forest -- you cannot tell exactly how\nfar in you are due to the amazing density of the foliage.  The leaves\nare so thick that even in the height of the afternoon no light is able\nto penetrate through the trees to the ground.  All about you are twisted\nvines and sounds of creatures walking, climbing, and thrashing about the\nbrush.  The humid air sticks to you and seems to suffocate you.  Sweat\nis barely permitted to escape your pores to cool your body.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27513,0,0,0,'A Rain Forest','  You are in the depths of a rain forest -- you cannot tell exactly how\nfar in you are due to the amazing density of the foliage.  The leaves\nare so thick that even in the height of the afternoon no light is able\nto penetrate through the trees to the ground.  All about you are twisted\nvines and sounds of creatures walking, climbing, and thrashing about the\nbrush.  The humid air sticks to you and seems to suffocate you.  Sweat\nis barely permitted to escape your pores to cool your body.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27514,0,0,0,'A Rain Forest','  You are in the depths of a rain forest -- you cannot tell exactly how\nfar in you are due to the amazing density of the foliage.  The leaves\nare so thick that even in the height of the afternoon no light is able\nto penetrate through the trees to the ground.  All about you are twisted\nvines and sounds of creatures walking, climbing, and thrashing about the\nbrush.  The humid air sticks to you and seems to suffocate you.  Sweat\nis barely permitted to escape your pores to cool your body.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27515,0,0,0,'Northeast Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches southwest of here, and a vast fog-covered\nocean extends to the north and east.  The forest is thick with leaves,\ntrunks, and vines, and the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves\nof the ocean to the north occasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of\nthe northeastern coast of this island, and marine birds are forced to\ntemporarily flee their rocky perches or be crushed against the jagged\nstones of the coast.  You are glad to be above the dangerous looking\nwaters, although the rain forest does not seem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27516,0,0,0,'Northeast Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches southwest of here, and a vast fog-covered\nocean extends to the north and east.  The forest is thick with leaves,\ntrunks, and vines, and the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves\nof the ocean to the north occasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of\nthe northeastern coast of this island, and marine birds are forced to\ntemporarily flee their rocky perches or be crushed against the jagged\nstones of the coast.  You are glad to be above the dangerous looking\nwaters, although the rain forest does not seem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27517,0,0,0,'Northwest Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches southeast of here, and a vast fog-covered\nocean extends to the north and west.  The forest is thick with leaves,\ntrunks, and vines, and the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves\nof the ocean to the north occasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of\nthe northwestern coast of this island, and marine birds are forced to\ntemporarily flee their rocky perches or be crushed against the jagged\nstones of the coast.  You are glad to be above the dangerous looking\nwaters, although the rain forest does not seem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27518,0,0,0,'Northwest Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches out to the southwest and northeast, and\na vast fog-covered ocean extends to the north and west.  To the southeast,\nthe moist earth drops away sharply and allows you to see over the top of\nthe forest and into a cove at the center of the island.  The cliff to the\nsoutheast seems too precarious to navigate despite the vines and roots\ngrowing out of it.  The forest is thick with leaves, trunks, and vines,\nand the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves of the ocean to the\nnorth occasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of the northwestern\ncoast of this island, and marine birds are forced to temporarily flee their\nrocky perches or be crushed against the jagged stones of the coast.  You\nare glad to be above the dangerous looking waters, although the rain\nforest does not seem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27519,0,0,0,'Edge of a Cliff in a Rain Forest','  A dense rain forest stretches out to the northeast and southwest.  To the\nsouth and east, the moist earth drops away sharply and allows you to see over\nthe top of the forest and into a cove at the center of the island.  The cliff\nto the southeast seems too precarious to navigate despite the vines and roots\ngrowing out of it.  The forest is thick with leaves, trunks, and vines, and\nthe air is dense with animal sounds.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27520,0,0,0,'Base of a Cliff in a Rain Forest','  To the northwest a tall, sharp cliff rises menacingly out of the moist\nearth of a dense green rain forest.  The forest itself stretches in all\nother directions, and its suprising density makes it impossible to see far.\nLeaves and vines twist around you and seem to grab at you like soft hands.\nFrom within the forest come occasional hollers and thrashing of the\nunderbrush.  A swarm of gnats buzzes around your head, and a bead of sweat\ndrips from your eyelid.  During the day, the canopy of leaves provides a\nwelcome respite from the intense sun, though it is impossible to evade the\nsweltering heat entirely.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27521,0,0,0,'A Rain Forest','  To the northwest you see a  sharp cliff rising menacingly out of the moist\nearth of a dense green rain forest.  The forest itself stretches in all\nother directions, and its suprising density makes it impossible to see far.\nLeaves and vines twist around you and seem to grab at you like soft hands.\nFrom within the forest come occasional hollers and thrashing of the\nunderbrush.  A swarm of gnats buzzes around your head, and a bead of sweat\ndrips from your eyelid.  During the day, the canopy of leaves provides a\nwelcome respite from the intense sun, though it is impossible to evade the\nsweltering heat entirely.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27522,0,0,0,'A White Silt Beach','  Beautiful, soft white sands stretch to the east and south on the edge of a\ncrystal clear turquoise-watered cove.  Surrounding the beach to the north and\nwest is a dense, verdant rain forest.  You see large insects crawling in the\nsilt near the forest line, and you hear hollers and chatter from a multitude of\nanimals from the trees above.  In the middle of the cove, to the southeast, is\na small islet.\n',168,131072,54,200,27522,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27523,0,0,0,'A White Silt Beach','  Beautiful, soft white sands stretch to the east and west on the edge of a\ncrystal clear turquoise-watered cove.  Bordering the beach to the north is a\ndense, verdant rain forest.  You see large insects crawling in the silt near\nthe forest line, and you hear hollers and chatter from a multitude of animals\nfrom the trees above.  In the middle of the cove, to the southeast, is a small\nislet.\n',168,131072,54,200,27523,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
