(27525,0,0,0,'A White Silt Beach','  Beautiful, soft white sands stretch to the east and west on the edge of a\ncrystal clear turquoise-watered cove.  Bordering the beach to the north is a\ndense, verdant rain forest.  You see large insects crawling in the silt near\nthe forest line, and you hear hollers and chatter from a multitude of animals\nfrom the trees above.  In the middle of the cove, to the south, is a small\nislet.\n',168,131072,54,200,27525,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27526,0,0,0,'A White Silt Beach','  Beautiful, soft white sands stretch to the east and west on the edge of a\ncrystal clear turquoise-watered cove.  Bordering the beach to the north is a\ndense, verdant rain forest.  You see large insects crawling in the silt near\nthe forest line, and you hear hollers and chatter from a multitude of animals\nfrom the trees above.  In the middle of the cove, to the south, is a small\nislet.\n',168,131072,54,200,27526,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27527,0,0,0,'A White Silt Beach','  Beautiful, soft white sands stretch to the west on the edge of a crystal clear\nturquoise-watered cove.  Bordering the beach to the north is a dense, verdant\nrain forest.  You see large insects crawling in the silt near the forest line,\nand you hear hollers and chatter from a multitude of animals from the trees\nabove.  In the middle of the cove, to the southwest, is a small islet.\n',168,131072,54,200,27527,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27528,0,0,0,'Northeast Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches northwest of here, and a vast fog-covered\nocean extends to the north and east.  To the south is a turquoise colored\ncove, and to the west you can see through thinning trees to a pale silt\nbeach.  The forest is thick with leaves, trunks, and vines, and the air is\ndense with animal sounds.  The waves of the ocean to the north and east\noccasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of the northeastern coast of\nthis island, and marine birds are forced to temporarily flee their rocky\nperches or be crushed against the jagged stones of the coast.  You are\nglad to be above the dangerous looking waters, although the rain forest\ndoes not seem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27529,0,0,0,'Off the Northeast Coast of an Island','  This is a precarious area of water where the ocean waves smash up\nagainst the eastern coast of a jungle-covered island.  The coast of\nthe island curves to the northwest, and fog-covered ocean extends to\nthe northeast.  A cove is carved into the island to the southwest of\nhere, and a small rocky islet sits to the southeast, battered by\nfrothy sea water.  Marine birds perched on the rocks are forced to\ntake flight when a powerful wave sweeps against the coast.\n',168,131072,51,200,27529,0,100,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27530,0,0,0,'Off the Northeast Coast of an Island','  To the south is a small islet being battered by salty waves, and you\nsee even larger waves smashing into an island to the west.  Fog-blanketed\nocean spreads out to the horizon to the northeast, while a bright and\nshallow cove has been cut into the island to the southwest.\n',168,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27531,0,0,0,'West Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches east of here, and a fog-covered ocean\nextends to the horizon to the west.  The forest is thick with leaves,\ntrunks, and vines, and the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves\nof the ocean to the west occasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of\nthe western coast of this island, and marine birds are forced to\ntemporarily flee their rocky perches or be crushed against the jagged\nstones of the coast.  You are glad to be above the dangerous looking\nwaters, although the rain forest does not seem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27532,0,0,0,'Northwest Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches south and northeast of here, and a vast\nfog-covered ocean extends to the horizon northwest.  The forest is thick\nwith leaves, trunks, and vines, and the air is dense with animal sounds.\nThe waves of the ocean to the northwest occasionally smash against the\nrocky cliffs of the coast of this island, and marine birds are forced to\ntemporarily flee their rocky perches or be crushed against the jagged\nstones of the coast.  You are glad to be above the dangerous looking\nwaters, although the rain forest does not seem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27533,0,0,0,'Edge of a Cliff in a Rain Forest','  A dense rain forest stretches out to the northeast and south.  To the\neast the moist earth drops away sharply and allows you to see over the\ntop of the forest and into a cove at the center of the island.  The cliff\nto the east seems too precarious to navigate despite the vines and roots\ngrowing out of it.  The forest is thick with leaves, trunks, and vines,\nand the air is dense with animal sounds.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27534,0,0,0,'Base of a Cliff in a Rain Forest','  To the northwest a tall, sharp cliff rises menacingly out of the moist\nearth of a dense green rain forest.  The forest itself stretches in all\nother directions, and its suprising density makes it impossible to see far.\nLeaves and vines twist around you and seem to grab at you like soft hands.\nFrom within the forest come occasional hollers and thrashing of the\nunderbrush.  A swarm of gnats buzzes around your head, and a bead of sweat\ndrips from your eyelid.  During the day, the canopy of leaves provides a\nwelcome respite from the intense sun, though it is impossible to evade the\nsweltering heat entirely.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27535,0,0,0,'A Rain Forest','  To the northwest you see a  sharp cliff rising menacingly out of the moist\nearth of a dense green rain forest.  The forest itself stretches in all\nother directions, and its suprising density makes it impossible to see far.\nLeaves and vines twist around you and seem to grab at you like soft hands.\nFrom within the forest come occasional hollers and thrashing of the\nunderbrush.  A swarm of gnats buzzes around your head, and a bead of sweat\ndrips from your eyelid.  During the day, the canopy of leaves provides a\nwelcome respite from the intense sun, though it is impossible to evade the\nsweltering heat entirely.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27536,0,0,0,'A Rain Forest','  You are in the depths of a rain forest -- you cannot tell exactly how\nfar in you are due to the amazing density of the foliage.  The leaves\nare so thick that even in the height of the afternoon no light is able\nto penetrate through the trees to the ground.  All about you are twisted\nvines and sounds of creatures walking, climbing, and thrashing about the\nbrush.  The humid air sticks to you and seems to suffocate you.  Sweat\nis barely permitted to escape your pores to cool your body.  You faintly\nhear a sound like waves crashing on a beach to the east.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27537,0,0,0,'A White Silt Beach','  Beautiful, soft white sands stretch to the north and south on the edge of a\ncrystal clear turquoise-watered cove.  Bordering the beach to the west is a\ndense, verdant rain forest.  You see large insects crawling in the silt near\nthe forest line, and you hear hollers and chatter from a multitude of animals\nfrom the trees above.  In the middle of the cove, to the east, is a small\nislet.\n',168,131072,54,200,27537,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27538,0,0,0,'Shallows in a Cove','  This is the northwest part of a cove sheltered by a lush jungle-covered\nisland.  A beautiful white beach is to the northwest, and you can see an\nislet in the center of the cove to the southeast.\n',168,131072,51,0,0,0,100,7,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27539,0,0,0,'Shallows in a Cove','  This is the northern part of a cove sheltered by a lush jungle-covered\nisland.  A beautiful white beach is to the north, and you can see an\nislet in the center of the cove to the southeast.\n',168,131072,51,0,0,0,100,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27540,0,0,0,'Shallows in a Cove','  This is the northern part of a cove sheltered by a lush jungle-covered\nisland.  A beautiful white beach is to the north, and you can see an\nislet in the center of the cove to the south.\n',168,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27541,0,0,0,'Shallows in a Cove','  This is the northern part of a cove sheltered by a lush jungle-covered\nisland.  A beautiful white beach is to the north, and you can see an\nislet in the center of the cove to the south.\n',168,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27542,0,0,0,'Shallows in a Cove','  This is the northeast part of a cove sheltered by a lush jungle-covered\nisland.  A beautiful white beach is to the north, and you can see an\nislet in the center of the cove to the southwest.  The mouth of the cove\nlies to the east, and beyond that is a great fog-covered ocean.\n',168,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27543,0,0,0,'An Island Cove','  This is the mouth of a cove sheltered by a lush jungle-covered\nisland.  A beautiful white beach is to the northwest, and you can\nsee an islet in the center of the cove to the southwest.  To the\neast is a another tiny islet, and beyond that a great fog-covered\nocean.\n',168,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27544,0,0,0,'An Island Cove','  This is the mouth of a cove sheltered by a lush jungle-covered\nisland.  You can see an islet in the center of the cove to the\nsouthwest.  To the east is a another tiny islet, and beyond that\na great fog-covered ocean.\n',168,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27545,0,0,0,'<P>A Tiny Islet<z>','  This is a small rocky protrusion out of the ocean.  The surface of this\nislet is covered in water-loving vines and grasses, and the dark black rock\nbarely pokes out from under this green blanket.  A brisk breeze is\nperpetually whipping about, from the vast fog-covered ocean to the east\ninto a cove cut into an island to the southwest.  The larger island to\nthe west is covered in a dense rain forest.\n',168,131072,47,300,27545,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27546,0,0,0,'West Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches east of here, and a vast fog-covered\nocean extends to the west.  The forest is thick with leaves,\ntrunks, and vines, and the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves\nof the ocean to the west occasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of\nthe western coast of this island, and marine birds are forced to\ntemporarily flee their rocky perches or be crushed against the jagged\nstones of the coast.  You are glad to be above the dangerous looking\nwaters, although the rain forest does not seem much more inviting.  The\nforest opens up a little to the south.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
