(27599,0,0,0,'An Island Cove','  Surrounding you on all sides of the cove is beach, and then a dense\ngreen rain forest.  The mouth of the cove, and beyond it the vast fog-covered\nocean, is off to the northeast.  You are able to see down to the bottom of this\nshallow area through crystal clear turquoise water, all the way to a white\nsilt floor.  A cool breeze arrives from the direction of the ocean.  Directly\nto the northwest is a small islet in the center of the cove.\n',168,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27600,0,0,0,'An Island Cove','  This is the eastern part of a cove sheltered by a lush jungle-covered\nisland.  To the southeast you can see a beautiful white beach, and\ndirectly to the east you see some thin rain forest.  To the northwest is\na small islet in the center of the cove.\n',168,131072,51,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27601,0,0,0,'Edge of an Island Cove','  A dense rain forest stretches southeast of here, and you see the sands\nof a beach to the south.  To the west and northwest is a beautiful cove\nsituated in the center of this jungle island.  On the far side of the\ncove you see a beach and more rain forest.  As you peer west over the\nisland, you see a raised area in the distance.  There is a small islet\nin the center of the cove to the northwest, and another even smaller\none to the north, across the mouth of the cove.  To the northeast lies\na great fog-blanketed ocean.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27602,0,0,0,'East Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches south of here, and a vast fog-covered\nocean extends to the horizon east.  To the northwest is a turquoise\ncolored cove, and to the west you can see through thinning trees to a\npale silt beach.  The forest is thick with leaves, trunks, and vines,\nand the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves of the ocean to\nthe north and east occasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of\nthe eastern coast of this island, and marine birds are forced to\ntemporarily flee their rocky perches or be crushed against the\njagged stones of the coast.  You are glad to be above the\ndangerous looking waters, although the rain forest does not\nseem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27603,0,0,0,'West Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches east of here, and a vast fog-covered\nocean extends to the west.  The forest is thick with leaves,\ntrunks, and vines, and the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves\nof the ocean to the west occasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of\nthe western coast of this island, and marine birds are forced to\ntemporarily flee their rocky perches or be crushed against the jagged\nstones of the coast.  You are glad to be above the dangerous looking\nwaters, although the rain forest does not seem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27604,0,0,0,'Edge of a Cliff in a Rain Forest','  A dense rain forest stretches out to the north and southwest.  To the\nsoutheast the moist earth drops away sharply and allows you to see over\nthe top of the forest and into a cove at the center of the island.  The\ncliff to the east seems too precarious to navigate despite the vines\nand roots growing out of it.  In the southeast corner of the island you\nsee a thin tendril of smoke rising from the ground level.  The forest\nis thick with leaves, trunks, and vines, and the air is dense with\nanimal sounds.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
