(27616,0,0,0,'East Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches south of here, and a vast fog-covered\nocean extends to the east.  The forest is thick with leaves,\ntrunks, and vines, and the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves\nof the ocean to the east occasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of\nthe eastern coast of this island, and marine birds are forced to\ntemporarily flee their rocky perches or be crushed against the jagged\nstones of the coast.  You are glad to be above the dangerous looking\nwaters, although the rain forest does not seem much more inviting.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27617,0,0,0,'West Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches east of here, and a vast fog-covered\nocean extends to the west.  The forest is thick with leaves,\ntrunks, and vines, and the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves\nof the ocean to the west occasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of\nthe western coast of this island, and marine birds are forced to\ntemporarily flee their rocky perches or be crushed against the jagged\nstones of the coast.  You are glad to be above the dangerous looking\nwaters, although the rain forest does not seem much more inviting.  To\nthe southeast a cliff drops away, permitting you to see over the tops\nof more rain forest in the area below.  Through the trees to the\nsoutheast you can see a waterfall rushing off the edge of the cliff,\nand you can hear it through the trees to the south.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27618,0,0,0,'Edge of a Cliff in a Rain Forest','  A dense rain forest stretches out to the north and southwest.  To the\nsoutheast the moist earth drops away sharply and allows you to see over\nthe top of the forest and into a cove at the center of the island.  The\ncliff to the east seems too precarious to navigate despite the vines\nand roots growing out of it.  In the southeast corner of the island you\nsee a thin tendril of smoke rising from the ground level.  To the south\nyou see a waterfall flowing over the edge of the cliff; you can hear its\nsource to the southwest.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27619,0,0,0,'Base of a Cliff in a Rainforest','  To the northwest a tall, sharp cliff rises menacingly out of the moist\nearth of a dense green rain forest.  The forest itself stretches in all\nother directions, and its suprising density makes it impossible to see far.\nLeaves and vines twist around you and seem to grab at you like soft hands.\nFrom within the forest come occasional hollers and thrashing of the\nunderbrush.  A swarm of gnats buzzes around your head, and a bead of sweat\ndrips from your eyelid.  During the day, the canopy of leaves provides a\nwelcome respite from the intense sun, though it is impossible to evade the\nsweltering heat entirely.  To the southwest you can hear the sound of\nwater splashing.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
