(27658,0,0,0,'Southwest Coast of an Island','  A dense rain forest stretches northeast of here, and a fog-covered\nocean extends to the southwest.  The forest is thick with leaves, trunks,\nand vines, and the air is dense with animal sounds.  The waves of the ocean\nto the southwest occasionally smash against the rocky cliffs of the\nsouthwestern coast of this island, and marine birds are forced to\ntemporarily flee their rocky perches or be crushed against the jagged\nstones of the coast.  You are glad to be above the dangerous looking\nwaters, although the rain forest does not seem much more inviting.  The\nforest opens up a little to the north.  To the northwest you can see a\nwaterfall splashing off the island and into the ocean.\n',168,131072,46,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
