(27828,51,54,-3,'Earthen Retaining Wall','  A deafening roar rattles you to your bones!  Gasping for breath, you ponder\nwhat the sea must be like on the OTHER side of this wall.   Looking at the wall\nitself, you see that its top is ice covered but flat.  The wall is not made\nup of piled up earth as you first thought, but rather granite blocks of\ntitanic proportions are stacked one atop the other.  Small growths of lichen\nand mussels dot the crevices between the blocks.  The growths seem mighty\nscarce here, almost as if someone or something has kept them scraped clean of\ndebris.\n',186,131072,9,0,0,0,40,3,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(27829,47,58,-3,'Bay of Baan\'Clor','   Gentle waves abound as far as your eyes can see, faintly, you think you can\nmake out some sort of wall.  Like lightning striking, insight comes to you!\nYou stand in the renowned bay of Amber.  Providing ships an easy port in any\ntype of weather.  The water\'s depth is just deep enough so that any ship you\ncan think of can at least drop anchor here.  Most avoid the piers due to the\nruffian type crowd that resides there.\n',186,131072,9,0,0,0,40,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
