(27889,0,0,0,'Inside an Igloo','  Small but cozy, this igloo is very warm compared to the sub-zero temperatures\nof outside.  A small stove radiates heat nicely from the center of the room\nwhile a tidy cot sits against one wall.  Something seems out of place here,\nit\'s right on the tip of your tongue.  Wait! The igloo is made out of ice,\nhow can a fire be burning?! Can only mean one thing.  Magic is at use here!\n',186,131081,11,0,0,0,0,-1,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(27890,51,54,-2,'Atop the Wall','  Woah! The surface here is covered by about six inches of ice.  Where you stand\nit\'s slightly indented as if many feet have trod along this route making a\npath.  Frigid winds bite into you, nearly deafened by the clamor of the sea\npounding the wall you must make a decision.  Push on and see what, if anything\nresides here or plunge yourself back into the icy bay.  A large well oiled\nlever protrudes from the ice here.\n',186,131072,11,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(27891,52,54,-2,'Atop the Wall','  Woah! The surface here is covered by about six inches of ice.  Where you stand\nit\'s slightly indented as if many feet have trod along this route making a\npath.  Frigid winds bite into you, nearly deafened by the clamor of the sea\npounding the wall you must make a decision.  Push on and see what, if anything\nresides here or plunge yourself back into the icy bay\n',186,131072,11,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27892,53,54,-2,'Atop the Wall','  Woah! The surface here is covered by about six inches of ice.  Where you stand\nit\'s slightly indented as if many feet have trod along this route making a\npath.  Frigid winds bite into you, nearly deafened by the clamor of the sea\npounding the wall you must make a decision.  Push on and see what, if anything\nresides here or plunge yourself back into the icy bay.  A small igloo lies to\nyour east.\n',186,131072,11,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27893,54,54,-2,'Inside an Igloo','  Small but cozy, this igloo is very warm compared to the sub-zero temperatures\nof outside.  A small stove radiates heat nicely from the center of the room\nwhile a tidy bed sits against one wall.  Something seems to be out of place\nhere, it\'s right on the tip of your tongue.  Wait!  The igloo is made out of\nice, how can a fire burn without melting it?  Can only mean one thing.\nMagic is at use here!  In the corner you can see where some inconsiderate\nperson has stained the ice a deep yellow.\n',186,131081,11,0,0,0,0,-1,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(27894,52,53,-2,'Atop the Wall','  Woah! The surface here is covered by about six inches of ice.  Where you stand\nit\'s slightly indented as if many feet have trod along this route making a\npath.  Frigid winds bite into you, nearly deafened by the clamor of the sea\npounding the wall you must make a decision.  Push on and see what, if anything\nresides here or plunge yourself back into the icy bay.  A small igloo lies to\nyour east, while the faint trail seems to lead south.\n',186,131072,11,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27895,53,53,-2,'Inside an Igloo','  Small but cozy, this igloo is very warm compared to the sub-zero temperatures\nof outside.  A small stove radiates heat nicely from the center of the room\nwhile a tidy cot sits against one wall.  Something seems out of place here,\nit\'s right on the tip of your tongue.  Wait! The igloo is made out of ice,\nhow can a fire be burning?! Can only mean one thing.  Magic is at use here!\n',186,131081,11,0,0,0,0,-1,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(27896,52,52,-2,'Atop the Wall','  Woah! The surface here is covered by about 6 inches of ice.  Where you stand\nit\'s slightly indented as if many feet have trod along this route making a\npath.  Frigid winds tear into you, nearly deafened by the clamor of the sea\npounding on the wall you must make a decision.  Push on and see what, if anything\nresides here or plunge yourself back into the icy bay.  A small igloo lies to\nyour east while the trail comes to an abrupt end.  Peering carfully over the\nedge, you can see the legendary Sea of Sorrows.  Huge icebergs float on its\nsurface like huge ghostly ships.\n',186,131072,11,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(27897,53,52,-2,'Inside an Igloo','  Small but cozy, this igloo is very warm compared to the sub-zero temperatures\nof outside.  A small stove radiates heat nicely from the center of the room\nwhile a tidy cot sits against one wall.  Something seems out of place here,\nit\'s right on the tip of your tongue.  Wait! The igloo is made out of ice,\nhow can a fire be burning?! Can only mean one thing.  Magic is at use here!\n',186,131081,11,0,0,0,0,-1,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(27898,55,54,-2,'Hermans Secret Stash','  Herman has left many of the things HE considers treasure here.  As you look\nabout the mess and items thrown all about the room you wonder if there is\ntruly anything of value here.  Is it really worth all your time and effort\nto search through all of this garbage? That same yellow cube catches your\neye in this room as well.  The yellow color seems to have permeated the ice.\n',186,131081,11,0,0,0,0,-1,2,100,0,'',NULL),
(27899,46,58,-4,'Nefkar\'s Old Shoppe of Ships','  Many ship building tools cover the walls here.  On the western wall there are\nbarrels filled with a thick black tar.  You know that this is the substance\nused to seal the inside of ships against leaking.  The northern wall is home to\na small wooden table.  Its surface is littered with many blueprints and tools.\n',186,163849,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27900,63,52,6,'Mining Tunnel','  The way before you is broad and swift, the roof is gently arched and small\nrunes have been carved into the timbers that support it.  It appears that\nall mining in this tunnel has been completed long ago.  There is almost no\ndebris littering the floor here.  Small crevices in the floor make you wary\nof your footing, in the distance you can hear a faint clinking noise as if\nsomeone still toils here.\n',188,131080,5,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27901,64,52,6,'Mining Tunnel','  The way before you is broad and swift, the roof is gently arched and small\nrunes have been carved into the timbers that support it.  It appears that\nall mining in this tunnel has been completed long ago.  There is almost no\ndebris littering the floor here.  Small crevices in the floor make you wary\nof your footing, in the distance you can hear a faint clinking noise as if\nsomeone still toils here.\n',188,131080,5,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
