(27962,68,48,-4,'Mining Tunnel','  This shaft descends deep into the bowels of the earth, as you climb down\nechos of the noises from your scrambling echo back to you.  You have reached\nthe bottom of the shaft, you hope that there is an easier way to the surface\nthan to risk that tough climb.  The air here is dank and rancid, you can feel\na slight breezy coming from the south going up the shaft.\n',188,131080,5,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27963,68,47,-4,'Mining Tunnel','  This area of the tunnel is less finished than anything you have come across\nso far.  The beams supporting the roof are still dripping sap and it looks\nas if many that would make this a safe place to walk in are missing.  A\ncave-in could occur at anytime here.  The walls are rich with terbium,\npeering about you can see the raw, silver-grey material running along in deep\nveins.  To your south you can see that the tunnel ends abruptly and a massive\ncavern opens up.\n',188,131080,5,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(27964,67,46,-4,'Massive Cavern','  As you step foot into this massive cavern your senses reel.  The expansive\nstone floor has been worn almost smooth, slight scratch marks can be seen\nhere and there etched deeply into the stones surface.  The air temperature\nhere is much warmer than that of outside.  Footsteps echo off the walls\nsending icy tendrils running up your spine.  The echos bounce about and the\nonly direction you know they are not coming from is the way you came in, or\nworse yet, perhaps you are surrounded!  A strong breeze wafts in from the\neast bringing fresh air into the cavern.\n',188,131080,5,0,0,0,0,-1,0,720,0,'',NULL),
(27965,68,46,-4,'Massive Cavern','  As you step foot into this massive cavern your senses reel.  The expansive\nstone floor has been worn almost smooth, slight scratch marks can be seen\nhere and there etched deeply into the stones surface.  The air temperature\nhere is much warmer than that of outside.  Footsteps echo off the walls\nsending icy tendrils running up your spine.  The echos bounce about and the\nonly direction you know they are not coming from is the way you came in, or\nworse yet, perhaps you are surrounded!  A strong breeze wafts in from the\neast bringing fresh air into the cavern.\n',188,131080,5,0,0,0,0,-1,0,720,0,'',NULL),
