(28035,73,55,-3,'Desolate Beach','  Desolate is the perfect word to describe this beach.  No life of any kind\ncould survive here.  Some seagull droppings litter the beach and patches of\nice dot the landscape.  Small rock piles have been disturbed here and there\nbut, no tracks can be made out on this hard ground.\n',188,131081,10,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
