(28086,66,63,-3,'Living Quarters','  This massive room has been carved from the iceberg itself.  The living\nquarters of some huge being.  Small replicas of the cisterns sit here casting\nthe same eerie light.  The air here is fresh and a slight breeze wafts through\nthe air.  A small window has been carved out of the ice in the eastern wall.  A\nlarge terbium door leads back to the west.\n',188,131144,11,0,0,0,0,-1,0,240,0,'',NULL),
(28090,72,54,-4,'Water Filled Corridor','  This large corridor is carved from solid ice.  Lichen grows in some cracks in\nthe ice casting an eerie green light.  There are deep nicks and scratches from\nthe tools used to make this corridor.  The creatures who made this place must\nhave used crude tools when making it.  The waters temperature is just above\nfreezing, the cold seeps into your limbs.\n',188,131081,30,0,0,0,20,7,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(28091,61,52,-1,'Helmsman\'s Post','  The wheel that steers this small ship has been lashed down so that the\nship can only go in a tight circle.  A small compass sits above the wheel\nand a sextant has been carelessly dropped here.  The sextant has shattered\ninto a million pieces and is not worth your bother.  Once again the lack\nof any crew sets the small hairs on the back of your neck on end.\n',188,131136,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28092,62,52,-1,'Up the Mast','  The mast isn\'t as slick as you first thought it would be but, climbing\nit is still no easy task.  The ropes that dangle all about you are tempting\nbut you know they wouldn\'t hold your weight.\n',188,131136,15,0,0,0,0,-1,9,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28093,62,52,0,'Up the Mast','  The mast isn\'t as slick as you first thought it would be but, climbing\nit is still no easy task.  The ropes that dangle all about you are tempting\nbut you know they wouldn\'t hold your weight.\n',188,131136,15,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28094,62,52,1,'Crows Nest','  The area you find yourself in is shaped like a large bucket.  It\'s about\nfive feet across and only three feet high.  From this perilous position\nyou can see far out over the Sea of Sorrows, looking downwards you see\nabsolutely no movement.  Where could the ships crew have gone?\n',188,131136,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28096,0,0,0,'Around an Iceberg','  The waters here send off brilliant lights in all directions as it\nstrikes against the sides of this iceberg.  You can faintly hear the\ncries of an ocean bird from far above, life does thrive even in the\nmost hostile of climates.  The icebergs surface is slick as well, ice.\nYou can see no way of climbing to its peak.\n',188,131072,9,0,0,0,50,7,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28097,0,0,0,'Inside a Shack','  This shack has been crudely made from pieces of ships and driftwood that\nthe Gargantuan has swallowed.  The floor is uneven and rough but at least\nyou\'re not on that repulsive stomach lining.  A large hammock hangs from\nthe wall and the room is otherwise bereft of furnishings.\n',188,139592,50,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(28098,0,0,0,'Around an Iceberg','  The waters here send off brilliant lights in all directions as it\nstrikes against the sides of this iceberg.  You can faintly hear the\ncries of an ocean bird from far above, life does thrive even in the\nmost hostile of climates.  The icebergs surface is slick as well, ice.\nYou can see no way of climbing to its peak.\n',188,131072,9,0,0,0,50,7,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28100,52,63,-3,'Cliffline','  Massive cliffs rise up and cause the waters here to rage and boil.  There\nis no way that you can see to ascend these cliffs.  Dark clouds above the\njagged cliff line give of an impression that you are in a very evil place.\nNow and again small rocks fall from the great height and land in the water\nwith a loud splash, a general feeling of danger permeates the very air.\nYou are tossed about hither and yon from the high seas here.  You hope just\nto be able to get safely away from these jagged menacing cliffs.\n',188,131072,9,0,0,0,50,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
