(28342,59,53,-3,'Sea of Sorrows','  The frigid water that surrounds you makes you shiver in trepidation.  Small\nicebergs float by you on their ocean journey.  All the rumors you have heard\nabout this forbidding place are true.  Fraught with danger and peril this\nsea is not a place for the wary.  True explorers have found unheard of wealth\nand power here, while the timid perish quickly.  Bright sunlight reflects\noff the large ice chunks and water.  Your visibility is cut to almost\nnothing.\n',188,131072,9,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28343,60,53,-3,'Around a Trawler','  The waves rock this small ship hither and yon and small chunks of ice\nbatter the hull.  You can see people on the deck of this small fishing\ntrawler.  Shouting and waving until your lungs are raw doesn\'t seem to be\nworking to get their attention.  The sea seems to be much calmer here then\nwhere you were, and you wonder if trying to get aboard this ship is wise\nsince you have heard multiple rumors of pirates on these seas.\n',188,131072,9,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28344,61,52,-2,'Aft Deck','  This area is a slight bit cleaner than the other parts of the ship you have\nseen so far.  Small brown-red stains are all over the planks here, looking at\nthem closely you realize they are blood stains!  As realization as to what\nhas happened to the crew becomes clear you can feel an odd sensation as if\nsomeone were looking at you.  Is it to late to escape this certain death\ntrap....\n',188,131136,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28345,62,52,-2,'At the Mast','  You stand before the main-mast of this ship, no sails hang from it now and\nthe ropes that still remain look worn and rotten.  The mast itself is in\ngood condition, far up you can make out the crows nest.  Netting hangs over\nthe side of the ship here allowing you easy access back into the sea.\n',188,131136,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28346,63,52,-2,'Ships Foredecks','  The foredecks are dirty and covered with a salty residue, looks as if\nnoone has scrubbed the decks in quite a long time.  The teak boards that\nmake up the planking seem to still be stout and firm.  They will be able\nto support your weight easily enough.  Still, the absence of any crew seems\nstrange.\n',188,131136,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28347,64,53,-3,'Around a Trawler','  The waves rock this small ship hither and yon and small chunks of ice\nbatter the hull.  You can see people on the deck of this small fishing\ntrawler.  Shouting and waving until your lungs are raw doesn\'t seem to be\nworking to get their attention.  The sea seems to be much calmer here then\nwhere you were, and you wonder if trying to get aboard this ship is wise\nsince you have heard multiple rumors of pirates on these seas.\n',188,131072,9,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28348,65,53,-3,'Sea of Sorrows','  The frigid water that surrounds you makes you shiver in trepidation.  Small\nicebergs float by you on their ocean journey.  All the rumors you have heard\nabout this forbidding place are true.  Fraught with danger and peril this\nsea is not a place for the wary.  True explorers have found unheard of wealth\nand power here, while the timid perish quickly.  Bright sunlight reflects\noff the large ice chunks and water.  Your visibility is cut to almost\nnothing.\n',188,131072,9,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
