(28944,0,0,0,'A Dirt Road','  You are standing on a well used dirt road, large enough for a horse and cart \nto easily travel upon.  Large ruts along the path give proof that the path is \nused often by carts that carry heavy loads.  Rocks randomly protrude from the\nground here and there.\n',202,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28945,0,0,0,'An Odd Bedroom','  This bedroom looks to have once been a shed.  Shelves adorn the walls, \ncovered in all manners of tools and no real decoration has gone into the room \nat all.  If it was not for the bed in the center of the room it is doubtful \nyou would ever guess someone had slept in here before.  In the southwestern \ncorner of the room is a door.\n',202,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,150,0,'',NULL),
(28946,0,0,0,'A Dirt Road','  You are standing on a well used dirt road, large enough for a horse and cart \nto easily travel upon.  Large ruts along the path give proof that the path is \nused often by carts that carry heavy loads.  Rocks randomly protrude from the\nground here and there.\n',202,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28947,0,0,0,'A Storage Area','  You are surrounded by large uncut wood, freshly cut from trees and left to \nallow the sap to dry.  Logs are piled upon each other haphazardly making the \npossiblity of logs accidentally falling on ones head a reason to be cautious.\n',202,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(28948,0,0,0,'In Front of a Large Table','  You stand before a large table, large enough to hold a very sizable tree.  \nWithin the center of the table is a sharp round blade.  Looking closer at the \nbase of the table you notice a set of pedals - possibly used to manipulate \nthe blade upon the top of the table.\n',202,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(28949,0,0,0,'A Warehouse','  You are surrounded by refined wood, cut into large planks and ready to be \nused in the building of new buildings.  Taking quick account of the cut \nplanks you surmise there is enough wood to build at least three large houses.\n',202,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,300,0,'',NULL),
(28950,0,0,0,'A Dirt Road','  You are standing on a well used dirt road, large enough for a horse and cart \nto easily travel upon.  Large ruts along the path give proof that the path is \nused often by carts that carry heavy loads.  Rocks randomly protrude from the\nground here and there.  Near dead brush blocks any exit to the south, while to\nthe east and west are large buildings.\n',202,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28951,0,0,0,'A Tidy Room','  Clean and without a speck of dust to be seen this room is a bedroom and \nkitchen in one, with a decent sized bed on one side of the room and a \ncookstove on the other.  To the northeast is a door.\n',202,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,150,0,'',NULL),
(28952,0,0,0,'A Small Grove','You are surrounded by stout trees, creating a small path.  At the end of the \npath is the largest tree you have ever seen.  It reaches so high that you can\'t \nsee the top branches from your current viewpoint. You notice some etchings a \nsmall distance up the tree.\n',-1,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28953,0,0,0,'A Dirt Road','  You are standing on a well used dirt road, large enough for a horse and cart \nto easily travel upon.  Large ruts along the path give proof that the path is \nused often by carts that carry heavy loads.  Rocks randomly protrude from the\nground here and there.  Through the brush to the east you can just make out the\nwall of a building while to the west you spy a small grove.\n',202,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28954,0,0,0,'A Tool Shed','  You are in a small room full of sharp tools used in the cutting of wood, \naxes and large saws lie cast sporadically around the room.\n',202,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,150,0,'',NULL),
(28955,0,0,0,'A Dirt Road','  You are standing on a well used dirt road, large enough for a horse and cart \nto easily travel upon.  Large ruts along the path give proof that the path is \nused often by carts that carry heavy loads.  Rocks randomly protrude from the\nground here and there.\n',202,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28956,0,0,0,'A Dry Well','  Behind a screen of brush to the north and and behind a pile of cut branches \nto the west, this well is hidden well - though the reason for the hiding itself \nis unknown.  The surrounding growth grows in abundance.\n',202,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28957,0,0,0,'A Vegetable Garden','  You stand within a large garden.  Large vegetables grow in the surrounding \nfertile soil.  To the south is the wall of a house, probably the owners of \nthis very garden.  To the east is a gate.\n',202,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28958,0,0,0,'A Dirt Road','  You are standing on a well used dirt road, large enough for a horse and cart \nto easily travel upon.  Large ruts along the path give proof that the path is \nused often by carts that carry heavy loads.  Rocks randomly protrude from the\nground here and there.  To the west is a small gate.\n',202,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28959,0,0,0,'A Dirt Road','  You are standing on a well used dirt road, large enough for a horse and cart \nto easily travel upon.  Large ruts along the path give proof that the path is \nused often by carts that carry heavy loads.  Rocks randomly protrude from the\nground here and there.\n',202,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28960,0,0,0,'A Bedroom','  You are in the master bedroom of the house. A large bed dominates the center \nof the room while along the southern wall is a set of drawers full of various \narticles of clothing.\n',202,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,150,0,'',NULL),
(28961,0,0,0,'A Dining Room','  You are in a small, but well used dining room.  A large table lies in the\ncenter of the room, and a couch is positioned in the southeastern corner\nbeside the fireplace.  Comfort is obviously an issue within these walls.\n',202,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,150,0,'',NULL),
(28962,0,0,0,'A Dirt Road','  You are standing on a well used dirt road, large enough for a horse and cart \nto easily travel upon.  Large ruts along the path give proof that the path is \nused often by carts that carry heavy loads.  Rocks randomly protrude from the\nground here and there.  To the west is the front door to a house, and to the\nsouth is a small chicken coop.\n',202,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28963,0,0,0,'A Dirt Road','  You are standing on a well used dirt road, large enough for a horse and cart \nto easily travel upon.  Large ruts along the path give proof that the path is \nused often by carts that carry heavy loads.  Rocks randomly protrude from the\nground here and there.\n',202,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28964,0,0,0,'A Dirt Road','  You are standing on a well used dirt road, large enough for a horse and cart \nto easily travel upon.  Large ruts along the path give proof that the path is \nused often by carts that carry heavy loads.  Rocks randomly protrude from the\nground here and there.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(28965,0,0,0,'A Bedroom','  You are in a very small bedroom.  A small bed has been pushed against the \nsouthern wall, and small set of drawers stands at the foot of the bed.  Items \nof various shapes and sizes are scattered across the floor.\n',202,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,150,0,'',NULL),
(28966,0,0,0,'A Kitchen','  This small room contains a small table and a large cookstove, giving away \nthe fact that this is a kitchen.\n',202,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,150,0,'',NULL),
(28967,0,0,0,'Chicken Coop','  You are in a small chicken coop.  Along the walls are many small nests for \nchickens to lay and take care of their eggs in.  Seed has been scattered \nalong the floor in a random pattern for chickens to eat if they ever get \nhungry.\n',202,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,30,0,'',NULL),
(28968,0,0,0,'The Top of the Stairs','  Deep red stains cover the stairs, still wet enough to cause traversing them \nto be dangerous.  Small pieces of bone and skin litter the floor, along with\nthe odd limb.  Looking through the carnage you cannot seem to find a single\nhuman body or limb amidst those of the slain trollocs.\n',202,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,150,0,'',NULL),
(28969,0,0,0,'A Destroyed Bedroom','  What once must have been a master bedroom is now a large mess of destroyed \nfurniture.  Blood stains the carpet everywhere, along with the odd piece of \ndried skin and innards.\n',202,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,150,0,'',NULL),
(28970,0,0,0,'A Destroyed Bedroom','  What once must have been a small childs room is now a large mess of destroyed \nfuniture.  Red stains soak the carpet everywhere.  Toys are shattered throughout\nthe room, never to be used by a child again.\n',202,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,150,0,'',NULL),
(28971,0,0,0,'A Smooth Tunnel','  You are in a smooth man made tunnel, made even more smooth by a once \ncurrent flow of water.  A thin slick of mud covers the floor of the tunnel \nshowing very clearly a set of large footprints.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28972,0,0,0,'<o>The Bottom of a Well<z>','<k>  You are at the bottom of a dry well, the ground is covered in a layer of\nmud that makes it hard not slip and fall over.  Above you is the entrance to\na well and to the west is a path that water once flowed through.<z>\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,150,0,'',NULL),
(28973,0,0,0,'A Moldy Hallway','  Looking around you notice a ruined hallway.  Thick layers of mud cover the \nfloor, and mold covers what remains of tattered banners upon the walls.  To \nyour east is a large pile of rubble, while to the southwest is a sanctuary of \nsome kind.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28974,0,0,0,'A Pile of Debris','  Full of rock and debris from what once could have been a wall to the\nsoutheast, what may have been a room of some kind is now destroyed.  Mud \ncovers the surrounding rubble and here and there you notice a footprint.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28975,0,0,0,'A Smooth Tunnel','  You are within a smooth man made tunnel, made even more smooth by a once \ncurrent flow of water.  A thin slick of mud covers the floor of the tunnel \nshowing very clearly a set of large footprints.  To the east you can make out \na large pit, possibly from where the water that once filled this system of \ntunnels originated.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28976,0,0,0,'<o>A Large Pit<Z>','  You are within a smooth man made tunnel, made even more smooth by a once \ncurrent flow of water.  Below you is a long drop into what looks to be a \nsmall amount of liquid.  You cant help but wonder if this was from whence the \nwater that once flowed freely within these tunnels originated.\n',202,131085,34,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28977,0,0,0,'A Smooth Tunnel','  You are within a smooth man made tunnel, made even more smooth by a once \ncurrent flow of water.  A thin slick of mud covers the floor of the tunnel \nshowing very clearly a set of large footprints.  To the west you can make out \na large pit, possibly from where the water that once filled this system of \ntunnels originated.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28978,0,0,0,'A Smooth Tunnel','  You are within a smooth man made tunnel, made even more smooth by a once \ncurrent flow of water.  A thin slick of mud covers the floor of the tunnel \nshowing very clearly a set of large footprints.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28979,0,0,0,'A Smooth Tunnel','  You are within a smooth man made tunnel, made even more smooth by a once \ncurrent flow of water.  A thin slick of mud covers the floor of the tunnel \nshowing very clearly a set of large footprints.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28980,0,0,0,'A Long Forgotten Sanctuary','  As soon as you enter the room you feel an intense feeling of peace and \nserenity.  Devoid of any decoration at all a simple altar stands within the \nmiddle of the room.  An urge to drop to your knees and pray begins to slowly \noverwhelm you.\n',202,166137,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28981,0,0,0,'A Pile of Debris','  Full of rock and debris from what once could have been a wall to the east,\nwhat may of been a room of some kind is now destroyed.  Mud covers  the\nsurrounding rubble and here and there you notice a footprint.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28982,0,0,0,'A Smooth Tunnel','  You are within a smooth man made tunnel, made even more smooth by a once \ncurrent flow of water.  A thin slick of mud covers the floor of the tunnel \nshowing very clearly a set of large footprints.  Rubble lies upon the floor \nof the tunnel, and the wall to the west looks to have been ripped apart from \nthe force of the water that once flowed within.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28983,0,0,0,'A Smooth Tunnel','  You are within a smooth man made tunnel, made even more smooth by a once \ncurrent flow of water.  A thin slick of mud covers the floor of the tunnel \nshowing very clearly a set of large footprints.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28984,0,0,0,'A Moldy Hallway','  Looking around you notice a ruined hallway.  Thick layers of mud cover the \nfloor, and mold covers what remains of tattered banners upon the walls.  To \nyour east is a large pile of rubble, while to the northwest is a sanctuary of \nsome kind.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28985,0,0,0,'A Pile Of Debris','  Full of rock and debris from what once could have been a wall to the\nnortheast, what may have been a room of some kind is now destroyed.  Mud \ncovers the surrounding rubble and here and there you notice a footprint.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28986,0,0,0,'A Smooth Tunnel','  You are within a smooth man made tunnel, made even more smooth by a once \ncurrent flow of water.  A thin slick of mud covers the floor of the tunnel \nshowing very clearly a set of large footprints.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28987,0,0,0,'A Smooth Tunnel','  You are within a smooth man made tunnel, made even more smooth by a once \ncurrent flow of water.  A thin slick of mud covers the floor of the tunnel \nshowing very clearly a set of large footprints.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28988,0,0,0,'A Smooth Tunnel','  You are within a smooth man made tunnel, made even more smooth by a once \ncurrent flow of water.  A thin slick of mud covers the floor of the tunnel \nshowing very clearly a set of large footprints.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28989,0,0,0,'A Smooth Tunnel','  You are within a smooth man made tunnel, made even more smooth by a once \ncurrent flow of water.  A thin slick of mud covers the floor of the tunnel \nshowing very clearly a set of large footprints.\n',202,131081,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28990,0,0,0,'Within A Cave','  You are in a cave too smooth to be natural.  There are neither stalagmites\nlittering the floor nor are there any stalactites protruding from above.  There\nare exits to the south and west.\n',202,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,50,0,'',NULL),
(28991,0,0,0,'Deep Within A Cave','  You are in a cave that can only be described as a den.  Too smooth to be \nnatural,  there are neither stalagmites littering the floor nor are there any\nstalactites protruding from above.  The scent of wolves is strong within the air.\n',202,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(28992,0,0,0,'Within A Cave','  You are in a cave too smooth to be natural.  There are neither  stalagmites\nlittering the floor nor are there any stalactites protruding from above.  There\nare exits to the north and west.\n',202,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,50,0,'',NULL),
(28993,0,0,0,'<o>A Smooth Vertical Tunnel<z>','  You are within a smooth Vertical Tunnel.  The walls are devoid of any kind of \ngrip and impossible to traverse.  You are able to make out the sound of \nflowing water from below.\n',202,131081,34,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28994,0,0,0,'<o>A Smooth Tunnel<z>','  You are within a smooth vertical tunnel.  Small hand holds can be found in \nvarious places along the walls of the tunnel making climbing just possible.  \nTo the northeast is a small recess.  You can hear the sound of flowing water \nfrom below.\n',202,140745,35,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28995,0,0,0,'<o>A Wet Tunnel<z>','  You are within a smooth vertical tunnel.  Small hand holds can be found in \nvarious places along the walls of the tunnel making climbing just possible.  \nWater splashes against the wall now and then from the flow of water below.\n',202,140745,35,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28996,0,0,0,'A Swift Flowing Underground River','  You are in a small natural room, to the north and south are two large grates \nwith water flowing through both of them.  The grate to the south looks able \nto block water from flowing through it, causing water to fill the large \ntunnels above, but the gears used to do so seem to have been damaged beyond \nrepair.\n',202,142793,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,130,0,'',NULL),
(28997,0,0,0,'Inside a Dark Tent','  Able to fit a thousand people at once, it is impossible to tell if you are \nstill inside the same tent you saw from outside.  Implements of torture are \nscattered around the place and are stained in blood from good use and a large \nrack, perfect for torturing lies in the center of the tent.\n',202,139592,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,140,0,'',NULL),
(28998,0,0,0,'<o>A Small Recess<z>','  Blood stains the walls of this small recess, with the odd fingernail left on \nthe floor.  It appears that this recess was dug from the very rock with bare \nhands.\n',202,131145,61,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(28999,0,0,0,'<o>A Vertical Shaft<z>','  You are within a straight vertical shaft, devoid of handholes. below you is \nthe bottom of the well and just above your head is the top of the well, which \nexits the well.\n',202,131085,34,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30701,0,0,0,'Private Quarters','  These are the private chambers of the tent.  Luxuriant furs and hides cover \nthe floor, keeping the cold of the ground from the family as they sleep.  \nThe scraped hide walls of the tent provide ample protection from the elements \nwhile beautiful paintings on scraped bark have been hung from the walls to \nprovide some color to the otherwise drab tent walls.\n',76,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30702,0,0,0,'Private Quarters','  Small tables hold various household objects in a tidy manner.  Small pillows\nand carpets line the floor of this private area.  The scraped bark paintings\nadd color the the otherwise drab walls of the tent.  The quality of the \nfurnishings suggests that this tent is occupied by an important person.  A \ncleverly designed sliding rail allows a small section of the screen to be \nopened and closed, allowing access into and out of these chambers. A cozy\nroom lies to the west.\n',76,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30703,0,0,0,'Kallam\'s Forge','  This tent is quite large as it accommodates Kallam and his family, as well as \nhis forge.  The smell of hot steel fills the room, but the tent is totally\nfree of smoke.  An odd contraption in the corner of the room whizzes and \nthumps as steam escapes from various valves.  It is attached to the forge\nhood by a thick pipe.  Another pipe exits from the machine and out the back\nof the tent.  Assorted pieces of armor and weaponry, in various states of\nrepair decorate large racks scattered about the tent floor.\n',76,164073,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30705,0,0,0,'Zoodon\'s Curiosities','  This small tent is filled with everything.  Shelves line every wall of the\ntent and stretch from floor to ceiling.  Bottles and jars, bags, heaps and piles\nof every imaginable collection of anything you may have ever wanted can be\nfound here.  \n',76,164025,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30706,0,0,0,'Before an Ornate Chair','   This is the seat of power in the village.  The room has been sparsely\ndecorated so that all supplicants must focus on the chief.  The chair is\nthe only piece of furniture, and besides the carpet of fine furs this\nroom is completely empty.  Those who seek an audience must stand to face\nthe judgement of the chief.\n',76,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30707,0,0,0,'Inside a Large Tent','  A large smoke hole at the apex of the tent allows smoke to escape when \nthe fires and lamps are lit.  The hard ground has been covered by a variety of \ntanned and cured animal hides to soften the hard earth for the tents \noccupants.  To the west the Chief\'s chair gleams softly in the flickering \nlamplight.\n',76,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30708,0,0,0,'Entrance to Large Tent','  A large smokehole at the apex of the tent allows smoke to escape when \nthe fires and lamps are lit.  The hard ground has been covered by various \ntanned and cured animal hides to soften the hard earth for the tents\noccupants.  A silk screen, painted with hunting scenes, provides a measure\nof privacy for the chambers to the north.\n',76,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30709,0,0,0,'Northern Path at a Large Tent','  To the west lies the entrance to a large tent.  The tent appears to \nbe made of some kind of animal hide, cleverly stitched with sinew to seal \nout the elements.  The carefully dyed hide of the roof, and large size \nof the tent suggests that this dwelling must belong to someone important\nto the village.  The path curves to the east where it runs through the \ntents of the village.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30710,0,0,0,'Craftsmen\'s Path','  The dirt path is considerably wider here than it is to the west, with \ntents lining both sides.  To the east you see tents with signs depicting \nthe various shops and services hanging on wooden poles.  To the west the \nred roof of a large tent is clearly visible above the tent village.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30711,0,0,0,'Craftsmen\'s Path','  This wide path has tents lining both sides. To the east you see tents with\nsigns depicting the various shops and services hanging on wooden poles.  To \nthe west the red roof of a large tent can still be seen peeking above the \ntents of the village.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30712,0,0,0,'Craftsmen\'s Path','  This wide path has tents lining both sides. To the north the sounds of \nmetal-working can be heard.  Craftsmen\'s path continues to the east and west.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30713,0,0,0,'Craftsmen\'s Path','  This wide path has tents lining both sides.  A few large, black cauldrons can\nbe seen behind the tent to the south hanging above a bed of coals, steam slowly\ncurling from the rims.  The exquisite aroma coming from the cauldrons promises \na delicious, hearty meal for the customers.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30714,0,0,0,'Craftsmen\'s Path','  The path peters out here, overrun by the hardy grasses of this vast \nplain.  The tents are spread out more here at the edge of the tent city.  \nA single sign hangs in front of a small, well-made tent to the north. \nThe small path leading to the tent mouth is lined by two, carefully \ntended gardens.  Exotic plants flourish in the dark soil.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30715,0,0,0,'Inside a Large Tent','  A large smokehole at the apex of the tent allows smoke to escape when \nthe fires and lamps are lit.  The hard ground has been covered by various \ntanned and cured animal hides to soften the hard earth for the tents\noccupants.  \n',76,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30716,0,0,0,'Inside a Large Tent','  A large smokehole at the apex of the tent allows smoke to escape when \nthe fires and lamps are lit.  The hard ground has been covered by various \ntanned and cured animal hides to soften the hard earth for the tents\noccupants.  \n',76,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30717,0,0,0,'Northern Path Near a Large Tent','  The red roof of a large tent is now clearly visible.  Bright red pinions \nhang from the top of the tent as well as from poles decorating the entrance.  \nThe path continues to the north and south.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30718,0,0,0,'Bartho\'s Fine Foods','  The aroma of cooking stew from the cauldrons out back fills the tent.  \nTables and benches fill the floor here, providing a comfortable place to \neat the delicious foods prepared by Bartho.  A smaller cauldron, used to \nserve the patrons, bubbles softly over a carefully tended fire in the\nback of the spacious, open sided, tent.\n',76,164025,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30719,0,0,0,'Northern Path','  This dirt path is almost worthy of the name street.  The hard packed \ncontours maintain their shape even during heavy rains.  The passage of \npeople to and from the craftsmen and the large tent keep the path free \nof vegetation.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30720,0,0,0,'Northern Path','  This dirt path is almost worthy of the name street.  The hard packed \ncontours maintain their shape even during heavy rains.  The passage of \npeople to and from the craftsmen and the large tent keep the path free \nof vegetation.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30721,0,0,0,'Northern Path','  This dirt path is almost worthy of the name street.  The hard packed \ncontours maintain their shape even during heavy rains.  The passage of \npeople to and from the craftsmen and the large tent keep the path free \nof vegetation.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30722,0,0,0,'Western Path','  The path here is little more then a dirt track formed by the passage of both\npeople and animals.  Small tufts of grass grow in patches on the edges of the \nnarrow dirt path.  The path continues to wend its way east and west.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30723,0,0,0,'Western Path','  The path here is little more then a dirt track formed by the passage of both\npeople and animals.  Small tufts of grass grow in patches on the edges of the \nnarrow dirt path.  The path continues to wend its way east and west.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30724,0,0,0,'Western Path','  The path here is little more then a dirt track formed by the passage of both\npeople and animals.  Small tufts of grass grow in patches on the edges of the \nnarrow dirt path.  The path continues to wend its way east and west.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30725,0,0,0,'Western Path','  The path here is little more then a dirt track formed by the passage of both\npeople and animals.  Small tufts of grass grow in patches on the edges of the \nnarrow dirt path.  The path continues to wend its way east and west.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30726,0,0,0,'Western Path','  The path here is little more then a dirt track formed by the passage of both\npeople and animals.  Small tufts of grass grow in patches on the edges of the \nnarrow dirt path.  The path continues to wend its way east and west.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30727,0,0,0,'Western Path','  The path here is little more then a dirt track formed by the passage of both\npeople and animals.  Small tufts of grass grow in patches on the edges of the \nnarrow dirt path.  The path continues to wend its way east and west.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30728,0,0,0,'Western Path','  The path here is little more then a dirt track formed by the passage of both\npeople and animals.  Small tufts of grass grow in patches on the edges of the \nnarrow dirt path.  The path continues to wend its way east and west.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30729,0,0,0,'Western Path','  The path here is little more then a dirt track formed by the passage of both\npeople and animals.  Small tufts of grass grow in patches on the edges of the \nnarrow dirt path.  The path continues to wend its way east and west.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30730,0,0,0,'Western Path','  The path here is little more then a dirt track formed by the passage of both\npeople and animals.  Small tufts of grass grow in patches on the edges of the \nnarrow dirt path.  The path continues to wend its way east and west.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30731,0,0,0,'Western Path','  The village square is just visible to the east.  The path here begins to\nwiden out as it approaches the main village.  The roof of the well can be\nseen sticking out above the gently rolling ground.  To the west the varied\ngrasses of the Veldt can be seen waving gently in the breeze.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30732,0,0,0,'Western Path Near Village','  The village square lies directly east, its broad expanse of trampled earth\na sign of a busy village.  The small, mud brick well lies in the centre of\nthe square, providing water for this community.  To the west, the vast \ngrasslands of the veldt can be seen stretching to the horizon.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30733,0,0,0,'Village Square','  Many feet have worn this patch of ground to hard packed dirt.  The four \nmain paths through the village all connect here.  A small, crude, well lies \nin the centre of the square providing fresh spring water to villagers and \ntravellers alike.  To the north lies a large tent, its bright red roof \nvisible even from here, also to the north are the village craftsmen.  The \nbones of various animals decorate the exterior of a tent to the south.  To \nthe west lies the plains of a veldt, while to the east open grassland \ngradually becomes scrub brush.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30734,0,0,0,'Unbridged Chasm','A yawning chasm spans the vista in front of you.  The result of some great\ngeological disaster in the distant past this chasm prevents you from reaching\nthe lowlands to the east.  The earthen scar stretches as far as the eye can \nsee to both the north and the south.  Tools and raw materials lay strewn over\na small clearing before the gap.  It appears as if someone is attempting\nto build a bridge to span the chasm.\n',0,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30740,0,0,0,'Holy Path','  The trail you walk on is narrow, but well tended.  The grasses along the \nedge of the path have been painstakingly trimmed to within inches of the \ndark earth.  A strangely adorned tent is visible to the south, its various \nskeletal decorations swaying slightly with the breezes.  Large stones in \nwhat appear to be concentric rings can also been seen farther to the south.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30741,0,0,0,'Holy Path','  The trail you walk on is narrow, but well tended.  The grasses along the \nedge of the path have been painstakingly trimmed to within inches of the \ndark earth.  A strangely adorned tent is visible to the south, its various \nskeletal decorations swaying slightly with the breezes.  Large stones in \nwhat appear to be concentric rings can also been seen farther to the south.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30742,0,0,0,'Before a Twisted Altar','  A grotesque altar dominates the far corner of this room.  Bleached animal\nskulls adorn the four supporting pillars, their empty eye sockets staring right\nthrough you.  Pools of blood and ichor stain the surface of the altar and the \nfloor of the tent.  The sound of buzzing flies and the stench of decaying flesh \nwafts in from the east.\n',76,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30743,0,0,0,'Beside the Altar','  You stand in front of a large pit next to the altar.  This dank area holds\nthe remnants from the ceremonies conducted there.  Decomposing corpses, in \nvarious states of decay, lie in puddles of blood and gore.  Maggots writhe \namongst the corpses, feasting on the rotting flesh.  This putrid collection\nfills the room with a horrific stench.\n',76,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30744,0,0,0,'Holy Path at an Odd Tent','  The path you walk on is narrow, but well tended.  The grasses along the \nedge of the path have been painstakingly trimmed to within inches of the \ndark earth. The entrance to an odd tent lies to the east, bordered by \nthe grinning skulls of the enemies of the tribe.  Various animal bones and \npelts decorate the exterior of the tent.  Intricately carved runes on the \nframe of the tent throb with magical force.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30745,0,0,0,'Tent Entrance','  The floor of this tent is somewhat bare, with an odd pillow or animal \nfur for decoration.  Bird feathers and animal parts, either preserved in \nglass jars, or hanging from the tent poles crowd the open area of the tent.  \nA wisp of smoke from a small fire curls up and through the smoke hole in \nthe top of the tent.  To the north you see what appears to be some kind of \naltar, surrounded with the bones of animals.  To the south a sleeping area \nis blocked by a decorative screen.\n',76,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30746,0,0,0,'Odd Tent','  This part of the tent is cluttered with a variety of tools and supplies.\nHere bones of animals lie in small piles surrounding a circle of small \ncushions.  In the center of the circle four panels make a hollow box which \nhas been filled with a finely raked <k>black<1> sand.  Tiny bones have been \nplaced in amongst precisely drawn figures on the sand.\n',76,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30747,0,0,0,'Holy Path','  The path you walk on is narrow, but well tended.  The grasses along the \nedge of the path have been painstakingly trimmed to within inches of the \ndark earth.  This ground is obviously very important to the people of \nthis village. To the south you can see the tops of the stone rings that\nmake up a mysterious cricle.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30748,0,0,0,'Private Chamber','These are the private chambers of the tent.  This small section is almost\nbare of any decoration or amenity.  A small pile of furs and cushions in the\ncorner serves as a bed.  A low table holds the room\'s only decoration.\n',76,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(30749,0,0,0,'Entrance to the Stone Circle','  The path narrows as you near the entrance to a mysterious circle.  The grass \nstops well short of the stone rings, which lie directly to the west.  No\nvegetation grows inside the stone rings.  The earth is hard packed dirt and \nunnaturally smooth.  Not a single rock lies outside the limits defined by\nthe stones.  Magical runes traced on the larger stones hum and throb with an\nunnerving regularity.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30751,0,0,0,'Outer Ring of the Stone Circle','  The stones in this first ring are quite large, and of varied color and cut.\nEach stone lies a few feet from its neighbour, as they trace a large ring\naround the outside of the circle.  The runes carved on the rock hum lightly\nwith magical energy.  The ground here is totally void of life.  No plants\ngrow in the hard earth, and no insects can be seen crawling amongst the stones.\nThe stones on the inner rings are smaller and closer together, and seem to\ncenter on a larger stone.  The center stone is still too far away to be seen\nclearly.  A small path to the south here connects to the second set of rings.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30752,0,0,0,'Outer Ring of a Stone Circle','  The stones in this first ring are quite large, and of varied color and cut.\nEach stone lies a few feet from its neighbour, as they trace a large ring\naround the outside of the circle.  The runes carved on the rock hum lightly\nwith magical energy.  The ground here is totally void of life.  No plants\ngrow in the hard earth, and no insects can be seen crawling amongst the \nstones. On the inner rings, the stones are smaller and closer together, \nand seem to center on a larger stone.  The center stone is still too far \naway to be seen clearly.  \n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30753,0,0,0,'Second Ring of a Stone Circle','  The second ring consists of uniformly grey stones of similar height and\ncut.  They are arrayed a few feet apart and line up perfectly with some \ninvisible line encircling the ring.  The ground here remains unblemished \nby any form of life or scuff in the dirt.  The stone in the center of the \ncircle is still blocked by the inner rings, but the throbbing of the runes \nseems to be growing stronger as you approach the center stone.\n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(30754,0,0,0,'Outer Ring of the Stone Circle','  The stones in this first ring are quite large, and of varied color and cut.\nEach stone lies a few feet from its neighbour, as they trace a large ring\naround the outside of the circle.  The runes carved on the rock hum lightly\nwith magical energy.  The ground here is totally void of life.  No plants\ngrow in the hard earth, and no insects can be seen crawling amongst the \nstones. On the inner rings, the stones are smaller and closer together, \nand seem to center on a larger stone.  The center stone is still too far \naway to be seen clearly.  \n',76,131072,42,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
