(30975,0,0,0,'A Spiraling Stairwell','  A wooden trapdoor caps the top of this circular stairwell.  The stairs, like\nthe walls, are cut from the stone of the hill.  They make their narrow,\nvertiginous descent out of the line of sight below.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30976,0,0,0,'A Spiraling Stairwell','  The stone stairs continue both up and down.  Further down, however, the\nwalls of the stairwell open suddenly into empty space.  A faint earthy odor\nwafts up from below.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30977,0,0,0,'A Spiral Staircase in the Arch of a Chamber','  The stairs climb through the vaulted arches of a high chamber.  The ribs\nconverge at a sturdy metal keystone doubling as the sleeve through which the\nstairs ascend.  While above the sleeve the stairs are of stone, from here to\nthe floor below they are of wrought iron and wood.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30978,0,0,0,'An Arched Vault','  Elegantly simple arches descend from the peak of this vaulted chamber,\ncoming to rest on six evenly spaced columns.  Two such columns bracket a\nhorseshoe shaped opening to a passage leading west.  The masonry is of a soft\nstone that muffles noise and exudes an earthy incense smell.  A spiral\nstaircase snakes its way upwards from the very center of the stone floor.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30979,0,0,0,'A Vaulted Passage','  Columns line the wall of this stone passage, supporting haphazardly\ncriss-crossed arches overhead.  To the east, an arched portal gives way to a\nhigh stone chamber while the southern wall is entirely open to a smaller\nstorage vault.  The passage continues to the west.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30980,0,0,0,'A Vaulted Passage','  A testament to quirky gnomish architecture, the arched vaults of the ceiling\nform a kaleidoscope of geometries.  While the stonework is plain, it is\nexcellently crafted.  An engraved lintel is set over a door leading south.  To\nthe east and west, the passage continues.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30981,0,0,0,'Turn in a Vaulted Passage','  The facets of stone between the arches of the ceiling clash violently where\nthe passage makes a turn to the northwest.  The passage continues\nuninterrupted to the east, marked by columns embedded in the soft stone walls. \nTo the southwest an ornately carved pair of columns gives way to a larger\nchamber. \n',224,131084,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30982,0,0,0,'A Vaulted Passage','  Columns support an irregular array of stone arches overhead as the passage\nslopes down to the north and begins a turn to the southeast.  Traces of dust\nand abandonment are evident, though the floor shows a small amount of wear\nfrom the passage of time and feet.  Openings to chambers on the east and west\nare visible.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30983,0,0,0,'A Vaulted Passage','  Plain columns line the walls of this passage, dutifully supporting a network\nof arches overhead.  A thin layer of dust and grime covers the stone floor and\nthe air is faintly damp.  The passage continues to the north and south.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30984,0,0,0,'Before the Shaft of a Well','  A gentle draft of moist air is drifting from an open arch to the north,\nwhere the shaft of a well is evident.  Grime covers the damp stone floor and\nthe supportive pillars built into the walls.  A very narrow ledge can be seen\ngoing around the shaft that might support an agile pair of feet.  Open\narchways to the east and west lead to more stone walled chambers.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30985,0,0,0,'In the Shaft of a Well','  The walls are covered with thick, clean tiles.  A narrow and wet ledge\nencircles the entire shaft, allowing for a small amount of footing.  Should\nthe ledge fail, the surface of the water lies only a short drop below. \nOpenings in the walls lead to passages north and south.  The shaft continues\nits ascent overhead.  \n',224,131080,35,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30986,0,0,0,'Before the Shaft of a Well','  The air here is damp and the stone columns and arches that support the\nceiling vaults are camouflaged with grime.  The floors are moist and cool,\nevenly smudged with small foot and handprints.  To the south a narrow ledge\nskirts around the open shaft of a well, and to the northwest the passage opens\nup into a large chamber.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30987,0,0,0,'Bottom of a Well','  The distinctively clean, sweet water of Gnath seeps from its aquifer here. \nThe echo of a distant breeze is magnified and distorted in the tiled shaft\nabove. There appears to be a ledge about ten feet above the water level.  \n',224,131080,29,200,30987,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30988,0,0,0,'A Vaulted Passage','  Columns line the walls of this passage, supporting a network of wild arches\noverhead. Age and use has worn a slight path into the soft stone floor.  The\npassage continues to the east and west.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30989,0,0,0,'A Vaulted Chamber','  The solid stonework of gnome engineers has taken on a fair amount of grime\nin this damp air, but the grace of the vaulted ceiling and numerous columns is\nstill evident.  Three thin columns form a loosely spaced triangle about the\ncenter of the room.  A strong fetid odor blankets everything.  To the\nsouthwest, northwest and northeast are openings to smaller chambers and an\narched passage is accessible to the southeast.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30990,0,0,0,'A Crypt','  The corners of this hexagonal stone chamber are marked by embedded pillars\nrising into arches that criss-cross the ceiling.  The air is damp and the odor\nof decay is strong.  Footprints smudge the floor and, curiously, the lower\nportions of wall.  An open section of the hexagon leads to a large chamber to\nthe southwest.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30991,0,0,0,'A Crypt','  The corners of this hexagonal stone chamber are marked by embedded pillars\nrising into arches that criss-cross the ceiling.  The air is damp and the odor\nof decay is strong.  Footprints smudge the floor and, curiously, the lower\nportions of wall.  An open section of the hexagon leads to a large chamber to\nthe southeast.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30992,0,0,0,'A Crypt','  The corners of this hexagonal stone chamber are marked by embedded pillars\nrising into arches that criss-cross the ceiling.  The air is damp and the odor\nof decay is strong.  Footprints smudge the floor and, curiously, the lower\nportions of wall.  An open section of the hexagon leads to a large chamber to\nthe northeast.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30993,0,0,0,'A Burial Chamber','  The barreled stone ceiling arches over the open portal to the west.  Solid\nbody benches or low tables carved from stone line the north and south walls. \nA single step down leads to a passage through the portal.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30994,0,0,0,'A Burial Chamber','  The barreled stone ceiling arches over the open portal to the east.  Solid\nbody benches or low tables carved from stone line the north and south walls. \nA single step down leads to a passage through the portal.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30995,0,0,0,'A Burial Chamber','  The barreled stone ceiling arches over the open portal to the west.  Solid\nbody benches or low tables carved from stone line the north and south walls. \nA single step down leads to a passage through the portal.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30996,0,0,0,'A Burial Chamber','  The barreled stone ceiling arches over the open portal to the east.  Solid\nbody benches or low tables carved from stone line the north and south walls. \nA single step down leads to a passage through the portal.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30997,0,0,0,'A Mourning Chamber','  The arches of the high ceiling disappear into the stone walls and a path of\nunpolished black tiles hugs the base of the circular wall.  A dark canopy of\ngauze hangs from the peak of the chamber\'s vaults.  Engraved stonework girds\nthe exit to the northeast.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30998,0,0,0,'Temple Records','  This is a perfectly unremarkable room of right angles.  Unlike the adjacent\nareas, though, every surface is covered in precise tilework.  The air feels\ndry and clean.  Tight fitting doors are placed in the north and east walls.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(30999,0,0,0,'Storage Area','  The room has a simple arched stone ceiling forming a half barrel running\nnorth and south.  The stone floor is scored with shallow scratches.  A door\nfits tightly into the west wall and the north is open to a passage.  \n',224,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(31000,0,0,0,'Versilard\'s Highway Near the Badlands ','  The desolate terrain of the Badlands stretches away to the south, while the\nancient highway of Emperor Versilard heads north towards a pass in the\nSympathian Mountains, which loom to the northwest.  The road is quite worn\ndown and large rocks lie in the way.  Few travelers come this way anymore.  \n',222,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
