(31082,0,0,0,'Drossway Road','  A wide road of pebble and cinder runs north and southeast.  To the south the\nroad splits the face of a hill.  The dull walls of a fortified city rise above\nthe plain to the north.  \n',223,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31083,0,0,0,'Drossway Road','  A wide pebbled road begins to climb a hill as it heads south and winds\nthrough the sparse trees of the plain to the northwest.  The dull walls of a\nfortified city notch the northern horizon.  \n',223,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31084,0,0,0,'Drossway Road','  A wide pebbled road climbs further up a hill as it heads south and winds\nthrough the sparse trees of the plain below to the north.  The dull walls of a\nfortified city notch the northern horizon.  \n',223,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31085,0,0,0,'Drossway Road','  A wide pebbled road climbs further up a hill as it heads south and winds\nthrough the sparse trees of the plain below to the north.  The dull walls of a\nfortified city notch the northern horizon.  \n',223,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31086,0,0,0,'Drossway Road','  A wide pebbled road climbs further up a hill as it heads south and winds\nthrough the sparse trees of the plain below to the north.  The dull walls of a\nfortified city notch the northern horizon.  \n',223,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31087,0,0,0,'Drossway Road','  A wide pebbled road climbs further up a hill as it heads south and winds\nthrough the sparse trees of the plain below to the north.  The dull walls of a\nfortified city notch the northern horizon.  A large stone house has been built\njust southeast of here.  \n',223,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31088,0,0,0,'Drossway Road','  A wide road of pebble and cinder runs north and south.  To the south the\nroad mounts the top of a hill.  The dull walls of a fortified city rise above\nthe plain to the north.  To the east is the yard of a stone house.  \n',223,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31089,0,0,0,'Drossway Road','  A wide road of pebble and cinder runs north and south.  To the south the\nroad mounts the top of a hill.  The dull walls of a fortified city rise above\nthe plain to the north.  A sturdy stone house is to the east.  \n',223,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31090,0,0,0,'<O>Posthouse Yard<1>','  To the west lies the Drossway Road, while a large stable stands to the east. \nA door to the south leads to the interior of a sturdy stone posthouse.  A sign\nhangs from a broad awning above the door.  The yard itself is of packed cinder\nand surrounded by a low rickety fence.  \n',223,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31091,0,0,0,'<O>Posthouse Stable<1>','  The stable has a low, sturdy stone base with wooden walls and rafters above. \nThe floor is packed earth and hay.  It is spacious, able to house and refresh\na good many horses.  A wide gate in the west wall leads to a yard.  \n',223,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(31092,0,0,0,'Drossway Posthouse','  The Posthouse is here to offer refreshment to travelers as they cross the\nrealm. Accordingly, the room is kept warm and clean.  The stone walls are\ncovered with warm tapestry and hay is scattered about the slate floor.  The\nmain room continues to the east and a door in the north wall leads to a well\nused yard.  A large window graces the far wall.  \n',223,131080,32,180,31092,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(31093,0,0,0,'Drossway Posthouse','  The posthouse is here to offer refreshment to travellers as they cross the\nrealm. Accordingly, the room is kept warm and clean.  The stone walls are\ncovered with warm tapestry and hay is scattered about the slate floor.  The\nlarge room continues to the west.  \n',223,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(31094,0,0,0,'Behind the Posthouse','  The wall of a single story stone posthouse is to the west and a steep drop\ndown leads to a rocky gully that has been carved into the hill.  A section of\nthe wall is covered by some carefully placed boards.  \n',223,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31095,0,0,0,'Rocky Gully','  The gully has been carved by years of heavy rains.  It is quite deep in\nparts and the rim is overgrown with brush and small trees.  A few large\nboulders have been unearthed and lie exposed on the dirt.  It is passable to\nthe northeast.  The back wall of a stone posthouse looms above, where the\ngully appears climbable.  \n',223,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31096,0,0,0,'Rocky Gully','  The gully has been carved by years of heavy rains.  It is quite deep in\nparts and the rim is overgrown with brush and small trees.  A few large\nboulders have been unearthed and lie exposed on the dirt.  It is passable to\nthe east and southwest.  \n',223,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31097,0,0,0,'Rocky Gully','  The gully has been carved by years of heavy rains.  It is quite deep in\nparts and the rim is overgrown with brush and small trees.  Rocks and brush\nblock deeper passage, although it remains navigable to the west and the wide\nmaw of a cave is visible to the southeast.  \n',223,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31098,0,0,0,'Mouth of a Cave','  A wide arch of rock leads to a shallow hollow to the southwest.  A deep,\nrocky gully lies to the northwest.  While boulders and brush block passage in\nmost directions, a path has been cleared between the gully and the cave.  \n',223,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31099,0,0,0,'A Shallow Cave','  This cave is wide, but does not extend deeply into the hillside.  The walls\nare encrusted with rock, and a wide opening to the northeast leads to the\noutside world.  Many large boulders have been deliberately moved to the base\nof the walls.  \n',223,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(31300,0,0,0,'In a Holding Pen','This pen serves to hold competitors in a peaceful state.  The\ngames you are about to participate in will be explained by the\nimmortal running the quest. Help PEELPK for minor details.\n',216,174585,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(31301,0,0,0,'In a Dream State of Battle','A strange mist envelops you as you walk through what is\nnot a reality nor total sleep.  The remains of past gladiators\nlitter the area and the smell of death lingers in the air.\n',216,139625,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(31302,0,0,0,'In a Dream State of Battle','A strange mist envelops you as you walk through what is\nnot a reality nor total sleep.  The remains of past gladiators\nlitter the area and the smell of death lingers in the air.\n',216,139625,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
