(31457,0,0,0,'Pass in the Parnithian Mountains','  The trail leads east-west through a seldom-used pass high in the mountains. \nTall, snow-covered peaks prevent travel to the north and south.  The trail\nitself is solid rock and the footing can be precarious.  A tunnel carved into\na cliff leads northeast.  \n',230,131072,5,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(31458,0,0,0,'A Tunnel Through the Parnithian Mountains','  This tunnel has been carved out of rock and frozen earth.  The wind howls\nand whistles as it blows through.  \n',230,131080,13,0,0,0,0,-1,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(31459,0,0,0,'A Tunnel Through the Parnithian Mountains','  This tunnel has been carved out of rock and frozen earth.  The wind howls\nand whistles as it blows through.  A collection of stones lines the north side\nof the trail. \n',230,131080,13,0,0,0,0,-1,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(31460,0,0,0,'A Tunnel Through the Parnithian Mountains','  This tunnel has been carved out of rock and frozen earth.  The wind howls\nand whistles as it blows through. \n',230,131080,13,0,0,0,0,-1,4,100,0,'',NULL),
