(32882,0,0,0,'The Base of the Sympathian Mountains','  Very little vegetation grows here.  Dotting the landscape are small clusters\nof discolored grass.  The ground is brown dirt with protruding rocks tripping\nthe unwary.  The air gets cloudy as the wind blows and picks up dust. An ancient\nhighway can be seen a little off to the east.\n',0,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(32883,0,0,0,'The Base of the Sympathian Mountains','  Very little vegetation grows here.  Dotting the landscape are small clusters\nof discolored grass.  The ground is brown dirt with protruding rocks tripping\nthe unwary.  The air gets cloudy as the wind blows and picks up dust. An ancient\nhighway can be seen a little off to the east.\n',0,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(32884,0,0,0,'The Base of the Sympathian Mountains','  The desolate landscape is dotted with small clusters of discolored grass.\nThe ground is brown dirt with protruding rocks tripping the unwary.  The air\ngets cloudy as the wind blows and picks up dust. An ancient highway can be seen\na little off to the east and a small construction lies to the south.\n',0,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(32885,0,0,0,'The Base of the Sympathian Mountains','\n  The desolate landscape is dotted with small clusters of discolored grass.\nThe ground is brown dirt with protruding rocks tripping the unwary.  East of\nhere lies an ancient highway constructed during the times of Emperor Versilard,\nconnecting the cities of Amber far to the north and Logrus away to the south.\nA small construction lies to the south.\n',0,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(32886,0,0,0,'Main Room','  The room is spacious but pretty empty.  The walls are blocks of stone with\nseveral layers of dust over them.  The floor is made of uneven wooden boards\nthat emit a cracking sound when stepped on.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(32887,0,0,0,'Main Room','  The room is spacious but pretty empty.  The walls are blocks of stone with\nseveral layers of dust over them.  The floor is made of uneven wooden boards\nthat emit a cracking sound when stepped on.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(32888,0,0,0,'Front Porch','  The lodge looks old and poorly kept.  The walls are made of blocks of stones\nand there are windows on the north and south sides.  The porch is quite big, as\nif meant to be a place of gathering.  The floor is made of uneven wooden boards\nthat emit a cracking sound when stepped on.  The ancient Versilard Highway is visible to the\neast.  The entrance to the lodge is through a door to the southwest.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(32889,0,0,0,'Main Room','  The room is spacious but pretty empty.  The walls are blocks of stone with\nseveral layers of dust over them.  The floor is made of uneven wooden boards\nthat emit a cracking sound when stepped on. A staircase in the corner\nleads to the second floor.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(32890,0,0,0,'Main Room','  The room is spacious but pretty empty.  The walls are blocks of stone with\nseveral layers of dust over them.  The floor is made of uneven wooden boards\nthat emit a cracking sound when stepped on.  The reception is south of here.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(32891,0,0,0,'Kitchen','The room has all the utensils that belong in a kitchen. Pots and pans hang from\nthe walls, but from the layers of dust they\'ve accumulated it doesn\'t seem like\nthey get used very often. A window on the north wall provides a clear view of\nthe front porch and who\'s coming in and out.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(32892,0,0,0,'Backroom','This room looks like a sleeping quarter of sorts. Contrasting with the rest of\nthe lodge, it\'s very clean and well kept. The floor doesn\'t even make that\nannoying cracking sound. There are pictures hanging from the walls showing\npeople in joyful moments. The space is a little cluttered, but everything is\norganized.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(32893,0,0,0,'Reception','  This room is better kept than the others in the lodge.  There is less dust\neverywhere but the floor emits the same cracking sound.  There is a portrait up\non the south wall and beneath it is a desk. A door leads west and a window on\nthe southeast wall looks out to Versilard\'s Highway.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(32894,0,0,0,'Bathroom','  The room isn\'t as bad as one would expect after visiting the rest of the\nlodge.  From the odor there is no mistake, this is a latrine, but other than\nthat everything looks in place.  There\'s a large opening in the floor with a\npipe leading off to the ground.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(32895,0,0,0,'Guest Room','Like everywhere else in the lodge, the walls are blocks of stone with several\nlayers of dust over them.  The floor is made of uneven wooden boards that emit\na cracking sound when stepped on.  There is some furniture scattered about the\nroom but apparently it hasn\'t been used in a while.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(32896,0,0,0,'Balcony','The balcony doesn\'t protrude off the main building, it\'s just an open area on\nthe second floor. A rugged, worn out wooden railing provides security, even\nthough it looks as if it could break down at any moment. The balcony overlooks\nthe front porch below.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(32897,0,0,0,'Hall','  The hall is pretty narrow and is completely bare.  Like everywhere else in\nthe lodge, the walls are blocks of stone with several layers of dust over them.\nThe floor is made of uneven wooden boards that emit a cracking sound when\nstepped on.  There are doors on the north and east side leading to the\nguest rooms.  A staircase in the corner leads to the first floor.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(32898,0,0,0,'Guest Room','  Like everywhere else in the lodge, the walls are blocks of stone with several\nlayers of dust over them.  The floor is made of uneven wooden boards that emit\na cracking sound when stepped on.  There is some furniture scattered about the\nroom but apparently it hasn\'t been used in a while.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(32899,0,0,0,'Balcony','The balcony doesn\'t protrude off the main building, it\'s just an open area on\nthe second floor. A rugged, worn out wooden railing provides security, even\nthough it looks as if it could break down at any moment. The balcony overlooks\nthe front porch below.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(33200,0,0,0,'A Hovel Under an Outlook Platform','It is not so much a building as a hole dug into the earthen rampart below the\ncorner watch platform. The facing walls are fashioned from a few random boards\nand rotting animal skins.  It is wet, muddy, cramped and messy. There is an exit\nto the east.\n',0,131080,36,0,0,0,0,-1,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(33201,0,0,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Outpost','A muddy and rutted road leads south and east. The road is a rough oval around\nthe center line of market stalls. There are pens and stalls along the outside of\nthe oval to the east and west and gates out of the post to the north and south.\nThere is a hovel under an outlook platform to the west.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33202,0,0,0,'A Muddy Road at the North Gate','A muddy and rutted road leads north, east and west. The road is a rough oval\naround the center line of market stalls. There are pens and stalls along the\noutside of the oval to the east and west and gates out of the post to the north\nand south. There is a gate in the wall to the north.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33203,0,0,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Outpost','A muddy and rutted road leads south and west. The road is a rough oval around\nthe center line of market stalls. There are pens and stalls along the outside of\nthe oval to the east and west and gates out of the post to the north and south.\nThere is a hovel under an outlook platform to the east.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33204,0,0,0,'A Hovel Under an Outlook Platform','It is not so much a building as a hole dug into the earthen rampart below the\ncorner watch platform. The facing walls are fashioned from a few random boards\nand rotting animal skins.  It is wet, muddy, cramped and messy. There is an exit\nto the west.\n',0,131080,36,0,0,0,0,-1,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(33205,0,0,0,'A Cage for Prisoners or Animals or Both','A crude cage or pen has been created by driving sharpened pickets into the muddy\nground. The eight foot tall pickets are lashed together at the top to a wooden\ncross brace and the tips are sharpened. The only exit is a gate to the east.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33206,0,0,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Outpost','A muddy and rutted road leads north and south. The road is a rough oval around\nthe center line of market stalls. There are pens and stalls along the outside of\nthe oval to the east and west and gates out of the post to the north and south.\nThere is a crude pen to the west and a market stall to the east.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33207,0,0,0,'Bindlewurdle\'s Armor','The stall is separated from the next by ratty sheets of canvas hung from poles\non the north and south. It is open to the east and west. A rope with faded\nstreamers hangs over each exit. This stall has several small piles of beaten and\nabused armor hanging from the stall.\n',0,131088,36,0,0,0,0,-1,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33208,0,0,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Outpost','A muddy and rutted road leads north and south. The road is a rough oval around\nthe center line of market stalls. There are pens and stalls along the outside of\nthe oval to the east and west and gates out of the post to the north and south.\nThere is a market stall to the west and the repairman\'s stall to the east.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33209,0,0,0,'Groop\'s Repair','The stall is separated from the next by ratty sheets of canvas hung from poles\non the north and south. It is open to the west and against the ramparts to the\neast. A rope with faded streamers hangs over the exit. This stall has several\nimplements of the repair trade.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33210,0,0,0,'Drangle\'s Provisions','The stall is separated from the next by ratty sheets of canvas hung from poles\non the north and south.  It is open to the east and against the ramparts to the\nwest.  A rope with faded streamers hangs over the exit.  This stall is cluttered\nwith many everyday items.\n',0,163840,36,0,0,0,0,-1,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33211,0,0,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Outpost','A muddy and rutted road leads south and west.The road is a rough oval around the\ncenter line of market stalls. There are pens and stalls along the outside of the\noval to the east and west and gates out of the post to the north and south.\nThere is a crude pen to the west and a market stall to the east.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33212,0,0,0,'Turlingdrome\'s Clothery','The stall is separated from the next by ratty sheets of canvas hung from poles\non the north and south. It is open to the west and the east. A rope with faded\nstreamers hangs over each exit. This stall has dirty, shabby clothes and leather\narmor scattered about.\n',0,131088,36,0,0,0,0,-1,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33213,0,0,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Outpost','A muddy and rutted road leads south and west. The road is a rough oval around\nthe center line of market stalls. There are pens and stalls along the outside of\nthe oval to the east and west and gates out of the post to the north and south.\nThere is a market stall to the west and a crude pen to the east.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33214,0,0,0,'Axmnck the Sharpener\'s Stall','The stall is separated from the next by ratty sheets of canvas hung from poles\non the north and south. It is open to the west and against the ramparts to the\neast. A rope with faded streamers hangs over the exit.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33215,0,0,0,'A Crude Gealgan','A rough hewn framework holds up a noose. There are additional posts behind the\ngealgan sporting the heads of the most recent entertainment.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,5,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33216,0,0,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Outpost','A muddy and rutted road leads north and south. The road is a rough oval around\nthe center line of market stalls. There are pens and stalls along the outside of\nthe oval to the east and west and gates out of the post to the north and south.\nTo the east is the only real building in the outpost, which houses the inn. To\nthe west is a mostly empty area with a noose suspended from a rough hewn\nframework.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33217,0,0,0,'The Grunting Whore Inn','The lower floor of this two story building is occupied by the inn. Part inn,\npart pub and part brothel, this slapdash wooden structure is perhaps the most\npatronized business in the outpost and the dirt and filth bear grim testament to\nthat fact. There are exits to the east and west and steps up to the overlord\'s\noffice on the second floor.\n',0,131096,32,0,0,0,0,-1,30,100,0,'',NULL),
(33218,0,0,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Outpost','A muddy and rutted road leads south and west. The road here is soggier and\nsmellier than other areas, though the orcs pay no notice. It seems that the\nmidden heap to the east is overflowing into the road. To the west is the only\nreal building in the outpost, which houses the inn.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33219,0,0,0,'A Midden Heap','Near knee deep in filth, this is where all the refuse of the outpost ends up. \nThe pile, banked high against the rampart wall to the east is threatening to\nooze out onto the road near the inn.\n',0,147456,36,0,0,0,0,-1,20,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33220,0,0,0,'A Cage for Prisoners or Animals or Both','A crude cage or pen has been created by driving sharpened pickets into the muddy\nground. The eight foot tall pickets are lashed together at the top to a wooden\ncross brace and the tips are sharpened. The only exit is a gate to the east.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33221,0,0,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Outpost','A muddy and rutted road leads north and south. The road is a rough oval around\nthe center line of market stalls. There are pens and stalls along the outside of\nthe oval to the east and west and gates out of the post to the north and south.\nThere is a crude pen to the west and a market stall to the east.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33222,0,0,0,'Hrothnar the Postmaster\'s Stall','The stall is separated from the next by ratty sheets of canvas hung from poles\non the north and south. It is open to the west and the east. A rope with faded\nstreamers hangs over each exit. This stall is cleaner and neater than most.\n',0,131088,36,0,0,0,0,-1,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
