(33227,0,0,0,'Gnorbert\'s Hypothecary','The stall is separated from the next by ratty sheets of canvas hung from poles\non the north and south. It is open to the west and the east. A rope with faded\nstreamers hangs over each exit. This stall has several mismatched cabinets and\ncrates.\n',0,131088,36,0,0,0,0,-1,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33228,0,0,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Outpost','A muddy and rutted road leads north and south. The road is a rough oval around\nthe center line of market stalls. There are pens and stalls along the outside of\nthe oval to the east and west and gates out of the post to the north and south.\nThere are market stalls to the east and west.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33229,0,0,0,'Gabbleblotchit\'s Arms','The stall is separated from the next by ratty sheets of canvas hung from poles\non the north and south. It is open to the west and against the ramparts to the\neast. A rope with faded streamers hangs over the exit. This stall has several\nimplements of the war trade stacked against the outlook\'s walls.\n',0,131088,36,0,0,0,0,-1,6,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33230,0,0,0,'A Hovel Under an Outlook Platform','It is not so much a building as a hole dug into the earthen rampart below the\ncorner watch platform. The facing walls are fashioned from a few random boards\nand rotting animal skins.  It is wet, muddy, cramped and messy. There is an exit\nto the east.\n',0,131080,36,0,0,0,0,-1,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(33231,0,0,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Outpost','A muddy and rutted road leads south and west. The road is a rough oval around\nthe center line of market stalls. There are pens and stalls along the outside of\nthe oval to the east and west and gates out of the post to the north and south.\nThere is a hovel under an outlook platform to the west.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33232,0,0,0,'A Muddy Road at the South Gate','A muddy and rutted road leads east and west. The road is a rough oval around the\ncenter line of market stalls. There are pens and stalls along the outside of the\noval to the east and west and gates out of the post to the north and south.\nThere is a gate on the southern wall of the outpost.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,15,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33233,0,0,0,'A Muddy Road Through the Outpost','A muddy and rutted road leads north and west. The road is a rough oval around\nthe center line of market stalls. There are pens and stalls along the outside of\nthe oval to the east and west and gates out of the post to the north and south.\nThere is a hovel under an outlook platform to the east.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,8,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33234,0,0,0,'A Hovel Under an Outlook Platform','It is not so much a building as a hole dug into the earthen rampart below the\ncorner watch platform. The facing walls are fashioned from a few random boards\nand rotting animal skins.  It is wet, muddy, cramped and messy. There is an exit\nto the west.\n',0,131080,36,0,0,0,0,-1,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(33235,0,0,0,'Atop a Rudimentary Outlook Platform','This is an outlook platform hanging precariously from the log ramparts in the\nnorthwest corner of the outpost. From this vantage point, there is an excellent\nview of the <p>forest<1>, the <p>outpost<1> and not much else. There is an exit\ndown.\n',0,655360,26,0,0,0,0,-1,4,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33236,0,0,0,'Atop a Rudimentary Outlook Platform','This is an outlook platform hanging precariously from the log ramparts in the\nnortheast corner of the outpost. From this vantage point, there is an excellent\nview of the <p>forest<1>, the <p>outpost<1> and not much else. There is an exit\ndown.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,4,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33237,0,0,0,'Atop a Rudimentary Outlook Platform','This is an outlook platform hanging precariously from the log ramparts in the\nsouthwest corner of the outpost. From this vantage point, there is an excellent\nview of the <p>forest<1>, the <p>outpost<1> and not much else. There is an exit\ndown.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,4,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33238,0,0,0,'Atop a Rudimentary Outlook Platform','This is an outlook platform hanging precariously from the log ramparts in the\nsoutheast corner of the outpost. From this vantage point, there is an excellent\nview of the <p>forest<1>, the <p>outpost<1> and not much else. There is an exit\ndown.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,4,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33239,0,0,0,'The Overlord\'s Quarters','This is perhaps the cleanest and most elegant space in the outpost, but that is\nonly in comparison.  There are <p>windows<1> overlooking the four ordinal\ndirections. There are stairs leading down to the first floor.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,20,100,0,'',NULL),
(33270,0,0,0,'The Hammer And Fist Construction Company','A large <b>blueprint<1> is hapazardly hung upside down on the wall,\noverlapping older specimens, and emblazoned with a poorly drawn\n<W>skull and crossbones<1>.  A work table pushed against one wall\nholds several drafting instruments, a small pile of <W>crumpled\npaper<1> and a full bottle of <o>rum<1> with a drawing compass wedged\ninto the cork.  Another table holds a scale model of the <r>GK\nHighrollers Casino<1>, with several tiny stick figures bearing\nminiscule <k>paper<1> <r>pirate<1> <k>hats<1> surrounding it, with a\nfew hanging off the sides and standing on top.  The table also holds\nan uncompleted scale model of the Grimhaven Mayor\'s mansion, half\ncrushed by the weight of a cannonball with a crudely chalk-drawn face\non it.  A small iron stove in the corner hosts a pot of boiling water\nand on the table next to it sits several half empty coffee cups, a\nhalf dozen empty bottles of <o>rum<1> and an opened bag of <o>ground\ncoffee<1>.  The wooden floor is speckled with <r>bloody footprints<1>,\n<o>sawdust<1> and a few stray splotches of <g>p<b>a<y>i<p>n<c>t<1>.  A\npallet of <r>bricks<1> have been stacked up near the rear wall,\nforming crude stairs leading up to the ceiling.\n',0,131097,32,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33271,0,0,0,'North End of the Docks','The wooden planks of the boardwalk lead east to a shop at the end of\nthe pier.  There is a small exit to a stone road to the west.  During\nthe day there are huge numbers of people milling around, and even the\nevening invites several people, though generally of a more rowdy\nnature.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33272,0,0,0,'Main Entrance to the Docks','This area is generally bustling with activity as merchants load and\nunload ships and bring their goods to and from town.  The road leads\nnorth and south.  To the west is a boat shop, which supplies the ships\nthat you can see docked east of here.  A massive <o>hospital<z> rises above\nthe other buildings of the town, and it is to the northwest of here.\n',248,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33273,0,0,0,'Main Entrance to the Docks','This area is generally bustling with activity as merchants load and unload\nships and bring their goods to and from town.  Attallal Boulevard, with its\nbluish moonstone tiles, leads to the south.  To the west is a <b>lapis lazuli<z>\ntiled road which leads to Cascade Plaza.  To the northwest you see a massive\n<o>hospital<z> standing above the other buildings of the town.  The road also\ncontinues north.  To the east is the busy dock area, and you can see several\nships have come in to port.\n',248,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33274,0,0,0,'Connecting Passage','This passage connects the police station to a large commercial\nbuilding, and through the windows in the north and south walls you can\nsee Attallal Boulevard below you.  People busily scurry through the\nstreets during the day.  Doors lead west and east.\n',-1,131081,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33275,0,0,0,'Amber Corporate Offices','This area has been provided by Amber for local corporations to\nconduct business.  A number of cluttered desks are layed out in rows\nand the walls are covered in charts and graphs.  Large accounting books\nare stacked up both on desks and in corners and messengers run in and\nout with packages and notes.  All of the tools a corporate officer\nwould need to run a corporation are available here.  A sky bridge\nleads to the police station to the west while the rest of building is\nzoned for commercial use.\n',0,131081,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33276,0,0,0,'Unfinished Shop','The basic building frame and floor of a shop has been built here.  Various remenants of construction lie about, a pile of boards here, a few blocks of concrete there, a pile of tools in the corner.  When this building has been purchased, construction will continue to fulfill the desires of the owner.\n',-1,131081,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33277,0,0,0,'Unfinished Shop','The basic building frame and floor of a shop has been built here.  Various remenants of construction lie about, a pile of boards here, a few blocks of concrete there, a pile of tools in the corner.  When this building has been purchased, construction will continue to fulfill the desires of the owner.\n',-1,131081,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33278,0,0,0,'Unfinished Shop','The basic building frame and floor of a shop has been built here.  Various remenants of construction lie about, a pile of boards here, a few blocks of concrete there, a pile of tools in the corner.  When this building has been purchased, construction will continue to fulfill the desires of the owner.\n',-1,131081,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33279,0,0,0,'Unfinished Shop','The basic building frame and floor of a shop has been built here.  Various remenants of construction lie about, a pile of boards here, a few blocks of concrete there, a pile of tools in the corner.  When this building has been purchased, construction will continue to fulfill the desires of the owner.\n',-1,131081,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33280,0,0,0,'Unfinished Shop','The basic building frame and floor of a shop has been built here.  Various remenants of construction lie about, a pile of boards here, a few blocks of concrete there, a pile of tools in the corner.  When this building has been purchased, construction will continue to fulfill the desires of the owner.\n',-1,131081,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33281,0,0,0,'Amber Town Dump','Tall stone walls surround this area where the trash of Amber is brought.\nThe entire area is recessed into the earth slightly, to help prevent spillage\nand runoff into the streets of the city.  The stench of civilization\nlingers in the air and piles of garbage lie strewn about.\n',-1,131072,2,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33282,0,0,0,'<W>A Magnificant Foyer<1>','  <W>Cream colored marble makes up the floor of this foyer, with <o>darker\nblocks<W> placed strategically to create eye catching <W>p<1><o>at<W>te<1><o>rns<W>.  Massive\nwhite columns rise up to the ceiling far overhead, giving the whole room\na feeling of openness and majesty.  The curved ceiling is covered in a\nmural of various scenes of combat.  Large, swinging <c>glass doors<W> lead out to\nthe streets of Amber while <o>two massive wooden doors<W> stand to the east, like\nstout guardians.\n',248,131081,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,360,0,'',NULL),
(33283,0,0,0,'<o>A Sweeping Staircase<1>','<o>This sweeping staircase is very broad and well crafted from the\nwood of the native arctic trees.  It leads upwards, circling like a\nhawk hunting for prey.  Two massive wooden doors stand to the west.<1>\n',248,139272,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33284,0,0,0,'<p>An Opulent Lounge<1>','<r>Thick, plush carpet lines the floor of this room, wall to wall.  A lack of\nwindows and low lighting gives this room a darkened lounge atmosphere.  A\nstout door adorned in red leather is in the west wall, while a large\nsweeping staircase leads both up and down.<1>\n',-1,139272,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33285,0,0,0,'<k>A Comfortable Bedroom<1>','<p>A large <Y>bay window<1><p> is mounted in the wall, providing a view \nover the west wall of Amber and into the <W>tundra<1><p> beyond.  Plush carpet\nand sturdy walls insulate the room from outside noises, providing a quiet\nrest area.  A stout door adorned in <r>red leather<p> is in the east wall.\n<1>\n',-1,139272,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33286,0,0,0,'<g>A Vibrant Garden<1>','<g>Despite the arctic climate, fertile imported soil has been laid down here\nto provide ground for a variety of carefully nurtured plant life.  Views of\nthe city of Amber can be seen to the north and east, and farther to the east\nthe <b>bay<g> reaches out to the retaining wall.  To the northeast, a tangle\nof sails and rigging define the dock area.  A mass of trees far to the south\nmark the location of the Arden forest.<1>\n',248,131072,2,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33287,0,0,0,'<C>A Sparkling Pool<1>','<W>White tile<B> has been carefully laid down, forming this rooftop\nrecreational pool.  The pool leads right to the edge of the\nbuilding and the water is level with the side of the pool, giving the \nappearance of stretching to the horizon.  A furnace in the building below\nheats up the water, keeping the pool comfortable year round.  Views of the\ncity and the surrounding lands can be seen all around, while a peek over\nthe edge of the building allows rooftop views of the busy streets below.<1>\n',248,139264,52,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33288,0,0,0,'<k>A Musty Cellar<1>','<k>Old crumbling <r>brick<k> barely retains the surrounding earth from caving\nin, while <o>roots<k> and <g>mold<k> invade through the cracks.  The stone\nfloor is a bit bumpy and uneven, but dry.  Heavy wooden beams cross the cellar\nin the low ceiling, supporting the large house above.\n',-1,139272,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33289,0,0,0,'<k>A Disused Cellar<1>','<k>This part of the cellar is covered in undisturbed dust, as though it\nis rarely visited.  Old crumbling <r>brick<k> barely retains the\nsurrounding earth from caving in, while <o>roots<k> and <g>mold<k>\ninvade through the cracks.  The stone floor is a bit bumpy and uneven,\nbut dry.  Heavy wooden beams cross the cellar in the low ceiling,\nsupporting the large house above.\n',-1,139272,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33290,0,0,0,'Spacious Living Area','This is the living area inside a cozy home.  Doors lead to inner rooms\nin the south and east walls.  A very sturdy looking door, made of some\n<D>glowing<1> metal is in the northern wall, leading out.\n',-1,139272,32,0,0,0,0,-1,100,300,0,'',NULL),
(33291,0,0,0,'A Comfortable Bedroom','You stand in awe of this well-equipped bedroom.  Even though this house has\nbeen built far from civilization, the occupant has managed to furnish it\nwith all amenities of modern life.  A small window provides a view of the\nclearing to the north.  A door leads out in the eastern part of the room.\n',-1,139272,32,0,0,0,0,-1,4,300,0,'',NULL),
(33292,0,0,0,'Storage Room','This storage room seems to be much larger than it appeared from the outside.\nShelves line all wall-space to maximize storage.  A small door leads out \ninto the living area to the north.\n',-1,139272,32,0,0,0,0,-1,100,300,0,'',NULL),
(33293,0,0,0,'Unfinished Shop','  The basic building frame and floor of a shop has been built here.  Various\nremnants of construction lie about, a pile of boards here, a few blocks of\nconcrete there, a pile of tools in the corner.  When this building has been\npurchased, construction will continue to fulfill the desires of the owner.\nContrasting with the room there is a great marble staircase leading up.\n',0,131080,12,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(33294,0,0,0,'The Serpent\'s Hall','  An immense and stately room, the Serpent\'s Faction Hall is approximately\ntwice as long as it is wide.  The white marble walls are complemented by great\ncolumns along the wall supporting a white domed ceiling that glows from hidden\nlighting.  Between the columns are rich tapestries of past Order of the Serpent\nheroes and legends.  There is a grand fireplace opposite the entrance in the\ncenter of the long walls.  The cornice, columns and fireplace carry a serpent\nmotif.  At the north end of the room is low dais with a floor to ceiling mosaic\nof the Coils of the Serpent.  A great marble staircase leads down.\n',0,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(33295,0,0,0,'The Overlord\'s Sanctum','  This spacious room is the private sanctuary of the Overlord of the Serpent\nOrder.  The room is lit by ornate oil lamps made of gold.  High ceilings add\nto the large feel of this room.  Bejeweled tapestries of beautiful, dazzling\ncolors hang from the ceiling towards the floor just high enough for an average\nsize ogre to pass.  Feet fall silently on luxuriant, imported rugs from\neastern lands.  The walls are adorned with magnificent works of hand-painted\nart depicting events of great historical significance.  At the south end of\nthe room is low dais with a floor to ceiling mosaic of the Coils of the\nSerpent. \n',0,131081,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(33300,0,0,0,'The Haon-Dor Forest','  Old stands of tall white birch trees add splashes of white to a backdrop of\ndark green pines.  The many trees and dense undergrowth occlude sight of all\nbut the nearest parts of the forest.  A well-traveled path continues to the\nnorth and south.\n',242,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33301,0,0,0,'The Haon-Dor Forest','  Old stands of tall white birch trees add splashes of white to a backdrop of\ndark green pines.  The many trees and dense undergrowth occlude sight of all\nbut the nearest parts of the forest.  A well-traveled path continues to the\nnorth and south.\n',242,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
