(33466,0,0,0,'The Ossuary','Nothing in this room has been touched by living hands in well over a thousand\nyears. It has been longer still since they were touched by the light of the\nsun. The stone floors lack signs of any wear or use and there is even a lack\nof natural deterioration that stone this old ought to have. The ceilings are\nstill intact and have not yet begun to crack from strain. Most of the sounds in\nthis room\nare stolen by the shadows, which are numerous. However, the distinct sound\nof voices echoes about. Apparenlty, whatever was buried here ages ago is awake.\nA thin layer of condensation has gathered upon the western wall.\n',0,139272,61,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
