(33477,0,0,0,'The Ossuary','Nothing in this room has been touced by living hands in well over a thousand\nyears. It has been longer still since they were touched by the light of the\nsun. The stone floors lack signs of any wear or use and there is even a lack\nof natural deterioration that stone this old ought to have. The ceilings are\nstill intact and have not yet begun to crack from strain. Most of the sounds in\nthis room\nare stolen by the shadows, which are numerous. However, the distinct sound\nof voices echoes about. Apparently, whatever was buried here ages ago is awake.\nThe wall to the east does not seem as unwelcoming as others in this place.\n',0,139272,61,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(33478,0,0,0,'Soaking Antechamber','Unlike the eerie silence of the ossuary, this room is terrifyingly loud. The\nstone floor is covered in a thin layer of cold water, and in the center of the\nroom is a large hole that opens up into the darkness below.\n',0,139528,61,0,0,0,0,-1,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(33479,0,0,0,'A Dark, Still Pool','While not stagnant, this body of water is completely still. Even when molested,\nthe surface quickly clears itself of any ripples.\nThis is particularly surprising in light of the rumble that becomes aubible when\nsubmersed.  The noise is constant and never raises or lowers in volume.\nIt sounds a little like running water. In fact, it sounds very much like the\nrock floor beneath your feet might be all\nthat separates you from a large, swift underground river.\n',0,139528,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33480,0,0,0,'Overseer\'s Den',' Each wall of this octagonal room is covered in a curtain of dark red cloth. It\nis lit by two single candles atop tall brass stands, one on the north wall and\none on the south.\nYour eye is drawn to a long, ornately decorated scabbard that lies on a large\ndesk, which occupies the center of the room.\nThe desk itself seems out of place against the otherwise lavish decor. A small\npile of wood and leather\nleans against the eastern wall.\n',0,139273,61,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(33481,0,0,0,'Tainted Summoning Chamber','The walls, floor, and celing of this room are covered in glowing runes.\nMost of them cast gentle blue light into the room, but when any of them\nare touched, they radiate an unbearable, blinding light. Other than the\nrunes, the room is bare.\n',0,132488,60,0,0,0,0,-1,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(33482,0,0,0,'The Mouth of a Wide Tunnel','The walls of this tunnel bear deep claw marks. It appears as if some enormous\ncreature accidentally stumbled\nupon the ossuary while digging out its burrow. The dirt floor is somewhat damp\nand there are footprints visible in some\nof the muddier areas.\n',0,139272,61,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(33483,0,0,0,'A Blocked Off Tunnel','The rock that forms the walls of this tunnel is smoother than other areas and it\ndoes not bear the same\ndeep claw marks. This width of tunnel is also a good deal smaller. Apparently\nthe beast that dug this hole found\nthis vein of rock a bit more disagreeable.\nA huge shield is lodged between some of the larger rocks in the side of the\nwall, forming a door that closes off the tunnel to the east.\n',0,139272,61,0,0,0,0,-1,18,100,0,'',NULL),
(33484,0,0,0,'The Den of a Large Beast','The stone that makes up the walls of this \nroom seems less tightly packed\nthan you might expect at this depth. The east wall angles down, which might\nsuggest that this tunnel collapsed at some point. The floor is covered with\na thick layer of scales that have been sloughed off. Surprisingly, there are\nno bones. That makes one of two things true. Either the beast devours the\nbones, or it has not eaten in quite a while. With any luck, it is the former.\n',0,140552,61,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33485,0,0,0,'Plateau Road','  This packed dirt road leads away from the foul borough that is the East Gate\nSettlement and continues off the plateau into the fertile farmlands below. \nScruffy shrubs and sparse clusters of weeds dot the western embankment.  Over\nthe eastern edge of the road, more road can be seen below. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33486,0,0,0,'Plateau Road','  This packed dirt road leads away from the foul borough that is the East Gate\nSettlement and continues off the plateau into the fertile farmlands below.\nScruffy shrubs and sparse clusters of weeds dot the western embankment.  Over\nthe eastern edge of the road, more road can be seen below.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33487,0,0,0,'Plateau Road','  This packed dirt road leads down off the plateau into the fertile farmlands\nbelow. The western embankment presents a rocky wall that drops off as the road\nturns into an eastern downward slope.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33488,0,0,0,'Plateau Road','  This packed dirt road leads down off the plateau into the fertile farmlands\nbelow.  The western embankment presents a rocky wall that drops off as the\nroad veers downward and to the south. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33489,0,0,0,'Plateau Road','  This packed dirt road leads down off the plateau into the fertile farmlands\nbelow.  Scruffy shrubs and sparse clusters of weeds dot the western\nembankment.  Just south the road turns to the east as the path levels out\nbelow the plateau. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33490,0,0,0,'Plateau Road meets a Road through a Valley','  This packed dirt road leads up to the plateau and east into fertile\nfarmlands.  Several farmhouses and some fields can be seen in the east.  To\nthe south a thick stand of brambles effectively blocks any would be travelers. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33491,0,0,0,'A Road through the Valley','  This packed dirt road leads east into a fertile farmland.  To the west it\nleads up onto a plateau.  To the south a thick stand of brambles effectively\nblocks any would be travelers.  Farther east, the road becomes fence lined and\nseveral farmhouses can be seen. \n',-1,131076,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33492,0,0,0,'A Road through the Valley','  This packed dirt road runs east and west through a fertile farmland. \nSeveral farmhouses can be seen behind the fences that line these roads and\nseparate the farm lots. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33493,0,0,0,'A Road through the Valley','  This packed dirt road runs east and west through a fertile farmland. \nSeveral farmhouses can be seen behind the fences that line these roads and\nseparate the farm lots. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33494,0,0,0,'A Road through the Valley','  This packed dirt road runs east and west through a fertile farmland.  The\nfencing parts to the north and to the south where there are small rose lined\npaths to farmhouses, there is another farm far to the east. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33495,0,0,0,'A Road through the Valley','  This packed dirt road runs east and west through a fertile farmland. \nSeveral farmhouses can be seen behind the fences that line these roads and\nseparate the farm lots. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33496,0,0,0,'A Road through the Valley','  This packed dirt road runs east and west through a fertile farmland. \nSeveral farmhouses can be seen behind the fences that line these roads and\nseparate the farm lots. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33497,0,0,0,'A Road through the Valley','  This packed dirt road runs east and west through a fertile farmland.  The\nfencing parts to the east where there is a small rose lined path to a\nfarmhouse, there are other farms far to the west. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33498,0,0,0,'A Little Path','  A tidy little path extends west to the road and east towards a farmhouse. \nThe path has been carefully swept clean of debris, the rose beds are in\nperfect order. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33499,0,0,0,'Inside a Farmhouse','  A large and airy white-washed room makes up the community space for the\nfarm.  Solid planks cover the floor, they are kept immaculately clean and\nshine with regular waxing.  There is a red door to the north, a green door to\nthe east and a blue door to the south. \n',-1,172221,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33500,0,0,0,'A Bedroom','  This is a small private room.  The walls are freshly white-washed and the\nfloor is composed of solid wood planks. \n',-1,172221,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33501,0,0,0,'A Bedroom','  This is a small private room.  The walls are freshly white-washed and the\nfloor is composed of solid wood planks. \n',-1,172221,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
