(33537,0,0,0,'A Road through the Valley','  This packed dirt road runs north and south through a fertile farmland. \nSeveral farmhouses can be seen behind the fences that line these roads and\nseparate the farm lots. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33538,0,0,0,'A Road through the Valley','  This packed dirt road runs north and south through a fertile farmland. \nSeveral farmhouses can be seen behind the fences that line these roads and\nseparate the farm lots.  Weedy growth, brambles and vines have taken over the\nunused fields to the north.  There is a small fenced in pasture to the east. \n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33539,0,0,0,'A Road through the Valley','  This packed dirt road runs north and south through a fertile farmland.  There\nare no fields visible here through the weedy growth, brambles and vines that\nhave taken over the unused fields along the roadside.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33540,0,0,0,'A Road through the Valley','  This packed dirt road runs north and south through a fertile farmland.  There\nare no fields visible here through the weedy growth, brambles and vines that\nhave taken over the unused fields along the roadside.  A large tree has fallen\nacross the road and blocks all passage to the north.\n',-1,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33541,0,0,0,'In a Pasture','  This is a big area that has been fenced in.  The grass is of a thick\nvariety, it grows richly except in a few areas that have been grazed upon.  A\nways to the north, there is a little grassy spot shaded by a very large willow\ntree.  There is an exit from the pasture through a gate to the west. \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33542,0,0,0,'In a Pasture','  This is a big area that has been fenced in.  The grass is of a thick\nvariety, it grows richly except in a few areas that have been grazed upon.  A\nways to the north, there is a little grassy spot shaded by a very large willow\ntree. \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33543,0,0,0,'In a Pasture','  This is a big area that has been fenced in.  The grass is of a thick\nvariety, it grows richly except in a few areas that have been grazed upon.  A\nways to the north, there is a little grassy spot shaded by a very large willow\ntree. \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33544,0,0,0,'In a Pasture','  This is a big area that has been fenced in.  The grass is of a thick\nvariety, it grows richly except in a few areas that have been grazed upon.  A\nways to the north, there is a little grassy spot shaded by a very large willow\ntree. \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33545,0,0,0,'A Grassy Spot','  The grass is rich but short here, it is a calm and soothing spot.  In the\ndistant east some farms can be seen.  A fenced in pasture can be seen directly\nto the south. \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33550,0,0,0,'Outside a Pasture','   The lane ends here with a gate to the south, over which a pasture can be\nseen.  A gentle breeze blows, making the blades of grass sway back and forth,\nalmost hypnotically.  A path around the pasture leads towards the farmhouse,\nvisable to the southeast.\n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33551,0,0,0,'The Path Around the Pasture','  The pathway around the pasture continues towards the east, leading towards a\nfarmhouse, while a gate allowing access to the pasture lies a short distance\nto the west.  Over the fence the pasture is well grazed and crows wheel\noverhead, calling to one another. \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33552,0,0,0,'The Path Around the Pasture','   The path continues here, leading further to the east around the northern\nedge of the pasture, while a farmhouse is growing larger on the horizon.  A\nsmall rodent darts across the path ahead, chased by a red-tailed hawk.  A tall\nmaple provides shade here, as the pathway starts to wind between the trees of a\nsmall wood.    \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33553,0,0,0,'A Wooded Pathway','  Several trees of the woods rise up on either side of the pathway here, but\nenough space remains between them which allows the fence surrounding the\npasture to still be visible.  A small bridge directly to the southwest has\nbeen built as a way of crossing over a small stream of crystal clear water. \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33554,0,0,0,'A Small Bridge','   The pathway continues over a wooden bridge that has been built here,\ncrossing over the stream.  From either side of the bridge, fish can be seen\nswimming lazily around, while a low-pitched croaking can be heard further\ndownstream.    \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33555,0,0,0,'A Wooded Pathway','   The pathway here winds though several stumps where a farmer may have\nobtained the wood necessary to build his house and barn, as well as the fence\nsurrounding the pasture.  From here, it appears as if a small clearing has been\nmade in the woods to the south.    \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33556,0,0,0,'The Edge of a Clearing','   The path ends here at the edge of a small clearing, with a farmhouse\nvisible a little ways to the south, with a small dirt path leading up towards\nit.  On either side the farmer has planted a small garden, with tomatoes,\nonions, cabbage, lettuce as well as some other unfamiliar ones.    \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33557,0,0,0,'A Small Path','   The path continues in a southerly direction, towards the front entrance of\na farm house.  To the east, a farmer has planted a small crop of lettuce, while\nto the west several tomato plants have started to grow.  Several small insects\nfly about, searching for something to eat, while a butterfly flutters above one\nof the plants.    \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33558,0,0,0,'A Small Path','   On either side of the path here, a farmer has planted a small garden. On\nthe east are onions, while to the west the farmer is growing what appears to be\nsquash.  The front entrance to the farm house lies directly to the south.    \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33559,0,0,0,'The Front Porch','A gentle breeze blows across the porch area, where a farmer has set out two\nwooden chairs that he has probably made himself.  From this vantage point, the\nwhole farm is visible; a pasture to the northwest, with the field of wheat to\nthe north.    \n',-1,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33560,0,0,0,'Inside a Farmhouse','The smell of cedar permeates the air here, with a wooden chest placed at the\nside of a set of stairs leading up to the second floor.  A short hallway leads\noff to the east, with a door directly to the south.  A carving of some sort\nsits on a shelf to the side of the door, while a rug covers the floor.    \n',-1,172201,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33561,0,0,0,'The Bottom of the Stairs','A wooden stairway leads to the second floor of the farmhouse, while a window\nin the western wall looks out over the garden.  The window in the northern wall\nis a bid cloudy, but gives a good view of the grain fields.    \n',-1,172201,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33562,0,0,0,'A Bedroom','This room is rather sparsely decorated, yet functional.  A featherbed stands\nagainst the eastern wall, with a handmade quilt thrown over it.  A small table\nsits beside the bed with a pitcher of water and a small basin which is used for\nwashing.  A rug covers the floor, while there is a window in both the south and\nwest wall.  A small chest sits beneath the latter.    \n',-1,172201,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33563,0,0,0,'A Hallway','The front room of the farmhouse leads into a small hallway here, with the\nsmell of apple pie and cinnamon filling the air from the north.  Another\ndoorway lies to the south, leading into another room, while a much larger room\nopens up towards the east.  The front entrance to the farmhouse lies to the\nwest.\n',0,172201,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33564,0,0,0,'A Bedroom','While this room resembles much of the other parts of the house in that it is\nnot overly elaborate, it gives the impression of being quite comfortable.  A\nlarge featherbed is arranged along the western wall, with a beautiful quilt on\ntop of it.  A small table with a basin and pitcher is next to it, while a\nwardrobe stands against the wall to the east.  A woven rug covers the floor,\nwhile a window looks out over a small pond.    \n',-1,172201,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33565,0,0,0,'The Farmhouse Kitchen','The smell of cinammon and other spices fill the air here, while a small table\nin the center of the room is covered with a blue and white tablecloth.  A large\nbasin sits underneath a large window in the northern wall, with a small stove\nnext to it.  A large cupboard stands against the eastern wall.  To the east,\nthe top of some stairs is visable, while the only other exit is the\nentranceway to the south.    \n',-1,164029,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33566,0,0,0,'The Gathering Room','This room is much larger than any of the other rooms in the farmhouse, with\na large fireplace built into the northern wall, with a set of windows on either\nside.  A large table with several place settings is situated in the center of\nthe room, with long benches on both sides.  Between the windows in the\neastern wall hangs a large rug.  A set of shelves on either side of the doorway\nhold several various items of importance to the family.    \n',-1,172201,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33567,0,0,0,'The Second Floor','A small hallway leads off to the south here, while to the east is a doorway.\nAn oil lamp hangs from the northern wall, while a woven rug covers the floor.\nA small window in the western wall overlooks the garden, and also provides a\nview of the pasture.    \n',-1,172201,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33568,0,0,0,'A Bedroom','This is one of the bedrooms for the farmer\'s sons, with several wooden toys\nscattered about, while two featherbeds stand against the eastern wall, one of\nwhich is not made, while the other has some clothes piled on top of it.  A\nwindow to the north is open, allowing a gentle breeze to blow through the room,\nbringing with it the smell of wheat.    \n',-1,172201,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33569,0,0,0,'The Second Floor','The second floor continues here, while a wooden door lies to the east.  In\nthe southern wall a window looks out over a small pond, where some ducks and\ngeese can be seen swimming around.    \n',-1,172201,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33570,0,0,0,'A Small Bedroom','This room appears to be that of a young girl.  A featherbed stands against\nthe eastern wall, where several dolls propped up against the pillow.  A small\ndresser stands next to it, with several ribbons scattered about the surface.  \nA throw rug covers the floor, while the window in the southern wall is open,\nallowing a fresh breeze to blow though the room.    \n',-1,172201,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33571,0,0,0,'The Pasture','   Tall blades of grass wave gently in the breeze, while a little ways to the\nsouth the sound of cattle lowing can be heard.  One of the farmers horses runs\nby, as it is enjoying the time it has outside.  Several insects fly about,\nwhile a butterfly alights on one of the wildflowers that grow here.  The gate\nto the pasture lies to the north.    \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33572,0,0,0,'The Pasture','   The pasture continues here, extending in all directions, except for north,\nwhere a fence blocks the way.  A little ways to the west the gate can be seen,\nbeyond which is a face of a cliff, providing a natural barrier.  A few insects\nfly about, while the grass waves gently back and forth in the breeze.    \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33573,0,0,0,'The Pasture','   The pasture continues here along the northern fence, but is soon blocked by\nthe eastern edge of the fence, which prevents travelling in that direction.  \nLooking to the south, the pasture continues, leading towards what appears to be\na small pond.    \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33574,0,0,0,'The Pasture','   The pasture extends in all directions from here, except east where a fence\nmarks the eastern boundary, beyond which a small pathway is visible, leading\ntowards the south.  From this vantage, it is also possible to see a small\nfarmhouse.  A small pond with cattails around it provides a water source for\nboth the horses and cattle that the farmer owns.    \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33575,0,0,0,'The Pasture','   The pasture extends in all directions from here.  To the southeast a small\npond is visible, while the gate lies a short distance to the northwest.  A\ngentle breeze makes the blades of grass wave back and forth, while all around\ncomes the sound of various insects.    \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33576,0,0,0,'The Pasture','   The grass waves gently in the breeze here, while the pasture extends in all\ndirections, except for west where a cliff face prevents travel that way.  The\ngate to the pasture lies a little distance to the north.    \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33577,0,0,0,'A Side Room Adjoining the Kitchen','A tall shelf of various cooking items lies to the east, with a stairway\nleading down to a dark cellar, where other supplies are kept.  To the north is\na door, which leads out to the barn, beyond which is a small wheat field.    \n',-1,164029,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33578,0,0,0,'The Farmhouse Cellar','This is a cellar where the farmer will keep the spices to dry after summer,\nand when they have completed the harvest.  Several bundles hang from rods that\nrun from one end of the cellar to the other, and include thyme, oregano, and\nrosemary.  Two large barrels of flour stand in the corner, while a small cask\nof wine sits on a shelf.    \n',-1,164029,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33579,0,0,0,'The Back Porch','This is a smaller porch than the one at the front of the house, with a small\nherb garden off to the east.  A small path leads to the barn, on the western\nside of the path.    \n',-1,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33580,0,0,0,'A Path Leading Towards the Barn','This is a small path which leads to a barn, the door lies directly to the\nwest.  The farmer\'s wife has planted a small flower garden on the eastern side\nof the path, which includes roses, snapdragons, forget-me-nots, and several\nothers.  To the south is the back entrance to a farmhouse, while beyond the\nbarn is a field of wheat.\n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33581,0,0,0,'Inside the Barn','This barn is rather small, but is quite sufficient for the farmer.  Various\nfarm tools, such as hoes and scythes hang from wooden pegs along the western\nwall.  A small ladder leads up to a small hay mow where the farmer keeps the\nhay for the winter months, while several stalls line the northern wall for the\ncattle and horses the farmer owns.    \n',-1,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33582,0,0,0,'Inside the Barn','A ladder stands here, leading up to the hay mow where the farmer keeps the\nhay needed for his animals.  To the north are several stalls for the animals,\nwhile to the east is the door to the barn.    \n',-1,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33583,0,0,0,'An Empty Stall','A dense layer of hay lies on the ground, which doubles as both fodder and\nbedding for the animals.  Currently, the stall is empty, as the animals have\nbeen led out to pasture.    \n',-1,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33584,0,0,0,'An Empty Stall','A layer of hay covers the ground, which is used for both bedding and for\nfodder.  Currently, the stall is empty, as all the animals have been let out to\npasture.    \n',-1,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33585,0,0,0,'A Hayloft','This is a hay loft where the farmer keeps extra hay for his animals \nwhen it is neccessary to bring them in to shelter. A rope mechanism is \nsituated above a doorway in the northern wall, which is used to bring \nthe hay up here for storage. A ladder provides the only exit.\n',-1,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(33586,0,0,0,'The Side of the Barn','   The gravel paved path continues here, with the eastern wall of a barn on one\nside, while a chicken coop lies on the other. A small wheat field lies\nto the north, beyond which the southern edge of a small woods is visable.    \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33587,0,0,0,'A Wheat Field','   This is the southwestern corner of the wheat field, which continues to the\nnortheast.  A barn lies to the southwest, while a farmhouse can be seen beyond\nthat.  A gentle breeze makes the wheat sway back and forth, almost like a sea\nof gold.    \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33588,0,0,0,'A Wheat Field','   The wheat field continues here, extending in all directions except to the \nsouth and east, where thick weeds provide a natural barrier, preventing travel \nin that direction.  Several birds fly overhead, looking for insects.    \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33589,0,0,0,'A Wheat Field','   The wheat field continues here, but travel is blocked to the west by a \nsmall patch of trees, with a thick wall of brambles and other bushes filling \nup the spaces between.  Far to the southwest a farmhouse and barn are visible.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33590,0,0,0,'A Wheat Field','   This is the middle section of a wheat field.  Travel is possible in any \ndirection.  To the distant southwest, a farm house and barn are visible.    \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33591,0,0,0,'A Wheat Field','   The wheat field extends to the north and west from here, while to the very \ndistant southwest a barn and a farm house are standing.\n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33592,0,0,0,'A Wheat Field','   This is the northwestern edge of the wheat field, which continues in all the\nother directions.  A gentle breeze makes the stalks of wheat blow gently in the\nbreeze.    \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33593,0,0,0,'A Wheat Field','   This is the northern edge of a wheat field, with a thick wall of\nbrambles preventing travel to the north. A small pond is visible to the\nvery distant east which serves as a barrier in that direction.    \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33594,0,0,0,'A Wheat Field','   A thick wall of brambles prevents travel to the north, however, the wheat\nfield continues in all the other directions.  A gentle breeze blows here,\nmaking the stalks of wheat wave back and forth.    \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33595,0,0,0,'A Wheat Field','   This is the northeastern corner of the wheat field, with a small pond\nblocking travel to the east and a thick bramble patch preventing travel to the\nnorth.  Looking to the very distant southwest, a farm house and barn are visible.    \n',-1,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33596,0,0,0,'A Wooded Lane','   The dirt lane winds between massive trees, which provide a covering for the\nroad here.  Scattered amongst the trunks of the trees are small clusters of\nwildflowers, in just about any color imaginable.  Further to the south, the\npath ends at a wooden gate, with a pasture on the other side.    \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33597,0,0,0,'A Wooded Lane','   Massive trees line the lane here, providing shade as it winds between the\ntrunks.  On either side of the path are small bushes intermingled with\nwildflowers in varying colors, while from the trees, the sound of a bird\'s \nsong can be heard.    \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33598,0,0,0,'A Wooded Lane','   A wooded lane continues towards the southeast, winding between the trunks of\nseveral tall trees, while a small creek runs along one side of the pathway.  A\nsmall clearing lies to the east where a small pond surrounded by cattails is\nvisible.    \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33599,0,0,0,'A Wooded Lane','The lane continues to wind between the trunks of trees, with the faint sign\nof wheel tracks still visible in the grass that has been crushed down.  A few\nbirds fly from tree to tree, while off in the distance a faint croaking can be\nheard further down the creek that runs along side the pathway.    \n',0,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33600,0,0,0,'A Wooded Lane','   The dirt lane winds between massive trees, which provide a covering for the\nroad here.  Scattered amongst the trunks of the trees are small clusters of\nwildflowers, in just about any color imaginable.  Further to the south, the\npath ends at a wooden gate, with a pasture on the other side.    \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33601,0,0,0,'A Wooded Lane','   The dirt lane winds between massive trees, which provide a covering for the\nroad here.  Scattered amongst the trunks of the trees are small clusters of\nwildflowers, in just about any color imaginable.  Further to the south, the\npath ends at a wooden gate, with a pasture on the other side.    \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33602,0,0,0,'A Wooded Lane','   The dirt lane winds between massive trees, which provide a covering for the\nroad here.  Scattered amongst the trunks of the trees are small clusters of\nwildflowers, in just about any color imaginable.  Further to the south, the\npath ends at a wooden gate, with a pasture on the other side.    \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33603,0,0,0,'A Wooded Lane','   The dirt lane winds between massive trees, which provide a covering for the\nroad here.  Scattered amongst the trunks of the trees are small clusters of\nwildflowers, in just about any color imaginable.  Further to the south, the\npath ends at a wooden gate, with a pasture on the other side.    \n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33604,0,0,0,'A Wooded Lane','  This road runs through the northern part of the foulborough, from the\nGrimhaven Market plaza toward the edge of the plateau on which Grimhaven is\nbuilt and eventually into the southern Haon-Dor Forest.  You are at the\nedge of the plateau.  The road slopes downward here, toward the trees of\nthe Haon-Dor Forest to the north.  In the distance to the south and west\nyou can see the outskirts of Grimhaven.\n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33605,0,0,0,'Outside a Pasture','   The lane ends here with a gate to the south, over which a pasture can be\nseen.  A gentle breeze blows, making the blades of grass sway back and forth,\nalmost hypnotically.  A path around the pasture leads towards the farmhouse,\nvisable to the southeast.\n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33606,0,0,0,'Outside a Pasture','   The lane ends here with a gate to the south, over which a pasture can be\nseen.  A gentle breeze blows, making the blades of grass sway back and forth,\nalmost hypnotically.  A path around the pasture leads towards the farmhouse,\nvisable to the southeast.\n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33607,0,0,0,'Outside a Pasture','   The lane ends here with a gate to the south, over which a pasture can be\nseen.  A gentle breeze blows, making the blades of grass sway back and forth,\nalmost hypnotically.  A path around the pasture leads towards the farmhouse,\nvisable to the southeast.\n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33608,0,0,0,'Outside a Pasture','   The lane ends here with a gate to the south, over which a pasture can be\nseen.  A gentle breeze blows, making the blades of grass sway back and forth,\nalmost hypnotically.  A path around the pasture leads towards the farmhouse,\nvisable to the southeast.\n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33609,0,0,0,'Outside a Pasture','   The lane ends here with a gate to the south, over which a pasture can be\nseen.  A gentle breeze blows, making the blades of grass sway back and forth,\nalmost hypnotically.  A path around the pasture leads towards the farmhouse,\nvisable to the southeast.\n',-1,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33635,0,0,0,'A Misty Trail Through the Forest','A small trail twists and turns about on itself in a feeble attempt to\nprovide passage through the dense forest.  Small tremors shake the ground\ncausing a few frail trees to plummet to the ground.  A strange mist floats about\neverywhere, blanketing the area completely.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
