(33686,0,0,0,'Norman\'s Road','  A packed dirt road runs north and southwest through a sparse wood.  Thorny\nbrush blocks passage in other directions.  The road leads to a wide prairie to\nthe north, and denser forest southwest. \n',251,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33687,0,0,0,'Norman\'s Road','  A packed dirt road runs north and south through a sparse wood.  Thorny brush\nblocks passage in other directions.  The road leads to a wide prairie to the\nnorth, and denser forest south. \n',251,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33688,0,0,0,'Norman\'s Road','  A packed dirt road runs northwest and south through a sparse wood.  Thorny\nbrush blocks passage in other directions.  The road leads to a wide prairie to\nthe northwest, and denser forest south. \n',251,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33689,0,0,0,'Norman\'s Road','  A packed dirt road runs northwest and southeast through a sparse wood. \nThorny brush blocks passage in other directions.  The road crosses a metal\ngrating between two sections of fence to the northwest, where it leads to a\nwide prairie.  The forest is denser to the southeast. \n',251,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33690,0,0,0,'<g>A<1> <o>Horse<1> <g>Trail<1>','  A well used horse trail plunges into the woods to the west.  To the\nnortheast some brambles can be pulled in place or aside to block or open\npassage to another road.  Dense vine and brush limits passage and sight to the\npath.\n',251,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,4,'',NULL),
(33691,0,0,0,'<g>A<1> <o>Horse<1> <g>Trail<1>','  A well used horse trail cuts through the woods, heading east and west. \nDense vine and brush limits passage and sight to the path. \n',251,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33692,0,0,0,'<g>A<1> <o>Horse<1> <g>Trail<1>','  A well used horse trail cuts through the woods, heading east and west.  The\npath empties into a small meadow to the west.  The signs of a busy camp are\nevident in the meadow. \n',251,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33693,0,0,0,'A Meadow Camp','  Horse tracks pock the grass of this small meadow in the woods.  The edge of\nthe forest is lined with thick brambles.  A horse trail cuts into the woods to\nthe east and the meadow continues to the south.  A humble cabin, draped in\nvines and brush, overlooks the meadow to the west. \n',251,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33694,0,0,0,'A Meadow Camp','  Horse tracks pock the grass of this small meadow in the woods.  The edge of\nthe forest is lined with thick brambles.  The meadow continues to the north\nand west.  The corner of a humble cabin stands to the northwest, draped in\nvines and brush. \n',251,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33695,0,0,0,'A Meadow Camp','  Horse tracks pock the grass of this small meadow in the woods.  The edge of\nthe forest is lined with thick brambles.  The meadow continues to the east and\nwest. The entrance to a humble log cabin is to the north. \n',251,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33696,0,0,0,'A Meadow Camp','  Horse tracks pock the grass of this small meadow in the woods.  The edge of\nthe forest is lined with thick brambles.  The meadow continues to the west,\neast and north.  A watering hole can be seen to the north and a campfire to\nthe west.  The corner of a humble cabin stands to the northeast, draped in\nvines and brush. \n',251,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33697,0,0,0,'A Meadow Camp','  Horse tracks pock the grass of this small meadow in the woods.  The edge of\nthe forest is lined with thick brambles.  The meadow continues to the south. \nA humble cabin, draped in vines and brush, overlooks the meadow to the east. \n',251,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33698,0,0,0,'A Meadow Camp','A plush layer of grass carpets the meadow here.  The edge of the forest is\nlined with thick brambles.  The meadow continues to the east, where the edge\nof a cabin can be seen. \n',0,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33699,0,0,0,'<o>A Bush Cabin<1>','  Hooks for hanging gear line the walls of this single room log cabin. \nDespite the windows that have been placed in the east and west walls, a gamy\nodor permeates everything.  The floor is of packed dirt, and has been\nscattered with dry meadow grass.  A doorway in the south wall leads outside. \n',251,131400,32,0,0,0,0,-1,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(33700,0,0,0,'In the Foothills','  Rocks lie strewn about this rough terrain on the western side of the\nmountains.  A thin trail winds through the boulders heading east into a\nmountain pass or west toward a strange city near a thin forest.\n',255,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
