(33706,0,0,0,'In the Foothills','  Rocks lie strewn about this rough terrain on the western side of the\nmountains.  A thin trail winds through the boulders heading east into a\nmountain pass or west toward a strange city near a thin forest.\n',255,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33707,0,0,0,'In the Foothills','  Rocks lie strewn about this rough terrain on the western side of the\nmountains.  The mountain range to the east is dauntingly steep, and some\nof its peaks remain snow covered throughout the year.  Fortunately, the\nmountain pass to the east appears relatively passable. To the west, you\ncan just make out a peculiar looking city beyond a thin forest.\n',255,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33708,0,0,0,'In the Foothills','  Rocks lie strewn about this rough terrain on the western side of the\nmountains.  The mountain range to the east is dauntingly steep, and some\nof its peaks remain snow covered throughout the year.  Fortunately, the\nmountain pass to the east appears relatively passable. To the west, you\ncan just make out a peculiar looking city beyond a thin forest.\n',255,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33709,0,0,0,'In the Foothills','  Rocks lie strewn about this rough terrain on the western side of the\nmountains.  The mountain range to the east is dauntingly steep, and some\nof its peaks remain snow covered throughout the year.  Fortunately, the\nmountain pass to the east appears relatively passable. To the west, you\ncan just make out a peculiar looking city beyond a thin forest.\n',255,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33710,0,0,0,'In the Foothills','  Rocks lie strewn about this rough terrain on the western side of the\nmountains.  The mountain range to the east is dauntingly steep, and some\nof its peaks remain snow covered throughout the year.  Fortunately, the\nmountain pass to the east appears relatively passable. To the west, you\ncan just make out a peculiar looking city beyond a thin forest.\n',255,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33711,0,0,0,'Mountain Pass','  The path narrows as it winds its way through the mountains.  The peaks\ngrow taller and steeper toward the east where they practically scratch\nagainst the sky.  To the southwest you can see the mountains degrade into\nfoothills, and farther in the distance you can see the edge of a forest.\n',255,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33712,0,0,0,'Mountain Pass','  The path narrows as it winds its way through the mountains.  The peaks\ngrow taller and steeper toward the east where they practically scratch\nagainst the sky.  To the west you can catch glimpses of foothills between\nthe mountains, as the peaks gradually grow smaller.  The path here is\ndifficult to travel as you must navigate around ancient rockslides and\nin between natural crevices.\n',255,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33713,0,0,0,'Mountain Pass','  The path narrows as it winds its way through the mountains.  The peaks\ngrow taller and steeper toward the east where they practically scratch\nagainst the sky.  To the west you can catch glimpses of foothills between\nthe mountains, as the peaks gradually grow smaller.  The path here is\ndifficult to travel as you must navigate around ancient rockslides and\nin between natural crevices.\n',255,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33714,0,0,0,'Mountain Pass','  The path narrows as it winds its way through the mountains.  The peaks\ngrow taller and steeper toward the east where they practically scratch\nagainst the sky.  To the west you can catch glimpses of foothills between\nthe mountains, as the peaks gradually grow smaller.  The path here is\ndifficult to travel as you must navigate around ancient rockslides and\nin between natural crevices.\n',255,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(33715,0,0,0,'Mountain Pass near a Tremendous Peak','  The path here is littered with rocks and boulders.  Surrounded on all sides\nby mountains, your view is quite limited.  You stand amid some of the tallest\nmountains your eyes have ever seen.  To the east, a mammoth snow capped summit\ndwarfs even its monsterous peers.  Gale force winds whip whisps of snow off of\nthe peaks around you.  Fortunately, the pass continues through a natural\nvalley, and provides a fairly traversable route.\n',255,131072,5,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
