(34041,0,0,0,'A Thin Passage','The walls of this tunnel are tightly packed earth. Small root systems poke in\nfrom above,\nbut there is otherwise little to note about this passage. The packed floor\nsuggests\ntraffic. Yet, you feel the tunnel was somehow left unfinished.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(34042,0,0,0,'A Thin Passage','The walls of this tunnel are tightly packed earth. Small root systems poke in\nfrom above,\nbut there is otherwise little to note about this passage. The packed floor\nsuggests\ntraffic. Yet, you feel the tunnel was somehow left unfinished.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(34043,0,0,0,'Ledge Above A Foul-smelling Pit','The packed dirt floor of the tunnel has been interruped here by a deep sinkhole.\nLuckily,\nenough of the tunnel remains in the areas closest to the walls that it is\nstill traversable, if not dangerous. The scent in the area would indicate that\nsomething\nwas probably standing here when the sinkhole gave in, leading to the poor\ncreature\'s\ndemise. The darkness below you is thick and does not lead you to believe the\nbottom of\nthe sinkhole is anywhere close to where you are.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(34044,0,0,0,'Atop A Ledge','This is a most awkward room to be in. To the near south, a treacherous sinkhole\ndisrupts the path, and directly below you the tunnel drops sharply for a dozen\nfeet or so.\nThe discrepancy in relative elevations is nauseating and vertigo begins to creep\nin.\nLuckily, the earth beneath you is fairly solid. Or so it seems to be...\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(34045,0,0,0,'Cobweb-filled Passage','Every surface of this area serves as a place for cobwebs to hang. The strands\nare thick\nand much stickier than any you have seen in other places. It is hard to orient\nyourself\namid the mass of webbing. Sounds of clicking alert you to the presence of some\ncreature nearby.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(34046,0,0,0,'Cobweb-filled Passage','Every surface of this area serves as a place for cobwebs to hang. The strands\nare thick\nand much stickier than any you have seen in other places. It is hard to orient\nyourself\namid the mass of webbing. Sounds of clicking alert you to the presence of some\ncreature nearby.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(34047,0,0,0,'Cobweb-filled Passage','Every surface of this area serves as a place for cobwebs to hang. The strands\nare thick\nand much stickier than any you have seen in other places. It is hard to orient\nyourself\namid the mass of webbing. Sounds of clicking alert you to the presence of some\ncreature nearby.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(34048,0,0,0,'Bone Littered Tunnel','Very little floor is visible here through the vast piles of bones. Some of the\nbones most\nlikely belonged to forest creatures. Some appear to have once been birds of\nvarious sizes.\nSome, however, look suspiciously humanoid. The air in this section of the tunnel\nfeels and smells\nwetter than other areas.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(34049,0,0,0,'Bone Littered Tunnel','Very little floor is visible here through the vast piles of bones. Some of the\nbones most\nlikely belonged to forest creatures. Some appear to have once been birds of\nvarious sizes.\nSome, however, look suspiciously humanoid. The air in this section of the tunnel\nfeels and smells\nwetter than other areas.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(34050,0,0,0,'Bone Littered Tunnel','Very little floor is visible here through the vast piles of bones. Some of the\nbones most\nlikely belonged to forest creatures. Some appear to have once been birds of\nvarious sizes.\nSome, however, look suspiciously humanoid. The air in this section of the tunnel\nfeels and smells\nwetter than other areas. The cobwebs seem thicker here than in adjacent areas.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(34051,0,0,0,'Bone Littered Tunnel','Very little floor is visible here through the vast piles of bones. Some of the\nbones most\nlikely belonged to forest creatures. Some appear to have once been birds of\nvarious sizes.\nSome, however, look suspiciously humanoid. The air in this section of the tunnel\nfeels and smells\nwetter than other areas.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(34052,0,0,0,'Cramped Fissure','The tunnel narrows here so much that it is nearly impossible to travel through it\nwithout sidestepping. The walls are rough and not very forgiving. Some of the\nmost aggresive surfaces carry a dark red sheen in the light, suggesting\nthat someone or something once had a reason travel through in a hurry.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(34053,0,0,0,'Cramped Fissure','The tunnel narrows here so much that it is nearly impossible to travel through it\nwithout sidestepping. The walls are rough and not very forgiving. Some of the\nmost aggresive surfaces carry a dark red sheen in the light, suggesting\nthat someone or something once had a reason travel through in a hurry.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(34054,0,0,0,'Narrow Tunnel','Passage through this portion of the tunnel is slowed as the space constricts\ngradually. The walls\nhere are rockier then those of the tunnel to the north. Perhaps the tunnel\nnarrows\nbecause excavation became more difficult. Or perhaps the diggers found a reason\nnot to finish.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(34055,0,0,0,'Narrow Tunnel','Unlike in the tunnel to the north, most travelers are able to stand upright in\nthis tunnel.\nUnfortunately, it seems to narrow slowly, though noticably. There must be\ncountless\ntunnels in the world which are easier to navigate through than this one.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(34056,0,0,0,'Passage Under a Large Jutting Rock','A large flat stone seems to have fallen here, cutting the height of the tunnel\nnearly in half. Luckily, something\nseems to have prevented the rock from crushing the tunnel completely and\nmovement through, albeit slow and laborous,\nis possible.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,7,40,0,'',NULL),
(34057,0,0,0,'Passage Under a Large Jutting Rock','A large flat stone seems to have fallen here, cutting the height of the tunnel\nnearly in half. Luckily, something\nseems to have prevented the rock from crushing the tunnel completely and\nmovement through, albeit slow and laborous,\nis possible.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,7,40,0,'',NULL),
(34058,0,0,0,'Passage Under a Large Jutting Rock','A large flat stone seems to have fallen here, cutting the height of the tunnel\nnearly in half. Luckily, something\nseems to have prevented the rock from crushing the tunnel completely and\nmovement through, albeit slow and laborous,\nis possible.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,7,40,0,'',NULL),
(34059,0,0,0,'A Confusing Path Through Rubble','There is evidence here that this tunnel was once finely crafted using\nbeams of treated wood and lit with expensive looking oil lamps. Most of the\nwood, however,\nhas been torn to splinters, assumingly by whatever event destroyed the tunnel.\nLittle is left of the lamps aside from scraps of tarnished brass and broken\nglass. Passage\nthrough the rubble seems to be possible. Though it would require a traveller to\nsnake through several\ndangerous looking portals created by pairs of boulders leaning against one\nanother. If at anytime one of them\nwere to shift...\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,7,100,0,'',NULL),
(34060,0,0,0,'Above Some Natural Stairs','A makeshift set of stairs has been formed naturally by several pieces of stone.\nThe intervals betwen steps are irregular at best and the steps themselves\ncould hardly be called flat. Nonetheless, with a little effort, they are not\ndifficult to climb.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,5,100,0,'',NULL),
(34061,0,0,0,'A Collapsed Tunnel','The south side of this tunnel has collapses and, in sections, the ceiling of the\nnorth\nside has begun to sag. Large beams of treated wood lay where they fell and piles\nof rubble\nstand ominously about. It is doubtful this tunnel could be repaired easily. A sturdy-looking pile of rubble seems to allow travel upward.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(34062,0,0,0,'A Collapsed Tunnel','The south side of this tunnel has collapses and, in sections, the ceiling of the\nnorth\nside has begun to sag. Large beams of treated wood lay where they fell and piles\nof rubble\nstand ominously about. It is doubtful this tunnel could be repaired easily.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(34063,0,0,0,'Small Cave Beneath Some Rubble','This \'room\' has been created by several beams which crossed and became stuck\nwhen the tunnel collapsed. Larger rocks\nthen bridged the gaps between the beams and then were covered by smaller chunks\nof debris.\nThis place is not very accomodating, but it does appear safe to remain here.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,1,100,0,'',NULL),
(34064,0,0,0,'Ledge Before A Collapsed Tunnel','This ledge borders a descent down a portion of the tunnel which has apparently\ncollapsed.\nIt may very well be that this tunnel is unusable, or even too dangerous to\nattempt to travel through,\nbut little can be assessed from here.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(34065,0,0,0,'A Small Tunnel','This tunnel is small, likely having been made by and for one of the shorter\nintelligent races that populate The World.\nThere are remnants of oil lamps having once been on the walls, but they were\nmost likely \'borrowed\'\nby gnomes in some desperate time.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(34066,0,0,0,'A Small Tunnel','This tunnel is small, likely to have been made by and for one of the shorter,\nintelligent races that populate The World. There are remnants of oil lamps\nhaving once been on the walls, but they were most likely \'borrowed\' by some\ngnomes in a desperate time. The only present traces of the outside world are\nseveral large words painted on the walls, ceiling and floor. It might be wise\nto heed their message.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(34067,0,0,0,'End of a Small Tunnel','Rumor has it that this tunnel was meat to bridge two distant lands by allowing\neasy passage through the mountain which borders the village of Gnath to the\nsouthwest. Few of those that live on the northeastern side of the mountain have\never seen what is on the other side. It does not seem, however, that many of\nthe villagers of Gnath are excited to make the trip through the tunnel. Perhaps\nsomething dangerous has made its home inside. A brick on the ground here catches\nyour attention.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,4,100,0,'',NULL),
(34068,0,0,0,'Elaborate Bone Altar','Carved out of the rock, this small chamber is home to an enormous, and very\nelaborate bone altar.\nAside from this, the room contains little else and is otherwise relatively\nuninteresting. The altar,\nhowever, contains dozens of macabre objects. A small basin of a darkly colored\nmetal\nrests within the surface of the altar. The individual that created this altar\nmore than likely\nhas a very malicious use for it.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,3,100,0,'',NULL),
(34069,0,0,0,'Large Nest','This appears to be the home of what could be in upwards of a dozen large\narachnids.\nHalf-eaten corpses, all spun tightly in strong silk, are strewn about. Many of\nthem\nhave already started to decay. This is perhaps due to the poison of this\nchamber\'s occupants.\nThe room itself seems to be almost as large as a human dwelling, allowing\nplenty of room for the family to increase in size.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(34070,0,0,0,'Large Nest','This appears to be the home of what could be in upwards of a dozen large\narachnids.\nHalf-eaten corpses, all spun tightly in strong silk, are strewn about. Many of\nthem\nhave already started to decay. This is perhaps due to the poison of this\nchamber\'s occupants.\nThe room itself seems to be almost as large as a human dwelling, allowing\nplenty of room for the family to increase in size.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(34071,0,0,0,'Large Nest','This appears to be the home of what could be in upwards of a dozen large\narachnids.\nHalf-eaten corpses, all spun tightly in strong silk, are strewn about. Many of\nthem\nhave already started to decay. This is perhaps due to the poison of this\nchamber\'s occupants.\nThe room itself seems to be almost as large as a human dwelling, allowing\nplenty of room for the family to increase in size.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(34072,0,0,0,'Large Nest','This appears to be the home of what could be in upwards of a dozen large\narachnids.\nHalf-eaten corpses, all spun tightly in strong silk, are strewn about. Many of\nthem\nhave already started to decay. This is perhaps due to the poison of this\nchamber\'s occupants.\nThe room itself seems to be almost as large as a human dwelling, allowing\nplenty of room for the family to increase in size.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(34073,0,0,0,'Egg-filled Room','This must be the room where the queen drops her eggsacs. Virtually\nevery corner and nook of this roughly hewn area is being used to\nhost several hundred spider eggs. It is likely that within weeks these eggs will\nbegin to hatch.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(34074,0,0,0,'Hidden Treasure Room','Cobwebs fill this room, but it does not seem to be used by the spiders. The\nwalls\nseem to have been cut out of the rockface in a much more meticulous manner. In\nsome places,\nit even seems that cracks in the wall have been patched with mortar.\n',0,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(34075,0,0,0,'<o>Deep Under the Maze<z>','<o>Under the earth of the maze lies this room full of large piles of\n<k>rubble<z>.  <o>It\'s big enough to accommodate an ogre but meant for the\nfaeries smaller cousins, the pixies.<z>\n',0,139272,33,0,0,0,0,-1,40,100,0,'',NULL),
(34076,0,0,0,'<k>Room of Rubble<z>','<k>The walls of this room, once smooth to the touch, have been reduced to a rugged surface and rubble. \nHere and there are tiny sprouts of <z><g>ivy<z> <k>poking from between the\ngaps.<z>\n',0,139272,33,0,0,0,0,-1,5,50,0,'',NULL),
(34077,0,0,0,'<k>Room of Rubble<z>','<k>The walls of this room, once smooth to the touch, have been reduced to a rugged surface and rubble. \nHere and there are tiny sprouts of <z><g>ivy<z> <k>poking from between the\ngaps.<z>\n',0,139272,33,0,0,0,0,-1,5,50,0,'',NULL),
