(34108,0,0,0,'<r>The Dead End<z>','<k>Tall and thick rectangular slabs of granite stone join together to form a\ndead end.  Whatever living overgrowth that was once here has since died.  Long\nand thin, leafless <o>brown vines<z><k> drape from stone wall to stone wall.<z>\n',0,139264,26,0,0,0,0,-1,100,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34109,0,0,0,'Wegort\'s Room','<o>Long ago, an ogre named Wegort accidentally found himself in the maze of the\nfaerie folk.  Lost and heartbroken, he decided this was where he should be.  Giving\nhim this room and the freedom to walk wherever he wanted in the maze, the\nfaerie folk treated him as one of their own.  One day, something horrible\nhappened!  Pieces of <W>faeries<z><o> and <P>pixies<z><o> tossed around\neverywhere!<z>\n',0,139272,33,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(34110,0,0,0,'<G>Norman\'s<1> <W>Road<1>','  A road of white cobbled stones runs west and east through low hills and\npastures. The windows and terraces of hobbit burrows dot the hillsides.  To\nthe east, the road crosses a small bridge as it heads into a shire.  \n',258,131072,22,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34111,0,0,0,'<G>Norman\'s<1> <W>Road<1>','  A road of white cobbled stones runs northwest and east through low hills and\npastures. The windows and terraces of hobbit burrows dot the hillsides, one\nsuch window overlooking the road immediately southwest.  Not far to the east,\nthe road crosses a small bridge as it heads into a shire.  \n',258,131072,22,0,0,0,30,7,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34112,0,0,0,'<G>Norman\'s<1> <W>Road<1>','  A road of white cobbled stones runs west and southeast through low hills and\npastures. The windows and terraces of hobbit burrows dot the hillsides.  A\ngrassy path leads north towards a fenced enclosed pasture.  \n',258,131072,22,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34113,0,0,0,'<G>Norman\'s<1> <W>Road<1>','  A road of white cobbled stones runs west and east through low hills and\npastures. The windows and terraces of hobbit burrows dot the hillsides.  A\nsmaller road forks off to the south here, towards a large burrow.  \n',258,131072,22,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34114,0,0,0,'<G>Norman\'s<1> <W>Road<1>','  A road of white cobbled stones runs northwest and east through low hills and\npastures. The windows and terraces of hobbit burrows dot the hillsides.  To\nthe northwest the cobblestones give way to a pale gravelly surface.  \n',258,131072,22,0,0,0,30,7,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34115,0,0,0,'<G>Norman\'s<1> <w>Road<1>','  A pale gravel road runs west and southeast through low hills and pastures. \nThe windows and terraces of hobbit burrows dot the hillsides.  A brightly\ncolored hobbit burrow faces the road to the north.  To the southeast the road\nis cobbled with white stones.  \n',258,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34116,0,0,0,'<G>Norman\'s<1> <w>Road<1>','  A pale gravel road runs west and east through low, brush spotted hills. \nWhile the road is worn with well established wagon grooves, patches of hardy\ngrass shoot up here and there.  \n',258,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
