(34156,0,0,0,'<G>Norman\'s<1> <w>Road<1>','  A pale gravel road makes its way northwest and east trough low scrub and\nbrush. A copse of scrub and trees comes to the south edge of the road.  While\nthe road is worn with well established wagon grooves, patches of hardy grass\nshoot up here and there.  \n',258,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34157,0,0,0,'<G>Norman\'s<1> <w>Road<1>','  A pale gravel road makes its way west and southeast trough low scrub and\nbrush. The occasional copse of trees dots the landscape.  While the road is\nworn with well established wagon grooves, patches of hardy grass shoot up here\nand there.  \n',258,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34158,0,0,0,'<G>Norman\'s<1> <w>Road<1>','  A pale gravel road makes its way west and east trough low scrub and brush. \nThe occasional copse of trees dots the landscape.  While the road is worn with\nwell established wagon grooves, patches of hardy grass shoot up here and\nthere. \n',258,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34159,0,0,0,'<G>Norman\'s<1> <w>Road<1>','  A pale gravel road makes its way west and east trough low scrub and brush. \nThe occasional copse of trees dots the landscape.  While the road is worn with\nwell established wagon grooves, patches of hardy grass shoot up here and\nthere. \n',258,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34160,0,0,0,'<G>Before a<1> <o>Burrow<1>','  This lane of pale gravel continues to the west.  The entrance to a hobbit\nburrow is to the south.  Its copper trimmed door and flamboyantly colored\nawning and window stand out like candles on a cake.  The lane merges into a\ncobblestone road to the north.  \n',258,131076,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34161,0,0,0,'<G>Before a<1> <o>Burrow Gate<1>','  This lane of pale gravel continues to the east.  A large gate has been set\ninto the hill to the southwest, over which hangs a painted wooden sign.  Low\nhills rise from the land in all directions, many sporting burrow doors and\nwindows. \n',258,131076,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34162,0,0,0,'<w>A<1> <o>Burrow<1> <w>Sitting Room<1>','  The walls of this large burrow are papered with an understated firework\npattern on a pale blue background.  Broad mouldings display the work of\nskilled carpenters.  A window and a door are in the north wall.  Another room\ncan be reached by going east and a sliding door leads to a room to the south.\n',258,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,12,72,0,'',NULL),
(34163,0,0,0,'<w>A<1> <o>Burrow<1> <w>Kitchen<1>','  The dark blue walls of this kitchen are trimmed with engravings of barnyard\nanimals. The odors of many richly prepared meals linger in the air.  A window\nfaces northeast and a larger room is to the west.  \n',258,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,8,72,0,'',NULL),
(34164,0,0,0,'<w>A<1> <o>Burrow<1> <w>Bedroom<1>','  The walls of this room describe a perfect circle.  They are papered with a\nwhite and blue striped pattern.  A window provides an outdoor view to the\nsouth and a sliding door leads into another room to the north.  \n',258,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,6,72,0,'',NULL),
(34165,0,0,0,'<w>Top of<1> <o>Tradeburrow<1> <w>Ramp<1>','  The floor here is made of tiled stone and appears to suffer a good deal of\nwear. The walls and high arched ceiling are of thick wooden planks.  A ramp\nleads down and the passage ends in a wide gate to the northeast.  \n',258,139336,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(34166,0,0,0,'<w>Bottom of<1> <o>Tradeburrow<1> <w>Ramp<1>','  The floor here is made of tiled stone and appears to suffer a good deal of\nwear. The walls and high arched ceiling are of thick wooden planks.  A ramp\nleads upwards and the passage empies into a large atrium to the south.  \n',258,139336,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(34167,0,0,0,'<o>Tradeburrow<1> <w>Stashroom<1>','  The high ceilings and walls of this open storage atrium are built of\nhorizontally layered thick wooden planks.  Sturdy beams arch from the stone\ntiled floor up to a large ceiling joist.  Access to a ramp leading upwards is\nto the north.  The storage area continues to the south, east and southeast.  \n',258,139336,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(34168,0,0,0,'<o>Tradeburrow<1> <w>Stashroom<1>','  The high ceilings and walls of this open storage atrium are built of\nhorizontally layered thick wooden planks.  Sturdy beams arch from the stone\ntiled floor up to a large ceiling joist.  The storage area continues to the\nwest, south and southwest.  \n',258,139336,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(34169,0,0,0,'<o>Tradeburrow<1> <w>Stashroom<1>','  The high ceilings and walls of this open storage atrium are built of\nhorizontally layered thick wooden planks.  Sturdy beams arch from the stone\ntiled floor up to a large ceiling joist.  An office has been built into the\nwestern part of the atrium.  To the south, a wide gate leads out of the\ntradeburrow. The storage area continues to the north, east and northeast.  \n',258,139336,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(34170,0,0,0,'<o>Dockmaster\'s Office<1>','  This high ceilinged office has been built into a corner of the tradeburrow\'s\nlarge storage atrium.  The walls and ceiling are made of thick wooden planks,\npainted avocado green.  A door in the east wall serves as the office\'s only\nexit. A window facing south provides a view of the dock area outside.  \n',258,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(34171,0,0,0,'<o>Dock Access Road<1>','  Pale gravel, apparently made by crushing the white stones that line the\nnearby riverbank, surfaces a short road that connects a riverdock to the south\nto a wide gate built into the hill to the north.  A grassy footpath follows\nthe bank going east.  \n',258,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34172,0,0,0,'<o>A Dock on the<1> <W>Silver<1><w>stone<1>','  A dock built of thick wooden planks provides a spot for cargo boats to tie\nup on the Silverstone.  Shining white stones and thick wooden legs support the\ndock against the gentle river currents.  A road leading to a large burrow gate\nleads north while the river flows around the dock to the east and south.  \n',258,131072,22,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34173,0,0,0,'<G>Path Along the Riverbank<1>','  A grassy footpath follows the bank of the river that flows to the south.  A\nlarge burrow hill rises to the north.  The path runs into a road to the west\nand continues along the bank to the east.  \n',258,131072,20,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34174,0,0,0,'<G>Picnic Spot and Path Along the Riverbank<1>','  A grassy footpath coming from the west ends here in a comfortable picnic\nspot. To the south, a quiet river makes its progress to western lands.  A\nlarge burrow hill rises to the north.  \n',258,131072,20,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34175,0,0,0,'<g>A Small Copse of Trees<1>','  A stand of tall beech and ash trees towers like a sentinel over a riverbank\nto the southwest.  To the north, just beyond a wall of bushes at the edge of\nthe grove, is a road.  Lush patches of moss climb many of the trunks and\ncarpet much of the ground here.  \n',258,131072,36,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34176,0,0,0,'<G>Bank Above the<1> <W>Silver<1><w>stone<1>','  Not far below this precarious perch flows a glittering river.  Large white\nstones embedded in the steep bank provide enough footing to scale down, though\nan unskilled climber would likely tumble uncontrollably into the waters below. \nThe landscape across the river appears to be rolling and grassy with a few\nwoody patches, much as it is along the north bank.  A copse of tall trees can\nbe entered to the northeast.  \n',258,131072,35,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34177,0,0,0,'<G>Before a<1> <o>Livestock<1> <G>Pasture<1>','  This small clearing is nestled between several low hobbit burrows, each\nsporting brightly trimmed windows and doors.  Trampled grass separates the\nroad to the south from a fenced livestock pasture to the north.  A swinging\ngate in the wooden fence provides a means to enter the pasture.  \n',258,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34178,0,0,0,'<o>Livestock<1> <G>Pasture<1>','  Most of the grass in this pasture has been trampled down.  Small hoof prints\nsprinkle the ground, suggesting a culprit.  A wooden rail fence surrounds the\npasture, which continues to the west.  A gate in the fence leads south.  The\nwhole lot is nestled amongst the burrow spotted green lumps of several low\nhillocks. \n',258,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34179,0,0,0,'<o>Livestock<1> <G>Pasture<1>','  Most of the grass in this pasture has been trampled down.  Small hoof prints\nsprinkle the ground, suggesting a culprit.  A wooden rail fence surrounds the\npasture, which continues to the east.  A section of the fence to the north\nappears to have come unlashed from its supporting post.  The whole lot is\nnestled amongst the burrow spotted greenery of several low hillocks.  \n',258,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34180,0,0,0,'<w>The Back Patio of a<1> <o>Burrow<1>','  This gaily colored patio has been carved into the hill to the west.  A\nfence, damaged at one post, separates the patio terrace from a pasture to the\nsouth. The doorway into a small shack is just to the north, and another leads\ninto the burrow to the west.  While several burrowed hills swell up nearby, a\nline of sight can be made to a creekbed not far east.  The patio can be easily\nclimbed to reach the hilltop above, though it is clearly not intended to\nprovide such access.  \n',258,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34181,0,0,0,'<w>On Top of a<1> <o>Patio<1>','  This position on top of a burrow patio is halfway up the small hill it has\nbeen built into.  A yard with a small shack, bordered by a livestock pasture\nand small hillocks is visible below.  To the west the hill slopes gently up to\nits flat peak.  While several burrowed hills swell up nearby, a line of sight\ncan be made to a creekbed not far east.  The yard can be easily reached by\nclimbing down the facade of the patio.  \n',258,131072,35,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34182,0,0,0,'<G>Atop a<1> <o>Burrow<1>','  Neighboring hillocks seem to bump heads from this burrowtop vantage.  Not\nfar to the east a creekbed and the low buildings and burrows of a hobbit shire\nare visible.  To the south, a white road runs from the shire into the hills\nto the west.  The dark glint of a river can be seen a little further south as\nit threads through those very same hills.  The burrowtop continues to the\nwest, and ends atop a precarious patio roof to the east.  \n',258,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34183,0,0,0,'<G>Atop a<1> <o>Burrow<1>','  Neighboring hillocks seem to bump heads from this burrowtop vantage.  Not\nfar to the east a creekbed and the low buildings and burrows of a hobbit shire\nare visible.  To the south, a white road runs from the shire into the hills\nto the west.  The dark glint of a river can be seen a little further south as\nit threads through those very same hills.  The burrowtop continues to the\neast, and ends atop a colorful awning to the south.  \n',258,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34184,0,0,0,'<w>An<1> <G>A<1><y>w<1><G>n<1><y>i<1><G>n<1><y>g<1> <w>Over a<1> <o>Burrow<1> <w>Entrance<1>','  This position on top of a burrow awning is halfway up a small hill.  The\nentrance into the burrow can be seen directly below, and a pale road further\nsouth. To the north the hill slopes gently up to its flat peak.  A skilled\nclimber should have no trouble scaling down the awning to the ground below.  \n',258,131072,35,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34185,0,0,0,'<G>Before a<1> <o>Burrow<1>','  A dirt path leads north to the door of a hobbit burrow.  To the south it\nconnects to a wider paved road.  A gaily colored awning shades a stoop and\nwindow from direct contact with the elements.  Small hills pop up from the\nsurrounding land like green welts.  \n',258,131072,23,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34186,0,0,0,'<w>Inside a<1> <o>Burrow<1>','  The east wall of this sitting room has been painted yolk yellow and the west\ngreen. In between is a creamy white.  Light and dark sections of the wood\nfloor form regular geometric patterns.  A window and door have been placed in\nthe south wall.  An open archway leads into another room to the east.  \n',258,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,8,60,0,'',NULL),
(34187,0,0,0,'<w>A<1> <o>Burrow<1> <w>Kitchen<1>','  Woodwork and fanciful mouldings have been done in the manner of a country\nkitchen. The walls are a deep sky blue.  The east wall is broken up by a\nwindow lined with potted plants and a door leading outside.  An open archway\nleads into another room to the west.  \n',258,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,6,60,0,'',NULL),
(34188,0,0,0,'<g>A<1> <o>Curing<1> <g>Shack<1>','  The loosely fit boards of this small shack provide a good deal of\nventilation. Nevertheless, it smells strongly of pipeweed.  A door in the\nsouth wall leads outside.  \n',258,139592,32,0,0,0,0,-1,4,60,0,'',NULL),
(34189,0,0,0,'<o>Tradeburrow<1> <w>Stashroom<1>','  The high ceilings and walls of this open storage atrium are built of\nhorizontally layered thick wooden planks.  Sturdy beams arch from the stone\ntiled floor up to a large ceiling joist.  The storage area continues to the\nnorth, west and northwest.  \n',258,139336,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(34190,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from northeast to west here.  At water\'s edge can be\nseen the white rocks that give the river its name.  A junction with a creek\ncan be seen upstream.  Above the junction are the low pastoral buildings and\nburrows of a hobbit shire.  The view to the south is of drier grassland and a\ndusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34191,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to southwest here.  At water\'s edge can be\nseen the white rocks that give the river its name.  Low grassy hillocks line\nthe north bank, some marked as hobbit burrows by brightly colored windows or a\nterrace. The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34192,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from northeast to west here.  At water\'s edge can be\nseen the white rocks that give the river its name.  Low grassy hillocks line\nthe north bank, some marked as hobbit burrows by brightly colored windows or a\nterrace. The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34193,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to west here.  At water\'s edge can be seen\nthe white rocks that give the river its name.  To the north, low grassy\nhillocks rise like soft green pillows.  A small path runs along the north\nbank, leading to a boat dock further west.  The view to the south is of drier\ngrassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34194,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1> <o>near a Dock<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to southwest here.  At water\'s edge can be\nseen the white rocks that give the river its name.  To the north, low grassy\nhillocks rise like soft green pillows.  Immediately west of here, beneath one\nsuch hill, a boat dock juts into the river.  A path runs along the north bank. \nThe view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34195,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1> <o>near a Dock<1>','  The Silverstone flows from northeast to west here.  At water\'s edge can be\nseen the white rocks that give the river its name.  Along the north bank, low\ngrassy hillocks rise like soft green pillows.  Immediately north of here,\nbeneath one such hill, a boat dock juts into the river.  The view to the south\nis of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34196,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to west here.  At water\'s edge can be seen\nthe white rocks that give the river its name.  Low grassy hillocks line the\nnorth bank, some marked as hobbit burrows by a brightly colored window or\nterrace. To the east, at the base of one such hill, a boat dock juts into the\nriver. The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34197,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to west here.  At water\'s edge can be seen\nthe white rocks that give the river its name.  Low grassy hillocks line the\nnorth bank, some marked as hobbit burrows by a brightly colored window or\nterrace. To the east, at the base of one such hill, a boat dock juts into the\nriver. The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34198,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to southwest here.  At water\'s edge can be\nseen the white rocks that give the river its name.  Low grassy hillocks line\nthe north bank, some marked as hobbit burrows by a brightly colored window or\nterrace. To the east, at the base of one such hill, a boat dock juts into the\nriver. The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34199,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from northeast to west here.  At water\'s edge can be\nseen the white rocks that give the river its name.  Low grassy hillocks line\nthe north bank.  The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty\nplain. \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34200,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to west here.  At water\'s edge can be seen\nthe white rocks that give the river its name.  Low grassy hillocks line the\nnorth bank.  The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34201,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to west here.  At water\'s edge can be seen\nthe white rocks that give the river its name.  Low grassy hillocks line the\nnorth bank.  The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34202,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to northwest here.  At water\'s edge can be\nseen the white rocks that give the river its name.  Low grassy hillocks line\nthe north bank.  The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty\nplain. \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,7,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34203,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from southeast to west here.  At water\'s edge can be\nseen the white rocks that give the river its name.  Low grassy hillocks line\nthe north bank.  The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty\nplain. \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34204,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to west here.  At water\'s edge can be seen\nthe white rocks that give the river its name.  Low grassy hillocks line the\nnorth bank.  The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34205,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to west here.  At water\'s edge can be seen\nthe white rocks that give the river its name.  Low grassy hillocks line the\nnorth bank.  The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34206,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to west here.  At water\'s edge can be seen\nthe white rocks that give the river its name.  Grassy pastures line the north\nbank. The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34207,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to southwest here.  At water\'s edge can be\nseen the white rocks that give the river its name.  Grassy pastures line the\nnorth bank.  The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34208,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from northeast to west here.  At water\'s edge can be\nseen the white rocks that give the river its name.  Grassy pastures line the\nnorth bank.  The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34209,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to west here.  At water\'s edge can be seen\nthe white rocks that give the river its name.  Grassy pastures line the north\nbank. The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34210,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to west here.  At water\'s edge can be seen\nthe white rocks that give the river its name.  Grassy pastures line the north\nbank. The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34211,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to west here.  At water\'s edge can be seen\nthe white rocks that give the river its name.  Grassy pastures line the north\nbank. The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
