(34219,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from southeast to west here.  At water\'s edge can be\nseen the white rocks that give the river its name.  Grassy pastures line the\nnorth bank.  The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain. \nFurther east the banks become steeper, and are lined with brush and trees.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
