(34221,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to west here.  At water\'s edge can be seen\nthe white rocks that give the river its name.  Grassy pastures line the north\nbank. The view to the south is of drier grassland and a dusty plain.  Further\neast the banks become steeper, and are lined with brush and trees.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34222,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from east to west here.  At water\'s edge can be seen\nthe white rocks that give the river its name.  The brush and tree lined banks\nare too high to see over.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
