(34237,0,0,0,'<W>Silver<1><w>stone<1> <B>River<1>','  The Silverstone flows from southeast to west here.  At water\'s edge can be\nseen the white rocks that give the river its name.  The brush and tree lined\nbanks are too high to see over.  The bank can be climbed here to reach a copse\nof trees overhead.  \n',258,131072,29,0,0,0,30,3,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
