(34600,0,0,0,'The Top of a Narrow Staircase','This room feels like a crypt.  Cold concrete walls rise on all sides and smoke\nwafts up constantly from the steep well-worn staircase below.  A dull orange\ntorchlight flickers up from the bottom of the stairway, casting shivering\nshadows on the pale grey walls.\n',0,131080,21,0,0,0,0,-1,4,105,0,'',NULL),
(34601,0,0,0,'A Security Checkpoint','This narrow underground hallway is stifling.  Cold concrete walls loom on both\nsides and smoke fills the air.  A dark stairway leads up at the north end of the\nhallway, while a secure iron door stands to the south.\n',0,131080,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34602,0,0,0,'Spectator\'s Balcony','This is the north end of a large balcony that has been constructed inside this\ncavernous semi-underground building.  The heavy wooden structure appears to loop\nall the way around the single, large room, allowing spectators to peer down over\nthe railing in the center to the cockfighting ring below.  The distinct smell of\nstraw and animal feces is overwhelmed only by the smell of pipeweed smoke and\nspilled ale.  The balcony continues looping around to the east and west.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34603,0,0,0,'Spectator\'s Balcony','This is the northeast side of a large balcony that has been constructed inside\nthis cavernous semi-underground building.  The heavy wooden structure appears to\nloop all the way around the single, large room, allowing spectators to peer down\nover the railing in the center to the cockfighting ring below.  The distinct\nsmell of straw and animal feces is overwhelmed only by the smell of pipeweed\nsmoke and spilled ale.  The balcony continues looping around to the west and\nsouth.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34604,0,0,0,'Spectator\'s Balcony','This is the east side of a large balcony that has been constructed inside this\ncavernous semi-underground building.  The heavy wooden structure appears to loop\nall the way around the single, large room, allowing spectators to peer down over\nthe railing in the center to the cockfighting ring below.  The distinct smell of\nstraw and animal feces is overwhelmed only by the smell of pipeweed smoke and\nspilled ale.  The balcony continues looping around to the north and south. \nThere is a sign over a small, barred window on the eastern wall.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34605,0,0,0,'Spectator\'s Balcony','This is the southeast side of a large balcony that has been constructed inside\nthis cavernous semi-underground building.  The heavy wooden structure appears to\nloop all the way around the single, large room, allowing spectators to peer down\nover the railing in the center to the cockfighting ring below.  The distinct\nsmell of straw and animal feces is overwhelmed only by the smell of pipeweed\nsmoke and spilled ale.  The balcony continues looping around to the north and\nwest.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34606,0,0,0,'Spectator\'s Balcony','This is the southern end of a large balcony that has been constructed inside\nthis cavernous semi-underground building.  The heavy wooden structure appears to\nloop all the way around the single, large room, allowing spectators to peer down\nover the railing in the center to the cockfighting ring below.  The distinct\nsmell of straw and animal feces is overwhelmed only by the smell of pipeweed\nsmoke and spilled ale.  The balcony continues looping around to the west and\neast.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34607,0,0,0,'Spectator\'s Balcony','This is the southwestern part of a large balcony that has been constructed\ninside this cavernous semi-underground building.  The heavy wooden structure\nappears to loop all the way around the single, large room, allowing spectators\nto peer down over the railing in the center to the cockfighting ring below.  The\ndistinct smell of straw and animal feces is overwhelmed only by the smell of\npipeweed smoke and spilled ale.  The balcony continues looping around to the\nnorth and west.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34608,0,0,0,'Spectator\'s Balcony','This is the western part of a large balcony that has been constructed inside\nthis cavernous semi-underground building.  The heavy wooden structure appears to\nloop all the way around the single, large room, allowing spectators to peer down\nover the railing in the center to the cockfighting ring below.  The distinct\nsmell of straw and animal feces is overwhelmed only by the smell of pipeweed\nsmoke and spilled ale.  The balcony continues looping around to the north and\nsouth.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34609,0,0,0,'Spectator\'s Balcony','This is the northwestern part of a large balcony that has been constructed\ninside this cavernous semi-underground building.  The heavy wooden structure\nappears to loop all the way around the single, large room, allowing spectators\nto peer down over the railing in the center to the cockfighting ring below.  The\ndistinct smell of straw and animal feces is overwhelmed only by the smell of\npipeweed smoke and spilled ale.  The balcony continues looping around to the\neast and south.  A sturdy wooden stairway leads down to the lower level.  A\nchain hangs on the stairway with a small sign reading \"Restricted Access\".\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34610,0,0,0,'The Cockfighting Ring','This is where the action is.  The ceiling stands two stories up, visible through\nlarge circular opening in the balcony above.  Scratch marks, feathers and blood\nmark the earthen floor.  The area is open on all sides, except to the south\nwhere a large window looks out from what appears to be a spectating room.\n',0,172040,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34611,0,0,0,'At the Foot of a Wooden Staircase','The stairs coming down from the balcony meet the earthen straw-covered floor\nhere on the ground level of the club.  Thick wooden beams rise up from the\nground supporting the balcony above.  Heavily trodden paths on the straw lead\neast toward what looks like a staging area, and south toward a collection of\nbenches and cages.  A ring of hay bales demarcates the main fighting ring to the\nsoutheast.  A small chain hangs on the stairway leading up to the balcony.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34612,0,0,0,'Ringside Walkway','This narrow but heavily trodden walkway allows people to walk around the ring to\nthe south without interfering with the fight.  A heavy wooden balcony stands\noverhead, while straw and rooster pellets cover the earthen ground below.  The\npath continues toward the staging area to the east and to the stairs to the\nwest.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34613,0,0,0,'Staging Area','The staging area is where the owners prepare their roosters for the big event. \nWhile this theoretically involves things like grooming and beak sharpening, the\nmore unscrupulous owners have been known to sneak spells or poisons into the\nmatch.  Straw lines the floor here, and heavy wooden beams rise up to support\nthe balcony above.  The ring lies surrounded in straw bales to the southwest,\nwhile the ringside area continues to the south and west.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34614,0,0,0,'Ringside Before a Small Office','This small open space to the east of the ring allows people to walk around the\nring to the west without interfering with the fight.  Heavy wooden beams rise\nout of the floor supporting the balcony above.  The floor is strewn with straw\nin the northern part of the room appears to have been swept down to the bare\nsoil in the southern half.  The cockfighting ring lies surrounded with hay bales\nto the west.  To the north is a staging area, while a ringside walkway continues\nto the northwest and south.  A half door in the eastern wall provides a view\ninto the manager\'s office.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34615,0,0,0,'Outside the VIP Room','The floor has been swept clear of straw here and a clearly worn path in the dirt\nleads from the north toward a wooden door in the western wall.  A large sign\nwith the letters V.I.P. is posted above the door.  There is little room to walk\nhere between the heavy wooden beams supporting the balcony above.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,4,120,0,'',NULL),
(34616,0,0,0,'The VIP Room','Walled off from the rest of the club, this room holds some of the best seats in\nthe house.  The ring can be seen through a large window in the north wall.  The\nglass, preventing blood and dust from entering this strikingly tidy room, is\ncleaned after each fight.  An ornately carved wooden door on the eastern wall\nappears to be the only exit.\n',0,139272,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34617,0,0,0,'Cage Room','This small cramped room is where the roosters are stored before and after the\nfights.  Cages are piled four to five high along the south wall, and a large\nburlap bag sits in the corner full of ground corn.  Some of the cages are empty,\nwhile others hold younger roosters awaiting training.  Two that sit on the floor\nalong the eastern wall hold rooster carcasses, covered in peck and scratch\nmarks.  A collection of benches is visible to the north, while the ring stands\nilluminated to the northeast.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34618,0,0,0,'Handler\'s Lounge','Lounge is hardly the word for this dark ringside collection of benches. \nNonetheless, this is where gamecock handlers sit and wait for their match to\noccur.  The view of the ring to the east is good here, provided one is not\nstuck behind a support beam for the balcony which stands overhead.  A collection\nof cages is visible to the south, while the ringside area continues to the north\nand northeast.\n',0,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34619,0,0,0,'A Small Tidy Office','This small but tidy office is where the manager of the cockfighting club takes\ncare of business.  The undecorated concrete walls and minimal furniture suggest\nthat the manager is a strictly-business kind of guy.  That, or the place needs\nto be cleared out rapidly on short notice.  A half door leads to the west,\nallowing a view of the cockfighting ring through the top half even when closed.\n',0,655368,32,0,0,0,0,-1,5,120,0,'',NULL),
(34620,0,0,0,'Betting Alcove','This small secure room sees most of the cash that flows through the club. \nFeeling like the inside of a small prison cell, thick concrete walls stand on\nall sides, matching the equally cold and solid concrete ceiling and floor.  The\nonly exit appears to be a sturdy iron door in the western wall with a small\nbarred window.\n',0,139272,32,0,0,0,0,-1,5,120,0,'',NULL),
(34624,0,0,0,'Entrance to a Cockfighting Club','Posters line the halls along this narrow entryway, advertising fights and\nspecial events, most of which have long passed.  The stone floor is littered\nwith pipeweed ash, peanut shells, and wrinkled betting slips.  A door leads to\nthe north and the hallway opens into a large chamber to the south.\n',0,131080,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(34627,0,0,0,'Treeline Above A Valley','The trees and brush part here slightly and lead \ndown a rough path\ninto the valley below. The vegetation below looks much more sparse\nthan that along the rim. There is evidence that the lack of vegetation\nis not natural. Among the clues is the faint sound of large scale\nmanual labor eminating from below.\n',-1,131072,50,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34650,0,0,0,'A Thin Trail across the Tundra','  A wide, featureless plain spreads out before you.  Short, stubby crabgrass\nprotrudes through the surface in clumps scattered about.  A mountain range\nlines the horizon to the east, while little can be seen to the west.  A\nbitterly cold wind seems to sweep down from the northeast.\n',56,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34651,0,0,0,'A Thin Trail across the Tundra','  A wide, featureless plain spreads out before you.  Short, stubby crabgrass\nprotrudes through the surface in clumps scattered about.  A mountain range\nlines the horizon to the east, while little can be seen to the west.  A\nbitterly cold wind seems to sweep down from the northeast.\n',56,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(34652,0,0,0,'A Thin Trail across the Tundra','  A wide, featureless plain spreads out before you.  Short, stubby crabgrass\nprotrudes through the surface in clumps scattered about.  A mountain range\nlines the horizon to the east, while little can be seen to the west.  A\nbitterly cold wind seems to sweep down from the northeast.\n',56,131072,3,0,0,0,0,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
