(35411,0,0,0,'A Dusty Path','  The small path is narrow here, the width only enough for one or two.  The\ndry cracked dust is tamped down by foot travel.  Fields of some grain dominate\nthe lands on either side of the path, though a dense thicket of weeds encroach\nthe pathway and bar exploration into those fields.\n',276,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35412,0,0,0,'A Dusty Path','  The small path is narrow here, the width only enough for one or two.  The\ndry cracked dust is tamped down by foot travel.  Fields of some grain dominate\nthe lands on either side of the path, though a dense thicket of weeds encroach\nthe pathway and bar exploration into those fields.  A dusty little yard\nsurrounds a tired looking farmhouse to the west.\n',276,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35413,0,0,0,'A Dusty Path','  This wandering path is wide enough to accomodate a fairly good sized party\nof travelers.  The dry cracked dust is heavily rutted, two grooves indicate\nregular wagon travel.  Fields of some grain dominate the lands on either side\nof the path, though a dense thicket of weeds bar exploration into those fields.\nThe sounds of peasant life can be heard far off to the south.\n',276,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35414,0,0,0,'A Dusty Path','  This wandering path is wide enough to accomodate a fairly good sized party\nof travelers.  The dry cracked dust is heavily rutted, two grooves indicate\nregular wagon travel.  Fields of some grain dominate the lands on either side\nof the path, though a dense thicket of weeds bar exploration into those fields.\nThe sounds of peasant life can be heard some ways off to the south.\n',276,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35415,0,0,0,'Before a Stockade Fence','  This wandering path is wide enough to accomodate a fairly good sized party\nof travelers, a smaller pathway leads to the east.  The dry cracked dust is\nheavily rutted, two grooves indicate regular wagon travel.  A rather\nweatherbeaten stockade fence stops further travel to the south.  There is a\nrusty gate directly in the center of the fence.  The land on either side of the\npath is choked with weeds.\n',276,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35416,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant\'s village.  A small guardhouse\nstands to the east, the rusty gate in a stockade fence leads to the north.  A\nbusy shop, Tig\'s, makes fine clothing to the west.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35417,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant\'s village.  A rickety stockade\nfence, complete with rusty gate, is to the north, a small guardhouse to the\neast of the gate.  The shabby town square is to the south.  Shops line the\nsquare, aged timbers, but still sturdy wood frame buildings, most of them\nappear busy.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35418,0,0,0,'A Shabby Village Square','  Wood frame shops, bearing the silvering of time, proliferate the square.\nOld straw is scattered over the ground, adding to the dust of the dry earth\nbelow.  To the far north a stockade fence serves more as a visual deterent than\na real protection.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35419,0,0,0,'A Shabby Village Square','  Wood frame shops bearing the silvering of time proliferate the square.  Old\nstraw is scattered over the ground, adding to the dust of the dry earth below.\nA dusty path runs through town to the south, more shops and a few meager homes\ncan be seen from here.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35420,0,0,0,'A Shabby Village Square','  Wood frame shops bearing the silvering of time proliferate the square.  Old\nstraw is scattered over the ground, adding to the dust of the dry earth below.\nThe aroma of fresh baked goods wafts from the bakery to the north.  The din of\ntavern revelry can be heard coming from a tavern to the east.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35421,0,0,0,'A Shabby Village Square','  Wood frame shops bearing the silvering of time proliferate the square.  Old\nstraw is scattered over the ground, adding to the dust of the dry earth below.\nThe Inn of the Weasel is directly to the east offering rest to weary travelers.\nThere is a fairly good sized general store to the south.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35422,0,0,0,'A Shabby Village Square','  Wood frame shops bearing the silvering of time proliferate the square.  Old\nstraw is scattered over the ground, adding to the dust of the dry earth below.\nTig\'s, the towns fine clothing store is directly to the north.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35423,0,0,0,'A Shabby Village Square','  Wood frame shops bearing the silvering of time proliferate the square.  Old\nstraw is scattered over the ground, adding to the dust of the dry earth below.\nThe south to the shop glows from within, many candles light up the glass paned\nwindows.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35424,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant\'s village.  The shabby town square\nis to the north.  Shops line the square, aged timbers, but still sturdy wood\nframe buildings, most of them appear busy.  A church of wood frame is to the\nsouth, doors always open to welcome the weary and the poor.  To the southeast,\nis the village garden.\n',276,131076,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35425,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant village.  Small homes can be seen\nclustered in the west.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35426,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant village.  Small homes can be seen\nclustered in the west.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35427,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant village.  Small homes can be seen\nclustered a ways to the west.  Another small building is found a ways\nsouthwest.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35428,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant village.  What appears to be a\nvillage school house can be seen directly to the west.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35429,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant village.  There is a shabby stockade\nfence in the south, a rusty iron gate leads beyond the fence.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35430,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','The path leads through an aging peasant village.  A rickety stockade fence\nis here with a rusty gate that leads south into the desert.\n',-1,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35431,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant\'s village.  The shabby town square\nis to the east.  Shops of aged timbers line the square.  The sturdy wood frame\nbuildings appear to be busy.  In the shop to the south tanned goods of various\nuses can be purchased.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35432,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant\'s village.  The shabby town square\nis to the east.  Shops of aged timbers line the square.  The sturdy wood frame\nbuildings appear to be busy.  The jailhouse to the north has been constructed\nof sturdy stone.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35433,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant\'s village.  Towards the west are\nclusters of small comfortable homes.  Loud hammering comes from the smiths shop\nto the north.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35434,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant\'s village.  Towards the west and the\nsouth are comfortable looking homes.  To the north is another home.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35435,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an ageing peasant\'s village.  Towards the west is a\ncomfortable looking home.  To the south are more homes.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35436,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an ageing peasant\'s village.  Towards the west is a\nbusiness of some kind.  To the south are some modest homes.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35437,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an ageing peasant\'s village.  A modest building to\nthe west has many and various sizes of barrels stacked in front of it.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35438,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant village.  Big potholes are\neverywhere in the dusty path.  Small homes can be seen clustered in the general\nwestern and southern directions.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35439,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant village.  Big potholes are\neverywhere in the dusty path.  A small home can be seen to the east.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35440,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant village.  Big potholes are\neverywhere in the dusty path.  A small home can be seen to the south.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35441,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant village.  Big potholes are\neverywhere in the dusty path.  A small home can be seen to the south, \nfrom the west smoke drifts from the chimney on a little shed.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35442,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant village.  Big potholes are\neverywhere in the dusty path.  A small home can be seen to the east.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35443,0,0,0,'Path Through a Small Village','  The path leads through an aging peasant village.  Big potholes are\neverywhere in the dusty path.  Small homes can be seen clustered in \nthe south, west, and southwest.\n',276,131072,43,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35444,0,0,0,'A Cobblestone Road','  Neat cobblestones line the road bed.  The road is farely wide and swept\nclean of debris.  Tall trees shade the boardwalk that runs through the entire\nneighborhood.\n',276,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35445,0,0,0,'A Cobblestone Road','  Neat cobblestones line the road bed.  The road is farely wide and swept\nclean of debris.  Tall trees shade the boardwalk that runs through the entire\nneighborhood.  A fairly elegant home sits on the land to the south.\n',276,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35446,0,0,0,'A Cobblestone Road','  Neat cobblestones line the road bed.  The road is farely wide and swept\nclean of debris.  Tall trees shade the boardwalk that runs through the entire\nneighborhood.  A fairly elegant home sits on the land to the north.\n',276,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35447,0,0,0,'A Cobblestone Road','  Neat cobblestones line the road bed.  The road is farely wide and swept\nclean of debris.  Tall trees shade the boardwalk that runs through the entire\nneighborhood.  A fairly elegant home sits on the land to the south.\n',276,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35448,0,0,0,'A Cobblestone Road','  Neat cobblestones line the road bed.  The road is farely wide and swept\nclean of debris.  Tall trees shade the boardwalk that runs through the entire\nneighborhood.\n',276,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35449,0,0,0,'The Village Garden','  The back of a wooden frame church can be seen to the west.  Heavily laden\ntomato plants grow in this part of the garden.  There are turnips, corn,\nsquash, and greens growing in other parts of the garden.\n',276,131072,46,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35450,0,0,0,'The Village Garden','  Row upon row of tall corn stretches skyward, many colorful squashes wind\naround the base of the corn plants  There are turnips, tomatoes and greens\ngrowing in other parts of the garden.  The rickety stockade fence that\nsurrounds town borders the eastern side of the garden.\n',276,131072,46,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35451,0,0,0,'The Village Garden','  Turnip greens grow abundantly here.  No doubt the tops as tasty as the\nroots.  There are tomatoes, corn, squash, and salad greens growing in other\nparts of the garden.  The rickety stockade fence that surrounds the town\nborders the southern edge of the garden.\n',276,131072,46,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35452,0,0,0,'The Village Garden','  Salad greens of all sorts grow here, from heads of lettuce, to spinach, leaf\nlettuces and more.  There is even a tiny row of green onions.  There are\ntomatoes, corn, squash, and turnip greens growing in other parts of the garden.\nThe rickety stockade fence that surrounds the town borders the southern and\neastern edges of the garden.\n',276,131072,46,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35453,0,0,0,'Tiny Path Through Some Weeds','  This very narrow path is choked with weeds.  It appears to get little use,\nand then only on rare occasions.  The rickety stockade fence that surrounds a\ntowns borders is directly to the west.\n',276,131076,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35454,0,0,0,'Tiny Path Through Some Weeds','  This very narrow path is choked with weeds.  It appears to get little use,\nand then only on rare occasions.  A little way off to the east a tiny cottage\nstands in solitude.\n',276,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35455,0,0,0,'Tiny Path Through Some Weeds','  This very narrow path is choked with weeds.  It appears to get little use,\nand then only on rare occasions.  Directly to the east a tiny cottage stands in\nsolitude.  Well kept beds of medicinal herbs surround the cottage on all\nvisible sides, the healthy plants growing towards the weeds that encroach the\ntiny path.\n',276,131072,44,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35456,0,0,0,'Inside The Sour Grape','  The wood floor is covered thickly with dirty crushed straw.  Two tables fill\nthe better portion of this smokey room.  The air is sour, like old spilled\nwine, mead and beer, added to this, the smoke from a poorly ventilated\nfireplace refuses to use the chimney.  By the eastern wall is a small raised\nplatform.\n',276,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35457,0,0,0,'Inside The Sour Grape','  The wood floor is covered thickly with dirty crushed straw.  A long low\ntable serves as a communal eating place.  Remnants litter the table, spilled\nturnip stew has congealed in thick puddles, stale crusts of bread, upon close\nexamination, reveal mold.  The overpowering odor of bad meat fills the air.\n',276,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35458,0,0,0,'Inside The Sour Grape','  This well used room provides storage for the tavern.  Oaken casks are\nstacked upon the western wall, several hams hang from the rafters.  A large bin\nis filled with rough, slightly off brown flour.  The walls have been paneled in\nrich burnished wood.\n',276,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35459,0,0,0,'The Auction Room','  The large wooden platform in the western part of the room is made up of\nscuffed boards.  Large oil lamps line the back of the stage area providing a\nclear view of the goods for sale.  Several long benches fill the floorspace,\npresumably for auction participants seating.  The walls have been paneled in\nrich burnished wood.\n',276,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35460,0,0,0,'Inside The Inn of the Weasel','  This tiny foyer holds only a long counter and a rack of cubbyholes for\nmessages.  Though small it is tidy, the floor shows not a speck of tracked\ndirt, no cobwebs grace the ceiling.  A narrow stairwell leads up to the\nsleeping loft.\n',276,174585,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35461,0,0,0,'Loft at The Inn of the Weasel','This wide, open room provides a place for the weary traveler to rest.\nStraw pallets are covered with crisp, clean, if threadbare looking sheets.\nTwo sturdy hooks hang above each pallet, at the foot of each is folded a rough\nwoolen blanket.\n',-1,174585,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35462,0,0,0,'Loft at The Inn of the Weasel','This wide, open room provides a place for the weary traveler to rest.\nStraw pallets are covered with crisp, clean, if threadbare looking sheets.\nTwo sturdy hooks hang above each pallet, at the foot of each is folded a rough\nwoolen blanket.\n',-1,174585,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35463,0,0,0,'Bartley\'s Tannery','The tannery is filled with tanned hides and products made from hide.  There\nare several large open cabinets, the shelves contain a variety of leather\ngoods.  The floor is open, and swept clean.\n',-1,174585,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35464,0,0,0,'Bartley\'s Tannery','The scent of freshly tanned skins pervades the room, the skins are stacked\nin big piles that cover most of the floor.  A long low table resides in against\none wall, rolls of sinew, large hooked needles and other assorted sewing\nsupplies are scattered about it.\n',-1,174585,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35465,0,0,0,'Kort\'s Smithey','A wide counter divides the room.  The larger section, behind the counter,\nholds a wide assortment of metal objects.  An open ended room can be seen\nthrough an open doorway to the north, another door leads out of the shop to the\nsouth.\n',-1,174585,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35466,0,0,0,'Kort\'s Smithey','A large kiln sits in the open air to the south, the roof stopping just\nbefore it.  There are some large barrels filled with water near an anvil, some\ntongs rest on the wall nearby.  A door to the south leads to another section of\nthe shop.\n',-1,174585,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35467,0,0,0,'A Small Schoolhouse','This is a long room, in a wood frame building.  Along the back of the room\nis a big shelf holding assorted jars.  Directly in front of the shelf start\nrows of desks, small wooden desks with small chairs to fit.  An occasional\nscorch mark darkens the ceiling, the walls and the floor.  A slate blackboard\nhangs on the front wall, strange symbols cover it in some kind of equation.  A\nbrass plaque adorns a door to the northwest, there is another door to the east.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35468,0,0,0,'Master Beltair\'s Office','This is a long room, in a wood frame building.  An ornate glassed cabinet\nfills the northwestern corner of the room.  It is filled with delicate\nornamented vials and curious knick knacks.  A large crystal hangs, seemingly\nsuspended, in the center of a woven talisman that has been hung in the window\non the western side of the room.  There is a doorway exiting to the southeast.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35469,0,0,0,'A Tiny Cottage','The fireplace holds a brightly burning fire, little odds and ends decorate\nthe wide mantle.  Each and every rafter of the cottage holds bundled herbs,\nwhich creates a heady aroma.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35470,0,0,0,'The Sweet Tart','The most delectable scents waft about the store.  The atmosphere is warm and\ncomforting.  Look through the glass of the bakery counter, it is most likely\nfilled with tempting refreshments.\n',-1,174585,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35471,0,0,0,'A Decrepit Farmhouse','  This farmhouse has seen better days, though it was never what one would call\nluxurious.  A hearth of creek stones contains a smokey fire, more of the smoke\nseems to be in the house than going out the chimney.  Two straw pallets serve\nas beds for the inhabitants.  One window faces the north, it is covered with\nthe skin of some animal.  There is a small table under the window.\n',276,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,60,0,'',NULL),
(35472,0,0,0,'A Decrepit Farmhouse','This farmhouse has seen better days, though it was never what one would call\nluxurious.  A hearth of creek stones contains a smokey fire, more of the smoke\nseems to be in the house than going out the chimney.  Three straw pallets serve\nas beds for the inhabitants.  There are no windows, which might account for\nsome of the smoke.  From the bare rafters hangs a slightly moldy looking ham.\nThere is a small table pushed against the north wall.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35473,0,0,0,'A Decrepit Farmhouse','This farmhouse has seen better days, though it was never what one would call\nluxurious.  A hearth of creek stones contains a brightly burning fire.\nWindows face north and east, while the panes are slightly cracked, they are at\nleast glassed and clean.  Two straw pallets serve as beds for the inhabitants.\nA small crockery vase filled with flowers adorns the table under the north\nwindow.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35474,0,0,0,'A Decrepit Farmhouse','This farmhouse has seen better days, though it was never what one would call\nluxurious.  A hearth of creek stones contains a smokey fire, more of the smoke\nseems to be in the house than going out the chimney.  Two straw pallets serve\nas beds for the inhabitants.  One window faces the north, it is covered with\nthe skin of some animal.  There is a small table under the window.  A bent up\nsaucepan has been placed in the corner to catch leaks when it rains.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35475,0,0,0,'Guardhouse by the Gate','A nearly empty grate stands in the fireplace along the north wall.  The\nfloor is sandy from dirty boots.  There is a stack of torches in one corner.\nA crusty table fills the center of the room, littered with the remnants of\nmeals eaten in great haste.  A filthy cot is leaned up against the east wall.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35476,0,0,0,'Garn\'s Coopery','Solid wood planks make up walls and floors of the coopery.  Thatched straw\ncovers the roof snuggly.  A small loft can be seen in the back of the shop,\nbarrels of all shapes and sizes fill the loft, stacked neatly in rows according\nto size.  Metal strips in various widths, thin wooden planks, all the coopers\nsupplys fill the area below the loft.\n',-1,174585,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35477,0,0,0,'Inside an Elegant House','Starkly white the painted walls are without dust, or scuff mark.  The deeply\nburnished floor is graced with rugs highly detailed colorful weaving.  A loom\ncan be seen before the southward facing window.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35478,0,0,0,'Inside an Elegant House','Starkly white the painted walls are without dust, or scuff mark.  The floors\nare deeply burnished, several paintings of gentle scenes grace the walls.\nThere is a partially finished painting of a woods scene on a large easel.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35479,0,0,0,'Inside an Elegant House','Starkly white the painted walls are without dust, or scuff mark.  The floors\nare deeply burnished.  The house is immaculately clean and absolutely empty.\nBare windows of polished glass face to the south.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35480,0,0,0,'Inside a Tidy House','The shingled roof looks securely fashioned.  Freshly whitewashed walls make\nthe house bright.  A globed candle holder hangs above the table that rests near\nthe wide fireplace.  A small alcove in the back of the house provides a cozy\nsleeping area.  The hardwood floors have been waxed to a glossy shine.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35481,0,0,0,'Inside a Tidy House','The shingled roof looks securely fashioned.  Freshly whitewashed walls make\nthe house bright.  A globed candle holder hangs above the table that rests near\nthe wide fireplace.  A small alcove in the back of the house provides a cozy\nsleeping area.  The hardwood floors have been waxed to a glossy shine.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35482,0,0,0,'Inside a Tidy House','The shingled roof looks securely fashioned.  Freshly whitewashed walls make\nthe house bright.  A globed candle holder hangs above the table that rests near\nthe wide fireplace.  A small alcove in the back of the house provides a cozy\nsleeping area.  The hardwood floors have been waxed to a glossy shine.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35483,0,0,0,'Inside a Tidy House','The shingled roof looks securely fashioned.  Freshly whitewashed walls make\nthe house bright.  A globed candle holder hangs above the table that rests near\nthe wide fireplace.  A small alcove in the back of the house provides a cozy\nsleeping area.  The hardwood floors have been waxed to a glossy shine.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35484,0,0,0,'A Shabby Peasant Hut','A low thatched roof sags in some places, shows sky in others.  A tiny loft\nhas been built into the back of the house.  A crumbling brick fireplace\nprovides heat and a means to cook.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35485,0,0,0,'A Shabby Peasant Hut','A low thatched roof sags in some places, shows sky in others.  A tiny loft\nhas been built into the back of the house.  A crumbling brick fireplace\nprovides heat and a means to cook.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35486,0,0,0,'A Shabby Peasant Hut','A low thatched roof sags in some places, shows sky in others.  A tiny loft\nhas been built into the back of the house.  A crumbling brick fireplace\nprovides heat and a means to cook.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35487,0,0,0,'A Shabby Peasant Hut','A low thatched roof sags in some places, shows sky in others.  A tiny loft\nhas been built into the back of the house.  A crumbling brick fireplace\nprovides heat and a means to cook.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35488,0,0,0,'A Shabby Peasant Hut','A low thatched roof sags in some places, shows sky in others.  A tiny loft\nhas been built into the back of the house.  A crumbling brick fireplace\nprovides heat and a means to cook.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35489,0,0,0,'A Shabby Peasant Hut','A low thatched roof sags in some places, shows sky in others.  A tiny loft\nhas been built into the back of the house.  A crumbling brick fireplace\nprovides heat and a means to cook.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35490,0,0,0,'A Shabby Peasant Hut','A low thatched roof sags in some places, shows sky in others.  A tiny loft\nhas been built into the back of the house.  A crumbling brick fireplace\nprovides heat and a means to cook.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35491,0,0,0,'Greb\'s General','Greb\'s general store overflows with products.  There are bins of dry\ngoods, various flours, beans, and grains.  One area holds lanterns, tents,\nblankets, and backpacks.  Chairs of differing sizes are placed around a\npotbellied stove, accomodating to the weary, but each bearing a tag with a\nprice.  A long counter holds jars of hard candies, nuts and other snacks.\nLarge rounds of cheeses can be seen on the shelf under the counter.  There is\neven a box of simple wooden toys in the corner.  A sign has been hung on the\nwall behind the counter.\n',-1,174585,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35492,0,0,0,'Church of the Wilted and Downtrodden','The shabby but tidy church is sparsely furnished.  Long wooden pews have\nbeen lined up into two rows upon the freshly scrubbed wood floor.  Two\nextraordinary stained glass mosaics grace the east and west walls, a modest\npulpit stands at the front of the church, there is a small door with a brass\nplaque behind it.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35493,0,0,0,'Father Crin\'s Sanctuary','Father Crin\'s Sanctuary is nothing more than a cubbyhole.  A small table by\nthe door holds the remains of many candles, stubs upon stubs dripped off the\nback.  A lumpy straw pallet fills the east side of the room.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35494,0,0,0,'Tig\'s','A long counter partitions the west side of the room from the east.  Behind\nthe counter, half finished suits hang on wicker manequins.  In the central part\nof the shop the floor is bare, save only for a wide footstool.  A full length\nmirror resides on the northern wall, next to the entrance to the section of\nshop where ladies apparel is fashioned.  Two large glassed windows look out\nupon the street to the east.\n',-1,174585,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35495,0,0,0,'Tig\'s','The lively colors of the shop are warm and inviting.  Displayed in the\nwindow are skirts and blouses of the latest fashion.  A table is cluttered with\nscissors, pins, scraps of cloth, and various colors of thread.  Paper patterns\nare folded neatly on the corner.  A treadle sewing machine sits by the west\nwall.\n',-1,174585,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35496,0,0,0,'The Wick and Tallow','The thick air of this illuminated shop smells strongly of a potpourri of\nfragrances, and of melted and burning fat.  Racks and racks of candles grace\nthe walls.  The window shelves are filled with burning candles, clearly\ndemonstrating the long lasting quality of the products sold here.\n',-1,174585,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35497,0,0,0,'Inside a Smokey Shed','  The small shed is thick with smoke.  Its very warm and quite dark.\n',276,131080,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35498,0,0,0,'The Jail','A small room, the walls are exposed rock, one window faces the path to the\nsouth.  There is a barred jail cell in the bare wooden floor.  A long wooden\nbench rests along the eastern wall.\n',-1,131081,55,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35499,0,0,0,'A Jail Cell','This cellar cell has been dug below the jailhouse.  The walls have been\nreinforced with blocks of some heavy grey stone.  A thick layer of tattered\nmuddy straw covers the floor.  High in the western wall is a tiny grated hole\nserving as a window.\n',-1,131080,56,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35700,0,0,0,'The Side of a Hill','   A small dirt path leads off to the south, completely surrounded by tall\ngrasses and colorful flowers.  Small insects make chirping noises and jump back\nand forth between the many growing plants.  There is a small hill immediately\nto the north which is covered in vegetation.  Between the grasses, a dark hole\nleads into the hill.  Skittering noises and high-pitched squeaking come from\ninside the hole, drifting slowly out of the darkness.\n',280,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35701,0,0,0,'A Dark Tunnel','   This dark tunnel has been dug from the earth by the hard work of many small\nclaws.  The walls and ceiling are covered in claw marks, and the dirt on the\nfloor has been packed down by tiny clawed feet.  Small plant roots hang down\ninto the tunnel from above.  Skittering and squeaking noises can be heard\ncoming from all around, as do the sound of tiny clawed feet running through\nsmall tunnels deep in the walls.  On the dirt floor there are a few piles of\nbones lying scattered about.  The tunnel leads north, and a hole leads to the\noutside to the south.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35702,0,0,0,'Bend in a Dark Tunnel','   The tunnel bends here, leading to the east and to the south.  No light\nsource enters this dark tunnel, leaving it black as night.  The earthen walls\nand ceiling are marked with the scratch marks of many small claws, but the\nground is packed and mostly smooth.  High-pitched squeaking comes from all\naround, filling the tunnel with odd sounding echoes.  A small hole in the west\nwall leads into some type of animal burrow.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35703,0,0,0,'A Dark Tunnel','   The dark tunnel continues to the east and west.  Claw marks cover the\ntunnel everywhere, and the dirt floor and walls seem to have been packed down\nby similarly clawed feet.  Skittering noises and high-pitched squeaking come\nfrom all around, creating strange echoes.  The tunnel is empty of roots and\nclumps of dirt that would normally be present in a dug out tunnel like this\none.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35704,0,0,0,'A Bend in a Dark Tunnel','   This dark tunnel dug from the earth bends to the south as well as heading\nwest.  The earthen walls are covered with scratch marks from tiny claws.\nSkittering noises and high-pitched squeaking can be heard from all around,\ncoming from down the corridors and behind the walls themselves.  A faint light\ncan be seen to the south.  Tiny bones lie scattered about in small piles.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35705,0,0,0,'Dark Tunnel','   This is the end of a dark tunnel carved from the earth.  The walls and\nceiling are covered with marks made by small claws.  The floor has been packed\ndown by similarly clawed feet.  Junk and trash lie scattered about, and bits of\nbone and pieces of wood cover the floor.  A pile of wood leans up against the\nwest wall.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35706,0,0,0,'Entrance to the Burrows','   This large burrow has been carved directly from the earth.  A large tunnel\ndrops steeply underground in the eastern part of this room.  A few small chairs\nand a small table lean up against the north wall; they seem crude in make and\nlook to fall apart at any moment.  Chittering noises, like that of a rat but\nlower pitched, drift about the room.  The walls and ceiling look to have been\ndug out with care as few claw marks are evident.  A small torch on a rope hangs\ndown from the center of the ceiling.  A pile of wood sits up against the east\nwall.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35707,0,0,0,'Tunnel Intersection','   This earthen tunnel leads to the north, east, and west.  A large, sloped\npassageway leads up in the southern part of the room.  Torches hang from the\nwalls, casting a strange, flickering light.  The tunnel itself is hot and\nhumid, and a bad, rank smell floats up from the floor.  Low-pitched squeaking\nand skittering noises come from all around.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35708,0,0,0,'Burrow Warrens','   This large burrow was dug from the earth by many small claws.  The burrow\ncontinues to the north and west, and a tunnel leads off to the east.  The walls\nare honeycombed with dozens of small alcoves, each the home of one or two small\ncreatures.  Small ladders, steps, and ropes with knots lead to each of these\nalcoves.  The burrow\'s floor is littered with many tiny tables, chairs, and\nbenches.  Torches flicker on the walls, casting strange shadows about the\nwarren.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35709,0,0,0,'Burrow Warrens','   This large burrow continues to the east and west.  A tunnel decends to a\nlower level, sloping steeply down from the middle of the room.  The walls are\nhoneycombed with dozens of small alcoves, the homes of one or two tiny\ncreatures.  Each of the alcoves is covered in fur and sometimes contain one or\ntwo small objects, obviously stolen from civilization.  Torches flicker on the\nwalls, casting strange shadows.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35710,0,0,0,'Burrow Warrens','   This large burrow continues to the north and east.  The walls of the\nburrow are honeycombed with dozens of small alcoves, the homes of one or two\ntiny creatures.  Small ladders, steps, and ropes with knots provide access to\nthe ones further up the walls.  The floor is littered with many tables, chairs,\nand benches that only seem big enough for a creature perhaps two or three feet\ntall.  Torches flicker on the walls, casting strange shadows.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35711,0,0,0,'Burrow Warrens','   This large burrow continues to the east and south, and a sloping tunnel\nleads down from the western wall.  The walls are honeycombed with many small\nalcoves, each big enough for only one or two small creatures.  Rats can be seen\nscurrying about, running in and out of small holes.  The floor in this room is\nlittered with tiny tables, chairs, and benches.  Torches on the walls cast\nstrange shadows about the room.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35712,0,0,0,'Burrow Warrens','   This large burrow continues to the east and west, and a tunnel leads off\nto the north.  The walls are covered in dozens of small alcoves, the living\nspaces for one or two tiny creatures.  Ladders, steps, and ropes with knots\nprovide access to the alcoves higher up on the walls.  Tables, chairs, and\nbenches, only big enough for creatures perhaps two or three feet tall, litter\nthe floor.  Torches flicker on the walls, casting strange shadows.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35713,0,0,0,'Burrow Warrens','   This large burrow continues to the south and the west, and a tunnel leads\noff to the north.  Dozens of small alcoves honeycomb the walls, each the home\nof one or two tiny creatures.  Small ladders, steps, and ropes with knots lead\nto the alcoves further up the walls.  The floor is littered with tables,\nchairs, and benches, each only big enough for creatures two or three feet tall.\nTorches flicker on the walls, casting strange shadows.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35714,0,0,0,'Tunnel in the Warrens','   This tunnel leads to the main warrens to the south and a large room to the\nwest.  There are no alcoves or torches on these walls, yet light drifts in from\nother places.  Soft squeaking, like that made by young rats, drifts softly\nabout the room.  A small table sits in the middle of the room, and a tiny\nweapons rack leans up against the north wall.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35715,0,0,0,'Warren Nursery','   This large room is almost perfectly round, the claw marked walls leading up\nto a large domed ceiling.  Baskets of all sizes and shapes hang down from the\nceiling and walls on thick ropes.  The baskets are all covered in rags and fur,\nand many contain small droppings and spilled milk.  A few torches are tied to\nthe walls, and they cast flickering shadows about the room.  A rank smell\ndrifts up from the floor.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35716,0,0,0,'Tunnel to the Warrens','   Almost perfectly round, this tunnel is covered in claw marks from small\nhands and feet.  The main tunnel is to the east, and the burrow warrens are to\nthe south.  Rats run about the floor and duck in and out of small holes.\nTorches hang from the walls, casting light on piles of garbage and junk\nlittered around the room.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35717,0,0,0,'Tunnel Through the Burrow','   The main tunnel leads north, south, and east from here.  Dug from the\nearth by many tiny claws, the tunnel is large enough to hold dozens of small\ncreatures.  Torches hang from the walls, flickering slightly and casting\nstrange shadows.  The tunnel is quite humid, and a rank smell drifts up from\nthe floor.  Squeaking can be heard coming from all around.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35718,0,0,0,'Tunnel Intersection','   Tunnels lead off to the north, northeast, south, and west.  Like all the\ntunnels in the burrows, this was dug from the earth and is large enough to hold\nmany small creatures.  Torches swing about on ropes hanging around the room,\nflickering slightly from a light breeze coming from tiny vents in the ceiling.\nA foul smell drifts up from the floor, and the tunnel itself seems hot and\nhumid.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35719,0,0,0,'Tunnel Through the Burrow','   This large tunnel continues to the north and west.  The tunnel itself is\nbig enough for dozens of small creatures.  Torches hang from the walls,\nflickering slightly and casting strange shadows about the room.  The tunnel is\nhot and humid, and a rank smell drifts up from the floor.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35720,0,0,0,'Large Room in the Burrow','   This large room was carved out of the earth much like the tunnels.\nPassageways lead north and east, and burrow tunnels lead out to the south and\nwest.  Somewhat nicer then the other rooms in the burrows, this room is\nfurnished with old trinkets and rotting tapestries.  The furniture here looks\nsomewhat well made, as if stolen from something that knew how to build such\nsmall tables and chairs well.  Strong, rank smells drift in from the east and\nsouth, but this room is somewhat more clean and less foul.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35721,0,0,0,'Private Warren','   Many alcoves honeycomb the walls in this large, private warren.  Saved for\nthe nobility of the Ratlings, the private warrens are the home to a single\nRatling family, even though that family might be more then 50 members in size.\nPersonal objects litter the floor and alcoves.  Tiny tables, chairs, and\nbenches sit around the floor in an orderly fashion.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35722,0,0,0,'Large Room in the Burrow','   This large room is somewhat cleaner then the other tunnels and warrens in\nthe burrow.  There is another large room to the west.  More rooms lie to the\nnorth, northeast, and east.  A curtain hangs over a large hole in the south\nwall.  The room itself is decorated with shiney objects and colorful, rotting\ntapestries.  A slightly rank smell drifts in from the west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35723,0,0,0,'Private Warren','   Many alcoves honeycomb the walls in this large, private warren.  Saved for\nthe nobility of the Ratlings, the private warrens are the home to a single\nRatling family, even though that family might be over 50 members in size.  The\nalcoves are larger then the ones in the common warrens, and contain many more\npersonal items.  Tiny tables, chairs, and benches lie about in an orderly\nfashion.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35724,0,0,0,'Large Rat\'s Nest','A rank small drifts up from the floor of this small cave.  The ground is\ncovered in loose fur, small bones, and animal droppings.  Large holes cover the\nwalls, and glimpses of movement can be seen deep within them.  A low-pitched\nsqueaking fills the room, coming out from the walls themselves.  A tunnel dug\nfrom the earth leads southeast.\n',0,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35725,0,0,0,'Private Warren','   A large burrow reserved for the nobility of the Ratlings, this private\nwarren is still large enough to accommodate a few dozen of the creatures.\nPersonal objects lie scattered around and fill several of the lower alcoves\nthat honeycomb the walls.  A few small tables and chairs sit about on the\nfloor.  A tunnel leads out to a larger room to the west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35726,0,0,0,'Large Living Area','   A large burrowed room, this living area has a few large alcoves dug into\nthe earthen walls, and the floor is littered with small tables and chairs.  A\nfew heaps of personal belongings, mostly shiny bits of metal and wood objects,\nlie scattered about.  Lit torches hang down from the ceiling on ropes,\nflickering slightly and casting strange shadows.  The burrow continues to the\neast and a curtain hangs over a large hole in the north wall.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35727,0,0,0,'Personal Living Area','   This is a large burrow carved from the earth by the hard work of many small\nclaws.  A few deep alcoves filled with bits of metal, shiney objects, and\npieces of wood are dug into the walls.  A few faded, torn tapestries hang down\nfrom the ceiling.  Torches line the walls, filling the room with a flickering\nlight.  Small tables and chairs, built for creatures only a few feet in height,\nlitter the room.  A small, wooden, rickety throne sits in the very center of\nthis burrow.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35728,0,0,0,'Tunnel Through the Burrow','   This tunnel is large and dark, with the only light sources filtering in\nfrom other tunnels leading north, south, and west.  The torches on the walls\nburnt out long ago and were never replaced.  A foul, rank smell, like that of\nburnt meat and wet fur, drifts about the room.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35729,0,0,0,'Burrow Cooking Area','   The burrow turns into a large, filthy room here.  Almost nothing can be\nseen through the cloud of foul smelling smoke.  Blotches of all colors stain\nthe walls and floor.  All about the cooking area are large, black cauldrons\nsitting on cooking fires.  The cauldrons are filled with a dark, foul, rank\nsmelling stew, and occasionally have a large crude wooden spoon sticking out of\nthem.  A large board lies over a tunnel opening to the west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35730,0,0,0,'Burrow Cooking Area','   The northern part of the cooking area is smoke filled and rank smelling.\nLarge, black cauldrons brew a dark, foul stew while cooking slowly atop small\ncooking fires.  Small shelves hang about the walls, filled with jars, cups, and\njugs, all full of unidentifiable foodstuffs.  A weapon rack leans against the\nnorth wall, but instead of weapons it holds several large wooden spoons.  A\nlarge wooden board lies over a tunnel opening to the west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35731,0,0,0,'Meat Storage Cave','   Partially a dug room and partially a natural cavern, this storage area\ncontains small metal racks and spikes.  On these racks and spikes are hung\nslabs of rotting meat, slowly dripping blood onto the floor.  Rats scurry about\nthe room, biting chunks off of the large pieces closer to the ground.  The\nsmell from the rotting flesh is putrid and rank.  A large board covers a small\ntunnel opening that leads to the east.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35732,0,0,0,'Grain Storage Cave','   Instead of a completely dug tunnel or room, this cavern looks at least\npartially natural.  Water drips from small stalagtites and tiny streams run\ndown the walls.  Large, moldy sacks sit about the room.  Much too complex for\nRatlings, these sacks, full of grain, must have been stolen.  Some of them are\nopen, and a few empty sacks lay in the corner.  A large wooden board lies over\na tunnel opening to the east.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35733,0,0,0,'Sloping Tunnel','   The walls of this tunnel look to have carved out by many small claws.  It\nis almost perfectly round, except for the floor which is somewhat flat.  Large\nbars, crudely carved from wood, stretch down from the ceiling to the floor,\npartially blocking the tunnel as it decends into the earth.  A few small tables\nand chairs sit to either side of the large bars.  The tunnel continues south\nand decends downward.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35734,0,0,0,'Tunnel Through the Burrow','   This small, well kept tunnel leads to the north and to the southwest.\nThe floor and walls have been smoothed out by the passage of many small\ncreatures, and only the ceiling remains slightly rough from the claw marks that\ndug it out.  A few torches flicker on the walls, casting strange shadows about\nthe passageway.  The floor is covered in a matted down carpet of dead grass\nwhich smells slighty rank.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35735,0,0,0,'Tunnel Leading Downward','   The tunnel here leads to the south, and slopes downward to the north.\nThe walls and floor have been smoothed down by the passage of many small\ncreatures, and only the ceiling remains rough from the tiny claws that dug it\nout.  A few torches hang down from the ceiling on ropes, swinging back and\nforth and casting strange shadows about the passageway.  The floor is covered\nin a matted down carpet of dead grass.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35736,0,0,0,'Burrow Guard Post','   A few small tables and chairs lie up against the east wall.  The furniture\nis tiny, obviously ment for a few smaller creatures.  Torches are tied to the\nwall, flickering slightly and casting strange shadows.  The tunnel has been dug\nfrom the earth, and continues to the north while sloping steeply upward to the\nsouth.  The western part of the room seems to be more of a natural cavern then\na burrow, and a thick wooden door blocks a cave entrance to the west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35737,0,0,0,'Fresh Tunnel','   This is a tunnel that has been recently dug from the earth.  The walls,\nfloor and ceiling are covered in claw marks, and have yet to be smoothed down\nby the passage of time and use.  Piles and clumps of dirt lie in small mounds\nnear the walls, waiting to be moved somewhere out of the way.  Whatever dug\nthis tunnel wasn\'t very thorough, as a large crack splits the east wall.  The\ntunnel continues north and south.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35738,0,0,0,'Dead End Tunnel','   The tunnel come to an abrupt end here.  A large slope of dirt leads up to\nthe ceiling, which is covered in claw marks.  The tunnel is being dug out from\nthe top down, and the earth slowly crumbles down the slop into the tunnel to\nthe south.  A torch on a stand provides a small bit of light for whatever is\nburrowing out the earth.  Roots hang down from above, not yet cleared away.\nThe tunnel continues to the south.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35739,0,0,0,'Dark, Dirty Cave','   This small natural cavern lies deep in the earth.  Water drips from\nstalagtites overhead onto the stalagmites below.  The walls are rough and dark,\nand dirt from the floor has gotten everywhere.  The cavern is inhabited by\nsomething, as fur and refuse litters the floor, and a few pieces of rotten\nmeat, swarming with bugs, are stuck on sticks poking up from the ground.  A\nlarge wooden door covers a cave opening to the east, and the cavern continues\nto the north, northwest, and west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35740,0,0,0,'Dark, Dirty Cave','   This is a small natural cavern deep in the earth.  Water drips down from\nthe ceiling to land on rock outcroppings, and slowly seeps through the dirt on\nthe floor.  Something makes this cave their home, as bits of fur, refuse, and\ngarbage litter the floor.  The walls of the cavern are covered in dirt and claw\nmarks.  The cavern continues to the north, northeast, and east.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35741,0,0,0,'Dark, Dirty Cave','   This is a small natural cavern deep in the earth.  The walls of this cave\nare rough and dirty, and are covered in small claw marks.  Large stalagtites\nhang from the ceiling, slowly dripping water down to the floor, creating mud\nout of packed dirt.  This is obviously the lair of something, as bits of fur,\ngarbage, and rotten meat lie scattered about.  The cavern continues to the\nwest, southwest, and south.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35742,0,0,0,'Dark, Dirty Cave','This is a small natural cavern deep in the earth.  Large stalagtites\nslowly drip water down through the air until the splash on the large stalamites\nand seep into the floor.  The walls of the cave are dirty and covered in small\nclaw marks.  Trash, fur, and refuse lie scattered about everywhere, and small\nbits of rotten meat are swarming with small insects.  The cave continues to the\neast, southwest, and south.\n',0,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35743,0,0,0,'Tunnel to the Deep Burrow','   The tunnel here is smooth from the passage of many small feet, with only\nthe ceiling being a bit on the rough side.  The tunnel leads to the north, and\nto the south the tunnel slopes upward into a slanted spiraling ramp that goes\nalmost fifty feet to the level above.  Small flickering torches are tied to the\nwalls, which provide enough light to see normally.  Several wooden poles stick\nout of the ground topped with rat skulls.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35744,0,0,0,'Burrow Common Room','   This large room has been burrowed from the earth by many small claws, the\nmarks of which still cover the upper walls and ceiling.  The lower walls and\nfloor have been worn flat with the passing of many small feet.  Tiny, rickety\nfurniture litters the floor everywhere.  Tables, chairs, benches, and stools\nall lie scattered about.  The room continues to the east, and tunnels lead\nnorth and south.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35745,0,0,0,'Large Burrow','   This burrow has been dug from the earth by many small claws, the marks of\nwhich are still evident on the walls and ceiling.  Tiny alcoves honeycomb the\nentire burrow, each of which contains fur, a torn, dirty rug, and even tiny\nweapon racks.  Ladders, small stairs, and ropes with knots provide access to\nall the alcoves.  A few torches on the end of ropes hang down from the ceiling,\ncasting flicking light about the area.  A tunnel leads to the south.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35746,0,0,0,'Burrow Common Room','   This room has been carved from the earth by the work of many small claws.\nClaw marks cover the ceiling and upper walls, but the floor is smooth and\npacked.  Tiny pieces of furniture litter the floor, which include tables,\nchairs, benches, and stools.  Fur and garbage cover the area, and a rank smell\ndrifts up from the floor.  A few torches on the end of ropes hang down from the\nceiling, providing a flickering light.  The room continues to the west, and\ntunnels lead north, east, and south.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35747,0,0,0,'Large Burrow','   This large burrow has been dug from the earth by the work of many small\nclaws, the marks of which are still evident on the upper walls and ceiling.\nThe walls are honeycombed with dozens of tiny alcoves.  Each alcove contains\nbits of fur, a dirty rug, some hay, and even small weapon racks.  Wooden\nladders, stairs, and ropes with knots provide access to all the alcoves in the\nroom.  A few torches are tied to the walls, and they cast about a flickering\nlight.  A tunnel leads out to the south.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35748,0,0,0,'Empty Cave','   Water drips down the walls of this natural cave.  A dug out tunnel leads in\nfrom the west, and several patches of earth have been cleared away by tiny\nclaws in an attempt to make this room a burrow.  The majority of the walls are\nstill natural, and large stalagtites and stalagmites litter the floor and\nceiling.  A tiny stream collects in the center of the room and flows into a\nhole in the south wall.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35749,0,0,0,'Large Tunnel','   The floor of this large tunnel is hard and packed down from the passage of\nmany small feet.  Claw marks from whatever dug this tunnel are still evident on\nthe ceiling and upper walls.  Fur and bits of garbage lie scattered about, and\na slightly rank smell drifts in from the north.  Torches line the walls, at\nleast ten tied to each side, lighting up the entire tunnel.  The tunnel travels\nnorth and south.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35750,0,0,0,'Decorated Guard Post','   This large tunnel has been dug from the earth by many small claws.  It\ncontinues to the north, and in the southern part of the tunnel it spirals\ndownwards almost fifty feet.  Large wooden poles are set into the floor and\nreach up to the ceiling, dividing the tunnel in two, although there is enough\nspace between them to go back and forth.  Ripped tapestries, shiney objects,\nand other stolen goods are tied to the poles.  A large ammount of fur covers\nthe southern part of the tunnel near the decline.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35751,0,0,0,'Burrow Harem','   This large room has been dug from the earth, and is smooth and even.\nEarthen walkways lead in between several large alcoves set into the floor.\nEach alcove contains a few personal items, a blanket of loose fur, and a dirty\nrug.  Torches are tied to wooden poles sticking up from the walkways, and they\ncast a flickering light about the area.  The room continues west, southwest,\nand south, and a tunnel leads east.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35752,0,0,0,'Burrow Harem','   This large burrow has been carefully carved from the earth, leaving the\nwalls and ceiling smooth and even.  Earthen walkways lead in between several\nlarge alcoves that have been dug into the floor.  Each of the alcoves is\ncarpeted in loose fur, as well as containing shiney objects and a dirty, torn\nrug.  Torches are tied to wooden poles that stick up out of the walkways, and\nthey cast a flickering light about the area.  The room continues east,\nsoutheast, and south.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35753,0,0,0,'Burrow Harem','   This large burrow has been dug from the earth with precision and care,\nleaving the dirt walls smooth, packed, and even.  Large earthen walkways lead\nin between several deep alcoves set into the floor.  Each alcove has a small\nstaircase leading down into it, and contains a carpet of loose fur, a dirty\nrug, and a few shiney, worthless objects.  Torches are tied to wooden poles\nthat stick out at angles from the dirt walls.  The room continues north,\nnortheast, and east, and a tunnel leads to the south.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35754,0,0,0,'Burrow Harem','   This large room has been dug from the earth by the hard work of many small\nclaws.  Time and precision were taken to make sure the dirt walls became and\nstayed smooth and even.  Several earthen walkways lead in between wide alcoves\nset into the floor.  Each alcove contains a carpet of loose fur, a dirty, torn\nrug, and a few shiney objects.  Lit torches are tied to poles that stick up out\nof the walkways, and they cast a flickering dull light about the area.  The\nroom continues north, northwest, and west, and small tunnels lead off to the\neast, southeast, and south.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35755,0,0,0,'Royal Burrow Living Area','   The walls and ceiling of the large dirt burrow have been dug with care and\nprecision, leaving them smooth and even.  Several sets of tiny furniture lie\nscattered about on the dirt floor, resting on top of a thick carpet of loose\nfur.  In the very center of the room there is a wide, shallow pit.  The bottom\nof the pit is stained with blood and other bodily fluids.  Tunnels lead out of\nthis burrow to the east, south, and west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35756,0,0,0,'Ratling Midwives Quarters','   A large carpet of fur covers the dirt floor in this burrow.  The walls and\nceiling have been dug out with precision and care, leaving them smooth and\neven.  The floor, however, has seen a great deal of use and is covered in loose\ndirt.  Alcoves are set into the walls, each containing dirty rugs and small\nshiney objects.  A few torn up baskets lie in the corner.  Tunnels lead off to\nthe north, northwest, and west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35757,0,0,0,'Harem Nursery','   Small droppings and spilled milk litter the floor in this large burrow.\nThe dirt walls and ceiling have been dug out with care and precision, leaving\nthem smooth and even.  Large baskets hang down from the ceiling everywhere on\nropes.  Torches are tied to the walls, casting flickering shadows about the\nroom.  A rank smell drifts up from the floor.  Tunnels lead off to the north\nand east.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35758,0,0,0,'Royal Chamber','   This large burrow has been dug from the earth by many small claws.  Much\ntime and precision was put into the excavation, so the dirt walls are packed,\nsmooth, and even.  The dirt floor can barely be seen beneath the thick carpet\nof loose fur.  A single deep, wide alcove has been dug into the south wall.\nInside the alcove there is a torn rug, several small pieces of furniture, and a\nlarge pile of shiney junk.  Many lit torches are tied to the walls, at least\nten on each side, lighting up the entire area.  A small tunnel leads out to the\nnorth.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35759,0,0,0,'Smooth Tunnel Through the Royal Burrow','   This tunnel intersection is wide enough for several large creatures, and\ndozens of tiny ones.  Time and effort were taken to make sure the dirt walls\nand ceiling are kept smooth and even.  A thick carpet of fur covers the floor\neverywhere.  Many lit torches are tied to the walls, at least a dozen on each\nside, and they light up the entire area.  The tunnel continues to the east,\nsouth, and west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35760,0,0,0,'Royal Burrow Kitchen','   The smooth dirt walls of this large burrow are stained with smoke and\ncovered in ash.  Large iron pots sit on top of hot cooking fires, each bubbling\nhot water and cooking some type of food.  Smoke from the fires fills the air,\nand the rank smell of whatever is cooking permeates the area.  In the corner of\nthe room there is a large pile of uncooked meat and grain.  A large wooden door\ncovers a tunnel leading south, and more tunnels lead off to the north,\nnorthwest, and west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35761,0,0,0,'Royal Food Storage','   This huge burrow has been dug from the earth by many small claws.  Time and\neffort were taken to make sure the walls and ceiling were smooth and even.\nLarge metal racks lie about the room on rocks.  Piles of raw meat sit on top of\nthe racks, dripping blood and goo onto the floor.  Sacks of grain lie stacked\nup in the corner.  A wooden door covers a tunnel leading north.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35762,0,0,0,'Royal Burrow Chambers','   A thick carpet of loose fur covers the floor in this large burrow.\nWhatever dug this room from the earth took care and presicion to make sure the\ndirt walls and ceiling were smooth and even.  A large table, built for small\ncreatures, dominates the center of the burrow.  Dozens of small rickety chairs\nlie scattered about.  Stains from food and bodily fluids cover the tiny\nfurniture and walls.  A slight but distinct rank smell drifts in from\nsomewhere.  A tunnel leads west, and the room continues to the north.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35763,0,0,0,'Royal Burrow Throne Room','   This large burrow has been carved from the earth, and the ceiling reaches up\nalmost fifty feet.  Time and effort have been taken to make sure the walls and\ndirt floor are kept smooth and even.  The floor is barely visible through a\nthick carpet of loose fur.  A wide, smooth mound of earth sits in the center of\nthe room, and on top of it is a small, well built wooden throne.  Torches are\ntied to long wooden poles that stick up out of the walls at odd angles.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35764,0,0,0,'Silent Cave','   Water drips down from the walls and ceiling of this large natural cavern.\nStalagtites and stalagmites litter the floor and the ceiling.  Dust and dirt\nlie about in piles on the floor.  Some effort has been taken to carve a small\nstaircase along the wall that twists upwards almost fifty feet to a ledge\nabove.  Other then a few tiny footprints, the floor is generally undisturbed.\nA faint smell of must drifts up from the floor.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35765,0,0,0,'Ledge in a Silent Cave','   Echoes of water slowly dripping down the walls and off of stalagtites sound\nloudly all about this large, natural cavern.  A small ledge hangs out over the\ncave floor which lies fifty feet down.  A staircase starts at the ledge and\nwinds and twists its way down the wall to the floor below.  Small piles of dirt\nand dust are scattered about, mostly undisturbed except for a few tiny\nfootprints.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35766,0,0,0,'Large, Smooth Tunnel','   This tunnel has been dug from the earth.  Whatever dug it took time and\neffort to make the dirt walls smooth, packed, and even.  A large ammount of\nfur, easily as thick as a carpet, litters the floor everywhere.  Crude\npaintings and colorful stains cover the walls.  Torches line the sides of the\ntunnel everywhere, at least ten tied to each side.  Tunnels lead off to the\neast, southeast, and west.  Another tunnel that spirals upwards leads out from\nthe north wall.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35767,0,0,0,'Rat\'s Nest','   Covered in hair and droppings, this burrow is the nest to a family of\nrats.  Small rat holes cover the walls in all directions.  Movement can readily\nbe seen in the holes, dashing behind the earthen walls from one hole to the\nnext.  Occasionally a rat can be seen inside a hole sniffing around and looking\nabout with its beady eyes.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35768,0,0,0,'Large Burrow Warren','   The burrow tunnel ends here in a large, round warren.  The walls are\nhoneycombed with many small alcoves, each the home of one or two small\ncreatures.  Torches are tied to the walls in several places, casting light\nabout the room and creating flickering shadows.  Tiny tables and chairs litter\nthe floor.  Small ladders and ropes with knots lead up the walls, providing\naccess to each of the alcoves.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35769,0,0,0,'Lower Burrow Warrens','   The walls of this tunnel are completely honeycombed with many small\nalcoves, each the home of one or two small creatures.  The alcoves are full of\nfur, the occasional personal object, and even a dropping or two.  Tiny tables\nand chairs litter the floor.  Ropes with knots lead up to a large hole in the\nceiling which leads to the warrens above.  The tunnels continue to the north,\neast, and west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35770,0,0,0,'Lower Burrow Warrens','   This tunnel is honeycombed with small alcoves, each the home of one or two\ntiny creatures.  Steps, ladders, and ropes with knots are everywhere, providing\naccess to each of the alcoves.  Torches hang down from the ceiling on ropes,\nflickering slightly and casting strange shadows.  Little tables and chairs,\nonly big enough for something two or three feet in height, litter the floor.\nThe tunnel continues east and west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35771,0,0,0,'Lower Burrow Warrens','   This large tunnel leads north and east.  The walls here are honeycombed\nwith many small alcoves, each the home of a few tiny creatures.  Tables and\nchairs, only large enough for creatures two or three feet in height, litter the\nfloor.  Torches hang down from the ceiling on hemp ropes, swinging back and\nforth and casting flickering shadows about the room.  Piles of fur lie\nscattered about.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35772,0,0,0,'Lower Burrow Warrens','   The warren tunnels continue to the north, northwest, and south.  The walls\nhere are honeycombed with many small alcoves, each the home of a few tiny\ncreatures.  Tables and chairs, each the size for something only a few feet in\nheight, litter the room everywhere.  Torches tied to ropes hang down from the\nceiling and swing slightly, casting their flickering light about the room.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35773,0,0,0,'Lower Burrow Warrens','   This large burrow is rank and full of garbage.  The walls here are\ncompletely honeycombed with many small alcoves, each the home of one or two\nsmall creatures.  Steps, ladders, and ropes with knots cover the room,\nproviding access to each of the alcoves, and a few ropes lead up through a hole\nin the ceiling.  Flickering torches are tied to the walls, and they cast a\nfeint light about the room.  Tunnels lead off to the north and west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35774,0,0,0,'Large Storage Room','   This is a large, burrowed room that is obviously ment for storage.  The\nceiling is about thirty feet up, and the walls are lined with wooden shelves.\nThe shelves are full of foodstuffs, mostly chopped mushrooms that smell like\nrefuse.  Small ladders and ropes with knots lead up to each of the shelves.\nTorches hang down from the ceiling on ropes, casting flickering light about the\nroom.  Tunnels lead to the north, east, and south.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35775,0,0,0,'Lower Burrow Warrens','   The walls of this tunnel warren are completely honeycombed with small\nalcoves, each the home of one or two tiny creatures.  Ladders and ropes with\nknots cover the walls, providing access to each of the alcoves.  Tables and\nchairs, old and rickety and only big enough for a creature 2 or 3 feet tall,\nlitter the floor.  Torches hanging down from the ceiling on ropes cast\nflickering light about the room, creating strange shadows.  The tunnel\ncontinues south and west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35776,0,0,0,'Lower Burrow Warrens','   Tiny alcoves honeycomb the walls of this warren tunnel, each the home of\none or two small creatures.  Ladders, small steps, and ropes with knots cover\nthe walls providing access to each of the alcoves.  Little tables and chairs,\neach only big enough for a creature perhaps two and a half feet tall, litter\nthe floor.  Torches hanging from the ceiling on ropes swing back and forth,\ncasting strange shadows about the room.  The tunnel continues to the east,\nsoutheast, south, and west.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35777,0,0,0,'Large Cave','   Dripping water and shadows characterize this large natural cavern.\nTunnels dug from the earth open up in the east and south walls.  Stalagtites\nand stalagmites fill the cave.  Several small paths lead from the tunnels\nfurther into the cave to the west.  A rank smell, like that of rotting refuse,\ndrifts in and floats about.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35778,0,0,0,'Mushroom Farm','   This is the southernmost part of a huge natural cavern.  The floor here is\ncovered in large mushrooms, from one to two feet in height.  Small paths snake\ninbetween the mushroom patches, which grow everywhere.  Stalagtites hang down\nfrom the ceiling, however the stalagmites have been cleared away for the\nmushrooms.  The refuse that the mushrooms grow in stinks up the room.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35779,0,0,0,'Underground Spring','   The southwestern part of this huge cavern is filled with a small lake\nwhich is fed from an underground stream that trickles out of a wall.  A small\nunderground river flows slowly to the north.  A few patches of mushrooms grow\nabout on the dry land, on top of piles of refuse.  A foul smell drifts up from\nthe ground and floats around.\n',280,131080,29,0,0,0,0,0,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35780,0,0,0,'Mushroom Farm','   This is the northeast corner of a large natural cavern.  The floor here is\ncovered in piles of refuse, and out of each small mound grows several large\nmushrooms.  The once mightly stalagmites have been broken down to stumps to\nallow more room for the mushrooms.  Paths lead inbetween many of the mushroom\npatches.  A small stream flows in from the west providing water for the\nmushroom farm, and then dissappears down a small hole near the east wall.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35781,0,0,0,'Mushroom Farm','   This is the northern part of a huge natural cavern.  The floor here has\nbeen somewhat leveled, and the large stalagmites have been broken down to mere\nstumps.  The ground is covered in piles of refuse, and out of each small mound\ngrows several large mushrooms.  Paths lead inbetween the flattened stalagmites\nand mushroom patches, providing access to all of them.  Small streams flow in\nfrom the west providing water for the mushroom farm.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35782,0,0,0,'Underground River','   Along the western wall of this huge cavern there flows a small underground\nriver.  It snakes it way inbetween several stalagmite stumps that are now\ncovered in patches of mushrooms.  Small streams lead off from the main river,\nirrigating the mushroom farms to the east.  Water condenses all over the walls,\nand it slowly drips down to the floor.  The river continues to flow to the\nnorth.\n',280,131080,29,0,0,0,0,2,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35783,0,0,0,'Refuse Pile','   This large underground cavern is almost completely full with a pile of\nrefuse.  Garbage, trash, and waste all lie piled up in a huge mound.  Several\ngiant mushrooms grow about the pile, and smaller ones grow in patches on the\ncavern floor.  An underground river flows in from the south but quickly turns\ninto the western wall and disappears.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35784,0,0,0,'Dark Tunnel','This small tunnel has been dug from the earth by small claws, and the walls,\nceiling and floor are still rough and uneven, covered in claw marks.  Loose\ndirt is everywhere, and dust covers everything.  Except for a few small\nfootprints in the dust, this tunnel has seen little use.  A few unlit torches\nhang down from the ceiling on ropes.  The tunnel leads north and northwest, and\nto the south it leads into a natural cave wall.\n',0,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35785,0,0,0,'Small Treasure Room','This small burrow has been dug from the hard earth by the work of many small\nclaws.  The walls and ceiling are still rough and covered in claw marks, and\nthe floor is covered in dust.  A few small footprints disturb the dust on parts\nof the floor.  Torches hang down from the ceiling on ropes, and while they have\nbeen lit in the past, they aren\'t lit now.  A small tunnel leads out to the\nsouthwest.\n',0,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35786,0,0,0,'Dark Tunnel','   This small, dark tunnel leads south and northeast.  It has been dug from the\npacked earth by the hard work of many small claws.  The walls, ceiling, and\nfloor of this round tunnel are still rough and uneven, and covered in claw\nmarks.  Piles of loose dirt sit around, and dust covers everything with the\nexception of a few small footprints.  Unused torches are tied to wooden poles\nsticking out of the walls.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35787,0,0,0,'Wide Dark Tunnel','   The small tunnel that leads in from the southwest widens slightly into a\nsmall room.  The walls, ceiling, and floor are covered in claw marks.  Garbage\nand refuse lie about, pushed into piles away from the north wall.  A few burnt\nout torches are tied to small iron rods that have been dug into the walls.  On\nthe north wall there is a tiny, round wooden door.  A rank smell drifts up from\nthe ground.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35788,0,0,0,'Treasure Room','   This large room has been dug from the earth by many small claws.  The walls\nand ceiling are rough and uneven, and covered in claw marks.  The floor has\nbeen smoothed over, but it is coated with a thick layer of dust.  Several large\nchests sit about the room, pushed up against the north wall.  Unlit torches\nhang down from the ceiling on ropes.  A tiny, round wooden door leads out to\nthe south.  \n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35789,0,0,0,'Top of a Deep, Hot Cavern','   This natural cave is large, wide, and twists down into the earth hundreds of\nfeet.  A dull, red glow comes up from the bottom of the cave, casting deep red\nshadows about the cavern walls.  A small ledge turns into an almost natural\nlooking staircase that leads downwards.  Small streams of water drip out of the\nwalls, quickly turning to steam and gathering near the top of the cavern.\n',280,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35790,0,0,0,'River Of Lava','   A wide, super heated river of lava flows through the bottom of this huge\nnatural cavern.  The red glowing magma rock casts a dull red light all around,\nleaving strange reddish black shadows.  Above, a ledge can be seen, from which\nan almost natural looking staircase slowly twists and turns down the cavern\nwall to the floor.  A few rock deltas sit here and there in the molten river\nwith rock bridges leading in between them.  Small drops of water instantly turn\ninto steam as they drip down from above.\n',280,131080,49,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(35791,0,0,0,'Dirt Path','This small dirt path is covered in small patches of grass.  Several shrubs\nand weeds lie along the edges of the path near the southwest, where it leads to\na wide dirt road.  Small plants and flowers grow to either side of the path,\nand small fields of grass stretch out to the northwest and southeast.  The path\ncontinues to the northeast.\n',-1,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35792,0,0,0,'Dirt Path','   This small dirt path is rough and uneven, and small patches of grass stick\nup here and there.  All around the path there are weeds and and colorful\nflowers.  Several small, clawed footprints lie about in the soft dirt, going in\nboth directions.  Fields of grass stretch out to the northwest and southeast.\nThe path continues to the northeast and southwest.\n',280,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35793,0,0,0,'Dirt Path','   This dirt path is somewhat rough and uneven, and small patches of a tall\ngrass stick up out of the path\'s surface here and there.  The path is\nsurrounded on all sides by weeds and colorful flowers.  Small fields of plants\nstretch east and west.  The dusty dirt path continues to the northwest and\nsouthwest.\n',280,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35794,0,0,0,'Dirt Path','   This small dirt path is somewhat rough and uneven, and small patches of\nplants stick up out of the path\'s surface.  Tall grasses and colorful flowers\nsurround the path on all sides.  Tiny, clawed footprints litter the area, going\nback and forth.  Fields of grass stretch out to the east and west.  The path\nleads north and southeast.\n',280,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35795,0,0,0,'Dirt Path','   This rough, uneven dirt path is covered in small patches of grass and\nsurrounded by small plants and colorful flowers.  Tiny clawed footfrints lie\neverywhere in the dirt, traveling back and forth on the path.  Fields of plants\nand weeds grow out to the east and west.  The dirt path continues to the\nnortheast and south.\n',280,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35796,0,0,0,'Dirt Path','   This small dirt path is rough and uneven, and patches of weeds grow up out\nof the path\'s surface.  Tall grasses and colorful flowers surround the path on\nboth sides.  Tiny clawed footprints lie scattered about in the soft dirt.\nFields of small plants stretch out to the east and west.  The path continues to\nthe northeast and southwest.\n',280,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(35797,0,0,0,'Dirt Path','   This small dirt path leads to the north, and turns slightly to the\nsouthwest.  Small clumps of green grass and weeds stick up out of the dirt\nsurface in several places.  Plants and colorful flowers surround the path on\nall sides.  Tiny insects make chirping noises and jump back and forth between\nthe ground and the plants.  A very faint skittering noise can be heard coming\nfrom the north.\n',280,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(36350,0,0,0,'A Raging Underground River','The current of this river is quite strong and the water is moving rather\nquickly. The stone walls are incredibly smooth and are speckled with \npatches of glistening metallic ore. There is very little clearance above \nthe water and what air may be found is quickly dispersed by the splashing\nof the current. ',0,8,53,0,0,0,-106,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36351,0,0,0,'A Raging Underground River','The current of this river is quite strong and the water is moving rather\nquickly. The stone walls are incredibly smooth and are speckled with \npatches of glistening metallic ore. There is very little clearance above \nthe water and what air may be found is quickly dispersed by the splashing\nof the current. \n',0,8,53,0,0,0,-106,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36352,0,0,0,'A Raging Underground River','The current of this river is quite strong and the water is moving rather\nquickly. The stone walls are incredibly smooth and are speckled with \npatches of glistening metallic ore. There is very little clearance above \nthe water and what air may be found is quickly dispersed by the splashing\nof the current. \n',0,8,53,0,0,0,-106,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36353,0,0,0,'A Raging Underground River','The current of this river is quite strong and the water is moving rather\nquickly. The stone walls are incredibly smooth and are speckled with \npatches of glistening metallic ore. There is very little clearance above \nthe water and what air may be found is quickly dispersed by the splashing\nof the current. ',0,8,53,0,0,0,44,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36354,0,0,0,'Massive Stone Grate','Water gushes at you through the holes of this enormous stone grate. Though\nobviously at a danger of erosion, the grate appears well maintained and\nshows a good deal of craftsmanship. It is obviously the product of a meticulous\nand experienced stone cutter.\n',0,8,52,0,0,0,10,8,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(36355,0,0,0,'A Raging Underground River','The current of this river is quite strong and the water is moving rather\nquickly. The stone walls are incredibly smooth and are speckled with \npatches of glistening metallic ore. There is very little clearance above \nthe water and what air may be found is quickly dispersed by the splashing\nof the current. ',0,8,53,0,0,0,44,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36356,0,0,0,'Tunnel Through Molten Lava','The walls and ceiling of this hallway are flowing, molten lava. Magic appears\nto be preventing the lava from rushing in towards the center, melting both the\nroom\'s occupants and the rock path the occupants may be standing on.\nSurprisingly,\nit is uncomfortable to be in this room but not unbearable. Though the obvious\ndangers in the room are a little unsettling.\n',0,4105,56,0,0,0,88,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36357,0,0,0,'Brick-walled Antechamber','Large bricks carved from grey rock have been used to wall in this area. The\nentire ceiling and parts of the floor have been covered with long, deadly-\nlooking spikes that point inward. Flecks of blood, or rust, decorate some of\nthe spikes on the floor to the north. This might be the only adorning feature\nin the room. The door to the west is quite warm to the touch, but the air \ncoming through the arch that forms the door to the east is clammy and smells\nmusty.\n',0,8,56,0,0,0,88,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36358,0,0,0,'A Cavernous Underground Room','In the middle of this immense room is a huge pedestal, much wider than it is\ntall. On the floor around the pedastal is a thick carpet of partial skeletons,\nwhich is occassionally mixed with small treasures that have been bespoiled by \nvarious kinds of carrion and other filth. The room is truly awful to behold. \nA stone door is set in the eastern wall.\n',0,8,56,0,0,0,88,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36359,0,0,0,'A Foul-smelling Treasure Room','Mismatched tapestries of various sizes decorate the walls of this room. Though it\nis quite apparent that they were not meant to hang here. The floor of this room is\ncoated in a sticky layer of blood. The remains of the guards that once protected \nthis treasure lay on the floor. Consequently, the air in here is rancid.\n',0,8,56,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36360,0,0,0,'A Musty Underground Prison','There is little to note about this room. Its walls are made of grey brick cut\nfrom\nthe existing wall, with the exception of the eastern wall. The eastern wall\nresembles\nthe bars of a prison cell.\n',0,8,56,0,0,0,118,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36361,0,0,0,'A Prison Cell','The stone floor of this cell glistens with what is probably urine. This is mostly reinforced by the emanating smell. The wall to the west is mainly composed of iron bars. The remaining walls are natural and have been carved to a flat, but not polished surface. Each of the stone walls is home to at least one pair of manacles. There is little evidence of torture. Perhaps the owner of the cell merely wants to possess his prisoners.\n',0,8,56,0,0,0,-18,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36362,0,0,0,'Quiet Marble Hall','This is the ground floor of the tower of the gnomish king Gnumble. Several\npillars ascend to the ceiling of this room, which is large and open by gnome\nstandards. Most of the time, this hall is rather silent.\n',0,8,21,0,0,0,-18,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(36363,0,0,0,'Quiet Marble Hall','This is the ground floor of the tower of the gnomish king Gnumble. Several\npillars ascend to the ceiling of this room, which is large and open by gnome\nstandards. Most of the time, this hall is rather silent.\n',0,131072,21,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(36364,0,0,0,'Quiet Marble Hall','This is the ground floor of the tower of the gnomish king Gnumble. Several\npillars ascend to the ceiling of this room, which is large and open by gnome\nstandards. Most of the time, this hall is rather silent.\n',0,8,21,0,0,0,-18,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(36365,0,0,0,'Quiet Marble Hall','This is the ground floor of the tower of the gnomish king Gnumble. Several\npillars ascend to the ceiling of this room, which is large and open by gnome\nstandards. Most of the time, this hall is rather silent.\n',0,8,21,0,0,0,-18,0,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(36366,0,0,0,'The Mouth of a Large Cave','The tunnel that the river flows through opens up into a cave that, while\nlarge, feels much larger compared to the cramped walls of the tunnel. Here,\nthe current slows as the banks of the river seperate. Comparatively quieter\nthan the tunnel to the west, this area is flooded with the noise of a\nconstant crashing that echoes in from the east.',0,8,52,0,0,0,-18,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36367,0,0,0,'A Gigantic Underground Waterfall','The water rolling in from the west floods here for a moment leisurely before\nit plummets down for what must be stories. Above the fall rises a nigh cavernous\nceiling covered in small stalagtites. This water way must have been formed by\na bizarre series of sinkholes and fissures. Given the noise in this room, this\nmust be high above the place where fall ends.\n',0,8,52,0,0,0,-80,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36368,0,0,0,'Down a Gigantic Underground Waterfall','Water rushes in from above with incredible force. In combination with a \ncomplete lack of light, the loud crash of water below becomes quite \ndisorienting, even for those that do not need light to see. If not for the \nobvious presence of gravity, the inherent stir of this place builds a sense\nof unrest. It seems that such a place could drive even the most peaceful \nbeing into a furious rage.\n',0,8,52,0,0,0,-80,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36369,0,0,0,'A Narrow Tunnel','This tunnel is quite narrow and the ceilings are remarkably low, even for the\nstandards of the gnomes that carved them. There is little of note here. Clearly,\nthis tunnel was meant to serve a purpose, as very little effort has gone into\nmaking it presentable.\n',0,8,56,0,0,0,-80,0,11,38,0,'',NULL),
(36370,0,0,0,'A Narrow Tunnel','This tunnel is quite narrow and the ceilings are remarkably low, even for the\nstandards of the gnoems that carved them. There is little of note here. Clearly,\nthis tunnel was meant to serve a purpose, as very little effort has gone into\nmaking it presentable. The tunnel angles downward sharply to the west and\na light glow emanates from the east.\n',0,8,56,0,0,0,-80,0,11,38,0,'',NULL),
(36371,0,0,0,'A Narrow Descending Tunnel','The walls of this tunnel have been carefully carved out with a small digging\ntool. There is only enough room for one climber to crawl through it at a time, and even\nthen it is a tight squeeze.  Small supports every few feet prevent the tunnel from\ncollapsing, though they appear to bow under the rock’s weight. The angle of descent is\nso near to vertical as to be perilous to a climber.\n',0,8,58,0,0,0,-80,0,11,38,0,'',NULL),
(36372,0,0,0,'A Narrow Descending Tunnel','The walls of this tunnel have been carefully carved out with a small digging\ntool. There\nis only enough room for one person to crawl through it at a time, and even then\nit is a tight squeeze.  Small supports every few feet prevent the tunnel from\ncollapsing,\nthough they appear to bow under the rock\'s weight. The angle of descent is so\nnear to vertical\nas to be perilous.\n',0,8,58,0,0,0,-80,0,11,38,0,'',NULL),
(36373,0,0,0,'A Narrow Descending Tunnel','The walls of this tunnel have been carefully carved out with a small digging\ntool. There\nis only enough room for one person to crawl through it at a time, and even then\nit is a tight squeeze.  Small supports every few feet prevent the tunnel from\ncollapsing,\nthough they appear to bow under the rock\'s weight. The angle of descent is so\nnear to vertical\nas to be perilous.\n',0,8,58,0,0,0,-80,0,1,38,0,'',NULL),
(36374,0,0,0,'The Top of a Colossal Tower','It is likely there is no position higher than this that is attainable by means\nnot magical in nature. The air here is thin, cold, and biting. It is, at first,\ndifficult to get your bearings due to the ferocious wind. Were it nof for\nsufficiently protective parapets, the chance of being swept off the tower\nwould be too high for many souls to dare. Much of The World is visible from this\ntower. Unfortunately, even some of the largest landmarks appear miniscule\nfrom this height.\n',0,8192,14,0,0,0,-80,0,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
(36375,0,0,0,'The Bottom of a Gigantic Underground Waterfall','The sound of this room is terrifying! Huge amounts of water pour in from\nabove and crash into the natural stone floor, filling the room with sprays\nof warm water. Centuries of this has worn away at the stone and created\na well beneath the waterfall. The river widens and slows as it continues to \nthe east, but not before the force of the current drags anything floating\nbeneath the surface.\n',0,4168,52,0,0,0,-80,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36376,0,0,0,'A Well Beneath a Gigantic Underground Waterfall','The current in this room is tumultuous and circles around as the waterfall\nfalls from above and cycles back to the surface. Unfortunately, any item\nor person caught in this undertow has the misfortune of being her for a while.\nDue to the circling, debris clouds the water in this natural room. A thick\nlayer of indeterminable junk coats the bottom and clutters this natural\nphenomenon. \n',0,4168,53,0,0,0,44,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36377,0,0,0,'A Slow, Wide Underground River','The river here lazily flows in from the west, where loud sounds of water\ncrashing can be heard. As those sounds fade, sounds of drumming are\npicked up from downriver to the east. Occassionaly wakes made by fish \nmove across the surface of the water. Bones and other remnants from\nvictims of some sad fate carpet the bottom of the river here.\n',0,4168,52,0,0,0,-106,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36378,0,0,0,'A Slow, Wide Underground River','The river here lazily flows in from the west, where loud sounds of water\ncrashing can be heard. As those sounds fade, sounds of drumming are\npicked up from downriver to the east. Occassionaly wakes made by fish \nmove across the surface of the water. Bones and other remnants from\nvictims of some sad fate carpet the bottom of the river here.\n',0,4168,52,0,0,0,-106,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36379,0,0,0,'A Rocky, Subterranean Shore','Jagged rocks hide just under the surface of this subterranean beach and appear\nas the water slowly dissolves into the loose gravel shore. It appears as if the\nriver once continued to the east. However, a large portion of the north wall has been removed to create a mouth into another section of cave. All that remains to the east now is the huge pile of stones that was once the northern wall.\n',0,4168,56,0,0,0,-106,0,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36380,0,0,0,'A Crude Antechamber','Ornaments of bone decorate the walls and ceiling of this small room. A basin \nof water sits on the packed gravel floor along the western wall. Though the room\nshows signs of use, the placement of objects suggests a certain sense of\nreverance, as mostly everything in this room appears to have gone untouched\nfor some time. \n',0,4168,56,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36381,0,0,0,'A Subterranean Hall','The lights of torches hung on the wall cast macabre shadows through\nthe many bone ornaments that adorn this hall and hang from its ceiling.\nThe walls are covered in rotting pelts taken from animals of all kinds. Among\nthem are bits of long, thick white hair that catch your eye. Drumming\ncan be heard from the end of the hall to the north.\n',0,4105,56,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36382,0,0,0,'A Subterranean Hall','The lights of torches hung on the wall cast macabre shadows through\nthe many bone ornaments that adorn this hall and hang from its ceiling.\nThe walls are covered in rotting pelts taken from animals of all kinds. Among\nthem are bits of long, thick white hair that catch your eye. Drumming\ncan be heard from the end of the hall to the north.\n',0,4105,56,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36383,0,0,0,'A Subterranean Hall','The lights of torches hung on the wall cast macabre shadows through\nthe many bone ornaments that adorn this hall and hang from its ceiling.\nThe walls are covered in rotting pelts taken from animals of all kinds. Among\nthem are bits of long, thick white hair that catch your eye. Drumming\ncan be heard from the end of the hall to the north.\n',0,4105,56,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36384,0,0,0,'A Subterranean Hall','The lights of torches hung on the wall cast macabre shadows through\nthe many bone ornaments that adorn this hall and hang from its ceiling.\nthe walls are covered in rotting pelts taken from animals of all kinds. Among\nthem are bits of long, thick white hair that catch your eye. Drumming\ncan be heard through the door to the west.\n',0,4105,56,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36385,0,0,0,'A Large Stone Hall','This room has been carved out of an existing underground cave. The walls\nhave been given a smooth finish, but they still bear many tool\nmarks. The ceiling is tall and the light created by braziers that line\nthe walls does not reach it. Though the lower portion of the room is well lit,\nit is quite an ominous place.\n',0,4105,56,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36386,0,0,0,'Long, Steep Spiral Stairs','This staircase leads to the top of King Gnumble\'s tower. The marble stairs are\nsteep\nby gnome standards and the banister is awkwardly low for any of the taller\noccupants of The World. The stairs themselves are slightly worn, suggesting\nquite\na bit of traffic.\n',0,4105,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(36387,0,0,0,'Long, Steep Spiral Stairs','This staircase leads to the throne room of King Gnumble’s tower. The marble stairs are\nsteep by gnome standards and the banister is awkwardly low for any of the taller\noccupants of The World. The stairs themselves are slightly worn, suggesting\nquite a bit of traffic.\n',0,4105,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(36388,0,0,0,'Long, Steep Spiral Stairs','This staircase leads to the throne room of King Gnumble’s tower. The marble stairs are\nsteep by gnome standards and the banister is awkwardly low for any of the taller\noccupants of The World. The stairs themselves are slightly worn, suggesting\nquite a bit of traffic.\n',0,4105,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(36389,0,0,0,'Tiny Maintenance Closet','This small room is little more than an alcove used for storage by the\nstaff of gnomes charged with the castle\'s upkeep. A small registry on the wall\nnotes the times of scheduled cleanings. A tiny desk in the corner seems to\nbelong to the group\n',0,4105,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(36390,0,0,0,'Before A Large Pit','This outcropping of rock overlooks a large pit. Stairs carved into the side of\nthe chamber lead down to the bottom of the chamber, where groups of gnomes are\nbattling against large black cats. There is a strange and foul stench in the\nchamber. The smell is reminiscent of a bad mixture of urine, sweat, blood and mold.\n',0,4105,56,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36391,0,0,0,'The Bottom of a Large Pit','The stone of the floor here has been carved out of solid rock. The face of the rock is smooth and worn, save several gouges which were surely made by bladed weapons. A light detritus covers the floor. Crude torches and makeshift oil lamps have been hung on the wall of the room, providing this area with enough light to allow combatants to see what they might be fighting.\n',0,4105,56,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36392,0,0,0,'The Bottom of a Large Pit','The stone of the floor here has been carved out of solid rock. The face of the rock is smooth and worn, save several gouges which were surely made by bladed weapons. A light detritus covers the floor. Crude torches and makeshift oil lamps have been hung on the wall of the room, providing this area with enough light to allow combatants to see what they might be fighting.\n',0,4105,56,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
