(36397,0,0,0,'Fire-filled Walkway','The floor of this wide walkway is pitted with small holes, which intermitently\nvent cones of flame and pockets of steam. Though this room may have at once been \ndecorated, these pitfalls have destroyed any object not made of stone. Every surface\nis warm to the touch and covered in a layer of soot. At best, this walkway is \nuncomfortable to be in.\n',0,4105,56,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36398,0,0,0,'Fire-filled Walkway','The floor of this wide walkway is pitted with small holes, which intermitently\nvent cones of flame and pockets of steam. Though this room may have at once been \ndecorated, these pitfalls have destroyed any object not made of stone. Every surface\nis warm to the touch and covered in a layer of soot. At best, this walkway is \nuncomfortable to be in.\n',0,4105,56,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36399,0,0,0,'Fire-filled Walkway','The floor of this wide walkway is pitted with small holes, which intermitently\nvent cones of flame and pockets of steam. Though this room may have at once been \ndecorated, these pitfalls have destroyed any object not made of stone. Every surface\nis warm to the touch and covered in a layer of soot. At best, this walkway is \nuncomfortable to be in.\n',0,4105,56,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36400,0,0,0,'Tunnel Through Molten Lava','The walls and ceiling of this hallway are flowing, molten lava. Magic appears\nto be preventing the lava from rushing in towards the center, melting both the\nroom\'s occupants and the rock path the occupants may be standing on.\nSurprisingly,\nit is uncomfortable to be in this room but not unbearable. Though the obvious\ndangers in the room are a little unsettling.\n',0,4105,56,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'',NULL),
(36401,0,0,0,'Royal Antechamber','Used by the Royal Elite Cadre, this room at the top of the tower stairs serves\nas a means of defending the throne room of assailants. Here guards strip\nvisitors and verify items to be brought to Gnumble for inspection.\n',0,4105,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(36402,0,0,0,'Throne Room','This vast room serves as a court to King Gnumble. Here visitors approach\nthe king for all matters that pertain to the kingdom. It is often whispered that\nbecause Gnumble is so devoted to properly running the kingdom, this room\noften serves as a bed chamber. Several open windows span from floor to ceiling,\noffering light and surveyance of the land below. Short marble pillars hold\naloft copper braziers to illuminate and warm the room when the occassion\nrequires.\n',0,4105,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(36403,0,0,0,'Long Spiral Staircase','This staircase leads from the throne room of King Gnumble to his personal watchtower. Guards have begun to patrol it occassionally, but the most frequent visitor is the king himself. The stairs themselves are steep and there is no rail to hang onto.\n',0,8201,21,0,0,0,0,-1,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(36404,0,0,0,'Long Spiral Staircase','This staircase leads from the throne room of King Gnumble to his personal watchtower. Guards have begun to patrol it occassionally, but the most frequent visitor is the king himself. The stairs themselves are steep and there is no rail to hang onto.\n',0,8201,21,0,0,0,0,-1,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(36405,0,0,0,'Long Spiral Staircase','This staircase leads from the throne room of King Gnumble to his personal watchtower. Guards have begun to patrol it occassionally, but the most frequent visitor is the king himself. The stairs themselves are steep and there is no rail to hang onto.\n\n',0,0,21,0,0,0,0,-1,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(36406,0,0,0,'Alchemist\'s Chamber','This chamber is used for experiments by Gnefrod, the royal alchemist of Gnumble. Gnefrod, aside from being a talented mage and alchemist, is a skilled metalsmith and jeweler. Consequently, this room is cluttered with tools, both arcane and mundane.\n',0,8201,21,0,0,0,0,-1,8,100,0,'',NULL),
(36407,0,0,0,'Top of a Long Spiral Staircase','The long, dangerous spiral stairs that lead up from Gnumble’s throne room end here, at a trapdoor. Through the wooden portal above you, the sounds of cold wind can be heard. It is said that from the watchtower, an observer can peer over the mountain range that borders the tower to the north.\n',0,8201,21,0,0,0,0,-1,6,100,0,'',NULL),
(36408,0,0,0,'Before a Set of Large Wooden Doors','This is the entrance to the tower of King Gnumble. The area is, for the most part, undecorated. Due to its location, the tower receives few visitors that do not have some sort of official reason to be there. The doors, however, are covered with relief carvings.',0,8192,24,0,0,0,0,0,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
(36409,0,0,0,'Moat Around a Very Tall Tower','This moat is wide and deep. There is no current, which suggests that it is artificial. Undoubtedly, such a project required countless hours of labor.',0,8192,29,0,0,0,0,-1,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
(36410,0,0,0,'Moat Around a Very Tall Tower','This moat is wide and deep. There is no current, which suggests that it is artificial. Undoubtedly, such a project required countless hours of labor.',0,8192,29,0,0,0,0,-1,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
