(36949,0,0,0,'<Y>Barn Tower<1>','<o>  The barn tower is unadorned, but provides an excellent view of the\nsurrounding country side.<1>\n',-1,139593,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,144,0,'',NULL),
(44765,0,0,0,'Underground Channel','This wide <B>channel<z> has silky smooth <k>walls<z> due to the many years of\nconstant flowing water. Although the space is vast within the <k>walls<z>, not\nan ounce of breathable <B>air<z> is present.\n',0,8,30,0,0,0,15,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44766,0,0,0,'Underground Channel','This wide <B>channel<z> has silky smooth <k>walls<z> due to the many years of\nconstant flowing water. Although the space is vast within the <k>walls<z>, not\nan ounce of breathable <B>air<z> is present.\n',0,8,30,0,0,0,15,5,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44767,0,0,0,'Slightly Deeper in the Channel','The pressure of the deep is greater here than the surface. This wide\n<B>channel<z> has silky smooth <k>walls<z> due to the many years of constant\nflowing water. Although the space is vast within the <k>walls<z>, not an ounce\nof breathable <B>air<z> is present.\n',0,8,30,0,0,0,15,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44768,0,0,0,'Underground Channel','This wide <B>channel<z> has silky smooth <k>walls<z> due to the many years of\nconstant flowing water. Although the space is vast within the <k>walls<z>, not\nan ounce of breathable <B>air<z> is present.\n',0,8,30,0,0,0,15,8,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44769,0,0,0,'Underground Channel','This wide <B>channel<z> has silky smooth <k>walls<z> due to the many years of\nconstant flowing water. Although the space is vast within the <k>walls<z>, not\nan ounce of breathable <B>air<z> is present. Upwards there is a noticeable gap\nbetween the water and the ceiling of the <B>channel<z>.\n',0,8,30,0,0,0,15,5,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44770,0,0,0,'Cramped Air Pocket','A slight raise in elevation has allowed a small pocket of air to get trapped in\nthe channel. The thick walls are not as smooth as below the surface due to the\nlack of water rubbing against them. A small drop of water falls from a miniscule\ncrack in the ceiling resulting in a tiny splash.\n',0,131080,29,0,0,0,0,-1,10,100,0,'',NULL),
(44771,0,0,0,'Deep in the Channel','The tremendous amount of pressure here is vastly greater than above the surface.\nThe <B>channel<z> appears to widen to the south. The silky smooth <k>walls<z>\nseem to be made of a beautiful quartz in this section. Although the space is\nvast within the <k>walls<z>, not an ounce of breathable <B>air<z> is present.\n',0,8,30,0,0,0,15,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44772,0,0,0,'Change in Current','Oddly enough, the current has been flowing deep into the underground\n<B>channel<z>, but for some unknown reason it has changed directions here.  As a\nresult, the <k>walls<z> of the channel are smooth in spots and rough in others.\n',0,8,30,0,0,0,15,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44773,0,0,0,'Opening to a Reservoir','The channel begins to widen as an underground reservoir of water opens up to the\nsouth.  The waters become a more tranquil place to be as it lacks the constant\npull of the current.\n',0,8,30,0,0,0,15,0,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44774,0,0,0,'Center of a Large Reservoir','This vast space of calm water provides an ease to the constant pull of the\nstrange, magical currents to the north.  To the south the channel begins to\nnarrow as if it were a path one could walk on.\n',0,8,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44775,0,0,0,'A Large Reservoir','This vast space of calm water provides an ease to the constant pull of the\nstrange, magical currents to the north. To the south the channel begins to\nnarrow as if it were a path one could walk on.\n',0,8,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44776,0,0,0,'A Large Reservoir','This vast space of calm water provides an ease to the constant pull of the\nstrange, magical currents to the north.  To the south the channel begins to\nnarrow as if it were a path one could walk on.\n',0,8,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44777,0,0,0,'Narrowing Channel','Calm water fills this narrowing channel. The cold rock walls surround you and appear to be littered with deep crevices and long spidery cracks.',0,8,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44778,0,0,0,'Narrowing Channel','Calm water fills this narrowing channel. The cold rock walls surround you and appear to be littered with deep crevices and long spidery cracks. Looking up one would notice a small separation between the water and ceiling creating a small pocket of air.',0,8,30,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44779,0,0,0,'Cramped Air Pocket','A slight raise in elevation has allowed a small pocket of air to get trapped in the channel. Many layers of different rocks create the ceiling of this cramped space. \n',0,8,29,0,0,0,0,-1,10,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44780,0,0,0,'Salamander Creek','This calm creek splits off the Kranor river and flows south into a small swamp. The water looks clean and the riverbed is covered in smooth round rocks.',0,139520,29,0,0,0,30,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44781,0,0,0,'Salamander Creek','This calm creek splits off the Kranor river and flows south into a small swamp. The water looks clean and the riverbed is covered in smooth round rocks. The silt glitters with false gold.',0,139520,29,0,0,0,30,1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44782,0,0,0,'Salamander Creek','This calm creek splits off the Kranor river and flows south into a small swamp. The water looks clean and the riverbed is covered in smooth round rocks. Tree roots protrude into the creek here.',0,139520,29,0,0,0,30,8,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44783,0,0,0,'Salamander Creek','This calm creek splits off the Kranor river and flows south into a small swamp. The water looks clean and the riverbed is covered in smooth round rocks.',0,139520,29,0,0,0,30,2,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44784,0,0,0,'Salamander Creek','This calm creek splits off the Kranor river and flows south into a small swamp. The water looks clean and the riverbed is covered in smooth round rocks. To the southwest, a small swamp is visible.',0,139520,29,0,0,0,30,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44785,0,0,0,'Salamander Swamp','This serene pool of water is punctuated by tall, reedy grasses. Bright green lilypads are scattered over the surface of the water, and under the water a thick silt is churned by the occasional bottom-feeder. Algae clings to the smooth rocks resting underwater and strands of algae sway to the surface of the water. A sedate creek feeds in from the northeast.',0,139520,29,0,0,0,30,9,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44786,0,0,0,'Salamander Swamp','This serene pool of water is punctuated by tall, reedy grasses. Bright green lilypads are scattered over the surface of the water, and under the water a thick silt is churned by the occasional bottom-feeder. Algae clings to the smooth rocks resting underwater and strands of algae sway to the surface of the water. The lilypads give off a pleasant scent.',0,139520,29,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44787,0,0,0,'Salamander Swamp','This serene pool of water is punctuated by tall, reedy grasses. Bright green lilypads are scattered over the surface of the water, and under the water a thick silt is churned by the occasional bottom-feeder. Algae clings to the smooth rocks resting underwater and strands of algae sway to the surface of the water. The lilypads give off a pleasant scent.',0,139520,29,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44788,0,0,0,'Salamander Swamp','This serene pool of water is punctuated by tall, reedy grasses. Bright green lilypads are scattered over the surface of the water, and under the water a thick silt is churned by the occasional bottom-feeder. Algae clings to the smooth rocks resting underwater and strands of algae sway to the surface of the water. The lilypads give off a pleasant scent.',0,139520,29,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44789,0,0,0,'Salamander Swamp','This serene pool of water is punctuated by tall, reedy grasses. Bright green lilypads are scattered over the surface of the water, and under the water a thick silt is churned by the occasional bottom-feeder. Algae clings to the smooth rocks resting underwater and strands of algae sway to the surface of the water. The lilypads give off a pleasant scent.',0,139520,29,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44790,0,0,0,'Salamander Swamp','This serene pool of water is punctuated by tall, reedy grasses. Bright green lilypads are scattered over the surface of the water, and under the water a thick silt is churned by the occasional bottom-feeder. Algae clings to the smooth rocks resting underwater and strands of algae sway to the surface of the water. A grassy path is visible to the east.',0,139520,29,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44791,0,0,0,'Grassy Path','Tall, soft blue-green grasses sway in the occasional breeze. They are trampled down to form a narrow path through the wetlands, leading to a small swamp to the west or to a drier path to the east.',0,139520,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44792,0,0,0,'Grassy Path','The grass here is interspersed with thistles and other small brush. The grass is matted down in several places, and chewed-up vegetation is littered in those spots.',0,139520,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44793,0,0,0,'Grassy Path','The grass here is interspersed with thistles and other small brush. The grass is matted down in several places, and chewed-up vegetation is littered in those spots. A few rows of carrots and peas are growing here.',0,139520,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44794,0,0,0,'Secluded Glade','Lush vegetation grows all around the glade. A tall deciduous tree grows here, and ivy winds around its trunk and lower branches. A vegetable garden flourishes here with rows of vigorously growing carrots, squash, onions, potatoes and peas. Softly glowing magical lilies are perpetually in bloom here, spreading a pleasant scent around the glade.',0,139520,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44795,0,0,0,'Brushy Patch Next To An Opening','Nestled between a rock face and the adjacent forest, this patch of\nthistly brush and brambles is the buffer between the territories\nof two competing birdmen. The woodland to the north is home to the lesser\nof the two, who have been pushed from the coveted rock-face by a \nmore aggressive group. The soil here, though being rich, does not\nsupport anything more than low-lying plants. Mostly, this is due to the\nshadow cast by the large oak tree to the northwest.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44796,0,0,0,'A Rough Path Next to An Enormous Tree','The path to the south ends here where it meets a clearing\nformed by the shadow of a massive tree. The sounds of many birds\necho in from the northwest, as does a gentle breeze. To the south\nthe path leads on towards a rock face.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44797,0,0,0,'The Base of an Enormous Tree','Little more than low lying foliage grows here, as all else is starved of\nsunlight due to the massive nature of the tree to the northwest. Several\nfamilies of wildlife have made homes from the nooks created by\nthe massive root structure here.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44798,0,0,0,'The Base of an Enormous Tree','Little more than low lying foliage grows here, as all else is starved of\nsunlight due to the massive nature of the tree to the north. Several\nfamilies of wildlife have made homes from the nooks created by\nthe massive root structure here.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44799,0,0,0,'A Blanket of Leaves','It appears that someone or something has begun to gather leaves in this spot.\nAside from the occassional twig, there is very little else other than leaves\non the ground here. Perhaps the culprit has the intention of creating\na bed out of natural materials. It does look like an inviting pile of leaves.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44800,0,0,0,'A Stony Patch of Soil','The soil here is harder, and holds many stones. Several of the much larger\npieces of stone have become makeshift perches for several of the\nspecies of bird common to the forest floor. Consequently, many of them are\ncovered in a thick coating of white droppings.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44801,0,0,0,'Within the Trunk of an Enormous Tree','The inner most portion of this tree has been carved out, creating\na very hospitable and pleasant-smelling room. The floor is\nnatural, but has been covered with a light layer of gravel. Arches\nhave been constructed from the existing root system of the tree\nto allow access into and out of the trunk without killing the tree.\nHigh above this room, the hollow opens into a fantastic spread of foliage. \n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44802,0,0,0,'The Base of an Enormous Tree','Little more than low lying foliage grows here, as all else is starved of\nsunlight due to the massive nature of the tree to the east. Several\nfamilies of wildlife have made homes from the nooks created by\nthe massive root structure here.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44803,0,0,0,'A Shady Spot Beneath Some Low Branches','The branches above are particularly close together, making the foliage\nrather thick. Here, even on the brightest of days, these branches provide\nquite a bit of shade. This also means that this spot is particularly unique\namong the other spots that surround the enormous tree to the southwest.\nThe atmosphere here is calm and peaceful.\n',0,131088,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44804,0,0,0,'A Serene Pool','The water that is caught on the leaves and branches of the enormous\ntree to the south trickles down the trunk and puddles here before\ndisappearing either into the roots of the tree or into the mouths\nof the local wildlife. There are, at any time, dozens of kinds of\nhatching insect larvae in the area surrounding the pool.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44805,0,0,0,'The Base of an Enormous Tree','Little more than low lying foliage grows here, as all else is starved of\nsunlight due to the massive nature of the tree to the southeast. Several\nfamilies of wildlife have made homes from the nooks created by\nthe massive root structure here.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44806,0,0,0,'A Meeting of Branches Under The Canopy','The main branches of the tree stem from this point and grow outward in a myriad\nof directions. Several of them have been bent toward the center to form\na platform above the hollow trunk below that might be suitable enough to walk\nor rest on.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44807,0,0,0,'Above A Small Clearing','The dense forest breaks slightly here. A little to the south a naturally formed\nwall\nof rock impedes the forest\'s spread. An enormous tree sits to the immediate\nnorthwest, and a path\nthrough the forest leads southeast toward the rock wall. There is evidence that\nmany animals travel through\nthis spot.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44808,0,0,0,'Under The Canopy','The canopy is just above this area, which buzzes with activity. Courtship\nrituals, feeding, and territory squabbles all abound here among the branches.\nAs altitude increases, there are fewer and fewer suitable hand-holds among the\nnetwork of branches.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44809,0,0,0,'Among Some Bare Branches','The branches here are without most of their leafage. Though the bark of the tree\nhas turned gray and fallen off of many of the nearby branches, it is unclear\nwhether or not\nthe limb lost its leaves because the limb died or if the limb died because it\nlots its leafy plumage.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44810,0,0,0,'On A White Branch','This is obviously a popular sitting spot for many aviary creatures. Many, if not\nmost, of the branches\non this limb are covered with white and blue speckled guano. There does not,\nhowever,\nappear to be any nests or any insects nearby. Perhaps the birds gather here for\nanother reason.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44811,0,0,0,'Under The Canopy','The canopy is just above this area, which buzzes with activity. Courtship\nrituals, feeding, and territory squabbles all abound here among the branches.\nAs altitude increases, there are fewer and fewer suitable hand-holds among the\nnetwork of branches.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44812,0,0,0,'A Larger Branch','This branch is much larger than many of the others and appears to have\ngrown out rather than up. This affords those beneath it with a shady glen and\nthose\non it with an opening into the air. The smaller branches stemming from\nthis larger branch are dotted with the nests of many birds.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44813,0,0,0,'Above A Pool','There are fewer branches on this side of the tree as compared to some and\nthere are few places fit for resting birds. Below here is a pool that\nhas gathered from a recent rainfall.\n',0,131072,35,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44814,0,0,0,'Under The Canopy','This area is just above the base of the tree, which buzzes with activity. Courtship\nrituals, feeding, and territory squabbles all abound here among the branches.\nAs altitude increases, there are fewer and fewer suitable hand-holds among the\nnetwork of branches.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44815,0,0,0,'A Perch On The Tallest Branch','Atop this branch, which is the tallest on the tree, only the strongest of\nthe local birds reside. The smaller branches have been picked from this limb\nby many birds over many seasons in order to build nests strong enough to survive\nthe wind up here.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44816,0,0,0,'At The Top of the Canopy','Above you the tree line erupts into open sky. The leaves and branches at the\ntops of the trees sway as\nthe wind washes over them. Generally, only larger birds inhabit the limbs at\nthis altitude.\n',0,131072,34,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44817,0,0,0,'At The Top of the Canopy','Above you the tree line erupts into open sky. The leaves and branches at the\ntops of the trees sway as\nthe wind washes over them. Generally, only larger birds inhabit the limbs at\nthis altitude.\n',0,131072,34,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
