(44822,0,0,0,'At The Top of the Canopy','Above the tree line erupts into open sky. The leaves and branches at the\ntops of the trees sway as\nthe wind washes over them. Generally, only larger birds inhabit the limbs at\nthis altitude.\n',0,131072,34,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44823,0,0,0,'At The Top of the Canopy','Above you the tree line erupts into open sky. The leaves and branches at the\ntops of the trees sway as\nthe wind washes over them. Generally, only larger birds inhabit the limbs at\nthis altitude.\n',0,131072,34,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44824,0,0,0,'A Small Makeshift Hut','To call this a \'hut\' is to overstate it drastically. Mostly, this space is\nconstructed out of four thick pine limbs that create the back wall, side walls,\nand ceiling. The \'door\' to this enclosure is a mass of poorly tied together\ntwigs. The floor of the enclosure has been trampled down through use\nover time. Jars of what appear to be polstice\nare scattered about, some half empty. Used bandages and tiny splints are\nstrewn about, but most of them look broken or used.\n',0,196608,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44825,0,0,0,'A Wall of Elm Trees','A tightly-planted line of elm trees forms this wall, which is frequented\nby the Treetop guards. The trees themselves are bushy, but mostly branchless\nbelow\nthis spot, which suggests ages of selective pruning for a single purpose.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44826,0,0,0,'A Wall of Elm Trees','A tightly-planted line of elm trees forms this wall, which is frequented\nby the Treetop guards. The trees themselves are bushy, but mostly branchless\nbelow\nthis spot, which suggests ages of selective pruning for a single purpose.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44827,0,0,0,'The Hatch House','This area is riddled with nests of various age, size, and composition.\nThe young citizens of Treetop use this enclosure for warmth and shelter and\ndo not begin to spend their nights in the rookery until well into fledglinghood.\nSplit reeds have been woven into the surrounding branches to protect\nthe feathers of the young from the wind and rain.\n',0,131080,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(44828,0,0,0,'A Wall of Elm Trees','A tightly-planted line of elm trees forms this wall, which is frequented\nby the Treetop guards. The trees themselves are bushy, but mostly branchless\nbelow\nthis spot, which suggests ages of selective pruning for a single purpose.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44829,0,0,0,'The Hatch House','This area is riddled with nests of various age, size, and composition.\nThe young citizens of Treetop use this enclosure for warmth and shelter and\ndo not begin to spend their nights in the rookery until well into fledglinghood.\nSplit reeds have been woven into the surrounding branches to protect\nthe feathers of the young from the wind and rain.\n',0,131080,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(44830,0,0,0,'A Wall of Elm Trees','A tightly-planted line of elm trees forms this wall, which is frequented\nby the Treetop guards. The trees themselves are bushy, but mostly branchless\nbelow\nthis spot, which suggests ages of selective pruning for a single purpose.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44831,0,0,0,'A Wall of Elm Trees','A tightly-planted line of elm trees forms this wall, which is frequented\nby the Treetop guards. The trees themselves are bushy, but mostly branchless\nbelow\nthis spot, which suggests ages of selective pruning for a single purpose.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44832,0,0,0,'A Path Through the Treetops','Thick, leafy foliage obscures most of the visibility at this height.\nTo the south and to the west, lines of extremely tall, and mostly branchless,\nelm trees form a wall that secludes this portion of the forest from\nthe clearing around the magnificently large oak tree to the southwest.\nThe wall and the nearby clearing below are quiet.\nHowever, all other directions surrounding this place foster a host of different\nsounds.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44833,0,0,0,'A Walkway Through Treetop','Many of the citizens of Treetop prefer simply to fly from place to place.\nHowever, the community is ever mindful of its young, and even those members that\nhave not yet become proficient at flying are welcome anywhere in the village.\nTo prevent injury and relieve some of the worry of the Treetop mothers and\nfathers,\nthe chief had these walkways constructed by bending down some of the taller\nbranches.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44834,0,0,0,'The Home of the Chief of Treetop','This small enclosure does not have doors, in accordance with the wishes of its\nowner, the chief of Treetop. Treetop is a village that emphasizes the\ncommunity, and so it was the chief\'s desire that his home never be closed.\nSeveral \'walls\' have been constructed from woven blankets of leaves\nand reeds, from which memorabilia from the community can often be found hanging.\n',0,131080,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'',NULL),
(44835,0,0,0,'An Open-Air Rookery','The very tallest of the nearest trees come together here to form the\nmesh-like ceiling of this long bunkhouse. There are no walls to this\nrookery, per se. But long reeds have been woven through the outer\nbranch formations to act as walls for shade. The villagers of Treetop\nprefer to raise their young in a separate enclosure, and so there are\nfew nests in this area.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44836,0,0,0,'An Open-Air Rookery','The very tallest of the nearest trees come together here to form the\nmesh-like ceiling of this long bunkhouse. There are no walls to this\nrookery, per se. But long reeds have been woven through the outer\nbranch formations to act as walls for shade. The villagers of Treetop\nprefer to raise their young in a separate enclosure, and so there are\nfew nests in this area.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44837,0,0,0,'A Walkway Through Treetop','Many of the citizens of Treetop prefer simply to fly from place to place.\nHowever, the community is ever mindful of its young, and even those members that\nhave not yet become proficient at flying are welcome anywhere in the village.\nTo prevent injury and relieve some of the worry of the Treetop mothers and\nfathers,\nthe chief had these walkways constructed by bending down some of the taller\nbranches.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44838,0,0,0,'Meeting Place Among the Tree-top Walkways','This place is the social hub of Treetop. During most of the day, many\ncitizens and visitors to the village rest upon the natural furniture\nprovided by the myriad limbs that converge upon this spot. A cloud rests\nin the sky overhead. \n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44839,0,0,0,'The Perch of the Elders','The northeast portion of the village is known as the \'Perch of the Elders.\'\nHere the oldest and wisest of Treetop\'s citizens rest while they look across\nthe forest and rivers into the city beyond.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44840,0,0,0,'The Residence of the Treetop Shaman','There are few branches in this home that might be considered \'flooring.\' For\nwhatever reason,\nit is clear that the owner feels the need to differentiate himself from the\nland-walking races of The World. Bones from various woodland animals hang in\nstrange arrangements from some of the higher branches, and many of the\nlarger branches here have been scrawled upon in some strange tongue\nwith what appears to be blood.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44841,0,0,0,'The Nest of the Treetop Healer','Treetop\'s most gifted cleric spends much of her time in this nest-like\nhome. In fact, so high is the learning curve for the Treetop fledglings that\nthe healer\'s home has also become her workplace. Unlike the other homes,\nthis place does not have a ceiling or anything resembling it.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44842,0,0,0,'The Perch of the Elders','The northeast portion of the village is known as the \'Perch of the Elders.\'\nHere the oldest and wisest of Treetop\'s citizens rest while they look across\nthe forest and rivers into the city beyond.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44843,0,0,0,'The Perch of the Elders','The northeast portion of the village is known as the \'Perch of the Elders.\'\nHere the oldest and wisest of Treetop\'s citizens rest while they look across\nthe forest and rivers into the city beyond.\n',0,131072,26,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44844,0,0,0,'Fresh, Open Air','The air up here is kept fresh by a mostly gentle breeze that pushes in from the\nwest.\nInsects and smaller birds do not often inhabit this area, as they\nare often hunted by some of the younger citizens of Treetop. Treetop, itself,\nbegins to blend into the greenness of the surrounding canopy. Just above,\na noticeably thick cloud blocks vision upwards, but does not darken the area. \n',0,131072,34,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
(44845,0,0,0,'Fresh, Open Air','The air up here is kept fresh by a mostly gentle breeze that pushes in from the\nwest.\nInsects and smaller birds do not often inhabit this area, as they\nare often hunted by some of the younger citizens of Treetop. Treetop, itself,\nbegins to blend into the greenness of the surrounding canopy. Just above,\na noticeably thick cloud blocks vision upwards, but does not darken the area. \n',0,131072,34,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'',NULL),
