(45378,0,0,0,'Reinforced Tunnel','This excavated tunnel is larger than usual and seems sturdier than the others.  The ceiling is supported by large wooden beams anchored to the ground with stacks of neatly squared rocks chiseled out of the earth.  The walls are smoother but there are still patches of black and green mold growing in large colonies on the surface.  The ground is squishy and small rivulets of water stream in from the north.  To the south is a gigantic dig site.\n',0,139532,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(45379,0,0,0,'Collapsed Sinking Tunnel','This portion of the tunnel is slowly sinking due to the natural limestone rock found in this section of the cave.  Muddy water is seeping up from a subterranean body of water making this a dangerous place to be.  The mold covered ceiling, usually supported by large wooden beams anchored to the ground with stacks of chiseled rocks, is sagging dangerously low as the rocks sink lower and lower.\n',0,139528,29,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(45380,0,0,0,'Dimly Lit Cave','There is a <o>faint<z><y> glow<z> emanating from the thick patches of soft <G>green<z> <g>moss<z> growing on every surface of this small cave.  On the walls are strange <p>runic<z> symbols of ancient design.  A strange vibration is in the air, which more than likely caused the wall to the west to collapse into rubble.\n',0,139528,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,40,0,'',NULL),
(45381,0,0,0,'Jalashzach\'s Quarters','This room belongs to Jalashzach, the feared and strict supervisor in charge of drilling and training the guards in their duties.  The room is orderly and spacious with functional stone furniture.  The floor is covered with woven moss and a large chair carved out of stone rests  in the southwest corner.\n',0,139528,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(45382,0,0,0,'Guard Quarters','Large stone beds, lining both walls and spanning the entire length of this large cave are the dominating feature in this room.  Oversized lockers are at the foot of each bed lending a sense of orderliness.  A lingering stench of trolls is in the air.',0,139528,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(45383,0,0,0,'Gigantic Dig Site','The dig site is massive.  Huge excavated sections of the ground are dug to different depths in a haphazard sort of way that makes no sense, almost as if they were digging for something specific.  The air is thick with floating particulates from all the dust and debris.  Broken tools and various devices are scattered about the area.  The sound of a gigantic rattling contraption echoes loudly in the distance.',0,139528,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
