(45392,0,0,0,'Reinforced Tunnel','This excavated tunnel is larger than usual and seems sturdier than the others.  The ceiling is supported by large wooden beams anchored to the ground with stacks of neatly squared rocks chiseled out of the earth.  The walls are smoother but there are still patches of black and green mold growing in large colonies on the surface.  The tunnel leads north and to the south is a gigantic dig site.',0,139528,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(45393,0,0,0,'Reinforced Tunnel','This excavated tunnel is larger than usual and seems sturdier than the others.  The ceiling is supported by large wooden beams anchored to the ground with stacks of neatly squared rocks chiseled out of the earth.  The walls are smoother but there are still patches of black and green mold growing in large colonies on the surface.\n',0,139528,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(45394,0,0,0,'Reinforced Tunnel','This excavated tunnel comes to an abrupt halt.  Although it is large like the other reinforced tunnels and it\'s clear that a good amount of work went into making it secure,  the workers seem to have inexplicably stopped further digging.  The northern wall looks like it\'s made of a stone that their crude tools couldn\'t penetrate as evidenced by the large amount of broken tools scattered around the room.  There is an exit to the south.\n',0,139528,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
(45395,0,0,0,'Reinforced Tunnel','This excavated tunnel is large and spacious.  The ceiling is supported by large wooden beams anchored to the ground with stacks of neatly squared rocks chiseled out of the earth.  The walls are jagged and on their surface are patches of black and green mold growing in large colonies.  The tunnel continues to the east and west.\n\n',0,139528,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'',NULL),
