(2700,-4,-4,0,'A Well Worn Path Near the Outer Pathway and the Trader\'s Camp','The hardened earth path widens as it meets the outer pathway from the south and narrows as it\ncontinues northward into an encampment among the trees.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2701,-4,-3,0,'A Well Worn Path Near the Outer Pathway and the Trader\'s Camp','  The hardened earth path serves as the main entrance for the camp.  Short\ntowers sit on small bulwarks of earth and rock far off to the north and east.\nThe path north continues towards the interior of the camp.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2702,1,-2,0,'A Copse of Small Trees and Scrub Brush',' The trail here is lined with thick bushes. They open up to the northwest, where\nit looks like a large animal has begun to create a game path. Paw prints of many\nkinds dot the dirt, going many directions. Strangely, they go south and east\ninto some suspicious-looking scrub brush. Past the brush you can hear the hustle\nand bustle of a city street.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,2,36,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2703,0,-1,0,'Path Through Some Low, Rocky Hills','A path winds around a copse of trees and brush as it traveses the low rocky\nhills. The path continues to the southwest and east, there is a small clearing\nto the southeast and a game path into the brush to the north.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2704,-4,-2,0,'A Well Worn Path Near the Outer Pathway and an Encampment','  The hardened earth path serves as the main entrance for the camp.  Short\ntowers sit on small bulwarks of earth and rock far off to the north and east.\nThe path north continues towards the interior of the camp. The scent of smoke\nhangs in this area.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2705,-3,-2,0,'A Sleeping Yurt','The yurt is a four foot, domed hut made with woven sticks, vines and bark from\nthe forest. It provides more than adequate protection from the elements as long\nas mainenance is kept up.\n',27,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,48,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2706,-3,0,2,'Atop a Crude Wooden Tower','A rickety platform that sways with the wind gives an excellent view of the\nGrimhaven wall, its outer pathway and the Eastgate Settlement. Looking further\nout, the mage academy of Grimhaven, Haon-Dor Forest and even the Sympathian\nMountains can be seen.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2707,-3,0,1,'Rocky Bulwark','Haphazardly heaped rocks and earth support a tower that allows lookouts to keep\nwatch over the camp and the surrounding area. The pastures and outer pathway can\nalso be seen from this vantage point.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2708,-3,0,0,'At the Base of a Rocky Hill','A faint path picks its way up a small rocky hill while the trail continues to\nthe east. The backs of the buildings in the East Gate Settlement can be seen to\nthe south.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2709,-2,0,0,'A Small Clearing','A small clearing in the scrub brush and trees. Much of the grass is trampled, as\nif there has been a lot of traffic recently. There is a watch tower atop a small\nhill to the west and paths to the northwest and east.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,5,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2710,-1,0,0,'A Small Game Path','A faint path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. The path ends in a\nclearing to the west and continues to the east.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2711,0,0,0,'A Bend in the Path','The path changes direction here, continuing to the west and south. There is a\ncopse of trees to the north, its contents obscured by brush and vines.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2712,-4,6,0,'Game Path between the a Fence and the Stables','The fence  between the paddocks and the cornfield turns southeast around the\npaddocks, edging on the forest. The path to the west has to bend around a large\nstand of trees and brush.  Noises and smells from the paddock hang in the air.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,3,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2713,-6,5,0,'Path Near the Haon-Dor Forest.','The path widens as it merges with a more traveled path on the edge of the\nHaon-Dor forest. It joins the second path to the northwest and continues through\nthe hills to the southeast.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,7,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2714,0,0,0,'A Muddy Clearing Inside a Copse of Trees and Brush','The clearing is a secluded space, effectively hidden from the outside world by a\ndense perimeter of trees and bushes. Water burbles from a hollow bamboo pipe,\nwhich has been inserted into a small rock formation. The water saturates the\nearth, creating a muddy swamp in the immediate vicinity. Several logs and rocks\nare scattered around the clearing, their surfaces covered in a diverse array of\nfungi and lichen.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,2,36,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2715,-4,-1,0,'Camp Entrance',' The path is wider and well worn here as it merges with the surrounding camp.\nSmoke fills the area, suggesting that somewhere nearby there is a large\nfire. The smell of roasted meat that follows confirms this. Sounds of\nlaughter and conversation filter in from the north and the east.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2716,-3,-1,0,'Fire Circle',' Around the fire pit is a well-worn circle where the camp denizens gather for\nwarmth and camaraderie. Directly north of this part of the circle is the\ncommunal fire pit, which fills the area with smoke and the scents of roasted\nmeals. The sounds of work and labor echo in from the east.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2717,-2,-1,0,'Work Area','Between the yurts and the firepit is a small work area where the traders prepare\ntheir meals and products. Larger flat rocks were brought back to the camp to\nprovide a surface to work on. Dried patches of blood and tiny crunched animal\nbones suggest that some butchery must happen here. Lush green bushes line the eastern and southern perimeter.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2718,0,0,0,'Game Path Near the Main Camp','A faint game path runs along the south edge of camp.The sounds and smells of the\nmain camp grow louder and stronger to the west.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,3,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2719,-3,1,0,'A Fork in the Path','On a path through the scrub and rocks, it continues to the west, northeast and\nsoutheast. Immediate to the south is a mound of rocks and dirt with a rickety\ntower on top and camp can be heard to the west.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2720,-5,0,0,'Inside a Gnomish Caravan','The caravan is a wooden cabin on wheels. The interior is clean, but cluttered,\nfull of the owner€s personal belongings and supplies. The floor is covered in\nbedding, the walls are thick with hides and herbs, and the air smells of leather\nand dried herbs. A couple of glowing glass globes are suspended from the ceiling\nproviding a dim light.\n',27,9,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,100,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2721,-4,0,0,'Fire Circle','  Around the fire pit is a well-worn circle where the camp denizens gather for\nwarmth and camaraderie.  Directly east of this part of the circle is the\ncommunal fire pit, which fills the area with smoke and the scents of roasted\nmeals.  The sounds of work and labor echo in from the north.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2722,-3,0,0,'Fire Pit','A small stone circle surrounds a fire that smells of burnt grease and herbs.\nThere is a banner to the southwest, a large hut to the northeast, work areas to\nthe northwest and southeast and a circular area around the fire.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2723,-2,0,0,'Fire Circle','  Around the fire pit is a well-worn circle where the camp denizens gather for\nwarmth and camaraderie.  Directly west of this part of the circle is the\ncommunal fire pit, which fills the area with smoke and the scents of roasted\nmeals.  The sounds of work and labor echo in from the south.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2724,-1,0,0,'Sleeping Yurt','The yurt is a four foot tall, domed hut made with woven sticks, vines and bark\nfrom the forest. It provides more than adequate protection from the elements as\nlong as mainenance is kept up. There is an exit to the southwest.\n',27,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,48,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2725,0,0,0,'Midden Heap','A small clearing functions as the camp\'s midden heap. Staves driven into the\nground, with rough bark and twigs woven between them to form a crude fence, mark\nthe area\'s rough circumference. A makeshift roof covers a small sleeping area.A\nsmall clearing functions as the camp\'s midden heap. Staves driven into the\nground, with rough bark and twigs woven between them to form a crude fence, mark\nthe area\'s rough circumference. A makeshift roof covers a small sleeping area.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,5,36,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2726,-2,2,0,'Game Path on the Southeast Edge of Camp','A faint path is visible through the tall grass and rocks. Walled in by tall\nbrush and small trees on one side and the forest on the other, it is eerily\nquiet here.\n\n\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,3,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2727,-4,1,0,'Work Area','Between the yurts and the firepit is a small work area where the traders\nprepare their meals and products.  Larger flat rocks were brought back to the\ncamp to provide a surface to work on. A small, multi-hued trailer and a small,\ndomed hut face opposite to the circle around the fire pit.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2728,-3,1,0,'Fire Circle','  Around the fire pit is a well-worn circle where the camp denizens gather for\nwarmth and camaraderie.  Directly south of this part of the circle is the\ncommunal fire pit, which fills the area with smoke and the scents of roasted\nmeals.  The sounds of work and labor echo in from the west.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2729,-2,1,0,'Hitching Posts','Between the stable and the fire pit is an open area where beasts can be tied-off\noutside. There is a large hut to the northeast that looks like it has been\nexpanded several times and the firepit is to the southwest. Hitching posts line\nthe outer wall of the yurt.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,6,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2730,-1,1,0,'The West End of a Long Garden','Long rows of unrecognized plants stretch to the end of the large clearing. A\npath of carefully laid flat stones connects the east and west ends of the\ngarden. A wall of fieldstone collected in situ surrounds the rows, protecting\nthe precious plants from the denizens of the forest.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,3,72,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2731,0,0,0,'The East End of a Long Garden','Long rows of unrecognized plants stretch to the end of the large clearing. A\npath of carefully laid flat stones connects the east and west ends of the\ngarden. A wall of fieldstone collected in situ surrounds the rows, protecting\nthe precious plants from the denizens of the forest. A gate in the western wall\nexits the garden.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,3,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2732,-2,3,0,'An Intersection in a Game Path','A game path follows the eastern edge of camp and the tall grass and rocks are\nmore worn away as the path meets another to the west. It€s very quiet this far\nfrom camp, only the random bird and rustling of trees disturbing the peace.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2733,-5,2,0,'Path through Some Low, Rocky Hills','The hard packed earth leaves the camp to the north and enters the work area and\nthe fire, beyond,  to the southeast. A small path winds up the side of a hill to\nthe east. The sounds and smells of the camp center are much louder here.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,5,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2734,0,0,0,'At the Base of a Rocky Hill','A faint path picks its way up a small rocky hill while the trail continues to\nthe west. The city wall can be seen to the west and farm fields to the north.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,2,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2735,-3,2,0,'Stoarge Yurt','The yurt is a four foot tall, domed hut made with woven sticks, vines and bark\nfrom the forest. It provides more than adequate protection from the elements as\nlong as maintenance is kept up.\n',27,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,4,48,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2736,0,0,0,'Stable Paddock',' An enclosed area for housing various animals. The edges of the paddock are\ndefined by tallish staves driven into the ground as pickets and interwoven with\nvines at regular intervals. While neat and well-maintained, the area bears the\nwear and smell of its occupants.\n',27,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,20,-1,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2737,-1,2,0,'Stable Yurt','This yurt is bigger and taller than the others, but it\'s still not much of\neither. The animal wrangler and his stable hands keep a neat work place with\nonly a few hay bales and bags of feed marring the well-packed, earthen floor.\nThere are three gates leading to paddocks besides the main exit.\n',27,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,8,84,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2738,0,0,0,'Stable Paddock','An enclosed area for housing various animals. The edges of the paddock are\ndefined by tallish staves driven into the ground as pickets and interwoven with\nvines at regular intervals. While neat and well-maintained, the area bears the\nwear and smell of its occupants.\n',27,8,24,0,0,0,0,0,20,-1,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2739,-2,4,0,'Game Path between a Paddock and the Forest','In the narrow area between the paddock fence and the trees of the forest, a game\npath enters from the northwest and continues south. Noises and smells from the\npaddock hang in the air.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2740,-5,3,0,'Path through Some Low, Rocky Hills','A path traverses the low rocky hills. The path continues to the north out of and\nand south towards the sounds and smells of camp.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2741,0,0,0,'Rocky Bulwark','Haphazardly heaped rocks and earth support a tower that allows lookouts to keep\nwatch over the camp and the surrounding area. The pastures and outer pathway can\nalso be seen from this vantage point.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,4,-1,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2742,0,0,0,'Atop a Crude Wooden Tower','A rickety platform that sways with the wind gives an excellent view of the\nGrimhaven wall, its outer pathway and the Eastgate market place. Looking further\nout,  the mage academy of Grimhaven, Haon-Dor Forest and even the  Sympathian\nMountains can be seen.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,8,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2743,-5,5,0,'A Bend in a Game Path','A game path bends through the tall grass and rocks. There seems to be another\npath heading north, but it immediately ends in a copse of brush and trees.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,-1,4,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2744,-1,3,0,'Stable Paddock','An enclosed area for housing various animals. The edges of the paddock are\ndefined by tallish staves driven into the ground as pickets and interwoven with\nvines at regular intervals. While neat and well-maintained, the area bears the\nwear and smell of its occupants.\n',27,0,32,0,0,0,0,0,5,72,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2745,-3,5,0,'Game Path between the Stable and the Forest','A path runs diagonally near the northeast end of camp, picking its way through\nthe tall grass and rocks in the space between the stables and the forest. Noises\nand smells from the paddock hang in the air.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,3,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2746,-5,4,0,'An Intersection Near Camp','The widest path heads northwest out of camp to the outer pathway. The path to\nthe south narrows a bit as one gets closer to the noise and smoke of camp. A\nsmall game path wanders east to points unknown.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,5,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2747,-7,6,0,'Game Path Near a Field of Corn.','A path is visible through the tall grass and rocks traversing between an\nintersection in the west and farther down the trail in the east. The area\nborders a corn field with a dilapidated fence.  A gap at the base makes it look\nlike someone is sneaking over on a fairly regular basis.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,0,4,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2748,-6,6,0,'Game Path Near a Field of Corn.','A path follows the fence line between the south end of a corn field and the\nnorth end of camp. This area is fairly isolated from the business and noise of\nthe camp with hills, the watch tower and buildings in the way. The path bends\nsoutheast around a large stand of trees and brush.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,-1,3,0,0,'Jimbus',2),
(2749,-5,6,0,'A Copse of Small Trees and Scrub Brush','This clearing abuts a fenced cornfield to the north and is surrounded by trees\nand scrub brush. The grass  is well worn by repeated trampling and shows a\nvariety of animal and large bird tracks.\n',27,0,24,0,0,0,0,-1,3,36,0,'Jimbus',2),
(45895,14,0,1,'Top of a Ramp Between Roads','At the top of a ramp between the flat sections of road. The road continues southand ramps down to the lower road.',0,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,8,-1,0,'jimbus',1),
(45896,14,1,1,'Terrace Road on Mount Apocryphia','Despite being carved from the side of the mountain, the road is wide, wellmaintained and somewhat level as it curves along the wall. The wall is nearlyvertical and made of heavy blocks. Metal doors and crude windows interrupt theit in regular intervals. The road continues to the north and east and there is adoor to the south.',0,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,8,-1,0,'jimbus',1),
(45897,15,1,1,'Terrace Road on Mount Apocryphia','Despite being carved from the side of the mountain, the road is wide, well maintained and somewhat level as it curves along the wall. The wall is nearly vertical and made of heavy blocks. Metal doors and crude windows interrupt the it in regular intervals. The road continues to the east and west and there is a door to the south.',0,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'jimbus',1),
(45898,16,1,1,'Terrace Road on Mount Apocryphia','Despite being carved from the side of the mountain, the road is wide, well maintained and somewhat level as it curves along the wall. The wall is nearly vertical and made of heavy blocks. Metal doors and crude windows interrupt the it in regular intervals. The road continues to the south and west.',0,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'jimbus',1),
(45899,16,2,1,'Terrace Road on Mount Apocryphia','Empty',0,131072,25,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'jimbus',1),
