(13600,0,0,0,'A Feces-Riddled Space Beneath the Mezzanine','The stench is even worse here amid the haphazard pile of crates. A staircase\n missing multiple boards leads up to the mezzanine, and below that the floor\nis covered with feces in every available space. The goblins apparently have\nflawed ideas of sanitation.\n\n',109,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13601,0,0,0,'Inside a Revolting Flop-House','The stench in this old warehouse is overwhelming. The local gutter-goblins\nhave infested even the rafters above with hammocks jury-rigged out of soiled\ncanvas. The cockroaches would skitter out of sight if they could, but there are\ntoo many of them. Feces dot the floor everywhere, but oddly there are also\nsome clumps of fresh earth.\n',109,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'Therias',1),
(13602,0,-1,0,'A Disorganized Pile of Sacks and Crates','This corner of the flop-house appears to see a lot of traffic based on the dirt\nthat\'s been kicked and pushed aside from the sacks and crates being moved\naround. One crate stands out if for nothing else other than that it\'s actually\nlined up with the wall, while the rest look as though they were simply poured\nfrom the hold of a galleon.\n',109,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13603,0,0,0,'A Whimsically Decorated Backlot','This backlot seems wildly out of place in the drab squalor of the Foulborough,\nalmost€joyful. Glass bowls and bottles and vases in a rainbow of colors hang\nfrom the branches of an old oak tree. Some of the glassware serve as\nbird-feeders, some as bird-baths, some as wind-chimes, setting the stage for\na symphony of bird song. A solitary but splendid clematis vine struggles up\nthe brick wall of the building with the help of a trellis.\n',109,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'Therias',1),
(13604,0,0,0,'A Long Neglected Backlot','This backlot might not have seen maintenance since the warehouse in front\nwas first built. A mess of young alder trees grows everywhere they haven\'t\nbeen suppressed by either foot-traffic or debris. The foot-trails lead right up\nto the stone wall to the west, and continue through the backlot to the east.\nClods of fresh earth stand out to the eye along the path to the east.\n',109,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'Therias',1),
(13605,1,0,0,'A Long Neglected Backlot','This backlot might not have seen maintenance since the warehouse in front\nwas first built. A mess of young alder trees grows everywhere they haven\'t\nbeen suppressed by either foot-traffic or debris. The foot-trail here continues\nthrough the backlot to the west, though the path dotted with clods of earth\nappears to go over the cliffside.\n',109,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'Therias',1),
(13606,0,0,0,'Cliffside Ledge Behind the Brewery','This ledge is precarious as it is out of the way, which seems to have attracted\nthe sorts who want to stay out of the way while still in Grimhaven. The brick\nexterior of the brewery next door rises to the west, and to the north is another\nbacklot, and cliffside drops away in all other directions. A small squatter\'s\ncamp encircles a firepit here, exposed to the elements.\n',109,131072,24,0,0,0,0,-1,0,-1,0,'Therias',1),
(13607,0,0,0,'Flop-House Rafters','The gutter-goblins squatting in this warehouse certainly know how to make full\nuse\nof the space. Sheets of canvas have been strung between the rafters, sometimes\neven with the aid of rope, to serve as hammocks. Still it seems to require some\ndegree of acrobatics to move between the rafters.\n',109,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,10,0,'Therias',1),
(13608,1,0,0,'Flop-House Mezzanine','This mezzanine level is almost clean by contrast to the rest of the flop-house.\nThe floors are swept, and only a few bedrolls are laid here in a nearly\norganized fashion. A door to the south leads into what would have been the\nforeman\'s office in the days this space was used for a warehouse.\n',109,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'Therias',1),
(13609,0,-1,0,'Flop-House Rafters','The gutter-goblins squatting in this warehouse certainly know how to make full\nuse\nof the space. Sheets of canvas have been strung between the rafters, sometimes\neven with the aid of rope, to serve as hammocks. Still it seems to require some\ndegree\nof acrobatics to move between the rafters.\n',109,131080,35,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'Therias',1),
(13610,1,-1,0,'A Luxuriantly Ramshackle Quarters','A single, broken four-post bed sits in this room, along with other run-down\nfurniture.\nA dirty red rug looks as if it were cut from the carpet of an abandoned home\nwith a\nsword, and likely-looted silverware is placed randomly around the room as if\nonly to\nshow off the extravagance. A painting of a broad-chested goblin wearing a crown\nand\nrobes adorns the wall behind the bed.\n',109,131080,32,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'Therias',1),
(13611,0,-1,-1,'A Fork in a Crudely Dug Tunnel','This tunnel looks like it either shouldn€t stand or like it should collapse at\nany moment.\nThree walls here are boarded in around the ladder leading upwards, and two\ntunnels\nbranch off to the west and southwest from here, without the boarding to help\nforget the\nlikelihood a tunnel may collapse.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'Therias',1),
(13612,-1,-1,-1,'An Unevenly Dug Staircase Leading Down','This staircase looks as though real effort at engineering was put into it, and\nthen goblins\nput that engineering into action and this hazardous and uneven staircase\nspiraling down\ninto the darkness below is the natural result.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'Therias',1),
(13613,0,-2,-1,'A Concealed Storeroom','The low ceilings of this storeroom are only high enough to allow crates to be\nshoved\naround inside. Its design looks little different from what a large rodent might\ncarve out\nof the earth to store nuts.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,3,60,0,'Therias',1),
(13614,-1,-2,-1,'A Crudely Dug Tunnel','This tunnel looks like it either shouldn€t stand or like it should collapse at\nany moment.\nRoughly-hewn timbers frame the tunnel as if designed to give the appearance of\nreinforcement, only.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13615,-2,-2,-1,'A Crudely Dug Tunnel','This tunnel looks like it either shouldn€t stand or like it should collapse at\nany moment.\nRoughly-hewn timbers frame the tunnel as if designed to give the appearance of\nreinforcement, only.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13616,-3,-2,-1,'A Crudely Dug Tunnel','This tunnel looks like it either shouldn€t stand or like it should collapse at\nany moment.\nRoughly-hewn timbers frame the tunnel as if designed to give the appearance of\nreinforcement, only.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13617,-4,-2,-1,'A Crudely Dug Tunnel','This tunnel looks like it either shouldn\'t stand or like it should collapse at\nany moment.\nRoughly-hewn timbers frame the tunnel as if designed to give the appearance of\nreinforcement, only.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13618,-5,-2,-1,'A Crudely Dug Tunnel','This tunnel looks like it either shouldn€t stand or like it should collapse at\nany moment.\nRoughly-hewn timbers frame the tunnel as if designed to give the appearance of\nreinforcement, only. Water drips steadily from the ceiling here, and a very\ntight diversion\nreinforced with boards leads to the northwest around a seemingly predictable\ncave-in\nto the west.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13619,-6,-1,-1,'Diversion Around a Cave-In','This diversion appears sturdy and well-designed by comparison to the tunnel it\ndiverts\nfrom. Boards are evenly placed behind a timber-frame and a pair of wide planks\nlaid on\nthe muddy ground make for a crude path. The cave-in barely looks settled.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,4,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13620,-7,-2,-1,'A Crudely Dug Tunnel','This tunnel looks like it either shouldn€t stand or like it should collapse at\nany moment.\nRoughly-hewn timbers frame the tunnel as if designed to give the appearance of\nreinforcement, only. A stream of water seeps from the mud and rocks of the\ncave-in to\nthe east, and a diversion cuts around the cave-in to the northeast.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13621,-8,-1,-1,'A Steep and Cramped Tunnel Leading Deeper','This tunnel is almost more of a narrow pit, so steep it can just barely be\nwalked and\nclimbed. A steady stream of water running down the middle of it further\ncomplicates travel.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13622,-8,-3,-1,'A Crudely Dug Tunnel','This tunnel looks like it either shouldn€t stand or like it should collapse at\nany moment.\nRoughly-hewn timbers frame the tunnel as if designed to give the appearance of\nreinforcement, only. The sounds of poultry strangely echo through the tunnel\nfrom the\nsouthwest.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13623,-9,-4,-1,'A Cavern Strewn with Feathers and Webbing','Large timbers frame out this long and wide cavern, and cages of chickens lining\nboth\nsides make the purpose of this chamber obvious. There are feathers and\nspider-webs\neverywhere, and a small ring of hay-bales in the middle of the cavern.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'Therias',1),
(13624,-9,-5,-1,'A Cavern Strewn with Feathers and Webbing','Large timbers frame out this long and wide cavern, and cages of chickens lining\nboth\nsides make the purpose of this chamber obvious. There are feathers and\nspider-webs\neverywhere, and a small ring of hay-bales in the middle of the cavern.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,120,0,'Therias',1),
(13625,-9,-6,-1,'A Narrow Passage','Straw covers the ground of this extremely tight and crudely-dug passage. There\nis barely\nenough room to move in here. It must lead somewhere.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,2,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13626,-8,-1,-2,'A Dimly-Lit and Half-Flooded Cavern','The tunnel here begins to break through hard shale, and water pours down through\nthe\ntunnel above but also likely through the shale itself. Thankfully the water\nlevels are only a\nfew feet deep, though it looks as though a good rainstorm would flood this\ncavern\ncompletely. Something about the water here triggers instinctive fear.\n',109,131080,27,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13627,-8,0,-2,'A Dimly-Lit and Half-Flooded Cavern','The tunnel here begins to break through hard shale, and water pours down through\nthe\ntunnel above but also likely through the shale itself. Thankfully the water\nlevels are only a\nfew feet deep, though it looks as though a good rainstorm would flood this\ncavern\ncompletely. Something about the water here triggers instinctive fear.\n',109,131080,27,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13628,-9,0,-2,'A Shale Beach in a Dimly-Lit Cavern','The pool of water flooding the cavern ends abruptly here against a bank of\nbroken\nshards of shale. The water must be draining away somewhere through the shale.\nThe\ntunnel continues deeper to the southwest, and into the pool to the east.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13629,-10,-1,-2,'Dimly-Lit Tunnel Beneath Grimhaven','This damp and dimly-lit tunnel is carved through brittle and crumbling shale.\nThe\nuneven floor crunches and scrapes underfoot as the shards of shale slide against\nshale,\nmaking passage hard to go unnoticed.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13630,-11,0,-2,'Dimly-Lit Tunnel Beneath Grimhaven','This damp and dimly-lit tunnel is carved through brittle and crumbling shale.\nThe\nuneven floor crunches and scrapes underfoot as the shards of shale slide against\nshale,\nmaking passage hard to go unnoticed. A ladder leans against the back wall of a\ntunnel-shaft rising up here.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
(13631,-12,-1,-2,'Dimly-Lit Tunnel Beneath Grimhaven','This damp and dimly-lit tunnel is carved through brittle and crumbling shale.\nThe\nuneven floor crunches and scrapes underfoot as the shards of shale slide against\nshale,\nmaking passage hard to go unnoticed.\n',109,131080,33,0,0,0,0,-1,0,100,0,'Therias',1),
