(16453,0,0,0,'<W>Drainage Pipe<z>','  This large, seemingly unused, drainage pipe is just big enough to allow\nsomeone to squeeze into.  Sloping down to the west the pipe becomes even\nsmaller.  To the east leads back into the sewers.\n',143,131080,33,0,0,0,0,0,3,43,0,'Vasco',101),
(34044,-47,-34,-1,'Atop A Ledge','This is a most awkward room to be in. To the near south, a treacherous sinkhole\ndisrupts the path, and directly below you the tunnel drops sharply for a dozen\nfeet or so.\nThe discrepancy in relative elevations is nauseating and vertigo begins to creep\nin.\nLuckily, the earth beneath you is fairly solid. Or so it seems to be...\n',276,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'Vasco',2),
(34045,-47,-34,-2,'Cobweb-filled Passage','Every surface of this area serves as a place for cobwebs to hang. The strands\nare thick\nand much stickier than any you have seen in other places. It is hard to orient\nyourself\namid the mass of webbing. Sounds of clicking alert you to the presence of some\ncreature nearby.\n',276,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'Vasco',2),
(34046,-48,-33,-2,'Cobweb-filled Passage','Every surface of this area serves as a place for cobwebs to hang. The strands\nare thick\nand much stickier than any you have seen in other places. It is hard to orient\nyourself\namid the mass of webbing. Sounds of clicking alert you to the presence of some\ncreature nearby.\n',276,8520,33,0,0,0,0,-1,11,100,0,'Vasco',2),
